        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002zqpn4AAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002zqpn4AAA/venture-trust",
            "name": "Venture Trust",
            "website": "https://www.venturetrust.org.uk",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hm5y5YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hm5y5YAB/impact-digital-storytelling-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-14",
                    "title": "Impact & Digital Storytelling Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHelp Share Stories That Change Lives\nAre you an experienced social media whiz or a talented student looking to boost your portfolio? We need your help! Venture Trust is searching for a passionate volunteer to create engaging content for our platforms.\n\nVenture Trust is looking for enthusiastic volunteers to help showcase the positive impact of our work in communities across Scotland. This is an exciting opportunity to gain experience in communications, marketing and digital storytelling while helping raise awareness of Venture Trust's impact and ensuring more people across Scotland can benefit from our programmes.\n\nAs an Impact & Digital Storytelling Volunteer, you'll help bring Venture Trust's work to life by gathering stories, creating engaging content and promoting opportunities and events across our platforms.\n\nWhether you're looking to build your portfolio, develop your skills or use your experience to make a difference, we'd love to hear from you.\n\nWhat You'll Do\n\nYou could:\n•\tSupport the creation of photography, video and multimedia content.\n•\tDevelop engaging content for social media, websites, newsletters, campaigns and publications.\n•\tCapture participant stories through case studies, blogs, interviews and impact content.\n•\tUpdate and maintain website content.\n•\tSupport email marketing and e-newsletter production.\n•\tAssist with the creation of marketing materials, brochures, presentations and promotional campaigns.\n\nNo two volunteering experiences will be exactly the same, and we'll work with you to shape the role around your interests and skills.\n\nAbout Venture Trust\n\nVenture Trust is dedicated to helping people facing challenging life circumstances, including trauma, poverty, involvement in the justice system, homelessness, and mental health issues. Through outdoor-based personal development programmes and therapeutic support, we empower individuals to build confidence, develop resilience, and make positive, lasting changes in their lives. By helping us share stories of change and achievement, you'll play an important role in raising awareness of our work and inspiring others to get involved.\n\nInterested?\n\nWe’d love to hear from you!\nEmail us at comms@venturetrust.org.uk\n\n## Experience required\n\nWhat We're Looking For\n\nWe're keen to hear from people who:\n•\tEnjoy storytelling and creating content.\n•\tHave an interest in social media, communications or marketing.\n•\tHave photography, videography or graphic design skills.\n•\tAre comfortable using social media platforms and design tools such as Canva and video editing software.\n•\tAre creative, organised and reliable.\n•\tHave good communication and people skills.\n•\tAre passionate about supporting people and communities across Scotland.\n\nIt Would Be Great If You Also Have\n•\tExperience creating content for organisations, clubs, charities or community groups.\n•\tAn interest in wellbeing, outdoor learning, employability or community development.\n\n## Training details\n\nWhat You'll Gain\n•\tPractical experience in communications, marketing and digital content creation.\n•\tOpportunities to build your portfolio and develop new skills.\n•\tTraining, guidance and ongoing support from the Venture Trust team.\n•\tExperience working with a national charity making a real difference across Scotland.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThere’s no formal application process – just tell us a little about yourself and how you’d like to get involved. We’ll work out together what fits your time and interests.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a home-based opportunity.",
