                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FiDDpYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FiDDpYAN/volunteer-fundraising-support",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-30",
                    "title": "Volunteer Fundraising Support",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSOHTIS is a growing, vibrant and dynamic organisation, with justice at it's heart.  We are eager to go further, reaching many more victims and survivors of human trafficking across Scotland.  In order to achieve our this, we are looking for likeminded, justice seeking, people to help us to build and diversify our funding streams.  The Volunteer Fundraising Supporter will work with senior members of the team to identify and support the development of diverse funding streams.   This could include: community fundraising, retailing, grant funding and other opportunities.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers should have either excellent literacy skills for, ie. preparing newsletters, written communications, grant funding applications and/or confidence in verbal communications, ie. advertising fundraising initiatives to local community groups, faith groups, or others.\n\n## Training details\n\nHuman trafficking awareness training will be provided and induction to SOHTIS work.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nNo minimum commitment.  According to volunteers availability.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMinimum travel requirements.  Use of SOHTIS facilities in Glasgow and/or Edinburgh.  Remote working possible.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReimbursement of expenses as agreed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FiDDpYAN#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Fundraising Support",
                        "description": "Volunteers should have either excellent literacy skills for, ie. preparing newsletters, written communications, grant funding applications and/or confidence in verbal communications, ie. advertising fundraising initiatives to local community groups, faith groups, or others.",
                        "commitment": "No minimum commitment.  According to volunteers availability.",
                        "applyLink": "https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfbaFP5A5H47uzH8Ps81vmxxaqtzqyes9S6nayEOdQ5-7gsFg/viewform?usp=header",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": true,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/AntiPoverty",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Anti-Poverty"
                            },
