        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002sVE8DAAW",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002sVE8DAAW/girvan-prom-parkrun-sa",
            "name": "Girvan Prom Parkrun (SA)",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhnbLAAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhnbLAAR/girvan-prom-parkrun-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2023-02-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-02",
                    "title": "Girvan Prom Parkrun Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nVolunteering at parkrun is an opportunity to get outside, make new friends, have fun, learn new skills and to be a valuable part of your local community. We are always looking for new volunteers. This page explains how to get involved.\r\n\r\nWhat would I do at the Event?\r\nFirst, and most importantly, we never ask anybody to do anything they're not comfortable with. If you don't want a particular task, please let us know and we will happily give you an alternative job. Nevertheless, none of our tasks are too stressful. You could be marshaling, or using the parkrun volunteer app to record times or scan barcodes, operating the timer, or scanning barcodes using the simple Virtual Volunteer app. If you really want to do something in particular, please let us know and we'll see what we can do. To find out more, please visit our website https://www.parkrun.org.uk/girvanprom/ or have a look at our page on Facebook.\r\n\r\nThe core team: Girvan Prom parkrun happens largely because of our fantastic volunteers. The weekly team of volunteers are led by a small group of parkrun enthusiasts who form what we call the 'core team': They make sure the event is setup and packed away each week, the results published, the tokens resorted, event reports written and so much more.\r\n\r\nEvent Director - Moira McDowall. We're very grateful to the help provided by everybody, both now and in the past, who've helped make Girvan Prom parkrun happen.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nEvery Saturday at 9:30am. https://www.parkrun.org.uk/girvanprom/futureroster/",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F2293c393-6d28-47d7-b6b6-b287df4b1830%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=dbdc7aa4-8bf5-4edd-a5ba-73bb35dd4823",
