        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002sVFlgAAG",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002sVFlgAAG/abbeyfield-monifieth-society-ltd",
            "name": "Abbeyfield (Monifieth) Society Ltd",
            "description": "Abbeyfield is an organisation providing independent living for older people. We provide very sheltered en-suite accommodation for up to 12 tenants at Tullis House in Monifieth. Lunch and Dinner are prepared, cooked and served daily in the dining room and ingredients for breakfast and teas and coffees are provided in shared kitchens for tenants own use.",
            "website": "https://www.abbeyfield.com",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC000267"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/HousingAssociation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Housing Association"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000GvZbCAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000GvZbCAAV/treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTreasurer to join our Committee in running the financial side of Tullis House, Monifieth, Computer based accounting, income, expenditure, producing monthly accounts, paying suppliers and finalising for auditors and charity commission (OSCR).\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteer required as Treasurer with financial skills to carry out the day to day computer based work involving income and expenditure of the house then reporting accounts to the Executive Committee on a monthly basis at meetings.\r\n\r\nControlling income from rents and paying suppliers, approximately 12 - 15 monthly accounts, payed by cheque or bank transfer. Setting budgets, Supervising Staff wages which are currently processed by an outside company but net wages figures returned to us to be paid by bank transfer. Yearly accounts for auditors as well as Charity Commission (OSCR).\r\n\r\nTime required to carry out work would be approximately 2 hours per week with extra time at the end of the month producing the figures for the monthly meetings.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA financial background in Accountancy.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe volunteer would have to be experienced in Accounting so training would not really by required - just an Induction into what Abbeyfield is and what would be required of them.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nApproximately 2-3 hours weekly controlling day to day accounting and extra each month to produce monthly accounts. Also attend monthly Executive Committee meetings on a Wednesday evening.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTullis House, 6-8 Maule Street, Monifieth, Angus, DD5 4JN\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note: No expenses are paid for this opportunity\n\n## Taster details\n\nAttend a monthly meeting to find out all about Abbeyfield and discuss the position with the current Treasurer who can give them an idea of exactly what the work entails.",
