        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002sVLuLAAW",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002sVLuLAAW/police-scotland-south-ayrshire",
            "name": "Police Scotland (South Ayrshire)",
            "website": "https://www.scotland.police.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunitySafety",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Safety"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhnZ5AAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhnZ5AAJ/police-scotland-youth-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2023-02-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Police Scotland Youth Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nPSYV is the Police Scotland Youth Volunteering programme  that  aims to strengthen relationships with young people, break down barriers and promote ways to make Scotland's communities safer. We're open to applications from young people aged 13 – 17 that wish to gain an insight into policing in Scotland and want to do something positive in their communities. \r\n\r\nEach PSYV group consists of 24 young people who each give up their own time to volunteer on their communities. As a youth volunteer, you would be expected to complete the PSYV initial training programme which will prepare you for attending local and national volunteering events. The training contains multiple subjects across three units.\r\n- About the programme\r\n- Standards\r\n- Operational PSYV training\r\n\r\nThis training and subsequent local 'sessions' take place at a local venue on a weekly or fortnightly basis. During these sessions, youth volunteers will take part in additional training, educational inputs from the police and partner agencies as well as preparing for upcoming volunteering opportunities.\r\n\r\nIf you live in Scotland and are aged between 13-15 register your interest. You must attend weekly sessions and attend regular volunteering events in your community and occasionally other parts of the country. \r\n\r\nDiscover more about the training and support you will receive if you are selected as a Police Scotland Youth Volunteer. If your local group are recruiting, your local coordinator will be in touch to discuss the recruitment process. Please note that not all groups are actively recruiting and spaces are limited in all groups due to the popularity of the programme.\r\n\r\n​\n\n## Taster details\n\nAs a PSYV member you have the opportunity to gain qualifications for the training and volunteering that you do.\r\n \r\nYou can gain a PSYV Award with SCQF Level 4 accreditation awarded by  the Police Scotland College. This is useful as you move into college, university, work and adult life.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F540133ca-612a-4060-9a5a-f23060c9b52e%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=1a7c2ff3-aa44-440f-94a1-0b0af4758d9b",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhnZ5AAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Police Scotland Youth Volunteers",
                        "applyLink": "https://www.scotland.police.uk/secureforms/psyv-recruitment/",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "13",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/GeneralPublic",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "General Public"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/LocalAuthority",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Local Authority"
