                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhnZFAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhnZFAAZ/police-scotland-adult-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2023-02-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Police Scotland Adult Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe PSYV is heavily reliant on the goodwill of Adult Volunteers who give up their time to suport their local PSYV group and assist with the supervision of the Youth Volunteers at both local sessions and volunteering events.\r\n\r\nSee below for a list of groups across Scotland.\r\n\r\nEligibility\r\n\r\nTo become an Adult Volunteer you must be at least 18 years of age and be able to dedicate a minimum of three hours per month for volunteering events.\r\n\r\nEach Adult Volunteer will be required to join the Protecting Vulnerable Groups Scheme (PVG). This process will be managed by PSYV once you are accepted into the programme.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fb50a3ac9-560d-4a3a-bd3d-b06058233096%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=d331b579-3963-4cf5-8df7-e8d656d96341",
