        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002sXDqMAAW",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002sXDqMAAW/carrick-community-chest-heart-stroke-group",
            "name": "Carrick Community Chest, Heart & Stroke Group",
            "website": "https://www.chss.org.uk/group/carrick-community-chss/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7LN1AAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7LN1AAN/peer-support-volunteer-carrick-community-chest-heart-stroke-group",
                    "publishStart": "2022-12-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-19",
                    "title": "Peer Support Volunteer - Carrick Community Chest Heart & Stroke Group",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nChest Heart & Stroke Scotland supports groups across Scotland to meet the needs of people living with chest and heart conditions and following a stroke. Peer support groups give people the chance to share experiences with others who understand what they are going through. \r\n\r\nPeer support groups have various reasons for coming together. It may be to meet socially, take part in physical activity or learn how to live well with their condition. Each group is unique and tailored to the needs of its local community. Everyone involved with the group will have a say in how the group is run.  \r\n\r\nTasks may include setting up and clearing the room; organising refreshments; taking the register, and collecting subs; meeting, and greeting new members; organising, and taking part in the programme of activities; supporting, and taking part in fundraising (e.g., raffles); promoting the group; and working to the group’s health & safety and other procedures.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe ability to work with people and understand their needs; an awareness of boundaries; effective communication and listening skills; the ability to work confidentially.\n\n## Training details\n\nCHSS will provide training to support you in your role. Training may include First Aid; Infection and Prevention Control; and Moving and Handling.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCarrick Community Chest Heart & Stroke Group runs every Wednesday 10-12pm\n\n## Travel details\n\nSouth Parish Church, Montgomerie St, Girvan, KA26 9HE",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
