                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GYb5bYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GYb5bYAD/garden-volunteers-at-kyle-chemotherapy-unit-ayr-hospital",
                    "publishStart": "2022-11-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-09",
                    "title": "Garden Volunteers at Kyle Chemotherapy Unit, Ayr Hospital",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHelp us create a healing garden.\r\nWe are keen to recruit some volunteer gardeners to help look after Kyle garden on Ailsa Hospital. We are looking to create a rota of volunteers to help with light maintenance in the garden as soon as practical. \r\nTasks include: \r\nPlanting and weeding\r\nWatering and pruning\r\nMaking a difference for patients\r\n\r\nFlexible Hours. No experience required.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWhilst these roles are available Monday - Friday, morning and afternoon, we would not anticipate any individual volunteering any more than four hours a day, with a minimum commitment of two hours per week.  A rota will be developed to incorporate shifts and this will be co-ordinated by the local manager in charge.\n\n## Travel details\n\nPublic transport available",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F24ea249b-a43c-6baf-a2d4-c10e3afc7cc6%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=e2006a59-1947-44d0-b8e6-6efdaf44ab7a",
