            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7LmLAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7LmLAAV/volunteer-work-parties",
                    "publishStart": "2023-01-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-29",
                    "title": "Volunteer Work Parties",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are a small charity concerned with the restoration and care of the ancient woodlands of Troon. \r\nWe have been in operation since 2015, raising funds for improvements and planting. We host regular volunteer work parties, tackling jobs such as invasive species control, tree planting and repairing paths. Together with the South Ayrshire Ranger Service and Scottish Wildlife Trust, Ayrshire, we regularly involve schools and community groups in woodland activities.\r\nOur volunteer work parties are usually held on the last Sunday of the month, 10am-12noon. \r\nNo experience or tools required. We have tasks to suit all abilities. Age 15 and over. Meet us at the noticeboard, wear study footwear and clothing to protect you from brambles and nettles. Please come and give it a try - there's no commitment to turn up every time!\r\nPlease come and give us a hand - it's great fun!\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience required, just the joy of being outdoors and meeting like minded people with an interest in gardening/environmental conservation.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F154a56bb-3012-3707-241a-a283c91a4155%2F0nFCUqNjeiXPIFO483j0BVWArU43%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=cfee5087-6abb-46ff-886e-0fcaf7623314",
