        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002sU6w6AAC",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002sU6w6AAC/oshays-brain-domains",
            "name": "Oshay's Brain Domains",
            "description": "Oshay's Brain Domain's FASD (Fetal Alcohol Spectrum Disorders) has a new premises called The Centre in Ayr. We offer support for families, schools and professionals to understand the neurobehavioral approaches of children affected by FASD. We provide sensory groups for all ages, parent support groups and birth parent support group. Offering a non-judgmental and safe place for carers to share their experiences.",
            "website": "https://www.oshays.org/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000048lVhYAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000048lVhYAI/child-contact-centre-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2024-06-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-20",
                    "title": "Child Contact Centre Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOshay’s Centre is the home of Oshay's Brain Domains CIC which focuses on Fetal Alcohol Spectrum Disorder (FASD) education and advocacy. It provides education to professionals, schools, parents, and children about what FASD is and how it affects individuals’ brains and those around them. Oshay’s also offers resources and a sense of community to empower and support families and professionals working with individuals with brain-based disabilities. Additionally, our work extends to supporting various neurodiverse conditions like ADHD, Trauma, Autism, Dyspraxia, and Dyslexia, falling under the umbrella of “Neurodiversity.” Additionally, we have recently launched a much needed Child Contact, Mediation and Counselling Service within our Centre.\r\n\r\nOshay's are currently looking to recruit Child Contact Centre volunteers to facilitate supported or supervised child contact.\r\nThe central concept of a child contact centre is to offer a safe, friendly, neutral, child-centred environment for children to meet their non-resident parent or family member. They are designed to be a stepping stone to a more permanent arrangement for future contact.\r\n\r\nParents/family members can spend time with their children in a supported or supervised context.  They can also use the centres to collect and return the children to the other parent at the start and end of visits.  Adults do not have to see or speak to each other at contact centres.\r\n\r\nPlease see link for further information regarding our Contact Centre. https://www.oshays.org/oshay-s-contact-centre/\r\n\r\nDo you think you have the common sense and communication skills to effectively and safely support and/or supervise child contact sessions? Are you reliable and responsible?\r\n\r\nPlease email info@oshays.org to find out more.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication skills. \r\nCommon sense and understanding\r\nGood with children, able to be flexible.\r\nDependable and reliable\n\n## Training details\n\nAdditional relevant core training will be provided as required.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nOut of pocket expenses paid.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fcad0bada-70c6-0875-93d5-2c6ac3372e86%2F0nFCUqNjeiXPIFO483j0BVWArU43%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=6bd4428e-8aee-4dfe-af42-afa8c4c45325",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000048lVhYAI#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Child Contact Centre Volunteer",
                        "description": "Good communication skills. \r\nCommon sense and understanding\r\nGood with children, able to be flexible.\r\nDependable and reliable",
