        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002sUS2jAAG",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002sUS2jAAG/troon-community-council",
            "name": "Troon Community Council",
            "website": "https://www.trooncommunitycouncil.co.uk/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityCouncil",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Council"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GhPBeYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GhPBeYAN/secretary",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Secretary",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteer Secretary to support the work of Troon Community Council.\n\n## Description\n\nCommunity Councils are voluntary bodies which exist within a statutory framework and which have been granted statutory rights of consultation. The general purpose of the Troon Community Council is to ascertain, co-ordinate and express the wider views of the entire community within its boundaries. Community Councils will seek to represent and include all sections of their communities, regardless of age, gender, ability, ethnic origin, political or religious beliefs, or sexual orientation. They can complement the role of the local authority but are not part of local government.\r\n\r\nTroon Community Council are volunteers working to improve our town. We meet first Tuesday of every month at 7pm for a couple of hours,  (once or twice it has been 10pm, but that's very rare).  Though working under the Council umbrella, we are not affiliated to any one party, the 4 Ward Councillors attend, take back any information and they update us on anything they are aware of. \r\n\r\nWe are currently looking to recruit a volunteer Secretary.\r\nThe duties entail taking minutes at the meetings, then  distributing them via email to our community councillors and ward councillors, preparing agendas, and sending any communication if and when requested. \r\nWe have a great group of like minded people working to improve the town, and organise events, our Secretary would be more than welcome to participate in anything we do. \r\nExpenses would be covered.\r\n\r\nFor further information about this volunteering opportunity please call Diane on 07849006768",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fb328e087-b875-43d3-9010-5ded751c8545%2Fgpx6nnIWvxXFMLCpJdEzZH9maTg1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=562b4fde-40cc-47c0-981b-81a1d2d45b7e",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GhPBeYAN#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Secretary",
                        "applyLink": "https://www.trooncommunitycouncil.co.uk/",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
