                    "skos:prefLabel": "Charity Shop"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Helplines",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Helplines"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000CLrGwYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000CLrGwYAL/peer-group-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-09-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Peer Group Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nA new peer support group for people who have experienced a stroke or a brain injury has begun in Loanhead.  The purpose of the group is to bring people with these conditions together to socialise and gain support from others with shared experiences. Volunteers will help to provide a safe space for these people to support each other and try some new activities.\n\n## Experience required\n\nIt would be helpful to have some knowledge of stroke or brain injury either personal or in a caring role. The ability to get along with people and encourage them to try new things is essential.  A positive attitude and a supportive, caring approach is vital.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe current group in Bonnyrigg will offer mentoring and training in the beginning. Ongoing support will be given by the group leader and any training opportunities will be shared from CHSS.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe venue is The Loanhead Leisure Centre, George Avenue, Loanhead EH20 9LA",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
