            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000004mDALYA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000004mDALYA2/friends-of-rotary-general-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2024-07-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-29",
                    "title": "Friends of Rotary (general volunteer)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nRotary is a global network,1.4 million strong, who see a world where people unite and take action to create lasting change-in our communities, across the world and in ourselves.\r\nAyr Rotary Club is one of 46,000 clubs worldwide. We are very active in the local community supporting many charities. Examples of our current projects include a cycling event, a Primary Schools careers fair, fundraising for Poppy Scotland, a beach clean, Food bank support, youth pubiic speaking competitions, and a charity golf tournament. \r\nMembers aim to enjoy “fun and friendship while helping others”\r\nIt’s a great way to meet like-minded people and make long-lasting friendships.\r\nMen and women of all ages are welcome, and you choose the type of activities you would like to be involved with. \r\nThere are lots of different ways to become involved with Ayr Rotary, and you don’t have to become a member. With many projects ongoing, we always require help from non-members. We call our regular helpers and volunteers “Friends of Rotary”\r\nIf you have skills, experience or talents to offer, and would like to give something back to the community, we would love to hear from you!",
