        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002w7eYWAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002w7eYWAAY/aberdeen-independent-ms-aims",
            "name": "Aberdeen Independent MS (AIMS)",
            "description": "AIMS is a community which empowers people living with MS and similar neurological conditions to lead independent lives by providing accessible exercise, social connection and wellbeing support.\r\n\r\nWe run a range of digital activities via Zoom, from chair based exercise classes , mindful movement, seated yoga and mindfulness, to weekly online socials and online quizzes. In addition we have two weekly face to face exercise classes at Westhill, and arrange monthly coffee meet ups across Aberdeen city and Shire.\r\n\r\nDue to popular demand, we are looking to expand our activities in the next couple of months to include two new face to face classes  ( Technogym and Pilates)  two new online classes ( Seated Zumba and Stable and Able ).",
            "website": "https://www.youraims.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC051225"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IAR4oYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IAR4oYAH/activity-volunteers-milltimber-group",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-06",
                    "title": "Activity Volunteers - Milltimber Group",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you have a couple of hours to spare on a Friday afternoon? Are you looking for an opportunity to volunteer with a local group who support people living locally with MS and other neurological conditions? Do you enjoy meeting with and chatting to new people? If so, we would like to hear from you! \r\n\r\nWe are expanding our activities and are looking for an additional volunteer to assist with our new Pilates class which takes place at Milltimber Community Hall, The Meadows, Milltimber, AB13 0JT every Friday afternoon. You will help set up the session, get equipment ready and tidy everything away afterwards and will provide support to the participants and the class instructor, ensuring everything runs smoothly. You will help the host to create a welcoming, supportive and friendly space in line with our mission to empower people living with MS and similar neurological conditions to lead independent lives by providing accessible exercise, social connection, and wellbeing support and may also be asked to deputise for the host on occasion of their absence.\r\n\r\nExcellent support and guidance is provided to all volunteers on an ongoing basis. AIMS has recently been awarded a Kings Award for Voluntary Service in recognition of their outstanding volunteering and the positive difference we make for people and the community.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to make a real difference! All help is greatly appreciated. \r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Sandra Rosie, Administrator and Trustee at email:  sandra.rosie@youraims.org\r\n\r\nFurther details about Aberdeen Independent MS (AIMS) is also available at www.youraims.org and https://www.facebook.com/aberdeenMSsupport/\n\n## Description\n\nDo you have a couple of hours to spare on a Friday afternoon? Are you looking for an opportunity to volunteer with a local group who support people living locally with MS and other neurological conditions? Do you enjoy meeting with and chatting to new people? If so, we would like to hear from you! \r\n\r\nWe are expanding our activities and are looking for an additional volunteer to assist with our new Pilates class which takes place at Milltimber Community Hall, The Meadows, Milltimber, AB13 0JT every Friday afternoon. You will help set up the session, get equipment ready and tidy everything away afterwards and will provide support to the participants and the class instructor, ensuring everything runs smoothly. You will help the host to create a welcoming, supportive and friendly space in line with our mission to empower people living with MS and similar neurological conditions to lead independent lives by providing accessible exercise, social connection, and wellbeing support and may also be asked to deputise for the host on occasion of their absence.\r\n\r\nExcellent support and guidance is provided to all volunteers on an ongoing basis. AIMS has recently been awarded a Kings Award for Voluntary Service in recognition of their outstanding volunteering and the positive difference we make for people and the community.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to make a real difference! All help is greatly appreciated. \r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Sandra Rosie, Administrator and Trustee at email:  sandra.rosie@youraims.org\r\n\r\nFurther details about Aberdeen Independent MS (AIMS) is also available at www.youraims.org and https://www.facebook.com/aberdeenMSsupport/\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. Initially you will shadow one of our other co-ordinators who will also be able to provide support on an ongoing basis. \r\n\r\nAIMS have also been awarded a Kings Award for Voluntary Service in recognition of the outstanding volunteering at AIMS and positive difference we make for people and the community.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMeets at Milltimber Community Hall, The Meadows, Milltimber, AB13 0JT every Friday afternoon.\r\n\r\nAll help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTakes place at Milltimber Community Hall, The Meadows, Milltimber, AB13 0JT every Friday afternoon",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F082960d5-f5d1-4181-a8a8-2877910f8b8b%2FERE2jXPfcZZQ4iWUdOYIFX0Y8bH3%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=99bd29c4-6d0a-4310-be31-ffd6eb60a91b",
