                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IWMO1YAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IWMO1YAP/social-media-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-12",
                    "title": "Social Media Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAre you looking for an opportunity to demonstrate your social media skills? Would you like to volunteer with a local group who support people with MS and other neurological conditions, their families and carers? Can you spare a few hours each week to develop innovative and eye-catching content to promote our various activities on Facebook and Instagram? If so, we would love to hear from you!\r\n\r\nExcellent support and guidance is provided to all volunteers on an ongoing basis. AIMS has recently been awarded a Kings Award for Voluntary Service in recognition of their outstanding volunteering and the positive difference we make for people and the community.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to make a real difference! All help is greatly appreciated. \r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Sandra Rosie, Administrator and Trustee at email:  sandra.rosie@youraims.org\r\n\r\nFurther details about Aberdeen Independent MS (AIMS) is also available at www.youraims.org and https://www.facebook.com/aberdeenMSsupport/\n\n## Description\n\nAre you looking for an opportunity to demonstrate your social media skills? Would you like to volunteer with a local group who support people with MS and other neurological conditions, their families and carers? Can you spare a few hours each week to develop innovative and eye-catching content to promote our various activities on Facebook and Instagram? If so, we would love to hear from you!\r\n\r\nExcellent support and guidance is provided to all volunteers. You will report to the Trustee Administrator and support will be provided on an ongoing basis. AIMS has also been awarded a Kings Award for Voluntary Service in recognition of their outstanding volunteering and the positive difference we make for people and the community.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to make a real difference! All help is greatly appreciated. \r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Sandra Rosie, Administrator and Trustee at email:  sandra.rosie@youraims.org\r\n\r\nFurther details about Aberdeen Independent MS (AIMS) is also available at www.youraims.org and https://www.facebook.com/aberdeenMSsupport/\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. You will report to the Trustee Administrator and support will be provided on an ongoing basis.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times to volunteer. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCan be undertaken from home with the occasional meetings to attend either face to face or via zoom.",
