                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000006PmSbYAK",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000006PmSbYAK/volunteer-e-commerce-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2024-10-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-07",
                    "title": "Volunteer E-commerce assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWith a network of over 10 shops, including our online shop our diverse volunteers play an integral role in championing Ayrshire Hospice values, running the shops, working in our warehouse and promoting our messaging to the wider community.\r\nThe Role\r\nAre you a current or an aspiring ecommerce enthusiast looking to show off your online selling or marketing skills? You have the opportunity to showcase your skills and have your knowledge and enthusiasm used for social media and our online\r\nEbay platform and much more!\r\nAs an E-Commerce Volunteer you’ll be behind the scenes in our busy shops, learning all about selling donated gems through the Ayrshire Hospice Online Shop and other selling platforms. \r\nYou can get involved in everything from researching, describing, photographing, to posting. \r\nBest of all you will be helping to support our patients and families across Ayrshire.\n\n## Description\n\nBackground\r\nThe Ayrshire Hospice provides excellence in palliative and end of life care for patients and their families. \r\nWe support people who are aged 16 years and over, who have a diagnosis that is life limiting - this includes respiratory and heart diseases, neurological conditions as well as cancers and other illnesses. In addition, our Family Care Team also support children and young people – as well as the wider family unit – with counselling and bereavement services.\r\nWhere necessary, we provide a seamless transition from young adult hospice services to our care. Our care seeks to improve quality of life in various ways, for example; we support and advise on symptom control, provide emotional and spiritual care, social care and we provide personal care when it is needed at the end of life. \r\n\r\nWe also have pharmacy, physiotherapy and occupational therapy specialist services as well as our much-valued complementary therapy and Respite and Response services. Care is provided in a number of places including NHS Ayrshire and Arran hospitals, care homes and people’s own homes as well as in our In-Patient Unit and Living Well Hubs. In fact, we can provide care anywhere a person considers their home to be, regardless of the complexities associated with this. \r\nFamily members, close friends and carers are also supported both during a person’s illness and in bereavement.\r\n\r\nThe Role\r\nAre you a current or an aspiring ecommerce enthusiast looking to show off your online selling or marketing skills? You have the opportunity to showcase your skills and have your knowledge and enthusiasm used for social media and our online Ebay platform and much more!\r\nAs an E-Commerce Volunteer you’ll be behind the scenes in our busy shops, learning all about selling donated gems through the Ayrshire Hospice Online Shop and other selling platforms. \r\nYou can get involved in everything from researching, describing, photographing, to posting. \r\nBest of all you will be helping to support our patients and families across Ayrshire.\r\n\r\nKey responsibilities\r\nProvide excellent customer service\r\nOperating an EPOS till (full training provided)\r\nIdentify appropriate donated stock to sell on our online platforms\r\nPhotograph, edit & list Items on eBay with an accurate description\r\nSafely and securely pack up sold items to be sent out to customers\r\nAttend external events selling various new and pre-loved goods \r\nGeneral housekeeping duties\r\nRefer any enquiries, requests or complaints to appropriate person\r\n professionally and in line with our values.\r\nAttendance at relevant training and team meetings\r\nAdherence to the relevant policies and procedures of the hospice\r\n\r\nWhat you will gain\r\nThe opportunity to gain experience in the charity sector\r\nTake on a new challenge and meet new people\r\nOpportunity to make a difference to your community\r\nLearn and develop new skills and use existing skills to help others\r\nTraining and support to carry out your role\r\nReimbursement of expenses in accordance with our volunteer expenses policy\r\n\r\nIf you’re passionate about volunteering with us and want to make a meaningful impact in your community, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today to join our team and help us capture the heart of the Ayrshire Hospice. Please complete our enquiry form, which can be found on our website:\r\nAlternatively, call 01292 269200 to request a paper copy of the enquiry form. All successful applicants will be expected to attend a ‘get to know you chat’ and training before being appointed as an Ayrshire Hospice volunteer.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe Ayrshire Hospice welcomes applications from all sections of the community.\r\nExperience is not essential for this role, but ideally you should demonstrate:\r\nEssential Skills\r\nIT literacy.\r\n\r\nDesirable Skills\r\n\r\nCreativity, with a good eye for composition and ideas for eye catching images.\r\nAn interest in or experience of working in online selling platforms (eBay)\r\nGood knowledge of Microsoft packages\r\nComfortable using a digital camera\r\nAbility to work independently and as part of a team\r\nGood customer service and communication skills\r\nResponsible and reliable\r\nFriendly and approachable manner\r\nCreative merchandising skills\r\nCompetent numeracy skills\n\n## Travel details\n\ntravel expenses are paid\n\n## Travel expenses\n\ntravel costs refunded",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F8bf0b2d1-5d3e-8401-97a3-7866e02f5452%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=48c2845e-f374-4263-a87e-cab479edff6b",
