        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002wkoV0AAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002wkoV0AAI/rnib-scotland-sa",
            "name": "RNIB Scotland (SA)",
            "website": "https://www.rnib.org.uk/scotland",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC039316"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SensoryImpairment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005Dxx3YAC",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005Dxx3YAC/sooty-box-collectors",
                    "publishStart": "2024-08-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-15",
                    "title": "Sooty Box Collectors",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAbout RNIB\r\nWe are the Royal National Institute of Blind People (RNIB).\r\nEvery six minutes, someone in the UK begins to lose their sight. RNIB is taking a stand against exclusion, inequality and isolation to create a world without barriers where people with sight loss can lead full lives. A different world where society values blind and partially sighted people not for the disabilities they’ve overcome, but for the people they are.\r\nRNIB. \r\n\r\nThe Royal National Institute of Blind People (RNIB) celebrates Sooty’s 75th anniversary by launching a new Sooty Collection Box, which has been given a modernised glow-up.  \r\n\r\nSooty, the loveable bear and national treasure, has been a feature on RNIB’s collection boxes for over fifty years. The funds raised during this time have been millions, enabling the charity to support people with sight loss in Scotland and across the UK. \r\n\r\nContinuing the momentum of Sooty’s 75th anniversary*, RNIB has updated the Sooty boxes to reflect the 21st century. The sleek design includes brighter colours and a QR code that allows people to make a cashless donation by using their mobile phone to scan the code, which then leads donors to a donation page on their device’s browser. Supporters can choose any amount they would like to donate as well as registering for Gift Aid. \r\n\r\nRNIB Scotland are calling for people particularly in Glasgow, Dumfries and Ayrshire to join the community of incredible volunteer Sooty Box Collectors to help find a home for the Sooty boxes, to empty them as required and raise funds for blind and partially sighted people. \r\n\r\nNeil Grainey, Senior Stewardship Manager, said: “RNIB is incredibly lucky to have a network of amazing volunteers across the UK who dedicate their time to place our iconic Sooty Boxes in their local community. We’re thrilled to begin finding homes for our fantastic new Sooty Boxes, as well as being able to offer our supporters the option to make a cashless donation too.”\r\nFor more information about Sooty Boxes, please visit: www.rnib.org.uk/sooty.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining and information about current locations of Sooty boxes will be provided",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F79a289cb-d4e1-44b4-9353-0329d8fcf546%2F0nFCUqNjeiXPIFO483j0BVWArU43%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=f6a1dc5d-947c-4311-89b6-f73490a7d855",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005Dxx3YAC#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Sooty Box Collectors",
                        "applyLink": "https://www.rnib.org.uk/get-involved/fundraise/find-a-home-for-sooty/",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/GeneralPublic",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "General Public"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/PhysicalDisability",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/SensoryImpairment",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                            }
                        ],
                        "reward": [
