                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IGPL6YAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IGPL6YAP/counselling-feedback-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-30",
                    "title": "Counselling Feedback Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCounselling Feedback Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nAre you a good listener who can put people at ease over the telephone? Help RNIB understand people&rsquo;s experiences of its counselling service and improve support for blind and partially sighted people.\n\nAs a Counselling Feedback Volunteer, you will telephone people who have recently completed counselling sessions with RNIB&rsquo;s Sight Loss Counselling Team. Using a prepared script, you will gather feedback about their experiences and help RNIB understand the impact of the service.\n\nWhat you will be doing\n\n\n\tCalling people who have recently completed telephone counselling.\n\tBuilding rapport and helping them feel comfortable sharing feedback.\n\tFollowing a scripted evaluation to ask about their experiences.\n\tListening carefully and responding sensitively.\n\tAccurately recording responses to help RNIB evaluate and improve its service.\n\n\nYour role is to gather feedback; you will not be providing counselling.\n\nWho would suit this role?\n\nThis opportunity would suit someone with a calm, friendly telephone manner who enjoys listening to others. You should be comfortable discussing people&rsquo;s experiences sensitively and working independently from home, with support from RNIB.\n\nLocation and time commitment\n\nThis role is home based and can be carried out in Scotland.\n\nCalls take place Monday to Friday, between 9am and 5pm. Volunteering can be arranged across more than one weekday or on a single day.\n\nRNIB lists a commitment of two hours per week, although its description also mentions four hours. Please confirm the expected weekly commitment with the coordinator when applying.\n\nTraining and support\n\nYou will receive RNIB volunteer training and safeguarding training, alongside ongoing support from your volunteer manager.\n\nA prepared evaluation script will guide your conversations and help you gather feedback consistently.\n\nRequirements\n\n\n\tYou must be aged 18 or over.\n\tOne reference is required.\n\tYou will need access to a laptop or PC with Microsoft Word.\n\tYou should be available to make calls during weekday daytime hours.\n\n\nHow to apply and what happens next\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call.\n\nIf you have not heard back after five working days, the first step is to contact the organisation using the contact details provided. Please also check your email junk/spam folder in case the response is there. If you are still unable to make contact, please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\nThe coordinator will discuss the role, your availability and the next steps in RNIB&rsquo;s volunteer recruitment process, including the required reference. This is also an opportunity to confirm the weekly commitment and ask any questions about the role.\n\nIf you are offered a placement, you will receive volunteer and safeguarding training, with ongoing support from your volunteer manager.\n\nPlease note: Applying expresses your interest and does not guarantee a volunteering placement.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tGood listening skills and a friendly telephone manner.\n•\tAbility to build rapport and put people at ease.\n•\tSensitivity and respect when discussing personal experiences.\n•\tConfidence using IT equipment, systems and Microsoft Word.\n•\tAbility to follow a prepared script and record feedback accurately.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a home-based volunteering role, so no regular travel is required. You will carry out telephone calls and record feedback remotely, using your own laptop or PC with Microsoft Word.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease ask your RNIB volunteer coordinator whether any costs, including telephone calls, are reimbursed and how to claim them.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
