                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IGEb1YAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IGEb1YAH/library-collections-digital-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-30",
                    "title": "Library Collections Digital Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nLibrary Collections Digital Assistant\n\n## Description\n\nHelp make books more accessible to blind and partially sighted people while putting your digital skills to good use from home.\n\nRNIB Talking Books has been a much-loved service for 90 years. By joining the Library Collections Team, you will help more blind and partially sighted people around the world enjoy access to talking books and other digital library materials.\n\nWhat you will be doing\n\nYou will support the team with downloading, transferring, organising and accurately recording digital materials. Your tasks will include:\n\n\n\tKeeping digital collection records accurate and up to date.\n\tCarrying out quality checks and spotting errors or inconsistencies.\n\tIdentifying and resolving basic digital issues when they arise.\n\tLiaising with library colleagues and supporting the team&rsquo;s work.\n\n\nYou will gain experience in digital administration and library services while contributing to a team from home.\n\nWho would suit this role?\n\nThis opportunity would suit someone who enjoys working with digital information, is organised and has a careful eye for detail. You should be comfortable working independently while also contributing to a team.\n\nLocation and time commitment\n\nThis role is home based, with a commitment of three hours per week.\n\nSpecific volunteering days and times should be discussed with RNIB during the application process.\n\nTraining and support\n\nYou will receive RNIB volunteer training and safeguarding training, alongside ongoing support from your volunteer manager. You will also work with colleagues in the Library Collections Team.\n\nOut-of-pocket expenses incurred through the role are covered.\n\nRequirements\n\n\n\tYou must be aged 16 or over.\n\tOne reference is required.\n\tYou will need access to your own computer.\n\n\nHow to apply and what happens next\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call.\n\nIf you have not heard back after five working days, the first step is to contact the organisation using the contact details provided. Please also check your email junk/spam folder in case the response is there. If you are still unable to make contact, please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\nRNIB will discuss the opportunity, your availability and the next steps in its volunteer recruitment process. One reference is required. If you are offered the role, RNIB will provide volunteer and safeguarding training, with ongoing support from your volunteer manager.\n\nPlease note: Applying expresses your interest and does not guarantee a volunteering placement.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tGood digital and IT skills.\n•\tConfidence downloading, transferring and organising digital files.\n•\tAbility to work with computer systems and internal databases.\n•\tGood attention to detail and the ability to identify errors or inconsistencies.\n•\tAbility to work independently and contribute effectively to a team.\n\nPlease note that access to your own computer is needed for this role.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a home-based volunteering role, so no regular travel is required. You will need access to your own computer to carry out the tasks remotely.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nRNIB covers out-of-pocket expenses incurred through this volunteering role. Please discuss eligible expenses and how to claim them with your volunteer manager before incurring any costs.",
