                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IeZBBYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IeZBBYA3/festive-events-volunteer-join-us-for-the-linwood-christmas-event-with-lights-switch-on",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-19",
                    "title": "Festive Events Volunteer - Join Us for the Linwood Christmas Event with Lights Switch-On!",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFestive Events Volunteer - Join Us for the Linwood Christmas Event with Lights Switch-On!\n\n## Description\n\nJoin Us for the Linwood Christmas Event with Lights Switch-On!\n\nDate: 19th November 2026\nTime: 5:30pm - 7:30pm\nLocation: Tweedie Hall, 17 Bridge Street, Linwood, PA3 3DB\n\nWe are delighted to invite you to be part of the Linwood Christmas Lights Switch-On 2026. This festive community celebration brings local people together to enjoy an evening of Christmas entertainment, family activities, and festive cheer. We are looking for enthusiastic volunteers to help make the event a memorable experience for everyone attending.\n\nSnack Table Elf\n\n\nHelp manage the snack table outside the Lesser Hall during the children&#39;s disco.\nReplenish snacks and refreshments throughout the event.\nAssist in creating a fun and welcoming atmosphere for children and families.\n\n\nFestive Concert Ticket Steward\n\n\nBe a friendly face welcoming visitors to the panto and concert in the Main Hall.\nAssist with ticket checks and audience entry.\nHelp ensure visitors are seated safely and efficiently.\n\n\nSanta&#39;s Helper\n\n\nEscort Santa throughout the event and assist during meet-and-greet sessions.\nHelp families meet Santa and take photographs.\nWelcome visitors to the venue and support queue management for both Santa&nbsp;and the Snow Globe.\n\n\nYour support will play an important role in creating a magical and memorable festive celebration for the Linwood community.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
