        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002xlDjeAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002xlDjeAAE/cycling-without-age-scotland-lewis-and-harris",
            "name": "Cycling Without Age Scotland - Lewis and Harris",
            "description": "This is an exciting and innovative charity which enriches and enhances lives by enabling older and less independent people to once again be an active part of their communities and to “feel the wind in their hair” Volunteers (pilots) sign up to take people for bike rides as often or as rarely as they want to. The long term aim is to have multiple projects running in communities across the islands in order to help combat loneliness, empower individuals and build intergenerational\r\nrelationships.",
            "website": "https://cyclingwithoutage.scot/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000CL6czYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000CL6czYAD/befrienders-to-accompany-an-elderly-or-less-abled-body-person-in-the-trishaw-harris",
                    "publishStart": "2025-09-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-26",
                    "title": "Befrienders (to accompany an elderly or less abled body person in the trishaw) (Harris)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCycling Without Age Scotland is a transformational project which brings the elderly population closer to the outdoor environment through the power of Cycling. It offers the elderly or less able bodied, the chance to hitch a ride on a trishaw and enjoy the outdoors in a relaxing and invigorating way. Based on the national model, the Lewis and Harris Chapter has formed a core local committee and are keen to recruit volunteers to help establish and run the project. Our first aim is to raise enough money to purchase two trishaws, one for Stornoway and one for Tarbert. We then plan to link up (initially) with local care homes and organise to take elderly residents out on trishaws.\r\n\r\nVolunteers\r\nThe project would offer considerable opportunities for volunteers and taking part would increase confidence and social skills in all age groups.\r\nFor those who volunteer with the project, it is a chance to be part of something that makes a real difference to the lives of those in their community. They will form friendships and, from the stories they hear on the rides, learn more about their local community. They will develop important social skills and their own health will benefit from the exercise and fresh air.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000CL6czYAD#role",
                        "type": "Role",
