            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008ttX7YAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008ttX7YAI/team-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-08",
                    "title": "Team Member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nLooking for a rewarding way to make a difference? You can join the friendly Explorer Scout leadership team and help inspire young people aged 14 to 18 as they discover the world on their own terms. From hiking and camping to coding, community projects and big adventures, Explorers choose their own challenges, build lifelong skills and grow in confidence. As a volunteer, you’ll help make those opportunities happen as part of a supportive, welcoming team. No previous Scouting experience is needed – just enthusiasm, willingness to have fun, and a desire to encourage young people to achieve amazing things. Full training and ongoing support are provided. Life can be busy, so volunteering is flexible. You don’t have to commit every week; the team shares the responsibility and creates unforgettable experiences together. Come and be part of something that changes lives – including your own.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience required – full training and support provided (for free)\n\n## Training details\n\nScouts offers structured, flexible training through a bespoke learning system, designed to provide volunteers with essential safety, governance and practical skills. There are mandatory core elements, namely safety and safeguarding, which must be completed within the first 30 days. Other learning follows after. Scouts have volunteer learning assessors and advisers who provide ongoing support. Support also comes from the volunteer’s local Group.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMonday evenings during school term time, 7pm – 9m, at Auchtermuchty Scout Hall, Stratheden Place, Low Road Park, Auchtermuchty, Cupar, KY14 7BD\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nYes - travel for special events and on an individual basis",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
