        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002r2dDOAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002r2dDOAAY/freedom-of-mind-community-choir",
            "name": "Freedom of Mind Community Choir",
            "description": "We're a non-audition community choir - we sing because it makes us feel good!",
            "website": "https://freedomofmindcommunitychoir.com/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HznRpYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HznRpYAJ/volunteer-fundraiser",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Volunteer Fundraiser",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nFreedom Of Mind Community Choir are a welcoming, non-audition community choir based in Falkirk. They are dedicated to the physical, social, and emotional benefits of group singing.  The Community Choir meet on Wednesday afternoons to create a safe, supportive space where they explore folk, pop, and world music, and even write their own songs. The choir is open to anyone over 18 living in or near Falkirk with special priority spaces for individuals with lived experience of mental ill-health. As a community project, they operate on a \"pay what you can afford\" basis to stay completely inclusive. To cover accessible travel, venue costs, musical direction and project admin, support and management, and rely on grants and fundraising.\r\n\r\nFreedom Of Mind Community Choir based in Falkirk, Scotland, is looking for a passionate Volunteer Fundraiser to help keep this singing community thriving and accessible to all.\r\n\r\nWhat You Will Do\r\nExplore local, regional and national funding opportunities. \r\nUtilise local support: work with resources like the CVS Falkirk Grant Funding Portal to identify new funding opportunities.\r\nHelp write funding bids: review previously successful project funding applications and draft new applications to keep weekly sessions and outreach performances funded.\r\nOrganise local initiatives: Help plan creative community fundraising events or connect with local businesses in the Falkirk district.\r\n\r\nWhat You Will Gain\r\nThe reward of supporting a vital, life-changing local mental health arts project.\r\nHands-on experience navigating Scottish third-sector funding and grant applications.\r\nA chance to be part of a warm, joyful, and deeply supportive musical community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGreat communication skills and a friendly, professional writing style.\r\nBasic computer skills (emails and word processing).\r\nA strong belief in the vital connection between singing, community, and mental well-being.\r\nExperience in fundraising would be desirable but is not essential — enthusiasm for the cause matters most!\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers undergo an induction meeting with the project manager and/or admin and support worker. This can be undertaken in person or online. Subsequent to this meeting, the volunteer will undertake basic safeguarding training online and register for a basic disclosure (costs covered by Freedom Of Mind Community Choir). \r\nAfter this, volunteers will be supported by a named line manager within the staff team. When funding allows, training opportunities for volunteers will be offered.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible: around 2-4 hours per week.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a remote-friendly role you can do from home, though you would also be warmly invited, if you are able, to join the Wednesday afternoon sessions to see your impact firsthand!\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNot applicable for this role - however the organisation does have an expenses policy/procedure.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://www.freedomofmindcommunitychoir.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/LOGO2.png",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HznRpYAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Fundraiser",
                        "description": "Great communication skills and a friendly, professional writing style.\r\nBasic computer skills (emails and word processing).\r\nA strong belief in the vital connection between singing, community, and mental well-being.\r\nExperience in fundraising would be desirable but is not essential — enthusiasm for the cause matters most!",
                        "commitment": "Flexible: around 2-4 hours per week.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HznRpYAJ/volunteer-fundraiser?#modal_register_a0gQD00000HznRpYAJ",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
