                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hzn6rYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hzn6rYAB/volunteer-secretary",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Volunteer Secretary",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nFreedom Of Mind Community Choir are a welcoming, non-audition community choir based in Falkirk. They are dedicated to the physical, social, and emotional benefits of group singing.  The Community Choir meet weekly to create a safe, supportive space for adults, with priority spaces for those with lived experience of mental ill-health. As a community project, a well-run committee is vital to survival. Your administrative support will ensure the group stays organised so they can focus on singing for good mental health.\r\n\r\nFreedom Of Mind Community Choir is looking for a structured and reliable Volunteer Secretary to join a friendly committee and help keep operations running smoothly.\r\n\r\nWhat You Will Do\r\nPrepare Agendas: Work with the Committee Chair to draft and distribute meeting agendas in advance.\r\nTake Minutes: Attend online committee meetings to take clear, accurate notes of discussions and action points.\r\nDistribute Notes: Share the finalised minutes with committee members via email in a timely manner.\r\nMaintain Records: Keep a digital archive of past meeting agendas and minutes.\r\n\r\nVolunteers should have a strong belief in the vital connection between community music and mental well-being.\r\n\r\nWhat You Will Gain\r\nThe satisfaction of keeping a vital, life-changing local mental health arts project running smoothly.\r\nExperience in charity governance, committee administration, and minute-taking.\r\nA chance to connect with a warm, joyful, and deeply supportive local community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood computer literacy, including experience with email and word processing (Word, Google Docs, etc.) and reliable internet access.\r\nExcellent listening skills and the ability to summarise discussions clearly.\r\nReliable organisation and a friendly, collaborative approach.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers undergo an induction meeting with the project manager and/or admin and support worker. This can be undertaken in person or online. Subsequent to this meeting, the volunteer will undertake basic safeguarding training online and register for a basic disclosure (costs covered by Freedom Of Mind Community Choir). \r\nAfter this, volunteers will be supported by a named line manager within the staff team. When funding allows, training opportunities for volunteers will be offered.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n3- 6 meetings per year. \r\nAround 2-3 hours per meeting cycle (including prep, attending the online meeting, and writing up the minutes).\n\n## Travel details\n\nAll committee meetings take place online, so you can join comfortably from home.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNot applicable for this role - however the organisation does have an expenses policy/procedure.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
