            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000SsKn3AAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000SsKn3AAF/volunteer-drivers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer Drivers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCOG: Community Outreach Group provides support to homeless and vulnerable people in the City of Aberdeen.\r\n\r\nWe provide meals and essentials for the homeless and vulnerable people of Aberdeen on a Wednesday and Sunday evening. We are looking for drivers to pick up and drop off various food donations. \r\n\r\nThis is a vital role in what we do as an organisation, collecting all the donations and dropping them off so we have the food ready to serve. All help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor more details please contact Rebecca Fyfe at email: beccafyfe@hotmail.com or telephone: 07415723938.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. Also, we can provide naloxone training and if applicants feel the need for further training this can be looked into.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times to assist on either/or both Wednesday and Sunday afternoons. All help is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe main areas are city centre in Aberdeen.",
