                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Vup0jAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Vup0jAAB/volunteer-driver",
                    "publishStart": "2023-05-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Volunteer Driver",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you enjoy driving and chatting to people? If you have your own car and some free time, we would love you to consider becoming a driver for St Columba's Hospice Care. This role enables our clients to attend a range of services that we offer at St Columba's, supporting their wellbeing and physical health.\n\n## Description\n\nUsing your own vehicle to transport clients from their home to the Hospice to enable them to attend a wellbeing session or outpatient appointments and then transporting clients back to their home afterwards. This is a lovely role focussed on enabling our clients to attend our Wellbeing, Community Services, Complementary Therapy and Counselling services. Without our drivers, many of our clients would be unable to access these services.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnjoy driving with a clean driving licence. \nFriendly, warm personality.\nExcellent communication skills. \nCalm and unflappable.\nAn understanding of mobility issues. \nAn understanding of boundaries and confidentiality.\nFit and able to move/ lift/ store a wheelchair, for example.\n\n## Training details\n\nHospice Volunteer Induction Programme \nHospice Orientation  \nTeam / role induction and training  \nTeam meetings (if/as necessary)\n\n## Travel details\n\nSt Columba's Hospice is located at 15 Boswall Road Edinburgh, EH5 3RW. However, clients are picked up from various Edinburgh postcodes.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers are able to claim mileage. There is an expense form to fill out and expenses are paid monthly via BACS.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Vup0jAAB#role",
