                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNqj2AAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNqj2AAD/compassionate-neighbours",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-15",
                    "title": "Compassionate Neighbours",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCompassionate Neighbours volunteers are matched with people who may share similar interests, hobbies and geography, in the hope of developing genuine, caring friendships; which will ultimately change the lives of those who come together and strengthen the communities they live in.\n\n## Experience required\n\nHave a kind heart \r\nBe friendly and compassionate \r\nEnjoy meeting new people and building meaningful bonds \r\nHave good listening skills \r\nBe honest, trustworthy and reliable \r\n\tHave a good understanding of personal boundaries  \r\n\tBe respectful of confidentiality at all times \r\n\tUnderstand and follow St Columba’s Hospice guidelines and policies that apply to Compassionate Neighbours \r\n\tUnderstand and hold close our values of Respect, Trust, Partnership and Care & Compassion\n\n## Training details\n\nPre-training reading. Face to face session at St Columba’s Hospice or in a community setting and a follow-up session.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nYou will be entitled to claim travelling expenses incurred as a Compassionate Neighbour. Expenses are paid monthly via BACS.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNqj2AAD#role",
