        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002mwGrZAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002mwGrZAAU/community-gift-exchange",
            "name": "Community Gift Exchange",
            "description": "Community Gift Exchange is a charity situated in Ayrshire with a mission of creating a flourishing community in which everyone can participate in the fullness of life together. We believe that we can help build a community through the generous exchange of gifts such as our time, skills, expertise or funds. Community Gift Exchange enables volunteers to help release people into sustainable employment through working together on creative and practical projects that benefit our local community. At the core of CGX, our charitable purpose is the prevention and relief of poverty, the advancement of education, religion, health, citizenship and community development, and the relief of those in need.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC047814"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CharityShop",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Charity Shop"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Poverty",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Poverty"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNziwAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNziwAAD/stockroom-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2022-08-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-30",
                    "title": "Stockroom Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHow would you like to be part of a charity with a difference? Refurnish, 88 High Street,  is a charity shop run by Community Gift Exchange (CGX) where we believe everyone has a gift or skill to share. \r\n\r\nLittle or no experience? All the better! CGX aims to equip people with the skills they need to go onto sustainable employment or further training (see also training details for further info). We want to help you realise your goals no matter how small or big!  \r\n\r\nWe value our Volunteers so much that we offer everyone who gives their time a free hearty, home-made lunch. Past and current volunteers particularly appreciate making new friends and being part of a genuinely inclusive community.   \r\n\r\nThe Refurnish shop operates on the ethos that all efforts should be made to save perfectly good items from going to waste. We would love you to be part of this effort!  \r\n\r\nWhat might I be expected to do in this role?\r\n● Organising stock into boxes and onto shelves by product type\r\n● Picking out stock that would be a good fit for the Refurnish shop\r\n● Creating a buffer stock area to help the retail team stock the shop\r\n● Possibility of moving stock to and from the shop\r\n\r\nWe value creativity so if you have a particular interest or passion (eg books) let us know and we can tailor the role to suit you! \r\n\r\nCGX have conducted and implemented a Covid-secure Risk Assessment and follow government guidelines. The safety and wellbeing of our volunteers and staff is our highest priority.\n\n## Experience required\n\nOur ideal stockroom volunteer would be…\r\n●\tFriendly and approachable\r\n●\tAble to use their own initiative\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers can benefit from a dedicated support service \r\nOn the job training by their qualified Supervisor\r\nAccess to a qualified Occupational Therapist for vocational assessment and training\r\nOpportunity to gain a qualification in Customer Service through West College Scotland (remote access).\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n10am-12.30pm or 12.30pm-4pm (flexible) Volunteers receive a wholesome lunch and unlimited tea and coffee on shift.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\ntravel costs refunded\n\n## Taster details\n\nInformal interview (in person or over the phone) and then a trial shift to see if both parties feel it’s a right fit.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F6e69c6c7-6a8c-2797-9389-ef5aa8fd81c4%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=560cef0a-2b5e-4ad1-94f7-c3080e9cae89",
