                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNzimAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNzimAAD/bike-mechanic-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2022-08-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-30",
                    "title": "Bike mechanic Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHow would you like to be part of a charity with a difference? At Community Gift Exchange (CGX) we believe everyone has a gift or skill to share. \r\n\r\nLittle or no experience? All the better! CGX aims to equip people with the skills they need to go onto sustainable employment or further training (see also training details for further info). We want to help you realise your goals no matter how small or big!  \r\n\r\nWe value our Volunteers so much that we offer everyone who gives their time a free hearty, home-made lunch. Past and current volunteers particularly appreciate making new friends and being part of a genuinely inclusive community.   \r\n\r\nCycleworks aims to save bicycles from going to waste by repairing, fixing and restoring so they can be ridden once again! \r\n\r\nWhat can I expect to learn and do in this role?\r\n•\t Bicycle refurbishment including : bike ‘stripping’; brake and gear calibration; wheel   repair and building; pedal care and repair\r\n•\tHow to set up a bicycle for a customer \r\n•\tHow to fully clean and maintain a bicycle\r\n•\tHow to check parts for wear and sort accordingly\r\n•\tMaintain the workshop to a high standard of tidiness\r\n\r\nThis is a great opportunity if you are interested in going into mechanics or engineering to gain experience of a workshop environment. \r\n\r\nCGX have conducted and implemented a Covid-secure Risk Assessment and follow government guidelines. The safety and wellbeing of our volunteers and staff is our highest priority.\n\n## Experience required\n\nLittle or no experience? All the better! CGX aims to equip people with the skills they need to go onto sustainable employment or further training (see also training details for further info). We want to help you realise your goals no matter how small or big!\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers can benefit from a dedicated support service \r\nOn the job training by their qualified Supervisor\r\nAccess to a qualified Occupational Therapist for vocational assessment and training\r\nOpportunity to gain a qualifications in bike mechanics through ‘Velotech’ courses.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n10am-12.30pm or 12.30pm-4pm (flexible) Volunteers receive a wholesome lunch and unlimited tea and coffee on shift.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\ntravel costs refunded\n\n## Taster details\n\nInformal interview (in person or over the phone) and then a trial shift to see if both parties feel it’s a right fit.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fbc03b1ec-6974-8ed7-5ba7-9c314b385c0c%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=8c32576a-0946-41ed-882d-0d1222ad7ef7",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNzimAAD#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Bike mechanic Volunteer",
                        "description": "Little or no experience? All the better! CGX aims to equip people with the skills they need to go onto sustainable employment or further training (see also training details for further info). We want to help you realise your goals no matter how small or big!",
