                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009KPTJYA4",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009KPTJYA4/furniture-restoration-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-04-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-02",
                    "title": "Furniture Restoration Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHow would you like to be part of a charity with a difference? ‘Reusables’ is a charity shop run by Community Gift Exchange (CGX) where we believe everyone has a gift or skill to share. \r\n\r\nLittle or no experience? All the better! CGX aims to equip people with the skills they need to go onto sustainable employment or further training (see also training details for further info). We want to help you realise your goals no matter how small or big!  \r\n\r\nWe value our Volunteers so much that we offer everyone who gives their time a free hearty, home-made lunch. Past and current volunteers particularly appreciate making new friends and being part of a genuinely inclusive community.   \r\n\r\nThe Reuseables shop operates on the ethos that all efforts should be made to save perfectly good items from going to waste. We would love you to be part of this effort!  \r\nWe are currently looking for Furniture Restoration volunteers.\r\n\r\nWhat might I be expected to do in this role?\r\nThis role involves dining chair reupholstery and wood refurbishment work.\r\n\r\nWe value creativity so if you have a particular interest or passion let us know and we can tailor the role to suit you! \r\nCGX have undertaken Risk Assessments for all roles. The safety and wellbeing of our volunteers and staff is our highest priority.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAn interest in furniture restoration\r\nWillingness to learn\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers can benefit from a dedicated support service \r\nOn the job training by their qualified Supervisor\r\nAccess to a qualified Occupational Therapist for vocational assessment and training\r\nOpportunity to gain a qualification in Customer Service through West College Scotland (remote access).\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n10am-12.30pm or 12.30pm-4pm (flexible) Volunteers receive a wholesome lunch and unlimited tea and coffee on shift.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\ntravel costs refunded\n\n## Taster details\n\nInformal interview (in person or over the phone) and then a trial shift to see if both parties feel it’s a right fit.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F50579220-2f07-4515-8d8d-33ae06f1795c%2F0nFCUqNjeiXPIFO483j0BVWArU43%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=7d994410-9910-417f-9902-3b8a35d47b89",
