        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002mwn9xAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002mwn9xAAA/barnardos-south-ayrshire",
            "name": "Barnardos South Ayrshire",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC037605"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000003dtSjYAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000003dtSjYAI/ayrshire-intandem-volunteer-mentor",
                    "publishStart": "2024-05-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-29",
                    "title": "Ayrshire Intandem volunteer mentor",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAyrshire Intandem Mentoring Service offers support to young people looked after at home aged 8-14 years living in Ayrshire.\r\nVolunteer Mentors main tasks will be to:\r\n*Provide weekly 1:1 mentoring support\r\n*Build a positive, trusting, supportive and secure relationship with children & young people aged 8 – 14\r\n*Promote the wellbeing of every child through creative and fun approaches\r\n*Communicate and link with the Intandem Mentor Coordinator on a regular basis.\r\nYou have the potential to make a real difference in a young persons life by helping build confidence and self-esteem and most importantly being someone they can talk to about anything.\r\n\r\nThis role is subject to an application form being submitted, providing 2 references and completing a PVG Disclosure (is free for volunteers)\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe skills you need\r\nReliable, punctual and trustworthy.\r\nApproachable and welcoming.\r\nBeing passionate about making a difference in the lives of children, young\r\npeople and families.\r\nBeing non-judgmental and positive in their attitude to working with\r\nindividuals from different backgrounds.\r\nGood listening and communication skills.\r\nThe ability to manage and respond positively to challenging situations.\n\n## Training details\n\nWhat's in it for you:\r\n- Full induction and training.\r\n- Other training opportunities relevant to the volunteer role.\r\n- Regular supervision and support.\r\n- Out of pocket expenses agreed in advance.\r\n- Access to the Barnardo’s internal vacancy listing.\r\n- Our volunteers tell us about lots of other benefits of volunteering including; experience of working with children, young people and families; experience for your CV; supporting your local community; meeting new people; increasing self-confidence; feeling like you are making a difference; improving your health and wellbeing; and a chance to contribute to a worthwhile children’s charity.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWe ask for a 12 months commitment\n\n## Travel details\n\nIf you drive you can use your own car with business insurance or use public transport  which you will be reimbursed for.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAll out of pocket expenses are paid by Barnardos",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F3aa1a67b-2067-7182-6a66-5acb059f3ce0%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=b8d57f08-febe-4e7d-b3da-47706f0afe7c",
