        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002mwnEOAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002mwnEOAAY/carrick-rugby-club",
            "name": "Carrick Rugby Club",
            "description": "Carrick Rugby is a community based club offering access to rugby to everyone in North and South Carrick. We aim to provide opportunities to participate in rugby for people of all ages from our vibrant micro mini section, ages 5 to 12, through our midis 12 to 18 years and into our senior squad 18. We focus on partnership working within our community and working to provide our communities with a welcoming atmosphere and high quality coaching and playing opportunities as well as a great opportunity for social activities.",
            "website": "https://www.carrickrugby.co.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC050725"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7LLoAAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7LLoAAN/event-organiser",
                    "publishStart": "2022-12-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Event organiser",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCan you support Carrick Rugby? Do you enjoy hosting parties or small events? Are you a creative person and can multitask to create positive experiences for guests? You might like to volunteer with us as event organisers. \r\nYou could be doing the following duties:\r\n \r\n- Researching target audiences to find significant occasions.\r\n- Creating and maintaining a budget for the client.\r\n- Searching for, booking and organizing adequate locations to host events.\r\n- Designing event layouts and agendas, including creating pamphlets or event guides.\r\n- Marketing events through advertisements and working with PR professionals.\r\n- Training staff or volunteers\r\n- Overseeing operations during events and ensuring proper cleanup after it ends\r\n- Communicating with vendors to provide suitable resources for the event, including sound and electric equipment, security or stages.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe following skills would be ideal, however volunteers can take the opportunity to acquire or develop further these skills\r\n- Leadership\r\n- Attention to detail\r\n- Time management\r\n- Interpersonal skills\r\n- Collaboration\r\n- Multitasking\r\n- Negotiation",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F674bb06e-3403-8554-8415-b777de9a843b%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=93b4ac1c-3afc-47c4-8d2a-8600db282998",
