                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-10",
                    "title": "Outings Companion (Dunfermline)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBlind Veterans UK is looking for a friendly, reliable volunteer to support a veteran in Dunfermline.\n\n## Description\n\nCan you spare an hour a week to brighten someone’s day? \r\n\r\nBlind Veterans UK community volunteers provide vital companionship and social interaction for veterans who may otherwise feel isolated or lonely. By giving a small amount of your time, you can make a meaningful difference to someone's wellbeing and quality of life.\r\n\r\nThey're looking for a friendly, reliable volunteer to support a veteran in Dunfermline. The role involves meeting regularly to enjoy a coffee and a chat. The veteran is a keen music enthusiast with a particular love of 1960s and 1970s rock music, including bands such as The Beatles, Led Zeppelin, Queen, and The Who. They also enjoy discussing current affairs and staying connected to what's happening in the world.\r\n\r\nVolunteers must be aged 18 or over. Full training, guidance and ongoing support will be provided, ensuring you feel confident and well supported throughout your volunteering journey.\n\n## Experience required\n\nReliability and Punctuality. The role involves regular social interaction, so warmth and good communication are key.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction includes a history of the charity, professional boundaries, sight-loss awareness, GDPR and our online platform. On-going training available through our online platform and through ad hoc training opportunities.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDunfermline. Volunteers can use public transport or their own vehicle to meet the veteran.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nYou will be reimbursed for light refreshments and for your mileage to meet with the veteran at 55p/m.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
