        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002mxKLxAAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002mxKLxAAM/caramara-wellbeing-support",
            "name": "Caramara Wellbeing Support",
            "description": "Working across South Ayrshire, Caramara (formerly Three Sixty) helps people turn their lives around to get back to a place of health and happiness. We have been promoting mental wellbeing throughout South Ayrshire, with a focus on recovery and empowerment, since 1987. Three Sixty deliver activity-based supports to individuals aged 16 and over who are affected by mental ill health, including their families and carers when appropriate. The charity implements this by putting coaching, community and connection at the heart of mental health support and recovery. We aim to help those suffering from mental health issues to come full circle.",
            "website": "https://www.caramara.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC018398"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000006nyCWYAY",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000006nyCWYAY/group-host",
                    "publishStart": "2024-11-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-19",
                    "title": "Group Host",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are a mental health charity supporting the community within South Ayrshire.   You do not need any formal diagnosis to receive support from ourselves and anyone can self refer.  Support is available as a 1 to 1 support, group support, social.\r\nWe host several different groups to reduce social isolation and improve mental health and wellbeing.    We would be seeking volunteers to assist with hosting the various groups, initially in Ayr and then extending across South Ayrshire.  We are also currently seeking volunteers to join our Board of Trustees.\r\n\r\nMain duties: to facilitate groups within The Place.   Groups include – public living room, arts and crafts, maws paws & weans, Menopause café, mens group \r\n\r\n\r\nSkills & experience required:  Ability to chat with people from a wide range of societal backgrounds, ability to encourage and support people to participate in the group, ability to devise a timetable of activities for the group would be very beneficial.   Previous experience of working with groups would be desirable however support would be given on initial sign up.\r\n\r\nAll groups currently based at The Place, 56 Newmarket St, Ayr – travel to there would be required\n\n## Experience required\n\nSkills & experience required: Ability to chat with people from a wide range of societal backgrounds, ability to encourage and support people to participate in the group, ability to devise a timetable of activities for the group would be very beneficial. Previous experience of working with groups would be desirable however support would be given on initial sign up\n\n## Travel details\n\nAll groups currently based at The Place, 56 Newmarket St, Ayr – travel to there would be required",
