            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000G8coTYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000G8coTYAR/volunteer-evening-receptionist",
                    "publishStart": "2026-04-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Volunteer Evening Receptionist",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDigital Marketing volunteer within an alcohol counselling recovery service.\n\n## Description\n\nAyrshire Council on Alcohol is an alcohol counselling recovery service commissioned by East & South Ayrshire Health & Social Care Partnerships to provide free confidential advice, information & support to individuals aged 16 + whether they wish to stop drinking or reduce their drinking levels. Support is also available to those concerned about a loved one’s drinking. All counsellors are trained to professional standards and work from accessible venues throughout East & South Ayrshire. Daytime & evening appointments are available.\r\n\r\nACA are currently looking to recruit a Volunteer Evening Receptionist.\r\nYou will be the first point of contact when an individual arrives for their appointment and will greet them in a professional and welcoming manner, ensuring that they are comfortably seated with a glass of water in reception\r\nMain Tasks:\r\nMeet and greet individuals who use the service · Update the appointments diary · Answer the telephone & pass messages to the appropriate staff member · General office duties – photocopying, shredding, making up information packs & case records\n\n## Experience required\n\nAn empathic & non-judgemental approach towards individuals who are concerned about their own or a loved one’s drinking \r\n· A pleasant & courteous manner when dealing with individuals in person or via telephone · An understanding of working in an environment whereby policy & procedures must be followed and confidentiality strictly upheld at all times · The ability to carry out general office duties such as filing, shredding, photocopying etc. \r\n· To understand the boundaries within the role and seek support from the Director of Service when required\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction to ACA, including policies and procedures\r\nAccess to free in house & external training\r\nOngoing support and monthly supervision\r\nTravel expenses \r\nTea & coffee\r\nLunch if working 4+ hours\r\nThere is no lone working\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are reimbursed and lunch is provided if you work more than 4 hours",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F76df63fd-2321-4565-9111-908894bab747%2Fgpx6nnIWvxXFMLCpJdEzZH9maTg1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=dd14073f-75ad-4ce8-b316-863d39fc7018",
