                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000G8blxYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000G8blxYAB/digital-marketing-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-04-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Digital Marketing Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDigital Marketing volunteer within an alcohol counselling recovery service.\n\n## Description\n\nAyrshire Council on Alcohol is an alcohol counselling recovery service commissioned by East & South Ayrshire Health & Social Care Partnerships to provide free confidential advice, information & support to individuals aged 16 + whether they wish to stop drinking or reduce their drinking levels. Support is also available to those concerned about a loved one’s drinking. All counsellors are trained to professional standards and work from accessible venues throughout East & South Ayrshire. Daytime & evening appointments are available.\r\n\r\nACA are currently looking to recruit a Digital Marketing Volunteer.\r\nRole description:\t\r\n•\tYou will be an important member of the ACA team, improving and expanding the organisation’s digital marketing activities to raise awareness within our communities, engage with those looking for support and reach out to potential donors.\r\nMain tasks:\r\n•\tHelp develop & co-ordinate ACA’s digital marketing strategies\r\n•\tIncrease presence on social media platforms\r\n•\tImprove & update ACA website\r\n•\tSupport the Director of Service with the planning and delivery of any campaigns across the platforms\r\n•\tMonitor online performance & recommend improvements\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tExperience or a strong interest in digital marketing / promotion\r\n•\tAbility to work on multiple digital channels such as social media and websites\r\n•\tGood organisational skills\r\n•\tAn understanding of the importance of upholding confidentiality\r\n•\tInterest in working for a local charity to help support service promotion and raise awareness\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction to ACA, including policies and procedures\r\nAccess to free in house & external training\r\nOngoing support and monthly supervision\r\nTravel expenses \r\nTea & coffee\r\nLunch if working 4+ hours\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are reimbursed and lunch is provided if you work more than 4 hours",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
