        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002mxlmiAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002mxlmiAAA/kirkmichael-village-renaissance",
            "name": "Kirkmichael Village Renaissance",
            "description": "Kirkmichael Community Shop and Café is a well-stocked, not-for-profit, community run convenience store and café.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC046113"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityFacilities",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Facilities"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pv9OZAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pv9OZAAZ/volunteer-shop-cafe-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2021-07-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-30",
                    "title": "Volunteer Shop & Cafe Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nVolunteering as a member of the Café team you will play an integral part of Kirkmichael's community shop and cafe, by helping to deliver a café experience for our visitors and guests whether in the Café or at events.\r\n\r\nYour role as a Community Cafe volunteer will be: \r\n\r\nAssisting the Café team in the day to day running of the Café, such as the preparation and delivery of various hot and cold food and drinks and assisting with the day to day running of the Café.\r\n\r\n\r\nDealing with the visitors and customers in a friendly and polite manner.\r\n\r\nHandling cash.\r\n\r\nDelivering food and drink to our guests and clearing tables.\r\n\r\nEmptying waste bins.\r\n\r\n\r\nWe support all volunteers and offer to pay for training such as the online food handling course. Volunteers are always supported by trustee members and/or staff at the shop and cafe.\r\n\r\nTo apply or for more information call 01655 750443.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training is given in how the Shop and Café are run, the Health and Safety practices relating to Covid restrictions, how to work the coffee machine and the till and legislation related to the sale of Alcohol. Ongoing support is given by the paid staff and fellow volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWeekdays and Weekends\n\n## Travel details\n\nA car would be an advantage but Kirkmichael is on a regular bus route from Ayr.",
