        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002mxuZ1AAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002mxuZ1AAI/bfriend",
            "name": "Bfriend",
            "description": "South Ayrshire Befriending Project (SABP) provides one to one befriending support for socially isolated young people affected by multiple disadvantage and adversities. Each year SABP supports approximately 45 young people living in South Ayrshire, ranging in age from 8 to 18 years. The main aim of befriending is to reduce the social isolation of the young people we support and improve their emotional wellbeing, confidence and self-esteem. A further aim is to ensure young people are included, listened to and that they feel valued. Collectively these aims ensure young people can develop the life skills necessary to become more resilient and better equipped to overcome adversity, thus improving their future life chances.",
            "website": "https://www.bfriend.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC020989"
                }
            ],
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2Fef718f30-3542-8419-21a1-6ed5d96c22b4%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=ff959f06-3fd2-45ef-b01a-48b1a55e44a9",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNqUKAA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNqUKAA1/group-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2022-09-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-16",
                    "title": "Group Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nA group volunteer is someone who, after a period of training and assessment, will provide support to young people on a 1:1 basis or to the group as a whole at the Project’s group outings. Bfriend facilitates 12 group outings per year for socially isolated young people aged between 8 & 18, living in South Ayrshire.  \r\n\r\nTASKS \r\n\r\n•\tTo participate where possible in monthly group outings & volunteer support sessions and attend a minimum of 6 per year\r\n•\tTo read the volunteer handbook and be aware of Bfriend's policies and procedures and adhere to them.\r\n•\tTo comply with the team’s administrative procedures.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tBe comfortable working on their own independently and in group settings \r\n•\tBe able to seek advice and support from Project staff when  necessary\r\n•\tBe able to communicate well with others\r\n•\tBe non judgemental, respecting people’s differences\r\n•\tHave an understanding or awareness of some issues faced by young people referred to the team\r\n•\tBe willing to participate in a broad range of activities\n\n## Training details\n\n•\tGroup volunteers will be required to undertake a 4 week induction training course which consist of 4 x 3 hour sessions on a weekly basis\r\n•Required to refresh child protection training at least every 2 years as per the Project’s policies and procedures\r\n•\tVolunteers are encouraged to attend volunteer support sessions which are offered on a monthly basis and comprise of a mixture of training, information and social events \r\n•\tReferences can be given on request following 6 months commitment\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nTo participate where possible in monthly group outings & volunteer support sessions and attend a minimum of 6 per year\n\n## Travel details\n\nAble to travel locally either by walking, public transport or car in order to participate in outings with the young person.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n•\tAll out of pocket expenses will be reimbursed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://i.ibb.co/3kSkQ8C/Asset-1-2x-8.png",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNqUKAA1#role",
