                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QhjnlAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QhjnlAAB/board-of-management-trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2025-09-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-05",
                    "title": "Board of Management Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFor more information or to apply contact John Reid on 01292 270864 or email john@sacommunitytransport.org\n\n## Description\n\nSouth Ayrshire Community Transport was established in April 2016. Our purpose is to connect people and places, helping to enhance social inclusion across South Ayrshire. SACT operates a fleet of 16 vehicles, ranging from 7-seaters to 16-seater minibuses.\r\nWe are seeking to appoint new trustee/s to the Board of Management to support the organisation's development and long term sustainability. Trustees are collectively responsible for ensuring that SACT:\r\n•\tComplies with its governing documents, charity law, employment law, and all relevant legislation and regulations.\r\n•\tPursues its charitable objectives.\r\n•\tProvides clear strategic direction, including setting policies, goals, and targets, and monitoring performance.\r\n•\tSafeguards the good name, reputation, and values of SACT.\r\n•\tMaintains financial stability and ensures effective and efficient administration.\r\n•\tOversees the protection, management, and appropriate investment of the organisation’s funds.\r\n•\tAppoints the Project Manager and monitors their performance as part of the Board of Management.\r\nIn addition to statutory responsibilities, Trustees are expected to use their skills, knowledge, and experience to support effective decision-making. This may include:\r\n•\tScrutinising Board papers\r\n•\tLeading or contributing to discussions\r\n•\tFocusing on key strategic and operational issues\n\n## Experience required\n\nSACT are looking for individuals who can demonstrate:\r\n•\tCommitment to SACT and willingness to devote the necessary time and effort\r\n(The Board meets every eight weeks on Thursday afternoons at 1:00pm. Online attendance is available.)\r\n•\tAbility to think creatively and contribute to the development of SACT’s strategic vision.\r\n•\tUnderstanding and acceptance of the legal duties, responsibilities, and liabilities of being a Trustee.\r\n•\tGood independent judgement and the confidence to speak openly.\r\n•\tAbility to work effectively as part of a Board.\r\n•\tCommitment to Nolan’s Seven Principles of Public Life:\r\nSelflessness, Integrity, Objectivity, Accountability, Openness, Honesty, and Leadership.\r\n\r\nFor more information or to apply contact John Reid on 01292 270864 or email john@sacommunitytransport.org",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fe14fb53c-f320-47a7-8747-d9e9213a8d3c%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=d5beccd2-066c-45f1-85f5-771955b8c944",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QhjnlAAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Board of Management Trustee",
                        "description": "SACT are looking for individuals who can demonstrate:\r\n•\tCommitment to SACT and willingness to devote the necessary time and effort\r\n(The Board meets every eight weeks on Thursday afternoons at 1:00pm. Online attendance is available.)\r\n•\tAbility to think creatively and contribute to the development of SACT’s strategic vision.\r\n•\tUnderstanding and acceptance of the legal duties, responsibilities, and liabilities of being a Trustee.\r\n•\tGood independent judgement and the confidence to speak openly.\r\n•\tAbility to work effectively as part of a Board.\r\n•\tCommitment to Nolan’s Seven Principles of Public Life:\r\nSelflessness, Integrity, Objectivity, Accountability, Openness, Honesty, and Leadership.\r\n\r\nFor more information or to apply contact John Reid on 01292 270864 or email john@sacommunitytransport.org",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QhjnlAAB/board-of-management-trustee?#modal_register_a0g0800000QhjnlAAB",
