        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002myf1iAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002myf1iAAA/no-one-dies-alone-sa",
            "name": "No-One Dies Alone (SA)",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QhjMVAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QhjMVAAZ/local-events-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2023-08-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-16",
                    "title": "Local Events Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNo-one Dies Alone Ayrshire is a registered charity providing compassionate care to people in communities across Ayrshire who are alone and dying. Our experienced volunteers help people by being there in their final hours, offering a break and support to those with families who need it. \r\n\r\nWe offer our support free of charge and rely on alternative funding and events, which we organise from time to time. We are looking for volunteers to assist at local events. \r\nNODa Ayrshire (No-one Dies Alone) are looking for volunteers to operate stalls at events handing out leaflets and spreading awareness.  We can't underestimate how crucial this role is to helping us reach people who aren't on social media but need our services.  \r\nFull training and support offered and travel expenses paid.\r\n\r\nWhat you will be doing:\r\n\r\n• Engage with the public by operating a stall and handing out leaflets \r\n• Set up and break down on event days.\r\n• Ensure the safety and enjoyment of the visiting general public.\r\n• May also involve supporting people who visit the stall.\r\n\r\nVolunteering can be a rewarding and much valued service and has many benefits including meeting new people and gaining new skills.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo formal experience is required but a volunteers must be comfortable working with the general public and to have a caring, empathetic nature. This role is as and when required although regular events are held throughout the year.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QhjMVAAZ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Local Events Assistant",
                        "description": "No formal experience is required but a volunteers must be comfortable working with the general public and to have a caring, empathetic nature. This role is as and when required although regular events are held throughout the year.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QhjMVAAZ/local-events-assistant?#modal_register_a0g0800000QhjMVAAZ",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16",
