                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000G7CUfYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000G7CUfYAN/board-secretary",
                    "publishStart": "2026-03-31",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Board Secretary",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAge Concern Ayr SCIO is a charity working to support over 55s in South Ayrshire. We have a shop in Crown Street Ayr,  which is run totally by volunteers. The shop funds all our work, including our Advice Centre in Garden Street.  There we can assist people in maximising their income by helping them to access benefits they are eligible for, as well as assisting those who find it difficult to link to vital services in the digital age. This year alone we have granted £35,000 to other local charities and organisations to support older people. \r\n\r\nAge Concern Ayr has a Board of trustees, all volunteers, who meet monthly to ensure the smooth running of the charity. We currently are seeking to recruit a trustee who would take on the role of secretary.  We provide a friendly, supportive environment and the current secretary would be available to ensure a smooth handover.\r\n\r\nThe key aspects of the secretary role are: \r\n\r\n*  To produce a summary minute of the monthly Board Meetings. We meet on a Thursday at 12.30 pm to 2pm at our Advice Centre.\r\n*  To produce a Trustee Annual Report, although this year’s will be covered by the current secretary.\r\n*  To act with the other Trustees to take forward the work of the charity.\r\n\r\nIf you are interested in this role, please contact us at ageconcernayr@gmail.com .  We will be delighted to meet to give you further information.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEasy to communicate with, able to work on own initiative and able to follow instructions.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
