        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800002opRWeAAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800002opRWeAAM/kings-community-foundation",
            "name": "Kings Community Foundation",
            "description": "King’s Community Foundation exists to serve and enhance the living experience of people in communities. We achieve this by connecting people and giving opportunities to fulfil their potential in four key areas:\r\nCOMMUNITY INCLUSION \r\nCOMMUNITY REGENERATION\r\nCOMMUNITY PROVISION\r\nCOMMUNITY EDUCATION",
            "website": "https://www.kingscommunityfoundation.org/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FoodBanks",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Food Banks"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HtZ9pYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HtZ9pYAF/snowdrop-cafe-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-12",
                    "title": "Snowdrop Cafe Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe wonderful Snowdrop Café based at The Kings Way Centre, King's Way, Bridge of Don, AB23 8BL will be re-launched in September. It will be open every first and third Wednesday of the month at the King’s Way Centre, Bridge of Don, as a friendship & wellbeing space for those with Palliative Health Conditions & their carers. \r\n\r\nThe Snowdrop Cafe offers a calm space to foster friendship, wellbeing and care to individuals as well as their family, friends and carers who may also benefit from a listening ear. The cafe also provides free refreshments alongside activities such as jigsaws, games and crafts to bring enjoyment and relaxation amongst the guests to help improve emotional and mental wellbeing in difficult circumstances.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for compassionate, friendly volunteers who can offer a listening ear, give signposting information, serve refreshments and take part in the activities with the guests to create a warm, safe and enjoyable environment. Volunteers arrive at 1.30pm to set up, and finish around 4.15pm after tidying up. You will be put on a rota depending on your availability and how regular you would like to volunteer.\r\n\r\nAll help is greatly appreciated and will make a real difference.\r\n\r\nFor further details please contact Jessica Mustoe at email: kingsway@kingscommunityfoundation.org  ; telephone: 01224 518936 or complete the Volunteer With Us form at https://www.kingscommunityfoundation.org/join\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe Snowdrop Cafe will be taking place every 1st and 3rd Wednesday of the month, Volunteers arrive at 1.30pm to set up, and finish around 4.15pm after tidying up. You will be put on a rota depending on your availability and how regular you would like to volunteer.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Kings Way Centre, King's Way, Bridge of Don, AB23 8BL.\r\n\r\nThere are regular, direct buses to Bridge of Don from Aberdeen City. The King's Way Centre has lots of free parking available.",
