                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HU7NFYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HU7NFYA1/snowdrop-cafe-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-25",
                    "title": "Snowdrop Cafe Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe recently started running the Snowdrop Café but have currently paused it for summer to re-launch with a clearer aim in September. It will be open every first and third Wednesday of the month at the King’s Way Centre, Bridge of Don, as a friendship & wellbeing space for those with Palliative Health Conditions & their carers.\r\n\r\nThe Snowdrop Cafe offers a calm space to foster friendship, wellbeing and care to individuals as well as their family, friends and carers who may also benefit from a listening ear. The cafe also provides free refreshments alongside activities such as jigsaws, games and crafts to bring enjoyment and relaxation amongst the guests to help improve emotional and mental wellbeing in difficult circumstances.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for compassionate, friendly volunteers who can offer a listening ear, give signposting information, serve refreshments and take part in the activities with the guests to create a warm, safe and enjoyable environment.\r\n\r\nFor further details please complete the Volunteer With Us form at https://www.kingscommunityfoundation.org/join or email: kingsway@kingscommunityfoundation.org\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for compassionate, friendly volunteers who can offer a listening ear, give signposting information, serve refreshments and take part in the activities with the guests to create a warm, safe and enjoyable environment. A background in support or care work is desirable but not essential.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe Snowdrop Cafe will be taking place every 1st and 3rd Wednesday of the month starting from 2nd September 2026. Volunteers arrive at 1.30pm to set up, and finish around 4.15pm after tidying up. You will be put on a rota depending on your availability and how regular you would like to volunteer.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThere are regular, direct buses to Bridge of Don from Aberdeen City.\nThe King's Way Centre has lots of free parking available.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
