            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002PQ4faAAD/28th-braid-scout-group",
            "name": "28th Braid Scout Group",
            "description": "The Purpose of Scouting\nScouting exists to actively engage and support young people in their personal development, empowering them to make a positive contribution to society.\n\n\nThe Values of Scouting\nAs Scouts we are guided by these values:\n\nIntegrity - We act with integrity; we are honest, trustworthy and lo",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7KumAAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7KumAAF/leaderhelper",
                    "publishStart": "2022-02-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Leader/Helper",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nScouts is a young persons and adults experience – making friends, trying something new, doing something good for both your community and yourself and importantly making memories.   \n\nThis everyday adventure is possible thanks to our adult volunteers who don't need previous Scout Experience!\n\n## Description\n\nBeaver Scout Leaders/ Helpers- working with 6 and 7 year olds. Beavers meet on a Wednesday evening from 6.30-7.30pm\nScout Leaders/ Helpers - working with 1 to 14 year olds. Scouts meet on a Friday evening from 7.15 - 9.30pm\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnthusiasm, sense of humour, able to work either young people, happy to learn new skills, likes the outdoors.\r\n\r\nThe Scout Association has an award winning training scheme with lots of local support.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe training scheme is a mix of online and face to face training and supported by a Training Adviser that is one of the Leaders in our Group.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe meet in the Church Halls at Mayfield Salisbury Church, West Mayfieid which is well served by buses from the City Centre\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAn email to our Treasure that has been confirmed by a Leader",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7KumAAF#role",
