            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HKr81YAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HKr81YAD/volunteer-drivers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-14",
                    "title": "Volunteer Drivers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for volunteer drivers to join our wonderful team at Abernecessities.  We are a children's charity that work alongside local services and our wider community providing the everyday essentials and thoughtful extras that help children and families across Aberdeen and  Aberdeenshire because No Child Should Go Without.  \r\n\r\nVolunteer must hold a  full clean UK driving licence and be able to lift and move larger items of baby equipment  such as prams, flat pack cots,  etc as part of  a two person team.  Volunteers will work alongside another driver at all times who will go over the role alongside the Volunteer Co-ordinator. There are flexible times available during the week to help and all help is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nIf you have spare time during the week and would like to make a difference in the local community  we would love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Karen Macangus, Volunteer Co-ordinator at email: karen.macangus@abernecessities.co.uk or telephone: 01224 784000\r\n\r\nMore information about Abernecessities is also available at https://www.abernecessities.co.uk/\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for volunteer drivers to join our wonderful team at Abernecessities.  We are a children's charity that work alongside local services and our wider community providing the everyday essentials and thoughtful extras that help children and families across Aberdeen and  Aberdeenshire because No Child Should Go Without.  \r\n\r\nVolunteer must hold a  full clean UK driving licence and be able to lift and move larger items of baby equipment  such as prams, flat pack cots,  etc as part of  a two person team.  Volunteers will work alongside another driver at all times who will go over the role alongside the Volunteer Co-ordinator. There are flexible times available during the week to help and all help is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nIf you have spare time during the week and would like to make a difference in the local community  we would love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Karen Macangus, Volunteer Co-ordinator at email: karen@abernecessities.co.uk or telephone: 01224 784000\r\n\r\nMore information about Abernecessities is also available at https://www.abernecessities.co.uk/\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers must hold a  full clean UK driving licence and be able to lift and move larger items of baby equipment  such as prams, flat pack cots,  etc as part of  a two person team.\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant guidance and excellent support is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to help during weekdays. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.",
