        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002ZfoygAAB",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002ZfoygAAB/meal-makers",
            "name": "Meal Makers",
            "description": "Designed to be a fun volunteering opportunity based on an everyday activity, Meal Makers aims to tackle malnutrition and loneliness in older adults (55+), who struggle with the ability or motivation to prepare a home-cooked meal for themselves. As a Volunteer Cook Befriender, you will prepare an extra portion of food in your own home and deliver it to your 'Diner' at a time that suits you both. This opportunity is extremely flexible and meal sharing can occur as little or often as you like – weekly, fortnightly or just occasionally.",
            "website": "https://www.mealmakers.org.uk",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000Iqp0jAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000Iqp0jAAB/befriendercook",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Befriender/Cook",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nMeal Makers is a local neighbourhood food-sharing project that connects people who enjoy cooking and are happy to share an extra portion food with an older neighbour, who would really appreciate a home-cooked meal and some friendly company.\n\n## Description\n\nMeal Makers is a local neighbourhood food-sharing project that connects people with a love for cooking who are happy to share an extra portion of home cooked food with an older neighbour (or “diner”) who might be unable or lack the motivation to prepare a meal for themselves. Meals can be shared once a week, once a fortnight or every now and then, at times to suit. It is designed to be a flexible volunteering opportunity based on an everyday activity.\n\n## Experience required\n\nIt is essential that the volunteer has some people skills and is able to communicate with others. No training or formal cookery experience is required - just the ability to cook basic, nutritious meals.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteering with Meal Makers is an informal role. We will expect all volunteers to apply to become a member of the PVG scheme (at no cost to the volunteer) and take our short hygiene quiz. We have an informal chat to get to know our volunteers a little bit better and there will be ongoing support available from the Meal Makers team.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMeals are prepared at the volunteers’ home and delivered to the older person. We aim to match our volunteer cooks with a diner within walking distance but if you have a vehicle and are happy to travel a short distance, that is great!\nThis opportunity is Edinburgh-wide and we regularly have new Diners signing up to the service.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses paid.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000Iqp0jAAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Befriender/Cook",
                        "description": "It is essential that the volunteer has some people skills and is able to communicate with others. No training or formal cookery experience is required - just the ability to cook basic, nutritious meals.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000Iqp0jAAB/befriendercook?#modal_register_a0g1p00000Iqp0jAAB",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
