                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Gz9GTYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Gz9GTYAZ/charity-trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-21",
                    "title": "Charity Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCharity Trustee\n\n## Description\n\nArkbound Foundation is seeking new trustees to help guide and strengthen our work in social inclusion, publishing, education, and systems change.\n\nWe are a grassroots charity committed to amplifying underrepresented voices, supporting people facing barriers, and fostering a more just, compassionate, and interconnected society through creative expression, dialogue, and practical action.\n\nOur projects have included writing and mentoring programmes for people in prison and youth justice settings, publishing opportunities for emerging writers, educational initiatives, community workshops, and wider work exploring social, ecological, and economic transformation.\n\nWe are currently looking for thoughtful, values-driven individuals to join our Board of Trustees and contribute to the next stage of the charity&rsquo;s development.\n\nWhat the role involves\n\nTrustees play a vital role in supporting the governance, strategic direction, and long-term sustainability of the charity. Responsibilities include:\n\n\n\t\n\tHelping guide the charity&rsquo;s vision, strategy, and development\n\t\n\t\n\tSupporting good governance and ethical decision-making\n\t\n\t\n\tContributing ideas, insight, and constructive challenge\n\t\n\t\n\tReviewing key organisational matters such as finance, fundraising, partnerships, and project development\n\t\n\t\n\tActing as ambassadors for the charity and its mission\n\t\n\t\n\tSupporting the charity&rsquo;s commitment to inclusion, creativity, and social impact\n\t\n\n\nTrustees are not expected to manage day-to-day operations, but to provide oversight, guidance, and support alongside the wider team.\n\nTime commitment\n\n\n\t\n\tApproximately 4&ndash;8 hours per month minimum\n\t\n\t\n\tAttendance at quarterly trustee meetings (minimum expectation)\n\t\n\t\n\tOccasional additional input depending on availability and areas of interest\n\t\n\n\nMeetings are generally held online, allowing flexibility for trustees based in different locations.\n\nWho we are looking for\n\nWe welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds, particularly those who share the charity&rsquo;s ethos of compassion, inclusion, dignity, creativity, and systemic change.\n\nWe are especially interested in hearing from people with experience or interest in areas such as:\n\n\n\t\n\tPublishing, writing, or education\n\t\n\t\n\tYouth justice or social inclusion\n\t\n\t\n\tCommunity development\n\t\n\t\n\tFundraising or charity governance\n\t\n\t\n\tFinance or legal knowledge\n\t\n\t\n\tEcology, sustainability, or regenerative systems\n\t\n\t\n\tCommunications and partnerships\n\t\n\t\n\tLived experience of social barriers or marginalisation\n\t\n\n\nPrevious trustee experience is welcome but not required. Integrity, openness, collaborative spirit, and alignment with the charity&rsquo;s values are more important than formal credentials.\n\nWhy join Arkbound?\n\nArkbound is a small but ambitious charity that believes meaningful change often begins at the margins &mdash; through voice, creativity, community, and the courage to imagine alternatives.\n\nJoining the Board offers an opportunity to contribute to work that seeks not only to support individuals, but also to challenge deeper patterns of exclusion, disconnection, and inequality within society.\n\nWe are particularly interested in trustees who value both practical action and deeper reflection on the kind of society we wish to help build.\n\nHow to apply\n\nTo express interest, please send a short introduction outlining your background, interests, and why the role appeals to you.\n\nEmail: steve@arkbound.com\nWebsite: www.arkfound.org\n\nIf you are interested,&nbsp;please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when&nbsp;registered and&nbsp;logged in). You&nbsp;will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that&nbsp;doesn&rsquo;t&nbsp;work&nbsp;out,&nbsp;then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org.&nbsp;\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are seeking thoughtful, collaborative individuals who care about social impact and share the ethos of the charity. Strong communication skills, reliability, openness to dialogue, and the ability to think constructively and strategically are all valuable qualities for the role.\n\nWhile specific professional expertise is welcome, previous trustee experience is not essential. We particularly encourage applications from people with experience or interest in areas such as community development, e\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a remote volunteering role, meaning you can volunteer from the comfort of your own home - or anywhere with access to Wi-Fi.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses can be paid, and any reasonable expenses incurred as a result of performing the role",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
