                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000078NjNYAU/board-members",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-24",
                    "title": "Board Members",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for individuals to join our board of trustees at Tillydrone Community Campus SCIO in Tillydrone Aberdeen. Tillydrone Community Campus  SCIO (registered charity)  is a board of like minded members who have come together to help organise activities and services in the local area.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for people who have a passion for community led activities and empowering the community. We have some exciting times ahead with this amazing building and we would love to have board members that are good minute takers, have administration and finance experience or a community passion.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to make a real difference for people and the community. All help is greatly appreciated. For more information please contact Marie Strang, Project Coordinator at email: tillydronepc@gmail.com or telephone: 07799058495\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for individuals to join our board of trustees at Tillydrone Community Campus SCIO in Tillydrone Aberdeen. Tillydrone Community Campus  SCIO (registered charity)  is a board of like minded members who have come together to help organise activities and services in the local area.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for people who have a passion for community led activities and empowering the community. We have some exciting times ahead with this amazing building and we would love to have board members that are good minute takers, have administration and finance experience or a community passion.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to make a real difference for people and the community. All help is greatly appreciated. For more information please contact Marie Strang, Project Coordinator at email: tillydronepc@gmail.com or telephone: 07799058495\n\n## Training details\n\nThe board is very supportive of each other and relevant guidance, training and excellent support is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to volunteer. All help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTillydrone Community Campus SCIO\r\n52 Hayton Road \r\nAberdeen \r\nAB24 2UY",
