                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HuyKfYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HuyKfYAJ/minute-taker-volunteer-for-scio-charity-board-meetings",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Minute taker volunteer for SCIO (charity) board meetings",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for an individual who would be willing to come along to our monthly board meetings at Tillydrone Community Campus, the first Tuesday of every month and volunteer to take the minutes of our SCIO (charity) board meetings. Our meetings take place 6pm until 8pm.\r\n \r\nWe are looking for someone to take board meeting notes (we have been using Microsoft Co pilot) for our minutes. You would also liaise with our Chairperson for monthly Agenda topics to be added to the agenda. \r\n\r\nThe board would be happy to support and show how this has been done previously and our board is very welcoming.\r\n  \r\nWe are based at Tillydrone Community Campus 52 Hayton Road. We are on the number 19 bus route and have ample parking at the Campus\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to make a real difference for people and the community. All help is greatly appreciated. For more information please contact Marie Strang, Project Coordinator at email: tillydronepc@gmail.com\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for an individual who would be willing to come along to our monthly board meetings at Tillydrone Community Campus, the first Tuesday of every month and volunteer to take the minutes of our SCIO (charity) board meetings. Our meetings take place 6pm until 8pm.\r\n \r\nWe are looking for someone to take board meeting notes (we have been using Microsoft Co pilot) for our minutes. You would also liaise with our Chairperson for monthly Agenda topics to be added to the agenda. \r\n\r\nThe board is very welcoming, supportive and would be happy to support and show how this has been done previously.\r\n  \r\nWe are based at Tillydrone Community Campus 52 Hayton Road. We are on the number 19 bus route and have ample parking at the Campus\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to make a real difference for people and the community. All help is greatly appreciated. For more information please contact Marie Strang, Project Coordinator at email: tillydronepc@gmail.com\n\n## Training details\n\nThe board would be happy to support and show how this has been done previously and provide any guidance required.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe first Tuesday of every month. Our meetings take place 6pm until 8pm.  All help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTillydrone Community Campus SCIO\r\n52 Hayton Road \r\nAberdeen \r\nAB24 2UY\r\n\r\nWe are on the number 19 bus route and have ample parking at the Campus",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
