            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IObSJYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IObSJYA1/brunch-club-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-07",
                    "title": "Brunch Club Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nKLSB Community Group is a registered charity supporting people in Larbert, Stenhousemuir and surrounding communities. They run a community pantry and foodbank, emergency food support, a community café, seniors lunch clubs and local events. KLSB aim to bring people together, reduce isolation and offer practical help when it’s needed.\r\n\r\nThe Brunch Club gives people an opportunity to enjoy food, company and conversation in a welcoming setting. Your role will help the session run smoothly and make guests feel comfortable and included.  Tasks may include:\r\n\r\nHelping prepare tables and the café for the session.\r\nWelcoming guests and helping them get settled.\r\nChatting with guests and helping everyone feel included.\r\nHelping prepare snacks and drinks.\r\nSupporting the team with serving food and drinks.\r\nCarrying plates, cups and other items to and from tables.\r\nClearing tables and helping with washing up.\r\nKeeping serving areas clean and tidy.\r\nHelping tidy the café at the end of the session.\r\nFollowing food hygiene and health and safety instructions.\r\nPassing questions, dietary requests or concerns to the person responsible for the session.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers must be friendly, chatty and approachable, patient, respectful and non-judgemental.\r\nVolunteers should be reliable, comfortable talking with people from different backgrounds and willing to follow instructions and learn.\r\nVolunteers should be happy working as part of a team and be comfortable carrying out agreed tasks without supervision once trained.\r\n\r\nYou don’t need to be a confident cook or have worked in hospitality before. A welcoming manner and willingness to help are what matter.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou’ll receive an introduction to the café, the brunch club and the team, along with guidance on your duties and how each session runs.\r\n\r\nTraining will cover the tasks you undertake, including serving food and drinks, hygiene, health and safety, and respecting guests’ privacy. You’ll receive guidance during your initial sessions and know who to approach for help, questions or concerns.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nEvery 2nd Tuesday, 11.30am - 1.00pm\r\n1.5 hrs every 2nd week.  Minimum 3 month commitment.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Point Cafe, 17 King Street, Stenhousemuir, FK5 4HD.\r\nPublic parking and transport is nearby.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses are NOT available.",
