                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IOdaYYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IOdaYYAT/cafe-open-day-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-07",
                    "title": "Café Open Day Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nKLSB Community Group is a registered charity supporting people in Larbert, Stenhousemuir and surrounding communities. They run a community pantry and foodbank, emergency food support, a community café, seniors lunch clubs and local events. KLSB aim to bring people together, reduce isolation and offer practical help when it’s needed.\r\n\r\nThe Cafe Open Day gives people an opportunity to enjoy food, company and conversation in a welcoming setting. Your role will help the session run smoothly and make guests feel comfortable and included.  The role involves: \r\n\r\nHelping prepare tables and the café for the session.\r\nWelcoming guests and helping them get settled.\r\nChatting with guests and helping everyone feel included.\r\nAssisting in preparing simple snacks and drinks.\r\nSupporting the team with serving food and drinks.\r\nCarrying plates, cups and other items to and from tables.\r\nClearing tables and helping with washing up.\r\nKeeping serving areas clean and tidy.\r\nHelping tidy the café at the end of the session.\r\nFollowing food hygiene and health and safety instructions.\r\nPassing questions, dietary requests or concerns to the person responsible for the session.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers must be friendly, chatty, patient and reliable. You should enjoy spending time with older people, respect their privacy and treat everyone with dignity.\r\n\r\nYou’ll need to follow instructions, work well within a team and be comfortable carrying out agreed duties without constant supervision once trained.\r\n\r\nNo previous experience is required — full training will be provided.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou’ll receive an induction covering how the club operates, your duties, food hygiene, health and safety, and confidentiality. Guidance will be provided during your initial sessions, with ongoing support from the person responsible for the club.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThursdays from 9.30am - 1.30pm/\r\n3 hours per week, 3 months commitment.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Point Cafe, 17 King Street, Stenhousemuir, FK5 4HD.\r\nPublic parking and transport is nearby.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses are NOT available.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://www.klsb.org.uk/uploads/1/3/1/9/131929463/published/klsb-0.png?1655623243",
