                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VupvzAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VupvzAAB/wednesday-seniors-lunch-club-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-07",
                    "title": "Wednesday Seniors Lunch Club Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nKLSB Community Group is a registered charity supporting people in Larbert, Stenhousemuir and surrounding communities. They run a community pantry and foodbank, emergency food support, a community café, seniors lunch clubs and local events. KLSB aim to bring people together, reduce isolation and offer practical help when it’s needed.\r\n\r\nThe Wednesday Seniors Lunch Club brings older people together to enjoy lunch, conversation and companionship. Volunteers help create a friendly, welcoming atmosphere and support the team with running the session.  The role involves:\r\n\r\nPreparing tables and helping get the café ready.\r\nWelcoming guests and helping them get settled.\r\nChatting with guests and making everyone feel included.\r\nHelping prepare hot food and drinks.\r\nHelping serve hot food and drinks.\r\nClearing tables, washing up and keeping the café tidy.\r\nHelping tidy up at the end of the session.\r\nPassing dietary requests, questions or concerns to the person responsible for the club.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers who are friendly, chatty and approachable, patient, respectful and non-judgemental.\r\nVolunteer should be reliable, comfortable talking with people from different backgrounds and willing to follow instructions and learn.\r\nVolunteers should be able to work as part of a team, comfortable carrying out agreed tasks without constant supervision once trained.\r\n\r\nYou don’t need to be a confident cook or have worked in hospitality before. A welcoming manner and willingness to help are what matter.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive an introduction to the café, the lunch club and the team, along with guidance on your duties and how each session runs.\r\n\r\nTraining will cover the tasks you undertake, including serving food and drinks, hygiene, health and safety, and respecting guests’ privacy. \r\n\r\nVolunteers will receive guidance during initial sessions and know who to approach for help, questions or concerns.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWednesdays 11.30am - 1.30pm\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Point Cafe, 17 King Street, Stenhousemuir, FK5 4HD.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses are NOT available.",
