                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7IOnAAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7IOnAAN/foodbank-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-07",
                    "title": "Foodbank Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nKLSB Community Group is a registered charity supporting people in Larbert, Stenhousemuir and surrounding communities. They run a community pantry and foodbank, emergency food support, a community café, seniors lunch clubs and local events. Their aim is to bring people together, reduce isolation and offer practical help when it’s needed.\r\n\r\nKLSB are currently looking for one regular volunteer on Saturdays, 10.45am – 12.45pm, to help prepare the pantry/foodbank, welcome visitors, help them select items, sort donations, check food dates, restock shelves, and tidy up.\r\n\r\nVolunteers must be 18 or over, friendly, reliable, respectful and comfortable working without supervision once trained. Volunteers must respect visitors’ privacy and provide support without judgement.\r\n\r\nThe role involves bending, reaching and lifting or carrying food supplies. There is limited capacity to change these duties but would welcome a discussion on what’s involved before applying.\r\n\r\nNo experience is needed as full training will be provided. You’ll gain practical charity experience, develop communication and teamwork skills, and help deliver an essential community service.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers should be friendly, approachable, patient and reliable, with good communication skills and a respectful, non-judgemental attitude. They must be comfortable working as part of a team, follow instructions, and respect confidentiality.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive an induction covering how the pantry operates, their duties, safe food handling, health and safety, and confidentiality. \r\nFull training will be provided, with guidance during initial sessions and ongoing support from the person responsible for the pantry. \r\nVolunteers will know who to contact with questions or concerns.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nSaturdays, 10.45am – 12.45pm.\r\n2 Hours per week.  Minimum 3 months commitment.\n\n## Travel details\n\n38 King Street, Stenhousemuir, FK5 4HE (next to Farmfoods)\r\nFree parking is available nearby, and the location is accessible by public transport.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are NOT available.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://www.klsb.org.uk/uploads/1/3/1/9/131929463/published/klsb-0.png?1655623243",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7IOnAAN#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Foodbank Volunteer",
                        "description": "Volunteers should be friendly, approachable, patient and reliable, with good communication skills and a respectful, non-judgemental attitude. They must be comfortable working as part of a team, follow instructions, and respect confidentiality.",
                        "commitment": "Saturdays, 10.45am – 12.45pm.\r\n2 Hours per week.  Minimum 3 months commitment.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7IOnAAN/foodbank-volunteer?#modal_register_a0g0800000V7IOnAAN",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
