                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-23",
                    "title": "Snowdrop Cafe Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe aim of the Snowdrop Café is to bring people together, in an inclusive and friendly environment where they will be respected and accepted. The Snowdrop Café will welcome everyone from within the community with a focus on those feeling lonely and isolated. The main objective is to make friendships, enjoy each others company and activities together, forming a sense of belonging.\r\n\r\nThe Snowdrop Café are currently looking to recruit new volunteers within any of their current Cafes across the Falkirk area.  Tasks involved may include: \r\n\r\n*setting up tables and chairs\r\n*greeting people into the Cafe and making them feel welcome\r\n*preparing and serving tea and coffee\r\n*clearing up and washing dishes\r\n\r\nThis is a very flexible role and would welcome a conversation with anyone who would like to help!\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience required. \r\nSomeone who is friendly, sociable and willing to help.\n\n## Training details\n\nInitial induction and training for the role will be provided.\r\nOne to One support will be given on an ongoing basis as well regular catch-ups.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nDenny: Thursdays, 12-3pm\r\nHaggs: Mondays, 12.30pm-3pm\r\nBainsford: Tuesdays, 12-2pm\r\nFalkirk: Mondays, 12.30-3pm\r\nGrangemouth: Wednesdays, 1pm-3pm\n\n## Travel details\n\nDenny: Westpark Church, Duke Street, FK6 6NP\r\nBainsford: Bainsford Community Hall, David's Loan, FK2 7NS\r\nHaggs: Church Hall, Kilsyth Road, FK4 1HA\r\nGrangemouth: Kirk of the Holy Rood, Bowhouse Road, FK3 0EX\r\nFalkirk: Trinity Church, Manse Place, FK1 1JN\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses are NOT available.\n\n## Taster details\n\nTaster session can be provided if this would be beneficial.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
