        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002da3SXAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002da3SXAAY/samh-scottish-action-for-mental-health-aberdeen-services",
            "name": "SAMH (Scottish Action for Mental Health) Aberdeen Services",
            "description": "SAMH has been committed to Scotland’s mental health for nearly 100 years. Today, in over 60 communities we work with adults and young people providing mental health social care support, services in primary care, schools and further education, among others.  These services together with our national programme work in See Me, respectme, suicide prevention and active living; inform our policy and campaign work to influence positive social change.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GLBP4YAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GLBP4YAP/volunteer-at-the-nook",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-19",
                    "title": "Volunteer at The Nook",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe're looking for volunteers! \r\n\r\nThe Nook in Aberdeen will open its doors this summer, and we need your help. Located at Marischal Square, Upperkirkgate, Aberdeen City Centre, The Nook in Aberdeen offers free, drop-in mental health and wellbeing support seven days a week - without the need for an appointment or referral. A safe, stigma-free space where anyone can visit to speak about mental health. The Nook will provide visitors with access to support for themselves, or people they care about. \r\n\r\nWe're looking for friendly faces to join as either as a Wellbeing Volunteer, or a Peer Support Volunteer:\r\n\r\n-Wellbeing Volunteers\r\nYou’ll help create a welcoming, supportive space for people seeking mental health support. You'll greet visitors, offer a compassionate ear, and assist with setting up the space and wellbeing activities.  No qualifications are needed, just empathy, good listening skills and a commitment to helping others feel safe and respected.\r\n\r\n-Peer Support Volunteers:\r\nPeer Support Volunteers use their own experiences of mental health recovery to support others. You’ll help run support groups and conversation cafes, provide understanding through shared experience, and contribute to a safe, non-judgemental environment.  This role is an opportunity to use your lived experience in a purposeful way, with space for growth, learning and reflection.\r\n\r\nThese roles are flexible, all training and ongoing support is provided, and we can help you develop new skills and improve existing ones.\r\n\r\nVolunteering with SAMH provides the opportunity to:\r\n-Make a Difference – Using your own experience, help contribute to the delivery of timely compassionate support to those who need it most, ensuring they receive the help they deserve in a welcoming and safe environment.\r\n-Develop New Skills – Gain confidence and valuable experience, with the chance to develop your knowledge and skills through ongoing support and training opportunities.\r\n-Make Meaningful Connections - Join a supportive team of staff and volunteers who value inclusion, compassion, and mutual respect, where every voice is heard, and contribution valued\r\n\r\nRoss, a Wellbeing Volunteer with SAMH shares a bit about his experience so far in the role.: “My favourite thing about The Nook is the number of people I’ve got to meet and interact with.\r\n\"Everyone at The Nook is very responsive to the fact you're always learning. It's helped me develop my skills, but if I'm ever unsure, I can go to anyone on shift to get support.\r\n\"We do hear how much The Nook has supported people, and it's great to be able to provide that. It's a great service that's been really needed. The flexibility at The Nook is great. I've still got time to do my hospitality job in the evening, as well as balance university.\"\r\n\r\nIf you’re ready to be part of The Nook and help transform access to mental health support in Aberdeen we’d love to hear from you! \r\n\r\nFor more information and to register your interest please visit https://www.samh.org.uk/about-us/the-nook/volunteers and https://forms.cloud.microsoft/Pages/ResponsePage.aspx?id=jkS91ZsV3EiHi4qmYWs_FHMA_4s6y7BJiC7YiVGBNXNURjBQNldUQkU4WDZOVzNPM0w5ODQ4T1RGMS4u\n\n## Description\n\nWe're looking for volunteers! \r\n\r\nThe Nook in Aberdeen is located at Marischal Square, Upperkirkgate, Aberdeen City Centre. It offers free, drop-in mental health and wellbeing support seven days a week - without the need for an appointment or referral. A safe, stigma-free space where anyone can visit to speak about mental health. The Nook will provide visitors with access to support for themselves, or people they care about. \r\n\r\nWe're looking for friendly faces to join as either as a Wellbeing Volunteer, or a Peer Support Volunteer:\r\n\r\n-Wellbeing Volunteers\r\nYou’ll help create a welcoming, supportive space for people seeking mental health support. You'll greet visitors, offer a compassionate ear, and assist with setting up the space and wellbeing activities.  No qualifications are needed, just empathy, good listening skills and a commitment to helping others feel safe and respected.\r\n\r\n-Peer Support Volunteers:\r\nPeer Support Volunteers use their own experiences of mental health recovery to support others. You’ll help run support groups and conversation cafes, provide understanding through shared experience, and contribute to a safe, non-judgemental environment.  This role is an opportunity to use your lived experience in a purposeful way, with space for growth, learning and reflection.\r\n\r\nThese roles are flexible, all training and ongoing support is provided, and we can help you develop new skills and improve existing ones.\r\n\r\nVolunteering with SAMH provides the opportunity to:\r\n-Make a Difference – Using your own experience, help contribute to the delivery of timely compassionate support to those who need it most, ensuring they receive the help they deserve in a welcoming and safe environment.\r\n-Develop New Skills – Gain confidence and valuable experience, with the chance to develop your knowledge and skills through ongoing support and training opportunities.\r\n-Make Meaningful Connections - Join a supportive team of staff and volunteers who value inclusion, compassion, and mutual respect, where every voice is heard, and contribution valued\r\n\r\nRoss, a Wellbeing Volunteer with SAMH shares a bit about his experience so far in the role.: “My favourite thing about The Nook is the number of people I’ve got to meet and interact with.\r\n\"Everyone at The Nook is very responsive to the fact you're always learning. It's helped me develop my skills, but if I'm ever unsure, I can go to anyone on shift to get support.\r\n\"We do hear how much The Nook has supported people, and it's great to be able to provide that. It's a great service that's been really needed. The flexibility at The Nook is great. I've still got time to do my hospitality job in the evening, as well as balance university.\"\r\n\r\nIf you’re ready to be part of The Nook and help transform access to mental health support in Aberdeen we’d love to hear from you! \r\n\r\nFor more information and to register your interest please visit https://www.samh.org.uk/about-us/the-nook/volunteers and https://forms.cloud.microsoft/Pages/ResponsePage.aspx?id=jkS91ZsV3EiHi4qmYWs_FHMA_4s6y7BJiC7YiVGBNXNURjBQNldUQkU4WDZOVzNPM0w5ODQ4T1RGMS4u\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and training is provided to all volunteers. Includes:\r\n•\tFull induction and volunteer-specific training  \r\n•\tAccess to our Employee assistance programme and a tailored wellness plan \r\n•\tOngoing support, development and reflective practice opportunities. \r\n•\tAccess to support from The Nook \r\n•\tReasonable out-of-pocket expenses reimbursed (to be pre-approved in advance)\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWe offer flexible volunteering to support your availability, and, if suitable, we are looking for those who can commit to at least 2 hours per week, but we can accommodate more.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Nook-Aberdeen is located at Marischal Square, Upperkirkgate, Aberdeen City Centre, AB10 1BA\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable out-of-pocket expenses reimbursed (to be pre-approved in advance)",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F8907bd82-08fe-4202-9555-1757673dff10%2FsHgcy26YlBhDTQpnnnHUFa96Zib2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=1b0782e8-485e-4c15-bf42-c0ab490b59d4",
                    "role": {
