        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002BLxxRAAT",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002BLxxRAAT/bethany-christian-trust",
            "name": "Bethany Christian Trust",
            "description": "Bethany Christian Trust is a national charity whose mission is to relieve the suffering and meet the long term needs of homeless and vulnerable people in Scotland. We share a big vision – to work together towards the aim of Ending Homelessness in Scotland. We support people in a broad range of ways including: housing, education and employment, addiction recovery, emotional well-being, street outreach, community integration, offending reduction and social support",
            "website": "https://www.bethanychristiantrust.com",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VupVSAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VupVSAAZ/care-van-driver-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2023-07-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Care Van Driver Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for drivers to take the Care Van into the city and stop at 4 spots to allow volunteers to serve food and hot drinks.\n\n## Description\n\nThe Care Van, which Bethany runs in partnership with Edinburgh City Mission, is an all year round service that offers food and support to people who are experiencing homelessness in the city. Duties include:\nCheck the Care Van for damage or problems before leaving.\nDrive the Care Van, following the usual route.\nStay close to the Care Van at all times in case it needs moved in a hurry.  \nReport any incidents or damage to the Care Van.\n\n## Experience required\n\nDrivers must hold a full UK driving licence, be 25+ years old, have at least two years driving experience and annually submit a Driver Form and copy of their licence to Bethany.\nWe are looking for volunteers who have an understanding of appropriate boundaries and a willingness to work within these.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction provided.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteers are to meet at the Care Van located behind Bethany Christian Centre, at Jane Street.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nIf you have used public transport to travel to and from your role, or as part of your role, you are eligible to claim this money back – up to the equivalent of a Day Ticket on each occasion. You must retain a receipt.",
