                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNrViAAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNrViAAL/volunteer-support-bethany-christian-centre",
                    "publishStart": "2021-10-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Volunteer Support Bethany Christian Centre",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you have one night a week to offer as a Sleepover Volunteer? Are you passionate about the transformative power of Christ's love? Then this may be the role for you!\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for volunteers to support the Bethany Christian Centre staff team in giving quality support to residents in the evening. This includes tasks such as participating in recreational activities with residents and staff, cleaning and/or cooking duties as required and general administrative duties, including answering phones and taking messages.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers should:\nHave experience of providing general support to vulnerable people.\nBe mindful of personal wellbeing and appropriate boundaries.\nHave an interest in and some understanding of homelessness, mental health issues, and addiction problems.\nBe of Christian faith, in agreement with the vision and values of Bethany, and able to show God’s love in action.\n\n## Training details\n\nThere is mandatory training that the volunteer must complete at induction, and additional training may become necessary going forward.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nIdeally volunteer on a weekly basis.\n5pm to 9am. Starting no later than 9pm, spending time with the residents until later in the evening and sleeping accommodation provided overnight. Leaving at 9am.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBethany Christian Centre\n6 Casselbank Street,\nEdinburgh\nEH6 5HA\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nif you have used public transport to travel to and from your role, or as part of your role, you are eligible to claim this money back- up to the equivalent of a Day Ticket. You must retain a receipt.",
