                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Click and Connect Computer Drop-In Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAre you sociable, friendly and a P.C. Pro? Then this could be the role for you!\nClick and Connect is a computer drop-in held at Bethany Christian Trust’s Learning Centre. Volunteers are required to help participants learn new digital skills.\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteers should;\nFoster a supportive and encouraging environment; welcoming people to the group, facilitating social interactions through discussions and offering a listening ear.\nOffer digital support to those attending the group, as well as offering advice and support on issues such as CV writing, health and well-being, filling out online forms etc.\nHelp with the set-up and clean-up of the group, arriving on time in order to do so.\nAlert staff of any concerns.\n\nTuesdays from 10.30 to 12.30pm.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers should be;\nSociable and have an approachable manner.\nAble to listen sympathetically and communicate effectively.\nOrganised, with good time management skills.\nBe willing to work as part of a group, as well as independently.\nDigitally literate.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining will be given at induction, and on a regular basis as necessary.\n\n## Travel details\n\n65 Bonnington Road, Edinburgh, EH6 5JQ\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nBethany Christian Trust recognises the importance and value of volunteering and wishes to, as far as  possible, mitigate financial barriers to volunteering. Reasonable expenses that occur as a direct result of volunteering are eligible to be reimbursed if correct protocol is followed. An individual is eligible for reimbursement of expenses if they volunteer for a minimum of four hours per shift. Expense reimbursement for a shorter period will, however, be considered on a case-by-case basis, and at the discretion of the volunteer manager and/or supervisor.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pv9rMAAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Click and Connect Computer Drop-In Volunteer",
                        "description": "Volunteers should be;\nSociable and have an approachable manner.\nAble to listen sympathetically and communicate effectively.\nOrganised, with good time management skills.\nBe willing to work as part of a group, as well as independently.\nDigitally literate.",
