                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000L2jVgAAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000L2jVgAAJ/lunchtime-care-van-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2020-01-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Lunchtime Care Van Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe need volunteers to take Care Van into the city centre and distribute food, hot drinks and clothing to people who are experiencing homelessness.\nThis is a vitally important, practical way to serve others and we can't do it without you!\n\n## Description\n\nThis role includes\nStock the Care van with cups, lids, flasks and food.  \nServe food and drinks to guests.\nDistribute any donations of clothing.\nSpeak to clients; offer advice where appropriate.  \nReport any incidents, feedback or training needs in the report folders.\nClean the van on return to the Centre.\nDrivers:\nCheck the Care Van for damage or issues before leaving the Centre. The same should be done on return. \nDrive the Van, following the usual route & stay close to the Van at all times.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA volunteer should be able to;\nListen & communicate clearly\nWork as part of a team\nRemain patient & calm\nWork within appropriate boundaries\n\nVolunteers should be sympathetic with the aims of Bethany Christian Trust as expressed in its mission and values statements (found on our website)\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining will be given at induction and on an ongoing basis as required\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteers are to meet at the Care Van located behind Bethany Christian Centre, at Jane Street. The Van will return here.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nIf you have used public transport to travel to and from your role, or as part of your role, you are entitled to claim this money back- up to the equivalent of a Day Ticket .You must retain a receipt,.",
