                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000FmKllAAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000FmKllAAF/retail-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2021-04-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Retail Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBe part of our mission to relieve the suffering and meet the long term needs of homeless and vulnerable people in Scotland by helping to raise vital funds.\n\n## Description\n\nRetail volunteers are the backbone of our shops. A day can include sorting donations, operating the till or pricing stock – every day, and every shop, is different! Each volunteer brings their own skills, experience and character to a role.\n\n## Experience required\n\nDifferent roles have different requirements but largely we ask our volunteers to be friendly, willing to help, and ready to learn and committed to being part of the retail team.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction takes place when the volunteer starts.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe operate 6 shops across Edinburgh and one in Gullane.\nDuke Street.\nStockbridge.\n32B Haddington Place.\n33A Haddington Place (Bethany Bookshop).\nSummerhall Place.\nMorningside.\nGullane.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nIf you have used public transport to travel to and from your role, or as part of your role, you are entitled to claim this money back- up to the equivalent of a Day Ticket. You must retain a receipt.",
