                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000OUwnyAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000OUwnyAAD/passing-the-baton-befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2020-11-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Passing the Baton Befriender",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nLoneliness and social isolation in our communities kills more people than smoking 15 cigarettes per day.\nWe are looking for befrienders to help combat this through our Passing the Baton programme.\n\n## Description\n\nBefriending can make a huge impact in the lives of people who are at risk of homelessness or moving into new settled accommodation. You can help an individual in Edinburgh reconnect back into the community by taking them out and introducing them to social groups and activities in their area.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for volunteers who:\nHave integrity and are reliable.\nAre sociable and have an approachable manner.\nHave good time management and organisational skills.\nAre able to operate under the guidance and support of Passing the Baton staff.\nAre of Christian faith, rooted in a Christian community.\n\n## Training details\n\nThere are 2 initial traning sessions which cover things such as confidentiality, and ongoing traning is given as needed.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMeeting location arranged between you and the person you are befriending.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nIf you have used public transport to travel to and from your role, or as part of your role, you are entitled to claim this money back- up to the equivalent of a Day Ticket. You must retain a receipt,.",
