                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IBT5xYAH/volunteer-driver",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-29",
                    "title": "Volunteer Driver",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nBailliefields is the charitable arm of Westquarter & Redding Cricket Club in Brightons.  In addition to offering a variety of commercial groups such as yoga, pilates, line dancing, children's music and language classes, Bailliefields also runs a number of groups. These include a monthly 'Try Something New' dementia group, a weekly Social Café and a weekly community gardening project. \r\n\r\nBailliefields Community Hub are looking for a volunteer driver to help out with driving for their community garden project which currently takes place on Fridays.  Bailliefields have a 16 seat minibus which can be driven on a standard driving licence - the driver needs to be aged between 25 and 70 with 5 years driving experience. \r\n\r\nPick-ups are usually around 9.30am - 10am from locations such as Grangemouth, Bo'ness and Denny to bring them to Bailliefields in Brightons.  Drop-offs take place later in the day, anytime between 1.30pm and 3pm. \r\n\r\nAny volunteer drivers would be welcome to also take part in the garden project if desired, or just to do the driving - either is fine.  Lunch is served at approx. 12.30pm to the garden volunteers and the driver would be very welcome to join.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers need to hold a current driving licence and have been driving for a minimum of 5 years.\r\n\r\nYou will pick up a variety of people from the community; older people, sometimes with mobility restrictions, and people who English is not their first language. \r\nVolunteer drivers should be kind, patient and empathetic in addition to being confident drivers.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe volunteer would have an induction with the Community Hub Officer and trustees from Bailliefields. They would be given full training on the minibus and an opportunity to drive it before taking up any volunteer position. Any support required could be discussed prior to commencement of volunteering.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFridays: 9am-10.30am, 1.30-3pm (driving only).\r\n9am - 3.30pm if the volunteer would like to stay during the  gardening session.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBailliefields Community Hub, Brightons, FK2 0RN. \r\nLarge car park and are situated a couple of minutes from a stop on the number 1 bus route from Dunipace to Maddiston (via Denny, Camelon, Falkirk, Laurieston & Polmont). Approx. 15 minute walk (uphill) from Polmont train station.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nOwn car mileage paid at 40p per mile (10 miles each way maximum) or bus fare reimbursed to cover travel from home to Bailliefields and back.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://bailliefields.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Balliefields-logo-main-RGB-768x193.webp",
