        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002CJ2fkAAD",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002CJ2fkAAD/glasgows-gollden-generation",
            "name": "Glasgow's Gollden Generation",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/GlasgowsGoldenGeneration",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0IsDYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I0IsDYAV/day-centre-connectors-for-glasgows-golden-generation",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Day Centre Connectors for Glasgow's Golden Generation",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDay Centre Connectors for Glasgow's Golden Generation\n\n## Description\n\nAs a Day Centre Connector, you&#39;ll help create a warm, welcoming and inclusive environment where older people feel valued, supported and connected.\n\nWhether you&#39;re chatting over a cup of tea, helping with activities, welcoming new members or lending a hand behind the scenes, you&#39;ll play an important role in reducing loneliness and making sure our members enjoy a positive and meaningful experience every time they visit.\n\nWhat You&#39;ll Do\n\nYou may support the Day Centre by:\n\n\n\tWelcoming members, visitors and volunteers into the centre.\n\tHelping to create a friendly and inclusive atmosphere.\n\tSupporting staff with the delivery of activities, games and events.\n\tEncouraging members to participate in activities and social opportunities.\n\tAssisting with preparing rooms and activity materials.\n\tServing refreshments and supporting meal times where required.\n\tHelping members feel comfortable, included and connected.\n\tSharing your skills, interests or hobbies with members where appropriate.\n\tSupporting special events, celebrations and community activities.\n\tGathering feedback and ideas from members about activities they&#39;d like to enjoy.\n\n\nWe&rsquo;re looking for people who are friendly, patient and reliable, with good listening and communication skills, who enjoy supporting older people, working as part of a team, and are open to learning new things.\n\nWhat you&#39;ll get out of volunteering with us:&nbsp;\n\n\n\tMake a real difference by helping older people feel connected and valued.\n\tHelp reduce loneliness and isolation in your community.\n\tMeet new people and become part of a friendly team.\n\tBuild confidence and transferable skills through training and experience.\n\tReceive full training and ongoing support throughout your volunteering.\n\tShare your interests and talents while learning new things.\n\n\nIf you are interested,&nbsp;please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when&nbsp;registered and&nbsp;logged in). You&nbsp;will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that&nbsp;doesn&rsquo;t&nbsp;work&nbsp;out,&nbsp;then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org.&nbsp;\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe're looking for people who are:\n•\tFriendly, approachable and welcoming.\n•\tPatient and understanding.\n•\tGood listeners with strong communication skills.\n•\tReliable and dependable.\n•\tEnthusiastic about supporting older people in their community.\n•\tComfortable working as part of a team.\n•\tWilling to learn and try new things.\n\n## Travel details\n\n?? Location: David Cargill Centre, 166 Ledard Road, Glasgow, G42 9RA. The centre is easily accessible by public transport, with bus stops nearby and Mount Florida train station around a 5–6 minute walk away.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe'd never leave anyone out of pocket therefore if additional expenses are required for travel, this can be discussed for reinbursment (this is applicable to additional travel costs, we are unable to cover costs of travel for volunteering shifts)",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0IsDYAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Day Centre Connectors for Glasgow's Golden Generation",
                        "description": "We're looking for people who are:\n•\tFriendly, approachable and welcoming.\n•\tPatient and understanding.\n•\tGood listeners with strong communication skills.\n•\tReliable and dependable.\n•\tEnthusiastic about supporting older people in their community.\n•\tComfortable working as part of a team.\n•\tWilling to learn and try new things.",
                        "applyLink": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/volunteers/opportunity/10305194",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "14",
                        "service": [
                            {
