        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002YMoWPAA1",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002YMoWPAA1/cruse-scotland-bereavement-support",
            "name": "Cruse Scotland Bereavement Support",
            "description": "Cruse Scotland Bereavement Support exists to promote the well-being of bereaved people in Scotland. We seek to help anyone experiencing bereavement to understand their grief and cope with their loss. We work primarily through volunteers, providing free care to bereaved people. We also train and educate individuals and organisations who may in turn be able to contribute to the well-being of bereaved people.",
            "website": "http://www.crusescotland.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC031600"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Counselling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Counselling"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HaUU1YAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HaUU1YAN/walk-talk-volunteers-angus-dundee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-01",
                    "title": "Walk & Talk Volunteers (Angus & Dundee)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur Walk and Talk groups in Angus and Dundee help bereaved adults connect with others who understand their experience, while enjoying gentle outdoor exercise.\r\nWe’re looking for friendly, compassionate volunteers to support our Walk Leaders and help create a safe, welcoming space. No experience is needed, just a basic level of fitness and a caring approach. Each friendly group walk lasts between 1 and 1.5 hours and is paced to suit the abilities of those taking part. Training is provided.\r\nIf you want to make a real difference by helping people feel less isolated and more supported, we’d love to hear from you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood listening and communication skills\r\nA compassionate, patient approach\r\nEmpathy and understanding\r\nThe ability to work well as part of a team\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will have the opportunity to complete Paths for All Walk Leader training and access to all Cruse Scotland CPD & volunteer events.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nDundee group meets every second Thursday at 11am\r\nAngus group meets every second Thursday at 2pm\n\n## Travel details\n\nTravel to local walk meeting point.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMilage at 45p per mile. Reimbursement of public transport cost.",
