        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002ZEV7iAAH",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002ZEV7iAAH/glasgow-childrens-hospital-charity",
            "name": "Glasgow Children's Hospital Charity",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/https:www.glasgowchildrenshospitalcharity.orgsupport-usvolunteer",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IUn5pYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IUn5pYAD/sensory-bus-volunteer-driver",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-12",
                    "title": "Sensory Bus Volunteer Driver",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSensory Bus Volunteer Driver\n\n## Description\n\nGlasgow Children&rsquo;s Hospital Charity operates a Sensory Bus that travels to events and locations across Glasgow and Ayrshire. The Sensory Bus adds value to events by raising awareness of the charity and generating vital income to support its work. The Sensory Bus also operates as a commercial entity and can be booked by organisations, such as schools, in exchange for a donation to Glasgow Children&rsquo;s Hospital Charity.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\nSensory Bus Volunteer Drivers will be responsible for transporting the Sensory Bus to and from event locations. The role is focused on driving the vehicle, rather than delivering the sensory experience itself.&nbsp;\n\nMain Tasks:\n\n\n\t\n\tDrive the Sensory Bus safely to and from designated event locations.&nbsp;\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\n\tRepresent Glasgow Children&rsquo;s Hospital Charity in a friendly, positive and professional manner.&nbsp;\n\t\n\n\nVolunteers will be required on an ad hoc basis, depending on upcoming events and the needs of the charity.&nbsp;Volunteers will be contacted in advance of each activity to check their availability and confirm shift arrangements.&nbsp;\n\nVolunteer drivers will receive training through McGill&rsquo;s Driver Training Academy to prepare them for driving the Sensory Bus.&nbsp;&nbsp;All volunteers will receive a full induction to the Sensory Bus before undertaking their first shift. Volunteers will also receive guidance on relevant health and safety procedures to help ensure the vehicle is operated safely and responsibly.&nbsp;\n\nA member of Glasgow Children&rsquo;s Hospital Charity staff will be present at the bus-end location to provide guidance and support.&nbsp;A Sensory Bus Chaperone Volunteer will drive volunteers back to their own vehicle at the end of their shift.&nbsp;Support will be available to help volunteers manage any unexpected issues or challenges that may arise.&nbsp;\n\nJoin a friendly, supportive team; help raise vital funds for babies, children and young people in hospital.&nbsp;Travel expenses reimbursed.\n\nThe Role Is Ideal For:\n\n\n\t\n\tIndividuals looking to gain additional driving experience, develop their skills and build confidence through training.&nbsp;\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\n\tPeople who enjoy working as part of a team.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\n\tAnyone who wants to make a meaningful difference by helping raise vital funds for babies, children and young people in hospital.&nbsp;\n\t\n\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when registered and logged in). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nHold a full, valid driving licence. \n\nBe willing to undertake the necessary training to drive the vehicle safely and confidently. \n\nBe able to commit to agreed shifts and arrive punctually at the designated location.  \n\nBe reliable, dependable and able to follow instructions. \n\nBe able to work collaboratively with Glasgow Children’s Hospital Charity staff and fellow volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nLocations across Glasgow, depending on the specific event.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IUn5pYAD#role",
