                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaWJAAY",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kaWJAAY/befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Befriender",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nEach young person is matched with a volunteer befriender who meets with them weekly for up to four hours (including travel). When with their Befriender, young people are encouraged to develop social skills, enabling them to grow at a pace that their comfortable with. When ready our Befrienders' support young people to engage with others through seasonal group activities and are encouraged to attend local, age-appropriate groups and clubs, further cementing their feelings of belonging within their communities.\n\n## Description\n\nOur Befriending service offers 1-1 support to young people in Edinburgh, aged between 5 – 16-year-old who have been affected by current or historical parental substance use or harms caused through gambling.\nBefriending helps reduce isolation and loneliness and strengthens emotional and physical well-being which fosters a greater sense of self-worth and belonging. Our Volunteers help young people build confidence, resilience, and self-esteem whilst lowering feelings of social anxiety as they explore new interests, experiences and activities.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience necessary- the qualities we are looking for in a befriender are someone who is kind, caring, compassionate and a positive role model for children and young people.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training package will be held both online and face to face in the Broomhouse Hub.  Training will include all aspects of the befriending role.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCitywide.\nTo reduce travel time you will be matched with a young person within an appropriate travelling distance where possible.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel and activity expenses will be reimbursed within an agreed budget.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaWJAAY#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Befriender",
                        "description": "No experience necessary- the qualities we are looking for in a befriender are someone who is kind, caring, compassionate and a positive role model for children and young people.",
