        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002ZEtkzAAD",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002ZEtkzAAD/school-of-philosophy-psychology-language-sciences",
            "name": "School of Philosophy, Psychology & Language Sciences",
            "description": "We produce world-class research with many applications relevant to individuals and society.  We aim to use our research to engage and inspire people beyond academia.  Our researchers work with practitioners in health, policy, education and arts to make a difference.",
            "website": "https://www.volunteer.ppls.ed.ac.uk",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000IRmW4AAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000IRmW4AAL/research-participant",
                    "publishStart": "2019-07-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Research Participant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSupport world-leading research-join our volunteer panel to take part in studies investigating different aspects of human life.  We are seeking new volunteers who are interested in taking part in research studies conducted by the University of Edinburgh's School of Philosophy, Psychology and Language Sciences.\n\n## Description\n\nAs a volunteer you: play a vital role in our research, since many of our studies rely on collecting data from human participants.\nCan take part in research studies online and in-person at our research facilities.\nChoose which studies you want to get involved in.\nCan withdraw from the research at any time. \n\nWe email our volunteers with information about our current studies and they decide if they wish to take part.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo skills required to sign up as a volunteer.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction and support provided.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur research studies are either online or in person.  Most of our onsite research takes place at 7 George Square, Edinburgh.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses paid.",
