        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003Bt9M7AAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003Bt9M7AAJ/the-neuro-therapy-place",
            "name": "The Neuro Therapy Place",
            "description": "The Neuro Therapy Place is a small, independent Scottish charity based in Edinburgh ,dedicated to improving the lives of people with neurological conditions through physiotherapy, rehabilitation and oxygen therapy. The Neuro Therapy Place provides a unique blend of specialist therapies and support for individuals with neurological conditions, empowering clients to lead fuller and more independent lives. Our work combines hands - on rehabilitation, oxygen therapy and a supportive environment where clients and families feel genuinely cared for.",
            "website": "https://www.theneurotherapyplace.org.uk/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaMpAAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kaMpAAI/barochamber-oxygen-treatment-operator",
                    "publishStart": "2019-12-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Barochamber Oxygen Treatment Operator",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe're looking for committed, caring people who want to help people with MS and other conditions. You'll learn how to operate a  barochamber in a warm and welcoming Centre, and meet the people you're helping directly.\n\n## Description\n\nWe have been providing therapies and support for people living with MS and other conditions since 1984 from our Therapy Centre in Leith. We actively encourage and support volunteering opportunities – they are vital to our organisation and everything we do.  We welcome people from all walks of life who can support us and provide a welcoming and friendly face.  You will be trained and supported in the operation and delivery of our oxygen therapy service. This is a vital and beneficial therapy for many of our clients in the management of their long-term condition.   We also offer volunteering opportunities with our physiotherapy service, administration and in fundraising activities.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experienced required, good people and team skills, able to follow instructions, reliable, and a good sense of humour. Flexible volunteering times available.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe provide supervised training and support. Oxygen Operators are able to gain an oxygen operator certificate. We run regular volunteer support sessions where you can receive further coaching and get to know other volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur Centre is based  at 40c Swanfield, Bonnington Road, Edinburgh EH6 5RX Good public transport links and free parking. Travel expenses refunded.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses will be refunded in cash monthly, on production of receipts/completion of expenses claim form.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaMpAAI#role",
