                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7LBKAA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7LBKAA3/foodbank-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Foodbank  Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThis is an opportunity for us to show the kind of love for humanity that abides in this beautiful city of Aberdeen to the newest members (immigrants) during their integration and inclusion process. Helping in the way of supporting families and individuals in need of these food items due to lack of funding, no job, or even homeless situation (with no recourse to public funding from the government), amidst other integration and inclusion struggles will go a very long way.\r\n\r\nMost of these beneficiary members include men, women, children, and young ones, who are not necessarily asylum seekers or refugees but immigrants who have come to our beautiful host city and made it home. The cultural, social, and moral differences that exist between their home country and Aberdeen (host community), have made settling (integration and inclusion) more difficult for these members. No job equates to no money, which also equates to no food. Mamacita Foundation, as part of our social responsibility is partnering with other organisations and working endlessly to ensure a swift integration and inclusion process for these members of our community.\r\n\r\nIn our bid to manage food waste reduction as well as get it to persons in need of these food items, we are calling on you, yes you, to join us as we work with @CFINE, @ Fairshare, and @ Coop group in reaching out to persons.\r\n\r\nYour service to humanity is always appreciated and we look forward to working with you in supporting others in need. Nobody should feel alone.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference. All volunteer support is greatly appreciated. For more details please contact Vivian Draghici at email: info@mamacitafoundationuk.com or telephone: 07449826988.\r\n#Neverfeelalone\r\n#Aberdeencares\r\n#Bringinghopetohumanity\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant guidance and excellent support is provided to all volunteers. There will be an in-house induction on the management of the food bank process. Other volunteers or the welfare team leader will be readily available to welcome you into the team.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to help. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nFood share pick up - A coop food store close to you (Available ones we are currently registered with). From 8 pm - 9:30 pm Mondays & Thursdays. Drop off at the office in Hilton Convention Centre thereafter.\r\n\r\nFood share delivery Receipt: 10 am - 1 pm Every Tuesday & Friday at the office Hilton Convention Centre.\r\n\r\nFood Share sorting: Hilton Convention Centre, 13 Smithfield Road. AB24 4NR. From 9 pm to 9:30 pm Mondays & Thursdays.\r\n\r\nFood bank parcel Handing out: Hilton Convention Centre, 13 Smithfield Road. AB24 4NR. From 5 pm to 6:30 pm Every Tuesday & Friday.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7LBKAA3#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Foodbank  Volunteers",
                        "commitment": "Flexible times available to help. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7LBKAA3/foodbank-volunteers?#modal_register_a0g0800000V7LBKAA3",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/AntiPoverty",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Anti-Poverty"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/EthnicMinorities",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Ethnic Minorities"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/FamilySupport",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Family Support"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/GeneralPublic",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "General Public"
                            }
                        ],
                        "reward": [
                            "https://ns.volunteeringdata.io/TrainingProvided"
                        ]
                    },
