                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008T1LtYAK",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008T1LtYAK/retail-assistant-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Retail Assistant Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Retail Assistant is the friendly face of the Mamacita Foundation Charity Shop. As part of a team of volunteers, you will play a key role in creating a welcoming and supportive shopping experience for customers while helping to generate funds for our charitable activities.\n\nYour Tasks Will Include:\n Greeting and assisting customers with their shopping experience.\n Handling cash and processing transactions at the till.\n Sorting and replenishing stock to keep the shop well-organized.\n Visual merchandising – keeping displays attractive and engaging.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWhile no formal qualifications are required, the ideal volunteer should have the following skills and attributes:\n\n Customer Service Skills – Friendly and approachable attitude to assist customers with their shopping experience.\n Good Communication – Ability to engage with customers, fellow volunteers.\n Confidence in handling cash and processing transactions at the till.\n Ability to sort and arrange stock neatly and keep the shop well-presented.\nWillingness to work alongside others in a collaborative environment.\n Ensuring that stock is displayed attractively and correctly priced.\n  Ability to commit to a regular shift and be punctual.\n\n## Travel details\n\nGreat Northern Road",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FrCwMyvl0W5amNTM7QlAVsy0VOmz2%2FJqysj5jR37lnMifj-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=b7fb0cdc-69af-441e-8910-8e5fb2e4895a",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008T1LtYAK#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Retail Assistant Volunteer",
                        "description": "While no formal qualifications are required, the ideal volunteer should have the following skills and attributes:\n\n Customer Service Skills – Friendly and approachable attitude to assist customers with their shopping experience.\n Good Communication – Ability to engage with customers, fellow volunteers.\n Confidence in handling cash and processing transactions at the till.\n Ability to sort and arrange stock neatly and keep the shop well-presented.\nWillingness to work alongside others in a collaborative environment.\n Ensuring that stock is displayed attractively and correctly priced.\n  Ability to commit to a regular shift and be punctual.",
