        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003D30opAAB",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003D30opAAB/get-walking-lanarkshire",
            "name": "Get Walking Lanarkshire",
            "description": "Get Walking Lanarkshire is the health walk project which spans across both North and South Lanarkshire Council areas.\n\nHealth walks are free, short, friendly group walks for all ages and abilities and they are led by our trained volunteers. There are also opportunities for people to train as volunteer walk leaders themselves, helping local groups to take up walking and keep healthy.\n\nThe project was launched in early 2014 to encourage more people to get outdoors and enjoy the many benefits of walking. Walking is the simplest way to include exercise into our daily lives, and with fantastic parks and paths across Lanarkshire, there’s plenty of places to enjoy a walk at your own pace.\n\nRegular physical activity has been shown to lower the risk of early death, help control weight and reduce the risk of heart disease, stroke, type 2 diabetes, depression, some types of cancer and a host of other conditions. It helps maintain good mental health, keeps your brain active and lowers the risk of hip fractures.  Walking is a perfect start for people who wish to ease themselves in, and build up their fitness.\n\nIt’s healthy, fun and free – and there’s no better time to start. For more information or to find out more about a walk near you, please contact the project co-ordinator on 01698 402077 / 07903 358424 or getwalkinglanarkshire@northlan.gov.uk.",
            "website": "https://www.pathsforall.org.uk/walking-for-health/health-walks/health-walk-providers-in-your-area/walk-project/get-walking-lanarkshire",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eO3LAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eO3LAAU/health-walk-leader-across-lanarkshire",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Health Walk Leader - Across Lanarkshire",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nGet Walking Lanarkshire aims to improve the health and wellbeing of Lanarkshire’s residents by getting more people walking more often. Walking in a group is a great way to meet new people and enjoy your local green spaces. By volunteering with this project you will help others to become healthier and happier.\n\n## Description\n\nHelp others to become healthier and happier by leading our health walks. The walks are free, last no longer than an hour and go at a gentle pace. Apart from taking people on a walk, walk leaders will welcome new walkers, give route information (where, how long/ how far, hazards), encourage some social activity and deal with a bit of paperwork. Optional activities are assisting with promoting the walks. It is up to individual volunteers to decide how much they want to commit, but to ensure some continuity we would ask that you consider your availability for leading walks on a regular basis before doing the health walk leader training day. \n\nWe are specifically looking for walk leaders for the following walks, please get in touch if you can help:\n\nMonday morning: Carluke and Hamilton\nMonday evening: Motherwell\nTuesday morning: Coatbridge, Lesmahagow and Rutherglen \nWednesday morning: Motherwell and Stonehouse\nThursday morning: Airdrie, Newmains and Lanark\nThursday afternoon: Wishaw\nThursday evening: Cumbernauld and Carluke \nFriday morning: Bellshill and Cambuslang\nSaturday morning: Cumbernauld and Blantyre \nSunday morning: Hamilton\n\nAnd for potential new walks in: Coatbridge, Bellshill, Motherwell, Wishaw, Shotts, Rutherglen, Hamilton, Lanark, Forth and Douglas\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Open minded,Organised,Patient,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Social Conscience,Team Player,Trustworthy,\n\n## Training details\n\nFree 1 day training\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nBlantyre,Cambuslang,Carluke,Douglas,East Kilbride,Forth,Hamilton,Lanark,Larkhall,Rutherglen,Stonehouse,Strathaven,Symington,Uddingston,Airdrie\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses when on walk leader duty will be reimbursed.",
