        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003D3BTsAAN",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003D3BTsAAN/macmillan-cancer-support",
            "name": "Macmillan Cancer Support",
            "description": "Macmillan Cancer Support aim to improve the quality of life for cancer patients and their families by providing funding for Macmillan nurses, doctors and other posts, provide patient grants, fund building developments or refurbishments, and provide an information and support service.\nMacMillan Support Line: 0808 808 00 00 (open 7 days a week, 8am to 8pm)",
            "website": "https://www.macmillan.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC039907"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009eumHYAQ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009eumHYAQ/macmillan-cancer-support-information-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Macmillan Cancer Support & Information Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are looking for volunteers for our Macmillan Cancer Information and Support Hubs in Lanarkshire.\n\nWhat you will be doing:  \nMeeting and greeting people affected by cancer, providing a warm welcome to the Macmillan Service.\nOffering a listening ear and informal support, giving people an opportunity to talk about their experiences.\nAssessing their information and support needs in order to signpost/refer to appropriate local support services .\nHelping visitors to find appropriate information booklets.\nCollecting basic data on support provided to people affected by cancer.\n\nThis is a South Lanarkshire & north Lanarkshire opportunity with volunteers assisting in our cancer information & support hubs with libraries in \nEast Kilbride (Mondays 10am – 2pm), Coatbridge (Thursdays 10am – 12 noon), Wishaw (Wednesdays 1.30pm – 3.30pm) and Bellshill (Tuesdays 10.30am – 1.30pm) \nNot all venues have vacancies at any one time\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Open minded,Organised,Patient,Reliable / Dependable,Trustworthy,.We are looking for trustworthy, caring, non judgemental people who are good communicators, well organised and reliable. Being able to listen is a key requirement.  Bring your enthusiasm, understanding and empathy.  Together we can be right there for people affected by cancer\n\n## Training details\n\nNo previous experience required.  You will receive two days of training initially and then ongoing Learning & Development sessions to give you the skills needed to carry out this role. Full support given.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire Yes\nAcross South Lanarkshire,East Kilbride,North Lanarkshire\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReceive out of pocket expenses (reimbursed within our guidelines)",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
