            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7MQMAA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7MQMAA3/wateraid-speaker-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2023-01-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "WaterAid Speaker Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWaterAid Speakers are trained volunteers that deliver inspiring talks and workshops, to raise awareness about the importance of clean water, decent toilets and good hygiene, to transform peoples’ lives for good. Our Speaker volunteers engage audiences about the important work of WaterAid, inspiring them to take action, as they speak with schools, universities, businesses, youth groups, religious places of worship, service organisations, and many more.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWaterAid Speakers need an interest in the work of WaterAid, passion for public speaking, and confidence to speak publicly to a diverse range of community groups. Competence in PowerPoint an email also required.\n\n## Training details\n\nSpeaker Volunteers must complete an online training, followed by a brief Zoom interview and practice presentation with the WaterAid team. Ongoing support available following training, from team and fellow volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMust be available to deliver a minimum of four talks/workshops a year.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nSpeaker Volunteers can be reimbursed with travel expenses to talks/workshops.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
