        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003D4m4fAAB",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003D4m4fAAB/spirit-of-springburn",
            "name": "Spirit of Springburn",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/SpiritofSpringburn",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H2JJJYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000H2JJJYA3/special-events-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-24",
                    "title": "Special Events Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSpecial Events Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nHelp bring Springburn&rsquo;s community events to life &mdash; meet new people, support local activities, and make a difference without committing every week.\n\nWe are looking for enthusiastic volunteers who are available on an ad hoc basis to support our public events, from serving drinks at our Springburn Heritage Tea Party to helping set up the Springburn Community Street Festival.\n\nThis flexible role would suit someone who wants to get involved in the Springburn community but is not looking for a weekly volunteering commitment. Whether you enjoy meeting people, supporting local events, or helping behind the scenes, we&rsquo;d love to hear from you.\n\nAs a Special Events Volunteer with Spirit of Springburn, you&rsquo;ll help create welcoming, community-focused events that bring local people together and celebrate everything that makes Springburn special.\n\nWho are we?\n\nSpirit of Springburn is a Community Development Trust working to empower the residents of Springburn to enact positive change in our community. At the heart of our work is the Community Hub in Springburn Shopping Centre, which hosts our Heritage Project, Community Food services, and offers signposting and advice.\n\nWe also organise a variety of community events throughout the year, from tea parties in the Shopping Centre to the Springburn Community Street Festival.\n\nAs a Spirit of Springburn volunteer, you&rsquo;ll become part of a friendly, diverse and motivated team dedicated to strengthening community connections and creating positive local change.\n\nExamples of tasks you might do:\n\n\n\tSetting up and taking down gazebos, tables and event materials\n\tServing drinks and food at community events\n\tWelcoming and signposting visitors\n\tHelping create a safe, friendly and inclusive atmosphere\n\tSupporting activities, stalls and entertainment areas\n\tAssisting staff and other volunteers during busy events\n\n\nTraining &amp; Support\n\nVolunteers will receive an introduction and guidance from the Spirit of Springburn team before each event. Ongoing support will be available throughout volunteering activities, and volunteers will work alongside experienced staff and fellow volunteers in a welcoming environment.\n\nKey Dates\n\n\n\tSummer Heritage Tea &ndash; Thursday 30th July\n\tSpringburn Community Street Festival &ndash; Saturday 29th August\n\tChristmas Fair &ndash; Date TBC\n\n\nAdditional community events may also become available throughout the year.\n\nHours &amp; Commitment\n\nAs an Events Volunteer, we ask that you commit to volunteering at a minimum of two events each year.\n\nEvent times will vary depending on the activity, with some support needed before and after events for set-up and pack-down.\n\nAdditional Volunteering Opportunity\n\nTuesday evenings, 8:00pm&ndash;10:30pm:\nCan you help collect and store surplus food from local supermarkets for our Community Fridge? Drivers are especially welcome.\n\nBenefits of Volunteering\n\n\n\tMeet new people and become part of your local community\n\tGain experience supporting public and community events\n\tBuild confidence and teamwork skills\n\tSupport positive community activities in Springburn\n\tVolunteer flexibly around your availability\n\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on info@volunteerglasgow.org\n\nAfter You Hit &quot;Apply&quot;\n\n\n\tConfirmation email sent\n\tFollow-up contact by email or phone to arrange an informal chat\n\tBrief introduction or induction before your first event\n\tAdded to the volunteer contact list for upcoming events and opportunities\n\tBegin volunteering at agreed events that suit your availability\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tAdaptability (able to shift between tasks)\n•\tInitiative (step in where needed)\n•\tTeamwork\n•\tComfortable interacting with the public\n•\tEmpathetic & non-judgmental approach\n•\tAble to carry out light physical tasks\n\n## Travel details\n\n5 minutes walk from Springburn Train Station.\n2 minutes walk from Wellfield Street Bust Stop.\nFree parking for volunteers.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are payable to volunteers.\nFood expenses are payable for shifts over 4 hours.",
