                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H1hfRYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000H1hfRYAR/springburn-community-hub-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-24",
                    "title": "Springburn Community Hub Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSpringburn Community Hub Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nBe part of the heart of Springburn &mdash; support your local community through the everyday running of the Community Hub.\n\nDo you want to give back to your local community? We want volunteers to get involved with the everyday running of Springburn Community Hub. The Hub is the heart of our charity, and our wonderful volunteers make it a welcoming and safe space for all.\n\nAs a Hub Volunteer with Spirit of Springburn, you&rsquo;ll play a hands-on role in supporting a busy, community-led Hub at the heart of Springburn Shopping Centre &mdash; helping local people access food services, community activities, events, advice and support in a welcoming environment.\n\nWho are we?\n\nSpirit of Springburn is a Community Development Trust working to empower the residents of Springburn to enact positive change in our community. At our core is the Community Hub in Springburn Shopping Centre, which hosts our Heritage Project, Community Food services, and offers signposting and advice. We also hold events regularly, from tea parties in the Shopping Centre to the Springburn Community Street Festival.\n\nAs a Spirit of Springburn volunteer, you&rsquo;ll be part of a friendly, diverse and motivated team dedicated to strengthening community.\n\nExamples of tasks you might do:\n\n\n\tSetting up tables and display boards for activities\n\tMaintaining hygiene and health &amp; safety\n\tRestocking food from supermarkets for the Community Fridge\n\tKeeping posters and displays up to date\n\tSupporting community activities and events\n\tHelping create a welcoming and supportive environment for visitors\n\n\nTraining &amp; Support\n\nVolunteers will receive an induction and ongoing support from the Spirit of Springburn team. Guidance will be provided on health &amp; safety, community activities, and supporting Hub services. Volunteers will also have regular check-ins, opportunities to learn new skills, and support from experienced staff and fellow volunteers.\n\nHours\n\nThe Hub is open Monday to Friday, 11am&ndash;3pm. Volunteers are usually involved between 10am&ndash;3:30pm. Some volunteers come in every day, while others volunteer for just a couple of hours each week. We ask volunteers to commit to a regular schedule.\n\nTuesday evenings, 8:00pm&ndash;10:30pm:\nWe particularly need more volunteers to support supermarket collections to stock the Community Fridge. Drivers are especially welcome.\n\nApplication &amp; Key Dates\n\nIf you are interested in applying for this opportunity, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available if registered and logged in). We will reply to your email within 5 working days. If you have not heard from us within this time, please contact Volunteer Glasgow.\n\n\n\tApplication Form Deadline: Monday 22nd June\n\tInterview at Springburn Community Hub: Monday 29th June\n\tTraining Session: Monday 13th July\n\n\nAfter You Hit &quot;Apply&quot;\n\n\n\tConfirmation email sent\n\tFollow-up contact (email or call) to arrange a chat\n\tInduction session at the location\n\tStart volunteering with agreed shift times\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tGood at organizing space, keeping things tidy.\n•\tAttention to detail\n•\tBasic record keeping ability\n•\tPractical hands on\n•\tAble to carry out light physical tasks\n•\tHygiene & safety awareness (training provided)\n•\tAdaptability (able to shift between tasks)\n•\tInitiative (step in where needed)\n•\tTeamwork\n\n## Travel details\n\n5 minutes walk from Springburn Train Station.\n2 minutes walk from Wellfield Street Bust Stop.\nFree parking for volunteers.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are payable to volunteers.\nFood expenses are payable for shifts over 4 hours.",
