                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GwL65YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GwL65YAF/heritage-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-17",
                    "title": "HERITAGE VOLUNTEER",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHERITAGE VOLUNTEER\n\n## Description\n\nAre you passionate about local history, would you like to learn more about Springburn&rsquo;s rich heritage? Volunteer at the Springburn Heritage Project, hosted by Spirit of Springburn.\n\nAt the heart of the project is our bi-weekly display in Springburn Shopping Centre, where our volunteers get to chat to the public about photographs and objects from old Springburn. This is an exciting time for our project as we begin to catalogue and rethink our collection. We are working with Glasgow Life community artists to create a Springburn Heritage Health Walk, which we will launch at Springburn Community Street Festival on 29th August. We are planning a visit to the Mitchell Library&rsquo;s archive to investigate the catalogue from the former Springburn Museum.\n\nWho are we? \n\nSpirit of Springburn is a Community Development Trust working to empower the residents of Springburn to enact positive change in our community. At our core is the Community Hub in Springburn Shopping Centre, which hosts our Heritage Project, Community Food services, and offer signposting and advice. We also hold events regularly, from tea parties in the Shopping Centre, to the Springburn Community Street Festival. As a Spirit of Springburn volunteer, you&rsquo;ll be part of a friendly, diverse and motivated team, dedicated to strengthening community.\n\nExamples of tasks you might do:\n\n\n\tCreate captions for items from our collection\n\tDesign and create new displays\n\tEngage with the public at our bi-weekly display and special events\n\tSet up and take down display boards &amp; tables\n\n\nHours:\n\nThe Heritage Display runs Tuesdays &amp; Thursdays from 11am-2pm. Heritage volunteers would be needed from 10:45am-2:15pm.\n\nYou will also have the opportunity to volunteer at our events, like the Heritage Tea Party on Thursday 30th July, and the Springburn Community Street Festival on Saturday 29th August.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\nTraining &amp; Support\n\nFull induction and ongoing support will be provided by the Spirit of Springburn team. Volunteers will receive guidance on heritage displays, public engagement and working with historical materials.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nLocation\n\nSpringburn Community Hub, Springburn Shopping Centre, Glasgow.\n\nWhat We&rsquo;re Looking For\n\nWe welcome volunteers of all backgrounds and experience levels. You might enjoy this role if you are:\n\n\n\tInterested in local history or community heritage\n\tFriendly and comfortable chatting with people\n\tCreative or organised\n\tKeen to learn new skills\n\tReliable and enthusiastic about community involvement\n\n\nNo formal experience is required &mdash; support and guidance will be provided.\n\nApplication &amp; Key Dates:\n\nIf you are interested in applying for this opportunity please click &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; bottom below (available if registered and logged in). We will reply to your email within 5 working days. If you have not heard from us within this time, please contact Volunteer Glasgow.\n\n\n\tApplication Form Deadline: Mon 22nd June\n\tInterview at Springburn Community Hub: Mon 29th June\n\tTraining Session: Mon 13th July\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tGood written English\n•\tBasic IT Skills (word processing)\n•\tAble to carry out light physical tasks\n•\tInitiative (step in where needed)\n•\tTeamwork\n•\tCreativity\n\n## Travel details\n\nLocation\nSpringburn Community Hub, Springburn Shopping Centre, Glasgow.\n\n5 minutes walk from Springburn Train Station.\n2 minutes walk from Wellfield Street Bust Stop.\nFree parking for volunteers.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are payable to volunteers.\nFood expenses are payable for shifts over 4 hours.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
