        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003D4voyAAB",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003D4voyAAB/upward-mobility",
            "name": "Upward Mobility",
            "description": "Every day, and in everything we do, we’re committed to a shared set of beliefs and ambitions. Some are aspirational – such as our vision for a more inclusive world. Others shape our work and our people – and help make Upmo the friendly, expert, trusted, creative and nurturing organisation it is.\r\nOur vision is an inclusive world in which all adults with disabilities receive the respect, protection, support and opportunities they need to develop their potential and play an equal, rewarding and contributing role in their communities.\r\nWe provide high quality tailored support and opportunity for adults with learning disabilities and autism to develop confidence, fuel imagination and enhance life skill",
            "website": "https://upmo.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC037917"
                }
            ],
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2F1bacd2f1-615c-16a1-5528-abbd3964a26d%2FWkLzgT1VE9cAHEWcVMpdVMd5bL63%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=5d099220-033b-44a7-97c6-7f6b23c64202",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7LmaAAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7LmaAAF/general-workshop-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2023-01-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "General Workshop Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nUpmo supports adults with disabilities. We run a range of workshops such as art, music, drama, gardening and much more! We hope our volunteers can share skills and support our staff and students in workshops.   \r\nSupporting students with a variety of activities\r\nSupporting facilitators to plan and prepare for workshops\r\nContribute ideas and suggestions for workshops\r\nTake the lead in providing activities for students\r\nHelping to maintain pleasant surroundings, ensuring that spaces are tidy and clean enough to ensure safety of all participants\r\nMaintain effective relationships with students, their families and other staff and volunteers \r\nImplementation and adherence to all of Upmo’s policies and procedures including those relating to equity and health and safety.\r\nTo contribute to creating a pleasant, safe and enjoyable learning environment for Upmo´s \r\nstudents and all colleagues\r\nTo attend meetings and training as required.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAn understanding of the needs of adults with learning disabilities.\r\nA demonstrable ability to relate professionally and respectfully to people with learning disabilities.\r\nA creative background and skills the following subject areas – art, music, drama, dance, IT/digital media, cooking or outdoor education.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWe require all our volunteers to follow the same weekly pattern as routine is important to our students. \nUpmo is open Monday - Friday 10am to 4pm, our volunteers can discuss times that would work for them with the Operational Services Coordinator and come to an agreement that works for both Upmo and the Volunteer.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOn local bus routes",
