                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7M7OAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7M7OAAV/team-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2023-01-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-20",
                    "title": "Team Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCome and join our cause any time of the year. You don't have to wait up till Christmas to help make a real difference to the lives of families in Ayrshire. Volunteering with Night Before Christmas is a meaningful way to help some of Ayrshire’s most vulnerable children and families. It’s also an opportunity to develop and enjoy new experiences. You’ll connect with your community, meet new people, learn new skills and share what you know.\r\n\r\nAll our voluntary roles are supported: people come first. We’ll give you an induction and relevant training, and you’ll always have space to raise issues.\r\n\r\nYou don’t need specific skills for many of our roles. All we ask for is enthusiasm and a willingness to get involved. Tasks may include:\r\n- Sorting and tidying \r\n- Packing bags\r\n- Talking and greeting other volunteers\r\n- Driving and delivering bags\r\n- Keeping records\r\n- Fundraising\r\n- Participating in events\r\n- Creating social media posts\r\n- Photography",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
