                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GAFCfYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GAFCfYAP/volunteer-admin",
                    "publishStart": "2026-04-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-08",
                    "title": "Volunteer Admin",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNo matter how good our services are, we can’t properly support our users/community well if we don’t have good organisers in the team. If this sounds like you?... we would love you to consider volunteering with us for a few hours per week/month\r\n\r\nMentor Scotland is a peer to peer support group based in West Dunbartonshire. We have drop in sessions, male and female talking groups, cold water therapy, walk & talk group, and other activities. Our aim is to help end the stigma attached to mental health and provide a service to the community that supports wellbeing in all aspects of life. We value respect, care and we want to nurture those who attend our services to help them grow and thrive.\r\nOur welcoming office is the perfect environment to make the most of your administrative skills. The ideal candidate will have strong computer and organisational abilities, feel confident interacting with members of the public, possess an excellent telephone manner, and be proactive in maintaining accurate and up-to-date records.\r\n\r\nSo, whether you are looking to use your time well or update your skills, we would love to hear from you. In return we can offer you a warm welcome and all the support you could need.\r\nWe are seeing a rise in demand for our services everyday. Having your help will allow us to be there for the people who need us. Any time you can give will make a real difference.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased in Benview Resource Centre, Dumbarton",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
