        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003D6qX8AAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003D6qX8AAJ/home-start-glasgow-north-and-north-lanarkshire",
            "name": "Home Start Glasgow North and North Lanarkshire",
            "description": "Home Start is a voluntary organisation setup to increase the confidence and independence of families with children under 5 who are experiencing difficulties. We train and support volunteers to visit vulnerable families in their own homes on a weekly basis, offering support and helping to prevent crisis situations or family breakdown.",
            "website": "https://homestartgnnl.org.uk/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000002bWe5YAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000002bWe5YAE/peer-volunteer-home-visiting-family-supportgroup-support-for-families",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Peer Volunteer (Home-visiting family support/Group support for families )",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNo special qualifications are necessary to become a Home-Start volunteer, volunteers are usually parents or grandparents with an interest in, and experience of, young children and family life. We welcome volunteers from all sections of the community.\n\nTalking and listening can be empowering for families, helping them to overcome their difficult situations by realising their potential and building confidence. Volunteers are offered ongoing training and support, including opportunities to take part in activities with specialist speakers and services, as well as informal social gatherings. We offer a variety of volunteering opportunities, so read on to find out more. \n\nVolunteers join us for many reasons, but all share the same motivation – the desire to help others.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYouth / Childcare, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Open minded,Organised,Patient,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Trustworthy,\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining & Assessment Course\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire Yes\nGlasgow,North Lanarkshire\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses covered",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000002bWe5YAE#role",
