            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7Me9AAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7Me9AAF/childrens-befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2023-02-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Children's Befriender",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDo you enjoy spending time with children and helping them discover their confidence? As a Befriending Volunteer, you will spend 1:1 time with a child or young person aged between 5 and 18 who is affected by HIV or Hepatitis C and who could use a little extra support.\r\nMany of the children we support have faced or continue to face Adverse Childhood Experiences that have affected their wellbeing, development, and communication. As a Befriending Volunteer, you will build a connection with a child or young person through fun activities such as visiting museums and galleries, taking part in sports, or exploring nature. You will support a child to develop their interests and hobbies and expand their horizons while creating a safe and supportive environment for them to express themselves.\r\nConsistency is important for the children we support. We therefore ask our Befrienders to commit to a minimum of 1 year of volunteering in order to nurture feelings of trust and safety.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tPersonal qualities: Empathy, patience, reliability, and a caring, non-judgmental attitude.\r\n• Skills: Good listening, timekeeping, and relationship-building abilities. \r\n• Commitment to values: Upholding Service Users’ confidentiality and maintaining boundaries.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe provide comprehensive training and ongoing support to build valuable, transferable skills. Training includes Understanding HIV and Hep C, Stigma, Boundaries, Trauma-Informed Approaches, Safeguarding, and First Aid. We provide ongoing post-session support, guided peer-support, and one-to-one support meetings.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n3-4 hours fortnightly for at least 1 year\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur office is located on George Street, Edinburgh. However, befriending sessions can take place all over Edinburgh. This will be in a community location.\r\n\r\nVolunteers meet a child in a community location after collecting them from their home (depending on child’s age). The type of travel used can be chosen by the volunteer and will be reimbursed by Positive Help.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe fully reimburse travel, activity, and other reasonable expenses. We cover all driving expenses, and our mileage rate is 45p per mile. Expenses are paid weekly if submitted by volunteers by Thursday.",
