                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I1wsPYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I1wsPYAR/supportive-transport-driver",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-17",
                    "title": "Supportive Transport Driver",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nEver helped a neighbour, friend or family member by giving them a lift?\r\n\r\nOur Supportive Transport Drivers provide much more than a journey from A to B. You'll help people living with or affected by HIV and Hepatitis C get to medical appointments, community activities, and essential errands, supporting their independence and wellbeing.\r\n\r\nMany of the people we support face barriers to travelling on their own, including poor health, reduced mobility, social anxiety, or financial challenges. By offering reliable transport and a friendly, supportive presence, you'll help ensure they can access the care and services they need. Sometimes, a chat on the journey can be just as important as the lift itself.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAn empathetic, patient, and reliable person.\r\nA good listener with a caring, non-judgmental approach.\r\nSomeone who is respectful of confidentiality and boundaries.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
