                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ARXOjYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ARXOjYAP/ebay-store-volunteer-donation-packer-and-dispatcher",
                    "publishStart": "2025-06-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "eBay Store Volunteer Donation Packer and Dispatcher",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nVolunteer with Friends of the Broadway Prestwick.\r\n\r\nFriends of the Broadway Prestwick is a community group dedicated to bringing the former Broadway Cinema in Prestwick into community ownership.\r\n\r\nOur aim is to reopen the Broadway as a professional cinema, exciting multi-use venue, and inter-generational community hub. \r\n\r\nWe are looking for responsible volunteers to provide a considered and sensitive packaging service for items purchased from the Friends of the Broadway eBay store, ensuring timely and safe onward pick-up by couriers.\r\nResponsibilities will include:\r\n•\tTo regularly liaise with the Volunteer Store Administrator, the Donation Processor, and other volunteer packers regarding items to be packed\r\n•\tTo assess all health and safety aspects of lifting and moving donated goods and summon the Administrator if more support may be required\r\n•\tTo ensure all items are referenced with a suitable index system in place for ease of identification\r\n•\tEnsure adequate packaging materials are readily available, and stocks remain topped up\r\n•\tTo safely pack, parcel, and address sold items, ensuring a clear onward address is visible to couriers\r\n•\tTo maintain a safe and organised working environment\r\n•\tContact suitable preferred couriers to book and arrange for timely uplift and ensure items are positioned in place identified for pick-up\r\n•\tTo liaise with relevant Regency staff re items left out for couriers\r\n•\tTo update the Store Administrator of any perceived/issues that may arise\r\n\r\n\r\nIf you would like to volunteer in a role which allows you to give back to the local community while participating in a innovative project, and to join an enthusiastic, diverse and dynamic team of volunteers this could be the opportunity for you. The role can also allow you to make a significant contribution to the future of the Broadway. You will also be able to access a range of training and gain experience in a variety of new activities.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tAn ability to work flexibly\r\n•\tA willingness to work from the Regency store as required\r\n•\tExcellent interpersonal skills\r\n•\tPhysically capable of occasional heavy lifting\r\n•\tSound awareness of health and safety considerations and manual handling advice\r\n•\tGood time management and organisational skills\r\n•\tAbility to work under pressure \r\n•\tDiscretion and confidentiality",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F25bd3d91-5118-4a4a-b7b7-880d4989026d%2Fgpx6nnIWvxXFMLCpJdEzZH9maTg1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=8164488c-2783-413a-9542-6da7363702a4",
