                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000086i9pYAA",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000086i9pYAA/general-events-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-01-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-03",
                    "title": "General Events Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nVolunteer with Friends of the Broadway Prestwick.\r\n\r\nFriends of the Broadway Prestwick is a community group dedicated to bringing the former Broadway Cinema in Prestwick into community ownership.\r\n\r\nOur aim is to reopen the Broadway as a professional cinema, exciting multi-use venue, and inter-generational community hub. \r\n\r\nWe are looking for General Events Support Volunteers to provide personalised support to visitors to our events which are held in a variety of locations. \r\n\r\nResponsibilities include:\r\n- Welcome and safely escorting people to their seats or other areas of the building\r\n- Selling concessions, encouraging new membership and donations as appropriate\r\n- Attend events in a range of locations and become familiar with the layout and health and safety regulations\r\n- Cashing up post-event, reconciling all monies\r\n- General tidy-up after events\r\n\r\nIf you would like to volunteer in a role which allows you to give back to the local community while participating in a innovative project, and to join an enthusiastic, diverse and dynamic team of volunteers this could be the opportunity for you. You will also be able to access a range of training and gain experience in a variety of new activities.\n\n## Experience required\n\n- Good time management and organisational skills\r\n- Ability to work under pressure\r\n- Excellent people skills",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
