        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003F0re5AAB",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003F0re5AAB/think-circus",
            "name": "Think Circus",
            "description": "We are brought together by a belief that playfulness, connection and quality are really important and have been collectively creating circus for over a decade.\nOur vision is a supportive, connected society where all humans are seen as incredible and equally celebrated.",
            "website": "https://www.thinkcircus.co.uk/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Qhjp3AAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Qhjp3AAB/circus-class-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Circus Class Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nMake a Difference with Think Circus. Volunteer to Inspire, Empower, and Create Joy.\n\n## Description\n\nHelping teachers to establish a secure and motivating atmosphere for our students to flourish. Recognizing the accomplishments of young individuals and motivating them to explore new opportunities. Reporting any instances of abuse, inappropriate behaviour, or potential risks if observed. Contributing to the cleanliness and organisation of the classroom.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEssential: Friendly and kind to people of all ages and abilities. Work well in a team and find joy in collaboration. Reliable and punctual.\nWilling to complete a PVG check.\nDesirable: Enjoying the circus.\nPrevious experience working with youth.\nHaving a sense of fun.\n\n## Training details\n\nEach volunteer will receive an induction covering general information about Think Circus, health and safety requirements, role-specific descriptions, and the process for providing feedback or lodging complaints regarding their volunteering experience.\nTraining will be differed based on different roles and volunteers’ experience. For most volunteers, Safeguarding training, Circus Skill training, and Client Liaison training will be provided. We prefer to have long-term volunteering relationships and are able to offer additional opportunities such as masterclasses, SQA-approved training courses, and events for volunteers who have been with us for over one year.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCloud 9 (part of the Wee Hub), Ocean Terminal Shopping Centre, Ocean Drive, Leith, Edinburgh, EH6 6JJ.\nMultiple bus lines and a tram route provide convenient transportation to the shopping centre, where you can enjoy free parking. The bus services includes Numbers 11, 34, 35, 36, and 200.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
