        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003F1PzLAAV",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003F1PzLAAV/the-scottish-pantry-network",
            "name": "The Scottish Pantry Network",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/TheScottishPantryNetwork",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ISs9aYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ISs9aYAD/support-and-maintenance-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-10",
                    "title": "Support and Maintenance Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSupport and Maintenance Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nSupport and Maintenance Volunteer Needed for Community Food Project in East End of Glasgow.\n\nThe Scottish Pantry Network is a community-led organisation that supports collaboration and knowledge-sharing among local community groups that run food pantries in Scotland. Our network promotes a model of redistributing surplus food to reduce food waste, while also providing affordable and healthy food to those in need. We encourage collaboration among our member pantries, providing support and training to help them operate more efficiently and effectively.\n\nOur office is based in Tollcross and we&#39;re in need of volunteers to help us keep our space safe, well-maintained, and functional. Support and maintenance volunteers will help us with small maintenance and repair tasks in and around our space as well as respond to small requests.&nbsp;\n\nVolunteer tasks will include minor repairs in our building, assembling or installing furniture, performing routine maintenance work, and doing occasional painting and touch-ups.&nbsp;\n\nVolunteers are required to have experience in general building maintenance / handyperson tasks, basic knowledge of painting, carpentry, repair work, attention to detail, and the ability to work independently and manage multiple tasks.&nbsp;\n\nShifts can be flexible based on volunteer availability but will be a minimum of one shift every 2 weeks.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nHow to Apply:\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&#39; button (available when logged in and registered). You will then be contacted by the volunteer coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org\n\nWhat Happens After You Apply\n\n\n\tConfirmation &ndash; You&rsquo;ll receive an email acknowledging your application.\n\tContact &ndash; TSPN will get in touch to discuss the role, your availability, and next steps.\n\tInformal chat &ndash; A brief phone or in-person conversation may be arranged.\n\tStart date &ndash; If suitable, you&rsquo;ll be given a start date and any shift details.\n\tInduction &ndash; You&rsquo;ll get a short introduction to the role, safety info, and how things work.\n\tBegin volunteering!\n\n\nIf you have any questions, please contact enquiries@scottishpantrynetwork.org.uk, or contact our volunteer and employability coordinator at catherine@scottishpantrynetwork.org.uk.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers are required to have experience in general building maintenance / handyperson tasks, basic knowledge of painting, carpentry, repair work, attention to detail, and the ability to work independently and manage multiple tasks. \n\n## Travel details\n\nAccessible via 61, 240, 255 buses\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel reimbursement",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
