        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nbTjAAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nbTjAAI/st-columbas-shops-limited",
            "name": "St Columba's Shops Limited",
            "description": "St Columba’s Hospice provides care and support for patients in Edinburgh and East Lothian with life limiting conditions and their families. The Hospice is supported by 9 shops.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FamilySupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Family Support"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009SI1dYAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009SI1dYAG/morningside-shop-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-04-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Morningside Shop Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThis role helps in creating a friendly, welcoming and helpful environment in our Morningside shop. Our volunteers support the shop manager in the running of the shop to raise funds for the Hospice. It is a busy, interesting and rewarding place to volunteer where every day is different.\n\n## Description\n\nGreeting and serving customers, providing a warm and welcoming atmosphere and excellent customer service. Handling cash/ cards and operation of the till. Sorting donated second hand goods, bric-a-brac and books. Steaming, hanging, tagging and pricing goods ready to go out on the shop floor. Assisting with window displays. Keeping shop well stocked. Helping to keep the shop clean and tidy.\n\n## Training details\n\nShop orientation and training.\nHospice Induction Programme.  \nGroup supervision / continuing professional development updates.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThere are various buses that run to Morningside and there is both paid and free parking.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThere is a form to fill out and travel receipts/ tickets must be kept as proof of purchase. Expenses are paid monthly via BACS.",
