        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nbU7AAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nbU7AAI/the-big-project",
            "name": "The BIG Project",
            "description": "Our project aims to support children and young people to take part in a range of activities that will not only help them personally but aid their social development. We offer a range of activities including sports, drama, singing and the arts to help raise young people’s aspirations, increase self-esteem and develop self- control thus enabling young people to take pride in themselves and their community. For more information about our project please check out our website www.thebigproject.org.uk or contact Jordan on 0131 622 7784",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaLoAAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kaLoAAI/youth-and-childrens-worker",
                    "publishStart": "2017-04-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Youth and Childrens Worker",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe Big Project is a youth and Children's Project based in Broomhouse. We work with 5-15 year olds and offer a variety of services to children and young people including open access work, targeted group work, individual support, residential and holiday programme.\n\n## Description\n\nWould you like to make a positive difference to local children and young people? If you are enthusiastic, fun and engaging maybe a role as a volunteer youth and children's worker could be just what you are looking for. Support kids to build on their communication, confidence, teamwork and resilience skills in one of our Youth Clubs.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAbility to use your initiative; reliable; enthusiastic; committed; active listening skills; open minded; non-judgemental; sense of humour; likes children and young people and good communication skills. Experience of youth work is desirable but not necessary.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will undergo induction sessions before they take up the position. They will also be offered training as appropriate either delivered in house or by other organisations.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAll opportunities happen once a week term time and take place in Broomhouse Primary School. Buses to Saughton Road - no 22 from Princes Street. Buses to Calder Road - Nos 3, 33, 25 (Lothian Regional Transport). Nos 27 and 28 (First Bus)\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel vouchers available.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
