            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QhjNsAAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QhjNsAAJ/board-members",
                    "publishStart": "2023-08-19",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Board Members",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nLeith Festival needs new Board Members to make its annual community festival happen in 2026 and beyond. We are particularly interested in volunteers with either an interest in, or experience of ,working with local primary and secondary schools in order to strengthen our community involvement.\n\n## Description\n\nBoard members are responsible for all aspects of governance and finance with this long established registered charity. In addition, board members take an active role in planning and putting together its annual June community festival week. The 2026 project plan is underway. Regular board/planning meetings start from mid October 2025.\nNew board members will bring their own skills to the existing team and their chosen areas of active involvement can be flexible. We are particularly interested in volunteers with either an interest in, or experience of, working with local primary and secondary schools in order to strengthen our community involvement.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNeed to attend regular committee meetings. Must respect opinions/ ideas of other board members. Must be able to work in a team and  communicate well. must have an interest in contributing to the local community. Ideally be prepared to take action point minutes on a rotating basis. Practical skills useful too.\n\n## Training details\n\nApplicants will be asked to complete a short application form which will be considered by the exiting Board. An informal interview will take place. If successful, the prospective board member will attend 3 meetings as an observer before a final mutual decision is made.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMain office at Academy Street, Leith.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nProvide a receipt and bank details which the Treasurer will reimburse by bank transfer.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QhjNsAAJ#role",
