                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000LtoMKAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000LtoMKAAZ/pace-maker",
                    "publishStart": "2019-05-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Pace Maker",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHelp us build up the pace in Scotland by sharing our badges and displaying posters across your local area; playing your part in the future of Scottish medical research, taking on heart disease. 41 people die every day in Scotland from heart disease. Together we can keep those we love around for longer.\n\n## Description\n\nWe will provide posters for you to display in your local shops, community centres, libraries, supermarkets, pharmacies and doctors surgeries to help us reach as many people as possible. We can send you a box of badges to sell to friends, family and colleagues for donations, as well as asking local shops to have a box of badges on their counter (that we can send out directly).\n\n## Experience required\n\nConfident and outgoing. Happy to ask local shops/businesses to display posters or take badges\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will have a named contact who will offer ongoing support.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis will be undertaken in your local area. If transport/parking costs are required we can discuss and agree on an individual basis.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThis will be agreed on an individual basis. We use expense forms claimed via their dedicated contact.",
