                },
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaN7AAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kaN7AAI/assistant-cub-leader",
                    "publishStart": "2014-08-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Assistant Cub Leader",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe 64th Leith, the Stockbridge Scouts, have been providing Scouting to the Stockbridge Community for over 100 years. We are now in need of additional Cub Leaders to assist at a well run and well established Cub Pack. As part of the Scout Movement, our aim and the aim of Scouting is to promote development.\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for new volunteers both male and female to help to run a well established Cub Pack. The Cub Pack is part of an active Scout Group with Beavers (ages 6-8) and Scouts (11 to 15) ensuring a regular stream of new entrants. We meet regularly on a Friday evening, but also take part in various activities involving other Cub Packs. The main commitment needed is somebody who is going to be prepared to commit to regular attendance on a Friday evening: to get involved leading the activities.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnthusiasm, willingness to learn and teach new skills.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training given.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2 hours per week for 1 year. Weekdays\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe have a weekly meeting on a Friday evening between 18.00 and 19.30 using the hall at Stockbridge Primary School, Hamilton Place.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe will assist in training costs",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaN7AAI#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Assistant Cub Leader",
                        "description": "Enthusiasm, willingness to learn and teach new skills.",
                        "commitment": "2 hours per week for 1 year. Weekdays",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kaN7AAI/assistant-cub-leader?#modal_register_a0g24000008kaN7AAI",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
