                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaKtAAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kaKtAAI/assistant-beaver-leader",
                    "publishStart": "2017-04-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Assistant Beaver Leader",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe aim of Scouting is to promote the development of young people in achieving their full physical, intellectual, social and spiritual potential as individuals, as responsible citizens and as members of their local, national and international communities.\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for new volunteers both male and female to help to run the Beaver Colony. The Beaver Colony is part of an active Scout Group - together with Cubs (ages 8-10) ensuring a regular stream of new entrants. We meet regularly on a Wednesday evening, but also take part in various activities involving other Beaver Colonies. The main commitment needed is somebody who is going to be prepared to commit to regular attendance on a Wednesday evening: to get involved leading the youngsters.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnthusiasm, willingness to learn and teach new skills.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training given\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe have a weekly meeting on a Wednesday evening between 18.00 and 19.00 using the hall at Stockbridge Primary School, Hamilton Place.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses paid.",
