            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNs5MAAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNs5MAAT/sales-assistant-newington",
                    "publishStart": "2021-08-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Sales Assistant- Newington",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nPeople person required for busy charity shop.\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for friendly, creative & reliable people in our busy shop to help serve customers, operate the till and prepare, price & display stock. Hospices of Hope is the leading palliative care charity in South Eastern Europe. We think everyone deserves the best possible care at the end of life but in countries like Romania, Serbia and Moldova, many people still die in pain without physical, spiritual or emotional comfort.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for a team player, someone  friendly and flexible, with a good attitude, professional, trustworthy, an advocate for our charity and willing to learn.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe provide training for all aspects of the charity shop role that are open to our volunteers and are happy to help with developing skills for\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur shop is located at 42 South Clerk Street. We are just down from Sainsburys on the other side of the road. There is a bus stop outside where you can get the 2, 3, 5, 7, 29, 31, 33, 37, 47, 47b and 49.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses will be agreed on a case by case basis.  This will need to be discussed with the manager.",
