                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kaKqAAI/sales-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2012-01-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Sales Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAre you looking for work experience or to improve your CV? This is a great opportunity to meet new people and learn new skills while helping us in our busy shop.\nPlease pop in for a chat if you are interested in volunteering and we will see what we can do to match the role to your interests and experience.\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for friendly, creative & reliable people in our busy shop to help serve customers, operate the till and prepare, price & display stock. Hospices of Hope is the leading palliative care charity in South Eastern Europe. We think everyone deserves the best possible care at the end of life but in countries like Romania, Serbia and Moldova, many people still die in pain without physical, spiritual or emotional comfort.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPlease pop in for a chat if you are interested in volunteering and we will see what we can do to match the role to your interests or work experience needs.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe offer full training on all aspects of retail including customer service, cash handling & display.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur shop is at 260 Gorgie Road, Edinburgh and is served by excellent bus links\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nDependent on Volunteers situation.",
