                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000CKGjpAAH/committee-member",
                    "publishStart": "2018-02-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Committee Member",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAttend committee meetings and help with running our clubs.\n\n## Description\n\nThis role is to assist with the governance of the Branch; in particular by attending the monthly meetings of the Management Committee and by taking responsibility for agreed tasks suited to their abilities. Also to be one of the key-holders responsible for opening and locking the building before and after club meetings. To help with our three clubs (which include a disco, indoor games, arts and crafts, Scottish country dancing).\n\n## Experience required\n\nAbility to: 1. contribute constructively to committee discussions; 2. get on with people who have special needs;\n\n## Training details\n\nThe training takes place “on the job”; it is not certified.\n\n## Travel details\n\n95 Causewayside, Edinburgh EH9 1QG\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nGenerally speaking, we do not pay expenses but would consider doing so for people representing the Branch at specialist courses or events.",
