            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009SK1pYAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009SK1pYAG/youth-worker",
                    "publishStart": "2025-04-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Youth Worker",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe fundraiser volunteers’ tasks will be varied: Researching and applying potential funding sources such as charitable grants.\nPlanning and delivery of fundraising events and activities such as family days, sponsored walks and raffles.\n\n## Description\n\nFundraising Volunteer. We are looking for enthusiastic fundraising volunteers to join our friendly team at Starpic Youth Project. Starpic Project directly engages with, and supports, young people and their families in both Niddrie and Craigmillar. \nAround 10 local children attend Starpic clubs every week and are provided with fun, engaging, educational activities for no cost to parents or the community. We have children from 5 different local primary schools in attendance.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will receive induction to the company and have access to online training.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBingham Community Centre\n31 Bingham Avenue\nEH15 3HZ\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses.",
