        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZaZAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZaZAAU/ms-society-borders-branch",
            "name": "MS Society - Borders Branch",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC041990"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ID6tFYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ID6tFYAT/group-coordinator-and-coordinating-team-group-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-30",
                    "title": "Group Coordinator and Coordinating team Group Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are looking for volunteers to join our friendly, active group which aims to provide the best possible support for people living with MS (Multiple Sclerosis) in Central Scottish Borders.  The group provides therapies, grants, social and information events through local fundraising organised by the Group and through the wider community. \r\n\r\nThe roles are as follows:\r\n\r\n\r\n•\tMS Borders Group Coordinator \r\n•\tFundraising Lead volunteer \r\n•\tGrants and Therapies Lead Volunteer \r\n•\tCampaigning Lead volunteer\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nPeople living with MS, or their friends and family members, are an integral part of our Volunteer Team.\r\n Volunteers should have an either have an interest, directly or indirectly, in MS or be willing to learn about the support needs of people living with MS.  \r\n\r\nGroup Coordinator - This is the lead person for the Coordinating Team, who are all volunteers. They meet once a month to plan and monitor, and have an overview of all events, therapies, grants and campaigns, ensuring they are in the best interests of people and their families who are living with MS. \r\n\r\nThe Group Coordinator is responsible for coordinating, with support from lead volunteers in the areas of:\r\n\r\n*Fundraising \r\n*Social and information events\r\n*Provision of therapies and grants \r\n*Setting up and monitoring of Service Level Agreements with therapies     \r\n  providers. \r\n* Campaigning \r\n* Communication\r\n\r\nThey also work closely with the lead Finance Volunteer and are available to lead monthly meetings. \r\n\r\nOther Coordinating Team Volunteers required to lead on an area in which they have expertise and we welcome applications in any area of:\r\n\r\n*Fundraising  \r\n*Grants and therapies lead \r\n*Events Lead \r\n* Campaigning\r\n\r\nVolunteers can expect support and training appropriate to their role within a friendly volunteer team.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGroup Coordinator role:\r\n\r\n\r\nAbility to lead , energise and  motivate the Coordinating team of volunteers to provide support and services for people living with MS, their family and friends.\r\n\r\nInnovative ideas on how to support young people in the delivery of  services, ,support, fundraising and campaigning. \r\n\r\nGood communication skills and ability to engage with wider community, in particular voluntary, health and social care sectors.\r\n \r\nFamiliarity and some experience of IT, either through PC (Microsoft Outlook) or Mac (Microsoft Word for Mac) or ability to convert from Pages to Word/pdf etc. \r\n\r\nWe are looking for a two year commitment, but would prefer a 3 year commitment.\n\n## Training details\n\nNegotiated peer support at a local level. \r\n\r\nOnline training through national MS Society appropriate to role.\r\n\r\nPeer support as and when required.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nAvailability for monthly meetings . Other flexible requirements, according to role, is negotiable depending on the decisions made in Group meetings .\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses, monthly as required or shared car to meetings and events.\r\nMileage claim as required appropriate to role. \r\nCurrent monthly meeting are held in Galashiels.\r\n Events across Central Borders.\n\n## Taster details\n\nIf interested in finding out more about the role, please complete the expression of interest or email Margaret Teale on: msbordersgroup@gmail.com.\r\n\r\nThe existing Group Coordinator will then contact you to discuss the role.\r\n\r\nInvitation to a  Coordinating Team meeting; matching with a buddy; face to face meeting with existing Group Coordinator.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F6d892b83-731f-4262-8646-f60f4df8c518%2Fw0t4e9g3qPOhsLJ21RuqWlm5Hsj2%2Fheader.jpg?alt=media&token=92b6cdbe-5119-4baf-8b66-49828262a735",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ID6tFYAT#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Group Coordinator and Coordinating team Group Volunteers",
                        "description": "Group Coordinator role:\r\n\r\n\r\nAbility to lead , energise and  motivate the Coordinating team of volunteers to provide support and services for people living with MS, their family and friends.\r\n\r\nInnovative ideas on how to support young people in the delivery of  services, ,support, fundraising and campaigning. \r\n\r\nGood communication skills and ability to engage with wider community, in particular voluntary, health and social care sectors.\r\n \r\nFamiliarity and some experience of IT, either through PC (Microsoft Outlook) or Mac (Microsoft Word for Mac) or ability to convert from Pages to Word/pdf etc. \r\n\r\nWe are looking for a two year commitment, but would prefer a 3 year commitment.",
                        "commitment": "Availability for monthly meetings . Other flexible requirements, according to role, is negotiable depending on the decisions made in Group meetings .",
