                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H5gfyYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000H5gfyYAB/companion-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-01",
                    "title": "Companion Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nMarie Curie is looking for compassionate, everyday people to join our Companion Team within the surrounding areas of Inverurie, Banchory, Kemnay and Oldmeldrum.\r\n\r\nYou don’t need a medical background or all the answers – just a kind heart, a listening ear, and a little time to give. \r\n\r\nTake time to visit someone in their home - listen to them, share in their hobbies or interests, and enjoy meaningful conversations about life and the world around them. Even a simple chat over a cup of tea or coffee can offer comfort, companionship, and a steady, reassuring presence \r\n\r\nWhat you’ll be part of: \r\n\r\nOffering emotional comfort and conversation \r\n\r\nHelp someone express what matters most to them \r\n\r\nShare helpful information \r\n\r\nSupport family members or carers, before and after bereavement. \r\n\r\nYou’ll receive full training and ongoing support from the Marie Curie Team, and you’ll be joining a team who care just as much as you do \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nPlease note that Marie Curie will never ask you to do anything you’re not comfortable with\n\n## Experience required\n\nPatient and non-judgmental of others\r\nEmotionally steady during sensitive moments\r\nAble to commit to 3 hours per week\r\nComfortable using email and filling in a short visit report\r\nRespectful of personal boundaries and confidentiality\n\n## Training details\n\nFull induction and training will be provided",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
