        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZnJAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZnJAAU/health-in-mind-midlothian",
            "name": "Health In Mind (Midlothian)",
            "description": "Everyone has the right to live a full and satisfying life.  We can provide the tools, information and support to help you to cope with life's challenges and live the life you want to live.",
            "website": "https://health-in-mind.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC041281"
                }
            ],
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2Fbe7df95b-912a-4aab-3691-b3a77f769311%2FHi3K7lHa8wXatOHLGJFdBGJQtau2%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=2fe9284c-ba1b-4794-8354-ec89c058f610",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hqi81YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hqi81YAB/recovery-peer-connecting-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-02",
                    "title": "Recovery Peer Connecting Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHealth in Mind’s Midlothian Recovery Peer Connecting Service supports adults, aged 18+ who have current or past experiences of their drug and/or alcohol recovery and looking for support in their recovery, and to improve their mental health and wellbeing. As a Peer Connecting Volunteer, you will support someone on a one-to-one basis for up to 6 months for 1-2 hours per week. During this time, you will work with them to listen, understand how they are feeling, share experiences from your recovery journey and to explore what positive steps they can make in their lives. There may also be some opportunities to facilitate groups too.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for people who can demonstrate the following- stability, humility, compassion, patience, positivity and care. Modelling recovery and being able to share this hope is important.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will complete a 7 week training course before undertaking their role. This training covers: boundaries, active listening, cycles of change, stigma and mental health. Ongoing training and opportunities to gather with our other volunteers, along with monthly supervision to ensure you feel supported.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDepends where volunteer is based as the volunteering takes place in the community and not in a set location.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nCost of a tea/coffee reimbursed if they meet their client in a café. Bus fares or mileage at 55p per mile incurred (if business car insurance cover provided). Receipts must be submitted along with expenses form.",
