                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000004sCOTYA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000004sCOTYA2/volunteer-debt-advisor",
                    "publishStart": "2024-07-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer Debt Advisor",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSo many people in Midlothian have been impacted by the Cost-of-Living Crisis. You can make a real difference as a Debt Advice Volunteer with Dalkeith Citizens Advice Bureau, helping people access information and advice they need to move forward with their lives.\r\n\r\nThis is an excellent opportunity for someone who is “good with numbers,” seeking new skills for employment and the chance to help households facing financial challenges. Full training, ongoing support and reasonable out-of-pocket expenses will be provided.\r\n\r\nWe believe that everyone deserves access to independent, free and non-judgemental advice to help them deal with life’s problems and challenges - and you can help us to do that.\r\n\r\nVolunteers are at the heart of how we deliver the Citizens Advice service, whether it’s helping people online, by email, over the phone or in person. All we need is about 6 hours per week of your time.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAbility to communicate effectively (written and verbal) in English is important. Paid or unpaid experience of advice-giving or engaging with the public is helpful. Most important is a commitment to the aims of Dalkeith CAB.\r\nAbility to communicate effectively (written and verbal) in English and work confidently and accurately with figures are important. Ability to carry out correspondence, enter data into a computer and good telephone skills are required. Paid or unpaid experience of giving advice or otherwise engaging with the public is helpful. Most important requirements are willingness to learn and a commitment to the aims of Dalkeith CAB.\n\n## Training details\n\nInitial induction to organisation, team, premises and key policies and procedures. Ongoing training on our CAS portal and support from Volunteer manager and other staff as required. External training offered where needed.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBuses 3, 46, N3, 139, 140, 141, R1, R2, R3 and R4 stop on Eskbank Road. Buses 3, 46, 48, N3, 51 and 139 stop on Buccleuch Street. Approximately a 2-minute walk to the CAB. Free Car Park on Old Edinburgh Road, 4 minutes’ walk from the bureau.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel up to the cost of a one-day bus multi-trip ticket, or the equivalent in HMRC mileage reimbursement for car users. Refreshments will be provided when in the Bureau.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fd944d5f5-6f62-4cbc-81c1-b909a4142eca%2FWkLzgT1VE9cAHEWcVMpdVMd5bL63%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=c7ed43bc-c689-41fd-b404-dc415990e167",
