            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaWWAAY",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kaWWAAY/day-service-matching-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2016-09-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Day Service Matching Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you have a hobby or looking to find a new one? Could you share your interests this with someone new? If you have 2-3 hours a week to spare, you could join our team!\n\n## Description\n\nDo you want to make a difference to someone’s life? \nAre you patient, caring and a good communicator? \nAre you interested in volunteering? \nIf so, you could join our team! (PVG required).\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers need to be reliable and interested in meeting people. No previous experience is required as training and support is provided. We need volunteers of 18 years plus from all backgrounds.\n\n## Training details\n\nIn role training is available with topics covering brain injury awareness, boundaries, safety, epilepsy awareness, and PVA training – we value our volunteers and want to ensure you are equipped with the skills you need to fulfil your role.\n\n## Travel details\n\nUnit 4, 27 Peffer Place, Edinburgh, EH16 4BB\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nOut of pocket expenses will be reimbursed.",
