                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005SRs1YAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005SRs1YAG/thornton-rose-rda-session-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2024-09-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Thornton Rose RDA Session Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nVolunteering with us is a great opportunity to further your skills, such as teamwork and communication, while building your confidence by working in a constantly changing environment surrounded by horses and a fab team.\r\nVolunteers help ensure the smooth and safe running of an RDA session by helping with pony care duties, leading horses, side-walking with a rider, supporting participants in on-the-ground sessions or assisting the coach during a session. There are also opportunities to help with fundraising, administration, and general maintenance. Every week is different!\r\n\r\nPlease contact us by email at enquiries@thornton-rose-rda.org.uk or via social media to find out more and start your volunteering journey!\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo horsey or disability experience is required. A degree of fitness is necessary if taking part in RDA sessions. A variety of skills from horse care, working with disabilities, teamwork, communication and much more!\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will receive a site tour on arrival, induction booklets, and initial online training in the first 3 months. You will complete a “green card” to support your development; there are many paths after this.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAccessible by car, and the 49 bus stops approximately a 10-15 minute walk away from RDA.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe pay mileage for mandatory training opportunities, at HMRC rates.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005SRs1YAG#role",
