                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008ZAskYAG/management-committee-members",
                    "publishStart": "2025-02-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Management Committee members",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCAPS provides Individual Advocacy in East Lothian and Midlothian and runs several experience-led Collective Advocacy projects across Lothian. You will receive induction, training, guidance and support from CAPS staff. More information is contained within the Management Committee volunteer role description available online at https://capsadvocacy.org/about-caps/get-involved/join-our-management-committee/\n\n## Experience required\n\nDesirable skills include:\r\n• Knowledge of the duties of a charity trustee.\r\n• Knowledge of the effects of living with mental health issues\r\n• Understanding of conflict of interest\r\n• Ability to work as part of a team.\n\n## Training details\n\nCAPS CEO will liaise with the volunteer before they begin the role, they will have continuous support from the CEO and the Communications and Resources Manager.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe role is mostly done remotely but the volunteer must live in Scotland.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAs required, we will provide a policy on expenses.",
