            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eK6GAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eK6GAAU/volunteer-advisor",
                    "publishStart": "2018-07-31",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer Advisor",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAre you seeking opportunities to gain valuable training and workplace experience?  Interested in helping people deal with a wide range of issues?  Willing to commit to at least 6 hours per week and over 18?  We offer full training and on going support and an opportunity to undertake training in areas such as money advice, consumer problems and employment law.\n\n## Description\n\nPeople find volunteering with Penicuik Citizens Advice Bureau a stimulating and rewarding experience.  We provide full training and on-going support.  Apart from developing new skills, volunteers also enjoy being part of a team assisting the community on a wide range of issues.  We recognise that potential volunteers come from a a variety of backgrounds and value the diversity of experiences and life skills they bring with them.  We also re-imburse travel expenses for volunteers.  We are ideally looking for people who can commit to one session per week at 3 hours per session.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe bureau is a friendly place and everyone works very much as a team, training is provided so we are not looking for people who know all the answers, but  people with good common sense and life experience.  Volunteers receive plenty of support/training\n\n## Training details\n\nIn depth training on issues such as welfare benefits, consumer problems, money advice, employment law. Comprehensive computerised infomation system. Session supervision.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n3 to 6 hours per week\n\n## Travel details\n\nPenicuik CAB 14a John Street, Penicuik. Lothian buses 37, 47, 40 & 15/15A.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses paid",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eK6GAAU#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Advisor",
                        "description": "The bureau is a friendly place and everyone works very much as a team, training is provided so we are not looking for people who know all the answers, but  people with good common sense and life experience.  Volunteers receive plenty of support/training",
