            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eK8dAAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eK8dAAE/ranger-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2018-07-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Ranger Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWould you like to be involved with the Penicuik House Project?  We are looking for volunteers to assist the Rangers in conserving, enhancing and promoting the appropriate use and enjoyment of the area.\n\n## Description\n\nTo assist the Rangers in conserving, enhancing and promoting the appropriate use and enjoyment of the area. \r\nDuties include assisting with the management of key sites and promoted routes by carrying out regular checks, Practical maintenance on fences, signposts, gates and paths and Litter picking\r\nThis is a rewarding opportunity for someone who enjoys working outdoors on a variety of tasks.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience required. An interest in working outdoors. A moderate level of physical fitness as occasional manual lifting and walking over rough and steep terrain involved\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers will receive an induction giving information about the Penicuik Estate also covering all aspects of Health & Safety. Volunteers will be supported by the Ranger Service\n\n## Travel details\n\nPenicuik House. Lothian buses 37, 47, 40 & 15/15A.",
