            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005d6QrYAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005d6QrYAI/admin-assistantco-ordinator-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Admin Assistant/Co-ordinator Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThird Level Foundation CIC are a community interest company  (Social Enterprise and not for profit ), specialising in Counselling services and  workshops in the Community.  \r\n\r\nWe work alongside and within Community Centres - Cornhill, Middlefield, Fersands and Tillydrone.  We are building a base and planning to coordinate our services in these areas and have great opportunities for people to volunteer to assist in this.  We will work with you with travel so you would be based more in one of the centres than moving around. Some volunteering can also be carried out from home via zoom or online.\r\n\r\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. Volunteers will have detailed introduction to how we are working and will be involved in the systems we set up to do the work and reflect on it. Training will be provided in communication skills and confidence building.\r\n\r\nAn important, enjoyable opportunity to help and make a real difference. \r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Sheena Crossan, Director at email info@thirdlevelfoundation.co.uk or telephone: 07794 415410.\n\n## Description\n\nThird Level Foundation CIC are a community interest company  (Social Enterprise and not for profit ), specialising in Counselling services and  workshops in the Community.  \r\n\r\nWe work alongside and within Community Centres - Cornhill, Middlefield, Fersands and Tillydrone.  We are building a base and planning to coordinate our services in these areas and have great opportunities for people to volunteer to assist in this.  We will work with you with travel so you would be based more in one of the centres than moving around. Some volunteering can also be carried out from home via zoom or online.\r\n\r\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. Volunteers will have detailed introduction to how we are working and will be involved in the systems we set up to do the work and reflect on it. Training will be provided in communication skills and confidence building.\r\n\r\nAn important, enjoyable opportunity to help and make a real difference. \r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Sheena Crossan, Director at email info@thirdlevelfoundation.co.uk or telephone: 07794 415410.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent guidance, support and and any relevant training is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to help. All help is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe pay expenses such as bus travel etc. and this is paid weekly.\r\n\r\nIf other expenses cropped up unexpectedly we would also have a system to review and pay these.",
