        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008ncY0AAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008ncY0AAI/open-project",
            "name": "OPEN Project",
            "description": "The OPEN Peer Education Project provides training and support for young adults aged 16-25 to enable them to become peer educators, delivering workshops on issues that they feel are important to themselves and their peers in their local communities, e.g. sexual health and relationships, harm reduction in drugs awareness, young parenting.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC052681"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/DrugAlcoholIssues",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Drug / Alcohol Issues"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000CKzVXAA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000CKzVXAA1/peer-educator",
                    "publishStart": "2018-03-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-12",
                    "title": "Peer Educator",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOPEN trains young people aged 16-25 to become peer educators, to deliver workshops and training to other young people across Shetland. The harm reduction issue-based training focuses on various topics:\r\n•\tOnline Safety\r\n•\tDrugs\r\n•\tAlcohol\r\n•\tSexual Health\r\n•\tPositive Relationships\r\n•\tGrooming\r\n•\tMental health\r\n•\tChange\r\nWe believe in open minded information – not telling people what to do. We will give you the training and support you need so that you can volunteer as a part of the OPEN team to design and deliver workshops and activates to other young people. If you’re interested in being part of the OPEN project please get in touch!\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers just need an enthusiastic approach to learning with an outlook to present workshops to others.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nVarious.\nRegular volunteer meetings happen on Tuesdays 6.00-8.30pm (during school term time). Weekly meetings take place Tuesdays 6-8.30pm.  Workshops usually take place week days from 9am - 3.30pm (50 minute workshops)\n\n## Travel details\n\nAll over Shetland, but based in Market House, Lerwick.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
