            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eOOGAA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eOOGAA2/de-cafe-group-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-10",
                    "title": "De Cafe Group Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDe Café started in 2005 and is an informal setting for people living with or concerned about dementia. It is a relaxed environment where people can access information on dementia and local services in East Dunbartonshire. De Café is a place where people access information when they want, appropriate to what they want to know at the time of asking over a cup of tea.\r\nBishopbriggs De Café\r\nLocation: Woodhill Evangelical Church, Bishopbriggs, G64 2NA\r\nTime: 2pm - 3:30pm\r\nWhen: First Tuesday of the month\r\nLenzie De Café\r\nLocation: Lenzie Union Parish Church, Kirkintilloch Road, Lenzie, G66 4LD\r\nTime: 1:30pm - 3pm\r\nWhen: Second Monday of the month\r\nKillermont De Café\r\nLocation: Killermont Parish Church, Rannoch Drive, Bearsden, G61 2LD\r\nTime: 2pm - 4pm\r\nWhen: Fourth Tuesday of the month\r\nKirkintilloch De Café\r\nLocation: The Park Centre, 45 Kerr Street, Kirkintilloch, G66 1LF\r\nTime: 1:30pm - 3pm\r\nWhen: Last Friday of the month\r\nFor more information, please contact us at:\r\nPhone: 0141 775 0433\r\nEmail: info@ceartas.org.uk\r\nWebsite: www.ceartas.org.uk\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for an enthusiastic individual to provide support to our existing peer\r\nsupport groups, De Cafe’s, across East Dunbartonshire. The De Cafés are groups for\r\nanyone living with, or concerned about, dementia or memory loss. They are held in\r\ninformal settings where people and their carers, partners or family can meet and speak\r\nto each other. Assisting the group facilitator, you will play a vital role in supporting\r\nparticipants and ensuring the smooth running of the groups. These groups meet once a\r\nmonth for a duration of one and a half hours.\r\nMain tasks include:\r\n- Welcoming group members\r\n- Serving teas & coffees\r\n- Chatting with and listening to group members\r\n- Raising any issues/sign posting requirements with group facilitator\r\n- Venue clean and tidy up at end of session\r\nAll Volunteers must consent to a PVG Membership application being completed.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers must be 18+yrs & have an empathy for the aims of Ceartas and for people experiencing dementia, be reliable and trustworthy & have good communication skills.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers will be allocated a link staff member, a volunteer handbook is provided,\r\nvolunteers are invited to visit the groups for a taster session and to visit the office to be\r\nintroduced to the team. Ongoing relevant training is encouraged and supported which\r\nis volunteer led and specific to each individual. On a number of occasions throughout\r\nthe year we will organise volunteer lunches at our office to provide the opportunity for\r\npeer support and further development.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe will reimburse volunteers for all expenses incurred for travelling to and from the\r\ngroups. To be reimbursed volunteers can complete a simple form at a frequency that\r\nsuits their needs.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
