                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GTYDBYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GTYDBYA5/activities-support",
                    "publishStart": "2026-04-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-21",
                    "title": "Activities Support",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nTwechar Community Action and its projects including East Dunbartonshire Climate Action Hub focus on\r\nenhancing the lives of Twechar residents and residents from the wider East Dunbartonshire on climate\r\nemergency issues, well-being, youth and elderly projects as well as life long learning. With a host of\r\nactivities and events for the community to enjoy and get involved with.\r\nDescribe the volunteering Opportunity\r\nWe are looking for volunteers to help in various roles through out the organisation. This could be from\r\nyouth groups to projects that help the elderly Walking groups, Cycles, Summer clubs, Gala days, Strength\r\nand Balance classes. Also if you have a skill to share like sewing, cooking, gardening or you wish to help\r\nstart a group like book club or mums group we want to hear from you!\n\n## Experience required\n\nif you have a skill or talent we want to hear from you! Confident, kind, pleasant community minded\r\nindividual. Who works well with a team and who can also work well on their own.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTwechar Healthy Living & Enterprise Centre\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe do however offer a light meal and drink when the volunteer is on duty.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
