                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GTPLCYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GTPLCYA5/bike-mechanic",
                    "publishStart": "2026-04-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-21",
                    "title": "Bike Mechanic",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nTwechar Community Action and its projects including East Dunbartonshire Climate Action Hub focus on\r\nenhancing the lives of Twechar residents and residents from the wider East Dunbartonshire on climate\r\nemergency issues, well-being, youth and elderly projects as well as life long learning. With a host of\r\nactivities and events for the community to enjoy and get involved with.\r\nDescribe the volunteering Opportunity\r\nWe need skilled bike mechanics to work from our newly opened Outdoor Pursuits Centre in our state of the\r\nart Bike Maintenance workshop. We wish to offer regular drop in sessions for all residents of East\r\nDunbartonshire to have their bike fixed but also to learn the skills too needed to upkeep their bikes.\n\n## Experience required\n\nBike mechanics\n\n## Training details\n\nAfter an application is filled in and an informal chat taken place, if the post is to be filled is suitable for both\r\nparties then an induction will take place. This will include a tour of the building covering health & safety, fire\r\nregulations and relevant policy and procedure forms filled in. The volunteer will be introduced to key\r\nmembers of staff and be given a buddy to have as a contact who will meet at least once a month to check\r\nin, of course they can be contacted when the volunteer needs them. Further training will be offered to the\r\nvolunteer\n\n## Travel details\n\nTwechar outdoor Pursuits Centre, 15 Canal Row G659DT. There is a bus service that stops right outside\r\nthe gate.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GTPLCYA5#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Bike Mechanic",
                        "description": "Bike mechanics",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GTPLCYA5/bike-mechanic?#modal_register_a0gQD00000GTPLCYA5",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/GeneralPublic",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "General Public"
                            }
                        ],
                        "reward": [
                            "https://ns.volunteeringdata.io/TrainingProvided"
                        ]
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/LocalAuthority/EastDunbartonshire",
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "East Dunbartonshire"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H7RCzYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000H7RCzYAN/youth-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-02",
                    "title": "Youth Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are looking for Youth Volunteers to help us facilitate meaningful climate action projects. This could be\r\ngardening, food growing. youth work, walks, cycles.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAn interest in climate / social issues is preferred, IT and social media is a key skill needed too. Gardening,\r\ngood with people. We dont do Saltire awards, but we can offer Dynamic Youth Awards, John Muir Awards.\n\n## Training details\n\nOngoing training and support for the volunteer After an informal chat, and the volunteer is suitable then we will welcome them to Twechar Healthy Living\r\n& Enterprise Centre, where application form will be filled in discuss times and how they can help. Tour of\r\ncentre, introducing them to other staff and volunteers, covering health & safety and fire regulations. We will\r\nbuddy the volunteer with a paid member of staff, likelihood is it will our Outreach Officer. Regular feedback\r\nand support and happy to deliver some Youth Scotland awards if that is what the young person wants.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMostly at Twechar, but will join Outreach Officer at other groups around EDC\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nLunch and drink provided",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H7RCzYAN#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Youth Volunteers",
                        "description": "An interest in climate / social issues is preferred, IT and social media is a key skill needed too. Gardening,\r\ngood with people. We dont do Saltire awards, but we can offer Dynamic Youth Awards, John Muir Awards.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000H7RCzYAN/youth-volunteers?#modal_register_a0gQD00000H7RCzYAN",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "14",
