                    "publishStart": "2026-04-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-15",
                    "title": "Active Schools Sports Coach",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nIncrease participation in school sport\r\n* Organise extra-curricular sport/physical activity clubs in East Dunbartonshire schools\r\n* Develop school - community club links\r\n* Recruit, support and develop a network of volunteer coaches\r\n* Create sustainable activity pathways for young people\r\nAre you passionate about sport and physical activity? Do you want to make a positive difference in the\r\nlives of children and young people in East Dunbartonshire? The Active Schools team is looking for\r\nenthusiastic volunteers to help us inspire the next generation to get active.\r\nActive Schools offers year round volunteering opportunities supporting sport and physical activity\r\nprogrammes in local schools delivered during extra-curricular times:\r\n\r\nWe are particularly keen to hear from individuals who:\r\n* Have previous coaching experience\r\n* Are interested in a career in sports coaching/teaching\r\n* Have a direct connection to a local school (e.g. parents, carers)\r\nWhat You'll Do:\r\n* Support and help deliver fun, inclusive sports sessions\r\n* Encourage children and young people to participate and build confidence through sport\r\n* Act as a positive role model within the school community\r\nWhat We're Looking For:\r\n* A passion for sports coaching and working with young people\r\n* Enthusiasm, reliability and a positive attitude\r\n* Good communication skills\r\n* A willingness to learn and develop\n\n## Experience required\n\nPrevious coaching or involvement in sport/physical activity\r\n* Experience working or volunteering with children or young people\r\n* A connection to a local school (e.g parent or carer)\r\n* Good communication and interpersonal skills\r\n* Confidence leading or supporting group activities\r\n* Organisation and teamworking skills\r\n* A positive attitude and ability to motivate others\n\n## Travel details\n\nOpportunities are available across East Dunbartonshire including Bearsden, Milngavie, Bishopbriggs,\r\nKirkintilloch, Lenzie and surrounding villages. For school aged pupils, we can sometimes arrange taxis to\r\ntransport volunteers to local schools.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GNM6fYAH#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Active Schools Sports Coach",
                        "description": "Previous coaching or involvement in sport/physical activity\r\n* Experience working or volunteering with children or young people\r\n* A connection to a local school (e.g parent or carer)\r\n* Good communication and interpersonal skills\r\n* Confidence leading or supporting group activities\r\n* Organisation and teamworking skills\r\n* A positive attitude and ability to motivate others",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GNM6fYAH/active-schools-sports-coach?#modal_register_a0gQD00000GNM6fYAH",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16"
                    },
