        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nYLWAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nYLWAA2/east-dunbartonshire-access-panel",
            "name": "East Dunbartonshire Access Panel",
            "description": "EDAP aim to make East Dunbartonshire accessible to all by removing the barriers that obstruct people, allowing them to lead a full and active life.\r\n\r\nLocal groups of volunteers, including disabled people, carers and people with a genuine interest in access who work for better access for disabled people in their local community.",
            "website": "http://eastdunbartonshireaccesspanel.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC042284"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eIBmAAM",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eIBmAAM/admin-support",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Admin Support",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nEast Dunbartonshire Access Panel work with others to raise awareness of the positive impact disabled people have within their community and the daily difficulties they experience. They also consult with local authority, social work & health to ensure that local buildings/public spaces are accessible to all\n\n## Description\n\nEDAP require volunteers to assist with some of the work which is required.\r\nIt doesn’t mean that you need to commit huge amounts of time – you could just volunteer in an area that is of interest to you i.e. visiting buildings/open spaces in your area and taking notes or preparing agenda's and/or minutes. You could give as much or as little of your time as you are able and you would not be put under pressure to take on anything you weren’t comfortable with.\r\nIf you would like to raise awareness of issues around accessibility for disabled people and others then this is an ideal opportunity for you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAdministrative and organisational skills would be beneficial. The person doesn’t have to be disabled or have any knowledge of disability as information will be provided for any volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nEDAP meet in Kirkintilloch once a month but there may be opportunities to raise awareness of disability at a number of locations throughout East Dunbartonshire.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
