        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nYOOAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nYOOAA2/antonine-theatre-group",
            "name": "Antonine Theatre Group",
            "description": "The Antonine Players perform a variety of plays from serious drama to hilarious comedy. Our annual pantomime is always a favourite and includes performers from our excellent Youth Theatre Group.",
            "website": "http://forttheatre.org/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC033292"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000II1zRYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000II1zRYAT/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-02",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Antonine Theatre Group (ATG) is a volunteer-run amateur theatre company with its own venue, The\r\nFort Theatre in Bishopbriggs, one stop from Glasgow Queen Street by train. We put on several shows a\r\nyear. This year's programme has included Bull, Chatroom, God of Carnage, 2:22: A Ghost Story and our\r\nChristmas pantomime, Hansel & Gretel. We also look after and develop the theatre.\r\nWe're looking for several new volunteer trustees to join our Management Committee and help shape what\r\nThe Fort becomes next. We're also working towards becoming a Scottish Charitable Incorporated\r\nOrganisation (SCIO).\r\nATG has no paid staff, so trustees are hands-on. You'll help set the organisation's direction and use your\r\nexpertise to get things done. The Management Committee meets around six times a year, and we'd\r\nnormally ask trustees to give around two hours a week outside those meetings.\r\nTrustees also join a theatre company and creative community. If you'd like to, you can audition, direct,\r\nwork backstage, design lighting or sound, build sets, help choose future productions or try something new.\r\nNone of that is compulsory, and you're welcome to contribute as a trustee and watch the shows from the\r\naudience.\r\nThe closing date is 1 November 2026. If you'd like an informal chat first, just get in touch.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe're looking for several people, each with skills or experience in at least one of these areas. Nobody\r\nneeds to cover them all.\r\n(1) Finance and accountancy: budgets, financial reporting, financial controls and longer-term planning.\r\n(2) Fundraising and income development: fundraising strategy, grant applications, trusts and foundations,\r\ncorporate partnerships, or developing charitable and earned income.\r\n(3) Governance and organisational development: company or board secretary experience, charity\r\ngovernance, policies and procedures, or setting up a SCIO.\r\n(4) Theatre and the creative industries: dramaturgy or other professional creative experience, a strong\r\nunderstanding of stagecraft and theatre-making, or networks across theatre and the creative industries in\r\nScotland.\r\n(5) Theatre technology: knowledge of modern lighting, sound or video. You might work in the sector, be\r\nstudying technical theatre or production, or have practical experience elsewhere.\n\n## Training details\n\nNew trustees will get an induction covering the role and duties of a trustee, along with a detailed tour and\r\norientation of The Fort Theatre, the premises we run and that trustees are responsible for.\r\nWe're also happy to arrange further trustee training based on each person's needs.\r\nAs members of ATG, trustees can also learn to act, direct or work on the technical side of our productions,\r\nif they'd like to.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBishopbriggs - one stop on the train from Glasgow Queen Street",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000II1zRYAT#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Trustee",
                        "description": "We're looking for several people, each with skills or experience in at least one of these areas. Nobody\r\nneeds to cover them all.\r\n(1) Finance and accountancy: budgets, financial reporting, financial controls and longer-term planning.\r\n(2) Fundraising and income development: fundraising strategy, grant applications, trusts and foundations,\r\ncorporate partnerships, or developing charitable and earned income.\r\n(3) Governance and organisational development: company or board secretary experience, charity\r\ngovernance, policies and procedures, or setting up a SCIO.\r\n(4) Theatre and the creative industries: dramaturgy or other professional creative experience, a strong\r\nunderstanding of stagecraft and theatre-making, or networks across theatre and the creative industries in\r\nScotland.\r\n(5) Theatre technology: knowledge of modern lighting, sound or video. You might work in the sector, be\r\nstudying technical theatre or production, or have practical experience elsewhere.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000II1zRYAT/trustee?#modal_register_a0gQD00000II1zRYAT",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
