            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GbAtdYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GbAtdYAF/volunteer-peer-advocate",
                    "publishStart": "2026-04-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-29",
                    "title": "Volunteer Peer Advocate",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCarers Link was established in 2004 as a registered charity (Registered charity number SC034447) to\r\nsupport unpaid carers in East Dunbartonshire or care for someone in the area. The person cared for might\r\nbe living with a disability, an illness, a mental health problem or have issues around substance misuse or\r\naddiction.\r\nDescribe the volunteering Opportunity\r\nA peer advocate is someone who has personal experience as an unpaid carer and is ready to use that\r\nexperience to make a difference in the lives' of others. As a peer advocate with Carers Link, you will play a\r\nvital role in supporting unpaid carers across East Dunbartonshire. This is an exciting opportunity to be part\r\nof an innovative peer-led approach to carer support.\r\nYour insight and lived experience will help carers navigate challenges, access respite and social care\r\nservices and find the confidence to have their voices heard. We know that many carers struggle to seek\r\nsupport – not because they don’t need it, but because they lack the time, energy or confidence. That’s\r\nwhere you come in. Your understanding can help break down barriers and ensure carers feel supported,\r\nunderstood and empowered.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAny experience of being an unpaid carer\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteer peer advocates will go through an induction and training process.\n\n## Travel details\n\nEast Dunbartonshire Area\n\n## Taster details\n\nAll volunteer peer advocates will go through an induction and training process.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GbAtdYAF#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Peer Advocate",
                        "description": "Any experience of being an unpaid carer",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GbAtdYAF/volunteer-peer-advocate?#modal_register_a0gQD00000GbAtdYAF",
