                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BXryTYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BXryTYAT/volunteer-hub-support-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2025-08-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer Hub Support Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nTo help create a welcoming, organised, and inspiring environment at the MCA Volunteer Hub by supporting displays, resources, and day-to-day operations. \r\nTasks/Activities to be undertaken:   \r\n\r\nCreative Displays: \r\nDesign and maintain engaging wall and window displays that reflect current volunteer opportunities and community themes. \r\n\r\nRefreshment Station: \r\nKeep the tea and coffee area clean, stocked, and inviting for volunteers and visitors. \r\n\r\nInformation Management: \r\n- Keep volunteer opportunity folders up to date and accessible. \r\n- Organise and maintain promotional materials and items. \r\n\r\nResource Support: \r\n- Create and organise ESOL (English for Speakers of Other Languages) learning materials. \r\n- Assist with general admin and organisational tasks around the hub.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEssential:  \r\nGood general IT skills  \r\nA friendly, approachable attitude \r\nGood organisational skills and attention to detail \r\nAbility to work independently and as part of a team \r\nAn interest in supporting community and volunteer development \r\n\r\nDesirable: \r\nCreativity and an eye for presentation \r\nExperience in admin or resource organisation \r\nKnowledge or interest in ESOL (English for Speakers of Other Languages) \r\nKnowledge of using Canva\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers will be provided with an initial induction/training session. Ongoing training and support will also be provided including group facilitation training.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur office is in the center of Dalkeith which many bus routes serves. Our office does not have a car park.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BXryTYAT#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Hub Support Assistant",
                        "description": "Essential:  \r\nGood general IT skills  \r\nA friendly, approachable attitude \r\nGood organisational skills and attention to detail \r\nAbility to work independently and as part of a team \r\nAn interest in supporting community and volunteer development \r\n\r\nDesirable: \r\nCreativity and an eye for presentation \r\nExperience in admin or resource organisation \r\nKnowledge or interest in ESOL (English for Speakers of Other Languages) \r\nKnowledge of using Canva",
