                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008rl0dAAA",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008rl0dAAA/computer-club-leader",
                    "publishStart": "2018-01-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Computer Club Leader",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking to recruit volunteers who have IT skills to share. Volunteers will lead one of our computer clubs held in venues across Midlothian. The clubs are very informal and are aimed at complete beginners over the age of 50.\n\n## Description\n\nThe Volunteer Club Leader will run the group by helping learners, either one-to-one or in small groups, on a range of topics, depending on what learners would like to cover using resources provided by the coordinator and with the help of other volunteers.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood general IT skills and good communication and leadership skills are essential. Previous experience of working with the internet and email are essential. Other skills such as using Skype, social media and online shopping are desirable.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers will provided with an initial induction/training session. There will then be the opportunity for volunteers to attend a computer club to observe before beginning to volunteer. Ongoing training and support will also be provided.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nRequires a commitment of 2 hours per week for at least 6 months.\n\n## Travel details\n\nComputer Clubs are held in Dalkeith, Penicuik & Loanhead.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers travel expenses will be reimbursed for journeys to and from computer club venues. We will reimburse public transport rates or mileage at 45p per mile. Expenses can be reimbursed weekly or monthly.",
