                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000SsKhPAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000SsKhPAAV/activity-assistant-penicuik",
                    "publishStart": "2022-08-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Activity Assistant - Penicuik",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nYoung Volunteers between the ages of 15-24 will join Paula, (Youth Coordinator) in delivering games and social activities in sheltered housing.\r\nThe overall aim is to enhance the young people’s confidence and skills through volunteering and reduce social isolation for older people. The project will train, support and provide supervision for young volunteers to lead on delivering the sessions (with support and supervision from the Youth Coordinator) for older people, with those involved shaping the discussion and activity at each session.\r\nIt is hoped that in addition to the positive impact the project will have on residents, the befriending will allow volunteers to build confidence and gain valuable social skills under the support and supervision of the Youth Coordinator.\r\nHeinsberg House - Friday afternoon 13.30-14.30\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo skills required as training will be provided. The project is aimed at young people who would like support and supervision while volunteering, who are non judgemental, enjoy socialising and get on well with people.\n\n## Training details\n\nAn induction will be completed by the volunteer prior to starting. The induction will be activity based and fun and will focus on what befriending is, boundaries in befriending, confidentiality and befriending in a sheltered housing.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nHeinsberg House - Friday afternoon 13.30-14.30",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fec3a5531-70c7-3a8f-a774-1fa55971a68a%2FWkLzgT1VE9cAHEWcVMpdVMd5bL63%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=9d2946b2-2be1-4bd2-80a2-5641074709cc",
