                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000EqP3tYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000EqP3tYAF/activity-buddy-hawthorndean-primary-school",
                    "publishStart": "2026-01-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Activity Buddy - Hawthorndean Primary School",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWould you like to help us inspire and motivate young people through play?  We want to provide a fun and engaging experience for primary-aged pupils while helping them develop teamwork, problem-solving, and social skills. We’ll explore a variety of board and card games that encourage creativity and friendly competition. Volunteers will help facilitate games, support players, and create a positive, inclusive atmosphere.\r\nTaking on this volunteer opportunity would be a great way to gain experience for a future career in childcare, teaching, or youth work.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood reading skills required. The project is aimed at young people who would like support and supervision while volunteering, who are non judgemental, enjoy socialising and get on well with people.",
