                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer Support Group Assistant (Young People)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nPLUS Forth Valley is a charity that has been supporting children, young people and young adults with a range of support needs since 1988. What began as a single project has grown into a range of services supporting individuals from birth to 35 years of age across Stirling, Falkirk and Clackmannanshire.\r\nServices are delivered through three age-specific programmes: Under 5s, Children and Young People (ages 5-17), and Adult Services (ages 18+). Through person-centred support, play and social opportunities, they help individuals achieve outcomes that meet their emotional, physical, health, medical and personal care needs.\r\nIn addition, short break services provide vital respite for parents and carers, helping to strengthen family resilience and enabling them to continue in their caring roles. This creates positive outcomes not only for the individuals but for their whole family.\r\n\r\nAs a volunteer you will be actively engaging with young people who have disabilities through play.\r\nYou will join in games, sensory play and help build confidence with our young people.\r\nYou will work alongside staff and other volunteers in a group to create a safe, inclusive and fun environment. \r\nYou will be building meaningful connections with young people and make them feel supported and empowered.  \r\nYou will bring energy to the role and contribute to the young people's emotional wellbeing, social development and sense of belonging. \r\nYou will help set up and tidy up before and after the group.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication.\r\nA willingness to learn and have fun.\r\nReliable and dependable.\r\nFlexible in your thinking.\r\nNo formal qualifications or experience is required, but a willingness to meet new people.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction module - either in person or on line. \r\nNamed contact and regular Support meetings.\r\nWithin the groups there is an event coordinator that will support during session.\r\nTraining prior to starting will cover: A bit about the group and your role and responsibility, supporting dysregulated behaviour.\r\nFurther access to Autism, disability and communication training will be available.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n1st and 2nd weekend of the month.\r\n1st weekend: Saturday 9am - 1:15pm or 1:30pm - 6pm \r\n2nd weekend: Saturday 9am - 1:15pm \r\nVolunteers must be able to attend one of the full sessions.\n\n## Travel details\n\nEnable Building, Elgin Place, Falkirk, FK1 1QN.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are NOT available.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://plusforthvalley.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/PLUS-MAIN-LOGO-PURPLE-RED-Centred.png",
