        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nYUcAAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nYUcAAM/friends-of-kings-park-stirling",
            "name": "Friends of Kings Park Stirling",
            "description": "Friends of Kings Park is a local community organisation set up to to help improve and develop public facilities and resources in Stirling's main city public park for the benefit of the whole community. As volunteers,we work in partnership with Stirling Council, various Community Councils, local schools, other cpmmunity groups etc. Over  the last 7 years we have raised funds and secured grants to enable a number of  projects to be undertaken within Kings Park. Some of these projects have related to conserving various heritage assets and providing information leaflets and a heritage panel relating to the history of this ancient Royal Park and the important link between the Park and Stirling Castle and Scottish monarchs. We have also been engaged in a community gardening and biodiversity project over the last few years in partnership with Stirling User's Network with input from local schools.",
            "website": "https://www.friendsofkingspark.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038449"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityFacilities",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Facilities"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Heritage",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Heritage"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H5pZZYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000H5pZZYAZ/volunteer-trustee-secretary-or-treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Volunteer Trustee - Secretary or Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteer Trustee - Secretary or Treasurer\n\n## Description\n\n<h3>Help shape the future of Kings Park</h3>\n\n<p><strong>Could you spare a little time to help make Kings Park an even better place for the local community?</strong></p>\n\n<p>Friends of Kings Park is looking for new <strong>Volunteer Trustees</strong> to join our small and friendly committee, with opportunities to take on either the <strong>Secretary or Treasurer role</strong>.</p>\n\n<p>You don&#39;t need to have been a trustee before, and you don&#39;t need to be an expert in charity governance. We&#39;re looking for people who care about Kings Park and want to use their skills, experience or enthusiasm to help support a local community charity.</p>\n\n<h3>About Friends of Kings Park</h3>\n\n<p>Friends of Kings Park is a small charity made up of local residents who want to improve and protect Kings Park for everyone.</p>\n\n<p>We work on our own projects and in partnership with <strong>Stirling Council, local schools and other community and voluntary groups</strong> to make the park more attractive, sustainable, accessible and safer for everyone who enjoys it.</p>\n\n<p>We&#39;re a small committee, so you&#39;ll have the opportunity to make a genuine contribution and see the difference your involvement makes.</p>\n\n<h3>What could you get involved in?</h3>\n\n<p>We&#39;re particularly looking for people who would be interested in becoming our:</p>\n\n<p><strong>Secretary</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Help organise committee meetings and keep records</li>\n\t<li>Support communication with committee members and our wider membership</li>\n\t<li>Help keep the charity&#39;s administration organised</li>\n\t<li>Work alongside the Chair and other trustees to keep things moving</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Treasurer</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Help oversee the charity&#39;s finances</li>\n\t<li>Keep an eye on income and expenditure</li>\n\t<li>Support basic financial reporting and budgeting</li>\n\t<li>Work with the Chair and other trustees to ensure the charity&#39;s finances are well managed</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Don&#39;t worry if you&#39;ve never been a trustee before &mdash; support and guidance will be provided.</strong></p>\n\n<h3>What we&#39;re looking for</h3>\n\n<p>You don&#39;t need previous charity or trustee experience. We&#39;re particularly interested in people who have:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>An interest in Kings Park and the local community</li>\n\t<li>A willingness to get involved and work as part of a small team</li>\n\t<li>Good organisational skills and/or an interest in finance</li>\n\t<li>A reliable and practical approach</li>\n\t<li>A willingness to learn</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>For the Treasurer role, some experience or confidence with <strong>basic financial matters</strong> would be helpful, but you don&#39;t need to be a qualified accountant.</p>\n\n<h3>What&#39;s in it for you?</h3>\n\n<p>Volunteering as a trustee is a great way to:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Make a real difference to a much-loved local park</li>\n\t<li>Meet other people who care about the community</li>\n\t<li>Gain experience of charity governance and decision-making</li>\n\t<li>Develop skills in leadership, administration, finance or project management</li>\n\t<li>Learn more about how community organisations work</li>\n\t<li>Gain valuable experience that can support your personal or professional development</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Time commitment</h3>\n\n<p>The roles are <strong>not onerous</strong> and are designed to fit around other commitments. You&#39;ll be joining a small committee where responsibilities are shared and you&#39;ll have support from the existing trustees.</p>\n\n<p>The current Secretary and Treasurer are moving on to other commitments this autumn, so we&#39;re keen to hear from people who would like to get involved and help us continue the work of Friends of Kings Park.</p>\n\n<p><strong>If you care about Kings Park and would like to play a part in its future, we&#39;d love to hear from you. You don&#39;t have to be a trustee already &mdash; just bring your interest, enthusiasm and willingness to get involved.</strong></p>\n\n## Experience required\n\nCharity and administration experience is not necessary, but we would like our next Secretary to have:\n•\tInterest in Kings Park and local communities\n•\tStrong writing and communication skills\n•\tGood organisation and attention to detail\n•\tReliability and a willingness to learn\n•\tBasic digital skills (email, documents, etc.)",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H5pZZYAZ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Trustee - Secretary or Treasurer",
                        "description": "Charity and administration experience is not necessary, but we would like our next Secretary to have:\n•\tInterest in Kings Park and local communities\n•\tStrong writing and communication skills\n•\tGood organisation and attention to detail\n•\tReliability and a willingness to learn\n•\tBasic digital skills (email, documents, etc.)",
                        "applyLink": "https://stirlingvolunteering.org/volunteers/opportunity/10273593",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "13"
                    },
