            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000CJwvtAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000CJwvtAAD/childline-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-24",
                    "title": "Childline Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\n-Could you be there for children?\r\nAt Childline, our free counselling service for children, a child contacts us every 25 seconds.\r\n\r\nAnd thanks to our dedicated volunteers, who do a shift each week, we can offer support when it’s needed most.\r\n\r\nTo make sure it stays that way, we’re looking for more brilliant people who want to make a difference.\r\n\r\nAfter you get trained and set up in your local base, you’ll be helping children and young people who need someone to talk to. Listening to them at first and then offering support, information, or practical advice.\r\n\r\n-Interested? Then get ready to take a life-changing step forward – for you and for children.\r\n\r\nFor further details regarding this and other volunteer opportunities at our Aberdeen base or to apply to be a volunteer please: contact our volunteer recruitment team on 0121 227 7577, email: volunteerrecruitment@nspcc.org.uk or visit www.nspcc.org.uk/volunteer\n\n## Description\n\n-Could you be there for children?\r\nAt Childline, our free counselling service for children, a child contacts us every 25 seconds.\r\n\r\nAnd thanks to our dedicated volunteers, who do a shift each week, we can offer support when it’s needed most.\r\n\r\nTo make sure it stays that way, we’re looking for more brilliant people who want to make a difference.\r\n\r\nAfter you get trained and set up in your local base, you’ll be helping children and young people who need someone to talk to. Listening to them at first and then offering support, information, or practical advice.\r\n\r\n-Interested? Then get ready to take a life-changing step forward – for you and for children.\r\nFor further details regarding this and other volunteer opportunities at our Aberdeen base or to apply to be a volunteer please: contact our volunteer recruitment team on 0121 227 7577, email: volunteerrecruitment@nspcc.org.uk or visit www.nspcc.org.uk/volunteer\n\n## Experience required\n\nCommitment to children and young people\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and training is provided to all volunteers. Includes ongoing support from Volunteer Co-ordinator and Childline Supervisors.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible shifts available. All help is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAberdeen base is at:\r\nSuite A\r\nGround Floor West\r\nMeridian\r\nUnion Row\r\nAberdeen\r\nAB10 1SA\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAny relevant out of pocket expenses are re-imbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
