            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g2400000ApSj5AAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g2400000ApSj5AAF/community-development-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-03",
                    "title": "Community Development Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe have exciting opportunities at HALLA – Harlaw Area Lifelong Learning Association to help in the community as a Development Volunteer. This can involve aspects such as looking at the learning needs of people around the Kaimhill School area, encouraging volunteering with the charity/association, help develop new programmes and classes at the Kaimhill Learning Centre, help prepare funding proposals and applications, act as a ‘face’ of the charity/Learning Centre and help with room bookings at the Learning Centre.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to assist in the positive development of the Kaimhill community. Excellent support is provided to all volunteers e.g.: board members and part time admin. worker will always be there to help.  \r\n\r\nAll help makes a real difference and is  is greatly appreciated. Please contact us for more details on email: sandratindall.halla@gmail.com or tel.:  07443361505 (and mark for the attention of or ask for Olanre Amusan).\n\n## Description\n\nWe have exciting opportunities at HALLA – Harlaw Area Lifelong Learning Association to help in the community as a Development Volunteer. This can involve aspects such as looking at the learning needs of people around the Kaimhill School area, encouraging volunteering with the charity/association, help develop new programmes and classes at the Kaimhill Learning Centre, help prepare funding proposals and applications, act as a ‘face’ of the charity/Learning Centre and help with room bookings at the Learning Centre.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to assist in the positive development of the Kaimhill community. Excellent support is provided to all volunteers e.g.: board members and part time admin. worker will always be there to help.  \r\n\r\nAll help makes a real difference and is  is greatly appreciated. Please contact us for more details on email: sandratindall.halla@gmail.com or tel.:  07443361505 (and mark for the attention of or ask for Olanre Amusan).\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support and relevant training provided to all volunteers e.g.: board members and part time admin. worker will always be there to help. All help is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased at the Kaimhill Community Learning Centre, Garthdee, Aberdeen. The Centre is on the numbers 1, 2 and 9 bus routes and there is also parking on the premises.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses paid monthly with proof of bus or car travel.",
