                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000SsIaLAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000SsIaLAAV/halla-board-development-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "HALLA Board Development Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDevelopment Volunteers we need you !!!!!!!!!\r\n\r\nWe are looking for a person(s) to serve as a board member on the Management Board of HALLA (Harlaw Area Lifelong Learning Association).\r\n\r\nThe board run daytime and evening classes at Kaimhill Learning Centre (Garthdee).\r\n\r\nMain tasks and duties include:\r\n-Attend our monthly Board meetings\r\n-Taking notes and prepare a monthly report for the Board meeting. \r\n-Identifying the learning needs of the local community with the Board\r\n-Assist in sourcing funding\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a difference for the community. Your volunteering would be much appreciated, you would be a great addition to our tremendous Board!!!\r\n\r\nFor further details please contact Giuseppina Caligiuri, HALLA Vice Chair at email Hallaassociation@gmail.com or telephone: 01224 498164.\r\n\r\nWe also have a FB page (@HALLACommunity) where you can see some of our activities and tutored classes.\n\n## Experience required\n\n-Experience in community engagement work\r\n-Essential to be enthusiastic and have a keen interest in community work.\r\n-Office procedure, and I.T. skills (ECDL Award or equivalent).\r\n-Ability to work with all age groups and be a people person, customer focused, \r\nhave good communications skills.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided to all volunteers. All help is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWe meet on a Tuesday night at 6:15pm till around 8pm, at Kaimhill Learning Centre where we usually meet once a month, next meeting dates to be agreed. HALLA has a computer in the centre. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased at the Kaimhill Community Learning Centre, Pitmedden Terrace, Garthdee, Aberdeen, AB10 7HR. The Centre is on the numbers 1, and 2 bus routes and there is also parking on the premises.",
