                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HVBS1YAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HVBS1YAP/district-chair-board-trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-27",
                    "title": "District Chair (Board Trustee)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWant to help shape the future of Scouting in West Lothian?\r\n\r\nWest Lothian Scouts are looking for a volunteer District Chair to lead and support the District Trustee Board. This is a rewarding opportunity to use your leadership, communication, and organisational skills to help create positive experiences and opportunities for young people across the area.\r\n\r\nThe District Chair plays an important role in supporting the volunteer team, helping meetings run effectively, encouraging good governance, and working collaboratively to support the growth and development of Scouting locally.\r\n\r\nAs Chair, you’ll be part of a friendly and supportive team of volunteers who are passionate about helping young people gain skills for life through adventure, teamwork, and community involvement.\r\n\r\nThis role also offers valuable personal and career development opportunities. As leader of the District Trustee Board, you’ll gain experience in charity governance, leadership, strategic planning, and working with a wide range of people and organisations — experience that is highly transferable to many professional roles.\r\n\r\nThe role is flexible and can fit around existing work and family commitments, with a mixture of remote support and occasional evening meetings.\r\n\r\nFlexible volunteering • Leadership experience • Full support provided\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous Scouting experience is needed.\r\n\r\nWe’re looking for someone who:\r\n\r\nIs a good communicator and listener\r\nCan lead meetings and encourage teamwork\r\nIs organised and reliable\r\nHas an interest in supporting young people and the local community\r\nCan work collaboratively with volunteers and partners\r\n\r\nExperience in leadership, management, committee work, governance, community groups, or business would be helpful, but enthusiasm and a positive approach are just as important.\r\n\r\nTraining and ongoing support will be provided.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HVBS1YAP#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "District Chair (Board Trustee)",
                        "description": "No previous Scouting experience is needed.\r\n\r\nWe’re looking for someone who:\r\n\r\nIs a good communicator and listener\r\nCan lead meetings and encourage teamwork\r\nIs organised and reliable\r\nHas an interest in supporting young people and the local community\r\nCan work collaboratively with volunteers and partners\r\n\r\nExperience in leadership, management, committee work, governance, community groups, or business would be helpful, but enthusiasm and a positive approach are just as important.\r\n\r\nTraining and ongoing support will be provided.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HVBS1YAP/district-chair-board-trustee?#modal_register_a0gQD00000HVBS1YAP",
