        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nY4QAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nY4QAAU/generation-arts",
            "name": "Generation Arts",
            "description": "Generation Arts engages older people across West Lothian in non-competitive, expressive and creative activities that promote independence, confidence and good mental and physical health. We reach hundreds of people every year through our range of activities, which include arts groups, taster sessions, dance and intergenerational projects.",
            "website": "https://www.generationarts.co.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC036084"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hsf1BYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hsf1BYAR/seeking-voluntary-chair-of-the-board",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-21",
                    "title": "Seeking voluntary Chair of the Board",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGeneration Arts is an arts, health and wellbeing Charity based in West Lothian. We provide an inclusive programme of free arts activities provided by professional artists from creative movement and dance, to music projects, and remote cinema programmes. \n\nWe are currently seeking a voluntary Chair of the Board. A transitional period with the current Chair would be provided as well as training.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEssential Skills & Experience\n\nLeadership & Governance: Proven ability to lead a board or team effectively, ensuring strong governance and compliance with legal and regulatory requirements.\n\nStrategic Thinking: Experience in setting and guiding organisational strategy, with the ability to balance long-term vision and short-term priorities.\n\nCommunication & Influence: Excellent interpersonal skills, able to inspire confidence, facilitate constructive debate, and build consensus among diverse stakeholders.\n\nDecision-Making: Sound judgment, impartiality, and the ability to make difficult decisions in the best interests of the organisation.\n\nCharity Sector Understanding: Knowledge of the voluntary/non-profit sector, including trustee responsibilities and charity law.\n\n## Training details\n\nHandover period with the current Chair and external 'Chair of the Board' training also provided.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe Board meetings are once every two months from 1 - 3pm in person in Livingston.\n\n## Travel details\n\nFor further information please email the Director, Emma Stewart-Jones on; generationarts.info@gmail.com\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2F5jsW4cSWlGg8gq6s4rhyKkcmTtx1%2FfV8HSycv8iSk0mAC-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=4051afff-573f-482f-b553-74500df3ee60",
                    "role": {
