        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nY5MAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nY5MAAU/cancer-research-uk",
            "name": "Cancer Research UK",
            "description": "Our aim is to ensure more people survive cancer. We support the work of more than 4,000 researchers, doctors and nurses throughout the UK, fighting cancer on all fronts. Every day, our researchers make cutting-edge discoveries in our labs, and our doctors and nurses pioneer new treatments with patients in hospitals. We run high-profile health awareness campaigns and provide clear information to help people understand more about cancer and the steps everyone can take to reduce their risk of developing the disease. We also lobby the government to make sure cancer stays at the top of the political agenda.",
            "website": "https://www.cancerresearchuk.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC041666"
                }
            ],
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2F70abd87d-5edb-2e9a-53d8-adcf840b5f57%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=f9be1679-d918-437a-87b3-a9b56ddd2fe0",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000003MIXYA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000003MIXYA2/shop-volunteer-ayr",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-02",
                    "title": "Shop Volunteer Ayr",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nVolunteer in our shops.\r\n\r\nOur shop volunteers are helping us beat cancer right now.   \r\n\r\nIf you volunteer at a Cancer Research UK shop, you too could make a real difference to what we can achieve. Nothing we do would be possible without amazing volunteers like you.  \r\n\r\nYou’ll also gain valuable skills to help develop your CV and experience. And you’ll volunteer alongside a wonderful team of passionate, friendly people who will support you every step of the way.  \r\n\r\nVolunteering is open to everyone and no experience is required. So, if you’re looking for a new challenge, we’d love to hear from you.  \r\n\r\nWhat do shop volunteers do? \r\nVolunteering in our shops is varied, exciting and rewarding. No two days are the same and you have the chance to flex different skills regularly. There are always new opportunities to keep you engaged and help you grow and develop in your role.  \r\n\r\nWhile this list is not exhaustive, it gives you a flavour of some of the typical tasks in our charity shops:  \r\n- Serving customers, taking cash and providing good all-round customer service  \r\n- Sorting through donated items and pricing stock  \r\n- Working on window and shop displays  \r\n- Keeping the shop tidy, clean and well organised  \r\n- Interacting with the general public  \r\n\r\nYou don’t need any experience to volunteer . You just need to be motivated, hardworking and enjoy being part of a team. There’ll be a full induction as well as ongoing training opportunities to make sure you’re fully confident and able to excel in your role. \r\n\r\nWhy should I volunteer?\r\nVolunteering brings a wealth of benefits, both personal and professional.   \r\n\r\nEvery volunteer hour you donate means we can sell 6 items and make £20 of income. So, if you volunteer for a 7-hour day, this can generate £140. That means that every day you volunteer, you’ll be raising more funds to beat cancer.   \r\n\r\nYou’ll gain important skills that are hugely valued in the workplace such as teamwork, communication and using your initiative.  \r\n\r\nYou can boost your CV by working towards an NVQ in Retail with Derby College, and we'll provide you with a reference.  \r\n\r\nIt will allow you to get involved in your local community and to meet new friends.  \r\n\r\nOur friendly CRUK team will be there to support you all the way – offering guidance and helping you build your confidence.  \r\n\r\nIt’s fun – you’ll gain real satisfaction from volunteering alongside our warm, friendly shop volunteers who will make you feel right at home. \r\n\r\nThe minimum age for volunteering in our shops is 18 . If you’re aged between 16 -18 you may still be able to volunteer in our shops, but you must be on a recognised scheme, for example the Duke of Edinburgh. or the Saltire Award. ",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F8375c070-2fdc-4666-86c6-fc506ef10c60%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=917aca64-9f50-492d-9ec5-4303611dc46f",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000003MIXYA2#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Shop Volunteer Ayr",
                        "applyLink": "https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/shop-application",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/Volunteering",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
                            {
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "KA7 1PR",
                                "address": "KA7 1PR",
                                "latitude": 55.46257149770271,
                                "longitude": -4.629666523767053,
                                "simd": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/SIMD/KA71PR"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/LocalAuthority/SouthAyrshire",
