                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I1wKXYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I1wKXYAZ/one-to-one-befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-17",
                    "title": "One-to-One Befriender",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nONE-TO-ONE BEFRIENDER\r\n\r\nThrough our One to One/Befriending service, we support older people who may be experiencing one or more of the following:\r\n• Bereavement\r\n• Returning home after a recent stay in hospital and struggling to adjust. \r\n• Living distantly from family or friends\r\n• Depression and/or anxiety\r\n• A recent/early dementia diagnosis\r\n. Suffering from loneliness and isolation\r\n. a house move\r\n\r\n\r\nVolunteers provide a wide variety of support to clients including connecting with local community activities, companionship after bereavement, hospitalisation or a fall, or to just chat and share experiences.\r\nIt is a short term goal orientated service in that we support people to achieve a personal goal such as \r\n• integrating into a local social, activity or walking group \r\n• Going for a short walk\r\n• improve digital support skills \r\n• Attending the local Dementia café\r\n• building up confidence to socialise with a cup of tea and conversation \r\n.       Building up strength and stamina after an illness.\n\n## Experience required\n\n• Good listening skills\r\n• Good communication skills\r\n• Friendly personality \r\n• Reliable\r\n• Good time keeping \r\n• Patience/Empathy\r\n• Non-judgemental \r\n• Respect confidentiality\r\n• Able to work within set boundaries\r\n• Keeping accurate visit/call records and feeding back to the team",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I1wKXYAZ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "One-to-One Befriender",
                        "description": "• Good listening skills\r\n• Good communication skills\r\n• Friendly personality \r\n• Reliable\r\n• Good time keeping \r\n• Patience/Empathy\r\n• Non-judgemental \r\n• Respect confidentiality\r\n• Able to work within set boundaries\r\n• Keeping accurate visit/call records and feeding back to the team",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I1wKXYAZ/one-to-one-befriender?#modal_register_a0gQD00000I1wKXYAZ",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
