            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I7A6kYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I7A6kYAF/volunteer-drivers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Volunteer Drivers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are seeking the help of volunteer drivers with our 14 seater minibus to assist in:\r\n\r\n1.\tCollecting older residents from their building and run them to a local supermarket for them to get their shopping on a weekly basis on Thursdays between 11.45am and approximately 12.45pm. \r\n\r\nAnd/or\r\n\r\n2.\t Be available weekly on Thursdays between 1.15pm and 3.30pm to collect a group of  older residents to drive them all on local outings to places of interest within the wider Aberdeen/shire area.\r\n\r\nWe meet up each week during school term times. \r\n\r\nYou will be made to feel very welcome as we are a very friendly, dynamic group and greatly appreciate help that volunteers give. This is a great, enjoyable opportunity to help in the local community, make a positive difference and also the opportunity to develop new skills.  \r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Lesley Dunbar at email: lesley@middlefield.org.uk or telephone: 01224 697000\n\n## Description\n\nWe are seeking the help of people as volunteer drivers with our 14 seater minibus to assist with:\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-Collecting older residents from their building and run them to a local supermarket for them to get their shopping on a weekly basis on Thursdays between 11.45am and approximately 12.45pm. \r\n\r\nAnd/or\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-Be available weekly on Thursdays between 1.15pm and 3.30pm to collect a group of  older residents to drive them all on local outings to places of interest within the wider Aberdeen/shire area.\r\n\r\nWe meet up each week during school term times. \r\n\r\nYou will be made to feel very welcome as we are a very friendly, dynamic group and greatly appreciate help that volunteers give. This is a great, enjoyable opportunity to help in the local community, make a positive difference and also the opportunity to develop new skills.  \r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Lesley Dunbar at email: lesley@middlefield.org.uk or telephone: 01224 697000\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nPeople can assist either on  Thursdays between 11.45am and approximately 12.45pm or Thursdays between 1.15pm and 3.30pm, All help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fb8d7e456-3160-4323-ab6b-81fa73a6a59f%2FNAtFNfHzvOe92sAkJHcXgmoOE6p2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=c4283e71-e98b-4b44-b1d3-f5dd014e0aad",
