            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IS3mzYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IS3mzYAD/driver",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-12",
                    "title": "Driver",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAs a volunteer driver you'll be supporting our busy transport service which helps ensure older people can affordably access vital healthcare appointments.\r\n\r\nUsing your own car, you'll collect older people from their homes and drive them to/from medical appointments.\r\n\r\nTypically we supply nearly 2,000 (return) transports of this type every year, helping 500 individual older people stay fit and healthy - without it breaking the bank.\n\n## Training details\n\nMoving and Handling training may be provided\n\n## Travel details\n\nKincardine and Mearns - from Portlethen in the North to St Cyrus in the South and as far inland as Drumoak\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe pay mileage at the HMRC recovery rate of 45p per mile",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
