        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nYEGAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nYEGAA2/advocacy-north-east-ltd",
            "name": "Advocacy North East Ltd",
            "description": "Advocacy North East (ANE) is a charitable organisation that provides an independent advocacy service for residents in Aberdeenshire and Aberdeenshire residents who are receiving services at Royal Cornhill Hospital in Aberdeen. ANE also provides an independent advocacy service for carers.\r\n\r\nScottish charity registration no. SC024538",
            "website": "https://www.advocacyne.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC024538"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Advocacy",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advocacy"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/LawAndJustice",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Law and Justice"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/LearningDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Learning Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008hgfJYAQ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008hgfJYAQ/community-advocate",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-11",
                    "title": "Community Advocate",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDo you have spare time on your hands? Are you looking to put your life experience and skills to good use?\r\n\r\nOr maybe you are looking for a new direction and would like to brush up on your skills and confidence? \r\n\r\nDo you have two hours a week you could commit to supporting our organisation?\r\n\r\nWe can offer you a rewarding and meaningful opportunity to make a positive difference in the life of a vulnerable adult while growing your own experience and life skills.\r\n\r\nEstablished more than 25 years, Advocacy North East is a local, rights based, independent advocacy organisation that strengthens the voice of those who are most at risk of exclusion and speaks up for those that might otherwise go unheard. \r\n\r\nWe are currently looking for volunteer community advocates in all areas of Aberdeenshire. We will give you all the tools you need, including full training, mentoring and support. You will develop your skills and knowledge and support people who are less able, due to incapacity, mental health issues or a disability, to have their voice heard or make informed decisions in issues relating to their health and care. \r\n\r\nNo formal experience is required but we would expect you to have  good communication skills, and an interest in upholding human rights.\r\n\r\nIn return, you will be a valued member of our small team making a real difference in the community. But don’t just take our word for it, here is what some of our volunteers have had to say:\r\n\r\n‘Being a community advocate with ANE enables you to not only help the vulnerable who are struggling  but also gives advocates the opportunity to work with a fantastic group of people both within ANE and as clients. It is a role with a clearly defined purpose which leaves you feeling you have clearly given something back to someone in need’ \r\n\r\n‘Offers a far more challenging volunteering experience than most volunteering opportunities. This is helpful for career development but also for maintaining confidence and skills for those of us who no longer wish to develop a career.’\r\n\r\nIf you are passionate about social justice, equal opportunities and inclusion then please consider joining our well respected, effective, professional and friendly independent advocacy team. We would love to hear from you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood Communicator\r\nGood Listener\r\nOpen Minded\r\nOrganised\r\nPatient\r\nReliable/Dependable\n\n## Training details\n\nWe have a dedicated training and volunteer coordinator, mentoring and regular support and supervision. All volunteers can attend our monthly Practitioner’s meetings.\r\n\r\nIntroductory Basic Core Advocacy Skills and Adult Support and Protection training before commencing the role. Ongoing opportunities to attend bi-monthly training sessions either online or in person.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAll volunteers are paid travel expenses to and from the site of their volunteering activity. Other agreed expenses, incurred as a necessary part of the volunteers activity are also reimbursed. Expenses are paid monthly.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008hgfJYAQ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Community Advocate",
                        "description": "Good Communicator\r\nGood Listener\r\nOpen Minded\r\nOrganised\r\nPatient\r\nReliable/Dependable",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008hgfJYAQ/community-advocate?#modal_register_a0gQD000008hgfJYAQ",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
