        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nYEJAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nYEJAA2/aberdeenshire-north-citizens-advice-bureau",
            "name": "Aberdeenshire North Citizens Advice Bureau",
            "description": "Free, impartial, confidential advice & information on issues such as, money advice, welfare benefits, employment, consumer, housing, legal and much more.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC008276"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Employment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Employment"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/HousingHomelessnessness",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Housing / Homelessnessness"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/WelfareRightsBenefits",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Welfare Rights / Benefits"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Idt5VYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Idt5VYAR/volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-20",
                    "title": "Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAt Aberdeenshire North Citizens Advice Bureau (ANCAB), we believe volunteers are at the heart of everything we do. We value every contribution, whether you can offer one day per week (a minimum of 6 hours) or additional time.\r\n\r\nWe provide comprehensive training, ongoing support, and guidance throughout your volunteering journey, helping you develop confidence and skills at a pace that suits you.\r\n\r\nVolunteering with the bureau offers a variety of opportunities to match your interests and comfort level. Roles can include:\r\n\r\nSupporting clients by telephone\r\nAssisting with face-to-face appointments\r\nHelping with telephone appointments\r\nLearning the full advice process and developing into an adviser role\r\nSupporting the delivery of our services in other volunteer capacities\r\n\r\nNo previous experience is required. We are looking for people who are willing to learn, keen to help others, and committed to making a difference in their local community.\r\n\r\nOur service is built on key principles that ensure everyone receives the support they need. We provide advice that is free, impartial, confidential, and accessible to all.\r\n\r\nBy volunteering with ANCAB, you will be helping people navigate challenges, understand their rights, and improve their lives while gaining valuable skills, experience, and personal satisfaction. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds and experiences.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining provided throughout volunteering process. Training is consistently updated for advisors and volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe have main offices in Peterhead and Turriff as well as 5 outreaches across Abedreenshire North\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe can support with travel expenses",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Idt5VYAR#role",
