                    "title": "Guide Helper - 2nd Turriff Guide Unit",
                    "description": "## Description\n\n2nd Turriff Guide unit is part of Girlguiding Scotland, the leading charity for girls and young women in Scotland. Girlguiding helps members discover their full potential by having fun and enjoying new adventures.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of guiding are our regular group sessions, called unit meetings. These are run by volunteer teams of adult leaders, helpers, and young leaders. \r\n\r\nGuides run for those aged 10-14 and is a relaxed, safe space for young members to develop their interests and take on new challenges. \r\n\r\nWe are looking for an extra pair of helping hands to support our current leaders.\r\n\r\nOur Guide unit in Turriff meets on Wednesday evenings.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou’ll be supported to complete our required Leadership qualification and receive training on everything from admin and finance to child safety.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteering shouldn't cost you anything! You can speak to our volunteers how to claim expenses.",
