                    "description": "## Description\n\nHelp girls discover their full potential by having fun and enjoying new adventures.\r\n\r\nYou’ll meet new people, develop your own confidence, and experience the joy of guiding!Girlguiding Coastal South is part of Girlguiding Scotland, the leading charity for girls and young women in Scotland. Girlguiding helps members discover their full potential by having fun and enjoying new adventures.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of guiding are our regular group sessions, called unit meetings. These are run by volunteer teams of adult leaders, helpers, and young leaders.\r\n\r\nLeaders help to run our units, support the volunteer team, and are involved in planning and running the activities for girls with their fellow volunteers. You’ll be supported to complete our required Leadership qualification and receive training on everything from admin and finance to child safety.\r\n\r\nWe’re looking for volunteers in Inverbervie to support unit meetings for Brownies.\r\n\r\nBrownies are aged 7-10 and focus on fun, adventure, and even first nights away!\r\n\r\nIf you're not ready to start the leadership qualification or you want something more flexible, register your interest in the same way and a senior volunteer will get in touch to chat about other ways to volunteer.\r\n\r\nOur units meet on weekday evenings.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers need to complete an online module called Safer guiding. New leaders are also supported to complete our required Leadership qualification and receive training on everything from admin and finance to child safety.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteering shouldn't cost you anything! You can speak to our volunteers how to claim expenses.",
