                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000INmpZYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000INmpZYAT/hospitality-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-30",
                    "title": "Hospitality Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHospitality volunteers at the Royal Deeside Railway help create some of the most memorable parts of a visitor’s day.\r\n\r\nThe role can include helping with our popular Cream Tea services, where volunteers prepare tables, serve food and drinks, welcome guests and help make the experience feel relaxed, friendly and special. Hospitality volunteers may also support other events throughout the year, including our Santa Specials, where duties can include serving refreshments, helping visitors on the platform and supporting the wider event without necessarily travelling on the train.\r\n\r\nIt is a varied role that suits people who enjoy meeting others, working as part of a team and helping things run smoothly behind the scenes. No previous hospitality experience is required, and volunteers can build confidence and learn as they go.\r\n\r\nBecause many of our events and public services take place at weekends, particularly Sundays, regular weekend availability is useful. Some special events, such as Santa Specials, also run on Saturdays.\r\n\r\nThis is a great opportunity for someone who enjoys making people feel welcome and wants to be part of the atmosphere that turns a simple railway visit into a much more enjoyable experience. Hospitality is an important part of how we welcome visitors, encourage repeat visits and raise income that helps support the future of the railway.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous railway experience is required. We are looking for people who are reliable, safety-conscious, willing to learn and able to work well as part of a team. Good communication, practical awareness and the ability to follow instructions are important. Fireman training is physical and hands-on, so a reasonable level of fitness is useful. Regular Sunday availability is especially important, as most of our public running takes place on Sundays.\n\n## Training details\n\nNew volunteers receive an introduction to the railway, the hospitality role and the standards expected when welcoming and serving visitors. They will initially work alongside experienced volunteers, learning tasks such as preparing service areas, serving refreshments, food handling and supporting events such as Cream Teas and Santa Specials. Ongoing guidance is available throughout each event, with additional training provided where required for specific duties. Volunteers are encouraged to build confidence gradually and take on more responsibility as they become familiar with the role.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased at Milton of Crathes, a short drive from Banchory and close to Crathes Castle, the railway has free parking on site. There is also a bus stop across the road for those who do not have access to a car.",
