                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ICSkXYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ICSkXYAX/steam-fireman",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-30",
                    "title": "Steam Fireman",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHave you ever wondered what it takes to prepare, fire or drive a steam locomotive?\r\n\r\nThe Royal Deeside Railway at Milton of Crathes is looking for new volunteers interested in joining our Steam Operations team and working towards roles as a Steam Fireman or Steam Driver.\r\n\r\nYou do not need previous railway experience. What matters most is that you are reliable, willing to learn, safety-conscious and happy to work as part of a team. Full training will be provided, with volunteers learning gradually alongside experienced members of the railway.\r\n\r\nAs a Fireman, you will learn how to prepare the locomotive for service, manage the fire, maintain steam pressure, assist the driver and help look after the locomotive throughout the day. It is a physical and hands-on role, but also one that gives you a real understanding of how a steam locomotive works.\r\n\r\nThose who progress further may also have the opportunity to train towards becoming a Steam Driver, learning locomotive handling, safe operation, route knowledge, railway rules and the responsibilities that come with operating a heritage steam locomotive.\r\n\r\nOur trains mainly run on Sundays, so regular Sunday availability is important for anyone wishing to progress in operational roles. Training and maintenance work may also take place on other days depending on volunteer availability, but Sundays form the core of our public operating season.\r\n\r\nVolunteering with us is about more than trains. You will become part of a friendly volunteer team, learn practical skills, meet new people and help keep railway heritage alive in Royal Deeside. We are particularly keen to hear from people who want to learn, develop over time and become a regular part of the railway.\r\n\r\nWhether you already have a lifelong interest in steam or simply fancy learning something completely different, we would be happy to hear from you.\r\n\r\nIf you are interested in finding out more about becoming a Steam Fireman or working towards Steam Driver training, get in touch with us and we can talk you through what is involved and what your first visit would look like.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous railway experience is required. We are looking for people who are reliable, safety-conscious, willing to learn and able to work well as part of a team. Good communication, practical awareness and the ability to follow instructions are important. Fireman training is physical and hands-on, so a reasonable level of fitness is useful. Regular Sunday availability is especially important, as most of our public running takes place on Sundays.\n\n## Training details\n\nNew volunteers receive an initial welcome and introduction to the railway, followed by induction and Personal Track Safety training before undertaking work on or near the line. Steam Operations volunteers are then supported by experienced members and trained progressively in the practical and safety requirements of their role. Training is competency-based, with progress recorded as volunteers develop. Ongoing guidance, refresher training and opportunities to progress towards greater responsibility, including Fireman and Steam Driver roles, are provided where appropriate\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased at Milton of Crathes, a short drive from Banchory and close to Crathes Castle, the railway has free parking on site. There is also a bus stop across the road for those who do not have access to a car.",
