        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nbK4AAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nbK4AAI/woodcraft-folk-scotland",
            "name": "Woodcraft Folk Scotland",
            "description": "Woodcraft Folk are a UK wide voluntary organisation and a registered educational charity. We run groups for children and young people from toddlers to teenagers.  Groups meet weekly (school term time) and go on daytrips and overnight hostelling and camping trips at weekends and school holidays.  Groups do a wide range of activities including games, crafts, cooking and drama.  The organisation has an emphasis on outdoor activity including exploring nature, and bushcraft.\r\n\r\nAt our groups children and young people have fun, make friends and develop confidence.  We encourage them to celebrate and question the world they live in. We aim for our activities to raise awareness of local and global issues, and promote co-operation, social justice and environmental sustainability.",
            "website": "https://www.woodcraft.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC039791"
                }
            ],
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2F44c4d5b3-2435-3d38-56da-97230704400d%2F4WX3kxOmhYg5yp2v3octCSeFr5k2%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=58b6d551-4b72-4f09-8def-482128391569",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hqt6fYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hqt6fYAB/woodcraft-folk-childrens-group-leaders-and-helpers-edinburgh",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Woodcraft Folk - Children's group leaders and helpers - Edinburgh",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWoodcraft Folk are looking for group leaders and helpers for our Edinburgh, Portobello and Leith groups. There are 3 groups for children and young people of differing age ranges from 6 - 13 years old to 13+. The groups meet one evening a week (or fortnightly) in term time but also organise day trips, weekend hostels away and camps in school holidays.\r\n\r\nOur groups aim to develop children and young people's confidence and awareness of the world.  We promote big ideas like equality, co-operation and environmental sustainability through fun activities.\r\n\r\nWe do a wide range of activities including games, craft, exploring nature, bushcraft, drama, discussions and songs.  As well as weekly group nights we take part in day events and camps with groups from across Scotland.\r\n\r\nIf you are interested in joining our friendly team of volunteers please get in touch with Fleur Gayet, Scottish Officer by emailing scotland@woodcraft.org.uk.  We will provide induction information, taster sessions and training opportunities.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience is required. Volunteers need to be enthusiastic about engaging with and supporting children and young people and committed to Woodcraft Folk's Aims and Principles.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe offer training on the aims of Woodcraft Folk and putting these into practice in planning and running activities, safeguarding, promoting positive behaviour and working as part of a volunteer team.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nIdeally, we are looking for volunteers who can commit weekly during term time and are interested in attending and helping to organise weekend trips or camps. Edinburgh Venturers (13+ year olds) meet on a Monday evening, Portobello and the new Leith groups (6 - 13 year olds) meet on a Friday evening. If you can help less regularly, we would still be interested in hearing from you.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe can provide travel expenses.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses, expenses for agreed in advance materials provided for group activities",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F491ee76a-e86a-4ccc-80c0-283bab97399b%2F1p5F2XBUYWhvI8tJrDZcxCSF9Rw1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=3b83fffa-99de-4088-b85d-bf6621481821",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hqt6fYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Woodcraft Folk - Children's group leaders and helpers - Edinburgh",
                        "description": "No previous experience is required. Volunteers need to be enthusiastic about engaging with and supporting children and young people and committed to Woodcraft Folk's Aims and Principles.",
                        "commitment": "Ideally, we are looking for volunteers who can commit weekly during term time and are interested in attending and helping to organise weekend trips or camps. Edinburgh Venturers (13+ year olds) meet on a Monday evening, Portobello and the new Leith groups (6 - 13 year olds) meet on a Friday evening. If you can help less regularly, we would still be interested in hearing from you.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hqt6fYAB/woodcraft-folk-childrens-group-leaders-and-helpers-edinburgh?#modal_register_a0gQD00000Hqt6fYAB",
