            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HfnUPYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HfnUPYAZ/grampian-credit-union-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-14",
                    "title": "Grampian Credit Union Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are based at Grampian Credit Union Office on 250 Union Street, Aberdeen. AB10 1TN\n\n## Description\n\nGrampian Credit Union as an ethical financial co-operative, owned by our members offer a genuine alternative to High Street financial organisations and high interest lenders with our comprehensive range of savings and loans products designed with our members in mind.\r\n\r\nGrampian Credit Union is seeking  friendly, organised and proactive Office / Administration support to join our team on a volunteer basis. You will deliver a warm and professional service while providing efficient administrative support. The role is key to ensuring the smooth day-to-day running of the office and maintaining accurate records while delivering high-quality service in line with the Credit Union's policies, procedures and values. You will play an important role in promoting the credit union ethos and providing excellent support.\r\n\r\nAll volunteer receive relevant guidance and support. Includes one on one induction, training, named staff to shadow and refer to in terms of questions. Volunteers will join in all trainings and meetings. All  volunteers make a real difference and are greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nWant to know more about volunteering with us? Contact us via email - admin@grampiancreditunion.co.uk or telephone: 01224561506 and we will be pleased to hear from you.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and training is provided to all volunteers. Includes one on one induction and training. Named staff to shadow and refer to in terms of questions. Volunteers will join in all staff trainings and meetings.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available - all help is greatly appreciated.",
