            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaSdAAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kaSdAAI/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2016-12-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nJoin us and help us build communities and improve lives.  As a trustee with PEP, you will help guide the organisation, support the team, and ensure PEP continues to be an important part of North Edinburgh life.\n\n## Description\n\nAs a Trustee you will help support the strategic development of PEP to ensure that it continues to thrive and develop. Trustees will work with the manager and staff  to maintain high quality services and maintain PEP's vision, mission and values.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe welcome people of all backgrounds and life experiences.  Most important is willingness to take part in discussions, think creatively, work as a team and help make informed decisions to ensure PEP’s continued success.  Full induction on the role, responsibilities, and liabilities of being a trustee will be given.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe will provide training and support. Must be willing to undertake a disclosure through the PVG scheme.\n\n## Travel details\n\nPEP Centre- 3 West Pilton Park, Edinburgh EH4  4EL.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport and out of pocket expenses paid.",
