                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaMOAAY",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kaMOAAY/day-care-club-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2016-06-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Day Care - Club Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAssisting in coordinating and facilitating a small gathering of older people who meet for a cup of tea, play bingo and other games.\n\n## Description\n\nTo assist the Day Care Club Organiser with the delivery of the day club's service. To be a companion to service users who are comprised of older and vulnerable adults. Tasks include: to assist with the setting up and preparation of meals; to assist with the delivery of activities and to be a companion to service users who may otherwise be isolated.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFairly agile in ability to help or carry a tray. Able to work unsupervised. Reliable, honest, outgoing personality.\n\n## Training details\n\nConfidentiality, Boundaries, on going skills with Health and Hygiene and basic First Aid\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe clubs are situated at the PEP Centre, 3 West Pilton Park,Edinburgh,EH4 4EL, close to major bus routes. \nVolunteers are asked to meet at the club in time to prepare activities and set up.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport and out of pocket expenses paid.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
