            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000DH3wbAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000DH3wbAAD/esol-tutor",
                    "publishStart": "2018-08-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "ESOL Tutor",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nEdinburgh College Community Based ESL is looking for volunteers in Edinburgh, East Lothian, West Lothian and Midlothian to help tutor English to people from other countries who have settled in Edinburgh and the Lothians..\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteering as an English tutor could be for you if  you have good English and communications skills, You have an interest in language, You would like to teach in the future and need to gain some practical experience. You would be comfortable going into students' homes to teach them one-to-one. We are looking for volunteers who are interested in teaching English to Speakers of Other Languages (ESOL). We are looking for people with good communication skills and an interest in language learning.\n\n## Experience required\n\nOur volunteers do not require any skills or previous experience although a foreign language would be useful.\n\n## Training details\n\nInitial training and follow up training days, ESOL teaching experience and references after 6 months successful tutoring. Ongoing support from a qualified lecturer.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe training takes place at the Granton Campus of Edinburgh College. The tuition is done in the students home, with travel expenses paid.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses paid monthly on presentation of bus tickets or mileage rate 45p per mile after training.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
