                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I6DMnYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I6DMnYAN/branch-treasurer-inverness-shire-branch",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-30",
                    "title": "Branch Treasurer - Inverness-Shire Branch",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCould you give a few hours a month to look after the finances for the local SSAFA service in your area? You don’t need a military background, just good I.T and finance skills. If so, this could be the role for you.\r\n\r\nThere are SSAFA branches throughout the UK and each branch has a treasurer overseeing the branch finance. This is a key role involving financial planning and financial administration.  This flexible role involves using SSAFA’s on-line financial management system and on-line bank accounts and so can be done when and where suits you best. You will need to attend a number of branch committee meetings each year..\r\n\r\nYou would\r\n\r\n-Maintain and reconcile local bank accounts and record transactions\r\n\r\n-Support divisions to manage their local finances\r\n\r\n-Make and record all authorised payments\r\n\r\n-Prepare year end accounts and financial statements including arranging an independent review •\r\n\r\n-Work with others on a local fundraising programme to cover branch running costs\r\n\r\n-Provide reports to the branch committee and to SSAFA’s Central Office\r\n\r\n-Maintain accurate records using on-line finance management system\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly and approachable people with some experience of financial administration •\r\n\r\nAbility to be respectful and non-judgemental with volunteers, other agencies and SSAFA colleagues\r\n\r\nExperience of and willingness to use online financial administration systems/banking is preferable\r\n\r\nReliable attitude; contact volunteers promptly, keep appointments etc.\r\n\r\nAbility to maintain confidentiality and keep information safely\n\n## Training details\n\nSupport from the branch Chair, the Finance team, Volunteer Development Manager and the Volunteering Engagement Team based at SSAFA’s central office.\r\n\r\nOn-line training modules to complete at home, so you are up to date on how to keep clients, their families and personal information safe\r\n\r\nTreasurer training courses online.\r\n\r\nAccess to a range of e-learning courses\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMonthly commitment\n\n## Travel details\n\nHome Based, opportunity to attend branch meetings\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n55p per mile and all out of pocket expenses covered",
