        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nbRPAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nbRPAAY/lothians-conservation-volunteers",
            "name": "Lothians Conservation Volunteers",
            "description": "Lothians Conservation Volunteers carries out practical conservation work in and around Edinburgh (and further afield) nearly every Sunday and on many Saturdays throughout the year. Our work benefits the environment, wildlife and people.",
            "website": "https://www.lcv.org.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EnvironmentRecycling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Environment / Recycling"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaMHAAY",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kaMHAAY/conservation-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2013-05-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Conservation Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFancy a day out at the weekend? The work carried out by our volunteers can make a positive difference to an area immediately benefiting the environment, wildlife and people. It is worthwhile, fun and sociable. There is no application process, simply call to book your place on our minibus.\n\n## Description\n\nNo long term commitment, you can do just one day and there is no application process, simply call us with the date you want to come and we will book you a seat on our minibus. The work carried out by our volunteers can make a positive difference to an area immediately benefiting the environment, wildlife and people. It's worthwhile, fun and sociable. We do practical activities such as tree planting, tree weeding, control of invasive species, pathwork, pondwork, meadow raking, fencing and more.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo skills or experience required, but should be happy to work outdoors in all weathers.\n\n## Training details\n\nBefore each task the team leader describes how to do the work using tools and equipment safely. Attention is given to techniques and health and safety. One-off courses are also occasionally offered.\n\n## Travel details\n\nA range of wildlife sites in Edinburgh and the Lothians and further afield. Transport is provided from St Andrew Square, Edinburgh, approximately, EH2 1BB\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nFree transport provided",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaMHAAY#role",
