            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000O0sVjAAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000O0sVjAAJ/time-for-mum-buddy",
                    "publishStart": "2020-08-19",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Time for Mum Buddy",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nMake a lasting difference by meeting weekly with a mum by video call to chat and do an activity.\nShare an interest such as cooking, arts and crafts, exercise or help to  access courses.\nBuild confidence, reduce social isolation, empower women and encourage participation in groups.\n\n## Description\n\nFemale buddy/befriender required  to help a mum reach a personal goal over 16 weeks.  \nIncrease confidence building through sharing an interest and regularly meeting in the community or by videocall. \nSome note taking involved.\nGood verbal communication with mum and volunteer coordinator by video, text, phone or email.\nTime 4 Mum focusses on helping isolated parents and carers explore what is available to them in their local area. With the support of a volunteer parent/carers are encouraged to identify and try out an activity or hobby on a weekly basis until they are confident to attend without support and have built networks of their own.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEssential\nGood listener\nNon judgemental\nEmpathetic\nGood spoken and written communication skills\nSetting and maintaining boundaries\nPositive attitude\nDesirable\nSome IT knowledge - sending emails, doing videocalls -  but training can be provided\nCreative\n\n## Training details\n\nDelivered over 2 sessions to small groups (3 or 4) volunteers we cover a wide range of topics including relationship building, boundaries, active listening, planning, ideas for activities, recording of sessions. Training is informal and group discussion is encouraged.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2 hours a week for 6 months\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe work across the city of Edinburgh and whilst there may be some travel involved to meet with mum this will be reimbursed and / or can be paid in advance.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses forms are completed and money is transferred into personal accounts when receipts are produced.  Money can be given in advance for planned activities",
