                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000CAVBSAA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000CAVBSAA5/project-development-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2019-03-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Project Development Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nLINKnet is looking for volunteers (from all ethnic groups) to become development assistants to support the development team in the evaluation and prioritization of volunteer mentoring and befriending services.\n\n## Description\n\nLINKnet is looking for minority ethnic volunteers (from all ethnic groups) to become development assistants to support the development team in the evaluation and prioritization of volunteer mentoring and befriending services. Through a range of support structures, the voluntary job is likely to include: Assisting the development process of various projects, Helping in completing all project-related documentation, Working with the development team in project initiation.\n\n## Experience required\n\nProject development assistant will undertake a range of administration and support tasks. The candidate needs to be adaptable and a team player with good IT skills. The role will require to liaise with partners, staff and volunteers.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining is not certified and will cover the concept of volunteering, LINKnet policies and procedures etc.\n\n## Travel details\n\n31, Guthrie Street, Edinburgh, EH1 1JG.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses paid.",
