                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000MhzIbAAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000MhzIbAAJ/volunteer-mentor",
                    "publishStart": "2017-04-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Volunteer Mentor",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nMentors dedicate 1–2 hours per week to support an adult from an ethnic minority background in areas such as language development, employability, education, or personal growth either online or in-person. Each mentor is carefully matched with a suitable mentee to ensure a rewarding experience for both.\n\n## Description\n\nMentors dedicate 1–2 hours per week to support an adult from an ethnic minority background in areas such as language development, employability, education, or personal growth either online or in-person. Each mentor is carefully matched with a suitable mentee to ensure a rewarding experience for both.\n\n## Experience required\n\nInterest in helping people through transfer of skills/experience. You do not need to be a specialized person to support others. Mentors come from all walks of life and all they have in common is a willingness to give something back to the community and empower others who are in need for help.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe offer mentor training sessions both online and in person from time to time.\nWhile the training is not formally certified, it provides valuable insight into the mentoring process and covers LINKnet’s policies and procedures to prepare you for your mentoring journey.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a homebased role.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses paid.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000MhzIbAAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Mentor",
                        "description": "Interest in helping people through transfer of skills/experience. You do not need to be a specialized person to support others. Mentors come from all walks of life and all they have in common is a willingness to give something back to the community and empower others who are in need for help.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000MhzIbAAJ/volunteer-mentor?#modal_register_a0g1p00000MhzIbAAJ",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
