                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhrBLAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhrBLAAZ/board-member",
                    "publishStart": "2023-03-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Board Member",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBy joining our Board of Directors you will be contributing towards the success and development of a much loved and established community project.  We are a friendly and informal team who are committed to supporting older people living with dementia.  For further details please see our fuller description.\n\n## Description\n\nWe are seeking to increase the experience and skills of our Board, particularly in relation to fundraising / HR / organisational development / quality assurance.  If you have an interest or experience in any of these areas and can spare a few hours a month we'd love to hear from you.  Our Board meet up for 2hrs every 6 weeks and have overall responsibility for the governance of the project.\n\n## Experience required\n\nIdeally experience of fundraising, HR,\norganisational development or quality assurance.\n\n## Training details\n\nA new member of the Board will attend training which includes, Good Governance, Becoming a Company Director etc.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur Board of Directors meet at Carrick Knowe Church, 118-132 Saughton Road North, Edinburgh, EH12 7DR every 6 weeks.  Meetings generally start at 9.45am and last for 2 hours.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReceipts to be given to the Project Manager who will reimburse via bank transfer",
