                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IiBa6YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IiBa6YAF/peer-support-volunteer-mot-group-midlothian",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-19",
                    "title": "Peer Support Volunteer (MOT Group) - Midlothian",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCould your lived experience help another parent or carer feel understood, supported and hopeful about the future? Join us in creating a welcoming and supportive space where parents and carers can build confidence, connections and hope for the future.\r\n\r\nChildren First is Scotland’s national children’s charity. We stand up for children, keep them safe and support them to recover from trauma and abuse through our national and local services. Our Midlothian Family Wellbeing Service supports families affected by challenges such as substance use, poor mental health, poverty and social isolation. \r\n\r\nWe're looking for compassionate volunteers with lived experience of addiction, trauma and/or mental health difficulties or supporting a family member through these experiences. Your understanding, insight and encouragement can help people feel supported, less isolated and more able to manage the challenges they face.\r\n\r\nThis volunteer role will support the MOT Group within the Midlothian Service. The group provides a welcoming and supportive space where parents and carers can connect with others, take part in activities and build a sense of community. Through supportive relationships and shared experiences, the group helps people build confidence, reduce isolation and feel more connected to their local community.\r\n\r\nWhat will I be doing?\r\n\r\nWorking alongside Children First staff, you'll help create a safe, inclusive and trauma-informed environment where people feel respected, listened to and supported.  You'll play an important role in making the group sessions welcoming and ensuring they run smoothly and may be involved in:\r\n•\tWelcoming people to the group and help them feel comfortable and included\r\n•\tBuilding positive relationships and encouraging participation\r\n•\tOffering encouragement and support during activities\r\n•\tHelping with practical tasks such as setting up, preparing refreshments and tidying up\r\n•\tSupporting people to overcome barriers to attending sessions\r\n•\tSharing ideas and feedback to help shape and improve the group. \r\n\r\nWhat will I get from volunteering?\r\n\r\nVolunteering with us is more than just giving us your time, we want you to benefit from it as well. You'll have the opportunity to use your lived experience in a meaningful way, helping others while recognising the strengths, resilience and insights you have gained through your own journey. You'll gain experience of supporting people through challenging situations, work as part of a skilled team and build confidence that can benefit both your personal and professional life.\n\n## Experience required\n\nBecause this is a peer support role, relevant lived experience is essential. We're looking for people who feel ready to draw on their own experiences to build trust, offer encouragement and support others facing similar challenges. You'll be someone who:\r\n•\tHas relevant lived experience of addiction, trauma and/or mental health difficulties or supporting a family member through these experiences and feels able to use it positively to support others\r\n•\tIs compassionate, respectful and non-judgemental\r\n•\tCan build positive relationships and communicate well\r\n•\tHas an understanding of some of the challenges children, parents and carers may face\r\n•\tShares Children First's values\r\n•\tIs reliable and willing to learn and develop in the role\r\n•\tIs aged 18 or over\n\n## Training details\n\nWe'll make sure you feel confident and well supported throughout your volunteering journey and you'll receive:\r\n•\tAround eight hours of initial volunteer training before you begin volunteering which will take place in November 2026 (exact dates TBC)\r\n•\tTwo additional training sessions during your first few months\r\n•\tOngoing support from a named member of staff\r\n•\tOpportunities for reflection, learning and development throughout your time with us. \r\n\r\nYou'll be volunteering alongside Children First staff and will never be expected to do this alone. We'll support you to use your experience safely and positively in a way that feels comfortable for you.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nBuilding trusting relationships takes time, so we're looking for volunteers who can commit to the role for at least 12 months and are usually available on Wednesday mornings on a weekly or fortnightly basis from 9.00am to 1.00pm.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteering takes place at the Children First Midlothian base in Eskbank, Midlothian\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe believe that volunteering shouldn’t cost you anything and you will be able to claim for reasonable out-of-pocket expenses for travel to and from volunteering",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IiBa6YAF#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Peer Support Volunteer (MOT Group) - Midlothian",
                        "description": "Because this is a peer support role, relevant lived experience is essential. We're looking for people who feel ready to draw on their own experiences to build trust, offer encouragement and support others facing similar challenges. You'll be someone who:\r\n•\tHas relevant lived experience of addiction, trauma and/or mental health difficulties or supporting a family member through these experiences and feels able to use it positively to support others\r\n•\tIs compassionate, respectful and non-judgemental\r\n•\tCan build positive relationships and communicate well\r\n•\tHas an understanding of some of the challenges children, parents and carers may face\r\n•\tShares Children First's values\r\n•\tIs reliable and willing to learn and develop in the role\r\n•\tIs aged 18 or over",
                        "commitment": "Building trusting relationships takes time, so we're looking for volunteers who can commit to the role for at least 12 months and are usually available on Wednesday mornings on a weekly or fortnightly basis from 9.00am to 1.00pm.",
                        "applyLink": "https://www.childrenfirst.org.uk/get-involved/volunteer/peer-support-volunteer-mot-group/?_gl=1*1kbs341*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTg3OTk1MTk2Mi4xNzkyNTc2Mjgw*_ga_B5ZQYQG926*czE3OTI1NzYyODAkbzEkZzEkdDE3OTI1Nzc5MTgkajYwJGwwJGgxMTQ0Mzk3NjE3",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
                            {
