            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000DH2lCAAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000DH2lCAAT/community-volunteer-gardener",
                    "publishStart": "2018-08-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Community Volunteer Gardener",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThis is an excellent opportunity to be part of our vibrant community garden. Learn new skills, garden in an inclusive environment. Grow, taste and share the crops that are harvested here at Drylaw Neighbourhood Centre. Everyone is welcome. Come and grow with us!\n\n## Description\n\nThe aim of this project is to bring people together of all ages to grow and share the harvest from our community garden. Crops harvested from the garden will be used to create simple healthy meals or snacks, and feed the community. Tasks involved are basic gardening tasks (no prior knowledge needed), planting seeds, potting up, weeding, watering and harvesting of the crops. For the more experienced gardeners propagation and pruning techniques will be taught, and effort will be made to upskill as you need.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo prior gardening knowledge is needed. A willingness to learn and join in with the team is all that is required. Under 16's must be accompanied by an adult.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction takes place before volunteering at the centre to highlight the importance of health and safety\n\n## Travel details\n\nDrylaw Neighbourhood Centre, 67b Groathill Road North, Edinburgh, EH4 2SA\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses paid, up to the price of local bus services.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
