        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nbnHAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nbnHAAQ/university-of-dundee",
            "name": "University of Dundee",
            "description": "Advancement of Education",
            "website": "http://www.dundee.ac.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC015096"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008v84HYAQ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008v84HYAQ/peer-connections",
                    "publishStart": "2025-03-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Peer Connections",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nPeer Connectors are trained student volunteers who provide support and information to new students who are looking to make new friends and connections whilst at university.\n\n## Description\n\nPeer Connectors are trained student volunteers help other students get used to university life and provide support and information. If you've been at the University for a year or more and would like to become a Peer Connector, as part of the Peer Connections service, we would love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nWorking in small teams, Peer Connectors take on a variety of tasks such as:\r\n\r\no Welcoming new students\r\no Answering questions and showing students where to go\r\no Assisting at induction and social events\r\no Helping new students settle in · Buddying and mentoring \r\no Meeting regularly with students who need further support or information \r\no Acting as informal mentors - offering ideas \r\no Facilitating buddy groups for new students · Organising and promoting \r\no Distributing publicity materials for Student Services in relation to services or campaigns, for example, health, volunteering. \r\no Organising or assisting at social events for students. · Listening\n\n## Experience required\n\n* Minimum of one year study within University of Dundee as an undergraduate student or previous study in another University if Postgraduate\r\n* Friendly and approachable\r\n*Interested in helping people\r\n* Good communication and interpersonal skills, or willingness to work on these\r\n* Ability to handle any issues in a calm manner\r\n* Ability to volunteer flexibly\r\n*Must be able to work with minimal supervision\r\n*Knowledge and awareness of university service, Dundee city and student life as a whole.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining will take 2 hours and can be offered online or in person. Training will cover the following topics\r\n\r\n*Student Services information\r\n*Interpersonal and listening skills\r\n*Confidentiality\r\n*Student Issues and referrals\r\n*Personal safety/boundary setting\n\n## Travel details\n\nUniversity of Dundee campus – MUST BE A CURRENT UOD STUDENT TO ACCESS THIS OPPORTUNITY\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note - no expenses are payable for this opportunity.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008v84HYAQ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Peer Connections",
                        "description": "* Minimum of one year study within University of Dundee as an undergraduate student or previous study in another University if Postgraduate\r\n* Friendly and approachable\r\n*Interested in helping people\r\n* Good communication and interpersonal skills, or willingness to work on these\r\n* Ability to handle any issues in a calm manner\r\n* Ability to volunteer flexibly\r\n*Must be able to work with minimal supervision\r\n*Knowledge and awareness of university service, Dundee city and student life as a whole.",
