            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000CD9plYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000CD9plYAD/retail-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-05",
                    "title": "Retail Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDo you want to make a real difference in your local community? Do you have a flare for fashion and passion for customer service? Why not join a great organisation where you can use your existing skills and learn new ones whilst gaining experience in the exciting and evolving world of retail.\n\nThere are many aspects to retail and we can offer you the opportunity to shape your retail role that suits you. Are you interested in:\n\n•\tMeeting customers and taking payment for sales\n•\tSorting and pricing stock\n•\tReplenishing stock\n•\tStock merchandising\n•\tMaintaining a clean and tidy shop floor and back store\n\nWhat you can expect from us?\n\n•\tThe opportunity to gain experience in the charity sector\n•\tTake on a new challenge and meet new people\n•\tOpportunity to make a difference to your local community\n•\tContribute to the mission of the Hospice and be part of a caring,   compassionate team\n•\tLearn and develop new skills and use existing skills to help others\n•\tTraining and support to carry out your role\n•\tReceive reference letters in support of any future employment or opportunities for ongoing studies\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,Creative,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Hard Working,Organised,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Team Player,Trustworthy,\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire,Lanark",
