            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I69JBYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I69JBYAZ/garden-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-23",
                    "title": "Garden Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nGarden Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nGot green fingers &ndash; or would you like to develop them? Get outdoors, meet new people and help Kinning Park Complex&#39;s community garden grow!\n\nKinning Park Complex is looking for enthusiastic Garden Volunteers to help care for and develop our community garden and outdoor space at our community-owned venue in the Southside of Glasgow.\n\nOur garden is a place where local people can come together, connect with nature, grow food and plants, learn new skills and contribute ideas about how the outdoor space develops.\n\nYou don&#39;t need to be an experienced gardener to get involved &ndash; enthusiasm and a willingness to get stuck in are much more important.\n\nAs part of our friendly group of garden volunteers, you&#39;ll get involved in a variety of practical and seasonal activities. There&#39;s also the opportunity to contribute your own ideas and help shape the future of the garden.\n\nDifferent activities take place throughout the year, so there&#39;s plenty to learn. Our gardening programme has also included activities and workshops covering topics such as composting and herbal medicine.\n\nWhat You Will Be Doing\n\nDepending on the season and what needs doing, you could be:\n\n\n\tSowing seeds and helping to grow fruit, vegetables, flowers and other plants.\n\tWatering, weeding and carrying out general garden maintenance.\n\tFilling and emptying compost bins and learning more about composting.\n\tUsing wheelbarrows and a range of gardening tools and equipment.\n\tHelping keep the garden and outdoor areas tidy and welcoming.\n\tWorking alongside other volunteers on practical gardening tasks.\n\tTaking part in different gardening activities and workshops.\n\tSharing your ideas about how the garden could be improved and developed.\n\tHelping to plan and shape the future of the community garden.\n\n\nThere&#39;s plenty of opportunity to learn as you go, so you don&#39;t need to arrive with lots of gardening knowledge or experience.\n\nWhen and Where\n\nThe garden group currently meets every Monday from 2pm&ndash;4pm.\n\nWe&#39;re looking for volunteers who can commit to at least one Monday each month.\n\nThe opportunity takes place at:\n\nKinning Park Complex\n43 Cornwall Street\nGlasgow\nG41 1BA\n\nWho Would Suit This Role?\n\nThis could be a great opportunity for someone who enjoys being outdoors, would like to meet new people and wants to make a practical contribution to their local community.\n\nIt could particularly suit someone who:\n\n\n\tHas an interest in gardening, plants, growing food or nature.\n\tEnjoys practical, hands-on activities and doesn&#39;t mind getting their hands dirty.\n\tWould like to learn new gardening skills or share skills they already have.\n\tEnjoys working alongside others as part of a friendly team.\n\tWould like an opportunity to get outdoors and become more involved in their local community.\n\tIs interested in helping develop a welcoming community garden and sharing ideas for its future.\n\n\nWhether you&#39;re an experienced gardener or a complete beginner, you&#39;re welcome to get involved.\n\nSupport for Volunteers\n\nYou&#39;ll be supported by the experienced Kinning Park Complex team while volunteering in the garden.\n\nThe team will help you get started, explain the tasks you&#39;ll be doing and provide guidance on using gardening tools and equipment safely.\n\nYou&#39;ll work alongside other volunteers, so you won&#39;t be expected to manage the garden or carry out activities on your own.\n\nGardening gloves, tools and equipment are provided, so you don&#39;t need to bring your own.\n\nIf you&#39;re new to gardening, that&#39;s absolutely fine &ndash; you&#39;ll have opportunities to learn as you go and develop your skills with the support of the team.\n\nApply\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on info@volunteerglasgow.org\n\nWhat Happens After You Apply?\n\nOnce you click Apply, your details and expression of interest will be sent to Kinning Park Complex.\n\nA member of the team will then get in touch with you to discuss the Garden Volunteer role, your availability and what you can expect from volunteering with them.\n\nThis will also give you an opportunity to ask any questions about the gardening activities, support available and travel expenses.\n\nIf the opportunity is a good fit for you, the team will explain the next steps and arrangements for getting started.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou don't need previous gardening experience to volunteer – enthusiasm and a willingness to get involved are more important.\nWe're looking for people who:\n•\tHave an interest in gardening, plants, growing food or the outdoors.\n•\tEnjoy practical, hands-on activities.\n•\tAre willing to learn new gardening skills.\n•\tAre happy working outdoors and getting their hands dirty.\n•\tCan work alongside other volunteers as part of a team.\n•\tAre willing to use gardening tools and equipment safely.\n•\tCan\n\n## Travel details\n\nTravel Information\nKinning Park Complex is located at 43 Cornwall Street, Glasgow, G41 1BA and is easily accessible by public transport.\n\nKinning Park Subway Station is very close to the Complex, providing connections to Glasgow city centre and the wider Subway network. Local bus services also operate in and around the Kinning Park area.\n\nAgreed travel costs for volunteering are available and can be discussed with the Kinning Park Complex team.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses paid",
