                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I3Wk9YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I3Wk9YAF/website-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-23",
                    "title": "Website Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nYMCA Glenrothes is an independent local charity, governed by a dedicated team of volunteers from across Fife and proudly affiliated with the worldwide YMCA movement. Committed to supporting the local community, the charity delivers practical services, information, and opportunities that help people thrive, build connections, and overcome challenges.\r\n\r\nYMCA Glenrothes is looking for a Website Volunteer to help maintain and develop its online presence, ensuring that local people can easily access up-to-date information about the charity's services, activities, and events.\r\n\r\nThis is a valuable behind-the-scenes role that supports the smooth running of the organisation and helps promote the positive impact YMCA Glenrothes has within the local community.\r\n\r\nMain duties include:\r\n- Keeping website content accurate, relevant, and up to date.\r\n- Adding new events, activities, and news stories to the website.\r\n- Checking website pages regularly to ensure links, documents, and contact information are working correctly.\r\n- Suggesting improvements to website content, layout, and user experience where appropriate.\r\n- Helping ensure information is easy to navigate and accessible for website visitors.\r\n- Working with the YMCA team to showcase volunteer opportunities, success stories, and the organisation's impact in the community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThis role would suit someone who is organised, has good attention to detail, and is confident using websites and online systems. It offers a flexible way to support YMCA Glenrothes while helping the organisation connect with and inform the local community.\n\n## Travel details\n\nHome based with space available at the organisations Head Office in Glenrothes when required.",
