                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-23",
                    "title": "Social Media Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nYMCA Glenrothes is an independent local charity, governed by a dedicated team of volunteers from across Fife and proudly affiliated with the worldwide YMCA movement. Committed to supporting the local community, the charity delivers practical services, information, and opportunities that help people thrive, build connections, and overcome challenges.\r\n\r\nThis role focuses on maintaining and enhancing the organisation’s social media presence across a range of platforms. From capturing Instagram-worthy photos and creating engaging Facebook posts to producing creative TikTok reels, you’ll help showcase the organisation’s work and connect with a wider audience. If you’re social media savvy, creative, and enjoy creating engaging content, this could be the perfect role for you.\r\n\r\nThis flexible volunteering role can fit around your existing commitments. You'll receive all the necessary training, have your travel expenses reimbursed, and be supported by a friendly team.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe ideal volunteer will have confidence in using a broad range of social media platforms. Although access to their own device is desirable, suitable equipment can be supplied if necessary.\n\n## Travel details\n\nHome-based or space available at the organisations Head Office in Glenrothes.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I3WaTYAV#role",
