            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GNPyzYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GNPyzYAH/group-leader",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Group Leader",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAgape Wellbeing Centre and Sensory Hub delivers a weekly programme of group services and activities for vulnerable adults and families with young children. Our sessions create opportunities for people across the community to connect, build confidence, and take part in meaningful activities that support positive mental health and wellbeing.\n\nWe are looking for enthusiastic and compassionate volunteers to support and lead a range of engaging group sessions, including board games, music, crafts, and sensory play.\nWhat you’ll do:\nPrepare and set up activities and refreshments before each session\nFollow session plans to deliver structured, engaging group activities\nCreate a warm, inclusive, and supportive environment for all participants\nEncourage participation through positive conversation and individual support\nHelp ensure sessions are fun, interactive, and accessible to everyone\nComplete basic procedures such as sign-in sheets\nTidy and clean the space at the end of each session\n\nWhat you can bring:\nWe welcome volunteers from all backgrounds. Whether you have experience or simply enthusiasm, you’ll have the opportunity to contribute your own skills and interests. This could include helping to develop new sessions in areas such as drama, music, creative writing, dance, or fitness as part of our holistic wellbeing programme.\n\nWhat you’ll gain:\nValuable experience in health and social care and community work\nOpportunities to develop leadership, communication, and organisational skills\nThe chance to make a real difference in your local community\nReferences to support your future career or education.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Hard Working,Organised,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Team Player,\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will be provided with induction training and ongoing training and support to support their work and future development.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nEast Kilbride\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgape Wellbeing will reimburse the cost of public transport used when travelling to and from your volunteering role.",
