                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000DwbpJYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000DwbpJYAR/sensory-hub-group-leader",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-01",
                    "title": "Sensory Hub Group Leader",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are seeking a warm, caring, and reliable volunteer to lead sessions in our Sensory Hub for families and young children. The role involves creating a welcoming and inclusive environment where children can explore sensory play in a safe and engaging space. Key tasks include setting up sensory activities, supporting families as they engage in play, and tidying the room after each session to maintain high standards of cleanliness. You will also follow health, safety, and safeguarding procedures, including recording attendance and reporting any concerns. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys working with families, has an interest in early years development, and is passionate about supporting others and promoting positive wellbeing.\n\n## Experience required\n\nBefriending / Mentoring,Community Development / Social work,No Expertise,Youth / Childcare, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Hard Working,Reliable / Dependable,\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers receive an induction and will be given all the training and support necessary to feel confident in the role. Staff members are on hand to provide ongoing help and support.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgape Wellbeing will reimburse public transport expenses for volunteers.",
