            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eNIRAA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eNIRAA2/youth-work-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Youth Work Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are currently expanding our volunteers and are looking for people to assist and engage with the young people attending the Youth Outreach Bus in a positive and encouraging manner. \n\nThis is an exciting and unique opportunity to help with the only mobile youth drop in centre like this in Aberdeen.\n\nA great opportunity to help, make a difference for young people and the local community and be part of a friendly, supportive team of volunteers.\n\nFor more information please e-mail: info@dyceyob.org.uk\n\n## Description\n\nThe Youth Outreach Bus or ‘Red Bus’ as it has become known is a converted double decker bus which has been completely re-designed inside to become a mobile youth drop in centre for ages s1-s6 (secondary school). It has Playstations, Music System (which plays both internally and externally) and a widescreen TV which can play DVD’s and be connected to the Nintendo Wii.\n\nWe are currently expanding our volunteers and are looking for people to assist and engage with the young people attending in a positive and encouraging manner. \n\nThe bus currently operates in Dyce and Seaton, but is mobile and we are actively looking to expand to working in other parts of Aberdeen as well.\n\nThis is an exciting and unique opportunity to help with the only mobile youth drop in centre like this in Aberdeen.\n\nA great opportunity to help, make a difference for young people and the local community and be part of a friendly, supportive team of volunteers.\n\nFor more information please e-mail: info@dyceyob.org.uk\n\n## Experience required\n\nIndividuals with an interest and heart for working with young people. Good communication skills.\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. All the Project Trustees are ‘hands on’ volunteers as well and will provide ongoing support. All volunteers are greatly appreciated by the charity and the people we work with.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe bus currently operates in Dyce and Seaton in the evening time. All volunteer help is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe bus currently operates in Dyce and Seaton, but is mobile and we are actively looking to expand to working in other parts of Aberdeen as well. Current location is close to bus route and also 5 minutes from train station.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe assess on a ‘case-by-case’ basis the approval and re-imbursement of any relevant expenses for volunteering in this role.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eNIRAA2#role",
                        "type": "Role",
