            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HhNh7YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HhNh7YAF/garden-maintenance-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-10",
                    "title": "Garden Maintenance Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAberdeen Sands is a registered charity and part of the Sands UK-wide network of local groups. Aberdeen Sands supports anyone who has been affected by the death of a baby before, during or shortly after birth. We offer emotional support and information for parents, grandparents, siblings, children, families and friends, health professionals and others. Aberdeen Sands is managed by a committee of volunteers, all of whom are bereaved parents.\r\n\r\nDo you like taking part in garden maintenance? We have a joint garden with MISS (Miscarriage Information Support Service)-the Forget Me Not Garden  and are seeking people to help as Garden Maintenance Volunteers. Our next volunteer gardening session takes place on Friday 11th December between 10.30 to 12.30.\r\n\r\nAll help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated. For more information please contact us at email: support.aberdeen@sandsvolunteer.org.uk\r\n\r\nMore information about Aberdeen Sands is also available at https://www.aberdeen-sands.org/\r\n\r\n*Please note that due to current UK Home Office rules, we are only able to recruit volunteer applicants who are already eligible to live and work in the UK. We are also not sponsoring Charity Workers under the Tier 5 visa scheme. Therefore, if you do not have the right to work and live in the UK, we ask that you do not contact us as we will not be in a position to progress your application. Thank you.\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant guidance and excellent support is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nOur next volunteer gardening session is on: 11th December Friday 10.30 to 12.30\r\n\r\nAll help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fa64f4df6-2cea-4181-8989-421ed77fc730%2FTJgEBk9eynOtboKxnBrDgc4yZmH2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=e73bd1d0-cede-4d0a-90f9-c448c0cefd23",
