                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hv289YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hv289YAB/fundraising-team-volunteer-can-collector",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-16",
                    "title": "Fundraising Team Volunteer – Can Collector",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFundraising Team Volunteer – Can Collector\n\n## Description\n\nDo you enjoy getting out in your community and building relationships? Our Can Collector volunteers help place and collect donation cans in local shops, caf&eacute;s, and businesses, turning everyday generosity into vital funds.\n\nThis role is perfect for someone who enjoys being out and about, meeting people, and making a meaningful difference in a flexible way.\n\nDuties include:\n\n\n\tDistributing and collecting donation cans\n\tBuilding relationships with local businesses\n\tRecording and returning funds securely\n\tEnsuring cans are clean and well-presented\n\n\nSkills required:\n\n\n\tFriendly and confident communicator\n\tOrganised and reliable\n\tFull UK driving licence and access to a vehicle\n\tTrustworthy when handling cash\n\n\nTime commitment:\nA few hours per week, flexible to suit you.\n\nTraining, support and benefits:\n\n\n\tFull induction and ongoing support\n\tMileage expenses covered\n\t20% discount in our community charity shops\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly and confident communicator\nOrganised and reliable\nFull UK driving licence and access to a vehicle\nTrustworthy when handling cash\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses paid at the end of every month",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
