                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hv26XYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hv26XYAR/volunteer-driver-market-sales",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-16",
                    "title": "Volunteer Driver – Market Sales",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteer Driver – Market Sales\n\n## Description\n\nDo you enjoy being on the road and supporting your community? We&rsquo;re looking for Volunteer Drivers to help our market sales team transport goods, equipment, and team members to local events.\n\nAs part of our retail team, you&rsquo;ll play a key role in ensuring our market stalls run smoothly. Every mile you drive helps support the sale of goods that contribute to funding compassionate care for patients and families in our community.\n\nThis role is perfect for someone who enjoys driving, working as part of a team, and being involved in community events.\n\nDuties include:\n\n\n\nDriving the hospice transit van to and from market locations\n\n\nLoading and unloading stock and equipment\n\n\nAssisting with stall set up and pack down\n\n\nEnsuring goods and equipment are transported safely\n\n\nCarrying out basic vehicle checks and reporting any issues\n\n\nSupporting the market team as required\n\n\n\nSkills required:\n\n\n\nFull UK driving licence and confidence driving a transit van\n\n\nReliable, responsible, and organised\n\n\nAbility to assist with lifting and moving stock\n\n\nFriendly and able to work as part of a team\n\n\nPositive attitude and willingness to support fundraising activities\n\n\n\nTime commitment:\n\nThis role typically involves early weekend mornings to align with market trading times. Flexibility is needed depending on event schedules, with tasks including transporting stock, setting up stalls, and returning goods.\n\nTraining, support and benefits:\n\n\n\nFull induction and ongoing training to support you in your role\n\n\nOngoing support from a member of staff throughout your volunteering\n\n\n20% discount in our community charity shops\n\n## Experience required\n\nFull UK driving licence and confidence driving a transit van\n\nReliable, responsible, and organised\n\nAbility to assist with lifting and moving stock\n\nFriendly and able to work as part of a team\n\nPositive attitude and willingness to support fundraising activities",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hv26XYAR#role",
