                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hv21hYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hv21hYAB/reception-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-16",
                    "title": "Reception Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nReception Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nWe are currently looking for friendly and organised people to help welcome visitors to the hospice and provide admin support to our staff teams.\n\nThis role is an important first point of contact that many members of the public have with the hospice and is an ongoing point of contact for them for information.\n\nDuties include:\n\n\nAdministration tasks to support our staff teams.\nGreeting patients and visitors to the hospice and guiding them through our sign in process.\nAnswering calls from families and friends to arrange visiting times, transferring calls to the clinical teams and taking messages where required.\nPrinting out and distributing patient and visitor information leaflets.\nSign-posting visitors to tea and coffee facilities, rest rooms etc\nSign-posting visitors and callers to various hospice services including information about referrals.\nProviding information to families and friends of patients who want to contact someone to make an in-memory donation to the hospice\n\n\nSkills required:\n\n\nPleasant and welcoming manner.\nReliability and good timekeeping.\nWillingness to learn new skills.\nAbility to work independently and as part of a team.\nBasic knowledge of Microsoft word, Excel and email interfaces.\nWillingness to adopt infection control procedures (self) and encourage others to comply with the same.\n\n\nTime Commitment:\n\n1 shift per week or fortnight to be chosen from:\n\n\nMonday to Sunday 9am&ndash;7pm\n\n\nTraining, support and benefits:\n\n\nA full induction and further skills training to enable you to fulfil your role as required.\nA staff member will support you throughout your time as a volunteer.\n20% discount in our community charity shops.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPleasant and welcoming manner.\nReliability and good timekeeping.\nWillingness to learn new skills.\nAbility to work independently and as part of a team.\nBasic knowledge of Microsoft word, Excel and email interfaces.\nWillingness to adopt infection control procedures (self) and encourage others to comply with the same.",
