                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-16",
                    "title": "Day Services Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDay Services Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for friendly and organised people to help support the running of our Day Service programme for people with various needs. Volunteers will work as part of a team to make a positive impact on the patients by helping provide enjoyable activities. They will be supported by the day service coordinator to encourage and enable patients to participate in a range of social activities and groups and help build confidence and self-esteem.\n\nThey will empower people to socially interact while engaging in fun activities, helping to promote independence and reduce social isolation as well as providing an enjoyable experience.\n\nDuties include:\n\n\nGreeting patients and visitors to the hospice and guiding them through our sign in process.\nAssisting day patients with mobility, diet, eating and drinking assistance.\nWorking with people who may have additional needs and variety of communication needs.\nRegular communication with other team members and reporting any incidents.\n\n\nSkills required:\n\n\nPleasant and welcoming manner with the ability to interact with people in a way that takes account of their individual, cultural and religious needs.\nReliability and good timekeeping.\nAbility to work independently and as part of a team.\nWillingness to learn new skills.\nDiscretion and the ability to keep information confidential.\nA good listener with a person centred approach\nWillingness to adopt infection control procedures (self) and encourage others to comply with the same.\nPrevious experience or knowledge of working with a vulnerable client group is desirable but is not essential as training will be provided.\n\n\nThis role will require a PVG check to be carried out.\n\nTime Commitment:\n\nDay Services will run 7 days a week. We are ideally looking for volunteers who can commit to one 2-3 hour shift a week but could discuss other arrangements.\n\nTraining, support and benefits:\n\n\nA full induction and further skills training to enable you to fulfil your role as required.\nA staff member will support you throughout your time as a volunteer.\n20% discount in our pre -loved shops.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPleasant and welcoming manner with the ability to interact with people in a way that takes account of their individual, cultural and religious needs.\nReliability and good timekeeping.\nAbility to work independently and as part of a team.\nWillingness to learn new skills.\nDiscretion and the ability to keep information confidential.\nA good listener with a person centred approach\nWillingness to adopt infection control procedures (self) and encourage others to comply with the same.\nPrevious exp",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hv1yTYAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Day Services Volunteer",
                        "description": "Pleasant and welcoming manner with the ability to interact with people in a way that takes account of their individual, cultural and religious needs.\nReliability and good timekeeping.\nAbility to work independently and as part of a team.\nWillingness to learn new skills.\nDiscretion and the ability to keep information confidential.\nA good listener with a person centred approach\nWillingness to adopt infection control procedures (self) and encourage others to comply with the same.\nPrevious exp",
