                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HsyqDYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HsyqDYAR/ebay-shoes-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-08",
                    "title": "Ebay Shoes Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nEbay Shoes Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nDo you have a passion for fashion and an eye for detail? We&rsquo;re looking for volunteers to join our eBay team, helping us turn pre-loved shoes into vital funds for St Vincent&rsquo;s Hospice.\n\nAs part of our online retail team, you&rsquo;ll play a key role in identifying, preparing, and listing shoes for sale on our eBay store. Every pair sold directly supports compassionate care for patients and families in our community.\n\nThis role is perfect for anyone interested in fashion trends, sustainable shopping, or online selling.\n\nDuties include:\n\n\n\tAssessing pre-loved shoes for quality, style, and resale potential\n\tCleaning, photographing, and preparing shoes for online listings\n\tResearching and pricing items to maximise sales\n\tWriting clear and engaging product descriptions\n\tSupporting with general organisation of the workspace\n\n\nSkills required:\n\n\n\tGood attention to detail and ability to assess quality\n\tOrganised, reliable, and punctual\n\tComfortable using eBay or willing to learn\n\tPositive attitude and ability to work as part of a team\n\n\nTime commitment:\n\nWe are looking for volunteers who can commit to a few hours per week. There is flexibility depending on stock availability and team needs, with opportunities to increase hours during busy periods.\n\nTraining, support and benefits:\n\n\n\tFull induction and ongoing training to support you in your role\n\tOngoing support from a member of staff throughout your volunteering\n\t20% discount in our community charity shops\n\n## Experience required\n\nFamiliar with a smartphone",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
