        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nWzZAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nWzZAAU/clydebank-stroke-club",
            "name": "Clydebank Stroke Club",
            "description": "To improve the quality of life of our members and encourage self confidence, with the onset of their stroke.",
            "website": "https://www.chss.org.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009oi8jYAA",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009oi8jYAA/group-support",
                    "publishStart": "2025-05-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-14",
                    "title": "Group Support",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNo matter how good our services are, we can't properly support our users/community well if we don't have skilled people in the team. If this sounds like you?... we would love you to consider volunteering with us for a few hours per week.\r\n\r\nClydebank Stroke Club have been providing support to people who have experienced a stroke for a number of years, we provide social activities for those who otherwise might not interact with other people.\r\n\r\nOur friendly environment is an ideal place for you to put your support skills to great use -experience of supporting individuals and groups is desirable but not essential, ability to support people in a social setting, be objective, have good listening skills, be non-judgemental and encourage the whole group to participate.  \r\n\r\nSo, whether you are looking to use your time well, update your skills or have the chance to do something a bit new, we would love to hear from you. In return, we can offer you a warm welcome and all of the support and help you could need.\r\n\r\nWe are seeing a rise in demand for our services, everyday. Having your help will allow us to be there for the people who need us. Any time you can give will make a real difference.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased in the Hub CE Centre Clydebank",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009oi8jYAA#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Group Support",
