                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009ohe5YAA",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009ohe5YAA/bus-escort",
                    "publishStart": "2025-05-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-14",
                    "title": "Bus Escort",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNo matter how good our services are, we can't properly support our users/community well if we don't have skilled people in the team. If this sounds like you?... we would love you to consider volunteering with us for a few hours per week.\r\n \r\nClydebank Stroke Club have been providing support to people who have experienced a stroke for a number of years, we provide social activities for those who otherwise might not interact with other people.\r\n \r\nLooking for someone to support our members to get to and from the club on our hired bus, ideally we would like someone with a qualification in moving and handling to escort our members from their home to the club venue.  You will be  reliable, have good communication skills and be patient. The role involves being flexible, physically fit and having good people skills.\r\n\r\nSo, whether you are looking to use your time well, update your skills or have the chance to do something a bit new, we would love to hear from you. In return, we can offer you a warm welcome and all of the support and help you could need.\r\n \r\nWe are seeing a rise in demand for our services, everyday. Having your help will allow us to be there for the people who need us. Any time you can give will make a real difference. \n\n## Experience required\n\nAbility to support people\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased at the Hub CE Centre",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009ohe5YAA#role",
