                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-03",
                    "title": "Voluntary Secretary",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNo matter how good our services are, we can't properly support our users/community well if we don't have a good committee behind the team. If this sounds like you?... We would love you to consider volunteering with us for a few hours per month.\r\n\r\nThe Rockvale rebound provides printed information e.g. local newspapers etc. on audible digital, free to print impaired people i.e.. blind, deaf-blind & partially sighted people in West Dunbartonshire. The service is only provided thanks to the invaluable help of our team of volunteers. Currently we are seeking someone to become our secretary.\r\nSomeone with some clerical or secretarial knowledge or experience is required by the Rockvale Rebound talking newspaper for the blind, in Dumbarton.\r\n\r\nDuties: To work/liaise with other volunteers to ensure the production of our fortnightly recordings. Arrange/call committee meetings, (currently held by telephone conference call) and produce minutes. Be the focal point and front facing contact for the organisation.\r\nWe are a small friendly group and any volunteers will be made most welcome.\r\nFor any further information on what is involved or required, please do not hesitate to contact for more information.\r\nSo, whether you are looking to use your time well, update your skills or have the chance to do something a bit new, we would love to hear from you. In return, we can offer you a warm welcome and all of the support and help you could need.\r\n\r\nWe are seeing a rise in demand for our services every day. Having your help will allow us to be there for the people who receive our service. Any time you can give will make a real difference.\n\n## Experience required\n\nSomeone with some clerical or secretarial knowledge or experience.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDumbarton\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses may be reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000006Yw4XYAS#role",
