                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityTransport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Transport"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BTGELYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BTGELYA5/knitting-and-crochet-tutor",
                    "publishStart": "2025-08-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Knitting and Crochet Tutor",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBased in the grounds of Linvale school - once a month\n\n## Description\n\nNo matter how good our services are, we can't properly support our users/community well if we don't have good organisers in the team. If this sounds like you... we would love you to consider volunteering with us for a few hours per week.\r\n\r\nDouble L centre is a community space run by volunteers for people in the Linvale area and beyond.\r\n\r\nThe purpose of this role will be to lead on supporting attendees to knit and crochet. There are varied activities also included in this role, this can include supporting the group with getting out materials, setting up tables, cleaning up after sessions, welcoming new members – showing them the kitchen/toilets/ materials etc.\r\n\r\nSo whether you are looking to use your time well, update your skills or have the chance to do something a bit new, we can offer you a warm welcome and all of the support and help you could need.\r\n\r\nWe are seeing a rise in demand for our services everyday. Having your help will allow us to be there for the people who need us. Any time you can give will make a real difference.\n\n## Experience required\n\nKnowledge and Knitting & crochet",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
