                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Epk7BYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Epk7BYAR/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe’re looking for caring, committed people to join our Board of Trustees. Whether you have skills in fundraising, marketing, or lived experience of the challenges families face, your voice matters. We’re particularly hoping to find a Vice Chair who can support our current Chair too. No trustee experience needed,  we’ll support you every step of the way.\r\n\r\nOur board meets on a monthly basis online, and you’ll help ensure families across the North East of Aberdeenshire can access the baby essentials they need. We welcome trustees from all backgrounds and walks of life. If this sounds like something you’d enjoy being part of, we’d love to hear from you. Download our trustee pack on our website at bairnecessities.co.uk or get in touch for an informal chat.\r\n\r\nPlease note, all of our trustees must reside in a AB41, AB42, AB43, AB44, AB45, AB51 or AB53 postcode area.\n\n## Training details\n\nIntroduction to the staff team and\r\nour work\r\nTrustee training and development\r\nopportunities\r\nSupport from experienced trustees",
