        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002iig6YAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002iig6YAAQ/empty-kitchens-full-hearts",
            "name": "Empty Kitchens Full Hearts",
            "description": "Empty Kitchens Full Hearts aims to relieve poverty in Edinburgh by providing healthy meals and follow-up support to people across the city. All our meals are made from surplus food, are free of charge and served without judgement. Since we began in April 2020,our volunteers have produced, packed and delivered more than 2 million meals to people who need them.",
            "website": "https://www.emptykitchens.co.uk",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FgZk4YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FgZk4YAF/welcome-desk-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-07-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Welcome Desk Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nIn order for people to access our delivery service, we require them to be ‘onboarded’, an essential task done by our Welcome Desk Volunteers.  These volunteers are also a big part of helping ensure that we provide a comfortable and friendly environment for our volunteers, staff and the people we support.\n\n## Description\n\nWhat follows is a brief list of the most common tasks; more detail will be provided when you come in to chat to us about the role.\nOnboarding new service users over the phone.\nUsing our task management system.\nWelcoming volunteers and visitors.\nChecking the phone for voicemails and messages. Ensuring the ‘welcome area’ of the office and the volunteer break areas are tidy and stocked. Organising the washing and drying of uniforms (chef whites). Cleaning duties. Sending volunteer communications.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will be expected to carry out a 6 week training programme (one day a week). Training would occur on a morning (9am-2pm) and on a Monday, Thursday or Friday.\nWe use Zendesk to manage tasks. You will be given full training on how to use it.\nSimilarly, Google mail, Drive and Calendar are used so some familiarity with this is helpful, though you will be trained how to use them.\n\n## Travel details\n\nYou can find us on 11 West Granton Road, Edinburgh, EH5 1HG. We are the old school building just off Granton Square. Bus routes: 8, 14, 16, 38, 47, 113, 17 Cycle: We have a bike shelter around the back of the building. Parking: On street free parking available.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nCompleting an online expenses form, or discussing with our finance officer. These will be paid over bank transfer.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FgZk4YAF#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Welcome Desk Volunteer",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FgZk4YAF/welcome-desk-volunteer?#modal_register_a0gQD00000FgZk4YAF",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "service": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Service/WheelchairAccessDisabledAccessToilet",
