        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002kW3SLAA0",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002kW3SLAA0/shelter-scotland",
            "name": "Shelter Scotland",
            "description": "Shelter Scotland help individuals struggling with bad housing or homelessness by providing support, advice, information and advocacy to people in housing need.. They exist to defend the right to a safe home and fight the devastating impact the housing emergency has on people and society. They do this with campaigns, advice and support – and we never give up. They believe that home is everything.",
            "website": "https://scotland.shelter.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC002327"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008rkh6AAA",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008rkh6AAA/cash-desk-telephone-operators",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-01",
                    "title": "Cash Desk & Telephone Operators",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nOur aim is to work with families who are homeless and give them practical help and emotional support to settle in a new tenancy. In particular, we work with families who have been homeless a few times, or where for some other reason they may find it difficult to settle in a new tenancy. Our shops help sustain the work we do and provides a helping hand for those suffering homelessness or badly housed situations.\n\n## Description\n\nWe require cash desk volunteers to help out within the Shelter Scotland shop by providing help with the following roles: Completing till transactions accurately and effectively; Completing delivery dockets and delivery slots; Accepting customer donations; Promoting the benefits of the Gift Aid Scheme\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Good Communicator,Good Listener,Hard Working,Organised,Reliable / Dependable,Trustworthy,\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nRutherglen",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
