                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GStpxYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GStpxYAD/volunteer-delivery-helper",
                    "publishStart": "2026-04-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-26",
                    "title": "Volunteer Delivery Helper",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nFood Train supports older people across Scotland to live healthier, more independent lives by improving access to food, reducing isolation, and promoting dignity in later life. Our vision is that every older person in Scotland has the access to nutritious food, compassionate support, and the social connections they need.\r\n\r\nFood Train is an award winning charity providing services to older people who are no longer able to manage independently, through age, ill health, frailty or disability. Helpers, along with the Drivers, collect prepared shopping orders from the shop and deliver to our customers.  Tasks involved in this role include:\r\n\r\n• Collecting shopping orders from shops\r\n• Stack van to ensure shopping boxes are secure\r\n• Deliver and unpack shopping orders for customers\r\n• Complete small amount of paperwork\r\n• Report any matters of concern to Food Train staff\r\n• To maintain confidentiality\r\n• Representing Food Train in a professional manner to customers and the wider community\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood literacy and numeracy skills.\r\nFriendly, sociable and patient with a caring manner.\r\nGood level of fitness, motivated, reliable, trustworthy and enthusiastic individual.\r\nGood communication and listening skills are needed as well as being a people person with a sense of humour.\n\n## Training details\n\nStaff will organise a taster day. \r\nTraining will be offered to support with the role - paperwork completion. \r\nVolunteers will be provided with a Volunteer Handbook and be invited to watch training videos. \r\nStaff will always be available to answer questions. \r\nA PVG will be organised. \r\nFurther training includes Dementia Awareness and any other relevant local training.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n6hrs – 9am to 3pm approximately\r\nTuesday, Wednesday or Thursday (number of days and commitment is flexible based on volunteer availability).\n\n## Travel details\n\nStart and End day at the Food Train office: Castlelaurie Works, Bankside Industrial Estate, Ironworks Business Centre, Falkirk, FK2 7XE.  There is also the option to start directly at nearby Asda or Morrisons supermarket within Falkirk.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are reimbursed.  45p per mile or any bus fare expenses.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F79d94654-779b-96e4-22be-ed4a90868031%2FXPrpz4zVmiRWRuGPAUiQ4SyLdVd2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=b7630f1d-97e8-4205-ad19-187161463bed",
