        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002fP41kAAC",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002fP41kAAC/youre-never-too-old",
            "name": "You're Never Too Old",
            "description": "We carry out stimulating and meaningful activities and outings Picking people up from their homes and bringing them together on a Monday and Tuesday to help improve their wellbeing and stop social isolation.",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000LRKi4AAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000LRKi4AAH/group-support",
                    "publishStart": "2020-02-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Group Support",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteers role – to support elderly people getting on and off transport, carrying out various activities, such as arts and crafts gentle exercise, board games, dominoes, quizzes, singing etc., going on outings. Help serving lunch and clearing up. Bringing your own skills to the group would also be welcomed.\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteers role – Passenger assisting by supporting elderly people to get on and off transport.  Carry out various activities, i.e.,  arts and crafts, gentle exercise, board games, dominoes, quizzes, singing, we do indoor bowling and Kurling we also go on outings. Help by serving lunch and clearing up. Bringing your own skills to the group would also be welcomed. The group is on a Monday and Tuesday, for passenger assist 9am-3pm, for group support 10am-2pm.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA dedicated volunteer, showing empathy, support old people on and off transport , have a cheery outlook on life, good communication skills, be willing to learn new skills and bring their own skills to the group. A volunteer wanting to make a difference to someone's life good social interaction skills\n\n## Training details\n\nA new volunteer will shadow someone until they feel confident in carrying out their role\n\n## Travel details\n\n72 Craigmount Brae, Laura Ferguson Court, Edinburgh EH12 8SF just across from the East Craigs bus terminus no.31. bus stop on Drum Brae  1, 21, 26 200\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses paid.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
