                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-27",
                    "title": "Volunteer Finance Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteer Finance Assistant\n\n## Description\n\nAbout Babayangu Foundation\n\nBabayangu Foundation supports children and young people from ethnic minority backgrounds, with a focus on mental health, wellbeing and strengthening relationships between families and communities.\n\nAbout the Opportunity\n\nDevelop your finance skills while helping a community charity make a difference.\n\nAre you studying finance, accounting, business or a related subject, or interested in gaining practical experience in charity finance?\n\nBabayangu Foundation is looking for a Volunteer Finance Assistant to support its Treasurer with a range of financial administration tasks.\n\nThis is an opportunity to gain hands-on experience in bookkeeping, budgeting and financial reporting while contributing to a charity supporting children, young people and families.\n\nYou&#39;ll receive training in Xero accounting software, work alongside the Treasurer and develop practical skills that could support your studies, career development or future employment.\n\nWhat You&#39;ll Be Doing\n\nWorking under the guidance of the Treasurer, you&#39;ll help with:\n\n\n\tRecording income and expenditure using Xero accounting software.\n\tChecking and organising financial records and supporting basic bookkeeping activities.\n\tAssisting with bank reconciliations and maintaining accurate financial information.\n\tHelping prepare financial summaries, reports and budget information.\n\tGathering financial information to support funding and grant applications.\n\tOrganising financial documents and maintaining appropriate records.\n\tSupporting the Treasurer with other agreed finance-related tasks.\n\n\nAll activities will be undertaken with appropriate guidance and oversight from the Treasurer, who retains responsibility for the charity&#39;s financial management and reporting.\n\nWho Would This Role Suit?\n\nThis opportunity would suit someone who:\n\n\n\tShares Babayangu Foundation&#39;s commitment to supporting children, young people and families.\n\tIs studying, or has an interest in, finance, accounting, economics, business or a related subject.\n\tEnjoys working with numbers and has good attention to detail.\n\tHas basic IT skills, particularly Microsoft Excel and Office applications.\n\tIs organised, reliable and comfortable handling information confidentially.\n\tIs willing to learn and follow guidance.\n\tCan work independently on agreed tasks while keeping in contact with the Treasurer.\n\n\nPrevious bookkeeping experience would be helpful but isn&#39;t essential, as training and guidance will be provided.\n\nTime, Commitment and Location\n\nLocation: Hybrid volunteering, combining home-based tasks with occasional in-person meetings.\n\nTime commitment: Approximately 4&ndash;8 hours per week, to be agreed around your availability.\n\nSuggested duration: Ideally 3&ndash;6 months, allowing time to develop your skills and contribute to the Foundation&#39;s activities.\n\nThe volunteering arrangements will be discussed and agreed with you, recognising the importance of flexibility around studies, work and other commitments.\n\nTraining and Support\n\nYou&#39;ll work alongside the Foundation&#39;s Treasurer, who will provide guidance and support throughout your volunteering.\n\nThis includes:\n\n\n\tTraining in Xero accounting software.\n\tGuidance on financial administration and bookkeeping tasks.\n\tSupport in understanding charity finance procedures.\n\tOpportunities to ask questions, receive feedback and develop your skills.\n\tRegular contact with the Treasurer, including support when volunteering remotely.\n\n\nWhat You&#39;ll Gain from Volunteering\n\nBy volunteering with Babayangu Foundation, you&#39;ll have opportunities to:\n\n\n\tGain practical experience in charity finance and financial administration.\n\tDevelop bookkeeping, budgeting and financial reporting skills.\n\tLearn to use Xero accounting software.\n\tBuild confidence using financial information and spreadsheets.\n\tGain insight into charity funding, grant management and governance.\n\tDevelop transferable skills to strengthen your CV and future employment prospects.\n\tMeet new people and become part of a friendly, community-focused team.\n\tParticipate in organised volunteer social activities and days out.\n\n\nYour contribution will help the Foundation organise its financial information and support the delivery of activities benefiting children, young people and families.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested in developing your finance skills while supporting a community charity?\n\nClick the Apply button below (available when logged in and registered with Volunteer Glasgow).\n\nYour application will be forwarded to Babayangu Foundation, who will contact you by email or telephone to discuss the opportunity and next steps.\n\nIf you haven&#39;t heard back within five working days, please contact the organisation using the contact details provided and check your email junk/spam folder.\n\nIf you&#39;re still unable to make contact, please email Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tGood numerical and analytical skills.\n•\tAttention to detail and accuracy.\n•\tBasic IT skills, particularly Microsoft Excel and Office.\n•\tGood organisational and time management skills.\n•\tAbility to work independently and as part of a team.\n•\tGood communication and interpersonal skills.\n•\tAbility to handle confidential information responsibly.\n•\tWillingness to learn bookkeeping and Xero accounting software.\n•\tInterest in finance, accounting or charity administration.\n•\tReliability, flex\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a hybrid volunteering opportunity, with most tasks undertaken from home and occasional in-person meetings. Travel arrangements and meeting locations will be agreed in advance with the organisation.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease check with Babayangu Foundation whether reasonable travel expenses for agreed in-person meetings and any other out-of-pocket volunteering expenses can be reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000J96HnYAJ#role",
