                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ISxPNYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ISxPNYA1/youth-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-30",
                    "title": "Youth Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nYouth Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nBaba Yangu supports children and young people from ethnic minority backgrounds, with a focus on mental health and on bridging the gap between families.\n\nAs a Youth Volunteer, you&rsquo;ll work with children across a range of ages, from quite young up to older children.\n\nOur programmes include group wellbeing sessions, mental health training and community workshops.\n\nYou&rsquo;ll be part of a friendly team, and we also organise days out for our volunteers. There are opportunities to progress into paid positions with us.\n\nClick the Apply button below (available when logged in and registered with Volunteer Glasgow). Your application will be passed to the Rainbow Friendship Centre, who will contact you by email or telephone to discuss the opportunity and next steps.\n\nIf you have not heard back within five working days, please contact the organisation using the contact details provided and check your email junk/spam folder. If you are still unable to make contact, please contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\n- Empathy and a caring, supportive approach with children and young people\n- Safeguarding or first aid training is welcome but not required\n- A PVG check is needed before you start, and we’ll guide you through the process\n\n## Travel details\n\nCentral location for students. Travel for volunteers can be reimbursed.",
