            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002h5G49AAE/1st-lerwick-rainbows-and-brownies",
            "name": "1st Lerwick Rainbows and Brownies",
            "description": "We empower girls to experience life-changing adventures to achieve their potential and to do their best.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HtFKnYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HtFKnYAN/rainbow-leaders-and-helpers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-11",
                    "title": "Rainbow Leaders and Helpers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGirlguiding Shetland is part of Girlguiding Scotland, the leading charity for girls and young women in Scotland. Girlguiding helps members discover their full potential by having fun and enjoying new adventures.\r\nAt the heart of Girlguiding are our regular group sessions, called unit meetings. These are run by volunteer teams of adult leaders, helpers, and young leaders.\r\n\r\nAs a helper, there's no responsibility for planning, but you'll be the extra pair of hands needed to make unit meetings happen. You can help behind the scenes with tasks like admin, or face to face with girls, helping with activities, crafts, adventures, and supporting them to reach their potential.\r\nNo two units are the same which means that all unit helpers do slightly different things.\r\nWe’re looking for volunteers in Lerwick to support unit meetings for our Rainbows group\r\nRainbows are aged 4-7 and focus on fun, friendship and adventure.\r\n\r\nOur unit meets on Tuesday evenings.\r\n\r\nregister online https://volunteer.girlguiding.org.uk/#/vacancydetail/shetland-division-h3iskny,\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou don’t need any experience to volunteer, just enthusiasm, a willingness to learn and to be friendly and welcoming. Our units are a safe space for our young members to express and challenge themselves.",
