        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002h5TOhAAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002h5TOhAAM/edinburgh-food-social",
            "name": "Edinburgh Food Social",
            "description": "Our goals are to:\nEnhance lives and improve health through learning about food.\nBuild confidence by giving people the skills and resources to provide for themselves and their families.\nProvide safe places for community meals and food events.\nNourish people by providing easier access to sources of good food.",
            "website": "https://edinburghfoodsocial.org/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0eazYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I0eazYAB/board-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-12",
                    "title": "Board Member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nMembers of the Board of EFS are also called the Directors of the organisation. They are responsible for the governance of EFS, including setting our strategic direction, overseeing our policies, employment practices, financial health and legal compliance, and promoting the organisation and its work.\n\nThe commitment is about 1-2 days per month, with Board members expected to attend meetings and follow up on their action points outside of these meetings.\n\nIn return, you get to be part of helping us help people across the city and creating the most effective organisation to ensure that everyone can access good food and knows what to do with it.\n\n## Experience required\n\nCommitment to the vision, mission and values of Edinburgh Food Social\nStrategic vision \nGood, independent judgement \nWillingness and ability to devote the necessary time and effort to carrying out the Director role effectively, including participating in Board meetings and conference calls in between meetings, scrutinising Board papers, and responding promptly to Board email discussions\nUnderstanding and acceptance of the legal duties, responsibilities and liabilities of Directorship, especially those set out in:\nEdinburgh Food Social’s Memorandum & Articles of Association\nGood working knowledge of Google Workspace\nAbility to think creatively \nWillingness to speak their mind \nAbility to work effectively as a member of a team \nCommitment to ongoing training and development\n\n## Training details\n\nNo specific training provided\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe commitment is about 1-2 days per month, with Board members expected to attend in person meetings and follow up on their action points outside of these meetings from home.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe commitment is about 1-2 days per month, with Board members expected to attend in person meetings in the Niddrie/Craigmillar area and follow up on their action points outside of these meetings from home.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nBoard membership is voluntary and unpaid. However, EFS can pay some pre-agreed expenses associated with being a Board member where needed.\n\n## Taster details\n\nPlease feel free to email admin@edinburghfoodsocial.org to arrange a chat.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FMrlH6QoMmghkl1aEkYYhLZ5oLPk1%2FF84torjmEPFOxBAa-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=553ef34b-2df4-4f9c-b351-7029d8e04d4d",
