        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002e3QuEAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002e3QuEAAU/scottish-spca",
            "name": "Scottish SPCA",
            "description": "As Scotland’s animal welfare charity, we’ve been on-hand to protect animals and prevent cruelty for 180 years. Over almost two centuries, we’ve grown to become a national charity which celebrates the strength of the human-animal bond and enriches the lives of animals and people.\r\n•\tWe champion animal welfare and encourage respect and kindness for animals across all our communities\r\n•\tWe educate people of all ages about the welfare of animals in our mission to eradicate\r\n•\tanimal cruelty and create a better future for all of us\r\n•\tWe promote the importance of the human/animal bond, and the myriad medical, social and psychological advantages gained from animal companionship\r\n•\tWe bring those who abuse animals to justice\r\n•\tWe care for, rescue, rehabilitate, release and rehome",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC006467"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AnimalWelfare",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Animal Welfare"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000F1FcIYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000F1FcIYAV/scottish-spca-micro-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-01-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Scottish SPCA Micro-volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCould you give up a small amount of your time to raise awareness of our work in your local community or to help us raise vital funds for Scotland's animals?\r\n\r\nThere are a variety of different tasks to choose from, and you can tailor your volunteering role around your current commitments, undertaking only the tasks that interest you. All we ask is that you commit 5 minutes each month to sharing links to our news, campaigns and events with your social network. You also have the option to get involved events in your local area should you be interested.\r\n\r\nThis role can be applied for via the SPCA website.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPassionate about animal welfare and the mission of the Society, access to social media and willingness to share posts with your network.\n\n## Training details\n\nFollowing the application process, new volunteers are required to complete some online training relevant to their role. The will then receive a full induction and practial training & support from our team.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a home-based role, involving social media with the option to get involved in events in your local area. You can pick and choose which events suit you in terms of timing and travel.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses - 45p per mile for fuel, up to max of 30 miles per day or equivalent public transport costs. Paid fortnightly directly to your bank account.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000F1FcIYAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Scottish SPCA Micro-volunteer",
