                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000F1HqzYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000F1HqzYAF/fundraising-engagement-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-01-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Fundraising & Engagement Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCould you give up a small amount of your time to raise awareness of our work in your local community or to help us raise vital funds for Scotland's animals?\r\n\r\nThere are a variety of different tasks to choose from, and you can tailor your volunteering role around your current commitments, undertaking only the tasks that interest you. All we ask is that you commit to helping with 2 events per year.\r\n\r\nOur friendly and active team will look after you well! You will be given a full induction and training and can claim expenses for your fuel costs when volunteering.\r\n\r\nThis role can be applied for via the SPCA website.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPassionate about animal welfare and the mission of the Society, confident to speak to the public at events, punctual and reliable.\n\n## Training details\n\nFollowing the application process, new volunteers are required to complete some online training relevant to their role. The will then receive a full induction and practial training & support from our team.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe will contact you about events in your local area. You can pick and choose which events suit you in terms of timing and travel.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n45p per mile for fuel, up to max of 30 miles per day or equivalent public transport costs. Paid fortnightly directly to your bank account.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
