        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002fOAY6AAO",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002fOAY6AAO/heart-of-newhaven-community-scio",
            "name": "Heart of Newhaven Community SCIO",
            "description": "The advancement of community development principally within the Community;\nthe advancement of education and social welfare principally within the Community\nthe provision of recreational facilities principally within the Community",
            "website": "https://heartofnewhaven.co.uk/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pv9MYAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pv9MYAAZ/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2021-07-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThree new trustees with business or management experience to aid a community-led charity.\n\n## Description\n\nDo you have a passion for our local community and a desire to share your skills with us? Do you live within our area of benefit? Would you like to help us to sustain this valuable community resource? Since taking ownership of \"The Heart\" , the previous Victoria primary school, in 2022, we have made leaps and bounds in transforming our vision for the building into reality. We are now recruiting for some new trustees to help our small dedicated team of staff and volunteers continue this work. Our vision is to turn The Heart into a sustainable place for inspiration, exploration and enjoyment where the aim is to enrich lives through active, inter-generational learning and discovery.\nhttps://heartofnewhaven.co.uk/\n\n## Experience required\n\nExperience in Finance or HR would be particularly useful, but a background in business, charity management, building maintenance and/or fund-raising would also be very welcome.\n\n## Training details\n\nNew trustees will be given the opportunity to attend Board meetings as observers prior to committing to the role. Current board members will provide support and mentoring and an induction pack will be provided.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVictoria Primary School Newhaven, Edinburgh. Trustees should live locally.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
