        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXKhAAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXKhAAM/growbiz-enterprising-eastern-perthshire",
            "name": "Growbiz (Enterprising Eastern Perthshire)",
            "description": "Community-based enterprise support service covering Eastern and Highland Perthshire. \nWe provide support to anyone thinking of becoming self-employed, or starting (or growing) a small bYou will find a range of services including: one to one meetings with our enterprise co-ordinator, peer support, specialist advices from the GrowBiz Panel, mentoring and training. \nTypes of support vsary from business to business but can include personal development, business planning, identifying training needs and helping you access resources from providers like Business Gateway.\nAs well as being friendly and approachable, all of our services are free and confidential.\nusiness or social enterprise. There is no age limit either upper or lower, and we work right across the community including people from all backgrounds, and those with health issues or disabilities. \n\nYou will find a range of services including: one to one meetings with our enterprise co-ordinator, peer support, specialist advices from the GrowBiz Panel, mentoring and training. \nTypes of support vsary from business to business but can include personal development, business planning, identifying training needs and helping you access resources from providers like Business Gateway.\nAs well as being friendly and approachable, all of our services are free and confidential.",
            "website": "http://www.growbiz.co.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC043278"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SocialEconomySocialEnterprise",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Social Economy / Social Enterprise"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IRWZKYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IRWZKYA5/trusteedirector",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-11",
                    "title": "Trustee/Director",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nPosition(s) available to join energetic Board in providing oversight and governance for this unique, nationally recognised, accredited and client focused business support charity. A healthy and vibrant rural economy is essential for Scotland’s future. The heartbeat of the rural economy are the self-employed, micro/small businesses and start up entrepreneurs who form the majority of GrowBiz clients. GrowBiz provides free services covering mentors, enterprise facilitators as well as online line training and network building events.\nIf you feel you have the skills and business and/or Board experience to add to our team of Trustees and help guide GrowBiz towards it progressive future we would like to hear from you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nExperience - small businesses, charity, business support, Board.\nSkills - in any of Legal, Finance and Accounting, Governance, IT or Public Relations\n\n## Training details\n\nOther than an induction to the organisation and regular Trustee training the expectation is that you will have the necessary knowledge and expertise to contribute to our Board.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe Board meets every two months. Occasionally there is the need for ad hoc meetings. These are generally conducted online.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMeetings are held both in person and by video. The in person meetings are held in the Perth area and happen 3/4 times a year.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses are covered\n\n## Taster details\n\nAn opportunity to see the Board at work will be available before any appointment.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FnJuLgq3tyHdry3C6egswaeHHGwj2%2Fr9XzBq48x6VanAkN-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=b6652f52-d728-45c7-9741-16e1409b6f42",
