        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXNJAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXNJAA2/orkney-district-scouts",
            "name": "Orkney District Scouts",
            "description": "Orkney has several Scout groups, including the registered 2nd Orkney (Kirkwall) and 11th Orkney (West Mainland) groups, as well as the 5th Orkney (South Ronaldsay & Burray) group and the John Rae Explorer Unit which covers the entire district. These groups offer activities like camping, hiking, and water sports, catering to young people aged 6 to 18 and are supported by volunteers. The 2nd Orkney group in Kirkwall, for example, has Beaver, Cub, and Scout sections meeting at the Scout Hall on Junction Road.",
            "website": "https://www.orkneyscouts.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC033345"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ICKdJYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ICKdJYAX/team-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-30",
                    "title": "Team Member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe 2nd Orkney (Kirkwall) Scouts are looking for new Team Members to help support and run their groups. \r\n\r\nTeam Members are volunteers who plan, deliver, and support an amazing programme for young people.\r\n\r\nThey can volunteer flexibly. Some may give their time every week, while others may give as much or as little time as they want.\r\n\r\nWhat could a volunteer gain from the experience:\r\nHaving easy, fun, and accessible learning opportunities, so they can gain knowledge on how to volunteer with young people and adults in a safe and inclusive way, develop various skills through volunteering, and grow in confidence.\n\n## Experience required\n\n-Effective Communication: The ability to explain tasks clearly to young people and collaborate smoothly with other adult leaders.\r\n-Activity Planning & Organisation: Helping design programs, manage time, and keep track of resources for weekly meetings or camps.\r\n-Safety & Risk Awareness: Keeping a sharp eye on safety procedures, safeguarding practices, and basic first aid.\r\n-Positive & Inclusive: Bringing an encouraging, patient, and welcoming energy so that every young person feels included.\r\n-Resilient & Flexible: Being able to smile and pivot to a backup plan when an outdoor activity gets rained out or things don't go perfectly.\r\n-Servant Leadership: A willingness to guide and mentor young people to help them build \"skills for life\" rather than just dictating rules.\r\n\r\nNo formal prior background in scouting is typically required, as full training is provided. Any transferable experience working with children, volunteering in the community or handling basic admin is highly desirable.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll training with the exception of First Aid is completed online, it's is in simple modules that has online support built in. Completing wood badges are optional.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n1-2 hours a week, on a Friday Evening.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable out-of-pocket expenses are reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F7cbf4a65-d63e-4a6a-92d2-37e3f4d21327%2FRvwxG9uqoDbW7EgdeOrBT3kav1g1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=47148dbd-e4f6-4c9a-af36-1d7fd9064b22",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ICKdJYAX#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Team Member",
                        "description": "-Effective Communication: The ability to explain tasks clearly to young people and collaborate smoothly with other adult leaders.\r\n-Activity Planning & Organisation: Helping design programs, manage time, and keep track of resources for weekly meetings or camps.\r\n-Safety & Risk Awareness: Keeping a sharp eye on safety procedures, safeguarding practices, and basic first aid.\r\n-Positive & Inclusive: Bringing an encouraging, patient, and welcoming energy so that every young person feels included.\r\n-Resilient & Flexible: Being able to smile and pivot to a backup plan when an outdoor activity gets rained out or things don't go perfectly.\r\n-Servant Leadership: A willingness to guide and mentor young people to help them build \"skills for life\" rather than just dictating rules.\r\n\r\nNo formal prior background in scouting is typically required, as full training is provided. Any transferable experience working with children, volunteering in the community or handling basic admin is highly desirable.",
