        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002ZiddBAAR",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002ZiddBAAR/guide-dogs",
            "name": "Guide Dogs",
            "description": "Over the years we’ve developed a wide range of services with and without dogs to support people living with a vision impairment. Children and adults. Friends and family. Whoever you are, our expert staff, dedicated volunteers and life-changing dogs are here to help you live actively, independently, and well.\r\n\r\nWe’re a charity, almost entirely funded by donations, and we are the world’s largest assistance dog organisation. As world leaders in puppy socialisation and dog training, we’re the only organisation to breed and train guide dogs in the UK. We’re also the largest employer of specialists dedicated to helping children and young people overcome the challenges of sight loss.",
            "website": "https://www.guidedogs.org.uk/volunteer",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038979"
                }
            ],
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2F5b9b3cf2-049e-03ed-8b4a-a3e52250a1eb%2FmQsKXYYIupgt1ub9BeDSGFfo1O33%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=5c773a3b-d6d9-420f-8bfb-af5a6805a9c5",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SensoryImpairment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000AjXrhYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000AjXrhYAF/deputy-fundraising-group-co-ordinator-east-ren",
                    "publishStart": "2025-07-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-28",
                    "title": "Deputy Fundraising Group Co-ordinator (East Ren)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCould you help support a team of volunteer fundraisers in your local area to get things done as the Deputy Fundraising Group Co-ordinator?\r\n\r\nThe Deputy Fundraising Group Co-ordinator role can make all the difference and help your group smash their goal!  You can chat with the Fundraising Group Co-ordinator about how you share the role and what areas you both can concentrate on.\r\n\r\nYou can help by:\r\n\r\n* Building lasting partnerships with the fundraising groups and your local community, inspiring people to get involved and have fun\r\n* Bringing your own ideas and personality to the group, the more great minds that we get together the better plans we can make\r\n* Working with the Fundraising Group Co-ordinator to share the organisation between you; this is all about working to you and your group’s strengths\r\n* Leading the fundraising group when the Group Co-ordinator is away\r\n* Talking to local businesses and identifying places that can host and get involved in events, bringing these suggestions to the group and working together to make these plans a reality\r\n* Championing Guide Dogs and our work, sharing our stories in your local community\r\n* Inspiring more volunteers to join Guide Dogs and become fundraising volunteers\n\n## Travel details\n\nAcross Glasgow, East Renfrewshire, Renfrewshire or Ayrshire, on discussion with volunteer",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F6478fcd8-c2b0-4e7e-bbfb-b1b985ce0c2f%2FEjZvvKGWRXNe0jtznRGKObRZWCg2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=1f768e7a-8ac9-4d57-9b9a-a0a9e2869372",
