        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002b5eeoAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002b5eeoAAA/polwarth-parish-church",
            "name": "Polwarth Parish Church",
            "description": "Polwarth Parish Church is a place of wholeness and wellbeing. We provide a safe place for people to meet. A place where people can come on their own or with friends. We are mindful of issues of isolation and loneliness and welcome everyone, offering sensitivity, a listening ear and good hospitality.",
            "website": "https://polwarth.org.uk",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Sbqb3AAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Sbqb3AAB/cafe-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2022-06-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Cafe Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCommunity Cafe Volunteer. Catering Assistant wanted for Polwarth Parish Church Pop Up Cafe. General catering duties required but the main aim is to create a safe and welcoming space. Our hope is to create a community hub and within this space offer digital skills to those excluded from online activities.\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteers wanted for Polwarth Pop Up Café. The role includes welcoming customers, serving pre-made food, hot drinks, clearing tables, taking payments, help to tidy away and return hall ready for other users. We are open Tues mornings with volunteers forming small teams rotating every week. Our aim is to meet members of the community, creating a safe space to come to on your own or with friends. Mindfull of isolation and loneliness, we will offer sensitivity, a listening ear and good hospitality.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEssential - good time keeping, reliable, can work as part of a team, ability to adapt to different duties and  help other volunteers if required. Interpersonal skills - someone who is friendly and approachable and enjoys working with people.\nDesirable - confident when handling cash.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training will include an overview of the building and a conversation with our Health and Safety Officer. There will be a check list of duties and verbal and written food handling guidance. Ongoing training will involve working with the wellbeing director looking at community development aspects of the Pop Up Cafe. For those who are interested an opportunity to gain REHIS Elementary Food Hygiene Certificate.\n\n## Travel details\n\nPolwarth Parish Church, 36-38 Polwarth Terrace, Edinburgh, EH11 1 LU. Buses number 10 and 27 stop outside the church. On street parking which you must pay for.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThe claims form would be completed and emailed to our Treasurer.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
