                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hvmu9YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hvmu9YAB/scotlands-gardens-scheme-media-volunteer-edinburgh-district-including-midlothian-and-west-lothian",
                    "publishStart": "2026-04-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Scotland's Gardens Scheme - Media Volunteer Edinburgh district (including Midlothian and West Lothian)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nScotland’s Gardens Scheme is Scotland’s growing, giving and inspiring community of garden-lovers. Our mission is to raise funds for charity by encouraging, promoting and supporting garden openings, whilst making the experience inspiring, rewarding and enjoyable for all. \r\n\r\nWe are seeking a new Media Volunteer to support our Edinburgh gardens which open for charity by promoting their open garden days effectively through the medium of social media, helping to support gardens to open their gates to the public and raise money for charity. This is a wonderful opportunity to: \r\n\r\n· Be part of a volunteer team which helps to raise funds for hundreds of charities by sharing gardens with visitors \r\n\r\n· Use your skills to help promote and/or support gardens to open their gates to the public and raise money for charity \r\n\r\n· Meet lovely, like-minded people and share the joy of gardens and gardening \r\n\r\nWe have a variety of other opportunities to match your interests and availability, including event volunteers, district organiser, area organiser and treasurer roles in different parts of Scotland.  Visit our website for full details and to fill in our expression of interest form.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFor some roles it may be helpful to be comfortable with IT and have numeracy skills but training will be provided.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe hold regular online welcome events for new volunteers and offer training via zoom or in person for specific activities such as using our database; ongoing support is also available from our Head Office team.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nAveraging between 1 - 4 hours per week, depending on opportunities and location.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Media Volunteer role can be carried out from home. there may be occasional district gatherings which they would be encouraged to attend and, if the roleh holder is keen to visit gardens, then travel to those would be required.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
