            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000J8q4vYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000J8q4vYAB/treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-29",
                    "title": "Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHow would you like to be part of an organisation which makes a difference to the lives of young people in Cardenden by giving them the opportunity to experience new things and develop new skills, supporting them for the future? 4th Cardenden Scout Group play a valuable role in the local Cardenden community giving young people new experiences and helping them to thrive.\r\n\r\nThe Group currently support 35 local young people and they require a Treasurer. As a Treasurer you will assist with the financial aspects of the Group including checking monthly subscription payments, supporting with the financial elements of events, banking, updating spreadsheets and keeping accurate financial records, preparing Board reports and attending Board meetings. This is rewarding role which has a huge impact on young people.\r\n\r\nIf you enjoy working with figures, want to give something back and make a meaningful contribution to the Cardenden community they would love to hear from you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience is required as full training will be provided for the role. The volunteer needs to enjoy working with figures, be comfortable using spreadsheets and have good communication and organisational skills\n\n## Training details\n\nA full induction and ongoing training will be provided. The volunteer will be required to complete training on safeguarding, health and safety, Data Protection (GDPR) and the role and responsibilities of a trustee. A PVG is also required for this role.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoard meetings are held every 2 – 3 months in the Scout Hall, Orebank Road, Cardenden, KY5 0JW\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReimbursement of expenses will be considered on a case by case basis.",
