        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008ndRHAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008ndRHAAY/glenrothes-foodbank",
            "name": "Glenrothes Foodbank",
            "description": "Foodbank, supplying emergency food and support for people in crisis",
            "website": "https://www.glenrothes.foodbank.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC045445"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Poverty",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Poverty"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Foodbanks",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Foodbanks"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000GvcwVAAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000GvcwVAAR/van-driver",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-01",
                    "title": "Van Driver",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nVolunteers are the life and blood of Foodbanks, your qualities could be just what they need.\r\nAs the demand for support continues to rise, Glenrothes Foodbank are looking for Van Drivers on a Monday from 8:30am -10am and 11.30am - 3pm, Wednesday 11.30am - 5pm and a Friday between 8.30am - 10am and 11.30am-3pm. \r\n\r\nThe Foodbank have their own van and the volunteers would use this to deliver food parcels and pick up donations from community centres, supermarkets, schools etc all around Glenrothes.\r\n\r\nDrivers should be aged at least 25 (due to insurance), be able to lift and move multiple boxes of donations and have a friendly and respectful manner with people receiving a service or making donations. You will usually be volunteering with a helper, sometimes alone, after an initial period of training and support with another volunteer/staff member.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers should have a clean driving license and be able to lift multiple boxes. You should also be willing to be part of a team and take part in training provided, as well as having a friendly and respectful manner to people receiving or donating to the service\n\n## Training details\n\nThere are various volunteer polices and procedures that you will be made aware of as part of your induction. You will also be asked to complete online Manual Handling Training.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased at the Saltire Centre, Glenrothes KY6 2AQ with travel throughout the wider Glenrothes area during the volunteering, in Foodbank vehicles.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPre-agreed travel expenses will be reimbursed.",
