        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008ndWVAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008ndWVAAY/live-borders",
            "name": "Live Borders",
            "description": "Live Borders is a charitable company limited by guarantee with a clear vision to make our communities HEALTHIER, HAPPIER and STRONGER\r\nLive Borders offer residents and visitors to the Scottish Borders a wealth of services that inspire positive lifestyle choices through the use of our libraries, community sports centres, museums and galleries, archives, country park and community venues. Every penny spent with Live Borders is reinvested into supporting active, creative and healthy communities in the Scottish Borders.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Heritage",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Heritage"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hkz57YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hkz57YAB/bsle-non-executive-director",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-11",
                    "title": "BSLE Non-Executive Director",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWho are we?\r\n\r\nBorders Sport and Leisure Enterprises (BSLE) (SC244374) is the trading subsidiary of Live Borders, a registered charity (SC034227), and which supports the charitable goals and endeavours of the Trust. The commercial activities such as cafes, cinema and retail which we undertake are accounted for within BSLE. \r\n\r\nYou will play an important part in leading and governing the company, working with like-minded people who have a passion for our values and are fully committed to this leadership role.\r\nIdeally you will have knowledge of Live Borders services across the Scottish Borders and Live Borders services (as a user).\r\n\r\n\r\nThe role\r\n\r\nThis unpaid non-executive role is an opportunity to make a real difference to the lives of those living in and visiting the Scottish Borders by supporting the commercial trading arm of the Live Borders charitable trust. \r\n\r\nThe successful candidate will be expected to attend two board meetings per year with an additional AGM, and contribute to decision making and governance processes.  \r\n\r\nOur ideal candidate will currently have experience of one of the following professional disciplines:\r\n\r\n•\tHospitality \r\n•\tFinance & Accountancy\r\n•\tBusiness Development\r\n•\tGovernance\r\n•\tMarketing and Commercial Development\r\n•\tPerformance, Scrutiny and Review\n\n## Experience required\n\nIdeally the candidate will have experience of: \r\n•\tWorking as a Board Member/Trustee and /or company Director \r\n•\tWorking in commerce and business \r\n•\tWorking with Charity Boards or committees as a member or advisor\r\n•\tLive Borders services (as a user)\r\nWith experience either:\r\n•\tThe legal duties, responsibilities and liabilities of being a non-executive director\r\n•\tCharitable and company law and the role of a Border Member/Trustee \r\n•\tEffective business management\r\n•\tFinancial planning and monitoring\r\n\r\nAnd:\r\n•\tExcellent communication skills (verbal, non-verbal and listening)\r\n•\tWillingness to devote additional time and effort to the role as required\r\n•\tExcellent business acumen, leadership and advocacy\r\n•\tGood independent judgement, political impartiality and the ability to think creatively in the context of the organisation and external environment\r\n•\tBalancing tact and diplomacy with willingness to challenge and constructively criticise\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive a short induction to introduce them to the role. Live Borders officers will provide ongoing volunteer support.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe process\r\n\r\nIf you are interested in being considered for this role, please upload an expression of interest highlighting why you would be a good fit for the role. https://liveborders.bamboohr.com/careers/184\r\n\r\n\r\nIf you would like further information, please contact Recruitment@liveborders.org.uk and we can arrange for a discussion with our Head of Finance and Business Services, who sits on the Board.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hkz57YAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "BSLE Non-Executive Director",
                        "description": "Ideally the candidate will have experience of: \r\n•\tWorking as a Board Member/Trustee and /or company Director \r\n•\tWorking in commerce and business \r\n•\tWorking with Charity Boards or committees as a member or advisor\r\n•\tLive Borders services (as a user)\r\nWith experience either:\r\n•\tThe legal duties, responsibilities and liabilities of being a non-executive director\r\n•\tCharitable and company law and the role of a Border Member/Trustee \r\n•\tEffective business management\r\n•\tFinancial planning and monitoring\r\n\r\nAnd:\r\n•\tExcellent communication skills (verbal, non-verbal and listening)\r\n•\tWillingness to devote additional time and effort to the role as required\r\n•\tExcellent business acumen, leadership and advocacy\r\n•\tGood independent judgement, political impartiality and the ability to think creatively in the context of the organisation and external environment\r\n•\tBalancing tact and diplomacy with willingness to challenge and constructively criticise",
                        "applyLink": "https://www.liveborders.org.uk/",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": true,
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/LocalAuthority",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Local Authority"
                            }
                        ],
                        "specialistRole": [
