        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008ndaNAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008ndaNAAQ/guide-dogs-for-the-blind-association",
            "name": "Guide Dogs for the Blind Association",
            "description": "To provide guide dogs and other rehabilitation services that meet the needs of the blind and partially sighted people.  Guide dogs want a world in which all people who are blind and partially sighted to enjoy the same rights, opportunities and responsibilities as everyone else.",
            "website": "https://www.guidedogs.org.uk/scotland",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038979"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009TXt4YAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009TXt4YAG/collection-box-coordinator",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Collection Box Coordinator",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nIf you love getting out and about but also want to support a cause in achieving it’s aim, then becoming a Collection Box Coordinator could be the right step for you. You will be involved in displaying our iconic collection boxes in your local community to help raise funds for Guide Dogs.\r\n\r\nIn this community-spirited volunteer role, your support will include getting involved in these activities:\r\n\r\nGetting out and about to display our iconic collection boxes in your local community.\r\nEmptying and banking funds in the collection boxes, meaning you can see how much money you have helped us raise.\r\nNetworking with organisations to share our cause and encourage them to display our collection boxes.\r\nBeing an ambassador for Guide Dogs!\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication skills to spread the word about Guide Dogs.\r\nGood organisational skills to organise distribution of collection boxes.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009TXt4YAG#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Collection Box Coordinator",
                        "description": "Good communication skills to spread the word about Guide Dogs.\r\nGood organisational skills to organise distribution of collection boxes.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009TXt4YAG/collection-box-coordinator?#modal_register_a0gQD000009TXt4YAG",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/LocalAuthority/NorthAyrshire",
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "North Ayrshire"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000CNEF5AAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000CNEF5AAP/fundraiser-north-ayrshire",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Fundraiser (North Ayrshire)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWhat does the role involve?\r\nYou will have the chance to take part in some or all of the following:\r\n•\tStreet collections on ‘flag’ days\r\n•\tHelp on stalls at local events\r\n•\tTake Collection Boxes to local businesses\r\n•\tAttending local events organised by Branches or Community Fundraiser and keeping track of what we sell on our stalls (including the cuddly toys!)\r\n•\tCount donations\r\n•\tFundraisers are usually members of the local fundraising group\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tGood communication skills\r\n•\tWorking as part of a team\n\n## Training details\n\n•\tRegular and ongoing support from your branch and Guide Dogs\r\n•\tPayment of out of pocket expenses\n\n## Travel details\n\nLocal, often outdoors",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
