            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JhKgUYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JhKgUYAV/secretary-board-of-trustees-for-ferryhill-community-centre",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-03",
                    "title": "Secretary - Board of Trustees for Ferryhill Community Centre",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nJoin the  Board of Trustees all volunteers: responsible for ensuring the Centre is well run, financially stable and serving community needs. Meetings on the last Tuesday of the month at 6.30 at Centre. Board members:\r\n\r\n· Read the constitution – ask questions if you don’t understand it\r\n· Comply with OSCR requirements regarding the duties of trustees\r\n· Help to organise group activities\r\n· Prepare for meetings by reading papers, relevant emails etc\r\n· Contribute to groups collective decision for the good of Ferryhill Community Centre\r\n· Take joint responsibility for the activities and decisions of the committee\r\n· Support the Chairperson, other office bearers and the work of the committee\r\n· Read all policy documents relevant to Ferryhill Community Centre\r\n· Keep up to date with what is going on that might help the Centre\r\n· Tell other people about the Centre and encourage new members to join.\r\n\r\nSpecific Chair duties:\r\n· Plan and chair meetings effectively\r\n· Ensure everyone has the chance to speak\r\n· Make sure people do the things they agreed to do at meetings\r\n· Be a leader and public face of the organisation\r\n· Be fair and open in all dealings\r\n· Cheque signatory.\r\n\r\nA great opportunity to make a difference for people and the community. We are a warm, welcoming and supportive team, provide important activities for the community and all help is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact William Rae, Chair at email: fcccommittee@ferryhillcommunitycentre.org.uk or telephone: 01224 584118\r\n\r\nMore information about Ferryhill Community Centre is also available at https://ferryhillcommunitycentre.org.uk/\n\n## Description\n\nJoin the Board of Trustees- volunteers who ensure the Centre is well run , financially stable and meets the needs of the community in Ferryhill.  \r\n\r\nThe Centre  provides a range of activities including a school breakfast club, sports and exercise classes and recreational activities. It also runs a thriving cafe which serves drinks and snacks throughout the week. \r\n\r\nWe  are currently seeking a secretary for our Board of Trustees. Duties include : \r\n\r\n· Plan meetings, agree agenda etc with the Chairperson\r\n· Book and prepare rooms for meetings\r\n· Let everyone know when and where meetings are well in advance\r\n· Send members the agenda, the minutes of the last meeting and any relevant reports etc\r\n· Ensure that everyone receives the information they need to make decisions\r\n· Complete and circulate meeting minutes\r\n· Keep and share information you find out which might be useful for the group\r\n· Keep the register of Trustees and the Register of Members up to date\r\n· Provide relevant information to members of the public should they request it\r\n· Coordinate OSCR (Office of the Scottish Charity Regulator) Annual Returns and ensure this are correct and completed on time\r\n\r\nA great opportunity to make a difference for people and the community. We are a warm, welcoming and supportive team, provide important activities for the community and all help is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact William Rae, Chair at email: fcccommittee@ferryhillcommunitycentre.org.uk or telephone: 01224 584118\r\n\r\nMore information about Ferryhill Community Centre is also available at https://ferryhillcommunitycentre.org.uk/\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMeetings are on the last Tuesday of the month at 6.30pm. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nFerryhill Community Centre, Albury Road,  Aberdeen AB11 6TN\r\n\r\nNear bus routes in Aberdeen city centre,  parking available",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F6a5b82fd-c380-4272-baba-3ca442b31f02%2FmqUkJgEPQEWkHKxngocCJ4ObI7f2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=0f72c114-7ac1-47c9-991b-6d0171ea185c",
