                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I3eOLYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I3eOLYAZ/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-23",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nStable Life is looking for new Trustees to help shape the future of our charity and support our work improving the wellbeing, confidence and life chances of children and young people through our unique equine-based service. We are particularly interested in people who can bring new skills, experience, ideas and perspectives to our Board and who are passionate about making a positive difference in the Scottish Borders.\n\n## Description\n\nStable Life is looking for new Trustees to join our Board and help shape the future of an established and respected Scottish Borders charity.\r\n\r\nStable Life supports children and young people who are experiencing difficulties or disadvantage, using our unique equine environment and Equine Facilitated Wellness approach to help build confidence, resilience, wellbeing, life skills and positive relationships. We are continuing to develop as a Wellbeing and Education Centre, expanding the opportunities we can offer young people and strengthening the sustainability of the charity for the future.\r\n\r\nAs a Trustee, you will be part of the Board responsible for providing strategic leadership, oversight and good governance. You will work alongside the Chief Executive and fellow Trustees to ensure Stable Life remains well governed, financially sustainable and focused on achieving the best possible outcomes for the children and young people we support.\r\n\r\nThe role includes:\r\n\r\n* Attending monthly Board meetings.\r\n* Contributing to strategic discussions and helping shape Stable Life’s future direction and development.\r\n* Providing appropriate oversight of the charity’s finances, governance, safeguarding, risk and organisational responsibilities.\r\n* Bringing your own knowledge, skills, experience and perspective to the Board.\r\n* Supporting the Chief Executive and Board where appropriate.\r\n* Helping Stable Life build relationships, raise its profile and identify opportunities for partnership, funding and development.\r\n* Acting in the best interests of Stable Life and the children, young people and families we support.\r\n\r\nWe are particularly keen to hear from people who can bring skills or experience that will complement our existing Board. This could include finance, fundraising, business or commercial experience, HR, education, governance, legal knowledge, communications, marketing, community development, experience of working with children and young people or experience of working with horses. We are also interested in people who can bring different perspectives, networks, lived experience or simply a strong commitment to our purpose.\r\n\r\nYou do not need previous Trustee experience, as support and induction will be provided. What matters most is a willingness to contribute, ask questions, listen, work collaboratively and share your skills and perspective.\r\n\r\nThis is a voluntary role, although reasonable out-of-pocket expenses can be reimbursed. Trustees can expect to gain experience of charity governance and strategic leadership while making a meaningful contribution to a small charity with a strong local impact.\r\n\r\nWe welcome applications from people from a wide range of backgrounds and particularly encourage anyone who feels they have something valuable to contribute to get in touch and find out more.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for people who are passionate about Stable Life’s purpose and want to use their skills, experience and perspective to help the charity develop and grow.\r\n\r\nPrevious Trustee or Board experience is not essential, and full induction and support will be provided.\r\n\r\nWe would particularly welcome people with experience or knowledge in one or more of the following areas:\r\n\r\n* Charity governance, leadership or strategic planning\r\n* Finance, accounting or financial management\r\n* Fundraising, income generation or bid writing\r\n* Business, commercial or organisational development\r\n* Human resources, employment or people management\r\n* Health and safety, risk management or compliance\r\n* Education, youth work, social care or working with children and young people\r\n* Marketing, communications or public relations\r\n* Community development or partnership working\r\n* Legal knowledge or experience\r\n* Equine, rural or agricultural experience\r\n* Experience of the Scottish Borders community and local networks\r\n\r\nThere are no specific qualifications required to become a Trustee, and we welcome enquiries from people who may be new to trusteeship but feel they have something valuable to contribute.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are also keen to hear from people who can bring different perspectives, skills, networks or lived experience that could benefit Stable Life.\r\n\r\nMost importantly, we are looking for people who are willing to contribute constructively, ask questions, listen to others, work collaboratively and act in the best interests of the charity and the children and young people we support.\r\n\r\nThere are no specific qualifications required to become a Trustee, and we welcome enquiries from people who may be new to trusteeship but feel they have something valuable to contribute\n\n## Training details\n\nFull induction and ongoing support will be provided to all new Trustees.\r\n\r\nAs part of the induction, Trustees will have the opportunity to learn more about Stable Life, our history, purpose, services, governance and future plans, as well as meeting staff and gaining an understanding of the work we do with children and young people.\r\n\r\nTrustees may also be asked to complete other relevant training or checks appropriate to their role and responsibilities. Full induction and support will be provided.\r\n\r\nThere are no specific physical requirements for the role, and previous experience of working with horses is not required.\r\n\r\nStable Life holds appropriate insurance cover for its activities, staff, volunteers and Trustees. This includes Public Liability Insurance, Employers’ Liability Insurance, Activities Insurance and Management Liability Insurance.\r\n\r\nVolunteers, including Trustees, are covered by the organisation’s insurance arrangements when carrying out agreed volunteering activities and Trustee duties on behalf of Stable Life, subject to the terms and conditions of the relevant policies.\r\n\r\nVolunteers and Trustees are expected to follow Stable Life’s policies, procedures and reasonable instructions while carrying out their role. Further information about our insurance cover and any specific circumstances or activities can be discussed as part of the induction process.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n•\tEach Trustee will have a named contact within Stable Life, with support available throughout their time as a volunteer.\r\n\r\n•\tTrustees can contact the Chief Executive or Chair whenever they have questions or need advice, with more regular contact around Board meetings and during their induction.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n•\tSupport is flexible and tailored to the individual. New Trustees will be supported to understand their role and responsibilities and will have opportunities to ask questions and discuss anything they are unsure about.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n•\tOur yard and meeting facilities have wheelchair/disabled access and an accessible toilet. We are happy to discuss any additional accessibility or support requirements with volunteers in advance.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoard meetings and Trustee activities take place at Stable Life’s yard in the Scottish Borders, in a rural location.\r\n\r\nTrustees will generally be expected to make their own travel arrangements to attend meetings and any other activities they choose to participate in. The rural location means that access by car is generally the easiest option, although we are happy to discuss individual travel or accessibility requirements.\r\n\r\nWhere appropriate, some meetings or discussions may be able to take place remotely, depending on the purpose and circumstances.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable and necessary expenses incurred while carrying out volunteering duties, including attending Board meetings and other agreed Stable Life activities, will be reimbursed in accordance with Stable Life’s Volunteer Expenses Policy.\r\n\r\nExpenses should be agreed where appropriate and supported by receipts or other relevant evidence. Volunteers can submit claims through Stable Life’s usual expenses process, and claims will be reimbursed in line with the organisation’s policy and any applicable limits.\r\n\r\nTrustees are entitled to claim expenses on the same basis as other Stable Life volunteers.\n\n## Taster details\n\nWe would be very happy to arrange an informal visit to Stable Life for anyone interested in becoming a Trustee.\r\n\r\nThis provides an opportunity to meet the team, see our yard and facilities, find out more about our work with children and young people, and have an informal conversation about the Trustee role and what it involves. There is no obligation to commit to the role following a visit.\r\n\r\nWe can arrange visits at a mutually convenient time.\r\n\r\nOnce we receive an application, we will contact the applicant to arrange an informal conversation and, where possible, an opportunity to visit Stable Life and meet members of the team.\r\n\r\nThis is an opportunity for us to find out more about the applicant, their skills, experience and interest in Stable Life, and for the applicant to ask questions, see our facilities and learn more about what being a Trustee involves.\r\n\r\nFollowing the initial conversation, interested applicants may be invited to meet with the Chair and/or other members of the Board before a decision is made about progressing the appointment.\r\n\r\nWe aim to keep the process friendly, informal and transparent, and will keep applicants updated throughout. The timescale will depend on the availability of those involved, but we will aim to progress applications as promptly as possible.\r\n\r\nAny appointment will be subject to the appropriate checks, including PVG membership, and completion of the required induction and safeguarding training.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
