            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005yG0bYAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005yG0bYAE/board-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Board Member",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nScarf is a charity/social enterprise delivering a range of services to householders, communities, and businesses throughout the Northeast of Scotland. For almost 40 years we have been offering free and impartial energy saving advice to help people lower their fuel bills and carbon emissions.\r\n\r\nWe are very excited to be able to offer this opportunity for the right person to join our Board and contribute to the good governance of the organisation as well as assisting in achieving its aims and objectives moving forward.\r\n\r\nOur Board is focused on:\r\n\r\n*Working closely with our customers, being responsive; innovative and ambitious whilst remaining accountable and providing value for money in everything we do.\r\n*Creating connected communities with more successful households that can prosper.\r\n*Making a difference to health and wellbeing\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help make a real difference with a leading charity and value driven social enterprise. For further details please contact Lawrence Johnston, Co-CEO at email: lawrence.johnston@scarf.org.uk\n\n## Description\n\nScarf is a charity/social enterprise delivering a range of services to householders, communities, and businesses throughout the Northeast of Scotland. For almost 40 years we have been offering free and impartial energy saving advice to help people lower their fuel bills and carbon emissions.\r\n\r\nWe are very excited to be able to offer this opportunity for the right person to join our Board and contribute to the good governance of the organisation as well as assisting in achieving its aims and objectives moving forward.\r\n\r\nOur Board is focused on:\r\n\r\n*Working closely with our customers, being responsive; innovative and ambitious whilst remaining accountable and providing value for money in everything we do.\r\n*Creating connected communities with more successful households that can prosper.\r\n*Making a difference to health and wellbeing\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help make a real difference with a leading charity and value driven social enterprise. For further details please contact Lawrence Johnston, Co-CEO at email: lawrence.johnston@scarf.org.uk\n\n## Experience required\n\nAre you:\r\n*Willing to give your time and play your part\r\n*Eager to learn and get involved\r\n*Passionate, committed, sharing our values\r\n\r\nPrevious Board experience is preferred but not essential, and this opportunity is open to all ages (18+), all backgrounds and all abilities. The positions are unremunerated however travel and expenses will be reimbursed; training and development are also part of the offer.\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant training, development and excellent support is provided to all volunteers/Board Members.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to help.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoard meetings happen once a month and generally take place at our Aberdeen HQ, 1 Cotton Street, Aberdeen, AB11 5EE. However we do have some flexibility for joining online.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005yG0bYAE#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Board Member",
                        "description": "Are you:\r\n*Willing to give your time and play your part\r\n*Eager to learn and get involved\r\n*Passionate, committed, sharing our values\r\n\r\nPrevious Board experience is preferred but not essential, and this opportunity is open to all ages (18+), all backgrounds and all abilities. The positions are unremunerated however travel and expenses will be reimbursed; training and development are also part of the offer.",
                        "commitment": "Flexible times available to help.",
