            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaKzAAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kaKzAAI/cafe-connect-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Cafe Connect Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for motivated and enthusiastic volunteers to serve coffee and snacks to members of the public and staff in our busy centre. The funds from the sale of coffee and snacks raised will support the work we do in the local community.\n\n## Description\n\nThe Eric Liddell Centre provides a number of services including a Day Care service for people with dementia, a Befriending service, the leasing of office space to several charities, as well as room hire for all sorts of different events, from professional workshops to pilates classes! The Centre is a busy place with a real buzz and a huge variety of people come through the doors each day. Café Connect is situated on the ground floor of the Centre and offers hot drinks, light meals and cakes.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for individuals who are interested in customer service and hospitality. No experience is necessary but good communication skills are desirable.The candidate should be enthusiastic, committed and be able to work independently or as part of a team.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining is provided.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased at the Eric Liddell Centre 15 Morningside Road Edinburgh EH10 4DP Travel costs will be covered.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPaid weekly on production on valid bus ticket.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
