                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzRj3YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HzRj3YAF/event-operations-and-driving-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-08",
                    "title": "Event Operations and Driving Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe’re looking for an enthusiastic, proactive and reliable volunteer to support our Bespoke Events and Experiences Team in bringing our exceptional events to life.\r\n\r\nYou’ll be 25 or over with a full, clean UK driving licence for at least two years and comfortable driving a large van/light commercial vehicle. You’ll also need to be physically fit and able to cope with substantial manual handling activities.\r\n\r\nAs an event \"runner\", you will play a key role behind the scenes and on the day, helping ensure everything runs smoothly. Working alongside our experienced team, you'll provide practical and logistical support in the lead up to events, during event delivery, and afterwards. No two days are the same, making this a varied, hands-on and rewarding opportunity for someone who enjoys being busy, meeting people and making things happen. You'll be helping CHAS create memorable experiences for our supporters while contributing to the care and support we provide to children and families across Scotland.\r\n\r\nWe are currently looking for support for the following events and it’s essential that you are available for these dates:\r\n\r\n• Fawkes-y Ladies Lunch, Edinburgh – Friday 6 November\r\n\r\n• Winter Wonderland, Aberdeen – Thursday 3 December\r\n\r\n• Capital Sci Fi Con, Edinburgh – Fri 19 - Sun 21 February 2027\r\n\r\nWhat you will be doing:\r\nSupporting the planning and coordination of events through:\r\n-Assisting with venue preparation, event set-up and pack-down activities, including uplifting and delivering prizes, props and equipment\r\n-Driving a van to transport event materials safely and efficiently where required\r\n-Providing practical on-the-day event support to ensure activities run smoothly and resolving issues as they arise, coordinating volunteers, suppliers and event partners where appropriate\r\n-Welcoming and assisting guests, helping to create a positive and professional experience\r\n-Capturing feedback, photographs and event highlights to support post-event publicity and future planning\r\n-Supporting post-event activities and contributing to debriefs and event evaluations\r\n-Working collaboratively with our colleagues across Income Generation and Engagement to optimise our events\r\n-Supporting with a variety of other ad hoc activities and tasks which are essential to the success of each event.\r\n\r\nWhat's in it for you:\r\n-You’ll be part of a busy team, attending and working on an exciting portfolio of prestigious events which raise vital funds and make a real difference to the families we support across Scotland\r\n-You’ll gain valuable experience in event operations and logistics\r\n-You can develop your confidence, teamwork and event management skills\r\n-You’ll meet new people, have new experiences and we hope you have fun too.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe skills you need:\r\n\r\n-Full clean UK driving licence holder for over two years, preferably with experience of driving a light commercial vehicle (a large van)\r\n-Good physical fitness, able to undertake manual handling activities and spend lengthy periods on your feet\r\n-A calm, resourceful and solutions-focused approach in busy and fast-paced event environments\r\n-Able to work as a dependable part of our team and to follow instructions with energy and reliability and a willingness to support different aspects of event delivery\r\n-Excellent communication and interpersonal skills - able to engage positively with staff, volunteers and guests, representing CHAS enthusiastically and appropriately\r\n-Confidence using Microsoft Office: Outlook, Word, Teams and Excel\r\n-An understanding of the need for confidentiality, data protection and GDPR compliance\n\n## Training details\n\nIt’s important to us that you feel happy, safe and confident in your role. As a CHAS volunteer you will be invited to complete a short core learning package that is tailored to your role. This can be done online or face to face with support. We also offer a full induction process where we provide full training on all aspects of the role.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nDays and times are flexible, however we are currently looking for support for the following events and it’s essential that you are available for these dates:\r\n\r\n• Fawkes-y Ladies Lunch, Edinburgh – Friday 6 November\r\n\r\n• Winter Wonderland, Aberdeen – Thursday 3 December\r\n\r\n• Capital Sci Fi Con, Edinburgh – Fri 19 - Sun 21 February 2027\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses are paid in line with the CHAS expenses policy.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
