                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzM3RYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HzM3RYAV/event-management-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-08",
                    "title": "Event Management Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nJoin our Bespoke Events and Experiences Team, based in our Edinburgh head office, and help bring our exceptional events to life across Scotland. Working alongside experienced colleagues, you'll support all stages of event delivery, from planning and preparation to on-the-day support and post-event follow-up.\r\n\r\nWhether you're an experienced event professional looking to give back or someone keen to build their skills and confidence in event management, this rewarding volunteering opportunity offers valuable experience while helping CHAS create unforgettable experiences for our supporters.\r\n\r\nWe are currently looking for support for the following events and it’s essential that you are available for these dates:\r\n\r\n• Fawkes-y Ladies Lunch, Edinburgh – Friday 6 November 2026 \r\n• Winter Wonderland, Aberdeen – Thursday 3 December 2026 \r\n• Capital Sci Fi Con, Edinburgh – Fri 19 - Sun 21 February 2027 \r\n• Highlands to Islands Challenge (Inverness to mystery island destination) – Thurs 18 – Sun 21 March 2027\r\n\r\nWhat you will be doing\r\n-Supporting the planning and coordination of events through:\r\n-Securing high value prizes and ensuring we have pictures and compelling copy for event programmes\r\n-Capturing feedback, photographs and event highlights to support post-event publicity and future planning\r\n-Maintaining guest lists, tracking RSVPs and preparing event materials; maintaining accurate records and updating event databases\r\n-Sourcing and organising event resources, equipment and supplies, e.g. goody bags, signage and supporter materials\r\n-Venue preparation, event set-up and pack-down activities\r\n-Welcoming guests, supporters and volunteers to events\r\n-Providing on-the-day event support to ensure activities run smoothly – cash-handling, coordinating volunteers, suppliers and event partners where appropriate\r\n-Supporting post-event activities: managing thanking communications, collating feedback and contributing to debriefs and event evaluations\r\n-Working collaboratively with our colleagues across Income Generation and Engagement to optimise our events\r\n-Supporting with a variety of other ad hoc activities and tasks which are essential to the success of each event.\r\n\r\nThe skills you need\r\n-A good understanding and experience of event management or a desire to learn more, building your skills and expertise\r\n-Able to work as a dependable part of our team and to follow instructions with energy, reliability and a willingness to support different aspects of event delivery\r\n-Good communication, numeracy and organisational skills with a keen eye for detail\r\n-Strong interpersonal skills – able to engage positively with staff, volunteers and guests, representing CHAS enthusiastically and appropriately\r\n-Able to reliably and proactively manage a variety of tasks and prioritise workload effectively to fulfil your role\r\n-Ability to work as part of our team and to follow instructions\r\n-Confident using Microsoft Office: Outlook, Word, Teams and Excel\r\n-Able to remain calm and positive in a busy event environment\r\n-An understanding of the need for confidentiality and adherence to GDPR\r\n\r\nWhat's in it for you\r\n-You’ll be part of a busy team, working on events which raise vital funds and make a real difference to the families we support\r\n-Opportunities to travel to and be a key part of each event\r\n-You’ll gain valuable experience you can add to your cv, or you’ll be able to share your existing skills to help us create memorable events and raise money\r\n-You’ll meet new people, have new experiences and we hope you have fun too.\n\n## Experience required\n\n-A good understanding and experience of event management or a desire to learn more, building your skills and expertise\r\n-Able to work as a dependable part of our team and to follow instructions with energy, reliability and a willingness to support different aspects of event delivery\r\n-Good communication, numeracy and organisational skills with a keen eye for detail\r\n-Strong interpersonal skills – able to engage positively with staff, volunteers and guests, representing CHAS enthusiastically and appropriately\r\n-Able to reliably and proactively manage a variety of tasks and prioritise workload effectively to fulfil your role\r\n-Ability to work as part of our team and to follow instructions\r\n-Confident using Microsoft Office: Outlook, Word, Teams and Excel\r\n-Able to remain calm and positive in a busy event environment\r\n-An understanding of the need for confidentiality and adherence to GDPR\n\n## Training details\n\nIt’s important to us that you feel happy, safe and confident in your role. As a CHAS volunteer you will be invited to complete a short core learning package that is tailored to your role. This can be done online or face to face with support. We also offer a full induction process where we provide full training on all aspects of the role.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe hours and times are flexible, however we are currently looking for support for the following events and it’s essential that you are available for these dates:\r\n\r\n• Fawkes-y Ladies Lunch, Edinburgh – Friday 6 November 2026 • Winter Wonderland, Aberdeen – Thursday 3 December 2026 • Capital Sci Fi Con, Edinburgh – Fri 19 - Sun 21 February 2027 • Highlands to Islands Challenge (Inverness to mystery island destination) – Thurs 18 – Sun 21 March 2027\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe will pay your out-of-pocket expenses in line with the CHAS volunteer expenses policy.",
