                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hvr0zYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hvr0zYAB/edinburgh-bucket-shake-coordinator",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Edinburgh Bucket Shake Coordinator",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAcross Scotland, CHAS volunteers give their time because they want to make a difference - and our bucket collections are a brilliant way to do just that. They help raise vital funds and share CHAS’s work with more people, so we can be there for children with life-shortening conditions and their families.\r\n\r\nAs Edinburgh Bucket Shake Coordinator – Fundraising Group Lead, you’ll bring people together to make bucket collections happen in Edinburgh City Centre. You’ll plan a calendar of collections, arrange the permissions needed to collect funds, and work with the CHAS Community Fundraising team to make sure volunteers have the materials, information and support they need.\r\n\r\nThis is a great opportunity to use your organisation, leadership and local knowledge to do good, meet new people and help create a fun, positive volunteering experience for others.\r\n\r\nWhat activities will I be involved in?\r\nYou’ll coordinate bucket shakes across Edinburgh City Centre, with a particular focus on collections around Murrayfield Stadium. You’ll look ahead at game fixtures, concerts and other major events, then build a calendar of collection opportunities where CHAS volunteers can be out and about, raising funds and awareness.\r\n\r\nYou’ll apply for the licences to collect funds through City of Edinburgh Council, help recruit volunteers to fill shifts, collect materials from the CHAS Head Office in Craiglockhart, and drop off any funds raised so they can be counted and banked.\r\n\r\nAs the role grows, you’ll help build and lead an Edinburgh Bucket Shake volunteer fundraising group. As Group Lead, you’ll welcome new volunteers, support group membership, and help plan and deliver activities that feel organised, enjoyable and worthwhile for everyone involved.\r\n\r\nYou won’t be doing this alone. You’ll stay in regular contact with your local Community Fundraiser, who will offer guidance, answer questions and support you throughout your role.\r\n\r\nWhat ongoing learning/support/guidance will I receive?\r\nWe want you to feel happy, safe and confident in your role. You’ll be invited to complete a short core learning package tailored to what you’ll be doing, so you feel ready to get started.\r\n\r\nYou’ll also have ongoing support from your Community Fundraiser, plus opportunities to learn, build confidence and connect with other CHAS volunteers along the way.\r\n\r\nWe have also partnered with the Skills Network to offer all our volunteers the chance to develop new skills and explore further learning opportunities.\r\n\r\nWhat are the benefits to the children and families supported by CHAS?\r\nBy organising bucket collections in Edinburgh, you’ll help raise vital funds and give more people the chance to hear about CHAS. Every collection creates a friendly, visible way for the public to support children with life-shortening conditions and their families.\r\n\r\nCHAS have launched the More Than a Hospice Appeal – a campaign to raise £20m to transform children’s palliative care in Scotland by:\r\n\r\n• Rebuilding Rachel House into a world-class, flexible, and welcoming space that meets the most complex needs of today’s families. • Renewing Robin House, ensuring it remains a world-class home from home. • Reimagining our services, expanding our reach so every family in Scotland has real choice, whether that’s care in a hospice, at home, or in hospital.\r\n\r\nYour role will support fundraising for this appeal, helping CHAS transform the care we can provide and making sure families across Scotland have more choice, support and moments that matter.\r\n\r\nWhat else should I know?\r\nPLEASE NOTE - A driving license and access to a car will be required for this volunteer role as you will be transporting materials and cash from events.\r\n\r\nWe will pay your out of pocket expenses in line with the CHAS volunteer expenses policy.\r\n\r\nCHAS is committed to providing a quality volunteering experience to all volunteers, free from discrimination and prejudice. Ensuring that CHAS is an equal, diverse, and inclusive organisation improves the quality of care we provide, helps us reach more families and children, and maximises a wide variety of knowledge, experience and expertise.\r\n\r\nWe welcome volunteer applications from those who are refugees, asylum seekers, benefit claimants and those with a disability. We can provide more information about your eligibility to volunteer and any reasonable adjustments we can put in place to ensure your volunteering experience is a positive one.\r\n\r\nWhat’s the next step?\r\nIf you’re interested in the role you can apply online or if you have any questions, please contact the Volunteering Team at volunteering@chas.org.uk or 01577 866065\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe skills you need\r\n-Strong organisational skills to plan collections, arrange council licences, coordinate volunteers and keep materials moving.\r\n-A friendly, encouraging approach to leading and being part of a team.\r\n-A willingness to get outdoors in all weathers for a great cause.\r\n-Local knowledge of Edinburgh and links to your community.\r\n-Enthusiasm for representing CHAS positively and appropriately.\r\n-Confidence chatting with members of the public in an outgoing and welcoming way.\r\n-Respect for confidentiality and a commitment to following GDPR guidance.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe want you to feel happy, safe and confident in your role. You’ll be invited to complete a short core learning package tailored to what you’ll be doing, so you feel ready to get started.\r\n\r\nYou’ll also have ongoing support from your Community Fundraiser, plus opportunities to learn, build confidence and connect with other CHAS volunteers along the way.\r\n\r\nWe have also partnered with the Skills Network to offer all our volunteers the chance to develop new skills and explore further learning opportunities.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe will pay your out of pocket expenses in line with the CHAS volunteer expenses policy.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
