                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HvqOHYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HvqOHYAZ/fundraising-and-events-support-volunteer-placement",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Fundraising and Events Support Volunteer - Placement",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWhy we want you\r\n\r\nWe have an exciting opportunity to undertake a volunteer placement with\r\nCHAS in our Head Office as part of the fundraising team. You’ll work amongst\r\nour Community Fundraisers, Challenge Events team and wider Income\r\nGeneration and Engagement teams, gaining experience in fundraising, events\r\nplanning, marketing and more.\r\n\r\nWhat you will be doing\r\n\r\n-Assisting with the development and delivery of key fundraising projects.\r\nResearch tasks – researching potential donors, events, and other\r\nfundraising development opportunities across Income Generation and\r\nEngagement teams.\r\n-Stewardship – supporting relationship building to deepen fundraising\r\nopportunities with our existing supporters (thank you cards, good luck\r\nphone calls, supporting with meetings, etc).\r\n-Data handling and preparation – helping to keep our supporter database\r\nup to date, supporting with segmenting and preparing our supporter data\r\nahead of key mailings and engagement opportunities.\r\n-Banking – supporting banking administration where necessary to process\r\ndonations in a timely manner.\r\n-Event support– assisting with marketing and volunteer recruitment,\r\npreparing materials, and capturing content at events.\r\n-You will work mostly with the Community Fundraising and Challenge\r\nEvents team, but may also be required to support with ad-hoc tasks from\r\nother teams.\r\n-Undertaking any training that will help you in your role.\r\n\r\nThe skills you need\r\n\r\n-An understanding of events, events marketing, and an enthusiasm to\r\nlearn more.\r\n-Excellent IT skills – including knowledge of Microsoft (Word and Excel).\r\n-Good organisation, communication and numeracy skills.\r\n-Patience, empathy and tact.\r\n-An ability to represent CHAS enthusiastically and appropriately.\r\n-Adherence to rules around GDPR and a strong understanding of\r\nconfidentiality.\r\n-An ability to relate to people of all ages.\r\n\r\nWhat's in it for you\r\n\r\n-The opportunity to be part of a busy fundraising team, working on exciting\r\nprojects with national impact.\r\n-Gaining valuable experience in fundraising and events to add to your CV.\r\n-Gaining experience in an office environment and building professional\r\nworking relationships.\r\n-Making a real difference to the families of children with a life-shortening\r\ncondition across Scotland.\r\n-Having fun!\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe skills you need\r\n\r\n-An understanding of events, events marketing, and an enthusiasm to\r\nlearn more.\r\n-Excellent IT skills – including knowledge of Microsoft (Word and Excel).\r\n-Good organisation, communication and numeracy skills.\r\n-Patience, empathy and tact.\r\n-An ability to represent CHAS enthusiastically and appropriately.\r\n-Adherence to rules around GDPR and a strong understanding of\r\nconfidentiality.\r\n-An ability to relate to people of all ages.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe want you to feel happy, safe and confident in your role. You’ll be invited to complete a short core learning package tailored to what you’ll be doing, so you feel ready to get started.\r\n\r\nYou’ll also have ongoing support from your Community Fundraiser, plus opportunities to learn, build confidence and connect with other CHAS volunteers along the way.\r\n\r\nWe have also partnered with the Skills Network to offer all our volunteers the chance to develop new skills and explore further learning opportunities.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe will pay your out of pocket expenses in line with the CHAS volunteer expenses policy.",
