                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Board Members",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCrossroads Fife is looking to recruit innovative, enthusiastic board members to expand on skills and expertise of their Management Committee.\r\n\r\nCrossroads Fife is one of the leading providers of home based respite care for Carers. They offer a respite service to people in the community who care for someone of any age and any disability. The service is provided by trained, paid staff in the service user’s home or in the community. They are also a registered provider of Self Directed Support and Purchased Care.\r\n\r\nCrossroads Fife has charitable status and is led by an experienced Board who have overall responsibility for the governance and strategic direction of the organisation’s work.\r\n\r\nThey are looking for individuals who possess knowledge, skills and experience of business and charity work with entrepreneurial skills or have an understanding of the caring role.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe organisation are looking for individuals who possess the knowledge, skills and experience of business and charity work with entrepreneurial skills or an understanding of the caring role.\n\n## Training details\n\nThese will be accessed as individual needs required – TVA training available\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Board meet 4 times per year (both online and in person) for 2 hours on a Wednesday evening.\r\n\r\nAGM once per year held Glenrothes/Kirkcaldy\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n55p per mile",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
