                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7Ij5AAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7Ij5AAF/trustees",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Trustees",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSunrise Partnership is a small local charity established in 2014.  We provide free, therapeutic confidential support for children and young people up to the age of 18 experiencing loss and bereavement.  We work in Aberdeen City and Aberdeenshire.  Our website is at: www.sunrisepartnership.org \r\n\r\nWe are looking for new Trustees to join us at an exciting time in our history and help us create a resilient model for the future, so that we can support even more young people.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference.\r\n\r\nFor more information please email vacancies@sunrisepartnership.org\n\n## Description\n\nSunrise Partnership is a small local charity established in 2014.  We provide free, therapeutic confidential support for children and young people up to the age of 18 experiencing loss and bereavement.  We work in Aberdeen City and Aberdeenshire.  Our website is at: www.sunrisepartnership.org \r\n\r\nWe are looking for new Trustees to join us at an exciting time in our history and help us create a resilient model for the future, so that we can support even more young people.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference.\r\n\r\nFor more information please email vacancies@sunrisepartnership.org\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnthusiasm, time to spare and motivation are essential. An understanding of the issues around childhood bereavement would be helpful.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided. Includes role of the Trustee and Safeguarding.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times. All help is greatly appreciated and makes a positive difference.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTrustees meetings are held monthly (online), plus some other events during the year, where we’d love our trustees' input.   The roles are unremunerated, though reasonable out of pocket expenses can be reimbursed.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable out of pocket expenses can be reimbursed. Milage 45p per mile, reimbursed via expenses claim",
