            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nd7QAAQ/digital-fife",
            "name": "Digital Fife",
            "description": "Digital Fife aim to promote the advancement of learning through the use of digital tools, innovative technologies and integrated teaching methods, and to provide computer and IT services such as website development, online learning, and tutor development. They hope to advance community development and active citizenship through partnership work, volunteer recruitment and increasing the numbers of people able to go online. Their support enables community groups to access and experience new technologies.",
            "website": "https://www.digitalfife.com/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC052429"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/DigitalITTech",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Digital / IT / Tech"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FoCbdYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FoCbdYAF/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-18",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDigital Fife is seeking to recruit volunteer charity trustees to join their Board.\n\n## Description\n\nDigital Fife is a charity which seeks to promote and develop digital inclusion. The tools provided by the charity allow community groups to design and build attractive websites without the need for specialist IT knowledge. This is a free service offered to community groups in Fife.\r\n\r\nDigital Fife is seeking to recruit volunteer charity trustees to join their Board. Trustees are collectively tasked with the overall control and management of the charity in line with Digital Fife’s governing document. You will not be responsible for the day to day running of the organisation or the direct delivery of the service but will have responsibility for governance and strategy and ensuring that the organisation is run effectively.\r\n\r\nTrustee meetings take place online bimonthly for 1-2 hours.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAn understanding of charities and the third sector would be beneficial. It would also be useful to have an understanding of digital tools.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction to Digital Fife. Access to ‘How to Guides’ on the Digital Fife website Ongoing support, advice and guidance from a named individual.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTrustee meetings take place online bimonthly for 1-2 hours.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAll out of pocket expenses will be reimbursed.",
