                    "title": "Session Supporter, Calderwood",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDo you love talking about sport? Our clubs support older people who enjoy reminiscing about sport. Our volunteers love a bit of banter and sessions are about everyone having fun!\r\nSporting Memories needs volunteers who can communicate well with others and are able to support club members who may have memory or physical health problems. The most important skill is to be able to listen to club members and help them to get involved in the discussion. You will be part of a team of volunteers who will work together to improve the well-being of club members. One of our volunteers has said: \"It is rewarding watching club members become more confident and start talking about their favourite sport.\"\r\nOur volunteer induction process involves:\r\n* An initial phone call to have a chat to about volunteering with us.\r\n* An online training session re planning and running a club (3 hours).\r\n* Fortnightly online sessions where you can meet other volunteers and be supported.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience is required, just an ability to engage and communicate with people and to support those with who find it difficult to share their memories or have health problems. A sense of humour and an ability to listen to others.\n\n## Training details\n\nAn initial online training session (3 hours) and Dementia Awareness sessions available.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe Calderwood Club meets at Calderwood Baptist Church, Maxwellton Rd, East kilbbride on Tuesdays from 10.00 1200.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteers can claim expenses if they need to travel to a club (mileage, bus or train fares).\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses are paid monthly or in advance if necessary.",
