                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Administrator & Club Secretary",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAberdeen Amateur Boxing & Athletic Club is an organisation deeply seated into the community in and around Aberdeen.  It is one of the oldest boxing clubs in Scotland.\n\nThe organisation is making a formal call to recruit new voluntary members.  \n\nA great opportunity to assist in the development of a well established boxing club, with a high reputation and make a difference in the community. For further details please contact:\nLeroy Smith (Head Coach and Centre Manager)\nTel.: 07738 564855\nE Mail: leroy@boxingclubaberdeen.com\n\n## Description\n\nAberdeen Amateur Boxing & Athletic Club is an organisation deeply seated into the community in and around Aberdeen.  It is one of the oldest boxing clubs in Scotland.\n\nThe organisation is making a formal call to recruit new voluntary members.  The role of Administrator & Club Secretary is an integral part of the organisation and is a ‘backbone post’ due to its focus on the following key areas:\n-Managing all administrative business of the organisation:\n-Organising all meetings, preparations, follow-ups and all paperwork processes to achieve this.\n-Conduct the official secretarial duties of the Club, including minute taking of all official minutes\n-Liaise with Boxing Scotland and any affiliated organisations or groups.\n-Source and administer all funding requests.\n-Deal with all booking enquiries and classes, keeping appropriate databases of members.\n-Source and advise on matters that will improve the business of the organisation, wherever appropriate\n\nA great opportunity to assist in the development of a well established boxing club, with a high reputation and make a difference in the community. For further details please contact:\nLeroy Smith (Head Coach and Centre Manager)\nTel.: 07738 564855\nE Mail: leroy@boxingclubaberdeen.com\n\n## Experience required\n\nExcellent people skills with a good range of communication and organisational skills. Experience in the work of charitable organisation and general business understanding.\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support provided to all volunteers. Training provided will mainly be to orientate the person into the world of fitness and boxing, induction will be by the Head Coach or Managing Committee representative with the relevant experience.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible working hours applies.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCentral Aberdeen.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAll expenses need to receive pre-approval and only then can be met by Aberdeen ABC or other clubs if it is their event or the NGB Boxing Scotland Ltd’s event.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eNXMAA2#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Administrator & Club Secretary",
                        "description": "Excellent people skills with a good range of communication and organisational skills. Experience in the work of charitable organisation and general business understanding.",
                        "commitment": "Flexible working hours applies.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eNXMAA2/administrator-club-secretary?#modal_register_a0g24000000eNXMAA2",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
