        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nctYAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nctYAAQ/siblings-reunited-star-scio",
            "name": "Siblings Reunited (STAR) (SCIO)",
            "description": "Siblings Reunited (STAR) was set up in April 2013 to provide the opportunity for regular and quality contact for brothers and sisters separated in care who would otherwise have none. STAR is the only specialised service in Scotland offering support with contact for brothers and sisters in care.",
            "website": "https://www.siblingsreunited.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC043937"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Dl4lUYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Dl4lUYAR/animal-carer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-21",
                    "title": "Animal carer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDo you love the outdoors and looking after animals? Then, this is the opportunity for you!\r\n\r\nSiblings Reunited (STAR) reunites brothers and sisters separated in the care system, by providing the opportunity for quality and regular sibling contact.\r\n\r\nRun from its unique farmland setting, it provides a safe, natural, calming and fun environment, where children can foster emotional bonds and help overcome the trauma associated with being separated from their siblings.\r\n\r\nSTAR has a wide variety of furry friends, needing your care. These include Chip & Dale, the goats, Maggie, Grace, Rose, Ivy & Violet, the sheep, and Barney, Bella and Ava the Shetland Ponies, (as well as numerous ducks, chickens, rabbits and guinea pigs!).\r\n\r\nIn addition to building animal care skills, you will also benefit from being part of a committed and friendly team of volunteers and staff. Come and join them!\n\n## Experience required\n\nApplicants should be keen, enthusiastic and adaptable. They should be able to use their initiative but also to follow instructions/to do lists. They should have basic animal knowledge and caring skills, and be willing to feed, clean out and ensure the welfare of the animals.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction includes a tour of the site, expectations, an informal chat about the needs of the animals, health & safety policy and site risk assessment. Other volunteers and staff are available for ongoing support.\n\n## Travel details\n\nSiblings Reunited is located in NE Fife, between Gauldry and Newburgh, on the banks of the River Tay, at East Flisk Farm, Fife. KY14 6HP\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravelling expenses are paid at 0.45 per mile or public transport tickets up to a total of £15.00 per session, (due to funding limitations)",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Dl4lUYAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
