                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Ds9reYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Ds9reYAB/maintenance-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-04",
                    "title": "Maintenance Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDo you like to work outside, maintaining property and gardens? Then this is the opportunity for you ! \r\n\r\nSiblings Reunited (STAR) reunites brothers and sisters separated in the care system, by providing the opportunity for quality and regular sibling contact. \r\n\r\nRun from its unique farmland setting, it provides a safe, natural, calming and fun environment, where children can foster emotional bonds and help overcome the trauma associated with being separated from their siblings. \r\n\r\nIn your role, you would repair and maintain outbuilding, fences, sheds and the outside kitchen. \r\n\r\nIn addition to building maintenance  skills, you will also benefit from being part of a committed and friendly team of volunteers and staff. Come and join us!\n\n## Experience required\n\nApplicants should be keen, enthusiastic and adaptable.  They should be able to use their imitative but also follow instructions/to do list. They should have basic DIY skills and be willing to complete repairs and maintenance of outbuildings and general environment.  They should be familiar with a variety of tools and understand the importance of health & safety guidelines for themselves and others using the site.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction includes a tour of the site, location of tools  etc, expectations,  an informal chat about STAR's vision for its environment, health & safety policy and site risk assessment.  Other volunteers and staff are available for support and guidance.\n\n## Travel details\n\nSibling Reunited is located in NE Fife, between Gauldry and Newburgh, on the banks of the River Tay, at East Flisk Farm, Fife KY14 6HP.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTraveling expenses are paid at 0.45 per mile or public transport tickets up to a total of £15.00 per session, (due to funding limitations)",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Ds9reYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Maintenance Volunteer",
                        "description": "Applicants should be keen, enthusiastic and adaptable.  They should be able to use their imitative but also follow instructions/to do list. They should have basic DIY skills and be willing to complete repairs and maintenance of outbuildings and general environment.  They should be familiar with a variety of tools and understand the importance of health & safety guidelines for themselves and others using the site.",
