                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Heritage",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Heritage"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HSqwLYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HSqwLYAT/volunteertrustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-19",
                    "title": "Volunteer/Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nTrustee (Board of Trustees comprises hands-on specific and general roles responsible for the management and running of the museum which is a registered charity SCO43666. Monthly meetings by Zoom in addition to specific tasks/projects.)\r\nFront of House Volunteer (meeting and greeting visitors; learning about our exhibits and activities to help visitors of all ages enjoy the museum). Front of House volunteers work in pairs for morning or afternoon shifts. Regular weekly, bi-weekly or ad hoc shifts possible.\r\nCurator Support, Exhibitions and Collections Volunteer (most work and planning takes place in the closed season November to March/April. Includes research and preparation for new exhibits.)\r\nOther roles/opportunities –\r\nGeneral Administration\r\nEvents Group\r\nCommunity Outreach and Education Programmes\r\nResearch and Publications\r\nMarketing and Publicity\r\nFundraising and Grants\r\n\r\nFull Training and Induction given.\r\n\r\nRestrictions\r\nMinimum age: 16\r\nAvailability\r\nTrustee – Year-round.\r\nFront of House - Museum is open to the public April to End October Wednesday to Saturday 11 am to 4 pm.\r\nExhibition Team – Meets monthly in closed season November to March/April plus preparatory work in the museum and research (including at home).\r\nOther roles/opportunities – Potential all year-round activities and projects\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction and shadowing\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCommitment Flexible 4 Hours, Fortnightly",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
