        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nd0OAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nd0OAAQ/pencaitland-playgroup",
            "name": "Pencaitland Playgroup",
            "description": "Pencaitland Playgroup is a well-established organisation, founded in 1968 which provides childcare for 2-3 year-olds.\r\n\r\nWe have a dedicated team consisting of practitioners and a voluntary committee. Daily activities change regularly and include; sand & water play, art & craft activities, outdoor play, construction toys, role play, tabletop activities, baking, reading, music, and movement.",
            "website": "https://pencaitlandplaygroup.co.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC000003"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzMoDYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HzMoDYAV/playgroup-chairperson",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-08",
                    "title": "Playgroup Chairperson",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nPencaitland Playgroup is seeking a dedicated and community-minded individual to join us as our next Chairperson. This is an incredible opportunity to lead a vital community resource, support early years development, and guide our passionate team of staff and volunteers.\r\n\r\nAs Chairperson you would are also a Trustee of our charity. The Chairperson, in line with normal Charity practise is responsible for leading and managing the playgroup. They oversee administrative tasks, chair meetings and work with the playgroup’s Play Leader.\r\n\r\nSome specific parts of the role include:\r\n* Provide Leadership - The Chairperson is the leader in the Committee. They should be an effective strategist and networker.\r\n* Plan and Chair Meetings - The Chairperson ensures that meetings are planned effectively and conducted according to the playgroup’s constitution.\r\n* Communicate - The Chairperson ensures clear communication between the Committee and the playgroup’s staff.\r\n* Make Decisions - the Chairperson has the authority to make decisions on behalf of the Committee when time is of the essence.\r\n* Sign Legal Documents - the Chairperson may be responsible for signing legal and financial documents where necessary.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYouth / Childcare\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCommitment Flexible 6 Hours, Weekly",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzMoDYAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Playgroup Chairperson",
                        "description": "Youth / Childcare",
