            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eNSWAA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eNSWAA2/volunteer-teacher-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Volunteer Teacher Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSunny Garden: Bilingual (Russian-English) Playgroup provide a safe, caring bilingual environment which will promote a child’s health, individuality and dignity, and an opportunity for fun, learning through play, socialising with adults and children from a wide range of cultures free from any discrimination.\n\nFor further details about volunteering with us please contact:\nOlga Sevastyanova (Chairperson)\nTel No: 01224 478482 \nE Mail: olga_sevastyanova@yahoo.com\n\n## Description\n\nSunny Garden: Bilingual (Russian-English) Playgroup provide a safe, caring bilingual environment which will promote a child’s health, individuality and dignity, and an opportunity for fun, learning through play, socialising with adults and children from a wide range of cultures free from any discrimination.\n\nWe aim to provide and support knowledge and education that encourages children’s physical, social, emotional, intellectual and creative development through a wide range of activities suitable for their age range.\n\nWe have professional Russian-speaking stuff, but we have volunteer opportunities for people to simply speak English to children and read them English books. This would assist their further integration into community. \n\nA great, enjoyable opportunity where you will make a real difference. For further details please contact:\nOlga Sevastyanova (Chairperson)\nTel No: 01224 478482 \nE Mail: olga_sevastyanova@yahoo.com\n\n## Experience required\n\nNeeds to be a native English speaker\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to suit volunteers. All help is greatly appreciated and makes a difference.\n\n## Travel details\n\n27 Craigie Park\nAberdeen A255 2SE",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eNSWAA2#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Teacher Assistant",
                        "description": "Needs to be a native English speaker",
