                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-26",
                    "title": "Social media/Publicity Volunteer (Barra)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCitizen Advice Bureau need to raise and maintain their profile in the community. \r\nThis is to ensure that:\r\nEveryone who might need the bureau's services can easily find out what is offered and where it is available and when.\r\nPotential volunteers are aware of all the volunteering opportunities they have available.\r\nFunders recognise what great value there is in supporting their local CAB.\r\nPoliticians and decision makers see the social policy evidence provided by the Citizen Advice network in Scotland and by the individual bureau.\r\n\r\nSome of the task sthat may be done by volunteers are:\r\nWriting content and creating graphics for social media posts.\r\nPromoting the bureau by staffing stalls at local events/rural shows, student fayres, local markets/supermarkets. \r\nGiving talks about the bureau to interested local organisations.\r\nCreating leaflets and posters.\n\n## Experience required\n\nKnowlege of social media  and enjoy meeting new people.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses are covered .",
