                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H3kVyYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000H3kVyYAJ/food-cafe-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-28",
                    "title": "Food Cafe assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCosy Cafe exists to support people in Buckhaven who are facing some of the most significant challenges in Scotland today. The charity is based within Buckhaven Baptist Church and was established in 2016 in response to increasing food poverty and financial hardship within the community. And we are looking for someone that wants to expand there knowledge and be able to help themselves and others to bring a positive approach to the community and someone that wants to learn Food Hygiene and First Aid and other certificates for themselves, we are a small group of volunteers that mix well with the service users that come each week.  However, the support offered goes far beyond food. So please come and join our thriving team.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Skills Just wanting People that want to learn more about what goes on in Buckhaven and who are wanting to interact with Clients in a very friendly atmosphere.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe Have policies and procedures that we want all to read and adhere to, and if they want Food Hygiene, and first Aid and ongoing issues that we would keep all upto date with.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis post for you will be in the hall of Buckhaven Baptist Church, or in the Kitchen within the Building, or in the food Pantry within the Hallway.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThe Expenses will be Paid at the end of each Month",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
