            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000As4CAYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000As4CAYAZ/activities-and-events-volunteer-beath-high-school",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-24",
                    "title": "Activities and Events Volunteer -Beath High School",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nFancy helping at your local community centre, gaining skills and volunteering in a role tailored for you? The Activities and Events Volunteer typically supports the Community Use team in delivering activities to people, as part of the local programme on offer. The role is front-facing and may include engaging with individuals and groups (both children and adults) under the supervision of Community Use staff, as they lead and deliver activities.\r\n\r\nThe volunteer will:\r\n•\tAbide by Fife Council policies and procedures\r\n•\tBehave in a respectful manner, acting as a role model\r\n•\tHelp staff to set up equipment and areas for delivering activities and events\r\n•\tBe part of planning and programming Community Use activities\r\n•\tGet involved and/or facilitate activities\r\n•\tCommunicate well with both young people and adults\r\n•\tAssist with collection of entry fees, where required\r\n•\tComplete register/recording sheets, where required\r\n•\tAttend relevant training as and when required\r\n•\tPotentially help to serve drinks/snacks\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly, approachable, keen to help, learn and able to communicate with all members of the public.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe volunteer will be given a site induction at the venue. They will be given training around the activities they are supporting and the duties required. There will be opportunity to tailor the role toward the volunteer's skills and interests. Ongoing training to be offered as required and when available.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBeath High School, Cowdenbeath which is accessible by both public and private transport. \r\nPositions available at other locations in Fife\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nYes - Transport related costs will be calculated as follows: - - public transport costs up to the current cost of an East of Scotland DayRider Ticket - mileage costs @ 0.45p per mile - up to the current cost of an East of Scotland DayRider ticket.",
