        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008ndM7AAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008ndM7AAI/diabetes-scotland",
            "name": "Diabetes Scotland",
            "description": "We are Diabetes UK and it’s our mission to tackle diabetes, day in and day out, until it can do no harm.\r\n\r\nIt’s why we campaign for better care, give support in times of need and fund ground-breaking research into new treatments and a cure. \r\n\r\nDiabetes doesn’t stop, so neither do we.",
            "website": "https://www.diabetes.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC039136"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IIBAjYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IIBAjYAP/fundraising-volunteer-west-of-scotland-fundraising-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-04-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-07",
                    "title": "Fundraising Volunteer (West of Scotland Fundraising Volunteer)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nMake a difference in your community\r\n\r\nThe Fundraising Volunteer role works in partnership with the Community Fundraiser and local supporters to help increase fundraising income across the region. Volunteers support this work by attending local events, promoting fundraising activities, and acting as an ambassador for Diabetes UK within the local community.\r\n\r\nThe Community Fundraiser is responsible for developing income across their geographical area, with a strong focus on supporting volunteer fundraisers, regional corporate partners, and local fundraising groups. Fundraising Volunteers play an important role in extending this support and strengthening community engagement.\r\n\r\nFundraising Volunteers will be asked to provide practical support across a range of community‑based and supporter engagement activities.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo prior experience required — full training provided\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided to all volunteers. All our volunteers will get a general induction to Diabetes Scotland – covering safeguarding, who we are, values and mission – and further to that they will all receive role specific training to begin their roles. Ongoing through their time with us we will identify, source and deliver training to our volunteers on a number of topics. Our volunteering team will arrange and conduct 1-2-1’s with the volunteers on a regular basis to check in and provide support.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThis role is flexible and offered on an as‑and‑when‑required basis, making it ideal for volunteers who need adaptable involvement.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVarious locations across the West of Scotland.",
