                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000II4PQYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000II4PQYA1/impact-volunteer-impact-volunteer-scotland",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-02",
                    "title": "Impact Volunteer (Impact Volunteer Scotland)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nImpact volunteering is perfect for busy people who’d like to get involved and help Diabetes Scotland but don’t have much time to give. You’ll be helping us by carrying out quick activities when you get a few moments to spare that make a big difference to people with diabetes.\r\nA great benefit of being an Impact Volunteer in Scotland is that you can do it at any time or anywhere. Even the smallest actions can make a big positive difference to people with diabetes in your local area.\r\nOur Impact Volunteer Scotland role is designed to be flexible and independent, with volunteers completing short tasks each month sent to you online with no face‑to‑face meet‑ups or local volunteer manager. However, if any opportunities come up locally that could support our work, we may get in touch to see if you’d like to be involved\r\nWhy we want you\r\nWe are Diabetes UK. Our vision is a world where diabetes can do no harm. We’re leading the fight against the UK's biggest and fastest-growing health crisis. And it's a fight that involves us all – sharing knowledge and taking on diabetes together.\r\nWhat you will be doing\r\nEach month we will send you a few different tasks that you can choose to take part in, so this can be a varied role.\r\nLet us know what is happening in your area that we could be involved with\r\nSupport Diabetes UK campaigns\r\nTaking leaflets and posters along to local community venues such as libraries and community centres\r\nLiking and sharing posts on social media to help us reach more people\r\nThe skills you need\r\nYou don’t need any, just be excited to get involved\r\nYou need to have access to a smart phone or tablet/laptop/computer\r\nYou’ll need to be 16 or over. If you’re under 18 we’ll need the consent of your parent or guardian before you can start.\r\nWhat's in it for you\r\nGet involved with our work, even if you are busy\r\nYou get to make a difference to people living with diabetes\r\nWe’ll offer you the chance to learn and develop and you’ll hear about other volunteer roles with us.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCommunity Based",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
