                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IIBdmYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IIBdmYAH/scotland-family-group-committee-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-02",
                    "title": "Scotland Family Group Committee Member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAdjusting to the knowledge that you or a family member has diabetes takes time and it's often helpful to meet other people who have been through a similar situation. Our network of local groups can offer understanding, help and support at an important time. They are based in the community and are run by a committee of dedicated volunteers, each having different skills and experience.\r\nCommittee members are essential to helping the group run smoothly, from supporting group meetings to helping advertise the group in the local area. There is something for everyone to get involved.\r\nWhy we want you\r\nWe have an incredible network of local groups who support people in their local community living with diabetes. Our groups rely on having people to help them complete their work in a variety of different ways, be it helping to run a raffle at a meeting or helping organise promotion for the group in their local area. This role is flexible and varies between each group, however committee members are essential to helping the group run smoothly.\r\nWhat you will be doing\r\nWorking with the rest of the committee to plan and coordinate the group’s activities\r\nSupport the group to run events and hold meetings in the local area\r\nHelp to plan and identify new opportunities for the group\r\nHelp out at group meetings, for example welcoming people or helping to serve refreshments\r\nIdentify new places for the group to advertise\r\nHelp to run awareness stalls across the local area to raise the profile of the group and Diabetes UK\r\nThe skills you need\r\nGood organisational skills and the ability to work as part of a team\r\nGood communication and listening skills\r\nThe ability to motivate others and involve them in the work of the group\r\nWhat's in it for you\r\nThe opportunity to be part of reaching and supporting more people living with diabetes\r\nInduction and training\r\nRegular communication with Diabetes UK point of contact\r\nOpportunity to meet and network with other volunteers\r\nThe opportunity to learn new skills\n\n## Travel details\n\nCommunity Based",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IIBdmYAH#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Scotland Family Group Committee Member",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.diabetes.org.uk/opportunities/112429-scotland-family-group-committee-member-glasgow-family-group-2026-04-13/apply/%5B168776%5D#",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16",
