            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hw685YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hw685YAB/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-23",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWould you like to use your skills and experience to make a real difference?\r\nHomeland Trust-Fife is an award-winning independent charity based in Lundin-Links.  It provides high-quality, accessible holiday accommodation for people with disabilities, long-term health conditions and life-limiting illnesses, together with their families, friends and carers.  It also runs the Paxton Centre, a welcoming community hub offering a café, therapies, activities, room hire and volunteering opportunities. \r\nHomelands Trust-Fife is looking for enthusiastic new Trustees to help guide the charity through its next chapter.  As a Trustee, you will help shape strategy, support good governance and contribute to decisions that protect and develop its services. \r\nYou do not need previous Trustee experience, Homelands Trust-Fife welcomes people from different backgrounds who can bring fresh ideas, useful skills, lived experience or strong links to the local community.  You will receive a helpful induction and support from fellow Trustees and staff.\n\n## Experience required\n\nHomelands Trust-Fife welcomes people from all walks of life who can bring different skills, perspectives and experiences to its board.  Previous Trustee experience is not essential, as induction and support will be provided. \r\nPeople with experience in hospitality or tourism, law, finance, fundraising, community engagement, business or organisational development would be particularly welcome.  Lived experience of disability, long-term health conditions or caring would also be especially valuable.  Trustees should share Homelands Trust-Fife's values and be willing to give the time and commitment needed for the role.  They should be able to work as part of a team, listen to different viewpoints, contribute constructively to discussions and decisions, and act in the best interest of the charity and the people we support.\n\n## Training details\n\nTrustees will be invited to visit Homeland for a full tour of the accessible holiday accommodation and the new Paxton Centre with members of the staff team.  This will provide an opportunity to learn more about the services, facilities and the people supported by the charity. \r\nThey will receive an induction covering the Homelands Trust-Fife, the role and responsibilities of a charity Trustee, and relevant polices and governance information.  New Trustees will be guided and supported by existing Board members and the staff team.  Ongoing further support and training will be provided as required.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTrustee meetings are normally held approximately every six weeks at 5.30pm on a Tuesday at the Paxton Centre, Homelands Trust-Fife 14a Links Road Lundin Links, KY8 6AT.  Trustees can also attend meeting remotely.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport receipts can be reimbursed.  Mileage paid at the HMRC approved rate of 55p per mile.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hw685YAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Trustee",
                        "description": "Homelands Trust-Fife welcomes people from all walks of life who can bring different skills, perspectives and experiences to its board.  Previous Trustee experience is not essential, as induction and support will be provided. \r\nPeople with experience in hospitality or tourism, law, finance, fundraising, community engagement, business or organisational development would be particularly welcome.  Lived experience of disability, long-term health conditions or caring would also be especially valuable.  Trustees should share Homelands Trust-Fife's values and be willing to give the time and commitment needed for the role.  They should be able to work as part of a team, listen to different viewpoints, contribute constructively to discussions and decisions, and act in the best interest of the charity and the people we support.",
