        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nbIKAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nbIKAAY/glasgow-wood-recycling",
            "name": "Glasgow Wood Recycling",
            "description": "The GWRP aims to provide a wood recycling service that diverts waste wood from landfill and reduces our impact on the enviroment .\n\nThrough this activity we aim to create quality volunteer and training opportunities that advance citizenship and help people move in to employment.",
            "website": "https://www.glasgowwoodrecycling.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038772"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EnvironmentRecycling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Environment / Recycling"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HrptpYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HrptpYAB/help-keep-valuable-timber-out-of-landfill-volunteer-delivery-collections-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-03",
                    "title": "Help Keep Valuable Timber Out of Landfill – Volunteer Delivery & Collections Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHelp Keep Valuable Timber Out of Landfill – Volunteer Delivery & Collections Assistant\n\n## Description\n\nHelp keep valuable timber out of landfill while supporting deliveries that make a real difference across Glasgow.\n\nMake a practical difference every day. Join our friendly van team helping rescue valuable timber from landfill, deliver handcrafted products and support one of Glasgow&#39;s leading environmental social enterprises. With full training, flexible weekday volunteering and the chance to gain practical skills while staying active, you&#39;ll make a real difference to both the community and the environment.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nGlasgow Wood Recycling is an award-winning social enterprise and charity established in 2007. We are committed to reducing the amount of wood needlessly going to landfill by finding creative, sustainable and socially inclusive ways to reuse this valuable natural resource. Every year, we rescue tonnes of timber, transform it into high-quality products and create opportunities that benefit both people and the environment.\n\nVolunteers are at the heart of everything we do. Whether you have previous experience or not, all you need is enthusiasm, a willingness to get involved and a desire to make a positive difference.\n\nAs a Volunteer Delivery &amp; Collections Assistant, you&#39;ll support our van team with deliveries of finished products and collections of reclaimed timber from homes, businesses and construction sites across Glasgow and the surrounding area. This is a varied, hands-on role that&#39;s ideal for someone who enjoys being active, working outdoors and being part of a friendly team.\n\nWhat will I be doing?\n\nAs part of our delivery and collections team you will:\n\n\n\tHelp organise deliveries and safely load the van before each journey.\n\tAssist the driver with deliveries to customers across Glasgow.\n\tEnsure delivery paperwork is completed and signed by customers.\n\tCollect waste timber from construction sites for recycling and reuse.\n\tHelp unload and return reclaimed timber to our South Street site for sorting and grading.\n\tSupport the Yard &amp; Warehouse team when not out on deliveries.\n\tFollow all health and safety procedures, including safe manual handling practices.\n\tWear the PPE provided and help maintain a safe working environment.\n\n\nThis role is physically active and involves regular lifting, carrying and working outdoors, making it well suited to someone who enjoys practical, hands-on volunteering.\n\nTraining and Support\n\nNo previous experience is required. Before you begin, we&#39;ll make sure you feel confident and supported by providing:\n\n\n\tFull induction and role-specific training.\n\tManual handling and moving &amp; handling training.\n\tAll necessary PPE.\n\tOngoing guidance and support from our experienced and friendly staff team.\n\tOpportunities to develop practical, teamwork and customer service skills.\n\n\nWhen can I volunteer?\n\nWe have volunteer opportunities available:\n\n\n\tMonday to Thursday: 9:00am &ndash; 4:00pm\n\tFriday: 9:00am &ndash; 3:00pm\n\n\nWe&#39;re happy to be flexible and will work with you to agree a volunteering pattern that suits both you and the organisation.\n\nWhat happens after I apply?\n\nIf you&#39;re interested, please click the Apply button below (available when logged in and registered).\n\nOnce we receive your application, a member of the Glasgow Wood team will contact you by email or telephone to discuss the role, answer any questions and explain the next steps in the recruitment process.\n\nIf you haven&#39;t heard from the organisation within 5 working days, we recommend contacting them using the details provided on the opportunity. Please also check your junk or spam folder in case their email has been filtered. If you&#39;re still unable to make contact, you&#39;re welcome to get in touch with Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org for further assistance.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThis can be quite a physically demanding role as there is a lot of carrying timber involved.  We need people who are willing to learn new skills, meet new people and get involved in a team.\nNo previous experience is essential. They particularly welcome people who are:\n\n•\tFriendly and reliable.\n•\tPhysically able to assist with lifting (following safe techniques).\n•\tHappy working as part of a team.\n•\tInterested in sustainability and helping the local community.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThere are several buses that go along Dumbarton Road which is a 5 - 10 min walk from us.  There is no train station near us but you can get a bus from Partick train station along to Whiteinch.  There are loads of parking spaces for drivers and we have a bike shed for cyclists.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers get travel expenses and lunch money.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
