            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HMc01YAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HMc01YAD/sporting-memories-club-session-facilitators-supporters",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-14",
                    "title": "Sporting Memories Club Session Facilitators & Supporters",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you like to talk? Do you like to talk about sport? \r\nSport Aberdeen has partnered with Sporting Memories Foundation Scotland to launch new social clubs in Aberdeen, and we are seeking friendly volunteers to facilitate and help support the sessions. Our Sporting Memories community clubs support adults who want to meet up with likeminded people to reconnect and reminisce about sport.\r\nOur dementia-friendly clubs welcome local people, who may have chronic health conditions and/or are socially isolated, to meet up once a week to share their stories and enjoy inclusive activities with good company. \r\nSo, if you like to chat, can communicate well with others and have a good sense of humour, we want to hear from you! \r\nWe are looking for facilitators to ‘chair’ the group and supporters to help the sessions run smoothly. From leading a quiz to making tea, we welcome volunteers from all ages and backgrounds (sports fan or not!) because the most important quality is to encourage all club members to feel welcome, get involved and have fun!   \r\nNo experience required and full training, materials and support provided throughout. Volunteers can also claim expenses if they need to travel to the club (mileage, bus or train fare).\r\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to make a real difference to the wellbeing of club members while having a good bit of banter. \r\nYou can choose to volunteer at the club at:\r\n•\tNorthfield Community Centre, Byron Square, Aberdeen AB16 7LL on Wednesdays 10.30am – 12.00pm\r\nor\r\n•\tGreyhope Community Hub, Tullos Circle, Aberdeen AB11 8HD on Tuesdays 11.00am- 12.30pm\r\nTo find out more, contact Volunteer Coordinator Liz Price by emailing liz.price@sportingmemories.uk or fill in a Volunteer Enquiry Form at www.sportingmemories.uk/volunteer-form/ and someone will get back to you.\n\n## Description\n\nDo you like to talk? Do you like to talk about sport? \r\n\r\nSport Aberdeen has partnered with Sporting Memories Foundation Scotland to launch new social clubs in Aberdeen, and we are seeking friendly volunteers to facilitate and help support the sessions. Our Sporting Memories community clubs support adults who want to meet up with likeminded people to reconnect and reminisce about sport.\r\n\r\nOur dementia-friendly clubs welcome local people, who may have chronic health conditions and/or are socially isolated, to meet up once a week to share their stories and enjoy inclusive activities with good company. \r\n\r\nSo, if you like to chat, can communicate well with others and have a good sense of humour, we want to hear from you! \r\n\r\nWe are looking for facilitators to ‘chair’ the group and supporters to help the sessions run smoothly. From leading a quiz to making tea, we welcome volunteers from all ages and backgrounds (sports fan or not!) because the most important quality is to encourage all club members to feel welcome, get involved and have fun!   \r\n\r\nNo experience required and full training, materials and support provided throughout. Volunteers can also claim expenses if they need to travel to the club (mileage, bus or train fare).\r\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to make a real difference to the wellbeing of club members while having a good bit of banter. \r\n\r\nYou can choose to volunteer at the club at:\r\n•\tNorthfield Community Centre, Byron Square, Aberdeen AB16 7LL on Wednesdays 10.30am – 12.00pm\r\nor\r\n•\tGreyhope Community Hub, Tullos Circle, Aberdeen AB11 8HD on Tuesdays 11.00am- 12.30pm\r\n\r\nTo find out more, contact Volunteer Coordinator Liz Price by emailing liz.price@sportingmemories.uk or fill in a Volunteer Enquiry Form at www.sportingmemories.uk/volunteer-form/ and someone will get back to you.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training and support is provided to all volunteers, which includes\r\n* induction to Sporting Memories\r\n* An initial phone call to have a chat about volunteering with us.\r\n* An online training session regarding planning and running a club (3 hours).\r\n* Fortnightly online sessions where you can meet other volunteers and be supported.\r\n* Volunteers can claim expenses if they need to travel to the club (mileage, bus or train fares).\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nYou can choose to volunteer at the club at:\r\n•\tNorthfield Community Centre, Byron Square, Aberdeen AB16 7LL on Wednesdays 10.30am – 12.00pm\r\nor\r\n•\tGreyhope Community Hub, Tullos Circle, Aberdeen AB11 8HD on Tuesdays 11.00am- 12.30pm\n\n## Travel details\n\nYou can choose to volunteer at the club at:\r\n•\tNorthfield Community Centre, Byron Square, Aberdeen AB16 7LL on Wednesdays 10.30am – 12.00pm\r\nor\r\n•\tGreyhope Community Hub, Tullos Circle, Aberdeen AB11 8HD on Tuesdays 11.00am- 12.30pm\r\n\r\n\r\nVolunteers can claim expenses if they need to travel to a club (mileage, bus or train fares).\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers can claim expenses if they need to travel to the club (mileage, bus or train fares). Expenses are paid monthly or in advance if necessary.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
