                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eIzcAAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eIzcAAE/walk-leader",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Walk Leader",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWant to be involved in your local community getting people active?  We are looking for people to lead health walks as part of the Walk Aberdeen programme.  Full training is provided and this is a great opportunity to be active in your local area. \r\n\r\nFor further details please contact: Brian Harrison (Health Walks Coordinator):  E. bharrison@sportaberdeen.co.uk / Tel. 01224 047928 / Mobile 07719501361\n\n## Description\n\nWant to be involved in your local community getting people active?  We are looking for people to lead health walks as part of the Walk Aberdeen programme.  Full training is provided in the form of a one day fully recognised walk leader training course.  On completion of this the volunteer will have the opportunity to support or lead walking groups in your local community, encouraging others to get active and enjoy some social exercise. \r\n\r\nThis position is a great opportunity to be active in your local area. Full support is available to assist you taking on this role and gradually build the confidence to be a walk leader.\r\n\r\nAll volunteers are greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor further details please contact: Brian Harrison (Health Walks Coordinator):  E. bharrison@sportaberdeen.co.uk / Tel. 01224 047928 / Mobile 07719501361\n\n## Experience required\n\nOutgoing, enjoys being active, enjoys meeting people and taking responsibility.\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support and training is provided to all volunteers. Includes one day fully recognised (by the British Heart Foundation/Paths for All) walk leader training course. Full ongoing support is also available through the Development Officer.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible to suit volunteer.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOpportunities across Aberdeen City",
