        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZ7QAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZ7QAAU/dundee-age-concern",
            "name": "Dundee Age Concern",
            "description": "Age Concern Dundee exists to promote the wellbeing and social inclusion of older people by: identifying their changing needs, through consultation with them and their carers; and active involvement in policy planning and development of services. We provide day care for older people in our purpose built centre located at Fiveways, Caird Avenue. We provide clients with companionship in a safe and secure environment and provide a variety of activities.",
            "website": "https://www.agescotland.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC013975"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Equality",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Equality"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000AK7pBYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000AK7pBYAT/boardtrustee",
                    "publishStart": "2025-06-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Board/Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAs a Board Member having a shared interest in the welfare of the older generation in our community, you have the opportunity to share/gain knowledge, form links in the community helping to continue to develop the service.\n\n## Description\n\nAs a board trustee, you will actively contribute to board meetings, help to monitor and implement  decisions taken at the meetings. You will help to ensure the organisation complies with its governing document, charity law, etc.\r\n\r\nYou will provide leadership to support the Centre manager, You will help implement the organisational plan and business strategy. You will help review/agree any changes to the organisation. You will help monitor a regular and robust overview of principle risks facing the charity and manage any necessary actions.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communicator. respectful and understanding regarding the work Dundee Age Concern undertakes.\n\n## Training details\n\nAttendance at board meetings and networking.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDundee Age Concern, Caird Avenue, Dundee;\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nBus receipts. Mileage payable at £0.26 per mile.\n\n## Taster details\n\nThe opportunity to attend a board meeting",
