                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pv9PcAAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pv9PcAAJ/support-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Support Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe need outgoing, compassionate, fun loving and caring individuals to suppport our elderly clients get \r\nbusy living life to the fullest.\n\n## Description\n\nOur clients are pretty wonderful and incredibly special to us. Each has their own unique personality and reasons for attending our centre. Your role itself will be about supporting our clients achieve their outcomes. You will need to be a good communicator, (especially listening), and patient with it on some occasions. You will need a positive outlook, good at working in a team, innovate in your thinking, fun loving and care about the happiness of our clients. \r\n\r\nActivities based in the Fiveways centre include, music and dancing, dominoes, bingo, cards, gardening, hangman, play your cards right, painting and craftwork, baking, needlework, knitting, boccia, reminiscing, digital storytelling. Out with the centre we visit V&A, the DCA, Verdant works, McManus Galleries, garden centres, local parks, days out to coastal towns or even to a local bistro/pub for a bite to eat. At Christmas there is the Christmas parties and the obligatory pantomime.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou will need to be a good communicator, outgoing, open minded, a team player, patient, hard working, committed and reliable. Experience or knowledge in dementia, Care About Physical Activity in the \r\nelderly, and acitivity coordinating would be good but not essential.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe volunteer will receive induction training and regular support from the centre coordinator and the Manager\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nPotential volunteers can work between 1 - 5 days per week, preferably 10am - 3pm, however there is scope for afternoon work from 12noon - 3pm.\n\n## Travel details\n\nFiveways day centre, and various places of interest across the city\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nOur charity will reimburse bus tickets and fuel costs at 26p per mile.\n\n## Taster details\n\nPotential volunteers can attend at a time of mutual agreement to \r\nexperience service delivery at the 'Fiveways' centre.",
