                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000Fs1zlAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000Fs1zlAAB/assistant-sports-coach",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Assistant Sports Coach",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nInterested in sports coaching? The Sports Development Team of Leisure & Culture Dundee provide coaching sessions across the city for children and adults.  These sessions can provide excellent opportunities for volunteers wishing to develop their coaching and organisational skills within a sports setting.\n\n## Description\n\nThe Sports Development Team has priority sports to develop across the city.  These priority sports are currently athletics, football, gymnastics, netball, tennis and trampolining.  The team deliver term-time classes across the city in Leisure & Culture Dundee facilities (DISC, Douglas Sports Centre, Grove Swim & Sport, Harris Swim & Sport, Lynch Sports Centre, St Paul’s Swim & Sport) as well as at community centres and schools.  There are also holiday programmes and events throughout the year.  Volunteers can participate in programmes as assistant coaches, working alongside qualified coaches and receiving support from sports development officers.  By providing volunteering opportunities within these programmes, the Sports Development Team aim to provide experience, development opportunities and increase employability.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers should have an interest in sport, however, no previous coaching experience is required.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers can attend induction training and if there are certificated courses that would benefit the volunteer and Leisure & Culture Dundee these will be considered.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nPlease state number of hours, minimum time commitment and whether it is weekly, monthly, etc., i.e. 4 hours per week for a six month commitment.\nClasses are generally 1 hour in duration so this would be the minimum time commitment per week.  Volunteers will not be used as part of ratios so there is no requirement for a set period of time.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteers will be responsible for their own travel to venues.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport costs reimbursed on production of tickets purchased. \r\nMileage paid at 45p/mile.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
