                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000004WE7CYAW",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000004WE7CYAW/basketball-coach",
                    "publishStart": "2024-07-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-20",
                    "title": "Basketball Coach",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for someone fun, motivated and enthusiastic about coaching basketball with primary aged children.\n\n## Description\n\nAcross schools in Dundee, Active Schools provide extra-curricular activities for children in primary and secondary schools. Focusing on sports and physical activity this can be children’s first experience of sports. \r\n\r\nWith a focus on getting the inactive active, we are keen to provide more children with the opportunity to play basketball within the Grove Academy Primary Cluster (Eastern PS, Barnhill PS, Craigebarns PS, or Forthill PS). \r\n\r\nWe are looking for keen coaches to deliver sessions of basketball.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPrevious coaching experience in basketball\r\nWorking with children\r\nAble to lead as an individual\r\nPlan and deliver sessions\r\nMotivated and enthusiastic about getting children active\n\n## Training details\n\nCoaches will go through an introduction and followed up by regular catch ups to ensure the individuals are supported. \r\nOpportunities to attend courses will be on offer to upskill the volunteer.\n\n## Travel details\n\nGrove Academy.\n\n## Taster details\n\nWe can get the volunteer along to another session in which they can shadow or just observe",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000004WE7CYAW#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Basketball Coach",
                        "description": "Previous coaching experience in basketball\r\nWorking with children\r\nAble to lead as an individual\r\nPlan and deliver sessions\r\nMotivated and enthusiastic about getting children active",
