                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000004WLOnYAO",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000004WLOnYAO/assisted-needs-sports-coach",
                    "publishStart": "2024-07-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-20",
                    "title": "Assisted Needs Sports Coach",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for keen sports coaches to support us with our targeted projects for children with an additional support needs to be more physically active.\n\n## Description\n\nAcross schools in Dundee, Active Schools provide extra-curricular activities for children in primary and secondary schools. Focusing on sports and physical activity this can be children’s first experience of sports. \r\n\r\nWith a focus on getting the inactive active, we are keen to provide children with an additional support need more opportunities for being physically active. With support from our staff we are looking for keen coaches to deliver sessions that include ASN children. This can be sport specific or even just fun games, we aim to give children opportunities they wouldn’t \r\nnormal get access to.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPrevious experience of coaching/leading sports sessions is desirable but not essential.\r\nHaving previous experience coaching or in a sporting environment would definitely help the candidates but not \r\nessential. \r\nSimply willing to learn and help others is all that matters.\n\n## Training details\n\nCoaches will go through an introduction and followed up by regular catch ups to ensure the individuals are supported. A 6 week settling period will allow the candidates to build relationships with the participants and give them a better understanding.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVarious schools and community clubs across Dundee\n\n## Taster details\n\nWe can get you along to current session to give you a better understanding of it \r\nall",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
