            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008XLx7YAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008XLx7YAG/befriender-children-and-young-people",
                    "publishStart": "2025-02-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Befriender - Children and Young People",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteers to provide 1:1 (or 2:1 support alongside another worker/volunteer) to children and young people (up to the age of 18) out and about in the local community to help improve their wellbeing, help them to engage with activities and to be a listening ear. Befriending support can be weekly or fortnightly for around 2 hours per session. We look for a 6 months commitment for this role.\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteers to provide quality 1:1 time on a regular basis to help children and young people to access leisure and recreational opportunities in the local community and to help improve wellbeing. Activities can include going for a walk or going to a local park, doing some arts and crafts, local museums and going for a chat. \r\n\r\nThis quality time would allow a space for children and young people to talk about how they are feeling as well as a time for them to have time in their local community. Some of the befriender roles offered can also be on a 2:1 basis alongside another volunteer or worker which is a great opportunity for volunteers to build up confidence before lone working. Some befriender roles may take place in a school setting depending on the need of the child and may take place during school hours. We occassionally have befriender roles to help support a parent with their children to build up confidence in the local community. \r\n\r\nOur service that is looking for volunteers to support children, young people and parents is the Dundee Child and Family Support Service. This services supports children and young people with additional support needs.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers do not need to have previous experience supporting children and young people with additional support needs but if a volunteer does have previous experience it would be welcomed. We are looking for volunteers who are motivated, reliable and want to make a difference to children, young people and families lives.\n\n## Training details\n\nProvided with an induction process that covers: child protection, confidentiality, and professional boundaries (to name some). There are various training opportunities outside the induction and volunteers are also supported by the volunteer coordinator with regular supervision provided.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDundee.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMileage within Dundee Boundaries and Bus Travel within Dundee Boundaries. Receipts need to be provided when claiming.",
