                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ASQBVYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ASQBVYA5/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2025-06-19",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAdvocating Together support people with learning disabilities and autistic people to speak up and be heard. As a trustee, you will play a crucial role in guiding our organisation towards achieving its goals and ensuring its growth.\n\n## Description\n\nAdvocating Together support people with learning disabilities and autistic people to speak up and be heard. As a trustee, you will play a crucial role in guiding our organisation towards achieving its goals and ensuring its growth.\r\n\r\nA Charity Trustees role is to ensure the organisation is operating effectively. As part of a board, you would be responsible for the organisations governance ensuring that Advocating Together benefits our members and is working to our governing document.\r\n \r\nOur meetings take place every 6-8 weeks, on a Wednesday afternoon, including our AGM. Trustees would be expected to offer their time to the organisation, when needed, outside of board meetings.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAn interest in advocacy and human rights\r\nAwareness of issues which may affect our members\r\nGood communication and listening skills\r\nPatience and empathy\r\nExcellent team working\r\nConfidence to speak up and to ask questions\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction and ongoing support will be provided by our Chairperson, Team Support Manager, and fellow Trustees.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe are located on Ryehill Lane, adjacent to Perth Road Dundee.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel to and from the office will be paid if coming by bus or by car (45p/mile)",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ASQBVYA5#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Trustee",
                        "description": "An interest in advocacy and human rights\r\nAwareness of issues which may affect our members\r\nGood communication and listening skills\r\nPatience and empathy\r\nExcellent team working\r\nConfidence to speak up and to ask questions",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ASQBVYA5/trustee?#modal_register_a0gQD00000ASQBVYA5",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
