                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HdH5dYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HdH5dYAF/womans-group-self-advocacy-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-04",
                    "title": "Woman’s Group Self-advocacy Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFemale volunteer required to help facilitate a woman’s self-advocacy group for people with learning disabilities and autistic people.\n\n## Description\n\nWe’re currently looking for volunteers to support a woman’s group for people with learning disabilities and autistic people. Topics discussed in the group could be mental health, physical health, local services, national campaigns. Groups might also invite in guest speakers. The group help decide the topics.\r\n\r\nThis role involves providing direct peer support to our woman's group where a woman is essential to the effectiveness of the service. This is to ensure confidentiality and trust to members of the group.\r\n\r\nThis group will run once a month and require approximately 3 hours of volunteering a month. You will work with staff to prepare discussions and activities for the group and deliver them to the group, or support guest speakers visiting the group. These groups allow our members to speak out about a variety of topics that are important to them. We do not offer advice but can give members information or signpost them.\n\n## Experience required\n\nInduction training is provided, but a volunteer should be confident in facilitating a group and have an interest in advocacy and rights. Volunteers should value inclusion and equity.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining covers topics such as advocacy, communication, and health and safety.\n\n## Travel details\n\n13 Ryehill Lane, Dundee, DD1 4DD\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses will be reimbursed\n\n## Taster details\n\nA visit to one of our self-advocacy groups can be arranged.",
