            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ1QAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eJ1QAAU/listening-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Listening Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTo help us provide a 24-hour, 365 days a year befriending service to those going through crisis.\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteers are required to do four duties per month, one of which will be an overnight duty.  They listen to those who contact Samaritans, either on the telephone, by email or by visit.  However, as volunteers run the branch, many take on extra work.  Samaritans work is strictly voluntary.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAbility to listen.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining provided over a  month period\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n4 hours per week\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Samaritan Centre, 6 Old Glamis Road, Dundee.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses (Public transport or mileage at 25p per mile) paid upon submission of a claim form.",
