        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZ89AAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZ89AAE/headway-dundee-angus",
            "name": "Headway Dundee & Angus",
            "description": "The aim of Headway Tayside is to provide support to acquired brain injury survivors through social meetings and activities. This enables members to interact with people who have been through a similar trauma. The groups help to build confidence and allow members to re-integrate into their communities and society.",
            "website": "https://www.headway.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC008890"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Carers",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Carers"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SensoryImpairment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000061H3NYAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000061H3NYAU/committee-treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2024-10-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Committee Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe treasurer plays a vital role in ensuring Headway Dundee & Angus remains financially stable and maintains the longevity of the group.\n\n## Description\n\nHeadway Dundee & Angus aims to support and provide information for those people with a brain injury, their families, and carers.\r\n\r\nThe treasurer plays a vital role in ensuring Headway Dundee & Angus remains financially stable and maintains the longevity of the group. \r\n\r\nDuties: overseeing, and presenting budgets, accounts, and financial statements for approval. \r\nBeing assured that the financial resources of the organisation meet its present and future needs. Ensuring that the charity has an appropriate reserves policy. \r\nThe preparation and presentation of financial reports to the board. \r\nEnsuring that appropriate accounting procedures and controls are in place.\r\nMonitoring the organisation's investment activity and ensuring its consistency with the organisation's policies and legal responsibilities. \r\nEnsuring the organisation's compliance with legislation. \r\nEnsuring that the accounts are prepared and disclosed in the form required by funders.\n\n## Experience required\n\nCommitment to the organisation. Willingness to devote the necessary time and effort. Good, independent judgment. Ability to think creatively. Willingness to speak their mind.\r\nUnderstanding and acceptance of the legal duties, responsibilities, and liabilities of trusteeship. Ability to work effectively as a member of a team. Financial understanding and some previous experience (if possible).\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel Expenses reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000061H3NYAU#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Committee Treasurer",
                        "description": "Commitment to the organisation. Willingness to devote the necessary time and effort. Good, independent judgment. Ability to think creatively. Willingness to speak their mind.\r\nUnderstanding and acceptance of the legal duties, responsibilities, and liabilities of trusteeship. Ability to work effectively as a member of a team. Financial understanding and some previous experience (if possible).",
