                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000061A9zYAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000061A9zYAE/committee-member",
                    "publishStart": "2024-10-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Committee Member",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nMake a difference to your local community. Develop new and existing skills and gain experience volunteering in a charity. The satisfaction of knowing that you are making a vital difference to those with brain injury.\n\n## Description\n\nHeadway Dundee & Angus aims to support and provide information for those people with a brain injury, their families, and carers. \r\n\r\nAs a Committee Member, you can make a difference to your local community. Develop new and existing skills and gain experience volunteering in a charity. And gain the satisfaction of knowing that you are making a vital difference to those with brain injury.\n\n## Experience required\n\nOutgoing, friendly & proactive.\r\nEnjoy partnership & development work.\r\nApproachable & friendly.\r\nAbility to work on own, using initiative at times.\r\nCommitment to working with compliance, policies & procedures\r\nPerson selected will be required to be passionate about Headway Tayside's aims & objectives\n\n## Training details\n\nBrain Injury training is offered through Headway  UK.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
