        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZ8NAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZ8NAAU/tayside-re-users",
            "name": "Tayside Re-Users",
            "description": "Tayside Re-Users is an environmental reuse and recycling Social Enterprise.  Established in 1995 it diverts unwanted items from landfill for reuse and recycling, offers employment, volunteering and training opportunities to young people and others who struggle to secure work and provides low cost or no cost household items to people on fixed or low incomes.",
            "website": "https://www.taysidereusers.co.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC023578"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EnvironmentRecycling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Environment / Recycling"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ2kAAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eJ2kAAE/van-and-warehouse-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Van and Warehouse Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThis opportunity would be varied as there would be the opportunity to work on the vans, in the warehouse and possibly in our Emporium. Fantastic role working within a supportive team.\n\n## Description\n\nTayside Re-users receives donations from many sources and often these need to be collected - from our Hub, recycling centres, businesses and members of the public. Sold items also need to be delivered to the customer. As a Van & Warehouse Assistant, you help the Van Driver by collecting items from donors and making deliveries to customers. This involves handling heavy items such as furniture or white goods either on or off a van, into storage or into the sales area while keeping areas safe and tidy. You will need a good level of fitness for this role.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly and welcoming manner with the public, ability to work as part of a team. Joinery experience would be beneficial but not essential.  Due to the nature of the role physical strength would be advantage.\n\n## Training details\n\nIn house training will be provided, daily support will be given and training will be given as and when required.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nAvailability 15 - 25 hours per week. Can be discussed - our opening hours are Monday - Friday (9 - 5) and Saturday (10 - 4).\n\n## Travel details\n\nTayside Re-Users, Unit 1 South Dudhope Mill, 75 Douglas Street, Dundee. North of Verdant Works and buses 7, 17, 28, 29, 51, 57 & 59  - stop just up the road on Lochee Road near Smellies Lane.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nDaily/weekly travel expenses will be reimbursed. Lunch allowance £4 per day.",
