                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ2mAAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eJ2mAAE/furniture-repairer-joiner",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Furniture Repairer / Joiner",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTaqyside Re-use Centre believes that it is important to challenge the ideals of our 'throw-away' society and we would like you to help us further this cause by showing that old can be just as good as new.\n\n## Description\n\nTayside Re-Users need volunteers who can fix furniture. Furniture repairers play an important role in ensuring that many items which would otherwise be thrown away are recycled and sold in their shop. If you have a background in furniture repair or joinery, this role is perfect for you! Or come and learn some new skills in sanding, painting and varnishing.\n\n## Experience required\n\nExperienced Repairer/Joiner\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will be  introduced to the team and shown their area of work.   Initial training for the role will be given where appropriate.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nTo be discussed.Weekdays\n\n## Travel details\n\nTayside Re-Users, Unit 1 South Dudhope Mill, 75 Douglas Street, Dundee. North of Verdant Works and buses 7, 17, 28, 29, 51, 57 & 59  - stop just up the road on Lochee Road near Smellies Lane.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nDaily/weekly travel expenses reimbursed. Lunch £4 per day.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
