                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000001BTO5AAO",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000001BTO5AAO/upholsterer",
                    "publishStart": "2022-03-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Upholsterer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThis would be an exciting opportunity to upcycle some of the items instead of them going into landfill. As an environmental charity our aim is to keep as much as we can out of landfill.\n\n## Description\n\nTayside Re-Users try their best to avoid ditching furniture in landfill. Some of the household goods we receive require upholstering to make them suitable for resale in our shop. We have a dedicated area for upholstery but the ideal volunteer would be looking to develop their existing upholstery skills.\n\n## Experience required\n\nUpholstery skills would be required as there is nobody available to carry out training. This role is not largely public facing, however the ability work well as a team would be required.\n\n## Training details\n\nIn house training will be provided, daily support will be given and training will be given as and when required.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n10-15 hours per week. Can be discussed - our opening hours are Monday - Friday (9 - 5) and Saturday (10 - 4).\n\n## Travel details\n\nTayside Re-Users, Unit 1 South Dudhope Mill, 75 Douglas Street, Dundee. North of Verdant Works and buses 7, 17, 28, 29, 51, 57 & 59  - stop just up the road on Lochee Road near Smellies Lane.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nDaily/weekly travel expenses reimbursed. Lunch - £4 per day.",
