                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ2pAAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eJ2pAAE/retail-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2022-03-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Retail Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThis retail opportunity would be working in Tay Treasures which is our shop selling household textiles, clothing, shoes and bric-a-brac.  Working as part of a team, with customers and possibly the opportunity to merchandise.\n\n## Description\n\nTayside Re-users generates income to operate by recycling items and selling them from its warehouse shop in South Dudhope Mill. As a volunteer Retail Assistant, your main duties would include making sure the shop is clean, tidy, stocked up, merchandised-well and customers are dealt with in a friendly manner. You would be responsible for the stock displays, pricing, serving customers or helping with telephone or online enquiries and making sure that there is sufficient stock on display. You will enjoy helping the public and wish to develop good customer service skills.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly and welcoming manner with the public, ability to work as part of a team. Numeracy and literacy skills required for working the till.\n\n## Training details\n\nIn house training will be provided, daily support will be given and training will be given as and when required.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n15-25 hours per week Can be discussed - our opening hours are Monday - Friday (9 - 5) and Saturday (10 - 4).\n\n## Travel details\n\nTayside Re-Users, Unit 1 South Dudhope Mill, 75 Douglas Street, Dundee. North of Verdant Works and buses 7, 17, 28, 29, 51, 57 & 59  - stop just up the road on Lochee Road near Smellies Lane.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nDaily/weekly travel expenses will be reimbursed. Lunch - £4 per day.",
