                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ5FAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eJ5FAAU/bike-repairs",
                    "publishStart": "2022-03-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Bike Repairs",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThis is an opportunity where you could use your current skills, whilst gaining further on the job experience.  Bicycle repairs are carried out on any bikes we have been donated.\n\n## Description\n\nTayside Re-users regularly receives donations of bicycles. Some require repair before they are ready for resale in our shop. We have a dedicated repair area and this has repair equipment and supplies of spare parts. This opportunity would suit someone who has a passion for bikes, experience of bike repairs and able to carry out basic repairs to bikes to give them a new lease of life.\n\n## Experience required\n\nStrong knowledge and experience in bike repairs are required.\n\n## Training details\n\nIn house training will be provided, daily support will be given and training will be given as and when required.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nAvailability 15 - 25 hours per week. Can be discussed - our opening hours are Monday - Friday (9 - 5) and Saturday (10 - 4).\n\n## Travel details\n\nTayside Re-Users, Unit 1 South Dudhope Mill, 75 Douglas Street, Dundee. North of Verdant Works and buses 7, 17, 28, 29, 51, 57 & 59  - stop just up the road on Lochee Road near Smellies Lane.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nDaily/weekly travel expenses reimbursed. Lunch - £4 per day.",
