                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eJADAA2/electrician",
                    "publishStart": "2022-03-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Electrician",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTayside Re-Users believes that it is important to challenge the ideals of our 'throw-away' society by showing that second hand goods are just as acceptable as new and we would like you to help us further this cause by testing and repairing electrical appliances.\n\n## Description\n\nTayside Re-Users believes that it is important to challenge the ideals of our ‘throw-away’ society by showing that second-hand goods are just as acceptable as new ones. We are looking for an experienced electrician to help us by testing and repairing appliances before they are re-sold to the community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou will need some experience of working with electrical appliances for this role.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will be introduced to the team and shown their area of work.   Initial training for the role will be given and any further training will be carried out if required.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n10 - 20 hours per week. To be agreed.Weekdays\n\n## Travel details\n\nTayside Re-Users, Unit 1 South Dudhope Mill, 75 Douglas Street, Dundee. North of Verdant Works and buses 7, 17, 28, 29, 51, 57 & 59  - stop just up the road on Lochee Road near Smellies Lane.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nDaily/weekly travel expenses reimbursed. Lunch - £4 per day.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
