        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZ8eAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZ8eAAE/peoples-trust-for-endangered-species",
            "name": "Peoples Trust for Endangered Species",
            "description": "PTES looks to the future with the hope of preserving wildlife for the future generations to enjoy. We fund scientific research  in the UK and abroad, purchase threatened land, commision surveys and reports and hold symposia and conferences.",
            "website": "http://www.ptes.org/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ3ZAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eJ3ZAAU/wildlife-spotters",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Wildlife Spotters",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you want to actively help with essential conservation work? One of the most valuable ways for you to do this is to take part in a PTES wildlife survey. With the help of volunteers nationwide, these surveys will provide essential information to help us monitor the state of our wildlife and enable us to take action if the results are concerning.\n\n## Description\n\nOur planet is changing. The climate and biodiversity are in crisis. We can turn the tide, but to do so, we need to keep an eye on wildlife and the natural habitats that support it. We’re looking for volunteers to join a citizen science project recording wild mammals in the green spaces of our towns and cities. Whether a squirrel or fox, wood mouse or bat, every sighting is important and goes to building a bigger picture of how wildlife is faring. The online survey provides information on how to recognise the different species on our doorstep, and is part of an active conservation effort. For more information, visit https://ptes.org/get-involved/surveys/\n\n## Experience required\n\nNone.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n1 hours per Week. Minimum Commitment: 8 Week\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe survey can be done at any time of day, from early morning to late evening, and for as long as is convenient. Participants should choose a convenient, local site to survey, such as a garden, park, allotment or other green space. Travel expenses are not paid.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nSurvey sites should be local—a garden, park, allotment or other green space—and travel  expenses are not paid.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ3ZAAU#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Wildlife Spotters",
                        "description": "None.",
                        "commitment": "1 hours per Week. Minimum Commitment: 8 Week",
