        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZ94AAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZ94AAE/monifieth-befriending-scheme-dundee",
            "name": "Monifieth Befriending Scheme (Dundee)",
            "description": "To bring friendship to socially isolated older people and bereaved people of any age living in Monifieth.",
            "website": "https://www.monifiethbefriending.co.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC030685"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Elderly",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Elderly"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FamilySupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Family Support"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ2UAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eJ2UAAU/befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Befriender",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nA number of older people in Monifieth have been identified as lonely or socially isolated. A need has also been identified to provide a befriending service for bereaved people in Monifieth. We require caring people to visit on a one-to-one basis, offering a little quality time not otherwise available.\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteers receive a \"feel good factor\" and a sense of satisfaction helping others, opportunity to give something back to the community, to gain experience which may be useful if later seeking a career in caring. The Friend gains contact with the outside community, befriender visits and spends quality time with user providing stimulation and conversation. The befriender may take the user out, where this might not otherwise be possible.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe main criteria is a caring person who is interested in others and can visit a lonely, isolated older person in Monifieth on a weekly basis for up to 2 hours. This would ideally be a long term commitment of at least 6 months.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining covers confidentiality,boundaries, safety, communication/listening skills, organic impairment, mytha about ageing.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2 hours per week with a minimum commitment of 6 months.Weekdays\n\n## Travel details\n\nIn the home of the older person or bereaved person in Monifieth or on outings within the local community, if the client Friend is physically able to go out.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses reimbursed - bus fares or fuel currently 45p per mile.\n\n## Taster details\n\nPeople interested in volunteering with us would be welcome to come along and meet some of our volunteers at our monthly volunteer meeting on the first Friday of each month. ‘Buddying’ a volunteer may also be arranged.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ2UAAU#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Befriender",
                        "description": "The main criteria is a caring person who is interested in others and can visit a lonely, isolated older person in Monifieth on a weekly basis for up to 2 hours. This would ideally be a long term commitment of at least 6 months.",
                        "commitment": "2 hours per week with a minimum commitment of 6 months.Weekdays",
