                    "skos:prefLabel": "Employment"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Elderly",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Elderly"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IwsTxYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IwsTxYAJ/driver-food-collections",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-26",
                    "title": "Driver – Food Collections",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for volunteer drivers to help collect food donations from supermarkets and other local collection points and bring them back to the Boomerang Centre.\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for volunteer drivers to help collect food donations from supermarkets and other local collection points and bring them back to the Boomerang Centre. Your support will help keep our community larder stocked and make food available to people in our local community.\r\n\r\nThe role involves collecting donations at agreed times, helping load and unload them, and keeping in touch with the team about collections.\r\n\r\nEven helping with one regular collection could make a real difference. As more drivers join us, we can arrange additional collections and increase the support we provide.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for reliable, friendly volunteers with a valid driving licence and access to their own vehicle. You should be comfortable driving locally and handling food donations.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteer drivers will receive an induction to Boomerang Community Centre, including an overview of our services, relevant policies and procedures, and guidance on food collection, safe lifting and handling. Ongoing support will be provided by our staff team, with a named point of contact available for any questions or concerns.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoomerang Centre, 10 Kemback Street, Dundee, DD4 6ET, with travel to local collection points.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMileage for volunteer collections will be reimbursed at 45p per mile. If a change to your vehicle insurance is required for the role, we will cover the cost of that change.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IwsTxYAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Driver – Food Collections",
                        "description": "We are looking for reliable, friendly volunteers with a valid driving licence and access to their own vehicle. You should be comfortable driving locally and handling food donations.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IwsTxYAJ/driver-food-collections?#modal_register_a0gQD00000IwsTxYAJ",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "17",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/AntiPoverty",
