                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhnUyAAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhnUyAAJ/larder-helper",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-24",
                    "title": "Larder Helper",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for volunteers to help our larder volunteers with additional tasks such as collecting donations, stocking shelves, stock rotation and helping those accessing larder.\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for volunteers to help with stocking shelves and stock rotation, helping with the deliveries, collecting donations from supermarkets, helping those accessing the larder, collecting basic information for monitoring purposes and cash handling.\n\n## Experience required\n\nOwn car if collecting donations. Experience or interest in retail work. Interest in helping those at a disadvantage\n\n## Training details\n\nShadowing another volunteer/staff, any other relevant training will be offered.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nweekly. 1-2 hours per session, minimum of 1 session per week\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoomerang Centre, 10 Kemback Street, Dundee DD4 6ET\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses for getting to the centre may be reimbursed and for travel for collecting donations\n\n## Taster details\n\nCan trial one session to see if the role suits",
