                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QhjWBAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QhjWBAAZ/cosy-cafe-helper",
                    "publishStart": "2023-07-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-24",
                    "title": "Cosy Cafe Helper",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for volunteers to help at our Cosy café. The volunteer would assist our Cosy Café Support Worker with making tea/coffee and toast and setting up/clearing up.\n\n## Description\n\nThe volunteer role will involve helping to set up for the Cosy Café opening, serving those attending their tea and toast, chatting to them and signposting elsewhere if needed as well as helping to clear dishes and tidying up at the end of the session. The Cosy Café runs 10-1130 so we would be looking for volunteers to help the Cosy Café Support Worker from 930am-12pm.\n\n## Experience required\n\nExperience or interest in retail work. Interest in helping those at a disadvantage.\n\n## Training details\n\nShadowing another volunteer/staff, any other relevant training will be offered.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nweekly. 1-2 hours per session, minimum of 1 session per week\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoomerang Centre, 10 Kemback Street, Dundee DD4 6ET\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses for getting to the centre may be reimbursed\n\n## Taster details\n\nCan trial one session to see if the role suits.",
