                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "School Savings Collection Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCan you help out at Save By The Bell school savings collections and encourage children and young people to realise the importance of saving their money? www.savebythebell.org\n\n## Description\n\nSave By The Bell is a project that encourages children and young people to develop a savings habit. We run weekly collections in participating primary schools across Dundee, where pupils can deposit money into their savings account. Our trained primary 6/7 pupils act as 'tellers' and are supervised by adult volunteers. We need more adult volunteers to support and monitor our pupils during these collections, helping them to develop their cash handling and numeracy skills. There are positions available in various schools and collections usually last no more than one hour. All volunteers will be required to commit to attending one collection per week and to undergo a Disclosure Scotland check. Support and training will be provided by Save By The Bell staff.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers should be patient, honest, enthusiastic and enjoy working with children. Basic numeracy skills are required and some experience of cash handling would be an advantage. All volunteers must undergo a Disclosure check and provide 2 references.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will be invited to the office for an informal chat. They will be given the opportunity to attend a few collections with SBTB staff and will be shown how to process our forms.Staff are always available to provide support & advice.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nVarious timeslots available in different locations. A minimum of 1 hour per week during school term-time.Weekdays\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe have opportunities in various schools across Dundee.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are paid monthly where volunteers are travelling to collections.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ5fAAE#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "School Savings Collection Assistant",
                        "description": "Volunteers should be patient, honest, enthusiastic and enjoy working with children. Basic numeracy skills are required and some experience of cash handling would be an advantage. All volunteers must undergo a Disclosure check and provide 2 references.",
