        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZ9bAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZ9bAAE/one-world-centre",
            "name": "One World Centre",
            "description": "The objectives of the OWC are to promote Development Education and: a) to enable people to understand the links between their own lives and those of people throughout the world b) to increase understanding of the economic, social, political, cultural and environmental forces which shape all our lives c) to enable people to find ways to bring about change by acting locally to create a more just, peaceful and sustainable world.",
            "website": "https://www.oneworldcentredundee.org.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VupEWAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VupEWAAZ/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2023-06-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe OWC is looking for a young trustee to join our management committee. This is an opportunity to design and shape projects which will be taken forward with young people across Tayside.\n\n## Description\n\nOur vision is a world where power and resources are more equitably shared amongst the world’s people, where human rights are valued and respected, and where people are living sustainable lifestyles within the environmental limits of the planet. We promote and practise Global Citizenship Education by supporting teachers, schools and community groups in Angus, Dundee, Fife and Perth & Kinross with professional learning and the provision of mentoring, advice and resources. \r\n\r\nBeing a trustee offers the opportunity for professional development. It can let you gain experience of strategy and leadership, and boost your CV. It will give you experience of influencing direction and managing risk.\n\n## Experience required\n\nOur new trustee will have one or more skills in these areas: social media/pr , finance, funding finding and or community youth work.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nOur management committee meet approximately every 6 weeks. These meetings are a hybrid of in person and online and last approximately 2 .5 hours\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Roundhouse DD4 0HU.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note: No expenses are paid for this opportunity\n\n## Taster details\n\nYou may join one of our committee meetings to get an idea of the requirements of being a Trustee",
