                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000027EY9YAM",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000027EY9YAM/global-citizen-ambassador",
                    "publishStart": "2024-01-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-30",
                    "title": "Global Citizen Ambassador",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for enthusiastic volunteers to assist in delivering global citizenship education to a variety of community groups.  The successful applicants will have a strong interest in sustainability, fair trade and  a fairer more equal society.  Training will be given\n\n## Description\n\nOver the past 38 years the OWC has worked with schools and community groups across Tayside to increase understanding of issues of global, social and environmental justice. We believe that how we behave locally impacts on the lives of others globally.  \r\n\r\nOur Global Citizenship Ambassadors  would be expected to lead community group sessions exploring the links between our lives and those of people throughout the world - for which training will be given.  Our volunteers will be supported by trustees of the OWC.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for enthusiastic volunteers who want to make a difference.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA commitment to global citizenship issues and good communication skills\n\n## Training details\n\nGCAs will be supported throughout\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nVolunteers would be expected to sign our Volunteer Agreement and commit to a regular commitment which would probably be at least 1 day a week although this is flexible\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nlocal travelling expenses",
