        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZ9cAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZ9cAAE/hot-chocolate-trust",
            "name": "Hot Chocolate Trust",
            "description": "Hot Chocolate Trust (HCT) is a youth work organisation, working with young people aged 12-25 who hang out in the city centre, building relationships and supporting them through their journey to become agents of change in their lives and communities. HCT is open to all young people without prejudice or distinction of religion, rage, culture, disability, gender identity, sexuality or politics.",
            "website": "https://www.hotchocolate.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC035714"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SelfHelpSupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Self-Help / Support"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Vhwp2AAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Vhwp2AAB/youth-worker",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Youth Worker",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHot Chocolate Trust is built around youth work volunteers giving their time to build relationships with young people who come through the doors. Interested in working with young people? We'd love to hear from you!\n\n## Description\n\nYouth Work volunteers are a vital part of the team at Hot Chocolate Trust. As a volunteer, you will be part of our weekly open sessions, where you will work as part of the team with a focus on building relationships with the young people who come through the doors, and supporting their holistic development. You can also choose to be involved in a variety of group work, trips, projects, and individual support.\r\n\r\nVolunteers can expect a high level of learning and support from us, including a full induction and ongoing training opportunities. We encourage volunteers to bring their unique skills, passions, interests and experiences to HCT and their work with young people. We support volunteers to identify areas they would like to grow and develop too, and seek out opportunities to make this happen.\r\n\r\nTimings for Youth Work are 4 hours weekly on Tuesdays 5-9pm or Thursdays 3-7pm.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo prior experience is required to volunteer with Hot Chocolate Trust. Key skills required are good listening and team working skills, and an openness to learn and develop youth work practice. We encourage volunteers to bring any of their skills/interests to their youth work, whether this is art, music, games, cooking, or any other skills/interests!\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will undertake a four week induction, covering youth work practice, vision and values, safeguarding/child protection, and policies & procedures. They will be offered regular support and\r\nsupervision. Volunteers will be invited to be part of any available training.\n\n## Travel details\n\nHot Chocolate Trust, The Steeple Church, Nethergate, Dundee, DD1 4DG\n\n## Taster details\n\nPeople who are interested in volunteering will be invited to visit one of our open sessions. During this visit, there will be an opportunity to meet some of the youth work team and young people, and see what the open sessions look like in action.",
