        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZ9mAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZ9mAAE/ardler-environmental-group",
            "name": "Ardler Environmental Group",
            "description": "On Wednesday morning if the weather is fine, Ardler Environmental Group gets together for a gardening session. Its fun, educational and helps to keep Ardler green and tidy and when we are finished we all enjoy tea and a natter. We also visit other gardens and garden centres to explore ideas for our garden.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EnvironmentRecycling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Environment / Recycling"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ6KAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eJ6KAAU/community-gardener",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Community Gardener",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteers help to keep the Ardler community gardens an area of beauty for the community to experience and enjoy. Experienced and learner gardeners are equally welcome to join in on Wednesday mornings and stay for tea and a chat.\n\n## Description\n\nArdler Environmental Group are responsible for the maintainance and upkeep of the Ardler Community Garden area. Our volunteers meet once a week on Wednesday mornings to develop and maintain the gardens for the enjoyment of the community. You will help with weeding beds and planting new plants both for the gardens and for selling at community festivals. You can learn about different plants and their upkeep, hanging baskets and how to layout a garden. More experienced gardeners can share their knowledge with the rest of the group who are always keen to learn. When the weather is less clement the group organises trips to garden centres and other gardens to get ideas which you are welcome to take part in.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAn interest in gardening and the environment, enthusiastic.\n\n## Training details\n\nBasic induction training is available at the present time.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWednesday mornings 9.30 to 12.00.\n\n## Travel details\n\nArdler Community Centre, Turnberry Avenue, Dundee. Bus Number 1 will drop you outside the centre.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note: No expenses are paid for this opportunity",
