                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GwAozYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GwAozYAF/activities-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-21",
                    "title": "Activities Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThis role is to support the facilitation of tabletop gaming for children and young people in a library setting.\n\n## Description\n\nWork alongside library staff to deliver fun and creative activities for children and young people, including crafts, tabletop games, Lego sessions, and more.\r\n\r\nThis role is suitable for someone who has an interest in crafts, tabletop gaming etc. \r\n\r\nThe role includes preparing resources and setting out equipment; welcoming children and parents/guardians as they arrive; facilitating activities and encouraging participation; helping with refreshments; clearing up materials and equipment at the end of the session; and, maintaining records and sharing feedback with library staff.\r\n\r\nPVG required for this role.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThis role is suitable for someone who is friendly, organised, and comfortable working in a community setting. You should be reliable, confident in communicating with children and young people.\n\n## Training details\n\nIntro to Table Top Gaming and role shadowing with experienced volunteers\n\n## Travel details\n\nVarious branch libraries across Dundee\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note - no expenses are payable for this opportunity.\n\n## Taster details\n\nIntroduction session + role shadowing.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
