                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GwB9yYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GwB9yYAF/social-media-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-21",
                    "title": "Social Media Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTo support Dundee Libraries to increase their online presence and engagement through regular, creative and meaningful social media activity across platforms.\n\n## Description\n\nYour role as a volunteer will be to support Dundee Libraries to increase their online presence and engagement through regular, creative and meaningful social media activity across platforms.\r\n\r\n· Work closely with staff & other volunteers to gather relevant content and information as directed by the Social Media Team\r\n\r\n· Create engaging content (posts, stories, graphics, short videos, electronic newsletter) in line with the organisation’s voice and mission\r\n\r\n· Support campaigns to promote services and events\n\n## Experience required\n\nFamiliarity with social media platforms, especially Facebook and Instagram \r\nStrong written communication skills with an eye for tone and detail  \r\nCreative and comfortable using design tools like Canva, Sway (or willing to learn) \r\nOrganised, self-motivated, and reliable - \r\nExperience in social media content planning or marketing is a plus, but not essential\n\n## Training details\n\nRole shadowing with experienced volunteers\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note - No expenses are payable for this opportunity.\n\n## Taster details\n\nIntroduction session + role shadowing",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
