                },
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ8LAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eJ8LAAU/kitchen-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2022-03-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Kitchen Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for an enthusiastic and friendly person to join our team and assist in the kitchen where we provide a warm and healthy lunch for the families we support.\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for a enthusiastic person to join our team here at St. Ninian's where we work with and support the families in the community. Your role is to assist in setting up an attractive lunch following our Healthy Eating Plan. This is a simple lunch and consists of homemade soup, sandwiches, drinks and fruit. We also take into account the various ages of the children attending, this includes the needs of babies at different stages. We also take into account any allergies and other dietary requirements.\r\n\r\nDuring lunch we also offer taster sessions and encourage the families to enjoy this opportunity. After lunch you will be doing the washing up and cleaning the kitchen for the next day with the help of another volunteer.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAn interest in working around young children and their parents. An interest in food for young children would be valued.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers are assigned to an established worker, shown the building as part of their introduction and resource areas. As part of the team they will be included in meetings and meal ideas are discussed.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nA weekly commitment is preferred to give continuity to build up relationships with the team and families.\n\n## Travel details\n\nSt. Ninian's Stay and Play Family Support Group St.Ninian's Church Kingsway East Dundee DD4 7RW.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nBus fares will be reimbursed on production of a ticket.\n\n## Taster details\n\nAfter being in touch with the contact person, a visit will be arranged. This is a time for you to meet staff and other volunteers have a look around and ask any questions.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ8LAAU#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Kitchen Assistant",
                        "description": "An interest in working around young children and their parents. An interest in food for young children would be valued.",
