            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Gvc99AAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Gvc99AAB/community-garden-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Community Garden Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nLooking for volunteers who enjoy working outdoors and want to play a role in the development of a beautiful urban garden/growing space.\n\n## Description\n\nVictoria Gardens is a new exciting urban growing/social space located on the edge of Balgay Park. We have exciting plans for the space including a community kitchen and picnic benches. \r\n\r\nNow we are looking for volunteers to help us to build a pond, club house, mud kitchen, and sow seeds.\r\n\r\nThe Garden is open we open Thursday, Friday and Saturday 10 to 3 pm in winter time and in spring / summer it will be open 5 days a week 10am to 4pm.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnjoy working outdoors\n\n## Training details\n\nAt the start of the session, they will be introduced to the garden, the organisation, its policies. The volunteer will be given opportunities of different roles at the garden. After they commit they will be supported with ongoing training by our on site gardener.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nGarden is open 5 days a week. Volunteering can happen any time Monday/Tuesday/Wednesday 10am - 3pm or Friday/Saturday 11am - 4pm. Volunteers can be flexible on the role they want to play at the garden and the time commitment\nthey would have. Tea/coffee facilities are available on site.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVictoria Gardens, 301 Blackness Road. DD2 2BH\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe can cover bus travel expenses. They would keep a receipt and paid by the Manager on site.",
