            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ58AAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eJ58AAE/mentor",
                    "publishStart": "2022-03-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Mentor",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTo support young people (10-19) who are vulnerable as a result of substance misuse (their own or others) and/or offending/anti social behaviour. Male mentors particularly welcome.\n\n## Description\n\nTCA Youth Mentoring Service provides a mentoring support to vulnerable young people living within the boundaries of Dundee City. The target group are those young people who are affected by someone else's (parents, siblings, grandparents etc) substance use. The service recruits, trains, supports and supervises volunteer mentors who are then matched with individual young people. Mentoring matches are closely monitored and reviewed to ensure they remain purposeful. You must be able to commit 2-4 hours per week for at least 1 year. Volunteers will be supported by the Mentoring Coordinator and full training will be provided. Having your own transport would be beneficial but is not necessary.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNon judgemental, reliable, ability to work as part of a team, empathic attitude, flexible, sense of humour, honest, understanding of and commitment to confidentiality and to the work of TCA, understanding of child protection issues.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining consists of 5 core sessions covering legal frameworks, children's rights,methods of helping/engaging with young people, child protection, role of the volunteer mentor. Support offered through monthly group as well as individual meetings.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nVaries to suit volunteer but approx 2-4 hours per week and would expect a minimum commitment of 1 year after training.Weekdays\n\n## Travel details\n\nWithin Dundee.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses paid at rate of 45p per mile.",
