                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000007vVFxYAM",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000007vVFxYAM/intandem-mentor",
                    "publishStart": "2025-01-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Intandem Mentor",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nMake a difference to a young person living in kinship care by joining Intandem! As mentor, you’ll meet weekly and through spending time together, be that positive, consistent role model they can depend on.\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for volunteers to train as Intandem mentors supporting young people (7-15) living in kinship care in Dundee. You’ll be trained and matched with a young person who you’ll meet weekly for approx one year and spend time getting to know each other. \r\n\r\nYou might try new activities together, visit new places and support your mentee to set goals. Young people tell us the most important qualities of a mentor are being able to listen, be up for having fun, and turn up consistently to spend time with them. If you can be there for a young person in kinship care we’d love to hear from you. It could be the best thing you’ve ever done!\n\n## Experience required\n\nNon-judgemental, reliable, ability to work as part of a team, empathetic attitude, flexible, sense of humour, honest, understanding of and commitment to confidentiality and to the work of TCA, understanding of child protection issues.\n\n## Training details\n\nOur comprehension training programme covers five keys areas to equip you with essential mentoring skills. We also provide continuous development opportunities along with monthly support and supervision throughout your volunteering journey.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDundee\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses paid at the rate of 45p per mile.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
