                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000007tnX9YAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000007tnX9YAI/volunteer-group-mentor",
                    "publishStart": "2025-01-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Volunteer Group Mentor",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTCA is recruiting volunteers to co-facilitate our youth groups in Dundee. If you’re passionate about supporting youth, creating positive environments, and making a difference in your community, this role could be ideal for you!\n\n## Description\n\nOur Youth Groups provide mentoring support for young people who are affected by another's substance use or are at risk of offending to reach positive destinations.\r\n\r\nAs a group Co-Facilitator your primary responsibilities would include:\r\n\r\n1. Session Planning: · Assist with the preperation and organisation of youth group sessions · Help insure that the activities are relevant, engaging and appropriate for the young people involved. \r\n2. Supporting Facilitation: · Provide hands – on support during the delivery of group activities, ensuring the smooth running of each session · Co – Facilitate alongside other volunteers and staff members, ensuring active participation from all attendees. \r\n3. Engaging Young People: · Work to encourage participation, build relationships with the young people and create a positive environment where everyone feels included. · Support the young people as they engage in activities, ensuring that their voices are heard, and they are motivated to take part.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNon-judgemental, reliable, ability to work as part of a team, empathetic attitude, flexible, sense of humour, honest, understanding of and commitment to confidentiality and to the work of TCA, understanding of child protection issues.\n\n## Training details\n\nOur Comprehensive training programme covers 5 key areas to equip you with essential mentoring skills.\r\n\r\nWe also provide continuous development opportunities along with monthly support and supervision throughout your volunteering journey.",
