        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZBAAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZBAAA2/tayside-cancer-support-dundee",
            "name": "Tayside Cancer Support (Dundee)",
            "description": "Tayside Cancer Support offers the opportunity for anyone affected by cancer in Tayside and the surrounding area to receive emotional, social and practical support, either on an individual basis or in a group setting.\r\n\r\nThe charity has been in existence since July 1994 and is made up of an Executive Committee of voluntary Trustees, two part-time paid employees and approximately 30 volunteers of whom around 20 are befrienders. We work with cancer patients, their families, carers and friends. We do this alongside healthcare professionals and other charities and support groups to provide vital support and information.",
            "website": "http://www.taysidecancersupport.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC054674"
                }
            ],
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2Fc89f80d9-51a0-69ab-04a6-f9f8ffa2662b%2FxSUy0SH8QeWhG7vceR9mPpvgE6A2%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=5204b6da-ade5-4a91-830b-91ff26ee5c14",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Counselling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Counselling"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FamilySupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Family Support"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FundraisingFunding",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Fundraising / Funding"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QhixLAAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QhixLAAR/befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2023-07-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Befriender",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWho are we?\r\n\r\nTayside Cancer Support offers the opportunity for anyone affected by cancer in Tayside and the surrounding are to receive emotional, social and practical support, either on an individual basis or in a group setting.\r\n\r\nThe charity has been in existence since July 1994 and is made up of an Executive Committee of voluntary Trustees, two part-time paid employees and approximately thirty volunteers of whom around 20 are befrienders. \r\n\r\nWe work with cancer patients, their families, carers and friends. We do this alongside healthcare professionals and other charities and support groups to provide vital support and information.\r\n\r\nAnyone can utilise our services who, either has or has had, a cancer diagnosis or is supporting someone on their cancer journey, e.g. family, friends or professional supporters. They don’t need a specific referral; they can just get in touch. There are no costs associated with our services.\r\n\r\nOur annual numbers in a story:\r\n\r\n· Roughly 20 befrienders working with clients for around 3-4 hours a month each.\r\n· We spend around £1,800-£2,000 a month on counselling and oncology massage therapies for our clients, this is roughly 30-50 client appointments.\r\n· The Drop-in Café has had visits from around 50 people over the year. \r\n\r\nSupport we need\r\n\r\nAs we continue to raise our profile and support more clients living with cancer we need to ensure we have a fantastic pool of befrienders who are willing to give up their time to support those clients. We are seeing a noticeable increase in demand across our services and want to know we can respond quickly to requests. Time is so often a vital factor in requests for our clients. When people are going through tough times, it can help to have a friendly, non-judgemental ear. A problem shared is a problem halved! \r\n\r\nWe provide befriending support to those living with cancer throughout the Tayside and NE Fife area. This support is invaluable to those we support. We’d love to hear from you if you’d like to become a befriender. Here’s what’s involved:· \r\n\r\nWhat you’ll receive:\r\n\r\n* Full training and ongoing support\r\n* Opportunities to develop new skills\r\n* A rewarding volunteer experience\r\n* The chance to make a real difference in someone’s life\r\n\r\nNo previous experience is necessary—just kindness, reliability, and a willingness to help.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe’re looking for people who are\r\n\r\n* Friendly, caring, and non-judgemental\r\n* Good listeners with empathy and compassion\r\n* Able to commit a to a couple of hours each month\r\n* Keen to support people in their local community.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe commitment is a minimum 1 hour a month.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAround Tayside and north Fife.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAll reasonable expenses covered.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QhixLAAR#role",
