                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ9FAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eJ9FAAU/shopper",
                    "publishStart": "2022-03-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Shopper",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWould you like to support older people across Dundee by doing their shopping in the supermarket? Volunteer shoppers work as part of a team in store to collate the groceries ready for the delivery people to load onto our van\n\n## Description\n\nWorking as part of a team of shoppers you will take one of our customer’s orders and go around the store gathering the required items. You will then pack the groceries into shop boxes and help put them through the checkout. Once all the orders are made up we pay the balance of the grocery bill and help the delivery people load the boxes onto the vans ready for delivery.\r\n\r\n8.30 am til approx. 12 Noon Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday.\n\n## Experience required\n\nInterest in supporting older people, good reading skills, able to work as part of a team.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe new volunteers will be supported by an experienced shopper on the first few days. We offer ongoing support and training through our regular volunteer meetings.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMinimum time commitment is 4 hours per week, either Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday morning.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAt Supermarkets; Asda (Milton) and Tesco (South Road)\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe reimburse public transport and mileage at £0.45 per mile paid by cheque.\r\nWe also pay expenses by BACS",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ9FAAU#role",
                        "type": "Role",
