                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eJ9CAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eJ9CAAU/van-driver",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Van Driver",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWould you like to support older people across Dundee by delivering their shopping? Van drivers work as part of a team on our delivery vans, delivering groceries to older people throughout the city.\n\n## Description\n\nVan Drivers support our delivery service going out on one of our vans with a Helper. You will pick up shopping boxes from the supermarkets and make multiple deliveries to our customers. You and the Helper will take the groceries into the customer’s house, unpack the groceries, check the order over with the customer and receive the payments. \r\n\r\nMinimum time commitment is 6 hours per week, either Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday morning.\n\n## Experience required\n\nInterest in supporting older people, a full current driving licence and a knowledge of road network in Dundee.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe new volunteers will be supported by an experienced Van Helper on the first few days. We offer ongoing support and training through our regular volunteer meetings.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMinimum time commitment is 6 hours per week, either Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday morning.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe reimburse public transport and mileage at £0.45 per mile paid by cheque.",
