        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZCwAAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZCwAAM/faith-in-community-dundee",
            "name": "Faith in Community Dundee",
            "description": "The organisation’s purposes are:\r\n\r\nTo promote the prevention and relief of poverty and/or disadvantage in Dundee and its environs through encouraging and enabling local faith communities to prevent and relieve poverty and/or disadvantage.\r\n\r\nTo increase awareness and promote learning of the impact of poverty and/or disadvantage with decision makers and wider society through developing and supporting the voices of those in poverty and/or suffering disadvantage.\r\n\r\nTo encourage the development of partnerships across agencies in local communities and in the city of Dundee and its environs; working together to alleviate and prevent poverty with those in poverty and/or disadvantage.\r\n\r\nTo promote the elimination of discrimination (whether on the grounds of race, religion, disability, sexual orientation, poverty or otherwise).",
            "website": "https://www.faithincommunitydundee.org",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FaithReligionBelief",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Faith / Religion / Belief"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Poverty",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Poverty"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HJLq9YAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HJLq9YAH/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-15",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for trustees to join our board of trustees. Our trustee meetings are held on Monday evenings approximately every 6-8 weeks or as required, in person at our Whitfield office.\n\n## Description\n\nAs Trustees, we are responsible for controlling the management and administration of Faith in Community Dundee as a charity, and for ensuring that our income and property are used for the purposes set out in our governing document (constitution) and for no other purpose. \r\n\r\nWe have a responsibility to act reasonably and prudently in all matters relating to the charity and have a responsibility to act in the best interests of the charity. Above all, we need to work together as a team to ensure that Faith in Community Dundee is run effectively and efficiently. \r\n\r\nAs a body, we aim for our Trustees to contain people who collectively have the skills and confidence that will enable us to develop our work effectively. Trustee meetings are held on a Monday evening at our offices in Whitfield and last approximately 2 hours. Meetings are held approximately every 6-8 weeks with additional meetings called if required.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThose who have an interest in our purpose, we are particularly interested in those with admin, finance or hr skills but are open to anyone with any relevant skills.\n\n## Training details\n\nTrustee pack provided, ongoing support from the chair and other trustees and the Director.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Roundhouse, Lothian Crescent, Dundee, DD4 0HU\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nbus fares or mileage can be claimed\n\n## Taster details\n\nOpportunity to discuss the position with the chair and go along to a board meeting to see if it is the right fit.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HJLq9YAH#role",
                        "type": "Role",
