        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008naV6AAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008naV6AAI/highland-hospice-highland",
            "name": "Highland Hospice (Highland)",
            "description": "Highland Hospice offers pallative care throughout the Highlands allowing terminally ill patients the best quality of life possible and to die in dignity.  We support friends and family throughout and after the patients illness.  We offer daycare, respite care and in-patient facilities as well as palliative care consultants who visit patients in their own homes.",
            "website": "https://www.highlandhospice.org",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HacY1YAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HacY1YAJ/hospice-services-experience-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-01",
                    "title": "Hospice Services Experience Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAt Highland Hospice, we believe that everyone in the Highlands facing life‑shortening illness, death, or bereavement deserves the highest standard of care and support. Our aim is to provide compassionate, person-centered hospice care to those we support and their families. \r\n\r\nListening to the experiences of the people who use our services is essential. Their feedback helps us understand what we are doing well and where we can improve. As a volunteer in this role, you will play a key role in gathering these valuable insights, enabling us to continually enhance the quality of care we provide.\n\n## Training details\n\nOnline \r\n\r\n•\tMoving and Handling Training inanimate objects approx. 30 minutes \r\n•\tCyber Security and GDPR – approx. 30 minutes  \r\n•\tFire Safety Awareness for Volunteers – approx. 30 minutes \r\n•\tEquality and Diversity – approx. 30 minutes \r\n\r\nIn person \r\n\r\n•\tSafeguarding and adult support and protection - 1 hour face to face  \r\n•\tListening skills  \r\n•\tRole specific induction with quality team  \r\n•\tInduction to the IPU including Infection Prevention and Control for volunteers",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
