            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009rOTdYAM",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009rOTdYAM/general-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-05",
                    "title": "General Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nTalk now is a service for male and female who have suffered truama, in\nChildhood and adulthood, we offer 1 to 1 counselling and group work to support survivors of sexual, domestic, physical and emotional abuse. Talk now is a safe and confidential environment for people to\nExplore their experiences. Opportunities for volunteers would be to gain experience in how our services will improve the lives of people who have been impacted by trauma and other traumatic experiences. We are all committed to the service we provide and very passionate about the work we do which creates a unique opportunity to be part of this. We value all the staff and people who use our services which creates a positive environment.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFundraising,General Admin / Office Support, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Hard Working,Open minded,Organised,Patient,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Team Player,Trustworthy,Knowledge of charities\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers will have an induction kit to provide them with the information they need to be prepared to help them with their work.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe don’t have funding for expenses at the moments. We will apply for funding for this",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
