            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nYuyAAE/age-concern-eastwood",
            "name": "Age Concern Eastwood",
            "description": "Promoting the interests of older persons in our community, proving lunch clubs with available transport, general advice and information supplied and wheelchair loans.",
            "website": "http://www.ageconcerneastwood.com",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC012395"
                }
            ],
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2F10385193-42e7-8f59-36b0-006c125b937b%2FmQsKXYYIupgt1ub9BeDSGFfo1O33%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=f5830cf1-93cd-4905-9181-da1939773d0e",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pc76RAAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pc76RAAR/lunch-club-helper",
                    "publishStart": "2022-05-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-19",
                    "title": "Lunch Club Helper",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAs a volunteer Lunch Club Helper, you will welcome the people that come along and encourage them to feel as comfortable as possible while chatting and playing games.  The role will also involve helping our friendly team of volunteers set up our halls, serving lunch/meals and tidying up afterwards.\r\n\r\nThe role requires a PVG (Disclosure) check, which will be paid for by Age Concern.\r\n\r\nLunch clubs run from 10 am - 2.30 pm with some time for prep added on, therefore, if suitable, we are looking for volunteers to help out for 5½ hours.\r\n\r\nIn this role, you are making a difference in people's lives who may feel lonely or isolated; it's enjoyable and rewarding also.  You will become part of a friendly team of volunteers who share the same passion for helping others.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWeekly, from last fortnight in August until December 2022\n\n## Travel details\n\nCurrently only looking for volunteers for the club that runs in Albertslund Hall in Newton Mearns - own transport required",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F97d46a09-a797-230e-7393-37c87b08723f%2FmQsKXYYIupgt1ub9BeDSGFfo1O33%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=184d6fc3-c7d0-41c8-b1b8-e67bb9dbb812",
