        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nYxcAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nYxcAAE/15th-glasgow-scouts-eaglesham-waterfoot",
            "name": "15th Glasgow Scouts - Eaglesham & Waterfoot",
            "description": "Scouting is a worldwide Movement, with a membership of over 28 million.In Scotland, The Scout Association is responsible for the provision of Scouting; challenge and adventure for young people aged between 6 and 25, including males and females. It is all about fun with a purpose – helping members to fulfil their potential as individuals and active members of society. We believe that young people develop most when they are learning by doing, when they are given responsibility, work in teams, take acceptable risks and think for themselves.  Everything we do is guided by the balanced programme which is a continuous progression of training, activities, badges and awards for young people from 6 to 25.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC040378"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eIwKAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eIwKAAU/eaglesham-scout-group-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2012-12-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-11",
                    "title": "Eaglesham Scout Group Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWould you like to help young people achieve their full physical, intellectual, social and spiritual potential? Scouting today provides challenge and adventure for young people aged between 6 and 25, including males and females. It is all about fun with a purpose - helping members to fulfill their potential as individuals and active members of society.\n\n## Description\n\nDo you have a couple of hours spare to help young people in your local community? We are looking for volunteers to support the operation of the Eaglesham Scout troop (age 10 – 14) in delivering our programme of activities. We provide young people with exciting and challenging experiences and then help them use those experiences in their personal and social development. The level of your involvement is entirely up to you and could vary from helping out for a couple of hours each week at the local Scout Hall to participation in outdoor weekend events & challenges.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnthusiasm\r\nInitiative \r\nA willingness to get involved\r\nTeam working\r\nAcceptance of the attitudes, beliefs and lifestyles of others\n\n## Training details\n\nLeaders at the troop will be on hand to offer support & training and will provide all necessary materials for the volunteer role. We arrange your criminal record check (most of our volunteers need a PVG check), and you will be insured during your voluntee\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe level of commitment is flexible, but we would look for at least a couple of hours each week. The group meets every Tuesday evening from 19.30 to 21.00 at the Eaglesham Scout Hall.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAt  Eaglesham Scout Hall\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nLocally agreed expenses paid",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Ff0d5cf11-05ee-9933-4e68-10c8d443245e%2FmQsKXYYIupgt1ub9BeDSGFfo1O33%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=40ba93d3-d748-4b78-b01d-334f9c3a3c99",
