        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nYyOAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nYyOAAU/east-renfrewshire-soccer-development-association",
            "name": "East Renfrewshire Soccer Development Association",
            "description": "The East Renfrewshire Soccer Development Association (ERSDA) was established to promote and develop grassroots football for young people within East Renfrewshire and surrounding areas.  Its main aims are to:\r\n\r\n* Provide organised and competitive football opportunities for children and young people of all abilities\r\n* Support the development of players by improving their football skills, teamwork, confidence and sportsmanship\r\n* Encourage participation and enjoyment in football within a safe, inclusive and positive environment\r\n* Support local clubs, coaches and referees through the effective organisation and development of grassroots football programmes\r\n* Promote long-term involvement in sport and healthy lifestyles among young people\r\n\r\nIn summary, ERSDA's primary purpose is to develop and manage youth football opportunities while fostering personal growth, participation and enjoyment through the game.",
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2Fac12157f-12ce-0914-8eff-cfc2fc7f990c%2Fj61M7uJZH9fX6Dz3Lhi5Q5Zimd03%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=831cfc4b-7fa9-404d-9d0b-d98e9ed6ef80",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HmLtBYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HmLtBYAV/administration-organisation-communications-or-community-sport-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-15",
                    "title": "Administration, Organisation, Communications or Community Sport Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nERSDA is looking to recruit enthusiastic and committed individuals to join our committee and volunteer team.  This is an exciting opportunity to play an active role in supporting grassroots sport, helping local communities thrive, and contributing to the continued growth and development of the association.\r\n\r\nWhether you have previous experience in administration, communications, event organisation, or simply a passion for community sport, we would love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nWhat You Can Expect to be Doing\r\nAs a committee member or volunteer you may be involved in a range of activities including:\r\n*Supporting the planning and organisation of meetings, events and association activities\r\n* Assisting with administration tasks, record keeping  and maintaining important documents\r\n* Helping to co-ordinate communications with clubs, members, volunteers and partner organisations\r\n* Supporting the promotion of ERSDA through social media, newsletters and community engagement activities\r\n* Contributing ideas and helping to shape the future direction of the association\r\n* Assisting with the organisation and delivery of events, competitions and development opportunities\r\n* Working alongside other committee members and volunteers to ensure the smooth running of the association\r\n* Acting as an ambassador for ERSDA and promoting positive participation within the local sporting community\r\n\r\nSkills & Experience\r\nWe welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experience levels.  The following qualities would be particularly valuable:\r\n* An interest in community sport and volunteer-led organisations\r\n* Good organisational and administrative skills\r\n* Strong communication and interpersonal abilities\r\n* Experience with social media, marketing or digital communications (desirable but not essential)\r\n* The ability to work effectively as part of a team\r\n* A willingness to contribute ideas and support new initiatives\r\n* Reliability, enthusiasm and a positive attitude\r\n\r\nPrevious committee or volunteering experience is welcomed but not required.  Support and guidance will be provided and the role offers an excellent opportunity to develop new skills and gain valuable experience\r\n\r\nTime Commitment\r\nERSDA understands that volunteers have other commitments and aims to offer flexible opportunities wherever possible:\r\n* Attendance at occasional committee meetings (typically monthly or as required)\r\n* Support for events and activities throughout the year\r\n* Additional volunteer time can be tailored to individual availability and interests\r\n* Most roles can be undertaken alongside work, study or family commitments\r\n\r\nWhy Volunteer with ERSDA?\r\nBy joining ERSDA, you will have the opportunity to:\r\n*Make a meaningful difference to the development of local sport\r\n* Help shape opportunities for participants, clubs and communities\r\n* Develop valuable skills in leadership, administration, communications and event management\r\n* Meet like-minded people and expand your professional and community networks\r\n* Gain rewarding experience that can enhance your CV and personal development\r\n* Be part of a dedicated team working to create positive sporting experiences for others\r\n\r\nThis is a rewarding opportunity for anyone who wants to give something back to their community while helping ERSDA continue to grow and succeed.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMainly from home.  In person meetings will be held at:\r\n1 Burnfield Avenue, Giffnock, G46 7TL or Barrhead Foundry, Main Street, Barrhead, G78 1SW",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F6ef7aad9-c531-4919-8000-4d7903b938f0%2Fj61M7uJZH9fX6Dz3Lhi5Q5Zimd03%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=a958485d-8e17-49c9-8d77-a683b2dd1afa",
                    "role": {
