                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BNh5xYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BNh5xYAD/chat-plant-gardening-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-08-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-04",
                    "title": "Chat & Plant Gardening Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nJoin our Chat & Plant Garden Team and help create and care for beautiful green spaces that support sustainability, biodiversity and food growing.\r\n\r\nOur volunteers play a vital role in maintaining grass areas, planters and growing spaces across the site, helping to make it a welcoming and environmentally conscious place for all.\r\n\r\nAs part of the team, volunteers are involved in planning, planting and looking after a wide variety of plants in our greenhouse and polytunnels.  From sowing seeds to nurturing plants as they grow, there are plenty of opportunities to learn new skills and get hands-on experience in gardening.\r\n\r\nWhether you’re an experienced gardener or just starting, you’ll be part of a friendly group working together to grow plants, support wildlife and create a thriving community space.\n\n## Travel details\n\n4D Rouken Glen Park, Thornliebank, G46 7UG.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F15dce625-966e-4292-b777-fc31a6b78d55%2FD5Fkl21abnNxZzKb66uMENQLQQn2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=bf2e10cb-1bf6-4ede-ac34-ad6c582e9f19",
