            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZ2yAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZ2yAAE/cosgrove-care-east-renfrewshire",
            "name": "Cosgrove Care (East Renfrewshire)",
            "description": "All the work carried out by Cosgrove Care is underpinned by a strongly held set of values and beliefs known as the values of inclusion.  This philosophy, where all people, regardless of ability, are seen to be citizens of worth, drives us in our mission to support people who are isolated or at risk of isolation to take power and control in their own lives.  Our work is about Justice, Empowerment, Relationships, Trust and Support.",
            "website": "https://www.cosgrovecare.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC013208"
                }
            ],
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2F6f64e5f6-1e87-1836-31bc-967bc63e1717%2FmQsKXYYIupgt1ub9BeDSGFfo1O33%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=e9fc36aa-81b2-4bf3-984c-01e03f0845b0",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IVLXFYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IVLXFYA5/social-sundays-helper",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-15",
                    "title": "Social Sundays Helper",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nVolunteers help the group facilitator ensure things run smoothly:\r\n\r\n* Helping with the setting up and clearing up of the sessions\r\n* Serving soup and refreshments\r\n* Chatting with the attendees\r\n\r\nWe are looking for volunteers who are warm, friendly and good listeners.\r\n\r\nThis volunteering opportunity offers the chance to develop your communication and social skills and to gain understanding and experience of volunteering with adults with learning disabilities in a supportive setting.\r\n\r\nThe group meet fortnightly on Sunday afternoons from 1-3.30 pm.\r\n\r\nPVG membership is required.\n\n## Travel details\n\nFinn's Place, 167 Ledard Road, Glasgow, G42 9QU.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F7cc01926-bec2-49d9-8e0e-f78e28421553%2FUNDN5Y8p1wZyo4kGYUEGmLnXPf12%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=6b85f8be-76c8-4c83-9535-43c8adac7a85",
