        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZ32AAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZ32AAE/nhs-voluntary-services",
            "name": "NHS Voluntary Services",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0gPtYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I0gPtYAJ/royal-alexandra-hospital-welcome-guide-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-10",
                    "title": "Royal Alexandra Hospital - Welcome Guide Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nRoyal Alexandra Hospital - Welcome Guide Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nThis is an&nbsp;exciting opportunity to be part of a new volunteer team&nbsp;who&nbsp;are&nbsp;committed to contributing to and enhancing the experience of our patients,&nbsp;family&nbsp;members&nbsp;and other visitors to&nbsp;the Royal Alexandra Hospital.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\nA&nbsp;considerable number of visitors&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;patients&nbsp;come&nbsp;through the front entrance of&nbsp;our busy hospital sites,&nbsp;on a daily basis. Some may require guidance to find their way&nbsp;around&nbsp;and they may have questions they wish to ask.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\nOur Volunteer Welcome&nbsp;Guides will be&nbsp;located&nbsp;at the Main Entrance of the RAH.\n\nVolunteers offer a friendly and helpful welcome to patients, family&nbsp;members&nbsp;and visitors and&nbsp;direct&nbsp;them to where they want to go. This may involve accompanying people&nbsp;to their&nbsp;destination&nbsp;if this is&nbsp;required.&nbsp;\n\nKey responsibilities;\n\n\n\nActively&nbsp;observe&nbsp;for patients / visitors in the hospital entrance who may appear in need of&nbsp;assistance&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\n\n\n\n\nBe&nbsp;welcoming,&nbsp;by chatting to patients and visitors,&nbsp;to&nbsp;make them feel at ease.&nbsp;\n\n\n\n\n\nProvide guidance on the use of self&ndash;service check-in kiosks, as&nbsp;appropriate.&nbsp;\n\n\n\n\n\nGuide&nbsp;people from main entrances towards where they wish to go, accompanying them if they wish this.&nbsp;\n\n\n\n\n\nSignposting patients to waiting areas.&nbsp;\n\n\n\n\n\nLiaising with staff&nbsp;from various departments (Medical records, Outpatients,&nbsp;Facilities)&nbsp;to resolve any issues that come up.&nbsp;\n\n## Experience required\n\nAbility to communicate with people in a friendly, sensitive, caring and calm manner. \n\nWillingness to undertake training and comply with policies and procedures. \n\nAbility to use your own initiative appropriately and contribute to the overall efforts of the team.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBuses connect directly with the hospital from areas across Renfrewshire. There is a visitor car park, but spaces can be limited at peak times.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReimbursement is provided for public transport and mileage costs  to the hospital from the volunteer home address, as prior agreement.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0gPtYAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Royal Alexandra Hospital - Welcome Guide Volunteer",
                        "description": "Ability to communicate with people in a friendly, sensitive, caring and calm manner. \n\nWillingness to undertake training and comply with policies and procedures. \n\nAbility to use your own initiative appropriately and contribute to the overall efforts of the team.",
