        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nb8yAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nb8yAAA/kirkcaldy-old-kirk-trust",
            "name": "Kirkcaldy Old Kirk Trust",
            "description": "We are a building preservation trust with responsibility for preserving and maintaining Kirkcaldy Old Kirk, now in our ownership, as a community venue, heritage centre and community music hub.  We aim to develop it as an inspirational setting for a wide range of performance and creative arts and heritage activities.",
            "website": "https://www.kirkcaldyoldkirktrust.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC042128"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EnvironmentRecycling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Environment / Recycling"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000DOIh3YAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000DOIh3YAH/gardening-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-26",
                    "title": "Gardening Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nKirkcaldy Old Kirk Trust is responsible for preserving and maintaining Kirkcaldy Old Kirk as a community venue, heritage centre and community music hub. The Trust is looking for a volunteer gardener to help with maintaining the garden. The external flower beds provide an area for quiet contemplation and people enjoy viewing them when they pass the church. The kirk also rents out space to a local café and they have a “secret garden” which can be used by customers. Volunteers can be involved in activities such as weeding and general maintenance of the flower beds. and also, to take on a more creative role, linking with existing Old Kirk volunteers or the café owner. This will be dependent on volunteer’s confidence and skills. –. As a volunteer you could be part of designing garden layout and suggesting new and different planting. The recent success of Kirkcaldy in the Britain in Bloom Awards shows us that Kirkcaldy Town Centre plants and flowers are getting noticed.\r\n\r\nThis role is ideal if you enjoy gardening, have time to spare and ideas you wish see bloom!\r\n\r\nTake the opportunity to use your gardening skills to make a real difference to a small local charity and help maintain a heritage site of national importance\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnthusiasm and a love for and interest in the outdoors and gardening\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers are required to complete an induction. All volunteers have a named contact. A tour of the garden and discussion relating to planting will be provided and guidance on gardening tasks can be offered to those who would like a little support with tasks. There will also be an introductory session with a volunteer who currently takes responsibility for the garden. All tools and safety equipment will be provided.\r\n\r\nThe induction will cover a brief history of the KOKT and the roles and responsibilities of volunteers, the policies and procedures as they appertain to the volunteers and an introduction to the named person for their role. We will explain the procedure for claiming expenses and include a tour of the Kirk/Gardens\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Old Kirk is situated in Central Kirkcaldy on Kirk Wynd within easy reach of the bus and train stations.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are paid as required on a fortnightly/monthly basis.  Public transport rates of 40p per mile apply.",
