        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nb9VAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nb9VAAQ/equal-voice",
            "name": "Equal Voice",
            "description": "Equal Voice is a Citizen Advocacy project. We are a registered charity and we provide independent advocacy for Central Fife residents who have a learning disability, physical disability or a mental health difficulty which makes them unable to look after their own affairs.<br><br> Our project offers assistance to adults aged 16 -65 years old who need support speaking up for themselves. Citizen Advocates develop a voluntary long-term partnership with a person who has a vulnerable adult who has difficulty being listened to or has difficulty speaking up for themselves.",
            "website": "http://www.equalvoice.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038052"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Advocacy",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advocacy"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eLLXAA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eLLXAA2/citizen-advocates",
                    "publishStart": "2025-11-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-09",
                    "title": "Citizen Advocates",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAre you passionate about making a real difference in someone's life?\r\nEqual Voice brings together local volunteers and vulnerable people. We are looking for volunteers who are willing to give a few hours of their time each month to make a difference in a vulnerable person's life by becoming their Citizen Advocate.\r\n\r\nBeing a Citizen Advocate is your chance to stand alongside an individual who may need a stronger voice in their community. It’s not about being an expert - it’s about being a genuine friend, a good listener and a champion for fairness. You’ll help someone feel seen, heard, and valued, while discovering new perspectives and connections yourself. Whether it’s supporting someone through a challenge or meeting up for a chat. Simply sharing a coffee, enjoying a catch-up that reduces loneliness and builds confidence can make such an incredible difference.\r\n\r\nNo special qualifications are needed and there’s no set amount of time required – it’s all about what you can offer – just an open mind and a caring heart. Make your voice count by helping someone else find theirs.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe most important qualities for a volunteer Citizen Advocate are empathy, reliability, and a genuine interest in people and their individual needs. They don’t need any special qualifications – just a kind heart, be a good listener and have the confidence to give a voice to a vulnerable person who is not being listened to or cannot speak up for themselves.\n\n## Training details\n\nEveryone taking on the role of a Citizen Advocate is invited to complete an Advocacy Preparation Course, which provides an induction to the principles of Advocacy. Including the definition and importance of Advocacy, the role of an Advocate in supporting individuals and the Equal Voice guidance for Advocates.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place in the Kirkcaldy, Glenrothes, and Leven areas, supporting people within their own communities. Most connections happen locally – whether that’s meeting for a coffee, going for a walk, or catching up somewhere nearby. This is a mutual arrangement between the Citizen Advocate and their Partner.\r\n\r\nVolunteers can choose to be matched with someone close to home, and travel be kept to a minimum as the organisation aim to match their Advocate with someone in their local area. The organisation will work with you to make sure everything feels easy and accessible.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses reimbursed on an individual basis",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eLLXAA2#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Citizen Advocates",
                        "description": "The most important qualities for a volunteer Citizen Advocate are empathy, reliability, and a genuine interest in people and their individual needs. They don’t need any special qualifications – just a kind heart, be a good listener and have the confidence to give a voice to a vulnerable person who is not being listened to or cannot speak up for themselves.",
