                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-13",
                    "title": "Citizen Advocate (North East Fife)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nInclude Me provides a free independent Citizen Advocacy service in North East Fife to vulnerable people aged 16-65 who need help to safeguard their well-being, rights and other interests.\r\n\r\nCan you be the difference in someone’s life? Volunteers do not have to have experience of advocacy or come from a Health & Social Care background but should have a strong sense of social justice and a desire to promote inclusion. Our advocates stand alongside their advocacy partner, supporting them to have a voice and be a lead decision maker in their own life. This is an opportunity to champion someone who may be excluded, ignored or isolated and who feels they have no control over what is happening to them. Sometimes, a Citizen Advocate is the only person in a vulnerable adult’s life who is not paid to be there. Citizen Advocates provide support, friendship, a sounding board, information and solidarity.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for individuals with a strong sense of fairness and a desire for marginalised groups to be included in society. Citizen Advocates are ordinary people who choose to get to know and stand by someone in their own community who may be vulnerable and cannot safeguard their own rights.\r\n\r\nCitizen Advocates don’t need formal qualifications or professional experience.\n\n## Training details\n\nThey aim to provide as much support and information as each individual citizen advocate needs.\r\nThey will e-mail/post information to you about citizen advocacy and their project & arrange a meeting/telephone/video call to introduce themselves and to answer any questions you might have. They will leave/send an application form to you\r\nIf selected as a potential advocate, they invite you to their preparation training which may be in a small group or on a 1:1 basis depending on numbers. Preparation training usually involves 2 x 2.5hr sessions at a time and place to suit.\r\nIf they make a successful match between a volunteer advocate and advocacy partner, they may arrange ongoing training to support the individual needs of the partnership if need be.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThere are opportunities throughout North East Fife. We try to match our volunteers with vulnerable adults living in their own communities to minimise travel. Occasionally, volunteers may be matched with someone who lives outwith their local area.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses can be reimbursed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
