                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000006S63pYAC",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000006S63pYAC/trusteeboard-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-12",
                    "title": "Trustee/Board Member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nInclude Me provides a free independent Citizen Advocacy service in North East Fife to people aged 16-65 affected by: Physical disabilities, Learning Disabilities, Mental Health Issues, Early Onset Dementia, Autism Spectrum Disorder, Brain Injury or Long Term Health Issues and who need help to safeguard their well-being, rights, care and other interests.\r\n\r\nThey are looking for volunteers to join their Management Committee to help shape the organisation, manage operational issues and raise the profile of advocacy in North East Fife. Their current committee members have a wide range of skills and experience from a variety of different backgrounds which are invaluable in helping us to meet the needs of the vulnerable communities.\r\n\r\nApplicants do not have to have experience of advocacy or come from a Health & Social Care background but should have a strong sense of social justice and a desire to promote inclusion.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for individuals with a strong sense of fairness and a desire for marginalised groups to be included in society. Volunteers should be reliable and willing to attend meetings both online and in person and should have basic computer skills including the ability to use Microsoft Teams. While knowledge of advocacy or the voluntary sector would be an advantage, it is not necessary as full training is provided.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction will involve 1:1 time with committee members and staff to learn about the organisation. Volunteers will be required to complete an online Adult Protection module, as well as FVA Trustee training and Include Me Citizen Advocacy Awareness Training\"\n\n## Travel details\n\nCommittee meeting are held every 4-6 weeks with the majority taking place online. Face to face meetings are usually held in St Andrews. Support can be given with travel arrangements.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe pay public transport rates and reimburse volunteers monthly. If necessary, a mileage rate of 55p per mile will be paid.",
