            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nbAAAAY/circle-of-comfort",
            "name": "Circle of Comfort",
            "description": "They fund a team of highly qualified and experienced Complementary Therapists who support people living with Cancer.   Circle of Comfort is a registered Scottish charity which offers reflexology, massage or aromatherapy treatments to people in Fife and Perthshire who are living with the side effects of cancer.  Clients are given their treatments in the comfort of their own home free of charge, by one of their fully qualified therapists.",
            "website": "https://www.circleofcomfort.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038004"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HwftpYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HwftpYAB/trustee-with-grant-writing-experience",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-25",
                    "title": "Trustee with grant writing experience",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe charity is seeking a Trustee with experience of grant writing. Grant funding is an important source of income for Circle of Comfort so we can continue to deliver complementary therapies to those diagnosed with cancer and would benefit from a treatment. The ideal candidate will have experience of researching new income streams and preparing bid applications.\r\n\r\nAs a trustee, you will attend committee meetings and make decisions on behalf of the organisation. You will ensure that the charity meets its legal, regulatory, and constitutional duties while staying true to its vision and values.\r\n\r\nYou will also have the opportunity to be involved in fundraising and events.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood people skills,\r\nGood attention to detail,\r\nExperience as a Trustee is desirable but not essential, training will be provided\n\n## Training details\n\nThe successful candidate will be provided an overview of the charity including day to day activities, the charities aims, objectives and governance\n\n## Travel details\n\nHybrid role – there will be a need on occasion to attend face to face meetings in Dunfermline\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nreasonable expenses for public transport or mileage for car owners.",
