            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eOHQAA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eOHQAA2/volunteer-befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Volunteer Befriender",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nFife Women’s Aid’s Befriending Service offers support to women across Fife who have experienced domestic abuse.\r\n\r\nTheir volunteer befrienders usually meet their befriendee weekly for 1-3 hours. This gives women a chance to talk. Befrienders encourage and support women to get out of their home and do something together – like going for a walk, a coffee, shopping, going to the gym or maybe engaging in a class in the local community.  They adopt a person-centred approach, so this will be different for every woman’s journey.\r\n\r\nThe goals of the befriending service are to;\r\n\r\n-Empower Women\r\n-Build Independence\r\n-Build Confidence\r\n-Reduce Isolation and Loneliness\r\n\r\nOnly women are eligible to apply for this post due to Genuine Occupational Requirement (Schedule 9; Equality Act 2010). Fife Women’s Aid welcomes applications from women from all sectors of the community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou will need;\r\n-An interest in supporting recovery from domestic abuse\r\n-Non-judgemental, empathetic and trauma-informed approach to working with women\r\n-Self-awareness and an ability to reflect on your work and progress\r\n-Good communication skills\r\n-Ability to maintain confidentiality\r\n-Able to volunteer within guidelines without direct supervision\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training and support will be offered throughout your time with FWA. You will have the option to attend volunteer meetings, training and social events throughout the year.\r\n\r\nThe initial training will be carried out over 3-4 sessions held weekly, in the evenings at our office for around 2.5 hours per session.\n\n## Travel details\n\nFife Women’s Aid supports women throughout Fife. They will match you with someone in your local area or within a reasonable and agreed travelling distance.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThey will cover all travel and out of pocket expenses agreed with the Befriending Coordinator. These are reimbursed monthly. Mileage is reimbursed at 45p per mile.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
