                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNqooAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNqooAAD/digital-gardener",
                    "publishStart": "2021-09-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Digital Gardener",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTo provide digital support for the creation of digital trails and experiences within the Ninewells Community Garden.\n\n## Description\n\nThis volunteer role is intended to support the creation of specific digital tools within the Ninewells Community Garden and is expected to involve:\r\n\r\n• Liaising with staff on project requirements and specifics to ensure that content and methods meet existing quality criteria.\r\n• The creation of garden activities which can be accessed online.\r\n• The creation of trails and information which can be accessed digitally within the garden.\r\n• Updating staff and trustees on progress through presentations at board meetings.\r\n• Working with other garden volunteers on content creation and information. \r\n• Other activities which would support this work. \r\n\r\nIt is expected that this role will be shared amongst a number of volunteers who will form the basis of a small team working collaboratively.\n\n## Experience required\n\n• An excellent working knowledge of Microsoft Office, the creation of QR codes or WordPress is essential, along with suitable IT equipment to enable access to online accounts and documents.\r\n• An enthusiasm for community gardening would be advantageous.\r\n• A willingness to work as part of a wider team of volunteers is essential.\n\n## Training details\n\n• An initial induction will be given to all new volunteers\r\n• Additional training and support is available depending on need.\r\n• It is expected that volunteers will identify any support needs required.\r\n• We offer regular volunteer meetings to provide an opportunity to give feedback and contribute ideas.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nTo be arranged but ideally at least 2 hours across the week. Any visits to the garden would need to be done during facilitated hours unless otherwise negotiated. It is expected that this project take appproximately 6 months to complete once started.\n\n## Travel details\n\nHome-based with some visits to Ninewells Community Garden.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe do not routinely reimburse travel expenses but may be able to dependent on individual need.",
