        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZpmAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZpmAAE/risk-factory-the",
            "name": "Risk Factory (The)",
            "description": "To provide a high quality, interactive community safety education resource for all people living in and visiting the Lothians.  In particular to: improve community safety; increase community involvement; change attitudes; modify behaviour; reduce health risks",
            "website": "https://www.theriskfactory.org",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunitySafety",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Safety"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000MbsfGAAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000MbsfGAAR/safetytour-guide",
                    "publishStart": "2019-08-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-27",
                    "title": "Safety/Tour Guide",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe role is a Safety / Tour Guide escorting small groups round the scenario area delivering safety messages and running simple activities.\n\n## Description\n\nThe Risk Factory is a purpose built centre set up like a film set of everyday situations where visitors can experience risk in a safe environment covering topics such as fire, home and road safety.  Our volunteer Safety / Tour Guides escort small groups round the lifelike scenarios delivering safety messages and running simple activities that enable them to think about dangers and actions to reduce and / or avoid risk.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication skills; reliable, responsible and trustworthy; and willing to learn about safety / everyday life skills.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training, shadowing existing volunteers and scenario training will be provided.  No volunteer is expected to start leading small groups round the scenario area until they feel confident to do so.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2 sessions per month ideally.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Risk Factory, 20 New Mart Road, Edinburgh EH14 1RL.\n\nA small car park and free on-street parking is available and there are various LRT buses to the area.  The closest bus stop wold be Slateford Station and The Risk Factory is a short 5 minute walk from there.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses should be claimed on an expenses claim form on a monthly basis.  Lunch will be provided if volunteering to do two sessions in a single day.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
