                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SocialEconomySocialEnterprise",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Social Economy / Social Enterprise"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000DrC8QYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000DrC8QYAV/relationship-developer-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-24",
                    "title": "Relationship Developer Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\n-About TAMS\r\nTAMS (The Allotment Market Stall) helps local allotment holders share their surplus produce with the community. We collect and sell fresh, local fruit and vegetables at affordable prices, reducing food waste and celebrating community growing. You can find out more at www.tamstheallotmentmarketstall.org.uk\r\n\r\n-About the Role\r\nWe’re looking for a friendly person to help us stay in touch with allotment sites and build connections with the people and groups that make TAMS what it is.\r\nYou don’t need to do everything on the list – we’re happy to chat about what you enjoy and what fits your time and interests. You’ll be part of a supportive volunteer committee who meet roughly every six weeks.\r\n\r\n-What You Might Do\r\nHere are some examples of how you could help – we’ll tailor things to you:\r\n•\tKeep in touch with one or more allotment sites – pop by now and then, or stay in touch by email or WhatsApp for instance.\r\n•\tEncourage allotment holders to take part in TAMS activities – like donating produce, helping at stalls, or joining collections.\r\n•\tRepresent TAMS at allotment or community events – spreading the word about what we do.\r\n•\tHelp us connect with other local groups and build friendly partnerships.\r\n•\tCome along to our committee meetings (every 6 weeks or so) to share updates and ideas.\r\nEverything is flexible – we’ll chat about what feels right for you!\r\n\r\n-Who We’re Looking For\r\nYou don’t need any special qualifications – just enthusiasm and a friendly approach. This role could suit someone who:\r\n•\tEnjoys chatting with people and making connections\r\n•\tLikes being part of a community project\r\n•\tIs organised and reliable, but also happy to go with the flow\r\n•\tCares about local food, growing, or reducing waste\r\n•\tCan give a small but regular amount of time (we’ll agree what works for you)\r\n\r\n-What You’ll Get\r\n•\tA warm welcome from a small, friendly team of volunteers\r\n•\tThe chance to help your community and support local growing\r\n•\tOpportunities to meet new people and build local links\r\n•\tExperience in community engagement and teamwork\r\n•\tSupport and guidance from the committee and other volunteers\r\n\r\n-Interested?\r\nWe’d love to have a chat!\r\nDrop us an email at theallotmentmarketstall@gmail.com\n\n## Description\n\n-About TAMS\r\nTAMS (The Allotment Market Stall) helps local allotment holders share their surplus produce with the community. We collect and sell fresh, local fruit and vegetables at affordable prices, reducing food waste and celebrating community growing. You can find out more at www.tamstheallotmentmarketstall.org.uk\r\n\r\n-About the Role\r\nWe’re looking for a friendly person to help us stay in touch with allotment sites and build connections with the people and groups that make TAMS what it is.\r\nYou don’t need to do everything on the list – we’re happy to chat about what you enjoy and what fits your time and interests. You’ll be part of a supportive volunteer committee who meet roughly every six weeks.\r\n\r\n-What You Might Do\r\nHere are some examples of how you could help – we’ll tailor things to you:\r\n•\tKeep in touch with one or more allotment sites – pop by now and then, or stay in touch by email or WhatsApp for instance.\r\n•\tEncourage allotment holders to take part in TAMS activities – like donating produce, helping at stalls, or joining collections.\r\n•\tRepresent TAMS at allotment or community events – spreading the word about what we do.\r\n•\tHelp us connect with other local groups and build friendly partnerships.\r\n•\tCome along to our committee meetings (every 6 weeks or so) to share updates and ideas.\r\nEverything is flexible – we’ll chat about what feels right for you!\r\n\r\n-Who We’re Looking For\r\nYou don’t need any special qualifications – just enthusiasm and a friendly approach. This role could suit someone who:\r\n•\tEnjoys chatting with people and making connections\r\n•\tLikes being part of a community project\r\n•\tIs organised and reliable, but also happy to go with the flow\r\n•\tCares about local food, growing, or reducing waste\r\n•\tCan give a small but regular amount of time (we’ll agree what works for you)\r\n\r\n-What You’ll Get\r\n•\tA warm welcome from a small, friendly team of volunteers\r\n•\tThe chance to help your community and support local growing\r\n•\tOpportunities to meet new people and build local links\r\n•\tExperience in community engagement and teamwork\r\n•\tSupport and guidance from the committee and other volunteers\r\n\r\n-Interested?\r\nWe’d love to have a chat!\r\nDrop us an email at theallotmentmarketstall@gmail.com\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F33833d3e-4f49-a4e2-6d2e-7c4eed3380ae%2FxaTtjdQJn6fMNwfjoZJ3hkqzJ6H2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=dfb7ff59-a688-4b8b-93fd-99a4b131cacf",
