                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Dr2lnYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Dr2lnYAB/fundraiser-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Fundraiser Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\n-About TAMS\r\nTAMS (The Allotment Market Stall) helps local allotment holders share their surplus produce with the community. We collect and sell fresh, local fruit and vegetables at affordable prices, reducing food waste and celebrating community growing. You can find out more at www.tamstheallotmentmarketstall.org.uk\r\n\r\n-About the Role\r\nWe’re looking for someone to help us keep TAMS thriving by supporting our fundraising efforts.\r\nThe Fundraiser will take the lead on looking for new grants and funding opportunities, coordinating applications, and helping to report back to funders when needed.\r\nYou don’t need to do this alone – the committee and other volunteers can help with writing, ideas, and gathering information. The Treasurer will support you with the financial parts of reports.\r\nAll tasks are open for discussion, so we can agree on what fits your interests, time, and experience.\r\n\r\n-What You Might Do\r\nHere are some examples of how you could help – we’ll shape the role around you:\r\n•\tKeep an eye out for grant or funding opportunities that fit TAMS’s work.\r\n•\tLead on writing or coordinating grant applications (with support from other volunteers).\r\n•\tHelp gather stories, photos, and outcomes that show the impact of TAMS’s activities.\r\n•\tSupport report writing for funders – with help from the Treasurer for financial information.\r\n•\tAttend committee meetings (about every 6 weeks) to share updates, ideas, and funding progress.\r\n•\tWork with the team to plan ahead for future funding needs.\r\nDon’t worry if you haven’t done all these things before – we can help you learn and support you along the way.\r\n________________________________________\r\nWho We’re Looking For\r\nThis role would suit someone who:\r\n•\tEnjoys writing, organising information, or researching opportunities.\r\n•\tIs interested in helping community projects stay sustainable and grow.\r\n•\tIs comfortable working independently but happy to collaborate with others.\r\n•\tCan give a little time regularly and keep an overview of funding activities.\r\n•\tHas some experience or interest in fundraising, grant writing, or community projects (though this isn’t essential).\r\n\r\n-What You’ll Get\r\n•\tA warm welcome into a friendly, supportive volunteer team.\r\n•\tThe chance to make a real difference by helping TAMS secure the funding that keeps it running.\r\n•\tOpportunities to build experience in community fundraising and teamwork.\r\n•\tSupport from the Treasurer and other committee members.\r\n•\tTravel expenses covered for meetings and events (if needed).\r\n•\tSatisfaction of seeing your efforts help local growers and the community.\r\n\r\n-Interested?\r\nWe’d love to hear from you!\r\nEmail us at theallotmentmarketstall@gmail.com\n\n## Description\n\n-About TAMS\r\nTAMS (The Allotment Market Stall) helps local allotment holders share their surplus produce with the community. We collect and sell fresh, local fruit and vegetables at affordable prices, reducing food waste and celebrating community growing. You can find out more at www.tamstheallotmentmarketstall.org.uk\r\n\r\n-About the Role\r\nWe’re looking for someone to help us keep TAMS thriving by supporting our fundraising efforts.\r\nThe Fundraiser will take the lead on looking for new grants and funding opportunities, coordinating applications, and helping to report back to funders when needed.\r\nYou don’t need to do this alone – the committee and other volunteers can help with writing, ideas, and gathering information. The Treasurer will support you with the financial parts of reports.\r\nAll tasks are open for discussion, so we can agree on what fits your interests, time, and experience.\r\n\r\n-What You Might Do\r\nHere are some examples of how you could help – we’ll shape the role around you:\r\n•\tKeep an eye out for grant or funding opportunities that fit TAMS’s work.\r\n•\tLead on writing or coordinating grant applications (with support from other volunteers).\r\n•\tHelp gather stories, photos, and outcomes that show the impact of TAMS’s activities.\r\n•\tSupport report writing for funders – with help from the Treasurer for financial information.\r\n•\tAttend committee meetings (about every 6 weeks) to share updates, ideas, and funding progress.\r\n•\tWork with the team to plan ahead for future funding needs.\r\nDon’t worry if you haven’t done all these things before – we can help you learn and support you along the way.\r\n\r\n-Who We’re Looking For\r\nThis role would suit someone who:\r\n•\tEnjoys writing, organising information, or researching opportunities.\r\n•\tIs interested in helping community projects stay sustainable and grow.\r\n•\tIs comfortable working independently but happy to collaborate with others.\r\n•\tCan give a little time regularly and keep an overview of funding activities.\r\n•\tHas some experience or interest in fundraising, grant writing, or community projects (though this isn’t essential).\r\n\r\n-What You’ll Get\r\n•\tA warm welcome into a friendly, supportive volunteer team.\r\n•\tThe chance to make a real difference by helping TAMS secure the funding that keeps it running.\r\n•\tOpportunities to build experience in community fundraising and teamwork.\r\n•\tSupport from the Treasurer and other committee members.\r\n•\tTravel expenses covered for meetings and events (if needed).\r\n•\tSatisfaction of seeing your efforts help local growers and the community.\r\n\r\n-Interested?\r\nWe’d love to hear from you!\r\nEmail us at theallotmentmarketstall@gmail.com\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.",
