                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000DrIIfYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000DrIIfYAN/communications-social-media-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Communications & Social Media Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\n-About TAMS\r\nTAMS (The Allotment Market Stall) helps local allotment holders share their surplus produce with the community. We collect and sell fresh, local fruit and vegetables at affordable prices, reducing food waste and celebrating community growing. You can find out more at www.tamstheallotmentmarketstall.org.uk\r\n\r\n-About the Role\r\nWe’re looking for a Communications & Social Media Volunteer to help us share the story of TAMS with the community — online, through our website, and with our volunteers.\r\nThis role involves helping to keep our website and social media pages up to date, sharing news about our events and activities, and supporting volunteer communications such as newsletters and email updates.\r\nYou don’t need to be an expert — just someone who enjoys writing posts, sharing photos, or keeping things organised online.\r\nAll tasks are open for discussion so we can find what best fits your interests, skills, and time.\r\n\r\n-What You Might Do\r\nHere are some examples of how you could help — you can do all or just some of these:\r\n•\tKeep the TAMS website up to date with current information and events.\r\n•\tPost regular updates and photos on TAMS social media (e.g. Facebook, Instagram).\r\n•\tShare news about stalls, collections, and community events.\r\n•\tCreate or coordinate a simple quarterly newsletter for supporters and volunteers.\r\n•\tHelp the Volunteer Coordinator send updates to our mailing list.\r\n•\tAttend a short committee meetings every 6 weeks to share updates and ideas.\r\n•\tSuggest new ways to spread the word and engage our community.\r\nWe’ll chat with you to find the mix of tasks that feels right for you.\r\n\r\n-Who We’re Looking For\r\nYou don’t need to be a professional communicator — enthusiasm and creativity are what matter most!\r\nThis role could suit someone who:\r\n•\tEnjoys social media, writing, or taking photos.\r\n•\tLikes sharing community stories or creative content.\r\n•\tIs organised and comfortable keeping things up to date.\r\n•\tCares about local food, sustainability, or community projects.\r\n•\tCan offer a few hours regularly (we’ll agree what fits your time).\r\nBasic familiarity with social media or simple website editing is helpful — but we’ll support you if you’re new to it.\r\n\r\n-What You’ll Get\r\n•\tA warm welcome from a friendly, supportive volunteer team.\r\n•\tA creative and flexible role where you can shape how TAMS shares its story.\r\n•\tExperience in community communications, social media, and digital content.\r\n•\tSupport and guidance from the committee and Volunteer Coordinator.\r\n•\tTravel expenses covered for meetings or events (if needed).\r\n•\tThe satisfaction of helping a local project grow its reach and impact.\r\n\r\n-Interested?\r\nWe’d love to hear from you!\r\nEmail us at theallotmentmarketstall@gmail.com\r\nThere’s no formal application process – just tell us a little about yourself and how you’d like to get involved. We’ll work out together what fits your time and interests.\n\n## Description\n\n-About TAMS\r\nTAMS (The Allotment Market Stall) helps local allotment holders share their surplus produce with the community. We collect and sell fresh, local fruit and vegetables at affordable prices, reducing food waste and celebrating community growing. You can find out more at www.tamstheallotmentmarketstall.org.uk\r\n\r\n-About the Role\r\nWe’re looking for a Communications & Social Media Volunteer to help us share the story of TAMS with the community — online, through our website, and with our volunteers.\r\nThis role involves helping to keep our website and social media pages up to date, sharing news about our events and activities, and supporting volunteer communications such as newsletters and email updates.\r\nYou don’t need to be an expert — just someone who enjoys writing posts, sharing photos, or keeping things organised online.\r\nAll tasks are open for discussion so we can find what best fits your interests, skills, and time.\r\n\r\n-What You Might Do\r\nHere are some examples of how you could help — you can do all or just some of these:\r\n•\tKeep the TAMS website up to date with current information and events.\r\n•\tPost regular updates and photos on TAMS social media (e.g. Facebook, Instagram).\r\n•\tShare news about stalls, collections, and community events.\r\n•\tCreate or coordinate a simple quarterly newsletter for supporters and volunteers.\r\n•\tHelp the Volunteer Coordinator send updates to our mailing list.\r\n•\tAttend a short committee meetings every 6 weeks to share updates and ideas.\r\n•\tSuggest new ways to spread the word and engage our community.\r\nWe’ll chat with you to find the mix of tasks that feels right for you.\r\n\r\n-Who We’re Looking For\r\nYou don’t need to be a professional communicator — enthusiasm and creativity are what matter most!\r\nThis role could suit someone who:\r\n•\tEnjoys social media, writing, or taking photos.\r\n•\tLikes sharing community stories or creative content.\r\n•\tIs organised and comfortable keeping things up to date.\r\n•\tCares about local food, sustainability, or community projects.\r\n•\tCan offer a few hours regularly (we’ll agree what fits your time).\r\nBasic familiarity with social media or simple website editing is helpful — but we’ll support you if you’re new to it.\r\n\r\n-What You’ll Get\r\n•\tA warm welcome from a friendly, supportive volunteer team.\r\n•\tA creative and flexible role where you can shape how TAMS shares its story.\r\n•\tExperience in community communications, social media, and digital content.\r\n•\tSupport and guidance from the committee and Volunteer Coordinator.\r\n•\tTravel expenses covered for meetings or events (if needed).\r\n•\tThe satisfaction of helping a local project grow its reach and impact.\r\n\r\n-Interested?\r\nWe’d love to hear from you!\r\nEmail us at theallotmentmarketstall@gmail.com\r\nThere’s no formal application process – just tell us a little about yourself and how you’d like to get involved. We’ll work out together what fits your time and interests.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.",
