                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pc7HtAAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pc7HtAAJ/market-garden-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Market Garden Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe Allotment Market Stall provides good-quality, well-priced, locally grown fruit and vegetables and reduces waste. We have opportunities this season for volunteers to be a part of developing our nature friendly market garden, based at Grove Nursery, Hazlehead, Aberdeen, AB15 8LD on Thursdays 1-3pm and/or Saturdays 11am-1pm. This provides the opportunity to:\r\n\r\n•\tJoin in with the cultivation of a nature friendly market garden \r\n•\tWould suit someone who enjoys outdoors and nature and wants to be part of a community project promoting local food growing.\r\n\r\n-Main tasks involve:  \r\n•\tHelp make and plant up our no dig beds.\r\n•\tSowing seeds and looking after them.\r\n•\tPlanting and tending fruit and veg.\r\n•\tGarden maintenance and DIY.\r\n\r\nFull training will be given. Volunteers will be accompanied and supported at all times.\r\n\r\n-This is a great opportunity to:\r\n•\tMake a difference in your city and the environment.\r\n•\tBe a part of a community of growers.\r\n•\tLearn gardening skills.\r\n\r\nTo get involved/for more information please email us at: Theallotmentmarketstall@gmail.com \r\n\r\nMore information is also available at https://www.tamstheallotmentmarketstall.org.uk/get-involved\n\n## Description\n\nThe Allotment Market Stall provides good-quality, well-priced, locally grown fruit and vegetables and reduces waste. We have opportunities this season for volunteers to be a part of developing our nature friendly market garden, based at Grove Nursery, Hazlehead, Aberdeen, AB15 8LD on Thursdays 1-3pm and/or Saturdays 11am-1pm. This provides the opportunity to:\r\n\r\n•\tJoin in with the cultivation of a nature friendly market garden \r\n•\tWould suit someone who enjoys outdoors and nature and wants to be part of a community project promoting local food growing.\r\n\r\n-Main tasks involve:  \r\n•\tHelp make and plant up our no dig beds.\r\n•\tSowing seeds and looking after them.\r\n•\tPlanting and tending fruit and veg.\r\n•\tGarden maintenance and DIY.\r\n\r\nFull training will be given. Volunteers will be accompanied and supported at all times.\r\n\r\n-This is a great opportunity to:\r\n•\tMake a difference in your city and the environment.\r\n•\tBe a part of a community of growers.\r\n•\tLearn gardening skills.\r\n\r\nTo get involved/for more information please email us at: Theallotmentmarketstall@gmail.com \r\n\r\nMore information is also available at https://www.tamstheallotmentmarketstall.org.uk/get-involved\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is given and volunteers are accompanied and supported at all times.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThursdays 1-3pm and/or Saturdays 11am-1pm. All helps makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis volunteer role is based at Grove Nursery, Hazlehead, Aberdeen, AB15 8LD.",
