                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Agriculture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Agriculture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Horticulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Horticulture"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000AtPsTAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000AtPsTAAV/garden-maintenance",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Garden Maintenance",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are a non profit making company whose main aim is to make a positive contribution to our community, in the hope of enhancing the quality of life for some of the local people. We provide opportunities for work and vocational training, specifically, although not exclusively targeting the unemployed and disadvantaged. Our base is The Church at the Cross on Union Street and our first project is the proposal to create a community garden on a vacant site in the Hareleeshill area of the town.\n\n## Description\n\nGarden volunteer at Larkhall Community Garden is an exciting and unique opportunity to be part of a friendly horticulture team. The volunteer will help us maintain our Community Garden in Hareleeshill Larkhall which was previously derelict land. Volunteer will gain experience in working on raised beds, sensory garden wildlife garden and within our polytunnels.\nWe hold weekly drop-in volunteering sessions as part of our Garden hours. \nTo assist in seasonal gardening tasks throughout the year that will develop as the gardens develop. Volunteers will work in supervised groups led by a Garden Manager. Some tasks are physically demanding and require a level of manual dexterity. Volunteers will work to the Larkhall Community Growers health and safety policies and procedures.\n• Garden maintenance – including weeding, mulching, raking, digging over, staking and tying in, pruning, dead heading, bed preparation, tidying and path maintenance.\n• Seasonal propagation and growing on – including seed sowing, cuttings, potting up.\n• While support will be provided, from time to time volunteers may work independently or without one to one supervision\n\n## Experience required\n\nGardening / Conservation, Creative,Hard Working,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Team Player,Trustworthy,Hard Working, Practical, Reliable, Dependable, Team Player, Trustworthy, Flexible –willing to give support where necessary and be able to adapt to changing priorities.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2 hours per week\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nLarkhall",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000AtPsTAAV#role",
