            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FhqfRYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FhqfRYAR/volunteer-wellbeing-space-welcome-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Volunteer Wellbeing Space Welcome Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nA crucial role in creating a warm, friendly, and efficient atmosphere, often acting as the first point of contact for visitors.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities\r\n●\tCustomer Service & Welcoming: Greeting customers, providing a warm welcome, answering questions, and helping visitors\r\n●\tFood & Drink Service making hot/cold drinks, making and serving food. light food preparation, such as making sandwiches or handling cakes. Subject to food hygiene training and certificate.\r\n●\tSpace Maintenance: Clearing and cleaning tables, washing up (loading/unloading the dishes steriliser) , and ensuring the space is tidy.\r\n●\tOperational Support: Restocking snacks, assisting with opening/closing procedures, and ensuring health and safety standards are met.\r\n●\tOptional Tasks: opportunities may be available to assist with additional tasks\r\n\r\nMon-Fri 11am-3pm - Day Rota 4hrs\n\n## Experience required\n\n●\tFriendly & Polite: A cheerful, welcoming, and approachable personality.\r\n●\tCommunication Skills: Confident in talking to visitors, working independently and as part of a team.\r\n●\tReliability & Flexibility: Reliable, punctual, and willing to work as part of a rota.\r\n●\tPhysical Stamina: Capable of commitment to rota 11am till 3pm, answering the door and carrying hot cups.\r\n●\tExperience: Previous experience is not required; training is provided.\n\n## Training details\n\n●\tSkill Development: Gaining hands-on experience, customer service skills, training including Food Hygiene and First Aid certificates\n\n## Travel details\n\nLocation: GRACE HQ & Wellbeing Space, 22 Union street kirkintilloch G66 1DH",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FhqfRYAR#role",
