        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZxbAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZxbAAE/musselburgh-and-district-citizens-advice-bureau",
            "name": "Musselburgh and District Citizens Advice Bureau",
            "description": "Citizens Advice Bureaux are local, independent charities that provide free and confidential advice and information whoever you are and whatever your problem.  There is a CAB in almost every community in Scotland, across almost 300 locations, helping more that 260,000 people each year.",
            "website": "http://www.musselburghcab.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC013364"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MoneyDebtAdvice",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Money / Debt Advice"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/WelfareRightsBenefits",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Welfare Rights / Benefits"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Ji9uHYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Ji9uHYAR/reception-triage",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-11",
                    "title": "Reception Triage",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Reception Triage is the first point of contact within the bureau for our clients; they are part of our advice team but are not advisers. The Reception Triage will be responsible for ensuring the smooth running of our Reception phones and front desk, welcoming our clients and ensuring they receive excellent customer service from the moment they contact our bureau. They take steps to ensure that clients’ enquiries are managed effectively and record enough client information to allow the appropriate follow-up advice to be provided. Where additional support for the client might be available, they signpost to other local and national services. Additional tasks may include supporting completion of foodbank referrals.\r\n\r\nWhat might you be doing?\r\n\r\nWelcoming incoming clients appropriately and demonstrating good customer service\r\n\r\nSignposting clients when required, to other organisations that are more appropriate to advise and support the client\r\n\r\nExplaining CAB processes and timescales for dealing with enquiries\r\n\r\nGathering personal information from clients and the initial details of their enquiry\r\n\r\nPerforming administrative duties such as photocopying, scanning, etc. as required.\r\n\r\nUpdating the case recording system (database) with client information\r\n\r\nMaintaining stocks of forms and printed materials\r\n\r\nTake part in any training and development of skills/experience to be competent in role\r\n\r\nSupporting other teams in the bureau to ensure efficient and effective delivery of the CAB advice giving service\r\n\r\nAny other duties deemed appropriate to the role as and when required\r\n\r\nTraining for this role includes:\r\n\r\nA half day induction at the bureau to provide orientation in relation to the bureau and to introduce you to our triage team and set up your IT systems. \r\n\r\nSelf-directed training courses using our electronic learning system, Caslearn. These may be completed during a further half day per week in bureau or at home, at a time to suit the volunteer. Required courses will be set out in the role training plan.\r\n\r\nConcurrently with the above, 2.5 hours per week practical training with peers who will guide you through a process of shadowing them, involving you more and more in the process so that eventually you are leading the process and the peer is observing and supporting you.\r\n\r\nTo apply, please visit: https://search.volunteero.org/288680\n\n## Experience required\n\nComputer / IT / Web; General Admin / Office Support;No Expertise; Phone Support / Information Giver; Retail / Customer Service\n\n## Training details\n\nA mix of online, peer support and 1:1 sessions\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCommitment 3 Months 2.5 Hours, Weekly\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReimbursement of travel costs and lunch.\r\nReimbursement of lunch only if volunteering a full day.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
