                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HkTZtYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HkTZtYAN/general-adviser",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-11",
                    "title": "General Adviser",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDo you have the following skills?\r\n\r\n>Good listener and communicator\r\n>Research and problem-solving\r\n>Excellent IT proficiency\r\n>A drive to learn\r\n>Open-minded and non-judgemental\r\n>Ability to commit for 6 months*\r\n\r\nThen you sound like one of our General Adviser's.\r\n\r\nNo two days will ever be the same as each day comes with a new set of enquiries and learning opportunities. As a General Adviser you will support members of the local community with a variety of enquires, such as:\r\n>Benefits\r\n>Employment\r\n>Consumer\r\n>Relationships\r\n>Housing\r\nAnd much more!\r\n\r\nGeneral Advisers empower clients to understand their rights and understand what options they have so they can make informed decisions. As a General Adviser you could be helping your local community in the following ways:\r\n\r\n>Conducting appointments - by phone, email or in person\r\n>Researching advice and options and providing this to clients in clear manner\r\n>Managing client expectations\r\n>Ensuring client confidentiality\r\n>Updating and maintaining case records.\r\n>Identifying social policy concerns\r\n\r\n*As we commit to Scottish National Standard our General Advisers are also required to volunteer 6 hours per week.\r\n\r\nGeneral Adviser's who complete our online Adviser Training Programme receive 10 level 6 SCQF credits (equivalent to Scottish Highers)\r\n\r\nAvailability\r\nGeneral Adviser shifts are Monday to Friday; 10am -12.30pm & 1.30pm - 4pm. Flexibility of times can be discussed at interview.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGeneral Admin / Office Support; Literacy / Numeracy; No Expertise; Phone Support / Information Giver\n\n## Training details\n\nA mix of online Elearning training and 1:1 support.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCommitment 6 Months 6 Hours, Weekly\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel Expenses for driving and bus tickets.\r\nLunch expenses up to £4.00 if full day volunteering and lunch bought.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HkTZtYAN#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "General Adviser",
                        "description": "General Admin / Office Support; Literacy / Numeracy; No Expertise; Phone Support / Information Giver",
                        "commitment": "Commitment 6 Months 6 Hours, Weekly",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HkTZtYAN/general-adviser?#modal_register_a0gQD00000HkTZtYAN",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
