        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZxkAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZxkAAE/the-hollies-community-hub",
            "name": "The Hollies Community Hub",
            "description": "The Hollies provides meals for the elderly, a meeting place,  a cafe, a second hand shop, dementia club and other numerous activities almost entirely based on Volunteer Support.  We also have a line dancing class, dinner dances, trips, scrabble club etc.  Many people of mixed ages rely on it and volunteers gain a great deal by working there.",
            "website": "http://holliesmusselburgh.wixsite.com/home",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC010650"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/LunchClubs",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Lunch Clubs"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HxPLZYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HxPLZYA3/board-trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-31",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Board Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHelp Shape the Future of The Hollies:\r\n\r\nCould you help write the next chapter of one of East Lothian's most valued community charities?\r\n\r\nFor over 62 years, The Hollies has been a lifeline for older people across Musselburgh and surrounding areas, helping to tackle loneliness and social isolation while providing warmth, friendship, nutritious meals and practical support to those who need it most.\r\n\r\nToday, we're entering an exciting new chapter.\r\n\r\nWe have ambitious plans to build on our proud history, strengthen our long-term sustainability and expand the services we provide to our community.\r\n\r\nWe're now looking to appoint 3–4 new Trustees who share our passion for making a difference.\r\n\r\nWhy The Hollies matters:\r\n\r\nEvery day, we see the difference that connection makes.\r\n\r\nOur Lunch Club supports people over 60 who may be isolated, recovering from illness, living with frailty or experiencing dementia-related conditions. Many are referred by local GP surgeries and East Lothian Council Social Work teams.\r\n\r\nOur free accessible minibus brings clients safely to The Hollies, where they enjoy a nutritious three-course meal, companionship and a welcoming place where everyone belongs.\r\n\r\nOver the last year alone, we've increased the number of people we support by 50%, and demand continues to grow.\r\n\r\nThe Hollies is much more than a Lunch Club:\r\n\r\nOur thriving café welcomes hundreds of visitors each week, many of whom also benefit from the social connections it provides. Our community hub hosts local organisations, charities, veterans, writers, musicians, markets, celebrations and community groups, creating a vibrant space where people of all ages come together.\r\n\r\nTogether, these activities generate income that helps sustain our services while strengthening community life.\r\n\r\nWe're looking for people who can help us grow:\r\n\r\nAs we continue to develop, we're particularly interested in hearing from individuals with experience in:\r\n\r\n• Fundraising, income generation or grant funding\r\n• Strategy and organisational development\r\n• Operations or business management\r\n• Finance or accountancy\r\n\r\nPrevious Trustee experience isn't essential – training is provided and existing Board members are on hand to support.\r\n\r\nWhat matters most is your willingness to contribute your knowledge, ask thoughtful questions and help guide the future of a charity that makes a genuine difference to people's lives.\r\n\r\nThe opportunity:\r\n\r\nThe Hollies has exciting opportunities ahead.\r\n\r\nAlongside growing our services, we're progressing a long-term programme to improve and modernise our much-loved community building, ensuring it remains sustainable and fit for future generations while continuing to meet the needs of our local community.\r\n\r\nAs a Trustee, you'll help shape our strategic direction, support good governance and play an important role in ensuring The Hollies continues to thrive for many years to come.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like to use your experience to make a lasting impact in your local community, we'd love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nWe welcome applications from people of all backgrounds and are committed to building a diverse Board whose experience reflects the communities we serve.\r\n\r\nJoin us and help shape the next chapter of The Hollies.\r\n\r\nTo note your interest in this opportunity, please contact us on holliesmusselburgh@hotmail.co.uk\n\n## Experience required\n\nAccountancy / Finance; Business / HR / Management; Fundraising\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCommitment 2 Years + 2 Hours, Monthly",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HxPLZYA3#role",
                        "type": "Role",
