        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZxwAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZxwAAE/home-start-east-lothian",
            "name": "Home-Start East Lothian",
            "description": "Home-Start East Lothian provides volunteer befrienders to support families under stress, who have at least one pre-school child.  Families choose to have a volunteer, Home-Start recruits volunteers from all over East Lothian, and look for people who are committed, reliable, confidential, non-judgemental and most importantly have parenting skills.  Potential volunteers undergo a preparation course, and after being matched with a family receive support and supervision from the co-ordinator.",
            "website": "https://www.homestarteastlothian.co.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC030943"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FamilySupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Family Support"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000006PXi5YAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000006PXi5YAG/home-start-volunteer-befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-14",
                    "title": "Home-Start Volunteer Befriender",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAttend our preparation course to set you on your way to becoming a volunteer befriender!\r\nVolunteer Befrienders visit a family they are matched to every week and offer practical and emotional support. Families may be experiencing difficulties due to a large number of reasons including, parental mental health and perinatal illness, isolation, money issues, disability and illness, multiple birth, family conflict and many any other issues. We ask\r\nvolunteers to commit to at least 1 year as we will normally support a family for that length of time.\r\nVolunteers get an enormous amount out of belonging to Home-Start East Lothian! They gain worthwhile experience, feel a sense of purpose, are valued as part of a team, receive expenses, regular support and supervision, ongoing training and social gatherings.\r\nMany volunteers have included their volunteering experience in their CV's and this has been a stepping stone to further opportunities and employment\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise All we ask is you have parenting experience or childcare experience\n\n## Training details\n\nWe provide a training course before being matched to a family. We also provide Child Protection training and offer other training opportunities throughout.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCommitment 1 Year 3 Hours, Weekly\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses paid - monthly",
