                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpeRSYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HpeRSYAZ/haddington-bridge-centre-treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-28",
                    "title": "Haddington Bridge Centre Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nVolunteer Treasurer (Trustee)\r\nHaddington Bridge Centre – Haddington\r\n\r\nAre you someone who enjoys working with numbers and wants to make a difference in your local community?\r\nHaddington Bridge Centre is looking for a Volunteer Treasurer to join our Board of Trustees and help support the financial health of our welcoming, community-led hub.\r\n\r\nAbout the Role\r\nAs Treasurer, you’ll play a key role in helping us manage our finances responsibly and sustainably. You don’t need to be a qualified accountant — just confident with figures, organised, and committed to supporting the work of the Centre.\r\nThis is also a Trustee role, meaning you’ll be part of the team guiding the overall direction and governance of the organisation.\r\n\r\nWhat You’ll Do\r\n• Help oversee the Centre’s finances and ensure good financial practice\r\n• Present simple financial updates at Board meetings\r\n• Support budgeting and financial planning\r\n• Ensure appropriate handling of income and expenditure\r\n• Contribute to the overall governance and decision-making of the charity\r\n\r\nWhat We’re Looking For\r\n• An interest in community work and making a positive local impact\r\n• Basic financial awareness and attention to detail\r\n• Reliability and a willingness to get involved\r\n• Ability to explain financial information clearly (support provided)\r\nExperience in finance, bookkeeping or charity work is helpful.\r\n\r\nTime Commitment\r\nAround 6–10 hours per month, including attendance at Board meetings.\r\n\r\nWhat You’ll Gain\r\n• A chance to make a real difference in Haddington\r\n• Experience of charity governance and finance\r\n• The opportunity to develop new skills\r\n• Being part of a friendly and supportive team\r\n\r\nOther information\r\nBecoming a Board member will require a PVG for children and young people and an ID check with Companies House.\r\n\r\nInterested?\r\nWe’d love to have an informal chat. Please get in touch to find out more:\r\nhaddbridgecentre@outlook.com or 01620 823137\n\n## Experience required\n\nAccountancy / Finance\r\nBusiness / HR / Management\r\nCommunity Development / Social work\r\nFundraising\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining needs can be identified\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCommitment 2 Years + 6 Hours, Fortnightly\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAs and when required",
