                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005ZbWTYA0",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005ZbWTYA0/fundraising-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-04",
                    "title": "Fundraising Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCarers of East Lothian Fundraising Group is a group of Volunteer Fundraisers who work throughout the year to raise vital funds for the organisation, so that we can further increase the support we offer to unpaid carers across East Lothian. Fundraising is a fun and rewarding way to get involved in a cause that matters to you, with lots of opportunity to meet like-minded people. This is a flexible role, which can be adapted to suit your interests, skills and availability. The group meets monthly and members will be encouraged to put forward and action their own ideas - working alongside fellow volunteers and staff to devise a programme of exciting fundraising events and initiatives.”\n\n## Experience required\n\nSufficient IT skills to use Microsoft 365 software and organisational database (full training and support provided)\r\n\r\nGood Communicator\r\nOrganised\r\nPractical\r\nReliable / Dependable\r\nSociable\r\nTeam Player\r\nTrustworthy\n\n## Training details\n\nFull induction to the organisation, plus opportunities for further learning and development if wished\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPaid monthly",
