                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000SsKmKAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000SsKmKAAV/carer-support-group-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-04",
                    "title": "Carer Support Group Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCoEL offer a range of regular carer support groups, providing a non-judgemental and supportive environment for unpaid carers in the area and encouraging engagement in peer support. Some of these take place face to face and others online.\r\nWe're seeking volunteers to help with the organisation and facilitation of these groups on a monthly basis, alongside a Carer Support Worker\n\n## Description\n\nResponsibilities will include:\r\nHelp organising monthly carer support groups, including booking venues and inviting attendees, setting up and clearing down. In the case of an online group, this would involve providing administrative support via Zoom.\r\nAttending groups along with a Carer Support Worker to help facilitate, including meeting and greeting, provision of refreshments and promoting discussion and peer support.\n\n## Experience required\n\ngood listening and communication skills\r\nIf an online group reasonable level of confidence with IT\r\nWillingness to learn and develop skills\r\nGenuine interest in improving support offered to carers in local area\r\nA compassionate and non-judgemental attitude towards others.\r\nAbsolute respect for carers confidentiality\r\nAbility to maintain boudaries and seek help and support where needed\n\n## Training details\n\nSupervision with Volunteer and Training Coordinator. Opportunities to meet with and learn from other volunteers. If the volunteer begins to run regular sessions with CoEL, they will be provided with ongoing training and development opportunities.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n3 hours a week\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteers will have access to CoEL offices at East Lothian Community Hospital. Groups will be run at different venues around East Lothian. Some groups are online.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers will be reimbursed on a monthly basis for agreed expenses.\n\n## Taster details\n\nGeneral induction to volunteering with Carers of East Lothian",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000SsKmKAAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Carer Support Group Volunteer",
                        "description": "good listening and communication skills\r\nIf an online group reasonable level of confidence with IT\r\nWillingness to learn and develop skills\r\nGenuine interest in improving support offered to carers in local area\r\nA compassionate and non-judgemental attitude towards others.\r\nAbsolute respect for carers confidentiality\r\nAbility to maintain boudaries and seek help and support where needed",
