            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZyTAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZyTAAU/headway-east-lothian-scio",
            "name": "Headway East Lothian SCIO",
            "description": "Headway East Lothian's aim is to help people over 18 with Aquired Brain Injury (ABI) living in East Lothian, their families & carers to cope with the challenges of their changed lives. ABI may be caused by a trauma such as a road accident or fall, a stroke, tumours, interruption of the supply of oxygen or glucose to brain, as can happen with post operative complications, infections such as encephalitis or meningitis, poisons or complications of other diseases.",
            "website": "https://www.headway-eastlothian.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC035535"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FamilySupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Family Support"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SelfHelpSupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Self-Help / Support"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eKHDAA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eKHDAA2/board-membertrustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-20",
                    "title": "Board Member/Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nOur aim is to make a big difference to people who have suffered a brain injury and their families. We need volunteers with management or financial planning experience to help on our management committee.\n\n## Description\n\nPeople may have acquired their brain injury through an accident or assult, brain tumour, post operative problems, stroke or other illness which caused the brian to be starved of essential nutrients. People with ABI do not fit neatly into physical or mental disability. They may show no sign of injury on the outside but may find planning, communicating or concentrating very difficult. They may be severely physically disabled but have great mental skills and capabilities trapped by their physical disabilities. They will all be lonely and lacking in confidence and their families will be finding life tough. Headways helps to make it less tough. You would play a really pivotal role in keeping the current growing service going and planning for its long term support to these people and their families.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe're looking for volunteers who can enhance our Board with their skills.\r\nBasic computer skills and experience in accounting/book keeping. Secretarial duties, fundraising, experience of running management meetings and good networking skills etc.\r\nKnowledge and experience of business or financial planning would be ideal.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers will receive induction training which will explain the aims of the group, introduce committee members, staff and users. New Board members/Trustees will have access to Headway Scottish Development Officer for support and information.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMeetings held on the second Wednesday of every month.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoard Meetings are usually held on the second Wednesday of the month in the evening at our Haddington meeting place: Occupational Therapy Department, Herdmanflat Hospital, Aberlady Road, Haddington, EH41 3BU\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMileage paid at 40 pence per mile along with other reasonable expenses.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eKHDAA2#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Board Member/Trustee",
                        "description": "We're looking for volunteers who can enhance our Board with their skills.\r\nBasic computer skills and experience in accounting/book keeping. Secretarial duties, fundraising, experience of running management meetings and good networking skills etc.\r\nKnowledge and experience of business or financial planning would be ideal.",
                        "commitment": "Meetings held on the second Wednesday of every month.",
