                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I2IGDYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I2IGDYA3/session-support",
                    "publishStart": "2026-02-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-16",
                    "title": "Session Support",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHeadway East Lothian is looking for a friendly and reliable volunteer to help support one of our peer group sessions for people affected by acquired brain injury.\r\nThis is a short, practical opportunity to help create a welcoming, well-organised and inclusive session. You will work alongside the session lead and will not be expected to provide clinical advice or personal care.\r\nWhat you will do\r\n• Help set up and tidy the room.\r\n• Welcome group members and help them feel comfortable.\r\n• Assist with refreshments and session materials.\r\n• Join in activities and conversations, following the session lead’s guidance.\r\n• Respect confidentiality, boundaries and the needs of group members.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction face-to-face, online training, face-to-face training, group and self-guided\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCommitment Flexible 2 Hours, Weekly\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMonthly, reasonable out of pocket expenses",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
