        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZyjAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZyjAAE/changes-east-lothian",
            "name": "CHANGES (East Lothian)",
            "description": "CHANGES is a Community Health Project which promotes the positive wellbeing of people living in East Lothian. CHANGES works with local people and professionals to develop initiatives and services to help people manage their stress.",
            "website": "https://www.changeschp.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC025130"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IG1M2YAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IG1M2YAL/board-members-and-treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-03",
                    "title": "Board Members and Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nBoard members should be team players who value compassion, inclusivity, and community engagement. You should be passionate about mental health and wellbeing, with a genuine desire to make a lasting contribution to a vital cause.\r\n\r\nIf you join our board, you’ll play a vital role in guiding our strategic direction, ensuring we continue to meet the needs of East Lothian’s diverse community. You will be expected to add value and the benefit of your experience to help shape our efforts in providing compassionate, welcoming, and effective mental health support.\r\n\r\nAs Treasurer you will have specific responsibility for oversight of the organisation’s financial affairs and viability.\r\n\r\nAll Trustees will be required to attend board meetings 4-6 times per year to discuss and shape the direction of the organisation and provide support to the Changes CEO. You will also take part in some strategy sessions with the staff team and may be asked to help at some community events.\r\n\r\nIf you’re looking for a new challenge where you can also make a real difference to the wellbeing of the local community, we’d love to hear from you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAccountancy / Finance; Business / HR / Management\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction to Changes\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCommitment 2 Years + 3 Hours, Monthly",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
