            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Ji3qTYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Ji3qTYAR/instrument-library-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-30",
                    "title": "Instrument Library Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDescription:\r\nFollowing the hugely successful launch of the East Lothian Instrument Lending Library, we are now looking for volunteers to help us sustain and expand our offer. We need people to help clean and maintain the donated instruments as well as check them over and fix any issues when they come back from being out on loan. This would suit a musician who knows their own instrument(s) very well or someone handy who is happy to have a go. No experience is necessary, however as we will give full training and would only ask you to do what feels comfortable to you. We are also looking for volunteers to assist at community music events, mostly in libraries, where our instruments will be being enjoyed at workshops and performances! This role would suit anyone who enjoys music, arts and culture and/or being in the libraries! Again, no experience necessary. This is a super opportunity to give a few spare hours back to the community in a relaxed way. We hope to have a bank of volunteers we can call upon, so the time you offer can be as much or as little as you like. Volunteers do not have to be over 18 but please let us know if you're not when you apply.\n\n## Experience required\n\nArts / Music / Drama / Crafts; Cleaning / Tidying / Sorting; Event Management / Organising\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining available for instrument maintenance. For event support available once initial induction is complete.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCommitment 3 Months 3 Hours, Fortnightly\n\n## Travel expenses\n\ntravel expenses",
