        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZTPAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZTPAA2/borders-independent-advocacy-service-bias",
            "name": "Borders Independent Advocacy Service (BIAS)",
            "description": "We provide information support and representation to people with social care and other needs.  We promote all forms of advocacy.  We are going through a period of growth and change and expanding our remit.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC024967"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/DrugAlcoholIssues",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Drug / Alcohol Issues"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/LawAndJustice",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Law and Justice"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/LearningDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Learning Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Elderly",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Elderly"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HYUMrYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HYUMrYAP/trustee-board-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-30",
                    "title": "Trustee / Board member",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAbout Us\r\nBorders Independent Advocacy Service (BIAS) has established itself as one of Scotland’s leading providers of independent advocacy, delivering exceptional services since 1995. At the heart of our work are the rights of advocacy partners and the power of their voices to bring about positive change.\r\nWe provide individual, issue-based independent advocacy for people across the Scottish Borders. We work alongside corporate parents and communities to broaden understanding, and with policymakers, leaders and elected representatives locally and nationally to shape law, policy and practice based on the lived experience of advocacy partners in Scottish Borders. \r\nAbout the Role\r\nBIAS is seeking passionate, values-driven individuals to join our Board of Trustees and help shape the \r\nfuture of our organisation. If you have experience in finance, HR, law, or advocacy, and a passion for \r\nsupporting others, we would love to hear from you. We are looking to strengthen our Board to help guide \r\nthe charity forward.\r\nWhy Join Us?\r\n• Be part of a dedicated and experienced team.\r\n• Make a real impact in your community.\r\n• Flexible meeting options (in person and online).\r\n• Help us continue our important work and make a difference. \r\nWhat does the role involve?\r\nBoard Members support the strategic direction, governance, and sustainability of Borders Independent \r\nAdvocacy Service. Responsibilities include:\r\n• Attending quarterly Board meetings (held both online and in person).\r\n• Attending occasional additional meetings, particularly during key development periods.\r\n• Meetings usually lasting less than 2 hours \r\n• Reviewing Board papers in advance, which are circulated by email (hard copies available on request)\r\n• Supporting good governance and effective decision-making.\r\n• Acting as an ambassador for BIAS.\r\n• Contributing skills, expertise, and insight.\r\n• Supporting the organisation to achieve its strategic objectives.\r\nThis is a voluntary role, offering the opportunity to make a genuine difference in the lives of advocacy \r\npartners across the Scottish Borders and contribute to the organisation’s continued growth.\r\nWhat we offer\r\n• The opportunity to make a real difference in people’s lives.\r\n• A supportive, inclusive and values-led Board.\r\n• Induction, training, and ongoing development.\r\n• Opportunities to contribute strategically to a growing organisation.\r\n• Experience of charity governance and strategic leadership.\r\nApplication notes\r\nInterested candidates are asked to email a completed application to alicja@bordersadvocacy.org.uk by 17 \r\nJuly 2026.\r\nInterviews will be held virtually or face-to-face, dates TBC.\n\n## Description\n\nBoard Member Role Profile\r\nRole Title: Board Member / Trustee\r\nLocation: Scottish Borders (hybrid meetings available where appropriate)\r\nTime Commitment: Approximately 4 Board meetings per year, plus occasional sub-group \r\nReports to: Chair of the Board\r\n\r\nPurpose of the Role\r\nBoard Members are responsible for the overall governance, strategic direction, and sustainability of Borders Independent Advocacy Service (BIAS). Trustees work collectively to ensure the organisation delivers its charitable objectives, complies with legal and regulatory responsibilities, and operates in line with its mission and values.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities\r\nBoard Members are expected to:\r\n• Contribute to the strategic leadership and direction of Borders Independent Advocacy Service (BIAS).\r\n• Ensure strong governance, accountability, and effective decision-making.\r\n• Support the financial sustainability and oversight of the organisation.\r\n• Promote the mission, vision, and values of BIAS.\r\n• Act in the best interests of the organisation and the advocacy partners we work with.\r\n• Review and approve key policies, budgets, strategies, and organisational plans.\r\n• Monitor organisational performance, impact, and risk.\r\n• Support and constructively challenge the senior leadership team where appropriate.\r\n• Maintain confidentiality and declare any conflicts of interest.\r\n• Act as ambassadors for Borders Independent Advocacy Service within the wider community and sector.\r\n\r\nTime Commitment\r\n• Board meetings every 15 weeks (1.5-2 hours each).\r\n• Preparation in advance of meetings (reading papers, considering key decisions).\r\n• Occasional additional involvement in sub-groups, recruitment panels, or support with specific areas of expertise.\r\n\r\nPerson Specification\r\nWe are currently seeking new Trustees to share with us their experience, talents, and passions. We are particularly interested in those with experience in:\r\n\r\nSupport and Development\r\nBorders Independent Advocacy Service (BIAS) is committed to supporting Board Members through:\r\n• Full induction and onboarding.\r\n• Ongoing training and development opportunities.\r\n• Access to relevant policies and governance support.\r\n• Opportunities to contribute to strategic development and sector leadership.\r\n\r\nEquality and Diversity\r\nBorders Independent Advocacy Service (BIAS) is committed to building a diverse and inclusive Board. We \r\nactively encourage applications from individuals from underrepresented communities and those with lived \r\nexperience relevant to our work.\r\n\r\nExpenses\r\nThis is a voluntary unpaid role. Reasonable expenses will be reimbursed in line with Borders Independent \r\nAdvocacy Service (BIAS) policy\n\n## Experience required\n\nEssential\r\n• Commitment to Borders Independent Advocacy Service vision, mission and values.\r\n• Strong communication and interpersonal skills with collaborative approach.\r\n• Strategic thinker with sound judgement and effective decision-making abilities.\r\n• Finance or accountancy. \r\n• Human Resources.\r\n• Law, policy development.\r\n\r\nDesirable\r\nExperience or knowledge in one or more of the following areas is welcomed:\r\n• Marketing, communications, or fundraising and income generation.\r\n• Business or leadership\r\n• Health and social care.\r\n• Lived experience relevant to Borders Independent Advocacy Service.\r\n• Understanding of Board members responsibilities.\r\n\r\nAppointment to the position of Board Member may be subject to checks which may impact on eligibility, \r\nincluding Protection of Children and Protected Adults.  This post is subject to a Level 2 PVG check and the \r\nsuccessful candidate will be required to declare any convictions as per the Management of Offenders \r\n(Scotland) Act 2019.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a voluntary unpaid role. Reasonable expenses will be reimbursed in line with Borders Independent \r\nAdvocacy Service (BIAS) policy.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThis is a voluntary unpaid role. Reasonable expenses will be reimbursed in line with Borders Independent \r\nAdvocacy Service (BIAS) policy.",
