        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZUVAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZUVAA2/borders-pet-rescue",
            "name": "Borders Pet Rescue",
            "description": "Borders Pet Rescue (BPR) was established in 1988, as a small, registered, Scottish charity offering animal rescue, re-homing, and the promotion of responsible pet ownership through education and training across the Scottish Borders and adjoining areas. Our Rescue Centre is located at Craigsford, in Earlston. Each year we are able to find new homes for over 200 dogs, cats, rabbits, guinea pigs and exotics. We rely on donations from the public, on some fundraising, and primarily on the income raised by the four Borders Pet Rescue Charity Shops, located in Galashiels, Kelso, Duns, and Hawick. Like all animal charities, BPR relies on the generosity of the animal loving public to support the work and could not survive without the dedication of its many friends and volunteers.",
            "website": "https://www.borderspetrescue.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC001583"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AnimalWelfare",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Animal Welfare"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzNh3YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HzNh3YAF/stockroom-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-12",
                    "title": "Stockroom Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur Stockroom Volunteers play a vital role behind the scenes, helping us turn generous donations into valuable funds for our charity.\r\nDo you enjoy sorting, organising, discovering hidden gems and finding out what things are worth? Are you practical, hands-on and happy to get stuck in?\r\n\r\nWhat will you be doing?\r\n• Sorting donations – checking, categorising and selecting items for sale.\r\n• Cleaning and preparing stock – getting donated goods looking their best.\r\n• Steaming clothes – making clothing fresh and ready for the shop floor.\r\n• Organising stock – keeping our stockroom tidy and well organised.\r\n• Researching and pricing – discovering brands, checking values and helping price items.\r\n• Finding hidden gems – identifying vintage, designer, collectable and unusual items that could be sold online.\r\nWhat are we looking for?\r\n• Someone who enjoys practical, hands-on tasks.\r\n• A good eye for detail and quality.\r\n• An interest in second-hand goods, fashion, vintage or collectables.\r\n• Someone who enjoys learning and discovering new things.\r\n• A friendly, reliable team player.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat's in it for you?\r\n• Meet new people and make friends.\r\n• Learn new skills and discover interesting items.\r\n• Gain experience in retail, stock management and online selling.\r\n• Be part of a friendly and supportive team.\r\n• Most importantly, help raise vital funds for a great cause!\r\n\r\nEvery donation has potential. Every volunteer makes a difference.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous retail experience necessary, training will be provided.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction/ trial shift available\r\nSupport from Shop Manager and Retail Operations Manager\r\nAccess on online training via Charity Retail Learning Academy\n\n## Taster details\n\nTaster session/ trial shift available to meet the team and get an idea of what the role involves.\r\nWhen application is received or made instore, the shop manager will then be in touch to have an informal chat and arrange a trial shift.",
