                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Ijb7ZYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Ijb7ZYAR/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-21",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nOur Trustees provide strategic leadership, guidance and support to Borders Pet Rescue’s staff and volunteers, helping ensure the charity remains sustainable and continues to meet the growing needs of animals and their owners across the community. \r\nBy contributing skills, experience and networks, \r\nTrustees help strengthen fundraising, engagement and long-term planning to secure our charity’s future for another 40 years and beyond.\n\n## Description\n\nHelp Shape the Future of Borders Pet Rescue\r\nDo you have skills, experience or connections that could help protect the future of animal rescue in the \r\nScottish Borders?\r\nBorders Pet Rescue are looking for passionate, committed volunteers to join our Board of Trustees and help shape the future of our charity as we look ahead to our 40th anniversary in 2028. For almost four decades, we have been there for animals in need. Now, we want to make sure we’re still here for the next 40 years.\r\n\r\nWhy we need you \r\nCharities are facing increasingly challenging times. The number of animals and owners needing our support is growing, while operating costs continue to rise. Fundraising, community engagement and long term sustainability have never been more important.\r\nTo continue our vital work, we need people who can bring fresh ideas, practical expertise and new connections to help us navigate these challenges and build a strong, sustainable future.\r\n\r\nWhat could you bring to the table?\r\nWe’re keen to hear from people with skills or experience in any of the following areas:– HR & People Management– Finance & Business Planning– IT & Digital– Retail & Commercial Operations– Animal Welfare– Fundraising & Income Generation– Marketing & Communications– Governance & Charity Leadership\r\nYou don’t need to have experience in every area, nor do you need to be an animal welfare expert. We’re looking for people who care about our mission, are willing to share their knowledge and can work collaboratively to help the charity thrive.\r\n\r\nWhat does being a Trustee involve?\r\nOur Trustees play a vital role in guiding the charity, providing strategic direction, oversight and support to our small team of staff and dedicated volunteers across our animal rescue centre and charity retail shops. As a Trustee, you will help us make important decisions, explore opportunities, strengthen our fundraising and community engagement, and ensure we can continue supporting animals and the people who love them.\r\nThe commitment includes:\r\n– Board meetings every two months, plus our Annual General Meeting (AGM).\r\n– Meetings held in person, with virtual meetings available during the winter months.\r\n– An expected commitment of around two days per month.\r\n– Attending fundraising events and helping raise awareness of our work.\r\n– Using your existing networks, knowledge and connections to open doors and create opportunities for the charity.\r\nThis is a voluntary, unpaid role, but one with the opportunity to make a lasting difference.\r\n\r\nHelp us build the next chapter\r\nWe know that the future brings challenges, but it also brings opportunities. With the right people around the table, we can strengthen Borders Pet Rescue, reach more people, support more animals and build a charity that continues to serve our community for generations to come. If you have skills to share, ideas to contribute and a desire to make a meaningful difference, we’d love to hear from you.\r\nJoin us. Share your skills. Help secure the future of Borders Pet Rescue.\r\nTo apply, please complete our online application form and we’ll be in touch!\r\n\r\nSkills & Experience required:\r\n- Relevant professional skills or experience in one or more of the following areas: HR, finance, IT, retail, animal welfare, fundraising, marketing, communications, governance or business management.\r\n- Strategic thinking and planning to help shape the charity’s direction, sustainability and long-term future.\r\n- Financial awareness and an understanding of budgets, financial oversight, income generation or cost management.\r\n- Fundraising and networking skills, with a willingness to use existing contacts and connections to create opportunities and support income generation.\r\n- Communication and interpersonal skills to work collaboratively with fellow Trustees, staff, volunteers and the wider community.- Problem-solving and decision-making abilities, with a practical, solutions-focused approach to challenges.\r\n- Commitment to animal welfare and a genuine interest in supporting the aims and values of Borders Pet Rescue.- Understanding of, or willingness to learn about, charity governance, Trustee responsibilities, risk management and legal obligations.\r\n- Community engagement and a willingness to support fundraising events, promote the charity and raise \r\nawareness of its work.\r\n- Teamwork and leadership skills to provide constructive support and guidance to a small team of staff \r\nand volunteers.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPersonal qualities and commitment- Enthusiasm for the charity’s mission and a desire to make a positive difference.\r\n- Integrity, reliability and the ability to act in the charity’s best interests.\r\n- An open-minded, inclusive approach and willingness to listen to different perspectives.\r\n- A commitment to contribute approximately two days per month, attend Board meetings every two months and the AGM, and support fundraising and engagement activities.\r\n\r\nEssential: A genuine commitment to Borders Pet Rescue’s mission, the ability to work collaboratively and a willingness to fulfil Trustee responsibilities.\r\nDesirable: Professional expertise, previous Trustee or board experience, charity sector knowledge, or established networks that could help strengthen the charity. Previous Trustee experience should not be a requirement if the candidate is willing to learn and contribute their skills.\n\n## Training details\n\nMembership to various organisations to support Trustee knowledge and understanding including SCVO short courses.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
