                        "description": "Personal qualities and commitment- Enthusiasm for the charity’s mission and a desire to make a positive difference.\r\n- Integrity, reliability and the ability to act in the charity’s best interests.\r\n- An open-minded, inclusive approach and willingness to listen to different perspectives.\r\n- A commitment to contribute approximately two days per month, attend Board meetings every two months and the AGM, and support fundraising and engagement activities.\r\n\r\nEssential: A genuine commitment to Borders Pet Rescue’s mission, the ability to work collaboratively and a willingness to fulfil Trustee responsibilities.\r\nDesirable: Professional expertise, previous Trustee or board experience, charity sector knowledge, or established networks that could help strengthen the charity. Previous Trustee experience should not be a requirement if the candidate is willing to learn and contribute their skills.",
