            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IFhdNYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IFhdNYAT/volunteer-lead-community-garden",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Volunteer-lead Community Garden",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSupported by the Royal Voluntary Service, this volunteer‑led community garden aims to reduce loneliness\r\nand isolation by giving people meaningful opportunities to shape and nurture the outdoor landscape at the\r\nKatherine Elliot Centre. The project creates a shared, welcoming space that enhances wellbeing and\r\nbenefits everyone who uses the building\n\n## Description\n\nPurpose of the Role - \r\n\r\nSupported by the Royal Voluntary Service, Community Garden Volunteers help reduce loneliness and\r\nisolation by creating and maintaining a welcoming outdoor space at the Katherine Elliot Centre. \r\n\r\nVolunteers work together to shape the garden, nurture plants, and develop an environment that enhances wellbeing\r\nfor everyone who uses the building.\r\n\r\nWhat the Role Involves - \r\n\r\nContributing to the design, planting, and ongoing care of the garden areas.\r\n\r\nCreating a friendly, inclusive atmosphere where volunteers and visitors feel comfortable and connected.\r\n\r\nSupporting the development of a shared outdoor space that encourages social interaction, relaxation, and\r\npride in the local environment.\r\n\r\nWorking alongside other volunteers to complete gardening tasks safely and collaboratively.\r\n\r\nHelping ensure the garden reflects the needs and preferences of the centre’s service users.\r\n\r\nOffering ideas, creativity, and enthusiasm to help the project grow over time.\r\n\r\nExpected Outcomes - \r\n\r\nA vibrant, well‑maintained garden that enhances the Katherine Elliot Centre’s outdoor environment.\r\n\r\nIncreased social connection for volunteers and visitors, helping reduce loneliness and isolation.\r\n\r\nA sense of shared ownership and community pride in the space.\r\n\r\nOpportunities for volunteers to build confidence, skills, and wellbeing through meaningful activity.\r\n\r\nA welcoming outdoor area that benefits all service users and supports the centre’s wider Living Well aims.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnjoyment of outdoor activity and working with plants (no experience required).\r\n\r\nWillingness to work as part of a team.\r\n\r\nFriendly, inclusive approach to others.\r\n\r\nReliability and a positive attitude.\r\n\r\nOpenness to learning new skills and trying new tasks.\n\n## Training details\n\nGuidance from RVS staff and experienced volunteers.\r\n\r\nTraining in safe gardening practices where needed.\r\n\r\nA warm, supportive environment that values each volunteer’s contribution.\r\n\r\nE-learning portal that gives access to mandatory compliance support , for example, data protection, manual handling, health and safety etc. Also having other modules to support further development and other interests.\r\n\r\nLead contact service Deputy Service Manager, in first instance, support from Service Manager and Service Coordinator.\r\n\r\nExtra support through the online portal, safeguarding and volunteer partner teams.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nTimings and commitment - Flexible, during Katherine Elliot Centre opening times 09:00-16:30.\r\nVolunteers can contribute regularly or occasionally, depending on availability. \r\nSessions will be arranged to suit the group and seasonal needs.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteer expenses reimbursed. Claimed via service portal.\n\n## Taster details\n\nAfter receiving an application, we will call in the first instance and email if we are unable to connect. Once we connect we will work through a step by step process, that aims to match requirement with need.\r\n\r\nInduction, taster will also be available once the group is in practice: \r\n\r\n1. Welcome to the Community Garden Project - \r\nA warm introduction to the project, its purpose, and how volunteers make a difference.\r\n\r\n2. About the Katherine Elliot Centre - \r\nOverview of the centre, the people it supports, and how the garden enhances the environment.\r\n\r\n3. Supported by the Royal Voluntary Service -\r\nWho we are, our mission, and how we work alongside volunteers.\r\n\r\n4. Your Volunteer Role -\r\nClear description of the Community Garden Volunteer role, responsibilities, and expected outcomes.\r\n\r\n5. Taster & Induction Session -\r\nWhat to expect from your first visit, meeting the team, and settling into the space.\r\n\r\n6. Working Together in the Garden -\r\nTeamwork, communication, shared values, and how we create an inclusive environment.\r\n\r\n7. Safety, Wellbeing & Practical Guidance -\r\nSafe gardening practices, boundaries, safeguarding, and how we look after each other.\r\n\r\n8. Tools, Equipment & Garden Areas - \r\nWhere things are kept, how to use equipment safely, and an overview of the garden layout.\r\n\r\n9. Volunteer Support & Training - \r\nHow we support you, who to contact, and opportunities to learn new skills.\r\n\r\n10. Session Times & Seasonal Activities -\r\nHow sessions run, flexibility, and what gardening looks like across the year.\r\n\r\n11. Feedback, Ideas & Growing the Project -\r\nHow volunteers can share suggestions, shape the space, and help the project evolve.\r\n\r\n12. Next Steps & Getting Started -\r\nYour first few weeks, joining the team, and how we help you settle in.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
