                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IFkJVYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IFkJVYA1/bacon-butty-blether-volunteer-lead",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Bacon Butty Blether - Volunteer Lead",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nhe Bacon Butty Blether is a volunteer‑led social drop‑in designed to reduce loneliness and isolation by\r\ncreating a relaxed, welcoming space where people can enjoy a warm drink, a bacon butty, and friendly\r\nconversation. Volunteers help set up the space, prepare simple refreshments, greet attendees, and spark\r\ngentle social connection. This small but meaningful role brings people together, builds confidence, and strengthens community spirit within the centre.\n\n## Description\n\nPurpose of the Role- \r\n\r\nThe Bacon Butty Blether is a volunteer‑led social drop‑in designed to reduce loneliness and isolation by\r\noffering a warm, friendly space where people can enjoy a bacon butty, a cuppa, and relaxed conversation.\r\n\r\nVolunteers help create a welcoming atmosphere that encourages connection, confidence, and community\r\nspirit within the centre.\r\n\r\nWhat the Role Involves - \r\n\r\nCreating a Welcoming Environment.\r\n\r\nGreeting attendees with warmth and friendliness.\r\n\r\nHelping people feel comfortable, included, and valued.\r\n\r\nEncouraging gentle conversation and social interaction.\r\n\r\nSupporting Refreshments\r\n\r\nPreparing simple bacon butties and hot drinks.\r\n\r\nSetting up and clearing down the refreshment area.\r\n\r\nEnsuring food hygiene and safe handling practices are followed.\r\n\r\nSocial Connection & Engagement\r\n\r\nOffering light conversation and companionship.\r\n\r\nHelping people join in, especially those who may feel shy or isolated.\r\n\r\nNoticing when someone might need a bit of extra support or encouragement.\r\n\r\nWorking as Part of a Team - \r\n\r\nCollaborating with other volunteers to run the session smoothly.\r\n\r\nSharing ideas to help the Blether grow and evolve.\r\n\r\nCommunicating any concerns or suggestions to the DSM or RVS staff.\r\n\r\nExpected Outcomes - \r\n\r\nA warm, relaxed social space that encourages connection and reduces loneliness.\r\n\r\nIncreased confidence and engagement for attendees.\r\n\r\nA positive, uplifting atmosphere within the centre.\r\n\r\nVolunteers feeling valued, purposeful, and part of a supportive team.\r\n\r\nA consistent, friendly drop‑in that becomes a highlight of the week for service users\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly, approachable, and comfortable chatting with others.\r\n\r\nEnjoyment of simple food preparation (no experience required).\r\n\r\nReliability and a positive attitude.\r\n\r\nAbility to work well with others and contribute to a team.\r\n\r\nSensitivity to people who may feel anxious, lonely, or unsure.\n\n## Training details\n\nGuidance from RVS staff and experienced volunteers.\r\nTraining in safe food handling and safeguarding.\r\nA warm, supportive environment where every contribution is appreciated.\r\n\r\nE-learning portal that gives access to mandatory compliance support , for example, data protection,\r\nmanual handling, health and safety etc. Also having other modules to support further development and\r\nother interests.\r\n\r\nLead contact service Deputy Service Manager, in first instance, support from Service Manager and Service\r\nCoordinator.\r\nExtra support through the online portal, safeguarding and volunteer partner teams.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCurrently on a Monday and may extend into another morning.\r\n\r\nFlexible — volunteers can support weekly, fortnightly, or occasionally. \r\n\r\nSessions typically last 1–2 hours,\r\nincluding set‑up and tidy‑up.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses claimed via RVS online portal\n\n## Taster details\n\nAfter receiving an application, we will call in the first instance and email if we are unable to connect. Once we connect we will work through a step by step process, that aims to match requirement with need\r\n\r\nInduction Summary – Step by Step (60 mins)\r\n\r\n1. Warm Welcome (5 mins) - \r\nVolunteer is greeted, introduced to the space, and given a quick overview of the session’s purpose.\r\n\r\n2. Meet the Team (5 mins) - \r\nShort introductions to staff and volunteers involved in the Blether.\r\n\r\n3. Space & Setup Walk‑Through (10 mins) -\r\nTour of the refreshment area, equipment, seating layout, and how the session flows.\r\n\r\n4. Safety & Wellbeing Brief (5 mins) - \r\nBasic food hygiene, safeguarding awareness, and who to speak to if concerned.\r\n\r\n5. Supported Participation (25 mins) - \r\nVolunteer joins in gently with:\r\ngreeting attendees\r\nlight conversation\r\nsimple refreshment preparation\r\nThey choose what feels comfortable.\r\n\r\n6. Tidy‑Up Overview (5 mins) - \r\nQuick explanation of how the session ends and how the team works together to close down.\r\n\r\n7. Reflection & Next Steps (5 mins) - \r\nCheck‑in on how the volunteer found the induction, what they enjoyed, and when they’d like to return",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IFkJVYA1#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Bacon Butty Blether - Volunteer Lead",
                        "description": "Friendly, approachable, and comfortable chatting with others.\r\n\r\nEnjoyment of simple food preparation (no experience required).\r\n\r\nReliability and a positive attitude.\r\n\r\nAbility to work well with others and contribute to a team.\r\n\r\nSensitivity to people who may feel anxious, lonely, or unsure.",
                        "commitment": "Currently on a Monday and may extend into another morning.\r\n\r\nFlexible — volunteers can support weekly, fortnightly, or occasionally. \r\n\r\nSessions typically last 1–2 hours,\r\nincluding set‑up and tidy‑up.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IFkJVYA1/bacon-butty-blether-volunteer-lead?#modal_register_a0gQD00000IFkJVYA1",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
