                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HVZnhYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HVZnhYAH/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-28",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking to appoint a Trustee with a particular interest / knowledge of HR.\r\nThe Trustee would be offer support and guidance to the Board of Trustees and the Executive Director on HR issues around staffing / policies etc.\n\n## Description\n\nBorders Additional Needs Group (BANG) is a Scottish Borders charity supporting families of children and young people with additional support needs, including neurodivergent children and young people. We provide peer support, information, training and community programmes that help families feel connected, informed and confident in navigating services.\r\nIf you are interested in an opportunity to support a local charity and really make a difference then have a look at our website: https://www.bordersadditionalneeds.org/ or Facebook page and see some of the work we do and how you might be part of this great charity.\r\nThe Trustee would be offer support and guidance to the Board of Trustees and the Executive Director on\r\nHR issues around staffing / policies etc.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking to appoint Voluntary Trustees to complement the skills of our existing Board members, and\r\nare particularly keen to recruit Trustees who have experience in these areas:\r\n• Finance / accounting\r\n• HR\r\nBut above all, we are looking for caring, dynamic and committed individuals to help drive our charity\r\nforward. Both challenging and rewarding in equal measure our Trustee roles will provide you with an\r\nopportunity to support a local charity and make a difference. Previous Charity Board experience is\r\ndesirable but not as essential as a passion for what we do and a desire to make a positive contribution.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n• Attendance at Board Meetings usually monthly in the evening for around 2 hours\r\n• Occasionally we hold meetings on-line\r\n• Trustees are welcome to attend any events which are run for our members\r\n• Some work outside meetings which may be tasked following monthly meeting\n\n## Taster details\n\nInformal chat with current Board member\r\nOpportunity to see the charity in action\r\nOpportunity to 'sit-in' on a Board meeting before committing to the role",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HVZnhYAH#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Trustee",
                        "description": "We are looking to appoint Voluntary Trustees to complement the skills of our existing Board members, and\r\nare particularly keen to recruit Trustees who have experience in these areas:\r\n• Finance / accounting\r\n• HR\r\nBut above all, we are looking for caring, dynamic and committed individuals to help drive our charity\r\nforward. Both challenging and rewarding in equal measure our Trustee roles will provide you with an\r\nopportunity to support a local charity and make a difference. Previous Charity Board experience is\r\ndesirable but not as essential as a passion for what we do and a desire to make a positive contribution.",
                        "commitment": "• Attendance at Board Meetings usually monthly in the evening for around 2 hours\r\n• Occasionally we hold meetings on-line\r\n• Trustees are welcome to attend any events which are run for our members\r\n• Some work outside meetings which may be tasked following monthly meeting",
