                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HVY0PYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HVY0PYAX/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-28",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe role of Treasurer will oversee monthly accounts completed by an external accountant. \r\nLiaise with our Executive Director to present financial reports to the Board. Chair the monthly finance sub-group. \r\nPrepare the Treasurer's report for the yearly Trustee Annual Report which is shared with OSCR.\n\n## Description\n\nBorders Additional Needs Group (BANG) is a Scottish Borders charity supporting families of children and young people with additional support needs, including neurodivergent children and young people. We provide peer support, information, training and community programmes that help families feel connected, informed and confident in navigating services.\r\nIf you are interested in an opportunity to support a local charity and really make a difference then have a look at our website: https://www.bordersadditionalneeds.org/ or Facebook page and see some of the work we do and how you might be part of this great charity.\n\n## Experience required\n\nExperience in finance / accounting\n\n## Taster details\n\nInformal chat with an existing Board Member\r\nOpportunity to 'sit in' on a Board Meeting\r\nOpportunity to ask questions any time",
