            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HfUunYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HfUunYAF/trustee-board-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-06",
                    "title": "Trustee Board Member",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nPMH Borders is looking to recruit four new Trustee Board Members with experience in business management, change management, social media or HR.\n\n## Description\n\nPMH Borders is a much valued perinatal mental health charity established for over 16 years with a proven track record and evidence of growing demand. We provide psychological therapies and counselling to parents and families across the Scottish Borders from our base in Galashiels.\r\nAs we develop our service, we are looking to recruit four new Trustee Board Members with experience in business management, change management, social media or HR.\r\nThis is an exciting time to join our Team. We are at the start of a new chapter, with ambitious plans to redevelop our service and drive meaningful growth to become a sustainable and socially responsible charity.\r\nMain duties:\r\n1. To ensure PMH Borders carries out its purposes for the public benefit – making sure it only pursues its stated charitable aims, as specified in its constitution.\r\n2. To comply with its constitution and the law.\r\n3. To act in the best interests of the PMH Borders charity – making decisions that benefit the charity.\r\n4. To manage the resources of PMH Borders responsibly – overseeing finances, its property (East Lodge), staff and volunteers.\r\n5. To act with reasonable care and skill – giving sufficient time, attention and expertise to the role.\r\n6. To ensure that the PMH Borders charity is accountable – maintaining proper records, demonstrating good governance and reporting annually to OSCR.\n\n## Experience required\n\n• The ability to communicate and work effectively as part of a team \r\n• Commitment and reliability \r\n• The ability to become an ambassador for, and promote the work of the  charity\r\n• To work creatively, with self-direction and self-awareness\r\n\r\n• All our trustees are issued with our booklet “Staff and Trustee Information” and notes from a trustee training course “Trustee training”, together with a copy of our constitution. They must sign our “Declaration of Trustees” and “Code of Conduct for Trustees” documents.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining for Trustees includes induction training, online Public Protection Training, and opportunities to access any other training relevant to Trustees.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nAttendance at a minimum of 6 meetings per year on a Friday morning. Additional duties as agreed by the Board.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HfUunYAF#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Trustee Board Member",
                        "description": "• The ability to communicate and work effectively as part of a team \r\n• Commitment and reliability \r\n• The ability to become an ambassador for, and promote the work of the  charity\r\n• To work creatively, with self-direction and self-awareness\r\n\r\n• All our trustees are issued with our booklet “Staff and Trustee Information” and notes from a trustee training course “Trustee training”, together with a copy of our constitution. They must sign our “Declaration of Trustees” and “Code of Conduct for Trustees” documents.",
