        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZXUAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZXUAA2/the-abbotsford-trust",
            "name": "The Abbotsford Trust",
            "description": "Abbotsford is the home of the 19th century writer Sir Walter Scott and is run by The Abbotsford Trust, a registered Scottish charity. We offer a five star visitor experience to visitors from across the world including the historic house and collections, 100 acres of designed landscape, formal gardens, a free Visitor Centre with an exhibition on Sir Walter Scott, play trail, gift shop, restaurant, events and special exhibitions.",
            "website": "https://www.scottsabbotsford.co.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC037425"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Heritage",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Heritage"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HsauLYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HsauLYAR/trustee-financeaccountancy-experience",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-09",
                    "title": "Trustee - finance/accountancy experience",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThis role will suit someone with professional accountancy qualifications and experience of audited accounts. Your expert understanding will ensure that trustees exercise their financial responsibilities. You will act as lead trustee on overseeing the annual audit, and advise on financial procedures, regular financial reporting and forecasting. \r\nThis will involve chairing the Trust’s Audit Committee, which meets once a year to receive draft charity accounts and audit reports for The Abbotsford Trust and its subsidiary Abbotsford Trading Company. The Committee is responsible for recommending accounts for approval to the Board of Directors, and for making recommendations on the appointment of auditors. \r\n\r\nYou will exercise oversight of the Trust’s financial management throughout the year through membership of the Executive Committee, which meets up to 10 times a year to receive financial reports from management. Trading Company management accounts are the responsibility of a separate Trading Company Board.\r\n\r\nThe Board meets quarterly. \r\n\r\nAll Trustees have regular contact with the paid management team, providing them with guidance and support, and working through the Chief Executive to direct operations and strategy. In this role your primary relationship will be with the Chief Executive and the Finance & Admin Manager. \r\n\r\nWe are fortunate to have a very healthy volunteering and working culture across all parts of the organisation. Trustees, staff and the wider volunteer community are motivated, ambitious, creative, and very supportive towards each other. Challenge is encouraged, but in a positive and constructive way. \r\n\r\nThe Trust is financially secure, however growing cost pressures and constrained spending by visitors to Abbotsford since Covid ended require the Trust to achieve ambitious annual fundraising goals in order to deliver a full programme of high quality work at Abbotsford and beyond. From 2027 the Trust intends to launch an ambitious campaign to increase its Endowment Fund to provide a secure long term contribution to meeting core costs.\n\n## Experience required\n\nProfessional accountancy, ideally with experience of charity accounts.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll Trustees have regular contact with the paid management team, providing them with guidance and support, and working through the Chief Executive to direct operations and strategy. In this role your primary relationship will be with the Chief Executive and the Finance & Admin Manager. \r\n\r\nYour induction will be led by the Chief Executive who will ensure you are introduced to all relevant aspects of the charity and your role.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nAll meetings are mornings, and usually 2 hours long. All are hybrid.\r\n\r\nThe Board meets 1/4ly.\r\n\r\nThe Executive Committee meets up to 10 times a year.\r\n\r\nThe Audit Committee meets once a year.\r\n\r\nYou may wish to attend occasional evening donor events.\r\n\r\nMeetings are hybrid but we would expect you to attend a good number in person at Abbotsford.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses reimbursed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HsauLYAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Trustee - finance/accountancy experience",
                        "description": "Professional accountancy, ideally with experience of charity accounts.",
                        "commitment": "All meetings are mornings, and usually 2 hours long. All are hybrid.\r\n\r\nThe Board meets 1/4ly.\r\n\r\nThe Executive Committee meets up to 10 times a year.\r\n\r\nThe Audit Committee meets once a year.\r\n\r\nYou may wish to attend occasional evening donor events.\r\n\r\nMeetings are hybrid but we would expect you to attend a good number in person at Abbotsford.",
                        "applyLink": "https://www.scottsabbotsford.com/support-us/volunteer-opportunities/trustees-and-advisors",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/Children",
