        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nZZVAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nZZVAA2/tweeddale-youth-action",
            "name": "Tweeddale Youth Action",
            "description": "Youth project, offering activities and opportunities and support/advocacy for y/p aged 10-25",
            "website": "https://www.tweeddaleyouth.co.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC036135"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzRuLYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HzRuLYAV/peer-leader-youth-volunteer-opportunity",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-08",
                    "title": "Peer Leader & Youth Volunteer Opportunity",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe're looking for enthusiastic 16-25 year old's who want to get involved ,learn new skills and make a \r\npositive difference to younger people in their community.\n\n## Description\n\nWe're looking for enthusiastic 16-25 year old's who want to get involved ,learn new skills and make a \r\npositive difference to younger people in their community.\r\nWe will provide an induction, training and ongoing support, with opportunities to take part in further online \r\nand in person courses.\r\nIncluding working towards Saltire Award.\r\nThis would be at our drop in sessions Wednesday, Thursday or Friday nights.\r\nA typical drop in would be playing board games, pool, creative activities, art, gardening, cooking and much \r\nmore the list is never ending. \r\nWe would want you to bring your own skills, interests and ideas.\r\nNo experience is needed, just willingness to get involved, be reliable , have a positive attitude and work as \r\npart of a team.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWilling to work as a team , get involved , be reliable and have a positive attitude.\n\n## Training details\n\nOnce applied, please send an email to: info@tweeddaleyouth.co.uk\r\n\r\nThe response is dependant on how long the PVG etc takes.\r\nWe will contact the applicant and meet them for a chat and explain who we are what we do at the youth \r\nclub. what we expect etc.\r\nFull induction and in house training.\r\nOpportunity to complete online and in person training.\r\nLearn new skills and build confidence.\r\nA chance to develop leadership and teamwork skills\r\nSupport to work towards Saltire Award.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe volunteer would be alongside other youth workers and volunteers .\r\nIf they were able to do once a week, or once every two weeks we would help facilitate this and be around to support.\r\nEach person has different needs and we would try and help them where we can.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe would pay for the volunteers travel expenses- receipts will need to be provided.\r\nWe will provide refreshments and snacks at drop ins.\r\nWe would welcome the volunteers at each session.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses- receipts would need to be provided.\r\nIf we are away on a trip we would pay for the volunteers lunch /dinner.\r\nTrips would all be free as they are coming as a volunteer.\n\n## Taster details\n\nCome along and meet the team and show the volunteers where the space is .What we have at the youth club, games, pool table etc so they are aware  of what is available.\r\nWhat rules we have and expectations of them and us. This gives them an opportunity to ask any questions \r\nand make them feel comfortable in the space.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzRuLYAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Peer Leader & Youth Volunteer Opportunity",
                        "description": "Willing to work as a team , get involved , be reliable and have a positive attitude.",
                        "commitment": "The volunteer would be alongside other youth workers and volunteers .\r\nIf they were able to do once a week, or once every two weeks we would help facilitate this and be around to support.\r\nEach person has different needs and we would try and help them where we can.",
