        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008naJiAAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008naJiAAI/rnli-aberdeen-lifeboats",
            "name": "RNLI – Aberdeen Lifeboats",
            "description": "The RNLI is the charity that saves lives at sea. Powered primarily by kind donations, our search and rescue service has been saving lives for nearly 200 years.",
            "website": "https://www.rnli.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC037736"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EmergencyResponseDisasterRelief",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Emergency Response / Disaster Relief"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eKbpAAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eKbpAAE/volunteer-education-presenters-aberdeen",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Volunteer Education Presenters - Aberdeen",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWould you like to be part of a happy band of volunteers that are helping to save lives at sea without even getting wet!! Could you respond to a call to action from a local school, youth group or event in your community and deliver messages about the work of the RNLI and staying safe near water to groups of eager children?\n\nPlease join us in making a difference to the safety of young people.\n\nFor further information please contact:\nHeather Malkin\nTel: 07500 608222 \ne-mail: heather_malkin@rnli.org.uk\n\n## Description\n\nWould you like to be part of a happy band of volunteers that are helping to save lives at sea without even getting wet!! Could you respond to a call to action from a local school, youth group or event in your community and deliver messages about the work of the RNLI and staying safe near water to groups of eager children?\n\nVolunteering as part of the RNLI’s Education Team in Aberdeen is an important role within the charity as we aim to save the lives of young people through our fantastic education programme. A message given today could be a life saved tomorrow.\n\nYour role would be to engage with young people to deliver our vital water safety messages alongside promoting the work of the RNLI.\n\nJust as we give all our Lifeboat crews the right training and equipment to carry out their lifesaving work, we provide Education Volunteers with all the necessary training and support to carry out their role. Education volunteers have access to a range of online learning materials, as well as opportunities for one to one support from fellow volunteers and RNLI education specialists.\n\nAs an Education volunteer you will have the opportunity to meet lots of new people and develop your skills in talking to young people.\n\nAfter their first mission as Education Presenters our volunteers often say; ‘I feel like I am performing an important public service and its good to be a part of that’.\n\nPlease join us in making a difference to the safety of young people.\n\nFor further information please contact:\nHeather Malkin\nTel: 07500 608222 \ne-mail: heather_malkin@rnli.org.uk\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication skills, enthusiasm,  an interest in the RNLI and its activities.\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support and training is provided. Just as we give all our Lifeboat crews the right training and equipment to carry out their lifesaving work, we provide Education Volunteers with all the necessary training and support to carry out their role.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible to suit volunteers-all help greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVarious locations around Aberdeen. \nVolunteer must make own travel arrangements but reasonable travel and lunch expenses will be reimbursed\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel and lunch expenses will be reimbursed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eKbpAAE#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Education Presenters - Aberdeen",
                        "description": "Good communication skills, enthusiasm,  an interest in the RNLI and its activities.",
                        "commitment": "Flexible to suit volunteers-all help greatly appreciated.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eKbpAAE/volunteer-education-presenters-aberdeen?#modal_register_a0g24000000eKbpAAE",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
