        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008naNMAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008naNMAAY/highland-hospice-highland",
            "name": "Highland Hospice (Highland)",
            "description": "The Hospice aims:\r\n\r\nTo provide specialist inter-disciplinary palliative care to patients suffering from life threatening cancer and other appropriate terminal illnesses.\r\n\r\nTo provide continuing support into bereavement to carers, relatives and friends.\r\n\r\nTo act as an education and resource centre for health care professionals and others interested in furthering the work of palliative care.\r\n\r\nTo initiate and participate in audit and research projects within the field of palliative care.\r\n\r\nTo consolidate, expand and improve these services to achieve the highest possible standard of palliative care within a cost which is affordable.",
            "website": "https://www.highlandhospice.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC011227"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SocialCare",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Social Care"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009SoeEYAS",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009SoeEYAS/by-the-river-cafe-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-04-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-14",
                    "title": "By the River Café Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nBy the River Café @ Highland Hospice provides members of the public, patient visitors, staff and volunteers with home baking, snacks and lunches and is a valuable source of fundraising for the Hospice. The café is counter service and volunteers serve teas, coffees, baking and light lunches prepared in the kitchen. \r\n\r\nMain responsibilities: \r\n- To provide high standards of customer care to all who visit the café \r\n- To serve home baking, snacks, soup and lunches to customers \r\n- To handle cash and operate the computerized till and card machine \r\n- To operate the coffee machine \r\n- To clear tables and keep the café looking presentable for customers entering \r\n- To operate the dishwasher when required and return clean dishes to the café \r\n- To follow open / close down procedures for the café including cashing up and cleaning the coffee machine\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining: \r\nInduction - including health & Safety\r\n3 shadow training shifts \r\nFood Safety Hygiene – 2 yearly\r\nMoving and Handling (inanimate objects) – 2 yearly \r\nFire Awareness  - yearly",
