        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nafbAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nafbAAA/springside-community-association",
            "name": "Springside Community Association",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC029430"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNybVAAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNybVAAT/stock-room-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-08",
                    "title": "Stock Room Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Stock Room Assistant role requires some heavy lifting and manual handling. As a Stock Room Assistant you will be responsible for receiving goods and ensuring that they are stored correctly and in accordance with the larder’s FIFO policy (first in first out). You will also be responsible for completing weekly stock checks and temperature checks. Another key role is to ensure that the store room and all its equipment are kept clean and tidy.\r\n\r\nSummary of Main Activities and Tasks:\r\n\r\n· Manual handling\r\n\r\n· Assist with receiving deliveries and stock\r\n\r\n· Assist with placing food orders\r\n\r\n· To assist with correctly and safely storing goods\r\n\r\n· To ensure that goods are in date and in good condition\r\n\r\n· To operate a first in first out (FIFO) stock system\r\n\r\n· To keep the store room and all equipment clean and tidy\r\n\r\n· To complete all food safety and procedural paper work\n\n## Experience required\n\nPrevious experience of working with food or within a warehouse /stockroom environment is desirable, but all applications are welcomed.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis opportunity takes place at springside community centre",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNybVAAT#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Stock Room Assistant",
                        "description": "Previous experience of working with food or within a warehouse /stockroom environment is desirable, but all applications are welcomed.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNybVAAT/stock-room-assistant?#modal_register_a0g0800000QNybVAAT",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/LocalAuthority/NorthAyrshire",
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "North Ayrshire"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNybaAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNybaAAD/administration-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-08",
                    "title": "Administration Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThis role helps to ensure that the larder runs efficiently behind the scenes, supporting the network of stores to thrive. The role is largely office based clerical work, although there are opportunities to interact with the wider network and learn about all aspects of the organisation.\r\n\r\nShifts\r\n\r\nThis role requires a minimum of half a day each week (approximately 4 hours), although hours can be flexible.\r\n\r\nThere will be deadlines to work to – especially when we have seasonal promotional campaigns.\r\n\r\nSummary of Main Activities and Tasks:\r\n\r\n· Maintaining our membership databases, including inputting new forms and visit details;\r\n\r\n· Inputting stock checks to help us stay on track of our supplies;\r\n\r\n· Making telephone calls to obtain and order supplies;\r\n\r\n· Compiling our quarterly newsletter;\r\n\r\n· Overseeing our Facebook pages, including taking and publicising photos of the food we have on offer.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNybaAAD#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Administration Assistant",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNybaAAD/administration-assistant?#modal_register_a0g0800000QNybaAAD",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/LocalAuthority/NorthAyrshire",
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "North Ayrshire"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                }
            ]
