        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nanFAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nanFAAQ/robert-gordon-university",
            "name": "Robert Gordon University",
            "website": "https://www.rgu.ac.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC013781"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SocialEconomySocialEnterprise",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Social Economy / Social Enterprise"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzjT3YAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HzjT3YAJ/what-matters-to-you-patient-cafe-contributors",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-27",
                    "title": "What Matters to You - Patient Café Contributors",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAbout the Role:\r\n\r\nWe are seeking volunteers with lived experience of illness, health challenges, disability, mental health, long term conditions, or wellbeing to attend a Patient Café with first year pharmacy students. \r\n\r\nIn this role, you will share your personal experiences of health and care in a supportive, informal café style setting. Your story will help students understand the real world impact of healthcare, medicines, communication, and compassion — and what truly matters to people using services. \r\n\r\nYou are not expected to teach or give medical advice. Your role is to share, reflect, and support meaningful conversation.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat You Will Do: \r\n\r\n•\tTake part in an informal patient café alongside pharmacy students (20 min in each 1-hour slot) \r\n•\tShare your lived experience of illness, health, recovery, or wellbeing (what mattes to you in your health journey, how the illness impacts your daily life, what support you value most, etc.)  \r\n•\tTalk about your interactions with healthcare professionals and pharmacy services \r\n•\tHelp students explore what person centred care means in practice \r\n•\tSupport respectful discussions around listening, empathy, and partnership \r\n•\tContribute to shaping compassionate, values based pharmacy practice \r\n\r\n\r\nAbout What Matters to You \r\n\r\nThe NHS What Matters to You? initiative is about shifting conversations in health and care to encourage future healthcare professionals to understand people as individuals — their experiences, values, priorities, and wellbeing — not just their conditions or medicines. \r\n\r\nThis volunteer role brings that principle to life for pharmacy students at the very start of their professional journey. \r\n\r\n\r\nWhat You’ll Gain:\r\n\r\n•\tThe opportunity to influence the next generation of pharmacists \r\n•\tA chance to make a meaningful contribution to patient centred education \r\n•\tSupport and briefing before each café session and debriefing at the end \r\n•\tVoucher of £20 per 3-hour block for your time, refreshments on the day  \r\n•\tA welcoming environment where your voice and wellbeing are respected \r\n•\tAn opportunity to connect with other people with lived experience \r\n\r\n\r\nThe Patient Café takes place on Monday 30th November at Robert Gordon University, Garthdee Road, Aberdeen, AB10 7AQ. There are two sessions on the day you can participate in either: 9:00 - 13:00 & 13:00 - 17:00. \r\n\r\nHow to Get Involved \r\n\r\n•\tTo express interest, please tell us about your lived experience, why you would like to participate in the sessions and which session (morning and / or afternoon) you are available for. \r\n•\tPlease complete the sign up form at: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=nKagUU8OPUu2QhLgExmGNewTIOM3899KubMYObkFUl1UMzBIWDlTU1RSWE40SlNXNkdCRDdIUlJYWS4u&route=shorturl or email Gosia Singh at: g.singh3@rgu.ac.uk\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and guidance is provided to all volunteers.\r\n\r\nInduction and debrief will be given at the start and end of each block. We recognise that sharing lived experience is personal. You will be supported, can choose what and how much to share, and may step back at any time. Your wellbeing comes first.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe Patient Café takes place on Monday 30th November at Robert Gordon University, Garthdee Road, Aberdeen, AB10 7AQ. There are two sessions on the day you can participate in either: 9:00 - 13:00 & 13:00 - 17:00.\n\n## Travel details\n\nRobert Gordon University, Garthdee Road, Aberdeen, AB10 7AQ.\r\n\r\nBy bus: First Aberdeen Services 1 & 2: The buses run frequently between Aberdeen City Centre (including Union Street) and the RGU Garthdee Campus.\r\n\r\nBy train: When in Aberdeen, locate First Aberdeen Services 1 & 2: The buses run frequently between Aberdeen City Centre and the RGU Campus.\r\n\r\nBy car: Robert Gordon University, Garthdee Road, AB10 7AQ, Aberdeen. Parking permit will need to be arranged, please contact us in advance. \r\n\r\nCycling & walking: The campus can be reached by dedicated bike lanes, paths, and offers secure bike parking.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nYou will be compensated for the time you spend with students (£20 voucher per 3h block)",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fff29d0ba-d70e-4212-9c9c-cef73a988a2b%2FmldJRTFLqzgWHXFMADFj9shUhn02%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=56a23bbf-e597-4bac-bba5-5989fc325d06",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzjT3YAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "What Matters to You - Patient Café Contributors",
                        "commitment": "The Patient Café takes place on Monday 30th November at Robert Gordon University, Garthdee Road, Aberdeen, AB10 7AQ. There are two sessions on the day you can participate in either: 9:00 - 13:00 & 13:00 - 17:00.",
                        "applyLink": "https://forms.cloud.microsoft/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=nKagUU8OPUu2QhLgExmGNewTIOM3899KubMYObkFUl1UMzBIWDlTU1RSWE40SlNXNkdCRDdIUlJYWS4u&route=shorturl",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
