            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eNTEAA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eNTEAA2/community-befriender-kingdom-companions",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-05",
                    "title": "Community Befriender - Kingdom Companions",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nKingdom Companions aims to support adults who are facing social isolation and/or lacking in confidence through short-term goal-specific befriending.\n\n## Description\n\nKingdom Companions aims to support adults who are facing social isolation and/or struggling with their confidence in the community, through short-term goal-specific befriending. \r\n  \r\nA befriending service for adults experiencing isolation and loneliness,  Kingdom Companions aims to support individuals to achieve a goal for themselves. This might be getting back into the community, attending social groups, travelling independently, or getting involved in volunteering. \r\n \r\nVolunteers are asked to provide friendly, relaxed, practical, and encouraging support to the adult on a one-to-one, regular basis for 4-6 months. It will usually be within the community but may include visiting the home of the supported adult.  \r\n \r\nThere are roles all over Fife for community befrienders who have a couple of hours a week/fortnight to help someone with this. Could this be you? Befriending can be a terrific way to build confidence and skills for jobs such as social care, as well as increasing your confidence, helping someone – which can feel very fulfilling, and perhaps going to new places or trying new activities.  \r\n\r\nYour travel and other out-of-pocket expenses will be reimbursed. FVA aim to match you with someone who lives in your local area. \r\n\r\nYou will get detailed training, as well as ongoing support. Get in touch now!\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou should be friendly, relaxed and encouraging. Be yourself!\r\nAlso, you should be able to build good relationships; spend time sharing activities; be accepting, understanding and not judge; be able to establish and maintain appropriate boundaries (training given).\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers are required to complete the mandatory training programme covering communication, boundaries, safeguarding and the befriending role. Further training can be offered specific to the volunteer's needs. As the position involves working with vulnerable adults, volunteers will be subject to a PVG (Protection of Vulnerable Groups) check.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThere are opportunities all over Fife and FVA aim to match you with someone who lives in your local area or in an area that you are able to travel to.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport costs covered or mileage at 55p per mile, plus other out of pocket expenses by agreement (e.g. hot drinks)",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eNTEAA2#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Community Befriender - Kingdom Companions",
                        "description": "You should be friendly, relaxed and encouraging. Be yourself!\r\nAlso, you should be able to build good relationships; spend time sharing activities; be accepting, understanding and not judge; be able to establish and maintain appropriate boundaries (training given).",
