                    "title": "Foot Carer (Central Fife)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nIt's never just about feet...\r\nFor many people across Fife, a Footcare Fife appointment means comfort, confidence and independence. Age, illness and reduced mobility can make basic footcare difficult, but a little support can make a big difference to someone's everyday life.\r\nMary from Rosyth is a client who can no longer manage her own footcare due to health issues. After visiting the clinic, she described feeling \"much lighter\" and was incredibly grateful for the support she received.\r\n\r\nThere are hundreds of people like Mary across Fife. A simple footcare appointment can mean greater comfort, confidence and independence. As a volunteer, you can help make that difference.\r\nAs a Footcare Volunteer, you'll help people stay active, comfortable and connected to their communities while becoming part of a friendly and supportive team. For many clients, the appointment is also an opportunity to enjoy a friendly chat and social connection, something that can be especially important for those who are socially isolated or live alone.\r\n\r\nNo previous experience is necessary. Footcare Fife provide comprehensive training, ongoing support and all the equipment you'll need. All they ask is that you can commit around three hours per session, at least twice a month, and have a genuine desire to help others.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience necessary, all the training and support you will need is provided. Just a desire to be of assistance and we take care of the rest.  Comprehensive training and support provided.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll training will be provided by FVA.   Support will be provided by NHS and FVA staff and someone will be on site at all times. Volunteers will be required to join the Protection of Vulnerable Groups scheme.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCurrently, sessions in central Fife take place in the following venues: \r\n\r\nKirkcaldy - New Volunteer House, East Fergus Place \r\nWhytemans Brae Hospital. \r\n\r\n Glenrothes - Glenrothes Hospital\r\n\r\nLeven - Arden House. \r\n\r\nAll out of pocket travel expenses will be reimbursed.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport costs will be reimbursed and 55p per mile if travelling by car.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
