        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nb1IAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nb1IAAQ/royal-voluntary-service-fife",
            "name": "Royal Voluntary Service Fife",
            "description": "Across Fife, Royal Voluntary Service supports people as they age with community and patient transport; our volunteer drivers support people to get to various medical or social appointments. We offer companionship and activities at our community lunch clubs (open to anyone) and day centres (specifically supporting people living with dementia, and their carers). We also offer 1:1 befriending support in North East Fife, and have two Community Cafés in Dunfermline; one at the Jean Mackie Centre and another at Queen Margaret Hospital.",
            "website": "https://www.royalvoluntaryservice.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038924"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityTransport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Transport"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/LunchClubs",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Lunch Clubs"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I2We9YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I2We9YAF/community-club-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-16",
                    "title": "Community Club Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThis role is about supporting and empowering older people to be independent and stay connected to their communities.\r\n\r\nVolunteers transform the lives of people in their community, by helping them live as independently as they can, building community relationships and re-establishing their confidence and well-being.\r\n\r\nThis could include helping to provide lunch and healthy snacks, chatting and offering companionship to people, giving dementia-friendly support.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe volunteer will need to have a friendly personality and good communication skills, with a non-judgmental attitude towards an individual’s circumstances and a willingness to ensure confidentiality.\r\n\r\nThey will receive relevant training for the role and will be welcomed and supported by a friendly, local team.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe volunteer will be working with a team of volunteers and staff who will support the volunteer.\r\n\r\nRoyal Voluntary Service has a training website available for all volunteers. There are also workbooks available to anyone without access to a computer.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMorrisons, Largo Road, St. Andrews, KY16 8PJ\r\n\r\nThursday 11.45 a.m. to 1.45 p.m.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers can claim expenses incurred travelling to and from their duties. Drivers are re-imbursed at 55p per mile, we pay public transportation rates. Volunteers can claim weekly or monthly.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
