                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-11",
                    "title": "Healthy and Happy Lives Volunteer - St Monans",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThis role is about supporting and empowering older people to be independent and stay connected to their communities.\r\n\r\nVolunteers transform the lives of people in their community, by helping them live as independently as they can, building community relationships and re-establishing their confidence and well-being.\r\n\r\nThis could include helping to provide lunch and healthy snacks and social activities such as exercises to provide strength and mobility or taking part in crafts and hobbies with the older person\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe volunteer will need to have a friendly personality and good communication skills, with a non-judgmental attitude towards an individual’s circumstances and a willingness to ensure confidentiality.\r\n\r\nThey will receive relevant training for the role and will be welcomed and supported by a friendly, local team.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe volunteer will be working with a team of volunteers and staff who will support the volunteer.\r\n\r\nRoyal Voluntary Service has a training website available for all volunteers. There are also workbooks available to anyone without access to a computer.\n\n## Travel details\n\nSt. Monans Lunch Club\r\n\r\nSt. Monans Church Hall, Station Road, St. Monans, KY10 2BN\r\n\r\nWednesday 11.00 a.m. – 2.00 p.m.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers can claim expenses incurred travelling to and from their duties. Drivers are re-imbursed at 45p per mile, we pay public transportation rates. Volunteers can claim weekly or monthly.",
