                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNz2zAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNz2zAAD/day-service-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-19",
                    "title": "Day Service Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSupport older people in your local community to improve their quality of life.\r\nLater Life Choices Glenrothes is seeking Day Service Volunteers for client groups from Monday to Thursday (10.30 am to 2.15 pm) for a minimum of 3.75 hours per week. The key elements of this role are:\r\n•\tEngaging with clients and supporting them in a person-centered way\r\n•\tAssisting in supporting clients with activities \r\n•\tAssisting clients to and from their transport \r\n•\tServing lunch and refreshments to clients \r\n•\tOccasional dish washing or kitchen duties \r\n•\tEnsuring a warm, welcoming and friendly atmosphere for clients\r\nIf you enjoy helping others and meeting new people, this role could be for you! It could also be an excellent opportunity to boost your confidence, work on your interpersonal skills and promote personal development. Full training is provided.\n\n## Experience required\n\nExperience of working with/caring for older people, including people with dementia is desirable, however training is provided. A caring, professional approach to others is essential, with the ability to maintain confidentiality and work as part of a team. Reliability and a commitment to volunteering is also desirable.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteer training consists of an induction to the role and organisation, Moving & Assisting and Dementia Awareness.\r\nOngoing Support & Development also provided.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n3.75 hours per day\n\n## Travel details\n\nDay Sessions are held at Napier House, 300 Napier Road, Glenrothes, KY6 1BF. They are within walking distance from the town centre and bus station and are on a bus route. There is street parking available\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are reimbursed at 45p per mile within the Glenrothes boundary for those driving in, and bus fares are capped at £5 per session on receipt of tickets.",
