        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nb1cAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nb1cAAA/bums-off-seats-active-fife",
            "name": "Bums Off Seats (Active Fife)",
            "description": "Provides led health walks for people - particularly aimed at those that are inactive, and who are frail or have a long-term health condition.",
            "website": "https://www.activefife.co.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BWuYcYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BWuYcYAL/walking-group-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-03",
                    "title": "Walking Group Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nBums Off Seats is a Fife Walking Initiative. They provide free local health walking opportunities in Fife and all walks are led by a trained team of Volunteer Walk Leaders.  A health walk is a free, short, local walk and is suitable for most people, even if they have a long term health condition.\r\nBums Off Seats are looking for Walking Group Volunteers to support their walks across the Levenmouth, Dunfermline, and South West Fife areas.\r\n As a volunteer, you will lead or support short walks in your local area. You will speak to the people who attend to make sure they are comfortable during the walk. Walks can be an excellent opportunity to gain mental and physical health benefits as well as connecting socially with other local people.  Leaders need to be over 18 years old.\r\nBums Off Seats provide full training and support.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers should be able to walk comfortably, and should be confident speaking to the people who join the walks.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers need to attend Walk Leader training, and will receive ongoing support from the coordinators.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteers can get involved with a group that is local to them. Currently, Bums Off Seats are looking for volunteers for the following walks:\r\nDalgety Bay - Mondays\r\nDunfermline - Mondays, Wednesdays, Thursdays and Sundays\r\nInverkeithing - Tuesdays\r\nLeven - Mondays, Tuesdays and Thursdays\r\nRosyth - Mondays\r\nLimekilns - Wednesdays\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses will be reimbursed at public transport rates.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BWuYcYAL#role",
