                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhmvZAAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhmvZAAR/volunteer-buddy",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-02",
                    "title": "Volunteer Buddy",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWould you like to make a difference to lone parents and families across Fife?\r\n\r\nFife Gingerbread is looking for compassionate, kind and understanding people who can spare a couple of hours each week to become a Volunteer Buddy. This role is ideal for people who can listen without judgement, build trusting relationships, and understand the challenges and complexities that poverty and lone parenthood can bring.\r\n\r\nVolunteer Buddies help families build confidence and feel less isolated by offering emotional and practical support. This could involve being a listening ear, going for a walk, helping someone access local services, or supporting them to complete forms. Most importantly, buddies provide a safe, supportive presence where families feel heard, valued and understood.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFG are looking for friendly, approachable people who are good at listening and have a non-judgmental attitude. An understanding of some of the challenges that families and lone parents face is beneficial but full training will be provided.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers receive training and support to help them feel confident in their role. Training includes an introduction to Fife Gingerbread, the rights, challenges and barriers facing families, child protection, unconscious bias, boundaries and lone working safety. Ongoing supervision, peer support and shadowing opportunities are also provided.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2 hour per week\n\n## Travel details\n\nVarious Opportunities throughout Fife\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMileage is paid 45p per mile and public transport expenses reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhmvZAAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Buddy",
                        "description": "FG are looking for friendly, approachable people who are good at listening and have a non-judgmental attitude. An understanding of some of the challenges that families and lone parents face is beneficial but full training will be provided.",
                        "commitment": "2 hour per week",
