        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nb2bAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nb2bAAA/kasp-kingdom-abuse-survivors-project",
            "name": "KASP (Kingdom Abuse Survivors Project)",
            "description": "Provides specialist counselling and support to male and female adult survivors of childhood sexual abuse across Fife.  Provides support to those who are supporting survivors of abuse.  Provides training and consultancy to frontline staff in working sensitively with disclosures of abuse.",
            "website": "https://www.kasp.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC023079"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Counselling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Counselling"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/LearningDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Learning Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000007oHw6YAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000007oHw6YAE/volunteer-befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-07",
                    "title": "Volunteer Befriender",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nKingdom Abuse Survivors Project (KASP) is currently recruiting Befrienders to support adults in Fife who are affected by childhood sexual trauma.\r\n \r\nAs a Befriender, you’ll provide a vital connection, reducing loneliness and helping individuals build confidence, improve client’s well-being, and support in accessing local services. You’ll also help individuals reconnect with their community.\r\nThey’re looking for volunteers who are empathetic, non-judgmental, and can commit to at least 1 hour per week. In return, you’ll receive training in child and adult protection and trauma informed practices, ongoing support and supervision, and reimbursement for any expenses incurred during your time with clients.\r\n\r\nFor more information or to apply, please contact jordan@kasp.org.uk.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo prior experience required. They look for communication skills and an empathetic, caring attitude toward supporting survivors of CSA.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will begin with a comprehensive 2-day induction training, covering key topics such as childhood trauma, trauma-informed practice, child and adult protection, boundaries, protecting well-being and self-care, active listening, motivational interviewing, and the responsibilities of the role. After induction, the Volunteer Coordinator will inform volunteers of any additional relevant training opportunities, which, while not mandatory, will support the volunteer’s personal and professional development. Volunteers will also receive ongoing support and supervision throughout their role to ensure they feel confident and well-supported in their work.\n\n## Travel details\n\nFife-wide, with travel being reimbursed when meeting with clients.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers are reimbursed for any expenses incurred during their role. This includes a mileage rate of 34p per mile for travel, a £5 food and drink allowance, and bus ticket reimbursement for public transport costs. Expenses are reimbursed on a regular basis, and volunteers should submit their claims to the Volunteer Coordinator for processing, retaining receipts.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
