        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nb39AAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nb39AAA/base-east-fife-blind-activities-support-events",
            "name": "BASE East Fife (Blind Activities Support Events)",
            "description": "BASE (Blind Activities Support Events),which is a user led organisation, supports visually impaired people, resident in East Fife, by providing a monthly programme of leisure, educational and social activities. Transport is provided. Trained guides and volunteers offer extra support.",
            "website": "https://www.basefife.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC037538"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SensoryImpairment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000035EmzYAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000035EmzYAE/driver-sighted-guide",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-13",
                    "title": "Driver / Sighted Guide",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nBASE (https://www.basefife.org.uk/) is a Scottish Registered Charity established in 2005 by blind and partially sighted people. The management committee consists of nine Trustees and one co-opted member, the majority of whom are sight impaired. BASE depends entirely on fundraising from donations and applications to charitable trusts.\r\n\r\nBASE supports people with sight impairment resident in NE Fife by offering a monthly programme of social activities, including visits to places of interest, theatre visits, museums and outdoor activities. BASE is supported by a team of volunteers providing transport and guiding. These activities take place on the first Thursday each month.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBASE is looking to increase the number of Volunteer Drivers / Sighted Guides in the East Neuk, Cupar and St.Andrews areas.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe role includes transport to the destination (or a central pick up area), guiding our VIP’s and having fun. Lunch is usually included on our days out.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers need to be friendly and outgoing, interested in others, able to follow directions, adaptable and calm under pressure.\n\n## Training details\n\nAfter a PVG check, guide training will occur “on the job” as each VIP has different requirements. Support is available via the Volunteer Co-ordinator.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe location of the events is different every month.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMileage allowance 45p /mile paid on receipt of expense form.",
