        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nb3DAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nb3DAAQ/home-start-kirkcaldy",
            "name": "Home-Start Kirkcaldy",
            "description": "Home-Start Kirkcaldy offers support, friendship and practical help to parents with young children in Kirkcaldy, Kinghorn, Burntisland and Cardenden.   Since 1994, they have offered a unique service for families - recruiting and training volunteers to support parents with young children at home. Home-visiting volunteers visit a family once a week to help them deal with whatever life throws at them. We support parents as they learn to cope, improve their confidence and build better lives for their children. We also runa weekly family group, creche and organise trips and outings.",
            "website": "https://www.homestartkirkcaldy.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC020659"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FamilySupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Family Support"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008XKszYAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008XKszYAG/family-support-home-visiting-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Family Support Home Visiting Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHow would you like to make a difference to the lives of children and families in the Kirkcaldy area, supporting parents to give their children the best possible start in life?\r\n\r\nMany parents require support when their children are young. Home-Start Kirkcaldy helps families with young children through challenging times.\r\n\r\nAs a family support home visiting volunteer you will be matched with a local family. You will visit the same family weekly week for 2-3 hours and the role could involve helping a family settle into a new area, going to appointments, helping with shopping but above all talking and listening. The volunteer will take the lead from the family, building relationships with the parents and children to increase their confidence. The family could have health issues, lack confidence or have children with additional support needs. This is a rewarding role which can have a significant impact on the whole family.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers should be non judgemental, have good interpersonal and communication skills and should be good listeners. Flexibility and reliability are essential to build up trusting relationships\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers are given full induction training to prepare them for the role which includes confidentiality, boundaries, child protection & the role of play. Once matched with a family there are ongoing training sessions on relevant topics raised by the volunteer team e.g. domestic abuse,  autism. There are also regular volunteer meetups for peer support.\n\n## Travel details\n\nHome-Start Kirkcaldy covers Kirkcaldy, Kinghorn, Burntisland & Cardenden.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAll bus fares & out of pocket expenses are reimbursable with receipts. Mileage is paid at 45p per mile.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008XKszYAG#role",
