            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000004sdV7YAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000004sdV7YAI/board-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Board member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nJoin a Fife-wide charity to support and develop the effective governance of the organisation. \r\nThier key aim is to listen, provide people with a voice and respond to need by helping people to identify and access the services and resources which help them to remain independent and healthier for as long as is practicable, alongside encouraging people to utilise their own strengths and assets to help improve their circumstances and well-being.\r\nAs a Board Member you will have a key role in strategic decision-making, ensuring good governance and will be required to carry out your duties in line with legal responsibilities.   \r\n•\tAre you keen to support the good governance of a local charity which has people at its core?  \r\n•\tDo you possess skills which would support the management of the organisation?\r\n•\tAre you passionate about working to promote inclusion and engagement?\r\n\r\nThey want to hear from you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPrevious and current experience of management (financial, operational and governance) and HR would be welcomed alongside a commitment to equality (socio and economic)\n\n## Training details\n\nAn induction process involves issuing a Governance Brief with a role description and signposting to information and organisations including those which provide training relevant to the role.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport or mileage rates (55p per mile) will be reimbursed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
