                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-12",
                    "title": "Retail Volunteer (Dunfermline)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nApplications can be made online on the Volunteering Opportunities page of the Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland website: https://volunteer.chss.org.uk/opportunities. In line with our commitment to safeguarding, this role is subject to a basic disclosure check. CHSS are committed to equality of opportunity, and we aim to ensure no volunteer is unfairly treated on the grounds of an offending background. \n\n## Description\n\nFrom stunning boutiques full of designer gems to discount stores where you can grab a bargain, their charity shops are much-loved across Scotland.\r\n\r\nThey are looking for friendly volunteers to help the shop management team assist customers and donors, and ensure the shop is tidy and well stocked. Whether you have a passion for fashion and love chatting to customers, or you would prefer to be behind the scenes in the stockroom, your help could make a difference in your local community.\r\n\r\nThey believe everyone has the right to live life to the full following the diagnosis of a chest or heart condition, long Covid, or a stroke. Their shops are vital in helping us raise the funds needed to provide services such as community support services, specialist nurses, advice and information, education, and peer support.\r\n\r\nJoin the fabulous team of Retail volunteers and learn new skills, make great friends, and make a real difference to people in Scotland who are isolated, scared, or anxious about their condition.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThis is an opportunity to undertake a satisfying and rewarding role. As part of our team of volunteers, you will provide customer support, whilst working in a friendly atmosphere, providing an extremely useful and appreciated service to the charity. The role includes welcoming and assisting customers, customer service and sales service, stock control, sorting donations, hanging, and ticketing stock and helping to keep the shop clean and tidy.  \n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers are supported by their line manager, usually the manager of the shop. Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland will provide all necessary training about shop procedures, which will be carried out under the guidance of the shop manager. Formal training will include online Manual Handling and Gift Aid Training.\n\n## Travel details\n\n6 East Port, Dunfermline KY12 7LJ\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable out-of-pocket expenses will be reimbursed. These should be discussed with your Line Manager prior to outlay and must be submitted within the prescribed guidelines as detailed in the CHSS Volunteer Expenses Policy.\n\n## Taster details\n\nTrial shift will be provided.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
