                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000006qZflYAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000006qZflYAE/volunteer-energy-champion",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Volunteer Energy Champion",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGreener Kirkcaldy (Cosy Kingdom) are recruiting volunteer Energy Champions to help them speak with people about their project and inspire the community to get involved in their events and activities. The role will allow you to help the energy advice project to support people to take action to manage their energy use and reduce their carbon footprint.\r\n\r\nVolunteers are at the heart of their work. They currently have more than 100 active volunteers supporting a range of projects and activities within the key themes of climate action, energy, food & growing and active travel.\r\n\r\nThis role will allow you to gain/develop skills relating to providing energy advice, supporting Cosy Kingdom and your local community.\r\n\r\nAre you interested in helping people in your community to manage their household energy use and reduce their carbon footprint? If so, Greener Kirkcaldy’s energy advice project (Cosy Kingdom) may be the volunteering opportunity for you.\n\n## Experience required\n\n-Happy to work in a team\r\n-Friendly, approachable and welcoming\r\n-Organised, enthusiastic and flexible\r\n-Good communication skills\r\n-Reliable\r\n-Basic administration skills\n\n## Training details\n\n-Mentor support and 121 development\r\n-Training including - climate literacy, first aid, renewable energy, fuel poverty, saving energy, presentation & communication skills,\r\n-A full induction will be given regarding Greener Kirkcaldy’s (Cosy Kingdom) policies & values\n\n## Travel details\n\nLocation - These roles are available across Fife.\r\n\r\nGreener Kirkcaldy/Cosy Kingdom will support you to volunteer in the area of Fife you live in or are comfortable travelling too.\r\n\r\nGreener Kirkcaldy volunteers can operate in Levenmouth, Kirkcaldy, Cowdenbeath, Dunfermline & South West Fife. People wanting to volunteer in Glenrothes and North East Fife can volunteer with St Andrews Environmental Network (StAndEn) to support Cosy Kingdom.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNormally public transport rates will be reimbursed on the production of a receipt. If mileage needs to be claimed, due to no available public transport, 45p per mile will be reimbursed\r\n\r\nGreener Kirkcaldy (Cosy Kingdom) aim to have volunteers in their local area of where they are happy to volunteer but with an aim to keep travel to a minimum.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000006qZflYAE#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Energy Champion",
                        "description": "-Happy to work in a team\r\n-Friendly, approachable and welcoming\r\n-Organised, enthusiastic and flexible\r\n-Good communication skills\r\n-Reliable\r\n-Basic administration skills",
