        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nb76AAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nb76AAA/cancer-research-shop-dunfermline-high-st",
            "name": "Cancer Research Shop - Dunfermline High St",
            "website": "https://www.cancerresearchuk.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC041666"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000B9TqrYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000B9TqrYAF/charity-shop-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-07",
                    "title": "Charity Shop Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCancer Research Shop Volunteers are helping to beat cancer right now. Every volunteer hour you donate means they can sell 6 items and make £20 of income.  These funds are helping them start new clinical trials and research treatments as we speak.\r\nIf you volunteer at a Cancer Research UK shop, you too could make a real difference. You will also gain valuable skills to help develop your CV and experience.  And you will volunteer alongside a wonderful team of passionate, friendly people who will support you every step of the way.\r\nSome of the tasks you’ll be able to choose from are:\r\n\r\n-Serving customers\r\n-taking payments and providing good all-round customer service \r\n-Sorting through donated items and pricing stock\r\n-Working on window and shop displays\r\n-Keeping the shop tidy, clean and well organised\r\n-Interacting with the general public\r\n-Following new health, safety and social distancing measures\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou do not need any experience to volunteer. You just need to be motivated, hardworking and enjoy being part of a team.\n\n## Training details\n\nThere’ll be a full induction as well as ongoing training opportunities to make sure you’re fully confident and able to excel in your role.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe shop is located at 6 High Street, Dunfermline, KY12 7AR. It is a 2 minute walk from the bus station and a 15 minute walk from the train station, with parking nearby.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses can be reimbursed at public transport rates or 45p per mile.\n\n## Taster details\n\nTaster sessions are encouraged. These are normally 2 hours but can be shortened if that time would be too overwhelming for the volunteer.",
