        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nb7GAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nb7GAAQ/dunfermline-scouts",
            "name": "Dunfermline Scouts",
            "description": "Dunfermline Scouts are a member of the Scouting Association. Scouting today provides challenge and adventure for young people aged between 6 and 25, including males and females. It is all about fun with a purpose - helping members to fulfil their potential as individuals and active members of society. They believe that young people develop most when they are learning by doing, when they are given responsibility, work in teams, take acceptable risks and think for themselves. Everything they do is guided by the balanced programme which is a continuous progression of training, activities, badges and awards for young people from 6 - 25. They offer a huge range of activities and experiences to suit all ages, abilities and interests.",
            "website": "https://www.dunfermline-scouts.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC017511"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000006faldYAA",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000006faldYAA/scouts-trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2025-12-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-01",
                    "title": "Scouts Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWeek by week, Scouts volunteers empower thousands of young people aged 4 to 25 to try new things, make new friends and stand on their own two feet. You don’t have to work with young people to give them skills for life.\r\n\r\nThey are looking for trustees for their Dunfermline groups. As a trustee, you will have responsibility for the running of the group, and will work as a team with other trustees to make decisions, handle group finances, resolve issues and plan ahead.\r\n\r\nYou don’t need any previous experience as a trustee, and training will be given. You don’t need to have been a Scout when you were younger. Whatever your skillset, lend a hand for as little or as much time as you can spare, and they promise you’ll get more out of it than you put in.\r\n\r\nSounds fun? Worthwhile? It is.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience is required, as long as volunteers are enthusiastic about supporting a charity that helps children and young people gain experience and confidence, and have fun. Good organisational and team work skills would be a plus.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will have safety, safeguarding and GDPR training, as well as having the opportunity to engage in first aid and further ongoing learning.\r\n\r\nSupport is given by the group leader and other trustees.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThere are opportunities for team members in 10 Scout groups in Dunfermline, Carnock, Limekilns, and Crossford. The locations for these are Berrylaw Place, Piggies Lane, Viewfield Church, Carron Grove, Garvock Bank, St Leonard's Church, Abbeyview in Dunfermline; Carnock and Gowkhall Community Centre; Brucehaven Road, Limekilns; and George V Park.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on a case by case basis.\n\n## Taster details\n\nVolunteers are welcome to attend for a taster session before signing up to volunteer.",
