                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000A5bIvYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000A5bIvYAJ/scouts-treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-12-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-01",
                    "title": "Scouts Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWeek by week, Scouts volunteers empower thousands of young people aged 4 to 25 to try new things, make new friends and stand on their own two feet. You don’t have to work with young people to give them skills for life.\r\n39th Scout Group are looking for a treasurer. You could play a critical role in managing their financial health and ensuring transparency, working closely with their board and chairperson to support their mission.\r\nAs treasurer, you will:\r\n-\tOversee all financial aspects, including budgeting, accounting, and reporting\r\n-\tDevelop annual budgets and financial plans\r\n-\tEnsure compliance with charity laws\r\n-\tSupport fundraising initiatives and optimise resources for long-term sustainability\r\n\r\nYou can make a meaningful impact in your community as part of a supportive and passionate team. Ready to make a difference? Join the 39th Scout Group as Treasurer and help continue their mission of empowering young people!\n\n## Experience required\n\nThey are looking for:\r\n-\tExperience in financial management or accounting\r\n-\tUnderstanding of financial software and tools\r\n-\tExcellent communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively\r\n-\tCommitment to the values and mission of the Scouts\r\nExperience of the charity sector is a plus.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will have safety, safeguarding and GDPR training, as well as having the opportunity to engage in first aid and further ongoing learning.\r\n\r\nSupport is given by the group leader and other trustees.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMeetings held at 39th Fife Scout Group – Carron Grove, Dunfermline, KY11 4LN. \r\nVolunteering can be completed outwith the meetings from home or in the scout hall if required.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are available at public transport rates or 45p per mile if using a car.",
