        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nb7jAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nb7jAAA/brag-enterprises",
            "name": "BRAG Enterprises",
            "description": "To assist in the creation of a vibrant economy in Central Fife by developing communities, investing in people and building business.\n\nTo be open friendly, and approachable and to provide good value by working in partnership to deliver services in the most efficient way.\n\nTo provide a local economic development service which creates jobs and overcomes barriers, and provide access to learning and training which increases peoples qualification levels and promotes life long learning.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000006Mc4nYAC",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000006Mc4nYAC/community-garden-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-08",
                    "title": "Community Garden volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nBrag Enterprises helps disadvantaged communities across East Central Scotland achieve a more prosperous future by offering a range of initiatives including employability programmes, business support and retraining services for the community and beyond. BRAG is committed to community driven enterprise.\r\n\r\n\r\nBRAG are looking for community garden volunteers for their beautiful community garden. Volunteers can learn, grow vegetables and enjoy being outside or gardening in the warm and dry environment of the polytunnel. The gardening is a welcoming and relaxing place and volunteers can be involved in a variety of tasks including planting and pruning. These tasks are suitable for all abilities and there is something which will interest everyone. There is no requirement to be a regular visitor, just when it suits you; you will always be welcomed. If there is produce ready to harvest you are welcome to take some home too.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe garden is a mental health space where food is grown and donated to the community. The garden is not completely disability friendly, however this is our aim. Volunteers will be shown what to do, so no experience is necessary. Attitude is one of kindness, the rest we can teach and help with.\n\n## Training details\n\nAn induction will be provided which includes a tour of the garden, and informal assessment and work required will be demonstrated highlighting risks and covering health and safety,\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe garden is located at the back of the old school in Crosshill Community Enterprise Centre, Main Street, Crosshill, Fife , KY5 8BJ where BRAG is located.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers will be reimbursed for travelling by bus on the day of volunteering. Bus tickets may also be provided in advance for those volunteering regularly.\r\n\r\nTravel by car is reimbursed at a rate of 45p per mile. All travel expenses are capped at £5 per volunteering session attended.",
