        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nb8KAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nb8KAAQ/linkliving-older-persons-service",
            "name": "LinkLiving: Older Persons Service",
            "description": "The Older Person's Service provides a variety of support including volunteer befrienders and paid staff who support older people in their own homes to reduce social isolation and loneliness. It provides support for social activities within the local community and practical support such as trips to local shops and medical appointments.  It also hosts five Social Cafes per week where people aged 65+ can drop in for a bit of fun and a cuppa. \r\n\r\nThese services are offered across Fife.",
            "website": "https://www.linkliving.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC032418"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNvDpAAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNvDpAAL/driver-torryburn",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-04",
                    "title": "Driver (Torryburn)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCould you help reduce the loneliness and social isolation of an older person by becoming a volunteer driver? LinkLiving need drivers to take people to and from their social cafe at Torryburn Community Centre. The cafe offers older people the chance to meet others for a chat over a cuppa. They also offer quizzes and a range of other activities.\r\n\r\nYour role would be the first point of contact with their members, getting to know them and building a positive relationship. This involves:\r\n\r\n- collecting one of the members from their home and bringing them to the Community Centre for 10.30am\r\n- taking them home at the end of the session, 12.30pm (stay or leave in between as you wish)\r\n- talking to, and getting to know the members\r\n- raising any concerns regarding members wellbeing with the Project Workers\r\n- attending volunteer meetings and information sessions to help you with this role\r\n- making sure your car is road worthy, taxed and properly insured\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou should have access to a car, appropriate insurance and a clean current driving licence.\r\n\r\nYou will be friendly and approachable, dependable and trustworthy. An ability to maintain confidentiality is essential while understanding the need to share information/concerns with paid (Assistant) Project Workers as required.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe provide a volunteer handbook and training in various topics relevant to the role e.g. first aid, confidentiality, safeguarding\n\n## Travel details\n\nTorryburn Community Centre, off Main Street, Torryburn KY12 8SR (near Primary School)\r\nThere are cafes on other mornings in Rosyth & Cowdenbeath and you may help with journeys there if you wish too/instead.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n45p per mile\n\n## Taster details\n\nYou're welcome to come along to the cafe (by arrangement) and see what it's like.",
