        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nb8YAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nb8YAAQ/debra-charity-shop",
            "name": "Debra Charity Shop",
            "description": "Debra is the national and international charity raising funds and awareness for people affected with the genetic skin condition Eb.",
            "website": "https://debra.org.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Employment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Employment"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BvSUHYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BvSUHYA3/shop-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Shop Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDEBRA are recruiting new volunteers for their popular charity shop in Glenrothes. Join their friendly team and do something you'll really love! Whether you're looking to learn new skills, gain experience in retail, meet new people or just have fun, DEBRA provide a wide range of activities, finding the perfect role for everyone.\r\n\r\nThe role will involve:\r\n\r\n-Serving customers and using the computerised till to take payments for purchases\r\n-Sorting donated stock, clothing and bric-a-brac\r\n-Recording donor details for gift-aid\r\n-Using a steaming appliance on donated clothes\r\n-Assisting the shop manager with any other task to keep the shop running efficiently\r\n\r\nDEBRA is the national charity that funds research and healthcare to support individuals and families affected by Epidermolysis Bullosa (EB) – a painful genetic skin blistering condition which, in the worst cases, can be fatal.\r\n\r\nIf you are passionate about helping to make a difference through giving your time, then get in touch!\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe organisation are looking for reliable, committed volunteers who are happy to work as part of a team.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers are inducted into the organisation and offered continual training appropriate to their role.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDEBRA Glenrothes, 2 Lyon Way, Glenrothes, Fife, KY7 5NW\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteer travel expenses will be reimbursed on a weekly basis.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
