                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008fvP7YAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008fvP7YAI/volunteer-board-member-uist",
                    "publishStart": "2025-02-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-26",
                    "title": "Volunteer Board Member (Uist)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nEach Citizens Advice Bureau is a separate registered Charity and for your local bureau to be effective a wide range of experience is required. You don’t need to be a qualified professional to sit on a Citizens Advice Bureau board / management committee – bureaux need people of all ages, skills and experiences so that everyone can learn from each other.\r\n\r\nDoes this sound like you?\r\nAware of local issues\r\nCommitted to the Aims and Principles of the Service\r\nAble to think creatively and exercise good, independent judgement\r\nWork effectively as a team\r\nHappy to improve awareness of Equality and Diversity issues\r\nAble to understand and accept the responsibility of being a trustee and employer\r\nPerhaps you have a specific skill you can offer\n\n## Description\n\nEvery citizens advice bureau has a board of directors or management committee responsible for running the organisation and meeting the aims of the Citizens Advice Bureau service in Scotland.\r\nThe board / management committee is a voluntary group of people with the key role of ensuring that the bureau fulfils all its legal obligations and operates efficiently and according to good practice guidelines.\r\n\r\nFinancial matters, for example budget reviewing, fundraising and planned service developments\r\nPromotion and awareness raising, to make sure that the bureau is well known in the area it serves\r\nWorking with the bureau manager and Citizens Advice Scotland to make sure that quality standards are being met in the bureau\r\nDevising the bureau’s business plan, and monitoring its implementation\r\nMaking sure the bureau is fulfilling its responsibilities as an employer of paid staff\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nTo be discussed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008fvP7YAI#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Board Member (Uist)",
                        "commitment": "To be discussed",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008fvP7YAI/volunteer-board-member-uist?#modal_register_a0gQD000008fvP7YAI",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16",
                        "specialistRole": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/SpecialistRole/BoardTrusteeRole",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Board/trustee role"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
