            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000APuqsYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000APuqsYAD/one-off-activity-leader-scouts-wi-lewis",
                    "publishStart": "2025-06-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-26",
                    "title": "One-off Activity Leader: Scouts WI (Lewis)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nGot time, skills or energy to share? Scouts Western Isles need YOU! If you can share your skills or hobbies, as a one-off or over a few sessions to work towards a badge, with support from the Scout Leaders, get in touch today.\n\n## Description\n\nIf you have a skill or interest which you could share with Scouts Western Isles, please get in touch. Scouts are keen to learn new skills and work towards badges. Scouts Western Isles (Lewis) have groups for children and young people from age 6+: Beavers (age 6-8), Cubs (8-10 1/2), Scouts (10 1/2- 14) and Explorers (14-18). Scouts do lots of activities from fun games to camps, to arts and music - there's always a badge for it!\n\n## Experience required\n\nAny skills or knowledge welcomed to help support children and young people learn, lots of enthusiasm and interest in working with children and young people within a uniformed organisation.\n\n## Travel details\n\nGroups based in Lewis.",
