                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000AQ4jlYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000AQ4jlYAD/admin-support-scouts-wi-lewis",
                    "publishStart": "2025-06-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-26",
                    "title": "Admin Support: Scouts WI (Lewis)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nGot time, skills or energy to share? Scouts Western Isles need YOU! If you can share your time to provide admin support, get in touch today.\n\n## Description\n\nIf you would like to support Scouts Western Isles, are a whizz with spreadsheets or social media, but aren't so keen on camping there is a place for you! Scouts WI would welcome volunteers who can provide admin support to the team. \r\nScouts Western Isles (Lewis) have groups for children and young people from age 6+: Beavers (age 6-8), Cubs (8-10 1/2), Scouts (10 1/2- 14) and Explorers (14-18). Scouts do lots of activities from fun games to camps, to arts and music - there's always a badge for it!\n\n## Experience required\n\nAdmin skills are welcomed, an interest in working with children and young people within a uniformed organisation.\n\n## Travel details\n\nGroups based in Lewis.",
