                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hnb6HYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hnb6HYAR/bookbug-session-assistant-barra",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-19",
                    "title": "Bookbug Session Assistant (Barra)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTo support the delivery of Bookbug sessions that support early literacy, songs, stories, and positive family engagement in a safe and welcoming environment.\n\n## Description\n\nRole Purpose\r\nTo support the delivery of Bookbug sessions that support early literacy, songs, stories, and positive family engagement in a safe and welcoming environment.\r\nKey Responsibilities\r\n•\tSupport Bookbug Leader to deliver sessions using approved materials\r\n•\tEngage children and parents/carers positively\r\n•\tSet up and clear session spaces\r\n•\tPromote Bookbug and library services\r\nSkills and Attributes\r\n•\tEnjoy singing, stories, and working with families\r\n•\tConfident and enthusiastic\r\n•\tReliable and punctual\r\n•\tComfortable following structured session guidance\r\n\r\nTraining details\r\nThe volunteer will liaise with the branch manager at their local library, who will guide them through their induction, and will be the first point of contact for any issues, questions, or problems should they arise.\r\nComplete free Bookbug Session Leader Training. \r\nRestrictions\r\nMinimum age: 17\r\nPVG Scheme membership is required\r\nSafeguarding and Child Protection\r\n•\tAlways follow safeguarding procedures\r\n•\tUnderstand the role of parents/carers as supervising adults\r\n•\tNever supervise children without a responsible adult present\r\n•\tReport concerns or incidents immediately to staff\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tEnjoy singing, stories, and working with families\r\n•\tConfident and enthusiastic\r\n•\tReliable and punctual\r\n•\tComfortable following structured session guidance\n\n## Travel details\n\nLocation: Library branches",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hnb6HYAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Bookbug Session Assistant (Barra)",
                        "description": "•\tEnjoy singing, stories, and working with families\r\n•\tConfident and enthusiastic\r\n•\tReliable and punctual\r\n•\tComfortable following structured session guidance",
