                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008hGbBYAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008hGbBYAU/community-group-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-02-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-26",
                    "title": "Community Group Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nMain duties and responsibilities\r\n•\tSupport a community group as requested by group leader.\r\n•\tTo enable individuals to meet with others with similar interests. \r\n•\tTo communicate with people with dementia, family members and staff within the community group setting. \r\n•\tTo attend training to be informed about dementia and to attend any other necessary training relevant to volunteering role. \r\n•\tTo carry out any other reasonable duties requested of the volunteer\r\n•\tAccountability and support\n\n## Description\n\nThe purpose of this role is to support a range of community groups Alzheimer Scotland operate.  Our Community Groups are there to be enjoyed by anyone living with dementia or experiencing difficulties with their memory, including their families and friends. All are welcome, these groups are for people who can attend independently and/or for those unable to do so should come with a companion who can provide any support for them.\r\nThese groups may include the Football Memories, musical memories, dementia cafés and gardening projects.  This list is not exhaustive and this role may support a range of community groups.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008hGbBYAU#role",
                        "type": "Role",
