                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JhxMrYAJ/patient-belongings-bags-nov-26-jan-26-lewis",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-26",
                    "title": "Patient Belongings Bags (Nov 26- Jan 26, Lewis}",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nPacks are available by  e-mailing lewis@volunteercentrewi.org \r\nMaterial, pattern and thread supplied\n\n## Description\n\nThe Volunteer Centre Western Isles have set up the NHS Western Isles Absent Friends Patient Belonging Bags Project in partnership with NHS Western Isles\r\nThe initiative, which builds on the success of an earlier project powered by volunteer stitchers, involves sewing tote bags to a straightforward pattern. These handmade bags will replace the standard plastic property bags used to return a patient’s personal belongings to their family following a death in hospital.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tAbility to read and follow sewing pattern;\r\n•\tAbility to use own sewing machine;\r\n•\tSewing skills experience;\r\n•\tAble to work on own or part of a team",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JhxMrYAJ#role",
