            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7M1fAAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7M1fAAF/treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are a small local charity run by volunteers for the people of Grampian who have been affected by an acquired brain injury.  We are looking for someone to take the role of treasurer within our organisation.  Your role will include the day to day payment of expenses, applying for funding and some general book keeping.  This role is not onerous as we have no staff and our overheads are minimal.  You will have had previous experience of working or volunteering in book keeping / finance and will have a knowledge of legal requirements.  As we are a small committee we all work together and have a lot of fun.\r\n\r\nAll help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated. For further details please contact Karen Stewart, Interim Convenor at email: karen.stewart40@googlemail.com or telephone: 07922559790.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPlease have previous experience in book keeping / accountancy.  Excellent team skills and literacy skills.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided to all volunteers. Our current treasurer will offer training and a period of hand over.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available. All help greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe meet every 6 weeks, or there abouts, as part of the committee.  We meet in Aberdeen city but also virtually.  We offer a programme of activities for our members, you will not be expected to attend activities but would be very welcome.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
