            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IW75fYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IW75fYAD/treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-20",
                    "title": "Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThere is an exciting opportunity for an enthusiastic individual who is interested in financial data and record keeping to become their new treasurer.\n\n## Description\n\nFriends of Queen Margaret Hospital (FQMH) raise funds to relieve the needs of patients and staff attending and working in the Hospital and West Fife.\r\n\r\nThere is an exciting opportunity for an enthusiastic individual who is interested in financial data and record keeping to become their new treasurer. The roleholder will ensure the FQMH finances are managed appropriately to ensure legal compliance. The individual will become a member of FQMH and a trustee of the executive board. They will attend four members meetings and ten board meetings per year, and report on the organisation's finances at these meetings. The charity uses Excel to manage their books and a SumUp system to take electronic payments. Cash is also taken at events and the treasurer will be responsible for banking cash and maintaining a float.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAn interest in supporting the local community by improving services and facilities for patients, staff and visitors. Aptitude in financial record keeping, basic bookkeeping, microsoft excel, and email. Experience in a treasurer role would be an advantage but not essential.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining and support will be provided by the current role holder until confident. An informal induction to the organisation and their work will be provided by the current trustees. Ongoing support will be provided from the chair and trustees.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis role can be largely managed from home and a laptop and printed will be provided. Business and board meetings are held in primarily at Lynebank Hospital, Dunfermline and fundraising events are held in Queen Margaret Hospital, the Kingsgate Shopping Centre, and the Vine Centre, Dunfermline.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses can be discussed on an individual basis.",
