                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HaRG1YAN/treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-07",
                    "title": "Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTalkmatters, a mental health charity based in Dunfermline, is looking for Treasurer to join their team.\n\n## Description\n\nTalk Matters, a mental health charity based in Dunfermline, is looking for Treasurer to join their team and help create a brighter future for those affected by mental health challenges across Fife, regardless of their ability to pay.\r\n\r\nThey are seeking an individual with diverse skills, experiences, and perspectives who share a passion for mental health. Whether you bring expertise in business, finance, marketing, fundraising or lived experience with mental health challenges, your contribution will be vital to their success. They operate with an independent bookkeeping service so some finance experience would be useful but is not essential. As a Treasurer you will prepare and present financial reports, ensure appropriate budgeting and accounting procedures and controls are in place, provide advice on the financial implications of strategic decisions and plans, and ensure compliance with charity laws.\r\n\r\nReady to make a difference? They'd love to hear from you!\n\n## Experience required\n\nThey are seeking individuals with diverse skills, experiences, and perspectives who share a passion for mental health. Volunteers should have good communication and interpersonal skills, logical thinking and problem-solving abilities, and an understanding of charity governance.\n\n## Training details\n\nA named experienced Trustee will be appointed for each new Trustee and will arrange initial introductory meeting to walk through the role and responsibilities of the Trustee including an overview of the resources available from OSCR and related Charity support organisations. There will be a handover period from the existing Treasurer to the new Treasurer.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Board of Trustees meets in the Pittencrieff Room at Dunfermline Business Centre, Izatt Avenue, Dunfermline, KY11 3BZ, on the last Thursday of every month, 7 - 9pm.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTrustees can choose to apply for reasonable travel expenses to/from meetings, and these will be paid at either public transport rates or at a current mileage rate.",
