                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HFOufYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HFOufYAH/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-07",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nTalkmatters, a mental health charity based in Dunfermline, is looking for dedicated trustees to join our team and help create a brighter future for those affected by mental health challenges.\r\n\r\nWant to help shape the future of mental health support in Fife?\r\nPassionate about mental health and making a positive impact in your community? \r\nHave the drive and expertise to contribute to a growing charity that is committed to providing life-changing support? \r\n\r\nThey are seeking individuals with diverse skills, experiences, and perspectives who share a passion for mental health. Whether you bring expertise in business, finance, marketing, fundraising, advocacy, policymaking, or lived experience with mental health challenges, your contribution will be vital to their success.\r\n\r\nReady to make a difference? They’d love to hear from you!\n\n## Experience required\n\nThey are seeking individuals with diverse skills, experiences, and perspectives who share a passion for mental health. Whether you bring expertise in business, finance, marketing, fundraising, advocacy, policy-making, or lived experience with mental health challenges, your contribution will be vital to their success.\n\n## Training details\n\nA named experienced Trustee will be appointed for each new Trustee and will arrange initial introductory meeting to walk through the role and responsibilities of the Trustee including an overview of the resources available from OSCR and related Charity support organisations. Trustees will be given a full induction pack along with a walk through of key policies and documents by their named Trustee. These are all held on Microsoft Teams and accessible to the Trustees.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Board of Trustees meets in the Pittencrieff Room at Dunfermline Business Centre, Izatt Avenue, Dunfermline, KY11 3BZ.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTrustees can choose to apply for reasonable travel expenses to/from meetings, and these will be paid at either public transport rates or at a current mileage rate.",
