        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nb0hAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nb0hAAA/trust-in-fife",
            "name": "Trust in Fife",
            "description": "Trust In Fife is a Fife-wide homeless organisation running two hostels which accommodate single people. One of these projects offers a tenancy share option assisting homeless/potentially homeless people to meet, learn about, and be supported to move into a shared private tenancy. \r\n\r\nFife Private Rental Solutions is Fife’s private rented sector advice hub (previously Fife Keyfund) with the team assisting tenants and landlords in Fife with all their private sector housing needs.",
            "website": "http://www.trustinfife.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC021786"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/HousingHomelessnessness",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Housing / Homelessnessness"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HnBWnYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HnBWnYAN/board-director-lived-experience",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-19",
                    "title": "Board Director - Lived Experience",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTrust in Fife is a homeless charity, who provide a range of services throughout Fife.\n\n## Description\n\nTrust in Fife is a voluntary organisation, providing a range of services to homeless people and people threatened with homelessness throughout Fife.  They are a Scottish registered charity, a Company Limited by Guarantee, and their activities are regulated by the Care Inspectorate and the Scottish Governance letting agency regulations.\r\n\r\nThey are looking for individuals who have lived experience of homelessness, who can help to shape their services to better support people in this situation and have a genuine interest in being involved. \r\n\r\nThey are looking to strengthen their voluntary Board of Directors and are looking for people who have an ability to work as part of a team; an understanding of the pressures facing charitable organisations in the current economic climate; and a genuine interest in being involved.\r\n\r\nThis role will involve attending board meetings and making decisions for the charity alongside the rest of the board.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThey are looking to strengthen their voluntary Board of Directors and are looking for people who have an ability to work as part of a team; an understanding of the pressures facing charitable organisations in the current economic climate; and a genuine interest in being involved. Most importantly, they are looking for volunteers with lived experience of homelessness.\n\n## Training details\n\nNew board members are given information about the organisation set up and opportunity to tour the sites and meet with employees. They are provided with an induction handbook including training on data protection and confidentiality and have opportunities to meet with CEO and other board members for ongoing training.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMeetings take place in Craig House, Ellon Road, Kirkcaldy, KY2 6FB. Car parking available.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMileage is paid at 55p per mile. Public transport rates are reimbursed.",
