                    "publishStart": "2026-11-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Cook",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHow can you have fun, gain coinfidence and help others at the same time? By becoming a lunch cook with Express Group Fife!\r\n\r\nExpress Group Fife is a mental health charity, operating in Fife for almost 50 years. They provide social group activities and engage with people over 18 experiencing poor mental health.\r\n\r\nThey are looking for Cooks who can prepare simple cooked lunches for groups between 5 and 15 people. Groups meet once or twice a week but there is no need to commit to both days. Groups run from 9:30 am to 1:00 pm with lunch served at 12 noon; the cook can start at a suitable time to achieve this, finishing when clearing up has finished. Each venue has a good size and well-equipped kitchen. Lunch provided, travel expenses reimbursed, free parking at all venues.\r\n\r\nA Volunteer from Central Fife said  - I really enjoyed volunteering here over past 10 months, it will be sad to leave, it's been a very meaningful experience, and I have learnt a lot.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGeneral cooking skills. Food hygiene certificate desirable but not essential. You should be approachable, dependable and trustworthy. An ability to maintain confidentiality is essential while understanding the need to share information/concerns with paid staff as required.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will be made aware of the relevant organisational policies and procedures and will get ongoing support from staff. Relevant training opportunities will be offered.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2 hours per week\n\n## Travel details\n\nMethil / Methil Community Education Centre/ Thursday\r\n\r\nLochgelly / St Finnians Church/Wednesday\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses can be reimbursed\n\n## Taster details\n\nDetails on request",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QO1hMAAT#role",
