                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000GveyKAAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000GveyKAAR/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-12",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nExpress Group Fife is a charity working with people who require support to improve and/or maintain their mental health and wellbeing.\r\n\r\nThe aim is to promote positive mental wellbeing by providing a safe place for sharing experiences and peer support in a group setting. There are currently Eleven groups in eight locations across Fife each week. \r\n\r\nThe organisation is looking to recruit enthusiastic people to the Board of Trustees who will be responsible for setting the strategic vision and direction of the organisation and monitoring the management provided by the service manager.\r\n\r\nThe Board needs a range of skills, but commitment and enthusiasm are most important. Experience of working in the third sector, management, finance, health or social care is an advantage, but applications from other people who wish to gain experience of working at board level are also welcomed.\n\n## Experience required\n\nExperience of working in Mental Health and an interest in the voluntary sector.  A knowledge of finance, fundraising or HR would be an advantage, but enthusiasm and understanding is most important.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction by the service manager & existing board members. Free training on Trustee role and responsibilities available via Fife Voluntary Action. Ongoing support from the service manager and existing board members. Ongoing training for Trustees available via Fife Voluntary Action.\n\n## Travel details\n\nZoom to Teams.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\ntravel expenses: public transport fares or mileage (45p per mile).",
