            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009pbtBYAQ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009pbtBYAQ/committee-member",
                    "publishStart": "2025-12-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-01",
                    "title": "Committee Member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nENeRGI SCIO is a mental health charity based in the East Neuk of Fife. Volunteers are needed to join its committee.\r\n\r\nYou will be responsible for governing the charity, helping to shape policy and its vision for the future. ENeRGI is a SCIO registered charity established since 1995.\r\n\r\nCommittee Members are asked to attend Committee Meetings, which take place once every two months, and usually last 1 hour to 90 minutes, and the ENeRGI Annual General Meetings, usually held in December.\r\n\r\nCommittee roles available or you can remain as an ordinary trustee with just attendance and input expected.\r\n\r\nThis is an opportunity to gain new skills and contribute to a great community project.\r\n\r\nInterested parties over the age of 16 are welcome to apply.\n\n## Experience required\n\nSeveral roles such as HR, health and safety and secretary are required. Some experience here would be preferred.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining in governance and specific committee role if required.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe committee meets either via Zoom or at the drop-in centre at 32 East Street, Saint Monans, Fife, KY10 2AT.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\ndetails on request",
