            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BYw6WYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BYw6WYAT/community-group-volunteer-for-kirkcaldy-snooker-group",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-04",
                    "title": "Community group volunteer for Kirkcaldy Snooker Group",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThis role will directly support people living with dementia who attend our local weekly Snooker Group' in Kirkcaldy alongside our staff team. You will be part of a small team offering person centred, individualised support that meets the needs of each person who attends. The group enjoy playing snooker and having a blether.\r\n\r\n-Supporting a community group as requested by the group leader.\r\n\r\n-To enable individuals to meet with others with similar interests\r\n\r\n-To communicate with people with dementia, family members and staff within the community group setting.\r\n\r\n-To attend training to be informed about dementia and to attend any other necessary training relevant to volunteering role.\r\n\r\n-To carry out any other reasonable duties requested of the volunteer.\n\n## Experience required\n\n· Contribute positively to the role and Alzheimer Scotland’s vision for change, demonstrating commitment to its values\r\n\r\n-Excellent interpersonal skills.\r\n\r\n-Ability to recognise and respect the rich diversity that exists within our communities, views, attitudes and lifestyles.\r\n\r\n-Participate in induction training and any refresher updates or ongoing learning.\r\n\r\n-Willing to follow Alzheimer Scotland’s guidance, feedback and implement changes to practice where necessary.\r\n\r\n-Willing to follow Alzheimer Scotland’s policies, procedures and guidelines, and honestly reflect in practice\n\n## Training details\n\nThe volunteer will have a volunteer induction training session with the Volunteer Co-Ordinator before they join the Snooker Group. Then ongoing training relevant to the volunteer role and corporate policies e.g. Dementia Friends training; Brain Health training etc.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe group takes place at Brain Health & Dementia Resource Centre, Hill Street, Kirkcaldy, KY1 1AH , on a Monday morning from 10.30 to 12 noon. No parking at the venue, public bus service available.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport expenses will be reimbursed on production of a receipt. Mileage will be reimbursed at 45p per mile when the volunteer uses their own vehicle. These will be reimbursed monthly and processed by the Volunteer Co-Ordinator.\n\n## Taster details\n\nTaster available",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
