                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0bWfYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I0bWfYAJ/community-group-volunteer-rosyth",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-12",
                    "title": "Community Group Volunteer (Rosyth)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThis role will directly support people living with dementia who attend Alzheimer Scotland's get together group in Rosyth.\n\n## Description\n\nThis role will directly support people living with dementia who attend Alzheimer Scotland's get together group in Rosyth alongside their staff and volunteer team. You will be part of a small team offering person centred support. The group enjoy a range of fun activities and an opportunity to develop friendships.\r\n\r\nThe role will include:\r\nSupporting a community group as requested by the group leader\r\nTo enable individuals to meet with others with similar interests\r\nTo communicate with people with dementia, family members and staff within the community group setting\r\nTo attend training to be informed about dementia and to attend any other necessary training relevant to volunteering role.\n\n## Experience required\n\nContribute positively to the role and Alzheimer Scotland’s vision for change. It would be great if volunteers had excellent interpersonal skills, an interest in table top activities such as quizzes; dominoes, singing, and the ability to recognise and respect the rich diversity that exists within our communities, views, attitudes and lifestyles.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe volunteer will have a volunteer induction training session with the Volunteer Co-Ordinator before they join the Friday Meet Up Group. Then ongoing training relevant to the volunteer role and corporate policies e.g. Brain Health training etc.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe group meets in Parkgate Community Centre, 23 Parkgate, Rosyth, KY11 2JW every Friday from 11 am to 3 pm. Parking is available at the Community Centre.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThey will reimburse public transport expenses as long as the volunteer keeps the receipts. They will pay fuel mileage (45 p per mile) when the volunteer uses their own vehicle. These will be reimbursed monthly. This will be processed by the Volunteer Co-Ordinator",
