                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000OUuq9AAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000OUuq9AAD/family-support-group-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Family Support Group Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHome-Start Glenrothes is a Family Support charity offering support and friendship for parents with young children (0-5 years of age). This service is delivered throughout Glenrothes, through home visiting volunteers and Family Support Groups.\r\n\r\nThe purpose of the Family Support Group is to bring together parents and children who may be feeling isolated or lacking in confidence and who may like the opportunity to meet other families. Children can play with their peers and form friendships and are also encouraged to play with parents. We provide activities that are designed to allow families to play and grow together and to build confidence in a relaxed atmosphere. \r\n\r\nVolunteers assist the Family Support Group Coordinator to provide the activities. The organisation is particularly interested in hearing from you if you have experience of supporting families and have ideas for activities to engage our younger children. Perhaps you have an interesting hobby or a creative mind? Either way, the organisaton is keen to build on the range of activities offered and would love to hear your ideas.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe organisation ask that volunteers have parenting experience, enthusiasm and be able to offer non-judgemental practical and emotional support to families.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers are required to attend a volunteer preparation course\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis opportunity takes place in the gardens of Home-Start Glenrothes - 47-48 Greenlaw Crescent, Glenrothes KY6 1JQ",
