            "name": "Seescape",
            "description": "Providing support to people in Fife with sight impairment",
            "website": "https://www.seescape.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC001354"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SensoryImpairment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000A8xwPYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000A8xwPYAR/social-group-volunteer-glenrothes",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-04",
                    "title": "Social Group Volunteer (Glenrothes)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSeescape run social groups which are designed to help people with visual impairments to reduce the impact of loneliness and social isolation, and encourage them to live their lives to the full by meeting likeminded people and forging new friendships.  The groups meet either weekly or fortnightly for coffee, cakes and entertainment/activities such as local musicians or guest speakers,  They are looking for fun-loving, enthusiastic and  compassionate volunteers who are able to assist in the running of these groups and who may, in time, take some of the responsibilities from the existing group lead volunteers.  This is a brilliantly rewarding role.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe volunteer will have to be compassionate, calm and have a caring nature.  They should be able to make measured decisions, show initiative, be positive and innovative in their thinking, and take lead when required.  Life experience and a can-do attitude are the biggest assets for the role\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will be given training on relevant protocols and policies before starting and will be peer mentored by lead volunteers.  Training on supporting visually impaired people and annual training sessions will also be given\n\n## Travel details\n\nGlenrothes (Lomond Centre)\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses will be reimbursed at 45p per mile for travel by car or public transport rates.",
