            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000D9QJxYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000D9QJxYAN/conservation-gardener",
                    "publishStart": "2025-11-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-01",
                    "title": "Conservation Gardener",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSCI are looking for volunteers to help maintain the area. Volunteers can get involved in a mix of physical and gentler tasks, and something can be found to suit everyone.\n\n## Description\n\nThis is an opportunity to help create a more bio-diverse ecosystem for local wildlife. On the small site of 1.6 acres there is a burn, small woodland, grassy areas and a forest garden to nurture into providing more diversity for wildlife. \r\n\r\nThe site is adjacent to Pitmedden Forest, home of red squirrels, pine martens and so much more. It is a tranquil location with lots of possible learning – what does the land want to do, what do the non-human residents need, and how can human and wildlife co-exist here?\r\n\r\nThe site will provide a valuable wildlife corridor for native species and provide important data to conservation groups studying red squirrels and other species found here.\r\n\r\nSCI are looking for volunteers to help maintain the area. Volunteers can get involved in a mix of physical and gentler tasks, and something can be found to suit everyone.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNeeds to enjoy working outdoors and be able to dress themselves appropriately for that.\r\nNeeds to be interested in wildlife and gardening.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe support person has a high level of skills using empathic listening and identifying needs. They will be observing the volunteer/s to ensure they are getting their needs met. In the informal chat they will help the volunteer identify the needs they  have and any useful strategies to reduce anxiety, stress, dissatisfaction. \r\nThe volunteer sessions will begin and end with a check-in and check out – the check in helps SCI to know how everyone is feeling that day and using a decision-making tool, decide on task delegation together.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe site is adjacent to Pitmedden Forest. Volunteers will be collected and dropped off in the village of Auchtermuchty.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on a 1-1 basis.",
