        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nYbuAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nYbuAAE/transform-community-development",
            "name": "Transform Community Development",
            "description": "Transform Community Development works with vulnerable individuals within the city to provide accommodation, support, advice and opportunities in a variety settings. The organisation also aims to increase public awareness of issues surrounding homelessness through education. All the organisation's services are provided in a non-judgemental way and without prejudice.",
            "website": "https://www.transformcommunity.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC014961"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EnvironmentRecycling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Environment / Recycling"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/HousingHomelessnessness",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Housing / Homelessnessness"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000FMGXbAAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000FMGXbAAP/delivery-porter",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Delivery Porter",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWould you like to help feed people in need? Assist our driver and deliver to groups in and around the local area.  Helping out on our vans,  deliver to charities who feed those experiencing hardship.\n\n## Description\n\nWe redistribute food, which would end in in waste, to non-profit organisations in Tayside and Fife. These groups then provide meals for people who are experiencing food poverty, social isolation or other hardship.\r\n\r\nWe need driver's assistants who can give a few hours to help deliver food to our members. This is a vital part of providing a valuable service to thousands of individuals in need. Working as part of a team, the van crew load and unload crated food to local community food members.\r\n\r\nIf you are reasonably fit and able bodied and can give a few hours you could make a real difference to a project that is so important to so many.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPhysically able, public facing desirable\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training on what the organisation does, manual handling and warehousing.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n3-5 Hours per Shift\n\n## Travel details\n\nAlasdair Macqueen House, 95 Douglas Street, Dundee, DD1 5AZ\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReceipted travel expenses reimbursed. Food provided on shift.\n\n## Taster details\n\nFor a taster session with tour of the premises, call David 01382 224966",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
