                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000SbqZpAAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000SbqZpAAJ/warehouse-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2023-07-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Warehouse Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHelp feed those in food poverty and save the environment from food waste- Warehouse Assistant for FareShare\n\n## Description\n\nAssisting in our FareShare warehouse, you will pick food orders to be delivered to other charities throughout Tayside and Fife. The food is delivered to groups serving those experiencing food poverty. FareShare receives donated food from the supply chain that is surplus and would end up in the waste stream. Environmentally and socially this is a great cause and we welcome those interested in helping in whatever way possible.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWorking in a Warehouse, tackling food waste, helping those in need\n\n## Training details\n\nOnce you have received an induction you will shadow a member of staff/volunteer until you are happy with your role. You will also be able to speak with the volunteer co-ordinator about any issues or queries you have.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nBetween 10 and 20 hours weekly.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAlasdair Macqueen House, 95 Douglas Street, Dundee, DD1 5AZ\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport costs reimbursed.\n\n## Taster details\n\nCome into the building to find out information on what our project is and speak with staff to see what would be required from them.",
