                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QO1kGAAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QO1kGAAT/driver",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Driver",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for a Volunteer driver to join our exciting new CommuniTay café and supermarket at the Wellgate Centre Dundee.  You will be based at Deaf Links Dundee, which is a Deaf Led charity.  We provide support, training and advocacy services on behalf of the deaf community in Tayside, Angus and Perth.\n\n## Description\n\nThe role will be for 15/20 hours a week as a driver, helping to assist with the day to day deliveries and collections.  You will be working between both CommuniTayfood café and the Wellgate café/shop. Good sound knowledge of Dundee area, as you will be required to collect and distribute food.   The candidate should have a willingness to learn and a can do attitude, be reliable, friendly and good at time keeping.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFull current driving license is required.\n\n## Training details\n\nWill be inducted and training provided within Deaf links to cover all policy and procedures.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n15/20 hours per week, covering mornings and afternoons, when required.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCommuniTayfood café and supermarket, Wellgate Centre.  Dundee\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses will be paid and reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
