            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eIUZAA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eIUZAA2/shop-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Shop Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nOXFAM: We raise funds to support our projects, help people less fortunate than ourselves.  Support emergency and long term projects.\r\n\r\nFor further details please pop in to one of our shops or contact:\r\n13 Rosemount Viaduct - 640335 (Janice Davidson - Manager)\r\n5 Back Wynd - 642490 (bookshop)(Marion Craigie - Manager)\r\nChapel Street - 637662( Pamela Reid - Manager) or 645275\r\nOpening Hours - Mon-Sat 10am-5pm and on Thursdays open until 7pm.\n\n## Description\n\nA range of interesting task to get involved in, help Oxfam in its vital work and gain good experience. Roles & Tasks can incude:\r\n* Sales Assistant inc: sorting out, pricing of donated goods & till operation and customer care.\r\n* Books Assistant - sorting out, pricing of donated goods & till operation and customer care.\r\n* Bric a Brac Assistant - sorting out, pricing of donated goods & till operation and customer care.\r\n\r\nFor further details please pop in to one of our shops or contact:\r\n13 Rosemount Viaduct - 640335 (Janice Davidson - Manager)\r\n5 Back Wynd - 642490 (bookshop)(Marion Craigie - Manager)\r\nChapel Street - 637662( Pamela Reid - Manager) or 645275\r\nOpening Hours - Mon-Sat 10am-5pm and on Thursdays open until 7pm.\n\n## Experience required\n\nReliable\r\nEnthusiastic\r\nTrustworthy\r\nGood Team player/member\r\nFriendly\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support and relevant training for all volunteers. Full training is given inc Health & Safety & Induction Specific Task related Training also avaialable through Oxfam plus telephone & shop support.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible shifts.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCity Centre:\r\n13 Rosemount Viaduct - 640335 (Janice Davidson - Manager)\r\n5 Back Wynd - 642490 (bookshop)(Marion Craigie - Manager)\r\nChapel Street - 637662( Pamela Reid - Manager) or 645275\r\nOpening Hours - Mon-Sat 10am-5pm and on Thursdays open until 7pm.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nBus fares, provided ticket is produced, a four hour shift is required - mileage and/or parking fee.\r\nSandwich Lunch if 5 Hr shift",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eIUZAA2#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Shop Volunteer",
                        "description": "Reliable\r\nEnthusiastic\r\nTrustworthy\r\nGood Team player/member\r\nFriendly",
                        "commitment": "Flexible shifts.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eIUZAA2/shop-volunteer?#modal_register_a0g24000000eIUZAA2",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16",
