        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nYorAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nYorAAE/moray-citizens-advice-bureau-cab",
            "name": "Moray Citizens Advice Bureau (CAB)",
            "description": "To provide a free, impartial, confidential and independent information and advice service to the community of Moray.",
            "website": "http://www.moraycab.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC018026"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/LawAndJustice",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Law and Justice"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000CJj1tAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000CJj1tAAD/volunteer-adviser",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-01",
                    "title": "Volunteer Adviser",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nMoray Citizens Advice Bureau are looking for a Volunteer Receptionist for their Elgin branch.\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteering at CAB as an adviser is hugely rewarding. Each session is different and clients come to us with issues as diverse as consumer issues through to housing problems and those simply looking to be signposted to another organisation. We are looking for people who love to work as part of our friendly team and have an open and enthusiastic manner. Advisers help clients reach informed decisions and may assist in drafting letters, making phone calls and filling in forms.\r\nWe are looking for people who would be able to commit to giving six hours per week to CAB although this may be negotiable. This would be split over two sessions per week.\r\nWe provide fantastic training and ongoing support with our next training group starting late September. If you would like to make a positive difference to Moray residents this is your chance.\r\n\r\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills\r\nGood computer skills\r\nAbility to work as part of a team and with the general public\r\nBe able to extract relevant information and present it to clients appropriately\r\nBe willing to undertake training\n\n## Experience required\n\nCompetent IT skills, good communication skills, ability to work as part of a team, commitment to equality and diversity\n\n## Training details\n\nWe would offer any potential volunteer the opportunity to come into bureau a couple of times to experience a volunteering session and receive an induction prior to training. Training is initially classroom based and takes approximately 12 weeks.\r\nOngoing support from a session supervisor, management, staff and fellow volunteers is always available.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n6hrs per week for 6 months.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteering takes place at the Moray Citizens Advice office - 6 Moss Street Elgin.  Travel expenses (by public transport or a mileage rate) are available.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses (by public transport or a mileage rate) are available.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000CJj1tAAD#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Adviser",
                        "description": "Competent IT skills, good communication skills, ability to work as part of a team, commitment to equality and diversity",
                        "commitment": "6hrs per week for 6 months.",
                        "applyLink": "https://www.moraycab.org.uk/help-us",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16",
                        "theme": [
