        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nYpcAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nYpcAAE/keith-dufftown-railway-association",
            "name": "Keith & Dufftown Railway Association",
            "website": "http://www.keith-dufftown-railway.co.uk/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eIi8AAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eIi8AAE/railway-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-01",
                    "title": "Railway Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe Keith and Dufftown Railway is an eleven mile line linking the World’s Malt Whisky Capital, Dufftown, to the market town of Keith.  It is completely run by vvolunteers. Be a part of the UK's most northly railway by with maintenance of the railway's buildings, yard, ground & rolling stock or helping visitors make the most of this fantastic rail journey!\n\n## Description\n\nThis wonderful railway is operated entirely by volunteers and maintenance work to keep this railway in top shape has not stopped during the pandemic. Throughout the year a vast programme of work is undertaken by volunteers, ranging from working on the track, running the trains to rolling stock maintenance and building maintenance… and the list goes on. In fact, many of our volunteers try their hand at most of these various jobs as and when required – and a significant number started volunteering without having specialist skills in these areas in the first place. If you would like to lend a hand at the Railway, spend some time doing something truly hands-on, let us know.\n\n## Experience required\n\nno skills or qualifications are required.\n\n## Training details\n\nSafety awareness talk along with any other training that is necessary.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDufftown and/or Keith - volunteers require to make their own way to and from Dufftown.\n\n## Taster details\n\nAn induction to the opportunity is available.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
