                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Vhn3iAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Vhn3iAAB/clan-listening-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2023-02-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-18",
                    "title": "Clan Listening & Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nClan is here for anyone impacted by a cancer diagnosis. We provide emotional and physical support to people who have a cancer diagnosis, their family, carers and friends. Our services are offered to all free of charge, from pre-diagnosis, through treatment and beyond at our support and wellbeing centres located across the north-east of Scotland and Northern Isles.\r\n\r\nAbout the Role\r\nYour role as a Clan LISTENING & SUPPORT VOLUNTEER is to provide 1:1 confidential, non-advisory, non-medical, emotional support to people affected by a cancer diagnosis. Support is delivered to our clients in person at our centres, by telephone or online.\r\n\r\nLocation\r\nClan LISTENING & SUPPORT VOLUNTEERS are needed in all of Clan’s wellbeing centres and outreach locations across the north-east of Scotland and Northern Isles.\r\n\r\nReporting To\r\nThe Local Services Co-ordinator (LSC) or Local Area Co-ordinator (LAC) responsible for your chosen Clan wellbeing centre or outreach.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities\r\n· Providing impartial, non-advisory emotional and wellbeing support to Clan clients;\r\n· Signposting clients to appropriate Clan services and external services if required;\r\n· Recording client session notes and debriefing with your LSC/LAC;\r\n· Receiving monetary donations from donors and providing support as appropriate;\r\n· Welcoming Clan Haven guests and assisting with check-ins (Clan House only);\r\n· Activities may vary depending on the location of your chosen wellbeing centre.\r\n\r\nClan will make sure:\r\n· The wider Clan team is on hand to answer any questions and support you as needed;\r\n· Your line manager holds check-ins to discuss how you are getting on in your role;\r\n· You receive a debrief at the end of each volunteer shift;\r\n· You have access to ongoing training, supervision and development opportunities;\r\n· Expenses incurred whilst volunteering are reimbursed, when claimed in accordance with Clan’s Volunteer Expenses Policy.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou must be over 18 years of age and should be caring, compassionate and a great listener!\r\n\r\nYou should also be:\r\n· Able to build rapport with clients through the use of active listening, your excellent interpersonal skills and your ability to be non-judgmental;\r\n· Able to recognize the boundaries of your role (and Clan) and signpost clients to a more appropriate internal or external service if required;\r\n· Confident when engaging with people from a variety of backgrounds;\r\n· A flexible, reliable and enthusiastic team player, who’s able to comply with Clan Policies & Procedures in all aspects of the role;\r\n· Willing to undertake additional training to enhance the services delivered by Clan;\r\n· Dedicated to raising awareness of Clan, our services and fundraising opportunities.\n\n## Training details\n\nYour role as a Clan LISTENING & SUPPORT VOLUNTEER may involve dealing with difficult situations. Clan will provide you with the relevant training, induction and ongoing supervision to support you in your role.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nIdeally, you will complete one shift of 4 hours on a rota basis either weekly, fortnightly or monthly. We ask that you commit to volunteering for a minimum of 12 months unless otherwise agreed.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses incurred whilst volunteering are reimbursed, when claimed in accordance with Clan’s Volunteer Expenses Policy.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fb0a153fa-4793-4d1d-9212-87a9f287112d%2FliLEC2s9ZwYA46gEa6AxGTVGunx2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=46acb02c-763c-463b-87a5-7a5fe6d16f72",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Vhn3iAAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Clan Listening & Support Volunteer",
                        "description": "You must be over 18 years of age and should be caring, compassionate and a great listener!\r\n\r\nYou should also be:\r\n· Able to build rapport with clients through the use of active listening, your excellent interpersonal skills and your ability to be non-judgmental;\r\n· Able to recognize the boundaries of your role (and Clan) and signpost clients to a more appropriate internal or external service if required;\r\n· Confident when engaging with people from a variety of backgrounds;\r\n· A flexible, reliable and enthusiastic team player, who’s able to comply with Clan Policies & Procedures in all aspects of the role;\r\n· Willing to undertake additional training to enhance the services delivered by Clan;\r\n· Dedicated to raising awareness of Clan, our services and fundraising opportunities.",
                        "commitment": "Ideally, you will complete one shift of 4 hours on a rota basis either weekly, fortnightly or monthly. We ask that you commit to volunteering for a minimum of 12 months unless otherwise agreed.",
