                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Vhn3sAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Vhn3sAAB/clan-events-volunteer-orkney",
                    "publishStart": "2023-02-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-18",
                    "title": "Clan Events Volunteer - Orkney",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nClan is here for anyone impacted by a cancer diagnosis. We provide emotional and physical support to people who have a cancer diagnosis, their family, carers and friends. Our services are offered to all free of charge, from pre-diagnosis, through treatment and beyond at our support and wellbeing centres located across the north-east of Scotland and Northern Isles.\r\n\r\nAbout the Role\r\nYour role as a Clan EVENTS VOLUNTEER is essential in helping to generate the income needed to enable Clan to deliver vital services to people affected by cancer in your community. You could get involved with a variety of activities; supervising a cheering point at our runs, walks or cycles, accepting monetary donations at a village fair, welcoming guests at our flagship events or handing out information at one of our open days – there are lots of options!\r\n\r\nLocation\r\nClan EVENTS VOLUNTEERS are needed to support all of our locations across the north-east of Scotland and Northern Isles.\r\n\r\nReporting To\r\nYou may be reporting to one of Clan’s Community Development Co-ordinators, an Events Team Lead Volunteer or one of our Local Services Co-ordinators. At the time of your onboarding, you’ll be advised who your main point of contact is.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities\r\nTypical activities might include: \r\n•\tHelping to construct an information stand/gazebo for an event, putting out signage for runs/walks/cycles, arranging merchandise on a stall or setting out chairs/tables;\r\n•\tProviding a warm and friendly welcome to attendees of Clan events, answering their questions and encouraging people to get involved;\r\n•\tSupporting larger scale events such as the Annual Ball or Lunch. We need volunteers to do things like steward the car park, greet attendees, give out information, supervise stalls, assist with activities, sell tickets and accept donations;\r\n•\tCarrying out tasks alongside Clan staff to ensure the best possible experience for our events attendees/participants and signposting towards Clan services where appropriate;\r\n•\tHelping to raise awareness of Clan services.\r\n\r\nThere are a variety of tasks and activities that you could get involved in to suit your existing skillset and to perhaps give you new and different experiences.\r\n\r\nClan will make sure; \r\n•\tThe wider Clan team is on hand to answer any questions and support you as needed; \r\n•\tYou have any essential kit that you might need (High Vis tabard, clip board, card machine etc.) but you will need to dress appropriately for the task and conditions. E.g. if you are supervising an information tent on a frosty Winter morning, you must ensure you wear warm, waterproof clothing, or if outside in the sun distributing water on a Summer day, you must bring sunscreen;\r\n•\tYour line manager holds check-ins to discuss how you are getting on in your role;\r\n•\tYou receive a debrief at the end of each volunteer shift;\r\n•\tYou have access to ongoing training, supervision and development opportunities;\r\n•\tExpenses incurred whilst volunteering are reimbursed, when claimed in accordance with Clan’s Volunteer Expenses Policy.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou must be over 18 years of age and should be willing to get involved. \r\n \r\nYou should also be; \r\n•\tKeen to take part in activities as part of a team and on your own initiative;\r\n•\tAble to recognize the boundaries of your role (and Clan) and signpost clients to a more appropriate internal or external service if required;\r\n•\tConfident when engaging with people from a variety of backgrounds;\r\n•\tFlexible, reliable, enthusiastic and able to comply with Clan Policies & Procedures in all aspects of the role;\r\n•\tWilling to undertake additional training to enhance the services delivered by Clan;\r\n•\tDedicated to raising awareness of Clan, our services and fundraising opportunities.\n\n## Training details\n\nYour role as a Clan EVENTS VOLUNTEER may involve dealing with difficult situations. Clan will provide you with the relevant training, induction and ongoing supervision to support you in your role.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses incurred whilst volunteering are reimbursed, when claimed in accordance with Clan’s Volunteer Expenses Policy.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fb0801741-ef71-4cfc-94d4-6dd01d2d64d2%2FliLEC2s9ZwYA46gEa6AxGTVGunx2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=a057bbf7-f800-4b72-82d0-a5a7b8403bf1",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Vhn3sAAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Clan Events Volunteer - Orkney",
                        "description": "You must be over 18 years of age and should be willing to get involved. \r\n \r\nYou should also be; \r\n•\tKeen to take part in activities as part of a team and on your own initiative;\r\n•\tAble to recognize the boundaries of your role (and Clan) and signpost clients to a more appropriate internal or external service if required;\r\n•\tConfident when engaging with people from a variety of backgrounds;\r\n•\tFlexible, reliable, enthusiastic and able to comply with Clan Policies & Procedures in all aspects of the role;\r\n•\tWilling to undertake additional training to enhance the services delivered by Clan;\r\n•\tDedicated to raising awareness of Clan, our services and fundraising opportunities.",
                        "commitment": "Flexible",
