            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eOarAAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eOarAAE/cfine-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "CFINE Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteers are always welcome at CFINE and we can offer a range of opportunities tailored to suit each individual. \r\n\r\nVolunteering is about giving - time, ideas, experience, expertise - but it is also about receiving. For example, you will grow in confidence, learn new skills, meet people and can develop social networks and you will feel good contributing to your community, to tackling vulnerability and disadvantage.\r\n\r\nVolunteers can be involved in a range of ways:\r\n - Warehouse duties\r\n - Stock control\r\n - Fruit & veg packing\r\n - Selling at community food outlets\r\n -Food Pantry Volunteers\r\n - Weekend events, e.g. galas & food fairs\r\n - Financial management and administration\r\n - Customer care, serving at the food bank\r\n - Data management\r\n - Marketing and PR\r\n - Driving\r\n\r\nGood support is provided to all volunteers. Induction and start up training.  All volunteer help is greatly appreciated. \r\n\r\nIf you are interested please contact Kian Donald at email KDonald@cfine.org\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteers are always welcome at CFINE and we can offer a range of opportunities tailored to suit each individual. \r\n\r\nVolunteering is about giving - time, ideas, experience, expertise - but it is also about receiving. For example, you will grow in confidence, learn new skills, meet people and can develop social networks and you will feel good contributing to your community, to tackling vulnerability and disadvantage.\r\n\r\nVolunteers can be involved in a range of ways:\r\n - Warehouse duties\r\n - Stock control\r\n - Fruit & veg packing\r\n - Selling at community food outlets\r\n -Food Pantry Volunteers\r\n - Weekend events, e.g. galas & food fairs\r\n - Financial management and administration\r\n - Customer care, serving at the food bank\r\n - Data management\r\n - Marketing and PR\r\n - Driving\r\n\r\nGood support is provided to all volunteers. Induction and start up training.  All volunteer help is greatly appreciated. \r\n\r\nIf you are interested please contact Kian Donald at email KDonald@cfine.org\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support is provided to all volunteers. Induction and start up training.  All volunteer help is greatly appreciated and volunteers receive certificates in recognition of the help they provide.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times and days available to suit volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased in Poynernook Road with outlets across the city\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAny relevant out of pocket expenses are re-imbursed e.g.: bus fares.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Ffdf4f48c-9520-4a59-163d-1767fa426102%2FcG0Yqfo1FmU2EcSHv3tu2v9q1wu2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=2c7c53ac-c8ea-4334-8969-865c0896794e",
