                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Fi7unYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Fi7unYAB/volunteering-opportunities-for-young-people-under-18-years-old",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Volunteering Opportunities for Young People (under 18 years old)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nInchgarth Community Centre prides itself in offering young people volunteering opportunities where they can get experience while helping the community.\r\n\r\nIf you are under 18 and are looking to volunteer, this is the place for you!\r\n\r\nWe have different clubs you could volunteer with, or you could help at the café over the weekend to get some barista experience (only for people 16 and above).\r\n\r\n-Monday, 4.45-6.15pm, GAMING CLUB\r\nOur gaming club is open to kids aged 7 to 12 years old.\r\nAs a volunteer, you will help set up and tidy up the Club. During the club, you will be playing video and board games alike as well as pool, making sure the kids are having fun and letting the kids win sometimes.\r\n\r\n-Monday, 7-9pm, PHOENIX CLUB\r\nOur Phoenix Club is a social club for adults with additional needs. \r\nAs a volunteer, your role is to engage with our members while having fun! It can be:\r\n-by playing pool or games, \r\n-by serving teas and coffees to the members, \r\n-by having wee chat with our members,\r\n-by helping them at the arts and crafts group.\r\n\r\n-Friday, 3.45-5.15, FRIDAY YOUTH CLUB\r\nOur Youth Club is for kids from P1 to S1.\r\nAs a volunteer, your role is to engage with the kids while having fun! it can be:\r\n-by paying pool or games,\r\n-by helping with the activities we have on the day,\r\n-by helping out with the arts and crafts group\r\n\r\nWe receive a lot of application throughout the year and we have limited spaces. \r\nBest time to apply is during the summer, when we are recruiting young volunteers for the next year.\r\n\r\nAll volunteer roles also provide excellent opportunities to undertake Duke of Edinburgh Awards and Saltire Awards.\r\n\r\nAll volunteers are greatly appreciated and provided with excellent support. Please contact us to find out more, join our amazing team of volunteers and make a real difference in the community pleasecontact Jules Ory, Volunteer Coordinator at email: volunteerinchgarth@gmail.com or tel: 01224 479061 \r\n*(if you are over 18 years we also have great volunteer opportunities for you as well - please vist our website website at: https://www.inchgarth.co.uk/volunteer.html or email volunteerinchgarth@gmail.com for details).\n\n## Description\n\nInchgarth Community Centre prides itself in offering young people volunteering opportunities where they can get experience while helping the community.\r\n\r\nIf you are under 18 and are looking to volunteer, this is the place for you!\r\n\r\nWe have different clubs you could volunteer with, or you could help at the café over the weekend to get some barista experience (only for people 16 and above).\r\n\r\n-Monday, 4.45-6.15pm, GAMING CLUB\r\nOur gaming club is open to kids aged 7 to 12 years old.\r\nAs a volunteer, you will help set up and tidy up the Club. During the club, you will be playing video and board games alike as well as pool, making sure the kids are having fun and letting the kids win sometimes.\r\n\r\n-Monday, 7-9pm, PHOENIX CLUB\r\nOur Phoenix Club is a social club for adults with additional needs. \r\nAs a volunteer, your role is to engage with our members while having fun! It can be:\r\n-by playing pool or games, \r\n-by serving teas and coffees to the members, \r\n-by having wee chat with our members,\r\n-by helping them at the arts and crafts group.\r\n\r\n-Friday, 3.45-5.15, FRIDAY YOUTH CLUB\r\nOur Youth Club is for kids from P1 to S1.\r\nAs a volunteer, your role is to engage with the kids while having fun! it can be:\r\n-by playing pool or games,\r\n-by helping with the activities we have on the day,\r\n-by helping out with the arts and crafts group\r\n\r\nAll volunteers are greatly appreciated and our volunteer roles also provide excellent opportunities to undertake Duke of Edinburgh Awards and Saltire Awards.\r\n\r\nWe receive a lot of applications throughout the year and we have limited spaces. Therefore we encourage people to apply as soon as possible.\r\n\r\nFor more details and to join our amazing team of volunteers and make a real difference in the community please contact Jules Ory, Volunteer Coordinator at email: volunteerinchgarth@gmail.com or tel: 01224 479061 \r\n*(if you are over 18 years we also have great volunteer opportunities for you as well - please visit our website at: https://www.inchgarth.co.uk/volunteer.html or email volunteerinchgarth@gmail.com for more information).\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nInchgarth Community Centre, Aboyne Place, Garthdee, Aberdeen, AB10 7DR",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fab4c79c8-0fea-4d4d-8808-2ff1890b6b02%2FgVtdkYeYkBeVMdGUL22XXV0JoCi1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=1691a3b9-a3b2-4dd0-8d00-67297c73f317",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Fi7unYAB#role",
