        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXelAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXelAAE/ms-society-aberdeen-group",
            "name": "MS Society Aberdeen Group",
            "description": "One aim: to beat MS.\r\nWe’re the MS Society – a community of people living with MS, scientists, campaigners, listeners, organisers, ambassadors and fundraisers. 68% of all our activity is delivered through voluntary contribution. Our local groups are run by volunteer teams who fundraise and deliver a range of activities and services to support people living with MS. Over 13,000 people affected by MS accessed information, support and services delivered by volunteers through our national network of local groups in the past year. \r\nScotland has one of the highest incidences of MS in the world. We make it our mission to beat it. We raise awareness of MS, make it a priority and provide support and information to people affected by MS.",
            "website": "https://www.mssocietyscotland.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC041990"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Carers",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Carers"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FundraisingFunding",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Fundraising / Funding"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SelfHelpSupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Self-Help / Support"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005Sz8vYAC",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005Sz8vYAC/group-coordinator-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Group Coordinator Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThis is an opportunity for someone who is  passionate about community development and working with communities to use their own assets to make a real difference to improving life in the Multiple Sclerosis community? \r\n\r\nOur ideal candidate will have experience of working with volunteers, although this is not essential. More importantly they will be a great communicator with fantastic organisational skills, who will play a key part in looking after our volunteers, helping them to grow and ensuring our volunteering processes run smoothly and efficiently. They will be self-motivated with a naturally collaborative working style; and thrive working in a small, enthusiastic team making a difference to the MS community. Working with the Volunteer Support Team, the Group Coordinator is responsible for coordinating all aspects of volunteering, delegating work and supporting the effective development and delivery of services in the area. You will help to support and retain volunteers to deliver our services – leading on volunteer recruitment, communication, and stewardship of the Coordinating Team with a commitment to equality and inclusion as well as healthy and safe working practices. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. Applicants must be over 18.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference for people with MS.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Lynda Boyce, Volunteer Support Officer at email: lynda.boyce@mssociety.org.uk or tel.: 020 8438 0700.\n\n## Description\n\nThis is an opportunity for someone who is  passionate about community development and working with communities to use their own assets to make a real difference to improving life in the Multiple Sclerosis community? \r\n\r\nOur ideal candidate will have experience of working with volunteers, although this is not essential. More importantly they will be a great communicator with fantastic organisational skills, who will play a key part in looking after our volunteers, helping them to grow and ensuring our volunteering processes run smoothly and efficiently. They will be self-motivated with a naturally collaborative working style; and thrive working in a small, enthusiastic team making a difference to the MS community. Working with the Volunteer Support Team, the Group Coordinator is responsible for coordinating all aspects of volunteering, delegating work and supporting the effective development and delivery of services in the area. You will help to support and retain volunteers to deliver our services – leading on volunteer recruitment, communication, and stewardship of the Coordinating Team with a commitment to equality and inclusion as well as healthy and safe working practices. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. Applicants must be over 18.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference for people with MS.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Lynda Boyce, Volunteer Support Officer at email: lynda.boyce@mssociety.org.uk or tel.: 020 8438 0700.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. Includes 1-1 induction with the Volunteer Recruitment Officer.  Online training in safeguarding, health & safety and GDPR. Ongoing support from the MS Society Volunteer Support Team.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available-all help greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCan mainly be done from home. Meetings can be done on zoom or face to face with the coordinating team.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed out of pocket expenses are reimbursed by the Group Finance Volunteer by BACS or cheque.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005Sz8vYAC#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Group Coordinator Volunteers",
                        "commitment": "Flexible times available-all help greatly appreciated.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005Sz8vYAC/group-coordinator-volunteers?#modal_register_a0gQD000005Sz8vYAC",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
