        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXgAAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXgAAAU/denis-law-legacy-trust-street-sport",
            "name": "Denis Law Legacy Trust Street Sport",
            "description": "Denis Law Legacy Trust is a registered Scottish Charitable Incorporated Organisation that operates and delivers a number of free to access programmes and positive destination activities for young people.",
            "website": "https://www.streetsport.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC054873"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eHFcAAM",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eHFcAAM/streetsport-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Streetsport Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nStreetsport provides young people across Aberdeen City with the opportunity to play sport for free in a fun and safe environment. \r\n\r\nWe run week night sessions year-round and are looking for volunteers to help at these sessions. Working as part of a team, you will assist with organising and participating in activities while building relationships with the young people that attend the sessions. \r\n\r\nVolunteering with Streetsport is a fantastic opportunity to make a positive difference in the local communities. In addition to enhancing your CV / excellent experience for future employment, you will also have the opportunity to attend internal and external coaching and training courses.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to assist and make a real difference. All help is greatly appreciated.  For further details please contact Nikki Fyfe, Volunteer Officer – Denis Law Legacy Trust at email:  n.fyfe1@rgu.ac.uk or telephone: 01224 263681.\n\n## Description\n\nStreetsport provides young people across Aberdeen City with the opportunity to play sport for free in a fun and safe environment. \r\n\r\nWe run week night sessions year-round and are looking for volunteers to help at these sessions. Working as part of a team, you will assist with organising and participating in activities while building relationships with the young people that attend the sessions. \r\n\r\nVolunteering with Streetsport is a fantastic opportunity to make a positive difference in the local communities. In addition to enhancing your CV / excellent experience for future employment, you will also have the opportunity to attend internal and external coaching and training courses.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to assist and make a real difference. All help is greatly appreciated.  For further details please contact Nikki Fyfe, Volunteer Officer – Denis Law Legacy Trust at email:  n.fyfe1@rgu.ac.uk or telephone: 01224 263681.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAn interest in sport and a willingness to motivate young people. We provide a variety of sports, not just football.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent training and support provided to all volunteers. Induction provides an overview of Streetsport, DLLT and sessions. We run regular training sessions on topics requested by our volunteers and provide additional support as required. We also support volunteers working towards their Saltire Awards.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to suit volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nLocations across Aberdeen. Currently we run sessions in the City Centre, Northfield, Torry, Garthdee and Woodside. We can usually provide support with travel to and from sessions if needed.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe will reimburse any volunteer their public transport rate to and from their coaching venue on a monthly basis on production of completed paperwork attached with their public transport tickets.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
