            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008tZGfYAM",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008tZGfYAM/shmufm-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "shmuFM Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nshmuFM supports our local communities to create their own radio shows - we broadcast a variety of issue based, music and community radio programming online, on 99.8FM and on DAB. \r\n\r\nThere are various volunteering roles in shmuFM: you can be a studio presenter, part of a community news gathering team, specialist music presenter, or get involved behind the scenes. \r\n\r\nFull training and excellent support is provided to all volunteers. Volunteers will be given induction into the role and will be fully supported by our shmu staff team.\r\n\r\nIf you live in Woodside, Tillydrone, Seaton, Torry, Northfield, Cummings Park, or Middlefield - get in touch to find out about becoming a shmuFM volunteer.\r\n\r\nFor further information please contact Sarah Igesund, Senior Adult Development Worker  at email volunteer@shmu.org.uk or telephone 07592355131.\n\n## Description\n\nshmuFM supports our local communities to create their own radio shows - we broadcast a variety of issue based, music and community radio programming online, on 99.8FM and on DAB. \r\n\r\nThere are various volunteering roles in shmuFM: you can be a studio presenter, part of a community news gathering team, specialist music presenter, or get involved behind the scenes. \r\n\r\nFull training and excellent support is provided to all volunteers. Volunteers will be given induction into the role and will be fully supported by our shmu staff team.\r\n\r\nIf you live in Woodside, Tillydrone, Seaton, Torry, Northfield, Cummings Park, or Middlefield - get in touch to find out about becoming a shmuFM volunteer.\r\n\r\nFor further information please contact Sarah Igesund, Senior Adult Development Worker  at email volunteer@shmu.org.uk or telephone 07592355131.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience required. Full training and excellent support is provided to all volunteers. Volunteers will be given induction into the role and will be fully supported by our shmu staff team.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times to volunteer. All help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nshmu HQ: Station House Media Unit, Station Road, Woodside, Aberdeen, AB24 2WB",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
