            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7MiQAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7MiQAAV/board-members",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Board Members",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you believe that all disabled people in Aberdeen City should live in housing that meets their needs?\r\n\r\nDPHS Aberdeen (Disabled Persons Housing Service) is a registered Charity and was formally established in 2001.  \r\n\r\nOur mission is DPHS will provide a comprehensive housing advice service to people with disabilities within the city of Aberdeen.\r\n\r\nDPHS offers information, advice and advocacy to people with a disability, their families and carers about housing options in and around the Aberdeen Area.\r\n\r\nWe are seeking passionate and experienced people who can dedicate some of their free time to the charity to join our Board of Directors .\r\n\r\nThe Board of Directors, which meets quarterly, administers the company.  A Manager, appointed by the Directors, manages DPHS’s day-to-day operations.   \r\n\r\nThe Board will:\r\n• Set and review the strategy in liner with Memorandum and Articles of Association\r\n• Ensure DPHS complies with legislation and documentation lodged in accordance with both Companies House and THE Office of Scottish Charities Regulator.\r\n• Receive reports relating to DPHS staff activity\r\n• Secure the organisation’s on-going financial viability\r\n\r\nMeetings usually take place on Microsoft Teams, however any travel expenses will be reimbursed for any in person meetings held.\r\n\r\nAll help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated. To discuss/for further information please contact Cheryl Robbie at email: cheryl@dphsaberdeen.org or telephone: 07986530507\n\n## Description\n\nDo you believe that all disabled people in Aberdeen City should live in housing that meets their needs?\r\n\r\nDPHS Aberdeen (Disabled Persons Housing Service) is a registered Charity and was formally established in 2001.  \r\n\r\nOur mission is DPHS will provide a comprehensive housing advice service to people with disabilities within the city of Aberdeen.\r\n\r\nDPHS offers information, advice and advocacy to people with a disability, their families and carers about housing options in and around the Aberdeen Area.\r\n\r\nWe are seeking passionate and experienced people who can dedicate some of their free time to the charity to join our Board of Directors .\r\n\r\nThe Board of Directors, which meets quarterly, administers the company.  A Manager, appointed by the Directors, manages DPHS’s day-to-day operations.   \r\n\r\nThe Board will:\r\n• Set and review the strategy in liner with Memorandum and Articles of Association\r\n• Ensure DPHS complies with legislation and documentation lodged in accordance with both Companies House and THE Office of Scottish Charities Regulator.\r\n• Receive reports relating to DPHS staff activity\r\n• Secure the organisation’s on-going financial viability\r\n\r\nMeetings usually take place on Microsoft Teams, however any travel expenses will be reimbursed for any in person meetings held.\r\n\r\nAll help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated. To discuss/for further information please contact Cheryl Robbie at email: cheryl@dphsaberdeen.org or telephone: 07986530507\r\n\r\nFurther information about our work and the difference we make is also available at https://www.dphsaberdeen.org/\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to volunteer. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAny travel costs for a private car incurred will be reimbursed at £0.45 per mile along with other travel costs such as bus fares.",
