                    "title": "Voluntary Board Members",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nLooking for a rewarding role as a voluntary Board member with an organisation company passionate about excellent customer service?\r\n\r\nKirkgate Developments (KDL) extends the range of housing options available to\r\ncustomers in the North East of Scotland, including homes for mid-market and market rent. \r\n\r\nAs a Board member you will:\r\n-have the opportunity to contribute to and sustain KDL’s growth;\r\n-gain valuable leadership experience that can support your future career;\r\n-receive training and skills development to support you in your new role;\r\n-attend a minimum of five Board meeting annually and an away day.\r\n\r\nIt is an exciting and challenging time at KDL and we are looking for new Board members with the drive and ambition to help us achieve our strategic aims.\r\n\r\nWe are extremely interested in recruiting people with:\r\n-Experience of delivering success within a commercial environment\r\n-Knowledge and understanding of finance\r\n-Customer service experience\r\n-An appreciation of good governance and what it can contribute\r\n-An ability to support and guide effective relationships with stakeholders of Kirkgate Developments Limited\r\n\r\nThe Grampian Group is an equal opportunities employer and encourages, supports and celebrates diversity on its Boards. This helps us to expand our perspectives leading to better decision making and greater innovation as well as higher engagement and satisfaction from tenants and employees alike.\r\n\r\nBecome part of a business that makes a difference in North East communities NOW!\r\n\r\nInterested? Want to find out more?\r\n\r\n-For an informal chat, please contact Malcolm McNeil, Company Secretary at email: malcolm.mcneil@grampianhousing.co.uk or tel.:  07801 794241\r\n\r\n-Or to apply, please visit https://www.grampianhousing.co.uk/board-member-recruitment, download, complete and return the application form, your CV and brief covering letter to communications@grampianhousing.co.uk\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and training provided. You will receive training and skills development to support you in your new role and gain valuable leadership experience that can support your future career.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nBoard meetings are held quarterly in Grampian Housing Association's office at Huntly House, 74 Huntly Street, Aberdeen, AB10 1TD. The option to attend online  is available.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoard meetings are held quarterly in Grampian Housing Association's office at Huntly House, 74 Huntly Street, Aberdeen, AB10 1TD. The option to attend online  is available.",
