        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXhUAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXhUAAU/archie-foundation",
            "name": "Archie Foundation",
            "description": "The Archie Foundation was formed in 2000, to support the build of a new Royal Aberdeen Children’s Hospital.  The charity started with a simple mission – to make the difference for local sick children, providing much-needed extras not already catered for by the NHS.\r\n\r\nR.A.C.H opened in 2004 and the charity’s impact was clear to see. Our support at RACH is ongoing and wide-reaching and Archie has now helped over one million children by funding vital “extras” to complement the excellent care provided by NHS Grampian.  Evidence of the tangible difference Archie had made through partnership with NHS Grampian invited calls for the charity to extend its geographical reach and widen its range of services, leading the charity to become a key provider of vital support to families across the North of Scotland.",
            "website": "https://archie.org/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC039521"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityFacilities",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Facilities"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNr4RAAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNr4RAAT/archie-foundation-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Archie Foundation Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Archie Foundation exists to make the difference for children and their families accessing local NHS healthcare and in bereavement. By working with our NHS colleagues, child development and childcare professionals, Archie provides a lifeline of support for local children and their families.\r\n\r\nWhatever age you are, and whatever your background is, if you have an interest in supporting the work that we do we would love to hear from you! There are many activities that volunteers can help us with, here are just a few examples:\r\n•\tPlace and gather back in our collection cans – lots of pennies soon mount up and make a huge difference.\r\n•\tAdministrative support in our donor care office – writing thank you letters and cards to let our donors know how appreciated they are.\r\n•\tVolunteering at events, both on the day and to help us plan for their success.\r\n•\tDelivering leaflets and putting up posters on community noticeboards.\r\n•\tStaffing a stall at a local market or community centre to help spread the word about the work we do.\r\n•\tSpeaking on behalf of the charity at community events.\r\n•\tAssisting with our supporters/groups e.g.: knitting and craft groups who\r\n•\tOrganising your own fundraising events with friends and family.\r\n•\tTraining to become a Volunteer Responder as part of Archie’s Child Bereavement Service team.\r\n\r\nAll help from people volunteering makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor full details and links for volunteering with us please visit https://archie.org/volunteer/ or email hello@archie.org\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and any relevant training is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible-variety of activities, tasks, events and times to suit volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur Head Office office is based at the Royal Aberdeen Children’s Hospital, Aberdeen.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
