                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BqWwkYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BqWwkYAF/volunteer-befrienders",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer Befrienders",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBefriending beats loneliness. \r\n\r\nIf you are friendly, like to chat and can spare an hour weekly or fortnightly you could be a Volunteer Befriender with our Project.\r\n\r\nVolunteers are offered training, guidance and support. \r\n\r\nBecoming a Volunteer can give you the opportunity to do something special within your communities.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Avril Cooper, Project Worker at email: befriending@thelivingwellproject.org.uk or telephone: 07475 940726\r\n\r\nMore details are also available at https://thelivingwellproject.org.uk/\n\n## Description\n\nBefriending beats loneliness. \r\n\r\nIf you are friendly, like to chat and can spare an hour weekly or fortnightly you could be a Volunteer Befriender with our Project.\r\n\r\nVolunteers are offered training, guidance and support. \r\n\r\nBecoming a Volunteer can give you the opportunity to do something special within your communities.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Avril Cooper, Project Worker at email: befriending@thelivingwellproject.org.uk or telephone: 07475 940726\r\n\r\nMore details are also available at https://thelivingwellproject.org.uk/\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers are offered ongoing support and guidance. As members of the Befriending Networks there are a number of training courses available. Volunteers are given opportunities to meet together to share their experiences.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to suit volunteers and the people we support.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur Befriending Service covers the Bridge of Don, Bucksburn, Dyce Newhills and Kingswells communbities and provides befriending support to anyone over 65 years who may be lonely or socially isolated.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel costs can be reimbursed using our expenses form.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
