                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eHMfAAM",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eHMfAAM/volunteer-drivers-cis-project",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Volunteer Drivers (CIS Project)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDrivers are required to support elderly service users with severe sensory loss to keep connected with their local community.  This would include supporting people to attend appointments, visit local community groups and attend NESS group activities.\n\nThis is a great, enjoyable opportunity to help in the local community, make a positive difference and also the opportunity to develop new skills and interests as well.\n\nFor more information please contact:\nClare Harris\ne-mail: Clare.Harris@nesensoryservices.org\nTel.: 0845 2712345\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for an enthusiastic person(s) to work with us in our CIS (Connect Include Support) service assisting the members to get to and from our groups as well as participation in the group activities. CIS is a support service for older people with hearing and sight loss and we provide social group opportunities across Aberdeen City.\r\n\r\nInterested? then please contact Sheila at email: sheila.ogden@nesensoryservices.org or telephone: 0345271234 for more information!\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication skills with an interest in supporting older people. Able to drive and have a clean driving licence and access to own vehicle (expenses are paid). Willing to learn about, or have experience of, sensory loss. An open and interested attitude with a willingness to learn as training will be provided.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and  relevant training is provided to all volunteers. Basic training involves Adult Protection, Sensory Awareness, manual handling, social inclusion, wheelchair use and accessing cars.\r\n\r\nOngoing training is geared around the service needs at any particular time.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible-various times available. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe run groups every week day afternoon throughout Aberdeen City.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are paid monthly by BACS on production of a completed expenses form.",
