            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hy5mDYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hy5mDYAR/gardener-and-general-outdoor-maintenance-playfauld-house",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-03",
                    "title": "Gardener and General Outdoor Maintenance - Playfauld House",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThis role is to support a Very Sheltered Housing Service in the town of Inverurie, we have 32 self contained flats supporting elderly care. We need someone to keep the garden looking tidy, with a bit of weeding of flower beds, paths and hard standing areas. We have various benches and outdoor furniture that requires annual maintenance of cleaning/painting when required. In the winter support would be sought to keep the paths clear and to grit areas where staff/tenants would be walking. We have a great community here with staff and tenants alike. The kettle is always on and you would be welcome to come in and have a chat with tenants or just say hello while you get a cuppa or a cold drink in the summer.\r\nWill provide equipment/materials required from garden tools to paint and painting equipment, snow shuffle and grit.\n\n## Training details\n\nIf any further training is identified, this will be considered.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
