        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXi2AAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXi2AAE/m26-road-to-recovery",
            "name": "M26 Road to Recovery",
            "description": "We work with males over the age of 26 years who have had a drug or alcohol problem. Our aim is to give people back their self esteem and a purpose in life away from addiction. We do this by having monthly outings e.g.: fishing gorge walking, bowling. We also do a community garden. This helps people give something back to their communities and helps break down stigma.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Addictions",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Addictions"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000003T6uyAAC",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000003T6uyAAC/m26-road-to-recovery",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "M26 Road to Recovery",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe work with males over the age of 26 years who have had a drug or alcohol problem. We meet on a Tuesday from 12-2.30pm. We also do a Thursday from 10am-12.30pm which is a drop-in with activities such as board games and arts and crafts. We are looking for volunteers to help out at the groups. It is very enjoyable, rewarding work and you would gain good experience and make a very positive difference.\r\n\r\nAll help is greatly appreciated and makes a real difference to people and the community. For further details please contact: \r\nAileen Goymer-Davidson on: aileengoymer@hotmail.co.uk\n\n## Description\n\nWe work with males over the age of 26 years who have had a drug or alcohol problem. Our aim is to give people back their self esteem and a purpose in life away from addiction.\r\n\r\nWe do this through a variety of ways such as having monthly outings e.g.: fishing gorge walking, bowling. We also do a community garden. This helps people give something back to their communities and helps break down stigma. \r\n\r\nWe meet on a Tuesday from 12-2.30pm.  We also do a Thursday from 10am-12.30pm which is a drop-in with activities such as board games and arts and crafts. We have opportunities for people to volunteer to help out at the groups.\r\n\r\nIt is very enjoyable, rewarding and you would gain good experience and make a very positive difference. All help is greatly appreciated and makes a real difference to people and the community. \r\n\r\nFor further details please contact: Aileen Goymer-Davidson on: aileengoymer@hotmail.co.uk\n\n## Experience required\n\nTo be able to communicate with males who have social issues. A good listener.\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support is provided to all volunteers and any help you give will be greatly appreciated.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWe meet on a Tuesday from 12-2.30pm and also do a Thursday from 10am-12.30pm which is a drop-in with activities.\n\n## Travel details\n\nUnit 5, Tillydrone Shopping Arcade, Hayton Road, Tillydrone (if people have to travel to get there We can pay/re-imburse bus fares).\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe can pay/re-imburse bus fares.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000003T6uyAAC#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "M26 Road to Recovery",
