                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008XjwDYAS",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008XjwDYAS/visiting-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-02-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Visiting Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you have a dog or cat that loves attention and has an excellent temperament, do you like meeting new people and have great communication skills. If the answer is “yes” this role is for you.\n\n## Description\n\nAs a Pets As Therapy volunteer, you will be at the heart of what we do. PAT Volunteers are dedicated pet owners who give up their spare time to help others. Along with their dog or cat, volunteers visit all types of establishments including residential care homes, hospitals, hospices and both special needs and mainstream schools. Our volunteers and their pets bring comfort and companionship to people living in residential care homes who may feel isolated, confused and lonely. We support schools to help young people improve their literacy skills and encourage confidence and concentration in the classroom.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication skills, pet must have an excellent temperament.\n\n## Training details\n\nSafe guarding and access to training platform.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note - no expenses are paid for this opportunity.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
