        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXPPAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXPPAA2/cosca-counselling-psychotherapy-in-scotland",
            "name": "COSCA (Counselling & Psychotherapy in Scotland)",
            "description": "Our vision is a listening, caring society that values people's well-being.  As Scotland's professional body for counselling and psychotherapy, COSCA seeks:\r\n\r\n- to advance and support all forms of counselling, psychotherapy, and the use of counselling skills\r\n- to promote high quality counselling supervision and continuing professional development for all individuals and agencies delivering counselling services and education in Scotland.",
            "website": "http://www.cosca.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC018887"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Counselling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Counselling"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HwOo9YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HwOo9YAF/treasurer-of-cosca-counselling-psychotherapy-in-scotland",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-16",
                    "title": "Treasurer of COSCA (Counselling & Psychotherapy in Scotland)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCOSCA Treasurer (Voluntary Position)\r\nCOSCA (Counselling & Psychotherapy in Scotland) is Scotland’s professional body for counselling and psychotherapy. We are a recognised charity, and a company limited by guarantee.\r\nWe are seeking to appoint a new Treasurer.\r\nThe Treasurer is an office bearer on COSCA’s Board and has the general responsibilities of a Trustee.\r\nThe Treasurer has the particular responsibility for maintaining an overview of COSCA’s financial affairs, including:\r\n\r\n\r\n- ensuring appropriate accounting procedures and controls are in place, along with reserves, investment and risk management policies\r\n\r\n- providing advice to relevant staff as requested.\r\n\r\nYou will be required to attend 4 meetings of the Board per annum and COSCA’s AGM. You will also be required to prepare short quarterly financial reports and assist with the preparation of an annual budget.\r\n\r\nA professional working background that lends itself to working strategically with financial information is required.\r\nFurther information including a full job description can be found on COSCA’s website under vacancies. www.cosca.org.uk\r\n\r\nTo apply, please send a letter of application detailing how your knowledge and skills relate to the job description to brian@cosca.org.uk The submission deadline is 12 noon on Friday 25 September 2026. Short-listed candidates will be invited to discuss their letter of application.\n\n## Experience required\n\nfinancial skills\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n4 meetings of 2 hours each per annum, 2 in person and 2 onlikne, plus one AGM with some preparation time.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTr\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed in advance out of pocket expenses",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
