                },
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I2KI1YAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I2KI1YAN/swan-volunteer-crew",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-18",
                    "title": "Swan Volunteer Crew",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSwan is a 126-year-old traditional wooden sailing vessel. Fully restored in the 1990s she has been used since to\r\n\r\nprovide a range of sail training opportunities for young people and public trips on board, giving people a hands\r\n\r\non experience.\r\n\r\n\r\nSwan has a core crew of fully qualified and paid staff, but as a charity operation, the boat also relies on a\r\n\r\nnumber of volunteers to help with additional crewing responsibilities during the summer season. (April to\r\n\r\nSeptember)\r\n\r\n\r\nNo sailing qualifications are necessary as the core crew retain responsibility for navigation and instruction. The\r\n\r\norganisation has a comprehensive safety management manual and set of procedures in line with MCA industry\r\n\r\nregulations. As part of this, crew training days are provided at the start and end of each season and new\r\n\r\nvolunteers are assessed by the Skipper on suitability and physical ability to crew on a public trip.\r\n\r\n\r\nVolunteers are expected to adhere to all on board rules and procedures, and to support others to do the same,\r\n\r\nin order to deliver a safe and enjoyable voyage for all on board.\r\n\r\n\r\nVolunteers cannot be assigned to a passenger trip until training has been completed, however there may still\r\n\r\nbe opportunities available to volunteer on delivery trips to various locations in Shetland and Scotland.\r\n\r\n\r\nCrewing opportunities are usually advertised early in the year for volunteers to sign up, depending on\r\n\r\navailability and subject to completion of crew training.\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is an excellent way to see Shetland by sea, or travel further afield with participation in the international\r\n\r\nTall Ships Races. The opportunity provides skill development in sailing, teamwork, maintenance activities,\r\n\r\nleadership and a chance to be part of Swan’s ongoing heritage story.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood physical fitness and a willingness to actively participate in the team.  An interest in sailing is expected, and experience is an advantage but not required.  No qualifications required, though training such as First Aid, Food Hygiene are beneficial.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVarious locations - main departure points in Shetland are Lerwick or Scalloway but can vary.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
