                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eH3zAAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eH3zAAE/club-volunteers-at-ability-shetland-childrens-rural-clubs-in-unst-yell-mossbank-north-roe-and-urafirth",
                    "publishStart": "2009-05-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-27",
                    "title": "Club Volunteers at Ability Shetland children’s rural clubs in Unst, Yell, Mossbank, North Roe and Urafirth.",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you have a few hours free on Wednesdays? If so why not help out occasionally with the Wednesday Club?  We would need you to attend outings with our clients who are wheelchair users\n\n## Description\n\nSupporting children and young people to take part in activities such as sports, arts and crafts; games; visits to places of interest such as the fire station, open days and cinema.\n\n## Experience required\n\nSociable; energetic; good communicator; dependable and punctual; encouraging to participants; willing to try new activities.\n\n## Training details\n\nIntroduction to the Club.  Trial session to pop along the Club and meet members.  Volunteer can meet with Disability Shetland Staff or Committee for support.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWednesday 10-3pm, however it may not be the entire day - Weekdays\n\n## Travel details\n\nVarious locations, depending on activity",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
