        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXQSAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXQSAA2/girl-guiding-shetland",
            "name": "Girl Guiding Shetland",
            "description": "The Guide Association, as part of a worldwide movement, enables girls and young women to fulfil their potential to take an active and responsible role in society through its distinctive, stimulating and enjoyable programme of activities delivered by volunteer leaders.",
            "website": "https://www.girlguiding.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC022677"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HudXxYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HudXxYAJ/unit-and-division-helpers-girl-guiding-shetland",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-19",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-17",
                    "title": "Unit and Division Helpers - Girl Guiding Shetland",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAre you enthusiastic about giving girls opportunities for fun, friendship, challenge and adventure? If the answer is yes, then you’d make a great Girlguiding volunteer! Whether you want to help with a specific event, on a casual or remote basis, or attend regularly; you can be involved in a way that works for you, suiting your skills, interests and availability. \r\n\r\nGirlguiding Shetland division is looking for a variety of volunteers to help us support units across Shetland. Whether it’s helping with our existing units in Sandwick, Scalloway, Lerwick, Whiteness & Weisdale, Aith and Unst or even helping us open /re-open units in Whalsay, Walls, and possibly Brae and Yell - but we are open to any suggestions! \r\n\r\nFor anyone interested in more flexible opportunities, we also appreciate help at a division level, perhaps helping out at individual units as needed, helping at one-off events or in an administrative role.\r\n\r\nRegister to volunteer here: https://volunteer.girlguiding.org.uk#/vacancydetail/shetland-division-h3iskny\r\n\r\nWhat you'll be doing \r\n\r\nOur local areas are all quite different, which means all our volunteers do slightly different things. Whatever your skills, interests and availability, there’s a role to suit you.  Each role is vital to running guiding locally. \r\n \r\nYou might: \r\n\r\n•\tHelp directly with girls in your community, giving them a space to discover their potential – whether that’s at your local groups regular meetings, at one-off events, on trips or adventures! \r\n•\tBe the behind-the-scenes superhero that makes the magic of guiding happen in one of our supporting roles. Admin could include anything from keeping records up to date remotely to communicating with girls’ parents and carers about the exciting adventures coming up.  \r\n•\tShare a specific skill or passion – to teach girls new things or help guiding run locally. Perhaps you play football and could run a one-off session for girls? Maybe you could lend your DIY skills to help with the upkeep of your local guiding building? Or if you’re a finance or communications whizz, could you help manage accounts or run a local group’s social media?  \r\n  \r\nWhat you’ll get \r\n\r\n•\tLoads of opportunities to learn new things and build your skills. You’ll have access to training, from first aid to delivering adventurous activities, with webinars and elearnings on our learning platform to in-person sessions near you to choose from.   \r\n•\tSafeguarding training to make sure you’re fully equipped and confident to make Girlguiding a safe space for everyone. \r\n•\tThe chance to connect with like-minded people in your area and beyond. You’ll be part of WAGGGS, a worldwide movement inspiring girls across over 150 countries. \r\n•\tThe satisfaction of helping girls in your community know they can do anything! \r\n\r\nWhat we need from you \r\n\r\nWhat we need from you depends on the role you choose. For all our roles we’ll ask you to  \r\n•\tProvide 2 character references.  \r\n•\tComplete our safeguarding training. For roles directly with girls this is safer guiding, for behind-the-scenes roles this is safer guiding basics.  \r\n\r\nFor some roles we’ll also ask you to  \r\n\r\n•\tComplete a criminal record disclosure check (Become member or update PVG scheme) \r\n•\tSome of our roles are open to women only – we believe that ensuring our leadership roles are held by women creates the best environment for girls to thrive.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThere are no specific skills required - we welcome volunteers from all backgrounds and experiences.  Just bring yourself and your enthusiasm!\r\nFriendly and willing to learn and reliable are all qualities of a Girlguiding volunteer.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HudXxYAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Unit and Division Helpers - Girl Guiding Shetland",
                        "description": "There are no specific skills required - we welcome volunteers from all backgrounds and experiences.  Just bring yourself and your enthusiasm!\r\nFriendly and willing to learn and reliable are all qualities of a Girlguiding volunteer.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HudXxYAJ/unit-and-division-helpers-girl-guiding-shetland?#modal_register_a0gQD00000HudXxYAJ",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "13",
