                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-17",
                    "title": "Community Transport Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nOur community transport service helps older people to get out and about when walking or public transport is not an option.\r\nMain duties include escorting clients from their home to the car and providing transport for a variety of reasons.  These can be taking the client to visit family or friends, go to a lunch club, shopping or to an appointment.  A friendly helpful approach is all that is needed.  This role is flexible and depends on your availability.\n\n## Description\n\nOur community transport service helps older people to get out and about when walking or public transport is not an option.\r\nMain duties include escorting clients from their home to the car and providing transport for a variety of reasons.  These can be taking the client to visit family or friends, go to a lunch club, shopping or to an appointment.  A friendly helpful approach is all that is needed.  This role is flexible and depends on your availability.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly personality, understanding of the needs of older people, ability to observe and identify areas of concern.  Good communication and listening skills, non judgmental attitude and good confidentiality.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible\n\n## Travel details\n\nShetland wide.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n45p per mile or public transport costs.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eKD5AAM#role",
