        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXRAAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXRAAA2/crossreach-walter-and-joan-gray-home",
            "name": "CROSSREACH Walter and Joan Gray Home",
            "description": "To provide residential care and short break opportunities (respite care) to sixteen older people as well as  ten day care places between Monday and Friday.  The care is offered in Christ's name and we seek to retain and regain the highest quality of life which the individual is capable of experiencing at any given time.",
            "website": "https://www.crossreach.org.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/LearningDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Learning Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eH4JAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eH4JAAU/volunteer-person",
                    "publishStart": "2010-05-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Volunteer Person",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe role of the volunteer person is to visit residents; read the newspaper, assist staff with facilitating activities for residents which may include arts and crafts, baking, outings and general chat.\n\n## Description\n\nResidents at the Walter and Joan Gray home all have individual care plans, within the care plans are recorded their interests and hobbies.\r\nThe role of the volunteer person would be to visit residents and encourage them with their interests and hobbies.  For some residents this may just be general chat, whilst others enjoy having the daily newspaper read to them.\r\nSome group work may also be required such as assisting staff with a baking group, an arts and crafts group, or reading group.  Or perhaps you have hobbies and interests of your own which you are willing to share with others.\r\nDuring the spring and summer we arrange bus trips for residents and there may be an opportunity for the volunteer to accompany staff and residents on these trips.\r\nYou will not be expected to assist residents with personal care, toileting or feeding.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA volunteer should have an interest in old people\n\n## Training details\n\nInducton - would read Crossreach policies and procedures relating to the role.  An agreed induction period between management and volunteer. Meeting residents and introduction to activity recording\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nNegotiable - Weekdays\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Walter and Joan Gray, Scalloway\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n40p per mile if driving /cost of bus ticker.  Monthly mileage form to be completed and paid monthly",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eH4JAAU#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Person",
                        "description": "A volunteer should have an interest in old people",
