        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXRZAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXRZAA2/active-schools-shetland",
            "name": "Active Schools Shetland",
            "description": "We aim to get more children, more active, more often.  To achieve this we work closely with coaches, volunteers, school staff, parents etc to run a wide variety of fun opportunities.  These can be during our outside curriculum time.  Any activity is considered and all active ideas are welcome!",
            "website": "https://www.shetland.gov.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eH49AAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eH49AAE/activity-leader",
                    "publishStart": "2009-10-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-03",
                    "title": "Activity Leader",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nIf you would like the chance to have fun working with children and running active games sessions then we would love to hear from you.  Almost any activity considered.  No experience necessary, just bundles of enthusiasm.\n\n## Description\n\nAs part of our role in making more children, more active, more often, we are seeking volunteers to help set up and run a variety of activities.\r\nOur activities mostly take place outside curriculum time but can sometimes take place during the school day.  Groups usually consist of around 10-20 children.\r\n\r\nWe will consider any activity that will help the children to be active and that they will enjoy- this could take the form of sport, walking, fun games, fitness activities or even gardening!  For example, a volunteer may wish to run 6 weeks of after-school badminton or football at their local primary school for an hour a week.  Or maybe they prefer to help out with playground games at lunchtime.  We can also supply a volunteer to assist them.\n\n## Experience required\n\nMust enjoy working with children.  No qualifications necessary but must be comfortable and confident in delivering their chosen activity.  Enthusiasm and a positive attitude are much more important than experience!\n\n## Training details\n\nWhere appropriate we can offer training.\r\nIf there are suitable training opportunities locally we would offer this to volunteers - sports coaching/first aid/child protection/sessions can be supervised initially by an active schools team member if required\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nUsually an hour a week.\nWe expect volunteers to commit to at least 6 sessions in a year.\nTiming depends on volunteer availability and when the children are able to attend at their locallity - Weekdays Usually an hour a week. We expect volunteers to commit to at least 6 sessions in a year. Timing depends on volunteer availability and when the children are able to attend at their locallity - Weekdays\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe work with every school in Shetland and while our activites are usually based in or around school, some can take place at local community halls, sports centres or sports clubs.  \r\nIf volunteers need assistance with travel expenses, we can consider this on an individual basis.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nIndividual negotiation",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eH49AAE#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Activity Leader",
                        "description": "Must enjoy working with children.  No qualifications necessary but must be comfortable and confident in delivering their chosen activity.  Enthusiasm and a positive attitude are much more important than experience!",
                        "commitment": "Usually an hour a week.\nWe expect volunteers to commit to at least 6 sessions in a year.\nTiming depends on volunteer availability and when the children are able to attend at their locallity - Weekdays Usually an hour a week. We expect volunteers to commit to at least 6 sessions in a year. Timing depends on volunteer availability and when the children are able to attend at their locallity - Weekdays",
