            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pc6ncAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pc6ncAAB/sports-event-marshalling",
                    "publishStart": "2022-04-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-03",
                    "title": "Sports Event Marshalling",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nShetland Triathlon Club require marshalls for their junior and senior events, as well as timekeepers and lane counters.  No experience is necessary, as duties will be explained on the day.  Marshallling means that you will direct competitors to the correct route and ensure that all competitors are accounted for at the correct turning points / finish line etc.  You will never be asked to stop or direct traffic.  You could also help with lane counting at the swimming part of the events, or time keep using a stop watch too.\n\n## Experience required\n\nHappy to be outside! Good communication skills.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe have events all across Shetland but mainly Lerwick, Tingwall, Sandwick, Aith and Brae.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
