        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXSjAAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXSjAAM/mind-your-head",
            "name": "Mind Your Head",
            "description": "We are a Shetland based charity who promote mental health positively throughout Shetland.\r\n\r\nWe want Shetland to be a place where mental health is supported positively in the community. Our aims are:\r\nTo deliver mental health support services across Shetland\r\nTo research and respond to mental health and associated needs within the community\r\nTo work in partnership with existing organisations to further the aims of the charity\r\nTo raise mental health and wellbeing awareness in Shetland",
            "website": "https://www.mindyourhead.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038381"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SelfHelpSupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Self-Help / Support"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Fj3U9YAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Fj3U9YAJ/board-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-03-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-08",
                    "title": "Board Member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe have vacancies for individuals to join our board of trustees who have an interest in helping to shape our mental health services and supporting the work of our charity.  We would be particularly keen to hear from individuals who have a good understanding of social media and marketing as well as applications from younger people who would like to represent younger people living in Shetland .\r\n\r\nWe have 6 meetings per year both in person and online.  We offer a thorough induction and support for all our trustees.  We have Team Days three times a year where trustees are invited to come and have lunch with other trustees and staff and we have an annual strategy day where management and trustees develop the strategy and focus of the charity for the year ahead.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEach Trustee must have:\r\nA commitment to the mission of Mind Your Head.\r\nA willingness to meet the minimum time requirement.\r\nPersonal integrity at all times and to declare any conflicts of interest and abide by the MYH Trustee Code of Conduct.\r\nStrategic vision.\r\nGood independent judgement.\r\nAn ability to think carefully and solve problems.\r\nEnthusiasm and willingness to be flexible.\r\nA willingness to speak their mind, participate in discussions and decision-making and abide by decisions made.  Trustees must give adequate notice and apologies when unable to attend Board meetings.\r\nAn understanding and acceptance of the legal duties, responsibilities and liabilities of trusteeship.\r\nAn ability to treat all information, gained by virtue of being a Trustee, in strictest confiedence.\r\nAn ability to work effectively as  a member of the team and to take decisions for the good Mind Your Head.\r\nA willingness to continuous professional development.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMarket House, Lerwick and online.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Fj3U9YAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Board Member",
                        "description": "Each Trustee must have:\r\nA commitment to the mission of Mind Your Head.\r\nA willingness to meet the minimum time requirement.\r\nPersonal integrity at all times and to declare any conflicts of interest and abide by the MYH Trustee Code of Conduct.\r\nStrategic vision.\r\nGood independent judgement.\r\nAn ability to think carefully and solve problems.\r\nEnthusiasm and willingness to be flexible.\r\nA willingness to speak their mind, participate in discussions and decision-making and abide by decisions made.  Trustees must give adequate notice and apologies when unable to attend Board meetings.\r\nAn understanding and acceptance of the legal duties, responsibilities and liabilities of trusteeship.\r\nAn ability to treat all information, gained by virtue of being a Trustee, in strictest confiedence.\r\nAn ability to work effectively as  a member of the team and to take decisions for the good Mind Your Head.\r\nA willingness to continuous professional development.",
