        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXSwAAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXSwAAM/hoswick-visitors-centre",
            "name": "Hoswick Visitors Centre",
            "description": "The Visitor Centre provides a welcoming venue for locals and visitors to the area.  The Cafe provides delicious homebakes and light lunches all made to order as well as space to display items collected and preserved.  The Centre includes weaving machinery, local items and an interpretation of the Hoswick Whale case.",
            "website": "https://hoswickvisitorcentre.com/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Heritage",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Heritage"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eOeHAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eOeHAAU/hoswick-visitors-centre-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2019-06-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-16",
                    "title": "Hoswick Visitors Centre Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\n.Volunteers taking up an opportunity to help in the Visitors Centre have a variety of activities to choose from: \r\nWelcome visitors including visitors from coaches.\r\nDo you have good local knowledge? Share it with visitors and advise on the visitors information resources. \r\nHelp in the Café. \r\nHelp provide an enjoyable experience for 12,000 visitors coming to the centre annually.  Local people mingle with visitors, browsing the visitors' information or the Shetland crafts on sale and the displays of local heritage\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteers taking up an opportunity to help in the Visitors Centre have a variety of activities to choose from: \r\nWelcome visitors including visitors from coaches.\r\nDo you have good local knowledge? Share it with visitors and advise on the visitors information resources. \r\nHelp in the Café. \r\nHelp provide an enjoyable experience for 12,000 visitors coming to the centre annually.  Local people mingle with visitors, browsing the visitors' information or the Shetland crafts on sale and the displays of local heritage\n\n## Experience required\n\nWith a range of tasks from which volunteers can choose to help with, the skills and experience would depend on that choice. Good communication skills.\n\n## Training details\n\nFamiliarisation with the business and its aims together with training as appropriate for the volunteer's chosen activity.\r\nFood Hygiene if appropriate for the volunteer's activity.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nDirect contact with visitors finishes at the end of September.  Other opportunities are ongoing.\nVisitor Centre is open May to September 10 -5 Direct contact with visitors finishes at the end of September.  Other opportunities are ongoing. Visitor Centre is open May to September 10 -5\n\n## Travel details\n\nHoswick Visitors Centre.  \r\nSouth Mainland has a good bus service which has a convenient stop a five minute walk from the Visitors Centre.",
