                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000SsL4YAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000SsL4YAAV/listening-and-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2022-09-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Listening and Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nYour role as a Clan LISTENING & SUPPORT VOLUNTEER is essential in helping to provide our vital Listening and Support service to people affected by a cancer diagnosis (directly or indirectly) in your local community. The listening and support service offers a welcoming, relaxed, safe and confidential environment for people to talk about the cancer experience with someone who can listen and provide emotional and wellbeing support.\r\n\r\nTraining will be provided.  We ask that volunteers give back one year of their time - at least one session per week (3-4 hours)\r\n\r\nAn interview will take place to make sure potential volunteers understand what is expected from them.\r\n\r\nPossibly assist with surveys.\n\n## Experience required\n\nUnderstanding and non-judgemental.  Resilient.\r\nTraining will be provided and we ask that volunteers give back one year of their time, at least one session a week (3 to 4 Hours).\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining will be provided.  We ask that volunteers commit one year of their time - at least one session a week (3 to 4 hours).\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nClan-s service runs: \nMonday - Friday\n10am - 4pm\nVolunteers are required to be available for either a morning shift or an afternoon shift on a rota basis. Working on a rota basis attending a 4-hour shift either weekly, fortnightly or monthly to a minimum of 12 months and on occasions be flexible and available to help at short notice.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMostly in Lerwick:\r\nClan Cancer Support\r\nFirst floor Islesburgh Community Centre\r\nKing Harald St\r\nLerwick\r\nZE1 0EQ\r\nWe have outreach in Whalsay and would like to start up in Unst, Yell and Bressay.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses reimbursed in accordance with CLAN Expenses policy\n\n## Taster details\n\nYes, subject to reference check and PVG",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000SsL4YAAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Listening and Support Volunteer",
                        "description": "Understanding and non-judgemental.  Resilient.\r\nTraining will be provided and we ask that volunteers give back one year of their time, at least one session a week (3 to 4 Hours).",
                        "commitment": "Clan-s service runs: \nMonday - Friday\n10am - 4pm\nVolunteers are required to be available for either a morning shift or an afternoon shift on a rota basis. Working on a rota basis attending a 4-hour shift either weekly, fortnightly or monthly to a minimum of 12 months and on occasions be flexible and available to help at short notice.",
