        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXTCAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXTCAA2/1st-whiteness-and-weisdale-guide-unit",
            "name": "1st Whiteness and Weisdale Guide Unit",
            "description": "Guides",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038537"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/UniformedGroups",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Uniformed Groups"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HuZZBYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HuZZBYA3/guide-unit-helper",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-19",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-17",
                    "title": "Guide Unit Helper",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGirlguiding Shetland is part of Girlguiding Scotland, the leading charity for girls and young women in Scotland. Girlguiding helps members discover their full potential by having fun and enjoying new adventures.\r\nAt the heart of Girlguiding are our regular group sessions, called unit meetings. These are run by volunteer teams of adult leaders, helpers, and young leaders.\r\n\r\nAre you enthusiastic about giving girls opportunities for fun, friendship, challenge and adventure? If the answer is yes, then Guide unit helper is a great role for you! Whether you want to help with a specific event or attend regularly; you can be involved flexibly in a way that works for you and your local unit. \r\n \r\nWhat is a Guide unit?  \r\nGuides is a relaxed, welcoming space where girls age 10-14 can have fun, learn and be themselves. They meet regularly in groups, called units. \r\n \r\nThe 1st Whiteness & Weisdale Guide weekly unit meetings currently alternate between Whiteness & Weisdale Public Hall and Staneyhill Hall 7.00-8.30pm, term time.\r\n \r\nWhat you’ll be doing as unit helper \r\nOur units are all quite different, which means all unit helpers do slightly different things. There’s a lot of space to make this role your own. But you'll likely: \r\n•\tBe an extra pair of hands to help make unit meetings happen. \r\n•\tWork with other volunteers to help girls get involved in activities, earn badges and awards – and celebrate when they achieve them!  \r\n•\tTogether with other volunteers, run fantastic activities that inspire girls, whilst helping to keep everyone safe. \r\n•\tYou might get to go on planned sleepovers, events, trips or adventures! \r\n•\tLearn new things, make new friends, and demonstrate our values of caring, challenging, empowering, inclusive, fun and inspiring in all you do.\r\n \r\nThe skills and qualities you’ll need  \r\n•\tThere are no specific skills required - we welcome volunteers from all back grounds and experiences. Just bring yourself and your enthusiasm! \r\n•\tFriendly, willing to learn and reliable are all qualities of a great unit helper.\r\n\r\nWhat you’ll get \r\n•\tLoads of opportunities to learn new things and build your skills. You’ll have access to training on our learning platform, from first aid to delivering adventurous activities with webinars, elearnings or in-person sessions near you to choose from. \r\n•\tSafeguarding training to make sure you’re fully equipped and confident to make Girlguiding a safe space for everyone. \r\n•\tThe chance to connect with like-minded people in your area and beyond. You’ll be part of WAGGGS, a worldwide movement inspiring girls across over 150 countries. \r\n•\tThe satisfaction of knowing you’re helping girls in your community know they can do anything! \r\n•\tThe rewarding feeling of watching girls learn and grow, whether that’s during one impactful activity or over their time at Guides. \r\n\r\nWhat we need from you \r\nWe’ll also ask you to \r\n•\tProvide 2 character references.  \r\n•\tComplete a criminal record disclosure check (Join or update PVG membership scheme). \r\n•\tComplete our online safer guiding training because this role involves working directly with girls. \r\n\r\n\r\nRegister your interest to volunteer here: https://volunteer.girlguiding.org.uk#/vacancydetail/1st-whiteness-weisdale-guide-unit-ci5e4o3\n\n## Experience required\n\nThere are no specific skills required - we welcome volunteers from all back grounds and experiences. Just bring yourself and your enthusiasm! \r\nFriendly, willing to learn and reliable are all qualities of a great unit helper.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HuZZBYA3#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Guide Unit Helper",
                        "description": "There are no specific skills required - we welcome volunteers from all back grounds and experiences. Just bring yourself and your enthusiasm! \r\nFriendly, willing to learn and reliable are all qualities of a great unit helper.",
