        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nX62AAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nX62AAE/the-phoenix-community-hub",
            "name": "The Phoenix Community Hub",
            "description": "The Phoenix is a Community Hub in Dumbarton West, it was set up in 2018 by Rock Community Church. The Rock is a vibrant church community serving Dumbarton and the surrounding area. The Phoenix is designed to primarily serve the people of Dumbarton West, namely the residents of Castlehill, Westcliff, and Brucehill. The Phoenix includes a community cafe and a wide and varied activities programme including youth work, toddler provision, adult learning, intergenerational events, art classes, fitness classes, wellbeing programme and volunteer opportunities.",
            "website": "https://www.rockcommunitychurch.org.uk/phoenix",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC042716"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FaithReligionBelief",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Faith / Religion / Belief"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000DJZRgAAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000DJZRgAAP/cafe-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2022-12-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-06",
                    "title": "Cafe Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nRoles within the Café can vary from taking orders and serving customers to helping with food preparation. \r\nSetting/clearing up the tables in the cafe, ensuring that all the furniture is clean.\r\nPreparing and serving food.\r\nMeeting and greeting people.\r\nTaking orders.\r\nMaking hot drinks.\r\nUnderstanding and applying basic health and hygiene.\r\nA commitment to equal opportunities and a non-judgmental approach. \r\nEffective listening and communication skills.\r\nReliability and punctuality.\r\nAn interest in hospitality and creating a welcoming environment.\n\n## Experience required\n\nHaving a friendly and engaging personality\r\nBe comfortable working with members of the public\n\n## Training details\n\nIn this role we will offer you: \r\n\r\n●\tFood Hygiene training / qualifications.\r\n●\tBarista training.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased in the Phoenix Centre, Castlehill, Dumbarton",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000DJZRgAAP#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Cafe Volunteer",
                        "description": "Having a friendly and engaging personality\r\nBe comfortable working with members of the public",
