            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009ZoZUYA0",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009ZoZUYA0/volunteer-mealtime-helpers",
                    "publishStart": "2023-11-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Volunteer Mealtime Helpers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nServing meals. Provide support to residents during mealtimes, assisting with any needs they may have and ensuring a comfortable dining experience.\nCompanionship: Engage in friendly conversations, connecting with residents, fostering a sense of community and encouraging residents’ nutrition and hydration.\n\n## Description\n\nAre you someone who finds joy in providing support and creating a pleasant dining experience for others? Erskine Care Home in Gilmerton, Edinburgh, is looking for caring individuals to join our team as Volunteer Mealtime Helper. As a Volunteer Mealtime helper, you will be an essential part of creating a positive dining experience for residents at Erskine Care Home. This volunteer position involves providing support and companionship during mealtimes.\n\n## Training details\n\nLocal induction at the Edinburgh Care Home and assisting residents with mobility.\nOther trainings available when capacity affords e.g dementia awareness, speech and language training etc\n\n## Travel details\n\nErskine Edinburgh\n468 Gilmerton Road\nEH17 7SA\n\nThe home is close to Morrisons supermarket on Gilmerton Road. As public transport schedules are often subject to change please check your journey in advance with https://www.traveline.info/\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nComplete an expenses form.\nHave it signed off by named contact or Volunteer Development Manager.\nCan be given in cash or paid into bank account.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009ZoZUYA0#role",
