                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FWFcnYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FWFcnYAH/share-your-skill-glasgow-southside",
                    "publishStart": "2026-02-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-01",
                    "title": "Share your Skill - Glasgow Southside",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nShare Your Skill – Change a Life\r\nVolunteer with Aberlour\r\n\r\nDo you have a talent or passion you'd love to share? Whether it's football, gardening, photography, painting, music, baking, mechanics, crafts – or any other skill – you could make a lasting difference in a child or young person's life.\r\nAberlour is looking for kind, patient, and enthusiastic volunteers to join our services. This is a rewarding opportunity to spend time with a young person or child who would benefit from extra support, encouragement, and someone who cares.\r\n\r\nWhat’s Involved:\r\n•\tShare your hobby, sport, or special interest on a regular basis as part of a group, or 1:1 with a young person \r\n•\tBuild a positive, trusted relationship over time\r\n•\tHelp build confidence, self-esteem and new skills\r\n•\tBe a consistent, reliable presence in a child’s life\r\n\r\nWho You’ll Support:\r\nYou’ll spend time sharing your skill in a group setting, or you could be matched with a child or young person who would benefit from friendship, new experiences, and encouragement from an adult outside of their family or school life.\r\n\r\nWhy Volunteer?\r\n•\tMake a real and lasting difference in a young person’s life\r\n•\tGain experience, confidence and fulfilment\r\n•\tBe part of a supportive community of volunteers\r\n•\tFull training and ongoing support provided by Aberlour\r\n\r\nEvery skill has the power to inspire. Every moment shared can be meaningful.\r\n\r\nTo find out more or apply go to https://www.aberlour.org.uk/help-us/volunteer/role/709 or contact us at volunteering@aberlour.org.uk.\r\n\r\nPlease note: You must be 18+ for this role. A PVG check and satisfactory references are required.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tA skill or hobby you can share (anything from gardening to games, art to sport)\r\n•\tA friendly, reliable, and patient personality\r\n•\tCommitment to spending regular time (a few hours a week or fortnight)\r\n•\tNo formal experience needed – just your time and willingness to make a difference\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training provided, along with on going support.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nA few hours a week or fortnight, or a one off group.",
