                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HYL0DYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HYL0DYAX/young-person-befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-30",
                    "title": "Young Person Befriender",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAberlour Children’s Charity has built an excellent reputation over the past 30 years for supporting children and young people who have experienced disadvantage and trauma arising from early childhood experiences. \r\nWe are deeply committed to a child-centred approach, placing the emotional, social, physical, and intellectual development of every child at the heart of what we do.\r\nAs a Volunteer Befriender, you will play a key role in supporting a child or young person in foster care by providing consistent, positive, and supportive companionship. Your involvement will contribute meaningfully to their healing journey and support their re-engagement in healthy, positive social relationships.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for volunteers who are:\r\n\r\nCompassionate, patient, and non-judgemental\r\nReliable and able to offer consistency and commitment\r\nGood listeners with strong communication skills\r\nUnderstanding of (or willingness to learn about) trauma-informed care\r\nComfortable working with children and young people from diverse backgrounds\r\nEmotionally resilient and able to maintain healthy boundaries\n\n## Travel details\n\nAberdeenshire/Peterhead, car not essential but would be and advantage\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses paid monthly or in advance by arrangement\n\n## Taster details\n\nAberlour is committed to supporting all volunteers. You will receive:\r\nComprehensive induction and training, including safeguarding and trauma awareness\r\nOngoing supervision and support from a dedicated staff member\r\nOpportunities for additional learning and development\r\nReimbursement of agreed out-of-pocket expenses",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
