                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008y2tZYAQ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008y2tZYAQ/group-activities-volunteer-moray",
                    "publishStart": "2026-03-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-01",
                    "title": "Group Activities Volunteer – Moray",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWould you like to support young people to participate in group activities to build their skills and confidence?  Could you spare a few hours on a regular basis?  If the answer is yes, we are currently looking for volunteers with experience in a range of activities and in supporting group activities.  This could include interests in music, arts, and crafts; cooking, sports and health and wellbeing skills which can help improve the health and social wellbeing of our young people. \r\n\r\nWhat will I be doing? \r\n- To help build on the young person’s existing and emerging life skills including independence, friendship and social skills      \r\n- Supporting young people to express their ideas and views on group activities \r\n- Supporting the young people to organise and plan their time and contribute to the development of the group \r\n- Supporting young people on outings and activities \r\n- Spending your time talking to the young people, helping them to feel valued and listened to \r\n- Assisting young people with group activities  \r\n- Building young people’s confidence and self esteem \r\n- Being a positive role model \r\n- Supporting staff at outings\r\n\r\nWhat will I gain from the role? \r\n- A sense of satisfaction in helping young people build their confidence and self-esteem to achieve their full potential \r\n- Practical experience of working with young people \r\n- Learning new skills \r\n- Experience to get back into the workplace or education \r\n- Attend social events, awards and recognition events  \r\n- Be part of a professional and supportive team \r\n- Have FUN!\n\n## Experience required\n\n- A specific skill set in a social activity \r\n- Experience of working with children and young people \r\n- A knowledge of some of the issues affecting children and young people \r\n- Ability to work well with children and young people \r\n- Good communication and listening skills \r\n- Experience with building confidence and self esteem \r\n- Ability to encourage and motivate young people to participate in activities. \r\n- To have a non-judgemental approach to people, have empathy \r\n- To have a good value base, be open minded and level headed \r\n- A positive, can do approach.  \r\n- Ability to communicate and engage with young people in a way that meets their individual communication needs \r\n- An approach that assists in empowering young people.     \r\n- Be enthusiastic, flexible and committed \r\n- To be reliable and have a commitment to treat all information in a confidential manner.\n\n## Training details\n\n- Induction and child protection training \r\n- Role specific training  \r\n- Expenses – all out of pocket expenses will be reimbursed  \r\n- Supervision and support.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n- After school and evenings or during school holidays \r\n- 2-3 hours per week/ fortnightly or monthly depending on your availability \r\n- Minimum commitment of 6 months required.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F7f1db292-614f-4656-8b4b-cce2eaf511de%2FU0kwMHn6rJQ4tIXOW3xXfhaQc333%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=8dee5e8f-2ccf-4cb7-944e-5886f10c29e0",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008y2tZYAQ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Group Activities Volunteer – Moray",
                        "description": "- A specific skill set in a social activity \r\n- Experience of working with children and young people \r\n- A knowledge of some of the issues affecting children and young people \r\n- Ability to work well with children and young people \r\n- Good communication and listening skills \r\n- Experience with building confidence and self esteem \r\n- Ability to encourage and motivate young people to participate in activities. \r\n- To have a non-judgemental approach to people, have empathy \r\n- To have a good value base, be open minded and level headed \r\n- A positive, can do approach.  \r\n- Ability to communicate and engage with young people in a way that meets their individual communication needs \r\n- An approach that assists in empowering young people.     \r\n- Be enthusiastic, flexible and committed \r\n- To be reliable and have a commitment to treat all information in a confidential manner.",
                        "commitment": "- After school and evenings or during school holidays \r\n- 2-3 hours per week/ fortnightly or monthly depending on your availability \r\n- Minimum commitment of 6 months required.",
