                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008xzPTYAY",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008xzPTYAY/befriender-for-young-people-moray",
                    "publishStart": "2026-03-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-01",
                    "title": "Befriender for Young People - Moray",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are looking for befrienders to befriend young people as part of our Youthpoint Moray Service. As a volunteer befriender you would be matched with a young person, who you would spend regular time with on a 1:1 basis, building a trusting relationship having fun and supporting young people to transition out of service and onto the next stage of their journey. You would take part in activities that a young person enjoys such as playing football/cooking or introduce them to new activities or hobbies that they may not have the opportunity to take part in.  \r\n\r\nWhat will I be doing? \r\n- Making a difference in a young person’s life.  \r\n- Spending regular time with a young person and/or their family \r\n- Supporting young people and families when difficulties arise \r\n- Sharing an activity/hobby within the local community \r\n- Attending and supporting young people and families to take part in a range of indoor and outdoor activities  \r\n- Completing a diary log after each visit \r\n- Attending regular support and supervision sessions. \r\n\r\nWhat will I gain from the role? \r\n- Excellent training \r\n- Make new friends and meet new people \r\n- Get out and about \r\n- Have FUN! \r\n- Attend social events\n\n## Experience required\n\n- A genuine interest in the well-being of children and families \r\n- A few hours to spare each week \r\n- Reliability, commitment and discretion \r\n- Friendly and approachable \r\n- Non-judgemental attitude \r\n- Good communication and listening skills \r\n- Responsible and dependable\r\n- To have a non-judgemental attitude and approach to working with children and families \r\n- To be empathetic \r\n- To be able to treat all information in a confidential manner \r\n- Be friendly, helpful and understanding \r\n- Be enthusiastic, flexible, committed and patient.\n\n## Training details\n\n- Induction and child/adult protection training \r\n- Specific befriending training \r\n- Role specific training for supporting children & families \r\n- Ongoing support and supervision.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n- Befrienders will spend regular time with a young person on a weekly or fortnightly basis.  \r\n- As our young people may be at school, outings and activities may take place after school hours. \r\n- A minimum of 6 months commitment is required for this role.",
