            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005gAxlYAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005gAxlYAE/vollie-driver-lunch-club-meals-delivery",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Vollie Driver (lunch club meals delivery)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nBraehead Lunch Club operated from Braehead Community Hall, Forth, before its closure Summer 2024.  Meals for the club are prepared in Braehead Primary School (easily delivered as community hall was across the road from P.S.)\n\nCommunity Hall in middle of Asset Transfer from SLC to local group, however, outstanding repairs required so not sure if this will go ahead.\n\nWillie Waddle Sports Centre (WWSC) Forth can host the lunch club, but meals would require to be picked up from Primary School 12 ish every Thursday term time date the lunch club meets and delivered to WWSC.  Hot boxes that contain meals will be required to be returned to school same day.\n\nI have contacted Forth Community Trust, and Forth Resource Centre, and also asked club organiser Mary Gibson, to check with her group members who they could enlist to help.  Nothing forthcoming currently.\n\n## Experience required\n\nBefriending / Mentoring,Driving, Caring,Good Communicator,Patient,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Trustworthy,Lunch club has operated for many years, also organises own trips and outings, not just a lunch club.\n\n## Training details\n\nWould hope that VASLAN can help the group here, I am acting as intermediary.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire Yes\nAcross South Lanarkshire,Forth\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nLunch club members pay for meals, outings etc, not sure they will cover expenses.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
