                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000GE5mXAAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000GE5mXAAT/community-car-volunteer-driver",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-01",
                    "title": "Community Car Volunteer Driver",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nLarkhall and District Volunteer Group (LDVG) are looking for volunteer drivers who can help support clients to and from their non-emergency appointments to the local GP surgery or Hospital. Volunteers would drive our new electric Nissan Leaf car or use their own car to transport the patient from their home, to their appointment before assisting them in returning home again. Passengers may be frail, elderly, children or other vulnerable people. Volunteers will need to have a clean, current driving licence. \nWe now have 5 minibuses for hire or self-hire, 3 of our new buses can be driven on a standard car licence.\n\n## Experience required\n\nDriving, Caring,Patient,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Trustworthy,Must be patient, understanding and good with people.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire,Ashgill,East Kilbride,Larkhall,Stonehouse,Airdrie,North Lanarkshire\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable expenses are reimbursed.  Mileage is 45p per mile.  Expenses for valeting of vehicle will be paid as and when required.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
