                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Community Volunteer - Shopping and prescription Service",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are looking for dedicated volunteers to help with our shopping and prescription service. This essential service ensures that those struggling to get out the house or who aren’t fully able to get a shop for themselves can get shopping delivered and maintain independence and have agency of their own shopping. Volunteers will be added to a Whatsapp group where call outs will be made for the shops that week. If the volunteer is available then they offer to do the shop and a member of staff will email the service users details and shopping list, the volunteer with then do the shopping then deliver it the service users’ home then you will be reimbursed for the shop and your millage. This is role is perfect for anyone who wants to help out and make a difference but can’t commit to set weekly time slots.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Organised,Patient,Reliable / Dependable,Team Player,Trustworthy,\n\n## Training details\n\nWe will go through 4 week induction period, with regular calls and check ins.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe volunteer is free do the shop any time on the agreed day within working day hours. The volunteer is free do the shop any time on the agreed day within working day hours. This applies to expense payment frequency\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nEast Kilbride\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThe volunteer will fill out a monthly expenses sheet for petrol/diesel and will be be reimbursed 45p per mile.",
