            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nXdLAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nXdLAAU/headway-south-lanarkshire",
            "name": "Headway South Lanarkshire",
            "description": "Headway, the brain injury association is a charity set up to give help and support to people affected by brain injury. Headway aims to promote understanding of all aspects of brain injury and to provide information, support and services to people with a brain injury and their family and friends.\n\nHeadway South Lanarkshire meet every Tuesday in the Burnbank Centre in Hamilton, between 6.00pm - 8.00pm. Activities include Art/Crafts, Holidays/Outings and Service User Groups.",
            "website": "https://www.headway.org.uk/supporting-you/in-your-area/groups-and-branches/scotland/headway-south-lanarkshire/",
