                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000CStCLYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000CStCLYA1/committee-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-09",
                    "title": "Committee Member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nMake a difference to your local community. Develop new and existing skills and gain experience volunteering in a charity. The satisfaction of knowing you are making a vital difference to those with brain injury.\n\nSkills required:\n\nImaginative\nProactive\nApproachable and friendly\nGood interpersonal skills, \nImpartiality\nFairness \nAbility to respect confidences\nTo work as a team or on their own using initiative at times.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,Creative,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Hard Working,Open minded,Organised,Patient,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Social Conscience,Trustworthy,\n\n## Training details\n\nVarious online training opportunities available\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nHamilton\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nOut of pocket expenses will be paid",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
