                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000007uvfWYAQ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000007uvfWYAQ/chair-and-new-members-for-our-board",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Chair and new members for our Board",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nInstant Neighbour, based in Aberdeen City and Shire, has been supporting the local community since 1984. As a charity dedicated to alleviating poverty and improving quality of life, we provide essential services such as emergency food parcels, affordable furniture and household goods, and wrap-around support through initiatives like our Community Connector. We are also proud to be an environmental charity, actively promoting sustainability through reuse and recycling initiatives.\r\n\r\nAs we approach an exciting new chapter in our development, Instant Neighbour is seeking passionate and skilled individuals to join our Board of Directors. This includes recruiting a new Chair, as our current Chair is retiring after a successful 10 years of dedicated leadership at the helm.\r\n\r\nWe are particularly interested in professionals with expertise in digital, marketing, or branding, to help guide us through a period of growth and innovation. This is a unique opportunity to contribute to the strategic direction of a well-established charity while making a tangible difference to individuals and families in need.\r\n\r\nOur focus for the future includes expanding our environmental credentials, enhancing our digital presence, and continuing to meet the evolving needs of our community. With your skills and passion, you can play a pivotal role in shaping the future of Instant Neighbour and making a lasting impact on the lives of those we serve.\r\n\r\nThe Chair is expected to commit approximately 2-3 days per month, including attendance at quarterly Board meetings, strategic planning sessions, and additional meetings as required.\r\nBoard Members should expect to commit around 1 day per month, with quarterly Board meetings.\r\n\r\n*What We Offer\r\n• The chance to make a real difference to those experiencing poverty and hardship in Aberdeen.\r\n• The opportunity to work with a passionate and committed team of staff and volunteers.\r\n• Full support from the existing Board and Chief Executive as you transition into the role.\r\n• Networking opportunities within Aberdeen’s charity, business, and public sectors.\r\n\r\nIf you are committed to creating a sustainable and inclusive future for Aberdeen and beyond, we’d love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nAn excellent opportunity to make a real difference as a Charity Trustee. For more information please contact Sophy Green, Instant Neighbour CEO at email: sophy.green@instantneighbour.co.uk\n\n## Description\n\nInstant Neighbour, based in Aberdeen City and Shire, has been supporting the local community since 1984. As a charity dedicated to alleviating poverty and improving quality of life, we provide essential services such as emergency food parcels, affordable furniture and household goods, and wrap-around support through initiatives like our Community Connector. We are also proud to be an environmental charity, actively promoting sustainability through reuse and recycling initiatives.\r\n\r\nAs we approach an exciting new chapter in our development, Instant Neighbour is seeking passionate and skilled individuals to join our Board of Directors. This includes recruiting a new Chair, as our current Chair is retiring after a successful 10 years of dedicated leadership at the helm.\r\n\r\nWe are particularly interested in professionals with expertise in digital, marketing, or branding, to help guide us through a period of growth and innovation. This is a unique opportunity to contribute to the strategic direction of a well-established charity while making a tangible difference to individuals and families in need.\r\n\r\nOur focus for the future includes expanding our environmental credentials, enhancing our digital presence, and continuing to meet the evolving needs of our community. With your skills and passion, you can play a pivotal role in shaping the future of Instant Neighbour and making a lasting impact on the lives of those we serve.\r\n\r\nThe Chair is expected to commit approximately 2-3 days per month, including attendance at quarterly Board meetings, strategic planning sessions, and additional meetings as required.\r\nBoard Members should expect to commit around 1 day per month, with quarterly Board meetings.\r\n\r\n*What We Offer\r\n• The chance to make a real difference to those experiencing poverty and hardship in Aberdeen.\r\n• The opportunity to work with a passionate and committed team of staff and volunteers.\r\n• Full support from the existing Board and Chief Executive as you transition into the role.\r\n• Networking opportunities within Aberdeen’s charity, business, and public sectors.\r\n\r\nIf you are committed to creating a sustainable and inclusive future for Aberdeen and beyond, we’d love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nAn excellent opportunity to make a real difference as a Charity Trustee. For more information please contact Sophy Green, Instant Neighbour CEO at email: sophy.green@instantneighbour.co.uk\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant training and support is provided to all volunteers. Includes an oppportunity to attend and observe a meeting and the option to have another Board member as a mentor.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe Chair is expected to commit approximately 2-3 days per month, including attendance at quarterly Board meetings, strategic planning sessions, and additional meetings as required.\r\nBoard Members should expect to commit around 1 day per month, with quarterly Board meetings.\r\n\r\nAll help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAn expenses form is issued and all reasonable expenses are paid.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000007uvfWYAQ#role",
