            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000000ELnoYAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000000ELnoYAG/home-start-aberdeen-charity-shop-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Home-Start Aberdeen Charity Shop Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\n*School leaver or student?\r\n\r\n*Getting back into work?\r\n\r\n*Recently retired?\r\n\r\nIf you have time to support a local charity, we want to hear from you! Home-Start Aberdeen are looking for enthusiastic and energetic volunteers to meet and greet customers, organise donations and take cash and card payments at our city-centre charity shop at 101 George Street Aberdeen.\r\n\r\nIn return we offer:\r\n\r\n· a great working environment\r\n· a chance to learn new skills (or share existing ones)\r\n· and the opportunity to gain experience and confidence in the retail sector\r\n\r\n… all while making a difference for young families in Aberdeen!\r\n\r\nFor further details please contact Karen Milne, Charity Shop Manager, E Mail: shop@homestartaberdeen.org.uk or telephone : 01224 622390.\n\n## Description\n\n*School leaver or student?\r\n\r\n*Getting back into work?\r\n\r\n*Recently retired?\r\n\r\nIf you have time to support a local charity, we want to hear from you! Home-Start Aberdeen are looking for enthusiastic and energetic volunteers to meet and greet customers, organise donations and take cash and card payments at our city-centre charity shop at 101 George Street Aberdeen.\r\n\r\nIn return we offer:\r\n\r\n· a great working environment\r\n· a chance to learn new skills (or share existing ones)\r\n· and the opportunity to gain experience and confidence in the retail sector\r\n\r\n… all while making a difference for young families in Aberdeen!\r\n\r\nFor further details please contact Karen Milne, Charity Shop Manager, E Mail: shop@homestartaberdeen.org.uk or telephone : 01224 622390.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience necessary.\r\nThe willingness to commit time and energy to Home-Start Aberdeen, with a positive attitude to meeting new people and learning new skills.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provide to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to suit volunteer.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur shop is at 101 George Street, Aberdeen – directly across from the old John Lewis store.",
