            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IQslbYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IQslbYAD/treasurer-on-the-board-of-aberdeen-citizens-advice-bureau",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-16",
                    "title": "Treasurer on the Board of Aberdeen Citizens Advice Bureau",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAberdeen Citizens Advice Bureau (ACAB) seeks a Board Member with a finance background to continue the work done by our current Treasurer and play an active role in preparing the Bureau for the demands of the future.\r\n\r\nABOUT CAB\r\nACAB is an independent Scottish charity and a member of the Citizens Advice Scotland network.\r\n\r\nThe Bureau provides free, independent, confidential and impartial advice to the citizens of Aberdeen and its environs that is accessible and tailored to meet the needs of the community.\r\n\r\nTHE ROLE\r\nThe core role of the Treasurer is to advise the Board on all financial matters and to oversee the financial affairs of ACAB and ensure that they are legal, constitutional and within accepted accounting practice.\r\n\r\nTHE PERSON\r\nThe Treasurer will have the ability and the experience to oversee the financial affairs and governance of the Bureau and will have the skills to analyse key financial matters and to present fellow Board Members with clear option appraisals and recommendations.\r\n\r\nHOW TO APPLY\r\nTo apply for a copy of the detailed role description and person specification please e-mail Kristi Kelly, Bureau Manager, at kristi.kelly@aberdeencab.casonline.org.uk \r\nFor an informal discussion on the role, please contact the Chair of the Board, Sheila Thomson at sheila.thomson@aberdeencab.casonline.org.uk\r\n\r\nApplication is by CV and a covering letter indicating your suitability to the role emailed to Kristi Kelly, Bureau Manager, at kristi.kelly@aberdeencab.casonline.org.uk \r\n\r\nThe closing date is Monday 16th November 2026.\n\n## Description\n\nAberdeen Citizens Advice Bureau (ACAB) seeks a Board Member with a finance background to continue the work done by our current Treasurer and play an active role in preparing the Bureau for the demands of the future.\r\n\r\n\r\n-ABOUT CAB:\r\n\r\nACAB is an independent Scottish charity and a member of the Citizens Advice Scotland network.\r\n\r\nThe Bureau provides free, independent, confidential and impartial advice to the citizens of Aberdeen and its environs that is accessible and tailored to meet the needs of the community.\r\n\r\n\r\n-THE ROLE:\r\n\r\nThe core role of the Treasurer is to advise the Board on all financial matters and to oversee the financial affairs of ACAB and ensure that they are legal, constitutional and within accepted accounting practice.\r\n\r\n\r\n-THE PERSON:\r\n\r\nThe Treasurer will have the ability and the experience to oversee the financial affairs and governance of the Bureau and will have the skills to analyse key financial matters and to present fellow Board Members with clear option appraisals and recommendations.\r\n\r\n\r\n-HOW TO APPLY:\r\n\r\nTo apply for a copy of the detailed role description and person specification please e-mail Kristi Kelly, Bureau Manager, at kristi.kelly@aberdeencab.casonline.org.uk \r\n\r\nFor an informal discussion on the role, please contact the Chair of the Board, Sheila Thomson at sheila.thomson@aberdeencab.casonline.org.uk\r\n\r\nApplication is by CV and a covering letter indicating your suitability to the role emailed to Kristi Kelly, Bureau Manager, at kristi.kelly@aberdeencab.casonline.org.uk \r\n\r\nThe closing date is Monday 16th November 2026.\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant training and excellent support is provided to all volunteers/Board Members.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAberdeen Citizens Advice Bureau are based at 41 Union Street Aberdeen.",
