                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009DKjiYAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009DKjiYAG/aberdeen-citizens-advice-bureau-board-members",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Aberdeen Citizens Advice Bureau Board Members",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFor over 80 years Aberdeen Citizens Advice Bureau has been improving the lives of the people of Aberdeen. Aberdeen Citizens Advice Bureau is a fully independent registered charity with its own Board of Directors/Trustees. The advice service offered is independent, holistic, free, confidential, effective, impartial and accessible to everybody. \r\n\r\nAre you interested in being an Aberdeen Citizens Advice Bureau Board Member?\r\n\r\n*Summary of role\r\n•\tAs a Board Member you are responsible for the strategic management of the Bureau.  Each CAB is a separate registered Charity and for your local bureau to be effective a wide range of experience is required.  We welcome Board Members who are enthusiastic about helping their community, even if they don’t feel they have specific professional skills.\r\n\r\n*What might you be doing?\r\n•\tAttend Board Meetings regularly (approximately 6 each year)\r\n•\tTake an active part in the discussions at the meetings\r\n•\tTake an interest in the work of the bureau\r\n•\tYou might have a specific skill you can bring to the board eg financial management \r\n•\tHelp set policies, local objective and bureau projects\r\n•\tProvide enthusiastic support for bureau volunteers and staff locally\r\n\r\n*Does this sound like you?\r\n•\tAware of local issues\r\n•\tCommitted to the Aims and Principles of the Service\r\n•\tAble to think creatively and exercise good, independent judgement\r\n•\tWork effectively as a member of a team\r\n•\tHappy to improve awareness of Equality and Diversity issues\r\n•\tAble to understand and accept the responsibility of being a trustee and employer\r\n•\tMay have a specific organisational skill.\r\n\r\nPlease make initial enquiries  by email to bureau@aberdeencab.casonline.org.uk , or by phone on 01224 569750 between 10am and 3pm, Monday to Friday, for the attention of Kate Dean, Deputy Manager.\n\n## Description\n\nFor over 80 years Aberdeen Citizens Advice Bureau has been improving the lives of the people of Aberdeen. Aberdeen Citizens Advice Bureau is a fully independent registered charity with its own Board of Directors/Trustees. The advice service offered is independent, holistic, free, confidential, effective, impartial and accessible to everybody. \r\n\r\nAre you interested in being an Aberdeen Citizens Advice Bureau Board Member?\r\n\r\n*Summary of role\r\n•\tAs a Board Member you are responsible for the strategic management of the Bureau.  Each CAB is a separate registered Charity and for your local bureau to be effective a wide range of experience is required.  We welcome Board Members who are enthusiastic about helping their community, even if they don’t feel they have specific professional skills.\r\n\r\n*What might you be doing?\r\n•\tAttend Board Meetings regularly (approximately 6 each year)\r\n•\tTake an active part in the discussions at the meetings\r\n•\tTake an interest in the work of the bureau\r\n•\tYou might have a specific skill you can bring to the board eg financial management \r\n•\tHelp set policies, local objective and bureau projects\r\n•\tProvide enthusiastic support for bureau volunteers and staff locally\r\n\r\n*Does this sound like you?\r\n•\tAware of local issues\r\n•\tCommitted to the Aims and Principles of the Service\r\n•\tAble to think creatively and exercise good, independent judgement\r\n•\tWork effectively as a member of a team\r\n•\tHappy to improve awareness of Equality and Diversity issues\r\n•\tAble to understand and accept the responsibility of being a trustee and employer\r\n•\tMay have a specific organisational skill.\r\n\r\nPlease make initial enquiries  by email to bureau@aberdeencab.casonline.org.uk , or by phone on 01224 569750 between 10am and 3pm, Monday to Friday, for the attention of Kate Dean, Deputy Manager.\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant training and excellent support is provided to all volunteers/Board Members.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAberdeen Citizens Advice Bureau are based at 41 Union Street Aberdeen.",
