                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Aly30YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Aly30YAB/trustees",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Trustees",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\n*Join our team as a Trustee.\r\n*Looking to help your community and have commitment and passion? Then we need you.\r\n\r\nRuthrieston Community Centre is located on Holburn Street and has been at the heart of the community for  over150 years.  The centre offers a range of physical activities such as pilates and yoga, hobbies for example sewing and drawing and  community groups meet ups. Our community cafe encourages our residents to come and interact and foster community spirit and resilience.\r\n\r\nRuthrieston Community Centre have fantastic opportunities for people to help. We are looking for people to help. As a Trustee you would:\r\n•\tAttend Trustee meetings once a month, which can be in person or remotely.\r\n•\tUse strategic skills and understanding to help develop Ruthrieston Community Centre for the future.\r\n•\tHave a can do attitude and communicate with a wide range of stakeholders.\r\n•\tBring ideas to the table that benefit the local community.\r\n•\tExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers and is fantastic, enjoyable opportunity to help and make a real difference at a vibrant community centre serving the community. All assistance is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to help/for further details please get in touch with Amanda Stephen, Manager at email: RuthriestonDevelopmentManager@gmail.com\n\n## Description\n\n*Join our team as a Trustee.\r\n*Looking to help your community and have commitment and passion? Then we need you.\r\n\r\nRuthrieston Community Centre is located on Holburn Street and has been at the heart of the community for  over150 years.  The centre offers a range of physical activities such as pilates and yoga, hobbies for example sewing and drawing and  community groups meet ups. Our community cafe encourages our residents to come and interact and foster community spirit and resilience.\r\n\r\nRuthrieston Community Centre have fantastic opportunities for people to help. We are looking for people to help. As a Trustee you would:\r\n\r\n•\tAttend Trustee meetings once a month, which can be in person or remotely.\r\n•\tUse strategic skills and understanding to help develop Ruthrieston Community Centre for the future.\r\n•\tHave a can do attitude and communicate with a wide range of stakeholders.\r\n•\tBring ideas to the table that benefit the local community.\r\n•\tExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers and is fantastic, enjoyable opportunity to help and make a real difference at a vibrant community centre serving the community. All assistance is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to help/for further details please get in touch with Amanda Stephen, Manager at email: RuthriestonDevelopmentManager@gmail.com\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times to help. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nRuthrieston Community Centre\r\n532-536 Holburn Street\r\nAberdeen\r\nAB10 7LL",
