            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhrkrAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhrkrAAB/volunteer-befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2025-09-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-13",
                    "title": "Volunteer Befriender",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nBecome a Volunteer befriender and help reduce loneliness and social isolation across North East Fife.  As a befriender, you'll be matched with an older person who would benefit from regular companionship.  Whether it's enjoying a cup of tea, having a chat, going for a walk or supporting someone to reconnect with their community, your time can make a lasting difference to someone's wellbeing and confidence.  Visits usually take place once a week at a mutually agreed time, allowing you to build a meaningful  and supportive friendship.  Full training, ongoing support, regular check-ins and volunteer expenses are provided, making this a rewarding opportunity for anyone who enjoys meeting new people and giving something back to their community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience required and full training will be provided. \r\nCastle Furniture Project is looking for people who are friendly, approachable and compassionate; good listeners with excellent communication skills; reliable and able to commit to regular visits; respectful of confidentiality and professional boundaries; patient, empathetic and non-judgemental; comfortable working independently while maintaining  contact with the Volunteer Coordinator; and willing to undertake a PVG check and complete Volunteer induction and training.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers will be initially provided with around 1-2 hours induction covering everything from role specifics, expectations and boundaries, health and safety, manual handling and everything else needed to succeed in the role. PVG checks will be done and costs covered if don't already have one. Continued support will be provided throughout by the Volunteer Coordinator and opportunities for continual ongoing training provided depending on the needs of the role and personal interests.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMost often the clients own home or at an agreed upon place in the community such as a café or social club.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses are reimbursed in line with Castle Furniture Project's volunteer expenses policy.",
