                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I1fBdYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I1fBdYAJ/van-crewdrivers-mate",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-16",
                    "title": "Van Crew/Drivers Mate",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nJoin Castle Furniture's Van Crew and help make a real difference to individual's and families across Fife.  As a Driver's Mate you'll work alongside a driver to collect donated furniture and deliver affordable household items to people in need.  Every collection and delivery helps support Castle Furniture Project's mission of reducing furniture poverty while funding vital community services.  This is a hands-on role where no two days are the same, offering the chance to meet new people, stay active and be part of a friendly, supportive team.  Full training, ongoing support and volunteer expenses are provided, making this a rewarding opportunity for anyone who enjoys practical work and given back to their community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience is necessary, as full training and support are provided.  Castle Furniture Project is looking for volunteers who are friendly, reliable and enthusiastic; physically able to assist with lifting and moving furniture safely; happy working as part of a team; good communicators with a positive attitude; respectful and courteous when interacting with customers and donors; able to follow health and safety guidance and manual handling procedures; and willing to complete volunteer induction and any required training.\n\n## Training details\n\nVan crew members will be taken through their manual handling course, tail lift training, driver training/assessments/ and banksman training.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe role is based at Castle Furniture Project and involves travelling throughout Fife in one of its vehicles.  Volunteers meet at the depot before heading out on planned collections and deliveries.  Travel to and from the depot is the volunteer's responsibility travel expenses reimbursed in line with Cast Furniture Project's volunteer expenses policy.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses will be reimbursed in line with Castle Furniture Project's volunteer expenses policy.",
