                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I1cLpYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I1cLpYAJ/social-media-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-16",
                    "title": "Social Media Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nYou can put your creativity and social media skills to good use as a Social Media Volunteer with Castle Furniture Project.  You will  help raise awareness of the charity and its impact across Fife by creating engaging content, taking photographs and videos, designing post, promoting volunteering opportunities, fundraising events and community services, and sharing the stories that make its work so special.  Whether you want to build your portfolio, gain marketing experience or use your creativity for a good cause, this flexible role will help you develop valuable skills while making a real difference.  You will receive full guidance and support, and your ideas for growing the charity's online presence will be welcomed.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPrevious experience isn't essential, although an interest in social media and content, familiar with platforms such as Facebook, Instagram and TiKTok, and confident in writing clear, friendly and engaging captions.  They should be comfortable taking photos and short videos using a smartphone, reliable, organised and able to meet agreed deadline, willing to learn and work part of a supportive team, and passionate about promoting the work of a local charity and making a positive impact in the community.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis role is primarily based at Castle Furniture Project, with opportunities to attend its shops warehouses and community activities to capture content.  Some aspects of the role, such as creating or scheduling post, can also be completed remotely by agreement, Reasonable travel expenses are reimbursed in line with Castle Furniture Project's volunteer expenses policy.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses are reimbursed in line with Castle Furniture Project's Volunteer expenses policy.",
