                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Vhu52AAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Vhu52AAB/appliance-cleaner-glenrothes",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-13",
                    "title": "Appliance Cleaner - Glenrothes",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHelp given essential household appliances a second life while making a real difference to local people.  As an Appliance Cleaner Volunteer, you'll prepare donated white goods such as washing machines, fridges cookers and microwaves for resale by thoroughly cleaning them to a high standard.  Your efforts help provide affordable household essentials to individuals and families across Fife while supporting Castle Furniture Project's mission to reduce waste and tackle furniture poverty.  This is a practical, rewarding role where you'll be part of a friendly team and see the direct impact of your work everyday.  Full training equipment and ongoing support are provided, making this an excellent opportunity for anyone who enjoys hands-on task and given back the their community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous is necessary, as full training will be provided.  Castle Furniture Project is seeking reliable, motivated volunteers who take pride in their work and have a keen eye for detail.  The role would suit someone who enjoys cleaning to a high standard, can work confidently both independently and also of a team, and is able to  undertake light manual task and remain on their feet for periods  of time.  Volunteers must also be willing to follow health and safety procedures, use cleaning products safely, and bring a friendly, positive attitude that reflects Castle Furniture Project's values.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll Domestic Appliance Cleaners are trained in Control of Substances Hazardous to Health (COSHH), before beginning cleaning within their role. Manual handling training will also be provided for movement of white goods.\n\n## Travel details\n\nGlenrothes Warehouse - Craig Mitchell House, Unit 6, Flemington Road, Queensway Ind Est, Glenrothes KY7 5QF\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses reimbursed in line with Castle Furniture Project's volunteer expenses policy.",
