            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002kYJ1SAAW/pause-breathe-cic",
            "name": "Pause & Breathe CIC",
            "description": "Pause & Breathe CIC is a not-for-profit organisation run by husband and wife Susie Hooper and Phil Blackburn. We are passionate about making wellbeing more accessible financially, as we believe everyone is entitled to access services to enable good mental, physical and emotional health. \r\nIt is our mission to promote the health and wellness of our local community through providing wellbeing sessions that are accessible to all. We encourage habits that contribute to improved physical, emotional and mental health by increasing awareness of factors and resources that contribute to wellbeing. \r\nWe have two Community Wellbeing Centres, both within Falkirk - Central Scotland",
            "website": "https://www.pauseandbreathe.co.uk/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hzp73YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hzp73YAB/chair-of-the-board",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Chair of the Board",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nPause & Breathe is a community wellbeing organisation based in Bonnybridge, with a second wellbeing centre in Bo'ness. Pause & Breathe believe everyone should have access to opportunities that support good mental, physical, emotional and social health, regardless of their circumstances. Through a wide range of accessible wellbeing activities—from baby massage and mindfulness to chair yoga, creative workshops and martial arts—they create welcoming spaces where people can connect, belong and develop the skills to support their own wellbeing.\r\nMany members of the community tell us they've finally found somewhere they feel accepted exactly as they are. Pause & Breathe are particularly proud to support a high number of people who are neurodivergent, living with long-term health conditions or disabilities, or who have struggled to find a place where they truly belong. \r\nAs the organisation continues to grow, they are reshaping their Board to better support the CEO and strengthen the strategic leadership. This is an exciting opportunity to become part of that journey.\r\n\r\nPause & Breathe CIC is looking for a new Chair of the Board to help guide the next chapter of growth.\r\nThey are looking for someone who shares their values and can work alongside the CEO as a trusted sounding board, mentor and strategic partner. Previous board experience would be an advantage, particularly within the charity or third sector, but most interested in finding someone who is collaborative, compassionate and excited by the opportunity to help a growing community organisation thrive.\r\n\r\nThe Chair plays an important role in supporting both the Board and the Chief Executive.  Rather than leading the organisation operationally, the Chair helps create the conditions for good governance, thoughtful decision-making and sustainable growth. Working closely with the CEO, the Chair acts as a trusted sounding board, mentor and strategic partner—offering encouragement, challenge and perspective while helping the organisation remain true to its purpose and values.\r\n\r\nThe Chair also leads Board meetings, helps the Board work effectively together and represents the organisation externally where appropriate. Pause & Breathe are looking for someone who shares the belief that wellbeing should be accessible to everyone and who is excited by helping Pause & Breathe continue to grow.\r\n\r\nWhy join?\r\nThis is an opportunity to make a meaningful difference within a growing community organisation that is ambitious, values-led and deeply committed to improving wellbeing.\r\n\r\nYou'll be joining a supportive Board and working closely with a passionate CEO and team who care deeply about creating welcoming spaces where everyone feels they belong.\r\n\r\nTogether, you'll help shape the future of Pause & Breathe and increase its impact across Falkirk and beyond.\n\n## Experience required\n\nSomeone who is:\r\n• collaborative and supportive\r\n• an experienced strategic thinker\r\n• community-minded\r\n• compassionate and encouraging\r\n• able to build positive relationships\r\n• confident facilitating discussion and bringing people together\r\n\r\nIdeally you'll also have:\r\n• previous Board experience (Chair experience would be welcomed but isn't essential)\r\n• an understanding of charity or CIC governance\r\n• experience within the voluntary or third sector\r\n• an interest in organisational growth and sustainability\n\n## Training details\n\nThere would be an induction with the CEO and orientation given prior to the first Board meeting attended. This opportunity is online, so is fully accessible.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nBoard meetings every two months (first Wednesday, 6pm –7.30 pm, via Zoom)\r\n• AGM currently held within one Board meeting each year\r\n• Some additional support for the CEO between meetings, agreed together\r\nIt is anticipated the role taking around 10 hours per month, although this will be developed collaboratively as the role evolves.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoard meetings take place online via zoom.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are NOT available.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/604123ee0e5c1277769dc75f/1622636669059-MB5CTLRQJQPXYNOIPL3W/PauseandBreathe_Mark_300RGB.png?format=1500w",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hzp73YAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Chair of the Board",
                        "description": "Someone who is:\r\n• collaborative and supportive\r\n• an experienced strategic thinker\r\n• community-minded\r\n• compassionate and encouraging\r\n• able to build positive relationships\r\n• confident facilitating discussion and bringing people together\r\n\r\nIdeally you'll also have:\r\n• previous Board experience (Chair experience would be welcomed but isn't essential)\r\n• an understanding of charity or CIC governance\r\n• experience within the voluntary or third sector\r\n• an interest in organisational growth and sustainability",
                        "commitment": "Board meetings every two months (first Wednesday, 6pm –7.30 pm, via Zoom)\r\n• AGM currently held within one Board meeting each year\r\n• Some additional support for the CEO between meetings, agreed together\r\nIt is anticipated the role taking around 10 hours per month, although this will be developed collaboratively as the role evolves.",
