        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002lJsb1AAC",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002lJsb1AAC/bonnie-dundee",
            "name": "Bonnie Dundee",
            "description": "Bonnie Dundee is a partnership between community groups, Dundee City Council, businesses, organisations and individuals across the city.\r\n\r\nVolunteers are involved in a wide range of projects and activities each year including tending over 50 city centre planters, gardening sessions, litter picks, encouraging biodiversity and community gardening. \r\n\r\nThose involved aim to improve Dundee’s environment for both residents and visitors alike.",
            "website": "http://www.dundeecity.gov.uk/dundeebloom/bonniedundee/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Employment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Employment"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000OEQ96AAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000OEQ96AAH/gardener",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Gardener",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBonnie Dundee is looking for volunteers to help make Dundee a greener, cleaner and brighter place for everyone. All are welcome to come and help us with our gardening activities and other tasks.\n\n## Description\n\nBonnie Dundee is looking for volunteers to help make Dundee a greener, cleaner and brighter place for everyone. All are welcome to come and help us with our gardening activities and other tasks.\r\n\r\nOur volunteers and are involved in a wide range of projects and activities each year. Including tending to over 50 planters, an urban orchard and two gardens in the city centre, plus carrying out litter picks and helping to encourage biodiversity. Those involved aim to improve Dundee’s environment for both residents and visitors alike, providing opportunities for people to get involved and make a difference in their community.\r\n\r\nBonnie Dundee has a great sense of community and enthusiasm, welcoming all volunteers regardless of age, experience or ability. Please do come and join us if you’d like to learn more, have fun and help make Dundee cleaner and brighter for everyone.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnthusiasm to improve Dundee’s environment, enjoys spending time in the fresh air and see the benefits of the difference they are making. Volunteers do not need any prior gardening experience to attend.\r\n\r\nThe opportunity would benefit someone looking to gain skills in gardening and also those looking to improve social skills and team working ability.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe induction training will involve an orientation session on the geographic area and information on health and safety relating to bending, stretching, manual handling and use of hand tools as supplied. Ongoing training will include becoming familiar with the plants and flowers throughout the year. Volunteers will be supported by the core members of the group.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nAverage of 2 hours per session on days to suit the volunteer (flexible), this is usually a weekly commitment but this is also flexible. More hours would be welcomed in the summer months including some weekends and evenings depending on the growing season.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAny city centre bus will get volunteers within 5-10 minutes of their location (usually Overgate or Union Street). Expenses regrettably cannot be reimbursed by Bonnie Dundee.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note: No expenses are paid for this opportunity\n\n## Taster details\n\nThis would be agreed after discussion with the volunteer on a case by case basis, to ensure the volunteer is happy with the tasks involved.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
