            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Vup1mAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Vup1mAAB/retail-stock-processor",
                    "publishStart": "2022-07-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Retail Stock Processor",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nPlease join our team of volunteers and be one of our Retail Stock Processors, sorting and selecting stock for the shop floor, whilst having fun with your new team.\n\n## Description\n\nIf you want to ease back into a workplace in a quieter role helping to sort, organise and process our donations, this could be the role for you at our Edinburgh shop. As a Retail Stock Room Volunteer you will be helping steam and tag clothing donations, sort out book, music and film donations or helping with other departments that interest you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nRetail skills are not essential, just a willingness to learn s training and support will be provided.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe induction is based around the volunteer being given enough information so that they are safe in their new surroundings, with follow up shop specific training to follow.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis role is available at various locations in Edinburgh, East Lothian and Midlothian.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAny expenses paperwork is completed by the shop staff and expenses are paid through the till.",
