        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002lKVvBAAW",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002lKVvBAAW/north-ayrshire-foodbank",
            "name": "North Ayrshire Foodbank",
            "description": "we want to see more people helped out of crisis and fewer people needing foodbanks in the future. That’s why The Trussell Trust and local foodbanks are working together to develop new ways to help people out of crisis through programmes like More Than Food.",
            "website": "https://northayrshire.foodbank.org.uk/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000OFOduAAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000OFOduAAH/pantry-team",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-08",
                    "title": "Pantry team",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Pantry is essentially a small shop with a membership. The team will be responsible for the safe operation of the Pantry including : cash handling, stock rotation, shelf packing, serving customers and signing up new members. Some of the work is IT based (laptop) to record members weekly shop visit as well as signing up new memberships. \r\nOther tasks are manual. It would be helpful if you were confident handling weekly subscriptions which can be paid either by cash or our card payer.  The pantry will initially operate two days a week as a pilot and if successful extend on a planned basis with the whole team suitably advised.\n\n## Experience required\n\nN/A\n\n## Training details\n\nFood hygiene will be a standard training course. In discussion training will be provided when identified.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity is based in the Ardrossan Church of the Nazarene.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPPE equipment will be provided ( chefs uniforms). Travel expenses are available for public transport and petrol costs.",
