        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nWrQAAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nWrQAAU/grangemouth-community-care",
            "name": "Grangemouth Community Care",
            "description": "We provide transport and transport with escort, to elderly and frail persons with limited mobility for lunch clubs at Talbot house on tuesdays and thrusdays. Hospital appointments if no relatives are available and hospital transport is unsuitable, special humanitarian/emergency journeys - Wednesday.  Day care to meet weekly - clients must have S.W.S referral.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC034036"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SocialCare",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Social Care"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I01zRYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I01zRYAR/volunteer-escortlunch-club-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer Escort/Lunch Club Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGrangemouth Community Care are a small local charity which has been helping the elderly in the town for over 40 years and are manned totally by volunteers. They provide specialised transport via Dial-a-Journey on Tuesday and Thursday to help the elderly attend at a lunch club taking place in Talbot House in Grangemouth. Pick ups start at around 10am and then taking people back home starting about 1pm. \r\n\r\nGrangemouth Community Care are looking for new volunteers to support the driver and collect people from their homes on specialist buses provided by Dial-a-Journey and bring them safely to the lunch club at Talbot House in Grangemouth.  Once at the club, the elderly enjoy socialising so if you feel you can chat about most subjects and interact with the elderly you will find it most interesting and rewarding.  The elderly range in ages from 71-95+ so have a wealth of experience and stories.  It is catered for both men and women and feel that there could be benefit from having more men volunteer.  All volunteers are still welcome so if you have a few hours to spare on a Tuesday or Thursday they would love to hear from you!\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnthusiasm, patience and good communication skills. Experience in a caring environment would be useful.\n\n## Training details\n\nSeveral shadowing sessions are available, handbook given to all new volunteers, experienced volunteers on hand for questions, use of group WhatsApp and Facebook page. First aid and manual handling training reviewed regularly.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nTuesdays and/or Thursdays from 10am until 2pm as your diary allows.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTalbot House, Talbot street, Grangemouth, FK3 8HU.  Next to the B&M store where there is sufficient parking.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are NOT available for this role.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I01zRYAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Escort/Lunch Club Assistant",
                        "description": "Enthusiasm, patience and good communication skills. Experience in a caring environment would be useful.",
                        "commitment": "Tuesdays and/or Thursdays from 10am until 2pm as your diary allows.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I01zRYAR/volunteer-escortlunch-club-assistant?#modal_register_a0gQD00000I01zRYAR",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
