                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7IiWAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7IiWAAV/lunch-club-helpers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-03-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Lunch Club Helpers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nTalbot House is a Day Centre running lunch clubs on a Tuesday & Thursday. Our community organisation promotes and assists the welfare of senior citizens in and around Grangemouth, encouraging involvement of the wider community. We combat loneliness by providing facilities for socialising and eating together.\r\n\r\nOur Lunch Clubs are a key part of our work, providing the opportunity for elderly community to be socially interactive and share a meal. \r\n\r\nLunch Clubs Helpers support us on Tuesdays and/or Thursdays between 9:30am and 1:30pm with various tasks, including: \r\n-Greeting visitors and making everyone feel welcome.\r\n-Serving and then clearing food, teas, and coffees.\r\n-Washing up plates, using our industrial dishwasher, and general cleaning of the room.\r\n\r\nWe usually feed between 50-60 people and each Lunch Club is run entirely by volunteers, so all help is very much appreciated.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience is required, we just ask that people work well in a team, have a friendly disposition, and are willing to help.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nTuesdays or Thursdays\r\n9:30am - 1:30pm\n\n## Travel details\n\nTalbot Street, Grangemouth, FK3 8HU.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReimbursement of travel expenses can be discussed with volunteers.\n\n## Taster details\n\nWe will offer an informal taster session, followed by a full run induction.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
