                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000Ls5vpAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000Ls5vpAAB/fundraising-collectors",
                    "publishStart": "2020-02-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Fundraising Collectors",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe Butterfly Trust are the lead providing agency of social support for Scotland's Cystic Fibrosis community.\nWe are looking for pro-active, enthusiastic volunteers to support our fundraising team at public collections, bag packs and to place/collect static collection cans in the community.\n\n## Description\n\nThe Butterfly Trust are the lead providing agency of social support for Scotland's Cystic Fibrosis community.\nWe are looking for pro-active, enthusiastic volunteers to support our fundraising team at public collections, bag packs and to place/collect static collection cans in the community.\n\nThe role involves:\nAttending collections in supermarkets, football grounds and street collections\nAttending bag packs in supermarkets\nPlacing & collecting collection cans in local businesses\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnthusiastic attitude\nGood communication skills\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining and support will be provided by Fundraising Manager\n\n## Travel details\n\nVoluntary work will take place throughout Edinburgh in local business and football grounds.",
