                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eGpoAAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eGpoAAE/befriender-for-young-person-affected-by-cystic-fibrosis",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-07",
                    "title": "Befriender for young person affected by Cystic Fibrosis",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nYou will be a breath of fresh air to someone with cystic fibrosis because they will have someone outwith their family life who will give them friendship, help, advice and understand what they are going through.  You would also be expected to attend team meetings and training sessions organised by the Trust. In return you will receive full training initially and regular re-training sessions in certain areas. It is anticipated that our Youth Befrienders will make a contribution for at least a year after your induction.\n\n## Description\n\nBefriending is a really fantastic and rewarding way to make a significant difference to the life of someone else. Apart from the personal satisfaction of helping someone, it is also an opportunity to enhance your own life and build new skills. A minimum commitment of 1 year is needed to ensure these goals can be met.\r\nAs a  Befriender you will offer friendship and help, introduce social activities to young people with Cystic Fibrosis. You would help introduce the Butterfly Trust and clarify the nature of the support offered as well as developing a supportive relationship with the young person and their family. You would facilitate discussion around difficulties or concerns being experienced by the young person and offer information about the support available from the Trust and other agencies.  We would need you to keep a suitable record of activities undertaken and send monthly recording forms to the Young Persons Support Organiser. You would also be expected to attend team meetings and training sessions organised by the Trust. In return you will receive full training initially and regular re-training sessions in certain areas. It is anticipated that our Youth Befrienders will make a contribution for at least a year after your induction.\n\n## Experience required\n\nCommunicate with young people, open and reliable.  Is able to listen to someone talking privately.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull induction and training in relation to young people, condition, etc. Ongoing training throughout the year.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThroughout Scotland. Own transport essential to travel to clients home and take young person out..\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n40p per mile. Any activities and refreshments. Paid by BACS. Must keep records and receipts",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eGpoAAE#role",
