        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nWstAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nWstAAE/citizens-advice-bureau-falkirk",
            "name": "Citizens Advice Bureau - Falkirk",
            "description": "Falkirk Citizens Advice Bureau provides a free, confidental and independent quality advocacy and advisory service to the inhabitants within the Falkirk Council area and strives to ensure every person in the Falkirk Council area has equal access to the Citizens Advice Bureau service.\r\n\r\nWe aim to:-\r\n\r\n- Ensure individuals do not suffer through lack of knowledge of their rights and responsibilities  or of the service available to them, or through an inability to express their needs effectively.\r\n\r\n- Ensure all citizens will have increased choices when it comes to financial products and services.\r\n\r\n- Increase people's understanding of the consequences of the choices they make with regards to their finances.\r\n\r\n- Maximise  the income of households that rely on benefits.\r\n\r\n- Reduce levels  of debt.",
            "website": "https://www.falkirkcab.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC006183"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000008AtRYAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000008AtRYAU/reception-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-01-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-09",
                    "title": "Reception Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSupport local people right here in Falkirk.\r\n\r\nYour Citizens Advice Bureau changes lives for the better by giving free, impartial and confidential advice to our community, empowering people to overcome challenges and secure their rights. But we can't do it without you.  \r\n\r\nAs a Reception Volunteer, you'll welcome clients into the Bureau, set them at ease, and work out what help they need. You'll be part of a friendly expert team, and receive first-class training and support.\r\n\r\nThis is a great opportunity to build experience of working in an office, working with the public, and learning about a wide range of issues.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience required! We'll give you all the training and support you need to become a key part of the team.\r\n\r\nStrong communication, teamwork, and organisational skills will be a big help to you.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe provide a comprehensive training programme, including details of frequent client enquiries, customer service skills, and data management. All Volunteers are supported by professional Session Supervision staff that empower you to excel.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMonday - Friday.  Usually between 10am - 3pm. \r\nSpecific days/times can be discussed with volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\n3 Meeks Road, Falkirk FK2 7EW\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n45p per mile (subject to change) and reimbursement of bus or train fares on production of a relevant ticket. \r\nOther reasonable expenses incurred in the course of volunteering will be considered and can be discussed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://e7.pngegg.com/pngimages/241/282/png-clipart-perth-citizens-advice-bureau-tain-citizens-advice-bureau-wiltshire-citizens-advice-angus-citizens-advice-bureau-others-miscellaneous-blue.png",
