                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000002W8ULYA0/boys-brigade-activity-helper-hallglen",
                    "publishStart": "2024-12-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-18",
                    "title": "Boys Brigade Activity Helper Hallglen",
                    "description": "## Description\n\n4th Falkirk Boys' Brigade are looking for enthusiastic volunteers to help lead games and sporting activities for their children and young people aged between 5 and 18 years old. \r\nThe group meets on Wednesday evenings during term-time, taking part in a wide range of activities including crafts, games, sports, cooking, life skills and community projects.\r\nFor more information you can visit https://boys-brigade.org.uk/who-we-are/\n\n## Experience required\n\nA passion and enthusiasm to support children and young people experience new activities and learn new skills. Training will be provided.\n\n## Training details\n\nSafeguarding Training, E-Learning and Virtual/In Person Training Course on a range of topics. You will also be supported by other volunteers to help you settle into the role.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWednesday evenings during term-time.\n\n## Travel details\n\nEttrick Dochart Community Hall, \r\nDochart Place, Hallglen, FK1 2QR.",
