                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-22",
                    "title": "Bookkeeper Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nForth Valley Migrant Support Network (FVMSN) is a community - based, grassroots organisation founded in October 2009 to provide information, advocacy, support and practical assistance to New Scots and people whose first language is not English and who live or work in Falkirk area.\r\n\r\nFVMSN are looking for a reliable, organised and motivated Bookkeeping Volunteer to support the financial and administrative work of the organisation. This is a valuable opportunity for someone who is currently studying accounting, bookkeeping, finance or business, a recent graduate, or someone who is between jobs and looking to develop practical experience and strengthen their CV.\r\n\r\nThe volunteer will work closely with the Treasurer and the wider team and will gain hands-on experience of maintaining financial records, processing transactions, supporting financial reporting, and organising financial documentation within a charitable organisation.\r\n\r\nThe volunteer will assist with a range of routine financial and administrative activities, including:\r\n- Recording financial transactions\r\n- Maintaining financial records\r\n- Bank reconciliation\r\n- Invoices and payments\r\n- Expenses and reimbursements\r\n- Month-end support: Assist the Treasurer with routine month-end checks and general financial administration.\r\n- Financial summaries and reporting\r\n- Financial filing\r\n- General administration\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for someone:\r\n- good with numbers and basic financial processes\r\n- great attention to detail and a methodical approach to tasks\r\n- familiar with spreadsheets such as Excel\r\n- reliable, discreet and a commitment to confidentiality\r\n- a calm, supportive approach and an ability to work well as part of a team\r\n- a willingness to learn and ask questions when something is unclear\r\n\r\nIt would be helpful if you have:\r\n- some coursework, training or experience in bookkeeping, accounting or finance administration\r\n- an interest in gaining practical experience in the charity or not-for-profit sector\r\n- previous experience using accounting software, although this is not essential\n\n## Training details\n\nThe volunteer will be provided with a full induction to help them feel comfortable and confident in their role. They will receive any training needed for their volunteering role and the activities they will be involved in.\r\nThe volunteer will also have regular one-to-one supervision and ongoing support.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n4-5 hours per week, minimum commitment of 3 months.\r\nThe office is open Monday - Friday during normal working hours.  Timing can be flexible for volunteers during this period.\n\n## Travel details\n\nNewhouse Business Park, Newhouse Road, Grangemouth, FK3 8LL.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nForth Valley Migrant Support Network will reimburse out of pocket/travel expenses.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://files.uk2sitebuilder.com/b5/0b/b50b3244-32d6-4771-b407-5489f41c994c.jpg",
