                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000003NmHxAAK",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000003NmHxAAK/office-and-admin-assistant-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-22",
                    "title": "Office and Admin Assistant Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nForth Valley Migrant Support Network (FVMSN) is a community based, grassroots organisation founded in October 2009 to provide information, advocacy, support and practical assistance to New Scots and people whose first language is not English and who live or work in Falkirk area.\r\n\r\nFVMSN are looking to recruit an admin assistant volunteer which is a supportive role in the office. As an admin assistant volunteer, you will help on reception and welcome visitors and service users to Forth Valley Migrant Support Network and perform a variety of administrative and clerical tasks to ensure the efficient and smooth day-to-day operation of the office. You will help provide support to the Committee, staff and other volunteers, assisting in daily office needs and managing our organisation’s general administrative activities.\r\n\r\nDepending on the needs of the office and the volunteer’s skills and interests, the admin assistant volunteer tasks that may include: \r\n• Providing general administrative support.\r\n• Greeting visitors and providing general support to service users. \r\n• Maintaining a physical and digital filing system. \r\n• Handling telephone calls. \r\n• Responding to emails other digital queries. \r\n• Updating paperwork.\r\n• Datasbase entry.\r\n\r\nThe position provides valuable experience for Office Administration students and anyone with a passion for working for a third sector organisation.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFVMSN are looking for someone with:\r\n• Good IT skills particularly word processing, spreadsheet and database packages\r\n• Good level of written and spoken English\r\n• Warm personality with good interpersonal and communication skills\r\n• Good organisational skills\r\n• Ability to work well under limited supervision and as part of a small team\r\n• Attention to detail and committed to meeting deadlines\r\n• Commitment to equal opportunities\r\n• Knowledge of Data Protection and understanding the necessity to maintain a strict confidentiality\r\n• Respect and understanding of different cultural behaviours, practices and religions\r\n• Ability to speak a second language is an advantage\n\n## Training details\n\nFull induction and training for the role, ongoing support and supervision.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n4-5 hours per week, minimum commitment of 3 months.\r\nThe office is open Monday - Friday during normal working hours.  Timing can be flexible for volunteers during this period.\n\n## Travel details\n\nNewhouse Business Park, Newhouse Road, Grangemouth, FK3 8LL.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nForth Valley Migrant Support Network will reimburse out of pocket/travel expenses.",
