                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzmPJYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HzmPJYAZ/community-language-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Community Language Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nForth Valley Migrant Support Network is a community organisation based in Falkirk that provide information, advocacy, language and practical assistance, and access to services to people whose first language is not English. They also run English conversation classes, women's breakfast group and offer volunteering opportunities.\r\n\r\nForth Valley Migrant Support Network are looking to recruit a bank of volunteer interpreters to enable them to support their service users to register and access service and activities, and to support with the delivery of activities where needed. They are looking for volunteers who speak fluently in both English and another language to be able to identify individual’s language needs and explain complex terms.\r\n\r\nThe main purpose of the community language volunteer role is to assist the service to communicate more effectively with individuals from ethnic minority groups, to help them access information and services equitably and confidently, and help people overcome barriers to participating fully within the local community.\r\n\r\nThis is an ad-hoc volunteering role that works flexibly around your own commitments.  Volunteers should have access to a smart phone and reliable internet to be able to provide virtual support.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFluency in English and another language.\r\nAbility to adapt language based on the level of the service user.\r\nFriendly personality. \r\nStrong interpersonal and communication skills. \r\nHave an understanding of confidentiality, safeguarding and data protection. \r\nHave cultural awareness and a commitment to professional boundaries. \r\nBasic knowledge of Microsoft packages, Zoom, WhatsApp and other virtual communication tools.\r\nCommitment to equal opportunities.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull induction and necessary training relevant to the volunteer role and the activities will be given. \r\nRegular one-to-one supervision and group supervision sessions.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible - 3 months commitment.\n\n## Travel details\n\nHybrid: Office based (Grangemouth) and remote. \r\nAccessible via public transport. Free parking available.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReimbursement of bus fares; mileage rate £0.55 per mile",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://files.uk2sitebuilder.com/b5/0b/b50b3244-32d6-4771-b407-5489f41c994c.jpg",
