        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nWu7AAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nWu7AAE/ben-view-resource-centre",
            "name": "Ben View Resource Centre",
            "description": "To promote the wellbeing of the people of West Dunbartonshire by:\r\n• Providing a lunch club in a safe, social and caring environment.\r\n• Providing a bathing service for adults who need assistance.\r\n• Providing a meeting place and office environment for Community Groups.",
            "website": "http://benviewcentre.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC024093"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityFacilities",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Facilities"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009oaZNYAY",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009oaZNYAY/youth-programme",
                    "publishStart": "2025-05-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-14",
                    "title": "Youth Programme",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNo matter how good our services are, we can't properly support our users/community well if we don't have good leadership in the team. If this sounds like you?... we would love you to consider volunteering with us for a few hours per week.\r\n \r\nOur Vision\r\nWe are committed to creating an environment where young people:\r\nFeel safe, included, and respected\r\nHave a sense of ownership over their space and experiences\r\nCan build positive, lasting relationships with peers and mentors\r\n\r\nWe offer opportunities based on the interests of the young people themselves. Activities may include:\r\n\r\nActivity-based games and team-building tasks\r\nGames consoles, laptops, and internet access\r\nArts & crafts and baking\r\nChill-out zones for downtime\r\nOutdoor play and creative sessions\r\n\r\nOur Group Sessions\r\nOur youth programs are age-specific, serving children and young people aged 5 to 16. Groups are carefully split by age to ensure all activities and mentoring are appropriate, engaging, and effective for each stage of development.\r\n\r\nMain Duties: \r\nTo ensure the room are prepared and set up in line with health and safety requirements\r\n\r\nTo mentor / supervise your allocated group session\r\n\r\nTo bring new ideas and activities appropriate to the age level of the group you are assigned to.\r\n\r\nTo support and assist in ensuring we have a wide range of activities/ games to keep the group stimulated while encouraging them to take ownership of activities.\r\n\r\nTo ensure recording of weekly attendance and any other administration duties required.\r\n\r\nTo follow protocols for ensuring the service is provided to a high standard.\r\n\r\nTo ensure risk assessments are in place for all activities.\r\n\r\nTo plan activities and risk assessment for any outings or trips out with Ben View.\r\n\r\nTo report to Youth Club leader and issues or concerns in line with the policies covered at induction.\r\n\r\nTo attend support sessions, induction sessions and periodic training events are required.\r\n \r\nSo, whether you are looking to use your time well, update your skills or have the chance to do something a bit new, we would love to hear from you. In return, we can offer you a warm welcome and all of the support and help you could need.\r\n \r\nWe are seeing a rise in demand for our services, every day. Having your help will allow us to be there for the people who need us. Any time you can give will make a real difference. \n\n## Experience required\n\nAn ability to get on with children from the age of 5 to 16\n\n## Travel details\n\nBen View Resource Centre, Strathleven Place Dumbarton G82 1BA",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009oaZNYAY#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Youth Programme",
                        "description": "An ability to get on with children from the age of 5 to 16",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009oaZNYAY/youth-programme?#modal_register_a0gQD000009oaZNYAY",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
