                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009oZbhYAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009oZbhYAE/volunteer-caretaker",
                    "publishStart": "2025-05-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-14",
                    "title": "Volunteer Caretaker",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNo matter how good our services are, we can't properly support our users/community well if we don't have skilled people in the team. If this sounds like you?... we would love you to consider volunteering with us for a few hours per week.\r\n \r\nBen View Resource Centre is a registered Charity which aims to promote the wellbeing of the people of Dumbarton and the surrounding area.\r\n \r\nVolunteer Caretaker – Help Us Welcome the Community\r\n\r\nDo you enjoy hands-on work and meeting new people? Our busy community centre hosts a wide range of groups and activities, mainly during evenings and weekends, and we’re looking for a friendly, practical person to help keep things running smoothly.\r\n\r\nThis is a great opportunity to put your DIY and caretaker skills to good use while playing an essential role in creating a welcoming space for all who visit.\r\n\r\nWhat You’ll Be Doing\r\nAs a volunteer caretaker, you’ll be the first point of contact for many of our visitors. Your role will include:\r\n\r\nWelcoming hall users and ensuring they feel supported and informed\r\nSetting up rooms for different bookings\r\nEnsuring the groups have left the rooms tidy after use \r\nCarrying out minor repairs and maintenance\r\nReporting any issues or faults identified throughout the centre\r\nHelping keep the centre safe, and well-organised\r\n\r\nWho We’re Looking For\r\nSomeone with a friendly, approachable manner\r\nBasic DIY or practical skills\r\nComfortable working mostly during evenings and weekends\r\nReliable and able to take initiative\r\n\r\nWhat You’ll Get\r\nA supportive team and full guidance in your role\r\nThe chance to meet new people and be part of a vibrant centre\r\nAn opportunity to give back and make a visible difference in your community\r\n\r\n\r\nWe are seeing a rise in demand for our services, every day. Having your help will allow us to be there for the people who need us. Any time you can give will make a real difference. \n\n## Experience required\n\nA knowledge of DIY and able to work with the general public\n\n## Travel details\n\nBen View Resource Centre, Strathleven Place Dumbarton G82 1BA",
