                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009oTg0YAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009oTg0YAE/befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2025-05-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-14",
                    "title": "Befriender",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nPurpose of the Role:\r\nTo provide companionship and social support to individuals aged 65 and over who have full mental capacity but are experiencing loneliness or social isolation. This service aims to help older adults reconnect with their local community, support emotional wellbeing, and reduce feelings of isolation.\r\nKey Responsibilities:\r\nVisit clients in their own homes for friendly conversation and company.\r\nAccompany clients on short local outings, such as to a café, park, or cinema, supporting social interaction and engagement with the community.\r\nBuild a positive, supportive relationship while respecting the client’s independence and decision-making.\r\nOffer a listening ear and empathetic conversation to support the client’s emotional and mental wellbeing.\r\nMaintain clear boundaries and confidentiality at all times.\r\nReport any concerns to the service coordinator and follow safeguarding and health and safety procedures.\r\nParticipate in basic training and maintain regular contact with the volunteer manager.\r\n\r\nWho the Service is For:\r\nIndividuals aged 65 or over\r\nLiving independently in the local community\r\nExperiencing loneliness or social isolation\r\nHave full mental capacity and are able to make informed decisions\r\n\r\nSkills & Qualities Needed:\r\n•\tFriendly, respectful, and compassionate\r\n•\tA good communicator and listener\r\n•\tDependable and consistent in attendance\r\n•\tNon-judgmental and able to build rapport with older individuals\r\n•\tComfortable working independently with appropriate support\r\n \r\nSo, whether you are looking to use your time well, update your skills or have the chance to do something a bit new, we would love to hear from you. In return, we can offer you a warm welcome and all of the support and help you could need.\r\n\r\nWe are seeing a rise in demand for our services, everyday. Having your help will allow us to be there for the people who need us. Any time you can give will make a real difference.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA friendly attitude and the ability to interact with older people\n\n## Travel details\n\nOut and about locally",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009oTg0YAE#role",
