                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/LunchClubs",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Lunch Clubs"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eOObAAM",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eOObAAM/general-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "General Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe HOPE Project provides a wide range of services specifically for over 50`s within the local community and throughout North Ayrshire. Our aim is to help older people remain independent within their own homes for longer and help them enjoy life in the company of others.\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for general volunteers to help out at the HOPE Project Office based in Stevenston to:\r\n• Assist at various Activities and Events within the centre\r\n• Assist with Activities, Health and Fitness Classes and Interest Classes\r\n• Help older people who have mobility issues to attend social outings\r\n If you like working alongside older individuals and would enjoy supporting them to attend various Events or Classes then this is the right opportunity for you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nLooking for people who have an interest in working alongside Older Individuals and would like to support them to take part in activities within their local area.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe induction session will be followed up by training sessions, disclosure check and ongoing training and support sessions thereafter.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOpportunity takes place at the HOPE Project Office in Stevenson, North Ayrshire. This is situated on a main bus route.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses will be paid on request - proof of bus/train tickets. Mileage will be paid for all travel connected with the project. (Training and Volunteer Work)\n\n## Taster details\n\nAn induction session will be provided to volunteers.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eOObAAM#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "General Volunteer",
                        "description": "Looking for people who have an interest in working alongside Older Individuals and would like to support them to take part in activities within their local area.",
