                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eOOfAAM",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eOOfAAM/telephone-befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Telephone Befriender",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe HOPE Project provides a wide range of services specifically for over 50`s within the local community and throughout North Ayrshire. Our aim is to help older people remain independent within their own homes for longer and help them enjoy life in the company of others.\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for Telephone Befrienders to help out at the HOPE Project Office in Stevenston. This role requires the following:\r\n\r\n• Someone who likes a good chat and is able to encourage and stimulate an older person to express themselves and feel comfortable engaging in conversation\r\n• Inspiring enough confidence further down the line to allow for attendance at a social activity\r\n\r\nIf you like the idea of working alongside older individuals and would enjoy this telephone service then this is the right opportunity for you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nLooking for people who have an interest in working with Older Individuals and would like to help older people remain independent within their own homes for longer and help to support them when necessary.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe induction session will be followed up by training sessions, disclosure check and on-going training and support sessions thereafter.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOpportunity takes place at the HOPE Project Office in Stevenston, North Ayrshire. This is situated on a main bus route.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses will be paid on request - proof of bus/train tickets. Mileage will be paid for all travel connected with the project. (Training and Volunteer Work)\n\n## Taster details\n\nAn induction session will be provided to volunteers.",
