                    "title": "Telephone Befriender",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe HOPE Project provides a wide range of services specifically for over 50`s within the local community and throughout North Ayrshire. Our aim is to help older people remain independent within their own homes for longer and help them enjoy life in the company of others.\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking forTelephone Volunteer Befrienders to help support Older People throughout North Ayrshire  This role requires the following:\r\n• Someone to provide companionship and support by telephoning the individual \r\nIf you like the idea of working alongside older individuals to prevent isolation then this is the right opportunity for you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nLooking for people who have an interest in working with Older Individuals and would like to help older people remain independent within their own homes for longer and help to support them when necessary.\n\n## Training details\n\nAn induction session will be provided to volunteers. The induction session will be followed up by training sessions, disclosure check and on-going training and support sessions thereafter.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOpportunity takes place at a time and suit both Volunteers and recipient.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses will be paid on request - proof of bus/train tickets. Mileage will be paid for all travel connected with the project. (Training and Volunteer Work)",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000EXm0zYAD#role",
