                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eGpWAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eGpWAAU/admin-support-worker",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Admin Support Worker",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nwe would like to recruit a  caring person who would be interested in becoming an Admin Support Worker.\r\n\r\nIt will only take 1 to 2 weeks before the volunteer will take up the placement.\n\n## Description\n\nWe aim to provide  services and Information and Advice to Older People . The Admin Support Volunteer would help to maintain records. The Special person would be responsible to the HOPE Co-ordinator.\n\n## Experience required\n\nIdeally the special person will have some previous admin experience. Will be happy to become part of a busy team and will have a caring nature.\n\n## Training details\n\nAn induction session will be followed with on the job training and any external training opportunities available. Regular individual and group support is planned.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nBetween 2 and 8 hours per week.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe volunteer post will be based at the C.L.A.S.P. Project Office in Stevenston.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel Expenses can be paid on request.",
