                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7LfxAAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7LfxAAF/boutique-shop-volunteer-save-the-children-stockbridge",
                    "publishStart": "2022-11-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Boutique Shop Volunteer - Save the Children Stockbridge",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHelp us improve the lives of children all over the world - we welcome your donation of time, creativity and kindness via fabulous retailing. \n\nActivities include customer service, creative merchandising, preparing items for sale and working as part of a diverse volunteer team. It's great fun!\n\n## Description\n\nOur Stockbridge Save the Children Shop has been a much loved part of the local community for years and continues to be hugely popular, thanks to the kindness,  generosity and creativity of the volunteer team.\n\nAll you need is some enthusiasm and a desire to make a difference. The role is diverse, taking place on the shop floor and behind the scenes. Volunteer activities include customer service, creative merchandising, preparing items for sale and working as part of a team.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience is required as all training will be provided on an ongoing basis.\n\nActivities include customer service, cash handling, creative merchandising, preparing items for sale and working as part of a large and diverse volunteer team.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe provide initial induction training and then ongoing training as required by the individual volunteer 0 usually in a buddy system.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMary's Living and Giving Shop for Save the Children\n34a Raeburn Place\nStockbridge, Edinburgh\nEH4 1HN\n\nLocated in the centre of Stockbridge, serviced by many bus routes including the 24,36,42\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe reimburse travel expenses on acceptance of receipt - either daily or weekly/monthly - whatever suits the volunteer best.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7LfxAAF#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Boutique Shop Volunteer - Save the Children Stockbridge",
                        "description": "No previous experience is required as all training will be provided on an ongoing basis.\n\nActivities include customer service, cash handling, creative merchandising, preparing items for sale and working as part of a large and diverse volunteer team.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7LfxAAF/boutique-shop-volunteer-save-the-children-stockbridge?#modal_register_a0g0800000V7LfxAAF",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16",
                        "service": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Service/WheelchairAccessDisabledAccessToilet",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Wheelchair Access/Disabled Access Toilet"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Service/TasterAvailable",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Taster Available"
                            },
                            {
