                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7LfvAAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7LfvAAF/shop-volunteer-save-the-children-morningside",
                    "publishStart": "2022-11-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Shop Volunteer - Save the Children Morningside",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHelp us improve the lives of children all over the world - wewelcome your donation of time, creativity and kindness via fabulous retailing. \n\nActivities include customer service, creative merchandising, preparing items for sale and working as part of a diverse volunteer team. It's great fun!\n\n## Description\n\nOur Morningside Save the Children Shop has been a much loved part of the local community for years and continues to be hugely popular, thanks to the kindness and generosity of the volunteer led team.\n\nAll you need is some enthusiasm and a desire to make a difference. The role is diverse, taking place on the shop floor and behind the scenes. Volunteer activities include customer service, creative merchandising, preparing items for sale and working as part of a team.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience is required as all training will be provided on an ongoing basis.\n\nActivities include customer service, cash handling, creative merchandising, preparing items for sale and working as part of a diverse volunteer team.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe provide initial induction training and then operate a buddying system thereafter - dependant on the needs of the individual volunteer.\n\n## Travel details\n\nSave the Children Shop\n390 Morningside Road\nEdinburgh\nEH10 5HX\n\nSituated opposite the Clock in Morningside and accessible by several bus routes including 5,11,16,36\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses can be reclaimed on acceptance of receipt - on the day or combined weekly/monthly - whatever suits the volunteer best.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
