                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7LfwAAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7LfwAAF/shop-volunteer-save-the-children-marchmont",
                    "publishStart": "2022-11-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Shop Volunteer - Save the Children Marchmont",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHelp us improve the lives of children all over the world - wewelcome your donation of time, creativity and kindness via fabulous retailing. \n\nActivities include customer service, creative merchandising, preparing items for sale and working as part of a diverse volunteer team. It's great fun!\n\n## Description\n\nOur Marchmont Save the Children Shop has been a much loved part of the local community for years and continues to be hugely popular with customers and supporters, thanks to the kindness and generosity of the volunteer team.\n\nAll you need is some enthusiasm and a desire to make a difference. The role is diverse, taking place on the shop floor and behind the scenes. Volunteer activities include customer service, creative merchandising, preparing items for sale and working as part of a team.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience is required as all training will be provided on an ongoing basis.\n\nActivities include customer service, cash handling, creative merchandising, preparing items for sale and working as part of a large and diverse volunteer team.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe provide initial induction training and then operate a buddy system where volunteers receive ongoing training  - dependant on their interests and skillsets.\n\n## Travel details\n\nSave the Children Shop\n144 Marchmont Road\nEdinburgh\nEH9 1AQ\n\nJA few blocks up from the Meadows - bus routes include 5 and 41\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses can be reimbursed on acceptance of receipt - either on the day or weekly/monthly, whatever suits the volunteer best.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
