            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000083tbGYAQ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000083tbGYAQ/community-cafe-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Community Cafe Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAberdeen North Parish Church hosts a vibrant community café called The Coffee Pot, offering a warm and welcoming space for visitors to enjoy a morning cuppa and for volunteers to make a positive contribution.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for enthusiastic helpers to assist in the café, which serves as a popular gathering spot. Volunteers will work as part of a friendly team, taking on tasks such as setting tables, serving coffee, clearing up, and keeping the space tidy.\r\n\r\nThe café is open to all, and you don’t need to be a church member to volunteer – everyone is welcome!\r\n\r\nVolunteers are greatly valued, and we offer full support, mentoring, and opportunities to learn new skills. This is a fantastic chance to give back and make a meaningful difference in the community.\r\n\r\nIf you feel you can spare a few hours to help in any way please contact us at Email: jthomas@churchofscotland.org.uk or telephone: 07526465105\n\n## Description\n\nAberdeen North Parish Church hosts a vibrant community café called The Coffee Pot, offering a warm and welcoming space for visitors to enjoy a morning cuppa and for volunteers to make a positive contribution.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for enthusiastic helpers to assist in the café, which serves as a popular gathering spot on a Friday between 11.00am-2.00pm (people can volunteer the whole or part of the time). Volunteers will work as part of a friendly team, taking on tasks such as setting tables, serving coffee, clearing up, and keeping the space tidy.\r\n\r\nThe café is open to all, and you don’t need to be a church member to volunteer – everyone is welcome!\r\n\r\nVolunteers are greatly valued, and we offer full support, mentoring, and opportunities to learn new skills. This is a fantastic chance to give back and make a meaningful difference in the community.\r\n\r\nIf you feel you can spare a few hours to help in any way please contact us at Email: jthomas@churchofscotland.org.uk or telephone: 07526465105\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly and approachable. A good listener and willing learner.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. The induction will be informal and completed at the volunteer’s pace. There is support available from the team on duty each day and there is also an overall café team leader, who is available should any specific issues arise.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe cafe is open on a Friday between 11.00am-2.00pm (people can volunteer the whole or part of the time). All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe cafe is located at:\r\nGreenfern Road, \r\nMastrick, \r\nAberdeen \r\nAB16 6TR",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FTZ1hMCZYN0XLk9Rj7bwy0TNJKa73%2Fq3komvuqyV9F4XKg-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=24d6e2eb-302f-4656-8c68-7ed0bec235e8",
