                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JBJMAYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JBJMAYA5/grampian-disability-sport-fundraising-trustee-voluntary",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-26",
                    "title": "Grampian Disability Sport Fundraising Trustee (Voluntary)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nJoin Grampian Disability Sport (GDS) as a Fundraising Trustee and be part of our aim to lead and support the development of sport and physical development opportunities for people with disabilities across Grampian.\r\n\r\nGrampian Disability Sport (GDS) is a voluntary organisation whose main aim is to lead and support the development of sport and physical development opportunities for people with disabilities across Grampian.\r\n\r\nGrampian Disability Sport supports participation, inclusion and training in sport for those with disabilities within the Aberdeen City, Aberdeenshire and Moray areas. We are made up predominantly of volunteers who have a passion for disability inclusion. We work in partnership with key local agencies, clubs, schools, and governing bodies to increase participation and improve access to inclusive sport opportunities across the region, along with providing our own sessions for participation and key events throughout the year.\r\n\r\nGDS is a member branch of Scottish Disability Sport (SDS). The national governing body for disability sport in Scotland, operating in line with SDS and is committed to maintaining appropriate governance standards and minimum operating requirements (MOR).\r\n\r\nOur mission is to inspire, encourage and support people of all ages and abilities with a physical, sensory, or learning disability to become more active.\r\n\r\nOur vision is that everyone in Grampian with a disability has the opportunity to participate in sport and physical activity.\r\n\r\nOur themes are;\r\n- Strong partnerships.\r\n- Participation opportunities for all.\r\n- Building capacity and advocating for our community.\r\n\r\nOur values are;\r\n- Inclusive\r\n- Collaborative\r\n- Inspiring\r\n- Determined\r\n\r\nWe also strongly encourage connection with our disabled participants and ask for support with attendance at a few events throughout the year to generally support the smooth running of the day and create visible representation and connections for the charity.\r\n\r\nVolunteers are offered an induction which will include familiarisation with the Charity systems, access to policies and procedures and familiarisation with the relevant platforms.\r\n\r\nVolunteers will be supported to find, or offered, Child and Wellbeing in Sport training which is renewed every three years.\r\n\r\nThe volunteer will be supported by the board members of the Charity.\r\n\r\nOther training will be offered throughout the year to support the charity values and mission.\r\n\r\nRoles and Responsibilities:\r\n\r\nSupport and help the GDS committee, Branch Coordinator or other employees to,\r\n- Development of a sustainable funding strategy \r\n- Identify potential funding streams \r\n- Provide advice and oversight on fundraising priorities.\r\n- Identify relevant grant opportunities\r\n- Support the preparation and review of funding applications\r\n- Ensure applications align with organisational strategy\r\n- Assist in identifying corporate sponsors and community partners\r\n- Support the development of relationships with organisations\r\n- Support reporting requirements to funders.\r\n- Monitor funding performance etc\r\n- Fulfil the duties of a charity trustee\r\n- Attend and contribute to meetings \r\n- Join the GDS PVG scheme\r\n- Complete Child Wellbeing and Protection in Sport training every three years.\r\n- Attend GDS events, around 4 per year.\r\n\r\nAn opportunity to make a real difference, with all help greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor more information  please contact Linda Gill, Interim Chair/Safeguarding at email: chair@grampiandisabilitysport.org.uk or telephone: 07807 937 989\n\n## Training details\n\nTrustees of Grampian Disability Sport (GDS) receive training on the systems used by the committee, they will be given, or be directed to, Child Wellbeing and Protection in Sport training every three years. Training opportunities for fundraising would be available through charity partner ship links and our governing body Scottish Disability Sport. Disability Sport specific training is also available every year\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nTime commitments are approximately 1 hour per week with some additionality at occasional points through the year.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe role is predominately virtual with occasional in person meetings. Event support can also include in person attendance within the region.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses are paid as per our policies and procedures.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
