                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Grampian Disability Sport Fundraising Trustee (Voluntary)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nRoles and Responsibilities\r\nSupport and help the GDS committee, Branch Coordinator or others to,\r\n\r\nDevelopment of a sustainable funding strategy \r\nIdentify potential funding streams \r\nProvide advice and oversight on fundraising priorities.\r\nIdentify relevant grant opportunities\r\nSupport the preparation and review of funding applications\r\nEnsure applications align with organisational strategy\r\nAssist in identifying corporate sponsors and community partners\r\nSupport the development of relationships with organisations\r\nSupport reporting requirements to funders.\r\nMonitor funding performance etc\r\nFulfil the duties of a charity trustee\r\nAttend and contribute to meetings \r\nJoin the GDS PVG scheme\r\nComplete Child Wellbeing and Protection in Sport training every three years.\r\nAttend GDS events, around 4 per year.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEssential\r\nInterest in supporting opportunities for disabled people in sport and physical activity.\r\nGood organisation and record keeping and the ability to work collaboratively as part of a trustee board.\r\nCommitment to good governance and the values of the organisation.\r\n\r\nDesirable\r\nExperience writing or reviewing grant applications.\r\nUnderstanding of fundraising, grant funding or sponsorship (professional or voluntary).\r\nKnowledge of the charitable or sports sector.\r\nExperience with trusts, foundations or corporate fundraising.\r\nLocal connections within the Grampian business or community sector.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training will be provided.\r\nIn addition access to Child Wellbeing and Protection in Sport Training along with disability sport specific training each year. Fundraising training or support is available via our governing body or charity volunteer partnerships.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nTime commitments are approximately 1 hour per week with some additionality at occasional points through the year.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMostly virtual with occasional in person meetings around the Grampian area.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses are paid as per our policies and procedures.",
