                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IEDMPYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IEDMPYA5/grampian-disability-sport-general-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Grampian Disability Sport- General Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGrampian Disability Sport(GDS) is a charitable, voluntary organisation whose main aim is to lead and support the development of sport and physical development opportunities for people with disabilities across Grampian. GDS works in partnership with key local agencies, clubs, schools, and governing bodies to increase participation and improve access to inclusive sport opportunities across the region. GDS Is a member branch of Scottish Disability Sport, the national governing body for disability sport in Scotland.\r\nGrampian Disability Sport is an equal opportunities employer\r\nCharity Number: SCIO SC030188\r\n\r\nRoles and Responsibilities\r\n- Assisting delivering activities\r\n-Variable time commitment/flexible\r\n- Communicate effectively with children and vulnerable adults\r\n- Basic knowledge of the sport (not essential as you will be guided by others or receive training)\r\n- Under the direction of the coach, or activity leader, work with a small group of athletes to help them achieve the aims of the session, whether it be practising skills or playing a game\r\n- Take on a supervisory role during the session \r\n- Take a register of those attending at the beginning of the session, along with details of any particular needs they have\r\n- Ensure that you are well briefed about any special needs of the participants involved i.e. significant medical conditions, physical, learning or sensory disabilities\r\n- Help setting up and pack away equipment at the beginning/end of the session\r\n- In liaison with the Coach/Sports Leader ensure that the playing area is safe to use\r\n- Be aware of the clubs Health & Safety policy (i.e. procedures for recording accidents) and Emergency Procedures and take own responsibility for Health & Safety\r\n- Help with the smooth running of an event on the day, including offering directions and guidance.\r\n- GDS PVG required\r\n- Child and Wellbeing in Sport Training every 3 years\n\n## Experience required\n\nResponsible\r\nReliable\r\nFriendly\r\nSupportive\r\nMinimal sporting experience (if more is required training will be available)\r\nHave time to commit to events etc throughout the year (approximately 4 per year)\r\nBe able to follow instructions and also take own initiative\r\nGood communication skills\r\nWilling to join the GDS PVG scheme\r\nCommit to Child and Wellbeing in Sport Training every three years\n\n## Training details\n\nChild, Wellbeing and Protection in Sport Training\r\nPossibility to attend a once per year free disability and inclusion specific training each year.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nGDS runs approximately 4 to 6 events a year ranging from swimming galas to bowls, boccia and multi sports events. These run over one day each and vary in the time commitments required.\r\nThese are in person events and are held across Grampian, usually within Aberdeen and Aberdeenshire.\r\nThe hope is extend into Moray more with availability of volunteers in the region.\r\nOpportunities for sport specific, regular, short sessions, may be available to interested volunteers willing to be trained for this purpose.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTravel to event venues\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses paid.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
