                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IEBvhYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IEBvhYAH/grampian-disability-sport-trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Grampian Disability Sport Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGrampian Disability Sport(GDS) is a charitable, voluntary organisation who’s main aim is to lead and support the development of sport and physical development opportunities for people with disabilities across Grampian. GDS works in partnership with key local agencies, clubs, schools, and governing bodies to increase participation and improve access to inclusive sport opportunities across the region. GDS Is a member branch of Scottish Disability Sport, the national governing body for disability sport in Scotland.\r\nGrampian Disability Sport is an equal opportunity employer.\r\nCharity Number: SCIO SC030188\r\n\r\nTrustee Roles and Responsibilities\r\n- Support governance and compliance with GDS and SDS requirements\r\n- Familiarise yourself with the GDS constitution, governance procedures, and organisational policies.\r\n- Contribute to policy decisions during review\r\n- Contribute to sub groups, including, fundraising and securing funding,  opportunities, event planning and delivery, and communication and engagement with clubs, members, and partners\r\n- Support the Chair and other trustees in the overall direction of GDS\r\n- Attendance at regular trustee meetings, contributing to decision making (approx. 10 per year)\r\n- Attend a minimum of 70 % of committee meetings.\r\n- Attendance at events, competitions and additional time supporting the strategic priorities as required. (An estimated 4 events per year)\r\n- Support the GDS Constitution and the charities compliance to that, including support for powers to co-opted office bearer roles, if required for the continued compliance with the Constitution.\r\n- Agree and Abide by the GDS Policies and Procedures (available on the GDS website at GDS Website-Documents)\r\n- Maintain Child Wellbeing and Protection in Sport training every three years\r\n- Join the GDS PVG scheme\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnthusiastic and commited to disability Sport\r\n\r\nWilling to make regular and reliable time comittment.\r\n\r\nAble to contribute to discussion and decision making.\r\n\r\nA team player with a positive proactive approach.\r\n\r\nPassionate about inclusion and disability sport.\r\n\r\nExperienced or interested in disability sport or community sport.\n\n## Training details\n\nChild, Wellbeing and Protection in Sport training\r\nOnce per year opportunity for disability and inclusion in sport related training\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMonthly meetings (usually evenings)- mostly virtual but some in person (approx. 10 per year)\r\nApproximately one to two hours per month for other charity based support\r\nOccasional in person charity support for events etc- approximately 4 per year\n\n## Travel details\n\nMostly virtual/at home commitment\r\nOccasional travel within Grampian\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses available",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
