                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IEAZpYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IEAZpYAP/grampian-disability-sport-branch-secretary",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Grampian Disability Sport- Branch Secretary",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGrampian Disability Sport(GDS) is a charitable, voluntary organisation who’s main aim is to lead and support the development of sport and physical development opportunities for people with disabilities across Grampian. GDS works in partnership with key local agencies, clubs, schools, and governing bodies to increase participation and improve access to inclusive sport opportunities across the region. GDS Is a member branch of Scottish Disability Sport. The national governing body for disability sport in Scotland.\r\n\r\nKey Secretary Roles and Responsibilities\r\n- Attend all management committee meetings\r\n- Gather and populate committee reports in good time for meetings\r\n- Take minutes of meeting, complete and circulate before the next meeting, ensuring actions are recorded, dated and named.\r\n- Create Doodle Polls for meetings and send invites, including TEAMs invites and room booking if required.\r\n- Liaise with the chairperson on the agenda for each meeting and approve the minutes before they are circulated.\r\n- In conjunction with the Chairperson, prepare and present the annual report.\r\n- Be completely familiar with, and abide by, Grampian Disability Sport policies and procedures, constitution, and committee procedures including compliance with charity regulations, governance standards and charity law.\r\n- Amend policies and procedure documentation when there is a change of personnel, phone number or email.\r\n- Support administration for events such as Eventbrite and associated excel, or google sheet documents, including registration documentation.\r\n- Support the review of documentation, policies and procedures and admin surrounding it.\r\n- Support the monitoring of, and responding to, emails and correspondence.\r\n- Support the administration of the GDS website.\r\n- Support the monitoring of the GDS email.\r\n- Attend some events in a voluntary capacity to support. (approximately 4 per year)\r\n- Join the GDS PVG scheme.\r\n- Complete Child Wellbeing and Protection Training every 3 years.\r\n\r\nGrampian Disability Sport is an equal opportunity employer\r\nCharity Number: SCIO SC030188\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnthusiastic and committed to disability sport, inclusion and diversity.\r\n\r\nOrganised and methodical. \r\n\r\nAble to work as a team and be committed to our charity values and our policies and procedures.\r\n\r\nAble to keep accurate records, support preparation of reports, charity returns and branch adminiatration. \r\n\r\nRelevant skills to organise a meeting well.\r\n\r\nWilling to make regular and reliable time commitment and attend all committee meetings, supporting charity administration and events at other times.\r\n\r\nGood listening, oral and literacy skills\r\n\r\nExperience in using general IT platforms such as Word, Google Docs, basic Excel etc\r\n\r\nAble to contribute to discussion and decision making.\r\n\r\nA team player with a positive proactive approach.\n\n## Training details\n\nChild and Wellbeing in Sport Training will be available\r\nOnce per year availability to disability sport and inclusion type training\r\nCharity support with familiarisation of systems, policies and procedures.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nOne meeting per month (approximately 10 per year)- mostly virtual but some in person\r\nWeekly availability to complete admin tasks (at home) for the charity- approximately one to two hours.\r\nOccasional attendance at events to support in person- approximately 4 per year\n\n## Travel details\n\nPredominately virtual/at home working.\r\nOccasional in person working within Grampian- reasonable travel expenses available\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses available.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
