                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008SUszYAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008SUszYAG/allotment-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-02-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Allotment Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for a volunteer to get involved at our community allotment on Lauriston Farm!\n\n## Description\n\nOutline of typical tasks: \nPlanting and watering crops.\nAssisting with community events and collaborating with community members who want to get involved.\nCare of vegetables including netting, use of fleece for protection.\nHelp with disposing of slugs without use of chemicals.\nTying in peas and beans.\nHarvesting as needed for project users.\nUnderstanding when to water plants depending on the weather.\nLabelling of plants.\n\n## Training details\n\nA member of our staff will give you an induction at the allotment and will be available each week to check in and provide any support you need.\n\n## Travel details\n\nLauriston Farm, Lauriston Farm Road, Edinburgh EH4 5EX \nThe main entrance is at the back of the Toby Carvery car park.\nLothian Buses 16, 27, 29, 37 & 47 all stop within 5 minutes of the farm.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe will provide you with a monthly expenses form. Expenses will be paid out on the last working day of each month.",
