                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Fgl8LYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Fgl8LYAR/administration-awareness-raising-volunteer-racialised-communities-resources",
                    "publishStart": "2025-12-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Administration & Awareness Raising Volunteer (Racialised Communities Resources)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAdministrative support, updating materials, drafting communications and maintaining records. Essential skills include strong organisation, written communication, IT proficiency and confidentiality. Desirable qualities include experience in community engagement or an understanding of racial equality issues.\n\n## Description\n\nProject Esperanza seeks a skilled, organised volunteer to support administrative tasks and promote key resources for racialised communities, including the Charter, Culture Connections Kit, Fostering Equality Toolkit, and Socio-cultural Abuse Toolkit. The role involves organising, maintaining materials, supporting awareness activities, coordinating distribution and ensuring effective communication with partners and stakeholders.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction, guidance and ongoing support from Project Esperanza staff; opportunities to gain experience in community advocacy, equality work  and resource dissemination; development of administrative and professional communication skills and a supportive, inclusive working environment.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThron House, 5 Rose Street.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel Expenses.",
