                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BMNkPYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BMNkPYAX/english-language-class-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-08-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "English Language Class Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSupport the main instructor with class setup and materials distribution. Provide encouragement and one-to-one or small group support to learners during activities. Help learners with pronunciation, vocabulary, reading and writing tasks. Assist with managing the classroom.\n\n## Description\n\nTo assist the English Language instructor in delivering engaging, inclusive and supportive ESOL (English for Speakers of Other Languages) sessions for learners from migrant, refugee and minority ethnic backgrounds. The support volunteer will help create a welcoming environment and provide one-to-one or small group assistance to learners to build their confidence in spoken and written English. Must also be willing to take the class if the instructor is not available.\n\n## Travel details\n\nProject Esperanza, 12c McMillan Square, McMillan Hub, Edinburgh EH4 4AB\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nFill out an expenses claim form.",
