                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BMNSfYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BMNSfYAP/peer-mentors-and-befrienders",
                    "publishStart": "2025-08-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Peer Mentors and Befrienders",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nPromoting mental health through peer mentoring and befriending as part of our well-being service. Supporting individuals with long-term mental health, disability, frailty and physical health conditions such as diabetes, hypertension, cancer, hepatitis, HIV, substance dependency and other challenges.\n\n## Description\n\nProject Esperanza is looking for peer and mentor befrienders to  help build and maintain community relationships by promoting the mental health and social well-being  of chronically ill and socially isolated people. The aim of the service is to improve the physical, mental and social well being of people and help improve their outcomes by helping them to navigate health and social care systems and make informed choices, to gain an improved sense of belonging in the community.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining at the beginning and twice a year a refresher training will be completed.\n\n## Travel details\n\n12c MacMillan Square, Edinburgh.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nLunch and travel expenses paid for as per expenses policy.",
