                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BMNR3YAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BMNR3YAP/male-support-volunteer-for-mens-community-group",
                    "publishStart": "2025-08-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Male Support Volunteer for Mens Community Group",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nKey Duties & Responsibilities: Typical tasks include: Session preparation; Facilitating activities; Welcome participants, particularly new members and help them feel at ease;\nGardening: Support small-group gardening tasks (planting, weeding, maintenance); Keep Fit.\n\n## Description\n\nPurpose of the role: To help create a welcoming, supportive space where men can meet, socialise and improve their wellbeing through shared activities such as gardening, coffee and conversation, informal sports and discussions on men’s health. You will work alongside the session lead to set-up, run and pack-down the group, encouraging participation and positive peer support.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining 2 times a year with one at the beginning before the start.\n\n## Travel details\n\nProject Esperanza,\n12c McMillan Square, Edinburgh EH4 4AB. \nProject Esperanza Allotment at Lauriston Farm, Lauriston Farm Road. \nDrylaw Neighbourhood Centre, 67 Groathill Road North, Edinburgh EH4 2SA.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThey fill out an expenses form.",
