        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003B3qP0AAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003B3qP0AAJ/simy-community-development",
            "name": "SiMY Community Development",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/SiMYCommunityDevelopment",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Fh5obYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Fh5obYAB/board-members-for-a-thriving-youth-and-community-development-charity-in-the-city-centre-of-glasgow",
                    "publishStart": "2026-03-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-13",
                    "title": "Board Members for a thriving youth and community development charity in the city centre of Glasgow",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBoard Members for a thriving youth and community development charity in the city centre of Glasgow\n\n## Description\n\n<h3><strong>Join the Board of SiMY Community Development!</strong></h3>\n\n<p>SiMY Community Development is entering an exciting new chapter. With a new senior leadership team in place and ambitious plans for growth and development, we are looking for enthusiastic, community-minded individuals to join our Board of Trustees.</p>\n\n<p>We are a small but kind-hearted charity that has been delivering youth and community development work in the north of Glasgow for over 25 years. Every week, we support local young people and families through creative programmes, outdoor learning, gardening projects, and community activities that build confidence, skills and connection.</p>\n\n<h3>The Difference We Make</h3>\n\n<p>By joining our Board, you will be helping us to:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Create safe, welcoming spaces where young people feel heard, valued and supported</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Improve young people&rsquo;s mental health and wellbeing through creative expression, outdoor activity and trusted adult relationships</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Increase physical activity and reduce social isolation</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Develop skills, confidence and leadership in children and young people</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Support families facing financial hardship by providing free, high-quality activities in their local community</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Strengthen community connections across generations</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Our work has helped young people grow in confidence, try new experiences, build friendships, improve their wellbeing and feel more positive about their future.</p>\n\n<h3>Who We&rsquo;re Looking For</h3>\n\n<p>We are keen to hear from anyone interested in this role, but we are particularly keen to hear from people who <strong>live in Glasgow city centre and surrounding areas (G4, G1, G21)</strong> and who bring skills or experience in:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Communications (especially social media)</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Marketing and brand building</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Facilities management</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Mental health and wellbeing</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Safeguarding</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Community education</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Previous board experience is welcome but not essential. We are looking for people who care about their local community, can think strategically, and are willing to contribute their time and expertise to help SiMY grow sustainably and responsibly.</p>\n\n<h3>What You Can Expect</h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Board meetings are held once every two months, and these alternate&nbsp;between online and face-to-face.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>All SiMY board members commit to providing 2-3 hours/wk of their time.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>The opportunity to shape the future of a growing local charity that has been making a difference for over 25 years</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>To work alongside a committed and passionate senior leadership team</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>To be part of a values-driven, supportive Board</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>All reasonable volunteer expenses paid</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>This is a voluntary role and a meaningful opportunity to use your skills to make a tangible difference in your local area.</p>\n\n<p>If you are passionate about contributing to positive social change, supporting people to thrive despite difficult circumstances, and contributing to a charity that makes these things happen, we would love to hear from you.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Join us and help shape the next chapter of SiMY Community Development.</strong></p>\n\n<p><em>If you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone. If you don&rsquo;t hear back within 5 working days, please contact the organisation using the provided details. Check your junk/spam folder for responses. If there&rsquo;s still no response, contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org.</em></p>\n\n## Experience required\n\nWhile we are keen to hear from anyone who is interested in this role, we are particularly interested to hear from people with a background in: \nCommunications (especially social media)\n\nMarketing and brand building\n\nFacilities management\n\nMental health and wellbeing\n\nSafeguarding\n\nCommunity education\n\n## Travel details\n\nRemote with occasional travel to city centre.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel, subsistence and training expenses are covered by SiMY",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Fh5obYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
