        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003B4aGeAAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003B4aGeAAJ/scot-baby-box-appeal",
            "name": "Scot Baby Box Appeal",
            "description": "From Scotland with Love! Sending pre-loved baby boxes and other essential items from Scotland to help families with young children who have been caught up in the escalating crisis in Ukraine.",
            "website": "http://www.scotbabyboxappeal.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC051932"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/RefugeesAsylumSeekers",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Refugees / Asylum Seekers"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FzhXFYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FzhXFYAZ/baby-box-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-03-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-26",
                    "title": "Baby Box Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Scot Baby Box Appeal is a small registered charity that started when the war broke out in almonst 5 years ago. We initially started getting baby boxes back from new mums in Scotland who were no longer using the one they were given by the Scottish Government. We repacked them with all mum and baby essentials and shipped them out to Ukraine. Since then we’ve sent out over 20,000 baby boxes, more than 3,000 toddler boxes as well as any other aid that is required and we are able to provide.\r\n\r\nThe Scot Baby Box Appeal are currently looking for new volunteers to join team based at Callendar Business Park, Falkirk. \r\nVolunteer tasks involve:\r\n*Sorting through new donations\r\n*Storing and organising donations\r\n*Packing/sorting baby boxes (with a specific emphasis on Toddler Boxes)\n\n## Experience required\n\nThere are no special skills or experience required for this role.  We welcome volunteers who are willing to help and learn about the role.\n\n## Training details\n\nNew volunteers will be guided through every step of process by one of our volunteers or Trustees. They will work alongside another more experienced volunteer until they feel ready to work independently. There will always be someone with more experience on site to assist with any issues that may arise.\n\n## Travel details\n\nFalkirk unit at Callendar Business Park, Callendar Road Falkirk, FK1 1XR.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are not available.\n\n## Taster details\n\nA taster session can be arranged.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcThwA-VbIBNtMljMN5iSWFS3B_n2wcaS98Z5A&s",
