        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003B4aKqAAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003B4aKqAAJ/forth-valley-pandas",
            "name": "Forth Valley PANDAS",
            "description": "PANDAS is a charity with a mission: ‘To be the UK’s most recognised and trusted support service for families and their networks who may be suffering with perinatal mental illness, including prenatal (antenatal) and postnatal depression.’ \r\n\r\nOur aim is to make sure no parent, family or carer feels alone. We have a variety of support services available to ensure help is delivered in a way that is right for you. No one suffering any form of mental illness should feel they’re on their own.\r\n\r\nWe offer motivational, educational and positive content through our social media channels, which adds to our value for the parents who need our help the most.\r\n\r\nPANDAS Foundation values difference and diversity and does not discriminate on the grounds of age, gender, sexual preference, orientation, marital status, race, religion, colour, national origin, disability, heritage or political belief.",
            "website": "https://pandasfoundation.org.uk/groups/forth-valley/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC051814"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FamilySupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Family Support"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FZV8MYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FZV8MYAX/volunteer-group-leader",
                    "publishStart": "2026-02-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer Group Leader",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nForth Valley Pandas is a local, constituted group which is part of a national charity supporting families being impacted by perinatal mental health problems. In Forth Valley as well as running a Peer Support Group they also run a Mindful Crafting Group and a Parenting Multiples Group.\r\n\r\nForth Valley Pandas are currently looking to recruit Volunteer Group Leaders for their Parenting Multiples Group.  They are looking for people who would like to support families with multiples; twins, triplets or two or more singletons under nursery school age.  Volunteer tasks will include:\r\n*helping to set up toys or other equipment for the group\r\n*make tea/coffee\r\n*prepare snacks\r\n*hold a baby/play with toddlers\r\n*help to clear up after the group\r\n\r\nVolunteers must keep what is said in the group confidential and remain non-judgemental.  No formal training required but a PVG check is required for this role which Forth Valley Pandas will process for you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo formal training required, however volunteers must adhere to confidentiality, have an interest in interacting with young children and be non judgemental.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction: shadowing one of the other group leaders.\r\nNew volunteers will always be with other more experienced volunteers and will always have a named contact to speak to.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe group currently meets twice a month (the 1st and 3rd Thursday) from 10am - 11:30am. With setting up and clearing up times we are looking for approximately 4.5hours per month.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTryst Centre, Park Drive, Stenhousemuir, FK5 3BB.\r\nThere are buses that stop close by and there is a car park.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses are not available.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://pandasfoundation.org.uk/wp-content/themes/Pandas/assets/images/logo.svg",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FZV8MYAX#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Group Leader",
                        "description": "No formal training required, however volunteers must adhere to confidentiality, have an interest in interacting with young children and be non judgemental.",
