        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003B4vnGAAR",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003B4vnGAAR/sanctuary-care",
            "name": "Sanctuary Care",
            "website": "https://sanctuary-care.co.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityFacilities",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Facilities"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000049yaXYAQ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000049yaXYAQ/reception-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2024-06-19",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-23",
                    "title": "Reception volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nLooking for a fulfilling and rewarding experience? Join our team at our care homes for the elderly as a volunteer and make a difference in the lives of our residents. Whether its befriending and chatting with our residents or organising and participating in leisure and social activities, your contribution will have a significant impact on their well-being and  quality of life. As a volunteer, you will have the opportunity to develop new skills, meet new people and create meaningful connections with our residents. Join us today and be a part of a community that values and appreciates the importance of companionship and human connection. Opportunities are available for weekdays or weekends, day time or early evening at:\r\n\r\nGlenfairn House Care Home-Sanctuary Care, 28 Racecourse Road, Ayr KA7 2UX\r\nQueens Care Home, 34 Ardayre Road, Prestwick KA9 1QL.\r\n\r\nWe are a not-for-profit organisation specialising in care homes for the elderly and currently have over 110 care homes across England and Scotland. \r\n\r\nFor more info, please go to https://www.sanctuary-care.co.uk/jobs/volunteering/how-apply-be-sanctuary-care-volunteer\r\n\r\n\r\nIf you would like to help our care homes through volunteering, opportunities are available for weekdays or weekends, daytime or early evening.\r\n\r\nWe are currently looking to recruit Reception volunteers.  Do you enjoy meeting and helping people? Do you have good communication and social skills?  Could you be the welcoming face of our care homes/day care centres? We would love to hear from you!\r\n\r\nFor more info, please go to https://www.sanctuary-care.co.uk/jobs/volunteering/how-apply-be-sanctuary-care-volunteer to learn more and apply online.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication skills\r\nCommon sense\r\nReliable\n\n## Training details\n\nOnline course which includes safeguarding, dementia friends, GDPR, life in a care home etc.  A meet and greet and a show round will be arranged. Finally, you would need to complete an online course which takes approx. an hour to complete. The whole process could take 3 - 4 weeks to complete.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nIt may be necessary for a volunteer to travel to a location other than their normal place of volunteering, they will be reimbursed travel expenses in line with the Travel and Subsistence Group Procedure. It is at the discretion of each home to cover the travel expenses from the volunteers' home to the care home as a good will gesture.\r\nWe are mindful of individual financial situations, and we do not want to put up barriers to volunteering, so please feel free to have a chat with your supervisor.\n\n## Taster details\n\nA meet and greet and a show round are available",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fc7d89c5c-09ec-5a85-8a43-31e0de3b2c69%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=e10fc050-d1ae-4ed3-a940-57036796bae0",
