                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7IGeAAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7IGeAAN/volunteering-opportunities-at-a-care-home",
                    "publishStart": "2022-11-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-09",
                    "title": "Volunteering Opportunities at a Care Home",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur volunteers are a great asset to our homes and care teams. They support us to enrich our residents' lives and remain truly connected to the communities in which they live. From school children who volunteer to take part, to retired professional who want to give something back, our volunteers are as diverse as our teams and residents.\r\n\r\nWe are a not-for-profit organisation specialising in care homes for the elderly across England and Scotland. We have 18 services in Scotland, which provide tailored care and support to people with a range of care needs.\r\n\r\nGlenfairn House Care Home - Ayr \r\nQueens Care Home – Prestwick\r\nHoward House Care Home – Kilmarnock\r\nKintyre House Care Home – Invergordon\r\nMull Hall Care Home – Invergordon\r\nMillport Care Centre – Ayrshire\r\nBirch House Care Home – Aberdeenshire\r\nPark Lodge Care Home – Aberdeenshire\r\nPitcairn Lodge Nursing Home – Aberdeenshire\r\nThe Meadows Care Home – Dornoch\r\nTyneholm Stables Care Home – East Lothian\r\nWestwood House Care Home – East Kilbride\r\nForefaulds Care Home – Lanarkshire\r\nAbercorn House Care Home – Lanarkshire\r\nCamilla House Care Home – Edinburgh\r\nBridge View House Care Home – Dundee \r\nAllanbank Care Home – Dumfries\r\n\r\nTo learn more about each care home, please copy and paste the link to your browser - https://www.sanctuary-care.co.uk/jobs/volunteering/how-apply-be-sanctuary-care-volunteer\r\n\r\nIf you would like to help our care homes through volunteering, opportunities are available for weekdays or weekends, daytime, or early evening.\r\n\r\nVolunteer befriender\r\nLeisure and activities volunteer\r\nWalking volunteer\r\nVolunteer driver\r\nGardening volunteer\r\nVolunteer entertainer\r\nDay care centre volunteer\r\nHairdressing/beauty volunteer\r\nHousekeeping volunteer\r\nCatering assistant volunteer\r\nReception volunteer\r\n\r\nFor more info on our volunteering opportunities, please go to https://www.sanctuary-care.co.uk/jobs/volunteering/how-apply-be-sanctuary-care-volunteer to learn more and apply online.\n\n## Experience required\n\nListening skills\n\n## Training details\n\nOnline course which includes safeguarding, dementia friends, GDPR, life in a care home etc.  A meet and greet and a show round will be arranged. Finally, you would need to complete an online course which takes approx. an hour to complete. The whole process could take 3 - 4 weeks to complete.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis opportunity is accessible by foot, bus, car and train.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nIt may be necessary for a volunteer to travel to a location other than their normal place of volunteering, they will be reimbursed travel expenses in line with the Travel and Subsistence Group Procedure. It is at the discretion of each home to cover the travel expenses from the volunteers' home to the care home as a good will gesture.\r\nWe are mindful of individual financial situations, and we do not want to put up barriers to volunteering, so please feel free to have a chat with your supervisor.\n\n## Taster details\n\nA meet and greet and a show round are available",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
