            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7IjjAAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7IjjAAF/speakers",
                    "publishStart": "2023-07-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Speakers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWaterAid Speakers are trained volunteers that deliver inspiring talks and workshops across the UK.\n\n## Description\n\nWaterAid Speakers are trained volunteers that deliver inspiring talks and workshops across the UK, to raise awareness about the importance of clean water, decent toilets and good hygiene to transform peoples’ lives for good. Our Speaker volunteers engage people about the important work of WaterAid, inspiring them to take action, as they speak with schools, universities, businesses, youth groups, religious places of worship, service organisations, and many more community groups.  You can find out more about the Speaker Network at \r\n\r\nhttps://www.wateraid.org/uk/get-involved/volunteering/become-a-wateraid-speaker .\n\n## Experience required\n\nInterest in and commitment to the work of WaterAid. Passion, enthusiasm and confidence for public speaking. Competent in use of PowerPoint and email.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be given a Speaker Mentor to guide you.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note: No expenses are paid for this opportunity",
