        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003BrboTAAR",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003BrboTAAR/street-soccer-scotland-aberdeen",
            "name": "Street Soccer Scotland - Aberdeen",
            "description": "Street Soccer provide free football-themed training and personal development opportunities for socially disadvantaged groups across Scotland.",
            "website": "https://streetsoccerscotland.org/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC048756"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEvent",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Event"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7IwCAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7IwCAAV/street-soccer-scotland-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Street Soccer Scotland Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHave you ever wanted to volunteer all to do within the concept of Football?\r\n\r\nWell look no further! Street Soccer Scotland is currently looking for volunteers to join their team. No two days the same, working alongside our players developing them personally and mentally. \r\n\r\nThe role includes working with coaches and players pitch side, monitoring games, inputting data, building relationships with partner organisations. We work with all ages from 10 years old all the way to past retirement . \r\n\r\nWe currently run in Aberdeen: Walking Football, Kids 10-13 Year olds, Street 45 (Women's Programme) and Adult Sessions. Opportunities are available Monday to Friday - Please get in touch with Peter Wood, Programme Co-ordinator at email: peter@streetsoccerscotland.org or telephone: 07487603708, if you would like to know more.\n\n## Experience required\n\n-Social Skills \r\n-Communication \r\n-Confidence \r\n-Self belief \r\n-Motivated\r\n-Honest\r\n-Good Timekeeping and Attendance\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided. Includes Personal Journey Record, monthly updates and Tool Box Talk before/after each session.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe volunteering times are flexible\n\n## Travel details\n\nGoals Aberdeen Inverdee Pitches, AB12 5XA \r\n\r\nBus Tickets will be refunded if volunteering\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNamed person submits bus ticket and is paid same day.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
