        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003BswkTAAR",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003BswkTAAR/saving-and-rehoming-strays",
            "name": "Saving and rehoming Strays",
            "description": "Saving and Rehoming Strays is a small SCIO (Scottish Charitable Incorporated Organisation No SC051584) based in Scotland with a mission to rescue and rehome dogs in the UK. As well as UK dogs we also partner with organisations in Europe, principally Romania, to identify dogs in need and support their path to finding a forever home. We believe in rescue without borders and that every dog deserves an opportunity to find a family of their own.\r\nSaving and Rehoming Strays is run by small team, primarily volunteers, giving their time for admin, fundraising, and looking after of the dogs in our care plus experienced rescuers in Romania and the UK.\r\nWe have a small rehoming centre in Scotland where our dogs will go for assessment, rehabilitation and ultimately rehoming in an environment not like traditional rehoming centres. Where appropriate our dogs live in groups and experience time with volunteers to allow them opportunity to socialise and get them ready to go to a new home. Alternatively, our dogs go to forever foster homes for their retirement.",
            "website": "https://www.savingandrehomingstrays.org/volunteer",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC051584"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AnimalWelfare",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Animal Welfare"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7KrTAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7KrTAAV/animal-rescue-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2022-12-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-29",
                    "title": "Animal Rescue Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe rely on the help of the many volunteers who give their time and their talents to us freely. We always need dedicated and reliable volunteers that can help out and new volunteers are always welcome. \r\n\r\nThere are many volunteering opportunities including working directly with our dogs, manual and maintenance, fostering, becoming a home checker, fundraising and helping at our events. Yet for safety reasons, we ask you to start off as a general volunteer with us and once you have gained the trust of our rescues, then you can start to volunteer directly with our dogs.\r\n\r\nVolunteering not only benefits our dogs but also provides lots of benefits for our volunteers too including:   \r\n- Meeting like-minded people who are passionate about animal welfare\r\n- Gaining new skills or developing existing ones\r\n- Gaining a sense of achievement by doing something rewarding\r\n- Putting something back into the community\r\n- Developing personal skills and confidence\r\n\r\nPlease note that if you wish to volunteer at the centre, it does involve physical work and due to our location your own transport is essential. \r\n\r\nFor on-site roles you will be invited to attend an induction course with our team when you will be asked to show ID and full proof of address before you can take up a volunteering role with us. \r\n\r\nOn site sessions will currently be at our principle site in Ayr.\r\n\r\nThe different types of sessions are as follows:\r\n\r\nCORE session – daytime, on site including poop picking, kennel cleaning and water checks.\r\nSUPPORT sessions – other on-site activities which may include any of the activities listed below as required by SRS at the time.\r\nSORT session – on site (or may be at home) sorting and preparing donations (daytime or evening).\r\nBARTER session – offsite (with on-site collection – requires transport) supporting with bartering deals made, collecting donations and may also include help with taking washing to the large wash centres.\r\nEVENT sessions – preparing and running events such as car boot sales, tabletop sales etc.\r\n\r\nOther activities you can help with? Just get in touch with us and we'll find the perfect role for you.\r\nTHANK YOU!",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fa7080127-5fad-4522-32d4-b6e413499e6d%2F0nFCUqNjeiXPIFO483j0BVWArU43%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=de3873a7-201c-4f79-be46-2a1fbe9be057",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7KrTAAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Animal Rescue Volunteer",
                        "applyLink": "https://www.savingandrehomingstrays.org/volunteer",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/Animals",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Animals"
                            }
                        ],
                        "service": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Service/TasterAvailable",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Taster Available"
                            }
                        ],
                        "specialistRole": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/SpecialistRole/SuitableForGroups",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Suitable for groups"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/SpecialistRole/TasterAvailable",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Taster Available"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
                            {
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "KA6 5HD",
                                "address": "KA6 5HD",
                                "latitude": 55.45986462623873,
                                "longitude": -4.582898025494849,
                                "simd": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/SIMD/KA65HD"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/LocalAuthority/SouthAyrshire",
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "South Ayrshire"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000056OpZYAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000056OpZYAU/board-membercharity-trustee-fundraising",
                    "publishStart": "2024-08-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Board Member/Charity Trustee/ Fundraising",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThis is a key role within our team as an unfunded rescue we rely on our events and donations to support the continued running of the charity.\r\nWe are currently recruiting for volunteer(s) to join the board as a Trustee to lead our fundraising efforts and take responsibility for our fundraising/events and be involved in management activities. In addition the Trustee will sit on our Board to ensure the charity is run efficiently and in accordance with our constitution and purpose. Please request a copy of the fundraising Trustee Job Description if you are interested. \r\nThe successful applicant will be expected to commit a minimum of 6-8 hours per week to their \r\nvolunteering and trustee duties.\r\n\r\nVolunteer Role Summary\r\nYou will be a passionate individual with experience in fundraising and/or event management and an interest in animal welfare. \r\nYou will be organized with excellent communication skills, able to write engaging and professional appeals and be confident picking up the phone to follow-up on potential leads. \r\nYou will be confident using social media platforms to research and promote our events. You will be confident working with a team of enthusiastic volunteers and ensuring individuals are completing actions as promised. \r\nYou will be a team player, communicating and obtaining feedback from the trustees and our general manager. \r\n\r\nVolunteer Responsibilities\r\n• Investigate and bring creative ideas for fundraising to the table\r\n• Oversee and promote fundraising campaigns establishing the actions required for success of the event and where these are delegated, providing oversight. \r\nBring feedback for each event back to the trustee team.\r\n• Liaise with General Manager to ensure appropriate staffing levels are available for events and that preparations are completed in a timely manner\r\n• Commit to organizing and hosting at least one local event per quarter – includes booking locations, advertising, coordinating with volunteers, venue set-up and promotion of the event.\r\n• Outreach to organisations for donations to be used at charity events for auctions, tombolas, prizes etc.\r\n• Able to visit Ayr site at least every 2 months (and prior to/ following events) to sort, collect and return event supplies.\r\n• Ensure updates and trackers are maintained on the charities online workspace\r\n\r\nSkills\r\n• IT competence (including Excel, Word, Powerpoint, Publisher etc.)\r\n• Excellent written and verbal communications skills,\r\n• Fundraising/event experience preferred\r\n• Marketing experience (not critical but must be competent with social media)\r\n• Ability to operate within a small, passionate leadership team,\r\n• Ability to motivate and encourage volunteers.\n\n## Experience required\n\nSkills\r\n• IT competence (including Excel, Word, Powerpoint, Publisher etc.)\r\n• Excellent written and verbal communications skills,\r\n• Fundraising/event experience preferred\r\n• Marketing experience (not critical but must be competent with social media)\r\n• Ability to operate within a small, passionate leadership team,\r\n• Ability to motivate and encourage volunteers\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur rescue can be a little tricky to reach by public transport and therefore access to a car would be preferable (which would also be beneficial to running local events).",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
