        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003F4KtYAAV",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003F4KtYAAV/troon-parkrun",
            "name": "Troon Parkrun",
            "description": "What is Troon parkrun?\r\nA free, fun, and friendly weekly 5k community event. Walk, jog, run, volunteer or spectate – it's up to you!",
            "website": "https://www.parkrun.org.uk/troon/?fbclid=IwAR2a62HxKmw76E2TL7OlWGCjgqa51tyiq8xwl5oYX0vrA3DVXrrP2muKbNI",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEngagement",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Engagement"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhtzJAAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhtzJAAR/troon-parkrun-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2023-03-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-16",
                    "title": "Troon Parkrun Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nVolunteering at parkrun\r\nVolunteering at parkrun is an opportunity to get outside, make new friends, have fun, learn new skills and to be a valuable part of your local community. We are always looking for new volunteers. This page explains how to get involved.\r\n\r\nHow to get involved\r\nFinding out about Troon parkrun volunteering opportunities couldn't be easier. Simply open a recent parkrun newsletter, results email or volunteer email, click on 'manage my profile', then 'email options', then select the events you'd like to hear from and click 'save opt-in events list'. You will then receive regular emails from those events letting you know all about their volunteering opportunities.\r\nFuture volunteer roster\r\nYou can see an event's future volunteer roster via their specific future roster page. To get in touch with the event directly, just send an email to troon@parkrun.com\r\nWhat would I do at the Event?\r\nFirst, and most importantly, we never ask anybody to do anything they're not comfortable with. If you don't want a particular task, please let us know and we will happily give you an alternative job. Nevertheless, none of our tasks are too stressful. You could be organising the finish funnel, operating the timer, or scanning barcodes using the simple Virtual Volunteer app. If you really want to do something in particular, please let us know and we'll see what we can do.\r\n\r\nRemember as a volunteer you are the eyes and ears of parkrun. If you have any concerns that arise at a parkrun event, whether involving children or adults, you should discuss those concerns with the Run Director on the day, as soon as possible thereafter or email Head Office at eventsupport@parkrun.com.\r\n\r\nThe core team\r\nTroon parkrun happens largely because of our fantastic volunteers. The weekly team of volunteers are led by a small group of parkrun enthusiasts who form what we call the 'core team': They make sure the event is setup and packed away each week, the results published, the tokens resorted, event reports written and so much more.\r\nEvent Directors - Gregor Wilson & Rachel Cox\r\nWe're very grateful to the help provided by everybody, both now and in the past, who've helped make Troon parkrun happen.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nEvery Saturday at 9:30am.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
