        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003GeoG0AAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003GeoG0AAJ/dates-n-mates-falkirk",
            "name": "Dates-n-Mates (Falkirk)",
            "description": "We deliver a variety of social events and friendship opportunities in and around Falkirk for our members, with their ideas and input in the planning process. Events might include pub nights, meals out, bowling, bingo and parties.\r\n\r\nWe currently also offer some online events for members too. Dates-n-Mates Falkirk also attends local events and festivals in and around Falkirk",
            "website": "https://datesnmates.org.uk/dates-n-mates-falkirk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC052107"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/LearningDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Learning Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SocialCare",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Social Care"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhvBTAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhvBTAAZ/events-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2024-10-31",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Events Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWould you like to support people with learning disabilities to socialise and make friends?  \r\nDates-n-Mates is a friendship and dating charity for adults with a learning disability.  They facilitate events to provide members the opportunity to socialise, try new things and meet people and their work is underpinned by a human rights-based approach. Dates-n-Mates believe it is people's right to live life free of discrimination and to develop friendships and relationships of their choosing, to love and be loved.\r\n\r\nAs an Events Supporter, your role is to help members enjoy socialising in safe and friendly environments.  Events include going to restaurants, pubs, cinema, tenpin bowling, day trips and walks.  The events are sociable, great fun and your role is very rewarding.  A large number of people with learning disabilities feel lonely and socially isolated.  Your support will help to change this..\r\n\r\nEvents take place afternoons and evenings and usually last 2 hours.  \r\nDates-n-Mates ask for a minimum of 1 event per month, are very flexible and aim to accommodate volunteers availability.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA volunteer who is sociable, friendly and confident and has excellent people skills. You will be a good communicator; kind and patient when interacting with people who have different communication or mobility needs. \r\nYou will be able to interact respectfully with people from a range of different backgrounds.  As you will be representing dates-n-mates, you will be courteous and professional as well as being reliable and punctual.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers will undertake various training including Safeguarding Vulnerable Adults, First Aid Awareness and Adult Support and Protection Training.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n1 event per month (Around 2 hours per event).  \r\nAfternoons or evenings. \r\nDue to the nature of the opportunity, we ask for a 9 month minimum commitment.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVenues in Falkirk and surrounding areas.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic Transport costs will be reimbursed.\r\nMileage rates of 45p per mile will be reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
