            "name": "Tarbolton Community Council",
            "description": "Tarbolton Community Council is a voluntary organisation made up of local residents, each with a genuine interest in the community. Their main role is to be representative through consultation with the local community, and make it known to the local authority and other public bodies the views of local people on all matters affecting them.\r\n\r\n\r\nCommunity Council members serve on the council for a period of three years and the Officers are elected annually. Meetings are open for public attendance, with full minutes published for public consideration.",
            "website": "https://tarboltoncc.co.uk/?fbclid=IwY2xjawUY1VdwZG9mAWV4dG4DYWVtAjEwAGJyaWQRMEZ0ZE1Ob2drYUhSVERWZ3VzcnRjBmFwcF9pZBAyMjIwMzkxNzg4MjAwODkyAAEegywMl",
