        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00108000038mQZSAA2",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00108000038mQZSAA2/parentspace-scio",
            "name": "ParentSpace (SCIO)",
            "description": "The service is aimed at parents and carers of children from birth to adolescence. We support parents through drop in sessions, evidence based courses, workshops and offers one to one support and befriending.",
            "website": "https://www.parentspace.org.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FamilySupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Family Support"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HxbeTYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HxbeTYAR/volunteer-treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-31",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Volunteer Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nParentSpace is a parent-led charity based in the Scottish Borders. Our mission is to enable and support \r\nparents and carers to create a secure and healthy base for their children's emotional growth. We do this \r\nthrough evidence-based courses, one-to-one support, workshops and drop-ins, helping families build \r\npositive communication, resilience and stronger relationships.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for a new Treasurer to join an active board of volunteers in steering the charity forwards. \r\nWe are a small (approx £100k turnover) established charity with a very good track record of raising funds \r\nand ensuring they are used efficiently to benefit parents. We are looking to increase our service delivery \r\nacross the Borders and this will come with increasing funding and reporting requirements. \r\n\r\nThe treasurer role focuses on governance and is free from day-to-day duties. We have an excellent Finance \r\nOfficer who does the bookkeeping, payroll and reporting. We will engage an external accounting firm to \r\nprepare statutory filings to OSCR. And the Charity Manager leads on Funding applications. \r\n\r\nThe board meets quarterly and the treasure can also expect approximately monthly meetings with the \r\nemployed managers of the charity.\n\n## Description\n\nThe board are jointly responsible for all decisions, and it is expected the Treasurer will lead the board on:\r\nPolicies and procedures management\r\n• Ensuring proper systems are in place for budgeting, financial control, reserves and reporting; \r\n• Overseeing and monitoring procedures to reduce the risk of fraud; \r\n• Monitor the overarching strategic management of the organisation’s financial resources;\r\n• Meeting at least quarterly with the Finance Manager to ensure that bookkeeping, record keeping, and \r\nbudgeting are conducted effectively.\r\nReporting – management and statutory\r\n• Keeping all directors properly informed about the state of the organisation’s finances; \r\n• Reviewing and inputting into the quarterly management reports created by the Finance Manager;\r\n• Ensuring financial reports to the trustees are comprehensible and properly discussed and explain \r\ntechnicalities in plain language which is understood by trustees;\r\nPlanning and risk management\r\n• Lead on setting annual and longer term budgets together with the Charity Manager and board\n\n## Experience required\n\n- Understanding and acceptance of the legal duties, responsibilities, and liabilities of being a charity \r\ntrustee.\r\n- Knowledge and understanding of charity finances and reporting requirements.\r\n- Commitment to ParentSpace’s objectives, aims and values and willingness to devote time freely to carry out responsibilities.\r\n- Good, independent judgement, and the ability to think creatively in the context of the organisation and external environment.\r\n- Good communication and interpersonal skills and the ability to respect the confidence of colleagues.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe induction covers a full handover of Treasurer responsibilities, an introduction to the work of the \r\ncharity, meeting key colleagues and in-house training on the organisations financial systems and policies.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWhere travel is required, reasonable expenses are available.\n\n## Taster details\n\nThe taster session involves an informal meeting with several charity trustees and key team members to \r\nhear about the work of ParentSpace and running of the board. Following this first taster, the volunteer \r\nwould be invited to attend part of a board meeting to meet the full group of trustees.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HxbeTYAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Treasurer",
                        "description": "- Understanding and acceptance of the legal duties, responsibilities, and liabilities of being a charity \r\ntrustee.\r\n- Knowledge and understanding of charity finances and reporting requirements.\r\n- Commitment to ParentSpace’s objectives, aims and values and willingness to devote time freely to carry out responsibilities.\r\n- Good, independent judgement, and the ability to think creatively in the context of the organisation and external environment.\r\n- Good communication and interpersonal skills and the ability to respect the confidence of colleagues.",
