            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ATKYfYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ATKYfYAP/volunteer-befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2025-06-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-09",
                    "title": "Volunteer Befriender",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are looking for a Volunteer Befriender to support our residents who live in sheltered accommodation to stay connected and to be less socially isolated by making new friends. \r\n\r\nThe Volunteer Befriender helps residents who feel isolated or unable to get out very easily on their own by giving time on a one-to-one basis to help them maintain social contact, provide companionship, and reduce loneliness and social isolation. Volunteer Befrienders build a positive relationship with an individual and visit them on a regular basis in their own home. This could mean spending some time with a person for an hour or two every week/fortnight, but we also encourage getting out and about for a coffee or short walk. Generally, Befrienders are there to chat and get to know someone, and to have fun. Befrienders support their resident to continue with existing interests, whilst encouraging them to embark on new activities.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo qualifications are necessary. We are looking for volunteers who are confident with older people, have good communication and listening skills, are reliable and willing to work as part of a team.\n\n## Training details\n\nNo qualifications are necessary. We are looking for volunteers who are interested in working with older people, have good communication and listening skills, are reliable and willing to work as part of a team.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThis is a flexible role that can suit your availability - we ask for an hour every week or fortnight to meet with a resident, and a minimum commitment of around 6 months.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur opportunities are based in Bo'ness (EH51 9LN) and Falkirk (FK2 7RZ).\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport expenses will be paid monthly.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fc47c19ef-d41e-4858-9ede-adf3aa10feab%2FXPrpz4zVmiRWRuGPAUiQ4SyLdVd2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=a37c75c2-13ae-4721-9805-f0231a5f6fcc",
