        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001x9p6DAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001x9p6DAAQ/pet-fostering-service-scotland-aberdeen-aberdeenshire",
            "name": "Pet Fostering Service Scotland  (Aberdeen & Aberdeenshire)",
            "description": "Pet Fostering Service Scotland (PFSS) provides short-term, emergency foster care for pets whose owners are facing one of the following situations:\r\n*Ill health\r\n*Temporary homelessness\r\n*Domestic abuse",
            "website": "https://www.pfss.org.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AnimalWelfare",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Animal Welfare"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000EeIC9AAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000EeIC9AAN/home-visitor-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Home Visitor Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\n*Are you passionate about animal welfare?  Join our growing team of volunteer Home Visitors and play a vital role in supporting owners and pets in your local area who are facing an emergency situation.*\r\n\r\nPet Fostering Service Scotland (PFSS) provides short-term, emergency foster care for pets whose owners are facing one of the following situations:\r\n*Ill health\r\n*Temporary homelessness\r\n*Domestic abuse\r\n\r\nEvery year we provide temporary foster care for around 200 pets across Scotland – but we want to be able to support even more.  \r\n\r\nOur volunteer Home Visitors play a vital role in delivery of our service by visiting potential volunteer pet foster carers to assess their house, home situation and the fosterer. \r\n\r\nThis opportunity is home based with travel to other local locations to carry out home visits.  Travel can be by public transport or car and travel expenses will be provided. \r\n\r\nYou will be contacted by PFSS when there is a need for a home visit in your area.\r\n\r\nThe main tasks are:\r\n*Contact the potential fosterer and arrange a time for the home visit to take place\r\n*Carry out the home visit following the guidelines provided by PFSS.\r\n*Complete the home visit report and return a copy to the Home Visit Coordinator \r\n\r\nFull training and support is provided to all volunteers. Includes:\r\n*Handbook for the role, induction and informal training either face to face or over the phone when starting in role.  *Ongoing support provided and informal update training as required. \r\n\r\nIf you are an animal lover who wants to develop new skills and be part of a team making a difference to pets and owners in Aberdeen and/or Aberdeenshire then we'd love to hear from you! For more information please contact us at E Mail: volunteering@pfss.org.uk or Tel 0355 811 9909 (then choose option 8 then 1 after the welcome message).\n\n## Experience required\n\n*Willing to travel by car/public transport to home visits\r\n*Be comfortable visiting potential foster carers in their homes\r\n*Pleasant telephone manner, professional on home visit\r\n*Passionate about animal welfare\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training and support is provided to all volunteers. Includes:\r\n*Handbook for the role, induction and informal training either face to face or over the phone when starting in role.  *Ongoing support provided and informal update training as required.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nHours can be flexible.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAberdeen City and/or Aberdeenshire.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed out of pocket expenses will be reimbursed e.g. public transport costs (on production of receipts), mileage at 45p/mile. Expenses are usually claimed monthly but can be claimed more frequently if required.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000EeIC9AAN#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Home Visitor Volunteers",
                        "description": "*Willing to travel by car/public transport to home visits\r\n*Be comfortable visiting potential foster carers in their homes\r\n*Pleasant telephone manner, professional on home visit\r\n*Passionate about animal welfare",
                        "commitment": "Hours can be flexible.",
