            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002037ErAAI/blind-veterans-uk",
            "name": "Blind Veterans UK",
            "description": "We support vision impaired ex service people for life, whatever caused their sight loss. We provide rehabilitation, training, practical and emotional support at home, locally or remotely, supported by local teams and volunteers. We also offer specialist equipment and wellbeing breaks at our centres, helping veterans regain independence and live fulfilling lives.",
            "website": "https://www.blindveterans.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC039411"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SensoryImpairment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000INkkXYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000INkkXYAT/outings-companion",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-07",
                    "title": "Outings Companion",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDo you enjoy walking and spending time outdoors? We're looking for a friendly volunteer to accompany one of our blind veterans on local walks.\r\nOur veteran is a keen walked and would love the support of someone who can accompany them on a fortnightly or monthly walk. This is a great opportunity to share conversation, fresh air and the joy of walking while making a real difference.\r\nIf you'd like to help a veteran enjoy greater independence and wellbeing, please get in touch with volunteer coordinator Elaine on elaine.holland@blindveterans.org.uk\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will be fully trained and supported so they feel comfortable and confident in their volunteering. Training includes but not limited to safeguarding boundaries, visual impairments and sighted-guiding.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F6833a575-5065-4727-abab-e5c5208ecb7f%2FGKUbu3G4RiUFKC0iPx0fLszEQJy1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=dd1dfc51-6ca0-4fe8-a915-c7077425a9aa",
