                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7HlbAAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7HlbAAF/professional-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2022-10-19",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Professional Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nRepresentation matters, which is why we want our volunteers to reflect the diversity of the community groups we work with. We’re actively encouraging applicants from ethnically diverse backgrounds to apply as we are currently under-represented in this space.\r\n\r\nYou will meet the inspirational faces of community groups across the UK and immerse yourself in their work; use your existing skills whilst developing new ones; guide members to become more inclusive; network with like-minded individuals helping grassroots clubs. You'll use your professional skills to help groups overcome operational challenges, become better equipped for the future, and tackle inequality in sport.\r\n\r\nOur roles are quite flexible and work around your schedule. We only share opportunities we think are relevant to you. With most of our volunteering support being delivered digitally, it’s even easier to get started supporting members across our network, to help sports groups survive; and so much more.\r\nUse the link below to submit your application form\r\nhttps://sported3.beaconforms.com/form/e9bb0f3a\n\n## Experience required\n\nBusiness skills is required to be able fully support our members.\r\nFundraising, Financial Management, Business Planning, Governance, Marketing and Volunteer Management are a few of the skill sets we look for, with at least 2 years business or lived experience.\n\n## Training details\n\nAn informal discussion will take place upon receipt of an application, followed by an induction session and ongoing training is also available. Networking opportunities with our volunteering team are also offered.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n3 hours per month\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis opportunity can be delivered virtually or across Midlothian\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses in line with our policy are covered in the instances in-person meetings occur, upon receipt",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fb9010d2b-3592-7be0-0911-674fa33e29e7%2FWkLzgT1VE9cAHEWcVMpdVMd5bL63%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=352a991f-d98c-4ae5-beff-541d82c1e3b7",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7HlbAAF#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Professional Volunteer",
                        "description": "Business skills is required to be able fully support our members.\r\nFundraising, Financial Management, Business Planning, Governance, Marketing and Volunteer Management are a few of the skill sets we look for, with at least 2 years business or lived experience.",
                        "commitment": "3 hours per month",
