        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001aNB7fAAG",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001aNB7fAAG/sported-fife",
            "name": "Sported (Fife)",
            "description": "Sported is a leading Sport for Change charity, helping to transform the lives of disadvantaged young people across the UK. We’re a membership organisation, working with over 3000 amazing community groups and organisations that are using the power of sport to tackle the root causes of some of society’s biggest problems, and giving disadvantaged young people the opportunities to succeed in life. We support the inspirational local heroes and heroines that run these clubs by providing free business and financial support so that they have the skills, knowledge and resources to continue their amazing work. We have a network of volunteer business mentors who work with our members on a one-to-one basis, providing expert consultancy on a range of business issues.",
            "website": "http://sported.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC043161"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000004bIN3YAM",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000004bIN3YAM/sported-volunteer-business-consultant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-24",
                    "title": "Sported Volunteer Business Consultant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDo you want to give something back to your community?  If so, then this is the role for you!  \r\nSported consultants are paired with community sports clubs who need expertise in various areas to become sustainable and increase their capacity. These opportunities are very flexible - from a 15-minute call with a club leader who has questions in your skills area, to a 6 month placement. \r\nAs a Sported volunteer, you’ll share your professional skills and expertise with community groups, having a huge effect on these clubs. \r\nFull induction is offered, together with personal development opportunities, and you will join a network of skilled Sported consultants across the UK. You will help a diverse range of people and organisations and will receive support throughout from the Sported team. \r\nMost importantly you will have fun!\n\n## Experience required\n\nIf you have one or a few of the following professional skills or lived experience, you will be a huge help to group leaders who aren’t confident in these areas:\r\n-Business & strategic planning\r\n-Facilities management & asset transfer\r\n-Financial management\r\n-Fundraising\r\n-Sports development\r\n-Legal\r\n-Project management\r\n-Marketing & comms\r\n-Governance\r\n-Sustainability\r\n-Volunteer & staff management\n\n## Training details\n\nTheir induction covers their policies and resources available to help with each placement.  Support is given by their regional and national teams and Sported’s central Volunteer Services Team and you will have the opportunity both to share and develop your own skills.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTheir roles are mostly delivered virtually now, via Zoom or Teams, phone calls etc but sometimes are face to face, if you are linked with a group in your own community – the choice is entirely yours.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nIf you incur a valid expense on Sported's behalf while supporting a member, then you can be reimbursed. A valid expense could be mileage (paid at .45p per mile) coffee etc.  Claim within 3 months using an expense form, shared at induction.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
