            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008mafhYAA",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008mafhYAA/beach-wheelchair-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-03-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Beach Wheelchair Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nOur volunteers are key to what we do. This highly rewarding role is perfect for an individual who has the desire to help children and adults enjoy our beautiful beaches at Portobello. If you enjoy meeting people, being outside and flexible with your time this could be the perfect role.\n\n## Description\n\nSupporting Beach Wheelchairs customers access our specialised Beach Wheelchairs and enjoy Portobello beach. It  involves Opening up the container based in tumbles carpark in Portobello, get equipment ready and check condition, meet and greet customer, making sure they are happy with the chair of their choice, agree return time, meet customer for return hire. Clean down. chairs and safely lock up the container. Can also be involved with fundraising activities, open days, outreach events.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe would start with an informal chat and look around the container.\nDiscuss role and expectations.\nMeet other volunteers and allow you to chat about their experience.\nOver 2/3 sessions learn the equipment and paperwork.\nBuddy an experienced volunteer for 2/3 hires\nWhen confident you can do solo hires but always with the support of another volunteer on the phone. \nRefresher training ongoing but formally every 6 months.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur container is beside the car park at Tumbles on the seafield end of the promenade. Parking is in the Tumbles carpark. Portobello high street is a 3 minute walk away and several buses pass here on a regular basis.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpense reclaim form will be supplied by the treasurer.",
