            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000CNXvyAAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000CNXvyAAH/board-directors",
                    "publishStart": "2018-07-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Board Directors",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFull options  is an organisation which tackles social isolation; Campaigns for and Promote human rights, religious and racial harmony; works toward the relief of poverty; promotes the advancements of health and education for all.\n\n## Description\n\nIt is an importunity to work toward a better society and build links between communities by coming together and support those who are in need. We are looking for 4 volunteers to join our board of directors.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEach one of volunteers will be required to specify their fields of expertise.\n\n## Training details\n\nInitially all volunteer will have an induction about their role in the board as well as their knowledge of the organisation vision and activities; they will be a yearly training for all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nBoard meetings take place 4 times per year, with most board members serving for 1 year. Meetings will usually take place during the week (Mon-Fri) but may occasionally be on Saturdays.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe are looking for volunteers from Edinburgh, Midlothian & Scottish Borders.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe reimburse public transport fees.",
