        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001lnXyqAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001lnXyqAAE/lifestars-scio",
            "name": "Lifestars SCIO",
            "description": "At Lifestars, we believe every child deserves the right support to thrive. Our ultimate goal is to help children build essential life and social skills including communication, trust, leadership, pride, and confidence – empowering them to flourish and contribute positively to their communities.\r\n\r\nWe’re proud to work hand-in-hand with schools across the region, offering tailored programmes that foster youth empowerment and create inclusive learning environments. Each partnership allows us to make a real difference, helping children develop their confidence, leadership, and practical skills.\r\n\r\nOur Life Skills Programme is at the heart of what we do. These sessions are designed to bridge the gap between the classroom and the real world, giving children the tools they need to succeed in life. Through fun and engaging activities, we focus on developing child development skills, promoting children’s safety education, and providing career guidance for students.",
            "website": "https://lifestars.co.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC048590"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0LriYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I0LriYAF/lifestars-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-04",
                    "title": "Lifestars Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAt Lifestars, we believe every child deserves the right support to thrive. Our ultimate goal is to help children build essential life and social skills including communication, trust, leadership, pride, and confidence – empowering them to flourish and contribute positively to their communities.\r\n\r\nWe’re proud to work hand-in-hand with schools across the region, offering tailored programmes that foster youth empowerment and create inclusive learning environments. Each partnership allows us to make a real difference, helping children develop their confidence, leadership, and practical skills.\r\n\r\nOur Life Skills Programme is at the heart of what we do. These sessions are designed to bridge the gap between the classroom and the real world, giving children the tools they need to succeed in life. Through fun and engaging activities, we focus on developing child development skills, promoting children’s safety education, and providing career guidance for students.\r\n\r\nAs a Lifestars Volunteer, you will support the delivery of our Life Skills Programme within local schools, helping children build confidence, resilience, communication skills, and other key skills for life. Commitment and hours are negotiable per needs of both the charity and applicant.\r\n\r\nYou may also have opportunity to assist with additional activities, events, and projects throughout the year as and when these arise.\r\n\r\nRelevant guidance and excellent support is provided to all volunteers. Includes training and background information on the projects.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help brighten up children and young people’s lives across Aberdeen and ‘Shire. There are flexible times to help and all assistance makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor further information please contact Neve McPherson at email: neve.mcpherson@lifestars.net\n\n## Description\n\nAt Lifestars, we believe every child deserves the right support to thrive. Our ultimate goal is to help children build essential life and social skills including communication, trust, leadership, pride, and confidence – empowering them to flourish and contribute positively to their communities.\r\n\r\nWe’re proud to work hand-in-hand with schools across the region, offering tailored programmes that foster youth empowerment and create inclusive learning environments. Each partnership allows us to make a real difference, helping children develop their confidence, leadership, and practical skills.\r\n\r\nOur Life Skills Programme is at the heart of what we do. These sessions are designed to bridge the gap between the classroom and the real world, giving children the tools they need to succeed in life. Through fun and engaging activities, we focus on developing child development skills, promoting children’s safety education, and providing career guidance for students.\r\n\r\nAs a Lifestars Volunteer, you will support the delivery of our Life Skills Programme within local schools, helping children build confidence, resilience, communication skills, and other key skills for life. Commitment and hours are negotiable per needs of both the charity and applicant.\r\n\r\nYou may also have opportunity to assist with additional activities, events, and projects throughout the year as and when these arise.\r\n\r\nRelevant guidance and excellent support is provided to all volunteers. Includes training and background information on the projects.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help brighten up children and young people’s lives across Aberdeen and ‘Shire. There are flexible times to help and all assistance makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor further information please contact Neve McPherson at email: neve.mcpherson@lifestars.net \r\n\r\nMore details about Lifestars is also available at www.lifestars.co.uk\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant guidance and excellent support is provided to all volunteers. Includes training and background information on the projects.\n\n## Travel details\n\nLocal schools and community settings in Aberdeen & Aberdeenshire.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
