        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001lnv8qAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001lnv8qAAA/falkirk-settlers-support-group-friends-of-scottish-settlers-foss",
            "name": "Falkirk Settlers Support Group: Friends of Scottish Settlers (FOSS)",
            "description": "FOSS is an organisation of local people extending a hand of welcome and solidarity to newcomers to the Falkirk District. We began in 2016 as a community group welcoming Syrian families seeking refuge here. Since then, our links have grown to include people navigating the asylum system, Ukrainian arrivals, as well as those simply moving to the area to live and work. Through befriending, partnership working, and volunteer coordination, we empower newcomers to stand on their own two feet and quickly find the knowledge, networks, and services they need to live full, self-determined lives. FOSS trains up and supports volunteers to link up, lend a hand and point people in the right direction.",
            "website": "https://fossfalkirk.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC050254"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/RefugeesAsylumSeekers",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Refugees / Asylum Seekers"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000004RLfaYAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000004RLfaYAG/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2024-11-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-12",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nFriends of Scottish Settlers (FOSS) is seeking to appoint additional Trustees. This is an exciting opportunity for people, with or without previous Trustee experience, who would like to help drive forward our work in making Falkirk a welcoming haven for newcomers. We are intent on building real diversity of backgrounds, interests and experience in the makeup of our Board of Trustees.\r\n\r\nFOSS is a volunteer organisation offering holistic support through the provision of material needs, befriending and other activities to newcomers of many nationalities and with wide-ranging needs, including refugees and people in the asylum system.\r\n\r\nFOSS has grown rapidly and is a dynamic organisation. Those who depend on our support are often in very difficult circumstances. People placed in Falkirk face additional challenges because our area is only beginning to establish refugee-informed assistance. FOSS is at the forefront of building these local ecosystems of support.\r\n\r\nOur services are delivered by an excellent team of four part-time staff and around 30 dedicated volunteers. Trustees are volunteers expected to serve for three years, extendable to six years. They are responsible for the governance of the charity, helping to ensure that we achieve our objectives and make proper use of the grants and donations on which we depend. \r\n\r\nMore information is available on our website at https://fossfalkirk.org.uk. This includes our founding documents, annual report and accounts.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPrevious experience as a Trustee is beneficial but not required. This role is for you if:\r\n*You are committed to supporting newcomers to the Falkirk District \r\n*Committed to the FOSS values of empowerment, solidarity, respect, integrity and welcome.\r\n*You can listen and communicate well, showing tact and diplomacy.\r\n*You are dependable and able to follow through on your commitments.\r\n*You are patient and willing to help while also being honest about your own limits.\r\n*You can maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information appropriately.\n\n## Training details\n\nNew Trustees receive a full induction and have access to relevant training and support from an experienced Board of Trustees.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMeetings are held (usually in person) every six weeks on a Monday evening. \r\nWhere appropriate, Trustees can join online.\r\nPlus Ad hoc input in between meetings.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoard meetings are held in person in Falkirk. Where appropriate, Trustees can join online.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable expenses can be reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F7b5c9f87-9e45-4818-9ddd-a9f815d8f1c4%2FXPrpz4zVmiRWRuGPAUiQ4SyLdVd2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=dfb7abf7-98eb-4eed-bc5f-a46eacccb0c3",
