        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001mtHNbAAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001mtHNbAAM/mcr-pathways-aberdeen-and-aberdeenshire",
            "name": "MCR Pathways (Aberdeen and Aberdeenshire)",
            "description": "Our vision is that every care-experienced and disadvantaged young person in Scotland gets the same education outcomes, career opportunities and life chances as every other young person.",
            "website": "http://mcrpathways.org/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HrVGnYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HrVGnYAN/mcr-pathways-volunteer-mentors",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-18",
                    "title": "MCR Pathways Volunteer Mentors",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFor too many young people, an unfair start means navigating life's toughest challenges alone. You can change that.\r\n\r\nChanging lives through mentoring. Our award-winning programme believes in the power of connection, communication, and the overall transformational potential of mentoring in school and community settings. \r\n\r\nWe match adult volunteer mentors from all walks of life, careers and experiences with young people experiencing a range of challenging circumstances, to build confidence, overcome obstacles, awaken ambition and much more. \r\n\r\nJust one hour a week can ignite the vital spark in a young person, helping them find a path to positive futures. Change a life. Be the difference in ensuring young people don't have to navigate life's toughest challenges alone. \r\n\r\nWe support mentors from all walks of life, with different backgrounds and experiences. You may think you need to have a superpower or even a hero cape, but what we are really looking for is for you to see their potential, help them believe in themselves and pursue positive futures. \r\n\r\nThis means you are:\r\n* Full of experiences & ideas\r\n* Compassionate\r\n* Caring\r\n* Patient\r\n* A good listener\r\n\r\nIf you can tick all these off, you can help young people to see their incredible potential. \r\n\r\nFull support and guidance is provided. All mentors complete a training session prior to being matched with a young person and are fully supported by the team at MCR on every step of their mentoring journey.\r\n\r\nTo learn more go our our website: https://mcrpathways.org/become-a-mentor/ or sign up for an info session: https://my.mcrpathways.org/book/s/information-session\r\n\r\n\r\nFor further details/any questions please contact Rebecca Finnie, Community Delivery Lead at email: rebecca.finnie@mcrpathways.org or telephone: 07483 950811\n\n## Description\n\nFor too many young people, an unfair start means navigating life's toughest challenges alone. You can change that.\r\n\r\nChanging lives through mentoring. Our award-winning programme believes in the power of connection, communication, and the overall transformational potential of mentoring in school and community settings. You can help a young person to realise their potential and find a path to a brighter future.\r\n\r\nWe match adult volunteer mentors from all walks of life, careers and experiences with young people experiencing a range of challenging circumstances, to build confidence, overcome obstacles, awaken ambition and much more. \r\n\r\nJust one hour a week can ignite the vital spark in a young person, helping them find a path to positive futures. Change a life. Be the difference in ensuring young people don't have to navigate life's toughest challenges alone. \r\n\r\nWe support mentors from all walks of life, with different backgrounds and experiences. You may think you need to have a superpower or even a hero cape, but what we are really looking for is for you to see their potential, help them believe in themselves and pursue positive futures. \r\n\r\nThis means you are:\r\n* Full of experiences & ideas\r\n* Compassionate\r\n* Caring\r\n* Patient\r\n* A good listener\r\n\r\nIf you can tick all these off, you can help young people to see their incredible potential. \r\n\r\nFull support and guidance is provided. All mentors complete a training session prior to being matched with a young person and are fully supported by the team at MCR on every step of their mentoring journey.\r\n\r\nTo learn more go our our website: https://mcrpathways.org/become-a-mentor/ or sign up for an info session: https://my.mcrpathways.org/book/s/information-session\r\n\r\n\r\nFor further details/any questions please contact Rebecca Finnie, Community Delivery Lead at email: rebecca.finnie@mcrpathways.org or telephone: 07483 950811\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and training is provided to all volunteers. \r\n\r\nAll mentors complete a training session prior to being matched with a young person and are fully supported by the team at MCR on every step of their mentoring journey.\r\n\r\nMentor Services guide you through from the point of registration, and our Pathways coordinators are you point of contact once matched with a young person and will do a mentor induction with you and the young person.\r\n\r\nWe also have our mentor hub that has guidance and training courses and throughout the year we host coffee conversations and training on specific topics related to mentoring.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available - all help is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteer mentors are based in Aberdeen City. Volunteer mentors meet their young person for one hour a week in safeguarded community and educational venues such as community centres, schools, and colleges. \r\n\r\nMCR Pathways works across Aberdeen City so volunteer mentors decide what areas of the city they would prefer to mentor in and we will match mentors with a young person based in that area so meetings can be accessible to both mentors and young people.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fb9b936a3-6642-4171-8303-9b93cf311a96%2FG7eZllHn7IVctbaWrYTw0BgchTX2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=1298fed2-92e7-44bb-ae7e-37da96106ceb",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HrVGnYAN#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "MCR Pathways Volunteer Mentors",
                        "commitment": "Flexible times available - all help is greatly appreciated.",
                        "applyLink": "https://mcrpathways.org/become-a-mentor/",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "21",
                        "theme": [
