                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-07",
                    "title": "Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe Treasurer would keep a note/spreadsheet of income and expenditure for all LTCH projects. There are only a handful of payments made each month. This work is estimated to only take a couple of hours max each month. \r\nIdeally the new volunteer Treasurer would also play an active role on our volunteer management committee. We meet for 90 minutes once a month on Zoom. \r\nThey would attend a three-monthly Finance sub-committee meeting on Zoom and send a finance report of the previous month by email to committee members prior to the committee meeting. They would help the Project Manager report back to funders on financial matters. They may be asked to help the Project Manager set budgets for any prospective funding bids.\n\n## Description\n\nLTCH is a small voluntary organisation based on the Western Isles. We aim to help people help themselves and offer 4 sessions on Zoom each week with a monthly in-person meeting. All sessions are open to anyone living on the Western Isles. Attendance at any session is optional and we encourage LTCH members to drop-in to any session they wish – or none.\n\n## Training details\n\nLTCH can provide in-house training and can also offer specialist support through Inspiring Scotland Network of Expert Volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nExpenses are paid at 55p/mile for any travel to in-person meetings.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPaid within one week of invoicing/submitting expenses form.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
