            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GuELdYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GuELdYAN/community-worker",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-18",
                    "title": "Community Worker",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are now looking for compassionate, committed individuals to join us as Volunteer Community Workers, helping us grow awareness, strengthen community ties, and support families in meaningful ways. We are especially keen to welcome volunteers with group facilitation experience.\r\n\r\nAs a Volunteer Community Worker, you will:\r\n- Build relationships with local schools, community groups and organisations \r\n- Support and promote fundraising activities and awareness campaigns \r\n- Engage with bereaved families in a sensitive, compassionate manner \r\n- Help organise and assist at events, workshops and community activities \r\n- Act as an ambassador for Anam Cara Fasgadh within your local area \r\n- Contribute ideas to help expand the charity's reach and impact \r\n\r\nContact Irene on info@anamcarafasgadh.org\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining will be received via Child Bereavement UK",
