                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BtpefYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BtpefYAB/volunteer-business-consultant",
                    "publishStart": "2025-09-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-17",
                    "title": "Volunteer Business Consultant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSported is seeking professionals with expertise in business and strategic planning, finance, marketing and PR, fundraising, governance and impact measurement to support their growing network of community sport and youth groups.\r\n\r\nThey have volunteering opportunities in Scotland with a range of flexible options. As little as one hour of your time per month could make a massive difference to their network groups.\r\n\r\nWhat could a volunteer gain from the experience?\r\nSported knows that representation matters, which is why they want their volunteers to reflect the diversity of the community groups they work with. They are actively encouraging applicants from ethnically diverse backgrounds and other minoritised groups to apply as they are currently under-represented in this space.  You will get to meet the inspirational faces of community groups across the UK and immerse yourself in their work; use your existing skills in a rewarding fashion whilst developing new ones; guide members to become more inclusive; network with other like-minded individuals helping grassroots sports groups survive; and so much more.\r\n\r\nVolunteers say that making a positive difference to their network groups is what they most enjoy about volunteering at Sported.\r\n\r\nApply online at www.sported.org.uk/volunteering-at-sported/\n\n## Experience required\n\nSported is looking for skills and professional experience in any of the following: \r\n- Business & Strategic Planning\r\n- Facilities Management & Asset Transfer\r\n- Financial Management\r\n- Fundraising & Income Generation\r\n- Governance\r\n- Inclusion\r\n- Leadership Coaching & Mentoring\r\n- Marketing & Communications\r\n- Evaluation & Impact Measurement\r\n- Environmental Sustainability\r\n- Sports Development\r\n- Volunteer & Staff Management\r\n- Legal\r\n- Project Management\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction, training opportunities and local support available.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2 - 3 hours per month maximum.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAll expenses paid monthly.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fd77ec5ac-7cc4-4f8f-a323-a108d7667238%2FliLEC2s9ZwYA46gEa6AxGTVGunx2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=ef7626ef-dd78-46a5-ba5c-0d84dca82286",
