            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Vuq2gAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Vuq2gAAB/volunteer-facilitator",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-04",
                    "title": "Volunteer Facilitator",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe Ruby Boots project is seeking enthusiastic volunteers to help children and young people from Armed Forces families navigate their transition to civilian life.\n\n## Description\n\nAre you passionate about supporting young people? Looking for meaningful volunteer experience? Becoming a volunteer facilitator is perfect for people who want to develop professional experience in youth work, education, social care, or psychology, with flexible hour options available.\r\nThe Ruby Boots project is seeking enthusiastic volunteers to help children and young people from Armed Forces families navigate their transition to civilian life.\r\nWhat you'll do:\r\n-Support peer group sessions for children and young people, aged 5-18\r\n-Build positive relationships with young people during a significant life transition\r\n-Help facilitate discussions on important topics like confidence-building, managing change, and creating support networks\r\n-Opportunities to progress and develop experience in leading, training, administration, develop session plans, and more.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou must:\r\nHave Minimum of 5 years professional experience in a  youth work setting\r\n-Have great communication skills\r\n           -Enjoy working with children and young people\r\n\r\nTo foster a good balance, we would be especially keen to hear from more Male volunteers\n\n## Training details\n\n•\tComprehensive training (6 hours total - flexible delivery options), including the NSPCC Safeguarding training.\r\n•\tValuable experience in trauma-informed practice\r\n•\tRegular support and mentoring\n\n## Travel details\n\nVarious locations across Fife. You will be matched as close to your local area as possible.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport costs reimbursed or mileage at the rate of 45p per mile.",
