            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003K5g6rAAB/girlguiding-scotland",
            "name": "Girlguiding Scotland",
            "description": "Girlguiding Scotland is the leading charity for girls and young women in Scotland, supporting 45,000 young members and more than 9,000 amazing volunteers. \nGirlguiding helps members discover their full potential by having fun and enjoying new adventures.",
            "website": "http://www.girlguidingscotland.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC005548"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Qhia7AAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Qhia7AAB/youth-group-helpers-and-team-leaders",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Youth group helpers and team leaders",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWould you like to go on fun adventures, explore and laugh with friends?  \n\nAt Girlguiding we do everything from camping to campaigning! We’re all about girls and young women laughing, learning and having adventures. Why not join the fun? \n\nMeetings usually run on weekday evenings for about an hour, and you can choose how much or how little you can help out! Our different sections cover ages 4-18, so there’s something for everyone. Different groups meet on different days of the week, so you can help out on the day that is best for you. We can be flexible if you can't commit to coming every week, and we only run during the school term times.\n\nYouth volunteering with Girlguiding Scotland looks great on a CV, and can improve skills like teamwork, leadership, communication, creativity and IT. It’s great experience if you want a career in youthwork or education. You can get extra training like First Aid, the disclosure check for working with children is paid for by us and we’ll help you every step of the way. There are loads of meetings happening all over South Lanarkshire, so you can join one close to you. \n\nOur volunteers are what makes Girlguiding amazing, and we welcome people of all backgrounds and walks of life. Come have a chat with us, you won’t regret it!  You can develop transferable skills like communication, leadership, confidence, organisation, and more! You will get basic safeguarding training to work with children, and can pick up additional trainings like first aid, administration, accounts and team management. Someone in your team can act as a reference for a CV or job application. You are helping empower the next generation of girls and young women!\n\nBecome a volunteer - https://www.girlguidingscotland.org.uk/become-a-volunteer/ \n \nPVG (Disclosure Scotland): Yes, free of charge.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,Creative,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Open minded,Organised,Patient,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,No requirements, just a smile and a positive attitude!\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will get a basic level of safeguarding training to work with children, and a warm welcome into Girlguiding and what our organisation is all about.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nDifferent groups meet on different days of the week, so you can help out on the day that is best for you. We can be flexible if you can't commit to coming every week, and we only run during the school term times.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
