                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I1ihNYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I1ihNYAR/youth-group-leader-in-cambuslang",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Youth Group Leader in Cambuslang",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGirlguiding Cambuslang Division is part of Girlguiding Scotland, the leading charity for girls and young women in Scotland. \nGirlguiding helps members discover their full potential by having fun and enjoying new adventures.\n\nAt the heart of guiding are our regular group sessions, called unit meetings. These are run by volunteer teams of adult leaders, helpers, and young leaders. \n\nLeaders help to run our units, support the volunteer team, and are involved in planning and running the activities for girls with their fellow volunteers. You’ll be supported to complete our required Leadership qualification and receive training on everything from admin and finance to child safety. \n\nWe’re looking for volunteers in Cambuslang to support unit meetings for across our sections.\nRainbows are aged 4-7 and focus on fun, friendship and adventure.\nBrownies are aged 7-10 and focus on fun, adventure, and even first nights away!\nGuides run for those aged 10-14 and is a relaxed, safe space for young members to develop their interests and take on new challenges.\nRangers are aged 14-18, and are supported to be independent, take the lead on activities, and explore UK and international adventures!\n\nOur units meet on a Tuesday evening\n\nIf you're not ready to start the leadership qualification or you want something more flexible, register your interest in the same way and a senior volunteer will get in touch to chat about other ways to volunteer.\n\n## Experience required\n\n, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Open minded,Organised,Patient,Reliable / Dependable,Team Player,Trustworthy,\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a South Lanarkshire opportunity and takes place in   \nAcross South Lanarkshire,Cambuslang\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers can claim reasonable expenses, please speak to your local volunteer team about this",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
