                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H3iyoYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000H3iyoYAB/social-media-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-28",
                    "title": "Social Media Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Mindful Partnership is a charity committed to making mindfulness and compassionate living accessible for everyone. They offer tailored training, ongoing mentoring, workshops and retreats that provide the guidance and support needed to foster wellbeing, personal growth and stronger, more compassionate communities.\r\n\r\nWould you like to make a difference and develop your skills and experience to support them? They require a Social Media Assistant to develop their online presence and widen their reach increasing engagement and keeping the community updated about the organisation and the services available. This role involves:\r\n\r\n-Designing posters using Canva\r\n-Taking photos and videos of services in action\r\n-Uploading pictures and videos\r\n-Creating content and wording for social media posts\r\n-Monitoring social media engagement and responding to comments and questions\r\n\r\nIf you enjoy using social media and want to make a difference this could be the role for you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nKnowledge and confidence using social media is required. Volunteers should be organised and reliable with an ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to volunteer independently with support from local staff is essential\n\n## Training details\n\nA full induction and ongoing training will be provided.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity will take place in central Kirkcaldy with some travel required to take photos and/or videos. The role can also be home based.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses will be reimbursed at 45p per mile or public transport rates. Payments are made twice per month on the 15th and 30th and expenses can be reimbursed as incurred as required.",
