        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001ShZNxAAN",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001ShZNxAAN/equal-futures",
            "name": "Equal Futures",
            "description": "Equal Futures has been supporting people with an additional support need to make connections since its foundation by family carers in 2002. We work with adults (18 years plus) with an additional support need, this could be a learning disability or another significant lifelong condition, such as Down’s syndrome or autism.\r\nWe believe that people with Additional Support Needs are among some of the most isolated, our vision is a society without loneliness with your help we can try to achieve this for everyone. \r\nBefriending and Circle support can help someone with an additional support need make valuable connections: building their confidence, resilience and independence.\r\nOur services also provide reassurance and respite for their family members who have often undertaken a significant caring role. \r\nWe offer a flexible approach with services that are delivered at a time and pace to suit the individual and family at the centre of the support. The services we offer are entirely free of charge.",
            "website": "https://www.equalfutures.org.uk",
