        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001Shph8AAB",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001Shph8AAB/the-croft-visitors-support-and-advice-centre-hmp-barlinnie",
            "name": "The Croft, Visitors' Support and Advice Centre, HMP Barlinnie",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/TheCroftVisitorsSupportandAdviceCentreHMPBarlinnie",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Gz8SUYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Gz8SUYAZ/foodbank-helper-at-the-croft-support-and-advice-centre-at-hmp-barlinnie",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-20",
                    "title": "Foodbank helper at the Croft - Support and advice Centre at HMP Barlinnie",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFoodbank helper at the Croft - Support and advice Centre at HMP Barlinnie\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for foodbank helpers to support the work of The Croft at HMP Barlinnie and help make a positive difference to families and individuals experiencing food insecurity in our community.\n\nAs a foodbank helper, you will assist with:\n&bull; Preparing food bags for visitors\n&bull; Help to receive and organise the food bank delivery\n\nWe are currently looking for support on Tuesday mornings from 10am&ndash;12pm.\n\nThis is a great opportunity to get involved in meaningful community work, meet new people, and support a charity making a real impact.&nbsp;Volunteers will have the opportunity to gain accredited training, learn new skills in organisation, teamwork, and customer service, and gain experience in a community-focused, supportive environment. They will make a real difference for families during what can be a challenging time, meet new people and be part of a welcoming team, receive full induction and ongoing support, and be provided with a Croft volunteer T-shirt. If you are interested in becoming a foodbank helper or would like to find out more, we would love to hear from you.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nIf you are interested,&nbsp;please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when&nbsp;registered and&nbsp;logged in). You&nbsp;will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that&nbsp;doesn&rsquo;t&nbsp;work&nbsp;out,&nbsp;then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org.&nbsp;\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience required as full training will be provided\n\n## Travel details\n\nBy Car: Take exit 12 for Stepps and Riddrie. At Riddrie library, turn onto Teith Street, then left onto Smithycroft Road, and take the first right onto Lee Avenue, where the prison is located. By Bus: The most frequent buses to Barlinnie are 38, 38A, and 38C, operated by First Glasgow. These services run from Eastwood Toll through to Garthamlock/The Fort, passing both Queen Street and Central Stations in Glasgow City Centre—making them convenient for visitors using the rail network.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses, either public transport or mileage will be paid up to £6.30.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Gz8SUYAZ#role",
