        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001SiN4rAAF",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001SiN4rAAF/whiteinch-centre",
            "name": "Whiteinch Centre",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/WhiteinchCentre",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HTl9pYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HTl9pYAD/digital-engagement-lead",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-23",
                    "title": "Digital Engagement Lead",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDigital Engagement Lead\n\n## Description\n\nThe Whiteinch Centre - a community project in west Glasgow - seeks a&nbsp;Volunteer Digital Engagement Lead to play a key role in reducing digital exclusion and ensuring everyone has access to the benefits of technology.\n\nAre you passionate about helping others succeed? As a Volunteer Digital Engagement Lead, you&#39;ll empower learners to develop essential digital skills, build confidence with technology, and unlock new opportunities in work, learning, and everyday life. This is a rewarding role where you can make a lasting impact while developing your own professional skills and digital expertise.\n\nRole Overview\n\nAs a Volunteer Digital Engagement Lead, you will be responsible for:\n\n\n\t\n\tDeveloping comprehensive digital training programs tailored to various skill levels.\n\t\n\t\n\tCreating engaging and interactive learning materials that cater to diverse learning styles.\n\t\n\t\n\tDelivering training sessions &nbsp;in-person, ensuring a supportive and inclusive environment.\n\t\n\t\n\tEvaluating participants&rsquo; progress and adapting training methods to meet their needs.\n\t\n\t\n\tCollaborating with a passionate team to continuously improve our training offerings\n\t\n\n\nchanging lives through digital inclusion and confidence-building.\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). The coordinator will then contact you by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder for your emails, just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow at&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for someone who is:\nExperienced in digital tools and platforms, with a strong understanding of current technology trends.\nSkilled in creating educational content, with the ability to simplify complex concepts.\nAn excellent communicator and presenter, capable of engaging diverse audiences.\nPatient, empathetic, and supportive, committed to fostering a positive learning environment.\nCreative and adaptable, open to feedback and new ideas.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe centre is located in the North West Of Glasgow in Victoria Park Ward just off of Clydeside Express way and Dumbarton Road\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nOut of Pocket Expenses claimed monthly",
