        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001SikF6AAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001SikF6AAJ/st-marys-for-all",
            "name": "St Mary's for All",
            "description": "St Mary’s for All is a registered charity and social enterprise in Hamilton that offers four diverse fully accessible community spaces for hire and the Beech Tree Cafe, a community cafe serving a range of speciality coffees, teas, home baking, sandwiches and snacks. \n\nThe facility is open 9am-3pm, Monday to Saturday, and offers discounted rates for third sector organisations. For further information and to book, please see the charity's website.",
            "website": "https://www.stmarysforall.co.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC046051"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GtP4dYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GtP4dYAF/social-media-promotion-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-19",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-17",
                    "title": "Social Media & Promotion Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSt Mary’s for All Centre is a busy and vibrant community hub, and we want to share more of its stories, activities, and impact. We are looking for a creative volunteer to help with social media and promotion. This may include taking photographs at events where appropriate, helping draft social media posts, creating simple promotional content, sharing ideas for campaigns, and helping raise awareness of activities, volunteering opportunities, and room hire. This role would suit someone interested in digital content, photography, communications, or community storytelling. It is a chance to build practical experience while helping a local charity reach more people\n\n## Experience required\n\nSome confidence with social media or digital content would be helpful, but full professional experience is not needed. This role would suit someone who:\n\nEnjoys social media, photography, or creative communication\nHas good written communication skills\nIs interested in sharing positive community stories\nWould like to build experience in promotion or content creation\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training\nOngoing support from the Volunteer Coordinator\nGuidance on tone of voice, permissions, and safe use of photographs\nSupport with understanding the centre’s activities and priorities\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible across the week\nMostly weekday mornings and afternoons\nSome occasional evening or weekend event coverage may be available\nThis opportunity is flexible. Volunteers may contribute regularly each week or support around specific events, campaigns, or activities depending on availability.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis role will mainly be based at St Mary’s for All Centre in Hamilton, particularly when capturing activity content. Some content preparation may be possible remotely by agreement. The centre is accessible by train and bus.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable agreed travel expenses for centre-based volunteering can be discussed in advance with the Volunteer Coordinator.\n\n## Taster details\n\nAn induction is available. Volunteers can meet with the team to learn about the centre’s communication style, review examples of content, and discuss their own interests and skills.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FAfJLev2v3jaYKXUiNUL3CmhyKWx1%2FXcQhz1fPV3B7Cjr6-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=a8b8ebcc-1ee9-4cfe-8a96-651ad7a4d81e",
