                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GtRw1YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GtRw1YAF/gardening-and-outdoor-project-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-19",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-17",
                    "title": "Gardening and outdoor project volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSt Mary’s for All Centre is developing its outdoor spaces to make them more attractive, welcoming, and useful for the community. We are looking for volunteers to help with gardening and outdoor projects, including raised beds, planting areas, seasonal tidying, watering, and general upkeep. Volunteers may also support small community growing projects or help prepare outdoor areas for activities. This opportunity is ideal for someone who enjoys being outdoors, likes practical tasks, or wants to contribute to a greener and more pleasant community environment. No expert gardening knowledge is required — enthusiasm and a willingness to help are more important.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous gardening experience is necessary. This role would suit someone who:\n\nEnjoys being outdoors\nHas an interest in gardening, growing, or nature\nIs happy to take part in practical tasks\nWants to help improve a valued community space\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining available:\n\nInduction training\nOngoing volunteer support\nGuidance on tasks, tools, and safe working\nSupport from the Volunteer Coordinator and relevant centre contacts\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nVolunteering can be flexible and seasonal. Some volunteers may wish to help regularly, while others may prefer occasional gardening days or project-based support.\n\n## Travel details\n\nGardening activities take place at St Mary’s for All Centre in Hamilton. The centre is accessible by public transport and within walking distance of Hamilton Central railway station. Details will be provided before volunteering begins.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable agreed travel expenses can be discussed in advance with the Volunteer Coordinator, in line with the centre’s volunteer expenses arrangements\n\n## Taster details\n\nAn induction is available. Volunteers can visit the centre, see the outdoor areas, and discuss the types of tasks they would be comfortable supporting.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FAfJLev2v3jaYKXUiNUL3CmhyKWx1%2FsrSBwDNQHYAMxo2M-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=916f7f10-4144-4f45-93ab-292b5e184e18",
                    "role": {
