                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GtQ8jYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GtQ8jYAF/meet-greet-front-of-house-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-19",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-17",
                    "title": "Meet & Greet / Front of House Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSt Mary’s for All Centre is a busy, welcoming community hub in Hamilton. We are looking for friendly volunteers to help create a positive first impression for visitors, centre users, and community groups. This role is about helping people feel comfortable, included, and able to find their way around the centre. Volunteers may greet people as they arrive, provide simple information about activities taking place, direct visitors to rooms, and offer light front-of-house support. It is a great opportunity for someone who enjoys meeting people, wants to build confidence, and would like to play a visible role in a much-loved local community space.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience is required. This role would suit someone who:\n\nEnjoys meeting people and making them feel welcome\nIs friendly, patient, and approachable\nCan communicate clearly and kindly\nWould like to build confidence in a people-facing role\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining available:\n\nInduction training\nOngoing support and guidance\nSupport from the Volunteer Coordinator\nInformation about the centre, its activities, and how to welcome visitors confidently\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThis opportunity can be flexible. Volunteers may support weekly, fortnightly, or at agreed times that suit both the volunteer and the centre. We are happy to discuss a manageable commitment\n\n## Travel details\n\nSt Mary’s for All Centre is located in central Hamilton and is accessible by local bus and train services. Hamilton Central railway station is within walking distance. Full address and travel information will be provided to volunteers before starting.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable agreed travel expenses can be discussed in advance with the Volunteer Coordinator, in line with the centre’s volunteer expenses arrangements.\n\n## Taster details\n\nAn induction is available. New volunteers will have the chance to visit the centre, meet the Volunteer Coordinator, learn more about the role, and discuss what support would help them feel confident before beginning.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FAfJLev2v3jaYKXUiNUL3CmhyKWx1%2FV21BnS3Joaix8blh-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=b7d41622-8b22-4f2e-8e28-da10ff88fc49",
