        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003J0BMjAAN",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003J0BMjAAN/leith-sea-cadets",
            "name": "Leith Sea Cadets",
            "description": "The aim of Leith Sea Cadets is to equip young people with the skills they need for life. We help young people develop teamwork, leadership, determination, resilience and confidence - all essential skills! We follow the rank structure of the Royal Navy, but most importantly, we have FUN!",
            "website": "https://www.sea-cadets.org/leith/get-in-touch",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GwL66YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GwL66YAF/facilities-maintenance-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-19",
                    "title": "Facilities & Maintenance Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nMaintain facility records, to manage a safe, effective and successful Sea Cadet unit.\n\n## Experience required\n\nSome experience in administration and practical life experience will help. Having the right attitude and a passion for improving the lives of young people are most important! If you think the following sounds like you, please get in touch: you are reliable, honest and trustworthy; you are a good communicator; you enjoy working with a team; you are committed to safeguarding and supporting people from diverse backgrounds.\n\n## Training details\n\nNo experience is required! We provide online induction training, such as safeguarding and information management. \n\nRequirements: All candidates will have an interview. If successful, all volunteers undergo a Disclosure Scotland check, which is paid for by us. You will then complete our online induction process and short online training courses.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThis role can be flexibly negotiated with us in order to ensure tasks are completed in a timely way.  Some of the tasks could be performed remotely.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAll of these roles can be carried out remotely or on a hybrid basis - you choose how often you wish to volunteer and for how long! Our committee meet once every two months.\nSea Cadets Leith is located in the Prince of Wales Dock, Leith, Edinburgh, EH6 7DX. Cadets meet weekly on Tuesdays and Thursdays, 6.45pm - 9.30pm. Please note that we are behind a gate, so you will need to be let in. There is plenty of parking through the gate. Our closest tram stop is Port of Leith. Please let us know if you would like to visit and have any access requirements.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses for training courses are paid for. We will pay for your Disclosure Scotland background check.\n\n## Taster details\n\nWhat do you gain? Grow your network - meet new people and join our wonderful community. Gain new skills and experiences for your CV. Access free learning as a volunteer – some of our volunteers have completed degree-level management courses! Flexible roles – you choose your hours and days. Many roles are fully remote and flexible!",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FTqlqrBWy95el4YvWXlix99mzCE42%2FErDWxxzPscXy0RjN-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=35ac4d96-4c0e-47b5-bfc2-ccdc6988feb2",
