                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Helplines",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Helplines"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VupDYAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VupDYAAZ/fundraising-ambassador",
                    "publishStart": "2023-06-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Fundraising Ambassador",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nMDUK need Charity Ambassadors to help develop engagement across the country, to maximise opportunities to raise funds and increase support from the Community.\n\n## Description\n\nAs an Ambassador you will be a representative for Muscular Dystrophy UK. You will use your influence and contacts with local small businesses and individuals your local area to help build Muscular Dystrophy UK networks and fundraising partnerships. \r\n\r\nYou will be confident in speaking about the cause and the work of the charity; developing relationships with key supporters and individuals as part of the process. Raising awareness of who we are and what we do is very important to the charity so we are looking for a proactive volunteer who will seek out speaking opportunities and make asks on behalf of the charity to attend events where further awareness can be raised.\n\n## Experience required\n\n· Excellent oral communication\r\n· Confident to deliver key messages clearly and enthusiastically\r\n· Strong communication and influencing skills, especially over the phone and on email\r\n· Relationship building – when attending events you are the eyes and ears for your Regional Development Manager. There is great potential to develop leads and opportunities for the charity.\r\n· An understanding of how a charity partnership can benefit a company\r\n· You will need be adaptable to different situations\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2-3 hours a week, but flexible for the right individual\n\n## Travel details\n\nHome based/ out in Dundee community\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPayment of out of pocket expenses will be agreed in advance. Mileage of 45p per mile can be paid for\r\n\r\ndistances travelled to attend fundraising events, full guidance will be given during volunteer induction.\n\n## Taster details\n\nThere is always opportunity to see if it fits your life and try other types of volunteering to suit you.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VupDYAAZ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Fundraising Ambassador",
                        "description": "· Excellent oral communication\r\n· Confident to deliver key messages clearly and enthusiastically\r\n· Strong communication and influencing skills, especially over the phone and on email\r\n· Relationship building – when attending events you are the eyes and ears for your Regional Development Manager. There is great potential to develop leads and opportunities for the charity.\r\n· An understanding of how a charity partnership can benefit a company\r\n· You will need be adaptable to different situations",
                        "commitment": "2-3 hours a week, but flexible for the right individual",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VupDYAAZ/fundraising-ambassador?#modal_register_a0g0800000VupDYAAZ",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": true,
