                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VupDaAAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VupDaAAJ/fundraising-group-member",
                    "publishStart": "2023-06-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Fundraising Group Member",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nMDUK is offering this exciting opportunity to create a brand new Fundraising Group in Dundee to raise vital funds and awareness, so we can support more families who need our support in Scotland.\n\n## Description\n\nOur fundraising groups are the local face of MDUK, raising vital funds and constantly raising the profile of the charity so that we can reach more people and their families affected by a muscle wasting condition.\r\n\r\nIn order to be able to provide everyone the help and support they need; we are asking for your skills and enthusiasm to help us grow our fundraising groups! We need people to join our various groups across the UK and make Muscular Dystrophy UK the best-known local charity!\n\n## Experience required\n\n· Excellent oral communication\r\n· Confident to deliver key messages clearly and enthusiastically\r\n· Strong communication and influencing skills, especially over the phone and on email\r\n· Relationship building – when attending events you are the eyes and ears for your Regional Development Manager. There is great potential to develop leads and opportunities for the charity.\r\n· An understanding of how a charity partnership can benefit a company\r\n· You will need be adaptable to different situations.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible opportunity for the individual who can get involved in weekly or monthly activity dependent on other commitments\n\n## Travel details\n\nHome based/ out in Dundee community\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPayment of out of pocket expenses will be agreed in advance. Mileage of 45p per mile can be paid for\r\n\r\ndistances travelled to attend fundraising events, full guidance will be given during volunteer induction.\n\n## Taster details\n\nYou can’t learn about a role until often being in it so always opportunity for consult.",
