            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNscyAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNscyAAD/minute-secretary-for-community-council",
                    "publishStart": "2021-10-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Minute Secretary for Community Council",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGet to know what is happening in your local community. Meet new people online and in person. Gain administrative experience by taking meeting notes and typing them in a pre set meeting template.\r\n\r\nBonnyrigg and Lasswade Community Council would like to appoint a Minute Secretary to help with their meetings. This would be ideal for a person with a bit of time on their hands or maybe to gain some adminstrative experience. \r\nThe Community Council at present meet over the Zoom platform and attendance is over 10 meetings per year, 18.45-21.00 on the second Thursday of each month.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood listening and note taking skills. Access to a laptop or other device is essential.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFive hours per month. Second Thursday of the month for ten months of the year\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses will be paid as required for each meeting",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNscyAAD#role",
