                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-08",
                    "title": "Emergency Department Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nKey duties:\r\n• To meet and greet patients in the triage area and ensure they are seated in \r\nthe right waiting area\r\n• Serving refreshments and replenishing water jugs\r\n• Keeping the waiting areas tidy\r\n• Retrieve wheelchairs and return to the appropriate locations\r\n• To ensure patients know where facilities are located\r\n• To carry out Patient Experience surveys, helping those who require \r\nassistance where appropriate\r\n• Spending time with patients who are on their own\r\n• Referring any patient concerns about their clinical care to a nurse\r\nPersonal specification:\r\n• This is not a clinical role and you will not be shadowing or assisting staff \r\nhowever volunteering in this demanding environment will expose you to many \r\naspects of the Emergency Department so being calm and composed in these \r\nsituations is essential\r\n• Attention to detail\r\n• Ability to change direction of work to meet new demands\r\n• Good listening and communication skills are essential\r\n• Patience and composure\r\n• A caring, sympathetic, sensitive manner and a non-judgemental approach\r\n• Reliable/ dependable and flexible\r\n• Understanding of confidentiality\r\n• Have a positive outlook and enthusiastic approach",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNtWMAA1#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Emergency Department Volunteer",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNtWMAA1/emergency-department-volunteer?#modal_register_a0g0800000QNtWMAA1",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
