        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00108000030wiNSAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00108000030wiNSAAY/latnem-peer-support-aka-lets-all-talk-north-east-mums",
            "name": "LATNEM Peer Support (AKA Let’s All Talk North East Mums)",
            "description": "Did you know that around 1 in 5 Mums and birthing people will develop a mental illness in the ante/perinatal period? At LATNEM (AKA Let’s All Talk North East Mums) we have lived experience. We’ve been there and now provide a safe, free peer support group for mums and birthing people in the North East of Scotland. LATNEM is registered as a Scottish Charitable Incorporated Organisation with the Office of the Scottish Charity Regulator (OSCR)-registration number: SC051029.",
            "website": "https://latnem.org/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC051029"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Women",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Women"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNu9sAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNu9sAAD/volunteer-peer-supporters",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer Peer Supporters",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nA Peer supporter at LATNEM is a mum with lived experience of mental ill health who wants to share her own journey as a path finder, giving hope to others. A mum or birthing person with a passion for helping others. \r\n\r\nThe role involves preparing the space before a meeting and tidying up afterwards. You would help to prepare refreshments and make our service users feel welcome.\r\n\r\nYou would join the meeting as a mum with lived experience of mental ill health and encourage conversation, build supportive and respectful relationships with members, supporting others using the personal experience and confidence you have gained having overcome similar challenges. \r\n\r\nYou would be able to talk openly and honestly about your experiences, demonstrating that mental ill health is nothing to be ashamed of. \r\n\r\nYou would assist people to identify their own recovery goals, providing information and support to family and friends of members where required and signposting members to professional services, other 3rd Sector support. \r\n\r\nOur Aberdeen meeting is held at the community centre in Bucksburn on a Thursday evening and Friday morning.  All help during any of these times is greatly appreciated and makes a real difference. \r\n\r\nFor further information please contact Gill Skene, Volunteer Manager at email: gill@latnem.org or telephone  07392977339\r\n\r\nFurther details are also available on our website at: https://latnem.org/\n\n## Description\n\nA Peer supporter at LATNEM is a mum with lived experience of mental ill health who wants to share her own journey as a path finder, giving hope to others. A mum or birthing person with a passion for helping others. \r\n\r\nThe role involves preparing the space before a meeting and tidying up afterwards. You would help to prepare refreshments and make our service users feel welcome.\r\n\r\nYou would join the meeting as a mum with lived experience of mental ill health and encourage conversation, build supportive and respectful relationships with members, supporting others using the personal experience and confidence you have gained having overcome similar challenges. \r\n\r\nYou would be able to talk openly and honestly about your experiences, demonstrating that mental ill health is nothing to be ashamed of. \r\n\r\nYou would assist people to identify their own recovery goals, providing information and support to family and friends of members where required and signposting members to professional services, other 3rd Sector support. \r\n\r\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided to all volunteers. Peer supporters will be offered the opportunity to complete their Mental Health First Aid as well as other relevant training, subject to a commitment of volunteering time.  \r\n\r\nOur Aberdeen meeting is held at the community centre in Bucksburn on a Thursday evening and Friday morning.  All help during any of these times is greatly appreciated and makes a real difference. \r\n\r\nFor further information please contact Gill Skene, Volunteer Manager at email: gill@latnem.org or telephone  07392977339\r\n\r\nFurther details are also available on our website at: https://latnem.org/\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided to all volunteers. Peer supporters will be offered the opportunity to complete their Mental Health First Aid as well as other relevant training, subject to a commitment of volunteering time.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nOur Aberdeen meeting is held at the community centre in Bucksburn on a Thursday evening and Friday morning.  All help during any of these times is greatly appreciated and makes a real difference.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur Aberdeen meeting is held at the community centre in Bucksburn.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nApproved travel expenses are paid monthly.",
