        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00108000030y1GeAAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00108000030y1GeAAI/mcr-pathways-falkirk",
            "name": "MCR Pathways - Falkirk",
            "description": "Our aim is to help young people unlock their potential, no matter their circumstances. Working together with our inspiring mentor community and partners, we can help young people to realise their skills and progress onto a positive destination. Our vision is for all young people to experience equality of education outcomes, career opportunities and life chances.",
            "website": "https://mcrpathways.org/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC045816"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNxm6AAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNxm6AAD/volunteer-mentor",
                    "publishStart": "2024-12-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Volunteer Mentor",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nChanging lives through the power of mentoring.\r\n\r\nImagine a young person with incredible potential, but no one to help them see it. You can change that by sharing just one hour a week. Become a volunteer mentor with MCR Pathways.\r\n\r\nJust one hour a week can ignite the vital spark in a young person. Help confidence, ambition, and positive futures to glow. \r\n\r\nWe match our volunteers with a young person who has similar interests, and we also consider factors such as career aspirations, background, and personality. \r\n\r\nMentoring takes place in Falkirk High, Graeme High, Larbert High, Braes High, Grangemouth High, Bo'ness Academy and St Mungo's. We also operate in Forth Valley College. Each mentoring session lasts an hour with the aim to build a relationship with the young person as a trusted adult, whilst providing them with a listening ear and supporting them to achieve their goals.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for people who are willing to put the needs of a young person first and commit to meeting them for an hour a week. Anyone can become a mentor.\n\n## Training details\n\nMentors will have a 1:1 conversation with our mentor services team followed by a 3 hour training session. Additional safeguarding training is provided as well as CPD sessions.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMeet for one hour per week for at least one year (school term only). \r\nThe time can be arranged to suit your availability. \r\nFor our schools the times are Mon-Fri, 9am-3:30pm.\r\nFor our college settings, we can offer more flexibility for the time of the mentoring sessions.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMentoring takes place at a secondary school or at one of our college campuses within Forth Valley.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo travel expenses available.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://mcrpathways.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/MCR_LOGO-white.svg",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNxm6AAD#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Mentor",
                        "description": "We are looking for people who are willing to put the needs of a young person first and commit to meeting them for an hour a week. Anyone can become a mentor.",
