        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00108000039Z69VAAS",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00108000039Z69VAAS/slamannan-action-group",
            "name": "Slamannan Action Group",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEngagement",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Engagement"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000He7sDYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000He7sDYAR/treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-05",
                    "title": "Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSlamannan Action Group is a volunteer run community organisation. The Group provides a range of community events and activities in Slamannan for all in the community. \r\n\r\nSlamannan Action Group are currently looking for a volunteer Treasurer.  As Treasurer your role is to be responsible for the accurate and confidential keeping of the Slamannan Action Group’s financial details. You will also be responsible for supplying information to, and supporting the development of funding applications along with Slamannan Action Group's Chair and Secretary. \r\n\r\nTasks include:\r\n*Managing the Club’s money\r\n*Keeping accurate records\r\n*Paying bills\r\n*Collecting membership donations \r\n*Preparing the accounts for inspection at the Annual General Meeting (AGM)\r\n*Appropriately storing financial records\r\n\r\nThe majority of this role could be done remotely with the exception of attending meetings and presenting the up to date accounts.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood people skills.\r\nUnderstanding good governance.\r\nAbility to keep accurate financial records.\r\nRespecting confidentiality.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe Treasurer will be a member of Slamannan Action Group's Management Committee.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n3 hours per fortnight. \r\nMonthly meetings.\n\n## Travel details\n\nSlamannan Action Group meets in Slamannan Bowling Club, Station Road, FK1 3BQ.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are NOT available.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000He7sDYAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Treasurer",
