                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhvNtAAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhvNtAAJ/junior-environmental-conservation-volunteering",
                    "publishStart": "2023-04-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-05",
                    "title": "Junior Environmental Conservation Volunteering",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSouth Ayrshire Council Ranger Service are offering the opportunity for young persons aged between 13-18 to learn new, or develop existing, skills in practical outdoor work. These sessions will introduce essential environmental conservation skills like basic bushcraft, use of manual hand tools and invasive non-native species control. The programme will run on a fortnightly basis (every second Saturday) and from 10am-12pm. Booking is essential so to book a place, or for more information, please feel free to contact the ranger service via ranger.service@south-ayrshire.gov.uk\r\n\r\nSessions are suitable for one-off volunteering so attendance is not required at every session. \r\nOur meeting point is Rozelle Lodge, Rozelle Park, Monument Road, Ayr, KA7 4NQ\n\n## Experience required\n\nWilling to be outdoors and ready to learn and be active.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fb36e10ef-038b-4444-ae6e-e756c3c21451%2F0nFCUqNjeiXPIFO483j0BVWArU43%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=31357ba7-45b5-4fce-b8ed-c5c27a51c7e7",
