            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BDiHqYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BDiHqYAL/logistics-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-25",
                    "title": "Logistics Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAs a BRAVEHOUND Logistics Volunteer you will help as needed with veteran transport, delivering dog food, transporting dogs to the vets and any other logistics tasks that we need help with.\n\n## Description\n\nBravehound aims to help heal the invisible wounds of military veterans with their specially trained assistance dogs. They provide assistance dogs to veterans who have a clinical diagnosis of a mental health condition such as Post Traumatic Stress Disorder, depression and anxiety.\r\nAs a Bravehound Logistics Volunteer you will help as needed with veteran transport, delivering dog food, transporting dogs to the vets and any other logistics tasks that they need help with.\r\nThis opportunity takes place on an ad hoc basis, as there is no set timeline for when appointment will be needed.\r\nYou may drive a charity vehicle and as such need to have a full UK clean driving license. A PVG is required for this role.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou must have a full, clean UK driving license.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers are given an induction to Bravehound, and will be given any relevant training for the role. Support will be available from the operations manager.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTravel will be required within Fife and beyond, and a charity vehicle will be available.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses are reimbursed.",
