            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000003VRv3YAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000003VRv3YAG/trustee-scalloway-youth-and-community-centre",
                    "publishStart": "2024-05-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-03",
                    "title": "Trustee - Scalloway Youth and Community Centre",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Board of Trustees are urgently looking for more volunteers to join them.\r\nIf you are 18 or over and this is something you would like to be involved with, but not sure what is expected of you, then please come along to one of the open days to see what happens in the Centre and learn more about the Board of Trustees.\r\nScalloway Youth & Community Centre is a charity (SCO47950) and was built in 1996.  Last year the Centre had triple glazed windows installed and  insulation this year and plan to look at alternate heating systems to help become more energy efficient in the future.  \r\nThere is a main hall and sports cupboard.  There are three table tennis tables, boccia, exercise mats and equipment as well as a variety of sports equipment.  Though not quite a full sized badminton court, the hall has been lined to play a variety of sports.\r\nThe kitchen is fully equipped for cooking and serving hot food as well as having a good stock of crockery and cutlery.\r\nThe café area has a servery, TV and games console and a well stocked arts and crafts cupboard.\r\nUpstairs has a games room with pool table, full sized snooker table and dart board as well as a TV and games console.\r\nThe Music room has a drum kit and guitars, amps and keyboard for jamming sessions as well as a large TV suitable for a variety of purposes and a computer with recording software.  It is a great space for bands to practice and also used as a meeting room.\r\nWe are accessible to all and have a chair lift up to the second floor.\n\n## Experience required\n\nIf you are 18 or over and this is something you would like to be involved with, but not sure what is expected of you, then please come along to one of the open days to see what happens in the Centre and learn more about the Board of Trustees.\n\n## Travel details\n\nScalloway",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000003VRv3YAG#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Trustee - Scalloway Youth and Community Centre",
                        "description": "If you are 18 or over and this is something you would like to be involved with, but not sure what is expected of you, then please come along to one of the open days to see what happens in the Centre and learn more about the Board of Trustees.",
