            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ILSgTYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ILSgTYAX/houses2homes-volunteer-homelessness-project",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-04",
                    "title": "Houses2Homes Volunteer – Homelessness Project",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHouses2Homes Volunteer – Homelessness Project\n\n## Description\n\nHelp people moving on from homelessness make a fresh start.\n\nThe Halliday Foundation is looking for volunteers to support our Houses2Homes project, providing furniture, white goods and essential household items to people and families who need help turning an empty property into a home.\n\nThere are different ways to get involved, including:\n\n&bull; Helping our van driver collect donated furniture and white goods.\n&bull; Delivering essential items to people moving into their homes.\n&bull; Helping safely load and unload the van.\n&bull; Cleaning, preparing and organising donated items at our Royston warehouse.\n&bull; Keeping the warehouse tidy and helping prepare items for delivery.\n\nYou&rsquo;ll be part of a friendly team making a practical difference to people affected by homelessness and poverty across Glasgow.\n\nDriving is not essential&mdash;you can help as a van helper or support the warehouse. Collection and delivery tasks involve lifting and carrying, so please let us know what you feel comfortable doing so we can discuss suitable tasks.\n\nWhether you have relevant experience or simply want to give your time to help others, we would love to hear from you.\n\nTo find out more, email Admin@thehallidayfoundation.org.uk or call 0141 258 4728.\n\nIf you are interested,&nbsp;please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when&nbsp;registered and&nbsp;logged in). You&nbsp;will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that&nbsp;doesn&rsquo;t&nbsp;work&nbsp;out,&nbsp;then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe’re looking for reliable, friendly volunteers who work well with others and treat everyone with kindness and respect. You should be willing to follow safety guidance and respect the privacy of the people we support.\n\nNo previous experience or driving licence is essential. Collection and delivery roles involve physical tasks, including lifting and carrying furniture and white goods with the team. Warehouse tasks can be discussed to suit your abilities.",
