        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0010800003K9FhBAAV",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0010800003K9FhBAAV/aberdeen-fundraising-committee-for-the-leprosy-mission-scotland",
            "name": "Aberdeen Fundraising Committee for The Leprosy Mission Scotland",
            "description": "The Leprosy Mission Scotland is the Scottish partner in The Leprosy Mission Global Fellowship’s effort to defeat leprosy and transform lives. Everything we do in Scotland  help us move towards our ultimate goal of making leprosy a thing of the past.",
            "website": "https://leprosymission.scot/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC022411"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FundraisingFunding",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Fundraising / Funding"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Qhk5LAAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Qhk5LAAR/committee-members",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Committee Members",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThis is a great opportunity to be involved with a Christian Medical charity to raise funds for a neglected tropical disease. Leprosy still exists in over 120 countries with approximately 200,000 new cases every year despite there being a cure. \r\n\r\nThe group has been in existence in the local area for over 50 years. We meet 4 times per year to organise events eg coffee mornings, concerts, participating in sponsored walk such as the Kilt Walk and running events. Speaking opportunities are available to inform others of the charity.\r\n\r\nWe have a good relationship with various local churches who support us and send in donations.\r\n\r\nYou would be volunteering with a small group of friendly , welcoming people to use your ideas to participate in and enhance fundraising events. All new ideas for fundraising are always welcomed. \r\n\r\nWe feel new members to the group would enhance and refresh what we do.\r\n\r\nA warm welcome is extended to attend a meeting to decide whether this is something you would enjoy and find as rewarding as we do. \r\n\r\nThe Leprosy Mission Scotland ( Registered Scottish Charity SC022411 ) is part of The Leprosy Mission International.\r\n\r\nFor more information/to help please contact Stella Anderson, Chair at email stellaanderson20@gmail.com or telephone 07946626568.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteer.  Includes initial meeting with Chair and one other to chat informally about the charity and give written information and guide to relevant websites.  Introduction to our committee by attending a meeting for the volunteer to decide whether they wish to join. Full information about The Leprosy Mission will be given. Support at our events.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available for volunteers to help. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe meet four times each year to plan activities in a relaxed environment. At present we meet in Milltimber at the home of one of our committee members.\r\n\r\nThe coffee mornings are in Cults at Cults Kirk Centre or St Marys Church of Scotland in King Street, Aberdeen. Venues for other events vary but are usually within the city.",
