            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000EjGYPYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000EjGYPYA3/assistant-footballsports-coach-youth-team",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-12",
                    "title": "Assistant Football/Sports Coach (Youth Team)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Central Park Community Trust is a community-based football and sports charity which aims to give opportunities to all whether looking to play, coach or be involved in sport and football. Our Assistant Coaches will be supporting our lead coaches with delivery of fun recreational football & sports sessions to children aged between 3-12 years of age.  We offer a clear progression pathway for our volunteers, with many of our previous volunteers becoming lead coaches, contract roles/positions, with some now coaching in the United States. At our Charity Trust we ensure everyone is treated the same from volunteers to management, with all individuals being supported in their own pathway. The Trust will cover the cost of all Scottish FA coaching courses, First Aid, Child Well-being and any other courses an individual would like to attend.\n\n## Experience required\n\nDuring the activity sessions we ask that all our coaches (whether lead or assisting) are enthusiastic and join in as much as possible. Although this can be built over the weeks you attend.\r\n\r\nBe committed as much as you can. Begin with volunteering 1 hour minimum per week, and if you enjoy then hours can be increased\r\n\r\nCommunication - Community with Development Manager and Lead Coaches. We totally understand how busy everyone is with studying, work and home life - so if you are unable to attend for any reason, dropping us a text to say or a quick call is perfect, and we appreciate this communication.\n\n## Training details\n\nAn induction will be provided by the Development Manager and Lead Coaches. Volunteers will have the opportunity to complete FA coaching courses, First Aid, Child Wellbeing and any other appropriate courses for the role. The courses will be fully funded by the organisation'\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe deliver our fun activities in the Cowdenbeath and Lochgelly Communities. With the majority of sessions being schools. Assistant Coaches are required to make their own way to sessions however our lead coach at sessions can support with transport if they are going in the same direction or nearby.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses will be reimbursed for travel by bus or rail. Receipts will be required.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
