                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000DJRrRYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000DJRrRYAX/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-08",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nEnquiries can be sent to  dean.ewing@cowdenitc.com or 07791 801557\n\n## Description\n\nHelp us continue to grow and make a difference in the Cowdenbeath Area!\r\n\r\nThe Central Park Community Trust aka Cowden in the Community was formed as the Charitable arm of Cowdenbeath Football Club in 2021 to promote health and wellbeing initiatives within the Cowdenbeath Area. From initially providing football sessions for children and adults, the Trust has grown to provide physical and wellbeing activity sessions for ages 18 months to 80 plus years.\r\n\r\nThe Board of 5 Trustees, 2 full time staff and part time staff delivered over 2500 individual sessions in 2024/25.\r\n\r\nWorking with partners including the Scottish Football Association and Active Fife, the Trust is delivering Scottish Government funded programmes within local Primary and High Schools which seek to tackle issues caused by inequality and poverty.\r\n\r\nAs our organisation grows and increases its scope, the Trust needs enthusiastic people to help take it to the next level\n\n## Experience required\n\nPrior experience is not essential but experience in Charity governance, finance and legal matters would be beneficial. Community minded with a willingness to help and inspire others.\n\n## Training details\n\nStaff will provide induction training and Trustees will provide ongoing support\n\n## Travel details\n\nMeetings take place every month on a Wednesday evening in Cowdenbeath\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPayment of travel expenses will be considered on an individual basis",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
