                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pc738AAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pc738AAB/gardenerhandyman",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Gardener/Handyman",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThis role works alongside the relevant Locality Link Workers and New Scots to support the successful development of a new Sustainable Growing project for New Scots, based in the shared space of Eglinton Park Community Gardens. It will provide additional expertise, guidance and physical handyman/gardening skills to assist in the preparation of areas for growing vegetables and flowers and ensure ongoing successful growth and harvesting.\r\n\r\nTime commitment: Tuesday and/or Wednesday mornings with some extra possible\r\n\r\nMain Tasks\r\n\r\nVegetable & flower growing. Supporting New Scots to develop gardening skills.\r\n Making planters and structures as needed. \r\nSupporting the project’s collaborative role within the shared gardens\n\n## Experience required\n\nE = Essential D = Desirable\r\nGood knowledge/experience of growing vegetables/ flowers (E) \r\nPatience and sensitivity to the needs and culture of New Scots (E) (Support will be offered) \r\nGood people skills especially where language may be a barrier (E) \r\nReliability and commitment to the project (E) \r\n Able to travel to Eglinton Park at least once a week. North Ayrshire Council supports volunteer travel expenses if required. \r\nKnowledge/experience of building garden structures, planters etc (D)",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pc738AAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Gardener/Handyman",
                        "description": "E = Essential D = Desirable\r\nGood knowledge/experience of growing vegetables/ flowers (E) \r\nPatience and sensitivity to the needs and culture of New Scots (E) (Support will be offered) \r\nGood people skills especially where language may be a barrier (E) \r\nReliability and commitment to the project (E) \r\n Able to travel to Eglinton Park at least once a week. North Ayrshire Council supports volunteer travel expenses if required. \r\nKnowledge/experience of building garden structures, planters etc (D)",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pc738AAB/gardenerhandyman?#modal_register_a0g0800000Pc738AAB",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
                    },
