                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pc739AAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pc739AAB/esol-language-buddy",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "ESOL Language Buddy",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNorth Ayrshire Council ESOL team are looking for volunteers for the role of Language Buddy, ideally based in Scotland. This role requires you to offer a couple of hours a week (flexible) to give English Conversation practice via zoom to our ESOL learners either in 1-1 or in small groups. This is a great way to gain work experience whilst providing opportunities to people with refugee experiences with their acquisition of English. You do not need to be a native English speaker; we actively welcome applications from people who have learned English as second language.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPatience, understanding and empathy for learners for whom English is not their first language  \r\nAble to commit to scheduled day/time \r\nReliability, commitment and passion for supporting learning) \r\nAwareness of learner-centred approach or willingness to learn \r\nRespectful of the different needs and cultures of individuals \r\nRespond positively to feedback (E)\r\nKnowledge of working with learners with literacy support needs",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pc739AAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "ESOL Language Buddy",
                        "description": "Patience, understanding and empathy for learners for whom English is not their first language  \r\nAble to commit to scheduled day/time \r\nReliability, commitment and passion for supporting learning) \r\nAwareness of learner-centred approach or willingness to learn \r\nRespectful of the different needs and cultures of individuals \r\nRespond positively to feedback (E)\r\nKnowledge of working with learners with literacy support needs",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pc739AAB/esol-language-buddy?#modal_register_a0g0800000Pc739AAB",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
                    },
