                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pc73DAAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pc73DAAR/homework-helper",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Homework Helper",
                    "description": "## Description\n\n Homework Helper \r\nNorth Ayrshire Council’s Community Learning & Development Team works across North Ayrshire supporting new families to the area to successfully integrate.\r\n\r\nThe Homework Helper role responds to an identified need within some  families, where English is not the home language. Parents, therefore, may require additional support to help their school age children in their education.  This is a new development in our work and the Homework Helper role may take two forms:\r\n\r\nVolunteering within specific after school homework clubs  where there are enough children to enable a small group approach.\r\n\r\n    2. Volunteering to support individual children and families with homework within school or community venues.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPatience, understanding and empathy for learners for whom English is not their first language\r\nReasonable grasp of English, Maths and other primary school subjects (or specific knowledge in secondary school subjects, as appropriate) \r\nStrong communication skills and determination/problem solving approach (E) \r\nReliability, commitment and passion for supporting learning (E) \r\nRespectful of the different needs and cultures of individuals \r\nExperience of teaching, educational support",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pc73DAAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Homework Helper",
                        "description": "Patience, understanding and empathy for learners for whom English is not their first language\r\nReasonable grasp of English, Maths and other primary school subjects (or specific knowledge in secondary school subjects, as appropriate) \r\nStrong communication skills and determination/problem solving approach (E) \r\nReliability, commitment and passion for supporting learning (E) \r\nRespectful of the different needs and cultures of individuals \r\nExperience of teaching, educational support",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pc73DAAR/homework-helper?#modal_register_a0g0800000Pc73DAAR",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
                    },
