                    "title": "Befrienders for Young people  (ASN)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWould you like the opportunity to make a positive impact in helping young people get ready for life after leaving school? \nSereniti supports neurodiverse children, young people and their families in the Aberdeen and Aberdeenshire community (Aged 5 - 18).  A Young person volunteer  ( minimum age is 18 ) will support our young person on a one-to-one basis through compassion and kindness in establishing a trusting friendship. Befrienders will support young people with attending community activities and commuting on local buses within Aberdeen, reducing loneliness and increasing self-esteem, confidence while promoting independence.\n Our volunteers are expected to commit a few hours a week, Activities will be after school hours, weekdays, and on Saturdays.\nWe will provide you with all of the necessary training and support to carry out your responsibilities.\n All assistance will make a difference and be highly appreciated. We expect a six-month commitment from our befriender volunteers for the young people to experience a smooth transition process.\n\n## Experience required\n\nBe compassionate, helpful, empathetic, positive, and open-minded.  Must be able to work with neurodiverse young people of diverse backgrounds.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nA few hours for a couple of days a week.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOffice address - HQ Building, 3rd Floor,\n                           -  1 Berry Street, Aberdeen \n                               AB25 1HF",
