                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000006e0ibYAA",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000006e0ibYAA/ride-leader",
                    "publishStart": "2024-11-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Ride Leader",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSupport people to cycle more often in your local area\r\n\r\nWhat you will be doing \r\n-Planning and leading regular rides, often jointly with other ride leaders \r\n-Welcoming riders and helping to create a friendly and inclusive atmosphere \r\n-Supporting new and less experienced cyclists to build their confidence and ensure no one is left behind\r\n-Following the guidelines as set our in guidance such as risk assessing the route and reporting incidents etc.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat's in it for you \r\n- Skills development including leadership, management and communication skills \r\n-Increasing your knowledge of local cycle routes and areas of interest \r\n-Health benefits from regular cycling \r\n-Satisfaction of increasing health and wellbeing of your local community and supporting Cycling UK's mission of enabling millions more people to cycle\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe skills you need\r\n-A confident cyclist with knowledge of local cycle routes -A friendly, welcoming and encouraging attitude\r\n-Sensitive to others needs and able to assess someone’s general wellbeing, cycling level and bike before a ride\r\n-Ability to do simple repairs i.e. puncture repairs during rides\n\n## Travel details\n\nRides may take place at various locations throughout Shetland",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
