            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p0000296xvgAAA/tip-top-toes-carnoustie",
            "name": "TIP TOP TOES CARNOUSTIE",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000FAQi6AAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000FAQi6AAH/footcare-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-02-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-19",
                    "title": "Footcare Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSuitable for anyone from a wide range of backgrounds, not necessarily health related - retired or still working\r\nInterested in supporting and helping people with their wellbeing needs?\r\nFriendly and able to chat with people from all walks of life\r\nPositive and appreciative of good foot care and its importance in keeping us mobile, free of pain and discomfort on Tip Top Toes!\n\n## Description\n\nTip Top Toes is a low-cost toenail cutting and foot care service run by a dedicated community group in Carnoustie. The service is offered currently on a Thursday morning (by appointment only) for anyone unable to cut their own toenails and with no serious underlying medical conditions. \r\n\r\nA much valued and in demand service solely provided by volunteers who have received a programme of instruction on toenail cutting, filing and foot care checks, by qualified NHS Podiatrists. Volunteers are required to help run this not-for-private-profit alternative foot care option for people who cannot manage their own foot care needs. Suitable for volunteers aged 16 and over. No health related experience required. Training and guidance will be provided. May suit someone looking to gain experience for a health & social care related role or medical training interest but suitable to anyone able and keen to assist.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo skills required as training will be provide.   Toe cutting might suit people who have had some medical carer back ground,  however this is not a requirement\n\n## Training details\n\nA  full days training will be supplied by the Podiatry team from Carnoustie Health Centre.  This will be followed by the podiatrist shadowing the nail volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n3 to 4 hous  a week\n\n## Travel details\n\nN/a",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
