                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-26",
                    "title": "Charity Shop Volunteer - Dalgety Bay",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nJoin CHAS in their new shop in Dalgety Bay. Support with welcoming customers, sorting donations or creating beautiful window displays and help raise funds to support children with a life-shortening condition and their families.\n\n## Description\n\nJoin CHAS in their new shop in Dalgety Bay, and help to sell donated stock as well as new goods to raise the vital funds required to care for children and their families. Volunteers are needed to support with welcoming customers, sorting donations or creating beautiful window displays and help raise funds to support children with a life-shortening condition and their families.\r\n\r\nThis role will involve:\r\nVolunteering within a small team to sort, steam, hang and size clothing\r\nMaking sure all stock is in safe and working order\r\nPricing items under supervision and assisting with stock rotation\r\nKeeping the stock room clean, tidy and well organised\r\nWelcoming and assisting customers and serving at the till point\r\nAccepting donations and registering donors for Gift Aid\r\n\r\nUse your existing skills or learn new ones, meet new people and have fun all while making a real difference in your local community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication and attention to detail\r\nAn aptitude for team working\r\nStrong organisational skills\r\nA good understanding of what makes great customer service\r\nThe ability to represent CHAS enthusiastically and appropriately\n\n## Training details\n\nIt’s important to CHAS that you feel happy, safe and confident in your role. As a CHAS volunteer you will be invited to complete a short core learning package that is tailored to your role. They are always developing new opportunities for volunteers to learn and offer a range of options for volunteers.\r\nThey have also partnered with the Skills Network to offer all their volunteers the chance to develop new skills and explore further learning opportunities.\r\nThey also offer a full induction where we provide full training. Trial shifts can also be arranged to help you decide if this is the right role for you.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis opportunity takes place at 8 Bay Centre, Regent’s Way, Dalgety Bay, KY11 9YD, with free car parking and local public transport links close by.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nYes - CHAS reimburses reasonable out of pocket expenses incurred in the course of volunteering, including public transport on submission of receipts/tickets and car (current mileage rate = 45p), every month.\n\n## Taster details\n\nTrial shifts can be arranged to help you decide if this is the right role for you.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
