        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001nvI4qAAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001nvI4qAAE/link-east-fife-mental-health-befriending-project",
            "name": "LINK East Fife Mental Health Befriending Project",
            "description": "This project supports adults aged 18-65 in the East Fife and Levenmouth areas who may be experiencing isolation due to their mental health issues through one-to-one befriendnig and group events.",
            "website": "https://www.linkbefriending.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC027493"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000003ScUXAA0",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000003ScUXAA0/befriender-levenmouth-and-east-fife",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-08",
                    "title": "Befriender (Levenmouth and East Fife)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe need volunteers to befriend adults in the East Fife and Levenmouth area.\n\n## Description\n\nLINK supports adults aged 18 to 65 years old in the East Fife and Levenmouth areas who may be experiencing isolation due to their mental health issues through one-to-one befriending and group events.\r\n\r\nThey are looking for volunteers for their adult befriending project. Befrienders will assist the adults to increase their resilience, confidence, social skills and self esteem through consistent and reliable support, and engaging in activities together.\r\n\r\nIf you have a spare couple of hours a fortnight and would like to help adults who have been isolated due to mental health issues, LINK would like to hear from you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPositive attitude, good listening skills, good organisation skills, empathy, sense of fun, reliability and consistency. Experience of mental health issues not necessary.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive induction and on-going training and support. There will also be personal development opportunities.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place in East Fife and Levenmouth.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel and out-of-pocket expenses are paid, up to a set monthly amount.",
