        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001p0zkwAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001p0zkwAAA/super-power-agency",
            "name": "Super Power Agency",
            "description": "Founded in 2016, The Super Power Agency aims to improve the lives and literacy rates of some of Edinburgh's most under-resourced young people. Through a range of writing workshops, interdisciplinary creative programmes and the help of community volunteers, we aim to empower children and young people (8-18 years) through literacy. We are currently working with Leith Academy, with plans to expand to other schools and youth-serving organisations in Edinburgh and beyond.",
            "website": "https://www.superpoweragency.com",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000J70oNYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000J70oNYAR/classroom-writing-mentors-needed-help-young-people-write-their-story",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-27",
                    "title": "Classroom Writing Mentors needed - help young people write their story!",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nClassroom Writing Mentors needed - help young people write their story!\n\n## Description\n\nAt the Super Power Agency we work in some of Scotland&#39;s most under-resourced areas, encouraging and empowering young people to put pen to paper, build their writing skills and express themselves with confidence.&nbsp;\n\nAs a volunteer Writing Mentor you&#39;ll go into a school at a set time each week for an 8-week creative writing project, working alongside a facilitator and other super volunteers. Once the project finishes, the young people&#39;s work will be published in a book, and you&#39;ll celebrate with a book launch! You don&#39;t need to be an amazing writer - you just need to believe in the power of words to change the world!&nbsp;\n\nVolunteering offers the chance to develop new skills, gain fresh perspectives, meet new people and make a positive difference to young people at a crucial stage in their lives. A good level of spoken English is essential to support creative writing activities in an English Literature context.\n\nSuper Power Agency works across Edinburgh and Glasgow, but we are keen to focus recruitment on Glasgow right now. In terms of location, the programme covers a range of schools - at the moment we&#39;re in John Paul Academy, St Bride&rsquo;s Primary and St Anne&rsquo;s Primary. In 2027 we&rsquo;ll be in Govan High School and other schools tbc.&nbsp;\n\nWhen a potential volunteer gets in touch, they&rsquo;ll have an initial chat/interview with us, and then attend a training session with myself and one of our SPA Facilitators. They will need to be PVG checked before they start working in schools, and we will talk about safeguarding practice as part of our volunteer induction.&nbsp;\n\nIf you want to find out more about how it all works and next steps, please email volunteers@superpoweragency.com. Jo, our Volunteer Coordinator, will be in touch.\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when registered and logged in). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA good level of spoken English is required, as the sessions involve supporting young people with creative writing in an English Literature context. \n\n## Travel details\n\nIn terms of location, the programme covers a range of schools - at the moment we're in John Paul Academy, St Bride’s Primary and St Anne’s Primary. In 2027 we’ll be in Govan High School and other schools tbc. More info will be provided once the volunteer is on-boarded. \n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAs a small charity we cannot reimburse all volunteer travel expenses but if this is a barrier, please let us know when we have our initial chat. ",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000J70oNYAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Classroom Writing Mentors needed - help young people write their story!",
                        "description": "A good level of spoken English is required, as the sessions involve supporting young people with creative writing in an English Literature context. ",
                        "applyLink": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/volunteers/opportunity/10307455",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
