        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001vBaAAAA0",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001vBaAAAA0/cybersafe-scotland",
            "name": "Cybersafe Scotland",
            "description": "Cybersafe Scotland is a not-for-profit organisation which provides services aimed at reducing online abuse, harassment and exploitation, and offers wider support around digital safety. Cybersafe works with children, school staff and parents and carers.",
            "website": "https://www.cybersafescotland.org/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FamilySupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Family Support"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005FheTYAS",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005FheTYAS/respected-and-safe-project-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Respected and Safe Project Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\n-WHO ARE WE?\r\n\r\nCybersafe Scotland is an Aberdeen based social enterprise working to protect children online. Our current focus is reducing online abuse and harassment. Cybersafe works with schools, including classroom-based sessions working directly with children, as well as work with school staff, parents and carers.   \r\n\r\n-WHY DO WE NEED VOLUNTEERS?\r\n\r\nDuring the school year (from August -June each year) we have a programme of work in school including lessons delivered to classes P5 - P7. All these sessions are delivered by Cybersafe Scotland staff but we are look for volunteers to support their delivery, bringing extra support for the learners, and joy and care in keeping with our mission. \r\n\r\n-MAIN TASKS:\r\n\r\n•\tAssist Cybersafe staff in classroom sessions: \r\n•\tSetting up for lessons  \r\n•\tDistributing handouts  \r\n•\tHelping with practical demonstrations  \r\n•\tEncouraging pupils in small group or individual work   \r\n•\tTidying up after lesson  \r\n•\tBringing joy  \r\n\r\n-TIME\r\n\r\nLessons will take place within school hours between 0900-1500 Monday to Friday. The classroom based sessions are about 1 hour for each class including set up and tidy up time but multiple lessons will be delivered in a school in any one day. The more lessons a volunteer can commit to the better as you will learn valuable knowledge and skills through each lesson. However as a minimum volunteers must be able to offer 21 hours, split over half day periods of 3 hours. Please indicate availability when applying.  \r\n\r\n-QUALIFICATIONS\r\n\r\nNo formal qualifications are required, however volunteers will have to successfully apply for a PVG certificate for working with children. An interest in working with children and young people and demonstrable experience in doing so will be required. A qualification in teaching is desirable. An interest in the online world and knowledge and awareness of apps and games will be an advantage though this is not essential. We would also love to offer more adhoc volunteering opportunities this coming year to those who have a specific skill set that they think would contribute to the overall work of CyberSafe Scotland.   \r\n\r\n-HOW TO APPLY \r\n\r\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to help and all volunteers make a real difference and are greatly appreciated. For more information and to apply please email info@cybersafescotland.org\n\n## Description\n\n-WHO ARE WE?\r\n\r\nCybersafe Scotland is an Aberdeen based social enterprise working to protect children online. Our current focus is reducing online abuse and harassment. Cybersafe works with schools, including classroom-based sessions working directly with children, as well as work with school staff, parents and carers.   \r\n\r\n-WHY DO WE NEED VOLUNTEERS?\r\n\r\nDuring the school year (from August-June each year) we have a programme of work in school including lessons delivered to classes P5 - P7. All these sessions are delivered by Cybersafe Scotland staff but we are look for volunteers to support their delivery, bringing extra support for the learners, and joy and care in keeping with our mission. \r\n\r\n-MAIN TASKS:\r\n\r\n•\tAssist Cybersafe staff in classroom sessions: \r\n•\tSetting up for lessons  \r\n•\tDistributing handouts  \r\n•\tHelping with practical demonstrations  \r\n•\tEncouraging pupils in small group or individual work   \r\n•\tTidying up after lesson  \r\n•\tBringing joy  \r\n\r\n-TIME\r\n\r\nLessons will take place within school hours between 0900-1500 Monday to Friday. The classroom based sessions are about 1 hour for each class including set up and tidy up time but multiple lessons will be delivered in a school in any one day. The more lessons a volunteer can commit to the better as you will learn valuable knowledge and skills through each lesson. However as a minimum volunteers must be able to offer 21 hours, split over half day periods of 3 hours. Please indicate availability when applying.  \r\n\r\n-QUALIFICATIONS\r\n\r\nNo formal qualifications are required, however volunteers will have to successfully apply for a PVG certificate for working with children. An interest in working with children and young people and demonstrable experience in doing so will be required. A qualification in teaching is desirable. An interest in the online world and knowledge and awareness of apps and games will be an advantage though this is not essential. We would also love to offer more adhoc volunteering opportunities this coming year to those who have a specific skill set that they think would contribute to the overall work of CyberSafe Scotland.   \r\n\r\n-HOW TO APPLY \r\n\r\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to help and all volunteers make a real difference and are greatly appreciated. For more information and to apply please email info@cybersafescotland.org\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and training is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times during weekdays/school hours to help.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAll schools are located in the Northfield and St Machar areas.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
