        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001vBaXiAAK",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001vBaXiAAK/searchlight-scotland",
            "name": "Searchlight Scotland",
            "description": "Searchlight Scotland was founded in 2018 with a drive and hope to see societies most vulnerable receive trauma informed care and support in order for them to live the life that they deserve.  \r\n\r\nOver the past few years we have seen many individuals come through our doors and start a journey to freedom from addiction, abuse, exploitation and many other life controlling issues.  We are passionate about providing specialised care to those who have suffered trauma in their lives.    \r\n\r\nWe have a vision and a drive to identify and rescue those who are trapped in the travesty of human trafficking.  We want to raise awareness and provide training to front line professionals to see as many individuals identified in Scotland as we can.  We have a passion to see slavery ended in Scotland in our life time.    \r\n\r\nWe are committed to expanding and developing our services to see the long lasting recovery and restoration of many more individuals who have found themselves in very dark situations.",
            "website": "https://www.searchlightscotland.org/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
