        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002NA2GbAAL",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002NA2GbAAL/wester-loch-ewe-trust",
            "name": "Wester Loch Ewe Trust",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JdisfYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JdisfYAB/soup-lunch-support-team",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-10",
                    "title": "Soup Lunch Support Team",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe're looking for friendly, enthusiastic volunteers to help us run our weekly community soup lunches.\r\n\r\nOur soup lunches are a chance for local people to get together, enjoy some homemade soup and a chat, meet others and spend a little time in good company. We're looking for volunteers to help make these lunches happen, whether that's preparing the soup, serving our guests or helping with the general set-up and clear-up.\r\n\r\nYou don't need to commit to every week. We'd love to build a small team of volunteers who can share the responsibility through a rota, so you can offer as much or as little time as suits you.\r\n\r\nWhat could you help with?\r\n\r\nThere are a few ways to get involved:\r\n- Making soup: Prepare a pot of homemade soup for the weekly lunch. The cost of ingredients will be reimbursed.\r\n- Serving lunches: Welcome people, serve soup and help make everyone feel at home.\r\n- Setting up: Help arrange tables, prepare the space and get everything ready.\r\n- Clearing up: Help wash dishes, tidy the kitchen and put everything away.\r\nYou can choose to help with one activity or a combination of them.\r\n\r\nWhen would you be needed?\r\n\r\nOur weekly soup lunches follow this schedule:\r\n- 12.15pm: Volunteers arrive to help set up.\r\n- 1.00pm: Lunch is served.\r\n- 2.00pm: Clear-up begins.\r\n- 2.30/2.45pm: Finished!\r\n\r\nWhat we're looking for\r\n- A friendly, welcoming attitude and a willingness to help.\r\n- An interest in bringing people together and supporting the local community.\r\n- Reliability when you've signed up for a particular date.\r\n- A willingness to work as part of a small team.\r\nMinimum age: 16 years.\r\n\r\nNo previous experience is necessary, and you don't need to be a great cook to get involved!\r\n\r\nWe'll provide guidance and support and make sure everyone knows what needs doing.\r\n\r\nInterested in helping?\r\n- Whether you can help once a month, occasionally or more regularly, we'd love to hear from you. Every helping hand makes a difference.\r\n\r\nGet in touch to find out more or to add your name to our volunteer rota.\r\n\r\nThis project is supported by the HTSI Communities Mental Health & Wellbeing Fund for Adults - Year 6, helping us create opportunities for connection, friendship and improved wellbeing within our community.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction and ongoing training provided",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F990aee8c-5dac-40b0-8545-94a643f4e5f6%2FzXi5KTfdOxM2lV8QmhrgVF9DBeg2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=187f04c4-4a49-4f6d-b01b-0af4ca9edf21",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JdisfYAB#role",
