                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JdgUHYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JdgUHYAZ/heritage-projet-lead",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-10",
                    "title": "Heritage Projet Lead",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are looking for a motivated and community-minded volunteer to help develop our local heritage project, supporting the creation and growth of our exhibition and memory-based archive focused on the Wester Loch Ewe area.\r\n\r\nThis is a hands-on and creative role involving working with existing artefacts, helping to identify and source new locally relevant materials, and supporting the storytelling of our community’s past. You will also help shape how we preserve and share local history for future generations.\r\n\r\nA key part of the role will involve working collaboratively with other local charities, groups, and individuals to uncover lesser-known or forgotten aspects of the area’s history.\r\n\r\nWhat you would be doing\r\n- Supporting the development and organisation of the heritage room and exhibition space\r\n- Working with existing artefacts and help identify gaps in the current collection\r\n- Researching local history relevant to the Wester Loch Ewe area and surrounding communities\r\n- Helping source and document new artefacts, stories, and materials from local residents and networks\r\n- Assisting with planning and carrying out informal oral history conversations/interviews with local people\r\n- Supporting and helping organise the “Memories & Connections” group, ensuring it runs smoothly and remains welcoming and engaging\r\n- Working alongside partner organisations and community groups to strengthen shared heritage work\r\n- Helping ensure all materials are recorded, stored, and presented appropriately\r\n\r\nWhat We’re Looking For\r\n- An interest in local history, heritage, or community storytelling\r\n- Good communication skills and a friendly, approachable manner\r\n- An ability to work independently and also as part of a wider volunteer team\r\n- Confidence in speaking with members of the public (or willingness to develop this)\r\n- Basic organisational skills and attention to detail\r\n- Experience in research, archives, museums, or oral history is helpful but not essential\r\n\r\nWhat You’ll Gain\r\n- A meaningful opportunity to help preserve and celebrate local heritage\r\n- Experience in community research, oral history, and exhibition development\r\n- The chance to work with a wide range of people and community groups\r\n- Supportive environment with guidance from an established volunteer team\r\n- Opportunity to develop skills in research, project coordination, and heritage interpretation\r\n- A real and lasting contribution to preserving Wester Loch Ewe’s history for future generations\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction and support from Trustees will be provided",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F18baf29c-5878-4797-a323-d93bf8fe3b65%2FzXi5KTfdOxM2lV8QmhrgVF9DBeg2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=91a1902a-9773-4b0c-af50-e2b3e7bb4900",
