                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IT6dxYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IT6dxYAD/volunteer-support-excercise-after-stroke-inverurie-and-stonehaven",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-13",
                    "title": "Volunteer Support - Excercise after Stroke Inverurie and Stonehaven",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are an exercise after stroke class with about 12 participants and an instructor. Sometimes a participant may need a little assistance to carry out  the exercises given by the instructor.Maybe take an arm,help on to a piece of equipment or stand beside while exercising.The volunteer will with training notice when this is required. The volunteer will assist instructor put out and take back equipment. This is an opportunity to become a supportive caring part of a team. Our participants recovery  journey  is at different stages we are a friendly, encouraging group",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
