                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Events Volunteer (Stadium Soar at Barclays Hampden)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nBarclays Stadium Soar is an exhilarating zip slide experience at Scotland's National Stadium, Hampden Park. Participants will take on an unforgettable challenge, soaring across the stadium while raising vital funds to support charities across Scotland.\r\n\r\nVolunteers will play a key role in creating an incredible experience for every participant. From welcoming supporters and assisting with registration to cheering them on throughout the day, your enthusiasm and support will help make this event a huge success.\r\n\r\nWe have a range of volunteer opportunities available throughout the event, including:\r\n\r\n- Registration & Check-In\r\nWelcome participants as they arrive, assist with registration, answer questions, and help ensure everyone is ready for their Stadium Soar experience.\r\n\r\n- Event Support & Stewarding\r\nHelp guide participants and spectators around the venue, provide information, support event operations, and assist the event team as needed throughout the day.\r\n\r\n- Cheer Point Volunteers\r\nBring the atmosphere to life by encouraging participants, celebrating their achievements, and helping create a memorable event experience.\r\n\r\n- Finish Area Support\r\nCongratulate participants as they complete their challenge, distribute medals and event materials, support photo opportunities, and help ensure everyone leaves with a smile.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for enthusiastic, friendly volunteers who enjoy working with people and want to help create an unforgettable fundraising event. By volunteering at Barclays Stadium Soar, you'll be helping ensure that No Life is Half Lived while supporting thousands of people living with chest, heart and stroke conditions across Scotland.\r\n\r\nNo previous experience is required, just plenty of energy, enthusiasm, and a passion for making a difference.\n\n## Experience required\n\n- Enjoy engaging with people\r\n\r\n- Friendly, polite and cheerful\r\n\r\n- Ability to get to and from the event location safely\r\n\r\n- Ability to volunteer as part of a team\n\n## Travel details\n\nHampden Park, Letherby Drive, Glasgow, Glasgow City, G42 9BA, United Kingdom\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses Reasonable out-of-pocket expenses will be reimbursed. These should be discussed with your Line Manager prior to outlay and must be submitted within the prescribed guidelines as detailed in the CHSS Volunteer Expenses Policy.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F689f76b0-ca3d-4bab-a7e7-71ec453a502d%2FOdJUEl2EhNgsDT68cSLfbg9RQOw2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=2ad5cfb9-eb8e-4e76-93d8-eb307ef2641b",
