                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FfeH0YAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FfeH0YAJ/retail-volunteer-motherwell",
                    "publishStart": "2026-03-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-06",
                    "title": "Retail Volunteer - Motherwell",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nVolunteering at our NEW Motherwell Shop\r\n\r\nWhether you can give an hour a week or a little more, your time will help make a real difference in the community.\r\n\r\nEvery sale supports people in Scotland living with chest, heart, stroke and Long Covid conditions. Every hour you volunteer helps someone live life to the full.\r\n\r\n- What you could be doing:\r\nWelcoming customers and offering great service\r\nThanking donors and sorting stock\r\nKeeping the shop friendly, tidy and inviting\r\nWhether you enjoy being on the shop floor or helping behind the scenes, there’s a role for you.\r\n\r\n- Not sure how much time you can offer?\r\nWe’re flexible! Whether you can spare an hour or a few, we’ll work around your schedule. And if you have questions, we’re always happy to chat.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction, Ongoing Training & Support\n\n## Travel details\n\nBrandon Parade South, Motherwell, ML1 1RB, United Kingdom\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses Reasonable out-of-pocket expenses will be reimbursed. These should be discussed with your Line Manager prior to outlay and must be submitted within the prescribed guidelines as detailed in the CHSS Volunteer Expenses Policy. Safeguarding In line with our commitment to safeguarding, this role is subject to a basic disclosure check. Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland are committed to equality of opportunity, and we aim to ensure no volunteer is unfairly treated on the grounds of an offending background.",
