                    "title": "Supported Self Management Volunteer Facilitator (Lockerbie)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are looking for compelling communicators to help with the delivery and facilitation of six week self management workshops in Dumfries & Galloway.\r\n\r\n\r\nThis opportunity offers the chance to see the direct impact of sharing your communication skills, helping people achieve lasting positive change!\n\n## Experience required\n\nAs a volunteer facilitator, you will help create an inclusive group environment, using clear communication and facilitation skills. This role would suit someone with experience delivering in‑person training or similar group work, who enjoys building rapport, encouraging participation, and supporting individuals with varying needs and abilities.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe ideal candidate is reliable, patient, empathetic, and respectful of the opinions of others. An understanding of the need for confidentiality and ability to maintain boundaries is essential. \r\n\r\n\r\nWe are looking for someone who is happy to commit to initial and ongoing training and development. Lived experience of our conditions is advantageous but not essential.\n\n## Training details\n\nSupported Self-Management: Leader Training; Safeguarding Adults (L2) E-Learning; Conditions Awareness Training.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe commitment is one four‑hour session per week over six weeks, held on the same day each week, with flexibility on which day.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWorkshops may be delivered at different locations across Dumfries & Galloway, so the ability to travel independently within your own area would be an advantage.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable out-of- pocket expenses will be reimbursed. These should be discussed with your Line Manager prior to outlay and must be submitted within the prescribed guidelines as detailed in the CHSS Volunteer Expenses Policy.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F2c5d3cc2-a479-4f0f-9ada-aef846f90d4c%2FYuN3i0Q6twdcUJezmPl7xdMnmzx2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=a23f8be1-e305-481c-987f-2d02fb8ed265",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H9CbFYAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Supported Self Management Volunteer Facilitator (Lockerbie)",
                        "description": "As a volunteer facilitator, you will help create an inclusive group environment, using clear communication and facilitation skills. This role would suit someone with experience delivering in‑person training or similar group work, who enjoys building rapport, encouraging participation, and supporting individuals with varying needs and abilities.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe ideal candidate is reliable, patient, empathetic, and respectful of the opinions of others. An understanding of the need for confidentiality and ability to maintain boundaries is essential. \r\n\r\n\r\nWe are looking for someone who is happy to commit to initial and ongoing training and development. Lived experience of our conditions is advantageous but not essential.",
