                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HJY7RYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HJY7RYAX/chair-andor-secretary-role",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-15",
                    "title": "Chair and/or Secretary role",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Bathgate Stroke Support Group is looking for 1–2 volunteers to help take on key roles as Chair and/or Secretary.\nThis long-running group provides vital peer support to people affected by stroke in the local community. Due to ill health and changing circumstances, the current coordinators are now looking to step back.\n\n## Experience required\n\n- Friendly and approachable\nAble to create a warm, welcoming environment for group members\nComfortable chatting with people from different backgrounds\n\n- Organised (but not perfect!)\nAble to help plan meetings or keep basic notes\nComfortable with simple tasks like sending messages or coordinating dates\n\n- Good communicators\nAble to listen and respond with empathy\nComfortable sharing information with the group\n\n- Reliable and committed\nAvailable for a couple of hours each week\nHappy to take on a consistent role to help keep the group running\n\n- Team player\nWilling to work alongside another volunteer (shared Chair/Secretary role is possible)\nOpen to guidance and support from the current coordinators\n\n## Training details\n\nYou won’t be on your own – current coordinators will provide full guidance and handover support until Christmas 2026.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\none- off opportunity \nYou won’t be on your own – current coordinators will provide full guidance and handover support until Christmas 2026.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBritish Legion Social Club, 50 North Bridge Street, Bathgate, EH48 4PP",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FL2oO40jPTvQtUcSyHUYHY9JRVVT2%2FrUJiwlUKwYWfqrgF-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=c8571ab1-4309-4cf1-a017-6153a3e27122",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HJY7RYAX#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Chair and/or Secretary role",
                        "description": "- Friendly and approachable\nAble to create a warm, welcoming environment for group members\nComfortable chatting with people from different backgrounds\n\n- Organised (but not perfect!)\nAble to help plan meetings or keep basic notes\nComfortable with simple tasks like sending messages or coordinating dates\n\n- Good communicators\nAble to listen and respond with empathy\nComfortable sharing information with the group\n\n- Reliable and committed\nAvailable for a couple of hours each week\nHappy to take on a consistent role to help keep the group running\n\n- Team player\nWilling to work alongside another volunteer (shared Chair/Secretary role is possible)\nOpen to guidance and support from the current coordinators",
                        "commitment": "one- off opportunity \nYou won’t be on your own – current coordinators will provide full guidance and handover support until Christmas 2026.",
