        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001j4H87AAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001j4H87AAE/funeral-link",
            "name": "Funeral Link",
            "description": "Prevent fineral poverty in Dundee by offering a confidential support and helping the bereaved to save money on all things realting to the funeral.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC048691"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HnfppYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HnfppYAB/drop-in-host",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-20",
                    "title": "Drop-in Host",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFuneral Link prevent funeral poverty in Dundee by offering confidential support and helping the bereaved to save money on all things relating to a funeral. Working alongside Funeral Link staff, you will help us to support people who come into our Drop-In Centre for information, a meeting, a group or just a coffee.\n\n## Description\n\nFuneral Link prevent funeral poverty in Dundee by offering confidential support and helping the bereaved to save money on all things relating to a funeral. You will help us to support people who come into our Drop-In Centre for information, a meeting, a group or just a coffee.\r\n\r\nYou will work alongside Funeral Link staff to:\r\n\r\n· Welcome visitors to the Centre\r\n· Provide teas and coffees to visitors to the Centre\r\n· Provide an empathetic listening ear to visitors to the Centre\n\n## Experience required\n\nExperience of bereavement or loss, good listener, friendly manner.\n\n## Training details\n\nOne session about the ethos of the organisation, the work we do, our expectations of our volunteers and how we support our volunteers. A second about grief and listening skills.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCentral Dundee\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note: No expenses are available for this opportunity.\n\n## Taster details\n\nWe would welcome the volunteer to come along before they start.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
