                    "description": "## Description\n\nBy being at the forefront of textile reuse and recycling, Salvation Army Trading Company Ltd (SATCoL) helps fund Salvation Army’s vital work with vulnerable people in the UK. Join the SATCoL team to help care for local communities and our planet, by being a part of finding new homes for pre-loved clothes, household items, and collectibles.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe Kirkcaldy shop has roles to suit all skill sets: from behind the scenes to front of house, window-dressing to social media, donation sorting to customer service. Tasks include creating seasonal displays, helping customers, and operating the till.\r\n\r\n\r\nWith SATCoL, you will meet new people, build confidence, gain skills and experience for your first or next career move. You will have access to a Wellbeing & Benefits Platform (free mortgage advice, will writing, virtual GP, discounts for mainstream retailers, 24/7 confidential helpline), award-winning eLearning platform; 25% discount, and support from divisional Salvation Army colleagues.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAll levels of skills and experience are welcome.\r\n\r\nSATCoL asks that volunteers uphold the Company CARE Values: Compassion, Accountability, Respect and Equality.\n\n## Training details\n\nUpon starting, volunteers will be provided with an induction programme and any training needed to carry out their role. Volunteers will have ongoing access to an award winning eLearning Platform and will receive support and coaching from shop-based colleagues.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMercat Shopping Centre, Unit 55, Kirkcaldy, KY1 1NG\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport, mileage (45p per mile) and parking costs are reimbursed on the day when accompanied with a valid travel receipt.",
