        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001jQYZhAAO",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001jQYZhAAO/toll-community-centre-burntisland",
            "name": "Toll Community Centre, Burntisland",
            "website": "http://www.tollcentre.org.uk/Index.asp?MainID=8004",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC016430"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IOJNMYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IOJNMYA5/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-06",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nToll Community Centre is looking for new volunteer trustees to join their Board and help shape the future of the community centre in Burntisland. Trustees work together to provide good governance, support the Centre Manager and staff team, and help ensure the charity remains welcoming, sustainable and responsive to local people.\r\n\r\nThe organisation welcome people who can share skills or experience in areas such as finance, HR, supporting volunteers or community development. The centre also value lived experience, local knowledge and people who care about Burntisland and want to make a positive difference. No previous trustee experience is needed. Full induction, training and ongoing support will be provided.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe organisation is looking for people who care about Burntisland and want to support a welcoming, inclusive community space. You do not need previous trustee experience, and they welcome applications from people of different ages, backgrounds and experiences. Useful qualities include being reliable, willing to listen and contribute, able to work respectfully as part of a team, and committed to equality, inclusion and supporting the local community. The centre particularly welcome people who can share knowledge or experience in finance, HR, governance, fundraising, supporting people and volunteers, community development or local services. The organisation also strongly welcome people with lived experience of the issues affecting local people, and people with a passion for making Burntisland a stronger community. Training and support will be provided.\n\n## Training details\n\nNew trustees will receive a warm welcome and a structured induction to Toll Community Centre, the Board’s role and responsibilities, the Centre’s activities, finances, policies and key priorities. Trustees will be given relevant information in advance of meetings and will have a named point of contact for questions and support. Training will be available on trustee duties, charity governance, safeguarding, financial oversight, equality and inclusion, and any other areas identified by the trustee or Board. New trustees will be supported to build confidence at their own pace, and previous trustee experience is not required.\n\n## Travel details\n\nToll Community Centre, East Toll Park, Burntisland, Fife, KY3 9HA.\r\n\r\nBoard meetings are held at the Centre, with occasional online or hybrid meetings where appropriate. The Centre is centrally located in Burntisland and is accessible by public transport.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport or mileage costs will be re-imbursed.",
