                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000F0zfaYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000F0zfaYAB/scottish-spca-micro-volunteer-ayrshire",
                    "publishStart": "2026-01-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-28",
                    "title": "Scottish SPCA Micro-volunteer (Ayrshire)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Scottish SPCA needs your help to make Scotland the best place for all animals to live!\r\n\r\nVolunteering with the Scottish SPCA is a wonderful thing to do, not only for Scotland's animals in need and the people in your local community, but also for you!\r\n\r\nThis role is designed to be completely flexible - fit it in around your busy life to suit you! You can choose to simply share our news and campaigns with a monthly online task, or if you feel like getting a bit more involved now and again, we will keep you up-to-date with events and other initiatives in your area\r\n\r\nSo, what are you waiting for?\r\n\r\nSign up to be an SSPCA Micro-volunteer today and be part of the rescue!\r\n\r\nDid you know that it costs us £63,000 per day to look after all the animals in our care? As an SSPCA Micro-volunteer, you will help ensure that we can continue to provide our vital services.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnthusiasm... Lots of it!\r\nAbility to use social media channels (for online posts)\r\nAn understanding of the Society's work - we will give you training!\r\nA pleasant and polite manner when dealing with the public\r\nConfidence to interact with other people\r\nAbility to work as part of a small team\r\nAbility to take instruction and follow health & safety requirements at events\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will receive your own online volunteering account and need to complete a few online training courses. We will be in touch with you about available events and how to complete your monthly social media task\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n1 monthly online task, with option to get involved in events and fundraising as suits you\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe reimburse volunteer travel expenses at the HMRC rate of 45p per mile up to a max of 30 miles per day\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n45p per mile when attending events and fundraisers",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000F0zfaYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Scottish SPCA Micro-volunteer (Ayrshire)",
