        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00002UkJTmAAN",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00002UkJTmAAN/glasgow-clyde-rape-crisis-centre",
            "name": "Glasgow & Clyde Rape Crisis Centre",
            "website": "https://glasgowclyderapecrisis.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC006595"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Helplines",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Helplines"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ImLkXYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ImLkXYAV/support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-22",
                    "title": "Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur volunteers take a very important role in our centre, thanks to them our helpline has been running for decades. Volunteers are invaluable members of the Glasgow & Clyde Rape Crisis team.\r\nMost of our volunteers deliver our Connect Live phone and messaging support service. However volunteers also help us with fundraising and our drop in services or group work sessions.\r\n\r\nEvery year we are looking for new volunteers, we encourage all women, especially those who represent different minority groups to apply and join our team.\r\nVolunteers will support our ability to provide our vital helpline service, which is free and confidential and provides a listening ear and information on our services to women and girls who have been affected by rape and sexual violence, as well as their friends or family who are looking for information.  \r\n\r\nThe volunteer is expected to have a strong passion for women’s rights.  Volunteers are responsible to the GCRC Board of Trustees and Director for upholding and maintaining the working principles, values and policies of Glasgow and Clyde Rape Crisis Centre (GCRC).\r\nResponsibilities\r\n\r\n•\tTo provide trauma-informed emotional and practical support to women and girls who are survivors of sexual violence, through helpline support.\r\n\r\n•\tTo provide trauma-informed emotional and practical support to women and girls who are survivors of sexual violence, through structured face-to-face appointments or via the drop-in facility.\r\n\r\n•\tTo attend regular support and supervision meetings with Team Leaders\r\n\r\n•\tTo liaise with other workers or volunteers for information and advice to ensure an effective service is provided to women and girls who have experienced sexual violence.\r\n\r\n•\tTo be aware of and liaise with other agencies or relevant third parties where appropriate.\r\n\r\n•\tTo keep up to date with developments around sexual violence, including legal developments and ensure accurate information is disseminated to women. Developments will be communicated to you by the Team Leaders.\r\n\r\n•\tTo maintain and record statistical information on our Oasis system and call record book.\r\n\r\n•\tTo raise any issues or concerns arising in support work with the Team Leaders or Service Manager as soon as possible.\r\n\r\n•\tTo represent GCRC with integrity, in accordance with our values, working practices and policies.\r\nVolunteer Role Specification\r\n\r\nEssential Requirements\r\n•\tFeminist analysis of sexual violence\r\n\r\n•\tExperience of person-centred support work\r\n\r\n•\tKnowledge of issues relating to violence against women and girls\r\n\r\n•\tCommitment to anti-discriminatory practice\r\n\r\n•\tUnderstanding of confidentiality\r\n\r\n•\tAbility to work with existing volunteers and staff members.\r\n\r\n•\tStrong verbal and written skills\r\n\r\n•\tStrong IT skills\r\n\r\n•\tGood level of self-awareness \r\n\r\n•\tAlign with GCRC Values: Integrity, compassion, empower and challenge alongside our feminist principles.\r\nDesirable Requirements\r\n\r\n•\tExperience of working with women and girls who have experienced sexual violence.\r\n\r\n•\tExperience of the Women’s Movement\r\n\r\n•\tKnowledge of other agencies and organisations.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining will be provided on all aspects of the volunteer role requirements.  \r\n\r\nSuccessful completion of the training programme is mandatory before any support work can be undertaken.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ImLkXYAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
