                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000003diM1YAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000003diM1YAI/activities-supporter",
                    "publishStart": "2024-05-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Activities Supporter",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nA unique opportunity to support stroke rehabilitation of club members within a gym whilst under supervision of a fitness instructor and physiotherapist.\n\n## Description\n\nA unique opportunity to support stroke rehabilitation of club members within a gym whilst under supervision of a fitness instructor and physiotherapist.\r\n\r\nStand close to members to keep their balance while they carry out a variety of supervised exercises during circuit training. To assist and encourage when balance, walking and stepping exercises are practiced. Engage in  conversation  to promote a light hearted atmosphere.\n\n## Experience required\n\nTraining and support is provided. Helping others understanding physical disabilities\n\n## Training details\n\nwe have developed a volunteer handbook, shadow a senior volunteer for as long as it takes,  relevant courses will be organised,\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\neach class lasts 1 hour. There are  1 class on Monday, 3 classes on wednesday\n\n## Travel details\n\nDouglas Sports Centre.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nmaximum of £5 daily\n\n## Taster details\n\nshadow a fellow volunteer",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
