        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001UA9ALAA1",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001UA9ALAA1/moray-local-outdoor-access-forum",
            "name": "Moray Local Outdoor Access Forum",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HQC8cYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HQC8cYAH/forum-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-19",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-22",
                    "title": "Forum Member",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nLAF members will: Raise awareness of the Scottish Outdoor Access Code Uphold access rights Help avoid conflict & resolve disputes Comment on relevant Planning applications Advise on the Moray Local Outdoor Access Strategy Review & the Moray Core Path Plan\n\n## Description\n\nApplicants should specify the peer group(s) in which they have expertise and may submit an endorsement from a relevant body or organisation of which they are a member, supporting their appointment. The Forum has no more than 20 members with equal representation from 4 peer groups as follows: • Public agencies e.g. Forestry Commission, Scottish Natural Heritage, Moray Council • Landowners/land Managers e.g. estate owners, farmers • Community groups e.g. local access groups, Community Councils • Access users/activity groups e.g. walkers, cyclists, horse riders, canoeists, with one place here guaranteed for someone representing less able and disabled interests - Members are expected to attend four meetings per year, typically held quarterly in Elgin from 4:00pm to 6:00pm (Currently the penultimate Tuesday of each quarter). - Members will be entitled to claim reasonable travel expenses to attend any additional Forum related meetings or business. - Membership is for a three-year term, with the opportunity to renew upon completion.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining depends on knowledge and experience; ideally the successful applicant will bring their own expertise, knowledge, experiences and enthusiasm\n\n## Travel details\n\nSpecifically Elgin for meetings but throughout Moray\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMembers will be entitled to claim reasonable travel expenses to attend any additional Forum related meetings or business.",
