        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001UApLkAAL",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001UApLkAAL/friends-of-granton-castle-walled-garden",
            "name": "Friends of Granton Castle Walled Garden",
            "description": "To protect and restore the 15thC Walled Garden that was once part of the now-demolished Granton Castle. In doing this we aim to create a thriving, sustainable and productive community garden and heritage gateway to Edinburgh's waterfront through a community-led approach that will be accessible to existing and new populations and will contribute to community integration and cohesion.",
            "website": "https://www.grantoncastlewalledgarden.wordpress.com/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VuohDAAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VuohDAAR/gardeners",
                    "publishStart": "2019-01-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Gardeners",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nA wide variety of tasks are involved in the restoration project – digging, clearing, weeding, planting, laying bases for greenhouse and composting toilet, making tea, helping with planning, harvesting seasonal produce.\n\n## Description\n\nWho can resist the chance to help restore a 'lost' 15th century walled garden here in Edinburgh? Or to get fit without paying gym costs? We are keen to recruit volunteers for a wide variety of gardening tasks. You don't have to have specific gardening skills – enthusiasm counts. A wide variety of activities are involved in the restoration project – digging, clearing, weeding, planting, general repair and maintenance of sheds, greeting, helping with planning, harvesting seasonal produce being some of them.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnergy and enthusiasm. The volunteering  is suitable for all fitness levels and adaptable to individuals.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe would offer induction at the start of the volunteer's time with us.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMinimum commitment 2 - 4 hours, one day a week.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe garden is located next door to the Social Bite Village on West Shore Road, EH5 1QB\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VuohDAAR#role",
