        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0011p00001VD2moAAD",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0011p00001VD2moAAD/richmonds-hope",
            "name": "Richmond’s Hope",
            "description": "We believe that we can make a difference in the lives of children who have been bereaved by supporting them through their grief using therapeutic play providing a safe haven for them to work out their feelings.",
            "website": "https://www.richmondshope.org.uk",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HI9PeYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HI9PeYAL/board-members",
                    "publishStart": "2025-06-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "Board Members",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nRichmond's Hope, a Scottish-based children's bereavement charity are seeking passionate & committed individuals to join our Board. If you’re ready to make a meaningful difference in the lives of bereaved children & their families, we’d love to hear from you. Visit www.richmondshope.org.uk to find out more.\n\n## Description\n\nRichmond's Hope is a Scottish-based children's bereavement charity. We are seeking passionate and committed individuals to join our Board of Trustees and help shape the future of our vital work. As a Board Member, you will play a key role in the strategic leadership of Richmond’s Hope, ensuring we remain true to our mission and values while maintaining good governance and accountability.  This is a rewarding opportunity to make a real impact in the lives of bereaved children across Scotland.\n\n## Training details\n\nAn induction pack will be made available to Board members and free training will be offered.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoard Members would be expected to attend 8 Board meetings per year (generally held on Thursday evenings between 5pm-8pm at our offices at Norton Park, Edinburgh but could also be in Glasgow)\n2 x half day strategy meetings on Saturdays - held at the charity's offices at Norton Park, 57 Albion Rd,\nEdinburgh, EH7 5QY.\nhttps://www.nortonpark.org/\nNorton Park is easily accessible via public tranport and there is free carparking available on site.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable expenses for transport will be paid directly to the individual's bank account upon completion of a standard expense claim form.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HI9PeYAL#role",
