                    "title": "Event Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nJoin the fun as a Fundraising Group Volunteer with Canine Partners! Team up with fellow volunteers to \r\nhelp plan and deliver exciting local events that help raise vital funds for amazing assistance dogs. You’ll \r\nmeet monthly, share ideas, plan activities, and be the friendly face of Canine Partners in your community.\n\n## Description\n\nThis role involves being an active member of the Scottish Borders and North Northumberland Fundraising \r\nGroup for Canine Partners. You will be working alongside fellow volunteers to arrange, plan and attend \r\nfundraising events in your local community. You would attend regular group meetings, typically once a \r\nmonth, to discuss upcoming activities and ensure plans are in place for events throughout the year. \r\nThis is a flexible opportunity which can fit around your lifestyle.\r\nWhat’s involved\r\nWork with your fellow group volunteers to organise fundraising events and activities to raise money \r\nfor Canine Partners, such as Dog Shows and pop-up stalls\r\nTaking on tasks to assist with the organisation of fundraising events within the local area--\r\nBeing the public face of Canine Partners within your local area\r\nLiaising with Scotland's Community Fundraiser for Canine Partners\r\nRole Requirements\r\nNo experience is needed; all we ask is that you are over 18 and keen to get involved!\r\nSupport and Training----\r\nReimbursement of agreed expenses \r\nDedicated point of contact in the fundraising team\r\nGuidance on cash handling\r\nTraining and support in fundraising event management\r\nWhy Volunteer with us?\r\nWe breed, train, and support expert assistance dogs to create loving, life-changing partnerships with \r\ndisabled people. Across the UK, we support people with a variety of physical disabilities and their families, \r\ncarefully matching them with a dog that suits their needs, personality, and lifestyle. Our dogs bring \r\nconfidence and independence, love and companionship, reducing reliance on carers and giving people the \r\nfreedom to live life their own way.\r\nBy volunteering with us, you’ll help raise the awareness and vital funds that allow us to continue changing \r\nlives through the support of expertly trained assistance dogs.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience is required\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will receive training from your Community Fundraiser and Fundraising Group Leader. \r\nHave access to webinars and training on our Volunteer Portal\r\nHave access to the Health Assured Employee Assistance Program. This is provided by Health Assured and \r\noffers counselling and bereavement support as well as legal and medical advice should you need it.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis role has no fixed location. You will travel to different locations across the Scottish Borders and North \r\nNorthumberland.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses are reimbursed monthly through BACCS. All reasonable expenses such as public transport and \r\ncar mileage, will be paid.",
