        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00108000034SikRAAS",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00108000034SikRAAS/crossroads-south-ayrshire",
            "name": "Crossroads South Ayrshire",
            "description": "Crossroads South Ayrshire is a local charity which was founded in 1985. It provides a domiciliary service to relieve carers and their families in South Ayrshire from the stress of caring for persons who need constant supervision.",
            "website": "https://crossroads-sa.org.uk",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BDQKvYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BDQKvYAP/treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-07-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-12",
                    "title": "Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCrossroads are a charity that supplies respite support to carers - we employ staff to care for individuals for a few hours a week so their family carers can have some time to themselves as respite.  We are currently looking for a Volunteer Treasurer to:\r\nProduce management accounts quarterly on Excel\r\nReview the annual accounts  \r\nLiaise with the external accountants \r\nProduce an annual budget\r\nMonitor the bank accounts  \r\nMonitor payroll which is produced externally\r\nAttend board meetings or produces reports quarterly\r\nCan assist at fundraising events \r\n\r\nA full handover period with the current Treasurer would be given to smooth the transition. The time commitment is generally at the quarter end, and year end and is less than a day a quarter.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA qualified accountant or experienced bookkeeper would be best suited to the role which is an overseeing of the finances rather than a processing role.",
