            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HDsOzYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HDsOzYAL/central-wellbeing-community-ambassador",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-09",
                    "title": "Central Wellbeing Community Ambassador",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCentral Wellbeing is a peer support mental health charity established in 2021 and based in the heart of Falkirk dedicated to providing compassion, understanding and a safe space for those navigating the challenges of poor mental health. Central Wellbeing do this through facilitating peer support groups and community activities in the Forth Valley area.\r\n\r\nHelp make sure people can easily find out about what Central Wellbeing offer.\r\n\r\nCentral Wellbeing are looking for Community Ambassadors to help keep posters and leaflets visible and up to date in key places across the community. This might include checking noticeboards, topping up materials and helping ensure information about groups and activities is easy to find.\r\n\r\nYour support helps more people become aware of the support and connection available through Central Wellbeing.\r\n\r\nThis is a flexible role that can fit around your day-to-day life. It’s a simple way to stay connected to your community and make a positive difference.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo formal experience is required. An interest in your local community and a willingness to help keep information visible and up to date is helpful.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe Volunteer Coordinator will meet you and support you in this role, based on individual requirements.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible to suit you.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCommunity based - within your own local area.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses not required for this role.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://centralwellbeing.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/central-wellbeing-scio-logo.png",
