                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HDrvxYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HDrvxYAD/helping-hands-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-09",
                    "title": "Helping Hands Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCentral Wellbeing is a peer support mental health charity established in 2021 and based in the heart of Falkirk dedicated to providing compassion, understanding and a safe space for those navigating the challenges of poor mental health. Central Wellbeing do this through facilitating peer support groups and community activities in the Falkirk Valley area.\r\n\r\nSupport small practical tasks that keep the space running smoothly.\r\n\r\nCentral Wellbeing are looking for volunteers who are happy to help with small, practical tasks around the hub, such as putting up shelves, fixing simple items or helping with light maintenance.\r\n\r\nThese quick, one-off tasks help keep their space welcoming and accessible for everyone who uses it.\r\n\r\nThis is a flexible role you can dip in and out of when it suits you. It’s a great way to use practical skills, stay active and make a visible difference in your community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nTrades experience would be advantageous but not required.  A practical approach and willingness to help with small tasks is useful.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe Volunteer Coordinator will meet you and support you in this role, based on individual requirements.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible to suit you.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCentral Wellbeing Hub. 5 Manse Place, Falkirk, FK1 1JN.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses can be reimbursed - will be discussed with volunteers.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://centralwellbeing.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/central-wellbeing-scio-logo.png",
