                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HDr4jYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HDr4jYAD/peer-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-09",
                    "title": "Peer Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCentral Wellbeing is a peer support mental health charity established in 2021 and based in the heart of Falkirk dedicated to providing compassion, understanding and a safe space for those navigating the challenges of poor mental health. Central Wellbeing do this through facilitating peer support groups and community activities in the Forth Valley area.\r\n\r\nHelp create a warm, welcoming space where people can connect.\r\n\r\nCentral Wellbeing are looking for a Peer Support Volunteer to join their Forget Me Not Café - a friendly and supportive space for older members of the community who may feel lonely or isolated.\r\n\r\nYou’ll help with simple tasks such as setting up the space, offering a warm welcome, keeping cups topped up and supporting a relaxed, inclusive atmosphere where people feel comfortable to chat and connect.\r\n\r\nThis is a rewarding role where small acts of kindness can make a real difference. You don’t need any experience - just patience, a friendly approach and a willingness to connect with others.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo formal experience is required. \r\nWarm, patient and able to create a friendly, inclusive atmosphere. Being a good listener, showing empathy and being respectful of others’ experiences are key to this role.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe Volunteer Coordinator will meet you and support you in this role, based on individual requirements.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n3 hours per week.\r\nMonday afternoons, 12:30pm - 3pm.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDenny Library, Davies Row, Denny FK6 6FA.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses can be reimbursed - will be discussed with volunteers.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://centralwellbeing.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/central-wellbeing-scio-logo.png",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HDr4jYAD#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Peer Support Volunteer",
                        "description": "No formal experience is required. \r\nWarm, patient and able to create a friendly, inclusive atmosphere. Being a good listener, showing empathy and being respectful of others’ experiences are key to this role.",
                        "commitment": "3 hours per week.\r\nMonday afternoons, 12:30pm - 3pm.",
