            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HQ1ZlYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HQ1ZlYAL/fundraising-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-22",
                    "title": "Fundraising Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOrkney Dance and Fitness Ltd are a community‑focused fitness social enterprise dedicated to improving health, confidence, and wellbeing through accessible, low‑cost physical activity programmes.  To help us grow and reach more people, we are seeking enthusiastic Fundraising Volunteers.\r\n\r\nIn this role, you will support our sustainability by researching grants, assisting with fundraising campaigns, preparing simple proposal materials, engaging with local businesses, and helping with community fitness events. You’ll also contribute ideas to raise awareness and attract new supporters.\r\n\r\nVolunteering with us offers hands‑on experience in fundraising, community engagement, and health‑focused social impact work. You’ll develop valuable skills, work with a passionate team, and see the direct difference your contribution makes to people’s physical and mental wellbeing.\r\n\r\nThis role suits someone proactive, friendly, organised, and passionate about community fitness. No experience is required — just enthusiasm and a few flexible hours each week. Your support helps create healthier, more connected communities.\r\n\r\nVolunteering with us offers a meaningful opportunity to:\r\n- Build hands‑on experience in fundraising, community engagement, and health‑focused social impact work;\r\n- Develop transferable skills in communication, research, marketing, and project support;\r\n- Work alongside a passionate team committed to improving community wellbeing;\r\n- See the direct impact of your contribution on people’s physical and mental health;\r\n- Gain insight into how a fitness‑based social enterprise operates and grows sustainably.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThis role is perfect for someone who is:\r\n- Passionate about health, fitness, and community wellbeing;\r\n- Friendly, proactive, and comfortable speaking with a range of people.;\r\n- Organised and able to manage small tasks independently;\r\n- Interested in fundraising, community development, or the charity/social enterprise sector;\r\n- Able to offer a few hours a week — fully flexible around your schedule.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers receive a friendly and structured induction covering our mission, community fitness programmes, and how fundraising supports our work. We provide clear guidance on tasks, access to templates and resources, and ongoing support from our team. Volunteers are encouraged to learn at their own pace, with regular check‑ins, opportunities to ask questions, and optional shadowing of fundraising activities or community events.\r\n\r\nNo prior experience is needed — we offer all the training required to help you feel confident, valued, and part of the team.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThis is a flexible role.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F26ed1586-29ed-4d9d-9353-f3ed2ccaa602%2FyOcYupMgHYSAeTD2H8HLWDERqha2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=a77b6409-d608-4dd3-8523-1d67e6bf2f63",
