        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00108000034TwbHAAS",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00108000034TwbHAAS/nescan-hub",
            "name": "NESCAN Hub",
            "description": "The North East Scotland Climate Action Network (NESCAN) Hub is a regional community climate action support hub, fully funded by the Scottish Government, that covers Aberdeen City and Aberdeenshire.  \r\n\r\nOur vision is to contribute to the creation of a flourishing, connected and sustainable North East Scotland through the provision of dedicated training, help and support for community led climate action and the linkage of communities into the decision making process.",
            "website": "https://www.nescan.org",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EnvironmentRecycling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Environment / Recycling"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SocialEconomySocialEnterprise",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Social Economy / Social Enterprise"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000DRQRxYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000DRQRxYAP/nescan-hub-hr-board-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "NESCAN Hub HR Board Member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAn exciting opportunity has arisen to join the NESCAN Hub Board.  Are you passionate about community development and empowerment and acting on climate change? If so, we need you to help advise and steer the Board in relation to people management, alongside general Board work.\r\n\r\nBoard members contribute to the delivery of the Hub’s vision and aims by providing leadership and direction, ensuring good governance and advice to the NESCAN Hub staff team. This is a volunteer role that will provide the right candidate with the opportunity to be an integral part of our dedicated team and make a positive impact on the North East of Scotland, its communities, and environment.\r\n\r\n• About the role: This volunteer role requires approximately 4-6 hours commitment per month, including attendance at quarterly Board meetings (2 hours in person) in Aberdeen and the running of and attendance at our HR & People Subgroup. You will use your HR skills and experience to help support the Board and organisation in people development and management. Ideally, you will be a CIPD member, with relevant qualification or equivalent experience.\r\n• Time commitment: 4-6 hours per month\r\n• Impact: Helping a passionate, committed organisation deliver real change for people and planet.\r\n• Website: www.nescan.org\r\n\r\n• For further information and to apply for this exciting and rewarding role, please submit your CV, a covering letter and complete the Equality and Diversity form which can be found on our website https://nescan.org/work-with-us/\r\n\r\nPlease email all your documents and to recruitment@nescan.org \r\n\r\n• About NESCAN Hub\r\nThe North East Scotland Climate Action Network (NESCAN) Hub is a regional community climate action support hub, fully funded by the Scottish Government, that covers Aberdeen City and Aberdeenshire. NESCAN Hub Limited is a Charitable Company Limited by Guarantee and regulated by OSCR and Companies House.\r\n\r\nOur vision is to contribute to the creation of a flourishing, connected and sustainable North East Scotland through the provision of dedicated training, help and support for community led climate action and of communities being at the heart of a just transition.\r\n\r\nNESCAN Hub promotes equality, diversity and inclusion in our workplace and network and welcomes applications from all sections of society.\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant training and excellent support is provided to all Board Members/volunteers.",
