                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008fNLpYAM",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008fNLpYAM/nescan-hub-board-member-treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "NESCAN Hub Board Member - Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe’re seeking a knowledgeable and supportive individual to join the NESCAN Hub Board as Treasurer. This is an exciting opportunity to use your skills in charity and/or finance to provide oversight and guidance – helping us stay on strong financial footing as we deliver our vision for community led climate action across North East Scotland.\r\nThis is not an accountant role. We’re looking for someone who can bring strategic insight and governance, ensuring we make sound decisions and use our resources wisely.\r\n•\tTime commitment: 3–5 hours per month\r\n•\tRole: offering financial oversight and advice as part of the Board and to the NESCAN Hub team\r\n•\tImpact: helping a passionate, committed organisation deliver real change for people and planet\r\nIf you have experience in charity or finance and want to use it to make a genuine difference in your community, we’d love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact  Alison Stuart, CEO at email alison@nescan.org\n\n## Description\n\nWe’re seeking a knowledgeable and supportive individual to join the NESCAN Hub Board as Treasurer. This is an exciting opportunity to use your skills in and knowledge of accountancy or charity finance to provide oversight and guidance.\r\n\r\nHelp us stay on strong financial footing as we deliver our vision for community led climate action across North East Scotland.\r\n\r\nThis is not an accountant role! This is a volunteer role that would bring more financial experience and knowledge onto our Board to enable appropriate financial oversight over the governance of our charity. The right candidate with the opportunity to be an integral part of our dedicated team and make a positive impact to the North East of Scotland, its communities and its environment.  \r\n\r\nWe’re looking for someone who can bring strategic insight and governance, ensuring we make sound decisions and use our resources wisely.\r\n\r\n-Time commitment: 3–5 hours average per month\r\n-Role: offering financial oversight and advice as part of the Board and to the NESCAN Hub team\r\n-Impact: helping a passionate, committed organisation deliver real change for people and planet\r\n\r\nIf you have experience in charity or finance and want to use it to make a genuine difference in your community, we’d love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Alison Stuart, CEO at email alison@nescan.org\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant training and excellent support is provided to all Board Members/volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to volunteer. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAny relevant travel expenses will be paid at public transport rates",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
