                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QO1jrAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QO1jrAAD/community-coastal-safety-watchkeeper",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-07",
                    "title": "Community Coastal Safety Watchkeeper",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDo you want to make a real difference in your community? Do you care about safety, the coastline, and helping others?\r\n\r\nCoastwatch West Fife is a volunteer-based coastal safety and monitoring organisation - their role is simple but vital: Spot, Plot, Report, Update. Technology cannot always detect a distress flare, an overturned boat, someone in difficulty in the water, navigational hazards, or vulnerable people needing assistance, but a volunteer can. As a volunteer, you will monitor coastal areas; conduct observation patrols along coastal paths; spot and report incidents, hazards, and concerns; communicate using radio systems; support emergency services through structured reporting and updates; provide first aid assistance; assist during severe weather events; and promote public safety awareness.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThey are looking for enthusiastic, reliable individuals who understand the need for safety at sea. Full training will be provided. Even if you don’t know your latitude from your longitude, if you can spare a few hours each month, they would love to hear from you.\n\n## Training details\n\ntraining programme:\r\n\r\nWatchkeeper Core Training\r\nCoastal and community observation techniques\r\nPatrol procedures and situational awareness \r\nCommunity Resilience\r\nCB Radio operation\r\nMarine VHF familiarisation\r\nFirst Aid and emergency support skills\r\nGuidance on safely supporting emergency services\n\n## Travel details\n\nWest & Central Fife - coastal areas, harbours, shoreline locations, and community spaces as required.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nRe-imbursement of travel expenses are currently being considered on a case-by case basis for all volunteers.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
