            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000J8muDYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000J8muDYAR/social-media-and-content-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-29",
                    "title": "Social media and content assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAre you creative? Do you enjoy creating and sharing social media content? Raith Rovers Community Foundation is committed to supporting the local community to be active and improve their physical and mental health and wellbeing, create new social connections and improve their lives, offering activities including walking and football to all ages.\r\n\r\nYou can support them to maintain and enhance their social media presence, helping to engage a wide audience and demonstrate their impact on the local community. This role involves taking photos and videography of the sessions, creating inspiring and engaging content and uploading it to social media platforms. Resources and equipment will be provided .This is a great opportunity to develop new skills and gain valuable experience whilst also having fun. If this sounds like a role you would enjoy they would love to hear from you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience is required as full training will be provided. The ideal volunteer will be creative and passionate about social media/marketing with an eye for detail. Good communication skills are required for this role.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will be offered induction and ongoing training will be provided. A named contact will be available for support.\n\n## Travel details\n\nRaith Rovers, Starks Park football ground, Kirkcaldy accessible by public and private transport.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMileage will be reimbursed at 55p per mile or public transport costs will be reimbursed on production of receipts.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000J8muDYAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Social media and content assistant",
                        "description": "No experience is required as full training will be provided. The ideal volunteer will be creative and passionate about social media/marketing with an eye for detail. Good communication skills are required for this role.",
