        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008niL4AAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008niL4AAI/ayrshire-independent-living-network-ailn",
            "name": "Ayrshire Independent Living Network (AILN)",
            "description": "To provide free informative advice on self directed support.\r\nTo promote choice and control.\r\nTo support people to manage their social care budget.\r\nProvide peer mentor support.\r\nProvide a payroll service for people using self directed support.",
            "website": "https://www.ailn.org",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SelfDirectedSupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Self-Directed Support"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000G1jZmYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000G1jZmYAJ/dementia-cafe-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-03-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Dementia Cafe Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWho are we: AILN initially grew from a group of disabled people who wanted to see a change in the way that community care services were offered to people. When Direct Payments (DP) were first introduced in 2003, they were keen to promote this as an option for independent living. AILN have been providing high quality Self-Directed Support (SDS) advice and information to the people of Ayrshire for over 17 years. \r\nAILN is a peer-led, not-for-profit company limited by guarantee with charitable status. \r\nThis is an exciting time to join AILN as a volunteer.\r\n\r\nPurpose of the post\r\nOur dementia wellbeing cafes run for 2 hours each week, they provide a safe non judgmental environment with support and activities for people living with dementia and their paid or unpaid carers. Volunteers help facilitate activities, can serve teas and coffees, play games or do crafts with people or simply chat and provide companionship to someone experiencing loneliness due to their dementia or carers needing support. Volunteers don’t need to have any experience, just empathy and patience. Although the cafes run weekly volunteers can come along once or twice per month. \r\nWe are actively setting up new cafes in South Ayrshire. Please contact us for information about the one nearest to you. \r\nWe provide support, guidance, and regular supervision by the coordinator of the service\r\n•\tReceive formal recognition for your volunteering contribution and/or a reference which reflects positive contributions associated with your volunteering\r\n•\tSpecialised role training to develop skills and confidence in the role\r\n•\tReimbursement of agreed expenses directly related to the volunteering role\r\n•\tAccess to the Scotland Wellbeing Hub www.wellbeinghub.scot \r\n•\tFeel valued, supported, and respected\n\n## Training details\n\nMandatory training and Induction for the role: \r\n•\tAILN Introduction and Induction\r\n•\tSkilled Dementia Level training\r\n•\tDementia Friends\r\n•\tAdult support and protection training\r\n•\tAny other training deemed necessary for the role\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReimbursement of agreed expenses directly related to the volunteering role",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F7c4c278b-3a46-84f0-16ed-2edf2a3d3188%2FXiQTI9rs8XhdfYu2EPhcBTs4his2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=1f3b0a12-7bd1-4b2b-8169-f2147ed2731b",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000G1jZmYAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Dementia Cafe Volunteer",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000G1jZmYAJ/dementia-cafe-volunteer?#modal_register_a0gQD00000G1jZmYAJ",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "theme": [
                            {
