            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FqG1eYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FqG1eYAF/volunteer-bike-mechanics",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Volunteer Bike Mechanics",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nPlease provide a brief description of your charitable purposes\r\nEast Dunbartonshire Climate Action Hub is a community-driven adventure hub offering accessible outdoor \r\nlearning opportunities and shared space for individuals, groups and organisations across Twechar and the \r\nsurrounding areas. We provide a safe, inclusive environment where people can connect, develop new \r\nskills and enjoy the outdoors together.\r\nWe require volunteers with basic bike mechanic skills, a positive attitude and be friendly and helpful, \r\nwanting to give back to the community and get people back on their bikes safely. Work well with the \r\ngeneral public and help to share their knowledge with both the young and old.\n\n## Experience required\n\nBike Mechanic Skills\n\n## Training details\n\nAfter an informal chat and disclosure check we will meet at the centre and give volunteer a tour of the \r\nbuilding covering health & safety and fire. Ongoing training and support will be delivered\n\n## Travel details\n\nED Climate Action hub is based in Twechar Healthy Living Centre there is a bus from Kirkintillioch which runs to Twechar and stops \r\noutside the centre.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FqG1eYAF#role",
