                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Fv5S9YAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Fv5S9YAJ/trishaw-pilot",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Trishaw Pilot",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nEnable elderly people with limited mobility actually to access the outdoors. With huge beneficial impacts on\r\nhealth and wellbeing, mental and physical, for people in every part of Scotland with any kind of mobility\r\nchallenge or living in isolation or loneliness: people in all generations but especially the elderly.\r\n\r\nOur trained pilots would offer safe rides on our trishaw for care home residents and other third sector\r\norganisations. Most rides will be delivered from either the Twechar Healthy Living & Enterprise Centre or\r\nTwechar Outdoor Pursuits Centre.\n\n## Experience required\n\ncycling, generally fit although the trishaw are electric. Good communicator as the passenger probably\r\nexpects a little chat.\n\n## Training details\n\nAfter an informal chat with myself, full training is conducted by the main charity CWAS, then of course yu\r\nwill join our CWAS Twechar chapter. Meet our team of volunteers and be shown our trishaw and around\r\nboth facilities. Ongoing training and support given.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTwechar, there is a bus which runs through Twechar. Possibly other areas in East Dunbartonshire if we\r\ntransfer trishaw to say a community gala day.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Fv5S9YAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Trishaw Pilot",
