        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008niMCAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008niMCAAY/rspb-scotland",
            "name": "RSPB Scotland",
            "description": "The RSPB is the UK charity working to secure a healthy environment for birds and other wildlife, helping to create a better world for us all. The RSPB exists to conserve wild birds and the environment. We have more than one million members, over 13,000 volunteers, 1,300 staff, 200 nature reserves,9 regional offices, 4 country offices...and one vision - to work for a better environment rich in birds and wildlife.",
            "website": "https://www.rspb.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC037654"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AnimalWelfare",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Animal Welfare"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EnvironmentRecycling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Environment / Recycling"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IOhRFYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IOhRFYA1/rspb-wildlife-explorers-main-leader-8-12-yrs",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-29",
                    "title": "RSPB Wildlife Explorers (Main Leader) 8-12 yrs",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDid you know that there are brilliant RSPB Youth Groups across the UK? If you live in Aberdeenshire, you could be the person we need to help young people (8 - 12 yrs) in your area to learn about, explore and help the wildlife around them in a fun and engaging way.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou will need some experience of working with children or young people. \nExperience of creating and leading nature-based activities (or willingness to learn).\nGood communication skills with people of all ages, including children, other volunteers and parents.\nAbility to lead, motivate and organise people and work as a team to share tasks and responsibilities.\nSelf-motivated, with the ability to work on your own initiative and meet deadlines.\nA willingness to learn and undertake training (including online training) as needed for the role.\nAbility to represent the RSPB within the local community.\nBasic computer skills, such as email and Microsoft Office.\nExperience and knowledge of the following is beneficial but not required as training will be provided: writing and completing risk assessments,\nbudget management, GDPR and safeguarding best practice, leading teams of volunteers, promoting events\n\n## Training details\n\nThe RSPB if fuelled by our volunteers and we support them with excellent training and support.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThis opportunity requires attending the 3 hour sessions (which are Saturday or Sunday, once per month). As well as administration and training which can be done to suit your schedule.\n\n## Travel details\n\nActivities take place in various locations, but we also use the Village Hall in Monymusk as a base for indoor events. The Square, Monymusk, Inverurie AB51 7HJ\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThe RSPB will reimburse you for any costs associated with your volunteering.\n\n## Taster details\n\nA taster day can be set up by getting in touch with brock.lueck@rspb.org.uk",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FV2bP0spTcifwGkYv4spbsVjtxJu2%2FuHHPVR0X0ESyqG2A-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=a5d81683-2e92-49ce-94b4-393c29990cc0",
