                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HklyDYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HklyDYAR/loch-spynie-conservation-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-11",
                    "title": "Loch Spynie Conservation Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nJoin us on the first Tuesday of the month for a practical conservation volunteer day at RSPB Loch Spynie and help care for this fantastic reserve. Tasks will vary throughout the year, full training provided.\n\n## Description\n\nJoin us on the first Tuesday of the month for a practical conservation volunteer day at RSPB Loch Spynie and help care for this fantastic reserve. Led by the RSPB Warden, these hands-on volunteer days are a great way to get outdoors, learn new skills and make a real difference for local wildlife. Tasks will vary throughout the year, depending on seasonal priorities and may include trail checking and maintenance, hide cleaning and repairs, habitat management such as brash clearing and bonfire work, and occasional wildlife surveys or monitoring activities. Whether you're looking to give something back, meet like-minded people, or gain practical conservation experience, we'd love to welcome you to Loch Spynie. No previous experience is required – just enthusiasm and a willingness to get involved. Meeting at the Loch Spynie car park at 10am. Please bring water, lunch, appropriate clothing for the day and sturdy footwear. Work gloves and equipment will be provided. Under 18's must be accompanied by a responsible adult.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience required",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
