        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008niMdAAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008niMdAAI/new-lanark-trust",
            "name": "New Lanark Trust",
            "description": "New Lanark Trust is a Registered Scottish Charity (SC008552) which was established in 1974 with the aim of restoring and regenerating the former cotton mill village of New Lanark into a living and working community. The Trust has pioneered a radical approach to heritage management based tourism and hospitality, housing and commercial property rental and manufacture and retail.\n\nThe Trust and its trading subsidiaries provide a major source of employment and commercial activity in the area, employing around 150 people from the local area, with a further 70 or so employed by other businesses operating in New Lanark. In addition, many local Lanark businesses provide a range of goods and services to New Lanark which makes a very significant contribution to the regional economy, estimated at around £7-8 million per annum. \n\nNew Lanark Trust is a Registered Scottish Charity (SC008552) which was established in 1974 with the aim of restoring and regenerating the former cotton mill village of New Lanark into a living and working community. The Trust has pioneered a radical approach to heritage management based tourism and hospitality, housing and commercial property rental and manufacture and retail.\n\nThe Trust and its trading subsidiaries provide a major source of employment and commercial activity in the area, employing around 150 people from the local area, with a further 70 or so employed by other businesses operating in New Lanark. In addition, many local Lanark businesses provide a range of goods and services to New Lanark which makes a very significant contribution to the regional economy, estimated at around £7-8 million per annum.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC008552"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005egbyYAA",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005egbyYAA/learning-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Learning Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nLearning Volunteers will join an enthusiastic and diverse team who deliver world-class experiences at New \nLanark. The purpose of this role is to assist the Heritage and Visitor Attraction Teams in engagement with \nlocal schools, children, and young people. Learning Volunteers will have the chance to develop their skills \nby engaging with children of all ages during their visits to New Lanark. They will assist with the logistical \nsupport of Learning groups as well as communicating the site’s history to them in an engaging and \ninformative way. There are also opportunities for volunteers to develop their skills further by delivering tours \nand sessions themselves. \n\nWhat will you be doing?\n- Meeting and greeting learning groups on their arrival to site and providing directions\n- Supporting and assisting with the delivery of learning sessions on site\n- Assisting staff with the organisation and preparation of learning resources\n- Supporting and assisting with the planning of learning sessions where necessary \n- Developing your knowledge of New Lanark \n- Sharing the site’s history with groups in a fun and engaging way\n- Develop your facilitation skills with a view to delivering learning sessions to groups if comfortable\n\nWhat skills can you develop through this role?\n- Experience of working in the heritage sector\n- Experience of working with children and young people \n- Experience speaking to large groups of people \n- Confidence in leading events and groups of participants\n- Working as part of the Heritage Team and planning around different requirements\n\nTravel details:\nNew Lanark is around an hour's drive from Glasgow (25 miles/40 kms) or Edinburgh (35 miles/56 Kms) and is well sign-posted from all major routes. Postcode for SatNav. ML11 9BY Parking is available for volunteers free of charge in the village.\n\n2 trains run every hour (1 every hour on Sundays) from Glasgow Central or Motherwell to Lanark railway station (1.5 miles/2.5 km from New Lanark). Local buses and taxis are then available at the bus stance, adjacent to Lanark Railway station and Lanark Visit Scotland Information Centre. For local bus times contact Stuart's Coaches, on 01555 773533\n\nThere is a bus service between Buchanan Bus Station in Glasgow and Lanark. Details of this service are available by calling Stuart's Coaches on freecall 01555 773533. Please note this service does not run on a Sunday.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Good Communicator,Open minded,Sociable,experience working directly with the public\n\n## Training details\n\nNew Volunteers will be asked to attend a half day induction to get to know the site and their role more fully.  On going training will be provided in supporting and facilitating with Learning groups.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nOn a given day of volunteering, we ask volunteers to commit 4 hours of their time. The frequency of volunteering can be determined by the volunteer, e.g. once weekly, once fortnightly, once monthly.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire,Lanark\n\n## Taster details\n\nNew Volunteers will be asked to attend a half day induction to get to know the site and their role more fully.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FGUrEF83Bq6ffnwGTM5JbaeJ4Y6l1%2FYgCXFwfUxpgD4M0Y-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=f1bd1592-f9dd-4457-8aef-2e5b1f135f0e",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005egbyYAA#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Learning Volunteer",
