                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IMGwgYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IMGwgYAH/branch-coffee-group-volunteer-north-lanarkshire-branch-motherwell",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-05",
                    "title": "Branch Coffee Group Volunteer (North Lanarkshire Branch - Motherwell)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe have an exciting opportunity to get involved with our North Lanarkshire Branch and help out at their Coffee Group in Motherwell.\r\n\r\nThe Coffee Group provides an opportunity for autistic adults to meet in a relaxed, safe environment to gently socialise, enjoy some peer support and help reduce feelings of isolation.\r\n\r\nWe already have some great volunteers involved in this work, and we are keen to recruit more to develop the group.\r\n\r\nDo you have personal experience of autism and want to make a difference in your local community?\r\n\r\nAre you:\r\n\r\nApproachable, patient and understanding of the needs of others?\r\nConfident and able to speak to new people attending a group and make them feel welcome?\r\nAble to reliably commit a few hours a month to attend and support at our Coffee Group?\n\n## Experience required\n\nKnowledge and experience of the autism spectrum is an advantage but not essential as we can provide training.\r\nPatience and understanding of the needs of others.\r\nGood organisational skills.\r\nThe ability to see the world from a different perspective.\r\nApproachable.\r\nConfident in taking the lead at introducing themselves and speaking to new people attending the group.\r\nAn ability to make new people feel welcome\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be asked to complete our elearning modules\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWhen: Once a month during daytime.\r\n\r\nWhere: ASDA, Motherwell\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses reimbursed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IMGwgYAH#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Branch Coffee Group Volunteer (North Lanarkshire Branch - Motherwell)",
                        "description": "Knowledge and experience of the autism spectrum is an advantage but not essential as we can provide training.\r\nPatience and understanding of the needs of others.\r\nGood organisational skills.\r\nThe ability to see the world from a different perspective.\r\nApproachable.\r\nConfident in taking the lead at introducing themselves and speaking to new people attending the group.\r\nAn ability to make new people feel welcome",
