                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IMOpKYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IMOpKYAX/group-volunteer-scotland-in-person-north-ayrshire-branch-beith",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-05",
                    "title": "Group Volunteer Scotland In Person (North Ayrshire Branch- Beith)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe need a volunteer with a specific set of skills to help at our Gaming Group once a fortnight.\r\n\r\nWe seek someone with good knowledge of setting up gaming consoles and cable management, who can set-up the gaming consoles those attending use at their fortnightly session. You would be available at the session to help with any gaming or cable management issues, generally support the Gaming Group activities and help us after the session to dismantle and pack away consoles, etc.\n\n## Experience required\n\nHave patience, empathy and warmth and be able to maintain confidentiality.\r\nKnowledge and experience of autism\r\nReliable and punctual\r\nAble to communicate with group attendees, other volunteers and the Group Leader\r\nAble to communicate with group attendees, other volunteers and the Group Leader\r\nAble to handle situations sensitively and involve the Group Leader or Branch Chair where necessary.\r\nConfident in sending and receiving emails and able to use Microsoft Teams\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be asked to complete our elearning modules\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWhen: The Gaming Group runs every fortnight on a Saturday from 5.30- 7.30pm. You will be involved briefly before and after this time too, to set up the gaming consoles and then dismantle and them packing away after use.\r\n\r\nWhere: Beith Community Centre, Beith, North Ayrshire.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses reimbursed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IMOpKYAX#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Group Volunteer Scotland In Person (North Ayrshire Branch- Beith)",
                        "description": "Have patience, empathy and warmth and be able to maintain confidentiality.\r\nKnowledge and experience of autism\r\nReliable and punctual\r\nAble to communicate with group attendees, other volunteers and the Group Leader\r\nAble to communicate with group attendees, other volunteers and the Group Leader\r\nAble to handle situations sensitively and involve the Group Leader or Branch Chair where necessary.\r\nConfident in sending and receiving emails and able to use Microsoft Teams",
