                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpUNFYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HpUNFYA3/branch-coffee-group-volunteer-north-lanarkshire-branch-cumbernauld",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-27",
                    "title": "Branch Coffee Group Volunteer (North Lanarkshire Branch- Cumbernauld)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe have an exciting opportunity to get involved with our North Lanarkshire Branch and help out at their Coffee Group in Cumbernauld.\r\n\r\nThe Coffee Group provides an opportunity for autistic adults to meet in a relaxed, safe environment to gently socialise, enjoy some peer support and help reduce feelings of isolation.\r\n\r\nWe already have some great volunteers involved in this work, and we are keen to recruit more to develop the group.\r\n\r\nDo you have personal experience of autism and want to make a difference in your local community?\r\n\r\nAre you:\r\n\r\nApproachable, patient and understanding of the needs of others?\r\nConfident and able to speak to new people attending a group and make them feel welcome?\r\nAble to reliably commit a few hours a month to attend and support at our Coffee Group? If so, we’d welcome your application to become one of our Coffee Group Volunteers.\r\n\r\nWhat you will be doing\r\nOrganising and arranging a monthly Coffee Group with help from the Branch Chair\r\nEnsuring members are informed when there are Coffee Group coming up (via official branch NAS e-mail, social media or text, for example)\r\nAdvertising the Coffee Group (posters, leaflets, etc.)\r\nRunning the Coffee Group alongside another volunteer, this could be the Branch Chair or someone else\r\nSharing information if required at the Coffee Group (full training will be given)\r\nSignposting to other support, professionals, organisations etc.\r\nWelcoming new members.\r\nLiaising with other volunteers to ensure there is a volunteer present for the duration of the meeting.\n\n## Experience required\n\nKnowledge and experience of the autism spectrum is an advantage but not essential as we can provide training.\r\nPatience and understanding of the needs of others.\r\nGood organisational skills.\r\nThe ability to see the world from a different perspective.\r\nApproachable.\r\nConfident in taking the lead at introducing themselves and speaking to new people attending the group.\r\nAn ability to make new people feel welcome.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be asked to complete our elearning modules\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWhen and where\r\n\r\nWhen: Once a month on the 2nd Thursday of the month from 2-4pm.\r\n\r\nWhere: A cafe in Cumbernauld\r\n\r\nN.B. You need to be located in the UK and live in, or around the Cumbernauld/ North Lanarkshire area in Scotland and be able to reliably attend the Coffee Group in person.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses reimbursed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
