                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-27",
                    "title": "Branch Secretary Volunteer (North Ayrshire Branch)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Branch Secretary role is important to the running of the branch as they act as a coordinator and communicator for the branch. Without these roles, we would not have as many branches as we do.\n\n## Experience required\n\nCan write clearly and accurately.\r\nConfident in communicating with individuals or organisations by phone or email.\r\nConfident in editing information to a suitable format which is clear and concise.\r\nComputer-literate: a working knowledge of Word and a web browser, and ideally, familiarity with Excel and Outlook.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be asked to complete our elearning details\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWhen: Flexible time as required to deal with emails and to attend online (and occasional in-person) branch meetings.\r\n\r\nWhere: Home based (plus occasional travel to branch meetings in Beith)\r\n\r\nN.B. You need to be located in the UK and live in, or around the North Ayrshire area in Scotland and be able to attend occasional branch meetings in person\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses reimbursed",
