                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I4I41YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I4I41YAF/parent-support-group-volunteer-glasgow-branch",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-24",
                    "title": "Parent Support Group Volunteer (Glasgow Branch)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDo you have personal experience of autism and want to make a difference in your local community?\r\n\r\nWe are currently developing our team of volunteers to support the delivery of Parent & Carer Support Groups across the city. We currently have an evening group in the Partick area and have just launched a daytime group at The Nook (SAMH) in the city centre. We'd like to recruit more volunteers to build our capacity to offer more.\r\n\r\nThese groups provide an opportunity for parents and carers to meet others who are also living with a family member who is autistic and provide a safe environment for people to meet, share their own experience and to listen to others.\r\n\r\nWe already have some great volunteers involved this work, and we are keen to recruit more to develop other groups across the city.\r\n\r\nAs a Parent Support Group Volunteer, you will provide a friendly face to those coming along to the activities and support the Group Leader to host welcoming, friendly and supportive in-person monthly groups.\r\n\r\nWhen and where\r\n\r\nYou must live in, or near to Glasgow to do this role.\r\n\r\nWhen: A few hours per month- we have both daytime and evening opportunities available. Attendance in person once a month.\n\n## Experience required\n\nKnowledge and experience of the autism spectrum is an advantage but not essential as we can provide training.\r\nPatience and understanding of the needs of others.\r\nGood organisational skills.\r\nThe ability to see the world from a different perspective\r\nApproachable.\r\nConfident in taking the lead at introducing themselves and speaking to new people attending the group.\r\nAn ability to make new people feel welcome.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be asked to complete our elearning modules\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nA few hours per month- we have both daytime and evening opportunities available. Attendance in person once a month.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses reimbured",
