                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzoirYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HzoirYAB/walking-group-volunteer-south-lanarkshire-branch",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Walking Group Volunteer (South Lanarkshire Branch)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur South Lanarkshire Branch Walking Group provides people on the autism spectrum an opportunity to participate in short, guided walks to improve health and wellbeing and reduce social isolation.\r\n\r\nWe are seeking a friendly volunteer with an enthusiasm for walking who will work with the Walking Group Leader to help to plan and support walks along a specified route. You will follow NAS branch policies, and provide a friendly face to those coming along to the walk. These walks are regular activities.\n\n## Experience required\n\nConfident communicating with walking Group Members and listening to their thoughts and ideas.\r\nEnthusiasm for walking.\r\nConfident in taking the lead at introducing themselves and speaking to new people attending the walking group.\r\nAn ability to make new people feel welcome.\r\nUnderstanding of autism.\r\nEmpathy and understanding.\r\nGood communication and interpersonal skill.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be asked to complete our elearning modules\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWhen: One Saturday a month\r\n\r\nTime: TBC\r\n\r\nWhere: Set-off from Hamilton\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses reimbursed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzoirYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Walking Group Volunteer (South Lanarkshire Branch)",
