                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hzoe1YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hzoe1YAB/group-leader-volunteer-scotland-in-person-forth-valley-branch-falkirk",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Group Leader Volunteer Scotland In Person (Forth Valley Branch- Falkirk)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe have an exciting opportunity to get involved with our Forth Valley Branch and help lead their new monthly Autism Support Group in Falkirk, or a new group in the Forth Valley area.\r\n\r\nThe Autism Support Group in Falkirk provides autistic people and their families with a friendly, supportive and safe environment to meet others which can help to reduce feelings of isolation and where they can access information at these informal group sessions.\r\n\r\nWe already have some great volunteers involved with this work, and we are keen to recruit a volunteer Group Leader to lead the team of volunteers and facilitate and develop the group.\r\n\r\nDo you have personal experience of autism and want to make a difference in your local community?\r\n\r\nAre you:\r\n\r\nApproachable, patient and understanding of the needs of others?\r\nConfident and able to speak to new people attending a group and make them feel welcome?\r\nOrganised and able to help volunteers to work together as a small team?\r\nAble to reliably commit a few hours a month to attend and lead our Autism Support Group?\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood knowledge, skills and experience relevant to the role and user group.\r\nAble to engage participants in an inclusive way and support their involvement in the group in the way they feel most comfortable.\r\nAble to organise and plan ahead.\r\nAble to motivate people and help people work together.\r\nHave patience, empathy and warmth and be able to maintain confidentiality.\r\nKnowledge and experience of autism.\r\nAble to communicate confidently with group participants, other volunteers and Committee Members.\r\nAble to tackle difficult situations sensitively and involve the Branch Chair or Senior Branch Engagement Officer where necessary.\r\nAccess to a computer with internet access.\r\nConfident using Outlook, Word and Microsoft Teams\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be asked to complete our elearning modules\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nLast Friday of the month from 6-8pm\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses reimbursed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hzoe1YAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Group Leader Volunteer Scotland In Person (Forth Valley Branch- Falkirk)",
                        "description": "Good knowledge, skills and experience relevant to the role and user group.\r\nAble to engage participants in an inclusive way and support their involvement in the group in the way they feel most comfortable.\r\nAble to organise and plan ahead.\r\nAble to motivate people and help people work together.\r\nHave patience, empathy and warmth and be able to maintain confidentiality.\r\nKnowledge and experience of autism.\r\nAble to communicate confidently with group participants, other volunteers and Committee Members.\r\nAble to tackle difficult situations sensitively and involve the Branch Chair or Senior Branch Engagement Officer where necessary.\r\nAccess to a computer with internet access.\r\nConfident using Outlook, Word and Microsoft Teams",
                        "commitment": "Last Friday of the month from 6-8pm",
