                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzoanYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HzoanYAB/branch-social-media-volunteer-dundee-angus-branch",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Branch Social Media Volunteer (Dundee & Angus Branch)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are currently developing our team of volunteers at our busy Dundee & Angus Branch and seeking a Social Media Volunteer to help promote branch activities on Facebook and support good communication with followers of the branch.\r\n\r\nThe role will involve communicating with the committee and gathering information for social media each week and regularly updating this to the branch social media page to help keep it active.\r\n\r\nAre you:\r\n\r\nConfident using Facebook\r\nAble to write clear and accurate online posts\r\nAble to access a computer with internet access.\r\nConfident using Outlook, Word and Microsoft Teams\r\nAble to reliably commit 1- 2 hours a week\n\n## Experience required\n\nKnowledge and experience of the autism spectrum is an advantage but not essential as we can provide training.\r\nPatience and understanding of the needs of others.\r\nGood organisational skills.\r\nAre comfortable using a computer and can write clearly and accurately.\r\nThe ability to see the world from a different perspective.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be asked to complete our elearning modules\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWhen: Flexible. Approx. 1-2 hours per week\r\n\r\nWhere: Home based with occasional travel to branch meetings in Arbroath\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses reimbursed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
