                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzoULYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HzoULYAZ/branch-social-group-volunteer-forth-valley-branch",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Branch Social Group Volunteer (Forth Valley Branch)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe have an exciting opportunity to get involved with our new Forth Valley Branch and help out at their group in Falkirk, or at new groups they plan to develop across the Forth Valley area.\r\n\r\nThe branch currently run an Autism Support Group in Falkirk and this provides autistic people and their families with a friendly, supportive and safe environment to meet others which can help to reduce feelings of isolation and where they can access information at these informal group sessions.\r\n\r\nAs a Branch Social Group Volunteer, you will work with other volunteers to help facilitate a group, follow NAS branch policies, and provide a friendly face to those coming along to the activities. Branch Social Groups are regular activities but can be flexible to match your lifestyle.\r\n\r\nThe role is fully supported by the regional Senior Branch & Volunteering Engagement Officer and the other branch volunteers. You will receive full guidance and training for everything you’ll need to do.\n\n## Experience required\n\nKnowledge and experience of the autism spectrum is an advantage but not essential as we can provide training.\r\nPatience and understanding of the needs of others.\r\nGood organisational skills.\r\nThe ability to see the world from a different perspective.\r\nApproachable.\r\nConfident in taking the lead at introducing themselves and speaking to new people attending the group.\r\nAn ability to make new people feel welcome.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be asked to complete our elearning modules\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nVarious times depending upon the group/ activity you become involved with.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses reimbursed",
