                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hqu4LYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hqu4LYAR/fundraising-collections-support-volunteer-south-lanarkshire-branch-rutherglen-area",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-02",
                    "title": "Fundraising - Collections Support Volunteer (South Lanarkshire Branch- Rutherglen area)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur branch raises money to support our activities, through donations from the public collected via our collection tins located in local businesses and community settings across the Rutherglen area.\r\n\r\nMaintaining the relationship with these businesses and community settings is vital, as is regularly collecting and replacing these tins.\r\n\r\nWe're looking for a volunteer who can help us in the Rutherglen area, with this vital work.\r\n\r\nWhat you will be doing\r\n\r\nThe role would involve:\r\n\r\n• Collecting the tins from the branch and delivering them to a small list of existing locations in Rutherglen.\r\n\r\n• Periodically checking in with these local businesses/ community settings to check the tin collection is going ok.\r\n\r\n• Being a positive ambassador for the branch through these visits\r\n\r\n• Bringing the tins back to the branch when they are full so the contents can be counted and banked.\r\n\r\n• Providing empty replacement tins to these businesses/ community settings to enable further collections.\r\n\r\n• Identifying other potential sites in the Rutherglen area, who may be willing to host a collection tin for the branch.\r\n\r\nAre you:\r\n\r\nHonest and trustworthy\r\nWell-presented and personable\r\nWilling to learn about our branch and what we do and why we need to raise funds (we will help you with this)\r\nLocated in or near to the Rutherglen area\r\nReliably able to commit 2-3 hours every 2 months to collect, replace and return collection tins\n\n## Experience required\n\nHonest and trustworthy\r\nWell-presented and personable\r\nWilling to learn about our branch and what we do and why we need to raise funds (we will help you with this)\r\nLocated in or near to the specified area\r\nReliably able to commit 2-3 hours every 2 months to collect, replace and return collection tins\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be asked to complete our elearning modules\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nVisiting locations in the Rutherglen area to deliver and collect tins\r\nApprox 2 to 3 hours every 2 months\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses reimbursed",
