                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpUIPYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HpUIPYA3/walking-group-volunteer-north-lanarkshire-branch-cumbernauld",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-27",
                    "title": "Walking Group Volunteer (North Lanarkshire Branch- Cumbernauld)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur North Lanarkshire Branch Walking Group provides people on the autism spectrum an opportunity to participate in short, guided walks to improve health and wellbeing and reduce social isolation.\r\n\r\nWe are seeking a friendly volunteer with an enthusiasm for walking who will work with the Walking Group Leader to help to plan and support walks along a specified route. You will follow NAS branch policies, and provide a friendly face to those coming along to the walk. These walks are regular activities.\r\n\r\nWhat you will be doing\r\nBuilding up positive relationships with people on the autism spectrum and other volunteers in a walking group setting.\r\nSending a report to the branch to outline how the sessions are going etc.\r\nAttending the walking group sessions.\r\nWelcoming new individuals to the group.\n\n## Experience required\n\nConfident communicating with walking Group Members and listening to their thoughts and ideas.\r\nEnthusiasm for walking.\r\nConfident in taking the lead at introducing themselves and speaking to new people attending the walking group.\r\nAn ability to make new people feel welcome.\r\nUnderstanding of autism.\r\nEmpathy and understanding.\r\nGood communication and interpersonal skill\n\n## Training details\n\nComplete our elearning modules\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nAttendance of the Walking Group in person, to help facilitate and safely support the group sessions.\r\n\r\nYou need to be based in the United Kingdom and living in, or near Cumbernauld, North Lanarkshire, Scotland.\r\n\r\nWhen: One Saturday a month\r\n\r\nTime: Afternoon- time to be confirmed\r\n\r\nWhere: Set-off from Cumbernauld\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses reimbursed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpUIPYA3#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Walking Group Volunteer (North Lanarkshire Branch- Cumbernauld)",
                        "description": "Confident communicating with walking Group Members and listening to their thoughts and ideas.\r\nEnthusiasm for walking.\r\nConfident in taking the lead at introducing themselves and speaking to new people attending the walking group.\r\nAn ability to make new people feel welcome.\r\nUnderstanding of autism.\r\nEmpathy and understanding.\r\nGood communication and interpersonal skill",
                        "commitment": "Attendance of the Walking Group in person, to help facilitate and safely support the group sessions.\r\n\r\nYou need to be based in the United Kingdom and living in, or near Cumbernauld, North Lanarkshire, Scotland.\r\n\r\nWhen: One Saturday a month\r\n\r\nTime: Afternoon- time to be confirmed\r\n\r\nWhere: Set-off from Cumbernauld",
