                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpUBxYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HpUBxYAN/branch-social-group-volunteer-east-ayrshire-branch",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-27",
                    "title": "Branch Social Group Volunteer (East Ayrshire Branch)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe have an exciting opportunity to get involved with our East Ayrshire Branch and help out at their group activities in Kilmarnock, or at new groups they plan to develop across East Ayrshire.\r\n\r\nThe branch currently run an Autism Support Group in Kilmarnock and this provides autistic people and their families with a friendly, supportive and safe environment to meet others which can help to reduce feelings of isolation and where they can access information at these informal group sessions.\r\n\r\nAs a Branch Social Group Volunteer, you will work with other volunteers to help facilitate a group, follow NAS branch policies, and provide a friendly face to those coming along to the activities. Branch Social Groups are regular activities but can be flexible to match your lifestyle.\r\n\r\nWhat you will be doing\r\nAttending the monthly support group sessions\r\nSupporting the group leader with setting up and clearing away after a meeting\r\nWelcoming new members\r\nSignposting to other support, professionals, organisations etc\r\nLiaising with the group leader and the other volunteers to ensure there is a volunteer present for the duration of the meeting\n\n## Experience required\n\nKnowledge and experience of the autism spectrum is an advantage but not essential as we can provide training.\r\nPatience and understanding of the needs of others.\r\nGood organisational skills.\r\nThe ability to see the world from a different perspective.\r\nApproachable.\r\nConfident in taking the lead at introducing themselves and speaking to new people attending the group.\r\nAn ability to make new people feel welcome.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be asked to complete our elearning modules\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWhen and where\r\n\r\nWhen: Various times depending upon the group/ activity you become involved with.\r\n\r\nWhere: Kilmarnock and East Ayrshire\r\n\r\nN.B. You must live in the United Kingdom and live in, or near East Ayrshire to be able to reliably attend groups in person.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses reimbursed",
