                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpTFtYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HpTFtYAN/branch-chair-volunteer-north-ayrshire-branch",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-27",
                    "title": "Branch Chair Volunteer (North Ayrshire Branch)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Branch Chair role is vital to the running of the branch as they act as a leader and a coordinator for the branch. Without these roles, we would not have as many branches as we do.\n\n## Experience required\n\nConfident in volunteering with and communicating with other committee members, and individuals and organisations outside of the branch.\r\nConfident and comfortable speaking publicly.\r\nAble to motivate people and help people work together.\r\nAble to tackle difficult issues and problems and situations and involve other people where necessary.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be asked to complete our elearning modules\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWhilst you must be able to make a reliable commitment to the role, there is flexibility on days and the amount of time you commit. The majority of branch chairs give around 5 hours a week, but it depends how active the branch is\r\nYou must live in, or near to North Ayrshire in Scotland to do this role.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses reimbursed",
