        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008niRWAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008niRWAAY/irvine-sea-cadets",
            "name": "Irvine Sea Cadets",
            "description": "Aims to encourage valuable personal attributes and high standards of conduct in Young People, using a nautical theme based on customs of the Royal Navy.  It introduces cadets to an organised,disciplined and stimulating environment where they can learn new skills.",
            "website": "http://www.sea-cadets/Irvine/home.aspx",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FundraisingFunding",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Fundraising / Funding"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000GczSKAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000GczSKAAZ/cadet-forces-adult-volunteer-instructor",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-08",
                    "title": "Cadet Forces Adult Volunteer: Instructor",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe purpose of an Adult Instructor within the Sea Cadets is to assist in the development of young people as individuals and active citizens by providing training, guidance, direction and assistance.\r\nThe Sea Cadets aim to provide our young people with the best possible start in life through the application of nautical adventure and fun based on traditions of the Royal Navy.\r\nThe tasks of an Adult Instructor include but are not restricted to:\r\n(a) Promoting and safeguarding the welfare of Children and Young People for whom they are responsible or with whom they come in contact and ensuring compliance with the MSSC's Child Protection Policy and Guidance Document.\r\n(b) Delivering instruction and training to adults and cadets of the Sea Cadets in the subjects of the Sea Cadets syllabus and others as required by the Commanding Officer.\r\n(c) Providing supervision of cadets and other young people engaged in Sea Cadet activities and on Sea Cadets premises.\r\n(d) Assisting with the administrative functions of the Unit as required by the Commanding Officer.\r\n(e) Applications of relevant Health and Safety and Safeguarding measures as laid down in Sea Cadets documentation and external regulations.\r\n(f) Keeping up to date with changing Sea Cadet and external regulations on all matters pertaining to the training and supervision of Sea Cadets personnel.\r\n(g) Undertaking role or activity training within the Unit and elsewhere to allow performance of any of the above tasks.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNone, just the willingness to learn\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training consists of e-learning modules (Safeguarding, Health and Safety and GDPR) as well as a Induction Day Course held locally.\r\nInstructor training consists of core modules held over five weekends.\r\nOpportunities to specialise in specific areas throughout post.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses paid where appropriate.\r\nSome instructor opportunities qualify for volunteer allowance in accordance with ASCR 19.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000GczSKAAZ#role",
