        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008niSJAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008niSJAAY/inverness-womens-aid",
            "name": "Inverness Womens Aid",
            "description": "Support, information and safe accommodation for women, children and young people escaping domestic abuse.",
            "website": "https://www.scottishwomensaid.co.uk/inverness.html",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC016052"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IYDZyYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IYDZyYAP/financial-trustee-inverness-womens-aid",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-16",
                    "title": "Financial Trustee - Inverness Women's Aid",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nInverness Women's Aid (\"IWA\") is seeking a committed and enthusiastic individual to join our Board of Trustees as Financial Trustee.\n\nIWA is a women-led charity providing specialist support to women, children and young people affected by domestic abuse across Inverness and the surrounding area. Through our refuge accommodation and outreach services, we work to empower women, promote their safety and wellbeing and support them in rebuilding their lives.\n\nAs Financial Trustee, you will play an important role in supporting the Board's financial oversight and ensuring the organisation's resources are managed responsibly and effectively. Working alongside fellow trustees and IWA's management team, you will help review financial reports, monitor budgets, identify financial risks and contribute to informed decision-making to support the charity's long-term sustainability.\n\nWe are looking for someone with financial knowledge or experience, strong analytical skills, sound judgement and a commitment to IWA's work. Previous experience in charity finance or serving on a charity Board would be beneficial but is not essential.\n\nThis is a voluntary position, with Board meetings typically held every 4–6 weeks, alongside occasional additional meetings and responsibilities.\n\nHow to apply:\n\nPlease contact recruitment@invernesswa.org to request an Application Form. You will also be sent a Role Description and Person Specification to aid your application. \n\nThe deadline for applications is 16 November 2026.\n\nWe welcome applications from women who are passionate about making a meaningful difference to the lives of women, children and young people affected by domestic abuse.\n\n## Experience required\n\nApplicants should have a good understanding of financial management, budgeting and financial reporting, along with the ability to review and interpret financial information and identify potential risks. Strong analytical skills, attention to detail and the ability to communicate financial matters clearly to those without a financial background are particularly important.\n\nExperience in accounting, finance or a related field would be advantageous, as would an understanding of charity finances and relevant regulatory requirements. Previous experience as a charity trustee is not essential and we welcome applicants with transferable skills gained through professional or voluntary experience.\n\nNo formal qualifications required.\n\n## Training details\n\nAn induction will be provided to introduce the successful applicant to Inverness Women's Aid, its services, governance arrangements and the responsibilities of charity trustees. Fellow Board members and the management team will provide ongoing support, with opportunities to undertake relevant training and development.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe Board of Trustees typically meets every 4 - 6 weeks, with occasional additional meetings as required. The time commitment will vary depending on the charity's activities and priorities and therefore some flexibility will be required. We recognise that trustees balance their voluntary responsibilities with other commitments. \n\nThere is an expectation that trustees will commit to a 3-year tenure.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a virtual role. \nBoard meetings are held online via Microsoft Teams, and Trustees communicate via email. \n\nThere may be opportunities to travel to Inverness and the surrounding areas for training opportunities, AGMs or events.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FYmOd2WqKgZakaen0Upivx2S5d7w1%2Fw3TvSD9E5nVYxzRL-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=8db8e7c7-60f7-47f6-93f3-6a2ce9b2fae1",
