                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IYHVVYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IYHVVYA5/chair-of-the-board-inverness-womens-aid",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-16",
                    "title": "Chair of the Board - Inverness Women's Aid",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nInverness Women's Aid (\"IWA\") is seeking a committed and enthusiastic individual to join our Board of Trustees as Chair.\n\nIWA is a women-led charity providing specialist support to women, children and young people affected by domestic abuse across Inverness and the surrounding area. Through our refuge accommodation and outreach services, we work to empower women, promote their safety and wellbeing and support them in rebuilding their lives.\n\nAs Chair, you will play a key role in leading and supporting our collaborative Board, helping to ensure effective governance, strategic oversight and collective decision-making. Working alongside fellow trustees and IWA's management team, you will help guide the organisation's strategic direction, facilitate constructive Board discussions and ensure that our charitable purposes and values remain central to our work.\n\nWe are looking for someone with strong leadership, communication and interpersonal skills, sound judgement as well as a commitment to the work of Inverness Women's Aid. Previous experience in governance or serving on a charity Board would be beneficial, but is not essential.\n\nThis is a voluntary position, with Board meetings typically held every 4–6 weeks, alongside occasional additional meetings and responsibilities.\n\nHow to apply:\n\nTo apply, please contact recruitment@invernesswa.org to request an Application Form. This will be provided, along with a Role Description and Person Specification to aid your application. \n\nThe deadline for applications is 16 November 2026.\n\nWe welcome applications from women who are passionate about making a meaningful difference to the lives of women, children and young people affected by domestic abuse.\n\n## Experience required\n\nApplicants should be able to manage competing priorities, facilitate productive meetings, build consensus and approach sensitive or challenging matters with diplomacy and discretion. An ability to think strategically, understand organisational responsibilities and support effective decision-making is important.\n\nAn understanding of the third sector and charity governance would be advantageous, although relevant skills gained through professional, voluntary or other experience are equally welcomed. \nNo formal qualifications are required.\n\n## Training details\n\nAn induction will be provided to introduce the successful applicant to Inverness Women's Aid, its services, governance arrangements and the responsibilities of charity trustees. Fellow Board members and the management team will provide ongoing support, with opportunities to undertake relevant training and development.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe Board of Trustees typically meets every 4 - 6 weeks, with occasional additional meetings as required. As Chair, you will also be expected to dedicate some time between meetings to preparing agendas, reviewing relevant documents, liaising with fellow trustees and the management team, and providing guidance and support where needed.\n\nThe time commitment will vary depending on the charity's activities and priorities and therefore some flexibility will be required. We recognise that trustees balance their voluntary responsibilities with other commitments. \n\nThere is an expectation that trustees will commit to a 3-year tenure.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a virtual role. \nBoard meetings are held online via Microsoft Teams, and Trustees communicate via email. \n\nThere may be opportunities to travel to Inverness and the surrounding areas for training opportunities, AGMs or events.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FYmOd2WqKgZakaen0Upivx2S5d7w1%2Fr576KPoGRHlFNTIR-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=34c9c1b2-a2c9-43e1-b201-90cfb7928044",
