        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008ni4mAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008ni4mAAA/st-salvadors-episcopal-church-dundee",
            "name": "St Salvadors Episcopal Church: Dundee",
            "website": "https://www.stsalvadors.com",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC010596"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000003iMmHYAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000003iMmHYAU/food-cupboard-helper",
                    "publishStart": "2024-05-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Food Cupboard Helper",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAssisting at the Sunday Food Cupboard Drop-in, tasks include shopping and setting-up on Saturday, supervising and assisting distribution of groceries, other items, teas and coffees on Sunday afternoons, lifting, carrying, vacuuming, washing-up.\n\n## Description\n\nHelping out at the Food Cupboard Drop-in involves one or more of the following shared tasks:\r\n\r\nOn Saturday morning: shopping for basic items in (currently) Aldi Myrekirk (requires a car or van); collecting donated items from ASDA Myrekirk (or other locations); delivering items to the church (requires coordination with a keyholder); setting up tables and serving stations, sorting purchased and donated items into crates for distribution.\r\n\r\nOn Sunday afternoon: arriving early to assist at the drop-in (running between 1.00 and 2.00 p.m.), manning the door to let in clients one at a time; manning the distribution point to give out milk, loo paper, pet food; monitoring to ensure fair distribution and assisting where needed; manning the tea/coffee station; being a presence to show a friendly face and chat to clients where appropriate; clearing up at the end, vacuuming the floor, and washing-up, etc., in the kitchen.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEven tempered, assertive but friendly disposition, experience with similar voluntary work is helpful but not essential.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will be interviewed informally, given an explanatory leaflet and shown the tasks to do.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses reimbursed.\n\n## Taster details\n\nPotential volunteers are welcome to attend on Sunday and watch to get an idea of what we do.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
