                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000J0jFDYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000J0jFDYAZ/community-group-accounts-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-27",
                    "title": "Community Group Accounts Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nMain purpose of volunteering role:\r\n\r\nMany small community organisations provide some of the most essential services we rely on across West Dunbartonshire – playgroups, lunch clubs, social clubs, community growing spaces and many more.\r\n\r\nMost of these organisations rely on making applications for grant funding each year. To do this, groups need to be able to provide funders with an independently prepared end of year summary of their income and expenditure – and that’s where you come in.\r\n\r\nYou don’t have to be an experienced bookkeeper – just someone who likes working with numbers. We will provide you with the training and templates you need.\r\n\r\nMain Tasks:\r\n\r\n\r\n· Link in with group Treasurers to make sure you have all of the receipts and information needed to confirm their spend\r\n\r\n\r\n· Check through and ensure petty cash receipts and records are accurate\r\n\r\n\r\n· Checking income and payments against bank statements\r\n\r\n\r\n· Contacting group Treasurers with any follow up questions\r\n\r\n\r\n· Pulling together an outline income and expenditure report\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased in Clydebank",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000J0jFDYAZ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
