                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-16",
                    "title": "E- Commerce Assustant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAn understanding of the services the hospice can offer people with a life-limiting\r\nillness.\r\n→ Good interpersonal skills\r\n→ Be a team player and be willing to work within guidelines provided\r\n→ Be responsible and reliable\r\n→ Ability to keep up to date with hospice service provision developments\r\n→ Willingness to uphold the values of the hospice\r\nAre you a current or an aspiring ecommerce enthusiast looking to show off you're\r\nonline selling or marketing skills? You have the opportunity to showcase you're skills\r\nand have you're knowledge and enthusiasm used for social media and our online\r\nEbay platform and much more!\r\nAs an E-Commerce Volunteer you’ll be behind the scenes in our busy shops, learning\r\nall about selling donated gems through the Ayrshire Hospice Online Shop and other\r\nselling platforms.\r\nYou can get involved in everything from researching, describing, photographing, to\r\nposting. Best of all you will be helping to support our patients and families across\r\nAyrshire.\r\n__________________________________________________________\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe Ayrshire Hospice welcomes applications from all sections of the community.\r\nExperience is not essential for this role, but ideally you should demonstrate:",
