                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpRafYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HpRafYAF/area-treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-27",
                    "title": "Area Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSt John Scotland is seeking a volunteer Treasurer to support its Angus & Dundee Area Committee.\n\n## Description\n\nSt John Scotland is seeking a volunteer Treasurer to support its Angus & Dundee Area Committee.\n\nThis rewarding volunteer role offers an opportunity to help oversee local finances and support St John Scotland's work creating safer, healthier communities through services including patient transport, CPR training and increasing access to Public Access Defibrillators.\n\nThe Treasurer will work alongside fellow committee members to help ensure the effective management of local funds and support the delivery of activities and services across the area.\n\nAnyone interested in the role can find out more by reading the job description here - https://www.stjohnscotland.org.uk/sites/default/files/2026-07/Area%20Treasurer%20-%20Advert%20%26%20Role%20Description%202026.pdf \n\nTo apply, please send a cover letter outlining why you would be a good fit for the role to recruitment@stjohnscotland.org.uk. CVs are welcomed but not essential. \n\nApplications are welcomed from anyone with an interest in finance and a desire to support their local community. Previous experience as a charity treasurer is not essential, and support will be provided.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nYou can choose your hours (outside of committee meetings) and it is likely to be around 7-9 hours a month\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis role would be mostly home-based, but with attendance required at quarterly committee meetings, which take place in the Angus & Dundee area\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note: No expenses are payable for this opportunity.",
