            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000CKhdTAAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000CKhdTAAT/veterans-community-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2018-03-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-26",
                    "title": "Veterans Community Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThis project is to alleviate distress and isolation for those people who have served their country, as well as their dependents, who may now be finding it difficult to navigate their way through an increasingly complicated world\n\n## Description\n\nThe service that we offer might take the form of a fortnightly visit for tea and company, or a weekly session to help with a more specific issue, such as supporting the client to fill in forms and access services.  Perhaps the client could benefit from more intensive, more frequent support at times, and then be content with just a phone call at other times\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers must be a good communicator, enjoy company and have a desire to make a difference to those that may need their assistance\n\n## Training details\n\nThis process should take half a day with training for the position. Initial visits will be carried out jointly with the Veterans Community Support Co-ordinator who will provide future advice, guidance and training\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity happens throughout East Renfrewshire and volunteers should arrange their own transport, the expense of which will be reimbursed\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTransportation costs will be reimbursed monthly",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F373cefc1-3885-1b6e-9d4d-dad71d133a85%2FD5Fkl21abnNxZzKb66uMENQLQQn2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=b97da81f-db8c-48a0-8b1b-efac9c470402",
