        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nhMmAAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nhMmAAI/east-ayrshire-citizens-advice-bureau",
            "name": "East Ayrshire Citizens Advice Bureau",
            "description": "The Cab Service is independent and provides free, confidential and impartial advice to everybody regardless of race, sex, disability, sexuality or nationality.  It is the largest advice-giving network in the UK, with over 3,000 outlets and 20,000 volunteers.  We help people deal with nearly 6 million problems every year, in bureaux, by phone and email, at outreach sessions in places like GP surgeries and courts – even in people’s homes.",
            "website": "https://www.cas.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC028817"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/LawAndJustice",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Law and Justice"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MoneyDebtAdvice",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Money / Debt Advice"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Poverty",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Poverty"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/WelfareRightsBenefits",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Welfare Rights / Benefits"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HwhijYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HwhijYAB/volunteer-generalist-adviser",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-25",
                    "title": "Volunteer Generalist Adviser",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nEast Ayrshire Citizens Advice Bureau is a charity that ensures people in our local community have access to the advice they need, are informed about their rights and have the support available to assert them.  \n\nOur Generalist Advisers are essential members of our team.  Our Bureau management team and specialist advisors provide support and back-up but, we could not provide our service without our volunteer Generalist Advisers.\n\nGeneralist Advisers meet with clients attending our drop-in advice sessions or by appointment, discuss and diagnose their issue(s), provide relevant information and advice, agree next steps, offer practical support to ensure clients can take those next steps and write clear records of client contacts. \n\nGeneralist Advisers can provide advice on a wide range of topics, including benefits, debt and money, work issues, consumer issues, relationships, and housing.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou don't need previous experience. Many of our volunteers start with no prior knowledge. We look for people who are willing to learn, enjoy helping others, and can commit to volunteering regularly. \n\nOur volunteers are open–minded and don’t judge people or their circumstances and enjoy helping all kinds of people. You will need to be able to read and write English and have basic arithmetic skills.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining for this role is quite demanding and will typically take 6 months.\n\nYou will complete our Adviser Training Programme which has been credit rated against the Scottish Credit and Qualifications Framework (Level 6 and 10 credit points). This is a mixture of elearning and taught sessions.\n\nYou will have opportunities to shadow client interviews and to progressively take the lead until you are ready to meet with clients on your own.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWe understand that everyone has different commitments and will work with you to agree a volunteering pattern that suits both you and the bureau. \n\nFor the Generalist Adviser role we ask for at least 6 hours per week, this can be one full day (09:30 to 15:30) or split across two half days.\n\nWe also ask that you can commit to volunteering with us for at least 12 months.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe have offices in Kilmarnock (66 Portland Street, Kilmarnock, KA1 1JG) and Cumnock (79 Glaisnock Street, Cumnock, KA18 1BX). Both are well serviced by public transport.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe want to ensure that finances are not a barrier to you volunteering for us and we will reimburse reasonable volunteer expenses. We actively encourage all our volunteers to claim expenses so that we have an accurate understanding of the costs of delivering our services.\n\n## Taster details\n\nWe provide an induction to introduce you to the bureau, our people, premises, and key systems.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2Fjkcv6v7gQDSoG3NMkLoJmBra3dL2%2FvX0YxO3s3WpnoEI1-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=d2587bf3-bfc2-4dee-a9d1-782f91235dab",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HwhijYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Generalist Adviser",
                        "description": "You don't need previous experience. Many of our volunteers start with no prior knowledge. We look for people who are willing to learn, enjoy helping others, and can commit to volunteering regularly. \n\nOur volunteers are open–minded and don’t judge people or their circumstances and enjoy helping all kinds of people. You will need to be able to read and write English and have basic arithmetic skills.",
                        "commitment": "We understand that everyone has different commitments and will work with you to agree a volunteering pattern that suits both you and the bureau. \n\nFor the Generalist Adviser role we ask for at least 6 hours per week, this can be one full day (09:30 to 15:30) or split across two half days.\n\nWe also ask that you can commit to volunteering with us for at least 12 months.",
                        "applyLink": "https://www.eastayrshirecab.org.uk/volunteer",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16",
                        "theme": [
