                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HwjPZYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HwjPZYAZ/admin-and-reception-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-25",
                    "title": "Admin and Reception Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nEast Ayrshire Citizens Advice Bureau (CAB) is a charity that ensures people in our local community have access to the advice they need, are informed about their rights and have the support available to assert them. \n\nAdmin and reception volunteers play an essential role in ensuring that the bureau can operate as effectively and efficiently as possible. For most of our clients they will be their first point of contact with the bureau. Our admin and reception volunteers do not give advice to clients, but they ensure that clients feel welcomed and capture the key information required to enable the client to receive advice as quickly as possible. They perform essential ‘behind the scenes’ activities, supporting the smooth running of the bureau.\n\nTypical admin tasks include copying, scanning, printing, and uploading information, creating and maintaining filing systems, updating local information resources used by advisers and publicity materials and information resources made available to the public, receiving and sending mail and e-mail, and taking notes and minutes at meetings.\n\nTypical reception tasks include greeting clients and making them feel comfortable, providing information on the bureau and its services to clients, managing the waiting room and the booking of interview rooms, maintaining the reception area, and gathering client information with the support of checklists.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou don't need previous experience. Many of our volunteers start with no prior knowledge. We look for people who are willing to learn, enjoy helping others, and can commit to volunteering regularly.\n\nOur volunteers are open–minded and don’t judge people or their circumstances and enjoy helping all kinds of people. You will need to be able to read and write English and have basic arithmetic skills.\n\n## Training details\n\nAfter a general induction, admin and reception volunteers complete self-directed training topics using our electronic learning system. \n\nPractical training with mentors who will guide you through the bureau’s processes and how to use our systems.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWe ask for a commitment of at least three hours per week. \n\nWe also ask that people can commit to a minimum of 12 months volunteering with us.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe have offices in Kilmarnock (66 Portland Street, Kilmarnock, KA1 1JG) and Cumnock (79 Glaisnock Street, Cumnock, KA18 1BX). Both are well served by public transport.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe want to ensure that finances are not a barrier to you volunteering for us and we will reimburse reasonable volunteer expenses. We actively encourage all our volunteers to claim expenses so that we have an accurate understanding of the costs of delivering our services.\n\n## Taster details\n\nYou will undertake an induction that will introduce you to the bureau, our people, and the systems we use.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2Fjkcv6v7gQDSoG3NMkLoJmBra3dL2%2FgZIYynZhGjU3FcHM-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=357b65ee-0b7f-4083-963a-40d8553eb034",
