            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009Do6fYAC",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009Do6fYAC/mens-shed-buddy",
                    "publishStart": "2022-04-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Men's Shed Buddy",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe Men’s Shed Buddy will play a key role in helping new members access the shed, settle in and feel at home. Friendly and approachable, you will support them to join in activities and overcome any barriers they may face, whether by welcoming them, working alongside them or chatting over a cup of tea.\n\n## Description\n\nYou will play a key role in helping new members at the shed to settle in and feel at home.\nWhen new members visit, you will see if there are any barriers to accessing the shed that you can assist with, e.g. meeting them off the bus, buddying them to the shed, starting a joint project, chatting through hopes and expectations and what they want to get out of the project.\nWelcome members, and get to know them \nComplete DIY tasks in the shed alongside men.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction session with manager (specifically tailored to the project). Access to full range of online training via LearnPro e.g. health and safety, equalities.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Bowling Green Shed, behind the Robin Chapel, Queen’s Walk, Craigmillar, Edinburgh\nAccessible by bus – no 2, 14, 30 all stop on Niddrie Mains Rd., which is only a 5 minute walk.\nEH16 4EA\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThere will be a form to be completed - bus ticket / receipt needed. Preferably paid into bank account.",
