            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nhnWAAQ/blind-veterans-uk",
            "name": "Blind Veterans UK",
            "description": "Blind Veterans UK provide lifelong practical and emotional support to Armed Forces and National Service veterans regardless of when they served or how they lost their sight. We believe that no one who has served our country should battle blindness alone.",
            "website": "https://www.blindveterans.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC039411"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SensoryImpairment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Jee8iYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Jee8iYAB/outings-companion",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-10",
                    "title": "Outings Companion",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCan you spare an hour a week to brighten someone’s day? \r\n\r\nOur community volunteers provide vital companionship and social interaction for veterans who may otherwise feel isolated or lonely. By giving a small amount of your time, you can make a meaningful difference to someone's wellbeing and quality of life.\r\nWe're looking for a friendly, reliable volunteer to support a veteran in Dunfermline. The role involves meeting regularly to enjoy a coffee and a chat. The veteran is a keen music enthusiast with a particular love of 1960s and 1970s rock music, including bands such as The Beatles, Led Zeppelin, Queen, and The Who. They also enjoy discussing current affairs and staying connected to what's happening in the world.\r\nVolunteers must be aged 18 or over. Full training, guidance and ongoing support will be provided, ensuring you feel confident and well supported throughout your volunteering journey.\n\n## Experience required\n\nReliability & Punctuality. The role involves regular social interaction, so warmth and good communication are key.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull volunteer training provided including safegaurding, boundries, GDPR and sighted guiding. Volunteers\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWe're looking for a volunteer to meet with our veteran once a week on either a Monday or Friday morning for 1-2 hours.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteers to use either public transport or their own vehicle.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses reimbursed at 55p per mile and refreshments up to the value of £10 for volunteer.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Jee8iYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Outings Companion",
                        "description": "Reliability & Punctuality. The role involves regular social interaction, so warmth and good communication are key.",
                        "commitment": "We're looking for a volunteer to meet with our veteran once a week on either a Monday or Friday morning for 1-2 hours.",
