                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ImF7GYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ImF7GYAV/blind-golf-guide",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-22",
                    "title": "Blind Golf Guide",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nVolunteer Guide for Blind Golf\r\n\r\nWe're looking for a friendly and reliable volunteer to support a visually impaired veteran who enjoys playing golf. This is a rewarding opportunity to help someone continue taking part in a sport they love while building confidence, independence, and social connections.\r\n\r\nAs a volunteer guide, you'll accompany the veteran on the golf course, helping them navigate safely around the course and providing information about the direction and distance of shots. You may also assist with lining up putts, describing the layout of holes, and offering encouragement throughout the game.\r\n\r\nWe're looking for someone with a passion for golf, good communication skills, patience, reliability, and a positive attitude. Most importantly, you'll enjoy supporting others and helping them make the most of their hobbies and interests.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like to help a visually impaired veteran stay active and continue enjoying golf, we'd love to hear from you\n\n## Experience required\n\nA thorough understanding and passion for golf\r\nEmpathy for working with people with disabilities\r\nAbility to work in a team\r\nEffective verbal communication.\r\nHave held a full drivers license for a minimum of 2 years.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull volunteer training provided including safegaurding, boundries, GDPR and sighted guiding. Volunteers for this role are expected to have a good understanding of golf to be able to provide support.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteer must have access to their own car to be able to pick up member and take them to the golf course and back to their home.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses reimbursed at 55p per mile and refreshments up to the value of £10 for volunteer.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
