                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HeBPZYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HeBPZYA3/walking-companion-inverness",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-05",
                    "title": "Walking Companion (Inverness)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are committed to supporting our blind veterans no matter where they are.\r\n\r\nDo you enjoy walking and spending time outdoors? We’re looking for a friendly volunteer to accompany one of our blind veterans on regular local walks.\r\n\r\nOur veteran is keen walker and would love the support of someone who can accopany them on a weekly walk. This is a great opportunity to share conversation, fresh air, and the joy of walking while making a real difference.\r\n\r\nIf you’d like to help a veteran enjoy greater independence and wellbeing, please get in touch to find out more.\r\n\r\nVolunteers must be over the age of 18 and understand the importance of relationship boundaries. The role can be flexible around your other commitments, but we ask that you are reliable and punctual for our veterans. You will be fully trained and supported so you feel comfortable and confident in your volunteering.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly & welcoming\r\nGreat communicator\r\nPatient & attentive\r\nA love of the outdoors and walking\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction and full training provided including, but not limited to - sighted guiding skills, safeguarding, visual impairments and dealing with emergencies\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nonce a week/fortnight\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteers would need to use their own or public transport\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nreasonable expenses reimbursed including travel expenses. Fuel reimbured at 55p per mile.",
