                    "title": "Buchanan Galleries Festive Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBuchanan Galleries Festive Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\n<p><strong>Buchanan Galleries Festive Volunteer</strong><br />\n<strong>Organisation</strong>: Glasgow Children&rsquo;s Hospital Charity<br />\n<strong>Location</strong>: Buchanan Galleries Shopping Centre, 220 Buchanan Street, Glasgow, G1 2FF<br />\n<strong>Minimum Age</strong>: 14</p>\n\n<p><strong>Opportunity Summary</strong></p>\n\n<p>We&rsquo;re excited to be back at Buchanan Galleries for another magical Christmas season! Our much-loved activities are returning, with an extra sparkle added to Santa&rsquo;s Grotto this year &ndash; and we&rsquo;d love your support to make it all happen. We&rsquo;re looking for enthusiastic volunteers to help with:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><strong>Christmas Pop-Up Shop</strong> &ndash; greet customers and process sales</li>\n\t<li><strong>Gift Wrapping Station</strong> &ndash; wrap presents with care (from Friday 11th December onwards)</li>\n\t<li><strong>Choir Collections</strong> &ndash; help fundraise while our wonderful choirs perform</li>\n\t<li><strong>Santa&rsquo;s Grotto</strong> &ndash; support Santa and his elf by assisting children with their &lsquo;<em>Letters to Santa&rsquo;</em> and festive colouring sheets (every Saturday &amp; Sunday from 5th December onwards, plus Monday&ndash;Wednesday before Christmas)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Each role is clearly defined, so you can pick from the above activities and you&rsquo;ll know exactly what you&rsquo;re signing up for.</p>\n\n<p>Join us to spread Christmas cheer, get into the festive spirit, and help raise vital funds for the families we support.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Volunteer Tasks</strong></p>\n\n<p>Each activity has different tasks associated with it, volunteers will get a full view of what&rsquo;s involved with each activity prior to signing up.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Shift Times</strong></p>\n\n<p>Shift times vary depending on the centre&#39;s opening/closing times but we have morning, afternoon and evening shifts available EVERY day from the 13th of November until the 24th of December! This is a very flexible opportunity so whether you can do one, five, twenty shifts, we would love to hear from you.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Volunteer Benefits</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Join a friendly, supportive team and meet new people</li>\n\t<li>Receive a GCHC volunteer T-shirt and full training</li>\n\t<li>Travel expenses reimbursed</li>\n\t<li>Gain confidence and experience working with the public</li>\n\t<li>Make a direct impact in raising vital funds for young patients, their families and NHS hospital staff</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Volunteer Support Information</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong>Induction &amp; Training</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>All volunteers receive a full induction before their first shift.</li>\n\t<li>Training includes:\n\t<ul>\n\t\t<li>Health &amp; safety procedures for the event</li>\n\t\t<li>Basic cash handling procedures</li>\n\t\t<li>Customer service guidance for interacting with supporters</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Supervision &amp; Onsite Support</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Each shift has a GCHC staff member present.</li>\n\t<li>Volunteers are always supported while on duty&mdash;whether it&rsquo;s their first or fifth shift.</li>\n\t<li>Help is on hand to deal with any unexpected issues or questions from the public.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Wellbeing &amp; Inclusion</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>GCHC is committed to creating an inclusive, welcoming space for all volunteers.</li>\n\t<li>Volunteers can share any access or support needs during onboarding.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Recognition</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Volunteers are warmly recognised and thanked throughout their journey with us.</li>\n\t<li>Volunteer hours are recognised with a small gift with each hours milestone reached.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>The role is ideal for:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>People looking to gain experience in events or charity work</li>\n\t<li>Students or young people exploring future career paths</li>\n\t<li>Anyone who enjoys public-facing roles in a fun and rewarding setting</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Contact for More Information</strong><br />\nIf you&rsquo;d like more information before registering your interest, please get in touch with our Volunteer Team:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Email: volunteer@glasgowchildrenshospitalcharity.org</li>\n\t<li>Phone: 0141 212 8750</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>We look forward to welcoming you to <strong>Team GCHC</strong>!</p>\n\n## Experience required\n\n- No particular skills or previous experience required\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses reimbursed",
