        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008ngg4AAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008ngg4AAA/eyemouth-museum-trust-ltd",
            "name": "Eyemouth Museum Trust Ltd",
            "website": "http://www.eyemouthmuseum.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC012548"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpSBlYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HpSBlYAN/museum-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-27",
                    "title": "Museum Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThere are two aspects to the museum volunteering - behind the scenes working on the collection and front of house in the reception/shop.\r\n\r\nBehind the scenes - This is mainly involved with the museum's collection and looking to the future for exhibitions, etc.  The collection consists of a wide variety of artefacts and photographs  which we are in the process of checking against the catalogue database to check its accuracy.  There is also general organisation of the back office to ensure it is all up to date.. Most volunteers do this on a Monday morning.  \r\n\r\nReception/shop - Although seasonal most volunteers spend the winter behind the scenes but we would be looking for cover in the shop   You will be required to take the entry fees and payment from the shop.  However we also are the town's tourist information centre so you will get asked a lot of questions - this is often the most interesting part.  It is surprising what people want to know.  \r\n\r\nVolunteering here is varied and interesting, and although you may think you need to enjoy history this is not necessarily the case.\r\n\r\nThis volunteering can be reasonably flexible.  \r\nThe museum opens from April to October, seven days a week for 5 hours (11am - 4pm); but most volunteers usually work a few hours.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThere are no real skills required, as we would train the volunteers.  However, if you work in the shop you will need to be comfortable speaking to people and dealing with money.  \r\nAny skills the volunteers can bring to the Museum would be a bonus.; we would hope that if a volunteer has a special interest or some expertise in an area we would be able to find something that fits around that skill.  \r\nWe are always open to suggestions that could improve our experience.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou would come to the museum and shadow someone in the shop/back office to get an idea of what is required.\r\nIf volunteers were unsure we can offer shadowing for a longer period of time.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
