        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nglUAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nglUAAQ/waverley-housing",
            "name": "Waverley Housing",
            "description": "The provision of affordable social rented housing for people who need it, improving our houses to the Scottish Housing Association Quality Standard and beyond; working with residents to help create desirable communities; and creating a strong, successful and respected organisation.\r\nThe main services provided are:\r\n\r\nHousing management, including estate management and lettings, as well as being actively involved in tenant participation.\r\n\r\nProperty management, including responsive repairs and planned maintenance.",
            "website": "https://www.waverley-housing.co.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC026231"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/HousingAssociation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Housing Association"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HuuybYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HuuybYAB/join-our-board",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-18",
                    "title": "JOIN OUR BOARD",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBoard Member position within a growing RSL.\n\n## Description\n\nBoard Member position within a growing RSL.\r\n\r\nHelp shape the future of affordable housing in the Scottish Borders\r\n\r\nGood homes change lives. At Waverley Housing we’re committed to providing affordable, high-quality homes and supporting thriving communities across the Scottish Borders. We’re looking for new voluntary Board Members to help guide us through the opportunities and challenges ahead.\r\n\r\nAs a member of our Board, you’ll play an important role in setting the strategic direction of a respected Registered Social Landlord and charity. You’ll work alongside fellow Board Members and our Leadership Team to make decisions that have a lasting impact on our tenants, communities and the future provision of affordable homes in the area.\r\n\r\nFrom investing in existing homes to responding to Scotland’s housing emergency, embracing new opportunities and keeping tenants at the heart of everything we do, you’ll help to shape the future of Waverley Housing. \r\nWe’re looking for people who:\r\n• Enjoy working collaboratively and listening to different perspectives\r\n• Share our commitment to providing affordable homes and excellent services\r\n• Are willing to accept collective responsibility for decisions\r\n• Value equality, diversity and inclusion\r\n• Offer relevant personal, professional or lived experience\r\n\r\nYou don’t need previous Board experience. If you bring an aptitude for strategic decision-making and a commitment to making a positive difference to people’s lives, we’ll provide a full induction, training and ongoing support.\r\n\r\nA full description of the skills, knowledge and qualities we’re seeking is available in our Board Member recruitment pack. We welcome applications from people with a wide range of backgrounds and experience. We’re particularly interested in hearing from people with housing management or asset management experience. However, we’d welcome applications from anyone who shares our drive to ensure everyone has a safe, affordable place to call home.\r\n\r\nIf you’d like to use your skills to make a lasting difference to people in the Scottish Borders, we’d love to hear from you.\r\nPlease send your CV and a short cover letter outlining how you meet the skills, knowledge and qualities outlined here to our Executive Support Officer, June Wilson: June.Wilson@waverley-housing.co.uk.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to find out more about this opportunity before applying, our Chief Executive, Paul Scott, would welcome the opportunity to speak to you. To arrange a call with Paul, please contact June using the email address above or call us on 01450 364200.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou don’t need previous Board experience. If you bring an aptitude for strategic decision-making and a commitment to making a positive difference to people’s lives, we’ll provide a full induction, training and ongoing support.\r\nA full description of the skills, knowledge and qualities we’re seeking is available in our Board Member recruitment pack. We welcome applications from people with a wide range of backgrounds and experience. We’re particularly interested in hearing from people with housing management or asset management experience. However, we’d welcome applications from anyone who shares our drive to ensure everyone has a safe, affordable place to call home.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction sessions to get to know the Leadership Team and understand the role of a Board Member.\r\nA mentor from the Board can be put in place if required.\r\nOngoing training opportunities are made available.\r\nOngoing support from fellow Board Members and Staff.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThere are 6 Board meetings per year on the last Tuesday of the month they are taking place from 5:30-7:30pm. \r\n\r\nThere is an annual summer event in June and a Strategy Day in December.\r\n\r\nMeetings take place in Hawick.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nOut of pocket expenses are reimbursed.\r\n\r\nReceipts required.\n\n## Taster details\n\nApplication will be reviewed and contact will be made for an informal chat with Chief Executive within 7 days of receipt of application.\r\n\r\nInitial informal chat with Chief Executive.\r\n\r\nAttending a Board meeting in capacity of Observer.\r\n\r\nA full induction will be put in place once the Board Member has been elected to the Board.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HuuybYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "JOIN OUR BOARD",
                        "description": "You don’t need previous Board experience. If you bring an aptitude for strategic decision-making and a commitment to making a positive difference to people’s lives, we’ll provide a full induction, training and ongoing support.\r\nA full description of the skills, knowledge and qualities we’re seeking is available in our Board Member recruitment pack. We welcome applications from people with a wide range of backgrounds and experience. We’re particularly interested in hearing from people with housing management or asset management experience. However, we’d welcome applications from anyone who shares our drive to ensure everyone has a safe, affordable place to call home.",
