            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pc7b5AAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pc7b5AAB/visitor-experience-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Visitor Experience Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nFollowing a four-year refurbishment, David Livingstone Birthplace has opened our brand-new museum exhibition, shop, and café in July 2021. This is an exciting time to join us as we welcome visitors into the new museum for the 2022 season.\nWe are looking for enthusiastic Visitor Experience Volunteers to join our Visitor Experience team. This is a vital role in supporting the museum and interacting with the public as the face of the David Livingstone Birthplace. The Visitor Experience Volunteers will greet visitors and engage with them in a friendly and informative manner to ensure that they have an enjoyable experience.\nWe are particularly looking for Visitor Experience Volunteers that are excited about greeting visitors and selling tickets at the Welcome Desk. This is an important task as you will be the first point of contact for all visitors at the beginning of their journey around the museum. Full training will be given for Welcome Desk duties and volunteers will work closely with staff.\n\n## Experience required\n\nArts / Music / Drama / Crafts,Befriending / Mentoring, Creative,\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive till training and cash handling training as part of this role. We also endeavor to provide access to heritage-specific training and skills development opportunities for all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nAs our museum is open between 10am-4pm daily, we would expect volunteers to work sometime between these hours if possible.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nBlantyre\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAll volunteers will be able to claim £5 towards their travel expenses.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pc7b5AAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Visitor Experience Volunteer",
                        "description": "Arts / Music / Drama / Crafts,Befriending / Mentoring, Creative,",
                        "commitment": "As our museum is open between 10am-4pm daily, we would expect volunteers to work sometime between these hours if possible.",
