                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNpgbAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNpgbAAD/retail-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Retail Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\n•\tTo sell and promote retail products in the David Livingstone Birthplace Shop (EPOS). \n•\tTo merchandise products. \n•\tTalking to visitors. \n•\tCollecting feedback from visitors. \n•\tTo manage and monitor cash transactions. \n•\tTo help with the cleaning of the shop (particularly at the end of the day) - e.g. brushing and mopping the floor.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Good Communicator,Sociable,Team Player,Trustworthy,Good customer service skills\n\n## Training details\n\nRetail volunteers will do shadow shifts with experienced volunteers as part of their till training.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nA monthly rota broken down into 2 shifts per day (AM/PM) 7 days a week. Requesting these volunteers do a minimum of 4 hours per week. A monthly rota broken down into 2 shifts per day (AM/PM) 7 days a week. Requesting these volunteers do a minimum of 4 hours per week. Commitment 3 Months 4 Hours, Weekly\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nBlantyre\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers can claim up to £5 per shift for travel",
