            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Jpb4DYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Jpb4DYAR/energy-advice-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-13",
                    "title": "Energy Advice Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAs an Energy Advice Volunteer you will support colleagues from the Low Carbon Communities Team (LCC), the Affordable Warmth Team (AWT) and Home Energy Scotland (HES) and the Highland Energy Community Partnership (HECP) as they deliver outreach events across the Highlands.  \r\n\r\nYou will provide light touch energy advice to members of the public, helping them to understand how to reduce their energy use and minimise their carbon emissions.  \r\n\r\nVolunteering opportunities could involve attending local events, and/or supporting colleagues to deliver targeted energy advice to people through doorstep engagement in specific areas.  \r\n\r\nYou will support staff members and will maximise engagement and the support available. \r\n \r\nAdditional office-based volunteering opportunities may occasionally arise, i.e. helping with printing and posting and data entry tasks.\n\n## Training details\n\n2.5 hours of in-person (or only if preferred) training on how to deliver light touch energy advice and support is provided",
