        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nfBbAAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nfBbAAI/orkney-fencing-club",
            "name": "Orkney Fencing Club",
            "description": "The Orkney Fencing club is a community fencing club. We welcome all ages from 10 years old upwards. We welcome  all abilities of fencer from beginner to elite athlete. The club has been running for more than 25 years. We are affiliated to Scottish Fencing and welcome those who may need additional facilities and help in order to enjoy fencing including seated/ wheelchair fencing which we offer as part of our regular club sessions.\r\n\r\nWe meet Wednesdays 1930 to 2130 in the Pickaquoy Centre as well as some additional/ ad hoc sessions. We have fencers who go to competitions and arrange trips which are available to those interested in partaking .\r\n\r\nFeel free to come and give it a go.",
            "website": "https://orkneyfencingclub.co.uk/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IFqWzYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IFqWzYAL/secretary",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Secretary",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOrkney Fencing Club is looking for a club Secretary to aid in:\r\n- Membership management;\r\n- Use the SPOND Sports Team Management App (experience desirable but not essential);\r\n- Minutes and communications relating to club; \r\n- Other club Secretary duties that arise.\r\n\r\nThe volunteer does not need to be member of the club but may need to be PVG checked. \r\n\r\nWhat could a volunteer gain from the experience:\r\n- Administrative and Communication experience;\r\n- Aiding and help with continued running of Orkney Fencing Club;\r\n- IT skills and organisation;\r\n- Flexibility and ability to use initiative to make of position what they wish to contribute.\n\n## Experience required\n\nExperience not essential but a willingness and desire to assist is good.\r\n\r\n- Basic admin/IT skills desirable;\r\n- Experience with SPOND desirable but not essential;\r\n- Being friendly with a desire to assist main requirement and others positive to have but not essential.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe volunteer will have the support/assistance of rest of committee and club.  We will provide access and information as required and are contactable if any assistance needed. We are an amateur sports club so will not be overly formal but we will endeavour to assist as best we can.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThis is a flexible role.  There will be regular involvement with regards to membership management etc but no specific/set times. \r\n\r\nAttendance at committee meetings will be required when they occur.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable expenses will be reimbursed by club.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
