                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JltHSYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JltHSYAZ/board-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-12",
                    "title": "Board Member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAdvocacy Orkney are looking for new members to be part of their Advocacy Orkney Board.  The Board meets 4-5 times per year usually virtually, with a maximum of 1-2 meetings held in person in Kirkwall. \r\n\r\nThe role of the Board Member is to provide governance, oversight and direction to the service and team.\r\n\r\nWhat could a volunteer gain from the experience:\r\nTo gain satisfaction knowing that the service is moving forward in a way that is required for clients requiring the service in Orkney.\n\n## Experience required\n\n- An insight into governance, risk and performance management of a service;\r\n- Good communicator;\r\n- Able to provide constructive challenge.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining would be tailored according to what the potential Board member asks for.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses can be paid",
