            "name": "Orkney ZeroWaste",
            "description": "Orkney Zerowaste is a voluntary organisation set up to reduce the amount of material and goods that goes into landfill sites and incinerators. This means eliminating waste at its source, reusing what we have, and providing practical ways of recycling. \r\n\r\nWhether it is encouraging people to Love Food and Hate Waste, running a flexible business recycling service or providing a re-use yard to encourage re-purposing, Orkney Zerowaste endeavours to inspire people to live more sustainably.",
            "website": "https://www.orkneycommunities.co.uk/OZ",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC036522"
                }
            ],
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2F5d9d0151-82c3-80eb-79d6-3e2d48816771%2FBjA8itcPfHQ5QR1dwi2pYnBMdoW2%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=175192c1-e04e-4087-801b-048ac82b22d9",
            "cause": [
                {
