                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I2CnVYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I2CnVYAV/marketing-and-social-media-trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-18",
                    "title": "Marketing and Social Media Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nLocation\r\n\r\nRemote (UK-based preferred)\r\n\r\nCommitment\r\n\r\nApproximately 3–6 hours per month, including attendance at trustee meetings (typically held online).\r\n\r\nSalary\r\n\r\nVoluntary, unpaid position. Reasonable agreed expenses may be reimbursed.\r\n\r\nAs a Trustee with responsibility for Marketing & Social Media, you will work alongside the Board of Trustees to help shape the charity's public profile and communications. You'll provide strategic oversight while also helping to develop engaging content and campaigns that increase awareness and support for the charity.\r\n\r\nThis is an excellent opportunity for someone with marketing, communications or digital media experience who wants to use their skills to make a meaningful difference.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities\r\n\r\nProvide strategic guidance on the charity's marketing and communications.\r\nOversee and help develop our social media presence across relevant platforms.\r\nCreate and implement campaigns to increase awareness of Turner syndrome and the work of Ragdolls UK.\r\nHelp grow our online community and supporter engagement.\r\nSupport fundraising campaigns through effective marketing and digital communications.\r\nEnsure all communications reflect the charity's values and brand.\r\nAdvise the Board on marketing opportunities, trends and best practice.\r\nWork collaboratively with fellow trustees and volunteers.\r\n \r\n\r\nWhat are we looking for?\r\nWe're Looking For Someone With\r\n\r\nEssential\r\n\r\nExperience in marketing, communications, digital marketing or social media.\r\nExcellent written communication skills.\r\nCreativity and enthusiasm for engaging online audiences.\r\nAn understanding of branding and audience engagement.\r\nA commitment to the aims and values of Ragdolls UK.\r\nAbility to work collaboratively as part of a trustee board.\r\nDesirable\r\n\r\nCharity or voluntary sector experience.\r\nExperience with social media analytics.\r\nGraphic design skills (e.g. Canva).\r\nWebsite or email marketing experience.\r\nPR or media relations experience.\r\nFundraising marketing experience.\r\nKnowledge or personal experience of Turner syndrome (not essential).\r\nWhat difference will you make?\r\nRagdolls UK is a charity dedicated to supporting girls and women with Turner syndrome, along with their families and carers. We provide information, raise awareness, build supportive communities, and work to improve the lives of those affected by Turner syndrome across the UK.\r\n\r\nAs a trustee, you will share responsibility for the overall governance of the charity, ensuring it is well run, financially sustainable and delivers on its charitable objectives. Trustees are expected to act in the charity's best interests and comply with charity law and governance requirements.\r\n\r\nWhat You'll Gain\r\n\r\nThe opportunity to make a real difference to families affected by Turner syndrome.\r\nBoard-level governance experience.\r\nThe chance to shape the future direction of a national charity.\r\nExperience working with a committed and supportive trustee team.\r\nProfessional development and the opportunity to expand your network.\r\n \r\n\r\nBefore you apply\r\nIf you're passionate about using your marketing and communications skills to support an important cause, we'd love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nTogether, we can raise awareness of Turner syndrome and provide greater support for those who need it most.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
