                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HcwM9YAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HcwM9YAJ/volunteer-driver-inverurie-area",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-04",
                    "title": "Volunteer Driver - Inverurie Area",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAberdeenshire North Foodbank provide emergency food parcels and practical support to local people facing hardship. Volunteers play a crucial role in the daily operation of our foodbank centres, providing a warm welcome and friendly face to someone during a difficult period in their life. As a volunteer driver, you'll be asked to deliver emergency food to someone unable to collect from their nearest foodbank; this may be due to mobility or health issues, caring responsibilities, their rural location and lack of available or affordable transport options.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F8d84398b-9bb4-42f2-b3f3-1ca2bfcec168%2FQihUT0i1qRZmnHJ6Smt7hlTfVef2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=97bf27d4-6248-4577-9e05-0153cf32d507",
