        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400000VS0JCAA1",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400000VS0JCAA1/social-bite-aberdeen",
            "name": "Social Bite (Aberdeen)",
            "description": "Support homeless people through provision of food and employment opportunities, and raise money for good causes through social enterprise. We are a ‘Social Business’. This means that 100% (every single penny) of our profits are given to good causes and 1 in 4 of our team are formerly homeless people. We also feed the local homeless community through our ‘Suspended Coffee and Food’ initiative.",
            "website": "http://social-bite.co.uk/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/HousingHomelessnessness",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Housing / Homelessnessness"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SocialEconomySocialEnterprise",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Social Economy / Social Enterprise"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7HeBAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7HeBAAV/social-supper-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-23",
                    "title": "Social Supper Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\n-Aberdeen - Social Supper Volunteering\r\n\r\nWe believe in meeting people’s basic needs for nutritious food and shelter, while also building positive relationships. We want to provide individuals with opportunities to make the changes they want to make in their lives.\r\n\r\nFood is a great way of meeting the needs of people, as well as offering community, a listening ear, and sharing information about other services that people may need. Volunteers are an essential part of making this possible at our social supper every week.\r\n\r\nWhat will you be doing?:\r\nAs part of a team of volunteers and Social Bite employees, you will:\r\n•help set up the shop to offer the supper service, including preparing food, drinks and tables.\r\n•serve hot food or drinks to people at their table.\r\n•welcome people into the shop, be a friendly face and have chats with people as they wait for food.\r\n•share information about other services provided by our partner charities (housing, benefits advice, courses, drug/alcohol support).\r\n•help boxing up pre-made meals that can be taken as take-away.\r\n•help clean up after the supper has finished.\r\n\r\nWhen and where will you volunteer?:\r\nOur social supper takes place every Thursday. You would be volunteering from 3-5:15pm.\r\n\r\nLocation: Social Bite shop, 516 Union Street, AB10 1TT, Aberdeen.\r\n\r\nDoes this sound like you?:\r\nYou…\r\n•are friendly and able to make sure that everyone feels safe and welcome in the café.\r\n•enjoy engaging with people of all backgrounds.\r\n•do not judge people.\r\n•can work as part of a team.\r\n•do not mind doing different tasks (serving hot drinks, food etc).\r\n•understand personal and professional boundaries, including how to keep these whilst volunteering.\r\n•know the importance of keeping confidentiality as part of your volunteering.\r\n\r\nWe will provide guidance on how to do the tasks, as well as training on challenging behaviour, boundaries and how to maintain these.\r\n\r\nWe ask people to volunteer regularly, which can be every week (or every two weeks), depending on your availability. This is to provide familiarity and a consistent service for the people we support.\r\n\r\nWhat can you gain from this volunteering?:\r\n•Be part of a friendly and supportive team\r\n•Develop or enhance your interpersonal skills by engaging with people of all backgrounds\r\n•Contribute actively to providing food to people who needs it\r\n•Develop or enhance your service and catering skills\r\n•Get experience with direct community work\r\n•Meet new people and have opportunities to engage in our social activities for volunteers.\r\n•Opportunities for furthering your learning on different topics related to homelessness.\r\n\r\nYour accessibility:\r\nPlease let us know if you need any support or adjustments to make our first chat together and volunteering a positive experience for you.\r\n\r\nAny volunteering expenses for helping with these activities, which have been agreed, will be paid back to you. We cover local travel costs at public transport rate. The café is within walking or wheeling distance of public transport (bus or train). There is no free parking nearby. The café is wheelchair accessible to enter, but we do not have an accessible toilet.\r\n\r\nKeeping everyone safe:\r\nOur safeguarding policy details our commitment to keeping everyone safe. It is expected of everyone to adhere to these commitments. We expect all volunteers to do our relevant training, so you can help keep yourself and others safe from harm.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity and all help makes a real difference for people we support and is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Charlotte Laursen, Social Bite Volunteer Coordinator at email volunteering@social-bite.co.uk\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant training and excellent support is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nOur social supper takes place every Thursday. You would be volunteering from 3-5:15pm.\n\n## Travel details\n\nSocial Bite café, 516 Union Street, Aberdeen, AB10 1TT *(near top of Union Street/close to Holburn Junction). Central Aberdeen, easy to get to via various transport routes.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F235263cd-699a-7693-80c0-82bd57dc29e6%2FT6gq48nH9VPLVS0wxSilMKgSLmC2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=4cee680d-6fa5-4b83-9420-e40ff9f464e6",
