                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhvymAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhvymAAB/social-bite-breakfast-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-31",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-26",
                    "title": "Social Bite Breakfast Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\n-Aberdeen - Social Breakfast volunteering:\r\n\r\nWe believe in meeting people’s basic needs for nutritious food and shelter, while also building positive relationships. We want to provide individuals with opportunities to make the changes they want to make in their lives. \r\n\r\nFood is a great way of meeting the needs of people, as well as offering community, a listening ear, and sharing information about other services that people may need. Volunteers are an essential part of making this possible through our breakfast socials every morning. \r\n\r\nWhat will you be doing?:\r\nAs part of a team of volunteers and Social Bite employees, you will: \r\n\r\n•\thelp set up the shop to offer the take-away food service. \r\n•\tprepare and serve breakfast rolls and / or hot drinks to people. \r\n•\tbe a friendly face, having brief chats with people as they wait for food. \r\n•\tshare information about other services provided by our partner charities (housing, benefits advice, courses, drug/alcohol support). \r\n•\thelp clean up after the scran has finished. \r\n\r\nWhen and where will you volunteer?:\r\nFlexible times available to volunteer at social breakfast Monday to Friday. You would be volunteering from 7:45am – 9:45am.on the day(s) you choose to volunteer.\r\n\r\nLocation: Social Bite shop, 516 Union Street, AB10 1TT, Aberdeen. \r\n\r\nDoes this sound like you?:\r\nYou… \r\n•\tare friendly and able to make sure that everyone feels safe and welcome in the café. \r\n•\tenjoy engaging with people of all backgrounds. \r\n•\tdo not judge people. \r\n•\tcan work as part of a team. \r\n•\tdo not mind doing different tasks (serving hot drinks, food etc). \r\n•\tunderstand personal and professional boundaries, including how to keep these whilst volunteering. \r\n•\tknow the importance of keeping confidentiality as part of your volunteering. \r\n\r\nWe will provide guidance on how to do the tasks, as well as training on challenging behaviour, boundaries and how to maintain these. \r\n\r\nWe ask people to volunteer regularly on the same day, which can be every week (or every two weeks), depending on your availability. This is to provide familiarity and a consistent service for the people we support. \r\n\r\nWhat can you gain from this volunteering?:\r\n•\tBe part of a friendly and supportive team \r\n•\tDevelop or enhance your interpersonal skills by engaging with people of all backgrounds \r\n•\tContribute actively to providing food to people who needs it \r\n•\tDevelop or enhance your service and catering skills \r\n•\tGet experience with direct community work \r\n•\tMeet new people and have opportunities to engage in our social activities for volunteers. \r\n•\tOpportunities for furthering your learning on different topics related to homelessness. \r\n\r\nYour accessibility:\r\nPlease let us know if you need any support or adjustments to make our first chat together and volunteering a positive experience for you. \r\n\r\nAny volunteering expenses for helping with these activities, which have been agreed, will be paid back to you. We cover local travel costs at public transport rate. The café is within walking or wheeling distance of public transport (bus or train). There is no free parking nearby. The café is wheelchair accessible to enter, but we do not have an accessible toilet. \r\n\r\nKeeping everyone safe :\r\nOur safeguarding policy details our commitment to keeping everyone safe. It is expected of everyone to adhere to these commitments. We expect all volunteers to do our relevant training, so you can help keep yourself and others safe from harm. A fantastic opportunity and all help makes a real difference for people we support and is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity and all help makes a real difference for people we support and is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Charlotte Laursen, Social Bite Volunteer Coordinator at email volunteering@social-bite.co.uk\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant training and excellent support is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times to volunteer Monday-Friday, 7.45am-9.45am . All help is greatly appreciated and makes a difference.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThese services take place at out Social Bite Coffee Shop at 516 Union Street, Aberdeen, AB10 1TT. *(close to Holburn Junction).\r\n\r\nWe do offer to cover the travel expenses for volunteers when they are volunteering with us.",
