        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400000DiSNMAA3",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400000DiSNMAA3/tim-stead-trust",
            "name": "Tim Stead Trust",
            "description": "To save The Steading as a base for education in wood craft and art, for the benefit of traditional woodcraft heritage and for the benefit of the local community.\r\nTo establish a viable means of purchasing The Steading, Blainslie in the Scottish Borders  in order to safeguard its future as a significant piece of Scottish craftsmanship thereafter and., \r\nTo establish the Tim Stead Trust thereby making The Steading and its contents accessible to the public; and to provide educational activities interpreting Tim Stead’s furniture, sculpture, philosophy and poetry.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EnvironmentRecycling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Environment / Recycling"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000J1RxhYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000J1RxhYAF/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-27",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBased at the the category A Listed Steading, Blainslie, Scottish Borders, the former family home of Tim Stead MBE, the Board are responsible for managing and promoting The Steading and the archive, works and ethos of Tim Stead.  \r\nWe have just produced an ambitious new 5 year business plan and are currently seeking funding for it. \r\nOur current Board brings together a diverse range of skills, knowledge and experience that we are seeking to add to.\r\n\r\nThe ideal candidate will have legal, fundraising, marketing or property knowledge/ experience, but what we really want is people who understand what we are about, are interested in our activities and message and feel that they can bring something extra to the Board.\n\n## Description\n\nTo take part in 4 times per year Board meetings, take part in at least one of the regular Working Groups \r\n(Finance & Fundraising, Governance and HR, Public Engagement and Property and Archive) which meet on \r\na similar cycle to the Board.\r\nWe are also currently pursuing Museum Accreditation so input to that will be on an ad hoc basis. \r\nThe ability to prepare for meetings, reading and considering papers and taking an active part in discussions at meetings is expected.\r\nThe ability to challenge and to present ideas is welcome as is the ability to present innovative ideas.\r\nWe have one employee, our Director, and Trustees work closely with her. We hold regular tours between February and November and volunteer days throughout the year. Trustees are welcome to take part or lead these events (training will be provided where necessary).\n\n## Experience required\n\nUnderstanding/interest in arts and conservation; knowledge of wood; sharing of knowledge; ability to \r\nchallenge; willingness to take active part in discussions; problem solving; innovative and independent thinking\r\n\r\nNot essential, but desirable knowledge/experience in one or more of the following: \r\nLaw, property, fundraising, marketing/public engagement.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training is given to successful applicants including Codes of Conduct, expected time commitment and meeting attendance. \r\nBoard training opportunities are regularly reviewed and Board training is undertaken when required.\r\nFor new Trustees, a buddy is provided from existing Trustees to help navigate any questions.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nIf support requirements are identified, Board will consider what support can be reasonably provided, \r\nwhether it is appropriate/reasonable and how to provide it\n\n## Travel details\n\nTrustees are expected to have their own means of transport as The Steading is not on public transport \r\nroutes.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are reimbursed where requested at the recognised HMRC rate.\n\n## Taster details\n\nInitial exploratory chats with a Trustee will be followed by meeting at least one other Trustee.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
