        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400000GGd5PAAT",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400000GGd5PAAT/tlc-befriending-service",
            "name": "TLC – Befriending Service",
            "description": "Everyone can feel lonely or isolated at times, especially when facing hardship.\r\nIn April 2021, in response to the devastating impact of loneliness and isolation on people’s mental health and wellbeing — which the COVID-19 pandemic and the ongoing cost of living crisis have both intensified — TLC, together with partners across the city, launched a befriending service to help combat the effects of loneliness and isolation in Aberdeen.\r\nOur service matches trained and compassionate volunteers with individuals who would benefit from support — not only to offer friendship, but also to help build resilience and confidence to reconnect with their community, bringing joy and fulfilment back into their lives.\r\nWe provide a comprehensive training package and regular supervision, ensuring you’re supported every step of the way — you’ll never be left on your own.\r\nIf you’re interested in making a difference in someone’s life and helping your community thrive, we’d love you to apply to become a TLC Befriender.",
            "website": "https://www.tlc.org.uk/befriending",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
