        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400000IDPByAAP",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400000IDPByAAP/garthdee-field-allotments-association",
            "name": "Garthdee Field Allotments Association",
            "description": "GFAA is a community of allotment holders.  You will find us at the junction of Garthdee Road and Pitfodells Station Road. We have over 100 plots on the site, in 3 sizes – full, half and micro.  Plotters are members of our association and together we seek to:\r\n-To encourage the use of green and sustainable gardening methods;\r\n-To share good practice and gardening expertise;\r\n-To spread the benefits of plot working and green gardening into the wider community.",
            "website": "https://www.garthdeeallotments.org",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EnvironmentRecycling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Environment / Recycling"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000fwVzAAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000fwVzAAI/gardening-and-diy-outdoors",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-19",
                    "title": "Gardening and DIY Outdoors",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nGarthdee Field Allotments Association is a community of allotment holders.  You will find us at the junction of Garthdee Road and Pitfodells Station Road. We have over 100 plots on the site, in 3 sizes – full, half and micro.  Plotters are members of our association and together we seek to:\r\n-To encourage the use of green and sustainable gardening methods;\r\n-To share good practice and gardening expertise;\r\n-To spread the benefits of plot working and green gardening into the wider community. \r\n\r\nWe are looking for volunteers to help with our activities on our individual plots, on the Primary School Plot we host, on our raised beds, in the Community Orchard and across the site generally.\r\n\r\nA great opportunity to volunteer supporting the allotments and outdoors. All help is greatly appreciated. For more details please contact: Valerie Milne at email: secretary@garthdeeallotments.org or tel.: 07706248748\r\n\r\nMore details are also available on our website at: www.garthdeeallotments.org\n\n## Description\n\nGarthdee Field Allotments Association is a community of allotment holders.  You will find us at the junction of Garthdee Road and Pitfodells Station Road. We have over 100 plots on the site, in 3 sizes – full, half and micro.  Plotters are members of our association and together we seek to:\r\n-To encourage the use of green and sustainable gardening methods;\r\n-To share good practice and gardening expertise;\r\n-To spread the benefits of plot working and green gardening into the wider community. \r\n\r\nWe are looking for volunteers to help with our activities on our individual plots, on the Primary School Plot we host, on our raised beds, in the Community Orchard and across the site generally.\r\n\r\nA great opportunity to volunteer supporting the allotments and outdoors. All help is greatly appreciated. For more details please contact: Valerie Milne at email: secretary@garthdeeallotments.org or tel.: 07706248748\r\n\r\nMore details are also available on our website at: www.garthdeeallotments.org\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo skills or experience are required, except an enjoyment of working outdoors.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will have the chance to work alongside experienced plotters serving as mentors until they feel confident to take on activities by themselves.  We favour small team working on many projects.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to suit volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe are located on Garthdee Road as it meets Pitfoddels Station Road, opposite the Norwood House Hotel.  We have on site parking and our site is close to stops on the Number 1 and 2 bus routes from the city centre.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F717a1206-2da5-31cb-4ab7-a2e915593a0d%2F6z5OM5fLIhToM6Q8RA9YYsCAcZ33%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=1633b882-52ef-4edb-8fd6-ceb78eacef26",
