            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hp5VJYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hp5VJYAZ/charity-trustees",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-25",
                    "title": "Charity Trustees",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nOur organisation is a gymnastics club. We run gymnastics classes at Alex Collie Sport centre in Bridge of Don. We provide recreational classes for all ages and competitive pathways possibilities. We had the chance to train gymnast who became Scottish champions and even participated in the Northern European gymnastics championships.\r\n\r\nWe are a registered charity and are working toward developing our club culture and impact in the community.\r\n\r\nWe currently have opportunities for people to volunteer as a Charity Trustee for the organisation. This will involve decision-making, helping with the management of the club's structure, designing policies or approving expenses in the interest of the club.\r\n\r\nThere are regular meetings (every 2-3 months in Bridge of Don), with the possibility of attending online.\r\n\r\nFull guidance and support is provided and all Charity Trustee volunteers make a real difference and are greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Jolan Jaget, Trustee at email: facilities@coag.org.uk\n\n## Description\n\nOur organisation is a gymnastics club. We run gymnastics classes at Alex Collie Sport centre in Bridge of Don. We provide recreational classes for all ages and competitive pathways possibilities. We had the chance to train gymnast who became Scottish champions and even participated in the Northern European gymnastics championships.\r\n\r\nWe are a registered charity and are working toward developing our club culture and impact in the community.\r\n\r\nWe currently have opportunities for people to volunteer as a Charity Trustee for the organisation. This will involve decision-making, helping with the management of the club's structure, designing policies or approving expenses in the interest of the club.\r\n\r\nThere are regular meetings (every 2-3 months in Bridge of Don), with the possibility of attending online.\r\n\r\nFull guidance and support is provided and all Charity Trustee volunteers make a real difference and are greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Jolan Jaget, Trustee at email: facilities@coag.org.uk\n\n## Training details\n\nFull guidance and support is provided and all Charity Trustee volunteers make a real difference and are greatly appreciated.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nRegular meetings (every 2-3 months in Bridge of Don), with the possibility of attending online.\n\n## Travel details\n\nRegular meetings (every 2-3 months in Bridge of Don), with the possibility of attending online.",
