            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JRvwvYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JRvwvYAD/charity-trustees",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-20",
                    "title": "Charity Trustees",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nBe United is a Scottish Charitable Incorporated Organisation (SC044615) that advocates for, nurtures and champions Black people working in the performing arts, screen and cultural event sectors in Scotland. We also support people of colour and those from disadvantaged backgrounds. We aim to contribute to a more inspired and enriched world. \r\n\r\nOur values are equity, empowerment and excellence. \r\nWe are driven by the creation of the extraordinary. We create opportunities through our programmes, events and initiatives that foster sustainable development and strengthen collaboration for individuals and organisations within the industry. \r\n\r\nBe United is currently undergoing significant organisational growth, having received Creative Scotland’s Multi-Year Funding and being part of Edinburgh’s Regenerative Fund 10-year initiative. We are looking for Trustees to contribute to Be United’s growth and contribute to its goal of supporting 500 Black people up into and in the creative and cultural sectors in the next 5 years. \r\n\r\nAs a Trustee, you will contribute to supporting Be United’s mission and using your expertise to oversee strategic growth. Be United is currently looking for 4 Trustees, including a Board Secretary, who will provide administrative support to the Board.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for expertise in the following sectors: \r\nLegal & Governance\r\n Finance & Commercial Development \r\nCreative & Cultural Industries \r\nOperational Strategy & Development \r\nFundraising & Grants\r\n\r\nWe are looking for Trustees that can demonstrate: \r\nStrategic thinking \r\nGood judgement \r\nConstructive challenge \r\nCollaborative leadership \r\nCuriosity and willingness to learn \r\nCommitment to equity and fair work \r\nRespect for lived experience \r\nAbility to distinguish governance from operations \r\nReliability and preparation \r\nWillingness to act as an ambassador for Be United \r\n\r\nPrevious Trustee experience and experience in the charity sector is welcome but not required.   \r\n\r\nPractical information \r\nTerm of appointment: The term is 18 months at first instance, with option of reappointment thereafter. \r\nCompensation: The position is voluntary, however you can be reimbursed for reasonable expenses incurred while performing your role. \r\nExpected time commitment: Online meetings every 6 weeks, annual strategy meetings and training days, and an in-person AGM. \r\n\r\nApplication process \r\nPlease email your completed application to info@be-united.org.uk by 20th  November 2026 at 23:59.  \r\n\r\nIn your application you should include your CV, cover letter and in no more than 250 words each, the answer to these three questions:  \r\n\r\nWhy do you want to join Be United?  \r\nWhat skills and experience would you bring? \r\nWhat do you hope to contribute during your term? \r\nAll applicants will receive a response with the outcome of their application after the closing date. Successful candidates will  be interviewed by Trustees from our current Board. Please read our Recruitment Pack for more information.\r\n\r\nWe look forward to receiving your applications. If you have any questions or would like to discuss the role further, please email  info@be-united.org.uk",
