        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400000jmagbAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400000jmagbAAA/cats-protection",
            "name": "Cats Protection",
            "description": "Cats Protections vision is a world where all cats are treated with kindness and understanding of its needs. Our objectives are to help cats by 1.Homing: finding good homes for cats in need  2.Neutering: supporting and encouraging the  neutering of cats 3. Education: improving people’s understanding of cats in their care.",
            "website": "https://www.cats.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC037711"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AnimalWelfare",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Animal Welfare"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JI5PhYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JI5PhYAL/volunteer-cat-fosterer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-15",
                    "title": "Volunteer Cat Fosterer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nFrom elderly moggies to energic kittens, every day across the UK cats and kittens are in need of a temporary place to stay, and lots of love and TLC! We need more fosterers like you to provide a safe, temporary haven for cats and kittens and provide them with everything they need before they get their chance to land on their four paws and make a house a home.\r\n\r\nWe would need you to be able to provide a stable, safe and compassionate environment in your home or in a purpose-built pen in your garden provided by us\r\n\r\nWe would also need you to be willing to, enrich the cats’ experience in care including play, exercise and appropriate handling/interaction; to complete some training in order to provide high standards of cat welfare; to introduce cats to prospective adopters so they can find their forever home.\r\n\r\nYou can find more information on becoming a fosterer on our website www.cats.org.uk.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe initial modules are 'Welcome to Cats Protection', Safeguarding, Data Protection and Health & Safety. There is also an 'Introduction to Fostering' course that all fosterers would be expected to complete.\r\n\r\nThere are numerous training modules available on the volunteer portal and also online learning workshops.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F952f6a78-e59d-4a2a-9191-c92f93d500d7%2FyQtgfFOBwSNxO4OoLShS0rahK193%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=7b58112a-73f1-4ee6-a460-3a8eb2ebb9cb",
