                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BNd8pYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BNd8pYAD/trap-neuter-return-tnr-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-08-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-21",
                    "title": "Trap, Neuter & Return (TNR) volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nUnfortunately, thousands of cats each year are abandoned or have strayed and rely on charities like Cats Protection for help. Becoming a trap, neuter and return (TNR) volunteer is one way you can make a real difference to cats in your local area.  \r\n\r\nTNR volunteers help reduce the number of feral cats by raising awareness of TNR programmes, setting humane traps to safely capture cats, taking them to local vets to be neutered, and hopefully returning them back to their territory.  Local TNR programmes are crucial, as feral and abandoned cats present a huge challenge for communities across the UK.\r\n\r\nTNR volunteers can expect to be trapping cats using humane methods, taking them to local vets to be neutered and returning cats to their territory or finding a suitable alternative. \r\n\r\nThe role might also include:\r\n- Regular feeding of feral colonies;\r\n- Promoting neutering by building relationships with farmers, land owners and local businesses;\r\n- Liaising with vets to promote and arrange neutering.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA willingness to be part of a team or to be able to work alone where necessary. A willingness to follow Cats Protection's policies and guidelines. Knowledge of feral cats would be an advantage.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe volunteer coordinator at the Caithness branch will be their volunteer leader. There is a Branch Development Manager who will conduct the induction. There is a Learn Online portal where volunteers can complete training and also role specific training sessions held via Teams.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe role is flexible but the estimate is 2 to 3 hours per week.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fb55a8fb9-736b-44b4-9cdc-6a26de8c1da5%2FliLEC2s9ZwYA46gEa6AxGTVGunx2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=4a2f83cd-6d35-494d-87fd-7e35efb4f608",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BNd8pYAD#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Trap, Neuter & Return (TNR) volunteer",
                        "description": "A willingness to be part of a team or to be able to work alone where necessary. A willingness to follow Cats Protection's policies and guidelines. Knowledge of feral cats would be an advantage.",
                        "commitment": "The role is flexible but the estimate is 2 to 3 hours per week.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BNd8pYAD/trap-neuter-return-tnr-volunteer?#modal_register_a0gQD00000BNd8pYAD",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
