        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400000jmiXSAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400000jmiXSAAY/north-east-rider-volunteers-scotland",
            "name": "North East Rider Volunteers Scotland",
            "description": "Our mission is to deliver urgent medical samples, equipment and supplies free of charge between hospitals, healthcare sites and laboratories in the North East of Scotland when Healthcare Providers’ own transport services do not operate.\r\n\r\nNERVS is affiliated to the Nationwide Association of Blood Bikes (NABB).  NABB states that they “consist of independent Blood Bike Group Charities who work with their local hospitals, Air Ambulance services, and other NHS sites transporting medication, medical equipment, X-rays, scans, samples and human donor milk”.",
            "website": "http://nervs.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC048450"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EmergencyResponseDisasterRelief",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Emergency Response / Disaster Relief"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNqeaAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNqeaAAD/duty-controller-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Duty Controller Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur mission is to deliver urgent medical samples, equipment and supplies free of charge between hospitals, healthcare sites and laboratories in the North East of Scotland when Healthcare Providers’ own transport services do not operate.\r\n\r\nWe need Duty controllers working from the comfort of your own home to help us with this mission.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference. All volunteers are greatly appreciated. For more details please contact Graeme Scott, Membership Secretary at email: membershipsecretary@nervs.org.uk or telephone.: 07881460792.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience is required for this role as full training is given.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided to all volunteers. \r\n\r\nA video induction to our base facility is provided and also to our vehicles, as well as a physical induction. A shadow shift where you shadow another controller is available and encouraged. We have a training coordinator who organises on going training throughout your time with NERVS.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible-there are a range of times available to volunteer and all help is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nControllers are home based using their own PC, phone and internet connection.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
