                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNqefAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNqefAAD/duty-driver-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Duty Driver Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur mission is to deliver urgent medical samples, equipment and supplies free of charge between hospitals, healthcare sites and laboratories in the North East of Scotland when Healthcare Providers’ own transport services do not operate.\r\n\r\nWe need drivers over the age of 25 to help us achieve this mission.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference. All volunteers are greatly appreciated. For more details please contact Graeme Scott, Membership Secretary at email: membershipsecretary@nervs.org.uk or telephone.: 07881460792.\n\n## Experience required\n\nHas to be a driver who has held their licence for 2 years or over and has a clean licence ( minimal points may be accepted but it depends on our insurance company).\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided to all volunteers. \r\n\r\nA video induction to our base facility is provided and also to our vehicles, as well as a physical induction. A shadow shift where you shadow another rider is available and encouraged. We have a training coordinator who organises on going training throughout your time with NERVS. When you are on shift there is always either a duty controller or a board member on with you to provide support.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible-there are a range of times available to volunteer and all help is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe have a base at Dyce where our Vehicles are based. Travel happens all over the North East of Scotland during the volunteering.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
