        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400000lEEViAAO",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400000lEEViAAO/outlet",
            "name": "OutLET",
            "description": "OutLET is a Social Enterprise that provides inclusive outdoor programmes. OutLET work with the local authority, community groups, schools, and families.\n\nOutLET accepts all children and young people exactly as they are, recognises their potential and gives them outdoor space to play and explore without pressure.\n\nOutLET provides a safe and engaging environment that revolutionizes the learning experience. This has a particular impact on those who have had chaotic and traumatic life experiences and as a result, struggle to build healthy relationships, and need extra support for their social and emotional well-being. \n\nFor ALL the young people who attend, OutLET is a safe, fun space where they know they belong.",
            "website": "https://outlet.scot/play",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Ik7wzYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Ik7wzYAB/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOutLET – Trustee Opportunities\n\nCould you help us make a difference? Join our Board of Trustees and help shape the future of OutLET.\n\nOutLET is an ambitious, growing charity and social enterprise using nature-based experiences to support wellbeing, build confidence and create opportunities for people and communities to thrive.\n\nThrough our outdoor learning, therapeutic woodland experiences, wellbeing and training programmes, we help people connect with themselves, each other and the natural world. At the heart of our charitable purpose is a commitment to young people who have been let down by the rigid structures of our education system. We believe everyone deserves the opportunity to learn, grow and realise their potential, even when traditional approaches haven't worked for them.\n\nAs we continue to develop our work and extend our impact, we're looking for enthusiastic, committed individuals to join our Board of Trustees.\n\nCould you bring something to our Board?\nWe're looking for people who share our values and can bring fresh perspectives, skills and ideas to help shape our future. Experience in business, finance, leadership, fundraising, education, youth work, community development or other relevant areas would be valuable. Lived experience is equally important, and you don't need previous trustee experience – guidance, training and support are available.\n\nWhat's involved?\n- Attending 6–8 Board meetings a year, usually in person in our office in Hamilton, South Lanarkshire\n- Contributing to our strategy through annual strategic planning meetings.\n- Providing guidance, oversight and ideas to support our development and long-term sustainability.\n\nThis is a voluntary role, with reasonable out-of-pocket expenses reimbursed.\n\nHelp us build a Board that reflects our community\nWe particularly welcome applications from people with care experience, experience of living on a low income, lived experience of disability (including non-visible disabilities), and people from Black, Asian and other ethnic minority backgrounds. We value diversity, openness and collaboration, and believe different perspectives help us make better decisions.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAccountancy / Finance,Advocacy / Lobbying / Campaigning,Business / HR / Management,Community Development / Social work,Education / Training,Fundraising,Research / Policies,Youth / Childcare, Caring,Creative,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Open minded,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Social Conscience,Team Player,\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training will be provided, trustees will have be able to have access to OutLET's own staff training provision in outdoor learning if they wish to, as well as access to other relevant third sector training opportunities.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Ik7wzYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Trustee",
                        "description": "Accountancy / Finance,Advocacy / Lobbying / Campaigning,Business / HR / Management,Community Development / Social work,Education / Training,Fundraising,Research / Policies,Youth / Childcare, Caring,Creative,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Open minded,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Social Conscience,Team Player,",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Ik7wzYAB/trustee?#modal_register_a0gQD00000Ik7wzYAB",
