                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000V7LFlAAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000V7LFlAAN/it-support-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "IT Support Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\n“A digital world accessible to all”\r\n\r\nAward winning IT charity AbilityNet is looking for IT Support volunteers to help people get the most out of technology. We support older and disabled people to use technology, from setting up a new device, to showing how to use zoom or do an internet food shop. \r\n\r\nThe role would take place in your local area, face to face with clients or help over Teamviewer. You don’t need to be a tech guru to help out. If you use a computer at home or work, and perhaps support family and friends with their tech issues, you are likely to have the skills we are looking for. Relevant guidance and excellent support is provided to all volunteers.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference for people. All volunteer assistance is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Donna Baker-Smith at email community@abilitynet.org.uk or telephone 01926 956850.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou don’t need to be a tech guru to help out. If you use a computer at home or work, and perhaps support family and friends with their tech issues, you are likely to have the skills we are looking for:\r\n\r\n*A passion to help others.\r\n*Good IT and computer skills.\r\nKnowledge of standard operating systems and software would be useful\r\n*The ability to communicate well with people.\r\n*Patience and empathy.\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant training/guidance and excellent support is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to help. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe role would take place in your local area, face to face with clients or help over Teamviewer.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe pay travel expenses at 45p per mile and all public transport costs.",
