        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400000bCyaRAAS",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400000bCyaRAAS/7th-braid-edinburgh-george-heriots-school-scout-group",
            "name": "7th Braid Edinburgh (George Heriot's School) Scout Group",
            "description": "Scouting exists to actively engage and support young people in their personal development, empowering them to make a positive contribution to society. As Scouts we are guided by these values: Integrity - We act with integrity; we are honest, trustworthy and loyal. Respect - We have self-respect and respect for others. Care - We support others and take care of the world in which we live. Belief - We explore our faiths, beliefs and attitudes. Co-operation - We make a positive difference; we co-operate with others and make friends.\r\n\r\nScouting takes place when young people, in partnership with adults, work together based on the values of Scouting and: Enjoy what they are doing and have fun, Take part in activities indoors and outdoors, Learn by doing, Share in spiritual reflection, Take responsibility and make choices, Undertake new and challenging activities, Make and live by their promise.",
            "website": "https://7braid.btck.co.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC036159"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HIeRpYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HIeRpYAL/assistant-scout-leader",
                    "publishStart": "2026-02-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Assistant Scout Leader",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe 7th Braid Scouts need help! We meet on Monday evenings between 18:30 and 20:30 at George Heriot’s School. Scouts are aged 10.5 to 14 years old. An Assistant Leader  supports the operation of the troop, in particular the planning and delivery of a balanced programme.\n\n## Description\n\nScouting exists to actively engage and support young people in their personal development, empowering them to make a positive contribution to society. As Scouts we are guided by these values: Integrity - We act with integrity; we are honest, trustworthy and loyal. Respect - We have self-respect and respect for others. Care - We support others and take care of the world in which we live. Belief - We explore our faiths, beliefs and attitudes. Co-operation - We make a positive difference.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining is offered.  Initial Scout training, called Growing Roots, is modular and delivered online through e-learning.  Courses can be accessed at a convenient time and place.  It takes a total of between 2 to 3 hours to complete the training.  Although self-managed, support is available.   In addition to training, other support is also available.\nScout leader induction is call joining journey and has seven steps including the Growing Roots training.\n\n## Travel details\n\nGeorge Heriot's School, Lauriston Place, Edinburgh EH3 9EQ.\nLothian Buses service numbers: 12, 23, 27, 35, 45, 47, 47B and 60.\nTo City -Lauriston Building, Stop ID: 36236463\nFrom City - Lauriston Place, Stop ID: 36236465\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HIeRpYAL#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Assistant Scout Leader",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HIeRpYAL/assistant-scout-leader?#modal_register_a0gQD00000HIeRpYAL",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
