                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaW6AAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kaW6AAI/heriots-beaver-or-cub-scout-leader",
                    "publishStart": "2017-05-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Heriot’s Beaver or Cub Scout Leader.",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe Assistant Leader will support the operation of the group, in particular the planning and delivery of a balanced programme with the help of the Section Leaders. They will actively support and promote the achievement of badges and awards and support the delivery of a safe, exciting and stimulating Group.\n\n## Description\n\nThe 7th Scout Group need help!  We meet on Friday evenings.  The Beavers between 17:30 and 18:30.  The Cubs between 18:30 and 20:00 at George Heriot’s School.  Beavers are aged 6-8 years old and Cubs are aged 8-11 years old.  As an assistant leader you will help support the operation of the section, in particular the planning and delivery of a balanced programme with the help of the Section Leader.  You will actively support and promote the achievement of badges and awards and support the delivery of a safe, exciting and stimulating balanced programme.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience or skills necessary except for an enthusiasm for working with young people; a knowledge of Scouting would be beneficial, however training and support will be provided. during the 5 months of Provisional Appointment the relevant \"Getting Started\" modules must be completed and a Wood Badge must be\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining is offered.  Initial training, called Growing Roots, is modular and delivered online through e-learning.  Courses can be accessed at a convenient time and place.  It takes a total of between 2 to 3 hours to complete the training.  Although self-managed, support is available.   In addition to training, other support is also available.\n\n## Travel details\n\nGeorge Heriot's School, Lauriston Place, Edinburgh EH3 9EQ\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses paid, we do pay for uniform items, training and costs associated with the programme.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kaW6AAI#role",
