                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FgoKwYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FgoKwYAJ/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-03-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nOur Trustees, with their vital behind the scenes role, are dedicated to making sure Scouts runs smoothly, safely, and legally.\n\n## Description\n\nAs a Trustee, you’ll be part of a dynamic team working together to make Scouts locally operate like a well-oiled machine. Responsible for the governance matters, you’ll make sure everything is set up properly, so that young people have the best experience in Scouts. Our Trustees see the big picture, make decisions and work together. As a team, you’ll ensure that everything’s being done safely and legally, as well as connecting Scouts with your local community.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be required to complete some mandatory learning called Growing Roots and a joining journey within 180 days from appointment.  Learning is delivered as e-learning modules.\nThis role is regarded as a regulated role and so a Disclosure Scotland PVG membership obtained through the Scouts must be held before starting.  This is free and we will support you through this process. As part of the Scouts vetting process, eligibility checks to be a Trustee will be conducted.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Scout Group meets at George Heriot's School, Lauriston Place, Edinburgh EH3 9EQ.\nHowever Trustee Board meetings are moslly held in homes or onine (vidoe call)\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReimbursement for Agreed Activities (e.g. Telephone Calls)",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
