        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400000bOTGgAAO",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400000bOTGgAAO/go-youth-trust",
            "name": "Go Youth Trust",
            "description": "Go! Youth Trust is a Christian charity which serves young people, families and communities by encouraging and equipping the local church.  We are based in Central Scotland and work in partnership with schools, churches and the local community.\r\n\r\nGo! Youth Trust is supported by donations and any grants or funding which we can acquire.",
            "website": "https://goyouthtrust.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC044089"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FaithReligionBelief",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Faith / Religion / Belief"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FamilySupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Family Support"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005TtsPYAS",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005TtsPYAS/volunteer-mentor",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-20",
                    "title": "Volunteer Mentor",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGo! Youth Trust (GYT) is a Christian charity that supports young people to grow, explore and thrive. Working across Central Scotland with young people aged 8-25, they are passionate about helping young people get the best start in life.\r\n\r\nFor some this simply means having somewhere to go and feel safe, for others this means having a conversation every week with a positive role model while others need help gaining qualifications in an environment which is tailor made to ensure they can achieve their potential.  Whatever young people are looking for they can find the support they need at Go! Youth Trust to make an impact in the world.\r\n\r\nVolunteers are a vital part of Go! Youth Trust. Their work with young people simply wouldn’t be possible without people who are willing to give their time, energy, and care. Whether you’re new to youth work or bringing years of experience, there’s a place for you.  \r\n\r\nYou don’t need prior experience to volunteer. Full support and any necessary training will be provided by their experienced team. What matters most is a heart for young people and a desire to see young lives thrive. Volunteering is about building relationships, creating safe spaces, and being a positive, consistent presence.\r\n\r\nVolunteering at GYT is flexible. Whether you’re keen to work directly with young people or prefer to support behind the scenes.  Becoming a Go! Youth Trust mentor is one way to get involved.\r\n\r\nGYT mentoring programme provides young people with a trusted adult who is there to listen, encourage and support them as they navigate the challenges of growing up. Through regular one-to-one sessions, mentors build positive relationships with young people, helping them explore their goals, build confidence, develop new skills and recognise their own potential.\r\n\r\nMentoring can last between 6 months and 1 year, with volunteers meeting their mentee weekly for the first 6 months, fortnightly for the following 3 months, and monthly for the final 3 months. \r\n\r\nResearch shows that having one trusted adult in a young person’s life can make a lasting difference. Mentoring gives young people the opportunity to explore their potential, talk openly when they’re struggling, and build a positive relationship with someone who genuinely wants to see them succeed.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA GYT mentor should be a good listener, willing to be flexible and responsive to a young person’s individual needs, and genuinely want to see them succeed, grow in confidence and reach their full potential. \r\nBeing reliable and dependable is also incredibly important, as young people value having someone they can trust. It’s about being a consistent, positive presence who will listen without judgement, offer encouragement, build trust and walk alongside a young person as they work towards their goals.\r\n\r\nYou don’t need previous experience to become a mentor with GYT. What matters most is your willingness to invest in a young person and help them see their potential.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe first step of recruitment is an initial meeting with the volunteer coordinators to discuss the opportunities available, your interests and where best suits for volunteering. An expression of interest form is then filled out by the volunteer. \r\nGYT then take you through the necessary training with support from the team. \r\nPVG and reference checks are done and if successful, welcome to the team, complete your induction and get you started in the role!\r\n\r\nFull training, guidance and ongoing support provided, volunteer events and opportunities to connect with other volunteers throughout the mentoring journey.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2 hours per week. Flexible to suit mentor/mentee. \r\n6-12 months commitment. \r\nRegular training events and safeguarding refreshers throughout the year.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe mentoring can take place in the community or in school. This is dependant on the mentor availability and the mentee's preference.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n55p per mile. Reimbursement of public transport where necessary.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://goyouthtrust.org.uk/app/uploads/2021/05/company-logo.svg",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005TtsPYAS#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Mentor",
                        "description": "A GYT mentor should be a good listener, willing to be flexible and responsive to a young person’s individual needs, and genuinely want to see them succeed, grow in confidence and reach their full potential. \r\nBeing reliable and dependable is also incredibly important, as young people value having someone they can trust. It’s about being a consistent, positive presence who will listen without judgement, offer encouragement, build trust and walk alongside a young person as they work towards their goals.\r\n\r\nYou don’t need previous experience to become a mentor with GYT. What matters most is your willingness to invest in a young person and help them see their potential.",
                        "commitment": "2 hours per week. Flexible to suit mentor/mentee. \r\n6-12 months commitment. \r\nRegular training events and safeguarding refreshers throughout the year.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005TtsPYAS/volunteer-mentor?#modal_register_a0gQD000005TtsPYAS",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
                            {
