                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009tULGYA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009tULGYA2/recruitment-and-membership-co-lead-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Recruitment and Membership Co-lead Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAberdeen Climate Action (ACA) is seeking a Recruitment and Membership Co-lead volunteer to help with the recruitment and onboarding of volunteers for ACA. \r\n\r\nACA is a volunteer led organisation, which focuses on educating and prompting action on climate change in the North East of Scotland. Therefore, volunteers are crucial in our organisation. The recruitment and membership co-lead will help with administrative duties, such as interviewing potential volunteers, writing volunteer job adverts, attending team meetings, and keeping the volunteer database tidy. In addition, you may be expected to check in with existing volunteers to ensure they are happy in their volunteer role.\r\n\r\nYou’ll be volunteering alongside students, retirees, career professionals and specialists. A diverse collection of individuals who, like you, are helping ACA complete its valuable work in the North East of Scotland.\r\n\r\nOf course, you don’t need to be a Climate Action expert to volunteer with us. What matters most is you are positive and enthusiastic about making a difference in the world.\r\n\r\nACA wants to offer you an interesting and valuable opportunity that can help bolster your CV, develop or gain skills; make new friends; or just do your part to help the environment. No matter what, your time and the work you do helps ACA complete its valuable work in the North East.\r\n\r\nFor more information or any queries, please email our volunteer support team at: recruit@aberdeenclimateaction.org\n\n## Description\n\nAberdeen Climate Action (ACA) is seeking a Recruitment and Membership Co-lead volunteer to help with the recruitment and onboarding of volunteers for ACA. \r\n\r\nACA is a volunteer led organisation, which focuses on educating and prompting action on climate change in the North East of Scotland. Therefore, volunteers are crucial in our organisation. The recruitment and membership co-lead will help with administrative duties, such as interviewing potential volunteers, writing volunteer job adverts, attending team meetings, and keeping the volunteer database tidy. In addition, you may be expected to check in with existing volunteers to ensure they are happy in their volunteer role.\r\n\r\nYou’ll be volunteering alongside students, retirees, career professionals and specialists. A diverse collection of individuals who, like you, are helping ACA complete its valuable work in the North East of Scotland.\r\n\r\nOf course, you don’t need to be a Climate Action expert to volunteer with us. What matters most is you are positive and enthusiastic about making a difference in the world.\r\n\r\nACA wants to offer you an interesting and valuable opportunity that can help bolster your CV, develop or gain skills; make new friends; or just do your part to help the environment. No matter what, your time and the work you do helps ACA complete its valuable work in the North East.\r\n\r\nFor more information or any queries, please email our volunteer support team at: recruit@aberdeenclimateaction.org\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. Once the potential volunteer has expressed an interest in volunteering, they will be invited to an informal induction chat. There they will be asked a few questions and be able to ask their own to learn more about the organisation. Expectations will be covered and then they will be introduced to the team lead. Check-ins can also be done.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to assist-all help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nACA is an Aberdeen based group but has members who join in from afar using video call software. Please be aware that some face-to-face meetings may take place in Aberdeen.\r\n\r\nAs an organisation with no physical offices, our volunteers tend to work from home, with face-to-face meetings happening occasionally. When you join; you’ll be able to access our shared online platforms and video meeting conferences; which allow us to work as a team no matter where we are.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fe85db7d1-3d68-4383-b7b7-e1573c25795b%2FvFZa9WNv4MfDUfw8Jx6agqFb6Wh2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=1616cb03-1c88-4550-ae04-66ebf333c411",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009tULGYA2#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Recruitment and Membership Co-lead Volunteers",
