            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000002prXSAAY",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000002prXSAAY/instructor",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-11",
                    "title": "Instructor",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nLooking for someone to deliver personal safety classes\n\n## Description\n\nRole involves delivering classes on self defence this can either be on a theoretical or practical basis.  The classes can sometimes be victims who are looking to protect themselves or ethnic minority groups where sensitivity and an understanding is needed. Also looking for someone to deliver fitness based classes both these classes would suit someone from a martial arts/aerobics/ fitness background or interest.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience required but would prefer volunteer to come from a background in martial arts/aerobiocs/fitness with a keen interest in helping people but not necessary as training can be given.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers could go through First Aid training, Health & Safety trainingand Fire policy training.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Centre is on all the main bus routes ie no11, 12 and 585.  It is also located close to 2 train stations within Ardrossan.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses could be paid in future depending on Centre funds\n\n## Taster details\n\nCome in for a chat, have  a look around centre get a feel for the place",
