            "name": "Regal Radio SCIO",
            "description": "The organisation's purposes are: To advance active citizenship, community development and social responsibility across West Lothian through the making, presenting and distribution of radio programmes; To advance local culture and heritage to create a positive image of West Lothian; To advance education by providing training and development opportunities for volunteers of all ages, especially marginalised young people, in order to develop their self-confidence, skills and education and to provide an outlet for local talent to flourish. ? To inform and educate the community through a diverse range of programming.",
            "website": "http://www.regalradio.net/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC046057"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpqijYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HpqijYAB/station-manager",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-31",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-29",
                    "title": "Station Manager",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nRegal Radio is keen to engage a station manager to fill the role being made vacant later in 2026 when the current incumbent steps down.\r\nThe role is largely one of leading a committee, promoting the station in the local West Lothian community, liaising with community organisations and spearheading the drive for increased listenership.\r\nMost of the current station members are presenters. This is not required of the Station Manager role although the opportunity is open.\r\nThe role would suit someone who is interested in putting their coordination skills to good use in a community position.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication skills.\r\nEnthusiasm for community organisation integration.\r\nGood leadership.\r\nPositive promotion skills.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpqijYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Station Manager",
                        "description": "Good communication skills.\r\nEnthusiasm for community organisation integration.\r\nGood leadership.\r\nPositive promotion skills.",
