                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BFPsbYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BFPsbYAH/intergenerational-community-connector",
                    "publishStart": "2025-07-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-18",
                    "title": "Intergenerational Community Connector",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nJoin Generations Working Together (GWT) as we work towards a Scotland where generations are more connected. If you would like to get involved in intergenerational work, learn more about the practice, and help strengthen community connections, this could be the perfect volunteer role for you! \r\n\r\nAs an Intergenerational Community Connector, you’ll get the chance to:\r\n\r\n•\tHelp one of our development team members plan and run 2–3 local network meetings each year.\r\n•\tSpread the word about the benefits of intergenerational work within your community.\r\n•\tShare and promote GWT events, meetings, publications, and training opportunities.\r\n•\tConnect with local groups and encourage them to showcase their intergenerational projects through the network and GWT.\n\n## Experience required\n\n• An interest in bringing different generations together\r\n• Strong communication skills\r\n• Good organisational abilities\r\n• Confidence in building relationships with community groups\r\n• Enthusiasm for community involvement and connection\n\n## Training details\n\n• Induction of the role and one to one support from a GWT member.\r\n• Free CPD accredited training, giving you the skills to support intergenerational work in your own community.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2-3 hours per month.  Opportunity does not take place during the school holidays. \r\nTo stay with GWT for at least 12 months\n\n## Travel details\n\nCommunity Connectors volunteer within their geographical network.\r\nConnectors can also attend the annual Scottish conference and other local events such as Learning Roadshows.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n45p per mile.\r\nReimbursed monthly.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
