        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400000F7vITAAZ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400000F7vITAAZ/dyce-stoneywood-community-association",
            "name": "Dyce & Stoneywood Community  Association",
            "description": "The advancement of citizenship and community development and the provision of educational and recreational facilities for the benefit of the public of Stoneywood and Dyce and in furtherance of this.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityFacilities",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Facilities"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Vhwv0AAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Vhwv0AAB/activity-and-exercise-leaders",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Activity and Exercise Leaders",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDyce & Stoneywood Community Association is looking to recruit volunteers to help us with our programme, These opportunities are: \r\n\r\n•\tRunning exercise classes such as Technogym: Technogym is a light exercise class with the use of machines to help people of low fitness get back into exercising. You will need to go through a 2 hour training session for health and safety. These classes run weekly and you will be working alongside another volunteer to help with running the class and cover. \r\n\r\n•\tMovie Club: We run a monthly movie club and would require someone who enjoys movies to help run this for us. \r\n\r\n•\tYouth Activities: such as Lego club and potential summer and holiday activities. PVG (Protection of Vulnerable Groups check/scheme membership) will be required. \r\n\r\nFantastic opportunities to help and make a real difference for people and the community. All volunteer help is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Keri Thomas, Community Development Worker at email: kerithomasdsca@outlook.com\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant training and excellent support is provided to all volunteers. Technogym volunteers will undergo a 2 hour training session and work alongside other volunteers for support. Volunteers will also have support from association staff and other volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to volunteer. All help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDyce Community Centre, Gordon Terrace, Dyce, Aberdeen AB21 7BD. We reimburse travel/bus fares within a 10 mile radius.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nClaims to be made monthly showing receipts using association form.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
