            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FYTYPYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FYTYPYA5/trustees-for-our-board-of-committee-within-abbeyfield",
                    "publishStart": "2026-02-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-25",
                    "title": "Trustees for our Board of Committee within Abbeyfield",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTrustees for our Board of Committee within Abbeyfield\n\n## Description\n\n<p><strong>Lead with Vision: Become a Trustee!</strong></p>\n\n<p>Are you passionate about making a lasting impact in our community? Do you possess strategic vision and a commitment to strong governance? We are seeking inspiring individuals to join our dedicated <strong>Board of Trustees</strong> and help steer our vital work!</p>\n\n<p>As a <strong>Trustee</strong>, you&#39;ll play a crucial role in overseeing our charity&#39;s <em>strategic direction</em>, ensuring <em>financial stability</em>, and <em>upholding our mission</em> to empower individuals and strengthen communities. This isn&#39;t just about attending meetings; it&#39;s about <em>shaping policies</em>, <em>guiding initiatives</em>, and <em>championing our cause</em>.</p>\n\n<p>We&#39;re looking for individuals with diverse skills and backgrounds &ndash; perhaps expertise in finance, HR, marketing, legal, fundraising, or sector-specific knowledge. More importantly, we seek those with a <em>collaborative spirit</em>, <em>sound judgment</em>, and a <em>genuine desire to make a difference</em>. We particularly encourage applications from underrepresented groups to ensure our Board reflects the community we serve.</p>\n\n<p>This is an <em>exceptional opportunity</em> to use your experience to contribute to a meaningful cause, develop new leadership skills, expand your professional network, and truly leave your mark. You&#39;ll work alongside a committed team, guiding an organization that <em>transforms lives every day</em>.</p>\n\n<p>The role typically involves attending 4-6 main Board meetings per year, plus occasional sub-committee work and engagement with our programs. We understand the value of your time and offer a supportive and flexible environment.</p>\n\n<p>If you&#39;re ready to embrace a leadership role and contribute to a brighter future, we want to hear from you! Discover how your expertise can make a <em>profound difference</em>. Express your interest today and become a vital part of our journey.</p>\n\n## Experience required\n\nAll skills considered",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
