            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005puoUYAQ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005puoUYAQ/scout-leaders-helpers",
                    "publishStart": "2024-09-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-09",
                    "title": "Scout Leaders & Helpers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe 9th Dunipace Scout Group is a successful group trying to make things better for any youngster between the ages of 5 and 18 who wishes to join in! We are currently looking to expand and offer more opportunities to young people in the area, and we need more leaders and supporters to do so! \r\n\r\nVolunteering with Scouts is a great way to take part in new experiences, meet a lots of friendly people and have fun. The role involves supporting children in various sections (Squirrels/Beavers/Cubs/Scouts/Explorers) during weekly meetings, trips and camps. This can involve: \r\n- Welcoming young people and families to sessions and events.\r\n- Making sure everyone’s safe, supported, included and having fun.\r\n- Helping to plan and lead activities.\r\n- Getting involved with days out, camps and expeditions.\r\n- Sharing and learning skills – from coding to cake decorating to canoeing.\r\n- Celebrating young people’s achievements big and small.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like to get involved or learn more, then please reach out!\n\n## Experience required\n\nAnyone who likes engaging with young people and has a friendly disposition! Any experience of the Scout organisation is beneficial but not necessary - we simply ask for a commitment to providing an enjoyable experience to our members!\n\n## Training details\n\nAll essential training is provided by the Scout Association. There are also opportunities for ongoing training. PVGs are required and will be organised by Scouts.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nVolunteer timings are flexible and can be arranged to suit the volunteer. We have different groups meeting on different evenings during term time and we sometimes have weekend activities or trips away. We do ask that volunteers commit to approximately two hours a week.\n\n## Taster details\n\nLocal taster sessions are available, and induction is via the Scouting organisation website and the local team.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fc24f12b8-459b-4aca-b6f6-5eefc59f9932%2FXPrpz4zVmiRWRuGPAUiQ4SyLdVd2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=df15c9c9-caf2-44e1-9174-a52cccf66abf",
