                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000003SwLcAAK",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000003SwLcAAK/volunteer-assistant-manager",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer Assistant Manager",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to gain managerial skills volunteering for Cancer Research UK . This training and work experience will enhance your C.V. and be very rewarding knowing you are helping to beat cancer sooner.  \r\n\r\nFor more details please contact Agnes Keilloh, Shop Manager on E Mail: aberdeenunionshop@cancer.org.uk or tel: 01224 590580\n\n## Description\n\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to gain managerial skills volunteering for Cancer Research uk .  Suitable for someone with some retail background and an outgoing friendly personality. This training and work experience will enhance your C.V. and be very rewarding knowing you are helping to beat cancer sooner.  We are a very friendly hardworking team who also have a lot of fun   This position will include ongoing training on all aspects of managing a Cancer Research UK Charity shop. \r\nTraining will involve \r\n-Health and Safety       \r\n-Customer service   \r\n-Stock processing \r\n-Handling  cash \r\n-Fundraising   \r\n\r\nGood support and relevant training is provided-includes a taster session/shop visit and on going training and support.\r\n\r\nFor more details please contact Agnes Keilloh, Shop Manager on E Mail: aberdeenunionshop@cancer.org.uk or tel: 01224 590580\n\n## Experience required\n\nA friendly and helpful manner.\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support and relevant training is provided-includes a taster session/shop visit and on going training and support.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to suit volunteers. All help greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\n125 Union Street, Aberdeen City Centre.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteer travel expenses are available on agreement with Shop Manager, we pay for public transport if the volunteer can commit to certain number of hours. Reimbursement is on production of the relevant travel ticket.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
