            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000DhUszYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000DhUszYAF/tech-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-01",
                    "title": "Tech Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAre you passionate about the power of technology? Would you like to help bridge the digital divide? Do you have a few hours available each month?\r\n\r\nTechnology can help people to gain or regain their independence by allowing them to shop or bank online. It can battle isolation, as people can use the Internet and online services to connect to their family and friends. Technology can also provide something fun and relaxing to do though online games, TV, radio and other entertainment services.\r\n\r\nMany older people and disabled people experience difficulties with their technology and can’t find the support they need. Ability Net’s volunteers provide one-to-one technology support remotely and through home visits. Get involved today - apply to become a volunteer. This opportunity has flexible hours, driven and shaped by you and you will be given support to make a real difference in your area.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou don’t need to be a tech guru to help out. If you use a computer at home or work, and perhaps support family and friends with their tech issues, you are likely to have the skills needed.\n\n## Training details\n\nWhen joining AbilityNet as a volunteer you will be invited to Talent LMS, an online training platform. This contains induction and policy modules as well as technical training organised into sections. We offer regular live online volunteer training and forums sessions; you are also invited to the weekly ‘lunch and learn’ sessions run by RNIB. You are welcome to join as many of these as you would like to. We record and share the sessions for those who cannot attend on our private Volunteer YouTube channel.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTech volunteers work from home and support older and disabled people within their own homes and/or at local community hubs, so it is useful to have your own transport or good transport links. The area which you cover will be agreed between you and your coordinator. We have some gaps in coverage in North and East Fife at the moment, so are particularly interested in anyone willing to work in those areas. Ability Net pay travel expenses at 55p per mile for use of your own vehicle, or reimburse public transport expenses.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are reimbursed monthly - public transport costs or 55p per mile for own vehicle use",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
