                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000006SAfJYAW",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000006SAfJYAW/fundraising-driver-st-andrews",
                    "publishStart": "2025-11-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-08",
                    "title": "Fundraising Driver (St Andrews)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nMarie Curie is looking for volunteers to support their busy fundraising teams by delivering fundraising materials in your local community.\r\n\r\nAll tasks can be adapted to individuals’ skills and availability but may typically involve:\r\n\r\n-Supporting local fundraising groups by dropping off materials\r\n\r\n-Collecting and banking local cans in sites around the community\r\n\r\n-Helping to bank money\r\n\r\n-Collecting donations from local Marie Curie Supporters\r\n\r\n-Placing posters in local community.\n\n## Experience required\n\n- Enthusiasm and willing to be part of a team\r\n- A genuine interest in and desire to support the work of Marie Curie\r\n- Honest, committed and reliable\r\n- Flexible.\n\n## Training details\n\nAn induction, training, support and supervision in your role\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis role will take place within your local community.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPre-agreed, reasonable travel expenses will be reimbursed on a monthly basis",
