                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000GvdNbAAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000GvdNbAAJ/sensory-garden-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Sensory Garden Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are on the look-out for budding gardeners to help transform our Sensory Garden and outdoor space at the Aberdeen Science Centre.\r\n\r\nAn ideal opportunity for those who are interested in gardening; those who enjoy the outdoors; or want to be a bit more active, helping in the local community and supporting a local charity create an inspiring outdoor space and sensory garden for visitors.\r\n\r\nWe are flexible with times and working days, as long as you are keen to get stuck-in, we want to hear from you!\r\n\r\nPlease contact us at email: volunteer@asc.scot for more details. \r\n\r\nFurther information is also available on our website at https://aberdeensciencecentre.org/garden-volunteer/\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nA couple of hours a week - flexible times available to suit volunteers. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAberdeen Science Centre is based in Central Aberdeen at 179 Constitution Street, Aberdeen, AB24 5TU.",
