                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JUiOxYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JUiOxYAL/events-volunteers-stadium-soar-at-aberdeen-pittodrie",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-30",
                    "title": "Events Volunteers (Stadium Soar at Aberdeen Pittodrie)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nPittodrie Stadium Soar, which takes place from 2nd April 2027 to 4th April 2027 is an exhilarating zip slide experience at Scotland's iconic stadium in Aberdeen. Participants will take on an unforgettable challenge, zipsliding across the stadium while raising vital funds to support charities across Scotland.\r\n\r\nVolunteers will play a key role in creating an incredible experience for every participant. From welcoming supporters and assisting with registration to cheering them on throughout the day, your enthusiasm and support will help make this event a huge success.\r\n\r\nWe have a range of volunteer opportunities available throughout the event that people can help with:\r\n\r\n- Registration & Check-In Welcome participants as they arrive, assist with registration, answer questions, and help ensure everyone is ready for their Stadium Soar experience.\r\n\r\n- Event Support & Stewarding Help guide participants and spectators around the venue, provide information, support event operations, and assist the event team as needed throughout the day.\r\n\r\n- Cheer Point Volunteers Bring the atmosphere to life by encouraging participants, celebrating their achievements, and helping create a memorable event experience.\r\n\r\n- Finish Area Support Congratulate participants as they complete their challenge and help ensure everyone leaves with a smile.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for enthusiastic, friendly volunteers who enjoy working with people and want to help create an unforgettable fundraising event. By volunteering at Pittodrie Stadium Soar, you'll be helping ensure that No Life is Half Lived while supporting thousands of people living with chest, heart and stroke conditions across Scotland.\r\n\r\nNo previous experience is required, just plenty of energy, enthusiasm, and a passion for making a difference.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to be involved in a major event and to help Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland in the vital support we provide people.\r\n\r\nFor more details and to register to volunteer please visit: https://volunteer.chss.org.uk/opportunities/125479-events-volunteer-2026-10-06?cookieconsent=set  or email: volunteering@chss.org.uk\n\n## Description\n\nPittodrie Stadium Soar, which takes place from 2nd April 2027 to 4th April 2027 is an exhilarating zip slide experience at Scotland's iconic stadium in Aberdeen. Participants will take on an unforgettable challenge, zipsliding across the stadium while raising vital funds to support charities across Scotland.\r\n\r\nVolunteers will play a key role in creating an incredible experience for every participant. From welcoming supporters and assisting with registration to cheering them on throughout the day, your enthusiasm and support will help make this event a huge success.\r\n\r\nWe have a range of volunteer opportunities available throughout the event that people can help with:\r\n\r\n- Registration & Check-In Welcome participants as they arrive, assist with registration, answer questions, and help ensure everyone is ready for their Stadium Soar experience.\r\n\r\n- Event Support & Stewarding Help guide participants and spectators around the venue, provide information, support event operations, and assist the event team as needed throughout the day.\r\n\r\n- Cheer Point Volunteers Bring the atmosphere to life by encouraging participants, celebrating their achievements, and helping create a memorable event experience.\r\n\r\n- Finish Area Support Congratulate participants as they complete their challenge and help ensure everyone leaves with a smile.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for enthusiastic, friendly volunteers who enjoy working with people and want to help create an unforgettable fundraising event. By volunteering at Pittodrie Stadium Soar, you'll be helping ensure that No Life is Half Lived while supporting thousands of people living with chest, heart and stroke conditions across Scotland.\r\n\r\nNo previous experience is required, just plenty of energy, enthusiasm, and a passion for making a difference.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to be involved in a major event and to help Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland in the vital support we provide people.\r\n\r\nFor more details and to register to volunteer please visit: https://volunteer.chss.org.uk/opportunities/125479-events-volunteer-2026-10-06?cookieconsent=set  or email: volunteering@chss.org.uk\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nTakes place at Pittodrie Stadium , Aberdeen between the 2nd-4th April 2027. Flexible times available to assist. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTakes place at Pittodrie Stadium , Aberdeen between the 2nd-4th April 2027.\r\n\r\nPittodrie Stadium is located just over a mile from Aberdeen city centre and is easily accessible by bus, car, or a 20-minute walk from Aberdeen Railway Station.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses Reasonable out-of-pocket expenses will be reimbursed. These should be discussed with your Line Manager prior to outlay and must be submitted within the prescribed guidelines as detailed in the CHSS Volunteer Expenses Policy.",
