                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BcrbGYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BcrbGYAR/volunteer-your-way-with-chss-in-grampian",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Volunteer Your Way with CHSS in Grampian",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nChest Heart & Stroke Scotland (CHSS) is proud to announce the launch of a brand-new Health Defence hub in Grampian, bringing vital health services directly to the heart of the community. This exciting initiative is part of CHSS’s vision of a Scotland where people with our conditions can live their lives well.\r\n \r\nThe Health Defence team is here to empower people to take control of their health. From free health checks to specialist physical activity support, the hub will offer a range of services designed to help individuals live life to the fullest.\r\n\r\nWe’re currently recruiting Community Health Volunteers to carry out basic health assessments and share healthy lifestyle information messages with those who need it most. Whether you’re out and about in your local area or supporting us directly in the Health Defence hub, your role will be crucial in helping us to deliver these important services.\r\n \r\n*Why Volunteer?\r\nVolunteering with CHSS’s Health Defence Hub is a powerful way to make a real difference in your community—in a way that works for you. If you’d like to be part of an innovative organisation that recognises and celebrates your talents, while supporting vibrant communities across Grampian, there is place here for you.\r\n \r\nSam, a current Community Health Volunteer, shared his experience of volunteering for CHSS:\r\n“The work of CHSS is important to me on a personal level, and because of this I was motivated by the opportunity to provide support to help others”\r\n“I was impressed by the prompt response from the CHSS team following my application, and the friendly and professional contact from staff that I experienced both face to face and remotely.”\r\n\r\n*Make a Difference in Just a Few Hours\r\nIf you have a couple of hours to spare each month, you can help people in your community to thrive. Volunteering with CHSS is a chance to connect, contribute, and be part of something truly meaningful.\r\n \r\n*Apply now to become a Community Health Volunteer in Grampian: https://volunteer.chss.org.uk/opportunities/91101-community-health-volunteer-grampian-2025-06-12 or email volunteering@chss.org.uk if you require more information or have any questions.\r\n\r\nTogether, we can build a healthier Scotland—one conversation, one health-check, one volunteer at a time.\n\n## Description\n\nChest Heart & Stroke Scotland (CHSS) is proud to announce the launch of a brand-new Health Defence hub in Grampian, bringing vital health services directly to the heart of the community. This exciting initiative is part of CHSS’s vision of a Scotland where people with our conditions can live their lives well.\r\n \r\nThe Health Defence team is here to empower people to take control of their health. From free health checks to specialist physical activity support, the hub will offer a range of services designed to help individuals live life to the fullest.\r\n\r\nWe’re currently recruiting Community Health Volunteers to carry out basic health assessments and share healthy lifestyle information messages with those who need it most. Whether you’re out and about in your local area or supporting us directly in the Health Defence hub, your role will be crucial in helping us to deliver these important services.\r\n \r\n*Why Volunteer?\r\nVolunteering with CHSS’s Health Defence Hub is a powerful way to make a real difference in your community—in a way that works for you. If you’d like to be part of an innovative organisation that recognises and celebrates your talents, while supporting vibrant communities across Grampian, there is place here for you.\r\n \r\nSam, a current Community Health Volunteer, shared his experience of volunteering for CHSS:\r\n“The work of CHSS is important to me on a personal level, and because of this I was motivated by the opportunity to provide support to help others”\r\n“I was impressed by the prompt response from the CHSS team following my application, and the friendly and professional contact from staff that I experienced both face to face and remotely.”\r\n\r\n*Make a Difference in Just a Few Hours\r\nIf you have a couple of hours to spare each month, you can help people in your community to thrive. Volunteering with CHSS is a chance to connect, contribute, and be part of something truly meaningful.\r\n \r\n*Apply now to become a Community Health Volunteer in Grampian: https://volunteer.chss.org.uk/opportunities/91101-community-health-volunteer-grampian-2025-06-12 or email volunteering@chss.org.uk if you require more information or have any questions.\r\n\r\nTogether, we can build a healthier Scotland—one conversation, one health-check, one volunteer at a time.\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant guidance and excellent support is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to suit volunteers. All help greatly appreciated.",
