                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000AqiIXYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000AqiIXYAZ/events-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Events Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nOur Fundraising Heroes fight back against loneliness, stop fear in its tracks and keep people alive for longer – all while having fun at the same time!\r\n\r\nWe are looking for enthusiastic volunteers to join our events team in the north of Scotland. Help us ensure No Life is Half Lived by lending our community fundraisers a hand with registration, marshalling, cheering, and much more!\r\n\r\nVolunteering at our events is a great way to meet new people, boost confidence and have fun.\r\n\r\nJack, a CHSS volunteer says: “I’d never done any volunteering before, but it’s been truly rewarding. Volunteering is something you fold into your life, something you enjoy doing.\"\r\n\r\nJoin our fabulous team in the north of Scotland and make a real difference to people who are isolated, scared, or anxious about their condition.\r\n\r\nWant to find out more? Get in touch with our friendly volunteering team today and discover how you can make your time really matter:\r\n-please visit: https://volunteer.chss.org.uk/opportunities/75769-events-volunteer-regular-north-of-scotland-2024-10-30 and  https://www.chss.org.uk/supportus/volunteering/  \r\n-or email: volunteering@chss.org.uk\n\n## Description\n\nOur Fundraising Heroes fight back against loneliness, stop fear in its tracks and keep people alive for longer – all while having fun at the same time!\r\n\r\nWe are looking for enthusiastic volunteers to join our events team in the north of Scotland. Help us ensure No Life is Half Lived by lending our community fundraisers a hand with registration, marshalling, cheering, and much more!\r\n\r\nVolunteering at our events is a great way to meet new people, boost confidence and have fun.\r\n\r\nJack, a CHSS volunteer says: “I’d never done any volunteering before, but it’s been truly rewarding. Volunteering is something you fold into your life, something you enjoy doing.\"\r\n\r\nJoin our fabulous team in the north of Scotland and make a real difference to people who are isolated, scared, or anxious about their condition.\r\n\r\nWant to find out more? Get in touch with our friendly volunteering team today and discover how you can make your time really matter:\r\n-please visit: https://volunteer.chss.org.uk/opportunities/75769-events-volunteer-regular-north-of-scotland-2024-10-30 and  https://www.chss.org.uk/supportus/volunteering/  \r\n-or email: volunteering@chss.org.uk\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to assist. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
