                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000003p7SLYAY",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000003p7SLYAY/peer-group-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Peer Group Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe RVS Cuppa Club are one of over 100 affiliated peer support groups with Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland. They support people who have had strokes, or are living with other long-term health conditions, to come together and help them live their lives to the full. The group enjoy a cup of tea and a chat, and provide social activities like bingo and dominoes. You will be helping people to join others with similar lived experiences while also having a great time yourself and making new friends.\r\n\r\nThe group meet every Thursday morning from 10am-12pm at Froghall Community Centre, 14 Powis Place, Aberdeen, AB25 3TX. \r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference. All assistance is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor further details please contact Laura Campbell, Peer Support Coordinator at email: laura.campbell@chss.org.uk or telephone: 07392869309.\n\n## Description\n\nThe RVS Cuppa Club are one of over 100 affiliated peer support groups with Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland. They support people who have had strokes, or are living with other long-term health conditions, to come together and help them live their lives to the full. The group enjoy a cup of tea and a chat, and provide social activities like bingo and dominoes. You will be helping people to join others with similar lived experiences while also having a great time yourself and making new friends.\r\n\r\nThe group meet every Thursday morning from 10am-12pm at Froghall Community Centre, 14 Powis Place, Aberdeen, AB25 3TX. \r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference. All assistance is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nFor further details please contact Laura Campbell, Peer Support Coordinator at email: laura.campbell@chss.org.uk or telephone: 07392869309.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe group meet every Thursday morning from 10am-12pm at Froghall Community Centre, 14 Powis Place, Aberdeen, AB25 3TX.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe group meet every Thursday morning from 10am-12pm at Froghall Community Centre, 14 Powis Place, Aberdeen, AB25 3TX. Car sharing could be possible depending on location, but there is also a bus stop across the road.",
