                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HlYyvYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HlYyvYAF/tuesday-quiz-group-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-14",
                    "title": "Tuesday Quiz Group Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you have competent IT skills and are looking to do some online volunteering?\r\nThe Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland Peer Support Tuesday Quiz Group would be delighted to hear from you.\r\nThe Tuesday Quiz Group meet on Microsoft Teams every Tuesday evening at 7pm and are looking for people to help organise and host their meetings. It is a free, area-wide online Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland partnered Peer Support Group which offers a relaxed environment and  social connection for stroke survivors or people living with long-term respiratory, long covid or cardiac conditions. The quiz format is multiple-choice general knowledge quiz questions with no scoring system to keep it low-pressure, friendly, and fun. Attendees can choose to read their answers out loud or just play along quietly. Family members, friends, and carers are also welcome.\r\nA fantastic, enjoyable opportunity to assist. All help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated. \r\nWant to find out more? Please contact Laura Campbell, Peer & Involvement Coordinator (Digital), Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland at email: Laura.Campbell@chss.org.uk or telephone: 07392 869309\n\n## Description\n\nDo you have competent IT skills and are looking to do some online volunteering?\r\n\r\nThe Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland Peer Support Tuesday Quiz Group would be delighted to hear from you.\r\n\r\nThe Tuesday Quiz Group meet on Microsoft Teams every Tuesday evening at 7pm and are looking for people to help organise and host their meetings. The Quiz Group is a free, area-wide online Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland partnered Peer Support Group which offers a relaxed environment and social connection for stroke survivors or people living with long-term respiratory, long covid or cardiac conditions. The quiz format is multiple-choice general knowledge quiz questions with no scoring system to keep it low-pressure, friendly, and fun. Attendees can choose to read their answers out loud or just play along quietly. Family members, friends, and carers are also welcome.\r\n\r\nA fantastic, enjoyable opportunity to assist. All help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated. \r\n\r\nWant to find out more? Please contact Laura Campbell, Peer & Involvement Coordinator (Digital), Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland at email: Laura.Campbell@chss.org.uk or telephone: 07392 869309\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe Tuesday Quiz Group meet on Microsoft Teams every Tuesday evening at 7pm\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Tuesday Quiz Group meet on Microsoft Teams every Tuesday evening at 7pm",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
