        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400000aVws8AAC",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400000aVws8AAC/polmont-playgroup",
            "name": "Polmont Playgroup",
            "description": "Polmont Playgroup SCIO is a community-based children's and family charity in Brightons, Falkirk. Established in 1972, we have been supporting local children and families for more than 50 years.\r\nFrom our community building on Redding Road, we provide affordable, inclusive opportunities for children and families to play, learn, socialise and connect.\r\n\r\nOur activities include our weekday Playgroup for children aged 2–5, Breakfast Club, Stay & Play sessions, ASN sensory sessions, school holiday activities and a programme of family and community events throughout the year.\r\nWe aim to provide a welcoming and inclusive environment where children can learn through play, build confidence, develop social skills and have fun. We also work to support parents, carers and families by providing opportunities to meet others and connect with their local community.\r\n\r\nOur building is also available for children's parties, venue hire and community use, helping us make the most of our community-owned space and generate income to support our charitable activities.",
            "website": "https://www.polmontplaygroup.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC053631"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009LjZgYAK",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009LjZgYAK/play-assistant-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-04-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-09",
                    "title": "Play Assistant Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAt Polmont Playgroup we strongly believe in learning through play, for over 52 years, we have been providing a valuable service to our community and we are always looking for ways we can do more.  Our small team of experienced playleaders see c40-60 children aged 2.5 - 5years each week for their play sessions and our Facebook reviews will tell you all you need to know. \r\nSessions are two hours long and children are provided with a snack.\r\n\r\nTasks involved in the role will include:\r\n- Supporting playleaders to set up play spaces.\r\n- Interacting with children during play - outdoor play, crafts, music, roleplay, reading etc.\r\n- Some interaction with parents may occur so individuals should be confident to speak to other adults, questions and concerns can be handed to playleaders to assist parents. \r\n- Highlight & report any safety risks or accidents observed to ensure the playleader can take necessary action.\r\n\r\nThis will be a great opportunity for anyone that would like to volunteer with children or for anyone who is considering or currently studying towards a career in childcare.  Qualified playleaders can support you ensuring your time at the playgroup compliments your learning whilst gaining valuable hands on experience.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers with a keen interest and desire to volunteer/working with children.  No experience is required.  Volunteers should be reliable, approachable and friendly, caring and nurturing.\n\n## Training details\n\nDedicated Playleader to provide personalised plan to suit individuals and to ensure successful transition into volunteering role.  Further training can be looked as required, with ongoing support in form of check-ins.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nSessions take place Monday-Friday (term time)\r\n9:30am - 11:30am (2-4hours per week)\n\n## Travel details\n\nRedding Road, Brightons, Falkirk, FK2 0AA (next to Falkirk Braes Grange Centre).\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n45p per mile (maximum 10miles per day).",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F7f8d0c01-f40f-45d5-8c0c-38ed536f1ba6%2Fq19DcOWGQCRPIPMRCkAF0XcUA2l1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=3a78e926-13ff-4932-b40f-548369e855b7",
