            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhtvgAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhtvgAAB/social-walk-leaders",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-10",
                    "title": "Social Walk Leaders",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNo matter how good our services are, we can't properly support our users/community well if we don't have good leaders in the team. If this sounds like you?... we would love you to consider volunteering with us for a few hours per week.\r\n\r\nThe Vale of Leven Trust were established to develop the community of the Vale of Leven. VOLT is a local charity run by local people who have witnessed a slow deterioration of a town and area in general that was more economically prosperous but has seen all our industry and large companies move elsewhere. We have become a commuter town which results in many residents not routinely being part of the community or visiting our town centre, resulting in reduced footfall leading to market failure in terms of variety and scale of locally accessible services and economy.\r\n\r\nDo you love being outdoors, meeting new people and encouraging others to stay active? Why not become a walk leader? We are looking for enthusiastic and reliable people to become Social Walk Leaders.\r\n\r\nWhat’s in it for you?\r\nDevelop your leadership, management and communication skills.\r\nSatisfaction from supporting and encouraging members of the local community to become and stay active.\r\n \r\nWhat we ask of you: \r\nWe ask that initially you attend four of our social walks to give you a sense of what we do.\r\nComplete our short application.\r\nUndertake & complete a ‘Paths for All’ walk leader training session.\r\nUndertake a VOLT induction training session.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
