                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhtvhAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhtvhAAB/events-and-activities-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-10",
                    "title": "Events and Activities Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNo matter how good our services are, we can't properly support our users/community well if we don't have good leaders in the team. If this sounds like you?... we would love you to consider volunteering with us for a few hours per week.\r\n\r\nThe Vale of Leven Trust were established to develop the community of the Vale of Leven. VOLT is a local charity run by local people who have witnessed a slow deterioration of a town and area in general that was more economically prosperous but has seen all our industry and large companies move elsewhere. We have become a commuter town which results in many residents not routinely being part of the community or visiting our town centre, resulting in reduced footfall leading to market failure in terms of variety and scale of locally accessible services and economy.\r\n\r\nWe have a developing calendar of events and activities such as line dancing, bingo and much more! Why not volunteer and join our weekend activities team?\r\n\r\nOur volunteer role includes but is not limited to:\r\n\r\nWelcoming participants to activities / events making everyone feel included.\r\nHelping with set up & breakdown of activities.\r\nTaking photos of activities for social media\r\n\r\nWhat we ask from you: \r\nCome in for an initial chat with our team to get to know us\r\nComplete our short application\r\nAttend 2 of our activities to give you an idea of what we do.\r\nEnthusiasm\r\nCommitment\r\nAll we need from you is\r\nPositive mindset\r\n \r\nWhat’s in it for you?\r\nSupport from our team to develop skills and knowledge.\r\nBe a key part in your community\r\nHave fun while playing an important role\r\nWe will provide you with a reference\r\n \r\nAdditionally, if you have any experience running workshops of any kind, particularly craft or fitness related and have time to run regular or one-off activities, we would love to hear from you.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
