        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400000YTD6MAAX",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400000YTD6MAAX/fife-centre-for-equalities",
            "name": "Fife Centre for Equalities",
            "description": "Fife Centre for Equalities (FCE) was established in April 2014, as a joint initiative between Fife Council, Fife Voluntary Action and NHS Fife, to work with partners to develop more inclusive and responsive services for people in Fife, and to build a positive picture of Fifes modern and diverse population. FCE became an independent body on 1 July 2016.\r\n\r\nFCE wants to build a collective voice to champion equality, diversity, inclusion and social justice. The centre provides practical guidance and support to everyone working to tackle inequality; here in Fife, and beyond. We want to:\r\n- Make equality a normal part of everyday life in Fife\r\n- Promote the rights of individuals, because everyones story is unique\r\n- Help communities make their voices heard, and have their say in the planning and delivery of local \r\n- Develop relationships with partners and stakeholders from public, private and third sectors to advance equality, diversity, social justice and community cohesion.",
            "website": "https://www.centreforequalities.org.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Equality",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Equality"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I2YRRYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I2YRRYA3/community-navigator",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-16",
                    "title": "Community Navigator",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nFife Centre for Equalities are recruiting volunteers for an exciting new role, in which ‘Community Navigators’ will engage with local communities with the aim of finding out more about their needs. With a particular focus around mental health and wellbeing needs, Community Navigators will facilitate discussions around what can be done to help bring positive change.\r\n\r\nAs part of this role, the organisation and the volunteers, will hold community feedback drop-in sessions around Fife to hear local views.\r\n\r\nFull training will be provided, alongside many practice sessions to help you gain the confidence you need. So, if you enjoy talking to others, want to improve communication skills or want to help your community, this might be the role for you.\r\n\r\nFirst training session is on Wednesday 30th September 2026.\n\n## Experience required\n\nMust be empathetic, be confident, good communication skills, be adaptable, willingness and eagerness to learn if the above skills are not matched but are still interested.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe first training session will be held by an external organisation, where training will be for both staff and volunteers. There will be another external training session in early 2027. In between then we will host catch-up training sessions in October, November and December. There will also be a controlled practice session in February followed by monthly ongoing support and training for all volunteers which can include any pastoral care, covering any concerns and continue with any training support needed.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity will take place in Kirkcaldy until March 2027, after that we will be meeting once or twice a month and moving to different areas around Fife each time. Travel expenses will be reimbursed (within reason, for example, if you need to take a taxi, please inform us ahead of time). If you are unable to attend sessions further away, it’s not an issue, just attend when you can.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe pay 0.45pence per mile. We will reimburse public transportation tickets, although we recommend using the busses where possible, if not possible then trains will be reimbursed. If a taxi is required, we can reimburse, as long as prior notice is given.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I2YRRYA3#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Community Navigator",
                        "description": "Must be empathetic, be confident, good communication skills, be adaptable, willingness and eagerness to learn if the above skills are not matched but are still interested.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I2YRRYA3/community-navigator?#modal_register_a0gQD00000I2YRRYA3",
