                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhvLYAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VhvLYAAZ/companion-supporter-befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-24",
                    "title": "Companion-Supporter-Befriender",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nFife Centre for Equalities (FCE) has charitable aims of raising awareness and understanding of equality and diversity across all communities and community groups in Fife.\r\n\r\nAn exciting opportunity is available for volunteers from all walks of life to come together and meet with some of the older members of our community. we are currently focusing on finding volunteers to befriend members of our Fife Inclusion Network Project, a project in which we are helping older people from diverse communities to build meaningful connections, reduce social isolation and improve mental and emotional health. This is being achieved by monthly get togethers where project members and volunteers meet, chat, eat and participate in various activities and workshops. So, if you’re interested in learning more about other cultures, disabilities etc. we would love to have you join us on this amazing volunteering project.\n\n## Experience required\n\n-Willing to work with interpreter if needed.\r\n-Good communication skills and a good listener\r\n-Positive, reliable and adaptable\r\n-Person-centred.\r\n-Patient, tactful, caring and respectful\r\n-Understanding, sensitive, discrete and able to maintain confidentiality\n\n## Training details\n\nA full onboarding and training session will be provided, a mix of formal or informal chats. Their role as a volunteer will be explained, all necessary documents will be signed, and a handbook will be provided. Regular contact will be made by the volunteer co-ordinator informing them of upcoming events and both check-in and feedback sessions either in person, on the phone or a Teams call.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis opportunity is available around various locations in Fife with a different location selected for each event. Events are once a month, with no regular day or time of day, varying from morning to evening, so everyone has access to it. Travel is always considered with either parking being provided or a location close to public transport.\r\n\r\nHowever, with some locations being a litter further afield, volunteers would not be expected to attend every event, they can attend the ones closer to them.\r\n\r\nVolunteers would be expected to make their own way to the events close to their home.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport rates will be reimbursed. On rare occasions, if needed, a taxi can be provided. This willneed to be pre-authorised.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VhvLYAAZ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
