                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000002fJRHAA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000002fJRHAA2/community-cafe-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Community Cafe Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are recruiting volunteers to assist in a wonderful community café at Ferryhill Church.\r\n\r\nAll volunteers are welcome. Support, mentoring and learning opportunities will be available as and when required. A brilliant opportunity to help and make a difference in the community. \r\n\r\nIf you feel you can spare a few hours to help in any way please contact us at Email: admin@devanaparishchurch.org or telephone: 01224 213093 or 01224 961430.\n\n## Description\n\nDevana Parish Church (formerly Ferryhill Parish Church) operates a great community café in the heart of Ferryhill, which creates a welcoming environment for those who attend for a morning cuppa and also for those who volunteer their services. \r\n\r\nWe are requiring helpers, who can assist in the coffee shop, as it is a very popular meeting place. Helpers are required to volunteer with the team in the general running of the coffee shop. e.g. setting tables, serving coffees, clearing tables and generally tidying up. \r\n\r\nThe café is located in the church but people do not need to be church members to be volunteers-everyone is welcome.\r\n\r\nAll volunteers are welcome and greatly appreciated.  Support, mentoring and learning opportunities will be available as and when required. A brilliant opportunity to help and make a real difference in the community. \r\n\r\n\r\nIf you feel you can spare a few hours to help in any way please contact us at Email: admin@devanaparishchurch.org or telephone: 01224 213093 or 01224 961430.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly and approachable. A good listener and willing learner.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. The induction will be informal and completed at the volunteer’s pace. There is support available from the team on duty each day and there is also an overall café team leader, who is available should any specific issues arise.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available-all help greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDevana Parish Church (formerly Ferryhill Parish Church),\r\nFonthill Road,\r\nAberdeen,\r\nAB11 6UD",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
