        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400000Ycj2MAAR",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400000Ycj2MAAR/aberdeen-civic-society",
            "name": "Aberdeen Civic Society",
            "description": "Aberdeen Civic Society has the following objectives:\r\n1.To stimulate public interest in and care for the beauty, history and character of the city of Aberdeen and its surroundings. \r\n2.To encourage the preservation, development and improvement of features of general amenity and historic interest. \r\n3.To encourage high standards of architectural planning. \r\n4.The Society pursues these aims by means of illustrated lectures, film shows, discussions, visits and walkabouts. \r\n5.An important feature of the Society's work is its Awards and Commendations Scheme. Through this, encouragement and recognition are given to those who have contributed to the amenity of the city by means of new buildings or the restoration and preservation of old buildings. \r\n6.The Society keeps itself informed on planning applications made to the City Council. It submits comments and suggestions, and lodges objections when proposals are considered detrimental to the city.",
            "website": "http://www.aberdeencivicsociety.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC003089"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Heritage",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Heritage"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000003OLb3YAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000003OLb3YAG/executive-committee-members",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Executive Committee Members",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAberdeen Civic Society have great opportunities for people to help volunteering as Executive Committee Members.\r\n\r\nThe Executive Committee work to advance the objectives of the Society which are:\r\n\r\n•\tTo stimulate public interest in and care for the beauty, history and character of the city of Aberdeen and its surroundings.\r\n•\tTo encourage the preservation, development and improvement of features of general amenity and historic interest.\r\n•\tTo encourage high standards of architectural planning.\r\n•\tThe Society pursues these aims by means of illustrated lectures, discussions, visits and walkabouts.\r\n\r\nAn important feature of the Society's work is its Awards and Commendations Scheme. Through this, encouragement and recognition are given to those who have contributed to the amenity of the city by means of new buildings or the restoration and preservation of old buildings.\r\n\r\nThe Society keeps itself informed on planning applications made to the City Council. It submits comments and suggestions, and lodges objections when proposals are considered detrimental to the city.\r\n\r\nCommittee members are sought to help with the following activities: \r\n\r\n•\tto arrange the annual programme of talks\r\n•\tto organise the Society's social events- the annual Supper and Summer Outing\r\n•\tto research, discuss and respond to current Aberdeen City planning applications and to participate in public consultations on urban planning\r\n•\tto improve the Society's communication with the public through social and other media\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help with the preservation, development and improvement of features of general amenity and historic interest in Aberdeen.\r\n\r\nFor further information please contact Julia Strickland, Honorary Secretary at email info@aberdeencivicsociety.org.uk or telephone 07434540344.\r\n\r\nMore information about Aberdeen Civic Society is also available at https://www.aberdeencivicsociety.org.uk/ and https://www.facebook.com/AberdeenCivicSociety\n\n## Description\n\nAberdeen Civic Society have great opportunities for people to help volunteering as Executive Committee Members.\r\n\r\nThe Executive Committee work to advance the objectives of the Society which are:\r\n\r\n•\tTo stimulate public interest in and care for the beauty, history and character of the city of Aberdeen and its surroundings.\r\n•\tTo encourage the preservation, development and improvement of features of general amenity and historic interest.\r\n•\tTo encourage high standards of architectural planning.\r\n•\tThe Society pursues these aims by means of illustrated lectures, discussions, visits and walkabouts.\r\n\r\nAn important feature of the Society's work is its Awards and Commendations Scheme. Through this, encouragement and recognition are given to those who have contributed to the amenity of the city by means of new buildings or the restoration and preservation of old buildings.\r\n\r\nThe Society keeps itself informed on planning applications made to the City Council. It submits comments and suggestions, and lodges objections when proposals are considered detrimental to the city.\r\n\r\nCommittee members are sought to help with the following activities: \r\n\r\n•\tto arrange the annual programme of talks\r\n•\tto organise the Society's social events- the annual Supper and Summer Outing\r\n•\tto research, discuss and respond to current Aberdeen City planning applications and to participate in public consultations on urban planning\r\n•\tto improve the Society's communication with the public through social and other media\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help with the preservation, development and improvement of features of general amenity and historic interest in Aberdeen.\r\n\r\nFor further information please contact Julia Strickland, Honorary Secretary at email info@aberdeencivicsociety.org.uk or telephone 07434540344.\r\n\r\nMore information about Aberdeen Civic Society is also available at https://www.aberdeencivicsociety.org.uk/ and https://www.facebook.com/AberdeenCivicSociety\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe Committee meets once a month at the Royal Northern and University Club ( 9 Albyn Place, Aberdeen AB10 1YE). Parking is available. Meetings usually last for an hour to an hour and a half.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Committee meets once a month at the Royal Northern and University Club ( 9 Albyn Place, Aberdeen AB10 1YE). Parking is available. Meetings usually last for an hour to an hour and a half.",
