            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000058UdxYAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000058UdxYAE/volunteer-treasurer-as-part-of-the-management-committee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer Treasurer as part of the Management Committee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nKingswells Community Centre and Webster Park provide welcoming facilities for use by all members of the community and are continuing to develop and grow for the needs of our future generations. \r\n\r\nWe currently require a volunteer to be a  Treasurer on our Management Committee and would welcome anyone with finance experience to join us in helping develop our centres further and provide quality experiences for the community. It would involve attending regular 6 weekly committee meetings and liaising with the Manager of the centre to produce financial reports to present at the meetings. There would also be end of year reports required to be prepared for submitting for auditing.\r\n\r\nWe are a friendly group and we even provide biscuits at our meetings!\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help the local community. For more information please contact Gillian Millar, Chairperson at email: gill.millar@virgin.net or telephone: 07891088660.\n\n## Description\n\nKingswells Community Centre and Webster Park provide welcoming facilities for use by all members of the community and are continuing to develop and grow for the needs of our future generations. \r\n\r\nWe currently require a volunteer to be a  Treasurer on our Management Committee and would welcome anyone with finance experience to join us in helping develop our centres further and provide quality experiences for the community. It would involve attending regular 6 weekly committee meetings and liaising with the Manager of the centre to produce financial reports to present at the meetings. There would also be end of year reports required to be prepared for submitting for auditing.\r\n\r\nWe are a friendly group and we even provide biscuits at our meetings!\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help the local community. For more information please contact Gillian Millar, Chairperson at email: gill.millar@virgin.net or telephone: 07891088660.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. The Chairperson will work with the Treasurer to ensure that they know what is expected and provide access to the online training programmes for the software packages.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe meetings are held at Kingswells Community Centre, Kingswells every 6 weeks (usually on a Tuesday evening).\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe meetings are held at Kingswells Community Centre, Kingswells Avenue, Kingswells, Aberdeen, AB15 8TG every 6 weeks.",
