                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008IU33YAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008IU33YAG/toddlers-group-play-assistant-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Toddlers Group Play Assistant Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nKingswells Toddlers Group is a fun place for children from baby to pre-school age to come and play, and a safe place for parents and carers to socialise and play with their children. \r\n\r\nThrough the Centre, the children have access to a range of indoor equipment from climbing and slide structures to soft play and everyday toys, we are also in the process of setting up and outdoor area for the children to play.\r\n\r\nThe group is usually set up and tidied by parents, but we are looking for a volunteer to come in to the Centre on a Tuesday and Thursday morning from 9am-11.30am and set out all the toys, engage with the children and parents and organise a few small activities with the children like messy play, story telling or basic crafts, then tidy up again at the end of the group.\r\n\r\nThis would be a great opportunity for someone who is enthusiastic about working with smaller children and is sociable with adults.\r\n\r\nThe Community Centre would provide a PVG check and Introduction to Child Protection course.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference in the community. For more details please contact Nicole Farquharson, centre Manager at email: info@kccwp.co.uk or telephone: 01224 741806\n\n## Description\n\nKingswells Toddlers Group is a fun place for children from baby to pre-school age to come and play, and a safe place for parents and carers to socialise and play with their children. \r\n\r\nThrough the Centre, the children have access to a range of indoor equipment from climbing and slide structures to soft play and everyday toys, we are also in the process of setting up and outdoor area for the children to play.\r\n\r\nThe group is usually set up and tidied by parents, but we are looking for volunteers to come in to the Centre on a Tuesday and Thursday morning from 9am-11.30am and set out all the toys, engage with the children and parents and organise a few small activities with the children like messy play, story telling or basic crafts, then tidy up again at the end of the group.\r\n\r\nThis would be a great opportunity for someone who is enthusiastic about working with smaller children and is sociable with adults.\r\n\r\nThe Community Centre would provide a PVG check and Introduction to Child Protection course.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference in the community. For more details please contact Nicole Farquharson, Centre Manager at email: info@kccwp.co.uk or telephone: 01224 741806\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. \r\n\r\nThe volunteer will be given initial introduction to child support training, and training in the set up and running of the group. The volunteer will be able to contact staff at the Centre, chat over ideas about running and organising the group and gain support from the Centre Manager.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe Group takes place  on a Tuesday and Thursday morning from 9am-11.30am. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Toddlers Group is held at Kingswells Community Centre which is in the centre of the village. \r\n\r\nKingswells is served by the number 14 bus service from town and the number 5 & 6 take you from town to the Park & Ride in Kingswells.\r\n\r\nThere is car parking in front of and around the Centre.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F5642bb8d-dd09-4515-afaf-7d8ea48430e5%2FpcmZKQWRS7QuRLWYXELQ6C0DBbO2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=34f78dbf-afb1-4d3f-9b22-ecc3c8e0983f",
