            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000094XcvYAE",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000094XcvYAE/faceyouth-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "FACEYOUTH Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\n*Join FACEYOUTH and Make a Difference!\r\nFACEYOUTH—a grassroots-inspired charitable organisation dedicated to improving the lives of disadvantaged children and youth in Aberdeen and beyond, through mental health programs, educational initiatives, and community outreach.\r\n\r\n*About this Opportunity\r\nA Lifeline for Those Who Need It Most\r\n\r\nAt FACEYOUTH, we are committed to supporting disadvantaged children and youth, ensuring they have access to the mental wellbeing support, resources, and opportunities they need to thrive. While we work closely with children from ethnic minority and refugee communities, our services are not limited to them—we support all children and young people facing challenges, regardless of their background.\r\n\r\nTo continue making a meaningful impact, we need passionate volunteers to join us. Whether you have a few hours to spare or are looking for a deeper commitment, we welcome your support. We Need Volunteers Like You!  We are seeking enthusiastic individuals to support our work in various roles, including:\r\n\r\n•\tYouth Mentors & Well-being Champions – Provide guidance and emotional support to young people.\r\n•\tEvent & Fundraising Assistants – Help us organise impactful community events and fundraising initiatives.\r\n•\t Social Media & Marketing Volunteers – Raise awareness and promote our cause online.\r\n•\tAdmin & Project Support – Assist with behind-the-scenes operations to keep our programs running smoothly.\r\n•\tEducation & Skills Trainers – Share your knowledge and help young people develop valuable life skills.\r\n\r\nThis is an opportunity to be part of a growing movement that ensures no young person is left behind. We believe every child deserves access to mental health support, education, and a strong community to uplift them.\r\n\r\n*Why Volunteer with FACEYOUTH?\r\n•\t Make a real difference in the lives of vulnerable children and youth. Develop new skills while making a meaningful contribution\r\n•\tGain valuable experience and skills. Gain experience in youth work, mental health, and community engagement.\r\n•\tBe part of an inclusive, passionate and supportive team.\r\n•\tHelp build a brighter future for the next generation.\r\n\r\n*Location: Opportunities available in Aberdeen, across Scotland, and remotely.\r\n\r\n*Interested? Get in touch today!\r\nEmail: info@faceyouth.org\r\nPhone: 07526188267\r\n\r\nTogether, we can change lives—one young person at a time\n\n## Description\n\n*Join FACEYOUTH and Make a Difference!\r\nFACEYOUTH—a grassroots-inspired charitable organisation dedicated to improving the lives of disadvantaged children and youth in Aberdeen and beyond, through mental health programs, educational initiatives, and community outreach.\r\n\r\n*About this Opportunity\r\nA Lifeline for Those Who Need It Most\r\n\r\nAt FACEYOUTH, we are committed to supporting disadvantaged children and youth, ensuring they have access to the mental wellbeing support, resources, and opportunities they need to thrive. While we work closely with children from ethnic minority and refugee communities, our services are not limited to them—we support all children and young people facing challenges, regardless of their background.\r\n\r\nTo continue making a meaningful impact, we need passionate volunteers to join us. Whether you have a few hours to spare or are looking for a deeper commitment, we welcome your support. We Need Volunteers Like You!  We are seeking enthusiastic individuals to support our work in various roles, including:\r\n\r\n•\tYouth Mentors & Well-being Champions – Provide guidance and emotional support to young people.\r\n•\tEvent & Fundraising Assistants – Help us organise impactful community events and fundraising initiatives.\r\n•\t Social Media & Marketing Volunteers – Raise awareness and promote our cause online.\r\n•\tAdmin & Project Support – Assist with behind-the-scenes operations to keep our programs running smoothly.\r\n•\tEducation & Skills Trainers – Share your knowledge and help young people develop valuable life skills.\r\n\r\nThis is an opportunity to be part of a growing movement that ensures no young person is left behind. We believe every child deserves access to mental health support, education, and a strong community to uplift them.\r\n\r\n*Why Volunteer with FACEYOUTH?\r\n•\t Make a real difference in the lives of vulnerable children and youth. Develop new skills while making a meaningful contribution\r\n•\tGain valuable experience and skills. Gain experience in youth work, mental health, and community engagement.\r\n•\tBe part of an inclusive, passionate and supportive team.\r\n•\tHelp build a brighter future for the next generation.\r\n\r\n*Location: Opportunities available in Aberdeen, across Scotland, and remotely.\r\n\r\n*Interested? Get in touch today!\r\nEmail: info@faceyouth.org\r\nPhone: 07526188267\r\n\r\nTogether, we can change lives—one young person at a time\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and any relevant training is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to suit volunteers. All help is greatly appreciated.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F172caf63-bd48-45e5-aeee-32f260218576%2Ff5ZmTHJqJCejjF9I14kHWhOMp0A2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=dbf8f91e-55a5-4e7b-ab0c-00a2ee72e69d",
