            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ILwEsYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ILwEsYAL/police-scotland-adult-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-05",
                    "title": "Police Scotland Adult Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nPolice Scotland Youth Volunteers are a group of local young people aged 13-18 who are led by a police officer and supported by 3 school link police officers and civilian adult volunteers. The role of the Adult Volunteer is vital to keep the group running. We meet each Friday afternoon in the Musselburgh area from 1430-1630 and we do team building, drill, and learn about policing and confidence building. We also volunteer at local and national events, such as gala days, festivals, and the Edinburgh Military Tattoo. There are also visits to the Scottish Police College for events along with other PSYV groups.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCommitment Flexible 3 Hours, Weekly",
