            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000014fAlRAAU/debra-shop-stockbridge",
            "name": "DebRA Shop - Stockbridge",
            "description": "To provide funds for research and welfare for the condition Epidermolysis Bullosa (E.B) and it's sufferers.",
            "website": "http://www.debra.org.uk/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FundraisingFunding",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Fundraising / Funding"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000MdI2pAAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000MdI2pAAF/shop-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2020-01-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Shop Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nUnleash  your potential and become a DEBRA Volunteer today. Support the EB Community.\nBoosting your confidence and self-esteem. Making new friends and forging strong links with your local community.\nGaining meaningful experience to enhance your CV and career prospects. Training and flexible working hours.\n\n## Description\n\nThe is a varied role and could include lifting heavy furniture and electrical items, electrical testing ( testing our donated electrical items to make sure they work), customer service, helping to keep the shop spick and span,\nmaking our donated stock and shop floor clean and presentable, handyperson tasks (includes assembling and dismantling as necessary, occasional repair work), helping with rotation of stock, pricing, operating the till and visual merchandiser tasks such as creating displays.\n\n## Experience required\n\nShop retail or charity shop experience an advantage, but training will given.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will be issued within an induction pack to complete on all aspects of working in charity shop.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDEBRA, 35a High Street, South Queensferry EH30 9HW\nDEBRA, 15 Deanhaugh Street, Stockbridge, EH4 1LU\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
