                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GL5czYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GL5czYAD/peoples-experience-volunteer-lewis",
                    "publishStart": "2026-04-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-26",
                    "title": "People's Experience Volunteer (Lewis)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nPeople's Experience volunteer (PEVs) provide views, experience, opinions and challenge on issues that HIS has identified as priorities or areas of focus important to health and care in Scotland. \r\nPEVs may be involved in both regional and national projects, depending on the scope of activity.\r\nYou may be invited to share your views on various topics, review materials to ensure they are clear and accessible. or use your local knowledge to help shape engagement strategies.\r\nYou can give your time for as little or as much as you wish.  How you take part may vary depending on the activity and your personal circumstances.  Activities are usually online but occasionally may be by telephone or face to face.  The role is highly flexible and suited to individuals with varying availability.  Your contributions are  flexible and focused on shorter term projects and feedback.  All your feedback will be anonymous and we will make sure it isn't shared in a way that could identify you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo specific skills, just an interest in making health and care better for everyone.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThis role is flexible and you can give as little or as much time as you wish.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GL5czYAD#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "People's Experience Volunteer (Lewis)",
                        "description": "No specific skills, just an interest in making health and care better for everyone.",
                        "commitment": "This role is flexible and you can give as little or as much time as you wish.",
