        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000fotXzYAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000fotXzYAI/woolfords-auchengray-tarbrax-improvement-foundation-wat-if",
            "name": "Woolfords Auchengray Tarbrax improvement Foundation (WAT IF)",
            "description": "WATIF (Woolfords, Auchengray and Tarbrax Improvement Foundation) is a charitable community development trust established in 2011 based in rural Clydesdale on the border of South Lanarkshire and West Lothian. Our vision is of a beautiful and vibrant place, with a great quality of life for all.\n\nOur strategic objectives are:\n\nTo support local sustainable economic, environmental, and social development\nTo own well managed, financially sustainable land and buildings\nDue to our location, we face many challenges, and after over 12 years of consulting with our community we have a clear direction for our work going forward. We have had many successes including community transport, community broadband, housing, paths, our local grant schemes, and numerous successful community projects/activities. We continue to regularly consult with our community through our social impact work.\n\nWe currently receive regular community benefit income from six local windfarms and apply to external grant sources also to support our work programmes. Thanks to funding from the Scottish Land Fund in September 2023 we purchased Loanhead Farm, which includes a farmhouse, a range of outbuildings and 20 acres of land. The community ownership of this asset, along with our six work programmes and projects, can help to address many of our unmet needs and aspirations long-term.\n\nWe can’t do what we do without or fantastic staff team and all our wonderful volunteers, led by our team of 9 trustees who themselves all volunteer their time to make our vision a reality.",
            "website": "https://www.watif.scot/index.html",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC043606"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GQtNqYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GQtNqYAL/outdoors-growing-gardening",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Outdoors - Growing & Gardening",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe’re looking for volunteers to get involved in our gardening work at WATIF. \n\nThis is a hands-on role supporting the upkeep of our outdoor spaces - from planting and general maintenance to helping keep paths and shared areas tidy. \n\nThere’s also the chance to get involved in growing, including raising seedlings and working in our polytunnel to produce fruit and vegetables for the kitchen and wider community. \n\nSome tasks may include using equipment such as a ride-on mower, with full training provided. It’s a practical, outdoor opportunity where you can pick up new skills, be part of a team and contribute to something that directly benefits local people.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,Creative,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Organised,\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire Yes\nAcross South Lanarkshire,Tarbrax",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GQtNqYAL#role",
