        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000g96cHYAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000g96cHYAQ/citizens-advice-bureau-clydesdale",
            "name": "Citizens Advice Bureau (Clydesdale)",
            "description": "Clydesdale Citizens Advice Bureau works closely within the local community to meet local people's needs, offering free and impartial advice on financial or legal problems.\nThey provide a generalist advice service on all areas of civil law as they apply to Scotland including advice on: benefits, debt, employment, finances, relationships, housing, health, tax, travel and utilities.\nOpening hours:\nMonday - Thursday 9:30am - 12:30pm",
            "website": "https://www.clydesdalecab.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC017611"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000B6WA9YAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000B6WA9YAN/generalist-adviser",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-04",
                    "title": "Generalist Adviser",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are looking for new volunteers to join our wonderful team. This unique roles is providing a holistic, free and impartial advice service to our local residents. We are looking for someone who has the time and the commitment to learn. The roles includes interviewing clients, negotiating on behalf of clients, interpreting and communicating information to clients to help them make informed decisions and completing clear case records. \nThe training takes approx. 8-12 weeks adn we look for 1 full day per week proving advice once training is completed.\n\n## Experience required\n\nComputer / IT / Web, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Hard Working,Open minded,Organised,Patient,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Social Conscience,Team Player,Trustworthy,non-judgemental and impartial\n\n## Training details\n\nDue to the nature of the role, continuous training is required.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire\n\n## Travel expenses\n\ntravel expenses paid monthly in arrears",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
