        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000gabx2YAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000gabx2YAA/picts-poverty-intervention-charity-transforming-scotland",
            "name": "PICTS (Poverty Intervention Charity Transforming Scotland)",
            "description": "Knights Templar Goodwill Charity of Scotland is dedicated to supporting some of the most vulnerable in society, including veterans, individuals experiencing homelessness, people living in poverty, and those affected by mental health issues or social isolation. They offer a wide range of practical and emotional support through their welcoming community hub.",
            "website": "http://www.picts.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC051727"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Poverty",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Poverty"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SelfHelpSupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Self-Help / Support"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BGAmfYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BGAmfYAH/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-27",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nPICTS is dedicated to alleviating poverty and assisting those in need in Scotland by providing essential care packages, food, clothing and long-term support for veterans, homeless and those living in poverty.\r\n\r\nThey require two trustees to join their Board and share their skills and expertise to support the charity’s mission and aims. The trustees must live in Cowdenbeath or the surrounding area to meet funding requirements. The trustees will attend monthly face to face board meetings and ad hoc meetings such as the AGM.\r\n\r\nAs a trustee you will contribute to the strategic direction of the organisation, ensure the charity is meeting its financial and legal obligations, review Board reports and take responsibility for the leadership and management of the organisation.\r\n\r\nAll trustees are expected to take on additional duties when required. This could include a shift at the community hub.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThis role is suitable for anyone interested in the aims of the charity. Some experience would be desirable but is not essential. Good communication, interpersonal and decision-making skills are required and the ability to work well as part of a team.\n\n## Training details\n\nAn induction to the role will be provided and ongoing training and support will also be provided. The volunteer will have the opportunity to attend training relating to the roles and responsibilities of a trustee.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoard meetings are held on the last Wednesday or Thursday of every month on site at 12 Thistle Street, Cowdenbeath which is accessible by private and public transport. Meetings last between 2 – 3 hours\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReimbursement of travel expenses will be discussed on an individual basis.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
