        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000gc3ftYAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000gc3ftYAA/opeka",
            "name": "Opeka",
            "description": "OPEKA is deeply committed to empowering adults with additional support needs, ensuring they can lead fulfilling lives marked by security, dignity and respect.",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IStVUYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IStVUYA1/volunteer-driver",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-12",
                    "title": "Volunteer Driver",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are looking for a friendly, reliable and caring Volunteer Driver to join our team and help our participants get safely to and from our groups at the Carswell Centre in Eaglesham.\r\n\r\nFor some of the people we support, having reliable transport is essential to being able to attend our groups.  By volunteering as a driver, you'll be helping make sure our participants can access the activities and social opportunities they enjoy.\r\n\r\nYou will drive OPEKA's 9-seater vehicle, collecting participants from their homes and bringing them safely to the Carswell Centre.  At the end of the session, you will then transport participants home.\r\n\r\nThe regular hours are approximately 12.5 hours per week:\r\nWednesday: 12-3.30 pm\r\nThursday: 11.30 am - 4 pm\r\nFriday: 11.30 am – 4 pm\r\n\r\nYou must hold a full UK driving licence suitable for driving the vehicle and be a confident and responsible driver.\r\n\r\nPVG Scheme membership will be required for this role.  OPEKA will support the successful applicant with the necessary PVG process if required.  You must be comfortable transporting and supporting adults with additional support needs.\r\n\r\nAs OPEKA continues to grow, there may be opportunities for paid employment in the future, subject to funding becoming available and the needs of the charity.\r\n\r\nWhile volunteering does not guarantee future employment, we would be particularly interested in hearing from people who may be interested in developing their involvement with OPEKA over time.\r\n\r\nWe are ideally looking for someone who can regularly commit to Wednesday, Thursday and Friday.\r\n\r\nWe appreciate that 12.5 hours across three days is a significant volunteering commitment.  If you cannot commit to all three days but could regularly support us on one or two days, we would still love to hear from you.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCarswell Centre, Montgomery Street, Eaglesham, G76 0AS.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F99dc6a4b-e88a-48b8-8c4c-26c964cd0259%2FRFK1o96cbScBpCWmAYh5ZmyJ9Yx1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=0e7e67b3-513e-4c53-82fc-fee3bd28aa08",
