            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I2YknYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I2YknYAF/clothing-bank-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-19",
                    "title": "Clothing Bank Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Hive Kirkcaldy is a community hub providing vital support services and a safe and affirmative place.\r\n\r\nClothing Bank Assistants are needed to help The Hive Kirkcaldy provide individuals and families with access to good-quality clothing, footwear, toiletries and household essentials in a welcoming, respectful and non-judgemental environment.\r\n\r\nThe volunteer will welcome visitors, volunteers and referral partners in a friendly and respectful manner.\r\nKey tasks include sorting donated clothing, footwear, toiletries and household items, checking donated items are clean, safe and in good condition, organising clothing and other items by size, age and category, preparing clothing and essentials packs using referral forms, assisting with stock rotation, storage and stock records, helping to maintain a clean, safe and well-organised Clothing Bank and reporting damaged items, hazards or concerns to a member of staff.\r\n\r\nIf you want to make a difference in your local community this may be the role for you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience is required. Full training and ongoing support will be provided.\r\n\r\nFriendly, approachable, non-judgemental, compassionate and sensitive to the needs of others\r\n\r\nReliable, punctual and organized with the ability to follow processes.\r\n\r\nAble to work independently and as part of a team, carrying out light physical tasks such as lifting donation bags/boxes and stand for long periods.\r\n\r\nRespectful of confidentiality and personal information.\n\n## Training details\n\nA Volunteer induction and ongoing support. Training will include - health and safety; manual handling; equality, diversity and inclusion; safeguarding; confidentiality and GDPR; customer service; and fire safety.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Hive Kirkcaldy is located at 10 Whytescauseway, Kirkcaldy which is accessible by car and public transport.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe look on this on an individual basis",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
