        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000gu8MAYAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000gu8MAYAY/parents-for-future-scotland-aberdeen",
            "name": "Parents for Future Scotland Aberdeen",
            "description": "As parents and carers, we’re worried about climate change, the cost of living and social justice. We seek to offer mutual support and influence actions that change things for the better – in our school communities and beyond, with an emphasis on empowering communities whose voices are least often heard.  We also advocate for transformative policies to urgently protect life on Earth, give us clean air to breathe, and secure a happy and climate-safe world for all children and future generations.",
            "website": "https://www.parentsforfuturescotland.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC053173"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EnvironmentRecycling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Environment / Recycling"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BNYnRYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BNYnRYAX/parents-for-future-scotland-aberdeen-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Parents for Future Scotland Aberdeen Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nJoin the Movement for a Liveable Future or This isn’t just volunteering it’s legacy-building. \r\n\r\nAre you looking to volunteer for a cause that matters not just now, but for generations to come?\r\n\r\nParents for Future Scotland is calling on changemakers, caretakers, educators, and everyday heroes to join our grassroots climate movement. Whether you're a parent, grandparent, student, or simply someone who cares deeply about protecting our planet, your voice belongs here.\r\n\r\nFrom storytelling to campaigning, creative projects to community events, there’s space for every skill and every passion. No experience needed, just your willingness to stand up for climate justice and a better world for our children.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference for people, the community and our planet. For more details, please contact Sahar Abdulla,  Project Lead at email saharparentsforfuturescotland@gmail.com or telephone: 07435026497.\n\n## Description\n\nJoin the Movement for a Liveable Future or This isn’t just volunteering it’s legacy-building. \r\n\r\nAre you looking to volunteer for a cause that matters not just now, but for generations to come?\r\n\r\nParents for Future Scotland is calling on changemakers, caretakers, educators, and everyday heroes to join our grassroots climate movement. Whether you're a parent, grandparent, student, or simply someone who cares deeply about protecting our planet, your voice belongs here.\r\n\r\nFrom storytelling to campaigning, creative projects to community events, there’s space for every skill and every passion. No experience needed, just your willingness to stand up for climate justice and a better world for our children. Flexible times to volunteer-all help greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference for people, the community and our planet. For more details, please contact Sahar Abdulla,  Project Lead at email saharparentsforfuturescotland@gmail.com or telephone: 07435026497.\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant guidance and excellent support is provided to all volunteers.  Includes a high level of introduction to the charity and its work across Scotland and in Aberdeen.\r\n\r\nPotential training on few social media applications like Canva and other community training.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times to volunteer-all help greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nIn Aberdeen and online",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Feb4143b2-ddc8-47b7-b636-896be786fdc1%2Fm0xxJ3UJUJXbnqmGngt3RD8BTvI2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=aad66051-bfdf-4577-a200-a8bd29d70d8a",
                    "role": {
