                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FundraisingFunding",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Fundraising / Funding"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEngagement",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Engagement"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ILFXxYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ILFXxYAP/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-05",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\n‘Give a Dog a Bone… and an animal a home’ seek to expand their Board members, to support future growth.\n\n## Description\n\n‘Give a Dog a Bone… and an animal a home’ is a registered charity, founded in 2013.  They seek to expand their Board members, to support future growth. They are a unique and award-winning charity, tackling loneliness for older adults via animal companionship and friendship.\r\n\r\nTo meet their aims, they offer two projects:\r\n\r\nFinancial support to the over 60s to adopt a rescue pet companion.  It’s a WIN/WIN – the person gets a friend, and the animal gets a home.\r\n\r\n‘Companionship in the Community’ operating four community spaces in Scotland: Shawlands, Troon, Alloa and Dunfermline, which provide older adults a safe space to make new friends, learn new skills and mix with our special team of Companionship Dogs.\r\n\r\nThey are looking for our Trustees to make active and insightful contributions to the Board, using their wide-ranging skills, knowledge and experience, to ensure good governance and the development of future strategy.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThey are looking for someone who is passionate about the purpose and goals of Give a Dog a Bone and can demonstrate their commitment and support, has objective judgement and a willingness to speak to their mind, can give adequate time, thought and energy to the role and will act as an ambassador for Give a Dog a Bone. Skills in the areas of either Fundraising and IT are desirable.\n\n## Training details\n\nThey will provide information on the roles and responsibilities of Trustee.  This is an open and transparent group and support will be provided.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMeetings will take place at their Glasgow City Centre office and/or via Zoom.  Trustees are responsible for their own travel arrangements, out of pocket expenses can be reimbursed.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThey reimburse public transport rates within 7 days of meeting taking place.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ILFXxYAP#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Trustee",
                        "description": "They are looking for someone who is passionate about the purpose and goals of Give a Dog a Bone and can demonstrate their commitment and support, has objective judgement and a willingness to speak to their mind, can give adequate time, thought and energy to the role and will act as an ambassador for Give a Dog a Bone. Skills in the areas of either Fundraising and IT are desirable.",
