        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000hNbm7YAC",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000hNbm7YAC/brechin-and-edzell-girlguiding",
            "name": "Brechin and Edzell Girlguiding",
            "website": "https://www.girlguiding.org.uk/get-involved/become-a-volunteer/",
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2Ff40abba7-2f18-4e0e-b333-e4475b8625bb%2FAGGDoBIya9c8SYitlOjP1PmfFRL2%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=5bf53bdc-bb1e-4cab-b2fa-1e30f4e8a0c6",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BXImDYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BXImDYAX/unit-leaderassistant-leaders-and-young-leaders",
                    "publishStart": "2025-08-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-12",
                    "title": "Unit Leader/Assistant Leaders and Young Leaders",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nA creative, fun and inspiring role running units (groups) for:\r\n\r\nRainbows (aged 4-7), Brownies (aged 7-10), Guides (aged 10-14) and Rangers (14-18).\r\n\r\nWe have units across the Brechin and Edzell, so there is flexibility for the individual in location. Meetings occur throughout school term time.\n\n## Description\n\nA creative, fun and inspiring role running units (groups) for:\r\n\r\nRainbows (aged 4-7), Brownies (aged 7-10), Guides (aged 10-14) and Rangers (14-18).\r\n\r\nWe have units across the Brechin and Edzell, so there is flexibility for the individual in location. Meetings occur throughout school term time.\r\n\r\nKey activities include:\r\n• Working as a team/leading a team\r\n• Organising age-appropriate activities\r\n• Managing records\r\n• Managing the units' accounts\r\n\r\nThere are all sorts of roles to suit different availabilities, time commitments and skill sets :\r\n\r\nhttps://www.girlguiding.org.uk/get-involved/become-a-volunteer/\r\nVolunteers will develop teamwork and leadership skills, enhance their organisational abilities, and have the opportunity to make new friends while gaining valuable experiences and skills.\r\n\r\nVolunteers are asked to commit a few hours each week during school term time. Units typically meet on various days, usually in the evening, providing flexibility for participants.\n\n## Experience required\n\nOrganisation, team working, creative, fun and inspiring. We are open to anyone who has their own expertise they can bring to the role, such as arts, outdoors\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training, including safeguarding, first aid and age-appropriate training to the Girlguiding programme.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F1909a6ce-8a10-4303-b535-a7f1b0f2fc60%2FAGGDoBIya9c8SYitlOjP1PmfFRL2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=a3ceff09-4e93-4146-8854-e3c4adaa72fe",
