        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000aHdUrYAK",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000aHdUrYAK/biggar-youth-project-scio",
            "name": "Biggar Youth Project SCIO",
            "description": "Biggar Youth Project is dedicated to providing a range of activities for young people aged 11 to 18 living within the catchment area of Biggar High School.\nTerm-time schedule:\n•\tMonday to Thursday, 1 – 2 pm: Healthy snacks and a relaxing space during school lunchtimes.\n•\tFriday, 1:45 – 8pm: A place for young people to unwind at the end of the week including food and sessions. \n•\tMonday to Thursday, 11 am – 6pm: Community Fridge in partnership with Biggar Co-op.\n•\tMonday to Thursday, 3.45-6pm : Sessions and fun activities.",
            "website": "https://www.biggaryouthproject.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC051582"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009SoJFYA0",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009SoJFYA0/youth-work",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-05",
                    "title": "Youth Work",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCould you make a real difference in a young person’s life?\nDo you have a few hours to spare each week to share a hobby or just hang out with someone aged 11–18?\nBiggar Youth Project is looking for Volunteer Youth Workers to support young people in our local community.\nWhether it’s chatting over a game of table tennis, getting involved in creative activities, helping at lunchtime with meals — your time and presence can make a huge impact.\n\nWith rising levels of social isolation, poverty, and inequality, young people need positive role models now more than ever.\nAs a Volunteer Youth Worker, you’ll:\n• Be a consistent, encouraging adult in a young person’s life\n• Share your hobbies, interests, and time\n• Help them build confidence and try new things\n• Support them to feel more connected to their community\n• Make a meaningful difference — all in just a few hours a week\nIf you're passionate about supporting young people and giving back locally, we’d love to hear from you.\nContact us  to learn more or to get involved.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,Good Listener,Open minded,Organised,Patient,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Social Conscience,Team Player,\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire,Biggar",
