                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hul5hYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hul5hYAB/trustee-chairperson",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-01",
                    "title": "Trustee Chairperson",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nBiggar Youth Project SCIO is seeking an enthusiastic, committed and community-minded Chairperson to lead our Board of Trustees and help shape the future of our organisation.\n\nEstablished in 1996, Biggar Youth Project supports young people aged 10-18 across Biggar and surrounding rural communities, promoting wellbeing, inclusion, confidence and positive life opportunities through youth work and support services.\n\nThis is an exciting opportunity for someone with leadership, governance, business, community or professional experience who wants to use their skills to support a respected local charity making a real difference in young people's lives.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nAs Chairperson, you will provide leadership to the Board of Trustees and act as the primary governance support for the Head of Operations. You will help ensure that Biggar Youth Project remains well governed, financially sustainable and focused on delivering positive outcomes for young people across our communities.\n\nYou will work collaboratively with fellow trustees and staff to support the charity's strategic direction, oversee good governance and act as an ambassador for the organisation within the community.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nAs Chairperson, you will:\n\nLead and facilitate Board meetings.\nEnsure the Board operates effectively and fulfils its governance responsibilities.\nSupport strategic planning and the long-term development of the charity.\nWork closely with the Treasurer and fellow trustees to ensure strong financial oversight and governance.\nEncourage constructive discussion and effective decision-making.\nEnsure trustees receive appropriate information to make informed decisions.\nSupport compliance with charity governance requirements and OSCR expectations.\nRepresent and promote Biggar Youth Project within the local community and with partners, funders and stakeholders.\nFoster a positive, inclusive and collaborative Board culture.\nSupport the Head of Operations\n\nA key part of this role is providing support to the Head of Operations.\n\nYou will:\n\nMeet with the Head of Operations on a monthly basis to provide support and guidance.\nAct as a sounding board for opportunities, challenges and strategic issues.\nMaintain an understanding of the charity's activities, priorities and challenges.\nSupport the wellbeing, development and effectiveness of the Head of Operations.\nEnsure good communication between the Board and staff team.\nHelp identify strategic priorities, risks and opportunities while maintaining the distinction between governance and day-to-day operations.\nWe're Looking For Someone Who\nIs passionate about supporting young people.\nHas excellent communication and listening skills.\nCan lead meetings confidently, fairly and effectively.\nDemonstrates integrity, sound judgement and commitment.\nEnjoys working collaboratively with trustees, staff and stakeholders.\nCan think strategically and help guide the organisation's future development.\n\n\nPrevious trustee experience is desirable but not essential. Training and support will be provided.\n\nTime Commitment\n\nThe time commitment is variable, but typically around 6-8 hours per month and includes:\n\nAttendance at Board meetings (approximately 4-6 per year).\nA monthly support meeting with the Head of Operations.\nOccasional meetings with trustees, staff, funders and community partners.\nParticipation in strategic planning and governance activities.\n\nMeetings may take place online, in person, or a combination of both.\n\n\nThis role offers the opportunity to:\n\nMake a meaningful difference to the lives of local young people.\nLead and support a respected community charity.\nDevelop valuable governance and leadership experience.\nWork alongside a dedicated and passionate Board and staff team.\nHelp shape the future of youth services within rural communities.\n\nReasonable out-of-pocket expenses can be reimbursed. As a small local charity, our financial resources are limited, but we are committed to ensuring volunteers are not left out of pocket.\n\nAbout Biggar Youth Project\n\nBiggar Youth Project SCIO provides youth work, wellbeing support and community engagement opportunities for young people across Biggar and the surrounding area. We help young people navigate important life transitions and provide a safe, welcoming environment where they can build confidence, develop skills and access support when needed.\n\nFor more information, visit: www.biggaryouthproject.org.uk\n\nAdditional Information\n\nBiggar Youth Project SCIO is committed to equality, diversity and inclusion and welcomes applications from people of all backgrounds.\n\nTrustees are required to act in the best interests of the charity and fulfil the duties of charity trustees under Scottish charity law.\n\nThe successful applicant will be required to join the PVG Scheme and comply with the charity's safeguarding procedures.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Good Communicator,Good Listener,Open minded,Organised,Team Player,\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable expenses can be claimed. Although Biggar Youth Project is a small charity with limited resources, we are committed to supporting our volunteers and ensuring they are not out of pocket for approved volunteering costs.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hul5hYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
