        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000bQ5OXYA0",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000bQ5OXYA0/the-turing-trust-east-lothian",
            "name": "The Turing Trust (East Lothian)",
            "description": "Founded by Alan Turing’s Family, The Turing Trust works to improve education in Africa and the UK by providing schools with refurbished computers and IT training. By volunteering with us, you’ll play a key role in bridging the digital divide, providing young people with the tools and skills they need to succeed in today’s tech-centered world. By supporting our efforts, you’ll help open doors to education, digital literacy, and a brighter future for many.",
            "website": "https://turingtrust.co.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC046150"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EducationLearningTraining",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Education / Learning / Training"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000DW3UjYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000DW3UjYAL/it-refurbishment",
                    "publishStart": "2025-09-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-11",
                    "title": "IT refurbishment",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nJoin the Turing Trust as a Volunteer and Make a Difference!\r\nAre you passionate about IT and eager to make a lasting impact on education? Do you want to help bridge the digital divide and empower communities through access to technology? The Turing Trust is looking for enthusiastic volunteers to join our mission of improving education through the distribution of computers in schools and communities in Africa. Join our mission to provide refurbished computers and IT training to those who need it most, and empower the next generation of learners.\r\nVolunteering with The Turing Trust is an opportunity to try something new, learn new skills, and meet new people. Our volunteers come from a wide range of backgrounds and all have different skill sets. Collectively, the incredible contributions of all our volunteers is what enables us to create new opportunities for IT-supported learning in schools.\r\nWhat We Do: Founded by Alan Turing’s Family, The Turing Trust works to improve education in Africa and the UK by providing schools with refurbished computers and IT training. By volunteering with us, you’ll play a key role in bridging the digital divide, providing young people with the tools and skills they need to succeed in today’s tech-centered world. By supporting our efforts, you’ll help open doors to education, digital literacy, and a brighter future for many.\r\n\r\nVolunteer Roles Available:\r\nHelp us refurbish donated computers to ensure they meet high-quality standards for distribution.\r\nProvide technical support, advice, and training for our team, partners and recipients.\r\nWarehouse\r\nWhy Volunteer with Us?\r\nGain valuable experience in a growing non-profit sector.\r\nGain hands-on experience in IT refurbishment and technical support.\r\nHelp provide essential digital resources to schools and communities that lack access to technology.\r\nMake a tangible impact in the lives of young people across the world.\r\nJoin a passionate, supportive team and work in a friendly environment.\r\nAccess training and development opportunities to expand your skills.\r\nLearn new skills, from computer refurbishment to data management, and enhance your IT experience for your career.\r\nSkills & Requirements:\r\nA passion for education, technology, and social impact.\r\nNo prior experience needed, though technical skills or experience with fundraising and event planning are a bonus.\r\nA willingness to contribute your time and skills to our mission.\r\nFlexibility and enthusiasm to work with a diverse group of people.",
