        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000FPf95YAD",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000FPf95YAD/avenue-confidential",
            "name": "Avenue Confidential",
            "description": "Avenue is an Aberdeen based charity dedicated to providing comprehensive support services to families and individuals across the North-East of Scotland, with a focus on relationships, wellbeing, and children. Avenue supports people in Aberdeen City, Aberdeenshire, and Morayshire, occupying two sites with a large team offering a range of expertise.",
            "website": "https://avenuecharity.org/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC200545"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Counselling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Counselling"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000003e8ErYAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000003e8ErYAI/volunteer-charitylog-guru-data-systems-support",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer Charitylog Guru (Data Systems Support)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAvenue is looking for someone who has extensive expertise with our CRM system Charitylog, to help us navigate some improvements to data capturing processes, and crucially, help produce accurate reports. \r\n\r\nIf you know your way around Charitylog like you designed it, and you're a black-belt in Excel - We want to hear from you!!\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Cliff Watt,  CEO at email: c.watt@avenuecharity.org or telephone:  01224 587571.\n\n## Description\n\nAvenue is looking for someone who has extensive expertise with our CRM system Charitylog, to help us navigate some improvements to data capturing processes, and crucially, help produce accurate reports. \r\n\r\nIf you know your way around Charitylog like you designed it, and you're a black-belt in Excel - We want to hear from you!!\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Cliff Watt,  CEO at email: c.watt@avenuecharity.org or telephone:  01224 587571.\n\n## Experience required\n\nExtensive experience with CRM data management, particularly Charitylog\r\nExtensive experience with Excel data analysis functions\r\nGood understanding of how data helps with organisational management\r\nPractical problem solving skills\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. We will provide a broad-based induction process for volunteers that will give them a chance to get to know the organisation, and our team. \r\nFor this volunteering opportunity, we really need the volunteer to bring the relevant skills and knowledge with them, but there may be opportunities for some additional training if needed. \r\nRegular volunteering catch-ups will be available throughout this volunteering opportunity\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to volunteer. All help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAvenue is based in Aberdeen City Centre and we think this opportunity would be best delivered from our offices, but we're flexible, and open to working around what fits best for volunteers\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAs this role is predominantly digital, the volunteer can be entirely home-based and volunteer as and when they have time, if that would help with accessibility. \r\nAvenue pay reasonable out-of-pocket expenses for volunteers.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
