                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-07",
                    "title": "Community Garden Helper",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDuloch Community Garden runs a community garden in Duloch Park with flowers, vegetables and a fairy garden. Run entirely by volunteers, the group maintains an area of the park and provides a social space for people to get into nature and learn about gardening. Alongside other local groups, they have a shipping container hub that volunteers can use.\r\nThey are looking for Community Garden Volunteers. As a volunteer, you can get involved in tasks such as planting seeds, plants and bulbs; turning over compost; spreading bark; watering; weeding; strimming and mowing; pruning; sweeping; and other activities within the garden. You can also help to clean equipment after use and keep the hub clean.\r\nIf you would like to get outdoors, connect with others, and improve your gardening skills, while volunteering in a flexible role, this could be the perfect opportunity for you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers should be enthusiastic and positive. Gardening experience is helpful but not required as training will be offered.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive training to do all tasks, and support will be available from more senior volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDuloch Community Gardens are situated within Duloch Park, Nightingale Road, KY11 8LW.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses will be discussed on a case by case basis.\n\n## Taster details\n\nTaster sessions are encouraged within the garden.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
