        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000FudkmYAB",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000FudkmYAB/polmont-sports-centre-community-group",
            "name": "Polmont Sports Centre Community Group",
            "description": "Polmont Sports Centre is a community group planning to take over the running of Polmont Sports Centre in order to keep the centre open for the benefit of local residents. Entirely volunteer-led, the committee and volunteers are passionate about ensuring the Centre continues to operate.\r\nLocated next to Meadowbank Library, Polmont Sports Centre has a wide range of facilities available to book., including:\r\n\r\n5 a side football\r\ngames hall\r\nbadminton\r\nbasketball\r\nshort tennis\r\nWe also have a fitness room with a mixture of aerobic equipment and weights and a squash court.",
            "website": "https://www.polmontsportscentre.com/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC054374"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ASFCrYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ASFCrYAP/diy-maintenance",
                    "publishStart": "2025-06-19",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-16",
                    "title": "DIY & Maintenance",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur community group is preparing to take over the running of Polmont Sports Centre in order to keep the Centre open for the benefit of local residents. Entirely volunteer-led, the committee are passionate about ensuring the Centre continues to operate but more volunteers are needed who will be able to support its day-to-day running. \r\n\r\nWe are looking for a committed individual who could carry out small DIY type repairs and maintenance to help maintain the internal and external fabric of the building. Tasks might include:\r\n- painting\r\n- simple repairs\r\n- grass cutting\r\n\r\nBut these will vary depending on need and will generally include odd jobs. It might also include providing advice on larger maintenance and renovation work that ought to be carried out or is planned for the future. \r\n\r\nThis is an ad hoc and varied role that would fit the volunteer's schedule, and all help is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nWe welcome applicants from refugees, the disabled community, those with mental health issues, ethnic minority groups, older people and young unemployed people and can offer recognised training courses with qualifications and support you on your volunteering journey.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGeneral domestic DIY skills preferred – including painting & decorating, gardening, woodwork, electrical, plumbing, etc. \r\n\r\nA willingness to share and develop skills would also be beneficial.\n\n## Training details\n\nA full induction to the organisation and building will be provided, and training needs will be discussed with the Board.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThis is an ad hoc role that can take place to suit the volunteer.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nNo expenses paid",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F92d63d49-fe91-4929-a020-26d7b2ba81cf%2FXPrpz4zVmiRWRuGPAUiQ4SyLdVd2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=4edccb18-1370-4b24-bc86-c3646db12682",
