        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000MnyIsYAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000MnyIsYAJ/childrens-hearings-scotland",
            "name": "Children's Hearings Scotland",
            "description": "Children’s Hearings Scotland (CHS) is a public body that recruits, trains and supports around 2,500 volunteers across Scotland. Also referred to as the Children's Panel, CHS consists of Regional Area Support Teams which are key to the Children’s Hearings System. This system is Scotland’s care and justice system which makes sure that infants, children and young people are safe and cared for. Please see the CHS website for further information on the different volunteer roles available.",
            "website": "https://www.chscotland.gov.uk/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FW917YAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FW917YAD/panel-practice-adviser",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-04",
                    "title": "Panel Practice Adviser",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nChildren’s Hearings Scotland is recruiting volunteer Panel Practice Advisers!   \n\nChildren’s Hearings Scotland in South Lanarkshire is looking for people who have good assessment, observation, and communication skills to join our team as a Panel Practice Adviser.  \n\nWhat will you be doing?  \n\nPanel Practice Advisers are responsible for the quality assurance and they regularly observe Panel Members within children's hearings and feedback so improvements can be made.  They are also part of the recruitment and selection of new Panel Members while conducting Panel Members re-appointment reviews. Their goal is to support Panel Members through feedback to ensure the strongest possible decisions are being made for children and young people.  \n\nWho are we looking for?  \nYou’ll be enthusiastic and committed to securing the rights of children and young people and improving their outcomes and experiences; able to lead and be part of a team; a strong communicator. You should also be familiar with working with volunteers and be able to demonstrate a strong commitment to and understanding of the ethos of Children’s Hearings Scotland.  \nTo find out more about the role, please visit our web site\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,Good Communicator,Open minded,Organised,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Panel Practice Advisers bring the same strong commitment as our Panel Members  to our values - challenging, child-centred, creative, respectful fair and open. Above all, you must care about the welfare of infants, children and young people and to helping us achieve the best possible outcomes for the\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training is provided, with the aim to enhance your skills in: leadership, effective communication, managing conflict and influencing and negotiating – all of which are transferable into the workplace.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire Yes\nAcross South Lanarkshire,Hamilton,Lanark",
