            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FzEAIYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FzEAIYA3/fundraiser",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-20",
                    "title": "Fundraiser",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nOliver's Army are looking for a fundraiser to join their busy training centre in Lochgelly\n\n## Description\n\nOliver's Army Assistance and Therapy Dogs is a charity that helps people to train their own dog to become a fully qualified assistance or therapy dog. They offer structured weekly classes and connect dog owners with a supportive community. They support a diverse range of disabilities — from Autism and PTSD to MS, Arthritis, ADHD, Seizure Disorders, Chronic Pain, and more.\r\n\r\nOliver's Army are looking for a fundraiser to join their busy training centre. They are looking for a volunteer who interested in raising money for the charity and supports their aims. The role will involve planning fundraising activities and making calls to raise money.\r\n\r\nThey have lots to offer for the volunteer, including cuddles from the therapy dogs and ongoing training. They look forward to welcoming a new team member.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers should be comfortable asking people for money, and making calls. Fundraising experience would be a plus.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will be provided with an introduction to Oliver's Army and full training to complete the role. Support will be available from a named contact.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOliver's Army Assistance and Therapy Dogs will be based in Lochgelly Miners Institute, 129 Main Street, Lochgelly, KY5 9AF.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are available at public transport rates.",
