                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000EdYWPYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000EdYWPYA3/maintenancebuilding-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-01-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-16",
                    "title": "Maintenance/Building Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Falkirk Braes Grange Centre (FBGC) was formed in 2024 in order to progress a Community Asset Transfer of the old Grange Community Education Centre building, located in the Braes area of Falkirk. The new FBGC Committee, made up entirely of volunteers, successfully took on full community asset transfer ownership from October 2025. FBGCs vision is to create a well utilised, sport and wellbeing, community led asset that helps deliver long-term benefits to the local community.\r\n\r\nThe FBGC committee are looking to implement several large improvements to the building over the course of 2026 and are looking for volunteers to assist with the following tasks as part of these projects. We have a great team in place with lots of experience to help support you. You can choose how often you'd like to help out and which specific tasks/projects you feel confident to take on:\r\n\r\n* Assisting with writing contractor specifications\r\n* Engaging contractors and assessing quotes received for specified pieces of work\r\n* Opening the building and showing contractors around the centre\r\n* Setting contractors to work\n\n## Experience required\n\nExperience with building maintenance/renovation projects and/or relevant trades\r\nGood Communicator, reliable and trustworthy.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe FBGC building and maintenance team will always be on hand to answer any questions and provide any support. An induction/walkthrough of the building will be offered as well as an overview of the projects we are looking to carry out.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible to suit the volunteer.  Can be discussed.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Falkirk Braes Grange Centre, Redding Road, FK2 0AA. \r\nCar Parking available. Located near bus route 1 and F25.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are not available.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
