        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000OvHMWYA3",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000OvHMWYA3/west-dunbartonshire-boccia-club",
            "name": "West Dunbartonshire Boccia Club",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SensoryImpairment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BXHoXYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BXHoXYAX/boccia-leader-support",
                    "publishStart": "2025-08-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Boccia Leader Support",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNo matter how good our services are, we can't properly support our users/community well if we don't have good organisers in the team. If this sounds like you... we would love you to consider volunteering with us for a few hours per week.\r\n\r\nOur club helps support a variety of people from different backgrounds to help develop their personal and social skills in a friendly atmosphere.  Our members have disabilities or long-term health conditions which can lead to mental health issues and a danger of becoming socially isolated which can affect their wellbeing.  Our club allows people to socialise in a friendly and safe environment where they can learn a new sport and spend time with others.\r\n\r\n•     Assist in setting up the court for Boccia training, including laying out court markers and arranging equipment\r\n•     Help set up training games under the direction of coaching or lead volunteers\r\n•     Pick up Boccia balls during and after sessions as needed to support play and ensure a tidy court\r\n•     Assist with packing away equipment and tidying the space at the end of each session\r\n•     Attend training provided by the club to understand setup procedures and safety guidelines\r\n•     Promote a positive, inclusive atmosphere for all participants and fellow volunteers.\r\n\r\nSo whether you are looking to use your time well, update your skills or have the chance to do something a bit new, we can offer you a warm welcome and all of the support and help you could need.\r\n\r\nWe are seeing a rise in demand for our services everyday. Having your help will allow us to be there for the people who need us. Any time you can give will make a real difference.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased in Dalmuir Barclay Church",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BXHoXYAX#role",
                        "type": "Role",
