        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000PCLSAYA5",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000PCLSAYA5/the-base-midlothian",
            "name": "The Base (Midlothian)",
            "description": "To provide a safe space for children and young people",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005zvo5YAA",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005zvo5YAA/volunteer-for-the-base",
                    "publishStart": "2024-10-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer for the Base",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nMain Duties: \r\n\r\nTo organise and prepare for activities, where appropriate.\r\n\r\nTo supervise activities and discussions, and where appropriate to participate alongside the children and young people and to carry out these tasks in a way that meets the aims and values of The Base (Midlothian). \r\n\r\nTo attend and take part in planning and recording meetings weekly.\r\n\r\nTo work within the policies, guidelines and legal requirements of The Base (Midlothian). \r\n\r\nCommitment/Availability \r\n\r\nThis role is on a flexible basis whereby volunteers will be welcome to attend on a weekly basis or on an ad-hoc basis when required to assist.\r\n\r\nWe ask that regular weekly volunteers let us know in advance if they are unable to attend a session.\r\n\r\nFor ad-hoc volunteers, The Base (Midlothian) will inform you in advance if additional help is required.\r\n\r\nSessions will run on 1 weekday during term-time and volunteers will be expected to be available on the day for approx 3 hours.\r\n\r\nTravel Expenses\r\n\r\nWe firmly believe that no one should be out of pocket for volunteering at The Base (Midlothian). Therefore, we reimburse all travel and out of pocket expenses incurred through volunteering.\r\n\r\nRequirements\r\n\r\nTo be successful in this voluntary role you must:\r\n\r\nComplete an application form \r\nProvide two references \r\nComplete a PVG check (either new or an update if already an existing member)\r\nUndergo induction training and Child Protection training (training will be provided free of charge)\n\n## Experience required\n\nLikes dealing with children, is not shy and has energy to bring fun to the youth club, ideally has chid protection course,first aid\n\n## Training details\n\nThe Base youth club is registered with LAYC, which provide all training and support – PVG checks will also be included free of charge\n\n## Travel details\n\nCar or Bus to Danderhall",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005zvo5YAA#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer for the Base",
                        "description": "Likes dealing with children, is not shy and has energy to bring fun to the youth club, ideally has chid protection course,first aid",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005zvo5YAA/volunteer-for-the-base?#modal_register_a0gQD000005zvo5YAA",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16",
                        "theme": [
                            {
