        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000PpMpuYAF",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000PpMpuYAF/livingston-fencing-club",
            "name": "Livingston Fencing Club",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hpr5JYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hpr5JYAR/social-media-manager",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-31",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-29",
                    "title": "Social Media Manager",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nLivingston Fencing Club is looking for a volunteer Social Media Manager to help us grow our membership and raise our profile in the local community. In this role, you'll create engaging content for TikTok, Instagram and Facebook, aimed at reaching adults, parents and young people (ages 12–18), and help share our news through local community social media channels too. You'll attend club sessions from time to time to capture photos and video footage, taking this task off our coaches' hands so they can focus on teaching. You'll also monitor our social media channels and respond to queries from members and prospective members in a friendly, timely way. This is a great opportunity for someone with an interest in sport, community engagement or content creation to make a real difference to a growing local club — no fencing experience necessary, just enthusiasm, creativity and a willingness to get involved.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for someone who can create and inspire as well as manage general enquiries. Someone who knows privacy rules and social media guidance.\r\nNo knowledge of fencing required just an interest in supporting a small community club.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
