        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000Pw4bCYAR",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000Pw4bCYAR/swan-shetland",
            "name": "SWAN (Shetland)",
            "description": "SWAN is an autistic-led Charity run for and by autistic women, girls and non-binary people across Scotland. \r\n\r\nFounded in 2012 in response to a lack of visibility and support, we work to create opportunities, within SWAN and in our wider society in Scotland, for autistic women and non-binary people to live healthy, happy and fulfilling lives. \r\n\r\nSWAN brings autistic women and non-binary people together to meet others like them and access autistic-led services, information and support which respond to their whole life experiences. Our main services include in-person and online meet-up groups, pre- and post-diagnosis support, counselling, online peer support and wellbeing webinars. \r\n\r\nWe represent autistic women and non-binary people and their interests in policy, service-design and decision-making processes and work with our members to involve them in these opportunities.\r\n\r\nWe deliver autistic-led training to improve understanding and inclusion of autistic women and non-binary people, and work with organisations employing and supporting our members to help them achieve autistic-informed service-design and delivery.\r\n\r\nSWAN is a place for autistic women and non-binary people to be who we are, understand ourselves better, connect with others, and learn from and support one another.  \r\n\r\nEverything we do at SWAN is based on the professional and personal knowledge and experiences of real autistic women, girls and non-binary people.\r\n\r\nSWAN is proud to be autistic led.",
            "website": "https://www.swanscotland.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC046946"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Sexuality",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sexuality"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Women",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Women"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JCRazYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JCRazYAH/swan-places-shetland-meet-up-facilitator",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-30",
                    "title": "SWAN Places Shetland Meet-Up Facilitator",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSWAN is a registered charity (SCO46946) that supports (diagnosed, self-diagnosed, and questioning) autistic women (cis and trans) and non-binary individuals across Scotland. Alongside other projects, we do so through monthly online and in-person peer support groups and Wellbeing Walks. Due to funding, all of our groups are 18 and over. All SWAN staff and volunteers are autistic and we pride ourselves on creating psychologically safe and neuro-affirming spaces.\r\nWe are looking for volunteers to help support our in-person Shetland Meet-Up as facilitators. The group is the last Thursday of every month from 6pm until 8pm in the Sandveien Neighbourhood Centre (ZE1 0RJ).\r\nDuties include:\r\n•\tWelcoming all group attendees, new and old\r\n•\tCreating a safe and inclusive space for all attendees\r\n•\tEncouraging positive peer support conversations \r\n•\tReporting any issues the group is experiencing to ensure it runs as smoothly as possible\r\n•\tHelping to organise occasional events and activities that happen outwith the monthly Meet-Up\r\nTo apply, you must be a cis or trans woman or non-binary and diagnosed or self-diagnosed autistic. The role requires a minimum of 2 hours of volunteering over a month period. This may vary if there are additional events organised for the group within a month period. All volunteering roles with SWAN require a PVG as standard (we will support you with this, and there is no cost involved). All training will be provided for the role and references can be given upon request. All roles can have reasonable adjustments implemented. Please get in touch if you have any questions about the role.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication.\r\nEmbraces equality and diversity.\r\nUnderstanding of autism.\n\n## Travel details\n\nSandveien Neighbourhood Centre, Lerwick",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JCRazYAH#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "SWAN Places Shetland Meet-Up Facilitator",
                        "description": "Good communication.\r\nEmbraces equality and diversity.\r\nUnderstanding of autism.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JCRazYAH/swan-places-shetland-meet-up-facilitator?#modal_register_a0gQD00000JCRazYAH",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/HealthHospitalsHospices",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Health / Hospitals / Hospices"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/MentalHealth",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/PeopleWithIllHealth",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "People with Ill Health"
