        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400001IRoGhAAL",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400001IRoGhAAL/ms-society-scotland",
            "name": "MS Society Scotland",
            "description": "The MS Society is the UK's largest charity dedicated to supporting everyone whose life is touched by MS. We are a community of people living with MS, scientists, campaigners, listeners, organisers, ambassadors and fundraisers. Our volunteers are a key part of achieving our goals and their support is vital.",
            "website": "http://www.mssociety.org.uk/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FundraisingFunding",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Fundraising / Funding"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MoneyDebtAdvice",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Money / Debt Advice"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SelfHelpSupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Self-Help / Support"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ChTr3YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ChTr3YAF/communications-volunteer-ayrshire",
                    "publishStart": "2025-10-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-02",
                    "title": "Communications Volunteer (Ayrshire)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAcross the UK, our 270 local groups play a vital part in supporting people affected by MS. They provide sense of belonging, unity and friendship. And they deliver services and support for their local MS community.\n\nWe are looking to recruit a Communications Volunteer for the Ayrshire Group. As our Communications Volunteer you’ll make sure people know they have a local MS Society group to turn to.\n\nIn this role you’ll be able to develop your writing skills, and gain an experience of communicating across a range of digital channels. \n\nTime commitment\n\nWe estimate this role will need around 2 hours a week. Our roles are flexible and aim to fit around you. Time commitments for this role may vary depending on your activities. This is an ongoing role.\n\nThis is a great opportunity to gain experience within a large charity and develop your existing skills and learn new ones. We need you to get involved and help make positive changes to the lives of people affected by MS.\n\nAbout you\n\nYou’ll have an interest in the MS Society and the work that we do, as well as the enthusiasm to represent both us and our values locally. You will understand the needs of people affected by MS in your area and be sympathetic to the needs and motivations of volunteers. You’ll be confident using Microsoft Office, the internet and email. You’ll be able to apply disability, equality and inclusion practices and understand and apply our risk management system. Ideally you’ll understand the local area and organisations that provide local services.\n\nYou will be reliable and easy to contact and you need to live in or near the area the group to carry out this role.\n\nApply \n\n1. Read through the role description carefully\n\n2. Please apply online\n\nThe MS Society is committed to promoting diversity. We can only offer roles to over 18s.\n\n## Travel details\n\nKA7 1DR",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FQvr2p3A0lcO6et8wmWBWTWwggrk1%2Fnvy5Tro3Sm4RYdpQ-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=b2dd6204-da18-46f3-b91a-12969c56c55f",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ChTr3YAF#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Communications Volunteer (Ayrshire)",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteering.mssociety.org.uk/283347VLZ",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "0",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/GeneralPublic",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "General Public"
                            },
                            {
