        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD0000178MyHYAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD0000178MyHYAU/the-breastfeeding-network",
            "name": "The Breastfeeding Network",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC027007"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JfXjRYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JfXjRYAV/volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAt the heart of our organisation are our volunteers who give their time to support other families in their communities and over the helplines.  If you would like to support other mums with breastfeeding, please apply and complete our training via (https://www.breastfeediing.network.org.uk/get-involved/train-to-be-a-registered-volunteer/).  This helps us make sure that the support and information our volunteers offer is safe, up-to-date and consistent across the UK.\r\nWe are also always very happy to hear from people with specialist skills that they would be willing to offer free of charge to support us.  Some examples of these skills that we are especially keen to find are:\r\n\r\nVideo and film making; Photography; Art/Graphic Design; Writing press releases; Research & evaluation and support writing funding applications.\r\n\r\nFor more information about the role or to request a copy of the Volunteer Role profile, please contact admin@breastfeedingnetwork.org.uk",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JfXjRYAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JfXjRYAV/volunteer?#modal_register_a0gQD00000JfXjRYAV",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/LocalAuthority/EastAyrshire",
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "East Ayrshire"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IE8PxYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IE8PxYAL/volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAt the heart of our organisation are our volunteers who give their time to support other families in their communities and over the helplines.  If you would like to volunteer your time to support other mums with breastfeeding you will first need to complete  our Training (https://breastfeedingnetwork.org.uk/get-involved/train-to-be-a-registered-volunteer/).  This helps us make sure that the support and information our volunteers offier is safe, up to date and consistent across the UK.\r\n\r\nIf there is no training in your local area, you are waiting for your course to start or if you don't think doing the training is for you there are still lots of ways you can help support us.  There are some examples below of the type of things that you could do and we are always happy to hear other suggestions and ideas.\r\n\r\nGet in touch with your local BfN group and offer to distribute posters and leaflets to local health centres, libraries, cafes, swimming pools and other community venues- find your local group here:\r\n(https://www.breastfeedingnetwork.org.uk/drop-in/) .  Organise a fundraising event or take part in a sponsored challenge on behalf of the BfN, see our Fundraising pages. (https://www.breastfeedingnetwork.org.uk/get-involved/fundraising/) for more ideas.  Become a friend of the Breastfeeding Network (https://wwwbreastfeedingnetwork.org.uk/become-a-member/) to help support the work we do and to receive copies of our quarterly electronic newsletter.  Help with events for families who can be harder to reach, for example specific cultural groups or young parents.  Help us translate our resources into different languages to support more families.  Write an article for our newsletter, for example about your own breastfeeding experience, why you would like to train with us or what difference BfN support made to you.  Organise an event for families to come along and meet the BfN and find out more about breastfeeding and support.  Help so that mums with disabilities can more easily access our support e.g. Reading and recording our information sheets for those with sight difficulties, sign language support for mums with hearing impairment.\r\n\r\nWe are also always happy to hear from people with specialist skills that they would be willing to offer free of charge to support us.  Some examples of these skills that they would be willing to offer free of charge to support us.  Some examples of the skills that we are especially keen to find are below but please get in touch if you have other skills that you would like to volunteer.\r\n\r\nVideo and film making \r\nPhotography to help us build a bank of images that we can use\r\nArt/graphic design for producing leaflets, posters, Christmas cards etc\r\nWriting press releases and general media skills\r\nResearch and evaluation skills/statistics\r\nSupport writing funding applications\r\n\r\nFrom time-to-time we might ask for volunteers with other specific skills so look for these requests on our website, Facebook and Twitter! If you offer a specific skill that we can't currently use, we will ask permission to keep your details on a database so we can get back in touch in the future if new opportunities arise.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IE8PxYAL#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IE8PxYAL/volunteer?#modal_register_a0gQD00000IE8PxYAL",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
