                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpfXBYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HpfXBYAZ/social-media-and-content-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-28",
                    "title": "Social Media and Content Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nYou can support the smooth day-to-day running of Heartsong Live through social media and content support.\n\n## Description\n\nHeartsong Live is an innovative, community-focused Christian radio station committed to amplifying voices and enhancing lives. Inspired by their Christian values, they create uplifting radio programmes, podcasts and community initiatives that bring hope, encouragement and practical support to people from all walks of life.\r\n\r\nYou can support Heartsong Live’s digital presence by helping distribute, organise and repurpose content, alongside the social media manager. The role will involve scheduling social media content; uploading radio programmes and podcasts to Mixcloud; repurposing radio programmes into blog articles, website content, and social media posts; updating website content and event listings; and creating simple graphics using Canva templates.\r\n\r\nVolunteering with Heartsong Live is more than giving your time. It is an opportunity to develop new skills, gain valuable experience and become part of a team that is passionate about making a positive difference through media.\n\n## Experience required\n\nHeartsong radio is looking for volunteers who enjoy writing and storytelling, have an interest in social media and digital communications, are creative, and have good written English. Volunteers should respect and support Heartsong Live’s Christian ethos and values.\n\n## Training details\n\nA full induction will be provided. Ongoing support is available from the Heartsong Live team and project coordinator.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis role can be carried out remotely, with opportunities to attend broadcasts, meetings, training sessions and community events throughout the year.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on an individual basis.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
