                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpfNVYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HpfNVYAZ/operations-and-programmes-coordinator",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-28",
                    "title": "Operations and Programmes Coordinator",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nYou can support the smooth day-to-day running of Heartsong Live through admin support.\n\n## Description\n\nHeartsong Live is an innovative, community-focused Christian radio station committed to amplifying voices and enhancing lives. Inspired by their Christian values, they create uplifting radio programmes, podcasts and community initiatives that bring hope, encouragement and practical support to people from all walks of life.\r\n\r\nYou can support by coordinating Heartsong Live’s programmes, events and volunteer activities, ensuring projects run smoothly and everyone stays informed. The role will involve sending reminders and weekly updates to volunteers and presenters; supporting the planning and delivery of community events and outside broadcasts; maintaining operational calendars and project timelines; and helping ensure projects are delivered effectively.\r\n\r\nVolunteering with Heartsong Live is more than giving your time. It is an opportunity to develop new skills, gain valuable experience and become part of a team that is passionate about making a positive difference through media.\n\n## Experience required\n\nHeartsong radio is looking for volunteers who enjoy organising people and projects, are proactive and dependable, have strong communication skills, and enjoys working in teams. Volunteers should respect and support Heartsong Live’s Christian ethos and values.\n\n## Training details\n\nA full induction will be provided. Ongoing support is available from the Heartsong Live team and project coordinator.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis role can be carried out remotely, with opportunities to attend broadcasts, meetings, training sessions and community events throughout the year.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on an individual basis.",
