        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000017T4ryYAC",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000017T4ryYAC/scottish-borders-cash-for-kids",
            "name": "Scottish Borders Cash for Kids",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HqkplYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HqkplYAB/social-media-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-17",
                    "title": "Social Media Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAssist Charity Manager taking and posting content on to our Facebook and Instagram profiles throughout the Mission Christmas campaign. \r\n\r\nSocial Media Student Volunteer – Task List\r\n\r\nContent Creation\r\n• Create engaging social media posts for Facebook and Instagram @CashForKidsScottishBorders\r\n• Design graphics using Canva or similar design tools. \r\n• Film and edit short-form videos and Reels highlighting the campaign. \r\n• Write captions that encourage donations, volunteering, and community involvement. \r\n• Ensure all content aligns with the charity's brand guidelines and tone of voice. \r\nCampaign Promotion\r\n• Promote key campaign milestones, events, and deadlines. \r\n• Share donation drop-off locations and fundraising opportunities. \r\n• Highlight stories of local families and the impact of donations (following safeguarding and consent guidelines). \r\n• Support countdown campaigns leading up to Christmas. \r\nCommunity Engagement\r\n• Monitor social media channels for comments and messages. \r\n• Respond to enquiries or direct them to the appropriate team. \r\n• Engage with supporters by liking, commenting on, and sharing relevant posts. \r\n• Encourage user-generated content by resharing supporter posts where appropriate. \r\nPhotography & Video\r\n• Capture photos and videos at campaign events and donation collections. From Volunteers, Beneficiaries and Supporters. \r\n• Edit images and videos for social media. \r\n• Organise media files for future use – genetic can be used year on year. \r\n\r\nSocial Media Planning\r\n• Help maintain the social media content calendar. \r\n• Schedule posts using approved social media management tools. \r\n• Research seasonal trends, hashtags, and content ideas. \r\nCampaign Support\r\n• Assist in promoting fundraising events and volunteer recruitment. \r\n• Create content celebrating volunteers, donors, and community partners. \r\n• Support awareness campaigns around child poverty and Mission Christmas. \r\nSkills Developed\r\n• Social media marketing \r\n• Digital content creation \r\n• Graphic design \r\n• Video editing \r\n• Copywriting \r\n• Community management \r\n• Campaign planning \r\n• Data analysis and reporting \r\n• Teamwork and communication \r\n• Time management and organisation\r\n\r\nWe would ideally like someone to be available on Mondays, Wednesdays and Fridays taking a posting content. \r\n\r\nThis will be done on a CFK phone/ ipad - therefore we can have a new person per week if needs be!\n\n## Experience required\n\nSomeone who knows their way around Facebook/Instagram. \r\n\r\nSomeone who is up to date with any trends and able to work in a busy environment.\r\n\r\nInterest can be submitted to carly.mackenzie@bauermedia.co.uk, who will then organise a teams call to discuss the opportunities further and get to know individuals who are interested in the role.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HqkplYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Social Media Volunteer",
                        "description": "Someone who knows their way around Facebook/Instagram. \r\n\r\nSomeone who is up to date with any trends and able to work in a busy environment.\r\n\r\nInterest can be submitted to carly.mackenzie@bauermedia.co.uk, who will then organise a teams call to discuss the opportunities further and get to know individuals who are interested in the role.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HqkplYAB/social-media-volunteer?#modal_register_a0gQD00000HqkplYAB",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
