        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000017fMXzYAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000017fMXzYAM/crossreach-counselling-moray",
            "name": "CrossReach Counselling Moray",
            "website": "https://www.crossreach.org.uk/our-locations/crossr",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HsdaTYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HsdaTYAR/volunteer-counsellor",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-09",
                    "title": "Volunteer Counsellor",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCrossReach Counselling Moray provides counselling services for adults, children and young people, and people experiencing perinatal challenges.\n\nWe're looking for Volunteer Counsellors to provide one-to-one counselling support from our service based in Buckie (AB56 1EG). The role includes delivering counselling sessions, maintaining appropriate records, attending group supervision, and contributing to a safe, professional and person-centred service.\n\nWe welcome applications from qualified counsellors and counselling diploma students who have successfully completed their readiness to practise. Applicants should be committed to ethical practice, professional standards, and working collaboratively as part of a counselling team.\n\nVolunteers receive training, ongoing support, regular supervision, and opportunities to develop their skills and experience within an established counselling service.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA completed Diploma in Counselling, or currently undertaking a counselling diploma and have successfully completed readiness to practise.\nA commitment to ethical and professional counselling practice.\nEmpathy, professionalism, and a person-centred approach.\nWillingness to provide the name and contact details of an external supervisor.\n\nAdditional requirements\nVolunteers supporting perinatal counselling must have completed at least 50 clinical hours.\nVolunteers providing online counselling must have completed ACTO-approved online counselling training.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe provide induction, role-specific training, regular group supervision, and ongoing learning and development opportunities to support you in your role as a Volunteer Counsellor.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThis is an ongoing volunteer role requiring a regular commitment. Volunteers will deliver counselling sessions, attend group supervision, maintain client records, and take part in training and development opportunities. The time commitment is flexible and will be agreed with the service based on client needs and your availability.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCrossReach Counselling: Moray\n 1 Burnside Court\n Buckie\n Moray\n AB56 1EG",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FJuTfjQg1htO69RkjtgzMU7QwBoT2%2FIWqodRGVOZErv18X-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=3b620ea7-6ff5-443a-a0f5-dc96b21a3d0f",
