        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000017fRO2YAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000017fRO2YAM/the-prevention-collective-scio",
            "name": "The Prevention Collective (SCIO)",
            "description": "The Prevention Collective is a Scottish based social impact and charitable organisation dedicated to the prevention and disruption of sexual and gender-based violence (SGBV) through a proactive and evidence-led approach. Rooted in the socio-ecological model (which focuses interventions across the individual, interpersonal, community and societal levels), we move beyond reactive crisis management to focus on early detection, prevention, and systemic change. The Collective brings together a range of professional and lived experience perspectives to target and address core societal factors that often contribute to SGBV.  A key mission in our work is supporting individuals who are on the trajectory of instigating SGBV and require a robust and timely intervention to prevent their pathway into causing harm.",
            "website": "https://www.thepreventioncollective.co.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC055100"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IniOvYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IniOvYAJ/volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-22",
                    "title": "Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Prevention Collective is seeking a committed volunteer to support our administrative and events work. This flexible role is ideal for someone looking to build experience in the charity sector or an experienced professional, while contributing to our mission of preventing sexual and gender‑based violence across Scotland.\n\nWhat you’ll do: \n\nSupport our booking and scheduling systems\nAssist with planning and coordinating events and webinars\nHelp gather information and support funding applications and scoping\nSupport data collection\nFinancial experience desirable but not essential\nProvide general administrative support to the CEO and Deputy Director\n\nThis role offers meaningful professional development and a chance to build confidence in a supportive environment. You will gain:\n\nPractical administrative experience within a growing Scottish charity\nSkills in event planning, coordination and logistics\nExperience contributing to funding applications and charity development\nInsight into prevention, safeguarding and community‑based work\nTraining, supervision and ongoing support\nA professional reference after a sustained period of volunteering\nOptional research experience available\nOpportunities to build your CV, develop new skills and expand your network\n\n## Experience required\n\nDesired skills:\nExperience with excel and Microsoft 365\nExperience managing booking systems and events\nExperience within administration\nExperience of data collection and management desirable but not essential\nFinancial experience desirable but not essential\n\n## Training details\n\nAll training and induction will be provided.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWe welcome volunteers who can offer 1–2 days per week, with full flexibility around days and hours.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe are located in Glasgow City Centre.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses will be covered, discussed further pre-appointment.\n\n## Taster details\n\nFeel free to reach out for an informal discussion to explore the role and your responsibilities.",
