        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000hg5YsYAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000hg5YsYAI/cats-protection-north-ayrshire",
            "name": "Cats Protection North Ayrshire",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BdAxFYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BdAxFYAV/fundraising-volunteer-team-leader",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-08",
                    "title": "Fundraising Volunteer Team Leader",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAs a charity we are able to help thousands of cats each year thanks to the generous donations we receive from members of the public. Our fundraising team leaders have the exciting and varied role of inspiring our fundraising volunteers to plan and deliver local fundraising events. Using their passion and imagination, they oversee a small team of fundraising volunteers who come together to raise the vital funds needed to cover costs such as veterinary bills and food. Our fundraising team leaders support their team of volunteers in all aspects of their roles, making sure our volunteers are happy, confident and supported.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BdAxFYAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Fundraising Volunteer Team Leader",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BdAxFYAV/fundraising-volunteer-team-leader?#modal_register_a0gQD00000BdAxFYAV",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/LocalAuthority/NorthAyrshire",
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "North Ayrshire"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BdBN3YAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BdBN3YAN/branch-fundraising-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-08",
                    "title": "Branch Fundraising Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThis is a really flexible role – you can choose what you’d like to get involved with, for example:  \r\n\r\nface-to-face fundraising. Organising or helping with fundraising events, running supermarket collections and fundraising stands, monitoring collection tins \r\nonline fundraising. Setting up online appeals and writing impactful cat case studies that maximise donations\r\nmarketing. Spreading the word about our fundraising activities, for example on social media and with the local press\r\ncompleting administration. Processing donations, sorting and recording donated goods, completing Gift Aid paperwork  \r\nchampioning our work. Getting involved with developing new fundraising ideas and increasing community engagement\r\nphotography. Capturing images of cats in care, cats we are helping, events and all things Cats Protection\r\nYou’ll need to be aged 18+ to volunteer in this role. If you’re aged 16-17, you’ll need to be supervised by a friend, family member, or guardian over the age of 18 in order to carry out any fundraising activity.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BdBN3YAN#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Branch Fundraising Volunteer",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BdBN3YAN/branch-fundraising-volunteer?#modal_register_a0gQD00000BdBN3YAN",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/LocalAuthority/NorthAyrshire",
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "North Ayrshire"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000hgu55YAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000hgu55YAA/barnardos-scotland",
            "name": "Barnardo's Scotland",
            "description": "Barnardo's work throughout Scotland and the rest of the UK and provide many services to disadvantaged children, young people, families and communities to help ensure that every child has the best possible start in life. The services Barnardo's provide are Family support, Leaving Care, Employability Skills, Mental Health and many more please see on their website.",
            "website": "http://www.barnardos.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC037605"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BdQsLYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BdQsLYAV/charity-retail-volunteers-east-kilbride",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-05",
                    "title": "Charity Retail Volunteers - East Kilbride",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur amazing team of vibrant & diverse volunteers helps us run over 500 shops. Our stores sell lots of great donated & new goods to help raise vital funds to make a real difference to disadvantaged children, young people and families across the UK.\n\nOur retail stores are the face of our charity on the high-street and in local communities. We have loads of amazing stock donated to us every week, and this all needs to be sorted, tagged and put on the shop-floor for sale!\n\nMaking sure our shops look fantastic is another task you can get involved with. You may also be required to help out on the till too, but we will show you how that works during your time volunteering with us. We value the contribution of everyone who supports Barnardo’s.\n\nYou will be a friendly face of Barnardo’s by volunteering in one of our shops. It would be great if you could volunteer one shift a week (or even more if you want) but we’re always happy to be flexible to work around your availability.\n\nWhy we want you\nOur amazing team of vibrant & diverse volunteers helps us run over 500 stores. Our stores sell lots of great donated and new goods to help raise vital funds to make a real difference to disadvantaged children, young people and families across the UK.\n\nWhat you will be doing\nWork on the till processing sales and returns\nPrepare stock, including sorting, steaming and pricing\nCreate stylish window displays\nReplenish stock on the shop floor\nStock-take and other administrative tasks\nThe skills you need\nFriendly and helpful\nHappy to be part of an amazing team of staff and volunteers\nEnthusiastic about the work of Barnardo’s\nFlexible and willing to do a variety of the shop tasks\nWhat's in it for you\nHave fun and meet new people\nDevelop skills for your CV including confidence, teamwork and problem solving\nMake a difference to the lives of children, young people and their families\nLearning and development opportunities\nFull training and experience of working in retail as a volunteer\nIn-store discount (20%)\nDisclaimer\nWe look to recruit a diverse range of volunteers. If your skills don't fit the above, please do not let this put you off as we are able to be flexible with most of our roles. If you are unable to apply online through the link on this page, please visit your local store for a paper application form\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Reliable / Dependable,Social Conscience,Team Player,Trustworthy,\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire Yes\nAcross South Lanarkshire",
