        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000i3K4AYAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000i3K4AYAU/solas-festival",
            "name": "Solas Festival",
            "description": "Solas Festival takes place in June each year at Errol. We aim to entertain, inspire and challenge, and to celebrate music, arts, ideas and community. Our multi-arts programme makes space for challenging debate with activists, writers and thinkers from across the political, cultural and religious spectrum. The festival aims to create a welcoming space where festival goers of all ages and from a range of backgrounds can come together in a safe environment; everyone is welcome.",
            "website": "https://www.solasfestival.co.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FaithReligionBelief",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Faith / Religion / Belief"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Br01xYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Br01xYAB/board-member",
                    "publishStart": "2025-09-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-02",
                    "title": "Board Member",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAs board member, you help ensure that this fabulous wee arts festival continues to thrive. You will bring your own skills/experience and add to the whole team.\n\n## Description\n\nThe role of a Board member is to: \r\n\r\n• ensure that Solas Festival complies with relevant legislation or regulations and applies its resources in pursuance of its objects. \r\n• contribute actively to the board by giving strategic direction, setting overall policy, defining goals, setting targets, and evaluating performance \r\n• safeguard the good name and values of Solas Festival \r\n• help ensure the financial stability of the Festival.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe expect you to demonstrate: \r\n\r\n• a commitment to the aims of Solas Festival \r\n• a willingness to attend meetings, to speak your mind and to give of your expertise \r\n• integrity \r\n• an acceptance of the legal duties, responsibilities and liabilities of trusteeship \r\n• an ability to work effectively as a member of a team for the good of Solas Festival.\n\n## Training details\n\nWritten material on governance of Solas and generically; one to ones.\n\n## Travel details\n\nPrimarily at volunteer’s home, with a full weekend in June in Errol.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReimbursement of costs on receipt of receipts.\n\n## Taster details\n\nInvitation to away day.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Br01xYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Board Member",
                        "description": "We expect you to demonstrate: \r\n\r\n• a commitment to the aims of Solas Festival \r\n• a willingness to attend meetings, to speak your mind and to give of your expertise \r\n• integrity \r\n• an acceptance of the legal duties, responsibilities and liabilities of trusteeship \r\n• an ability to work effectively as a member of a team for the good of Solas Festival.",
