                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Br1KbYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Br1KbYAJ/treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-09-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-02",
                    "title": "Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAs Treasurer, you help ensure that this fabulous wee arts festival continues to thrive. You will bring your own skills/experience and add to the whole team.\n\n## Description\n\nThe role of the Treasurer: \r\n\r\nCreating budgets for board approval and monitoring progress.\r\nAnnual accounts – gathering material for the accountants and submitting. \r\nEnsuring effective financial management at the festival. \r\nProviding financial support to fundraising including grant applications. \r\nEnsuring compliance with any financial obligations including tax. \r\n\r\nThe Treasurer will also be a board member of the festival.\n\n## Experience required\n\nExperience in accounting or finance, especially in charitable or arts organisations. \r\nA commitment to the aims of Solas Festival. \r\nA willingness to attend meetings, to speak your mind and to give of your expertise to a team effort. \r\nIntegrity. \r\nAn acceptance of the duties of trusteeship.\n\n## Training details\n\nWritten material on governance of Solas and generically; one to ones.\n\n## Travel details\n\nPrimarily at volunteer’s home, with a full weekend in June in Errol.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReimbursement of costs on receipt of receipts.\n\n## Taster details\n\nInvitation to away day.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
