            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Bs6yAYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Bs6yAYAR/local-events-coordinator-fundraiser-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-09-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-05",
                    "title": "Local Events Coordinator/ Fundraiser Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHoneypot Children’s Charity supports young carers aged 5-12 years through residential short breaks, memory making days and ongoing pastoral support. Two years ago, we proudly opened the doors to our first Scottish Honeypot House in Dalleagles, Ayrshire. \r\nNow, as we look to raise our profile across Scotland and increase fundraising opportunities, we are seeking enthusiastic Event and Fundraising Volunteers to help us reach even more children who need our support. This is a key role within our team as we rely on our events and donations to allow us to continue supporting young carers aged 5-12. \r\nAs a volunteer, you will work alongside our Fundraising Manager and other Honeypot supporters to make events such as supermarket collections and community fayres a success. You might find yourself setting up stalls, welcoming guests, managing donations or raising awareness for Honeypot. You can support by spreading the word locally, sharing posts on social media or representing Honeypot at community and school events. \r\nBy volunteering, you will be helping us provide life changing opportunities to young carers in Scotland. Your time and energy will directly support Honeypot, ensuring that even more children have the chance to make happy childhood memories.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThis role is a great fit for someone who is friendly, approachable, and enjoys working with people. You don’t need prior experience, just good communication skills and a willingness to lend a hand. The time commitment is very flexible, some volunteers help out at single events, whilst others become more regularly involved.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe will pay travel expenses for any mileage done as part of the role.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
