        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000iT1abYAC",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000iT1abYAC/nhs-lothian-charity",
            "name": "NHS Lothian Charity",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BulFdYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BulFdYAJ/performing-music-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Performing Music Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nLooking for performance ready music volunteers, who play acoustic instruments eg violin or guitar.\r\nTo deliver high quality musical performances to patients (usually in ward settings) to provide stimulation, distraction and boast mood to aid wellbeing and recovery.\r\nWe are not looking for applications forms at this time just an email to NHS Lothian Charity: loth.charity@nhs.scot\r\n\r\nAn audition is the first part of the application process, before completing paperwork.\r\n\r\nTo plan of ‘set list’ of audience appropriate music Performance of ‘set list’\r\nEngage in friendly small talk with patients\r\nProvide brief summary of performance to the Tonic Arts Team\r\nLooking for excellent interpersonal skills, and great time keeping and music ability to enhance the patients stay in hospital.\r\nTraining is given in compliance with NHS Lothian Volunteering Service.\n\n## Experience required\n\nExcellent interpersonal, communication skills and music ability with confidence to perform and a commitment to the role. Comfortable in a hospital setting. Adhere to all NHS Lothian relevant policies and values.\n\n## Training details\n\nA comprehensive induction programme will be provided for all volunteers eg. Expectations, adult and child protection, scenarios and health and safety. Ongoing training and support offered too.\n\n## Travel details\n\nLocal buses available to Midlothian hospitals\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe pay public transport (receipts required) and mileage. Claim monthly",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
