                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000C06hdYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000C06hdYAB/admin-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-09-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-12",
                    "title": "Admin Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nLittle Acorns is a social enterprise delivering the highest quality nature-based and holistic learning opportunities for children and families in Ayrshire and SW Scotland.\r\nWe are currently looking for Admin Support Volunteers. Are you organised and know your way around Microsoft Office and Excel? Could you provide the warm welcome someone needs when they visit or calls us? If so, joining our administration team might be the volunteering role for you. \r\nEveryone who volunteers with us is different, but we ask anyone who works or volunteers with us to act in a way that reflects our values. This helps us make sure you feel you belong and means we can make a meaningful difference to people’s lives and provide the best service possible.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are ideally looking for people with some basic skills in Microsoft packages. All our volunteers complete induction training, which helps you settle in and makes sure you have the knowledge and support you need for your role. We also offer additional training relevant to your role if you want to broaden your skills more widely.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe offer travel expenses to our volunteers.",
