        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000jSwjwYAC",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000jSwjwYAC/right-there",
            "name": "Right There",
            "description": "Right There are a charity in Scotland working to prevent people becoming homeless and separated from their loved ones.\n\nRight There support children and adults who are living with the effects of poverty, addiction or broken relationships. Walking alongside people at home and in the community, they provide tailored support and form trusting relationships to help people feel happier, safer and more confident to live their lives.\nThey offer services for counselling and people support, emergency accommodation and help people to build community connections with Help to rent support.\n\nOpening hours:\nMonday - Friday 9am-5pm",
            "website": "https://rightthere.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC017093"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IesdeYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IesdeYAB/volunteer-mentor",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-20",
                    "title": "Volunteer Mentor",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are recruiting kind, empathetic and approachable volunteer mentors to support young people aged 12-26 who are living in supported accommodation or accessing our outreach programmes across Orkney.\r\n\r\nOur mentoring programme encourages personal growth, builds confidence, develops social connections and supports young people to become involved in their communities.\r\n\r\nMentors are carefully matched with a young person based on shared interests and will provide consistent, positive encouragement and guidance.\r\n\r\nLed by the young person’s goals and interests, mentoring sessions can include trying new activities, cooking together, exploring the local community or simply spending time with someone they can trust and rely on.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for reliable, friendly volunteers who enjoy connecting with others and are passionate about making a positive difference in a young person’s life.\r\n\r\nWhat could a volunteer gain from the experience:\r\nVolunteering as a mentor is a rewarding opportunity to make a meaningful difference in a young person’s life while developing your own skills and confidence.\r\n\r\nVolunteers will gain valuable experience in mentoring, communication, relationship building and supporting young people from a range of backgrounds.\r\n\r\nYou will have opportunities to build meaningful connections, meet new people, develop new skills through training and enjoy shared experiences and activities with your mentee.\r\n\r\nMost importantly, you will have the satisfaction of knowing you are helping a young person build confidence, develop independence and feel more connected to their community.\r\n\r\nWe are building a close community of mentors so you will have access to strong peer support and social opportunities with other mentors.\r\n\r\nThis opportunity takes place across Orkney, primarily within local community settings. Mentors and young people can meet in suitable community locations and take part in activities based on the young person’s interests and goals. Face-to-face meetings are encouraged to help build meaningful relationships, although virtual sessions can be arranged where needed.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for kind, empathetic and approachable individuals who are passionate about supporting young people and making a positive difference in their lives.\r\n\r\nIdeal volunteers will have good communication and listening skills, be patient, reliable and consistent, and enjoy building positive relationships with others.\r\n\r\nYou should feel confident engaging with young people from a variety of backgrounds and be open-minded, non-judgemental and respectful of individual experiences.\r\n\r\nAn interest in community activities and a willingness to try new experiences would be beneficial.\r\n\r\nPrevious mentoring experience is not essential, as full training and ongoing support will be provided. Most importantly, we are looking for someone who can offer encouragement, understanding and a friendly, supportive presence.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteer mentors receive full training before being carefully matched with a young person. Training will help prepare volunteers for their mentoring role and provide the knowledge, skills and confidence needed to build positive and supportive relationships.\r\n\r\nOur dedicated Mentoring Team will provide ongoing guidance and support throughout the mentoring journey, including regular check-ins and access to mentoring coordinators for advice and reassurance.\r\n\r\nWe aim to ensure every volunteer feels confident, valued and supported throughout their experience.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWe aim to make volunteering as flexible and accessible as possible while encouraging regular, consistent contact to help build a positive mentoring relationship. \r\n\r\nWe encourage volunteers to commit to a year-long mentoring relationship to provide consistency, stability and the opportunity to build trust and meaningful connections with their young person.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F454fbca4-7ace-45c5-9b9b-814d26e2bc5d%2Fm1racXp0VYMqifY5WyjEgJaJfuf2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=b1109508-dba2-4807-9078-e2a2da46f746",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IesdeYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Mentor",
                        "description": "We are looking for kind, empathetic and approachable individuals who are passionate about supporting young people and making a positive difference in their lives.\r\n\r\nIdeal volunteers will have good communication and listening skills, be patient, reliable and consistent, and enjoy building positive relationships with others.\r\n\r\nYou should feel confident engaging with young people from a variety of backgrounds and be open-minded, non-judgemental and respectful of individual experiences.\r\n\r\nAn interest in community activities and a willingness to try new experiences would be beneficial.\r\n\r\nPrevious mentoring experience is not essential, as full training and ongoing support will be provided. Most importantly, we are looking for someone who can offer encouragement, understanding and a friendly, supportive presence.",
                        "commitment": "We aim to make volunteering as flexible and accessible as possible while encouraging regular, consistent contact to help build a positive mentoring relationship. \r\n\r\nWe encourage volunteers to commit to a year-long mentoring relationship to provide consistency, stability and the opportunity to build trust and meaningful connections with their young person.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IesdeYAB/volunteer-mentor?#modal_register_a0gQD00000IesdeYAB",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/Children",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/LocalCommunity",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Local Community"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/YoungPeople",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                            }
                        ],
                        "service": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Service/ExpensesPaid",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Expenses Paid"
                            }
                        ],
                        "reward": [
                            "https://ns.volunteeringdata.io/ExpensesReimbursed",
                            "https://ns.volunteeringdata.io/TrainingProvided"
                        ]
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
                            {
