                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Fu7kXYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Fu7kXYAR/workshop-admin-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Workshop Admin Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAdelphe is looking for a workshop admin volunteer to provide behind-the-scenes support that helps them run smoothly and deliver high-quality training and workshops.\n\n## Description\n\nAdelphe Connect develops and delivers community projects specifically designed to uplift women, and foster a community where health, confidence and opportunity intersect. They work closely with ethnic minority women to offer customised support and empower every woman to truly thrive.\r\n\r\nAdelphe is looking for a workshop admin volunteer to provide behind-the-scenes support that helps them run smoothly and deliver high-quality training and workshops.\r\n\r\nThe main duties are to:\r\nSupport workshop registrations\r\nSend participant reminders\r\nCompile and print resources ahead of workshops\r\nCollect feedback after workshops\r\n\r\nAs an Adelphe Connect volunteer, you can be part of a friendly team, you can make a difference in your local community, and you can gain experience in admin.\n\n## Experience required\n\n●\tComfortable with IT and admin tasks.\r\n●\tReliable and discreet.\r\n●\tAble to manage time well.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive an induction to Adelphe, and will have ongoing support from other members of the team.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAdelphe runs a hub with the Community Support Hub in Dunfermline's Kingsgate Centre, KY12 7QU. This role can also be undertaken from home.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on a 1-1 basis.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
