                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Fu6lFYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Fu6lFYAR/newsletter-writer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Newsletter Writer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAdelphe Connect is looking for a newsletter writer for their weekly email newsletter that is sent through Mailchimp.\n\n## Description\n\nAdelphe Connect develops and delivers community projects specifically designed to uplift women, and foster a community where health, confidence and opportunity intersect. They work closely with ethnic minority women to offer customised support and empower every woman to truly thrive.\r\n\r\nAdelphe Connect is looking for a newsletter writer for their weekly email newsletter that is sent through Mailchimp. The role includes drafting, formatting and scheduling the weekly email, adding Eventbrite links, and tracking basic results like opens and clicks.\r\n\r\nAs an Adelphe Connect volunteer, you can be part of a friendly team, you can make a difference in your local community, and you can gain experience in content writing and transferrable skills for communications roles.\n\n## Experience required\n\n●\tGood organisational skills.\r\n●\tConfidence in writing content.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive an induction to Adelphe, and will have ongoing support from other members of the team.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAdelphe runs a hub with the Community Support Hub in Dunfermline's Kingsgate Centre, KY12 7QU. This role can also be undertaken from home.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on a 1-1 basis.",
