                    "title": "Eventbrite Admin Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAdelphe is looking for an Eventbrite admin volunteer to provide behind-the-scenes support that helps them run smoothly and deliver high-quality events.\n\n## Description\n\nAdelphe Connect develops and delivers community projects specifically designed to uplift women, and foster a community where health, confidence and opportunity intersect. They work closely with ethnic minority women to offer customised support and empower every woman to truly thrive.\r\n\r\nAdelphe is looking for an Eventbrite admin volunteer to provide behind-the-scenes support that helps them run smoothly and deliver high-quality events.\r\n\r\nThe main duties are to:\r\nSet up Eventbrite listings\r\nManage bookings\r\nKeep accurate attendee lists\r\n\r\nAs an Adelphe Connect volunteer, you can be part of a friendly team, you can make a difference in your local community, and you can gain experience in event admin.\n\n## Experience required\n\n●\tFamiliarity with Eventbrite platform.\r\n●\tComfortable with IT and admin tasks.\r\n●\tReliable and discreet.\r\n●\tAble to manage time well.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive an induction to Adelphe, and will have ongoing support from other members of the team.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAdelphe runs a hub with the Community Support Hub in Dunfermline's Kingsgate Centre, KY12 7QU. This role can also be undertaken from home.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on a 1-1 basis.",
