                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAdelphe Connect is looking for a community advertising volunteer to help keep the community updated about their activities and events.\n\n## Description\n\nAdelphe Connect develops and delivers community projects specifically designed to uplift women, and foster a community where health, confidence and opportunity intersect. They work closely with ethnic minority women to offer customised support and empower every woman to truly thrive.\r\n\r\nAdelphe Connect is looking for a community advertising volunteer to help keep the community updated about their activities and events. Your role will be to place flyers in community locations such as community centres and hubs, and to log where they’ve been shared.\r\n\r\nAs an Adelphe Connect volunteer, you can be part of a friendly team, you can make a difference in your local community, and you can gain experience in community outreach.\n\n## Experience required\n\n●\tKnowledge of local community venues.\r\n●\tCulturally sensitive and respectful.\r\n●\tEnthusiastic about Adelphe’s mission.\r\n●\tReliable and proactive.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive an induction to Adelphe, and will have ongoing support from other members of the team.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAdelphe runs a hub with the Community Support Hub in Dunfermline's Kingsgate Centre, KY12 7QU. This role will be undertaken in your local community.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on a 1-1 basis.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
