                    "title": "Graphic Design Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAdelphe Connect is looking for a graphic design volunteer to help keep the community updated about their activities and events.\n\n## Description\n\nAdelphe Connect develops and delivers community projects specifically designed to uplift women, and foster a community where health, confidence and opportunity intersect. They work closely with ethnic minority women to offer customised support and empower every woman to truly thrive.\r\n\r\nAdelphe Connect is looking for a graphic design volunteer to help keep the community updated about their activities and events. Your role will be to create simple, branded graphics for flyers and social media, using their templates and colours.\r\n\r\nAs an Adelphe Connect volunteer, you can be part of a friendly team, you can make a difference in your local community, and you can gain experience in graphic design.\n\n## Experience required\n\n●\tUnderstanding of graphic design\r\n●\tCulturally sensitive and respectful.\r\n●\tEnthusiastic about Adelphe’s mission.\r\n●\tReliable and proactive.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive an induction to Adelphe, and will have ongoing support from other members of the team.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAdelphe runs a hub with the Community Support Hub in Dunfermline's Kingsgate Centre, KY12 7QU. This role can also be undertaken from home.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on a 1-1 basis.",
