                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Fu3AgYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Fu3AgYAJ/online-community-supporter",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Online Community Supporter",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAdelphe Connect is looking for an online community supporter for their supportive online community of women.\n\n## Description\n\nAdelphe Connect develops and delivers community projects specifically designed to uplift women, and foster a community where health, confidence and opportunity intersect. They work closely with ethnic minority women to offer customised support and empower every woman to truly thrive.\r\n\r\nAdelphe Connect is looking for an online community supporter for their supportive online community of women. Your role will be to:\r\nCreate a warm, welcoming online space\r\nWelcome new people\r\nSupport conversation in the WhatsApp chat\r\nHelp participants know how to get involved and next steps\r\n\r\nAs an Adelphe Connect volunteer, you can be part of a friendly team, you can make a difference in your local community, and you can gain experience in community engagement.\n\n## Experience required\n\n●\tFriendly and approachable.\r\n●\tGood communication skills.\r\n●\tRespectful of confidentiality and cultural diversity.\r\n●\tReliable and willing to volunteer as part of a team.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive an induction to Adelphe, and will have ongoing support from other members of the team.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAdelphe runs a drop-in with the Community Support Hub in Dunfermline's Kingsgate Centre, KY12 7QU. This role can also be undertaken from home.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on a 1-1 basis.",
