                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000CMSd3YAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000CMSd3YAH/drop-in-session-supporter",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Drop-In Session Supporter",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAdelphe Connect is looking for a drop-in session supporter for their weekly drop ins in Dunfermline.\n\n## Description\n\nAdelphe Connect develops and delivers community projects specifically designed to uplift women, and foster a community where health, confidence and opportunity intersect. They work closely with ethnic minority women to offer customised support and empower every woman to truly thrive.\r\n\r\nAdelphe Connect is looking for a drop-in session supporter for their weekly drop ins in Dunfermline. Your role will be to:\r\nCreate a warm, welcoming space\r\nSet up for the drop in\r\nSign in participants\r\nServe refreshments\r\nOffer practical support during the drop in session\r\n\r\nAs an Adelphe Connect volunteer, you can be part of a friendly team, you can make a difference in your local community, and you can gain experience in community engagement.\n\n## Experience required\n\n●\tFriendly and approachable.\r\n●\tGood communication and listening skills.\r\n●\tRespectful of confidentiality and cultural diversity.\r\n●\tReliable and willing to volunteer as part of a team.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive an induction to Adelphe, and will have ongoing support from other members of the team.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAdelphe runs a drop-in with the Community Support Hub in Dunfermline's Kingsgate Centre, KY12 7QU.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on a 1-1 basis.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000CMSd3YAH#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Drop-In Session Supporter",
                        "description": "●\tFriendly and approachable.\r\n●\tGood communication and listening skills.\r\n●\tRespectful of confidentiality and cultural diversity.\r\n●\tReliable and willing to volunteer as part of a team.",
