        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000lCH5OYAW",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000lCH5OYAW/scottish-older-peoples-assembly-sa",
            "name": "Scottish Older People's Assembly (SA)",
            "website": "https://sopa.scot/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000CNmOPYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000CNmOPYA1/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2025-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-02",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAre you interested in ensuring that older people have a say about their present and future, that they are treated with \r\nrespect and their contribution to society is recognised and appreciated? \r\nThen why not consider joining us as a Trustee in SOPA, the Scottish Older People’s Assembly! \r\n\r\nSOPA is in a period of organisational redevelopment, renewal and resilience building. To reach our potential, we are looking to appoint new Trustees to our Board.  \r\nThis is an exciting time for SOPA, with challenges and opportunities which require strong support and leadership from \r\na skilled, active and inspiring Board.  \r\nTrustees will play a key role in supporting SOPA s mission to bring forth the voices of Scotland’s older population and to \r\nensure their huge contribution to Scotland’s social, cultural and economic landscape is recognised and appreciated - both within Scotland and beyond. \r\nExperience of working in the voluntary, public or private sector is desired. Good governance, leadership and team-working are desirable. \r\nWe seek new Trustees to bring knowledge and \r\nexperience of any of the following: knowledge of issues affecting older people or finance or funding strategies. \r\nWe are looking for team players who can bring new introductions, broker new \r\npartnerships, and breathe new life into existing ones.  \r\n\r\nContact Louisa Turner by email or call 07477506815 (Tuesday or Wednesday) for a Trustee Pack, more information, or for a chat.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000CNmOPYA1#role",
