        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000lJ01RYAS",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000lJ01RYAS/weekday-wow-factor",
            "name": "Weekday Wow Factor",
            "description": "We provide quality and therapeutic activities for older adults 50+, codesigned with participants to overcome leisure and health inequalities in deprived areas.\r\nWe aim to tackle loneliness by building regular, reliable friendship and community building opportunities, to keep everyone connected, and develop a culture of wellbeing and positive mental health.\r\nWe aim to tackle to effects of aging and long-term conditions by encouraging regular, at-your-own-pace movement, to keep everyone as independent as possible.\r\nWe aim to build resilience, in individuals and communities, and strive to develop brilliance in our groups.\r\nFun, laughter and interesting, engaging activities are key to everything we do. Including:\r\n•\tOur famous Daytime Discos with lunch\r\n•\tMinibus Adventures – day trips with purpose\r\n•\tOther online and in person activities include:\r\no\tTai Chi\r\no\tZoom Daytime Discos\r\no\tPick-n-mix activities\r\no\tAdapted games\r\no\tDiscussion groups.",
            "website": "https://www.weekdaywowfactor.com",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC050760"
                }
            ],
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2Ffaa5955a-3c08-4e7e-8a0a-b4d872d12ece%2FbHNYaxHxAUc1xaVAsL6LrYe7W5R2%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=fb266e60-bcb8-4a24-8e94-3eb607d28926",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HJkmvYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HJkmvYAD/volunteer-driver",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-15",
                    "title": "Volunteer Driver",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteering as a member of the Drivers team you will provide transport for our staff, members and their carers to and from activities.\r\nAs a Volunteer Driver you will be providing a service as part of a team and according to a coordinated rota with the need to be punctual and reliable.\n\n## Description\n\nWeekday WOW Factor is a community initiative that creates fun, inclusive social experiences—often themed events like daytime discos and group activities—designed primarily for older adults and people who may be at risk of isolation. The organisation focuses on bringing people together in a safe, welcoming environment where they can build friendships, stay active, and enjoy meaningful social interaction. By combining accessible venues, supportive staff and volunteers, and organised transport, Weekday WOW Factor helps remove barriers to participation and ensures more people can stay connected to their community.\r\nDo you enjoy driving and meeting new people? As a Volunteer Driver with Weekday WOW Factor, you’ll play a vital role in helping older adults and community members get to social activities that bring joy, connection, and purpose to their week.\r\nFor many of the people we support, attending these sessions wouldn’t be possible without reliable transport. That’s where you come in—helping to create a safe, welcoming journey that’s just as important as the destination.\r\nWhat you’ll do\r\n•\tSafely transport participants to and from WOW Factor events in Angus\r\n•\tSupport a friendly, inclusive atmosphere from pick-up to drop-off\r\n•\tWork as part of a coordinated team of drivers and staff\r\n•\tFollow agreed schedules and routes to ensure smooth running of activities\r\nSupport to the Volunteer\r\nVolunteers will receive an induction, clear guidance, and ongoing support from a coordinator. You’ll have access to schedules in advance, support from staff and fellow volunteers, and any required training or checks to help you feel confident in the role.\r\nWhy this role matters\r\nYour time behind the wheel helps reduce isolation and opens the door for people to reconnect with their community, build friendships, and enjoy meaningful experiences.\r\nYou’re not just driving—you’re helping people feel included, valued, and part of something positive.\r\nWhat we’re looking for\r\n•\tA full, clean driving licence\r\n•\tConfident, safe driving skills (minibus experience is a bonus)\r\n•\tFriendly, patient, and reliable approach\r\n•\tGood timekeeping and communication\r\nWhat you’ll gain\r\n•\tA rewarding role where you see the impact of your support straight away\r\n•\tThe chance to meet new people and be part of a welcoming team\r\n•\tExperience in community transport and supporting social inclusion\r\n•\tReimbursement of agreed travel expenses\r\nTime commitment\r\n•\tFlexible opportunities available across weekdays and weekends\r\n•\tSessions planned in advance with the team\r\n•\tYou can volunteer regularly or around your availability\r\nLocation\r\n•\tActivities take place across Angus\r\nIf you are interested, please click the ‘Apply’ button below (available when registered and logged in). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn’t work out, then please feel free to contact us directly on weekdaywowfactor@gmail.com \r\n\r\nWhat happens next?\r\nAfter applying, a member of the team will be in touch to discuss your availability, answer any questions, and guide you through the next steps, including any checks or induction needed before getting started.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tA full, clean driving licence\r\n•\tConfident, safe driving skills (minibus experience is a bonus)\r\n•\tFriendly, patient, and reliable approach\r\n•\tGood timekeeping and communication",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HJkmvYAD#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Driver",
                        "description": "•\tA full, clean driving licence\r\n•\tConfident, safe driving skills (minibus experience is a bonus)\r\n•\tFriendly, patient, and reliable approach\r\n•\tGood timekeeping and communication",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HJkmvYAD/volunteer-driver?#modal_register_a0gQD00000HJkmvYAD",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "21",
                        "theme": [
                            {
