        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000mFF4mYAG",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000mFF4mYAG/glasgow-film",
            "name": "Glasgow Film",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/GlasgowFilm",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JIHXNYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JIHXNYA5/christmas-usher-at-gft",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-24",
                    "title": "Christmas Usher at GFT!",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nChristmas Usher at GFT!\n\n## Description\n\nHelp Create Movie Magic and Festive Memories This December!\nSupportive team &bull; Flexible shifts &bull; Travel expenses covered &bull; Spread holiday joy\n\nAre you available this festive season and looking to be part of something fun, magical, and meaningful?\n\nThe Glasgow Film Theatre (GFT) &ndash; an educational charity and cultural icon &ndash; is looking for cheerful and committed Festive Volunteer Ushers to help us spread Christmas cheer from 11th&ndash;24th December. Every year, our cinema becomes a festive hub for families, friends, and film lovers, and you could be at the heart of it all!\n\nWe&rsquo;ve got a dedicated &ldquo;Die Hard&rdquo; crew of regular volunteers (see what we did there?), but the holiday season is our busiest time, and we&rsquo;re calling on some extra Christmas Elves to help make it magical.\n\nWhat You&#39;ll Be Doing:\n\nAs a Festive Volunteer Usher, you&rsquo;ll play a key part in bringing joy and seamless experiences to our audiences. Tasks include:\n\n\n\tChecking tickets and helping guests find their seats\n\tKeeping an eye on the audience and film presentation during screenings\n\tAssisting with tidying the cinema between shows\n\tSpreading festive cheer and chatting with visitors\n\n\nVolunteers are at the very centre of many Glasgow families&rsquo; cherished Christmas traditions &ndash; your presence will help create unforgettable memories.\n\n\nWhat You&rsquo;ll Get:\n\n\n\tFull support and guidance from our friendly volunteer coordinator\n\tFlexible shifts between 4&ndash;6 hours &ndash; perfect for working around your schedule\n\tTravel expenses reimbursed if travelling within the Glasgow City boundary\n\tA chance to be part of a fun, welcoming, and inclusive environment\n\tOpportunity&nbsp;to support GFT&rsquo;s wider impact&nbsp;\n\tAnd of course... Christmas jumpers and festive outfits encouraged!\n\n\n\nWhen: 11th &ndash; 24th December\nWhere: Glasgow Film Theatre (GFT)\nVolunteer Times: Between 11am and 11pm (flexible shifts)\nDress Code: All black (not provided) &ndash; festive touches very welcome!\n\nThis is a great opportunity for anyone who loves film, community spirit, and the magic of the festive season. Whether you can offer one day or the whole fortnight, we&rsquo;d love to hear from you.\n\n&nbsp;Ready to Join the GFT Elf Team?\n\n\n\tApplications open now&nbsp;Glasgow Film Theatre Christmas Volunteers 2026 &ndash; Fill in form&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\tOr contact Dean Browning&nbsp;directly at dean.browning@glasgowfilm.org for more info\n\n\nPlease allow up to 5 working days for a reply. Don&rsquo;t forget to check your spam/junk folders. If needed, you can also contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\nBring joy, meet new people, and be part of the festive magic at one of Glasgow&rsquo;s most loved venues. This Christmas, help us make the silver screen sparkle.&nbsp;\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when registered and logged in). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nMust be over 18 and have English strong enough to be able to competently aid a building evacuation. Must be friendly and people focused.\n\n## Travel details\n\nGFT can be accessed via a wide variety of public transport into the city centre. Car parking facilities can be found within a 5 minute walking distance.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe can cover public transport costs for anyone living within the Glasgow City Boundary.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
