                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Cn4DFYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Cn4DFYAZ/makerengineer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-10-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Maker/Engineer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDesigning and making pieces of equipment for individuals with specific needs.\r\nUsing your practical skills working with metal, wood, plastics, or electronics (or a combination of them)\r\nAttending a bi-monthly meeting\r\nWe can support you to develop the skills you need for this role, and there's an induction that covers all            the areas above. You'll also have the chance to discuss your role and any additional needs with us.\r\nEssential needs;\r\nPractical experience in working with one of the above materials.\r\nComfortable working with people, listening to them and understanding their needs.\r\nAble to apply;\r\nOur risk management system.\r\nDisability, equality, and inclusion practices.\r\nKeep peoples personal details safe.\r\nNB. No medical skills required; clients professional advisors offer guidance ref.the clients' medical condition. \r\nWilling to follow REMAP policies and procedures and a commitment to our values.\r\nDesirable needs:\r\nAccess to some/your own tools and a workshop\r\nAble to drive or have good transport links.\t\r\nYou'll also need to complete an induction checklist, as well as a PVG check (we cover the costs) and reference check\n\n## Experience required\n\nPractical skills, Communication skills, Inventive/Imaginative, patience, empathetic with clients who experience physical difficulties.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction to include policies and practices, with ongoing mentoring. Training and support based on volunteers' skills needs.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAble to drive or have good transport links.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTransport costs or £0.45/mile, plus out of pocket expenses for materials bought/used.",
