                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HtA6bYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HtA6bYAF/access-panel-admin-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Access Panel Admin Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe South Ayrshire Access Panel is a group of volunteers who meet monthly, and work to improve access and inclusion for disabled people in our local community. South Ayrshire Access Panel was formed in 2024 with help from Disability Equality Scotland to represent points of view in public forums for those who have different accessibility needs. \r\nWe are currently looking for an Admin volunteer to support the chair with the day to day running of the panel. You should ideally be able to attend the monthly meetings of the Access Panel which take place on the 3rd Thursday of every month from 10-12. \r\nTasks include:\r\n- Assisting with correspondence, including preparing letters and emails \r\n- Supporting the coordination of meetings, including producing an agenda \r\n- Managing records and keeping information up to date  \r\n- Supporting the notetaker\r\n- Ideally you would be able to occasionally support the treasurer with day to day tasks\n\n## Experience required\n\n- We are looking for someone who is familiar with Microsoft Packages including Office, Word and Excel.\r\n- It would be helpful if you had some experience of completing grant applications.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fb5695a63-0298-45d5-92d2-d50a71cf3bc0%2F3wQ4LNHTVDdv38i2OQS2H73Yrhd2%2Fheader.jpg?alt=media&token=e55ab6f7-a527-4daa-91a1-87c2fb5776e1",
