            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000EW6dJYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000EW6dJYAT/warm-welcome-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-11",
                    "title": "Warm Welcome Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Heart of Fife Parish Church are a new Church of Scotland Parish covering the historic parishes of the Glenrothes, Markinch, Thornton, and Leslie areas of Fife.\r\n\r\nThe Church provide a 'Warm Welcome' community space, open to the public, every Tuesday and Thursday. The space is offered to the local community, as a space to bring their children, engage in arts and crafts and to enjoy the company of others. A soup lunch is provided on a Tuesday and refreshments on a Thursday.\r\n\r\nVolunteers are required on both a Tuesday and Thursday to support this initiative. Typically, tasks will involve, welcoming members of the public, setting up, clearing away activities, and serving refreshments.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe organisation is looking for committed and reliable volunteers with a friendly an approachable manner who are willing to work as part of a team.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis opportunity takes place in St Drostan's Church Hall, Markinch, Fife, which is well served with a public bus and train service, in addition to on street parking in the near vicinity.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThis can be looked at, we would never want this to be a barrier to potential volunteers.",
