        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000pl0TrYAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000pl0TrYAI/glentanar-juniors-fc",
            "name": "Glentanar Juniors FC",
            "description": "Glentanar Junior Football Club is a proud semi-professional team based at Woodside Sports Complex in Aberdeen. Founded with strong community roots, the club has long been a key part of the local football scene, providing opportunities for players to develop and compete at a high level within the Scottish Junior Football Association structure. Our focus is on combining ambition on the pitch with a welcoming, inclusive environment for players, volunteers, and supporters alike.\r\n\r\nOver the years, Glentanar JFC has built a reputation for resilience, teamwork, and a strong sense of local pride. We strive to create an environment where football is accessible, enjoyable, and community-driven—encouraging both youth and senior players to reach their potential while representing Aberdeen with passion and respect. The club continues to grow steadily, driven by dedicated volunteers and loyal fans who share our vision for sustainable progress.\r\n\r\nToday, Glentanar JFC is more than just a football team—it’s a community hub where people come together to share in the excitement of the game. From match days filled with energy and camaraderie to ongoing efforts improving facilities and engagement, the club remains committed to fostering a spirit of togetherness. Whether on the pitch or behind the scenes, everyone involved plays a part in shaping the future of Glentanar and promoting grassroots football across the region.",
            "website": "https://www.facebook.com/share/17MLKifvMf/?mibextid=wwXIfr",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000DEjDuYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000DEjDuYAL/glentanar-juniors-fc-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-24",
                    "title": "Glentanar Juniors FC Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nGlentanar Junior FC is looking for enthusiastic volunteers to join our growing team as we continue to develop both on and off the pitch. This is a fantastic opportunity to be part of an ambitious semi-professional club at the heart of Aberdeen’s football scene.\r\n\r\nWe’re seeking local football fans who want to contribute their time, skills, and energy in a welcoming, team-focused environment. Whether you can spare a few hours on match days or take on a regular role behind the scenes, your support will help the club thrive.\r\n\r\nCurrent Volunteer Roles\r\n• Match Day Operations: Help with match preparation, stewarding, ticketing, and ensuring everything runs smoothly on game days. You’ll be at the centre of the action and a key part of our supporters’ experience.\r\n• Hospitality Team: Assist in providing a warm welcome to guests, sponsors, and visiting teams. Ideal for anyone who enjoys meeting people and creating a friendly, professional atmosphere.\r\n• Treasurer: Support the committee by managing club finances, budgets, and fundraising initiatives. Perfect for someone with an eye for detail and an interest in community sport management.\r\n• Social Media Manager: Manage the club’s social channels and help grow our online presence. Share match updates, player news, and behind-the-scenes stories with our fans and local community.\r\n• Club Photographer: Capture the spirit of Glentanar through action shots, team photos, and event coverage. Great opportunity for photographers looking to build a sports portfolio.\r\n• Club Secretary: A vital role supporting the committee with administration, correspondence, and fixture coordination. Ideal for someone organised who enjoys being part of a close-knit team.\r\n\r\nWhy Volunteer with Glentanar JFC?\r\n• Be part of a proud community club with deep local roots and ambitious plans for the future.\r\n• Gain valuable experience in sports management, media, event coordination, and community engagement.\r\n• Enjoy being close to the game, working alongside players, coaches, and supporters.\r\n• Meet new people, develop your skills, and make a real difference in grassroots football.\r\n\r\nNo previous experience is required for most roles — just enthusiasm, reliability, and a positive attitude. Training and guidance will be provided where needed, and all volunteers are fully supported by our club committee.\r\n\r\nIf you love football and want to play your part in supporting a semi-professional club that’s growing on and off the pitch, we’d love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nFantastic opportunities to assist and make a real difference. All help is greatly appreciated.  For further details please contact Jordan Gomez,  Chair ate email glentanarjfc@gmail.com or telephone: 07977461767\n\n## Description\n\nGlentanar Junior FC is looking for enthusiastic volunteers to join our growing team as we continue to develop both on and off the pitch. This is a fantastic opportunity to be part of an ambitious semi-professional club at the heart of Aberdeen’s football scene.\r\n\r\nWe’re seeking local football fans who want to contribute their time, skills, and energy in a welcoming, team-focused environment. Whether you can spare a few hours on match days or take on a regular role behind the scenes, your support will help the club thrive.\r\n\r\n-Current Volunteer Roles\r\n• Match Day Operations: Help with match preparation, stewarding, ticketing, and ensuring everything runs smoothly on game days. You’ll be at the centre of the action and a key part of our supporters’ experience.\r\n• Hospitality Team: Assist in providing a warm welcome to guests, sponsors, and visiting teams. Ideal for anyone who enjoys meeting people and creating a friendly, professional atmosphere.\r\n• Treasurer: Support the committee by managing club finances, budgets, and fundraising initiatives. Perfect for someone with an eye for detail and an interest in community sport management.\r\n• Social Media Manager: Manage the club’s social channels and help grow our online presence. Share match updates, player news, and behind-the-scenes stories with our fans and local community.\r\n• Club Photographer: Capture the spirit of Glentanar through action shots, team photos, and event coverage. Great opportunity for photographers looking to build a sports portfolio.\r\n• Club Secretary: A vital role supporting the committee with administration, correspondence, and fixture coordination. Ideal for someone organised who enjoys being part of a close-knit team.\r\n\r\n-Why Volunteer with Glentanar JFC?\r\n• Be part of a proud community club with deep local roots and ambitious plans for the future.\r\n• Gain valuable experience in sports management, media, event coordination, and community engagement.\r\n• Enjoy being close to the game, working alongside players, coaches, and supporters.\r\n• Meet new people, develop your skills, and make a real difference in grassroots football.\r\n\r\nNo previous experience is required for most roles — just enthusiasm, reliability, and a positive attitude. Training and guidance will be provided where needed, and all volunteers are fully supported by our club committee.\r\n\r\nIf you love football and want to play your part in supporting a semi-professional club that’s growing on and off the pitch, we’d love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nFantastic opportunities to assist and make a real difference. All help is greatly appreciated.  For further details please contact Jordan Gomez,  Chair ate email glentanarjfc@gmail.com or telephone: 07977461767\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant guidance and excellent support provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to suit volunteers. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWoodside Sports Complex, Station Road,  Aberdeen, AB24 2UL. \r\n\r\nIf involved in match day operations opportunity to travel across North East to away games. But no expectations",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
