        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000012YiD6YAK",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000012YiD6YAK/neighbours-to-friends-cic",
            "name": "Neighbours to Friends CIC",
            "description": "We are a Scottish Community Interest Company working to reduce loneliness among adults aged 18+ by creating regular in-person social opportunities where people can meet, talk more easily, feel included and build local connections. We seek volunteers across Scotland to start and support local community groups.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SocialEconomySocialEnterprise",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Social Economy / Social Enterprise"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEngagement",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Engagement"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEvent",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Event"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HyTq9YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HyTq9YAF/volunteer-social-night-host-bring-people-together-in-your-local-area-scotland",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-04",
                    "title": "Volunteer Social Night Host – Bring People Together in Your Local Area (Scotland)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCould you be the person who brings your local community together?\r\nImagine a welcoming evening at a local restaurant or another friendly venue, where adults who have never met before share a laugh, enjoy a simple group game and begin to make new friends. You could help make it happen, right where you live.\r\n\r\nNeighbours to Friends CIC is looking for friendly, reliable volunteer Social Night Hosts across Scotland to bring adults aged 18+ together through recurring community social evenings. Perhaps you've seen our poster in a restaurant. Or perhaps you've found us here on Volunteer Scotland. Either way, we can help you explore setting up a social evening in your own local area. No previous hosting or game experience is needed. We provide full induction and practical training, step-by-step instructions, all reusable game materials and ongoing support. What matters most is wanting to help people feel welcome and connected.\r\n\r\nWhat would you do?\r\n•\tWelcome participants, including people arriving on their own.\r\n•\tExplain and guide a simple social-deduction game that makes conversation easier.\r\n•\tEncourage a friendly, respectful and inclusive atmosphere.\r\n•\tLook after the materials supplied by Neighbours to Friends CIC.\r\n•\tShare a short attendance and feedback update after each evening.\r\n\r\nThe game is an icebreaker. The real purpose is helping people meet, talk and form local connections.\r\n\r\nWhere would you volunteer? \r\nNear you, in your own community, anywhere in Scotland.\r\n\r\nSaw our poster at a restaurant?\r\nTell us the name and location. We would love to explore hosting the evenings there, subject to that restaurant's agreement and suitable arrangements.\r\n\r\nFound this opportunity online?\r\nTell us your town or local area. We will work with you to identify and agree a suitable nearby venue.\r\nYou do not need to find or pay for a room yourself, own equipment or travel to another city.\r\n\r\nWhat support is provided?\r\nFull training from scratch; a chance to practise before leading; ready-to-use game equipment and guides; advice on welcoming newcomers, running an inclusive session and recording attendance; help with venue arrangements and launch; and ongoing CIC support.\r\n\r\nWho can apply?\r\nAdults aged 18+ who are friendly, dependable, patient and willing to learn. You do not have to be an experienced entertainer or game expert. This is an unpaid, ongoing local volunteering role.\r\n\r\nCommitment: We aim for a recurring weekday evening. Timing and frequency will be agreed with the volunteer and confirmed venue before launch. Our community social evenings have no ticket fee for participants.\r\n\r\nReady to bring people together?\r\nClick 'I want to volunteer'. Please tell us your town or local area and, if you saw our poster at a restaurant, its name and location. If you found us online, that's absolutely fine — no venue is required to express interest.\r\n\r\nYou bring the wish to connect people. We provide the training, equipment and support.\r\n\r\nNeighbours to Friends CIC — Real People. Real Conversations. Stronger Communities.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous hosting or game experience is needed. We provide full training and step-by-step guidance. We welcome friendly, reliable people who care about their community and are willing to learn how to facilitate a welcoming group activity.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull induction and practical training are provided, including how to run the social game, welcome newcomers, encourage inclusive participation, use the equipment and complete a simple session record. All game materials, written guidance and ongoing support are supplied by Neighbours to Friends CIC.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nOngoing local volunteering, normally one recurring weekday evening, with the precise frequency and schedule agreed with the volunteer and venue before launch.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteer locally in your own Scottish community. If you saw our poster at a restaurant, we can explore hosting sessions there. Otherwise, Neighbours to Friends CIC will work with you to identify a suitable nearby venue. Regular long-distance travel is not expected.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HyTq9YAF#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Social Night Host – Bring People Together in Your Local Area (Scotland)",
                        "description": "No previous hosting or game experience is needed. We provide full training and step-by-step guidance. We welcome friendly, reliable people who care about their community and are willing to learn how to facilitate a welcoming group activity.",
                        "commitment": "Ongoing local volunteering, normally one recurring weekday evening, with the precise frequency and schedule agreed with the volunteer and venue before launch.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HyTq9YAF/volunteer-social-night-host-bring-people-together-in-your-local-area-scotland?#modal_register_a0gQD00000HyTq9YAF",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
