                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzMzVYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HzMzVYAV/local-social-connection-host-selkirk",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-08",
                    "title": "Local Social Connection Host - Selkirk",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHelp create a welcoming recurring social evening in Selkirk. You will welcome adults who may arrive alone and facilitate a simple structured social game that makes conversation easier.\r\n\r\nNeighbours to Friends CIC reduces loneliness by creating recurring face-to-face social connection points for adults aged 18+. \r\n\r\nAs the local host, you would support one recurring evening in Selkirk, welcome newcomers, explain and facilitate a simple social-deduction format, encourage respectful participation, look after reusable CIC materials, coordinate basic session practicalities and send a short session record afterwards. The game is the icebreaker, not the purpose: the role is about helping strangers become familiar faces. No previous game-hosting experience is required.\r\n\r\nThe CIC provides induction, a hosting guide, reusable materials and ongoing support. \r\nThis is an unpaid volunteer role with no commission, donation share, franchise or ownership. A suitable local host will be confirmed before final venue and date arrangements; we are already developing a potential Selkirk venue route.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous game-hosting experience is required. \r\n\r\nReliability, warmth, confidence speaking to a group of around 10-20 adults, good communication, respect for newcomers and willingness to follow simple guidance and light-touch session logging are most important.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe CIC provides induction, a clear hosting guide, reusable activity materials, session templates and a named central contact. We support the host through launch, answer practical questions and review light-touch session feedback so the local point remains welcoming and consistent.\r\n\r\nA named CIC contact is available before and after sessions. We plan a weekly check-in during launch, then support as needed once the local point is established.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nOne recurring weekday evening, normally approximately 18:30-21:30. Exact day will be agreed with the volunteer and a viable local venue; Monday to Thursday evenings are the current planning window.\n\n## Travel details\n\nLocal role in Selkirk. The final recurring venue will be confirmed with the volunteer. \r\n\r\nWe aim to use a suitable Selkirk venue and will share exact access and transport details before the first session\n\n## Taster details\n\nWe aim to reply within 3 days, arrange a short informal call, confirm availability and fit, provide induction and the hosting guide, then agree the local venue and first date. We do not publicly launch the point until both the volunteer and venue practicalities are confirmed.\r\n\r\nA short online induction and structured walkthrough are provided before first delivery. A live session is only scheduled once the volunteer and venue practicalities are ready.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
