                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I5aZxYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I5aZxYAJ/local-social-connection-host-bearsden",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-25",
                    "title": "Local Social Connection Host - Bearsden",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNeighbours to Friends CIC is a Scottish Community Interest Company that reduces loneliness and social\r\nisolation among adults aged 18+ by creating recurring face-to-face social connection opportunities. We use\r\na simple hosted social game as a structured way for strangers and newcomers to speak, interact, return\r\nand become familiar faces. Any surplus and programme assets are used for community benefit.\r\nDescribe the volunteering Opportunity\r\nSupport a recurring local social evening for adults. The volunteer host welcomes newcomers, explains and\r\nfacilitates a simple structured social-deduction game, keeps the atmosphere friendly and inclusive, and\r\nsends a light-touch session record afterwards. The CIC provides induction, reusable materials and ongoing\r\nsupport. No previous game-hosting experience is required. This is an unpaid community volunteering role.\r\nThe volunteer does not buy a franchise, own the local point or receive a share of donations. No delivery\r\nwill begin until a suitable local venue and appropriate insurance cover are confirmed.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly and reliable; comfortable welcoming a small group of adults and helping everyone take part; clear\r\ncommunication; able to follow a simple event structure and submit a brief session record. Local knowledge\r\nof East Dunbartonshire is helpful. No previous game-hosting experience is required\n\n## Training details\n\nA short induction covers the CIC social purpose, the event structure, welcoming and inclusion, basic safety\r\nexpectations, use of the reusable kit, participant communication and the simple evidence record. Written\r\nhost guidance is provided, with a named director contact for questions and support before the first session and during early delivery.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBearsden / East Dunbartonshire. We are recruiting someone who lives in, works in or regularly spends\r\ntime locally. A Bearsden hospitality venue has expressed interest, but the exact venue and dates are not\r\nyet confirmed. For this volunteer opportunity, the CIC will only confirm a delivery venue that has wheelchair\r\naccess and wheelchair-accessible toilets, and only after host suitability and insurance are checked.\r\nRegular long-distance travel is not expected.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
