            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Gn44TYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Gn44TYAR/hermes-junior-fc-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-24",
                    "title": "Hermes Junior FC Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHermes JFC is a semi professional football team based in the Bridge of Don area.\r\n\r\nAs the club continues to grow, we are actively seeking volunteers to join our team. We have a number of volunteer roles available in every area of the club including kit volunteers, match day helpers,  shop servers. All skill sets are welcome as training will be available. No experience required.\r\n\r\nVolunteers make a real, positive difference helping to ensure that we provide the best experience for our club, supporters and the wider community. It is an opportunity to make a difference in your community, support the growth of our club, be part of a great team, gain new skills and experience.\r\n\r\nThe benefits and satisfaction of volunteering and also being part of our team cannot be underestimated. Any help, any time given is hugely appreciated.\r\n\r\nIf you are interested, please reach out to us for more information on how you can get involved! Email Steven Watson, Manager at  steven.watson@heli-one.com\n\n## Description\n\nHermes JFC is a semi professional football team based in the Bridge of Don area.\r\n\r\nAs the club continues to grow, we are actively seeking volunteers to join our team. We have a number of volunteer roles available in every area of the club including kit volunteers, match day helpers,  shop servers. All skill sets are welcome as training will be available. No experience required.\r\n\r\nVolunteers make a real, positive difference helping to ensure that we provide the best experience for our club, supporters and the wider community. It is an opportunity to make a difference in your community, support the growth of our club, be part of a great team, gain new skills and experience.\r\n\r\nThe benefits and satisfaction of volunteering and also being part of our team cannot be underestimated. Any help, any time given is hugely appreciated.\r\n\r\nIf you are interested, please reach out to us for more information on how you can get involved! Email Steven Watson, Manager at  steven.watson@heli-one.com\r\n\r\nFurther details is also available on our Facebook page at https://www.facebook.com/Hermesjfc\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant guidance and excellent support provided to all volunteers. All skill sets are welcome as training will be available.  No experience required.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to suit volunteers. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
