        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000013CKf5YAG",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000013CKf5YAG/leap-sports-scotland",
            "name": "LEAP Sports Scotland",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/leapsports",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ITbZkYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ITbZkYAL/communications-assistant-volunteer-help-make-sport-more-inclusive",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-11",
                    "title": "Communications Assistant Volunteer – Help Make Sport More Inclusive",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCommunications Assistant Volunteer – Help Make Sport More Inclusive\n\n## Description\n\nWould you enjoy using your creativity and communications skills to promote equality in sport?\n\nLEAP Sports Scotland works to remove the barriers that prevent lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender, intersex and queer (LGBTIQ+) people from accessing and participating in sport. We&rsquo;re looking for volunteers to help share our work, promote our projects and events, and reach more people through engaging, accessible content.\n\nYou&rsquo;ll support our growing communications activity, primarily on social media. We&rsquo;re also keen to hear from people interested in producing newsletters and other content that helps us connect with communities, partners and supporters.\n\nWhat you could be doing\n\nDepending on your interests and skills, tasks may include:\n\n\n\tHelping create a content calendar to plan what we share, when we share it and which channels we use.\n\tDesigning graphics for Instagram and exploring content for other social media platforms.\n\tCapturing and editing short videos to showcase our work.\n\tAdding captions to videos to make our content more accessible.\n\tHelping develop newsletters and other communications, where this matches your experience and interests.\n\n\nWho would suit this role?\n\nThis opportunity would suit someone who enjoys creating digital content and wants to use their skills to support LGBTIQ+ inclusion in sport. Relevant skills and interests include:\n\n\n\tExperience of creating content for social media.\n\tAn interest in graphic design, video production or newsletter writing.\n\tFamiliarity with video captioning, or a willingness to learn.\n\tCreativity, organisation and the ability to work independently with staff guidance.\n\tA willingness to contribute an average of approximately two hours per week.\n\n\nYou don&rsquo;t need experience in every task listed. Training and support will help you develop your skills.\n\nTime commitment and location\n\nWe&rsquo;re ideally looking for approximately two hours per week on an ongoing basis, with no fixed end date.\n\nYou can volunteer from home at times that fit around your other commitments, or come into our office during working hours. We&rsquo;ll discuss suitable tasks and arrangements with you.\n\nTraining, support and benefits\n\nWe offer:\n\n\n\tRegular support and supervision from a designated staff member.\n\tTraining in content creation, video captioning, tracking engagement and other aspects of the role.\n\tOpportunities to build practical communications skills and experience for your CV.\n\tSupport in developing your CV.\n\tFlexible volunteering arrangements.\n\tThe opportunity to help more people discover inclusive sport and physical activity.\n\n\nHow to apply\n\nClick &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; to register your interest. We&rsquo;ll send you a link to our application form. Once you&rsquo;ve completed it, we&rsquo;ll arrange an informal chat to discuss your interests, availability and how you could get involved.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tGood written communication skills and an interest in creating engaging content.\n•\tExperience of using social media and understanding what makes an effective post.\n•\tCreativity and an interest in graphic design, video editing or newsletter writing.\n•\tAwareness of accessible communications, including video captions, or a willingness to learn.\n•\tGood organisational skills and the ability to work independently with staff support.\n•\tAn interest in equality and LGBTIQ+ inclusion in sport.\nYou\n\n## Travel details\n\n5 minute walk from Glasgow Central, 10 minutes from Queen Street, many bus routes nearby.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nLEAP Sports Scotland is committed to ensuring that volunteering does not leave individuals out of pocket. As such, efforts will be made to reduce any costs associated and reasonable expenses will be paid (full policy available on starting).",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ITbZkYAL#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Communications Assistant Volunteer – Help Make Sport More Inclusive",
                        "description": "•\tGood written communication skills and an interest in creating engaging content.\n•\tExperience of using social media and understanding what makes an effective post.\n•\tCreativity and an interest in graphic design, video editing or newsletter writing.\n•\tAwareness of accessible communications, including video captions, or a willingness to learn.\n•\tGood organisational skills and the ability to work independently with staff support.\n•\tAn interest in equality and LGBTIQ+ inclusion in sport.\nYou",
