        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000013RsLzYAK",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000013RsLzYAK/forfar-music-group",
            "name": "Forfar Music Group",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HQKHRYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HQKHRYA5/volunteer-champion-coordinator",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-22",
                    "title": "Volunteer Champion (Coordinator)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThis voluntary position is best for natural organisers who are great communicators and enjoy building a supportive community. The role offers a mix of lone working, and on-site working, giving you the flexibility to manage the rota and communications from our space, or from home. Additional tasks, responsibilities and projects are available for candidates willing to expand their role.\n\n## Description\n\nEnsure our volunteer team is happy, informed, and organised as we grow The Music Rooms.\r\n\r\n\r\nHow you will make a difference:\r\nRota Management: Use a simple app or spreadsheet to ensure we have enough cover for bookings and sessions, record volunteer hours and measure our impact.\r\nWelcome: Act as the first point of contact for new volunteers, showing them the ropes and introducing them to the team.\r\n\r\nCommunication: Send out a monthly update to the team so everyone knows what’s happening at the charity. Promote a positive atmosphere by providing regular feedback, and asking for theirs in return.\r\n\r\nSafety & Compliance: Help ensure all volunteers understand our safety protocols under our public liability insurance. You will handle volunteer records with care to ensure we remain GDPR compliant and maintain strict confidentiality.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining & Support: We want you to feel confident being the voice of FMG! We provide full training, including:\r\n●\tA brief on our charity’s mission, history, and current projects.\r\n●\tGuidance on data protection (GDPR) and how to handle community enquiries.\r\n●\tSupport with event safety and how to represent us effectively at stalls.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F44a863c8-a809-49d9-95d5-5303a905651c%2F7HnVR4w7ogcOWRip5OnuXQp8T2f1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=0515892c-9c27-4370-b428-b147cada994f",
