                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HQJYHYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HQJYHYA5/fmg-ambassador",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-22",
                    "title": "FMG Ambassador",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe require outgoing individuals who are passionate about our mission and happy to strike up a conversation. This role is highly flexible and may involve lone working (Such as when distributing leaflets/posters) or working as part of a team at events. Additional tasks, responsibilities and projects are available for candidates willing to expand their role.\n\n## Description\n\nRepresent our charity in the community and help secure the funds that keep our doors open and The Music Rooms thriving.\r\n\r\nHow you will make a difference:\r\nMarket Stalls: Help run stalls at external events, chatting with the public and handing out flyers to raise awareness of our work.\r\n\r\nCommunity Outreach: Distribute posters for upcoming gigs or workshops to local shops and cafes in Forfar. Talk about Forfar Music Group on social media and within your own community.\r\nCreative Input: Help brainstorm and organize fun ways to raise money, from jamming marathons to local raffle prizes.\r\n\r\nSafety & Compliance: As a representative of FMG, you’ll help us maintain a high standard under our public liability insurance. You will also ensure any member or donor information you handle remains GDPR compliant and strictly confidential.\r\n\r\n\r\nIf you love chatting about music and want to help us grow, please send a brief note to info@forfarmusicgroup.org. Or, alternatively, you can pop into our premises and fill out an application form.\n\n## Experience required\n\nTraining: Don’t worry if you aren’t a technical expert. We provide full training to ensure you are confident in:\r\n●\tOperating our specific lighting and security systems.\r\n●\tSetting up music equipment and how to pack away.\r\n●\tUnderstanding our safety protocols.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining & Support: We want you to feel confident being the voice of FMG! We provide full training, including:\r\n●\tA brief on our charity’s mission, history, and current projects.\r\n●\tGuidance on data protection (GDPR) and how to handle community enquiries.\r\n●\tSupport with event safety and how to represent us effectively at stalls.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F44a863c8-a809-49d9-95d5-5303a905651c%2F7HnVR4w7ogcOWRip5OnuXQp8T2f1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=0515892c-9c27-4370-b428-b147cada994f",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HQJYHYA5#role",
