                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H2C1hYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000H2C1hYAF/co-chair-trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-04",
                    "title": "Co-Chair Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nKlinefelter Syndrome Support Scotland is recruiting a volunteer Co-Chair Trustee to work alongside the Founder and Trustee team to help guide, lead, and grow a developing Scottish charity supporting individuals and families affected by Klinefelter syndrome.\n\nAbout Us\n\nKlinefelter Syndrome Support Scotland is a Scotland-based charitable organisation dedicated to improving awareness, understanding, well-being, inclusion, and long-term outcomes for individuals affected by Klinefelter syndrome (XXY) and related variations, together with their families, partners, carers, friends, educators, employers, healthcare professionals, and wider support networks.\n\nThe organisation was created in response to the significant lack of awareness, accessible information, emotional support, community connection, and long-term guidance available to individuals and families affected by Klinefelter syndrome across Scotland and beyond.\n\nOur organisation exists to help bridge the gap in awareness, support services for emotional well-being, fertility support, education and employment, healthcare navigation, and community connection currently experienced by many individuals and families affected by Klinefelter syndrome.\n\nThis role will help provide leadership, strategic direction, and operational support while helping shape the future growth and long-term development of the organisation.\n\nResponsibilities may include:\n\n• Helping lead strategic planning and organisational growth\n• Supporting trustee leadership and governance\n• Participating in major organisational decisions\n• Helping identify funding opportunities and funding applications\n• Supporting fundraising activities and partnership building\n• Helping oversee charity operations and development activities\n• Supporting awareness campaigns and community engagement work\n• Assisting with ad hoc administration activities\n• Helping build long-term sustainability plans\n• Working collaboratively with trustees to strengthen the organisation's future\n\nWe welcome individuals with leadership experience, governance experience, charity leadership, management, community development, healthcare, lived experience, communications, organisational development or strategic planning backgrounds.\n\nTrustees should be passionate about helping build long-term awareness, fertility support, health and wellbeing support, education support, employment support, community support, and meaningful change for individuals and families affected by long-term conditions such as Klinefelter Syndrome.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAdvocacy / Lobbying / Campaigning,Business / HR / Management,Community Development / Social work,Computer / IT / Web,Education / Training,Event Management / Organising,Fundraising,General Admin / Office Support,PR / Marketing,Research / Policies, Creative,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Hard Working,Organised,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Social Conscience,Team Player,Trustworthy,Leadership, strategic planning, partnership building, funding development, awareness campaigns, community engagement, and organisational growth experience are welcomed.\n\n## Training details\n\nCharity induction, trustee guidance, and ongoing support are provided.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire Yes\nAcross South Lanarkshire,Glasgow,North Lanarkshire",
