        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000013gNFuYAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000013gNFuYAM/the-corstorphine-trust",
            "name": "The Corstorphine Trust",
            "description": "The Corstorphine Trust is a local community association, based at The Corstorphine Heritage Centre (The Dower House) in St Margaret’s Park, Corstorphine.\r\n\r\nWe are dedicated to the stimulation of public interest in the character and history of Corstorphine and encourage the preservation, development and improvement of features of general public amenity or historic interest. The Corstorphine Trust also plays an important role in safeguarding and forwarding local planning issues.\r\nWe are a registered Scottish charity (charity number SC000913) and are non-political and non-sectarian. Membership is open to all who are interested in Corstorphine and its well being. It is administered by an executive committee, elected from its membership.\r\n\r\nThe Trust organise social events, musical evenings and talks to name but a few.  The live diary on our Room Hire page lists all the different events that take place.  Small publications and items of local interest are on sale. On the upper level of the Dower House is a small local history museum and archive of many things relating to Corstorphine past and present.\r\n\r\nIf you are interested in taking out a membership you can via our shop or by dropping into the Heritage Centre on a Wednesday or Saturday morning.",
            "website": "https://www.corstorphinetrust.co.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC000913"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HKwUIYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HKwUIYA1/treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-01",
                    "title": "Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Corstorphine Trust is a local community association, based at The Corstorphine Heritage Centre (The Dower House) in St Margaret’s Park, Corstorphine.\n\nOur current treasurer has intimated that they will retire at the 2027 AGM (around April time).  We are looking to bring someone on board as soon as possible so that we can give a full and proper handover to the successful candidate and offer them the opportunity to shadow the current treasurer.\n\nThis is a busy and absolutely essential role within the charity.  There are three trustee roles: chair, secretary and treasurer.  The charity is run by an executive committee of up to 10 people (this number includes the trustees).  The executive committee are all members of The Corstorphine Trust.\n\nThe following is a high level list of tasks that the treasurer undertakes through a calendar year.\n\nYEARLY\n\n- Start of the year hand over previous year’s Excel worksheets accountants along with: \n+ all previous year’s executive meeting minutes\n+ previous year’s draft AGM minutes\n+ bank statements up to and including 31 December Attend and present accounts to the AGM\n- Assuming accounts are approved at the AGM, upload to OSCR along with a letter of authority.\n- If applicable, reapply for water exemption.\n- After tax year end, apply to HMRC for gift aid and gift aid small donations scheme refunds. \n- As required - negotiate energy provider provider contracts.\n- June-ish - check prices with telephone and broadband provider.\n- November - Renewal notification received for insurance policy which renews in December. Ensure policy is still fit for purpose.\n\nMONTHLY\n\n- Schedule payments for caretakers and administrative assistant. \n- End of the month - If still appropriate, enter gas meter reading for hall.\n- Filing of receipts/paper invoices.\n- Check for memberships due to expire next month and (if not paid by s/o) send a reminder.\n\nWEEKLY\n\n- Bank any cash or cheques.\n- Ensure spreadsheets are up-to-date and reflect bank accounts.\n- Liaise with administrative assistant iro rental payments.\n- Check  inbox and deal with any enquiries.\n- Ensure cashflow is sufficient in bank accounts for bills etc.\n\nADHOC/Minders\n\n- Pay bills as required via online banking.\n- Get a receipt for EVERYTHING (even if it's on the back of a fag packet!).\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou must be fully computer literate and have a working knowledge of Excel and online banking.  Proof of these skills will have to be demonstrated.\n\n## Training details\n\nA full handover will be given to the successful candidate with the opportunity to shadow the current treasurer.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nSo long as they are carried out in a timely fashion, the various tasks undertaken by the treasurer can be carried out whenever and wherever is suitable.  Our committee meetings are held monthly on a Wednesday evening and it would be essential and expected that the successful candidate would be able to attend the majority of these.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Corstorphine Trust is based in The Dower House (Corstorphine Heritage Centre), St Margaret's Park, Edinburgh EH12 7SX.\n\n## Taster details\n\nSee above.",
