                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HY9DbYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HY9DbYAL/alvn-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-30",
                    "title": "ALVN Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Ayrshire Litter Volunteer Network established in 2014, is a community based partnership of like-minded individuals who have great concern for the quality of their local environment; aiming to promote greater community responsibility towards the disposal of their rubbish.\r\n\r\nALVN is looking for a volunteer editor, with significant Facebook experience, to take ALVN forward by sharing individuals and groups posts in an interesting, eye catching and encouraging manner, to promote and encourage the efforts of volunteers, so  others consider joining in with existing groups or as individuals.\r\n\r\nThere are currently 864 followers and the objective is to increase these significantly.  The volunteer must be a resident in Ayrshire and will liaise with all three Ayrshire Councils where necessary.",
