        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000014Ex2SYAS",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000014Ex2SYAS/radio-south-west-cic",
            "name": "Radio South West CIC",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/RadioSouthWestCIC",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzODJYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HzODJYA3/social-media-volunteer-radio-south-west",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-06",
                    "title": "Social Media Volunteer – Radio South West",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSocial Media Volunteer – Radio South West\n\n## Description\n\nRadio South West CIC is a new community-focused radio station being developed to connect people, amplify local voices and support communities across Greater Glasgow and South West Scotland.\n\nWe are looking for a creative, enthusiastic and reliable Social Media Volunteer to help us build and grow our presence across social media and digital platforms.\n\nThis is an exciting opportunity to become part of Radio South West at an early stage and help shape how the station connects with listeners, volunteers, community groups, local organisations and the wider community.\n\nYou will help promote Radio South West, share our stories and activities, create engaging content, support campaigns and events, and help grow our online audience and community presence.\n\nYou do not need to have professional social media experience. We are interested in people who are creative, enjoy social media, have ideas to share and are willing to learn and contribute.\n\nThe role can be carried out primarily remotely, with opportunities to become involved in station activities, community events and projects as Radio South West develops.\n\nThis is initially a voluntary position. As Radio South West CIC develops and secures funding, we hope to be able to offer paid opportunities to members of the team, subject to funding being available.\n\nIf you are interested please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for a creative, enthusiastic and reliable person who is interested in social media and digital communications.\n\nThe following skills and qualities would be valuable:\n\nGood knowledge of social media platforms, such as Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, X or LinkedIn.\nCreativity and the ability to come up with engaging ideas for posts, campaigns and digital content.\nGood communication skills, with the ability to communicate clearly and positively with different audiences.\nContent c",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HzODJYA3#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Social Media Volunteer – Radio South West",
                        "description": "We are looking for a creative, enthusiastic and reliable person who is interested in social media and digital communications.\n\nThe following skills and qualities would be valuable:\n\nGood knowledge of social media platforms, such as Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, X or LinkedIn.\nCreativity and the ability to come up with engaging ideas for posts, campaigns and digital content.\nGood communication skills, with the ability to communicate clearly and positively with different audiences.\nContent c",
