                    "publishStart": "2026-06-08",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-07",
                    "title": "Trustee (Board Member)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Lochs is a new and developing charity supporting the mental health and wellbeing of people in our community through accessible counselling services. They require trustees to join their Board and guide the organisation as it grows. Trustees play a vital role in ensuring the charity is well-run, sustainable, and focused on its purpose.\r\n\r\nThey welcome individuals who are passionate about mental health and supporting others. No previous board experience is required—just a willingness to contribute your time, skills, and ideas. They are particularly interested in people with experience in areas such as governance, finance, mental health, legal or compliance, communications, community engagement, and digital systems, who can work collaboratively, bring thoughtful contributions, and are committed to making a difference. They value diversity and warmly encourage applications from people of all backgrounds and experiences. This is a rewarding opportunity to join a supportive board and have a meaningful impact in your community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous trustee experience is required as support will be provided. Knowledge and experience of HR/people management, funding applications, finance, governance, marketing, compliance or digital skills would be beneficial.\r\n\r\n\r\nA passion for mental health and wellbeing, a desire to support people in need, reliable with the ability to act with integrity and use a thoughtful, supportive approach, think collaboratively and contribute to group discussions\n\n## Training details\n\nAn induction will be provided to help you understand the role of a trustee and the work of The Lochs. Ongoing support will be available through regular board meetings, guidance from the Chair, and access to relevant training where appropriate.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMeetings are mainly held online via Zoom, with occasional in-person meetings in Fife (accessible venues).\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses need to be agreed in advance and will be reimbursed at 45p per mile or public transport rates following submission of an expenses claim form and receipts.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HBeZqYAL#role",
