            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000014PVXKYA4",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000014PVXKYA4/forth-valley-visually-impaired-bowlers",
            "name": "Forth Valley Visually Impaired Bowlers",
            "description": "The objectives of the Club are to further the physical and mental health of all blind or partially sighted persons in Fourth Valley to ameliorate their suffering and distress and to aid them in their handicaps specifically by promoting and encouraging their participation in, and playing of the game of bowls.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC013106"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SensoryImpairment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HE8woYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HE8woYAD/bowls-support-volunteer-for-visually-impaired",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-09",
                    "title": "Bowls Support Volunteer (for Visually Impaired)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nForth Valley Visually Impaired Bowlers are a group of people who are blind/partially sighted who play indoor and outdoor bowls in the Forth Valley.  They meet once a week for a 2 hour bounce game. \r\nDuring summer months they play at Larbert Bowling Club and during the winter months at Falkirk Indoor Bowling Centre.\r\n\r\nForth Valley Visually Impaired Bowlers are looking for volunteers to help assist the visually impaired bowlers during the two hour bounce game.  Volunteers would act as a guide and assist with the following: \r\n* getting bowlers on and off the green\r\n* guiding from one end of the green to the other\r\n* helping to pick up bowls\r\n* helping bowlers to understand where their bowl has landed using the clock system (full training is given).\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly, patient and helpful people who enjoy a bit of fun. Bowling experience would be beneficial but not essential.\n\n## Training details\n\nThere will be practical induction involving shadowing and instruction from experienced bowling directors. Ongoing support will be given by members of the committee.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2 hours weekly or fortnightly\r\nFridays 1-3pm (summer)\r\nWednesdays 1-3pm (winter)\n\n## Travel details\n\nLarbert Bowling Club, Pretoria Road, Larbert FK5 4NB (summer)\r\nFalkirk Indoor Bowling Club, Glasgow Road, Camelon, Falkirk FK1 4HJ (winter)\r\nAccessible via train and bus service. Parking is available.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are NOT available.",
