            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HFJ29YAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HFJ29YAH/squirrels-section-volunteer-team-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-10",
                    "title": "Squirrels Section Volunteer Team Member",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteers Wanted – Help Us Launch Squirrels at Tannadice Scouts! 🐿️\r\nWe’re excited to be looking at starting a new Squirrel Scout section at the 22nd Angus (Tannadice) Scout Group, and we’re looking for some friendly volunteers to help make it happen!\n\n## Description\n\nSquirrels is the youngest section in Scouts for children aged 4–6, focused on fun, games, adventures, crafts, outdoor activities and helping young people gain confidence and life skills from an early age.\r\n\r\nWe’re looking for adults from the local community who could spare a little time each week to help run sessions. No previous Scouting experience is needed at all — just enthusiasm, reliability and a willingness to get involved. Full training and support will be provided.\r\nYou could help with:\r\n🐿️ Running games and activities\r\n🎨 Crafts and creative activities\r\n🔥 Outdoor adventures\r\n☕ Helping behind the scenes\r\n😊 Supporting young people to have fun and grow in confidence\r\nVolunteering can be flexible, and even helping occasionally can make a huge difference.\r\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to help bring something new and valuable to local children and families in Tannadice and the surrounding area.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous Scouting experience is needed at all — just enthusiasm, reliability and a willingness to get involved. Full training and support will be provided.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
