                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HFM6TYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HFM6TYAX/explorers-section-volunteers-team-members",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-10",
                    "title": "Explorers Section Volunteers Team Members",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nYou could help with:\r\n-Running games and activities\r\n-Crafts and creative activities\r\n-Outdoor adventures\r\n-Helping behind the scenes\r\n-Supporting young people to have fun and grow in confidence\r\n\r\nVolunteering can be flexible, and even helping occasionally can make a huge difference.\r\n\r\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to help bring something new and valuable to local children and families in Tannadice and the surrounding area.\n\n## Description\n\nExplorers is the eldest section in Scouts for children aged 14–17, focused on Games, Adventures, crafts, outdoor activities and helping young people gain confidence and life skills for the next stages in life.\r\n\r\nWe’re looking for adult volunteers from the local community who could spare a little time each week to help weekly meetings and support larger events such as camps and trips away.\r\n\r\nNo previous Scouting experience is required but any and all skills you do bring are very valuable. over all Enthusiasm, reliability and a willingness to get involved is all a volunteer needs.\r\n\r\nFull training and support will be provided.\r\n\r\nYou could help with:\r\n-Running games and activities\r\n-Crafts and creative activities\r\n-Outdoor adventures\r\n-Helping behind the scenes\r\n-Supporting young people to have fun and grow in confidence\r\n\r\nVolunteering can be flexible, and even helping occasionally can make a huge difference.\r\n\r\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to help bring something new and valuable to local children and families in Tannadice and the surrounding area.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous Scouting experience is required but any and all skills you do bring are very valuable. over all Enthusiasm, reliability and a willingness to get involved is all a volunteer needs.\r\n\r\nFull training and support will be provided.",
