            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HFSgXYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HFSgXYAX/volunteer-with-girlguiding-in-cults",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-28",
                    "title": "Volunteer with Girlguiding in Cults",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGirlguiding Scotland is the leading charity for girls and young women in Scotland, with over 35,000 young members supported by 9,000 amazing volunteers. Girlguiding helps members discover their full potential by having fun and enjoying new adventures.\r\n\r\nAre you enthusiastic about giving girls opportunities for fun, friendship, challenge and adventure? If the answer is yes, then you’d make a great Girlguiding volunteer in Cults! \r\n\r\nWhether you want to help with a specific event, on a casual or remote basis, or attend regularly; you can be involved in a way that works for you, suiting your skills, interests and availability. \r\n\r\n-What you'll be doing: \r\n\r\nThere are lots of roles to choose from, we are always looking for youth group leaders, helpers, admin and support roles! Get in touch and we can find something that works for you.\r\n\r\n\r\n-You might: \r\n\r\n- Help directly with girls in your community, giving them a space to discover their potential – whether that’s at your local groups regular meetings, at one-off events, on trips or adventures!\r\n\r\n- Be the behind-the-scenes superhero that makes the magic of guiding happen in one of our supporting roles. Admin could include anything from keeping records up to date remotely to communicating with girls’ parents and carers about the exciting adventures coming up.\r\n \r\n- Share a specific skill or passion – to teach girls new things or help guiding run locally. Perhaps you play football and could run a one-off session for girls? Maybe you could lend your DIY skills to help with the upkeep of your local guiding building? Or if you’re a finance or communications whizz, could you help manage accounts or run a local group’s social media?  \r\n\r\nThere are no specific skills required - we welcome volunteers from all backgrounds and experiences. Just bring yourself and your enthusiasm. All volunteers make a real difference and are greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nPlease apply to volunteer at:  https://volunteer.girlguiding.org.uk/#/vacancylist/Interests=CAT-01000%2CCAT-01001%2CCAT-01002%2CCAT-01004%2CCAT-01005%2CCAT-01018&Postcode=Cults&Distance=5&AgeGroups=CAT-01017%2CCAT-01018%2CCAT-01019%2CCAT-01020%2CCAT-01095&DayAvailability=CAT-01002%2CCAT-01001%2CCAT-01003%2CCAT-01004%2CCAT-01005%2CCAT-01006%2CCAT-01007&TimeAvailability=CAT-01014%2CCAT-01015%2CCAT-01016&UnderEighteen=false&LocationCoordinates.lat=0&LocationCoordinates.long=0&LocationCoordinates.location=\r\nor\r\nFor more information please email cults@girlguidingaberdeenshetland.org.uk\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to help. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated. Unit meetings are usually once a week for around an hour plus prep time.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F7ba29801-0b44-4414-be3e-4d7e71675897%2FT1R0ZE5D6ZWXeJglY1nBViaV6pI3%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=1a2382e7-8cc8-4d92-bfcd-eb8e89b494a7",
