        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000014pkXeYAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000014pkXeYAI/boom-saloon",
            "name": "Boom Saloon",
            "description": "Boom Saloon is a non-profit, global media movement to democratise creativity for good, driven by our international members. We explore the UN's Sustainable Development Goals through the lens of creativity – this work supports a series of community projects which inspire and empower people facing challenges.",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H18UpYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000H18UpYAJ/bookshop-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Bookshop Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nLove books and love people? Help launch boom saloon's new pop-up bookshop in Leith. Every Saturday morning you'll open the doors, share our story and put our publications in the hands of new readers. 6hrs/week, Edinburgh.\n\n## Description\n\nBoom Saloon is an independent publisher using paper and ink to drive social change. We are launching a pop-up bookshop in Leith, Edinburgh, showcasing our publications alongside those from our global community. Our Bookshop Volunteer will set up the space each Saturday, man the shop, take sales, manage stock, speak to customers, share the boom saloon story and close down at the end of the morning – bringing our publications to new readers and turning browsers into buyers.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers complete a full onboarding to welcome them to boom saloon, with regular 121s utilised to deliver ongoing support. Free dementia awareness training is offered alongside ad hoc opportunities specific to the role and an internal mentor scheme.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe pop-up bookshop will be located at Brown's of Leith, a home for makers on the Shore. The nearest public transport routes are tram to Port of Leith (Ocean Drive - 275m) or Shore (Constitution St - 375m) or bus to Shore or Sandport St stops. Taxi drop off is available outside. There is limited on street paid parking in the area. The nearest blue badge on street parking is about 285m away on Burgess Street. Venue entrance is step free but has dropped kerbs onto cobbles. Wheelchair accessible toilets.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel Expenses",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H18UpYAJ#role",
