        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000014tRMhYAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000014tRMhYAM/west-lothian-litter-pickers",
            "name": "West Lothian Litter Pickers",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HVBlNYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HVBlNYAX/social-media-coordinator",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-27",
                    "title": "Social media Coordinator",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe West Lothian Litter Pickers are looking for a volunteer with social media experience to help grow\r\nour online presence and support our community environmental work.\r\nWe are a friendly volunteer-led group with over 4,000 members on Facebook who organise litter picks\r\nand environmental improvement activities across West Lothian. While Facebook has helped us build a\r\nfantastic community, we would love support expanding onto other platforms such as Instagram,\r\nTikTok, X, LinkedIn, or others that could help us reach more people.\r\nWhat the role could involve:\r\n• Advising the group on social media strategy\r\n• Setting up and managing additional social media accounts\r\n• Creating engaging posts, reels, or short videos\r\n• Promoting local litter picks and events\r\n• Sharing environmental news and success stories\r\n• Supporting positive community engagement online\r\nWhat you’ll gain:\r\n• Experience supporting a large community organisation\r\n• A chance to make a visible local impact\r\n• Opportunity to shape and grow our online presence\r\n• Be part of a supportive and motivated team\r\nThis is a voluntary position, but the impact you can make will be huge.\r\nIf you are interested, please send us a message through our Facebook page telling us a little about\r\nyourself and your experience.\n\n## Experience required\n\nHas experience using social media platforms effectively\r\nIs creative and enthusiastic\r\nHas good communication skills\r\nUnderstands community engagement\r\nCan volunteer a few hours each week remotely\r\nShares our passion for improving West Lothian",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
