                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Sexuality",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sexuality"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hwx17YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hwx17YAB/helpline-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-26",
                    "title": "Helpline Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are recruiting volunteers to support the smooth running of our LGBTQ+ Helpline. The Helpline provides emotional support, information, and signposting services to LGBTQ+ adults and their friends, family, and professionals. Volunteers answer calls, emails and live online webchats. They provide emotional support, information, and signposting to LGBTQ+ callers and those questioning their sexuality/gender as well as anyone supporting someone from the LGBTQ+ community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA good understanding of LGBTQ+ identities and the issues affecting a wide range of LGBTQ+ people. Excellent communication skills via telephone, email and live chat. Capacity to offer emotional support to others. A compassionate, patient, and non-judgemental approach. Self-awareness and ability to reflect. The ability to sensitively, supportively and confidently discuss topics including sex and relationship issues, sexual health, gender identity and transition, abuse, and emotional distress.\n\n## Training details\n\nMandatory in-person in Edinburgh 3-day Induction: Friday 30th October 2026 4pm - 8pm and Saturday 31st October 2026 10.30 am - 5.30pm and Sunday 1st November 2026 10.30am - 5.30pm\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n3 hours per week is required, ideally for at least 12 months. Each helpline shift lasts 3 hours. You will typically be on shift with a fellow volunteer each time (and/or the Helpline Coordinator will be available).\n\n## Travel details\n\nWill be home-based as helpline is delivered remotely. May be some scope to deliver from our office bases in central Edinburgh or Glasgow. If so full details will be provided. Support for remote set-up will be provided.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses on receipt of form and receipts. Helpline Coordinator can support with submitting expenses.\n\n## Taster details\n\nThere is mandatory 3-day in-person training for this role on Friday 30th October 2026 4pm - 8pm Saturday 31st October 2026 10.30 am - 5.30pm and Sunday 1st November 2026 10.30am - 5.30pm",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2F4VEV6Pihf3Pe96BHnpHd6Twimak2%2FNpg35AK1MrzKbUxC-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=a6ed3745-02dd-4b20-9c40-f7ac4823317d",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hwx17YAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Helpline Volunteer",
                        "description": "A good understanding of LGBTQ+ identities and the issues affecting a wide range of LGBTQ+ people. Excellent communication skills via telephone, email and live chat. Capacity to offer emotional support to others. A compassionate, patient, and non-judgemental approach. Self-awareness and ability to reflect. The ability to sensitively, supportively and confidently discuss topics including sex and relationship issues, sexual health, gender identity and transition, abuse, and emotional distress.",
                        "commitment": "3 hours per week is required, ideally for at least 12 months. Each helpline shift lasts 3 hours. You will typically be on shift with a fellow volunteer each time (and/or the Helpline Coordinator will be available).",
                        "applyLink": "https://lgbthealth.org.uk/volunteer/helpline-volunteer/",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": true,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/LGBT",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "LGBT"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/MentalHealth",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                            }
                        ],
                        "service": [
                            {
