        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000015KZG6YAO",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000015KZG6YAO/danestone-and-persley-community-council",
            "name": "Danestone and Persley Community Council",
            "description": "A Community Council is a voluntary organisation set up by statute by the local authority and run by local residents to act on behalf of its area.  As the most local tier of elected representation, community councils play an important role in local democracy.\r\nComprised by people who care about their community and want to make it a better place to live. They represent all people in the area equally.\r\nThey must ascertain and express the views of the community to local authorities and public bodies and to take action which is in the interests of its community. They should have a positive working partnership with the local authority.",
            "website": "https://www.facebook.com/p/Danestone-and-Persley-Community-Council-100091095893396/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityCouncil",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Council"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityFacilities",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Facilities"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityForum",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Forum"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunitySafety",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Safety"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEngagement",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Engagement"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEvent",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Event"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HTW9BYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HTW9BYAX/volunteer-administrator",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-21",
                    "title": "Volunteer Administrator",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nA Community Council is a voluntary organisation set up by statute by the local authority and run by local residents to act on behalf of its area.  As the most local tier of elected representation, community councils play an important role in local democracy.\r\n\r\nDanestone and Persley Community Council would like to support an individual that is interested in local democracy and community resilience, at the grassroots level to assist us with administration tasks. This will involve working with the Community Councillors, taking action notes; responding to correspondence and social media support.\r\n\r\nThe Community Council meetings take place every 6 weeks at Danestone Community Centre, Fairview Street, Aberdeen AB22 8ZP.  Meetings last approximately 2 hours and can be attended remotely.\r\n\r\nRelevant training is provided and the volunteer will have full support from the Community Council.  We can organise training from ACVO/TSI on relevant training required by the volunteer.\r\n\r\nA fantastic, enjoyable opportunity to help make a difference for people and the community. All help is greatly appreciated. For more information please contact Lyndsay Johnstone, Chairperson at email: danestonecommunitycouncil@gmail.com or telephone: 01224828333\r\n\r\nMore information about Danestone and Persley Community Council is also available at https://www.facebook.com/people/Danestone-and-Persley-Community-Council/100091095893396/\n\n## Description\n\nA Community Council is a voluntary organisation set up by statute by the local authority and run by local residents to act on behalf of its area.  As the most local tier of elected representation, community councils play an important role in local democracy.\r\n\r\nDanestone and Persley Community Council would like to support an individual that is interested in local democracy and community resilience, at the grassroots level to assist us with administration tasks. This will involve working with the Community Councillors, taking action notes; responding to correspondence and social media support.\r\n\r\nThe Community Council meetings take place every 6 weeks at Danestone Community Centre, Fairview Street, Aberdeen AB22 8ZP.  Meetings last approximately 2 hours and can be attended remotely.\r\n\r\nRelevant training is provided and the volunteer will have full support from the Community Council.  We can organise training from ACVO/TSI on relevant training required by the volunteer.\r\n\r\nA fantastic, enjoyable opportunity to help make a difference for people and the community. All help is greatly appreciated. For more information please contact Lyndsay Johnstone, Chairperson at email: danestonecommunitycouncil@gmail.com or telephone: 01224828333\r\n\r\nMore information about Danestone and Persley Community Council is also available at https://www.facebook.com/people/Danestone-and-Persley-Community-Council/100091095893396/\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. \r\n\r\nThe volunteer will have full support from the Community Council.  We can organise training from ACVO/TSI on relevant training required by the volunteer.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to help. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Community Council meetings take place every 6 weeks at Danestone Community Centre,  Fairview Street, Aberdeen AB22 8ZP.  Meetings last approximately 2 hours and can be attended remotely.",
