        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000015ZNEkYAO",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000015ZNEkYAO/portobello-town-hall",
            "name": "Portobello Town Hall",
            "description": "Portobello Town Hall is a registered charity, overseen by a volunteer Board of Trustees. Our focus is to ensure that the Town Hall is a well-managed community asset complying with the charitable purposes in our constitution. \r\n\r\nOur focus is on maintaining and developing the Town Hall and the surrounding grounds as recreational facilities to enhance citizenship, improve lives and develop our communities.\r\n\r\nThis can be in areas such as arts, heritage, culture and science.\r\n\r\nWe have a membership of people who are interested in the building and what happens in there.  Please consider becoming a member.\r\n\r\nA board of volunteer trustees are elected at our annual general meeting (AGM) to run the charity and who are responsible to the membership.\r\n\r\nWe currently have a small staff team, a board of trustees and an active volunteer community. If you are able to help with the running of the Town Hall please complete our volunteer form\r\n\r\nWe’d love to have a really wide and active membership and volunteer base.",
            "website": "https://www.portobellotownhall.org/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC051106"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityFacilities",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Facilities"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HYKEeYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HYKEeYAP/treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-30",
                    "title": "Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Treasurer plays a key role in supporting the financial health, transparency and long-term sustainability of Portobello Town Hall. As part of the board of trustees the Treasurer helps ensure that our  finances are properly managed, accurately reported and aligned with our charitable aims as a community and cultural hub in Portobello.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPerson Specification\n•\tAn interest in supporting Portobello Town Hall’s charitable and community purpose.\n•\tGood financial awareness and the ability to interpret financial information confidently.\n•\tExperience in bookkeeping, budgeting, accounting or financial management.\n•\tAbility to communicate financial information clearly to non-financial colleagues.\n•\tAttention to detail, sound judgement and a commitment to accuracy and transparency.\n•\tAbility to work collaboratively with trustees, staff, volunteers and external advisers.\n•\tUnderstanding of good governance and a willingness to meet relevant legal and regulatory responsibilities.\n•\tReliability, integrity and a commitment to acting in the best interests of the organisation.\n\n## Training details\n\nWhat the Role Offers\n•\tThe opportunity to make a meaningful contribution to an important local community venue.\n•\tA chance to use and develop financial, governance and leadership skills.\n•\tThe satisfaction of helping support arts, culture and community activity in Portobello.\n•\tOur current Treasurer will provide a full handover and be available to assist after standing down in November.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nTime Commitment and Accountability\nThis is voluntary role. The Treasurer is expected to attend regular meetings, contribute to financial planning and review, and provide additional support at key points in the financial year such as budget setting, year-end accounts and annual reporting.\n\n## Travel details\n\na mix of home working and meetings at Portobello Town Hall",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FSbEPeDGYcIbXuUYxpuG6EQ0WJny2%2FlYeHEQsYwwltr7eX-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=03726b0f-6b68-43de-b99b-91e9f05ac26b",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HYKEeYAP#role",
                        "type": "Role",
