                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SensoryImpairment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HuK8jYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HuK8jYAF/group-facilitator",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-16",
                    "title": "Group Facilitator",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe need Group Facilitators to run groups for autistic girls aged 13-18 in Dundee. Create a safe, validating space for autistic girls, and support them to share experiences and worries. Plan craft and other activities, games and chats. Sessions run fortnightly for 90 minutes in small groups of 10-15 girls.\n\n## Description\n\nRun, or help run, a peer support group for autistic teen girls to make friends, build a positive autistic identity, play games or do crafts to support the conversations. \r\n\r\nOur groups are co-produced so we encourage you to get the girls involved in planning sessions. We will provide resources on a variety of topics from alexithymia to interoception and everything autism related. \r\n\r\nWe have opportunities for people to set up the group right form the very start including finding the right venue and planning when and how it will run. \r\n\r\nWe will also need volunteers to support these groups as well once they are open. These will be our first groups in Scotland so it is a great opportunity to be involved right from the beginning and provide the support you may not have had as an autistic teenage girl.\r\n\r\nWe are a neurodivergent led charity\n\n## Experience required\n\nAutistic women are especially encouraged to apply.\n\n## Training details\n\nWelcome to the Autistic Girls Network, Autistic Girls Network Values, Basic Safeguarding for Children and Young People, GDPR and Data Protection, Health and Safety.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note - No travel expenses are payable for this opportunity.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HuK8jYAF#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Group Facilitator",
                        "description": "Autistic women are especially encouraged to apply.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HuK8jYAF/group-facilitator?#modal_register_a0gQD00000HuK8jYAF",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
