        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000015yqwRYAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000015yqwRYAQ/dress-for-success-scotland",
            "name": "Dress For Success Scotland",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/DressForSuccessScotland",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hei3lYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hei3lYAB/client-styling-boutique-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-03",
                    "title": "Client Styling & Boutique Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nClient Styling & Boutique Support Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nJoin Dress for Success Scotland as a Boutique Volunteer and play a hands-on part in helping women across Scotland step into work and life with confidence.\n\nThis is a varied, no-two-days-the-same role at the heart of our boutique. Your main focus will be our one-to-one suiting service: welcoming women, learning about their style, goals, and the occasion ahead, whether that&#39;s an interview, a new job, training, or another important milestone, and guiding them through a styling session. Each woman leaves with a complete outfit, from clothing and a coat to shoes, a bag, accessories, and beauty essentials, chosen to help her feel comfortable, capable, and ready for what&#39;s next. When a client secures employment, she&#39;s welcomed back for a capsule wardrobe so she can start work without spending her first pay packet on clothes.\n\nAlongside styling, you&#39;ll help keep the boutique running beautifully with tasks such as sorting and organising clothing donations, steaming and ironing garments, keeping fitting rooms and displays tidy, and making sure the space always feels warm, inviting, and professional. There may also be chances to lend a hand with administration, workshops, and events when they come up.\n\nYou don&#39;t need any formal fashion qualifications to thrive here. What matters is a genuine desire to help, a welcoming manner, and an eye for putting people at ease. We&#39;ll work with you to find the tasks that suit your strengths, so your time with us feels enjoyable, fulfilling, and genuinely makes a difference.\n\nOur boutique is open Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, 10am&ndash;4pm. We usually ask volunteers to commit to one day a week or fortnightly, though we&#39;re happy to be flexible as long as you keep us in the loop. Right now we&#39;re especially keen to hear from anyone who can join us on Wednesdays&nbsp;as it&#39;s the day we most need a helping hand!\n\nWe&#39;re committed to being a welcoming and inclusive space for everyone. Our boutique is disability-friendly and accessible by lift. If you have any access needs or would like to chat about how we can support you to volunteer with us, please just let us know.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA keen eye for style and a passion for empowering others\nFriendly, empathetic, and patient, with a willingness to learn\nAble to build trust and rapport with clients from diverse backgrounds\nHappy to work independently and as part of a team\nComfortable rolling up your sleeves for practical tasks (sorting, steaming, tidying)\nCommitted to equity, diversity, and inclusion\nAble to uphold confidentiality and our values at all times\nNo formal fashion qualifications required — just a genuine desi\n\n## Travel details\n\nNext to Buchanan Galleries, if you enter Bath Street and go in the Albert Chambers (the door before Jungle Rumble Adventure Golf), come to the 5th floor (lift available), and turn right, you will see the Dress for Success logo on the door. Press buzzer 7 and someone will let you in. There is a lift you have to take for floor 5.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAny travel to and from volunteering is payable at the end of each month with receipts of travel or screenshots of payments from bank app.",
