            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I1gsTYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I1gsTYAR/events-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-12",
                    "title": "Events Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCrosshouse Children's Fund is the charity for babies, children and young people in hospital in Ayrshire and Arran. From the tiniest babies in the neonatal unit at Ayrshire Maternity, to the children's wards at Crosshouse and across the community - Crosshouse Children's Fund is for Ayrshire's children in hospital. Each year more than 25,000 babies, children and young people from across Ayrshire and Arran are treated in the hospitals we support. Funds raised bring the very latest medical equipment to Ayrshire, help families navigate their child's journey, and help children cope in hospital.With the help of communities across Ayrshire and Arran, Crosshouse Children's Fund has already invested more than £430,000 in life-changing projects; but there is so much more to do.\r\nOur events raise vital funds to ensure babies, children, and young people in Ayrshire and Arran receive the best possible care in hospital. The charity supports children in the neonatal unit, maternity unit, and children's wards by providing enhanced equipment, funding projects, and creating comfortable, welcoming environments.\r\n\r\nCrosshouse Children’s Fund host lots of varied events and activities throughout the year and these are only possible with the support of our amazing volunteers. From holding a bucket outside Rugby Park to helping support our pop-up shop at Craig Tara, we have something for everyone! What's great too is that this role is very flexible, you pick and choose what you would like to be involved in and the time you can give to that activity.\r\n\r\nAs this role involves working alongside our team to interact with supporters and the general public, we are looking for sociable and outgoing volunteers to apply. Want to bring a friend or family member along with you to volunteer? Great! The more the merrier!\r\n\r\nIf you’d like more information before registering your interest, please get in touch with our Volunteer Team:\r\nEmail: volunteer@glasgowchildrenshospitalcharity.org\r\nPhone: 0141 212 8750\n\n## Experience required\n\n• Each event has different tasks associated with it, volunteers will get a full view of what’s involved with each event prior to signing up.\r\n•\tAble to commit to scheduled shifts\r\n•\tPunctual, dependable, and able to follow instructions\r\n•\tFriendly, approachable, and confident interacting with the general public\r\n•\tWilling to work collaboratively with staff and other volunteers\n\n## Training details\n\n•\tAll volunteers receive a full induction before their first shift.\r\n•\tTraining includes:\r\n-\tHealth & safety procedures for the event\r\n-\tBasic cash handling procedures\r\n-\tCustomer service guidance for interacting with supporters\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nNo minimum commitment required. You will be required on an ad hoc basis, as times for each event will vary. You will be alerted weekly of volunteering opportunities and can select an event accordingly.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n•\tTravel expenses reimbursed",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F62f30039-3e53-41d1-9555-ad3177802f34%2Fk8IiWFy67AR4lXg90w0e0kIeGug2%2Fheader.jpg?alt=media&token=5edc9d32-a55b-4176-ad36-7d3422f37b23",
