                    "title": "Events Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCrosshouse Children’s Fund host lots of varied events and activities throughout the year and these are only possible with the support of our amazing volunteers. From holding a bucket outside Rugby Park to helping man our pop-up shop at Craig Tara, we have something for everyone! What's great too is that this role is very flexible, you pick and choose what you would like to be involved in and the time you can give to that activity.\r\n\r\nOur events raise vital funds to ensure babies, children, and young people in Ayrshire and Arran receive the best possible care in hospital. The charity supports children in the neonatal unit, maternity unit, and children's wards by providing enhanced equipment, funding projects, and creating comfortable, welcoming environments.\r\n\r\nIf you’d like more information before registering your interest, please get in touch with our Volunteer Team:\r\nEmail: volunteer@glasgowchildrenshospitalcharity.org\r\nPhone: 0141 212 8750\n\n## Experience required\n\n• Each event has different tasks associated with it, volunteers will get a full view of what’s involved with each event prior to signing up.\r\n•\tAble to commit to scheduled shifts\r\n•\tPunctual, dependable, and able to follow instructions\r\n•\tFriendly, approachable, and confident interacting with the general public\r\n•\tWilling to work collaboratively with staff and other volunteers\n\n## Training details\n\n•\tAll volunteers receive a full induction before their first shift.\r\n•\tTraining includes:\r\no\tHealth & safety procedures for the event\r\no\tBasic cash handling procedures\r\no\tCustomer service guidance for interacting with supporters\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nNo minimum commitment required. You will be required on an ad hoc basis, as times for each event will vary. You will be alerted weekly of volunteering opportunities and can select an event accordingly.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n•\tTravel expenses reimbursed",
