        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000016QDyiYAG",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000016QDyiYAG/ayrshire-litter-network-volunteers-north-ayrshire",
            "name": "Ayrshire Litter Network Volunteers - North Ayrshire",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hlp8XYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hlp8XYAR/volunteer-editor",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-13",
                    "title": "Volunteer  Editor",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Ayrshire Litter Volunteer Network (ALVN), established in 2014 (website closed 2016), is a Community based partnership of like-minded individuals who have great concern for the quality of their local environment; aiming to promote greater community responsibility towards the disposal of their rubbish.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nALVN is looking for a volunteer editor, with significant Facebook experience, to take ALVN forward by sharing individuals & groups posts in an interesting, eye-catching and encouraging manner, to promote and encourage the efforts of volunteers, so encouraging others to consider joining in with existing Groups or as individuals  All this without spending money. Volunteer litter-pickers are starting to come forward as they see the occupation is no longer eccentric.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThe person applying must have a concern for the appearance of Ayrshire, be of a responsible age and wishes to effect a change in attitudes. There are 864 followers today. The objective is to increase these significantly.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nExpanding into other media, will be at the discretion of the volunteer, to reach a wider audience - the Irresponsible? \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThey must be resident in Ayrshire and will liaise with all three Ayrshire Councils where necessary, contacts will be provided.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hlp8XYAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer  Editor",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hlp8XYAR/volunteer-editor?#modal_register_a0gQD00000Hlp8XYAR",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/LocalAuthority/NorthAyrshire",
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "North Ayrshire"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000016QYeqYAG",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000016QYeqYAG/gulab-sorkh-foundation",
            "name": "Gulab Sorkh Foundation",
            "description": "Gulab Sorkh is a UK-based organisation supporting Afghan families as they rebuild their lives in Britain.  We connect newly arrived Afghan families with volunteers, local communities, and the resources they need to feel at home.\r\n\r\nWe want the Afghans we work with to settle into the UK as quickly as possible and maximise their potential. By doing so, they will become fully contributing members of UK society. We help them with their basic needs when they arrive in the UK, advise them on the British way of life, help them steer their way through the bureaucracy and access services and signpost educational and vocational training opportunities for them.",
            "website": "https://www.gulabsorkh.org/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/HousingHomelessnessness",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Housing / Homelessnessness"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SelfHelpSupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Self-Help / Support"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEngagement",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Engagement"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HsHuvYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HsHuvYAF/community-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-08",
                    "title": "Community Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAs part of the Government led Communities for Afghans programme, we are looking to recruit individuals or groups (UK BASED ONLY) to make up a team of 6 volunteers to support an Afghan family - you could be friends, neighbours, colleagues, faith groups, veterans, or community organisations are welcome.  \r\n\r\nWe are currently focused on supporting families across Wales, West Midlands and Scotland but be keen to support elsewhere geographically where possible.  With this in mind, you may live in these areas, but we are also delighted to bring volunteers together remotely to support a family. \r\n\r\nYou will be at the heart of this programme. It is a rewarding opportunity to make a real difference!\r\n\r\nThe Communities for Afghans programme is a community-led Government initiative supporting families as they rebuild their lives in the UK. It is a Government-approved scheme that enables local people to welcome Afghan refugee families into their community. Volunteers will be supported by us to find housing for a family, provide practical and emotional support enabling them to settle into daily life and feel a genuine sense of belonging in the community.\r\n\r\nHow community sponsorship work\r\n\r\nForm a Sponsor Group: Create a team of six or more volunteers — friends, neighbours, colleagues, faith groups, veterans, or community organisations.\r\nTraining & Ongoing Support: Our partners provide full training, so your group feels confident and well prepared. This simple, practical training is offered before you begin and continues throughout the sponsorship journey.\r\nIdentify Suitable Housing: With our guidance, your group helps find long-term accommodation. We then match an Afghan family of the appropriate size and ensure the property is suitable and affordable. Government funding is available for rent deposits and related costs.\r\nWelcome & Support the Family: Volunteers help the family register with schools, healthcare, benefits, and local services, while introducing them to the community and supporting them as they adjust to life in the UK.\r\nBe the Local Point of Contact: You act as the family’s trusted guide, helping them navigate the area, understand local systems, and access opportunities that only residents truly know.\r\nCommit for Three Years: Sponsor groups support the family for three years, providing consistency as they grow in independence, confidence, and resilience.\r\nWhy Your Support Matters\r\n\r\nVolunteering through Community Sponsorship is a powerful act of solidarity. You are not only helping one family — you are strengthening your entire community.\r\n\r\nYour support helps families: \r\n\r\nRebuild their lives in safety and dignity\r\nAccess education, healthcare, and employment\r\nLearn English and integrate into the community\r\nBecome confident and independent\r\nAnd your community benefits:\r\n\r\nStronger local connections\r\nCelebrated diversity\r\nPractical meaningful humanitarian action\r\nFull training and expenses covered.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training and DBS check provided",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HsHuvYAF#role",
                        "type": "Role",
