        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000016kdTuYAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000016kdTuYAI/nhs-24-engagement",
            "name": "NHS 24 Engagement",
            "description": "NHS 24 is a national Health Board which provides a range of services to people across Scotland. These services are available via the telephone, webchat, websites, and a mobile phone app.",
            "website": "https://www.nhs24.scot/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Helplines",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Helplines"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HnEUfYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HnEUfYAN/youth-forum-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-19",
                    "title": "Youth Forum Member",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nMake your voice count in the NHS 24 Youth Forum! NHS 24 are looking for young volunteers to help ensure that our services are designed with the people who use them in mind.\n\n## Description\n\nMake your voice count in the NHS 24 Youth Forum! NHS 24 are looking for young volunteers to help ensure that their services are designed with the people who use them in mind.\r\n\r\nAs an NHS 24 Youth Forum Member you will:\r\n-have regular opportunities to share your views on NHS 24’s work\r\n-be able to influence their strategy\r\n-help them to focus on what matters most to people\r\n-help share information about NHS 24 services within your local community\r\n-be part of a team dedicated to improvement\r\n-be treated as a colleague who actively contributes to NHS 24’s goals through volunteering\r\n\r\nNHS 24 welcome any young person aged 16 to 26 that is passionate about reducing health inequalities and is interested in shaping the future of their services.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNHS 24 is committed to creating an inclusive environment where everyone feels valued, respected, and able to contribute. They welcome young people from diverse backgrounds, cultures, identities, and experiences, including disabled people and members of the LGBTQIA+ community.\r\nTo be a Youth Forum Member you do not need any specific skills or experience. They do ask that you are:, committed to attend as many meetings as possible; open and willing to share your opinions and feedback; interested in addressing health inequalities; professional and timely in your communication; and willing to attend meetings with your camera on.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction will be held online currently planned for w/c 28th September.\r\nMembers will have access to non-role specific NHS 24 introductory training.\r\nMembers will be supported by a minimum of 3 staff.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMainly online, with the occasional in-person meeting, for which all travel expenses would be paid.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses include travel, food and accommodation when attending in-person meetings only.",
