        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000016ncUsYAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000016ncUsYAI/centred",
            "name": "Centred",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HndT3YAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HndT3YAJ/volunteer-walk-leaders",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-20",
                    "title": "Volunteer Walk Leaders",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nClarity Walk is one of our free initiatives here at Centred. The service offers free group walks in and around Inverness for people experiencing isolation, loneliness, or mental and/or physical health issues. The walks provide a supportive, inclusive space to connect with others in nature. The walks are open to everyone, although many participants do experience physical, mental, or social challenges.\r\n\r\nAbout the Walks\r\n- Open to everyone\r\n- Range of walks from gentle 2-mile walks, up to half-day hikes\r\n- Inclusive and supportive for all abilities\r\n\r\nWe’re looking for friendly, reliable volunteers to help lead walks.\r\n- Commit to as little as 2 walks per month\r\n- Full training provided\r\n- Must be approachable, reasonably fit, and confident working with diverse groups\r\n- Driving license and access to own vehicle is a plus\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training will be provided",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F87febcdd-15ed-41a1-8141-4f522c4c3797%2FFj5stk1rvJMukwYKvmprkcLrhUo1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=3a04b488-436f-4c0c-b092-9a1394d8bf19",
