        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000uBylTYAS",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000uBylTYAS/generations-working-together",
            "name": "Generations Working Together",
            "description": "GWT is the nationally recognised centre for excellence for the development and integration of intergenerational work across Scotland. It facilitates 16 local networks across Scotland, supporting practitioners from a wide range of fields interested or engaged in intergenerational practice. Networks meet twice a year, allowing members and those new to GWT to connect with other groups and organisations in their local community. GWT further raises awareness of intergenerational practice through events such as learning Roadshows the annual conference and Global IG Week.  GWT also delivers training and creates publications to support intergenerational practice.",
            "website": "https://generationsworkingtogether.org/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC045851"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000E9OUTYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000E9OUTYA3/volunteer-intergenerational-community-connector",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-05",
                    "title": "Volunteer Intergenerational Community Connector",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nJoin GWT in its vision to live in a Scotland where generations are more connected and help us on our mission to develop, expand and improve intergenerational practice across Scotland. If you would like to get more involved in intergenerational working, learn more about the practice and help grow intergenerational relationships in your local area this is the volunteering role for you. Let's work together and help create more intergenerational communities.\n\nAs a volunteer Intergenerational Community Connector for GWT core tasks include\n*Supporting one of our development team in planning and facilitating 2 – 3 network meetings a year in your local area.\n*Raising awareness of the benefits of intergenerational practice within your local network.\n*Sharing and promoting current GWT network meetings, events, publications, and training .\n*Connecting with your local community and encourage organisations and groups to share their intergenerational projects with their local network and GWT.\n\nVolunteers will have the opportunity to further develop their own knowledge and understanding of intergenerational practice through training as well as attending other GWT events.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Good Communicator,Organised,Reliable / Dependable,Team Player,\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction of the role from GWT.\nOne to one support with a named GWT employee.\nFree access to a wide range of training, both online and in person to develop greater knowledge and understanding of intergenerational practice.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire Yes\nAcross South Lanarkshire\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n45p per mile for use of own car, this is reimbursed monthly.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000E9OUTYA3#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Intergenerational Community Connector",
                        "description": "No Expertise, Good Communicator,Organised,Reliable / Dependable,Team Player,",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000E9OUTYA3/volunteer-intergenerational-community-connector?#modal_register_a0gQD00000E9OUTYA3",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": true,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
