        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000wPCzBYAW",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000wPCzBYAW/bowel-cancer-uk",
            "name": "Bowel Cancer UK",
            "website": "https://volunteer.engagerenfrewshire.org/profile/BowelCancerUK",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0aQvYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I0aQvYAJ/early-diagnosis-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-10",
                    "title": "Early Diagnosis Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nEarly Diagnosis Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nOur exciting new early diagnosis programme needs your support. We&rsquo;re working with local health partners across the UK, to run a yearlong programme of activities to improve early diagnosis. We&#39;ll be bringing local communities together to help more people spot bowel cancer symptoms early and increase bowel screening uptake.\n\nThis role focuses on the awareness side getting people talking about bowel cancer, feeling better informed, and confident about taking action for their health.\n\nIt&rsquo;s a one-year role and a great fit for anyone passionate about bowel cancer awareness. A personal connection to the cause is helpful but not required.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nWhy we want you\n\nOur exciting new early diagnosis programme needs your support.\n\nWe&rsquo;re working with local health partners across the UK, to run a year-long programme of activities to improve early diagnosis. We&#39;ll be bringing local communities together to help more people spot bowel cancer symptoms early and increase bowel screening uptake.\n\nIt&rsquo;s a one-year role and a great fit for anyone passionate about bowel cancer awareness. A personal connection to the cause is helpful but not required for this role.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nWhat you will be doing\n\n\n\tDeliver health stands and awareness talks within the local community\n\tAnswer questions the general public may have on bowel cancer symptoms and screening following guidance set out from Bowel Cancer UK\n\tEstablish connections with local organisations and community groups, ensuring any contacts are passed to your role manager\n\tEnsure information in the local community is relevant and up-to-date and carry out any relevant awareness tasks (such as putting up posters) that will support this work\n\tMonitor the progress of your activities and report back to the Early Diagnosis team\n\tWork alongside other local volunteers to share ideas, learnings and develop plan for future activity\n\tBe able to signpost to Bowel Cancer UK support and services\n\tAct as an ambassador for Bowel Cancer UK at a local level, displaying energy, enthusiasm and commitment to our aims\n\n\n&nbsp;\n\nThe skills you need\n\n\n\tExcellent interpersonal, listening and communication skills\n\tConfident speaking to the general public\n\tAbility to confidently carry out your role independently and reliably\n\tEnthusiastic and approachable\n\tAble to communicate with people from various backgrounds and with different levels of understanding\n\tAn understanding of the importance of confidentiality and data protection\n\n\n&nbsp;\n\nWhat&#39;s in it for you\n\n\n\tAwareness training around bowel cancer, signs and symptoms of bowel cancer and bowel screening programmes\n\tExperience of speaking to the general public and promoting public health initiatives\n\tKnowing you&rsquo;re making a difference by helping to increase early diagnosis of bowel cancer by raising vital awareness of signs, symptoms and screening\n\tRole specific training including but not limited to: GDPR, safeguarding and presentation skills\n\tRegular virtual and in-person volunteer social opportunities (optional)\n\tOngoing support from our dedicated staff\n\tRegular news, updates and development opportunities via the volunteer portal\n\tExpenses covered in line with our volunteer expense policy\n\n## Experience required\n\nExcellent interpersonal, listening and communication skills\nConfident speaking to the general public\nAbility to confidently carry out your role independently and reliably\nEnthusiastic and approachable\nAble to communicate with people from various backgrounds and with different levels of understanding\nAn understanding of the importance of confidentiality and data protection\n\n## Travel details\n\nTravel expenses payable as per our expenses policy\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses payable as per our expenses policy",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0aQvYAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Early Diagnosis Volunteer",
                        "description": "Excellent interpersonal, listening and communication skills\nConfident speaking to the general public\nAbility to confidently carry out your role independently and reliably\nEnthusiastic and approachable\nAble to communicate with people from various backgrounds and with different levels of understanding\nAn understanding of the importance of confidentiality and data protection",
