            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000F1XsYYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000F1XsYYAV/scout-group-team-leader-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Scout Group Team Leader Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCan you make it possible for young people aged 10-14 to experience life changing adventures and support them in decision making, taking the lead and developing independence, confidence and skills?\r\n\r\nWe are looking for enthusiastic Scout Leader Volunteers to grow a small Scout Troop.  Based in our own Scout Hut in Kincorth, we cover the whole south side of Aberdeen.  \r\n\r\nWorking as part of a team of adult volunteers you will help to deliver an exciting programme of outdoor activities, community projects, games and challenges,  learning about global issues and going on local, regional, national and even sometimes international camps and trips.\r\nCurrently the Scouts meet on a Thursday evening but this can be changed to suit your availability.  Full training and support will be given by the Scouting organisation and existing members of the 55th.  \r\n\r\nVolunteering can be a brilliant way to boost your mental wellbeing and it's a great feeling knowing you are helping young people get skills for life.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Claire Stewart, Cub Team Member at email: clairestewart75@hotmail.co.uk\r\n\r\nMore details are also available at https://www.facebook.com/55thKincorthScoutGroup\n\n## Description\n\nCan you make it possible for young people aged 10-14 to experience life changing adventures and support them in decision making, taking the lead and developing independence, confidence and skills?\r\n\r\nWe are looking for enthusiastic Scout Leader Volunteers to grow a small Scout Troop.  Based in our own Scout Hut in Kincorth, we cover the whole south side of Aberdeen.  \r\n\r\nWorking as part of a team of adult volunteers you will help to deliver an exciting programme of outdoor activities, community projects, games and challenges,  learning about global issues and going on local, regional, national and even sometimes international camps and trips.\r\n\r\nCurrently the Scouts meet on a Thursday evening but this can be changed to suit your availability.  Full training and support will be given by the Scouting organisation and existing members of the 55th.  \r\n\r\nVolunteering can be a brilliant way to boost your mental wellbeing and it's a great feeling knowing you are helping young people get skills for life.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Claire Stewart, Cub Team Member at email: clairestewart75@hotmail.co.uk\r\n\r\nMore details are also available at https://www.facebook.com/55thKincorthScoutGroup\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided to all volunteers.\r\n\r\nFull training and support will be given by the Scouting organisation and existing members of the 55th.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to suit volunteers. All help greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe have our own Scout Hut in Kincorth.  Kincorth Circle, Aberdeen AB12 5NX.  Free street parking outside and a nearby bus route.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
