                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-05",
                    "title": "SSPCA Micro-volunteer (18+)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWhy we want you\nThe Scottish SPCA needs your help to make Scotland the best place for all animals to live!\n\nVolunteering with the Scottish SPCA is a wonderful thing to do, not only for Scotland's animals in need and the people in your local community, but also for you!\n\nThis role is deigned to be completely flexible - fit it in around your busy life to suit you! You can choose to simply share our news and campaigns with a monthly online task, or if you feel like getting a bit more involved now and again, we will keep you up-to-date with events and other initiatives in your area\n\nSo, what are you waiting for?\n\nSign up to be an SSPCA Micro-volunteer today and be part of the rescue!\n\nPlease not: this role does not involve directly working with animals in our care\n\nDid you know that it costs us £63,000 per day to look after all the animals in our care? As an SSPCA ambassador, you will help ensure that we can continue to provide our vital services.\n\nWhat you will be doing\nOnline tasks - want to help, but only got a few minutes to spare? Why not help us by simply sharing information and campaigns on your social media channels? These quick and easy tasks can be done on your phone from home or anywhere you like!\n\nCommunity Events - Join our fabulous Community Engagement Team at events near you and help us spread the word about the SSPCA's great work and services! We attend local galas, shows, visit community groups and run pop-up events in all sorts of places! Short on time? You can help by simply handing a flyer in to your local cafe or supermarket or telling people about our work.\n\nFundraising - Help us to put the 'fun' into fundraising by joining our amazing Regional Fundraising Team for an event or two. Everything from bucket shakes to adrenaline events, or why not set up your own small event in your local community? Fundraising is a great way to meet people in your community while raising much needed cash for animals in need\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Organised,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Trustworthy,The skills you need\nEnthusiasm... Lots of it!\nAbility to use social media channels (for online posts)\nAn understanding of the Society's work - we will give you training!\nA pleasant and polite manner when dealing with the public\nConfidence to interact with other people\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be asked to complete some online training relevant to the role. After completion, you will receive full induction and training. Our Regional Fundraising Lead will support you to become confident attending events, while our volunteering team will support you with online tasks.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire Yes\nAcross South Lanarkshire\n\n## Travel expenses\n\n45p per mile (HMRC rate) up to 30 miles per day for events or up to £15 for costs on public transport per day (receipt/ticket required)",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
