        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000xU30AYAS",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000xU30AYAS/hamilton-district-twinning-association",
            "name": "Hamilton District Twinning Association",
            "description": "Hamilton District Twinning Association (HDTA) was formed in 1993 with the aim of preserving the centuries old links between the towns of Hamilton in Scotland and Châtellerault in France. HDTA's aim is to maintain the bonds of friendship between the two towns through reciprocal visits. Nevertheless, their main activities are within the local community.\n\nThe HDTA seeks to arrange events for their membership to socialise and support each other. To this end, the members attend regular meetings and after the meetings they socialise with tea or coffee. The association also have lunches and the committee arranges social events for the members and their friends. In the past away trips, sometimes with an overnight stay, were organised.\n\nIt is 33 years since HDTA was founded and has been very active within the community during that time.",
            "website": "https://hamiltontwinningassociation.weebly.com/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HtJHxYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HtJHxYAN/social-media-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-18",
                    "title": "Social Media Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHamilton District Twinning Association (HDTA) aims to maintain and preserve the centuries old links and cultural exchange between the towns of Hamilton in South Lanarkshire and Châtellerault in France. HDTA organise group visits for members to Châtellerault as part of a twinning visit, with a reciprocal visit by the French group to Hamilton the alternate year.\n\nWe are looking for a volunteer to build and manage our Facebook platform, to keep up to date and increase awareness of HDTA throughout Lanarkshire via Social Media. \n\nNo need to be an expert just a person who has basic IT skills with the ability to communicate.\n\nWhat you will be doing\nSome tasks you may be able to get involved with:\n• Writing posts for Facebook or any other Social Media platforms that may be relevant.\n• Keep our  Social Media pages up to date.\n• Monitoring  Social Media for likes, comments, notifications etc and responding appropriately \n• Devising campaigns for expanding awareness and  suggest new ways to assist in attracting new members.\n• Communicate with the Committee on social media issues.\n• Attend meetings\n\n## Experience required\n\nJornalism / Media, Good Communicator,Organised,\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a South Lanarkshire opportunity and takes place in   Yes\nAcross South Lanarkshire,Hamilton",
