                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hsyv3YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hsyv3YAB/sewing-volunteers-needed",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-08",
                    "title": "Sewing Volunteers Needed",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSewing Volunteers Needed\n\n## Description\n\nThe Preshal Trust is a charity dedicated to supporting people facing poverty, addiction, mental health struggles, and isolation. Based in Govan and Paisley, we provide practical help, emotional support, and a safe space to rebuild lives. Through a wide range of programmes, we aim to uplift, empower, and strengthen our local communities.\n\nWe are currently looking for a volunteer sewing tutor to lead a sewing class at our Paisley Centre.\n\nClass Details:\n\n\nWhen: Every Wednesday afternoon\nLocation: 20 Neilston Road, Paisley, PA2 6LN\nEquipment: We provide sewing machines and all necessary materials.\n\n\nTo learn more about The Preshal Trust, please visit www.preshaltrust.org.uk.\n\nIf you are interested in volunteering or would like more information, please contact us at admin@preshaltrust.org.uk.\n\nWe would love to hear from you!\n\n&nbsp;",
