        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000017ykUuYAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000017ykUuYAI/nhs-24",
            "name": "NHS 24",
            "website": "https://www.nhs24.scot/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HtIIfYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HtIIfYAN/youth-forum-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-11",
                    "title": "Youth Forum Member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNHS 24 is a national Health Board which provides a range of services to people across Scotland. These services are available via the telephone, webchat, websites, and a mobile phone app.\r\n\r\nAs an NHS 24 Youth Forum Member you will:\r\n• have regular opportunities to share your views on our work\r\n• be able to influence our strategy\r\n• help us to focus on what matters most to people\r\n• help share information about NHS 24 services within your local community\r\n• be part of a team dedicated to improvement\r\n• be treated as a colleague who actively contributes to NHS 24’s goals through volunteering\r\n\r\nWho should apply:\r\n1. We welcome any young person aged 16 to 26 that is passionate about reducing health inequalities and is interested in shaping the future of NHS 24 services.\r\n2. NHS 24 is also committed to creating an inclusive environment where everyone feels valued, respected, and able to contribute. We welcome young people from diverse backgrounds, cultures, identities, and experiences, including disabled people and members of the LGBTQIA+ community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe have no required skills or experience for this volunteer opportunity, however our expectations are that volunteers should be:\r\n• available in the evenings\r\n• commit to attend as many meetings as possible and engage with our work\r\n• be open and willing to share your opinions and feedback on NHS 24 work in a constructive and helpful way\r\n• be interested in addressing health inequalities\r\n• communicate in a timely and professional manner with staff\r\n• have access to a device with video calling capabilities (e.g. Teams)\r\n• be willing to attend meetings with your camera on\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be invited to attend an online induction where you will meet other new applicants for the Youth Forum Member volunteer role. Training is provided through NHS 24, non-role specific online modules.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nRoughly 3hrs every 2 months.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMainly online via Teams, with occasional (infrequent) in-person meetings.  The last couple of in-person meetings have been in Glasgow, for which travel expenses have been covered.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses will only be incurred for infrequent in-person meetings and in line with expenses policy.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://appnhs24wp222b8656a3.blob.core.windows.net/blobappnhs24wp222b8656a3/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/NHS24.svg",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HtIIfYAN#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Youth Forum Member",
                        "description": "We have no required skills or experience for this volunteer opportunity, however our expectations are that volunteers should be:\r\n• available in the evenings\r\n• commit to attend as many meetings as possible and engage with our work\r\n• be open and willing to share your opinions and feedback on NHS 24 work in a constructive and helpful way\r\n• be interested in addressing health inequalities\r\n• communicate in a timely and professional manner with staff\r\n• have access to a device with video calling capabilities (e.g. Teams)\r\n• be willing to attend meetings with your camera on",
                        "commitment": "Roughly 3hrs every 2 months.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HtIIfYAN/youth-forum-member?#modal_register_a0gQD00000HtIIfYAN",
