        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000018ABpzYAG",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000018ABpzYAG/the-preshal-trust",
            "name": "The Preshal Trust",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/ThePreshalTrust",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hwfk9YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hwfk9YAB/baking-class-leader-on-friday-morning-in-govan",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-23",
                    "title": "Baking Class Leader on Friday Morning in Govan",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBaking Class Leader on Friday Morning in Govan\n\n## Description\n\nMake a difference in your community with The Preshal Trust\n\nWould you like to give some of your time, share your skills and help make a positive difference in your local community?\n\nThe Preshal Trust is a community charity working in Govan and Paisley, providing practical, emotional and spiritual support in a safe and welcoming environment.\n\n&lsquo;Preshal&rsquo; is Gaelic for &lsquo;precious&rsquo;, reflecting the Trust&rsquo;s belief that every individual should be valued and supported. Through community activities, learning opportunities and practical support, Preshal helps people build confidence, develop skills and feel more connected to their community.\n\nThe Trust provides a wide range of activities, including arts and crafts, cooking, sewing, IT, literacy and numeracy, board games and quizzes, as well as opportunities for people to come together socially.\n\nWe are looking for a friendly and enthusiastic volunteer who enjoys baking and would like to help deliver baking classes at our Govan community centre on Friday mornings.\n\nWhat could you get involved in?\n\nAs a volunteer, you will help to deliver baking classes and spend time with members of our community on Friday mornings.\n\nYou&#39;ll have the opportunity to:\n\n\n\tShare your baking skills and knowledge with others.\n\tHelp guide and encourage people as they learn and take part.\n\tHelp create a friendly, relaxed and enjoyable environment.\n\tEncourage people of different abilities to get involved and have a go.\n\tShare ideas for things the group could bake together.\n\tYou don&#39;t need to be a professional baker or teacher. If you enjoy baking, have the practical skills to show others how to bake and would be comfortable supporting people to take part, we&#39;d love to hear from you.\n\n\nWho would this role suit?\n\nThis opportunity could be ideal for someone who enjoys baking and would like to share their skills with others in a community setting.\n\nIt would particularly suit someone who is:\n\n\n\tFriendly, patient and encouraging.\n\tConfident in their baking skills and comfortable showing others what to do.\n\tHappy to meet, engage with and support different people.\n\tAble to explain things in a clear and supportive way.\n\tKeen to help create a welcoming and inclusive environment.\n\tReliable and available to volunteer on Friday mornings.\n\n\nYou don&#39;t need previous teaching or workshop experience &ndash; what matters most is an enthusiasm for baking, a willingness to share your skills and an interest in helping others enjoy taking part.\n\nTraining, Support &amp; Supervision\n\nBefore you start, you&#39;ll have an informal chat with a member of our team to discuss the role, your interests and availability. You&#39;ll then receive an induction and ongoing support throughout your volunteering.\n\nTraining is provided, including Food Hygiene training, and we will support you with the PVG check where required.\n\nOur team will be available to answer questions, provide guidance and make sure you feel comfortable and supported in your role.\n\nAnd while you&#39;re volunteering with us, you can enjoy morning tea and toast and a delicious lunch as part of your day with the team!\n\nWhen and where?\n\nThe opportunity takes place at:\n\nThe Preshal Trust &ndash; Govan Centre\n8 Aboukir Street, Glasgow\nFriday mornings\n\nThe Govan Centre is open Monday to Friday, 9:00am&ndash;4:00pm.\n\nFurther details about the Friday morning time commitment can be discussed directly with The Preshal Trust.\n\nApplying\n\nIf you&#39;re interested in becoming a Baking Class Leader, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered with Volunteer Glasgow).\n\nWhat happens after I apply?\n\nAfter you apply, a member of The Preshal Trust team will contact you by email or telephone to arrange an informal chat.\n\nThis gives you an opportunity to:\n\n\n\tFind out more about the Baking Class Leader role.\n\tDiscuss your baking experience, interests and ideas.\n\tTalk about your availability on Friday mornings.\n\tAsk any questions you have about volunteering with Preshal.\n\n\nIf you and The Preshal Trust are both happy to proceed, you&#39;ll then be supported through the induction and relevant training, including Food Hygiene training and the PVG process where required, before getting started.\n\nIf you haven&#39;t heard back within five working days, please contact The Preshal Trust using the contact details provided. It&#39;s also worth checking your email junk/spam folder in case their response has been directed there.\n\nIf you&#39;re still unable to make contact, please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org for further support.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tGood practical baking skills and confidence sharing them with others. \n•\tFriendly, patient and encouraging. \n•\tComfortable demonstrating and explaining baking techniques. \n•\tGood communication and people skills. \n•\tAble to create a welcoming and inclusive environment. \n•\tWilling to follow food hygiene and kitchen safety guidance. \n•\tReliable and available on Friday mornings. \n•\tEnthusiastic about helping others learn, participate and enjoy baking. \nYou don't need to be a professional b\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Preshal Trust has volunteering opportunities at its centres in Govan and Paisley, both of which are accessible by public transport.\n\nGovan Centre:\n8 Aboukir Street, Glasgow. The centre is within walking distance of Govan Subway Station and is served by local bus services in the Govan area.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nUnfortunately, we cannot reimburse volunteers for their travel expenses. However, we do provide tea, toast, and community lunches, which volunteers are welcome to have while they are here.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hwfk9YAB#role",
