                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HvqphYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HvqphYAB/workshop-leaders",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-01",
                    "title": "Workshop Leaders",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWorkshop Leaders\n\n## Description\n\nMake a difference in your community with The Preshal Trust\n\nWould you like to give some of your time, share your skills and help make a positive difference in your local community?\n\nWorkshop Leader Needed - Art and Craft, Sewing, Baking, Cooking...\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\nThe Preshal Trust is a community charity based in Govan and Paisley, providing practical, emotional and spiritual support within a safe and welcoming environment.\n\nThe word &lsquo;Preshal&rsquo; is Gaelic for &lsquo;precious&rsquo;, reflecting the Trust&#39;s belief in the value of every individual who comes through its doors.\n\nThe Trust provides a wide range of community support, learning opportunities and activities. These include arts and crafts, cooking, sewing, IT, literacy and numeracy, board games, quizzes and opportunities for people to come together socially.\n\nWe are looking for friendly and reliable volunteers who can deliver the workshops in The Preshal Trust.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nWhat could you get involved in?\n\nWe are looking for friendly and enthusiastic people who are willing to voluntary&nbsp;deliver workshops in our community centre&nbsp;and spend time with members of our community.\n\nYou will need to:&nbsp;\n\n\n\tShare a hobby, interest or skill with others.\n\tLead&nbsp;a workshop or activity. You will have support and guidance from a member of our team, so you don&#39;t need to do it alone.\n\n\nWorkshops could include arts and crafts, sewing, cooking, baking, photography, or anything else you would enjoy sharing with our community.\n\nYou don&#39;t need to be an expert or professional. If you have a skill, hobby or interest that you think others would enjoy, we&#39;d love to hear your ideas.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nTraining, Support &amp; Supervision\n\nIn terms of training, support and supervision, prospective volunteers will first have an informal chat with the team to discuss the opportunity and make sure the role is a good fit. If they are happy to proceed, they will receive an induction covering their role, the activities they may be involved in and the support available to them.\n\nThroughout their time volunteering with The Preshal Trust, the staff team will be available to provide ongoing support, guidance and supervision and to answer any questions that may arise.\n\nAnd while you&#39;re volunteering with us, you can enjoy a delicious lunch and morning tea and toast as part of your day with the team!\n\n&nbsp;\n\nWhen and where?\n\nOpportunities are available through Preshal&#39;s centres in Govan and Paisley.\n\nGovan Centre\n8 Aboukir Street, Glasgow\nOpen Monday to Friday, 9:00am&ndash;4:00pm\n\nPaisley Centre\n20 Neilston Road, Paisley, PA2 6LN\nOpen Monday, Wednesday and Friday,&nbsp;9:00am&ndash;4:00pm\n\nVolunteer availability and what you would like to get involved with can be discussed directly with the Preshal Trust.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nWhat happens next?\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered).\n\nYou will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or telephone to discuss your interest in volunteering and how you might like to get involved.\n\nIf you have not heard back after five working days, the first step is to contact the organisation using the contact details provided. Please also check your email junk/spam folder in case their response has been directed there.\n\nIf you are still unable to make contact, please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nBasic English\n\n## Travel details\n\ntrain, bus and underground travel links to Govan",
