                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hvqo5YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hvqo5YAB/kitchencatering-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-01",
                    "title": "Kitchen/Catering Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nKitchen/Catering Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nMake a Difference in Your Community with The Preshal Trust\n\nWould you like to give some of your time, meet people in your local community and help make sure people have access to a warm, welcoming meal?\n\nWe are looking for a&nbsp;Kitchen/Catering Volunteer for to support with preparing and serving Community Meals.&nbsp;\n\nThe Preshal Trust is a community charity based in Govan and Paisley, providing practical, emotional and spiritual support in a safe and welcoming environment.\n\nThe Trust brings people together through community support, activities, learning opportunities and shared meals. Our centres are welcoming spaces where people can meet others, enjoy a meal and receive support when they need it.\n\nWe are looking for friendly, reliable and caring volunteers to support our community kitchen and help us provide meals for local people.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nHow can you help?\n\nOur community kitchen is an important part of what we do, and volunteers help us make it possible.\n\nYou could get involved with a range of tasks, including:\n\n\n\t\n\tHelping with food preparation and cooking\n\t\n\t\n\tServing meals to members of our community\n\t\n\t\n\tWashing dishes and keeping the kitchen clean and organised\n\t\n\t\n\tHelping with setting up and clearing away\n\t\n\t\n\tSupporting our kitchen team with day-to-day tasks\n\t\n\t\n\tSpending time with community members and helping create a friendly and welcoming atmosphere\n\t\n\n\n&nbsp;\n\nYou don&#39;t need to be an experienced cook. We welcome people with different levels of experience and will support you in your role.\n\nIf you enjoy cooking or preparing food, that&#39;s great. If you simply enjoy being part of a team, meeting people and helping others, we&#39;d also love to hear from you.\n\nYou can spare a few hours a week or volunteer regularly &mdash; we can discuss your availability and find out how you would like to get involved.\n\nYour support will help us make sure we can continue providing meals and welcoming people from our local community.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nTraining, Support &amp; Benefits\n\nBefore you start, you&#39;ll have an informal chat with a member of our team to discuss the role, your interests and availability. You&#39;ll then receive an induction and ongoing support throughout your volunteering.\n\nTraining is provided, including Food Hygiene training, and we will support you with the PVG check where required.\n\nOur team will be there to answer questions, provide guidance and make sure you feel comfortable and supported in your role.\n\nAnd while you&#39;re volunteering with us, you can enjoy a delicious lunch and morning tea and toast as part of your day with the team!\n\n&nbsp;\n\nWhen and Where?\n\nVolunteer opportunities are available at our centres in Govan and Paisley.\n\nGovan Centre\n\n8 Aboukir Street, Glasgow\nMonday to Friday, 9:00am&ndash;4:00pm\n\nPaisley Centre\n\n20 Neilston Road, Paisley, PA2 6LN\nMonday, Wednesday and Friday, 9:00am&ndash;4:00pm\n\nWe can discuss the days and hours that work best for you.\n\nJoin Us\n\nIf you have a few hours to spare and would like to help prepare and serve meals, meet people and make a real difference in your local community, we&#39;d love to hear from you.\n\nYou don&#39;t need to have all the answers before applying &mdash; just bring your time, enthusiasm and willingness to help.\n\nHow to Apply: Click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available once logged in and registered). After you apply, the coordinator will contact you by email or phone. If you don&rsquo;t hear back within 5 working days, double-check your junk/spam folder, or contact the organisation directly. If you need extra support, you can also reach out to Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nbasic cooking and food preparation skills\n\n## Travel details\n\nBus and Underground links to Govan",
