                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HvH0jYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HvH0jYAF/copy-community-activities-support-volunteer-at-the-preshal-trust",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-17",
                    "title": "COPY - Community Activities & Support Volunteer at The Preshal Trust",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCOPY - Community Activities & Support Volunteer at The Preshal Trust\n\n## Description\n\n<h2>Make a difference in your community with The Preshal Trust</h2>\n\n<p>Would you like to give some of your time, share your skills and help make a positive difference in your local community?</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Preshal Trust</strong> is a community charity based in <strong>Govan and Paisley</strong>, providing practical, emotional and spiritual support within a safe and welcoming environment.</p>\n\n<p>The word <strong>&lsquo;Preshal&rsquo; is Gaelic for &lsquo;precious&rsquo;</strong>, reflecting the Trust&#39;s belief in the value of every individual who comes through its doors.</p>\n\n<p>The Trust provides a wide range of community support, learning opportunities and activities. These include arts and crafts, cooking, sewing, IT, literacy and numeracy, board games, quizzes and opportunities for people to come together socially.</p>\n\n<p>We are looking for <strong>friendly and reliable volunteers</strong> who would like to get involved and support the work of The Preshal Trust.</p>\n\n<h3><strong>What could I be involved in?</strong></h3>\n\n<p>As a volunteer, you could:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Help with the <strong>day-to-day activities</strong> taking place at the centre.</li>\n\t<li>Support the range of activities available to people attending Preshal.</li>\n\t<li><strong>Share a skill, hobby or interest</strong> that could benefit others.</li>\n\t<li>Help with or potentially lead <strong>fun, interesting or creative activities and workshops</strong>.</li>\n\t<li>Bring forward your own ideas about ways you could contribute to the work of the Trust.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The exact nature of your volunteering can be discussed with the Preshal Trust, taking into account your <strong>interests, skills and what you would like to contribute</strong>.</p>\n\n<p>You don&#39;t need to have all the answers before applying. If you are interested in helping and have an idea or a skill you would like to share, Preshal would be happy to hear from you.</p>\n\n<h3><strong>Who would this role suit?</strong></h3>\n\n<p>This opportunity could suit someone who <strong>enjoys being around people and wants to make a positive contribution to their local community</strong>.</p>\n\n<p>You might already have a hobby, interest or skill you would enjoy sharing, or you may simply want to give some of your time and get involved in the activities taking place at the centre.</p>\n\n<p>You should be <strong>friendly, approachable, reliable and respectful</strong>, with a willingness to engage with people from a variety of backgrounds and circumstances.</p>\n\n<h3><strong>Training, Support &amp; Supervision</strong></h3>\n\n<p>In terms of <strong>training, support and supervision</strong>, prospective volunteers will first have an informal chat with the team to discuss the opportunity and make sure the role is a good fit. If they are happy to proceed, they will receive an induction covering their role, the activities they may be involved in and the support available to them.</p>\n\n<p>Throughout their time volunteering with The Preshal Trust, the staff team will be available to provide ongoing support, guidance and supervision and to answer any questions that may arise.</p>\n\n<h3><strong>When and where?</strong></h3>\n\n<p>Opportunities are available through Preshal&#39;s centres in <strong>Govan and Paisley</strong>.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Govan Centre</strong><br />\n8 Aboukir Street, Glasgow<br />\nOpen Monday to Friday, <strong>9:00am&ndash;4:00pm</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong>Paisley Centre</strong><br />\n20 Neilston Road, Paisley, PA2 6LN<br />\nOpen Monday, Wednesday and Friday,&nbsp;<strong>9:00am&ndash;4:00pm</strong></p>\n\n<p>Volunteer availability and what you would like to get involved with can be discussed directly with the Preshal Trust.</p>\n\n<h2>What happens next?</h2>\n\n<p>If you are interested, please click the <strong>&lsquo;Apply&rsquo;</strong> button below (available when logged in and registered).</p>\n\n<p>You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or telephone to discuss your interest in volunteering and how you might like to get involved.</p>\n\n<p>If you have not heard back after <strong>five working days</strong>, the first step is to contact the organisation using the contact details provided. Please also check your email junk/spam folder in case their response has been directed there.</p>\n\n<p>If you are still unable to make contact, please feel free to contact <strong>Volunteer Glasgow</strong> at <a href=\"mailto:info@volunteerglasgow.org\"><strong>info@volunteerglasgow.org</strong></a>.</p>\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous volunteering experience is necessary. The Preshal Trust is looking for people who:\n•\tAre friendly, approachable and welcoming \n•\tAre reliable and dependable \n•\tHave good communication and listening skills \n•\tEnjoy meeting and engaging with people \n•\tAre respectful of people from different backgrounds and circumstances \n•\tAre willing to work alongside staff and other volunteers\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Preshal Trust has volunteering opportunities at its centres in Govan and Paisley, both of which are accessible by public transport.\n\nGovan Centre:\n8 Aboukir Street, Glasgow. The centre is within walking distance of Govan Subway Station and is served by local bus services in the Govan area.\n\nPaisley Centre:\n20 Neilston Road, Paisley, PA2 6LN. The centre is close to Paisley town centre and can be reached by local bus services. Paisley Canal railway station is also nearby.\n\nVolunteers should discuss with The Preshal Trust which location they are interested in volunteering at when they are contacted following application.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nUnfortunately, we cannot reimburse volunteers for their travel expenses. However, we do provide tea, toast, and community lunches, which volunteers are welcome to have while they are here.",
