        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000018CLgOYAW",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000018CLgOYAW/girvan-wave-community-hub",
            "name": "Girvan Wave Community Hub",
            "website": "https://girvan.arc-methodists.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038086"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HuGrVYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HuGrVYAV/community-events-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-16",
                    "title": "Community Events Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAbout the Role \r\nWe are looking for friendly and reliable volunteers to help us deliver community events at the \r\nWave Community Hub. This could include family fun days, craft events, seasonal activities \r\nand other events that bring local people together. \r\nThere are no set weekly hours. Volunteers will be contacted when events are coming up and can choose whether they are available to help. \r\n\r\nWhat You Could Be Doing \r\n\r\nDepending on the event, volunteers may help with: \r\n● Setting up tables, chairs, decorations and activity areas before events \r\n● Welcoming people and helping create a friendly atmosphere \r\n● Helping with activities, crafts and family events \r\n● Supporting café duties, including making and serving refreshments, clearing tables and washing dishes \r\n● Keeping the Hub clean and tidy throughout events \r\n● Cleaning floors and dealing with spills as required \r\n● Checking and cleaning toilets during and after events \r\n● Clearing up and returning the Hub to normal after an event \r\n● Helping staff with other practical tasks needed to make events run smoothly \r\n\r\nWho We’re Looking For.\r\n \r\nYou don't need previous experience. We are looking for people who: \r\n● Are friendly, welcoming and happy to work with a range of people \r\n● Are reliable and willing to get stuck in \r\n● Are comfortable helping with both event activities and practical cleaning tasks \r\n● Can work as part of a team and follow instructions \r\n\r\nThe Wave Community Hub is owned by the Methodist Church and is an outreach project of \r\nPaisley Methodist Church, a registered charity in Scotland (Charity No. SC038086). \r\n● Share our aim of making the Wave Hub a welcoming place for everyone in our \r\ncommunity \r\nWhat You’ll Get From Volunteering \r\nVolunteering at Wave Hub is a chance to meet new people, be part of community events and \r\nmake a practical contribution to your local community. You'll be supported by the Wave Hub \r\nteam and can volunteer at events that fit around your other commitments. \r\nMost importantly, we want our volunteers to feel part of the Wave Hub community – \r\nhelping us create a warm, welcoming space where people can come together, connect \r\nand enjoy themselves. \r\n\r\nHow to Apply \r\nIf you’re interested in volunteering with the Wave Community Hub, simply email us at \r\ncp.wavehub@gmail.com and tell us a little bit about yourself and why you’d like to volunteer \r\nwith the Wave Hub. You’ll then be invited along to one of our Volunteer Selection Mornings \r\nto meet the team, find out more about the role and see if it’s a good fit for you.",
