            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000018DOduYAG/dalgety-bay-art-club",
            "name": "Dalgety Bay Art Club",
            "description": "Dalgety Bay Art Club offers a wide range of regular classes, workshops, demonstrations, and creative sessions that give members the chance to learn new skills and develop their artistic practice.\r\n\r\nThey run twice‑yearly exhibitions, held in the local church in May and November. These exhibitions, along with other events and community activities, showcase members’ work and help promote arts engagement within Dalgety Bay.\r\n\r\nThey also support the wider community by using the skills within the club to create items for charitable causes. Members make decorative hearts for a horse charity auction, cushions for breast cancer patients, knitted bereavement hearts, and hats and scarves for primary school children.",
            "website": "https://www.dalgetybayartclub.com/",
            "charityRegistration": [
