            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HuPmjYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HuPmjYAF/treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-18",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-16",
                    "title": "Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDalgety Bay Art Club is seeking a committed volunteer to train as their next Treasurer.\n\n## Description\n\nDalgety Bay Art Club is seeking a committed volunteer to train as their next Treasurer — a vital role that will safeguard the future of their much loved community art club. You’ll volunteer alongside the Assistant Treasurer who will remain in post for 12 months and provide full, supportive, hands on training while continuing to manage the load. This is an excellent opportunity for someone who is comfortable with computers, confident using Excel, and has good financial awareness and attention to detail.\r\n\r\nAs Treasurer, you’ll help ensure the club remains financially secure, enabling them to continue offering classes, workshops, exhibitions, and creative community projects. Your contribution will directly protect a valued local charity and keep a welcoming creative space open for nearly 100 members in Dalgety Bay.\r\n\r\nIf you want to make a meaningful difference in your community, they’d love to hear from you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers should be computer literate, intermediate in excel, have good financial awareness, and have strong attention to detail.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe treasurer will receive ongoing training and support from the assistant treasurer.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis role takes place at Dalgety Bay Art Club, located in Dalgety Bay, Fife. All Treasurer duties are carried out within the clubhouse, and no regular travel is required. The only exception is banking cash from membership fees or events, which involves a short trip to the bank in Dunfermline. Apart from this occasional task, the role is entirely based in Dalgety Bay.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThey are happy to reimburse any travel required as part of the Treasurer's duties (such as banking in Dunfermline or picking up supplies). If the volunteer does not live locally, they are also open to discussing support for travel to and from the clubhouse to ensure the role remains accessible to anyone who wishes to help.",
