        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000018KbuWYAS",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000018KbuWYAS/mark-williams-foundation",
            "name": "Mark Williams Foundation",
            "description": "Our purpose is to protect children’s access to loving relationships with good fathers, support the mental wellbeing of those fathers and to also empower the next generation of entrepreneurs.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of the Mark Williams Foundation is a deeply personal story - one born out of love, legacy, and a desire to remove the barriers that too many individuals face in business and in family life. The Foundation was established by Nicola Williams following the tragic loss of her husband, Mark Williams",
            "website": "https://markwilliamsfoundation.co.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC054415"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SelfHelpSupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Self-Help / Support"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HuxMzYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HuxMzYAJ/wellbeing-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-18",
                    "title": "Wellbeing & Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Mark Williams Foundation exists to protect children’s rights to loving relationships with good fathers, to challenge injustice, and to empower the next generation of entrepreneurs to build stronger futures for themselves, their families, and their communities.\r\nWe believe every child deserves the love and guidance of both parents, and that good fathers should never be pushed to the sidelines by a system that too often fails them. We’ve seen the damage caused when families are fractured unfairly, and we know that when fathers are supported, children thrive. At the same time, we recognise that building stronger futures also means investing in the dreams of young people, giving them the tools, confidence and opportunity to create something lasting.\r\nThe Foundation is a Scottish Charitable Incorporated Organisation (SCIO) with two core purposes:\r\n1.\tTo support good fathers at risk of losing access to their children\r\n2.\tTo empower young entrepreneurs through mentorship, education and opportunity\r\nOur Father Support Initiative provides financial assistance for legal representation, and emotional support through trained wellbeing volunteers who understand the challenges fathers face during separation. Volunteers offer a safe, non judgemental space for fathers to talk openly, feel heard, and regain a sense of connection and hope.\r\nThe Role\r\nThis voluntary role is ideal for someone who cares deeply about fairness, family relationships and emotional wellbeing. You will provide listening support to fathers experiencing separation or alienation from their children. This is not counselling or therapy — it is compassionate, human connection from someone who understands how isolating this journey can be.\r\nYou will also play a part in helping us build a supportive community by assisting with peer to peer events that bring fathers together, such as Father’s Day gatherings and informal connection activities.\r\nAll volunteers receive appropriate training in active listening, mental health awareness and safeguarding.\r\nKey Responsibilities\r\n•\tOffering one to one listening support to fathers experiencing separation or alienation\r\n•\tCreating a safe, respectful and confidential space for fathers to talk openly\r\n•\tShowing empathy, patience and understanding without giving advice or judgement\r\n•\tRecognising when someone may need additional or specialist support and signposting appropriately\r\n•\tMaintaining clear boundaries and following the Foundation’s safeguarding guidance\r\n•\tParticipating in training sessions and reflective practice\r\n•\tSupporting the organisation and delivery of peer to peer community events, such as Father’s Day gatherings, informal meet ups and connection building activities\r\n•\tHelping create a welcoming, inclusive environment at events where fathers can meet others who understand their experiences\r\n•\tCommunicating sensitively and upholding the Foundation’s values at all times\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou may have lived experience, have supported others through difficult times, or simply feel strongly about fairness and family connection. Most importantly, you care about people.\r\nYou are likely to have:\r\n•\tA warm, compassionate and non judgemental approach\r\n•\tGood listening skills and emotional maturity\r\n•\tComfort with sensitive conversations\r\n•\tReliability and respect for confidentiality\r\n•\tThe ability to work independently while staying connected to the team\r\n•\tAlignment with the Foundation’s values of integrity, compassion, resilience and empowerment\r\nLived experience or a personal connection to our mission is welcomed and valued, but not required.\n\n## Training details\n\nOnboarding begins with an induction to our mission and values, followed by a structured training pathway including Mental Health Level 2, ASIST and specialist development. Wellbeing & Support Volunteers receive weekly support and regular meetings with the Programme Lead to stay confident, grounded and equipped in their role.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible. Typically a few hours per week, depending on your availability. Support may take place online, by phone or in person, and events will be scheduled in advance.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses can be covered by the Foundation.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HuxMzYAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Wellbeing & Support Volunteer",
                        "description": "You may have lived experience, have supported others through difficult times, or simply feel strongly about fairness and family connection. Most importantly, you care about people.\r\nYou are likely to have:\r\n•\tA warm, compassionate and non judgemental approach\r\n•\tGood listening skills and emotional maturity\r\n•\tComfort with sensitive conversations\r\n•\tReliability and respect for confidentiality\r\n•\tThe ability to work independently while staying connected to the team\r\n•\tAlignment with the Foundation’s values of integrity, compassion, resilience and empowerment\r\nLived experience or a personal connection to our mission is welcomed and valued, but not required.",
                        "commitment": "Flexible. Typically a few hours per week, depending on your availability. Support may take place online, by phone or in person, and events will be scheduled in advance.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HuxMzYAJ/wellbeing-support-volunteer?#modal_register_a0gQD00000HuxMzYAJ",
