                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HuxDJYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HuxDJYAZ/fundraising-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-18",
                    "title": "Fundraising Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Mark Williams Foundation was established in memory of Mark Williams to support young people and families facing inequality and disadvantage across Scotland. Our work focuses on two core areas:\r\n•\tSupporting young people into entrepreneurship through mentoring and apprenticeships\r\n•\tProviding support to fathers who are struggling to maintain relationships with their children following separation\r\nWe are a small but growing foundation with a big heart, strong values and a clear purpose. As we continue to expand our impact, we’re looking for a Fundraising Volunteer to help us build the resources we need to support more families and young people.\r\nThe Role\r\nThis flexible, voluntary role is ideal for someone who enjoys connecting with people, building relationships and using their creativity to support a meaningful cause. You’ll help us develop fundraising opportunities, engage supporters and strengthen the Foundation’s financial sustainability.\r\nYou’ll work closely with the Founder and Trustees and will have genuine autonomy to shape how fundraising develops within the organisation.\r\nKey Responsibilities\r\n•\tSupporting the planning and delivery of fundraising campaigns and appeals\r\n•\tHelping identify potential donors, partners, community groups or local businesses\r\n•\tDrafting fundraising materials such as emails, social posts, event copy and supporter updates\r\n•\tAssisting with the organisation and promotion of fundraising events and challenges\r\n•\tHelping maintain positive relationships with supporters and donors\r\n•\tEnsuring all fundraising activity reflects our values and is carried out ethically and sensitively\r\n•\tTracking basic fundraising metrics and suggesting improvements\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou may be a student, early career professional, career returner or someone with fundraising or community engagement experience who wants to give back. Most importantly, you care about social impact and believe in the power of community.\r\nYou are likely to have:\r\n•\tInterest or experience in fundraising, community engagement or communications\r\n•\tConfidence speaking with people and building relationships\r\n•\tStrong written communication skills\r\n•\tCreativity and enthusiasm for generating ideas\r\n•\tGood organisation and the ability to work independently\r\n•\tAlignment with our values: integrity, compassion, resilience and empowerment\r\nFormal fundraising experience is welcome but not essential. Lived experience or a personal connection to our mission is equally valued.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible — typically a few hours per week, with occasional peaks around campaigns or events.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel Expense is covered by charity",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HuxDJYAZ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Fundraising Volunteer",
                        "description": "You may be a student, early career professional, career returner or someone with fundraising or community engagement experience who wants to give back. Most importantly, you care about social impact and believe in the power of community.\r\nYou are likely to have:\r\n•\tInterest or experience in fundraising, community engagement or communications\r\n•\tConfidence speaking with people and building relationships\r\n•\tStrong written communication skills\r\n•\tCreativity and enthusiasm for generating ideas\r\n•\tGood organisation and the ability to work independently\r\n•\tAlignment with our values: integrity, compassion, resilience and empowerment\r\nFormal fundraising experience is welcome but not essential. Lived experience or a personal connection to our mission is equally valued.",
