        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000018fJ9dYAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000018fJ9dYAE/swan",
            "name": "SWAN",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/SWAN",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HwSVBYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HwSVBYA3/swan-places-bridgeton-meet-up-group-facilitator",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "SWAN Places Bridgeton Meet-Up - Group Facilitator",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSWAN Places Bridgeton Meet-Up - Group Facilitator\n\n## Description\n\nSWAN is a registered charity (SCO46946) that supports (diagnosed, self-diagnosed, and questioning) autistic women (cis and trans) and non-binary individuals across Scotland. Alongside other projects, we do so through monthly online and in-person peer support groups and Wellbeing Walks. Due to funding, all of our groups are 18+. All SWAN staff and volunteers are autistic and we pride ourselves on creating psychologically safe and neuro-affirming spaces.\n\nWe are looking for volunteers to help support our in-person Bridgeton Meet-Up as facilitators. The group is every third Tuesday of the month from 1:30pm until 3pm in the&nbsp;Bridgeton Library&nbsp;(G40 2QH).\n\nDuties include:\n\n\n\tWelcoming all group attendees, new and old\n\tCreating a safe and inclusive space for all attendees\n\tEncouraging&nbsp;positive peer support conversations&nbsp;\n\tReporting any issues the group is experiencing to ensure it runs as smoothly as possible\n\tHelping to organise occasional events and activities that happen outwith the monthly Meet-Up\n\n\nThe role requires a minimum of 1.5 hours of volunteering over a month period. This may vary if there are additional events organised for the group within a month period. All volunteering roles with SWAN require a PVG as standard (we will support you with this, and there is no cost involved). All training will be provided for the role and references can be given upon request. All roles can have reasonable adjustments implemented. Please get in touch if you have any questions about the role.&nbsp;\n\nIf you are interested,&nbsp;please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when&nbsp;registered and&nbsp;logged in). You&nbsp;will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that&nbsp;doesn&rsquo;t&nbsp;work&nbsp;out,&nbsp;then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nMust have good time-keeping skills and be comfortable talking with a range of people. Must be diagnosed or self-diagnosed autistic.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAll travel expenses and material and resource costs for the volunteer to fully participate with their role.",
