        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001953xFYAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001953xFYAQ/skywave-ruralnet-scio",
            "name": "Skywave RuralNet SCIO",
            "description": "Skywave RuralNet SCIO is a Scottish Charitable Incorporated Organisation (SCIO) and not-for-profit organisation dedicated to tackling digital exclusion in rural Scotland through a research-informed, community-led approach that combines connectivity, access, and digital capability. We combine evidence-based connectivity solutions, community access hubs, and digital capability support to help ensure rural communities are connected and included in the digital world.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC055507"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SocialEconomySocialEnterprise",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Social Economy / Social Enterprise"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JCWE5YAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JCWE5YAP/volunteer-trustees-wanted-skywave-ruralnet-scio",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-30",
                    "title": "VOLUNTEER TRUSTEES WANTED – SKYWAVE RURALNET SCIO",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSkywave RuralNet, a registered Scottish charity based in Glasgow, is recruiting two passionate volunteer trustees. One will focus on computer refurbishment and digital inclusion, while the other will lead on research, community engagement and development. Applicants should be passionate about rural digital inclusion, reliable, and willing to dedicate at least a few hours monthly. We seek an intended two-year commitment. Previous trustee experience is not essential. To apply, email skywaveruralnet@gmail.com with your experience and motivation.\n\n## Experience required\n\n1. Computer Refurbishment and Digital Inclusion Trustee: Applicants should ideally have skills or experience in computer repairs, laptop and desktop refurbishment, hardware troubleshooting, software installation, secure data wiping, IT equipment recycling or technology reuse. A passion for making technology accessible to digitally excluded rural communities is essential.\n\n2. Research and Community Engagement Development Trustee: Applicants should ideally have skills or experience in research, community engagement, stakeholder communication, identifying community needs, project development, report writing, partnership building or evaluating social impact. An interest in rural affairs and digital inclusion is essential.\n\nPrevious trustee experience is not required. Both trustees must be reliable, collaborative and willing to dedicate at least a few hours each month, with an intended commitment of two years.\n\n## Training details\n\nSkywave RuralNet will provide an induction to the charity, its aims, activities and trustee responsibilities. Role-specific guidance will be provided for computer refurbishment, digital inclusion, research and community engagement, as appropriate. Trustees will also be signposted to relevant training and resources on charity governance, safeguarding, data protection and financial responsibilities. Previous trustee experience is not essential.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMost meetings will take place online, so volunteers can participate remotely without regular travel. Occasional in-person meetings or community activities may be arranged in advance, depending on the charity’s needs. Any travel requirements will be discussed beforehand.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses will be discussed and agreed in advance. As most meetings will take place online, travel should be minimal. Any reimbursement of reasonable travel expenses will be subject to the charity’s available funds and agreed arrangements.\n\n## Taster details\n\nVolunteers will be offered an online induction to introduce them to Skywave RuralNet, our mission to improve digital inclusion in rural communities, our current activities and future plans. The induction will explain the responsibilities of a charity trustee, the expectations of each role and how volunteers can contribute their skills and ideas. An informal online introductory meeting can also be arranged before accepting the role, giving prospective trustees an opportunity to ask questions and learn more about the charity. Role-specific guidance and ongoing support will be provided as needed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FoDLzlY2HIRXuDbzY5pJb1pf8D0A3%2FzaNkgWNC3D1BzNT7-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=f08292a7-4615-4ddb-a1f5-273e6d69363f",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JCWE5YAP#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "VOLUNTEER TRUSTEES WANTED – SKYWAVE RURALNET SCIO",
                        "description": "1. Computer Refurbishment and Digital Inclusion Trustee: Applicants should ideally have skills or experience in computer repairs, laptop and desktop refurbishment, hardware troubleshooting, software installation, secure data wiping, IT equipment recycling or technology reuse. A passion for making technology accessible to digitally excluded rural communities is essential.\n\n2. Research and Community Engagement Development Trustee: Applicants should ideally have skills or experience in research, community engagement, stakeholder communication, identifying community needs, project development, report writing, partnership building or evaluating social impact. An interest in rural affairs and digital inclusion is essential.\n\nPrevious trustee experience is not required. Both trustees must be reliable, collaborative and willing to dedicate at least a few hours each month, with an intended commitment of two years.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JCWE5YAP/volunteer-trustees-wanted-skywave-ruralnet-scio?#modal_register_a0gQD00000JCWE5YAP",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": true,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/AntiPoverty",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Anti-Poverty"
