                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0qibYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I0qibYAB/fundraising-sustainability-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-13",
                    "title": "Fundraising & Sustainability Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSKYWAVE RURALNET SCIO is seeking an enthusiastic volunteer to support our fundraising and long-term sustainability as we prepare to deliver our rural digital inclusion pilot.\r\n\r\nAbout SKYWAVE\r\n\r\nSKYWAVE works to reduce digital exclusion through:\r\n\r\nDigital connectivity;\r\nDigital devices;\r\nDigital skills training; and\r\nDigital support.\r\n\r\nWe are developing pilot projects in IV26, IV27 and IV28, informed by broadband research and further community needs assessment.\r\n\r\nThe Role\r\n\r\nThe Fundraising & Sustainability Volunteer will help SKYWAVE identify funding opportunities, develop sustainable income strategies and build the resources needed to support our charitable work.\r\n\r\nKey Activities\r\nResearch grant, charitable and public-sector funding opportunities;\r\nIdentify potential funders and funding programmes;\r\nSupport preparation of grant applications and funding proposals;\r\nMaintain a funding opportunities and application tracker;\r\nResearch potential partnerships and sources of support;\r\nExplore opportunities for long-term organisational sustainability;\r\nHelp develop fundraising materials and project information; and\r\nSupport the development of SKYWAVE's funding pipeline.\r\nSkills We Are Looking For\r\n\r\nUseful skills include:\r\n\r\nResearch;\r\nFundraising or grant writing;\r\nWritten communication;\r\nFinancial or business awareness;\r\nOrganisation and administration;\r\nStrategic thinking;\r\nPartnership development; or\r\nSustainability planning.\r\n\r\nPrevious fundraising experience is helpful but not essential.\r\n\r\nWhat We Offer\r\n\r\nThis is an unpaid volunteer opportunity providing practical experience in charity fundraising, grant development, sustainability and organisational growth.\r\n\r\nThe role can begin before funding is secured and will contribute directly to SKYWAVE's readiness to implement its pilot and develop its longer-term charitable activities.\r\n\r\nHow to Apply\r\n\r\nPlease send a CV or short skills profile and a brief statement explaining your interest.\r\n\r\nShortlisted candidates will have a brief informal discussion with SKYWAVE.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
