                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0qgzYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I0qgzYAB/community-engagement-research-digital-inclusion",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-13",
                    "title": "Community Engagement, Research & Digital Inclusion",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nSKYWAVE RURALNET SCIO is seeking an enthusiastic volunteer to help us understand the digital inclusion needs of people living in our proposed pilot areas.\r\n\r\nAbout SKYWAVE\r\n\r\nSKYWAVE works to reduce digital exclusion through:\r\n\r\nDigital connectivity;\r\nDigital devices;\r\nDigital skills training; and\r\nDigital support.\r\n\r\nWe are developing pilot projects in IV26, IV27 and IV28, building on existing broadband research and further community research.\r\n\r\nThe Role\r\n\r\nThe Community Engagement, Research & Digital Inclusion Trainee will help SKYWAVE gather information directly from communities and ensure that our pilot is based on identified local needs and evidence.\r\n\r\nKey Activities\r\nSupport community surveys and research;\r\nEngage with community organisations and residents;\r\nHelp gather information about connectivity, device access and digital skills;\r\nIdentify barriers to accessing essential online services;\r\nSupport community discussions and engagement activities;\r\nCollect and organise research findings;\r\nHelp identify groups experiencing digital exclusion; and\r\nContribute to the design of SKYWAVE's pilot based on the evidence gathered.\r\nSkills We Are Looking For\r\n\r\nUseful skills include:\r\n\r\nCommunity engagement;\r\nResearch and information gathering;\r\nSurvey work;\r\nCommunication and interviewing;\r\nData collection and analysis;\r\nReport writing;\r\nDigital inclusion; or\r\nCommunity development.\r\n\r\nPrevious experience is helpful but not essential. We are particularly interested in people who are good communicators, curious, organised and interested in understanding community needs.\r\n\r\nWhat We Offer\r\n\r\nThis is an unpaid volunteer trainee opportunity providing practical experience in community research, digital inclusion, needs assessment and evidence-based project development.\r\n\r\nThe role can begin before funding is secured and will directly contribute to shaping SKYWAVE's pilot.\r\n\r\nHow to Apply\r\n\r\nPlease send a CV or short skills profile and a brief statement explaining your interest.\r\n\r\nShortlisted candidates will have a brief informal discussion with SKYWAVE.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
