                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0qfNYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I0qfNYAR/technology-network-engineering-project-development-trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-13",
                    "title": "Technology, Network Engineering & Project Development Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nTechnology, Network Engineering & Project Development Trustee\r\n\r\nSKYWAVE RURALNET SCIO is seeking an enthusiastic and technically experienced volunteer trustee to help shape our rural digital inclusion programme.\r\n\r\nAbout SKYWAVE\r\n\r\nSKYWAVE works to reduce digital exclusion in rural and underserved communities through:\r\n\r\nDigital connectivity;\r\nProvision of digital devices;\r\nDigital skills training; and\r\nOngoing digital support.\r\n\r\nWe are developing pilot projects in IV26, IV27 and IV28, building on our broadband research and further community needs assessment.\r\n\r\nThe Role\r\n\r\nThe Technology, Network Engineering & Project Development Trustee will provide technical expertise, strategic advice and governance oversight to help SKYWAVE develop a practical and sustainable delivery model.\r\n\r\nKey Activities\r\nAdvise the Board on network and technology strategy;\r\nProvide technical input into rural connectivity and digital inclusion projects;\r\nReview technical feasibility, risks and proposed solutions;\r\nAdvise on network architecture, equipment and technical standards;\r\nContribute to pilot planning and project development;\r\nProvide appropriate oversight of external technical contractors; and\r\nHelp ensure SKYWAVE's technology model is scalable, secure and sustainable.\r\nSkills We Are Looking For\r\n\r\nExperience or knowledge in one or more of:\r\n\r\nNetwork engineering;\r\nWireless networking;\r\nTelecommunications;\r\nIT infrastructure or systems;\r\nCybersecurity;\r\nTechnical project management;\r\nNetwork architecture; or\r\nTechnology procurement.\r\n\r\nExperience in rural connectivity or digital inclusion is desirable but not essential.\r\n\r\nWhat We Offer\r\n\r\nThis is an unpaid volunteer trustee role offering an opportunity to use your technical expertise for public benefit and help shape a new rural digital inclusion charity from its development and pilot stage.\r\n\r\nThe role is primarily strategic and governance-focused. Physical network installation and specialist technical delivery will be undertaken by appropriately qualified contractors and partners.\r\n\r\nHow to Apply\r\n\r\nPlease send a CV or short skills profile and a brief statement explaining your interest and what you could contribute to skywaveruralnet@gmail.com\r\n\r\nShortlisted candidates will have a brief informal discussion with SKYWAVE.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0qfNYAR#role",
