        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD0000195L4aYAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD0000195L4aYAE/laurieston-community-council",
            "name": "Laurieston Community Council",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/LauriestonCommunityCouncil",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HyDOnYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HyDOnYAN/come-and-join-your-local-community-council",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Come and join your local Community Council!",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCome and join your local Community Council!\n\n## Description\n\nLaurieston Community Council is seeking Laurieston residents over the age of 16 to join them as a Community Councillor.\n\nWhat could YOU do as a Community Councillor?\n\n\n\tOrganise community events.\n\tLead campaigns on local issues.\n\tBring local people together.\n\tMake representations on planning applications, e.g. those coming from the North Laurieston Masterplan.\n\tRepresent Laurieston at Area Partnership meetings alongside local elected councillors.\n\tGather and share the views of local residents with Glasgow City Council and other public bodies on issues affecting the community and the environment.\n\tRun our website and/or our social media.\n\tTake on a role such as Chair, Secretary, or Treasurer.\n\tAttend training and development sessions.\n\n\nThere are opportunities to contribute to the running of meetings and community engagement activities in line with your interested and skills.\n\nNo experience or qualifications are necessary. You need to only be a resident of Laurieston, over the age of 16, and interested in participating in meetings and discussions to improve the local community.&nbsp;\n\nDates and weekday evening times of 2027 monthly meeting to be decided between all community councillors at our AGM on Tuesday 27 October 2026.\n\nFor more information and to download a nomination form, visit: https://www.glasgow.gov.uk/communitycouncils/elections\n\nEmail us at lauriestoncc@gmail.com if you have any questions, need a proposer / seconder, or require a printed form.\n\nWe can also send it to Glasgow City Council for you. It must be submitted to the council by Tuesday 29 September, 2026.\n\nWe aim to host all meetings in accessible venues. Meetings are usually held on weeknights, and will be within the Gorbals area.\n\nTime committment would be roughly two hours a month for meetings, and another two-four hours a month depending on your role, and tasks for which you volunteer.\n\n## Experience required\n\nIt depends on what you would like to do. There are opportunities for people skilled in IT, minute-taking, chairing meetings, planning community engagement activities, public speaking, working with finance/bookkeeping, graphic design, website building, social media. The ability and willing to attend meetings and participate in discussions - both in meetings, and outside of meetings with fellow community councillors, are the only aspects necessary in terms of skills.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMeetings and activities will take place within Laurieston.  Buses run along Bridge Street and Eglinton Street, and Gorbals Street.  There is also Bridge Street subway.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
