        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD0000195VjpYAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD0000195VjpYAE/visably",
            "name": "Visably",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/Visably",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HyDv3YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HyDv3YAF/telephone-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Telephone Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTelephone Support Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nAs a Telephone Support Volunteer with Visably, you&rsquo;ll provide a friendly point of contact for people living with sight loss after they have received their equipment.\n\nYou&rsquo;ll make follow-up calls to check that their equipment has arrived, find out how they&rsquo;re getting on and identify whether they need any further help or support.\n\nYou&rsquo;ll also make people aware of additional support available through Visably where appropriate and record the outcome of your conversations accurately on our CRM system.\n\nYou won&rsquo;t be expected to solve every problem yourself. If someone needs additional or specialist support, the Visably team will be there to help.\n\nThis is a flexible, remote role that can be carried out from home. Full induction, role-specific training and ongoing support will be provided.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly and confident on the telephone; good listener and communicator; patient and supportive; comfortable using a computer; willing to learn the Visably CRM; able to record information accurately; reliable and respectful of confidentiality. No previous CRM or volunteering experience required.",
