                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HyDjlYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HyDjlYAF/peer-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Peer Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nPeer Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nAs a Peer Volunteer with Visably, you&rsquo;ll use your own lived experience of sight loss to provide friendly and supportive peer-to-peer contact with other people living with sight loss.\n\nSometimes talking to someone who understands can help a person feel less alone and more confident about what comes next. You&rsquo;ll listen, offer encouragement and share relevant aspects of your own experience where this may be helpful.\n\nYou might also share practical tips and experiences, help people feel more confident engaging with Visably&rsquo;s services, and identify when someone may benefit from additional support from our team.\n\nYou won&rsquo;t be expected to provide counselling or professional advice. We&rsquo;ll provide a full induction, role-specific training and ongoing support.\n\nThe role is flexible and may take place remotely by telephone or online, or within community settings.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## Experience required\n\nLived experience of sight loss; friendly, patient and empathetic; good listener and communicator; non-judgemental; respects different experiences and choices; understands boundaries and confidentiality; reliable. No previous volunteering experience required.",
