        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000019A6GBYA0",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000019A6GBYA0/the-aitken-project",
            "name": "The Aitken Project",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/TheAitkenProject",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HyT29YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HyT29YAF/family-community-support-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-02",
                    "title": "Family & Community Support Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFamily & Community Support Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nThe Aitken Project is a new community-based project supporting children, young people and families affected by the imprisonment of a parent or close family member. We aim to provide compassionate, relationship-based support while helping to strengthen the networks and communities around families.\n\nAs a volunteer with The Aitken Project, you will have the opportunity to play an important role in helping us build a supportive and welcoming service for children and families.\n\nDepending on your interests and the needs of the project, you may support family activities, children&rsquo;s activities, community events, awareness-raising activities or other areas of our developing programme.\n\nYou will help us create spaces where children and families feel&nbsp;welcomed, listened to, respected and supported. You may also have opportunities to help us connect with local organisations and communities and raise awareness of the impact that imprisonment can have on families.\n\nWe are looking for people who are&nbsp;reliable, compassionate, approachable and willing to listen. You should be comfortable working as part of a team and committed to treating everyone with dignity and respect.\n\nThis opportunity would suit someone who is interested in&nbsp;working with children and families, community development, supporting others or making a positive difference within their local community. It could also provide valuable experience and skills for anyone considering a career in community work, social care, youth work, education or related fields.\n\nFull induction and appropriate training will be provided, with ongoing support and supervision throughout your volunteering.\n\nAs The Aitken Project is currently developing its services, volunteers will initially have opportunities to become involved in building the project, supporting community engagement and preparing for our programme launch. As the project develops, there will be opportunities to become involved in our direct support activities.\n\nIf you are interested in applying for this opportunity please click &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; below (available if registered and logged in). We will reply to your email within 5 working days when we will arrange to meet you for an informal chat. If you have not heard from us within this time, please contact Volunteer Glasgow.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for volunteers who are:\n\n* Caring, compassionate and approachable.\n* Reliable and committed to their volunteering.\n* Good listeners and communicators.\n* Respectful of different backgrounds, experiences and circumstances.\n* Able to maintain appropriate boundaries and confidentiality.\n* Comfortable working as part of a team.\n* Willing to learn and take part in relevant training.\n\nPrevious experience of working with children, families or within a community setting would be\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Aitken Project is based at Calton Old Parish Church in Glasgow’s East End. The venue is accessible by public transport, with local bus and train services available nearby. There is also parking available in the surrounding area.",
