        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000019DIPjYAO",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000019DIPjYAO/alpha-community-action-group-scio",
            "name": "Alpha Community Action Group SCIO",
            "description": "We support and empower Denny, Falkirk and Central Scotland through wellbeing programmes, environmental action, local engagement and strong community development.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC055437"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/EnvironmentRecycling",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Environment / Recycling"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000INvmPYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000INvmPYAT/litter-picking-community-clean-up-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-07",
                    "title": "Litter Picking & Community Clean-Up Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAlpha Community Action Group SCIO is a registered Scottish charity based in Denny and working across the wider Falkirk area. Their purpose is to support community development, environmental improvement, community wellbeing and participation. They work with local residents, volunteers and community partners to help create cleaner, safer and greener communities.\r\n\r\nAlpha Community Action Group are looking for volunteers to support community litter-picking and clean-up activities across Denny and the wider Falkirk area.  Volunteers will work as part of a friendly community team to help improve local streets, green spaces, pathways and other suitable public areas.\r\n\r\nTasks may include:\r\n\r\nLitter picking and collecting general litter.\r\nHelping with community clean-up activities.\r\nSorting and safely bagging collected litter.\r\nHelping identify areas that would benefit from future clean-up activities.\r\nSupporting other volunteers during organised clean-up sessions.\r\nHelping promote pride in the local environment.\r\n\r\nAll necessary litter-picking equipment and safety guidance will be provided. Volunteers will receive a briefing before activities begin and will be expected to follow the organisation's health and safety guidance.\r\n\r\nVolunteers can participate according to their availability and ability. The role involves outdoor activity and may include walking, standing and carrying lightweight bags of litter.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous skills or experience required.  Volunteers should be able to work as part of a team.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive a brief induction to Alpha Community Action Group, their role and health and safety procedures. A safety briefing and practical guidance will be provided before activities begin, including how to use equipment safely. Volunteers will be supported by an experienced volunteer lead throughout the activity and can ask questions or raise any concerns at any time.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible - 2 hours per week.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity will take place at various locations across Denny and the wider Falkirk area, depending on the location of each organised community clean-up. \r\nVolunteers will normally meet at an agreed meeting point before each activity. Locations and meeting arrangements will be provided to volunteers in advance. Volunteers are responsible for making their own way to the agreed meeting point.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWhere applicable, reasonable volunteer expenses such as local travel costs may be supported in line with Alpha Community Action Group SCIO's volunteer expenses policy.\n\n## Taster details\n\nA taster session can be organised.",
