                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0N3tYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I0N3tYAF/face-to-face-support-group-leader-with-alopecia-uk",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-11",
                    "title": "Face to Face Support Group Leader with Alopecia UK",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAt Alopecia UK, we understand how powerful peer support can be. For many people affected by alopecia, having the opportunity to speak openly with others who truly understand can be incredibly reassuring and empowering. We know that alopecia can bring up a wide range of emotions, and being able to share those feelings, ask questions, and connect with others who simply \"get it\" can make a real difference.\r\n\r\nAlopecia UK has a network of over twenty-five adult peer support groups across the UK, offering regular meet-ups for those affected by alopecia. These groups are led by dedicated volunteers—usually individuals with lived experience of alopecia themselves—who play a vital role in creating safe, welcoming spaces for conversation and connection.\r\n\r\nAs a Support Group Lead, you will take the lead in organising and delivering regular meetings, which includes finding and booking suitable venues, managing a dedicated AUK inbox, responding to enquiries, and sending updates to your group’s distribution list. On meeting days, you will welcome attendees and help to facilitate open, inclusive conversations among the group. While Support Group Leads are not trained counsellors, they offer valuable peer support by sharing their own experiences, providing a listening ear, and signposting to further resources where needed.\r\n\r\nWhat You’ll be Doing:\r\nOrganise, coordinate, and deliver local support group meetings\r\nFind and book suitable venues for meetings\r\nManage the Alopecia UK (AUK) support group inbox, responding to enquiries in a timely manner\r\nSend out communications to the support group’s distribution list\r\nWelcome attendees at meetings and help facilitate conversations within the group\r\nComplete brief data collection forms following each meeting\r\nAttend a short online induction and training session with the Volunteer Manager\r\nParticipate in regular support group lead team meetings and one-to-one check ins with the Volunteer Manager \r\nAdhere to Alopecia UK policies and procedures at all times\r\nMaintain appropriate boundaries with support group attendees\n\n## Experience required\n\nLived experience of alopecia, with the confidence and empathy to support others on their journey\r\nWarm, friendly, and approachable, with strong communication and active listening skills\r\nWillingness to openly share aspects of your own alopecia experience to help others feel less alone\r\nComfortable discussing sensitive and personal topics in a respectful and supportive manner\r\nReliable, compassionate, and non- judgemental, with a genuine desire to help others \r\nConfident using a computer and accessing the internet, with basic tech skills to manage emails and online communications\n\n## Training details\n\nFull induction and ongoing training will be available to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nAvailable to run at least 3 support group meetings per year. And undertake induction and ongoing training. Support group meeting dates/times are flexible and can be made to suit the volunteers other commitments.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAll support group costs will be covered.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0N3tYAF#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Face to Face Support Group Leader with Alopecia UK",
                        "description": "Lived experience of alopecia, with the confidence and empathy to support others on their journey\r\nWarm, friendly, and approachable, with strong communication and active listening skills\r\nWillingness to openly share aspects of your own alopecia experience to help others feel less alone\r\nComfortable discussing sensitive and personal topics in a respectful and supportive manner\r\nReliable, compassionate, and non- judgemental, with a genuine desire to help others \r\nConfident using a computer and accessing the internet, with basic tech skills to manage emails and online communications",
                        "commitment": "Available to run at least 3 support group meetings per year. And undertake induction and ongoing training. Support group meeting dates/times are flexible and can be made to suit the volunteers other commitments.",
                        "applyLink": "https://www.alopecia.org.uk/start-a-support-group",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
