        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000019ZOpnYAG",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000019ZOpnYAG/deaf-services-lanarkshire",
            "name": "Deaf Services Lanarkshire",
            "website": "https://vanl.teamkinetic.co.uk/profile/DeafServicesLanarkshire",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0TfZYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I0TfZYAV/trustee-board-chair",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Trustee - Board Chair",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTrustee - Board Chair\n\n## Description\n\nDue to the retiral of our current post holder, Deaf Services Lanarkshire is looking for a new Chair&nbsp;of its Board.\n\nThe successful candidate will&nbsp;lead&nbsp;our&nbsp;established&nbsp;group of&nbsp;Trustees, and our Service Manager, to further our work to strengthen and develop the Services and provisions provided by DSL and associated partners across Lanarkshire.&nbsp;\n\nWe are always keen to welcome new trustees to our Board as well, please contact us if you might be interested to join us.&nbsp;\n\nAbout the Role&nbsp;\n\nAnticipated time commitment is around 200 hours per year or up to 18 per month &ndash; this includes quarterly Board meetings; AGM and attendance at meetings/events with similar professional bodies.&nbsp;\n\nThis is a unique opportunity to contribute your skills, vision, and experience to guide our mission and drive positive change\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&zwj;For more information and/or to apply please contact:&nbsp;\n\nJune Greening (Interim Chair)&nbsp;\n\nPhone: 07834 989714&nbsp;(Text, Facetime, WhatsApp - BSL or written English)&nbsp;\n\nEmail: admin@deafserviceslanarkshire.co.uk&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## Experience required\n\nIdeally you will have: Experience in a senior or strategic leadership role, experience in either a Funding, Building transformation, Finance, Community Asset Transfers or other relevant Business or Charity experience, strong understanding of charity governance, charity finance, the role of a trustee plus chairing meetings and strong and inclusive leadership skills, able to motivate and support others.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0TfZYAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
