        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000019cCIpYAM",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000019cCIpYAM/phoenix-futures",
            "name": "Phoenix Futures",
            "website": "https://vanl.teamkinetic.co.uk/profile/PhoenixFutures",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0i57YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I0i57YAB/volunteer-peer-mentor",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-24",
                    "title": "Volunteer peer mentor",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteer peer mentor\n\n## Description\n\nJoin our dedicated team and make a real difference in the lives of individuals on their journey to recovery! We are seeking passionate and compassionate volunteers to support our vital drug and alcohol recovery service. Your contribution will directly impact those striving for a healthier, substance-free future.\n\nWhat you&#39;ll be doing:\n* Providing a listening ear and empathetic support to individuals in recovery.\n* Assisting with the facilitation of group activities and workshops.\n* Helping to create a welcoming and supportive environment within our service.\n* Contributing to the smooth running of our daily operations.\n\nReady to be a part of something truly meaningful? Your time and dedication can empower individuals to overcome challenges and build brighter futures. Sign up today and become a beacon of hope!\n\n## Experience required\n\nPrevious experience in supporting vulnerable adults beneficial but not essential\nGood communication skills\nTo be patient\nnon- judgemental\nApproachable\nFlexible\nAbility to work on own initiative as well as within a team\nHealth and Social care qulification (advantageous)\nKnowledge of addiction/recovery (advantageous)\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe are located in the centre of Coatbridge. Landmarks include ASDA which is across the road from the Fountain business centre where we are in. The police station is across the road from ASDA and is on the same road we are on. The Ball Room pool/snooker hall is located next door to us. Our post code is ML5 3AA\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses will be paid for any work related activities you take part in e.g. going to cafe to do 1:1 peer mentor support, Travel expenses will be paid.",
