            "name": "More Than Fibro",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/MoreThanFibroSC051049",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I0h7RYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I0h7RYAR/stalls-and-events-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-10",
                    "title": "Stalls and Events Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nStalls and Events Volunteers\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for motivated, passionate volunteers to join our volunteer bank to help at stalls and events across Scotland. These events may be to raise awareness of the charity and Fibromyalgie or to fundraise via a tombola or merchandise stall.\n\nfor this opportunity you do need to drive, be comfortable handling money and willing to travel.\n\nthese will range from large scale events such as pride, the pipe band championships or Mela Festival to school fairs or shopping centres\n\nIf you are interested,&nbsp;please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when&nbsp;registered and&nbsp;logged in). You&nbsp;will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that&nbsp;doesn&rsquo;t&nbsp;work&nbsp;out,&nbsp;then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication skills, cash handling, motivated, good timekeeping and a passion to make a difference\n\n## Travel details\n\nby car\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nwe pay 55p per mile when travelling by car, or bus and train fares, we also allocate £7 for lunch costs",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
