                    "title": "Amatuer Theatre Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAbout Crooked Tree Arts\r\n\r\nCrooked Tree Arts is a creative organisation dedicated to developing new writers, performers, theatre-makers and artists, while creating opportunities for people to participate in the arts.\r\n\r\nOur work spans creative writing, theatre, performance, workshops, community projects and live events. We want to create an environment where people can develop their skills, gain practical experience and contribute to exciting creative projects.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for enthusiastic volunteers who want to get involved and help us make, produce and promote great arts projects.\r\n\r\nThe Role\r\n\r\nAs an Arts & Theatre Volunteer, you will support Crooked Tree Arts across a range of creative and practical activities.\r\n\r\nThis is a flexible role, and your responsibilities can be shaped around your skills, interests and experience.\r\n\r\nYou could become involved in:\r\n\r\nSupporting theatre productions and rehearsals\r\nAssisting with backstage and production work\r\nSupporting actors, directors and creative teams\r\nHelping with set, props, costumes and scenery\r\nAssisting with lighting and sound\r\nSupporting workshops and creative-writing sessions\r\nHelping organise rehearsals, events and performances\r\nFront-of-house and audience support\r\nMarketing, publicity and social media\r\nPhotography, filming and content creation\r\nSupporting community arts projects\r\nHelping with fundraising and promotional activities\r\nResearching venues, opportunities and potential partners\r\nGeneral administrative and organisational support\r\nBringing your own creative ideas and projects to Crooked Tree Arts\r\nWhat We're Looking For\r\n\r\nYou don't need to have professional theatre experience. We are interested in people who are:\r\n\r\nPassionate about theatre, writing or the arts\r\nReliable and willing to contribute\r\nCreative and enthusiastic\r\nComfortable working as part of a team\r\nWilling to learn new skills\r\nOrganised and practical\r\nRespectful of other people's ideas and contributions\r\nInterested in helping create opportunities for other artists\r\nPrevious experience in theatre, writing, events, community arts, marketing or production is welcome but not essential.\r\n\r\nWhat You Can Gain\r\n\r\nVolunteering with Crooked Tree Arts can provide opportunities to:\r\n\r\nGain practical experience in theatre and the arts\r\nDevelop new creative and professional skills\r\nBuild experience for your CV or portfolio\r\nWork alongside writers, performers and theatre-makers\r\nDevelop contacts within the creative sector\r\nGet involved in live productions and events\r\nExplore different areas of theatre production\r\nTake part in creative workshops and projects\r\nContribute ideas and develop your own creative interests\r\nWhere appropriate, Crooked Tree Arts will provide references and confirmation of voluntary experience.\r\n\r\nOur Approach\r\n\r\nWe believe theatre should be collaborative.\r\n\r\nYou don't have to arrive knowing exactly what you want to do. You might start by helping backstage and discover a passion for production. You might volunteer at an event and end up developing your own creative project.\r\n\r\nWe're interested in what you can bring — and what you want to learn.\r\n\r\nCommitment\r\n\r\nVolunteer hours will vary depending on the project. We understand that volunteers have work, education and other commitments, so we will discuss availability with you and agree responsibilities on a project-by-project basis.\r\n\r\nHow to Apply\r\n\r\nIf you'd like to join Crooked Tree Arts as a volunteer, please get in touch with a short introduction telling us:\r\n\r\nWho you are\r\nWhat interests you about theatre and the arts\r\nAny relevant skills or experience\r\nWhat you'd like to get involved with\r\nYour general availability\r\nCome and help us grow something creative.\r\n\r\nWork Location: Hybrid remote in Dundee",
