            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000019ntgoYAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000019ntgoYAA/lauderdale-community-council",
            "name": "Lauderdale Community Council",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I1YIDYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I1YIDYA3/winter-warmer-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-02",
                    "title": "Winter Warmer Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWinter Warmers are a series of events being held once a week on a Tuesday from 20 October 2026 to 2 March 2027 in Lauder Public Hall for people to come and socialise, play games, participate in activities and have refreshments including a soup lunch. You would help set up regular activities such as jigsaws, crafts, newspapers and books for attendees to use; if necessary you will play activities with attendees; serve food at lunchtime and help tidy away activities and tidy the Hall at the end of the event. This is a new event for Lauder so it is an opportunity to shape how these events are run and be part of something new.\n\n## Description\n\nWorking with our Co-ordinator and other local volunteers you will help: \r\n- Ensure the weekly activities are set out at the start of each session. \r\n- Ensure refreshments are set out, and topped up including helping in the preparation of soup. \r\n- Welcome people to the event.\r\n- Play games with attendees as required\r\n- Set the dining table\r\n- Serve soup and other refreshments at lunchtime\r\n- Tidy up the weekly activities and hall at the end of each session.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo real skills but we are looking for someone who is friendly, motivated and reliability.\n\n## Training details\n\nAnyone interested in the role would get support from the Co-ordinator and other volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe Co-ordinator will be present at all the sessions to provide support to volunteers. \r\nAlthough expenses cannot be provided refreshments are available and a soup lunch will be provided at each session.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTransport will not be provided. However the venue is Located in Lauder and there is a bus service No 51 \r\nwhich has a bus stop near the venue. \r\nWe would be flexible with starting and finishing times to fit in with bus timetables. \r\nThere is ample parking at the venue.\n\n## Taster details\n\nAs this is a new event and the start date will be the first session we can't offer a taster session but we can \r\nspeak to anyone interested in the role to provide more information.",
