            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000019ocaoYAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000019ocaoYAA/action-on-hearing-loss",
            "name": "Action on Hearing Loss",
            "description": "Action on Hearing Loss provides a helping hand to those confronting deafness, tinnitus and hearing loss to live the life they choose. Action on Hearing Loss provide day-to-day care for people who are deaf and have additional needs, supply communication services and training, offer practical advice to help people project their hearing, campaign to change public policy around hearing loss issues and support research into eventual cure for hearing loss and tinnitus.",
            "website": "https://www.actiononhearingloss.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038926"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I1f6nYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I1f6nYAB/rnid-near-you-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-12",
                    "title": "RNID Near-You Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nVolunteer and make a valuable difference to the more than 18 million people in the UK who are deaf, have hearing loss or tinnitus.\n\nHelp us offer a free, in-person drop-in service for people who are deaf, have hearing loss or tinnitus, or want to get their hearing checked.\n\nOur volunteers support hearing aid users by cleaning their hearing aids and replacing batteries and tubing. They provide tips for getting the most from hearing aids.\n\nDon’t worry if you don’t have experience maintaining hearing aids. We give our volunteers full training so they’re knowledgeable and confident setting up and using the hearing aid maintenance kit.\n\nFull training will be provided by NHS Lanarkshire Audiology dept.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,Good Listener,Organised,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Social Conscience,Team Player,Trustworthy,We are particularly keen to hear from people who have a hearing loss and those who wear hearing aids, but neither are essential.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining on how to clean and change tubing on hearing aids is provided by NHS Lanarkshire Audiology Team. Local staff provide training on how to support  people to do our Hearing Check. Various RNID YouTube training videos are also accessible to volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a South Lanarkshire opportunity and takes place in   \nAcross South Lanarkshire\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAll travel expenses to and from drop-in sessions by car or public transport are reimbursed. After 6 month volunteering volunteers are enrolled in the RNID employee assistance program.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I1f6nYAB#role",
