        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000019svzsYAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000019svzsYAA/shahanara",
            "name": "Shahanara",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/Shahanara",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I20MXYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I20MXYAZ/social-media-digital-marketing-volunteer-help-grow-a-glasgow-community-charity",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-15",
                    "title": "Social Media & Digital Marketing Volunteer – Help Grow a Glasgow Community Charity",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSocial Media & Digital Marketing Volunteer – Help Grow a Glasgow Community Charity\n\n## Description\n\nShahanara is looking for a creative and enthusiastic Social Media &amp; Digital Marketing Volunteer to help us develop our online presence and share the impact of our work.\n\nWe are a Glasgow-based charity working with communities through projects focused on wellbeing, culture, inclusion, education and community development.\n\nYou will have the opportunity to take real ownership of our social media presence and help us communicate our work to the wider public.\n\nThe role may include:\n\n\n\tCreating engaging content for our social media channels\n\tDesigning simple graphics and posts using Canva or similar tools\n\tPlanning and scheduling regular content\n\tPromoting community events, activities and opportunities\n\tSharing photographs, stories and project updates\n\tHelping us tell the story and impact of our work\n\tSupporting the development of our overall digital presence\n\tLooking at engagement and helping us understand what content performs well\n\n\nThis would be a great opportunity for someone interested in social media, marketing, communications, content creation or the charity/community sector who would like practical experience and the freedom to develop ideas.\n\nWe are happy to hear from people with existing experience, but we are equally interested in someone who is creative, motivated and keen to learn.\n\nThe role can be flexible and shaped around the volunteer&rsquo;s availability.\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when registered and logged in). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for someone who is:\n\nComfortable using social media, particularly Facebook and Instagram\nCreative and able to think of engaging content ideas\nA clear and confident writer\nComfortable using Canva or willing to learn\nInterested in social media, digital marketing or communications\nReliable and able to work independently\nOrganised and able to plan content ahead\nRespectful of different cultures and communities\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is remote volunteering opportunity, meaning you can volunteer from home, or anywhere with access to WiFi.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\ntravel expenses will be reimbursed and refreshments will be provided",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I20MXYAZ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Social Media & Digital Marketing Volunteer – Help Grow a Glasgow Community Charity",
                        "description": "We are looking for someone who is:\n\nComfortable using social media, particularly Facebook and Instagram\nCreative and able to think of engaging content ideas\nA clear and confident writer\nComfortable using Canva or willing to learn\nInterested in social media, digital marketing or communications\nReliable and able to work independently\nOrganised and able to plan content ahead\nRespectful of different cultures and communities",
