        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000019uuxyYAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000019uuxyYAA/we-are-listening",
            "name": "We Are Listening",
            "description": "We aim to provide support to the large and growing section of the UK’s older population who are living alone, isolated and feeling vulnerable. They may feel socially excluded and our mission is to help relieve their isolation, assisting their integration back into society by providing a telephone and/or correspondence based befriending service.",
            "website": "https://wearelistening.online/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I3Fo9YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I3Fo9YAF/telephone-befrienders",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-22",
                    "title": "Telephone Befrienders",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nRole: Volunteer Telephone Befriender\r\nLocation: Remote / telephone-based\r\nCommitment: Approximately 1 hour per week for a minimum of 6 months\r\n\r\nFollowing recruitment, training and onboarding, volunteers are carefully matched with a client aged 50+ based on interests, availability and other relevant considerations.\r\n\r\nVolunteers arrange a suitable time with their client and make a regular weekly telephone call. Calls are friendly and informal and might include conversations about hobbies, family, current affairs, memories, books, music, television or simply how the client's week has been.\r\n\r\nVolunteers are supported throughout their placement by the We Are Listening team and are never expected to provide counselling, crisis support or professional advice.\n\n## Experience required\n\nActive listening and communication skills\r\nEmpathy and person-centred communication\r\nConfidence communicating with people from different backgrounds and life experiences\r\nUnderstanding of loneliness, social isolation and wellbeing\r\nSafeguarding awareness\r\nProfessional boundaries and confidentiality\r\nReliability, consistency and personal responsibility\r\nReflective practice\r\nRelationship-building skills\r\nExperience of volunteering within a structured charitable organisation\r\nExperience of supporting older adults within the community\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n1 hours per week for a minimum of 6 months\n\n## Travel details\n\nNo travel this is a remote telephone based role.",
