        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000019vV6VYAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000019vV6VYAU/trans-glasgow",
            "name": "Trans Glasgow",
            "description": "Our Mission:\r\nHave Trans Rights respected in Glasgow\r\n\r\nOur Purpose:\r\nTo create a community of peer support for transgender, transexual, non-binary, gender-fluid and intersex people living in Glasgow and the surrounding areas;\r\n\r\nTo promote developments of human rights for transgender, transexual, non-binary, gender-fluid and intersex people so they are included and prevent discrimination and,\r\n\r\nTo promote the need for gender affirming healthcare",
            "website": "https://transglasgow.com",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC055571"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Advocacy",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advocacy"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CampaigningLobbying",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Campaigning / Lobbying"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Equality",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Equality"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Sexuality",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sexuality"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEngagement",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Engagement"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I2OLdYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I2OLdYAN/charity-trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-18",
                    "title": "Charity Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nTrans Glasgow is a registered charity with OSCR which follows the requirements to meet the Charities (Regulation and Administration) (Scotland) Act 2023. Our registration number is: SC055571.\n\nTrans Glasgow’s mission is to have trans rights respected in Glasgow.\n\nTrans Glasgow supports transgender/ transsexual people from across the gender spectrum, who live in Glasgow (Scotland) and the surrounding areas to come together for support and activism. We also work closely with our trans allies to help make this happen.\n\nWe do this by campaigning for Trans Rights and community groups (online and face-to-face). \n\nYou may view more details regarding this voluntary position on our website:\nhttps://sites.google.com/transglasgow.com/transglasgow/get-involved/trustee-recruitment\n\nYou can view our information that is stored by OSCR publicly using this link below: \nhttps://www.oscr.org.uk/about-charities/search-the-register/charity-details?number=SC055571 \n\nThe role of a trustee of Trans Glasgow is to ensure that all money is being used for the charitable purposes that are approved by OSCR that are detailed in our constitution document.\n\nTo create a community of peer support for transgender, transexual, non-binary, gender-fluid and intersex people living in Glasgow and the surrounding areas; \nTo promote developments of human rights for transgender, transexual, non-binary, gender-fluid and intersex people so that they are included and prevent discrimination and, \nTo promote the need for gender affirming healthcare. \n\nThe role of a trustee for Trans Glasgow is to control and manage the charity. Trustees are responsible for the charity’s governance, strategy and making sure it is running smoothly. Trustees must act within the interests of the charity and comply with Charities (Regulation and Administration) (Scotland) Act 2023\n\nGeneral Duties\n\nYou MUST act in the interests of the charity\nYou MUST operate in a manner consistent with the charity’s purpose\nYou MUST act with care and diligence\nYou MUST manage any conflict of interest between the charity and any person or organisation who appoints charity trustees\n\nYou MUST comply with the 2023 Act (specific duties)\nYou MUST operate in a manner consistent with the charity’s purpose\n Charity details on the Scottish Charity Register\nReporting to OSCR making changes to your charity\nYou MUST manage any conflict of interest between the charity and any person or organisation who appoints charity trustees\nFinancial records and reporting\nFundraising\nProviding information to the public\n\nThe role of a trustee with Trans Glasgow is a completely voluntary role. It is NOT a paid role. of Trans Glasgow. Though, there are opportunities to claim out-of-pocket expenses where applicable, e.g. travel expenses.\n\nOSCR also has a criteria of who is not eligible to take up the role as a trustee within a charity. Please check this criteria. If you do believe that you may be unsuitable for the role as trustee (and are interested in the volunteer position) due to the criteria for disqualification, please contact: jamiekerr@transglasgow.com to discuss further. The criteria list can be found using the following link:\nhttps://www.oscr.org.uk/managing-a-charity/managing-charity-trustees/guidance-on-disqualification-criteria-for-charity-trustees-and-those-undertaking-a-senior-management-function/annex-1-criteria-for-disqualification/ \n\nPlease see the documents below for further details.\n\n\nTrustee Pack (provided by OSCR)\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1E2siVs9VB7B-_3umpg-7shtwxzHQ3z0T/view?usp=sharing\nTrustees’ Code of Conduct Policy\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1pR-BMFD_JH8ugvPxOlJK8ZCQjVhDIQoy/view\nRegister of Interest Policy\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1v1yqvylJcTOZBlDUqTJvltwC_GLCheJ2/view\nConstitution of Trans Glasgow\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1dBqda6rODhu8YQ33EZBcg3_6kdEj4WQW/view\n\nWe have four steps to become a trustee/ committee member for Trans Glasgow.\n\n1. Complete Trustee/ Committee Member Application Form\n2. Receive email inviting to interview and details about Trustee/ Committee Member role\n3. Attend an informal interview to learn more about the role(s)\n4. Complete an Onboarding Trustee Form or Onboard Committee Member Form, as applicable\n\n## Experience required\n\nLeadership\nTeam management\nIT skills\nCommunication\nPublic speaking\nActive listening\nMentorship\nTime management\nObjectivity\nGovernance knowledge\nChairing meeting\nConflict resolution\n\n## Training details\n\nOnboarding and Induction\nIT training\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThis is a volunteer role. We are looking for someone to be able to commit to meetings on Thursday evenings and to complete charity governance work in your spare time.\n\n## Travel details\n\nGlasgow and the surrounding areas\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThis is a voluntary role, out-of-pocket expense can be claimed in line with Trans Glasgow's Volunteer Expense Policy\n\n## Taster details\n\nThere will be a period of time to be inducted into the role of Trustee for Trans Glasgow",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
