            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IS7U1YAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IS7U1YAL/general-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-12",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-10",
                    "title": "General Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nGeneral Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nRole of a General Volunteer&nbsp;\nThe role of a General Volunteer is to support the board of trustees.\n\nComittee members will be involved in organising, planning, running and delivering Trans Glasgow activities, such as:\n\n\n\t\n\tFundraising,\n\t\n\t\n\tCampaign planning,\n\t\n\t\n\tSocial media management,\n\t\n\t\n\tWebsite development,\n\t\n\t\n\tCommunity outreach and,\n\t\n\t\n\tNetworking\n\t\n\n\nThis is an unpaid voluntary position.\n\nThis role does not hold voting powers at board meetings.\n\nIf you are interested in holding voting powers, please consider the position of Charity Trustee.\n\nAbout Trans Glasgow\n\nTrans Glasgow is a registered charity with OSCR which follows the requirements to meet the Charities (Regulation and Administration) (Scotland) Act 2023. Our registration number is: SC055571.\n\nTrans Glasgow&rsquo;s mission is to have trans rights respected in Glasgow.\n\nTrans Glasgow supports transgender/ transsexual people from across the gender spectrum, who live in Glasgow (Scotland) and the surrounding areas to come together for support and activism. We also work closely with our trans allies to help make this happen.\n\nWe do this by campaigning for Trans Rights and community groups (online and face-to-face).\n\nYou can view our information that is stored by OSCR publicly using this link below:\n\nhttps://www.oscr.org.uk/about-charities/search-the-register/charity-details?number=SC055571\n\n&nbsp;\n\nClick the Apply button below (available when logged in and registered with Volunteer Glasgow). Your application will be passed to the Rainbow Friendship Centre, who will contact you by email or telephone to discuss the opportunity and next steps.\n\nIf you have not heard back within five working days, please contact the organisation using the contact details provided and check your email junk/spam folder. If you are still unable to make contact, please contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## Experience required\n\nIT, Communication, Team Working, Fundraising, Public Speaking, Social Media, Resilience\n\n## Travel details\n\nHybrid\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteer Expenses",
