        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001A7yPRYAZ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001A7yPRYAZ/reach-out-community-wellbeing-and-support",
            "name": "Reach Out Community Wellbeing and Support",
            "description": "Reach Out Community Wellbeing and support helps people improve their Mental Health through person centred emotional support to anyone 16years and above.\nAiming to reduce Social Isolation and Loneliness, Supporting people to Thrive, Promoting Wellbeing for All.\nThey can offer 1-1 support and check-in service via in person or telephone.\nThere facilitate a service for Wellbeing to help, relive stress & stress management, mindfulness, coping techniques, boundaries and mindset workshops.\nThey run a community Book group, which meet on the last Friday of each month at 1.15pm, within the Central Library, East Kilbride, all abilities of reader welcome.\nThey offer a drop in service where teenagers and adults can study and complete work on their pc's in a safe environment, along with activity lead group sessions available too.\nThey have a food pantry which supplies food / personal care and other requested items to members of the community in need, working in partnership with the EK Community Foodbank. \nThey work in partnership with EK collective and other organisations within Strathmore house to ensure the community are assisted through times in life before the come to crises point, however can still offer help should a Crisis occur.\nThey gift Christmas gifts & food hampers to families in need, working in partnership with The EK Community Foodbank.\nThey can sign post to other services where further help is need, such as addiction services, medical services, adult social services.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC052710"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I35qtYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I35qtYAB/group-work-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-15",
                    "title": "Group Work Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHere at Reach Out Community Wellbeing and Support SCIO 52710 (Reach Out/RO) our community support services are crucial for us in the delivery of our mission to reduce social isolation and loneliness, improve mental wellbeing, and offer a listening ear to individuals across East Kilbride, South Lanarkshire. We are looking for a empathetic Group Working Volunteer to provide regular hosting at groups to support vulnerable adults in the local community.\n\nDescription:\nWe looking for group work volunteers to support us to deliver groups in the community, craft groups and peer support groups. These are aimed at getting those in our community who may be socially isolated or lonely have a place to go and join in a community. The Volunteer will work with our Support Coordinator and/or Group Leader, who will help them get to know our charity and our service users and our safeguarding policies. They will assist at groups with set up and breaking down of the equipment it tables and chairs, Greeting service users and encouraging participation in group.  \n\nWhat impact will they have?\nOur charity is deeply rooted in the local community, working hard to ensure no one has to struggle with isolation alone. Your time, empathy, and consistent presence will help ensure that vulnerable individuals feel valued, connected, and supported. By building a genuine connection, you will directly improve someone's mental wellbeing, boost their self-esteem, and help them feel part of the community once again.\n\nAbout the volunteer\n\nDescription:\nWe are looking for a volunteer who has:\nAn empathetic, warm, and approachable nature.\nExcellent listening and interpersonal communication skills.\nA patient, reliable, and non-judgmental attitude.\nAn understanding of, or a willingness to learn about, mental wellbeing challenges and the impact of isolation.\nA strong commitment to maintaining personal boundaries and strict confidentiality.\nWillingness to undergo a PVG (Protection of Vulnerable Groups) check.\n\nSkills:\nCommunity and Social Care: previous Befriending experience is desirable but not essential, and active listening skills.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,Creative,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Hard Working,Open minded,Patient,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Social Conscience,Team Player,Trustworthy,\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training provided, including safeguarding. ongoing training can be discussed if required.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire Yes\nEast Kilbride",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I35qtYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Group Work Volunteer",
                        "description": "No Expertise, Caring,Creative,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Hard Working,Open minded,Patient,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Social Conscience,Team Player,Trustworthy,",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I35qtYAB/group-work-volunteer?#modal_register_a0gQD00000I35qtYAB",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
