                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I36phYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I36phYAB/befriending-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-15",
                    "title": "Befriending Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nHere at Reach Out Community Wellbeing and Support SCIO 52710 (Reach Out/RO) our community support services are crucial for us in the delivery of our mission to reduce social isolation and loneliness, improve mental wellbeing, and offer a listening ear to individuals across East Kilbride, South Lanarkshire. We are looking for a empathetic Volunteer Befriender to provide regular companionship and emotional support to vulnerable adults in the local community.\n\nDescription:\nWe are looking for a Volunteer Befriender to support us by building meaningful, supportive relationships with individuals who may be isolated or going through a difficult time. The volunteer will work with our Support Coordinator, who will help the volunteer to get to know our charity, our service users, and our safeguarding protocols. Together, they will match the volunteer with a suitable individual based on shared interests and personality.\nThe volunteer will meet regularly with their matched individual, either in their home, out in the local East Kilbride community for a coffee, a walk, or via ‘check in’ telephone calls. They will provide a friendly, non-judgmental listening ear, engage in casual conversation, and encourage the individual to rediscover their confidence and connect with local activities.\nAfter this initial matching process, the volunteer will continue to maintain regular weekly contact with their match. They will log brief catch-ups with the Support Coordinator on a monthly basis to share how the match is progressing, flag any potential wellbeing concerns, and ensure the individual is getting the most out of our support framework.\n\nWhat impact will they have?\nOur charity is deeply rooted in the local community, working hard to ensure no one has to struggle with isolation alone. Your time, empathy, and consistent presence will help ensure that vulnerable individuals feel valued, connected, and supported. By building a genuine connection, you will directly improve someone's mental wellbeing, boost their self-esteem, and help them feel part of the community once again.\n\nAbout the volunteer\n\nDescription:\nWe are looking for a volunteer who has:\nAn empathetic, warm, and approachable nature.\nExcellent listening and interpersonal communication skills.\nA patient, reliable, and non-judgmental attitude.\nAn understanding of, or a willingness to learn about, mental wellbeing challenges and the impact of isolation.\nA strong commitment to maintaining personal boundaries and strict confidentiality.\nWillingness to undergo a PVG (Protection of Vulnerable Groups) check.\n\nSkills:\nCommunity and Social Care: previous Befriending experience is desirable but not essential, and active listening skills.\n\n## Experience required\n\nBefriending / Mentoring,No Expertise, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Open minded,Patient,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Social Conscience,Trustworthy,\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training provided, including safeguarding. ongoing training can be discussed if required.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire Yes\nEast Kilbride\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nFloat given and replenished upon return of reciepts. It is hoped that the service user will pay their own way or take turn about to cover costs of coffee etc.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I36phYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
