            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I4M61YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I4M61YAF/befriender-baby-loss",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-24",
                    "title": "Befriender - Baby Loss",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSands supports anyone who has been affected by pregnancy or baby loss. Sands Befrienders are an essential part of the support that Sands offers, providing group peer support—either face to face or online—for anyone affected by loss.\n\n## Description\n\nAs a bereaved parent, or someone with experience of baby and pregnancy loss, you will know first-hand how isolating this can be. Sands Befrienders have the ability to hold a welcoming and safe space for those who find themselves in a similar situation. We know from talking to bereaved families that the support received from Sands Befrienders is invaluable and can be life-changing. \r\n\r\nMany bereaved parents who received support from Sands local groups go on to volunteer at Sands.\r\n\r\nSands Befrienders volunteer in local groups of two or more volunteers to host regular support meetings, run events, and raise awareness. It is up to each local group to decide what activities best meet the needs of their community, so there is plenty of opportunity to be creative.\r\n\r\nWe have groups that organise support meetings in the form of coffee and chat, walk-and-talks, creative activity-based sessions, choirs, and running clubs. Current meetings take place at Boomerang Community Centre. There are other ways to befriend, online/phone, but primarily this role would be at the meetings.\n\n## Experience required\n\nActive listening skills\r\n› Sensitive communication and diplomacy skills\r\n› Empathy, openness, flexibility, resilience, and a willingness to engage\r\n› Non-judgmental attitude to others\r\n› Capacity to put aside your own story; to manage your own experience of bereavement\r\n› Self-awareness and emotional intelligence\r\n› Able to practise self-care\r\n› Awareness of the need for healthy boundaries\r\n› Awareness of the importance of confidentiality and data protection regulations\r\n› Cultural awareness and commitment to equality and diversity in support\r\n› Teamwork\r\n› Commitment to continued learning and development\r\n› Basic literacy and numeracy, and proficiency in English (if you would be able and willing to offer support in another language, please let us know)\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training via e-learning and live webinar sessions. Monthly befriender catch up sessions and yearly bridge training.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoomerang Community Centre/ Flexible",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I4M61YAF#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Befriender - Baby Loss",
                        "description": "Active listening skills\r\n› Sensitive communication and diplomacy skills\r\n› Empathy, openness, flexibility, resilience, and a willingness to engage\r\n› Non-judgmental attitude to others\r\n› Capacity to put aside your own story; to manage your own experience of bereavement\r\n› Self-awareness and emotional intelligence\r\n› Able to practise self-care\r\n› Awareness of the need for healthy boundaries\r\n› Awareness of the importance of confidentiality and data protection regulations\r\n› Cultural awareness and commitment to equality and diversity in support\r\n› Teamwork\r\n› Commitment to continued learning and development\r\n› Basic literacy and numeracy, and proficiency in English (if you would be able and willing to offer support in another language, please let us know)",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I4M61YAF/befriender-baby-loss?#modal_register_a0gQD00000I4M61YAF",
