        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001A8nexYAB",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001A8nexYAB/gha-rugby-club",
            "name": "GHA Rugby Club",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/GHARugbyClub",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I3EvJYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I3EvJYAV/pitch-bookings-associate-volunteer-gha-rfc",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-18",
                    "title": "Pitch Bookings Associate (Volunteer) – GHA RFC",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nPitch Bookings Associate (Volunteer) – GHA RFC\n\n## Description\n\nOverview \n\nGHA RFC is seeking an organised and customer-focused Pitch Bookings Associate to help manage external use of our pitches at Braidholm. GHA already uses Pitchbooking to automate much of the booking process for repeat customers. This role therefore isn&rsquo;t about manually processing hundreds of bookings. You&rsquo;ll be responsible for making sure the process around the technology works properly: dealing with enquiries, onboarding new customers, resolving problems and helping us make the best possible use of our available pitch capacity.\n\nYou&rsquo;ll also build relationships with our regular hirers and help ensure they have a good experience and continue using Braidholm.\n\nKey Responsibilities&nbsp;\n\n\n\tCustomer Enquiries - Respond to enquiries from organisations and individuals interested in hiring GHA&rsquo;s pitches.\n\tNew Customer Setup - Set up new customers within Pitchbooking and help them understand how the booking process works.\n\tBooking Approval - Approve new bookings against GHA&rsquo;s agreed tariff without needing separate approval for standard bookings.\n\tNon-Standard Requests - Escalate requests involving discounts, unusual arrangements or pricing outside the agreed tariff to Douglas Perrott, Commercial Director\n\tCustomer Support - Help existing customers resolve booking or facilities-related queries.\n\tCustomer Relationships - Maintain good relationships with regular external hirers and help encourage continued use of Braidholm.\n\tPitch Utilisation - Monitor booking patterns and identify periods when pitch capacity is available or underused.\n\tCommercial &amp; Marketing Opportunities - Alert the Commercial and Marketing teams to unused capacity so they can promote availability and generate additional demand.\n\tInternal Coordination - Work with the Facilities team and Club Manager to ensure external bookings work alongside GHA rugby activity and other use of Braidholm.\n\tProcess Improvement - Identify opportunities to make booking and customer management simpler and more effective\n\n\nSystems You&rsquo;ll Use\n\nYour principal system will be Pitchbooking, GHA&rsquo;s online pitch booking platform. You&rsquo;ll also use:\n\n\n\tMicrosoft 365\n\tEmail\n\tExcel / spreadsheets where required\n\tWhatsApp for appropriate internal communication\n\n\nPitchbooking already automates much of the repeat booking process, allowing you to concentrate on customers, exceptions and improving utilisation rather than routine administration.\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when registered and logged in). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEssential\n• Strong organisational skills.\n• Friendly and confident customer communication.\n• Comfortable using online systems.\n• Able to make straightforward decisions independently.\n• Reliable and responsive.\n• Good attention to detail.\nDesirable\n• Experience in customer service, administration, bookings or facilities.\n• Experience dealing with business or organisational customers.\n• Experience within sport, venues or community organisations.\nPrevious rugby experience is not required\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWhilst it is not anticipated that there will be any expenses, if any expenses incurred in the delivery of the volunteering will be covered, subject to prior discussion and approval with the Commercial Director.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I3EvJYAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Pitch Bookings Associate (Volunteer) – GHA RFC",
                        "description": "Essential\n• Strong organisational skills.\n• Friendly and confident customer communication.\n• Comfortable using online systems.\n• Able to make straightforward decisions independently.\n• Reliable and responsive.\n• Good attention to detail.\nDesirable\n• Experience in customer service, administration, bookings or facilities.\n• Experience dealing with business or organisational customers.\n• Experience within sport, venues or community organisations.\nPrevious rugby experience is not required",
                        "applyLink": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/volunteers/opportunity/10305601",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16",
                        "service": [
