                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I3Cn3YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I3Cn3YAF/membership-associate-volunteer-gha-rfc",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-18",
                    "title": "Membership Associate (Volunteer) – GHA RFC",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nMembership Associate (Volunteer) – GHA RFC\n\n## Description\n\nOverview\n\nGHA RFC is seeking an organised and member-focused Membership Associate to help manage the club&rsquo;s membership administration and ensure members receive a good experience when joining, renewing or dealing with the club. With hundreds of members across Minis, Midis, senior rugby, families and supporters, membership is a significant part of both the GHA community and the club&rsquo;s recurring revenue. For the 2026/27 season, VeryConnect is GHA&rsquo;s primary membership platform, managing member records, applications, renewals, payments and communications. We are also progressively moving more membership-related activity into Fanbase, so the role provides an opportunity to help us improve and simplify how membership is managed over time. This is a hands-on role. You&rsquo;ll deal directly with members, keep our membership information accurate, resolve problems and help make joining and renewing with GHA as straightforward as possible.\n\nKey Responsibilities \n\n\n\tMembership Administration - Take responsibility for the day-to-day administration of GHA memberships, including new applications, renewals, changes and member queries.\n\tVeryConnect Administration - Work directly within VeryConnect to manage membership records, applications, payments and communications.\n\tFanbase - Work with Fanbase as GHA progressively introduces more membershiprelated functionality through the platform.\n\tNew Members - Help new members through the joining process, answering questions and resolving any issues that prevent them from completing their membership.\n\tMembership Renewals - Coordinate membership renewal activity, identify members who haven&rsquo;t renewed and help resolve incomplete or unsuccessful renewals.\n\tMember Queries - Act as a point of contact for membership-related questions and make sure members receive prompt, helpful responses.\n\tPayment Issues - Identify incomplete, failed or outstanding membership payments and work with members and the Finance team to resolve them.\n\tMembership Records - Maintain accurate membership data and identify duplicates, missing information and other data-quality issues.\n\tMembership Reporting - Provide the Commercial Director and Club Manager with clear information on membership numbers, new members, renewals, outstanding memberships and other relevant trends.\n\tMembership Retention - Identify members who haven&rsquo;t renewed and help the club understand why, rather than treating membership purely as an administrative process.\n\tProcess Improvement - Help us simplify and improve membership processes, particularly&nbsp;as GHA progressively moves more activity from VeryConnect into Fanbase.\n\n\nSystems You&rsquo;ll Use\n\nYou&rsquo;ll primarily work with:\n\n\n\tVeryConnect &ndash; GHA&rsquo;s primary membership system for 2026/27, covering member records, applications, renewals, payments and communications\n\tFanbase &ndash; increasingly being used across GHA, with more membership-related activity expected to move onto the platform over time\n\tPitchbooking &ndash; GHA&rsquo;s primary tool for pitch and other facilities pre-bookings and invoicing\n\tMicrosoft 365\n\tExcel / spreadsheets where required\n\n\nCommitment \n\n\n\tFlexible involvement throughout the year.\n\tActivity will increase around the annual membership renewal period and beginning of the rugby season.\n\tThe majority of the role can be completed remotely.\n\tSome availability to respond to member queries during the working week would be useful.\n\tOccasional attendance at Braidholm would help you get to know the club and its members.\n\n\nApplication Process\n\nTo express interest, please contact GHA RFC at office@gharugby.co.uk with a brief outline of your experience and why you would like to support the club in this role.\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when registered and logged in). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEssential\n• Strong organisational and administrative skills.\n• Friendly and helpful approach to dealing with members.\n• Strong written communication.\n• Comfortable learning and working with digital systems.\n• Excellent attention to detail.\n• Reliable and responsive.\n• Able to take ownership of queries and see them through to resolution.\n\nDesirable\n• Experience in administration, membership, customer service or CRM.\n• Experience working with databases or membership systems.\n• Experien\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nIt is not expected that any expenses will be incurred, but should this occur these will be reimbursed provided they have been approved in advance by the Commercial Director.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I3Cn3YAF#role",
                        "type": "Role",
