            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I3Y7dYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I3Y7dYAF/trustees",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-19",
                    "title": "Trustees",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nASH - Autistic Social Hub - is a charity in Aberdeen. Our groups and support are designed for autistic (including Aspergers) adults who are 18 and over.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for autistic trustees to join our board. We are an autism led charity for other autistic people with a focus on having a place to be and activities to supplement socialization.\r\nAs a trustee you will have a say on the direction the charity is taking while performing roles involving governance.\r\n\r\nRoles include administration, managing and protecting assets, working with our staff members/volunteers, understanding and promoting our charitable purpose, ensure compliance with charity law, fundraising, promoting safeguarding and accounts.\r\n\r\nTraining or skillsharing can be provided where required, but any skills you bring along involving the above roles would be hugely beneficial.\r\n\r\nThis is a great opportunity for those looking to build a good CV as there's opportunity to express and work with a number of different skills.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Lee Baxter, Chairperson at board@ash-a.org.uk\r\n\r\nFurther details are also available at www.ash-a.org.uk\n\n## Description\n\nASH - Autistic Social Hub - is a charity in Aberdeen. Our groups and support are designed for autistic (including Aspergers) adults who are 18 and over.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for autistic trustees to join our board. We are an autism led charity for other autistic people with a focus on having a place to be and activities to supplement socialization.\r\nAs a trustee you will have a say on the direction the charity is taking while performing roles involving governance.\r\n\r\nRoles include administration, managing and protecting assets, working with our staff members/volunteers, understanding and promoting our charitable purpose, ensure compliance with charity law, fundraising, promoting safeguarding and accounts.\r\n\r\nTraining or skillsharing can be provided where required, but any skills you bring along involving the above roles would be hugely beneficial.\r\n\r\nThis is a great opportunity for those looking to build a good CV as there's opportunity to express and work with a number of different skills.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Lee Baxter, Chairperson at email:  board@ash-a.org.uk\r\n\r\nFurther details are also available at www.ash-a.org.uk\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided to all Volunteers/Trustees.\r\n\r\nUpon agreeing to be a trustee for the charity. We will induct you by taking part in Trustee Governance training. Any interest you have on focusing on an aspect of the charity will be looked at to see if we can upskill you via skillshare or training where required. We are the ones who decide support for volunteers and staff members, if you require support it would be through colleague interaction. \r\nTo be inducted, either you will be invited to the AGM or we will invite you to a board meeting to induct you.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe meet both online and at the charity premises, other meeting places are possible.\r\nThe charity is located in \r\nDavidson House, Innovation Park, Campus One, Balgownie Road, Bridge of Don, Aberdeen, AB22 8GT",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F9dbe9970-6085-4222-8a4a-a898d91bf06a%2FmyUUFBQSyzT7i2VzmwGsDAsiSW92%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=87e0b75e-c647-4332-a73d-8a0cde146ff2",
