        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001APpXLYA1",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001APpXLYA1/youth-economic-review",
            "name": "Youth Economic Review",
            "description": "The Youth Economic Review is a 100% volunteer-led, volunteer-run research group made up of only 15 to 18 year-olds who get to choose their own ideas and interests to write on, collaborate with others in creating research pieces, and have their work published and credited.",
            "website": "https://sites.google.com/view/youth-economic-review/home",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I7svlYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I7svlYAB/youth-author-volunteers-with-youth-economic-review",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-22",
                    "title": "Youth Author Volunteers with Youth Economic Review",
                    "description": "## Description\n\n-Are you interested in Economics, Finance or Politics?\r\n-Do you love to write about what interests you?\r\n-Are you struggling to find volunteering that would support your passion?\r\n-Consider the Youth Economic Review.\r\n\r\nMy name is Hemish Kumar. I'm a 16 year old student in Aberdeen who loves Economics and Politics. You probably don't know me, but I'm sure we share at least one common experience - struggling desperately to find anything, from volunteering, to work experience, essay competitions, research projects, Olympiads currently running, and more importantly, open to our age range, that would benefit your interests in politics and economics, and strengthen your applications for university.\r\n\r\nHowever, I think I have a solution. I am running a 100% volunteer-led, volunteer-run research group made up of only 15 to 18 year-olds who get to choose their own ideas and interests to write on, collaborate with others in creating research pieces, and have their work published and credited. \r\n\r\nIf that sounds interesting to you, consider applying/more information is available at https://sites.google.com/view/youth-economic-review/home or email hshecon@gmail.com\n\n## Experience required\n\nI'm looking for people interested in economics, finance and politics between the ages of 15 and 18. There's absolutely no experience necessary, but practice in writing and thinking like an economist would be great. Youth Economic Review exists to fill the gap between young people and a lack of opportunities to develop their passion, so no experience is necessary.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times to volunteer. All help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis opportunity is 100% online and there is no physical address. People can volunteer from anywhere they please.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F7adca582-542c-4444-88c8-e6726193483c%2Fs6MZxwrEw3Zwkq6E1iUJst7xf1F3%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=f87c1bb6-97d8-4ce4-b154-0656d76dd79a",
