        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001AXxO5YAL",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001AXxO5YAL/the-cloud-crew-cic",
            "name": "The Cloud Crew (CIC)",
            "description": "The Cloud Crew is a community-driven organisation helping people move into tech careers. Our mission is to bridge the gap between learning and employment. We help people gain tech experience, build confidence and make industry connections.  We believe that everyone deserves the chance to succeed, regardless of their background or barriers to employment.\r\n\r\nHow We Help Volunteers\r\nBy combining mentoring and real-world experience, we help skilled job-seekers to move from gaining skills to gaining employment. At the same time, we support organisations and communities to thrive in a digital world. Together, we create opportunities, empower communities, and drive positive change.\r\n\r\nHow We Help Charities\r\nThe Cloud Crew partners with charities to deliver skills-based volunteering, technical support, and mentorship.  Our volunteers and coaches work on real-world projects, helping organisations solve challenges, improve digital capabilities, and amplify social impact — all while developing leadership and professional skills.",
            "website": "https://thecloudcrew.io/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Employment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Employment"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEngagement",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Engagement"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/DigitalITTech",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Digital / IT / Tech"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IBSg9YAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IBSg9YAH/volunteer-mentor-remote",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-29",
                    "title": "Volunteer Mentor (remote)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur non-profit organisation creates pathways between learning and securing a technology-based career. We are deliberate in supporting people from under-represented and low-socio-economic communities. Join us and help us to support unemployed, aspiring Technology Professionals and help someone to reach their potential. \r\n\r\nWe have opportunities for Volunteer Mentors to connect with an unemployed, aspiring technology professional. Our Mentoring Programme runs for one-hour per week, for six weeks. Each Volunteer Mentor is connected with one job-seeker, to guide them through to clarity on their career plan, to support with professionals skills and to provide employability context. \r\n\r\nTraining and support for the Volunteer Mentors is available and we'll provide LinkedIn recommendations based on your volunteering activities. It's a great way to build leadership skills and experience, in a rewarding environment.\r\n\r\nWe create pathways between learning and technology careers for young people, female returners, mid-career re-skillers, people with disabilities, refugees and anyone else looking to launch their career in tech. We appreciate the support of existing industry professionals to support them in their pathway.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for anyone that has had an office-based job for two years or more. We want you to share your experiences of navigating the job market, interviews, entering into a professional workplace and building a career.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe support with coaching and mentoring skills. We provide a structured plan for the six-week sessions.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nOne, six-week cycle of one hour per week. 1:1, remote sessions.\n\n## Travel details\n\nNo travel required",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IBSg9YAH#role",
