        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001AgnarYAB",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001AgnarYAB/baton-of-hope",
            "name": "Baton of Hope",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IEABdYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IEABdYAP/volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAt the Baton of Hope, we believe everyone has something valuable to offer - whether its a skill, a passion, lived experience, or simply make a difference.  volunteers are at the heart of what we do, and together, we can help build a future where fewer lives are lost to suicide and more people find hope.\r\n\r\nYou do not need qualifications or previous experience - just compassion, commitment, and the willingness to be part of positive change.\r\n\r\nBy volunteering for the Baton of Hope, you can use your skills, to support a cause that matters; help break the stigma around suicide and mental health; meet like-minded people who care about making a difference, grow your confidence , learn new skills and be part of something meaningful and know that your contribution is changing lives.\r\n\r\nEvery volunteer, whether you give an hour a month or help with a major project, plays a part in creating hope.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IEABdYAP#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IEABdYAP/volunteer?#modal_register_a0gQD00000IEABdYAP",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": []
                    }
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001AokazYAB",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001AokazYAB/samh-scottish-action-for-mental-health",
            "name": "SAMH (Scottish Action for Mental Health)",
            "website": "https://vanl.teamkinetic.co.uk/profile/SAMHScottishActionforMentalHealth",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IHTUfYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IHTUfYAP/well-informed-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Well Informed Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWell Informed Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nThe Well-Informed Information Service helps people across North Lanarkshire to access a wide range of resources and services related to mental health and wellbeing.\n\nWe also attend&nbsp;events across North Lanarkshire, providing information and support on local mental health and wellbeing services.\n\nAs a Well-Informed volunteer you will have the opportunity to support Stalls, Pop-ups, workshops and events in North Lanarkshire: Promoting positive conversations about mental health and raising awareness of local support services. These interactive gatherings are likely to take place in venues such as Hospitals, Health Centres, Libraries, Leisure centres, Community Events, Conferences &amp; foodbanks, to name a few.&nbsp;\n\nAs a Well-Informed volunteer, you will play a vital role in raising awareness and addressing stigma and discrimination surrounding mental health issues. You will serve as a role model, offering support and directing individuals to local services that exemplify the Well-Informed service.&nbsp;\n\nTasks include:&nbsp;\n\n\n\t\n\tKeeping accurate records of resources given out&nbsp;\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\n\tContribute to the design and delivery of Community Engagement&nbsp;\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\n\tContribute to workshops to raise awareness around mental health&nbsp;\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\n\tPromote the need for self-management &ndash; Use pop-ups, workshops and events to highlight the importance of taking time for yourself to pursue activities that keep your mind and body healthy. &nbsp;\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\n\tWithin these parameters, volunteer&rsquo;s specific interests can be taken into consideration, and we welcome volunteers with lived mental health experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\t\n\n\nTo find out more or to apply directly please email Brain at:&nbsp;brian.reid@samh.org.uk\n\n&quot;From day one, the team at SAMH have made me feel welcomed, valued, and supported.&nbsp;You don&rsquo;t need to be an expert; you just need to have empathy, an open mind, and a willingness to show up.&quot;&nbsp;- Lyndsay, Well-Informed volunteer\n\n## Experience required\n\ngood communication and active listening skills\nempathy\nconfidentiality\nAble to handle distressing disclosures relating to sensitive issues associated with mental health",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IHTUfYAP#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Well Informed Volunteer",
                        "description": "good communication and active listening skills\nempathy\nconfidentiality\nAble to handle distressing disclosures relating to sensitive issues associated with mental health",
                        "applyLink": "https://vanl.teamkinetic.co.uk/volunteers/opportunity/10306386",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
