        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001B3YrNYAV",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001B3YrNYAV/beyond-the-chair",
            "name": "Beyond The Chair",
            "website": "https://stirlingvolunteering.org/profile/BeyondTheChair",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IMguHYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IMguHYAT/trustees-wanted-help-build-beyond-the-chair",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Trustees Wanted – Help Build Beyond the Chair",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTrustees Wanted – Help Build Beyond the Chair\n\n## Description\n\nBeyond the Chair is a new community initiative being developed in Stirling and surrounding areas, providing free professional haircuts, shaves and grooming alongside conversation, connection, active listening and appropriate signposting to support.\n\nThe project aims to support people experiencing homelessness, addiction and recovery, mental health challenges, financial hardship, disadvantage and social isolation - helping people feel seen, respected and valued.\n\nWe&rsquo;re looking for Trustees\n\nWe&rsquo;re looking for people who want to use their skills, experience and perspective to help shape Beyond the Chair as it develops towards becoming a Scottish Charitable Incorporated Organisation (SCIO).\n\nYou don&rsquo;t need previous trustee experience. We&rsquo;re interested in people who are reliable, willing to contribute, passionate about making a positive difference and able to bring their own perspective to the organisation.\n\nTreasurer / Trustee\n\nWe&rsquo;re particularly interested in hearing from someone with experience or an interest in finance, budgeting, accounts or financial governance who could take on the Treasurer role alongside being a trustee.\n\nHow you could help\n\n&middot; Helping shape the charity&rsquo;s direction and development\n\n&middot; Supporting good governance and decision-making\n\n&middot; Bringing your own skills, knowledge and experience\n\n&middot; Helping develop partnerships and funding opportunities\n\n&middot; Supporting financial oversight\n\n&middot; Contributing ideas and constructive challenge\n\n&middot; Helping ensure the project remains focused on its charitable purpose\n\nWe&rsquo;re especially interested in people with experience or knowledge in areas such as finance, charity or governance, community work, safeguarding, fundraising, business, HR or legal matters.\n\nLived experience and other skills that could strengthen the organisation are also valued.\n\nYou don&rsquo;t need to have all of these skills &mdash; what matters most is your willingness to contribute and help build something meaningful for the community.\n\nWhat we can offer\n\n&middot; The opportunity to help shape a new community organisation from the beginning\n\n&middot; A supportive and collaborative environment\n\n&middot; The chance to use your experience to make a practical difference\n\n&middot; Flexible involvement around your availability\n\n&middot; Opportunities to learn and develop your governance experience\n\nLocation: Stirling and surrounding areas\n\nTime commitment: Flexible and to be discussed, with trustee meetings and occasional additional involvement as the project develops.\n\nIf you&rsquo;d like to find out more about becoming a trustee of Beyond the Chair, we&rsquo;d love to hear from you.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nOut of pocket expenses payable with receipts",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IMguHYAT#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Trustees Wanted – Help Build Beyond the Chair",
