                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IMhjtYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IMhjtYAD/volunteer-youth-workerarts-worker",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-06",
                    "title": "Volunteer Youth Worker/Arts Worker",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteer Youth Worker/Arts Worker\n\n## Description\n\nJoin us for an exciting opportunity to make a real difference in the lives of care-experienced young people! Our program offers a vibrant and supportive environment where children aged 8-12 can explore their creativity and build confidence. We&#39;re looking for enthusiastic volunteers to help facilitate engaging sessions that blend fun arts and crafts with other enriching activities.\n\nWhat you&#39;ll be doing:\n* Guiding young people through a variety of creative arts and crafts projects, fostering imagination and self-expression.\n* Participating in interactive games and team-building activities designed to encourage social skills and positive peer relationships.\n* Providing a listening ear and a supportive presence, helping to create a safe and welcoming space for all participants.\n* Assisting with the setup and cleanup of activity spaces, ensuring a smooth and enjoyable experience for everyone.\n\n*Helping support away day trips and events.\n\nIf you&#39;re passionate about empowering young people and have a knack for creativity and fun, we&#39;d love to have you on board! These sessions meet fortnightly in Belshill on Tuesdays from 4pm to 5:30pm. Come be a part of something truly rewarding!\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication skills.\nPatience.\nBe a good listener.\nExperience of or hoping to gain experience of working with children.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
