            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ITzc3YAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ITzc3YAD/community-golf-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-09",
                    "title": "Community Golf Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAt Golf in Society, we run welcoming Golf Health Hubs at local golf clubs — inclusive spaces where people living with long-term conditions, along with carers and families, can move more, connect with others, and rediscover joy.\r\n\r\nWHY BECOME A COMMUNITY GOLF VOLUNTEER?\r\n\r\nThis isn't just a role - it's a chance to give something back through the sport you love.\r\n• See the difference you make, week after week\r\n• Use your love of golf for real purpose\r\n• A flexible role that fits around your life\r\n• Full training and ongoing support, every step of the way\r\n\r\nGIVE BACK THROUGH GOLF:\r\n\r\nGet in touch to find out more about the opportunities to get involved as a Community Golf Volunteer - please contact Tom Duff, Regional Lead (Scotland) at email: tom@golfinsociety.com or telephone: 07824440319\r\n\r\nMore information is also available at www.golfinsociety.com\n\n## Description\n\nAt Golf in Society, we run welcoming Golf Health Hubs at local golf clubs — inclusive spaces where people living with long-term conditions, along with carers and families, can move more, connect with others, and rediscover joy.\r\n\r\nWHY BECOME A COMMUNITY GOLF VOLUNTEER?\r\n\r\nThis isn't just a role - it's a chance to give something back through the sport you love.\r\n• See the difference you make, week after week\r\n• Use your love of golf for real purpose\r\n• A flexible role that fits around your life\r\n• Full training and ongoing support, every step of the way\r\n\r\nGIVE BACK THROUGH GOLF:\r\n\r\nGet in touch to find out more about the opportunities to get involved as a Community Golf Volunteer - please contact Tom Duff, Regional Lead (Scotland) at email: tom@golfinsociety.com or telephone: 07824440319\r\n\r\nMore information is also available at www.golfinsociety.com\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training and support is provided to all volunteers, which includes club online training and 1:1 training on site.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAberdeen and surrounding areas 1/2 hours per week",
