        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001CqHnBYAV",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001CqHnBYAV/invisible-cities-scottish-borders",
            "name": "Invisible Cities - Scottish Borders",
            "website": "https://invisible-cities.org/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IzxyTYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IzxyTYAR/tour-guide-support",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-27",
                    "title": "Tour Guide Support",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nJoin Invisible Cities in Galashiels and help us make a positive difference through walking tours, storytelling and community activities!\r\n\r\nWe are looking for friendly and enthusiastic volunteers to support our tour guides during practice sessions, assist with walking tours and get involved in occasional community events and activities across the Scottish Borders.\r\nVolunteering is flexible and opportunities are offered throughout the year, depending on upcoming activities. No previous experience is needed, just a willingness to get involved, meet new people and support your local community.\r\nIt is also a great opportunity to learn more about Invisible Cities, develop new skills and potentially explore becoming a walking tour guide yourself in the future!\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteering with Invisible Cities is a great opportunity to become part of a friendly and passionate team that supports people who have experienced homelessness and social hardship through tourism, storytelling and community activities.\r\n\r\nWe are developing our walking tours and community activities in Galashiels and are looking for enthusiastic volunteers who would like to get involved and support our work in the Scottish Borders.\r\n\r\nUnlike traditional volunteering roles, our opportunities are flexible and mostly occasional, depending on upcoming tours, training sessions, events and community projects. This makes volunteering with us a great opportunity for people who enjoy meeting others, learning new things and supporting their local community without committing to a regular weekly schedule.\r\nWhat might volunteering involve?\r\n\r\nVolunteers may support:\r\n• Tour practice sessions - joining our guides as they practise and develop their walking tours, providing encouragement, feedback and helping them build confidence.\r\n• Walking tours - supporting guides during tours, welcoming participants and helping ensure everyone has a positive experience.\r\n• Community events - representing Invisible Cities at local events, festivals and community gatherings.\r\n• Training and workshops - supporting occasional activities designed to help our guides and trainees develop their skills and confidence.\r\n• Other activities - getting involved in new projects, partnerships and opportunities as they arise across Galashiels and the Scottish Borders.\r\n\r\nWho are we looking for?\r\nWe welcome volunteers who are friendly, reliable, open-minded and interested in supporting their local community. You do not need previous volunteering experience or specialist knowledge of Galashiels – just enthusiasm, a positive attitude and a willingness to get involved.\r\n\r\nWhat can you gain from volunteering?\r\n• Experience supporting a social enterprise and community tourism activities.\r\n• Opportunities to meet new people and build connections within the local community.\r\n• Development of communication, teamwork and confidence-building skills.\r\n• Opportunities to learn more about Galashiels, its history and local stories.\r\n• A chance to support people in developing their skills and achieving their goals.\r\n• Flexible volunteering opportunities that fit around your availability. \r\n\r\nPotential candidates will be offered an informal chat either in person or online. They will be given all details about this opportunity and might ask any questions.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnthusiasm, a positive attitude and a willingness to get involved.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nVolunteers will be referring to the project manager at Invisible Cities.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteers will have opportunities to take part in ongoing training and development sessions alongside our tour guides and trainees. These sessions cover a variety of topics and help build confidence, communication skills, teamwork and knowledge relevant to our activities.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAll travels will be discussed before any activities.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IzxyTYAR#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Tour Guide Support",
                        "description": "Enthusiasm, a positive attitude and a willingness to get involved.",
                        "commitment": "Volunteers will be referring to the project manager at Invisible Cities.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IzxyTYAR/tour-guide-support?#modal_register_a0gQD00000IzxyTYAR",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/HomelessHousing",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Homeless / Housing"
                            },
                            {
