        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000tWoi4YAC",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000tWoi4YAC/culter-football-club",
            "name": "Culter Football Club",
            "description": "Culter FC, based at Crombie Park in Peterculter, Aberdeen has a proud history, deep local roots and ambitious plans for the future.",
            "website": "https://www.culterfc.co.uk/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Dr44PYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Dr44PYAR/culter-football-club-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-24",
                    "title": "Culter Football Club Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCulter FC is offering an exciting and meaningful opportunity for a motivated and community-minded individual to play a key role in the growth of one of the North Region’s most respected semi-professional football clubs. Based in Peterculter the club has a proud history, deep local roots and ambitious plans for the future and we’re now looking for someone who wants to help drive that vision forward.\r\n\r\nAs Commercial Manager, you will be at the heart of the club’s external relationships, helping to identify and secure new sponsorship and partnership opportunities that directly support team development, facilities improvements, and long-term sustainability. This is a brilliant chance to take on a visible, outward-facing role where your communication skills, creativity and enthusiasm can make a real difference.\r\n\r\nWorking closely with the club’s Executive Committee and management team, you’ll help develop tailored sponsorship packages, engaging proposals, and fresh commercial ideas that appeal to local businesses and organisations. Whether it’s matchday partnerships, advertising opportunities, themed events, or brand-new initiatives you help shape, you will have the space to bring your ideas forward and see them come to life.\r\n\r\nThis opportunity is perfect for someone with an interest or background in sales, business development, marketing, or community engagement or for someone simply looking to gain valuable experience in the sports industry. It provides an excellent platform to build your professional confidence, expand your local network, and contribute to a club that plays a meaningful role within its community.\r\n\r\nYou will also help maintain and strengthen relationships with Culter FC’s existing sponsors, ensuring they feel connected, appreciated, and engaged. Attending home fixtures and selected club events, you will act as an ambassador for the club, representing its values and helping foster positive engagement with partners and supporters.\r\n\r\n\r\nIf you’re self-motivated, confident in speaking with people, and excited by the prospect of creating new opportunities for a well-established community club, this role offers a fantastic chance to make a real impact. You’ll gain hands-on experience in sports commercial operations, develop lasting relationships, and be part of a warm, ambitious and forward-looking football environment.\r\n\r\nVolunteers will receive a full induction covering the club’s history, values, commercial objectives and current sponsorship portfolio. You’ll be introduced to key committee members, given guidance on our sponsorship packages, and supported in approaching local businesses. \r\n\r\nOngoing training is available through regular check-ins with the Executive Committee, who will provide mentoring, resources, and updates to help you succeed in the role. \r\n\r\nYou won’t be volunteering alone continuous support is offered to ensure you feel confident, informed, and part of the wider Culter FC team.\r\n\r\nThis is more than a volunteer role - it’s your chance to be part of Culter FC’s journey and contribute to the club’s long-term success both on and off the pitch.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Beth Towsey at email beth@protea-consult.com\n\n## Description\n\nCulter FC is offering an exciting and meaningful opportunity for a motivated and community-minded individual to play a key role in the growth of one of the North Region’s most respected semi-professional football clubs. Based in Peterculter the club has a proud history, deep local roots and ambitious plans for the future and we’re now looking for someone who wants to help drive that vision forward.\r\n\r\nAs Commercial Manager, you will be at the heart of the club’s external relationships, helping to identify and secure new sponsorship and partnership opportunities that directly support team development, facilities improvements, and long-term sustainability. This is a brilliant chance to take on a visible, outward-facing role where your communication skills, creativity and enthusiasm can make a real difference.\r\n\r\nWorking closely with the club’s Executive Committee and management team, you’ll help develop tailored sponsorship packages, engaging proposals, and fresh commercial ideas that appeal to local businesses and organisations. Whether it’s matchday partnerships, advertising opportunities, themed events, or brand-new initiatives you help shape, you will have the space to bring your ideas forward and see them come to life.\r\n\r\nThis opportunity is perfect for someone with an interest or background in sales, business development, marketing, or community engagement or for someone simply looking to gain valuable experience in the sports industry. It provides an excellent platform to build your professional confidence, expand your local network, and contribute to a club that plays a meaningful role within its community.\r\n\r\nYou will also help maintain and strengthen relationships with Culter FC’s existing sponsors, ensuring they feel connected, appreciated, and engaged. Attending home fixtures and selected club events, you will act as an ambassador for the club, representing its values and helping foster positive engagement with partners and supporters.\r\n\r\n\r\nIf you’re self-motivated, confident in speaking with people, and excited by the prospect of creating new opportunities for a well-established community club, this role offers a fantastic chance to make a real impact. You’ll gain hands-on experience in sports commercial operations, develop lasting relationships, and be part of a warm, ambitious and forward-looking football environment.\r\n\r\nVolunteers will receive a full induction covering the club’s history, values, commercial objectives and current sponsorship portfolio. You’ll be introduced to key committee members, given guidance on our sponsorship packages, and supported in approaching local businesses. \r\n\r\nOngoing training is available through regular check-ins with the Executive Committee, who will provide mentoring, resources, and updates to help you succeed in the role. \r\n\r\nYou won’t be volunteering alone continuous support is offered to ensure you feel confident, informed, and part of the wider Culter FC team.\r\n\r\nThis is more than a volunteer role - it’s your chance to be part of Culter FC’s journey and contribute to the club’s long-term success both on and off the pitch.\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Beth Towsey at email beth@protea-consult.com\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant guidance and excellent support provided to all volunteers.\r\n\r\nVolunteers will receive a full induction covering the club’s history, values, commercial objectives and current sponsorship portfolio. You’ll be introduced to key committee members, given guidance on our sponsorship packages, and supported in approaching local businesses. \r\n\r\nOngoing training is available through regular check-ins with the Executive Committee, who will provide mentoring, resources, and updates to help you succeed in the role. \r\n\r\nYou won’t be volunteering alone continuous support is offered to ensure you feel confident, informed, and part of the wider Culter FC team.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to suit volunteers. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place with Culter FC, based at Crombie Park in Peterculter, Aberdeen.\r\n\r\nMost activity happens locally, including attending home matches, meeting sponsors and engaging with nearby businesses. Travel is minimal and mainly within the Aberdeen and Aberdeenshire area. Occasional off-site meetings may occur depending on sponsor locations but arrangements are flexible and can be planned around your availability. \r\n\r\nReliable transport is helpful but not essential, as most duties can be carried out in and around Peterculter or remotely through email, phone and online platforms.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fbf354b25-f434-4c5c-8b8b-ee52a1555ee3%2F6q86WJLAgLMxNCdsi1m44oX1lIZ2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=d6acd166-2d67-4c57-a331-3783b96d629b",
