        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000ybCm5YAE",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000ybCm5YAE/glasgow-nw-foodbank",
            "name": "Glasgow NW Foodbank",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/GlasgowNWFoodbank",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HlZerYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HlZerYAF/volunteer-driver",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer driver",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteer driver\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteer Driver Wanted\n\nHelp Deliver More Than Food\n\nGlasgow NW Foodbank is looking for a reliable and friendly Volunteer Driver to help collect and deliver food donations that support people facing hardship across our local community.\n\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to make a real difference and become part of our dedicated volunteer team.\n\nWhat you&#39;ll be doing:\n\n\n\tDriving the foodbank van to collect donations from supermarkets, businesses and community collection points.\n\tDelivering food and supplies between our foodbank locations.\n\tLoading and unloading crates of food donations.\n\tHelping ensure donations are handled safely and respectfully.\n\tRepresenting Glasgow NW Foodbank in a friendly and professional manner when meeting donors and partner organisations.\n\n\nWe&#39;re looking for someone who:\n\n\n\tHolds a full, clean UK driving licence.\n\tIs physically able to lift and carry crates of food donations.\n\tIs available for a couple of hours on Monday, Tuesday and Wednesday mornings.\n\tIs reliable, punctual and trustworthy.\n\tHas good communication and people skills.\n\tEnjoys working as part of a team while also being confident working independently.\n\tShares our commitment to supporting people with dignity and compassion.\n\n\n&nbsp;\n\nIf you&#39;d like to join our team or would like more information, we&#39;d love to hear from you.\n\nEmail: info@glasgownwfoodbank.org.uk\nTelephone: 07787 334012\n\nHelp us ensure no one in our community has to face hunger alone.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous volunteering experience is necessary—just a willingness to help and a positive attitude.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBy train\nThe nearest station is Garscadden Station, which is about a short walk from the church (around 3 minutes according to local transport information).\nGarscadden is served by ScotRail services, including routes on the Argyle Line.\nBy bus\nA nearby option is the First Bus Route 1 along Dumbarton Road. Get off near Kingsway Flats, then follow signs towards Blawarthill Church.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HlZerYAF#role",
