                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FthIEYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FthIEYAZ/teacher-assistants-italian-language",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Teacher Assistants - Italian Language",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are a Scottish Charity who provide courses of Italian language to children and young people 5-17 years old (in Aberdeen at the Aberdeen Grammar School, Skene Street, Aberdeen AB10 1HT - Saturday mornings 9:30–10:30 (P2/7) and 10:30–11:30 (S1/5) and also online). We are funded by the Italian Ministry of Foreign Affairs.\r\n\r\nThis position involves supporting the teacher during class time. The assistant helps students with activities assigned by the teacher and, if desired, can be involved in preparing materials and lessons.\r\n\r\nThese are two 1-hour classes held on Saturday mornings 9:30-10:30 and 10:30-11:30 for 27 Saturdays between September and May.\r\n\r\nIt is necessary to have a good knowledge of the Italian language and some experience with children and teenagers, preferably but not necessarily in teaching.\r\n\r\nThe assistant must be available to enroll in the PVG scheme and already have a residence, work or volunteer permit in the UK (we cannot sponsor this).\r\n\r\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. We refund any travel/bus ticket.s and if the volunteer has children 5 year old and older they can bring them at the lesson for free.\r\n\r\nA great opportunity to assist in the teaching of Italian and the educational development of children. For more details please contact Valentina Tamanini at email: info@girotondoitalianschool.org.uk\r\n\r\nFurther information is also available at https://girotondoitalianschool.org.uk/\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers:\r\n-must  know the Italian language at a good level;\r\n-must be available to enroll in the PVG scheme\r\n-already have a residence, work or volunteer permit in the UK (we cannot sponsor this).\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nSaturday mornings 9:30–10:30 (P2/7) and 10:30–11:30 (S1/5) and also online.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBased at Aberdeen Grammar School, Skene Street, Aberdeen AB10 1HT - Saturday mornings 9:30–10:30 (P2/7) and 10:30–11:30 (S1/5) and also online).\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe refund the bus ticket. \r\n\r\nIf the volunteer has children 5 year old and older they can bring them at the lesson for free.",
