        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000zYbQMYA0",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000zYbQMYA0/debra",
            "name": "DEBRA",
            "description": "DEBRA is the national charity that supports individuals and families affected by Epidermolysis Bullosa (EB) - a rare genetic condition. As we receive no government funding DEBRA relies on the generosity of the public to carry out its vital work improving lives and giving hope.",
            "website": "https://www.debra.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC039654"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FvuXvYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FvuXvYAJ/volunteer-shop-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-04",
                    "title": "Volunteer Shop Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\n\"We're recruiting new volunteers for our popular charity shops across the UK. Join our friendly team and do something you'll really love! Whether you're looking to learn new skills, gain experience in retail, meet new people or just have fun, our wide range of activities mean we have a perfect role for everyone.\n\nIf you are passionate about helping to make a difference through giving your time, then why not get in touch? Please note this is an unpaid volunteering role even although the salary is shown as £0.01.\n\nThe role will involve:\n\n· Serving customers and using the computerised till to take payments for purchases\n\n· Sorting donated stock, clothing and bric-a-brac\n\n· Recording donor details for gift-aid\n\n· Using a steaming appliance on donated clothes\n\n· Assisting the shop manager with any other task to keep the shop running efficiently\n\nDEBRA is the national charity that funds research and healthcare to support individuals and families affected by Epidermolysis Bullosa (EB) – a painful genetic skin blistering condition which, in the worst cases, can be fatal.\n\nJob Type: Volunteer\n\nApplication question(s):\n\n\nDo you have any unspent convictions or are subject to any criminal registers /orders?\nIf you need some assistance with this question, please consult the official guidance on the 1974 Rehabilitation Act for further information. Please note that having a conviction will not necessarily stop you from volunteering. If a criminal conviction is declared, a risk assessment will be completed, taking into account the circumstances and background of the offence(s) before any offer of volunteering is made.\n\n\nWork authorisation:\n\n\nUnited Kingdom (required)\nWork Location: In person\"\n\n## Experience required\n\nCleaning / Tidying / Sorting,No Expertise,Retail / Customer Service, Caring,Creative,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Hard Working,Open minded,Organised,Patient,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Social Conscience,Team Player,Trustworthy,\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire,Lanark\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses are paid once training is complete",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
