        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000zrUjTYAU",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000zrUjTYAU/equi-innse-gall-cic",
            "name": "Equi Innse Gall CIC",
            "description": "The Community Interest Company was set up to offer Equine Assisted Learning through coaching and therapeutic experiences, individual personal development, group and team sessions.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AnimalWelfare",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Animal Welfare"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GwtqwYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GwtqwYAB/equi-innse-gall-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-20",
                    "title": "Equi-Innse Gall Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nEqui-Innse Gall CIC is seeking volunteers to support daily yard duties at its Equine Facilitated Learning Centre on the Isle of Lewis. Tasks include stable cleaning, feeding, paddock maintenance and caring for horses. Volunteers should be reliable, physically fit, caring and comfortable working outdoors in all weather conditions. No previous experience is required.\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteering opportunities are now available to assist with Equi-Innse Gall Community Interest Company which is an Equine Facilitated Learning Centre on the West coast of the Isle of Lewis. We provide bespoke sessions for people who encounter life challenges such as low confidence or self esteem, mental health issues, neuro-diversity, bereavement, family and relationship difficulties or ongoing health matters. We assist people with the support of our equine herd to explore and develop their life skills and coping strategies through one to one and small group coaching. Own transport arrangements are essential.\r\n\r\nTo volunteer with us you will need the following attributes and skills:\r\n\r\n•\tPatient and caring with a strong emphasis on animal welfare\r\n•\tGood listening skills and ability to follow instruction\r\n•\tHappy to work as a team member but able to work independently on tasks\r\n•\tClear and accurate communication skills\r\n•\tExhibit attention to detail\r\n•\tAccept that the role is to support with yard work not be involved in EFL sessions\r\n•\tHappy to work in all weathers*\r\n•\tGood physical fitness, lifting and general moving of bulky items can be needed\r\n•\tConsiderate to others and attentive to personal self care\r\n•\tBe punctual, commit to attend – mutually agreed times for at least 2 hours a week.\r\n\r\n*sometimes work will only be indoors especially in the worst weather and storms may mean volunteer sessions are cancelled.\r\n\r\nWhat you will be doing to help:\r\n\r\n•\tMucking out stables/ yards, ensuring cleanliness and good hygiene for horses\r\n•\tLearning about what the CIC does and what EFL offers participants\r\n•\tHelping to provide a safe, caring environment for the equines\r\n•\tStable/ Fence/ paddock/ pasture maintenance\r\n•\tPreparing feed and sometime helping at feed time\r\n•\tLearning how we handle and care for our equines - Natural Horsemanship skills\r\n•\tCleaning and maintenance generally, including Annual/ Bi-annual/ monthly tasks\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat you will gain from volunteering:\r\n\r\nVolunteering can be an incredibly rewarding use of your time and commitment, we’d appreciate your support at the islands only Equine Facilitated Learning Centre. You will gain invaluable experience helping Equi-Innse Gall CIC in providing support to islanders & the equines so we can provide vital services to our community. Natural Horsemanship ways of working with our herd enjoying the essential 3 F’s of freedom, forage and friendship will embed new ways of working and recognising the rich rewards of Equine and Human interaction. No experience is needed as we’re happy to train volunteers and upskill those who are interested. A trial period will be agreed initially. Codes of Conduct and Ethics which we will share with suitable applicants, must be agreed to before commencement of volunteering activities. Thanks for taking the time to consider this opportunity.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience is needed as Equi-Innse Gall CIC will provide  training for volunteers and upskill those who are interested. A trial period will be agreed initially.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMinimum of 2 hours per week, times to be agreed.\n\n## Travel details\n\nEqui-Innse Gall CIC is located on the West coast of the Isle of Lewis. Own transport arrangements are essential.\n\n## Taster details\n\nA trial period will be agreed initially.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Ff02f578e-6e10-4fff-8686-60b27f4fd99e%2Fq3QKxrkTqGVpou9MjTosfVMwM2K2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=91233379-89a3-449d-b230-66a6b974afa2",
