        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001CrUtPYAV",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001CrUtPYAV/anxiety-aid-international",
            "name": "Anxiety Aid International",
            "description": "A Scottish charity helping people understand worry and anxiety earlier, and build practical ways to cope.\r\nBased in Ayr. Currently working across South Ayrshire.",
            "website": "https://anxietyaidinternational.org/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC055392"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000J0CzJYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000J0CzJYAV/fundraising-and-donations-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-27",
                    "title": "Fundraising and Donations Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAyr and South Ayrshire.   Usually 2–4 hours weekly, flexibly agreed\r\n\r\nAbout the charity: \r\nAnxiety Aid International is a new Scottish charity providing free anxiety information, self-guided calming tools and Ask AAI, an online information and signposting assistant. \r\nToo many people struggle for too long before they understand what is happening or find the right support.\r\nChildren, teenagers, adults and families can all be affected. Existing health, statutory, charitable and community services do essential work, but demand is significant and accessible early support matters. AAI was created to help bridge that gap.\r\n\r\nYour role:\r\nRaise funds through approved appeals, donor relationships and fundraising activities. Our initial £20,000 campaign supports awareness materials, outreach and the free website platform. Premises and staff are longer-term aims for a later fundraising phase.\r\n\r\nWhat you could do:\r\n•\tApproach agreed potential supporters and businesses about donations or sponsorship, using trustee-approved appeal information.\r\n•\tHelp promote one-off and monthly giving once the website donation facilities are live, and follow up agreed donor enquiries.\r\n•\tSuggest and help organise approved fundraising activities, such as sponsored community walks, with the Volunteer Lead.\r\n•\tKeep accurate, secure records of approaches, donations and any stated restrictions, using approved charity systems.\r\n•\tAfter training and authorisation, help with collections, receipts and prompt transfer of funds through the charity’s agreed procedures.\r\nUse honest, approved messages explaining what funds are for. \r\nThis role does not provide treatment or individual anxiety support.\r\n\r\nWho would enjoy this:\r\n\r\nEnjoyment of conversations, organisation and following things through matters more than fundraising experience. You can develop fundraising skills and supporter relationships. There are no compulsory personal fundraising targets.\r\nLocation and support\r\nLocal activities and private meetings at Alloway House, Ayr, with some preparation possible remotely.  We provide a named backup, induction, approved materials, relevant training, regular check-ins and team catch-ups under our volunteer policies. Tasks and access needs are agreed before you start.\r\n\r\nTime and expenses\r\nUnpaid and flexible, including induction and support time. Reasonable expenses are agreed before costs arise and reimbursed under charity policy. \r\n\r\nGet involved\r\nEmail hello@anxietyaidinternational.org for an informal conversation. We welcome different backgrounds and experience; you do not need to disclose any personal experience of anxiety.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEnjoyment of conversations, organisation and following things through matters more than fundraising experience",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F3c89311c-7d96-4101-b1f1-e8aed70b4e20%2FgXz0VvDaMsRlbbav2QV4VMFr6sm1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=5680f0de-9b58-4498-a556-90b3cf015673",
