                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000J0GLGYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000J0GLGYA3/community-awareness-and-events-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-27",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-27",
                    "title": "Community Awareness and Events Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAyr and South Ayrshire.   Usually 2–4 hours weekly, flexibly agreed\r\n\r\nAbout the charity.\r\n\r\nAnxiety Aid International is a new Scottish charity providing free anxiety information, self-guided calming tools and Ask AAI, an online information and signposting assistant. \r\nToo many people struggle for too long before they understand what is happening or find the right support.\r\nChildren, teenagers, adults and families can all be affected. \r\n\r\nExisting health, statutory, charitable and community services do essential work, but demand is significant and accessible early support matters. AAI was created to help bridge that gap.\r\n\r\nYour role:\r\nYour focus will be to raise awareness: introducing our resources to local people and organisations, building community connections and attending information events. \r\n\r\nWhat you could do\r\n•\tIntroduce the charity to community groups, employers, colleges and local networks using approved information.\r\n•\tAttend agreed information events and awareness stalls, welcome visitors and show them how to find the website tools and online assistant.\r\n•\tDistribute approved leaflets and QR cards, and help with safe set-up and pack-down of information displays.\r\n•\tIdentify suitable awareness opportunities and maintain agreed community contacts.\r\n•\tRecord groups contacted, events attended and approximate numbers reached.\r\n•\tPass donation, sponsorship and fundraising enquiries to the Volunteer Lead for the fundraising role to follow up.\r\n\r\nClear responsibilities\r\nYou will explain and raise awareness of AAI approved resources and signposting. \r\nThis role does not include providing counselling, diagnosis, therapy, individual anxiety support or crisis assessment. \r\n\r\nLocation and support\r\nLocal activities and private meetings at Alloway House, Ayr, with some preparation possible remotely.  We provide a named backup, induction, approved materials, relevant training, regular check-ins and team catch-ups under our volunteer policies. Tasks and access needs are agreed before you start.\r\n\r\nTime and expenses\r\nUnpaid and flexible, including induction and support time. Reasonable expenses are agreed before costs arise and reimbursed under charity policy. \r\n\r\nGet involved\r\nEmail hello@anxietyaidinternational.org for an informal conversation. We welcome different backgrounds and experience; you do not need to disclose any personal experience of anxiety.\n\n## Experience required\n\nA welcoming manner, reliability and enjoyment of meeting people are valuable. Local knowledge or event experience is helpful but not essential. .",
