        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001DAHZKYA5",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001DAHZKYA5/bipolar-scotland",
            "name": "Bipolar Scotland",
            "website": "https://stirlingvolunteering.org/profile/BipolarScotland",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JBERKYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JBERKYA5/support-group-facilitator-no-experience-necessary",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-28",
                    "title": "Support Group Facilitator- No experience necessary",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSupport Group Facilitator- No experience necessary\n\n## Description\n\nWe run a number of online and in-person support groups across Scotland that bring together people living with bipolar to share experiences and learn from one another. We believe that peer support helps reduce isolation, increases understanding of the condition and encourages new ways of coping. To make this possible, we need dedicated facilitators who can ensure that groups are welcoming, safe, inclusive and positive spaces for everyone who attends.\n\nAs a facilitator, you will work alongside a co-facilitator to lead a group once per month for 2 hours. This involves welcoming participants, encouraging open discussion, and handling any issues or conflicts sensitively. You will also help the group run smoothly by keeping to time and making sure everyone has the opportunity to contribute if they wish.\n\nWe welcome applications from people with lived experience of bipolar, those who have supported others with mental health conditions, or anyone passionate about mental health.&nbsp;\n\nPVG checks and references are required, and facilitators of in-person groups can claim travel expenses.\n\nWe are in the process of setting up our group so have no fixed address as of yet .&nbsp;\n\n## Experience required\n\nExcellent listening and communication skills are essential, along with reliability, confidentiality, and a commitment to peer support. In return, you will gain valuable experience, build confidence and receive training, supervision and opportunities for development.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
