        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001DZ8UAYA1",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001DZ8UAYA1/penumbra-mental-health",
            "name": "Penumbra Mental Health",
            "website": "https://stirlingvolunteering.org/profile/PenumbraMentalHealth",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JQtXOYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JQtXOYA1/self-harm-network-scotland-live-chat-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-23",
                    "title": "Self-Harm Network Scotland - Live Chat Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSelf-Harm Network Scotland - Live Chat Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nThe Self-Harm Network Volunteer will utilise their unique understanding gained from managing their own mental health to assist staff in the smooth delivery of our Self Harm support web chat.\n\nTime Commitment: The chat operates between 6pm-10pm, 7 days a week.\n\nWe are looking for a commitment of one 4-hour shift a week, including 1 Friday or Saturday a moth. One year commitment.\n\nLocation: Remote &ndash; Based in Scotland\n\nClosing: Sunday 23rd Nov 2026 7pm\n\nInterview: Monday 14th Dec, and Wednesday 16th Dec 2026 interviews\n\nTraining dates:\n\n&bull; Self-Harm Awareness Training: Wednesday 13th January 2027 6.00 pm &ndash; 9.00 pm\n\n&bull; Text base support training: Saturday 23rd January 2027 9.00 am &ndash; 5.00 pm\n\n&bull; Escalation and Safeguarding training: Wednesday 27th January 2027 6.00 pm &ndash; 9.00 pm\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood communication and excellent listening skills \nOpen to supporting a diverse range of people with a non-judgemental \napproach \nA kind, caring and empathetic person with a positive and hopeful attitude \nReliable and respectful \nAbility to reflect and build on experience and ask for additional support if \nrequired \nConfidence in volunteering as part of a team",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JQtXOYA1#role",
                        "type": "Role",
