        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001DcVvgYAF",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001DcVvgYAF/scottish-council-on-archives",
            "name": "Scottish Council on Archives",
            "description": "The Scottish Council on Archives provides leadership and builds capacity for the archives and records management sector in Scotland. We work in partnership with many organisations throughout the UK to support and promote the management and use of archives services and collections. We run a busy programme of workshops and events and deliver projects and resources spanning engagement, education and advocacy.\r\n\r\nWe support the work of professionals through the development and delivery of a variety of resources and tools covering issues such as quality improvement, accreditation, retention schedules, preservation, copyright and digital archives.  Through our new community archives programme we also help voluntary groups who maintain or wish to start a local archive.",
            "website": "https://www.scottisharchives.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC044553"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Heritage",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Heritage"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JTptrYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JTptrYAD/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-02",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Scottish Council on Archives (SCA) is the charity that champions archives and records management across Scotland. We advocate for the sector, support its development, and help more people discover and use Scotland’s archives.\r\n\r\nNominations are now open for new trustees, to be elected at our Annual Members’ Meeting on 10th December 2026.\r\n\r\nThe role: trustees set SCA’s strategy, oversee its finances and governance, and support the Director and staff in delivering our work. The Board meets around 4 times a year, in person and online, with regular sub-committee work. The initial term is 3 years. The role is voluntary, and reasonable expenses are reimbursed.\r\n\r\nWho we’re looking for: The majority of SCA trustees have come from the archives, records management, conservation and related heritage sectors, including people who have retired from the sector in the last three years. However, any member can put themselves forward to join the board.\r\n\r\nHow to stand:\r\n\r\nYou must be an SCA member. If you are not, you can join here. Membership is free. Please allow time for your application to be processed.\r\nYou need to be nominated in writing by two SCA members.\r\nComplete the Nomination Form. It asks you to confirm that you are willing to serve and eligible to be a charity trustee, to declare any interests, and to give a short supporting statement (up to 150 words) on what you would bring to the Board. Your statement will be shared with members. For guidance on being a trustee, see the advice from the Scottish Charity Regulator (OSCR) here.\r\nWhat happens next: The Board reviews every nomination. Endorsed nominees will be circulated to members on 1 December, and the election will take place at the Annual Members’ Meeting on 10 December 2026\r\n\r\nDeadline: to be included in the AMM papers, nominations should reach the SCA Director, John Pelan, j.pelan@scottisharchives.org.uk by 5pm on Wednesday 25th November 2026. Nominations received after this date, but no later than Thursday 3 December 2026, will still be considered.\r\n\r\nFor an informal conversation about the role, contact John Pelan at j.pelan@scottisharchives.org.uk",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
