        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001DcsDtYAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001DcsDtYAJ/retina-uk",
            "name": "Retina UK",
            "description": "We are the only UK charity dedicated solely to working for people affected by inherited sight loss.\r\n\r\nBy stimulating and funding medical research, we increase the understanding of these conditions and accelerate the search for treatments for the future.  The information and support we provide helps people lead better lives, today. We ensure no-one with inherited sight loss need feel alone.\r\n\r\nWe are in the unique position of being small enough to listen and respond to our community’s needs, but with a big enough reputation to make our voice heard by those who matter.  We are proud of the difference we make, but we want to do so much more; with our passion and hard work, and the ongoing support of our amazing community, we will make our vision a reality.",
            "website": "https://retinauk.org.uk/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SensoryImpairment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JePfuYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JePfuYAF/local-peer-support-group-facilitator-scotlandedinburgh",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-25",
                    "title": "Local Peer Support Group Facilitator (Scotland/Edinburgh)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAbout the Role\r\nPlease note: To volunteer in this role, you must be living with an inherited sight loss condition supported by Retina UK.\r\nLiving with inherited sight loss can sometimes feel isolating. Connecting with others who share similar experiences can make a huge difference. As a Local Peer Support Group Facilitator, you will use your lived experience to help bring people together and create a welcoming local community for others affected by inherited sight loss.\r\nYou will help organise and facilitate local peer support meetings, creating opportunities for people to connect, share experiences, exchange practical advice, and support one another. Through your involvement, you'll play a key role in reducing isolation and helping people feel understood and supported.\r\nWhat You'll Be Doing\r\n•\tOrganising and facilitating local peer support meetings in Edinburgh.\r\n•\tHelping identify and arrange suitable accessible venues.\r\n•\tCommunicating with attendees before and after meetings.\r\n•\tWelcoming new attendees and helping them feel comfortable.\r\n•\tEncouraging discussion and participation during meetings.\r\n•\tCreating a safe, inclusive, and supportive environment.\r\n•\tLiaising with Retina UK staff regarding meetings and group activities.\r\n•\tPromoting Retina UK's services and support where appropriate.\r\nWhat We're Looking For\r\nEssential\r\n•\tLived experience of an inherited sight loss condition supported by Retina UK.\r\n•\tGood communication and listening skills.\r\n•\tFriendly, approachable, and empathetic.\r\n•\tReliable and organised.\r\n•\tAbility to create an inclusive and welcoming environment.\r\n•\tConfidence engaging with people from a range of backgrounds.\r\nDesirable\r\n•\tExperience volunteering or supporting others.\r\n•\tEvent planning or community engagement experience.\r\n•\tKnowledge of local services and opportunities for people with sight loss.\r\n•\tBasic IT and email skills.\r\nTime Commitment\r\nApproximately 6-8 hours per month.\r\nThis includes planning and facilitating meetings, communicating with attendees, arranging venues, and attending occasional training or volunteer meetings. Most activities can be undertaken flexibly around your existing commitments.\r\nLocation\r\nThe role is primarily home-based, with occasional travel to Edinburgh for peer support meetings, typically taking place at least twice per year.\r\nWhile applicants can live outside Edinburgh, being based in or near the city would be an advantage.\r\nAccessible venues will be used wherever possible, and reasonable travel expenses will be reimbursed in line with Retina UK's expenses policy.\r\nTraining and Support\r\nYou won't be expected to do this alone.\r\nYou will receive:\r\n•\tA full Retina UK volunteer induction.\r\n•\tTraining on peer support, safeguarding, accessibility, and role responsibilities.\r\n•\tOngoing guidance and support from Retina UK staff.\r\n•\tRegular check-ins and opportunities to share experiences with fellow volunteers.\r\n•\tAccess to resources and information to support you in the role.\r\nVolunteer Expenses\r\nReasonable expenses incurred while carrying out your volunteering role can be claimed in line with Retina UK's expenses policy.\r\nTo claim expenses, volunteers complete an expenses claim form and submit it with any relevant receipts. Claims are approved by a manager before being processed by the Finance Team, with reimbursement made directly to the volunteer.\r\nWhat You'll Gain\r\n•\tThe opportunity to make a meaningful difference to others affected by inherited sight loss.\r\n•\tThe chance to use your lived experience to support and inspire others.\r\n•\tNew skills in communication, facilitation, and community engagement.\r\n•\tOngoing training and personal development.\r\n•\tConnection to a supportive network of Retina UK volunteers and staff.\r\n•\tThe satisfaction of helping people feel less alone and more connected.\r\nInterested?\r\nWe would love to hear from you if you're passionate about supporting others and helping to build a stronger inherited sight loss community in Edinburgh.\r\nContact:\r\nAnish Nathwani\r\nVolunteer Manager, Retina UK\r\n✉️ Anish.Nathwani@retinauk.org.uk\r\n📞 07856 907 463\n\n## Experience required\n\nEssential Skills & Experience\r\nPersonal or lived experience of inherited sight loss.\r\nExcellent communication and active listening skills.\r\nFriendly, approachable and empathetic manner.\r\nAbility to build relationships with people affected by inherited sight loss.\r\nConfidence facilitating conversations and encouraging participation in group discussions.\r\nGood organisational and planning skills.\r\nReliable, dependable and able to commit to the role.\r\nBasic IT skills, including email and Zoom.\r\nAbility to work independently while following Retina UK policies and guidance.\r\nUnderstanding of the importance of confidentiality and safeguarding.\r\nCommitment to Retina UK's values and mission.\r\n\r\nDesirable Skills & Experience\r\nPrevious volunteering experience.\r\nExperience facilitating meetings, support groups, community groups or events.\r\nKnowledge of local services and organisations supporting people with sight loss.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers will receive a comprehensive induction to Retina UK, including an introduction to the organisation, its services and the expectations of the role. Volunteers are required to complete safeguarding training and any other role-specific training provided by Retina UK. Appointment to the role is subject to a satisfactory DBS/PVG check, where applicable. Ongoing guidance, support and development opportunities will be available throughout the volunteer journey.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nVolunteers typically contribute 6-8 hours per month, including planning, promotion and facilitation of local peer support meetings, as well as communication with group members and Retina UK staff. We are looking for volunteers who can make a long-term commitment to the role, helping to provide consistency and continuity for people affected by inherited sight loss. The role is primarily home-based, with occasional travel to Edinburgh, typically around twice per year, for volunteer meetings, training or other Retina UK events. Travel expenses will be reimbursed in line with Retina UK's volunteer expenses policy.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis role is primarily home-based. Volunteers will be expected to travel within their local area to attend and facilitate peer support meetings. In addition, volunteers may be asked to travel to Edinburgh for training, volunteer meetings or other Retina UK activities, typically around twice per year. Reasonable travel expenses will be reimbursed in line with Retina UK's volunteer expenses policy.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nRetina UK will reimburse volunteers for all reasonable out-of-pocket expenses incurred while carrying out their role. This includes the full cost of approved travel, as well as other agreed expenses such as refreshments, parking or venue-related costs where applicable. Expenses should be submitted in line with Retina UK's expenses policy and will be reimbursed promptly following approval.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
