                        "title": "Local Peer Support Group Facilitator (Scotland/Edinburgh)",
                        "description": "Essential Skills & Experience\r\nPersonal or lived experience of inherited sight loss.\r\nExcellent communication and active listening skills.\r\nFriendly, approachable and empathetic manner.\r\nAbility to build relationships with people affected by inherited sight loss.\r\nConfidence facilitating conversations and encouraging participation in group discussions.\r\nGood organisational and planning skills.\r\nReliable, dependable and able to commit to the role.\r\nBasic IT skills, including email and Zoom.\r\nAbility to work independently while following Retina UK policies and guidance.\r\nUnderstanding of the importance of confidentiality and safeguarding.\r\nCommitment to Retina UK's values and mission.\r\n\r\nDesirable Skills & Experience\r\nPrevious volunteering experience.\r\nExperience facilitating meetings, support groups, community groups or events.\r\nKnowledge of local services and organisations supporting people with sight loss.",
