        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00001DvWhcYAF",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00001DvWhcYAF/11th-bridge-of-allan-scout-group",
            "name": "11th Bridge of Allan Scout Group",
            "website": "https://stirlingvolunteering.org/profile/11thBridgeofAllanScoutGroup",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JevZSYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JevZSYAZ/team-members-required-to-work-as-part-of-a-team-to-help-deliver-scouting-at-11th-bridge-of-allan-scout-group-for-all-age-groups",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-08",
                    "title": "Team Members required to work as part of a team to help deliver Scouting at 11th Bridge of Allan Scout Group. (for all age groups)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTeam Members required to work as part of a team to help deliver Scouting at 11th Bridge of Allan Scout Group. (for all age groups)\n\n## Description\n\nScouting actively engages and supports young people in their personal development and empowers them to make a positive contribution to society. At 11th Bridge of Allan Scouts we aim to offer a quality, balanced Scout programme to as many young people as possible from age 4 up to 18. This offers an exciting programme of outdoor activities, games, crafts, exploring the outdoors, community projects, challenges and the excitement of a few days away in a tent! \n\nWe continually strive to deliver skills for life in all we do as well as offer a place to belong.\n\nVolunteering with Scouts is a great way to take part in new experiences, meet a lots of friendly people and have fun. The role involves supporting children in various sections (Squirrels age 4-6, Beavers age 6-8, Cubs age 8-10 1/2, &nbsp;Scouts age 10 1/2 to 14, Explorers age 14 to 18) during weekly meetings, trips and camps. This can involve:\n\n\nWelcoming young people and families to sessions and events.\nMaking sure everyone&rsquo;s safe, supported, included and having fun.\nHelping to plan and lead activities.\nGetting involved with days out, camps and expeditions.\nSharing and learning skills &ndash; from coding to cake decorating to canoeing.\nCelebrating young people&rsquo;s achievements big and small.\n\n\nIf you&#39;d like to get involved or learn more, then please reach out! \n\nYou could make all the difference!\n\nExperience required\n\nAnyone who likes engaging with young people and has a friendly disposition! Any experience of the Scout organisation is beneficial but not at all necessary - we simply ask for a commitment to providing an enjoyable experience to our members!\n\n## Experience required\n\nJust someone who likes to work with young people. We will provide all training needed!",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JevZSYAZ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
