                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-03",
                    "title": "Thrive Together Aberdeen Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThrive Together Aberdeen C.I.C. is looking for enthusiastic, friendly and caring volunteers to join our team and help make a real difference in our local community.\r\n\r\nWe have two exciting volunteering opportunities available: supporting our charity shop, Reloved by Thrive Together Aberdeen, in Bridge of Don, or helping with our children's groups:\r\n\r\n-Charity Shop Volunteers – Reloved:\r\n\r\nOur charity shop is more than just a place to shop; it helps support the work we do across Thrive Together Aberdeen. Volunteers can help welcome customers, sort and price donations, organise clothing and household items, create attractive displays and keep the shop looking its best. This is a fantastic opportunity to gain retail experience, develop customer service skills, meet new people and support a community-focused organisation.\r\n\r\n-Children's Group Volunteers:\r\n\r\nWe are also looking for volunteers who would enjoy helping children take part in fun, inclusive activities. This may include supporting arts and crafts, games, sensory activities and group sessions, while encouraging children to build friendships, develop social skills and grow in confidence. If you enjoy working with children and want to help create a positive, welcoming environment, this could be a rewarding opportunity for you.\r\n\r\n-Why volunteer with Thrive?\r\n\r\nThrive Together Aberdeen is committed to promoting inclusion, independence, confidence and community participation for children, young people and adults with additional support needs. By volunteering with us, you will be helping create opportunities for people to learn, connect and feel part of their community.\r\n\r\nWhether you are looking to gain experience for your future career, develop new skills, meet people, give something back or simply make a difference, we would love to hear from you. Previous experience is not essential for every role, as appropriate guidance and support will be provided.\r\n\r\nWe welcome enquiries from people with different skills, backgrounds and levels of experience. Relevant safeguarding checks, including PVG membership where required, will apply to roles depending on the duties involved.\r\n\r\nJoin Thrive and help us build a more inclusive community, one opportunity at a time!\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Kirsty Irvine at email: kirsty@thrivetogetherabz.co.uk or telephone: 07886631885\n\n## Description\n\nThrive Together Aberdeen C.I.C. is looking for enthusiastic, friendly and caring volunteers to join our team and help make a real difference in our local community.\r\n\r\nWe have two exciting volunteering opportunities available: supporting our charity shop, Reloved by Thrive Together Aberdeen, in Bridge of Don, or helping with our children's groups:\r\n\r\n-Charity Shop Volunteers – Reloved:\r\n\r\nOur charity shop is more than just a place to shop; it helps support the work we do across Thrive Together Aberdeen. Volunteers can help welcome customers, sort and price donations, organise clothing and household items, create attractive displays and keep the shop looking its best. This is a fantastic opportunity to gain retail experience, develop customer service skills, meet new people and support a community-focused organisation.\r\n\r\n-Children's Group Volunteers:\r\n\r\nWe are also looking for volunteers who would enjoy helping children take part in fun, inclusive activities. This may include supporting arts and crafts, games, sensory activities and group sessions, while encouraging children to build friendships, develop social skills and grow in confidence. If you enjoy working with children and want to help create a positive, welcoming environment, this could be a rewarding opportunity for you.\r\n\r\n-Why volunteer with Thrive?\r\n\r\nThrive Together Aberdeen is committed to promoting inclusion, independence, confidence and community participation for children, young people and adults with additional support needs. By volunteering with us, you will be helping create opportunities for people to learn, connect and feel part of their community.\r\n\r\nWhether you are looking to gain experience for your future career, develop new skills, meet people, give something back or simply make a difference, we would love to hear from you. Previous experience is not essential for every role, as appropriate guidance and support will be provided.\r\n\r\nWe welcome enquiries from people with different skills, backgrounds and levels of experience. Relevant safeguarding checks, including PVG membership where required, will apply to roles depending on the duties involved.\r\n\r\nJoin Thrive and help us build a more inclusive community, one opportunity at a time!\r\n\r\nFor more information please contact Kirsty Irvine at email: kirsty@thrivetogetherabz.co.uk or telephone: 07886631885\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and guidance is provided to all volunteers. \r\n\r\nAll volunteers will receive an induction to Thrive Together Aberdeen, including an introduction to our services, values, policies and procedures. Role-specific guidance will be provided for charity shop duties or supporting children's groups. Volunteers will work alongside experienced staff who will offer ongoing support, supervision and opportunities to ask questions. Relevant training, including safeguarding and child protection where appropriate, will be provided according to the role. Any required PVG checks will be discussed before starting. We aim to create a welcoming environment where volunteers feel confident, valued and supported throughout their volunteering experience.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to volunteer. All help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteering opportunities are based in Bridge of Don, Aberdeen, at Reloved by Thrive Together Aberdeen charity shop and our Thrive Together Aberdeen community hub at Silverburn Lodge. Both locations are within the local area and accessible by road and public transport. Volunteers are responsible for arranging their own travel to and from their volunteering placement. Specific locations and travel arrangements will be confirmed when discussing the role, including whether any travel support or expenses are available.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAny agreed volunteering expenses, such as reasonable public transport costs, will be reimbursed upon submission of receipts. Arrangements and payment timescales will be confirmed with volunteers before they start.",
