            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JrJMXYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JrJMXYA3/board-member-recruitment",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-26",
                    "title": "Board Member Recruitment",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for curious, committed and collaborative people who share our enthusiasm for contemporary art and creativity. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are particularly interested in people with experience or knowledge in:\r\n\r\n• Marketing and communications\r\n• Sales\r\n• Financial\r\n• Legal\r\n• HR\r\n• Contemporary visual arts and creative practice\r\n\r\nThese areas are not a checklist of requirements. You do not need previous Board experience or a professional background in the arts.\r\n\r\nWe want our Board to better reflect the communities we work with and particularly encourage applications from younger people and people from ethnically diverse backgrounds. We value different lived experiences, perspectives and connections to Aberdeen and the North East.\r\n\r\nOur Board provides strategic direction, oversees the organisation’s governance and financial sustainability, and supports the Director and staff team in delivering Peacock’s ambitions. The Board meets four times a year. \r\n\r\nFor more information and to apply please visit: https://peacock.studio/informations/call-for-board-members or email: jon@peacock.studio *(deadline for applications is the 27th November 2026).\n\n## Description\n\nWe are looking for curious, committed and collaborative people who share our enthusiasm for contemporary art and creativity. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are particularly interested in people with experience or knowledge in:\r\n\r\n• Marketing and communications\r\n• Sales\r\n• Financial\r\n• Legal\r\n• HR\r\n• Contemporary visual arts and creative practice\r\n\r\nThese areas are not a checklist of requirements. You do not need previous Board experience or a professional background in the arts.\r\n\r\nWe want our Board to better reflect the communities we work with and particularly encourage applications from younger people and people from ethnically diverse backgrounds. We value different lived experiences, perspectives and connections to Aberdeen and the North East.\r\n\r\nOur Board provides strategic direction, oversees the organisation’s governance and financial sustainability, and supports the Director and staff team in delivering Peacock’s ambitions. The Board meets four times a year. \r\n\r\nFor more information and to apply please visit: https://peacock.studio/informations/call-for-board-members or email: jon@peacock.studio *(deadline for applications is the 27th November 2026).\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant guidance is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe board meet quarterly in Aberdeen or online where necessary.\r\nVoluntary / Reasonable expenses covered.",
