                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000006qHXZYA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000006qHXZYA2/vsa-volunteer-opportunities",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "VSA Volunteer Opportunities",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteering Opportunities!\r\n\r\nOur award-winning volunteers at VSA are a vital part of our charity. Every hour contributed by our volunteers makes a difference. You truly are making an impact on the lives of vulnerable adults, we support across our services in the Northeast of Scotland, it’s with your support we can provide the very best of care to whom we support. \r\n\r\nWe have a variety of personal and corporate volunteering opportunities available for you to consider, whether you can gift an occasional hour, a whole day or make a regular commitment by volunteering every week, we would love to welcome you to the team.\r\n\r\nFrom learning new skills, meeting new friends, to just having fun, there are so many reasons to consider volunteering. - Give the gift of time.\r\n\r\nFind out about our current volunteering opportunities and inquire today by filling in the 'volunteer with us' form at: https://www.vsa.org.uk/volunteering and  https://vsa.tfaforms.net/120\r\n\r\nFor instance, you could help VSA as a:\r\n\r\n*Fundraising Event Volunteer:\r\nAssist VSA at our upcoming events. From community events such as Highland games and galas to our annual events such as Sing, Sing, Sing!  and the Best of Care Ball, volunteering is an exciting way to get involved in making an impact to VSA and their fundraising mission with events that draw hundreds if not thousands of attendees.\r\n\r\n*Fundraising Challenge Volunteer:\r\nGet involved in our fun challenges by volunteering. Perhaps you want to help marshal a fun-filled sporting activity, cheering on participants, handing out medals, or utilising your specialist skills - we have plenty of opportunities for you to get involved in.\r\n\r\n*Corporate Volunteering:\r\nWe offer corporate volunteering opportunities through our corporate partnerships for businesses to get involved in various projects and events that support VSA’s mission. By participating in these initiatives, companies can give back to the community, boost employee morale, and enhance their corporate social responsibility efforts. \r\n\r\n*Ready to Apply?:\r\nFrom learning new skills, meeting new friends, to just having fun, there are so many reasons to consider volunteering at VSA. Give the gift of time and apply to become a Volunteer today!  Please complete our 'Volunteer With Us' form at https://vsa.tfaforms.net/120   More information about volunteering at VSA is also available at: https://www.vsa.org.uk/volunteering\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteering Opportunities!\r\n\r\nOur award-winning volunteers at VSA are a vital part of our charity. Every hour contributed by our volunteers makes a difference. You truly are making an impact on the lives of vulnerable adults, we support across our services in the Northeast of Scotland, it’s with your support we can provide the very best of care to whom we support. \r\n\r\nWe have a variety of personal and corporate volunteering opportunities available for you to consider, whether you can gift an occasional hour, a whole day or make a regular commitment by volunteering every week, we would love to welcome you to the team.\r\n\r\nFrom learning new skills, meeting new friends, to just having fun, there are so many reasons to consider volunteering. - Give the gift of time.\r\n\r\nFind out about our current volunteering opportunities and inquire today by filling in the 'volunteer with us' form at: https://www.vsa.org.uk/volunteering and  https://vsa.tfaforms.net/120\r\n\r\nFor instance, you could help VSA as a:\r\n\r\n*Fundraising Event Volunteer:\r\nAssist VSA at our upcoming events. From community events such as Highland games and galas to our annual events such as Sing, Sing, Sing!  and the Best of Care Ball, volunteering is an exciting way to get involved in making an impact to VSA and their fundraising mission with events that draw hundreds if not thousands of attendees.\r\n\r\n*Fundraising Challenge Volunteer:\r\nGet involved in our fun challenges by volunteering. Perhaps you want to help marshal a fun-filled sporting activity, cheering on participants, handing out medals, or utilising your specialist skills - we have plenty of opportunities for you to get involved in.\r\n\r\n*Corporate Volunteering:\r\nWe offer corporate volunteering opportunities through our corporate partnerships for businesses to get involved in various projects and events that support VSA’s mission. By participating in these initiatives, companies can give back to the community, boost employee morale, and enhance their corporate social responsibility efforts. \r\n\r\n*Ready to Apply?:\r\nFrom learning new skills, meeting new friends, to just having fun, there are so many reasons to consider volunteering at VSA. Give the gift of time and apply to become a Volunteer today!  Please complete our 'Volunteer With Us' form at https://vsa.tfaforms.net/120   More information about volunteering at VSA is also available at: https://www.vsa.org.uk/volunteering\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant training and excellent support is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to volunteer. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.",
