        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008ndzsAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008ndzsAAA/royal-voluntary-service-dundee",
            "name": "Royal Voluntary Service (Dundee)",
            "description": "Royal Voluntary Service helps thousands of older people to live the life they want. We provide practical services in homes, in hospitals and in communities all across the UK so people can be independent and active. Much of our work is supporting older people. We provide practical solutions to everyday problems of loneliness and isolation.",
            "website": "https://www.royalvoluntaryservice.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038924"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FgsUnYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FgsUnYAJ/club-coordinator",
                    "publishStart": "2026-03-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Club Coordinator",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nLooking for an enthusiastic individual who can provide fun activities for adults aged 55+ in sheltered housing, anything from carpet bowls, quizzes, skittles, bingo etc\n\n## Description\n\n2 hourly weekly activity group, requires an enthusiastic person to deliver varied activities for residents (aged 55+) in sheltered housing. Very interested in quizzes, carpet bowls, darts, skittles, themed memory chats etc\r\n\r\nChairs need set up ready for which ever activity the group are doing. And then put back after wards. Most groups enjoy a game of BOCCIA – so divide into teams and keep scores.\r\n\r\nIts only for two hours and there are refreshments on site.\n\n## Experience required\n\nInterest in supporting elderly residents to enjoy their lives.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training,( safeguarding adults, dementia, strength and balance training and varied other opportunities).\n\n## Travel details\n\nCommunity clubs in Lochee and Martingale Gardens\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel to and from the venues.\n\n## Taster details\n\nThey can visit anyone of our clubs and see what we do and how we do it, supported by the team",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FgsUnYAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Club Coordinator",
                        "description": "Interest in supporting elderly residents to enjoy their lives.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FgsUnYAJ/club-coordinator?#modal_register_a0gQD00000FgsUnYAJ",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16",
