                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009DBuvYAG",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009DBuvYAG/dementia-support-volunteer-dundee",
                    "publishStart": "2025-04-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Dementia Support Volunteer - Dundee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteers transform the lives of people with dementia, by helping to enable them to take positive steps to connect to their community and reduce their isolation. Our dementia groups promote nutrition, hydration and mobility.\n\n## Description\n\nWe have four dementia groups across Dundee, as a volunteer you can choose one group or more it’s up to you! Our groups are weekly, but you can choose what days to come. \r\n\r\nAs a Dementia Support Volunteer, you will be part of a friendly team to help set up, welcome our clients, participate and ensure they leave safely for home. \r\n\r\nOur groups support older people living with dementia to be independent and stay connected to their communities. This is a fun and rewarding role interacting with staff, other volunteers, our clients and their carers/loved ones who accompany them. \r\n\r\nTasks include helping to provide tea/coffee and healthy snacks as well as supporting with various fun activities. You can join in our exercises to improve strength and mobility. Don’t let the word Dementia put you off, this is a rewarding role where you can really see the difference you make!\r\n\r\nOur groups are weekly you do not need to come every week, but we expect advance notice on when you can help. They are 2-hour sessions, but we expect volunteers to arrive early to help set up and stay behind to help clear up. Although if you can’t that’s not a problem. \r\n\r\nEach of our groups are on these days/times:\r\n\r\nSt Aidens Centre DD5 2EB \r\nThurs 1pm-3pm\r\n\r\nDundee Dementia Resource Centre Group, DD4 6QE \r\nTues 10:30am – 12:30pm\r\n\r\nMonifieth Activity Centre (Mac Centre) DD5 4NH\r\nWed 11:45am – 1:45pm\r\n\r\nCorso Street Dementia Group DD2 1EY\r\nWed 11am-1pm\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly personality, patience, good communication skills, with a non-judgmental attitude towards an individual’s circumstances and a willingness to ensure confidentiality.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will be supported by a friendly team through your induction, trial visit, online modules (Safeguarding and Understanding Dementia).\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe have four locations: St Aidens Centre DD5 2EB, Dundee Dementia Resource Centre Group DD4 6QE, Monifieth Activity Centre (Mac Centre) DD5 4NH, Corso Street Dementia Group DD2 1EY.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel to and from your home to the venue. We reimburse mileage 45p per mile or a bus journey if you retain your ticket.\n\n## Taster details\n\nOnce you have completed the application process and informal interview we can offer a trial visit.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009DBuvYAG#role",
