            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000003dpfFYAQ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000003dpfFYAQ/director",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-07",
                    "title": "Director",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nFEAT Trading CIC seek experienced and committed Directors\r\n\r\nCandidates must have previous board/governance experience, strong communication and committee skills, knowledge of both commerce and the third sector, and the ability to effectively manage the Board. It is an exciting time to join us as we are set to begin operations of the refurbished flax mill in Silverburn Park from 2026 as a visitor centre and community hub.\n\n## Experience required\n\nStrategic leadership, governance, efficiency and effectiveness, people management, external relations, commerce\n\n## Training details\n\nDirectors will receive an induction into the role supported by senior staff and existing Directors.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMeetings are held monthly in Silverburn Park, Leven or via video conferencing.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReimburse public transport costs and/or 25p per mile for vehicle use.",
