            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000A9tE1YAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000A9tE1YAJ/street-soccer-session-supporter",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-08",
                    "title": "Street Soccer Session Supporter",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteers support coaches in delivering fun, inclusive sessions – no prior football expertise needed!\n\n## Description\n\nStreet Soccer Scotland is a charity offering free weekly football sessions to people experiencing challenges like poverty, mental health issues, homelessness, or social isolation. Their goal is to build confidence, community, and pathways to positive change through sports.\r\n\r\nVolunteers support coaches in delivering fun, inclusive sessions – no prior football expertise needed! \r\n\r\nKey responsibilities:\r\n•\tHelping set up/pack down sessions\r\n•\tWelcoming participants and fostering a supportive environment\r\n•\tAssisting with drills, small-sided games, and participant engagement\r\n•\tEncouraging inclusivity and teamwork\r\n \r\n Volunteers can choose which activities they would like to help with, as the opportunity is very flexible to you. They have 4 sessions every week across Fife, and you can select which you would like to help with. These are Levenmouth, Dunfermline, Glenrothes and Kirkcaldy.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to uplift your community while gaining experience, training, upskilling and employability support, this is the opportunity for you. Get involved with Street Soccer today!\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tPassion for supporting vulnerable people\r\n•\tReliable, friendly, and team-oriented\r\n•\tEnthusiasm for sport\r\n•\tWillingness to learn and grow\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers are given support by the programme coordinator, and have access to ongoing training. Training included first aid, coaching badges and safeguarding.\n\n## Travel details\n\n•\tMondays: Levenmouth 11:30am-2pm Bayview Stadium\r\n•\tTuesdays: Dunfermline 12pm-1:30pm Pitreavie Soccer centre\r\n•\tWednesdays: Glenrothes 1pm-2:30pm Michael Woods Sports and Leisure\r\n•\tFriday: Kirkcaldy 1:30pm-4:00pm Stark’s Park Stadium\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on an individual basis.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
