            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000006uthVYAQ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000006uthVYAQ/absafe-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Absafe Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteer at Absafe and Make a Life-Saving Impact in Your Community!\r\n\r\nAbsafe is an award-winning, life-saving charity dedicated to educating and empowering young people and communities to make safer, informed choices. We are passionate about creating a lasting impact, whether it’s through our dynamic educational programs for schools, fostering responsible citizenship, or helping individuals develop life-saving skills. Volunteering with Absafe offers a variety of opportunities to make a difference. Whether you’re inspiring young minds through interactive safety sessions, enhancing our presence on social media, or assisting with the upkeep of our grounds and building, there’s a role for everyone. By joining our team, you’ll not only contribute to saving lives but also be part of a positive, inclusive, and forward-thinking charity making a real difference in Aberdeen and beyond. Together, we can create a safer future for all.\r\n\r\nAre you looking for an opportunity to make a meaningful difference in people’s lives while developing your own skills and being part of a passionate, dynamic team? Absafe is the perfect place for you! As a volunteer with our life-saving charity, you’ll play a vital role in delivering impactful safety education and community programmes that empower individuals and promote responsible choices.\r\n\r\nAt Absafe, we believe that everyone has a part to play in building safer, stronger communities. Our diverse volunteer roles mean you can contribute your unique skills and passions in a way that works for you. Love working with young people? Join our educational team to deliver engaging, interactive sessions that inspire and inform the next generation. Are you a social media whiz or creative thinker? Help us amplify our reach and share our mission by managing our online presence, creating compelling content, and connecting with supporters. Prefer hands-on work? Assist with maintaining our grounds and facilities to ensure we provide the best possible environment for our activities.\r\n\r\nWhat sets volunteering at Absafe apart is the variety and sense of purpose you’ll find in every role. Whether you’re delivering life-changing workshops, building connections with local communities, or improving the spaces where we work, your efforts will contribute directly to saving lives and making Aberdeen a better, safer place for everyone.\r\n\r\nVolunteering with Absafe isn’t just about giving back – it’s about growing and learning, too. You’ll gain valuable experience, meet like-minded individuals, and be part of a supportive team that values innovation, inclusion, and kindness. Every hour you spend with us brings you closer to creating a tangible, positive impact in the lives of others.\r\n\r\nJoin us at Absafe and be part of something extraordinary. Together, we can create a safer future for our community!\r\n\r\nFor more details please contact Louise Richardson at email: hello@absafe.org.uk or telephone: 07743944096.\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteer at Absafe and Make a Life-Saving Impact in Your Community!\r\n\r\nAbsafe is an award-winning, life-saving charity dedicated to educating and empowering young people and communities to make safer, informed choices. We are passionate about creating a lasting impact, whether it’s through our dynamic educational programs for schools, fostering responsible citizenship, or helping individuals develop life-saving skills. Volunteering with Absafe offers a variety of opportunities to make a difference. Whether you’re inspiring young minds through interactive safety sessions, enhancing our presence on social media, or assisting with the upkeep of our grounds and building, there’s a role for everyone. By joining our team, you’ll not only contribute to saving lives but also be part of a positive, inclusive, and forward-thinking charity making a real difference in Aberdeen and beyond. Together, we can create a safer future for all.\r\n\r\nAre you looking for an opportunity to make a meaningful difference in people’s lives while developing your own skills and being part of a passionate, dynamic team? Absafe is the perfect place for you! As a volunteer with our life-saving charity, you’ll play a vital role in delivering impactful safety education and community programmes that empower individuals and promote responsible choices.\r\n\r\nAt Absafe, we believe that everyone has a part to play in building safer, stronger communities. Our diverse volunteer roles mean you can contribute your unique skills and passions in a way that works for you. Love working with young people? Join our educational team to deliver engaging, interactive sessions that inspire and inform the next generation. Are you a social media whiz or creative thinker? Help us amplify our reach and share our mission by managing our online presence, creating compelling content, and connecting with supporters. Prefer hands-on work? Assist with maintaining our grounds and facilities to ensure we provide the best possible environment for our activities.\r\n\r\nWhat sets volunteering at Absafe apart is the variety and sense of purpose you’ll find in every role. Whether you’re delivering life-changing workshops, building connections with local communities, or improving the spaces where we work, your efforts will contribute directly to saving lives and making Aberdeen a better, safer place for everyone.\r\n\r\nVolunteering with Absafe isn’t just about giving back – it’s about growing and learning, too. You’ll gain valuable experience, meet like-minded individuals, and be part of a supportive team that values innovation, inclusion, and kindness. Every hour you spend with us brings you closer to creating a tangible, positive impact in the lives of others.\r\n\r\nJoin us at Absafe and be part of something extraordinary. Together, we can create a safer future for our community!\r\n\r\nFor more details please contact Louise Richardson, Absafe CEO at email: hello@absafe.org.uk or telephone: 07743944096.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training provided to all volunteers. At Absafe, we provide all volunteers with a comprehensive induction to familiarise you with our mission, values, and activities. You'll receive tailored training for your role, ensuring you feel confident and equipped to make a difference. From hands-on workshops for educational roles to guidance on social media management or facility upkeep, we’ll support you every step of the way. Our dedicated team always provides ongoing support, and regular check-ins ensure you’re thriving in your role. We’re committed to creating a positive and rewarding volunteering experience where you’ll feel valued and empowered to contribute effectively.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at Balgownie Lodge, Innovation Park, Campus 3, AB22 8GW our dedicated safety education hub in Bridge of Don, Aberdeen. Conveniently accessible by local bus Number 1, our location is easy to reach from across the city. For those driving, we offer free on-site parking, ensuring a hassle-free visit. Whether you’re traveling by public transport or car, getting to Balgownie Lodge is straightforward, making it easy to join us in creating safer communities.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
