                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VupfhAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VupfhAAB/creative-group-facilitator",
                    "publishStart": "2023-07-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Creative Group Facilitator",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBring your creativity to life while supporting adults with additional support needs! Help lead fun, hands-on sessions in art, music, baking, sewing, and more at our welcoming community hub in Dudhope Castle.\n\n## Description\n\nDo you love being creative and want to make a difference? Join our friendly team at Uppertunity to support adults with additional support needs and autism to explore their creativity and confidence.\r\n\r\nYou’ll help run small, relaxed group sessions in arts, crafts, music, sewing or drama. Tasks include setup and cleanup, encouraging participants to try ideas, offering practical support where needed, keeping the group flowing, and most importantly, socialising!\r\n\r\nOur materials are mostly donated or upcycled, so you’ll get to think inventively and resourcefully. We’re looking for someone kind, patient, and positive. Experience with creative activities or group facilitation is a bonus but not essential. Sessions run Tuesday to Friday (10am–12pm or 1–3pm). \r\n\r\nYou’ll always volunteer alongside one of our staff team, with plenty of laughter and learning along the way. We’re an inclusive space that believes in working together and to our strengths.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAn interest in creative activities and supporting others, plus a friendly, patient, and positive attitude.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining given in all aspects of role, on-the-job and in-person. All volunteers will receive welcome pack.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nOccasional weekend if volunteer wants to be involved with events.\n\n## Travel details\n\nGround Floor Left, The Circle at Dudhope Castle, Barrack Road, Dundee DD3 6TU\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note: No expenses are paid for this opportunity\n\n## Taster details\n\nYou can come in and see a group in action before you get more involved.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000VupfhAAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Creative Group Facilitator",
                        "description": "An interest in creative activities and supporting others, plus a friendly, patient, and positive attitude.",
                        "commitment": "Occasional weekend if volunteer wants to be involved with events.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000VupfhAAB/creative-group-facilitator?#modal_register_a0g0800000VupfhAAB",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/LearningDisabilities",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Learning Disabilities"
                            }
