            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000098OROYA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000098OROYA2/volunteer-group-helper",
                    "publishStart": "2025-03-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Volunteer Group Helper",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nJoin a fun and established community group in Currie Community Centre, as a volunteer helper.  A chance to make new friends and build community.  The group is for people aged 60+ to come together in a warm and welcoming space to socialise, and enjoy food in good company.\n\n## Description\n\nAs a community group helper you will welcome people, help set up the room, make teas and coffees for those who are unable, take part in fun activities, and help tidy up the space at the end.  If you live locally (or not!) this can be a great opportunity to meet new people and make new friends.  Lunch is also provided free of charge.  The group runs every Friday from 11am until 2pm.  We would ask that you can commit to helping at least one Friday a month.  All volunteers will require a PVG.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will meet 1-1 with staff to go through some basic training covering things like boundaries & confidentiality, and adult support and protection.  They will also have the opportunity to complete Food Hygiene training.  Once they have started in their role, ongoing support will be provided by Currie Community Centre.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCurrie Community Centre\n280 Lanark Road West\nCurrie\nEH14 5RU\n\nCurrie Community Centre is served by both the 32 and 44 bus routes which stop directly outside.\nThe 45 bus route also stops nearby.  For those that drive there is free parking.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses provided.",
