                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009scuLYAQ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009scuLYAQ/driver",
                    "publishStart": "2025-05-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Driver",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFriendly driver required to deliver food to charities throughout Central and Southeast Scotland. Help FareShare save food from being wasted and getting it to those who are really in need.\n\n## Description\n\nYou will be a link between the Depot and the charities, getting the food to where it is needed. You will be the friendly face of FareShare, doing tasks within food safety guidelines. Your tasks will include: \nloading up the delivery van with food alongside other volunteers;\ndropping off the weekly orders of food at local charities;\ncollecting surplus food from local businesses with the help of another volunteer;\nkeeping the delivery van clean and tidy.\nWe will provide support and training.\n\n## Training details\n\nNew drivers will be allocated a shift with an experienced driver and assistant.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteering starts at 5a Seafield Way at the Cyrenians FareShare Depot. Free parking available to those who drive. \nBuses: \nClermiston number 1 service, getting off near McDonalds and walking along for 19mins. \nGyle number 12, getting off at the Portobello bus depot and walking along for 11mins. \nKings Road 15, getting off at Goff Avenue and walking along for 17mins.\nClerwood 26, getting off at  Goff Avenue  and walking along 17 for mins.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMileage and bus fares reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
