        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008neO2AAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008neO2AAI/big-noise-torry-aberdeen",
            "name": "Big Noise Torry (Aberdeen)",
            "description": "Sistema Scotland is a charity set out to transform lives with music. Big Noise is an orchestra programme that aims to use music making to foster confidence, teamwork, pride and aspiration in the children taking part – and across their wider community. It is based on the methods of Venezuela’s “El Sistema” movement and is run by the charity Sistema Scotland. Big Noise Torry works with children to help them transform their lives through music. We run after-school and holiday clubs for children in Torry. The magic happens at our Big Noise centres.",
            "website": "https://www.makeabignoise.org.uk/big-noise/torry/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000AtSBGAA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000AtSBGAA3/big-noise-torry-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Big Noise Torry Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe believe every child and young person deserves the same opportunity to succeed and so we provide free, immersive, instrumental music tuition to pupils and pre-school children. This leads to an enhanced ability to learn in school, improvements in emotional wellbeing, confidence and esteem, as well as the acquisition of a range of social and life skills. To achieve this, volunteers are vital for our Big Noise Centre in Torry.  \r\nYou can become a positive role model in their lives and someone they look forward to spending time with.  Our volunteers help with everything including getting snacks ready, set-up and pack up, and helping the children and young people to play their instruments.  We particularly need volunteers to collect children from school in our walking lines.  You will benefit from this by receiving training, developing skills in communication and gaining experience of working with children and young people.  \r\nA fantastic opportunity to help with a major charity in Aberdeen. All volunteer help is greatly appreciated. For more details please contact Kirsty Jackson at  E Mail: kirsty.jackson@sistemascotland.org.uk or  Tel: 01224 974707.\n\n## Description\n\nWe believe every child and young person deserves the same opportunity to succeed and so we provide free, immersive, instrumental music tuition to pupils and pre-school children. This leads to an enhanced ability to learn in school, improvements in emotional wellbeing, confidence and esteem, as well as the acquisition of a range of social and life skills. To achieve this, volunteers are vital for our Big Noise Centre in Torry.\r\n\r\nAs a Big Noise volunteer, you'll be helping us transform children's lives through music. You don't need to have any musical experience, just a passion for making a difference to the lives of young people.\r\n\r\nVolunteers help in a variety of valuable ways, including:\r\n \r\n•\tHelping children stay focused and engaged during music lessons\r\n•\tWalk children from school to the Big Noise Centre\r\n•\tHelping set up for rehearsals and music lessons and assisting the children and young people to play their instruments if required\r\n•\tSupervise children during snack times, breaks, time-out etc.  \r\n•\tand much more...\r\n\r\nYou can become a positive role model in children’s lives and someone they look forward to spending time with. You will benefit from this by receiving training, developing skills in communication and gaining experience of working with children and young people. Big Noise Torry/Sistema Scotland have also achieved the Investing in Volunteers Award-a national quality standard for good practice in involving volunteers as part of our commitment to volunteering and providing excellent support to volunteers.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help with a major charity in Aberdeen and Scotland. All volunteer help is greatly appreciated and makes a real difference. For more details please either:\r\n-Visit our website at https://www.makeabignoise.org.uk/volunteering/ and apply online at https://www.makeabignoise.org.uk/volunteering/apply-online/aberdeen/ \r\nOr\r\n-Contact us at email: torry@sistemascotland.org.uk or telephone: 01786 462923.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided to all volunteers. Volunteers will be offered support from the Operations Manager on a regular basis.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nPeople can volunteer anything from a couple of hours to several days each week. All help makes a difference and is much appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe deliver our work in-school at Walker Road Primary School and Tullos Primary School in Torry, Aberdeen. Regular bus service, nos. 3,12 and 59 and car parking also available\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers can be reimbursed for public transport when they come to volunteer.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000AtSBGAA3#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Big Noise Torry Volunteers",
                        "commitment": "People can volunteer anything from a couple of hours to several days each week. All help makes a difference and is much appreciated.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000AtSBGAA3/big-noise-torry-volunteers?#modal_register_a0g1p00000AtSBGAA3",
