        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008ndrZAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008ndrZAAQ/rnid",
            "name": "RNID",
            "description": "We’re here for the 18 million people in the UK who are deaf, have hearing loss or tinnitus.\r\n\r\nWith our communities, we’ll change society to make it more inclusive for everyone, help people hear better now and fund world-class research.\r\n\r\nOur communities are huge: 1 in 3 adults in the UK are deaf, have hearing loss or tinnitus.\r\n\r\nIf our work doesn’t directly impact you, it will almost certainly be making a difference for someone you know and love.\r\n\r\nWe work with our communities and partners across health, employment, research, government and more to change life for the better.",
            "website": "https://rnid.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038926"
                }
            ],
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2F3521ebe3-39dc-31b2-699b-7c2d05b22fd4%2F4WX3kxOmhYg5yp2v3octCSeFr5k2%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=d9187b44-196e-4d67-b0a6-a43c18806f3e",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/AdviceInformation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Advice / Information"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CampaigningLobbying",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Campaigning / Lobbying"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FundraisingFunding",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Fundraising / Funding"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SensoryImpairment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sensory Impairment"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I1wfVYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I1wfVYAR/rnid-in-communities-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-17",
                    "title": "RNID in Communities Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAs an RNID in Communities Volunteer, you will help raise awareness of hearing loss, tinnitus and deafness within local communities across Orkney. Volunteers will deliver talks and presentations to community groups and organisations, sharing information about RNID services, support available and ways people can get involved. You will also support people to take the RNID online hearing check and help them understand the next steps if further support is needed. In addition, volunteers will promote RNID Near You services, increase awareness of local support available and signpost people with hearing loss, tinnitus and people who are deaf to relevant information, services and community resources. No previous experience is required, as full training, resources and ongoing support will be provided.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat could a volunteer gain from the experience:\r\n• Make a positive difference to the lives of local people affected by hearing loss, tinnitus and\r\ndeafness.\r\n• Develop presentation, public speaking and communication skills.\r\n• Build confidence engaging with community groups, organisations and members of the public.\r\n• Increase knowledge and understanding of hearing loss, tinnitus, deaf awareness and RNID\r\nservices.\r\n• Develop skills in providing information, guidance and signposting.\r\n• Be part of a friendly and supportive team of RNID staff and volunteers.\r\n• Meet new people and develop connections within the local community.\r\n• Gain valuable volunteering experience that can support personal and professional\r\ndevelopment.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience is required, as full training and support will be provided. We are looking for friendly, reliable and confident communicators who are comfortable speaking to groups and engaging with people from a wide range of backgrounds. Volunteers should be dependable, willing to follow volunteer guidelines, health and safety procedures, and confidentiality requirements. We also value people who are inclusive, work well with others, and are enthusiastic about raising awareness of hearing loss, tinnitus and deafness within their local community. Most importantly, we are looking for people who want to make a positive difference in the lives of local people who are deaf, have hearing loss or tinnitus.\n\n## Training details\n\nYou will receive a comprehensive induction and ongoing support to help you feel confident in your role. Volunteers complete essential training in safeguarding, data protection, equality and diversity, and health and safety. You will also receive training on delivering community talks and presentations, using RNID awareness resources, promoting RNID services, supporting people to complete the RNID online hearing check, and providing information and signposting to people who are deaf, have hearing loss or tinnitus. Throughout your volunteering journey, you will receive ongoing guidance, resources and support from your RNID Near You Coordinator, who will be available to answer questions, provide advice and help you develop in your role.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2 hours per month dependent on bookings. Ad hoc - weekday mornings, afternoons or evenings.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses incurred while carrying out your volunteering role will be reimbursed in line with RNID's volunteer expenses policy.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
