                        "description": "No previous experience is required, as full training will be provided. We are looking for friendly, reliable and empathetic people with good communication and listening skills who enjoy meeting and supporting others. Volunteers should be dependable, willing to follow volunteer guidelines, health and safety procedures, and confidentiality requirements. We also value people who are inclusive, work well with others, support fellow volunteers, and share ideas and feedback. Most importantly, we are looking for people who want to make a positive difference in the lives of local people who are deaf, have hearing loss or tinnitus by helping them access the information and support they need.",
