        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008ndsBAAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008ndsBAAQ/young-lives-vs-cancer",
            "name": "Young Lives vs Cancer",
            "description": "Young Lives vs Cancer (formerly Clic Sargent) is the UK’s leading cancer charity for children and young people, and their families. We provide clinical, practical, financial and emotional support to help them cope with cancer and get the most out of life. We are there from diagnosis onwards and aim to help the whole family deal with the impact of cancer and its treatment, life after treatment and, in some cases, bereavement.\r\n\r\nToday, 10 children and young people in the UK will hear the shocking news that they have cancer.",
            "website": "https://www.younglivesvscancer.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC039857"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Children",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Children"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FamilySupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Family Support"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FundraisingFunding",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Fundraising / Funding"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000CNbviAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000CNbviAAD/young-lives-vs-cancer-speaker",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Young Lives vs Cancer Speaker",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe know that for young lives, when the doctor says cancer, normal life stops. Cancer affects every part of life – relationships, confidence, money, school, work. Young Lives vs Cancer care teams will fight tirelessly to limit the damage cancer causes. \r\n\r\nBy becoming a Young Lives vs Cancer Speaker you’ll be giving your time to represent the charity in your local community; to be our voice, and to assist with fundraising and awareness raising activities near you.\n\n## Description\n\nBeing a Young Lives vs Cancer Speaker means being the face of the charity. You will become known for your effective, informative and interesting presentations on our work. This is a flexible role, and will largely involve presenting at evenings and weekends, or as and when a group requires a talk. \r\n\r\nThe role is a proactive one, with a focus on developing relationships with new supporters, and can include - Promoting the work of Young Lives vs Cancer by organising and giving talks and presentations; Proactively approaching local companies, groups and organisations in order to organise speaking opportunities; Collecting cheques from community groups, businesses and organisations – saying thank you and giving a talk on behalf of Young Lives vs Cancer. \r\n\r\nExperience of public speaking is desirable but not essential\n\n## Experience required\n\nAbility to use PowerPoint, Excel & Word; A good knowledge of your local area, Good communication and interpersonal skills, to represent Young Lives vs Cancer in a professional manner; You’ll be proactive in your approach to tasks and keen to build relationships – you don’t need to have lots of experience, just enthusiasm; Willingness to learn.\n\n## Training details\n\nYour dedicated Fundraising Engagement Manager will support you in your role and you’ll get an induction into Young Lives vs Cancer and our work \r\nAppropriate training to support you in delivering talks and presentations\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nSpeaking opportunities will often be in the evenings and weekends, so an ability to commit to evening time and weekends is a must for this role.\n\n## Travel details\n\nSome travelling may be required but you will be based in your local community.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000CNbviAAD#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Young Lives vs Cancer Speaker",
                        "description": "Ability to use PowerPoint, Excel & Word; A good knowledge of your local area, Good communication and interpersonal skills, to represent Young Lives vs Cancer in a professional manner; You’ll be proactive in your approach to tasks and keen to build relationships – you don’t need to have lots of experience, just enthusiasm; Willingness to learn.",
                        "commitment": "Speaking opportunities will often be in the evenings and weekends, so an ability to commit to evening time and weekends is a must for this role.",
