        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008ndsoAAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008ndsoAAA/dryburgh-athletic-community-club",
            "name": "Dryburgh Athletic Community Club",
            "description": "At Dryburgh Athletic Community Club we provide footballing activities to children in the local area of Lochee in Dundee. Currently we have over 350 player taking part in weekly activity, with children as young at three joining the club.\r\n\r\n“The advancement of public participation in sport through the provision of facilities, coaching, training and opportunities initially and primarily related to football” (from the Dryburgh Constitution)",
            "website": "https://www.dryburghacc.co.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC045585"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QNrMSAA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QNrMSAA1/sports-coach",
                    "publishStart": "2021-10-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-01",
                    "title": "Sports Coach",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDryburgh Athletic are recruiting coaches for our boys and girls teams. We will provide full coach kit and support you in gaining coaching badges and other relevant\r\nqualifiactions needed within the role .\n\n## Description\n\nDryburgh Athletic Community Club have over 350 players taking part in weekly football sessions. As this number continues to grow we are on the lookout for more volunteers to join us. \r\n\r\nPlayers as young as three join the communuty club and we have both a boys and grils pathway. All our teams will train at least once a week and play games or festivals at the weekend.\r\n\r\nAll new volunteers will be asked to complete the club's PVG process which is handled by our Child Protection and Wellbeing Officer. Once this process is complete we will support the new volunteer and fund coaching badges, first aid courses and any other relevant qualifications required. Coaching kit will also be provided.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience required but an interest in football would benefit, a willingness to learn and a time commitment\n\n## Training details\n\nThe new volunteer will be able to shadow sessions and supported by club development officer or by qualified and knowledgeable coaches already in place. Given the opportunity to gain SFA coaching badges\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nTime commitment weekly for training session maximum 1.5 hours and at the weekend either Saturday or Sunday for games / festivals\n\n## Travel details\n\nDryburgh Athletic Community Club\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note: No expenses are paid for this opportunity\n\n## Taster details\n\nAny new volunteer can come along and will meet with a member of the committee to discuss the process and to see where would best suit them to get involved",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
