                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0rQD00001KsudtYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/events/a0rQD00001KsudtYAB/13th-international-conference-on-violence-against-women",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-21",
                    "title": "13th International Conference on Violence Against Women",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nICOVAW 2026 – Our Collective Power is the International Conference on Violence Against Women, hosted by Time to Heal at Crowne Plaza Aberdeen Airport, 2 International Gate, Dyce, Aberdeen, AB21 0BE.\r\n\r\nThe conference brings together survivors, advocates, community and faith leaders, professionals and international delegates to share knowledge, strengthen partnerships and explore practical responses to violence against women. Through keynote presentations, interactive discussions and networking, participants will consider how individuals, organisations and communities can work together to prevent abuse and support recovery.\r\n\r\nThe theme, “Our Collective Power,” highlights the difference we can make through shared responsibility and coordinated action. The event provides opportunities to raise awareness, exchange experiences and build connections that support safer communities.\r\n\r\nVolunteers will help with welcoming guests, registration, event preparation, hospitality, delegate support and social media. Their contribution will help create a welcoming and organised conference while offering valuable experience and opportunities to connect with others committed to rebuilding broken lives.\n\n## Role description\n\nJoin Time to Heal in delivering the International Conference on Violence Against Women at Crowne Plaza Aberdeen Airport, 2 International Gate, Dyce, Aberdeen, AB21 0BE.\r\n\r\nWe welcome friendly, reliable volunteers for the following roles:\r\n- Welcome and Registration Volunteer: Greet guests, check registrations, distribute conference materials and answer general enquiries.\r\n- Event Operations and Logistics Volunteer: Help prepare the venue, arrange materials, guide guests between sessions and support the conference timetable.\r\n- Speaker and Delegate Support Volunteer: Welcome speakers and delegates, provide directions and assist with practical requests.\r\n- Hospitality Volunteer: Help welcome guests during refreshment breaks and dinner, working alongside venue staff.\r\n- Social Media and Content Volunteer: Help capture conference highlights and prepare updates, following consent and confidentiality guidance.\r\n- Conference Room Support Volunteer: Assist with seating, distribute session materials and support speakers and the organising team during discussions.\r\n\r\nPrevious experience is helpful but not essential for most roles. We value teamwork, willingness to learn, respect for confidentiality and a compassionate, non-judgemental attitude. Volunteers will receive a briefing and support from a designated coordinator. Roles and shifts will be agreed according to your skills, interests and availability.\r\n\r\nThis is an opportunity to gain practical event experience, meet people from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Time to Heal’s mission of “Rebuilding Broken Lives.”\r\n\r\nTogether, our voices are stronger.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/events%2FXIZqc9hDXQXnwLRM1ncdQHMpUsb2%2FIGelexqzubtI4MgJ-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=d73e288e-bc83-4c25-8d6c-c5a6d29dd4a6",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0rQD00001KsudtYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "13th International Conference on Violence Against Women",
                        "description": "Join Time to Heal in delivering the International Conference on Violence Against Women at Crowne Plaza Aberdeen Airport, 2 International Gate, Dyce, Aberdeen, AB21 0BE.\r\n\r\nWe welcome friendly, reliable volunteers for the following roles:\r\n- Welcome and Registration Volunteer: Greet guests, check registrations, distribute conference materials and answer general enquiries.\r\n- Event Operations and Logistics Volunteer: Help prepare the venue, arrange materials, guide guests between sessions and support the conference timetable.\r\n- Speaker and Delegate Support Volunteer: Welcome speakers and delegates, provide directions and assist with practical requests.\r\n- Hospitality Volunteer: Help welcome guests during refreshment breaks and dinner, working alongside venue staff.\r\n- Social Media and Content Volunteer: Help capture conference highlights and prepare updates, following consent and confidentiality guidance.\r\n- Conference Room Support Volunteer: Assist with seating, distribute session materials and support speakers and the organising team during discussions.\r\n\r\nPrevious experience is helpful but not essential for most roles. We value teamwork, willingness to learn, respect for confidentiality and a compassionate, non-judgemental attitude. Volunteers will receive a briefing and support from a designated coordinator. Roles and shifts will be agreed according to your skills, interests and availability.\r\n\r\nThis is an opportunity to gain practical event experience, meet people from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Time to Heal’s mission of “Rebuilding Broken Lives.”\r\n\r\nTogether, our voices are stronger.",
