                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eOHiAAM",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eOHiAAM/driver-for-medical-appointments-in-east-renfrewshire",
                    "publishStart": "2003-06-19",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-19",
                    "title": "Driver for Medical Appointments in East Renfrewshire",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAre you over 40?  Have some time to Spare? \nHelp Transport patients from across East Renfrewshire to & from hospitals and health centres.\nNo experience necessary.\nDrivers do require their own transport.\n\n## Description\n\nVolunteers use their own vehicles to take patients to and from medical appointments. Volunteers let us know availability i.e, which day/days they wish to do and what times. Volunteers can also let us know what hospitals they are happy to take patients to and what hospitals they would not like to go to.  Drivers pick up no earlier than 8.45 am and finish no later than 5.30 pm.  Normally it is one patient per driver per car.\n\n## Experience required\n\nReliability, happy to work in a one-to-one situation, conscientious driver.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nTimes will be arranged to suit the volunteer.  Weekdays.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDrivers pick up patients from the East Renfrewshire area and take them to medical appointments then return them home.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMileage allowance will be paid.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F0df11311-4f4f-8545-5b19-055628241946%2FmQsKXYYIupgt1ub9BeDSGFfo1O33%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=a896180e-d5e1-48c1-812e-578be21bbbe1",
