            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000QhjyKAAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000QhjyKAAR/bike-maintenanceled-cycle-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-04-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-19",
                    "title": "Bike Maintenance/Led Cycle Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDo you love bikes? Would you like to learn new bike repair and maintenance skills to help other people cycle?\r\n\r\nWe are looking for volunteers to help in our Bike Repair and Maintenance Group. This group:\r\n\r\n-Services bikes belonging to the community \r\n-Renovates donated bikes to give to people who could not have one otherwise\r\n-Maintains the fleet of bikes used by our team of volunteer lock keepers\r\n\r\nTraining will be given but we are particularly looking for people who already have some interest in bikes.  Committed volunteers will be given the opportunity to work towards certified Bike Mechanic Training.\r\n\r\nWe also run led cycles with the opportunity to qualify as lead cyclists, taking groups along the tow path and beyond.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAny practical skills would be helpful but what is important is an enthusiasm for making and repairing things, for learning new skills and passing on what you know.\r\n\r\nFull training provided. An interest in canals, heritage, exercise, well- being and or creativity.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction includes: Initial taster session and discussion to help ensure the volunteer is provided with the best possible opportunities to suit their needs. Tour of the site and introductions. Volunteer handbook provided, volunteer agreement signed. Ongoing training plans created to suit the needs of the individual.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWednesday mornings.\n\n## Travel details\n\nLock 16 Port Downie Camelon, situated at the side of the canal with easy access and parking on site.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses reimbursed. 45p per mile or bus/train fare.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F13ff0883-b1e6-4c5c-93d3-41faf1cb8c7a%2Fq19DcOWGQCRPIPMRCkAF0XcUA2l1%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=65cf5ce9-a8fd-4b84-8eae-95055eca1129",
