                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HqpW6YAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HqpW6YAJ/community-gardening-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-25",
                    "title": "Community Gardening Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGet Involved & Make a Difference!\r\n\r\nLooking for a chance to get outdoors, meet new people and give something back to your local community? Join Go Forth & Clyde's friendly volunteer team every Wednesday at Lock 16, Portdownie. \r\n\r\nFrom the cabins, they take a minibus to Barnardo’s Watling Lodge, where they get stuck in helping to keep the grounds looking welcoming and well cared for.  Activities include:\r\n\r\n🌱 Weeding\r\n✂️ Pruning\r\n🍃 General gardening and tidying\r\n🌿 Helping to improve and maintain the grounds\r\n\r\nNo gardening experience is needed — just bring yourself, some enthusiasm and a willingness to get involved!\r\n\r\nIt’s a great way to get outdoors, meet new people, learn new skills and make a real difference to a local community space. Come along and join the team! 🌻\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo gardening experience is needed — just bring yourself, some enthusiasm and a willingness to get involved!\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWednesday mornings from 10am.\n\n## Travel details\n\nLock 16, Portdownie in Falkirk – meet at the cabins.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses reimbursed. 45p per mile or bus/train fare.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://goforthandclyde.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/cropped-Go-Forth-and-Clyde-mauve-and-navy-on-white-e1659974113126.jpg",
