            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000COzoDYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000COzoDYAT/treasurer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-10-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-09",
                    "title": "Treasurer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDenny and Dunipace Citizens Advice Bureau (CAB) is a trusted local charity serving communities across Denny, Dunipace, Bonnybridge, Banknock, and surrounding area. We provide free, impartial, and confidential advice on a wide range of issues including benefits, debt, housing, employment, consumer rights, and more.\r\n\r\nEach year, our dedicated team of staff and volunteers supports over 2,000 local people, helping them find a way forward in times of crisis or uncertainty. As part of the national Citizens Advice network, we are committed to promoting social justice and tackling inequality in our community.\r\n\r\nWe welcome candidates from a variety of backgrounds, especially those with financial management, accounting, or bookkeeping experience. You don’t need previous trustee experience—what matters most is a commitment to our values and a willingness to contribute your expertise.\r\n\r\nKey responsibilities:\r\n\r\nOversee the financial health of the bureau\r\n\r\nEnsure financial compliance and accountability\r\n\r\nWork with the Manager on budgeting and reporting\r\n\r\nPresent clear financial reports to the Board\r\n\r\nSupport strategic decision-making through sound financial insight\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe welcome candidates from a variety of backgrounds, especially those with financial management, accounting, or bookkeeping experience. \r\nYou don’t need previous trustee experience—what matters most is a commitment to our values and a willingness to contribute your expertise.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll new volunteers receive a comprehensive induction to help them understand the role, the work of Citizens Advice, and the values we uphold.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMeeting takes place 4 times a year plus AGM.\r\nHowever further meetings can be requested where required over and above the set meetings quarterly.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Business Park, Carronbank Crescent, Denny, FK6 6DW.\r\nWe are on a bus route and have free parking within walking distance.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMileage 45p per mile and reimbursement of any public transport.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F9d610570-d3c8-4ded-8181-f4bfa27f9fab%2FXPrpz4zVmiRWRuGPAUiQ4SyLdVd2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=200a2446-0f2d-44cc-b5a8-77ddc40ceb46",
