                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-19",
                    "title": "Helpers for Gang Show",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHelpers for Gang Show\n\n## Description\n\nGang Show Volunteers Wanted!\n\nBe part of the team behind the show!\n\nWe&rsquo;re looking for enthusiastic volunteers to help make this year&rsquo;s&nbsp;Gang Show&nbsp;a success. There are a variety of roles available, from hair and make-up to backstage crew and operating a follow spot.\n\nWhether you have theatre experience or simply want to get involved and have some fun, we&rsquo;d love to hear from you!\n\n?? Hair &amp; Make-Up Volunteers\n\nHelp us get our cast of around&nbsp;120 performers&nbsp;show-ready!\n\nWe&rsquo;re looking for volunteers who can help with:\n\n\nCreating&nbsp;show braids&nbsp;for cast members with longer hair\nApplying&nbsp;basic stage make-up\nCreating some more&nbsp;creative make-up/face painting&nbsp;for a couple of our bigger numbers\n\n\nNo age restriction applies to hair and make-up volunteers.\n\nYou don&rsquo;t need to be a professional &ndash; just have an interest in hair, make-up or face painting and be happy to help!\n\n?? Backstage &amp; Stage Crew - 16+\n\nWe&rsquo;re looking for volunteers aged&nbsp;16 or over&nbsp;to join our backstage stage crew.\n\nYou could help with:\n\n\nMaking and painting staging, scenery and props in advance\nHelping to move staging on and off the stage\nSupporting the backstage team during performances\n\n\nIdeally, you would be available on&nbsp;Sunday 13 September&nbsp;to help get everything into the theatre, as well as&nbsp;Monday 14 to Saturday 19 September, approximately&nbsp;6pm-10pm. Ideally available for the full run, but please get in touch if you can help with some of the dates\n\n?? Follow Spot Operator - 16+\n\nWe&rsquo;re also looking for someone aged&nbsp;16 or over&nbsp;to operate a follow spot during the show.\n\nYou&rsquo;ll help spotlight performers at different points during the performance.\n\nNo previous experience is required - full training and direction will be provided.\n\nThe commitment is from&nbsp;Sunday afternoon through to Saturday evening.\n\n?? Why Volunteer?\n\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to:\n\n\nGet involved behind the scenes of a live theatre production\nMeet new people and be part of a team\nDevelop practical skills and experience\nSupport local young people and performers\nHave fun and help bring the Gang Show to life!\n\n\n?? Earn Saltire Awards Recognition\n\nIf you&rsquo;re aged&nbsp;11-25, volunteering with the Gang Show could also count towards your&nbsp;Saltire Awards!\n\nThe Saltire Awards recognise the time and commitment young people give to volunteering and are a great way to build skills, experience and confidence while making a difference in your community.\n\nSo whether you&rsquo;re helping with hair and make-up, working backstage or operating the follow spot,&nbsp;you could gain valuable volunteering experience and work towards your Saltire Award at the same time.&nbsp;??\n\nMake sure your volunteering hours are recorded so you can receive recognition for your contribution.\n\nInterested? Get in touch and let us know which role you&#39;d like to volunteer for.\n\nCome and be part of the team that makes the magic happen! ???",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
