        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nhW3AAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nhW3AAI/marie-curie",
            "name": "Marie Curie",
            "description": "Marie Curie is the UK’s leading end-of-life charity. We are the largest non-NHS provider of end-of-life care in the UK, the only provider across all 4 nations, delivering community nursing and hospice care across the country, while providing information and support on all aspects of dying, death, and bereavement. \r\n\r\nOur leading research pushes the boundaries of what we know about good end-of-life, and our campaigns fight for a world where everyone gets to have the best possible quality of life while living with an illness they’re likely to die from.\r\n\r\nThe care and support we provide is highly valued by the people we care for and their loved ones, but at present we are only reaching around 10% of dying people at the end of life. Right now, one in four people in the UK with a terminal illness, do not get the care or support they deserve at the end of their lives.",
            "website": "https://www.mariecurie.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC038731"
                }
            ],
            "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FAccount%2F70a3fc0f-67bc-3b79-5fa9-2dcd4b884730%2FKNiPmiKJ42h7TTxtkEFQSDk5VjE3%2Fuser-upload.jpg?alt=media&token=f5428d63-4117-48ab-8624-2b5e33065ff4",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000CofInYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000CofInYAJ/volunteer-companions-edinburgh-midlothian-and-west-lothian",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-30",
                    "title": "Volunteer Companions -Edinburgh & Midlothian and West Lothian",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nMarie Curie is looking for compassionate, everyday people to join our Companion Team within the surrounding areas of Edinburgh, Midlothian and West Lothian. \r\n\r\nYou don’t need a medical background or all the answers – just a kind heart, a listening ear, and a little time to give.\r\n \r\n\r\nAs a Companion Volunteer, you might visit someone and share stories, connect through hobbies/interests, chat about life, update them regarding local or wider activities. Sometimes just a conversation with a cup of tea/coffee in hand provides a steady presence. You may also have the opportunity to volunteer within various care homes across West Lothian. \r\n\r\nWhat you'll do:\r\n\r\nProvide companionship and support\r\nHelp someone express what matters most\r\nShare helpful information and point them to local resources\r\nSupport families and carers, before and after bereavement\r\n \r\n\r\nWhy you'd be a great fit:\r\n\r\nYou are patient, friendly, and a good listener\r\nYou are non-judgmental and emotionally steady\r\nYou can provide 3 of your time each week\r\nYou are comfortable using email and happy to complete short visit reports\r\n \r\n\r\nWhat you'll gain:\r\n\r\nA deep sense of purpose and connection\r\nOngoing support, training, and guidance\r\nA welcoming volunteer community\r\nRecognition for your time and dedication\r\nReimbursement for out-of-pocket expenses\r\n \r\n\r\nReady to get involved?\r\nYou’ll need to be 18 years or older and provide 2 non-family references in our online application form\r\n\r\nWant to chat before applying? We’re happy to answer your questions with no pressure to commit.\r\n\r\nContact Volunteer Services Officer Clare Scott: clare.scott@mariecurie.org.uk\r\n\r\nRef: 3589",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000CofInYAJ#role",
