                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pc8CAAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pc8CAAAZ/retail-volunteer-stranraer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-07",
                    "title": "Retail Volunteer- Stranraer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nPlay a key role in the day‑to‑day running of our charity shop.\r\nWhether you’re helping on the shop floor, sorting donations, pricing items, or creating a friendly and welcoming space, your time and support will make a real and meaningful difference.\r\n \r\nAvailability: 3 hours per week\r\nTime: Shifts available Monday, Tuesday and Thursday between 12pm-5pm and Fridays 9am-5pm\r\nLocation: Unit 4 Arndale House 1 Castle St Stranraer DG9 7RR\r\nCriteria: Aged 14 or over. No previous experience required.\r\n\r\nWhat you'll do:\r\nSort donations and uncover hidden gems\r\nPrep items - steam, tag, and style for sale\r\nChat with customers and operate the till\r\nSpruce up window displays and restock shelves\r\nKeep things clean, tidy, and fabulous\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat you'll receive and achieve:\r\nTraining, ongoing guidance and wellbeing support \r\nRecognition for your time and effort\r\nUpdates on the difference you’re making\r\nLong Service Awards\r\nBe part of the UK’s leading end-of-life charity\r\nTravel and expenses covered\r\nAccess to discounts on shopping, travel, entertainment, and more\r\n15% discount in-store at our Marie Curie Shops (Terms & Conditions apply)\n\n## Experience required\n\nWhy you’d be a great fit:\r\n\r\nA positive, can-do attitude\r\nFriendly and compassionate to those around you\r\nComfortable talking to people from all walks of life\r\nGood organiser and happy to provide support where necessary\r\nTeam spirit - contributing to a positive team dynamic\n\n## Training details\n\nAll of our volunteers receive full training when they join us, as well as ongoing training and wellbeing support from our friendly retail team.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWe are looking for volunteers who can commit to at least 3 hours per week. We welcome students seeking to complete work experience as part of their curriculum, participating in the Duke of Edinburgh's Award scheme, or wishing to gain valuable experience to enhance their CV.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable out-of-pocket expenses are reimbursed monthly",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F1fc54ca3-0e16-a71e-6d28-728363830c4f%2Fl0vZSDmOksVEVcLkMLegAVo7FN82%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=4a565e77-7845-4c13-9f3f-10ad5aed6d04",
