                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000SsKqWAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000SsKqWAAV/gym-assistant-glasgow-hospice",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-30",
                    "title": "Gym Assistant- Glasgow Hospice",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe're looking for a motivated, friendly and reliable volunteer to help our physiotherapist run an activity group for our patients on Thursday afternoons. You will be helping to get patients started with their gym programmes, assisting the physiotherapist with facilitating the group (note that you will not be running the group on your own), registering each gym session and recording patients' exercises and attendance. Our goal is to provide a relaxed and welcoming environment for our patients to achieve their desired outcome from attending the group. If you love helping others and want to be part of a team that is directly supporting our patients then this could be the opportunity for you.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe're looking for a reliable and committed volunteer who has an understanding of how to deal sensitively with our patients' needs. Good people skills will be important, as well as a sense of fun. An understanding of the importance of confidentiality will be essential. A qualification in physical fitness, coaching or sports medicine is not essential but will be desirable.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll volunteers will receive initial training and induction when they join us, as well as ongoing training and support from their volunteer manager. We are also happy to have a conversation with volunteers about any support they may need to help them get the most out of their volunteering.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n3 hours a week for a minimum of 6 months.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Marie Curie hospice is located in the grounds of Stobhill Hospital in Springburn. We are approximately a 20 minute journey from Glasgow City Centre by car. You can also get to us by public transport, buses number 87 and 88 stop on Balgrayhill Road across from the entrance to the Stobhill grounds. Our nearest train station is Springburn, approximately a half hour walk from the hospice. \r\nParking is available but may be of limited availability at busier times.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe pay any reasonable out of pocket expenses incurred by our volunteers. Your volunteer manager will be able to discuss this with you and help you claim any expenses you are entitled to. Expenses are paid on a monthly basis by bank transfer.",
