        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nhWPAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nhWPAAY/national-society-for-the-prevention-of-cruelty-to-children-nspcc",
            "name": "National Society For The Prevention Of Cruelty To Children (Nspcc)",
            "description": "The NSPCC is the UK’s leading children's charity specialising in child protection and the prevention of cruelty to children.  Its vision is of a society where all children are loved, valued and able to fulfil their potential.  The NSPCC runs services across the UK and the Channel Islands, including therapeutic services for young people who have experienced abuse, domestic violence projects and services for supporting families.  National helpline services include the NSPCC helpline for adults with concerns about a child and the ChildLine service for children and young people.  For more information, visit www.nspcc.org.uk.",
            "website": "http://www.nspcc.org.uk",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC037717"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eLbZAAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000000eLbZAAU/schools-service-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-12",
                    "title": "Schools Service Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nDo you believe that children should be safe and happy? You could join an amazing team of volunteers who strive to ensure children’s voices are heard.\r\n\r\nHalf a million UK children experience abuse every year. By volunteering with NSPCC you can help to change this.\r\n\r\nAs a highly valued Speak out, Stay safe Volunteer, you will help protect a generation of children, helping them understand abuse and giving them the confidence to speak out if they need help. Last year in Scotland they spoke to 60 thousand children. With your help they can do more.\r\n\r\nAs a volunteer, you will have the opportunity to visit primary schools in West Fife twice a month to deliver classroom based Speak out. Stay safe workshops for children aged 6-11 years. You will make a huge difference to children in Scotland, learn and develop valuable skills and take pride in empowering children to speak out and stay safe.\n\n## Experience required\n\nIf you are:\r\n\r\n· passionate about helping children and young people;\r\n\r\n· excited about communicating with others;\r\n\r\n· empathetic, perceptive and supportive;\r\n\r\n· able to think on your feet;\r\n\r\n· able to work well within a team;\r\n\r\nyou have the qualities that could make you a great fit for this volunteer team!\n\n## Training details\n\nThere will be training throughout your volunteer journey, and the NSPCC team will be there to support you. Training will take place both online and face to face; volunteers will then continue their learning in schools. A local Schools Coordinator provides ongoing support and team building opportunities.\n\n## Travel details\n\nYou will visit primary schools in west Fife twice a month.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers can claim public transport or mileage expenses at 45p per mile",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000000eLbZAAU#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Schools Service Volunteer",
                        "description": "If you are:\r\n\r\n· passionate about helping children and young people;\r\n\r\n· excited about communicating with others;\r\n\r\n· empathetic, perceptive and supportive;\r\n\r\n· able to think on your feet;\r\n\r\n· able to work well within a team;\r\n\r\nyou have the qualities that could make you a great fit for this volunteer team!",
