        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000008nhXNAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000008nhXNAAY/springer-rescue-for-scotland",
            "name": "Springer Rescue For Scotland",
            "description": "The aims of the organisation are that every Springer Spaniel in Scotland should have the chance of a happy, fulfilled life in an appropriate home, and that every person or family that owns a springer should find this to be a positive experience, and one that enhances their quality of life.",
            "website": "http://www.springerrescuescotland.org",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC040565"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Bbaz3YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Bbaz3YAB/home-visit-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-09",
                    "title": "Home Visit Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSRS are looking for Home Visit Volunteers to visit the homes of potential adoptive and foster families.\n\n## Description\n\nSpringer Rescue Scotland (SRS) is a Scottish charity founded in 2008 to champion the welfare and rehoming of Spaniels. SRS is dedicated to ensuring that every Spaniel in Scotland finds a loving home and that their owners have enriching experiences. SRS embodies a non-judgmental approach, providing a safe haven for Spaniels in need and promoting their well-being with unwavering commitment.\r\nThey are looking for Home Visit Volunteers to visit the homes of potential adoptive and foster families.\r\nAs a Home Visit Volunteer, you will be given the tools you need to assess the home, including the standard form used for this. This is a very important role to assure that dogs surrendered to SRS have a safe and loving home.\r\nYou will receive full support, and can choose the location where you would like to volunteer.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience is required, although volunteers should be good at communication.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive an induction to the organisation and the role, and will receive ongoing support from the committee and local area coordinators.\n\n## Travel details\n\nYou will need to travel between homes in your local area, within Scotland.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on a case by case basis.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
