                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BbeD3YAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BbeD3YAJ/grant-funding-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-09",
                    "title": "Grant Funding Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSRS are looking for Grant Funding Volunteers to support with seeking out opportunities for grant funding, and applying for funding.\n\n## Description\n\nSpringer Rescue Scotland (SRS) is a Scottish charity founded in 2008 to champion the welfare and rehoming of Spaniels. SRS is dedicated to ensuring that every Spaniel in Scotland finds a loving home and that their owners have enriching experiences. SRS embodies a non-judgmental approach, providing a safe haven for Spaniels in need and promoting their well-being with unwavering commitment.\r\nThey are looking for Grant Funding Volunteers to support with seeking out opportunities for grant funding, and applying for funding. This role is perfect for someone with knowledge of grant funding, although volunteers can learn and develop through this role.\r\nYou will receive full support, and can choose the location where you would like to volunteer.\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers will ideally have knowledge/experience with grant funding, however you can learn and develop your skills through this role.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive an induction to the organisation and the role, and will receive ongoing support from the committee and local area coordinators.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis opportunity can be undertaken from home, for volunteers within Scotland.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on a case by case basis.",
