                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BbcuPYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BbcuPYAR/fundraising-and-publicity-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-09",
                    "title": "Fundraising and Publicity Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWhether you’re brimming with fundraising ideas, have practical skills, or simply know where to place a poster for maximum visibility, your involvement in fundraising and publicity can make a substantial difference to SRS.\n\n## Description\n\nSpringer Rescue Scotland (SRS) is a Scottish charity founded in 2008 to champion the welfare and rehoming of Spaniels. SRS is dedicated to ensuring that every Spaniel in Scotland finds a loving home and that their owners have enriching experiences. SRS embodies a non-judgmental approach, providing a safe haven for Spaniels in need and promoting their well-being with unwavering commitment.\r\nTheir work, including educational initiatives promoting responsible ownership, relies on financial support. Whether you’re brimming with fundraising ideas, have practical skills, or simply know where to place a poster for maximum visibility, your involvement in fundraising and publicity can make a substantial difference.\r\nAs a Fundraising and Publicity Volunteer, you will receive full support, and can choose the location where you would like to volunteer.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience is required, simply enthusiasm for the cause.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will receive an induction to the organisation and the role, and will receive ongoing support from the committee and local area coordinators.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis opportunity can be undertaken locally, or from home, for volunteers within Scotland.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses can be discussed on a case by case basis.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
