            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I3eMjYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000I3eMjYAJ/telephone-befriender",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-23",
                    "title": "Telephone Befriender",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are looking for cheerful volunteers who will be calling people in the Easterhouse community who face issues with social isolation and loneliness. These calls would be at the same time each week for around half an hour for each call with the goal of providing enrichment for the service user. Each befriending match would typically last between 3-6 months and we would want volunteers to be prepared to continue for that agreed period. \n\nWe would provide training on befriending, active listening and safeguarding as well as having regular supervisor check ins to ensure that the match is positive for both the befriender and the service user. \n\nThis role would be well suited to people at any stage of life and a wide diversity of befrienders would let us match people better based on overlapping interests. For younger people looking to develop skills and experience, it will provide a good insight into social care. For older people, it provides a meaningful way to engage with the local community. \n\nIf you think you meet this description, please get in touch and we will try to get you involved.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience is necessary and we will provide training and support as required.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining will be an in-person session at the Connie centre where we will go through different topics related to befriending, active listening and safeguarding as well as working through role play scenarios\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMatches should run for 3-6 months and we would want volunteers to be able to do weekly commitments for this period. We will be looking to have befrienders call their matches each week at the same time. Befrienders will have up to 6 matches in a day which will take up to 6 hours depending on when calls are scheduled.\n\n## Travel details\n\nTraining will be delivered at the Connie which has good public transport links via bus. Connect is open to discussing hybrid volunteering/working from home.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nCurrently there are no compensation plans.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2F81DjrUBydXQ1PKKGkTSHNDUUGtF3%2FVh5QKS9yyuSacFbD-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=ea8152b0-e75a-40aa-ab7f-474a8f689618",
