                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000GveuSAAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000GveuSAAR/shop-till-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Shop Till Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Storehouse is a community owned shop and cafe, stocking local and ethically sourced products. We provide a space for local crafters to sell their items, and a community space for local groups.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for friendly people who would like to help out working on the till in our shop.  Volunteers would need to have basic numeracy skills for this role.  Full training is provided.  Shop till shifts are typically 3 hours long.  We are proud to be an inclusive organisation.  \r\n\r\nMain shop tasks include:\r\n\r\n· Serving customers at the till\r\n· Taking café orders\r\n· Keeping the shop and cafe clean and tidy\r\n· Restocking shelves, fridges and fresh product\n\n## Experience required\n\nA positive attitude towards creating a friendly environment and to helping people.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers don’t need any prior experience as we will provide full training.  Volunteers are supported on an ongoing basis through existing members of staff and a dedicated Volunteer Co-ordinator.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n3 hours per week\n\n## Travel details\n\nBus routes 37, 47, 101, 102, 140, X62\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe pay daily mileage to volunteers.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F333e463e-477f-039a-4c9d-7952147c12f8%2FHi3K7lHa8wXatOHLGJFdBGJQtau2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=856130eb-fbf1-4972-b85a-22fec43355f2",
