            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001240000161KFnAAM/north-of-scotland-research-ethics-service",
            "name": "North of Scotland Research Ethics Service",
            "description": "NHS Research Ethics Committees protect and promote the interests of patients and the public in health and social care research.\r\n\r\nThe committees review applications from research teams across the UK, and the Scientific Officer provides support and guidance on request to all applicants for ethical review and additional support for researchers within Grampian, Highland, Orkney, Shetland and Western Isles Health Boards.\r\n\r\nThe members of the committee are non-paid volunteers and include lay people who are not involved with clinical care or medical research and expert members with clinical or medical research expertise.\r\n\r\nThe North of Scotland Research Ethics Service is governed by the UK wide Health Research Authority and the Chief Scientist Office in Scotland. We are supported by the Grampian, Highland, Orkney Shetland and Western Isles Health Boards.",
            "website": "https://www.nhsgrampian.org",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000FJvZSAA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000FJvZSAA1/research-ethics-committee-members",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Research Ethics Committee Members",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nResearch Ethics Committees consist of up to 18 members from both clinical and non-clinical backgrounds. Our committees review health and social research, check that people are provided with the information they need to help them decide whether they wish to take part, and provide an opinion as to whether the research is ethical. \r\n\r\nWe currently have vacancies for members of the public who are not currently healthcare professionals, and who are interested in thinking about issues from the perspective of a potential research participant and would like to develop knowledge of research ethics. Members receive training in ethical review and have opportunities to debate challenging issues. Positions are voluntary but expenses are paid for.  \r\n\r\nThe Committee meets on average for half a day per month and carry out additional work by email correspondence.  Contact us for an application form or an informal chat on tel: 01224 558458, email gram.nosres@nhs.scot\r\n\r\nInterest can be registered at any time.\n\n## Experience required\n\nCommittee members need to be committed to public service values of accountability, probity, openness and equality of opportunity and be able to consider the interests of participants in health or social care research.\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support and training provided to all volunteers. Includes induction training and a minimum of one day training per year in ethical review..\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible - 11 meetings per year and additional sub- committee work by correspondence.\n\n## Travel details\n\nNHS Grampian \r\nSummerfield House \r\n2 Eday Road \r\nAberdeen \r\nAB15 6RE\r\nParking available and close to bus routes: Platinum 13, 23, N23 and x18, x40.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nRelevant out of pocket expenses are re-imbursed in line with NHS Grampian travel policy.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000FJvZSAA1#role",
