                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-06",
                    "title": "Children & families volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNo matter how good our services are, we can't properly support our users/community well if we don't have good organisers in the team. If this sounds like you... we would love you to consider volunteering with us for a few hours per week.\r\n\r\n3D Drumchapel is a Charity which has been working with children and families in Drumchapel and surrounding areas for 25 years. Our services include a perinatal programme, parent & child sessions, parenting programmes, learning & development sessions, outdoor play, peer support groups, 1-1 support, family support in schools and practical support including Bairn Necessities which redistributes clothing and equipment for 0-5 years. \r\n\r\nThis role offers various opportunities in the following play sessions: Messy Play, Tots to Toddlers & Shake, Rattle & Roll, Movin & Groovin \r\nOur Children and Families Volunteers support the 3D staff team to facilitate a variety of activities for children from 2-5 years. These activities include arts and crafts, singing, and interactive games. Volunteers are required to welcome and engage with families, play alongside them and encourage them to join in and meet people. Some families may require support during the session. This is a hands-on role and volunteers assist with the planning, set up and tidy up of each session. \r\n\r\nSo whether you are looking to use your time well, update your skills or have the chance to do something a bit new, we can offer you a warm welcome and all of the support and help you could need.\r\nWe are seeing a rise in demand for our services everyday. Having your help will allow us to be there for the people who need us. Any time you can give will make a real difference.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDrumchapel Community Centre",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
