        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000008E6qXYAS",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000008E6qXYAS/mere-apne",
            "name": "Mere Apne",
            "description": "Mere  Apne is focus on Indian Older Adults over 60years of age. We aim to promote positive mental health and well-being and provide opportunity for them to be able to go out of their house in order to prevent isolation which can lead to distress, anxiety. We aim to provide them with activities which they are familiar with and also introduce various other activities ie Arts & crafts. Music, card games,yoga, exercise, organise walks, Board games and various other activities to meet their. Culture & social needs.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BlackMinorityEthnic",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Black / Minority Ethnic"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/OlderPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Older People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FE07aYAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FE07aYAD/group-activity-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-06",
                    "title": "Group Activity Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nMere Apne is a community group based in Milngavie which provides a safe welcoming place for older\r\npeople to socialise. The focus of the group is for people from the Indian Community in East Dunbartonshire\r\nwho are over 60. The group meets every Monday; there is food, music and a range of activities all with the\r\naim of creating social interaction and improving people’s health & wellbeing.\r\nDescribe the volunteering Opportunity\r\nWe are looking for volunteers to help at our group. We are looking for assistance with setting up before the\r\ngroup and clearing away afterwards; help in the kitchen, serving refreshments and generally helping out at\r\nthe group which is on 1-4pm on Mondays in Milngavie.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for someone who will be friendly and welcoming, prepared to get stuck in practically setting\r\nup and clearing away.\n\n## Travel details\n\nFraser Centre, Milngavie (Temp closed until March 2026) currently meeting in a venue in Glasgow",
