        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000008SaK5YAK",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000008SaK5YAK/supported-the-linda-tremble-foundation-south-ayrshire",
            "name": "SupportED The Linda Tremble Foundation (South Ayrshire)",
            "description": "The charity was set up in 2014 by her family in memory of Linda Tremble, who sadly lost her battle with anorexia nervosa in 2011. \r\nSince 2019 we have expanded to become Scotland’s leading community eating disorder charity and now hold support group meetings for people over 18 with eating disorders and for parents, carers and families in Ayrshire, Fife, Forth Valley, Glasgow, Highland, Lanarkshire, Perth, Edinburgh and Tayside. In the future our strategy is to expand into other areas in Scotland so that we can ensure that everyone in Scotland affected by an eating disorder gets support and respect in the heart of their community.",
            "website": "https://supportedscotland.org/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC045002"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/BefriendingMentoring",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Befriending / Mentoring"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BG3BhYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BG3BhYAL/community-ambassador",
                    "publishStart": "2025-07-31",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-10",
                    "title": "Community Ambassador",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe charity was set up in 2014 by her family in memory of Linda Tremble, who sadly lost her battle with anorexia nervosa in 2011. \r\nSince 2019 we have expanded to become Scotland’s leading community eating disorder charity and now hold support group meetings for people over 18 with eating disorders and for parents, carers and families in Ayrshire, Fife, Forth Valley, Glasgow, Highland, Lanarkshire, Perth, Edinburgh and Tayside. In the future our strategy is to expand into other areas in Scotland so that we can ensure that everyone in Scotland affected by an eating disorder gets support and respect in the heart of their community.\r\n\r\nCommunity Ambassador - SupportED (The Linda Tremble Foundation)\r\n•\tRaising awareness of eating disorders and SupportED in your local community whether that be your city, town, village, wider region or University/College.\r\n•\tDoing public talks about eating disorders and SupportED services.\r\n•\tDistributing SupportED resources such as flyers.\r\n•\tAttending events such as University Fresher fayres.\r\n•\tArranging and/or participating in fundraising and awareness events for SupportED.  \r\n\r\nWhat’s In It For You:\r\nWe will provide you with the training and support to be able to complete your role to your best ability. You will be supported by a dedicated member of staff who will work closely with you. This will include helping you with public speaking, providing you with opportunities and helping you come up with ideas. Following 6 months of working with us, we would also be able to provide professional references.\r\nWhy We Want You:\r\nBy working with us, you can help us raise awareness of eating disorders and our services in your local community. We need volunteers like you in order to reach as many people throughout Scotland as possible.\r\nWhere:\r\nIn your local community and online.\r\nCommitment:\r\nOne Year\n\n## Experience required\n\nRequirements:\r\n•\tPassionate about raising awareness of eating disorders and making a change in your local community.\r\n•\tArticulate with an empathetic manner. \r\n•\tCommitted to attending regular training when required. \r\n•\tA go-getter attitude and strong initiative . \r\n•\tFeel able to engage in public speaking following relevant training and support. \r\n•\tKnowledge of mental health and eating disorders. \r\n•\tLived experience of an eating disorder or someone close to you who has/had one.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F5d66b692-d3ac-44e4-86c6-24dcdd7dbfcb%2F0nFCUqNjeiXPIFO483j0BVWArU43%2Fheader.jpg?alt=media&token=2ec454b3-61f8-4d2d-ad29-b7360a73b637",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BG3BhYAL#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Community Ambassador",
                        "description": "Requirements:\r\n•\tPassionate about raising awareness of eating disorders and making a change in your local community.\r\n•\tArticulate with an empathetic manner. \r\n•\tCommitted to attending regular training when required. \r\n•\tA go-getter attitude and strong initiative . \r\n•\tFeel able to engage in public speaking following relevant training and support. \r\n•\tKnowledge of mental health and eating disorders. \r\n•\tLived experience of an eating disorder or someone close to you who has/had one.",
