                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000B9PKDYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000B9PKDYA3/community-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-12",
                    "title": "Community Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nRNID are looking for Community Volunteers to get involved in multiple locations within their local area on a flexible, ad-hoc basis.\n\n## Description\n\nRNID are looking for Community Volunteers to get involved in multiple locations within their local area on a flexible, ad-hoc basis. As a community volunteer, you will:\r\n-\tDeliver presentations and talks to share information with local groups and organisations, either in-person or held remotely online. These raise awareness of deafness, hearing loss and tinnitus and the services and support available. You will provide information on RNID, their activities, and how people can support them.\r\n-\tPerform hearing checks, visiting groups in your community to help people take the RNID online hearing check. Supporting someone to take the online hearing check usually takes 10-15 minutes and will suggest if the person’s hearing is in normal range, or they may have hearing loss.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to get involved with a flexible opportunity and make a difference to people in your local area, register your interest today.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tConfidence\r\n•\tFriendly\r\n•\tBasic computing skills\r\n•\tReliable\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers attend an online (Zoom) Induction session with other new volunteers. After this this then undertake online Safegaurding training and Youtube “hearing check” training. Volunteers then have the option of shadowing an existing volunteer in  “in person situation” until they feel comfortable in the role.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis opportunity is a Fife wide role and you may need to be able to travel by car or public transport to different places.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nRNID reimburse public travel cost, or car milage at 0.45 per mile. Expenses can be claimed fortnightly and are paid by bank transfer.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000B9PKDYA3#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Community Volunteer",
                        "description": "•\tConfidence\r\n•\tFriendly\r\n•\tBasic computing skills\r\n•\tReliable",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000B9PKDYA3/community-volunteer?#modal_register_a0gQD00000B9PKDYA3",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
