                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HyEr7YAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HyEr7YAF/scout-leaderhelper",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Scout Leader/Helper",
                    "description": "## Description\n\n18th Ayrshire (St Columba) Scout Group are looking for Team Helpers/Leaders to help at either their Beavers, Cubs or Scouts Groups. Are you interested in working with young people, learning new skills and sharing your existing skills? You could be learning how to pitch a tent, light a campfire or cooking. It’s not just our young people that gain skills for life, but our Team Members, too.   \r\n\r\nScouts is open to everyone and that includes our amazing volunteers. We know you have something to bring to the team and tasks include:\r\n\r\n- Running adventurous activities and games \r\n- Helping and supporting young people\r\n- Chatting and collaborating with fellow volunteers, parents and carers\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWe are looking for volunteers who can commit to a couple of hours per week on a Thursday or Friday evening.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-volunteerscotland-search.appspot.com/o/opportunities%2FQ9yNn2TMsMcRXhwrj04qs0kOmFg1%2FayX6hN0jTf8VzmCV-thumbnail.jpg?alt=media&token=147d9ca7-8edc-4df6-ada2-a5ef3d3adb4f",
