        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000ARNm4YAH",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000ARNm4YAH/hareleeshill-community-hub",
            "name": "Hareleeshill Community Hub",
            "description": "Hareleeshill Community Hub provide much needed hall space for community events, hall hire and group activities. \nWe pride ourselves in being part of our local community working hard to build relationships with users of the facility, visitors and our neighbours.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEngagement",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Engagement"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000002FfT7YAK",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000002FfT7YAK/community-hall-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-21",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-26",
                    "title": "Community Hall Assistant",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Hub will shortly celebrate its 1st year operating in Hareleeshill, providing much needed hall space for community events, hall hire and group activities. With demand increasing we are looking for new volunteers, willing to be part of a team and help build a vibrant community asset. \nWe pride ourselves in being part of our local community working hard to build relationships with users of the facility, visitors and our neighbours. We require those joining the team to have the same ethos, to be investors in people and the local community. \n\n\nVolunteer Hall Assistants.\n\nAs a valued member of the team our Hall Assistants would be responsible for the following:-\n\nBefore Hire Starts\n\nOpen the Building for group/hall hires.\n\nEnsure the hall and facilities are clean and set up ready for use as agreed in hall hire application form.\n\nGreet those entering the facilities, be approachable.\n\n\nDuring Activity\n \nMust always stay on site.\n\nGreet those entering the facilities / be approachable.\n\nBe the point of contact during a group/hall hire.\n\nEnsure all equipment is available and ready for group activity.\n\nEnsure the building is evacuated in case of an emergency.\n\n\nAt End of Hall Hire\n\nEnsure the hall is left in an acceptable condition by group/hall hire.\n\nClean facilities at the end of each group ready to be used.\n\nTidy away any equipment.\n\nEnsure all electrical equipment is turned off.\n\nCarryout lockdown checks and ensure the building is secure at the end of the day.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Hard Working,Open minded,Organised,Patient,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Social Conscience,Team Player,Trustworthy,\n\n## Training details\n\nOn first day of volunteering every volunteer will go through a volunteer induction and ongoing training will be provided.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire,Larkhall\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAny expense incurred and to be reimbursed should be agreed in advance before the volunteer spends anything on work related items.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000002FfT7YAK#role",
