                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-30",
                    "title": "Driver for Community Tea Party",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you have a couple of hours once a month to help take an Older Person to a tea party? If yes, you can help combat loneliness and isolation in your community.\n\n## Description\n\nIsolation and Loneliness are on the rise especially with Older People in the Community. We are looking for friendly and caring people to help with our tea parties. Could you help drive one or two guests to tea parties? You will only be volunteering once a month, so this is perfect for fitting around your own availability and lifestyle.\r\n\r\nYou will help drive the same one or two guests to the group and then stay for some refreshments and a good blether. Normally the tea party will last for about 2 hours on a Sunday afternoon and is hosted by other Volunteers in their home. It is the same local group you volunteer with so you can make some real connections to your community and the Older Guests. \r\n\r\nAll training is remote, and you are supported by our team and Tea Party Co-ordinator in your role.\n\n## Experience required\n\nDriving License required.\r\n\r\nNo other experience or particular skills required. We just need you to be an empathetic person who is ready to work alongside Older People over the age of 75.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull remote training provided including PVG check and safeguarding, complete at your own pace. In your role you are also supported by our Support team and your Tea Party Co-ordinator for any questions or queries you have.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMonthly for approximately 2 hours on a Sunday\n\n## Travel details\n\nDundee wide\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note: No expenses are offered for this role.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
