                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000002ulcbYAA",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000002ulcbYAA/organiser-for-community-tea-party",
                    "publishStart": "2024-03-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-30",
                    "title": "Organiser for Community Tea Party",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAre you organised and passionate about combatting loneliness and isolation in your community? If yes, we need you to help organise our community tea party.\n\n## Description\n\nIsolation and Loneliness are on the rise especially with Older People in the Community. We are looking for organised and empathetic people to help with our tea parties. Could you co-ordinate and help welcome guests and volunteers to our tea parties? Our tea parties are once a month for two hours, so this is perfect for fitting around your own availability and lifestyle.\r\n\r\nYou will help arrange a schedule for Tea Party hosts and communicate timings with the group and of course stay for some refreshments and a good blether. Normally the tea party will last for about 2 hours on a Sunday afternoon and is hosted by other Volunteers in their home. It is the same local group you volunteer with so you can make some real connections to your community and the Older Guests. All training is remote, and you are supported by our Support team in your role.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo experience or particular skills required. We just need you to be an empathetic and organised person who is ready to work alongside Older People over the age of 75.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull remote training provided including PVG check and safeguarding, complete at your own pace.\r\n\r\nIn your role you are also supported by our Support team and your Tea Party Co-ordinator for any questions or queries you have.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe tea Parties are monthly for approximately 2 hours on a Sunday and you are not required to attend but you are invited to. This is a an administrative role that is flexible and can be fit around other commitments.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDundee wide.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease Note: No expenses are offered for this role.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
