            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000002wh3RYAQ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000002wh3RYAQ/trusteeboard-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-03",
                    "title": "Trustee/Board Member",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThey are looking for an individual or individuals with a passion for Dunfermline’s green spaces.\n\n## Description\n\nDunfermline Greenspace SCIO is a community-owned, membership based charity established in 2023. Its purpose is to support local groups and projects in delivering the Dunfermline Greenspace 2030 strategy, which supports the community to tackle the climate, nature, biodiversity and health emergencies.\r\n\r\nThey are looking for an individual or individuals with a passion for Dunfermline’s green spaces, a commitment to protecting the environment, and/or an interest in preserving the city’s heritage. They welcome applications from all sectors of Dunfermline society, particularly women and people from diverse backgrounds to the board of trustees.\r\n\r\nManagement and/or business experience would be useful but is not necessary for this position, and it may be a useful role for someone to build strategic management experience.\n\n## Experience required\n\nManagement and/or business experience would be useful but is not necessary for this position, and it may be a useful role for someone to build strategic management experience.\n\n## Training details\n\nThere will be an induction to cover the policies and procedures, a trustee pack with organisational information and signposting to relevant training sessions.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nOnce per month.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBoard meetings take place at Dunfermline Greenspace, Caretakers House, Baldridgeburn Community Centre, KY12 9EH.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses reimbursed at 45p per mile or public transport rates. Reasonable food requests will also be reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
