                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HrBGTYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HrBGTYA3/greenspace-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-03",
                    "title": "Greenspace Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThey are looking for volunteers/individuals with a passion for Dunfermline’s green spaces, a commitment to protecting the environment, and/or an interest in preserving the city’s heritage.\n\n## Description\n\nDunfermline Greenspace SCIO is a community-owned, membership-based charity established in 2023. Its purpose is to support local groups and projects in delivering the Dunfermline Greenspace 2030 strategy, which supports the community to tackle the climate, nature, biodiversity and health emergencies. \r\n\r\nThey are looking for volunteers/individuals with a passion for Dunfermline’s green spaces, a commitment to protecting the environment, and/or an interest in preserving the city’s heritage. \r\n\r\nThey have options to get involved in community gardening, digging; with their repair cafe and tool library, helping make and repair items and getting hands-on; and helping at their events.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo specific skills are required for this role, just a willingness to learn and an interest in making a different to green spaces in Dunfermline.\n\n## Training details\n\nThere will be an induction to cover the policies and procedures, and ongoing support and training available from the development officer.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nOnce per month.\n\n## Travel details\n\nOpportunities take place at sites across Dunfermline.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nExpenses reimbursed at 45p per mile or public transport rates. Reasonable food requests will also be reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
