            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HGBovYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HGBovYAH/musical-memories-volunteers-musicians",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-26",
                    "title": "Musical Memories Volunteers – Musicians",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you love music? Can you play the piano, guitar, or accordion?\r\nIf so, you could make a real difference by joining Musical Memories—a warm, welcoming singing group for people living with dementia, along with their partners, families, and friends.  \r\n\r\nWe’re looking for an experienced musician to support our regular Musical Memories sessions for people living with dementia and their family and friends. \r\n\r\nVolunteers take turns each week to provide live musical accompaniment, helping participants sing along to a variety of well-loved songs from different eras. \r\n\r\nEach session follows a themed playlist, with another volunteer leading the singing and making announcements. Your role will be to play the instrumental backing (backline) and help create a warm, engaging atmosphere through music.\r\n\r\nRun by a passionate team of volunteers, these sessions use the power of music to spark joy, boost brain activity, and encourage creativity and connection. Whether you're a seasoned performer or just enjoy playing for fun, your musical talents could help bring smiles and meaningful moments to others. \r\n\r\nPreviously held at the Alzheimer Scotland Dementia Resource Centre, this event now takes place every second Friday, 1.30pm-3.00pm at the Cowdray Hall (in/next to Aberdeen Art Gallery), Schoolhill, Aberdeen, AB10 1JQ, supporting larger audiences and growing community engagement.    \r\n\r\nExcellent support and relevant training provided to all volunteers. Volunteers will receive a full induction to Musical Memories sessions, a tour of the venue and a copy of the Aberdeen Archives, Gallery & Museums volunteer handbook. We will also provide training on Being Dementia Friendly.\r\n\r\nA fantastic, enjoyable opportunity to help and make a real difference. All assistance is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nTo volunteer with us/for further details please contact Sandra Still, Audience Insight Officer at email:  sstill@aberdeencity.gov.uk or telephone: 01224 069340\n\n## Description\n\nDo you love music? Can you play the piano, guitar, or accordion?\r\nIf so, you could make a real difference by joining Musical Memories—a warm, welcoming singing group for people living with dementia, along with their partners, families, and friends.  \r\n\r\nWe’re looking for an experienced musician to support our regular Musical Memories sessions for people living with dementia and their family and friends. \r\n\r\nVolunteers take turns each week to provide live musical accompaniment, helping participants sing along to a variety of well-loved songs from different eras. \r\n\r\nEach session follows a themed playlist, with another volunteer leading the singing and making announcements. Your role will be to play the instrumental backing (backline) and help create a warm, engaging atmosphere through music.\r\n\r\nRun by a passionate team of volunteers, these sessions use the power of music to spark joy, boost brain activity, and encourage creativity and connection. Whether you're a seasoned performer or just enjoy playing for fun, your musical talents could help bring smiles and meaningful moments to others. \r\n\r\nPreviously held at the Alzheimer Scotland Dementia Resource Centre, this event now takes place every second Friday, 1.30pm-3.00pm at the Cowdray Hall (in/next to Aberdeen Art Gallery), Schoolhill, Aberdeen, AB10 1JQ, supporting larger audiences and growing community engagement.    \r\n\r\nExcellent support and relevant training provided to all volunteers. Volunteers will receive a full induction to Musical Memories sessions, a tour of the venue and a copy of the Aberdeen Archives, Gallery & Museums volunteer handbook. We will also provide training on Being Dementia Friendly.\r\n\r\nA fantastic, enjoyable opportunity to help and make a real difference. All assistance is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nTo volunteer with us/for further details please contact Sandra Still, Audience Insight Officer anytime at email:  sstill@aberdeencity.gov.uk or telephone: 01224 069340\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training provided to all volunteers.\r\n\r\nVolunteers will receive a full induction to Musical Memories sessions, a tour of the venue and a copy of the Aberdeen Archives, Gallery & Museums volunteer handbook. We will also provide training on Being Dementia Friendly.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMeets every second Friday and is located at the Cowdray Hall (part of/next to Aberdeen Art Gallery) at 1.30pm - 3.00pm. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMusical Memories meets at the Cowdray Hall (in/next to Aberdeen Art Gallery), Schoolhill, Aberdeen, AB10 1JQ",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
