                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HG6UJYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HG6UJYA1/musical-memories-volunteers-it",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-20",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-12",
                    "title": "Musical Memories Volunteers – I.T.",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAre you confident using a laptop and familiar with Microsoft programs like PowerPoint?  If so, you could play a vital role in Musical Memories—a joyful singing group for people living with dementia, along with their partners, families, and friends.\r\n\r\nWe’re looking for someone to help run the technical side of our sessions, such as displaying lyrics, playing music tracks, or managing simple presentations. \r\n\r\nLed by a dedicated team of volunteers, these sessions promote wellbeing, spark memories, and encourage connection through music.  Your tech skills could help make the magic happen! \r\n\r\nPreviously held at the Alzheimer Scotland Dementia Resource Centre, this event now takes place every second Friday, 1.30pm-3.00pm at the Cowdray Hall (in/next to Aberdeen Art Gallery), Schoolhill, Aberdeen, AB10 1JQ, supporting larger audiences and growing community engagement.    \r\n\r\nA fantastic, enjoyable opportunity to help and make a real difference. All assistance is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nTo volunteer with us/for further details please contact Sandra Still, Audience Insight Officer at email:  sstill@aberdeencity.gov.uk or telephone: 01224 069340\n\n## Description\n\nAre you confident using a laptop and familiar with Microsoft programs like PowerPoint?  If so, you could play a vital role in Musical Memories—a joyful singing group for people living with dementia, along with their partners, families, and friends.\r\n\r\nWe’re looking for someone to help run the technical side of our sessions, such as displaying lyrics, playing music tracks, or managing simple presentations. \r\n\r\nLed by a dedicated team of volunteers, these sessions promote wellbeing, spark memories, and encourage connection through music.  Your tech skills could help make the magic happen! \r\n\r\nPreviously held at the Alzheimer Scotland Dementia Resource Centre, this event now takes place every second Friday, 1.30pm-3.00pm at the Cowdray Hall (in/next to Aberdeen Art Gallery), Schoolhill, Aberdeen, AB10 1JQ, supporting larger audiences and growing community engagement.    \r\n\r\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. Volunteers will receive a full induction to Musical Memories sessions, a tour of the venue and a copy of the Aberdeen Archives, Gallery & Museums volunteer handbook. We will also provide training on Being Dementia Friendly.\r\n\r\nA fantastic, enjoyable opportunity to help and make a real difference. All assistance is greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nTo volunteer with us/for further details please contact Sandra Still, Audience Insight Officer anytime at email:  sstill@aberdeencity.gov.uk or telephone: 01224 069340\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training provided to all volunteers.\r\n\r\nVolunteers will receive a full induction to Musical Memories sessions, a tour of the venue and a copy of the Aberdeen Archives, Gallery & Museums volunteer handbook. We will also provide training on Being Dementia Friendly.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nMeets every second Friday and is located at the Cowdray Hall (part of/next to Aberdeen Art Gallery) at 1.30pm - 3.00pm. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMusical Memories sessions take place fortnightly on a Friday from 1.30pm to 3.00pm in Aberdeen Art Gallery (Cowdray Hall), Schoolhill, Aberdeen, AB10 1FQ",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
