            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GmIELYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GmIELYA3/volunteer-gardener",
                    "publishStart": "2026-05-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-03",
                    "title": "Volunteer Gardener",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWhitecrook Community Action Group (WCAG) Garden Scheme is looking for volunteer gardeners to help with grass cutting and weeding in private gardens within the community.\r\nThis is a great opportunity to get outdoors, meet new people, and support local residents while helping us raise funds for our premises and community work.\r\nWhat you’ll do:\r\n•\tGrass cutting and lawn maintenance \r\n•\tWeeding and general+ garden tidying \r\n•\tHelping keep private gardens safe and enjoyable for residents \r\nWhat we’re looking for:\r\n•\tEnthusiastic and reliable volunteers \r\n•\tA willingness to work outdoors \r\n•\tNo formal gardening experience required \r\nTime commitment:\r\nA couple of hours per week, flexible scheduling.\r\nCome and help us make a positive difference in our community while enjoying fresh air and practical teamwork.",
