        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000EYNqAYAX",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000EYNqAYAX/davidson-legacy-cottage",
            "name": "Davidson Legacy Cottage",
            "description": "The organisation's purposes are: \r\n* To purchase in whole, the property known as Netherton Cottage, Aberlemno, By Forfar, Angus, DD9 6SH. To purchase Netherton Cottage Development company Ltd. To purchase The Davidson Legacy Ltd. \r\n* Preserve, secure, and maintain the historical cottage to be available to all members of the public. \r\n* The advancement of education, in non-formal activities. \r\n* The advancement of citizenship or community development, enable and enhance community access to 'Davidson Legacy' long-term for tourism and leisure purposes. \r\n* The advancement of the arts, heritage, culture, or science, preserve 'Heritage' and promote the historical site for generations to come.",
            "website": "https://thedavidsonlegacy.com/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC052174"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/ArtsAndCulture",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Arts and Culture"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Heritage",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Heritage"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HQ2UEYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HQ2UEYA1/heritage-ambassadors",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-23",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-22",
                    "title": "Heritage Ambassadors",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWho We Are & What We Do\r\n\r\nThis rural Angus cottage at Netherton, near Aberlemno, was the home of the Davidson family before they emigrated to America. It was there that their sons would make history by co-founding Harley-Davidson motorcycles in 1903.\r\n\r\nNow a registered Scottish charity (SC052174), this restored 1850s cottage operates as a community-owned living history site. It honours the enduring legacy of Scottish emigrants, who were renowned globally as the practical innovators, educators, and engineers of the modern world. By preserving the home of Sandy Davidson—a wright for a local smiddy before his family emigrated—the site stands as a direct bridge between traditional Angus craftsmanship and global industrial history. Today, this unique link draws motorcycle enthusiasts, Clan Davidson members, and history lovers from every corner of the globe.\n\n## Description\n\nWho We Are & What We Do\r\n\r\nThis rural Angus cottage at Netherton, near Aberlemno, was the home of the Davidson family before they emigrated to America. It was there that their sons would make history by co-founding Harley-Davidson motorcycles in 1903.\r\n\r\nNow a registered Scottish charity (SC052174), this restored 1850s cottage operates as a community-owned living history site. It honours the enduring legacy of Scottish emigrants, who were renowned globally as the practical innovators, educators, and engineers of the modern world. By preserving the home of Sandy Davidson—a wright for a local smiddy before his family emigrated—the site stands as a direct bridge between traditional Angus craftsmanship and global industrial history. Today, this unique link draws motorcycle enthusiasts, Clan Davidson members, and history lovers from every corner of the globe.\r\n\r\nThe Opportunity\r\nWe are seeking Volunteer Heritage Ambassadors of all backgrounds and experience levels to help us develop this unique site into a world-class visitor attraction. You do not need to be a mechanic or a historian; we simply look for individuals who are:\r\n\r\n•\tWelcoming & Reliable: Enjoy engaging with diverse visitors and can commit to regular or flexible hours.\r\n•\tCurious & Proud: Eager to learn the site's history (training provided) and passionate about promoting local Scottish heritage.\r\n\r\nKey Volunteer Roles\r\nAs a Heritage Ambassador, your involvement can be tailored to your skills and interests, including:\r\n•\tVisitor Experience & Storytelling: Greeting international visitors, providing tours, and sharing the history of the Davidson family's journey from Angus to Milwaukee.\r\n•\tSite Preservation & Curation: Maintaining the authenticity of the 1850s cottage, caring for artifacts, and contributing ideas to enhance the visitor experience.\r\n•\tGrounds & Facilities: Assisting with gardening and general site maintenance to keep the cottage and its surroundings pristine.\r\n•\tRetail & Operations: Handling merchandise sales to generate vital funds for the charity.\r\n•\tMarketing & Digital Media: Creating content for social media (Instagram, TikTok, Facebook) to expand our global digital reach.\r\n\r\nWhat We Offer\r\n•\tSkill Development: Gain experience in public speaking, hospitality, and heritage site management.\r\n•\tGlobal Networking: Connect with international visitors and a passionate local team.\r\n•\tFlexibility: Shifts are adaptable around your existing work, family, or study commitments.\r\n•\tCV Enhancement: Gain unique, hands-on experience with a internationally recognized heritage brand.\r\n\r\nNext Steps\r\nInterested in learning more? You are welcome to visit the cottage for an informal tour and a complimentary coffee or tea—no obligations attached.\r\nContact: The DLC Team | Davidson Legacy Cottage SCIO\r\nEmail: Hello@davidsonlegacycottage.com\n\n## Travel details\n\nPublic bus available.\n\n## Taster details\n\nFriendly informal chat with the team",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HQ2UEYA1#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Heritage Ambassadors",
                        "applyLink": "https://davidsonlegacycottage.com/",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/ArtsMusicDramaCrafts",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Arts (Music / Drama / Crafts)"
