            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Pc8NNAAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Pc8NNAAZ/committee-members",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Committee Members",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are seeking new Committee Members. To be a member of the committee and contribute to our recovery from COVID. Your skills will contribute to developments as well as continuation of the current programme. Our preferred means of development is to follow ideas that come from the community. \r\n\r\nThe committee meets monthly on Thursday evenings 6.30pm – 8.30pm at the Community Centre which is in the Bridge of Don Academy Building. Car Parking is good and the No 1 bus has a stop near to the building. \r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help and make a real difference for the community. All assistance is greatly appreciated. For further details please contact Catherine C Mason, Chair at email: katiecmason@btinternet.com  or telephone: 07534995560.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAbility to work with others. Ability to work with IT and social media will be useful but not essential.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant training is provided to all volunteers. We would discuss with the volunteer and provide necessary induction. Aberdeen City Council offers opportunities from time to time.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe committee meets monthly on Thursday evenings 6.30pm ? 8.30pm.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe committee meets monthly on Thursday evenings 6.30pm – 8.30pm at the Centre which is in the Bridge of Don Academy Building. Car Parking is good and the No 1 bus has a stop near to the building.",
