            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000DH8CkAAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000DH8CkAAL/volunteer-drivers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Volunteer Driver(s)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\n*Can you help driving members to our bingo group – all help greatly appreciated*\r\nWoodside Community Centre is looking for people to drive members from their homes in various locations across the city, to the centre to play bingo on a Wednesday, Friday and Sunday evening.  The minibus is parked in the car park at the Woodside Fountain Centre, Marquis Road, Aberdeen.  Good support is provided to all volunteers and all help makes a real difference. \r\n\r\nFor further details, please contact Angela McPherson, Secretary on 07802 838277 or email angelamcpherson355@yahoo.co.uk.\n\n## Description\n\n*Can you help driving members to our bingo group – all help greatly appreciated*\r\nWoodside Community Centre is looking for people to drive members from their homes in various locations across the city, to the centre to play bingo on a Wednesday, Friday and Sunday evening.  The minibus is parked in the car park at the Woodside Fountain Centre, Marquis Road, Aberdeen.  Good support is provided to all volunteers and all help makes a real difference. \r\n\r\nFor further details, please contact Angela McPherson, Secretary on 07802 838277 or email angelamcpherson355@yahoo.co.uk.\n\n## Experience required\n\nDriver - with D1 on driving licence\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support is provided to all volunteers. All help is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe bingo takes place Wednesday, Friday and Sunday evenings (people can either volunteer to drive at one or all of the sessions-all help greatly appreciated).\n\n## Travel details\n\nWoodside Community Centre is based at Marquis Road, Aberdeen.",
