        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400001OzIQbAAN",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400001OzIQbAAN/maryhill-burgh-hall-trust",
            "name": "Maryhill Burgh Hall Trust",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/http://www.maryhillburghhalls.org.uk/",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JkG8TYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JkG8TYAV/tree-planting-day-at-the-maryhill-burgh-halls-november-16th-one-day-commitment",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-16",
                    "title": "Tree Planting Day at the Maryhill Burgh Halls November 16th (One Day Commitment)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nTree Planting Day at the Maryhill Burgh Halls November 16th (One Day Commitment)\n\n## Description\n\nCommunity Tree and Hedge Planting Day\n\nMaryhill Burgh Halls Trust | Monday 16 November 2026\n\nPlant together. Grow a greener Maryhill.\n\nAbout Us\n\nMaryhill Burgh Halls Trust is a community-led charity that brings people together through heritage, culture and local activities. Join us for a planting day and help make our outdoor spaces greener and more welcoming&mdash;with no ongoing volunteering commitment.\n\nWhat Will You Be Doing?\n\nYou&rsquo;ll help plant hedges around the garden areas at Maryhill Burgh Halls, creating a more sheltered place where visitors can relax away from the busy Maryhill Road.\n\nWe&rsquo;ll also be planting around our nursery garden, helping create an outdoor learning space where children can discover nature and learn about growing food.\n\nWho Would This Suit?\n\nAnyone who enjoys being outdoors, meeting people and making a practical difference locally. No gardening experience is needed, just enthusiasm and a willingness to get involved.\n\nPlanting may involve bending, kneeling and handling soil and plants. Please contact us beforehand about any access or support needs so we can discuss how you could take part.\n\nDate, Time and Commitment\n\nDate: Monday 16 November 2026\nTime: 11.00am&ndash;3.00pm\nLocation: Maryhill Burgh Halls, 10&ndash;24 Gairbraid Avenue, Glasgow, G20 8YE\nCommitment: One day only. Stay for the full session or join us for as long as you can.\n\nWhat to Bring\n\nWear sturdy, closed-toe shoes and clothes suitable for the weather that you don&rsquo;t mind getting muddy.\n\nAll tools, equipment and gloves will be provided, with refreshments available throughout the day.\n\nSafety and Insurance\n\nVolunteers are covered by the Trust&rsquo;s insurance while taking part in agreed activities. Guidance on safe planting and tool use will be provided, along with tools, equipment and gloves. Please let us know about any access or support needs before the day.\n\nBenefits and the Difference You&rsquo;ll Make\n\n\n\tFor you: Enjoy time outdoors, meet local people and gain hands-on planting experience.\n\tFor the Trust: Help improve the gardens and create more welcoming outdoor spaces.\n\tFor the community: Create greener places for visitors to enjoy and opportunities for children to learn about nature.\n\n\nHow to Apply\n\nClick the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below, available when you are registered and logged in, to express your interest.\n\nFor questions about the day, contact Lynne at lynne@mbht.org.uk.\n\nWhat Happens After You Apply?\n\nLynne or a member of the team will contact you by email or phone to discuss when you can attend, answer your questions and explain the arrangements for the day. Please mention any access or support needs.\n\nAs the event takes place on Monday 16 November, please contact lynne@mbht.org.uk directly if you haven&rsquo;t received a response before the day. Check your junk or spam folder too.\n\nIf you&rsquo;re unable to reach the organisation, contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous gardening experience is needed. Bring:\n•\tEnthusiasm for helping improve local green spaces.\n•\tWillingness to work alongside others.\n•\tAbility to follow guidance and use tools safely.\nPlanting may involve bending and kneeling. Please discuss any access or support needs with the team beforehand.\n\n\nNo previous gardening experience is needed. Bring:\n\nEnthusiasm for helping improve local green spaces.\n\nWillingness to work alongside others.\n\nAbility to follow guidance and use\n\n## Travel details\n\nMaryhill Burgh Halls, 10–24 Gairbraid Avenue, Glasgow, G20 8YE.\n\nBy bus: From Glasgow city centre, take First Bus 60, 60A or 61 towards Maryhill. Get off near Maryhill Library, opposite the Halls. Service 61 departs from Hope Street.\n\nBy train: Take a train from Glasgow Queen Street to Maryhill station, then walk approximately 20 minutes along Maryhill Road towards the city centre.\n\nEnter through the courtyard archways on Gairbraid Avenue. Check First Bus or ScotRail for current services.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses paid up to the cost of a full-day bus ticket",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JkG8TYAV#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Tree Planting Day at the Maryhill Burgh Halls November 16th (One Day Commitment)",
                        "description": "No previous gardening experience is needed. Bring:\n•\tEnthusiasm for helping improve local green spaces.\n•\tWillingness to work alongside others.\n•\tAbility to follow guidance and use tools safely.\nPlanting may involve bending and kneeling. Please discuss any access or support needs with the team beforehand.\n\n\nNo previous gardening experience is needed. Bring:\n\nEnthusiasm for helping improve local green spaces.\n\nWillingness to work alongside others.\n\nAbility to follow guidance and use",
