                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000J8z3NYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000J8z3NYAR/community-outreach-for-maryhill-burgh-halls-trust",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-29",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-28",
                    "title": "Community Outreach for Maryhill Burgh Halls Trust",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCommunity Outreach for Maryhill Burgh Halls Trust\n\n## Description\n\nMaryhill Burgh Halls Trust\n\nHelp your neighbours discover what&rsquo;s on their doorstep.\n\nAbout Maryhill Burgh Halls Trust\n\nMaryhill Burgh Halls Trust is a community-led charity that brings people together through heritage, culture and local activities. Through Maryhill Burgh Halls and the Whitehouse Maryhill, we create welcoming spaces where people can meet, share stories, learn and get involved in community life.\n\nWhy Volunteer With Us?\n\nDiscover Maryhill while helping others discover it too. This role combines getting out and about, meeting neighbours and sharing opportunities connected to two historic community venues. A friendly conversation could help someone find a welcoming activity, a useful service or a new connection.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nAs a Community Outreach Volunteer, you&rsquo;ll help spread the word about events, activities and services at Maryhill Burgh Halls and the Whitehouse Maryhill.\n\nYou&rsquo;ll distribute flyers and chat with people around North Glasgow about opportunities such as the People&rsquo;s Kitchen, museum exhibitions, classes and public meetings. Along the way, you&rsquo;ll learn more about your neighbourhood and help local people feel informed, welcome and connected.\n\nWhat You Could Be Doing\n\n\n\tSharing flyers and information with local residents, organisations and community venues.\n\tHaving friendly conversations about upcoming activities and ways to get involved.\n\tHelping people discover services and events they might otherwise miss.\n\tPassing on community feedback, questions and ideas to the team.\n\tIdentifying local groups and organisations that may be interested in working with us.\n\n\nWho Would This Role Suit?\n\nThis role would suit someone who enjoys meeting people, exploring their local area and sharing useful information. You might want to build your confidence, gain experience in community engagement or contribute a few hours to your neighbourhood.\n\nYou don&rsquo;t need to be an expert on Maryhill or have previous outreach experience. A friendly approach, willingness to listen and an interest in the community are a good starting point. You should feel comfortable approaching people respectfully, recognising that some may prefer not to chat.\n\nThe role involves getting out and about around North Glasgow. Please speak with us about any access or support needs so we can discuss what would work for you.\n\nWhat You Could Gain\n\n\n\tBuild confidence and develop your communication skills.\n\tGain practical experience in community outreach and event promotion.\n\tMeet local residents and organisations.\n\tDiscover community spaces and learn more about Maryhill.\n\tMake a positive contribution through a flexible volunteering role.\n\n\nThe Difference You&rsquo;ll Make\n\nYour support will help Maryhill Burgh Halls Trust reach more people, hear community views and develop local partnerships.\n\nBy spreading the word, you&rsquo;ll help residents discover activities and services that support wellbeing, reduce isolation and offer opportunities to connect with neighbours and take part in community life.\n\nTime and Commitment\n\nAround 2&ndash;4 hours per week, with flexibility to agree times that suit you and the activities being promoted. You can discuss your availability with the Volunteer Lead.\n\nLocation\n\nOut and about in Maryhill and the wider North Glasgow area, promoting activities at Maryhill Burgh Halls and the Whitehouse Maryhill. Routes and areas will be coordinated with the team.\n\nSupport and Supervision\n\n\n\tRegular check-ins: A short chat with the Volunteer Lead after each shift to share how things went, ask questions and pass on feedback.\n\tKeeping connected: An online group chat to coordinate routes, share updates and stay in touch with other volunteers while out and about.\n\tExpenses: Travel expenses reimbursed up to the cost of a full-day bus ticket, along with lunch expenses while volunteering. Please check the arrangements with the Volunteer Lead beforehand.\n\tReferences: A reference reflecting your volunteering contribution can be provided to support future applications.\n\n\nHow to Apply\n\nIf you&rsquo;re interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below, available when you are registered and logged in.\n\nAfter You Hit &ldquo;Apply&rdquo;\n\nThe coordinator will contact you by email or phone for an informal chat about the role, your interests and availability, and any support you might need. This is also your chance to ask questions and decide whether the opportunity feels right for you. If you both agree to go ahead, the coordinator will explain the next steps and arrangements for getting started.\n\nIf you haven&rsquo;t heard back within 5 working days, please:\n\n\n\t\n\tCheck your junk or spam folder in case the response has landed there.\n\t\n\t\n\tContact Maryhill Burgh Halls Trust using the contact details provided.\n\t\n\t\n\tIf you&rsquo;re still unable to get a response, contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org for help.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous outreach experience is needed. We’re looking for:\n•\tA friendly, approachable manner and willingness to chat with people.\n•\tGood listening skills and respect for different backgrounds and views.\n•\tAn interest in Maryhill and its local community.\n•\tReliability and the ability to keep in touch with the Volunteer Lead.\n•\tWillingness to share information clearly and pass on questions or feedback.\n•\tBasic confidence using a phone and online group chat to coordinate with the team.\nTh\n\n## Travel details\n\nMaryhill Burgh Halls is at 10–24 Gairbraid Avenue, Glasgow, G20 8YE.\n\nBy bus: Take First Bus 61 towards Summerston from Hope Street in Glasgow city centre. Get off near Maryhill Library, opposite the Halls.\n\nBy train: Travel from Glasgow Queen Street to Maryhill station, then walk approximately 15–20 minutes along Maryhill Road towards the city centre to reach the Halls.\n\nThe entrance is through the courtyard archways on Gairbraid Avenue.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses reimbursed up to the cost of a full day bus ticket (£6.60)\nLunch expenses reimbursed up to £5",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
