                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HyTJtYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HyTJtYAN/litter-picking-at-maryhill-locks",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-05",
                    "title": "Litter Picking at Maryhill Locks",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nLitter Picking at Maryhill Locks\n\n## Description\n\nHelp Us With &#39;Keeping the Nolly Swanky&#39;&nbsp;\n\nScotland&#39;s canal network hosts over 22,000 visitors a year, with nearly 30,000 Glaswegians living on its banks. Every year the rates of littering and flytipping on waterways increases, up 67% in the last four years, resulting in significant impact to quality of life, access to safe and clean waterways and green spaces, and the wellbeing of Glasgow wildlife.&nbsp;\n\nHelp us address this problem with monthly litterpicks with &#39;Keeping the Nolly Swanky&#39; in collaboration with the Maryhill Burgh Halls Trust. Litterpicking events will occur every 1st Saturday of the month starting at 11:30am at the Whitehouse, near Lock 21. Litterpicking equipment and safety tools will be provided - just bring yourself and an enthusiasm for environmental change.\n\nUpcoming Dates:&nbsp;September 5, October 3, November 7, December 5\n\nIf you are interested in getting more involved, we are recruiting for&nbsp;co-leaders&nbsp;to help with overseeing volunteers, contributing to impact reporting, and planning routes. If you are interested, please contact volunteers@mbht.org.uk\n\nWhy Volunteer With Us?\n\nBenefits to Volunteers\n\n\n\tGet active and outdoors while providing for your community\n\tMeet likeminded neighbours and chat over a tea or coffee\n\tSee the impact of your work\n\tMake a real difference promoting the safety and health of Maryhill&#39;s waterways\n\n\nEnvironmental Benefits\n\n\n\tPromote Safety for Neighbours and Wildlife\n\tPrevent Pollution of Waterways\n\tImprove the Quality of Plant Life\n\tReduce Emissions\n\n\nCommunity Benefits\n\n\n\tEncourage Public Use of Maryhill Waterways\n\tPromote Community Spirit and Pride\n\tPromote Wellbeing\n\n\nAll are welcome!&nbsp;\n\nIf you are interested,&nbsp;please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when&nbsp;registered and&nbsp;logged in). You&nbsp;will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that&nbsp;doesn&rsquo;t&nbsp;work&nbsp;out,&nbsp;then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nLitterpicking is an active activity and may require traversing uneven terrain, bending, and lifting low weights. If you are interested in getting involved but are worried about participation due to injury or disability, please get in contact about ways you can get involved.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMultiple buses to Maryhill from surrounding areas. Maryhill train station is nearby",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
