                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HnyinYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HnyinYAB/community-outreach-volunteer-south-ayrshire",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-20",
                    "title": "Community Outreach Volunteer - South Ayrshire",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe are building a brand-new South Ayrshire team to bring the talking newspaper to blind, visually impaired and print-impaired people - and those with mobility issues - right across South Ayrshire. Each weekly edition must be recorded, edited and posted via freepost on the same day the local newspaper is released (e.g. every Wednesday), so our listeners get their news at the same time as everyone else.\r\nPurpose of the role\r\nOutreach works — our listener base doubled after volunteers visited local groups in person. This role builds relationships with sight loss groups, care providers, opticians, libraries and health services across South Ayrshire, signing up new listeners — including people with mobility issues who find it hard to get out — and spreading the word.\r\nWhat you'll do\r\n•\tVisit and present to community groups, sight loss clubs, care homes and day centres.\r\n•\tBuild relationships with opticians, GP surgeries, libraries and the sensory impairment team.   Sign up new listeners and help them get started with their weekly editions.\r\n•\tRepresent ARSB at South Ayrshire community events, galas and information days.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat We Offer Our Volunteers\r\n• A warm welcome and a full induction to the charity and your role.\r\n• Training and ongoing support \r\n\r\nHow to Apply\r\n\r\nApplying couldn't be simpler — there's no formal application form. Just get in touch and tell us a little about yourself, which area you're in (East, South or North Ayrshire), and which role (or roles) interest you. We'll invite you along for an informal chat, with no obligation on either side.\r\n\r\n\r\nAyrshire Recording Services I Scottish Charity No. SC054087\r\n\r\nThe Talking Newspaper for Ayrshire —free to every listener, every week, since 1983.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWhat we're looking for\r\n•\tA friendly, approachable manner and confidence speaking to groups.\r\n•\tEmpathy and patience, particularly with older or newly sight-impaired people.\r\n•\t A positive attitude and a genuinely good time meeting people.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F935fae5d-fc56-44a4-9111-52c151f1a0a0%2FPNprC3wmrFhb2vt6Q70SsC0gjh22%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=380c39bb-f677-4608-9cdf-510fa3bac943",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HnyinYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Community Outreach Volunteer - South Ayrshire",
                        "description": "What we're looking for\r\n•\tA friendly, approachable manner and confidence speaking to groups.\r\n•\tEmpathy and patience, particularly with older or newly sight-impaired people.\r\n•\t A positive attitude and a genuinely good time meeting people.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HnyinYAB/community-outreach-volunteer-south-ayrshire?#modal_register_a0gQD00000HnyinYAB",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "18",
