        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400001MXOYSAA5",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400001MXOYSAA5/sistema-scotland",
            "name": "Sistema Scotland",
            "description": "Sistema Scotland’s mission is to create permanent social change in some of the most deprived communities in Scotland.  We use participation in our Big Noise orchestra programmes to change lives by fostering confidence, discipline, teamwork, pride and aspiration in the children and young people.",
            "website": "https://www.makeabignoise.org.uk",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/FamilySupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Family Support"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000CL3vpAAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000CL3vpAAD/big-noise-after-school-club-helper",
                    "publishStart": "2023-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Big Noise After School Club Helper",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAfter School Club is at the heart of Big Noise.  Our team of volunteers helps us create a fun, safe and happy environment where children can learn to be part of the Big Noise Orchestra.\n\n## Description\n\nOur After School Club is currently open to children who go to school in Douglas (Dundee).   We need positive and enthusiastic people to help us make it happen. \r\n\r\n Volunteers’ main tasks are:\r\n\r\n•\tBefriend the children  - the strength of relationships we build with the children is key to our  success.  We need committed people who love being around children, cope well under pressure and who have a good sense of fun.\r\n•\tSupport the musicians in sessions – volunteers make a huge difference by encouraging children to concentrate and join in.  You will be a strong role model to support them to learn..\r\n•\tHelp with set up and tidying away – getting the right instruments and the right chairs in the right place…\r\n•\tSupervise children on the walk from their school to the club – chat with children and ensure they arrive safely.  Be with them during snack time, hearing about their day.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThe desire to be involved in a programme which is positive, ambitious and worthwhile.\r\nGood disposition, heaps of energy, interest in learning something new\r\nPassion and belief in the potential of children to amaze us and to achieve incredible things\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction includes: Child Protection, Positive Behaviour, Manual Handling, Health and Safety, Confidentiality\r\nOngoing training:  as available, including training days with the Big Noise team\r\nSupport:  Volunteers have a named person and regular support opportunities.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nVolunteers should be able to commit to a minimum of 2 hours per week (2.45 ? 4.45pm), and we ask you to plan to commit for at least a year if possible, because of the importance of building relationships with the young people.\n\n## Travel details\n\nClaypotts Castle Primary School is in Douglas, in the east of Dundee.   Reasonable out of pocket expenses for travel will  be reimbursed if in accordance with our policy.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nBy agreement, at public transport rate.   An expenses form must be properly completed before expenses can be reimbursed.  Public transport costs reimbursed on production of tickets purchased.   Mileage rate is 40p per mile.\n\n## Taster details\n\nPotential volunteers are invited to attend the After School Club.  They will be buddied with a senior volunteer or member of staff and will observe delivery and, where appropriate, participate.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000CL3vpAAD#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Big Noise After School Club Helper",
                        "description": "The desire to be involved in a programme which is positive, ambitious and worthwhile.\r\nGood disposition, heaps of energy, interest in learning something new\r\nPassion and belief in the potential of children to amaze us and to achieve incredible things",
                        "commitment": "Volunteers should be able to commit to a minimum of 2 hours per week (2.45 ? 4.45pm), and we ask you to plan to commit for at least a year if possible, because of the importance of building relationships with the young people.",
