                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-16",
                    "title": "Remote Shopping List Collectors",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHelp Food Train members get the shopping they need by collecting their weekly shopping lists over the phone. \r\nYou’ll enjoy friendly conversations with members while accurately recording their orders and helping our shopping service run smoothly.\n\n## Description\n\nAs a Remote Shopping List Collector, you will play an important part in Food Train’s weekly shopping service, helping older people across the Scottish Borders who are no longer able to shop independently.\r\n\r\nEach week, you will contact a list of Food Train members by telephone to collect their grocery shopping list. You’ll have a friendly conversation with each member, take the time to understand what they need, and accurately record their shopping requirements using our simple shopping list template. You may also need to clarify quantities, pack sizes or suitable substitutions to make sure our shoppers have all the information they need.\r\n\r\nThe role is carried out from your own home, so you’ll need access to a telephone and a computer or laptop. Shopping lists are generally collected on Mondays between 10am and 2pm, with lists completed and returned to the branch by 2pm.\r\n\r\nWhat you’ll be doing:\r\n- Calling Food Train members at an agreed time each Monday.\r\n- Having friendly, regular conversations with members while collecting their shopping list.\r\n- Recording shopping requests accurately using our provided template.\r\n- Checking quantities, pack sizes and any notes about preferred or acceptable substitutions.\r\n- Making sure lists are clear and complete before sending them to the Food Train team.\r\n- Letting the team know about any concerns or important information shared by a member.\r\n- Building positive relationships with members through regular contact and friendly conversation.\r\n- Working as part of the wider Food Train team to make sure members receive the shopping they need.\r\n\r\nWhat can volunteers expect?\r\nYou will receive full training and support before starting the role. Initially, you’ll be supported by the Food Train team as you become familiar with the process and will have someone available to answer questions whenever you need help.\r\nThis is a great opportunity for someone who enjoys talking to people, being organised and making a practical difference in their local community. You don’t need previous experience of working for a charity or in a similar role – we’re looking for reliable, friendly volunteers who are confident speaking on the phone and comfortable using basic computer skills.\r\n\r\nThe role offers the opportunity to develop meaningful relationships with Food Train members, many of whom really value having a familiar person to speak to each week. Although the role is carried out remotely, you will be an important part of the local Food Train team and your contribution directly helps us provide our shopping service.\r\n\r\nTime commitment\r\nWe ask volunteers to commit to a regular weekly Monday shift, normally between 10am and 2pm. The exact amount of time required will depend on the number of members you are calling. We appreciate that volunteers have other commitments, so we can discuss availability and agree a regular arrangement that works for you.\r\n\r\nPVG membership is required for this role, and Food Train will arrange and cover the cost.\r\n\r\nOnce we receive your application, a member of the Food Train team will review it and contact you within a few days to arrange an informal conversation. This gives us an opportunity to tell you more about the role, answer any questions you may have and find out a little more about you and your availability.\r\nIf you would like to go ahead, we’ll arrange your PVG check and your initial training. Food Train covers the cost of the PVG.\r\nOnce the necessary checks are complete, we’ll arrange your training and support you through your first calls. \r\nWe aim to make the process as straightforward as possible and, where PVG checks are returned promptly, you can usually expect to start volunteering within a few weeks of applying. We’ll keep you updated throughout the process so you always know what happens next.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous volunteering or charity experience is required – this role is open to beginners. Full training and ongoing support will be provided.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for someone who:\r\n- Is friendly, approachable and confident speaking to people on the phone.\r\n- Has good listening and communication skills and can have friendly conversations with older people.\r\n- Is patient, understanding and respectful of members’ individual needs.\r\n- Is organised and reliable, with good attention to detail.\r\n- Can accurately record information and follow simple processes.\r\n- Has basic computer skills and is comfortable using email and a Word shopping list template.\r\n- Can commit to a regular weekly Monday shift, normally between 10am and 2pm.\r\n- Understands the importance of confidentiality and protecting members’ personal information.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training will be provided before you begin volunteering, so no previous experience in this type of role is required. You will be shown how to contact members, collect and record shopping lists accurately, use the \r\nshopping list template, and follow Food Train’s procedures around confidentiality and member information.\r\n\r\nYour first calls will be supported by the Food Train team, giving you the opportunity to build confidence and ask questions as you learn. You will also have ongoing support from the branch team, who will be available to answer questions, provide guidance and help with anything you are unsure about.\r\nWe want our volunteers to feel confident, valued and supported in their role, so regular communication \r\nwith the team is encouraged.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nStaff are available anytime via telephone, email or whatsapp for questions and support.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses are reimbursed. A claim form must be completed and returned to the office staff. \r\nExpenses are paid directly into your bank account.\n\n## Taster details\n\nA video and handbook detailing the process will be provided, along with full training and support.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000I1ZMLYA3#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Remote Shopping List Collectors",
                        "description": "No previous volunteering or charity experience is required – this role is open to beginners. Full training and ongoing support will be provided.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for someone who:\r\n- Is friendly, approachable and confident speaking to people on the phone.\r\n- Has good listening and communication skills and can have friendly conversations with older people.\r\n- Is patient, understanding and respectful of members’ individual needs.\r\n- Is organised and reliable, with good attention to detail.\r\n- Can accurately record information and follow simple processes.\r\n- Has basic computer skills and is comfortable using email and a Word shopping list template.\r\n- Can commit to a regular weekly Monday shift, normally between 10am and 2pm.\r\n- Understands the importance of confidentiality and protecting members’ personal information.",
