        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400001MjPfkAAF",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400001MjPfkAAF/starter-packs-glasgow",
            "name": "Starter Packs Glasgow",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/StarterPacksGlasgow",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JuRXMYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JuRXMYA3/volunteering-at-magpies-eye-on-saturdays",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-13",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-13",
                    "title": "Volunteering at Magpie's Eye on Saturdays",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteering at Magpie's Eye on Saturdays\n\n## Description\n\nStock Assistant Volunteer &ndash; The Magpie&rsquo;s Eye Gallery (Saturdays)\n\nDiscover vintage treasures, share your interests, and help people across Glasgow make a fresh start.\n\nThis volunteer role is based on Saturdays, with the option to volunteer on other days too.\n\nTry a taster session first: Our one-hour taster session gives you an opportunity to see what the role and duties are like before deciding whether it suits you. Please note that the taster session takes place during the week, even though the main volunteering day is Saturday.\n\nAbout The Magpie&rsquo;s Eye Gallery\n\nThe Magpie&rsquo;s Eye Gallery is one of Starter Packs Glasgow&rsquo;s two charity shops and plays a vital role in helping the charity remain financially self-sustaining. The shop also supports our commitment to promoting re-use, reducing waste, and keeping quality items out of landfill.\n\nSpecialising in vintage treasures and high-quality high street brands, The Magpie&rsquo;s Eye Gallery offers an eclectic range of items including furniture, clothing, books, music, films, bric-a-brac, and a variety of collectible and higher-value pieces.\n\nBy helping prepare these donations for sale, you&rsquo;ll support Starter Packs Glasgow&rsquo;s work providing essential household items to people starting over in a new home.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nAs a Stock Assistant Volunteer, you&rsquo;ll be involved in a wide range of tasks that help keep the shop running smoothly and ensure donated items are presented at their very best. Tasks may include:\n\n\n\tSorting and processing donations as they arrive in the shop.\n\tCleaning and preparing items for sale.\n\tChecking the condition of CDs, DVDs, Blu-rays, vinyl records, and other media.\n\tAssessing items to ensure they meet the quality standards for sale.\n\tReplenishing and organising stock on the shop floor.\n\tSteaming clothing to ensure it is clean and presentable.\n\tPricing and tagging clothing, including adding the correct size markers to hangers.\n\tInspecting furniture to ensure it is clean, safe, and ready for sale.\n\n\nA Role Tailored to Your Interests\n\nWe recognise that our volunteers give their time generously, and we want that time to be enjoyable and rewarding. Wherever possible, we match volunteers with areas that reflect their interests and passions.\n\n\n\tLove books? You could help organise and replenish our book section.\n\tPassionate about music? You might enjoy organising our CD and vinyl collections.\n\tInterested in fashion and styling? Our clothing department could be the perfect fit.\n\n\nTraining and Support\n\nYou&rsquo;ll receive training in the tasks you take on, helping you build confidence and develop practical retail skills. Our shop team will explain how to carry out tasks safely, answer your questions, and provide guidance while you volunteer.\n\nYour one-hour weekday taster session will give you an opportunity to meet the team, try out tasks, and discuss any support you may need. Wherever possible, we&rsquo;ll match activities to your interests and abilities so you feel comfortable and supported in your role.\n\nWhen and Where\n\nLocation: The Magpie&rsquo;s Eye Gallery, 47 Burleigh Street, Govan, Glasgow, G51 3LB.\n\nMain volunteering day: Saturday. The shop is open 9.30am&ndash;5.00pm, with your volunteering hours agreed with the team.\n\nThere is also the option to volunteer on other days. Your initial one-hour taster session will take place during the week.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nClick the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below, available once you are registered and logged in, to express your interest in this opportunity. Applying is the first step towards finding out whether the role is right for you; it does not commit you to volunteering.\n\nWhat Happens After You Apply?\n\nA member of the Starter Packs Glasgow team will contact you by email to discuss your interest, availability, and arranging a weekday taster session. This is also an opportunity to ask questions and discuss any support you may need before deciding whether to continue.\n\nIf you haven&rsquo;t received a response within five working days, please:\n\n\n\t\n\tCheck your junk or spam folder.\n\t\n\t\n\tContact the organisation directly using the contact details provided.\n\t\n\t\n\tIf you still need assistance, contact Volunteer Glasgow on 0141 226 3431.\n\t\n\n\nWe look forward to welcoming you to our team and helping you make a real difference in your community.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou will be trained in store in order to do the tasks involved that you wish to take part in.\n\n## Travel details\n\nGovan subway station and bus station are minutes away from this opportunity\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nIf you work three hours or more we will cover your travel costs",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
