                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HrpAfYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HrpAfYAJ/administration-volunteer-help-people-make-a-fresh-start-at-starter-packs-govan",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-03",
                    "title": "Administration Volunteer – Help People Make a Fresh Start at Starter Packs Govan",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAdministration Volunteer – Help People Make a Fresh Start at Starter Packs Govan\n\n## Description\n\nUse your administration skills to help people make a fresh start in a place they can call home.\n\nThis is more than an office-based volunteering role. As part of our friendly team, you&#39;ll play a vital role behind the scenes, ensuring Starter Packs Glasgow can continue providing essential household items to people making a fresh start. Flexible hours, ongoing support from a Volunteer Coordinator, and the opportunity to make a real difference every day make this a rewarding way to volunteer.\n\nAbout Starter Packs Glasgow\n\nEvery day, Starter Packs Glasgow helps people across the city take the first steps towards rebuilding their lives. We support individuals and families moving into a new home after experiencing homelessness, leaving care, prison or the armed forces, recovering from a relationship breakdown, escaping domestic abuse, or being rehomed following a fire or flood.\n\nBy providing essential household items, we help people create a safe, comfortable home while reducing the financial pressure and anxiety that often comes with starting over. Every volunteer plays an important part in making this possible.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nWe&#39;re looking for a friendly, organised and reliable Administration Volunteer to join our busy office team.\n\nThis role is ideal for someone with previous administration experience who enjoys working with people, has good organisational skills and would like to use their abilities to support a local charity making a real difference across Glasgow.\n\nAs part of our office team, you&#39;ll help ensure enquiries are responded to efficiently and that the day-to-day administration of the charity runs smoothly.\n\nWhat You&#39;ll Be Doing\n\nAs an Administration Volunteer, you may:\n\n\n\tRespond to telephone calls and email enquiries in a professional and timely manner.\n\tWelcome and assist members of the public contacting or visiting the office.\n\tSupport the Administrator with a variety of administrative tasks.\n\tMaintain accurate records and help keep office systems organised.\n\tAssist with filing, data entry and general office administration.\n\tWork alongside staff to help ensure the office operates efficiently.\n\n\nSupport You&#39;ll Receive\n\nWe want every volunteer to feel welcomed, confident and valued throughout their volunteering journey. You&#39;ll receive:\n\n\n\tA full induction to Starter Packs Glasgow and your volunteer role.\n\tOngoing guidance, encouragement and regular support from our Volunteer Coordinator.\n\tA named point of contact who will be available to answer questions and provide advice whenever needed.\n\tRegular check-ins and feedback to help you develop your confidence and skills.\n\tA friendly, supportive team environment where your contribution is appreciated.\n\n\nTime Commitment\n\nOur office is open Monday to Friday, 9:00am&ndash;5:00pm.\n\nWe offer flexible volunteering across these hours and appreciate any time you can give. Whether you&#39;re available for a few hours each week or can volunteer more regularly, we&#39;d love to hear from you.\n\nEvery hour you volunteer helps Starter Packs Glasgow provide practical support to people making a fresh start in their new home.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on 0141 226 3431.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nWhat Happens Next?\n\nIf you&#39;re interested in becoming an Administration Volunteer, simply click the Apply button below (available when you&#39;re logged in and registered with Volunteer Glasgow).\n\nOnce we&#39;ve received your application, our Volunteer Coordinator will contact you by email or telephone to discuss the role, answer any questions you may have, and explain the next steps. If the role feels like a good fit for both you and Starter Packs Glasgow, you&#39;ll be invited to complete the induction process before starting your volunteering.\n\n## Experience required\n\nIdeally, you'll have:\n•\tSome administration experience.\n•\tA high level of proficiency in spoken and written English.\n•\tGood organisational skills and attention to detail.\n•\tConfidence using email, Microsoft Office and other basic computer systems.\n•\tExcellent communication and interpersonal skills.\n•\tThe ability to work independently as well as part of a team.\n•\tA positive attitude, reliability and willingness to learn.\n\n## Travel details\n\nWe are a few minutes away from Govan Subway and Bus station\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nIf you volunteer more than three hours we can pay for your public transport ticket",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HrpAfYAJ#role",
