                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009eOXUYA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009eOXUYA2/stock-assistant-in-magpies-eye-gallery-charity-shop",
                    "publishStart": "2025-04-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-22",
                    "title": "Stock Assistant in Magpie's Eye Gallery charity shop",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nStock Assistant in Magpie's Eye Gallery charity shop\n\n## Description\n\n<p><span style=\"color:black\">&quot;Compassion,</span>dignity<span style=\"color:black\">,support, help rebuild lives.&quot;&nbsp;</span><br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:black\">The Magpie&#39;s Eye Gallery is one of Starter Packs Glasgow&#39;s two charity shops and plays a crucial role in helping the charity remain self-sustaining. It also supports our efforts to promote re-use and reduce landfill waste. Specializing in vintage and high-end high street items, the shop offers a wide range of products, including furniture, bric-a-brac, clothing, books, music, and film, as well as various collectible and higher-value items.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:black\">Being a stock assistant has a variety of different tasks that are incredibly helpful to the charity. </span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><span style=\"color:black\">Helping to sort the donations that come through to the shop, washing or cleaning items before they can go out for sale. </span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"color:black\">Checking the condition of CDs, DVDs, Blue Rays and Records.</span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"color:black\">Making sure items are in good enough condition to go out in the shop. </span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"color:black\">Helping re-stock the shop floor. </span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"color:black\">Steaming the clothing donations to make sure they are clean and presentable for sale and price-tagging them and having the right size cube on the hanger ready for the shop floor. </span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"color:black\">Checking our furniture items are clean, in good condition and ready for sale is another task that is very helpful to the shop.</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><br />\nWe appreciate our volunteers time is precious to them, and we like to make sure that they get to be working in parts of the organisation that has an interest for them, so people who love books are placed in our book room, and music fans will get to look after the CD and vinyl racks, fans of fashion who have an eye for the aesthetic in clothing can be working with the clothes section. It is entirely up to you how much time you have to volunteer with us in this role. We can be very flexible with how often you come in and for how long you wish to be here for each volunteer session. The shop is open Monday to Saturday 9:30-5:00pm and we are happy for you to come in at times that suit you.<br />\n<br />\nIf you are interested please click the &lsquo;apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on 0141 226 3431.</p>\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou will be trained in store in order to do the tasks involved that you wish to take part in.\n\n## Travel details\n\nGovan Station and Underground are nearby, as are many bus connections from surrounding area\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel Expenses can be covered if you are here for a minimum of three hours per session.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
