        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400001MjPh3AAF",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400001MjPh3AAF/quarriers-volunteer-centre",
            "name": "Quarriers Volunteer Centre",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/QuarriersVolunteerCentre",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC001960"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HJffBYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HJffBYAT/handyperson",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-13",
                    "title": "Handyperson",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHandyperson\n\n## Description\n\nQuarriers is one of Scotland&rsquo;s leading social care charities, supporting children, young people, adults and families to overcome challenges and build brighter futures. Through a wide range of community-based services, Quarriers works alongside people to improve wellbeing, promote independence and reduce social isolation. Their volunteering programmes help create safe, supportive and inclusive spaces where individuals can build confidence, develop life skills and feel connected within their communities.\n\nJoin our amazing team and make a real difference in our community! We&#39;re looking for enthusiastic volunteers to help us spruce up our shared spaces and create more welcoming environments for everyone. If you enjoy hands-on work and want to contribute to a positive change, this is the perfect opportunity for you.\n\n\n\tAssisting with essential garden tidy-ups, from weeding to planting.\n\tAssembling flat pack furniture to furnish new community areas.\n\tApplying fresh coats of painting to brighten up our facilities.\n\tSkillfully putting up curtains, blinds, pictures to add the finishing touches.\n\tHelping with wallpapering to give spaces a vibrant new look.\n\n\nReady to roll up your sleeves and contribute your skills? Sign up today and be a part of something truly rewarding!\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). The coordinator will then contact you by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder for your emails, just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow at&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org\n\n## Experience required\n\n• A kind and caring nature\n• Patience\n• Positive attitude and outlook\n• Reliable and supportive approach\n• Inclusive and non-judgemental attitude\n*  DIY skills\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAgreed expenses only",
