                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g2400000ApfH5AAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g2400000ApfH5AAJ/donation-centre-shop-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2017-09-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Donation Centre Shop Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nWe are looking for someone interested in customer service to help maintain our shop floor and till area.\n\n## Description\n\nThe Salvation Army is opening a brand new Donation Centre which we hope will become a re-use hub for the local area and beyond.  Reducing how much we all send to landfill is so very important and we will offer people a convenient hub to donate items that still have re-use potential.  As well as collecting donations we will have a small charity shop. We are looking for someone who loves to engage with people and has an eye for detail to help maintain our shop and till areas and serve customers.\n\n## Experience required\n\nThis role would suit an outgoing individual keen on developing their skills within the customer service industry.  Literacy and numeracy are important for the role but formal qualifications are not required. All training will be given in house, with the ability to gain much responsibility over the shop floor.\n\n## Training details\n\nAll training and induction is conducted in house. Training is not currently certified\n\n## Travel details\n\nSalvation Army Donation Centre, 40 Piershill Place, Edinburgh, EH8 7EH\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses paid.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g2400000ApfH5AAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Donation Centre Shop Assistant",
                        "description": "This role would suit an outgoing individual keen on developing their skills within the customer service industry.  Literacy and numeracy are important for the role but formal qualifications are not required. All training will be given in house, with the ability to gain much responsibility over the shop floor.",
