        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400001CO6NlAAL",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400001CO6NlAAL/gig-buddies-with-thera-trust",
            "name": "Gig Buddies with Thera Trust",
            "description": "Gig Buddies is a project that supports people with a learning disability to get out to more gigs and live events by pairing them with a volunteer who shares the same interests as them. Our ‘Gig Buddies’ then go to what events they want, when they want, and enjoy their shared passion together. In addition to this, we also host regular social events where members can meet for a drink and chat while enjoying great live entertainment. Gig Buddies is an exciting, fast growing project with an ultimate goal to help bring an end to social isolation.",
            "website": "https://www.thera.co.uk/about/projects/gig-buddies/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/LearningDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Learning Disability"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SocialCare",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Social Care"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000009GL5VAAW",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000009GL5VAAW/gig-buddies-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2018-01-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Gig Buddies Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nGig Buddies enables people with a learning disability to get out to the events they love by pairing them with a volunteer who shares the same interests.\n\n## Description\n\nWant to get out to more gigs?\r\nGig Buddies with Thera Trust pairs volunteers to adults with a learning disability based on the gigs you both love going to!\r\nThis can be music, theatre, sport, or just going for coffee. It’s whatever your ‘gig’ is! Gig Buddies pairs get out together once a month to get to know each other and enjoy their shared passion together. You’ll also communicate regularly and plan your events together. The role requires roughly 4-6 hours per month, having a chat and getting out!\r\n \r\n\r\nVolunteer expenses are paid and we have relationships with a number of venues/event organisers that offer loads of great opportunities to our pairings, including DF Concerts, King Tuts, The Edinburgh Fringe and International Festivals, The RSNO, National Theatre Scotland, Sneaky Pete’s and more!\n\n## Experience required\n\nAt Gig Buddies, we don’t require our volunteers to have any previous experience in a supporting role. However, if you are thinking of applying to become a Gig Buddy, we do ask that you are:\r\n• Able to meet with your buddy roughly once or twice a month.\r\n• Able to commit to a day of training.\r\n• Friendly and kind, with a good sense of humour.\r\n• Willing to get to know someone and develop a friendship with them.\r\n• Proactive and reliable.\r\n• Around for at least a year.\n\n## Training details\n\nIn addition to a compulsory introductory training session, all volunteers will receive training relevant to the person they will be paired with. Volunteers will meet with the project coordinator every 3-4 months for  supervision meetings.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nWould require a commitment of 4/7 hours per month.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nEach volunteer has an annual expense budget of £120.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000009GL5VAAW#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Gig Buddies Volunteer",
                        "description": "At Gig Buddies, we don’t require our volunteers to have any previous experience in a supporting role. However, if you are thinking of applying to become a Gig Buddy, we do ask that you are:\r\n• Able to meet with your buddy roughly once or twice a month.\r\n• Able to commit to a day of training.\r\n• Friendly and kind, with a good sense of humour.\r\n• Willing to get to know someone and develop a friendship with them.\r\n• Proactive and reliable.\r\n• Around for at least a year.",
