        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400001GIGxNAAX",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400001GIGxNAAX/sue-ryder-aberdeen-george-street-store",
            "name": "Sue Ryder (Aberdeen George Street Store)",
            "description": "Sue Ryder Charity Shops raise millions of pounds each year to enable our charity to deliver hospice and neurological care for more conditions than any other UK charity.",
            "website": "https://www.suerydercare.org",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CharityShop",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Charity Shop"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Health",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kiK6AAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kiK6AAI/charity-shop-assistant",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-15",
                    "title": "Charity Shop Assistant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you have any spare time throughout the week? And would you like to use it to gain experience, develop skills and meet new people while supporting a wonderful charity? Then we have the role for you!!!\r\n\r\nSue Ryder Charity Shops raise millions of pounds each year to enable our charity to deliver hospice and neurological care for more conditions than any other UK charity. As a volunteer in our shop, not only would you be meeting new friends, gaining skills and experience, but you'd also be directly supporting us to care for people when they really need it. \r\n\r\nOur shops sell clothes, shoes and accessories, plus an amazing range of interesting bric-a-brac, and vintage items-so whatever you're interested in, we've got it!\r\n\r\nSue Ryder shops really needs help whenever you can give it-as little or as much as you like. Good support provided to all volunteers. Including to shadow a confident volunteer, be able to take their time if need be when learning, ask as many questions and will have an informal chat with the volunteer co-ordinator at any point. Can you help? If so, please get in touch! We'd absolutely love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help, gain/have a wonderful experience and help Sue Ryder in the important work we do locally and nationally. All help is greatly appreciated. For further details please contact Lucy Andrews, Volunteer Co-ordinator Sue Ryder North on E Mail: lucy.andrews@suerydercare.org or tel.: 07973794942.\n\n## Description\n\nDo you have any spare time throughout the week? And would you like to use it to gain experience, develop skills and meet new people while supporting a wonderful charity? Then we have the role for you!!!\r\n\r\nSue Ryder Charity Shops raise millions of pounds each year to enable our charity to deliver hospice and neurological care for more conditions than any other UK charity. As a volunteer in our shop, not only would you be meeting new friends, gaining skills and experience, but you'd also be directly supporting us to care for people when they really need it. \r\n\r\nOur shops sell clothes, shoes and accessories, plus an amazing range of interesting bric-a-brac, and vintage items-so whatever you're interested in, we've got it!\r\n\r\nSue Ryder shops really needs help whenever you can give it-as little or as much as you like. Good support provided to all volunteers. Including to shadow a confident volunteer, be able to take their time if need be when learning, ask as many questions and will have an informal chat with the volunteer co-ordinator at any point. Can you help? If so, please get in touch! We'd absolutely love to hear from you.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to help, gain/have a wonderful experience and help Sue Ryder in the important work we do locally and nationally. All help is greatly appreciated. For further details please contact Lucy Andrews, Volunteer Co-ordinator Sue Ryder North on E Mail: lucy.andrews@suerydercare.org or tel.: 07973794942.\n\n## Experience required\n\nReliable & trustworthy.\n\n## Training details\n\nGood support provided to all volunteers. Including to shadow a confident volunteer, be able to take their time if need be when learning, ask as many questions and will have an informal chat with the volunteer co-ordinator at any point.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nAll help is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis opportunity is in our Aberdeen 199 George Street store, Aberdeen AB25 1HX.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g24000008kiK6AAI#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Charity Shop Assistant",
                        "description": "Reliable & trustworthy.",
                        "commitment": "All help is greatly appreciated.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g24000008kiK6AAI/charity-shop-assistant?#modal_register_a0g24000008kiK6AAI",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/HealthHospitalsHospices",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Health / Hospitals / Hospices"
                            }
                        ],
                        "service": [
