            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000LF4QJAA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000LF4QJAA1/pop-in-play-support-team-member",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Pop In & Play Support Team Member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAs part of a team, to welcome, supervise and signpost visitors into the Pop In & Play Table Tennis facility in The Olympia, East Kilbride Shopping Centre.\n\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to support South Lanarkshire’s first and only Table Tennis Pop In & Play facility in East Kilbride Shopping Centre. The initiative is led by East Kilbride Table Tennis Club. The facility lets visitors to the centre literally “pop in and play” Table Tennis whilst they go about their normal business. \n\nWe need volunteers with an interest in sport/activity to help us supervise the facility by welcoming guests, showing them Table Tennis basics, managing table space and providing guests with additional information about where they can play Table Tennis in the region.  \n\nFor volunteers who are new to table tennis, we will buddy you up with experienced table tennis’ers in the early days – so don’t worry about that aspect!\n\nCurrent opening hours are 11am to 2pm, Mon-Fri. However, we want the facility to be open as many hours as possible and as such, we aim to support all your available volunteer hours as best we can.\n\n## Experience required\n\nFitness / Health / Beauty,PR / Marketing,Retail / Customer Service, Good Communicator,Good Listener,Open minded,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Team Player,\n\n## Training details\n\nFirst shifts will cover the basic operating procedures for the facility including Health & Safety and Fire Evacuation procedure.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nYou can volunteer for a regular day (or days) each week or let us know on a week to week basis. A rota will be created on a Friday for the following week based on availability of volunteers You can volunteer for a regular day (or days) each week or let us know on a week to week basis. A rota will be created on a Friday for the following week based on availability of volunteers 3 hours\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nEast Kilbride",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000LF4QJAA1#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Pop In & Play Support Team Member",
                        "description": "Fitness / Health / Beauty,PR / Marketing,Retail / Customer Service, Good Communicator,Good Listener,Open minded,Practical,Reliable / Dependable,Team Player,",
