            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Qhk3tAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Qhk3tAAB/collective-advocacy-eating-disorders",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-15",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Collective Advocacy-Eating Disorders",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you have experience of an eating disorder? By becoming a member of this group you’ll meet and get to know others with similar experiences. You will work together to raise awareness of eating disorders and campaign for change.\n\n## Description\n\nThis is not a traditional volunteering opportunity. It allows you to come together with others to use your lived experience of an eating disorder. Working as a team, ‘Seen but not Heard’ eating disorders collective advocacy have in the past developed training around eating disorders, two films, awareness events, attended conferences, responded to/developed consultations and have produced leaflets and resource packs. You’ll use your own experiences of eating disorders to challenge stigma.\n\n## Experience required\n\nYou will need lived experience of living with an eating disorder and be willing to draw on experiences to work as part of a collective advocacy group. Meetings take place every 4 to 6 weeks to suit participants availability.\n\n## Training details\n\nCAPS can provide skills development for group members.\n\n## Travel details\n\nMeetings take place in person or online.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nThere is a form to fill in, expenses will be paid by BACS transfer.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Qhk3tAAB#role",
