                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000005f7KQYAY",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000005f7KQYAY/community-history-project-participant",
                    "publishStart": "2021-06-14",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-31",
                    "title": "Community History Project Participant",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCAPS are looking for people with lived experience of mental health to join the ‘Oor Mad History’ community history project\n\n## Description\n\nThis is not a traditional volunteering opportunity. It allows you to come together with others to use your lived experience of mental health issues. Oor Mad History is a community history project, led by people with their own lived experience of mental health. In the past we have used oral history to record and promote the history of activism by people with mental health issues. Get in touch to find out more about joining this group and using your mental health lived experience.\n\n## Training details\n\nCAPS have a dedicated volunteer coordinator to provide training & mentoring for volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nEH7 5QY , online and various locations across the Lothians\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nOut of pocket expenses reimbursed (travel)",
