        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/00124000014bpGTAAY",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/00124000014bpGTAAY/bressay-park-run",
            "name": "Bressay Park Run",
            "description": "The main objective of the Bressay parkrun is to promote the island as a place to visit and to encourage people of all ages and abilities to take part in a safe free weekly community event which encourages healthy living and social fitness.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEvent",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Event"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g1p00000AtS9AAAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g1p00000AtS9AAAV/bressay-parkrun-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2018-01-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-27",
                    "title": "Bressay parkrun volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBressay parkrun will take place every Saturday morning at 9.30am (9am ferry over).  It is an organised run, jog or walk which is free to participate in.  Registration is online and participants print off their personalised barcode which is scanned at the finish line and results are emailed to the participant.  Bressay parkrun therefore requires volunteers to undertake the following roles: marshalls, photographer, barcode scanner, volunteer coordinator, run director, time keeper, funnel manager, finish token provider, tail walker, support for new volunteers, data processor.  This event promotes the health and wellbeing of our local community by encouraging social fitness.  There may also be an opportunity for someone to start a junior parkrun once the Bressay parkrun is well established and successful.  The event is ongoing and open to all ages, abilities, genders, races etc.  We want to encourage everyone to take part in some way.\n\n## Description\n\nBressay parkrun will take place every Saturday morning at 9.30am (9am ferry over).  It is an organised run, jog or walk which is free to participate in.  Registration is online and participants print off their personalised barcode which is scanned at the finish line and results are emailed to the participant.  Bressay parkrun therefore requires volunteers to undertake the following roles: marshalls, photographer, barcode scanner, volunteer coordinator, run director, time keeper, funnel manager, finish token provider, tail walker, support for new volunteers, data processor.  This event promotes the health and wellbeing of our local community by encouraging social fitness.  There may also be an opportunity for someone to start a junior parkrun once the Bressay parkrun is well established and successful.  The event is ongoing and open to all ages, abilities, genders, races etc.  We want to encourage everyone to take part in some way.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNone required.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nEvent takes place on Saturday mornings.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBressay.  Begins at Maryfield and ends at the Speldiburn Café.  Transport can be provided from the Café back to the ferry for those unable to/ not wishing to walk back.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
