            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000AiEJFYA3",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000AiEJFYA3/volunteer-cyclist",
                    "publishStart": "2025-07-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-05",
                    "title": "Volunteer Cyclist",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCWAS brings joy to communities across Scotland - particularly people living with limited mobility, loneliness or isolation - via the incredible social tool known as the Trishaw (specially adapted e-bike). Our volunteer cyclists (known as Pilots) provide FREE Trishaw rides along some of the most beautiful footpaths, cycle routes and quiet roads in Scotland. Our volunteer Outriders cycle alongside the Trishaw, getting to know the passengers and providing support to the Pilot and the passengers. \r\n\r\nOur passengers are people living with limited mobility, loneliness or isolation. They may be elderly people living in care homes, supported living or in their own homes, or they may be young people or adults with disabilities or additional support needs.\r\n\r\nOur volunteer Pilots and Outriders are outside in nature, sharing their daily discoveries with their passengers (who might otherwise have been stuck inside all day), bringing smiles to faces, enjoying a good blether and often a great laugh. Lasting friendships are made.\r\n\r\nCome for a spin in a Trishaw and find out why we love what we do! We are in:\r\n\r\n*** Aberdeen – Insch – Turriff – Westhills – Ellon – Kemnay – Portsoy – Stonehaven – Old Meldrum – Inverurie – Arbroath – Montrose – Carnoustie – Monifieth – Bute – Dunoon – Alloa – Dundee - Twechar - Musselburgh – North Berwick – Dunbar – Edinburgh – South Queensferry – Falkirk – Airth – Bo’ness – Grangemouth – Denny – Dunfermline – Lochore – Glasgow – Evanton – Cromarty – Ullapool – Fort William – Dingwall – Fortrose – Thurso – Wick – Gourock – Forres – Elgin – Largs – Isle of Cumbrae – Kilsyth – Westray – Aberfeldy – Auchterarder – Perth – Kinross – Comrie – Dunkeld – Eyemouth – Hawick – Selkirk – Galashiels – Peebles – Innerleithen – Troon – Ayr – Prestwick – Rutherglen – Stirling – Dumbarton – South Uist – Lewis & Harris – Fauldhouse - Linlithgow ***\r\n\r\nOther roles within CWAS include Co-passenger (befriender), Administrator, Trishaw Mechanic, Fund-raiser and Chapter Captain (lead contact and team leader).\r\n\r\nFor an informal chat about any of these roles, please call 01324 467 272 and ask for Gillian or Christine. Or you can email us by clicking \"I want to volunteer\" below - or by emailing info@cwas.org\r\n\r\nThank you!\n\n## Experience required\n\nVolunteers should have some cycling experience and good road sense (some routes include short stretches on quiet roads). They should be patient and responsible, good listeners and team players, enjoy chatting with people and enjoy being outside.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training is provided, and is free.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nAt least a couple of times a month, but the role is very flexible.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000AiEJFYA3#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Cyclist",
                        "description": "Volunteers should have some cycling experience and good road sense (some routes include short stretches on quiet roads). They should be patient and responsible, good listeners and team players, enjoy chatting with people and enjoy being outside.",
                        "commitment": "At least a couple of times a month, but the role is very flexible.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000AiEJFYA3/volunteer-cyclist?#modal_register_a0gQD00000AiEJFYA3",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "16",
