        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400001BdcWIAAZ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400001BdcWIAAZ/girlguiding-east-lothian",
            "name": "Girlguiding East Lothian",
            "description": "The Aim of Girlguiding East Lothian is to help girls and women develop emotionally, mentally, physically and spiritually, so that they can make a positive contribution to their community and the wider world, according to the principles of the Association and to facilitate Girlguiding for girls and young women in East Lothian.",
            "website": "http://www.girlguidingeastlothian.org/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC005512"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SportLeisureRecreation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Sport / Leisure / Recreation"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/UniformedGroups",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Uniformed Groups"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000He5SEYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000He5SEYAZ/youth-group-helper",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-05",
                    "title": "Youth Group Helper",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGirlguiding Scotland is the leading charity for girls and young women in Scotland, with over 35,000 young members supported by 9,000 amazing volunteers. Girlguiding helps members discover their full potential by having fun and enjoy new adventures.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of Girlguiding are our regular group sessions, called unit meetings. These are run by volunteer teams of adult leaders, helpers, and young leaders.\r\n\r\nAs a helper, there's no responsibility for planning, but you'll be the extra pair of hands needed to make unit meetings happen. You can help behind the scenes or face to face with girls. No two units are the same which means that all unit helpers do slightly different things. There is a lot of space to make this role your own.\r\n\r\nUnit meetings are split by our 4 main sections, defined by age range. It’s up to you what section you’d rather work with, and you can attend a variety of meetings to find the right fit for you.\r\n\r\nRainbows are aged 4-7 and focus on fun, friendship and adventure\r\n\r\nBrownies are aged 7-10 and focus on fun, adventure, and even first nights away!\r\n\r\nGuides run for those aged 10-14 and is a relaxed, safe space for young members to develop their interests and take on new challenges.\r\n\r\nRangers are aged 14-18, and are supported to be independent, take the lead on activities, and explore UK and international adventures!\r\n\r\nThe impact you'll have:\r\n\r\nHelp girls discover their full potential by having fun and enjoying new adventures.\r\n\r\nThe skills you'll need:\r\n\r\nYou will need to have the following skills in order to participate:\r\n\r\nEnthusiastic willing to learn\r\n\r\nFriendly and welcoming; our units are a safe space for our young members to express and challenge themselves.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nVolunteers can claim agreed expenses incurred as part of their role, including travel or materials.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000He5SEYAZ#role",
