        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/0012400001QbAohAAF",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400001QbAohAAF/broomhill-sports-club",
            "name": "Broomhill Sports Club",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/BroomhillSportsClub",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JUfCcYAL",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JUfCcYAL/volunteer-induction-coach-support-coordinator",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-04",
                    "title": "Volunteer Induction & Coach Support Coordinator",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteer Induction & Coach Support Coordinator\n\n## Description\n\nBSC Glasgow | Peterson Park, Knightswood\n\nHelp welcome and support the volunteers and coaches who make community sport possible!\n\nAre you friendly, organised and someone who enjoys helping others? BSC Glasgow is looking for a Volunteer Induction &amp; Coach Support Coordinator to help new volunteers and coaches feel welcomed, informed and confident as they get involved in community sport.\n\nBSC Glasgow is a community sports club based at Peterson Park in Knightswood, delivering sporting activities for children and young people across the west of Glasgow. The club encourages participation, teamwork and personal development, supported by the dedication of its volunteers and coaches.\n\nWhat You&#39;ll Be Doing\n\nYou&#39;ll help make joining BSC Glasgow a positive and straightforward experience, supporting new volunteers and coaches through their induction and initial registration requirements.\n\nYour activities will include:\n\n\n\tWelcoming new volunteers and coaches and helping them settle into the club.\n\tGuiding new recruits through the induction process, including relevant club policies and procedures.\n\tAssisting coaches with Scottish FA registration and training requirements through the COMET system.\n\tSignposting volunteers and coaches to relevant training and development opportunities.\n\tMaintaining simple, accurate records of induction progress and outstanding requirements.\n\tActing as a friendly point of contact, answering general questions and directing people to the appropriate club representative when needed.\n\tHelping ensure new volunteers and coaches feel supported and ready to contribute to the club&#39;s activities.\n\n\nNo previous knowledge of the Scottish FA COMET system is required, as training and guidance will be provided.\n\nWho This Opportunity Suits\n\nThis opportunity would suit someone who:\n\n\n\tEnjoys helping people and making them feel welcome.\n\tHas good communication and interpersonal skills.\n\tIs organised, reliable and pays attention to detail.\n\tHas basic IT and administrative skills.\n\tCan handle information sensitively and confidentially.\n\tHas an interest in community sport, volunteering or supporting others.\n\tIs willing to learn new systems and procedures.\n\n\nPrevious experience in volunteer coordination, administration or sports development would be helpful but is not essential.\n\nTime Commitment and Flexibility\n\nThis is a flexible volunteering opportunity on an as-and-when-required basis.\n\nSupport will be needed when new volunteers and coaches join the club or require assistance with induction, registration and training requirements.\n\nThere are no fixed weekly hours specified, and volunteering arrangements will be agreed in advance to suit your availability and the club&#39;s needs.\n\nTraining and Support\n\nYou&#39;ll receive an introduction to BSC Glasgow, its volunteering procedures and the systems relevant to your role.\n\nTraining and ongoing guidance will be provided, including support with the Scottish FA COMET system. You&#39;ll also have access to club representatives if you need advice or assistance.\n\nWhy Volunteer With BSC Glasgow?\n\nVolunteering in this role offers an opportunity to:\n\n\n\tDevelop communication, administration and organisational skills.\n\tGain experience in volunteer induction, coordination and support.\n\tBuild confidence using digital systems and maintaining records.\n\tLearn more about community sport and volunteer development.\n\tMeet new people and become part of a community sports club.\n\tMake a positive contribution by helping coaches and volunteers get off to a good start.\n\n\nYour contribution will help BSC Glasgow provide a welcoming and organised induction experience, supporting the volunteers and coaches who deliver sporting opportunities for children and young people.\n\nLocation and Travel\n\nBSC Glasgow is based at Peterson Park, Knightswood, Glasgow G13, with activities taking place at various sporting locations across the west of Glasgow.\n\nThe club will confirm where your volunteering activities will take place and any travel requirements before you begin.\n\nWhat Happens After You Apply?\n\nOnce you&#39;ve expressed your interest through Volunteer Glasgow, your details will be forwarded to BSC Glasgow.\n\nA club representative will contact you to discuss the opportunity, explain the responsibilities and flexible arrangements, and answer any questions.\n\nThis initial conversation will help both you and the club decide whether the opportunity is a good fit before progressing to induction.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tGood communication and organisational skills.\n•\tConfidence using email and basic online systems.\n•\tPatient, supportive and approachable manner.\n•\tCommitment to helping others get involved in sport and community activities.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBSC Glasgow is based at Peterson Park in Knightswood, Glasgow G13, with activities taking place at various locations across the west of Glasgow.\n\nPeterson Park can be reached by public transport from Glasgow city centre, with local bus services serving the Knightswood area. The nearest railway stations include Westerton and Scotstounhill, with onward travel required.\n\nAs this is an as-and-when-required volunteering opportunity, the club will confirm the location of activities and any travel arrangements in advance.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe can support travel and subsistance",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JUfCcYAL#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Induction & Coach Support Coordinator",
                        "description": "•\tGood communication and organisational skills.\n•\tConfidence using email and basic online systems.\n•\tPatient, supportive and approachable manner.\n•\tCommitment to helping others get involved in sport and community activities.",
                        "applyLink": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/volunteers/opportunity/10308214",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "14",
                        "service": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Service/NamedContactForVolunteer",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Named Contact For Volunteer"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Service/ExpensesPaid",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Expenses Paid"
                            }
                        ],
                        "reward": [
                            "https://ns.volunteeringdata.io/ExpensesReimbursed"
                        ]
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
                            {
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "G13 4PF",
                                "address": "G13 4PF",
                                "latitude": 55.89652984560277,
                                "longitude": -4.373780134024763,
                                "simd": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/SIMD/G134PF"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/LocalAuthority/Glasgow",
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "Glasgow"
                            }
