                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hynk1YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hynk1YAB/volunteer-manager-for-community-sports-club",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-03",
                    "title": "Volunteer Manager for Community sports club",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteer Manager for Community sports club\n\n## Description\n\nBSC Glasgow at Peterson Park has grown into one of the busiest volunteer hubs in the city. With volunteers supporting football coaching, groundskeeping, social media, community caf&eacute; operations, men&rsquo;s shed activities, and general admin, they truly are the lifeblood of our club.\n\nWe are now seeking a Volunteer Manager to help us continue building a strong, supportive, and well-organised volunteer community.\n\nThe project seek a Volunteer Manager for Community sports club and Community hall in the G13 area.&nbsp;\n\nThis role is ideal for someone who enjoys working with people, building partnerships, and helping others develop skills and confidence.\n\nBSC Glasgow is a community sports club who operate sports teams and a community hall&nbsp;\n\nIf you are interested please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly, organised, and confident communicator\nAbility to work with a wide range of people and backgrounds\nInterest in community development, sport, or social impact\nExperience in volunteer coordination is helpful but not essential\nReliability and a genuine passion for helping others thrive\n\n## Travel details\n\nYoker Train Station is 500m from the Hall. Numerous buses travel to and from Clydebank and can access the hall. Via Alderman Road, Dumbarton Road & Great Western Road.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe will support travel and any out of pocket expences in support of this role.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hynk1YAB#role",
