                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HPCQnYAP",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HPCQnYAP/first-aid-lead",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-09",
                    "title": "First Aid Lead",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFirst Aid Lead\n\n## Description\n\nBroomhill Sports Club seek a designated First Aid Lead is to manage training, application, and recording for a community sports club based in West Glasgow.\n\nRole Purpose\n\nThe Club First Aid Lead is responsible for overseeing first-aid readiness, injury-management procedures, and safety standards across all club activities. This is a non-clinical leadership role focused on coordination, compliance, and supporting coaches to deliver safe sessions.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n\n\t\n\tMaintain and update the club&rsquo;s first-aid and injury-management protocols\n\t\n\t\n\tEnsure all coaches hold valid first-aid training and understand club procedures\n\t\n\t\n\tOversee the stocking, distribution, and condition of first-aid kits\n\t\n\t\n\tProvide guidance and authority during injury situations when required\n\t\n\t\n\tReview and record injury incidents, identifying improvements\n\t\n\t\n\tLiaise with the committee on safety, compliance, and training needs\n\t\n\t\n\tSupport communication with parents and players regarding injury processes\n\t\n\t\n\tEnsure first-aid equipment is available at all training sessions and matches\n\t\n\t\n\tKeep accurate records of training, incidents, and kit checks\n\t\n\n\nIf you are interested,&nbsp;please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when&nbsp;registered and&nbsp;logged in). You&nbsp;will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that&nbsp;doesn&rsquo;t&nbsp;work&nbsp;out,&nbsp;then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org.&nbsp;\n\n## Experience required\n\nCalm and confident decision-maker\nGood communicator\nOrganised and reliable\nBasic first-aid knowledge (training provided)\nComfortable supporting and advising coaches\n\n## Travel details\n\nAccessible by train, Yoker station is 500m away. Multiple buses run through the area from Glasgow and Clydebank\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe will fund training and travel",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
