                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000H562zYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000H562zYAB/catering-team-member-for-community-sports-club",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-11-28",
                    "title": "Catering Team Member for community sports club",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCatering Team Member for community sports club\n\n## Description\n\nAbout Us\n\nThe Parent Community Sports Trust is a Glasgow-based charity (SC044806) dedicated to promoting healthy living and strengthening local communities through sport, social activity, and inclusive programmes.\n\nVolunteer Opportunity: Catering Team Member\n\nWe&rsquo;re looking for enthusiastic volunteers to join our Catering Team at Paterson Park Hall, Knightswood. Our small community caf&eacute; supports hall users and the football teams playing on the adjacent pitches, and we also provide simple post-match buffets.\n\nWhat the Role Involves\n\n\n\t\n\tPreparing teas, coffees, and light snacks\n\t\n\t\n\tAssisting with post-match buffet preparation\n\t\n\t\n\tKeeping the kitchen clean, tidy, and welcoming\n\t\n\t\n\tHelping create a friendly, community-focused atmosphere\n\t\n\n\nNo experience is required &mdash; just a positive attitude and a willingness to help. This is a great role for someone who enjoys meeting people and being part of a supportive local team.\n\nFlexible and Supportive\n\nYour role can be shaped around your interests and skills. We&rsquo;ll arrange an informal chat to explore what you&rsquo;d like to do and how you can get involved.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nClick the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (visible when logged in and registered). Our coordinator will contact you by email or phone.\n\nIf you haven&rsquo;t heard back within 5 working days:\n\n\n\t\n\tContact the organisation using the details provided\n\t\n\t\n\tCheck your email junk/spam folder\n\t\n\t\n\tIf you still need assistance, contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org\n\n## Experience required\n\nHigh standards of hygiene. Basic English is needed, but it is an opportunity to practise language skills\n\n## Travel details\n\nAccessible by train, Yoker station is 500m away. Multiple buses run through the area from Glasgow and Clydebank.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe can offer some expenses if travel is involved, and we will feed people.",
