            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/0012400001QbiDwAAJ/euans-guide",
            "name": "Euan’s Guide.",
            "description": "Euan’s Guide is the disabled access review website where disabled people, their friends and families can review, share and discover accessible places. The charity now has thousands of disabled access reviews and listings for places all over the UK and beyond. .",
            "website": "https://www.euansguide.com",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/PhysicalDisability",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Physical Disability"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0g0800000Qhj1rAAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0g0800000Qhj1rAAB/content-creator",
                    "publishStart": "2023-07-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Content Creator",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nIf you’re a writer, blogger, or fan of using social media who wants to help make a positive difference to the lives of other disabled people by sharing your own experiences then we’d love to hear from you. We want to provide you with a platform to share stories because we know it’s those first-hand experiences that count. \r\n\r\nWe have varying levels of content creation roles available, from submitting simple reviews of places you’ve visited to writing articles and creating video content for our social media platforms.\n\n## Experience required\n\nInterest in writing and sharing their experiences of disabled access. Some knowledge and experience of writing blogs and social media content for our website would be helpful, but not essential.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction training includes how to start reviewing and what makes a good review. Ongoing training includes learning how to write blogs for the website and taking part in review days\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe reimburse pre-agreed travel expenses for meetings and events that volunteers attend.\n\n## Taster details\n\nWe can offer in person training or online over zoom on how to write reviews and how to sign up to the website",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
