        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000002Gtc6YAC",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000002Gtc6YAC/solidaritee",
            "name": "SolidariTee",
            "description": "SolidariTee is an international charity run and led by young people. We work to make lasting change in the way refugees and other people forced to flee persecution and violence are treated through fundraising for grassroot NGOs and awareness-raising.",
            "website": "https://www.solidaritee.org.uk/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/RefugeesAsylumSeekers",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Refugees / Asylum Seekers"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000AxUFfYAN",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000AxUFfYAN/team-members-of-aberdeen-university-solidaritee-team",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Team Members of Aberdeen University SolidariTee Team",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSolidariTee is an international charity run and led entirely by volunteers who are students and young people. We're working to make lasting change in the way refugees and other people forced to flee persecution and violence are treated, through a combination of awareness-raising, advocacy, and fundraising to support grassroots NGOs providing vital refugee legal aid and mental health support.\r\n\r\nWe are currently looking for volunteers to join our Regional (uni), Central, and Leadership teams.\r\n\r\nPositions on our University of Aberdeen Regional SolidariTee Team:\r\n• Team Lead\r\n• Regional Events & Fundraising Officers\r\n\r\nAs part of your university team, you’d be involved in organising fundraising and awareness events – anything from club nights, fashion shows and balls to panel discussions, film screenings and pub quizzes – and selling our SolidariTee t-shirts to raise funds for legal aid and mental health support for refugees. It’s also a great opportunity to expand your own knowledge of topics relating to migration and forced displacement and to spark meaningful conversations with the student community and members of the public. No prior knowledge is required, just motivation and dedication to raise funds and stand in solidarity with people who have been forced to flee their homes.\r\n\r\nPositions on our Central Team:\r\n• Events Officers\r\n• Partnerships Officers\r\n• Publicity Officers (social media team)\r\n• Digital Education Officers (social media team)\r\n\r\nOur Central Team includes students and other young people from around the UK and works together to coordinate SolidariTee’s core functions and organise opportunities to bring our volunteers and supporters together. This includes organising our annual conference, creating content for our central Instagram page @teesofsolidarity, and developing partnerships with uni societies, student groups, fashion shows, balls and more!\r\n\r\nPositions on our Leadership Team:\r\n• Secretary\r\n• Social Media Manager\r\n• Events Lead\r\n• Partnerships Lead\r\n\r\nOur Leadership Team provides overall coordination and oversight to the activities of our Central Team and Regional Teams, and it is a great opportunity to be involved with leading the direction of the SolidariTee movement on a national level.\r\n\r\nFor full role descriptions and information about how to apply, please visit our website: https://www.solidaritee.org.uk/join-us. Most roles will be filled on a rolling basis, so please see our website for the most up to date information on the positions we are currently looking to fill.\n\n## Description\n\nSolidariTee is an international charity run and led entirely by volunteers who are students and young people. We're working to make lasting change in the way refugees and other people forced to flee persecution and violence are treated, through a combination of awareness-raising, advocacy, and fundraising to support grassroots NGOs providing vital refugee legal aid and mental health support.\r\n\r\nWe are currently looking for volunteers to join our Regional (uni), Central, and Leadership teams.\r\n\r\nPositions on our University of Aberdeen Regional SolidariTee Team:\r\n• Team Lead\r\n• Regional Events & Fundraising Officers\r\n\r\nAs part of your university team, you’d be involved in organising fundraising and awareness events – anything from club nights, fashion shows and balls to panel discussions, film screenings and pub quizzes – and selling our SolidariTee t-shirts to raise funds for legal aid and mental health support for refugees. It’s also a great opportunity to expand your own knowledge of topics relating to migration and forced displacement and to spark meaningful conversations with the student community and members of the public. No prior knowledge is required, just motivation and dedication to raise funds and stand in solidarity with people who have been forced to flee their homes.\r\n\r\nPositions on our Central Team:\r\n• Events Officers\r\n• Partnerships Officers\r\n• Publicity Officers (social media team)\r\n• Digital Education Officers (social media team)\r\n\r\nOur Central Team includes students and other young people from around the UK and works together to coordinate SolidariTee’s core functions and organise opportunities to bring our volunteers and supporters together. This includes organising our annual conference, creating content for our central Instagram page @teesofsolidarity, and developing partnerships with uni societies, student groups, fashion shows, balls and more!\r\n\r\nPositions on our Leadership Team:\r\n• Secretary\r\n• Social Media Manager\r\n• Events Lead\r\n• Partnerships Lead\r\n\r\nOur Leadership Team provides overall coordination and oversight to the activities of our Central Team and Regional Teams, and it is a great opportunity to be involved with leading the direction of the SolidariTee movement on a national level.\r\n\r\nFor full role descriptions and information about how to apply, please visit our website: https://www.solidaritee.org.uk/join-us. Most roles will be filled on a rolling basis, so please see our website for the most up to date information on the positions we are currently looking to fill.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. We have resources and induction workshops available.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times to help. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2F66c92cc9-6377-4191-8606-376d626e6d25%2F6GvuqzbpFKWXOePEC1v41h0KVnD2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=22a0f887-421f-4fc1-9b03-ef333a032fcc",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000AxUFfYAN#role",
