                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008pKrKYAU",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008pKrKYAU/vegan-community-organisers-aberdeen",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Vegan Community Organisers (Aberdeen)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDo you want to take part in vegan volunteering around Aberdeen?\r\n\r\nThe Vegan Society's mission is to make veganism mainstream.\r\n\r\nWe're working tirelessly to make veganism an easily-adopted and widely-recognised approach to reducing animal suffering and environmental damage. We do so through peaceful and factual dialogue with individuals, organisations and businesses.\r\nWe have an ever-growing Community Network of vegans just like you, who have a passion to volunteer and promote veganism in the local area. \r\n\r\nEvery month, our Network choose from a range of outreach tasks. These could include town/city centre stalls, writing to a councillor or MP, sharing our campaigns on social media or contacting local businesses. You're in control of how much or how little you do.\r\n\r\nRelevant training and excellent support is provided to all Community Organisers.\r\n\r\nA great opportunity to help and make a real difference. For more information please contact: Katy Malkin, Volunteering Coordinator at email: communitynetwork@vegansociety.com or tel.: 01217285855\n\n## Description\n\nDo you want to take part in vegan volunteering around Aberdeen?\r\n\r\nThe Vegan Society's mission is to make veganism mainstream.\r\n\r\nWe're working tirelessly to make veganism an easily-adopted and widely-recognised approach to reducing animal suffering and environmental damage. We do so through peaceful and factual dialogue with individuals, organisations and businesses.\r\nWe have an ever-growing Community Network of vegans just like you, who have a passion to volunteer and promote veganism in the local area. \r\n\r\nEvery month, our Network choose from a range of outreach tasks. These could include town/city centre stalls, writing to a councillor or MP, sharing our campaigns on social media or contacting local businesses. You're in control of how much or how little you do.\r\n\r\nRelevant training and excellent support is provided to all Community Organisers.\r\n\r\nA great opportunity to help and make a real difference. For more information please contact: Katy Malkin, Volunteering Coordinator at email: communitynetwork@vegansociety.com or tel.: 01217285855\r\n\r\nMore details about our work and volunteering is also available at:  https://www.vegansociety.com/ and https://www.vegansociety.com/get-involved/volunteering-vegan-society\n\n## Training details\n\nRelevant training and excellent support is provided to all volunteers. There will be a full induction to the role, with a gradual introduction of new tasks and responsibilities. To start with, we will provide an initial training session to cover the basics of community organising, communication skills and event planning. This will be done remotely from wherever you are. Along with this, we will provide a full pack of resources that covers a range of work that we do. \r\n\r\nFrom there, there will be regular conversations and reviews, where we can discuss other training requirements. Staff are always available to Organisers for any questions, via phone or email.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nThe volunteering times are flexible. All help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nAround the vicinity of where you live - in and around Aberdeen ideally. You will be attending various local events.",
