        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD0000036zLfYAI",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD0000036zLfYAI/re-engage",
            "name": "RE-engage",
            "description": "Re-Engage is the only national charity solely dedicated to tackling loneliness and social isolation among older people.\nSupported by a network of volunteers, the charity organises remote and in-person services for people aged 75-years and older. Offering a regular and vital friendship link every\ntime.\n\nOur services are a real lifeline of friendship for our older guests who have little or no contact with family or friends. They bring people of all ages together, develop fulfilling friendships and support networks, and give everyone involved something to look forward to each time.\n\nWe provide monthly tea parties, monthly Pickleball for Wellbeing, and weekly telephone befriending calls. \n\nOur services are completely free, entry level accessibility and there is no time limit on service access. Loneliness manifests itself differently and can be different for every person so we support people for as long as they need us.",
            "website": "https://reengage.org.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC039377"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Jq4SpYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Jq4SpYAJ/telephone-befriender-for-elderly-person",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-30",
                    "title": "Telephone Befriender for Elderly Person",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nA friendly phone call can make someone's day. Could you be the person who makes it?\n\nRe-engage is looking for friendly, caring volunteers to provide regular telephone companionship to older people experiencing loneliness or social isolation.\n\nAs a Call Companion, you'll be matched with an older person for regular, relaxed telephone conversations. Whether you're sharing stories, discussing everyday life or simply enjoying a laugh together, your calls can help someone feel connected, valued and less alone.\n\nOver time, you'll have the opportunity to build a meaningful friendship, bringing enjoyment and companionship to both you and the person you support.\n\nWhat will you be doing?\nMaking friendly telephone calls to your matched older person 2–4 times per month, at mutually agreed times.\nSpending approximately 30 minutes per call chatting, listening and sharing stories.\nBuilding a positive, supportive relationship through regular contact.\nFollowing Re-engage's training and guidance to ensure conversations are safe, appropriate and enjoyable.\nKeeping in regular contact with the Re-engage team.\nVolunteering times and commitment\nThis is a flexible, home-based opportunity, requiring approximately 1–2 hours per month for telephone calls.\n\nYou'll agree suitable days, times and call frequency directly with the older person you're matched with. Calls can be arranged around your work, family and other commitments.\n\nRe-engage asks volunteers to commit to the role for a minimum of 12 months, helping provide continuity and build a lasting friendship.\n\nTraining and support for volunteers\nYou'll receive guidance, training and ongoing support from Re-engage to help you feel confident and comfortable in your role.\n\nSupport includes:\n\nOnline induction and introductory training before you begin.\nGuidance on making friendly, appropriate and supportive telephone calls.\nInformation on confidentiality, safeguarding and maintaining appropriate boundaries.\nOngoing contact and support from the Re-engage team.\nA point of contact if you have questions, concerns or need additional guidance.\nCalls are made through a secure telephone system, helping protect your personal contact details.\n\nWho can volunteer?\nYou don't need previous befriending experience. We're looking for people who enjoy conversation, are good listeners and genuinely want to make a difference.\n\nYou'll need to:\n\nBe 18 years or older.\nBe friendly, patient, reliable and comfortable speaking on the telephone.\nRespect confidentiality and personal boundaries.\nComplete Re-engage's volunteer training.\nProvide one reference and complete an identity check & PVG membership\nWhat happens after you apply?\nIf you're interested, click the Apply button below (available once you're registered and logged in to Volunteer Glasgow).\n\nA coordinator from Re-engage will then contact you by email or telephone to discuss the opportunity and next steps.\n\nIf you haven't received a response within five working days, please check your email junk or spam folder and contact Re-engage using the details provided.\n\nIf you still have difficulty getting a response, you can contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nBefriending / Mentoring, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Patient,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Trustworthy,\n\n## Training details\n\nKey Aims of the Training\n\n• Understand the service: Learn the core purpose of the Call Companion program and what to expect in the volunteer role.\n• Effective communication: Develop skills in active listening, putting older people at ease, respecting silences, and using open questions.\n• Handling challenges: Anticipate potential difficulties and learn appropriate responses.\n• Safeguarding and procedures: Understand what steps to take if you have any worries or concerns about the person you are calling.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThis is a South Lanarkshire opportunity and takes place in   Yes\nAcross South Lanarkshire",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Jq4SpYAJ#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Telephone Befriender for Elderly Person",
                        "description": "Befriending / Mentoring, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Patient,Reliable / Dependable,Sociable,Trustworthy,",
