                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000AOleLYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000AOleLYAT/pickleball-helper-with-older-people",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-01",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Pickleball Helper with Older People",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nCould you help an Older Person combat loneliness and stay active all in one? Re-engage and Pickleball Scotland are looking for helpers for their new monthly Older People's Pickleball Group in East Kilbride.\n\nYou don't need to have ever played before, all you need is a heart to help your community and Older people. Pickleball for Wellbeing is a new formatted game that is accessible and suitable for everyone since it can be played seated or standing. The group is led by an accredited coach and your job as Helper is to to just that- help! \nYou will help welcome people into the group, maybe help set up the courts and help set up chairs. The group will also meet for a coffee or tea afterwards so we would ask you help with conversation and connecting with people. \n\nThis is a low commitment flexible opportunity and a chance to try a new sport if you have never tried before!\n\n## Experience required\n\nBefriending / Mentoring,No Expertise, Caring,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Patient,Sociable,Team Player,\n\n## Training details\n\nOnline and ongoing training offered.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire,East Kilbride",
