            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD000003je9KYAQ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD000003je9KYAQ/african-relief-support",
            "name": "African Relief support",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/AfricanReliefSupport",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HawwXYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HawwXYAR/community-hub-admin-support-volunteer-people-relief-support-pollok",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-03",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-30",
                    "title": "Community Hub Admin & Support Volunteer – People Relief Support (Pollok)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCommunity Hub Admin & Support Volunteer – People Relief Support (Pollok)\n\n## Description\n\nPeople Relief Support is a diverse, community-led charity based at Leithland Neighbourhood Centre in Pollok. We run a busy community hub supporting local families, young people, migrants, and individuals facing poverty, isolation, or barriers to opportunity.\n\nWe are looking for friendly and organised volunteers to support our day-to-day admin and office operations. This role is essential in helping us deliver programmes such as ESOL classes, community support sessions, youth activities, wellbeing programmes, and outreach work across Greater Pollok.\n\nAs an Admin &amp; Support Volunteer, you will help with tasks such as welcoming visitors, answering enquiries, updating records, supporting project administration, assisting with volunteer coordination, and helping our team keep the hub running smoothly. Your contribution directly strengthens the services our community relies on.\n\nIf you enjoy working with people, have good attention to detail, and want to make a meaningful difference in Pollok, we would love to hear from you.\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone. If you don&rsquo;t hear back within 5 working days, please contact the organisation using the provided details. Check your junk/spam folder for responses. If there&rsquo;s still no response, contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tFriendly and approachable manner\n•\tBasic IT skills (email, Microsoft Office or similar)\n•\tGood communication skills\n•\tAbility to work as part of a team\n•\tOrganised and reliable\n•\tWillingness to learn and support a busy community hub\n\n## Travel details\n\nRoute Breakdown: Bus from City Centre: Board the No. 3 bus (heading towards Drumchapel/Govan) from Renfield Street or St Vincent Street. The Tesco Highlight: The bus travels along Crookston Road. Keep an eye out for the Tesco superstore at 588 Crookston Road. Connecting Step: To continue to Leithland, get off just after passing Tesco at the Crovie Road stop,  From there, the Leithland Neighbourhood Centre is just a 3-minute walk (182 meters) down the road.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPeople Relief Support reimburses all reasonable out of pocket expenses for volunteers. This includes travel costs (bus, train or mileage), lunch expenses when volunteering for longer shifts, and any materials purchased specifically for volunteer duties. We want to ensure that no volunteer is left out of pocket while supporting our community hub.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
