            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000077cm5YAA",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000077cm5YAA/food-bank-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2024-12-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Food Bank Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Salvation Army – it’s a name familiar to just about everyone. But, there is so much more to The Salvation Army than meets the eye! In every community where you find The Salvation Army, you will discover a ministry that is unique. For more than a hundred and twenty years, The Salvation Army has been a vital part of the South Ayrshire evangelical and social community.\r\n\r\nAyr Salvation Army are currently seeking volunteers to enable us to continue to offer  Food Bank services within the community.  The Food Bank is currently open on a Wednesday 12 - 2pm.  Ayr Salvation Army are keen to recruit new volunteers to enable us to continue to offer this and to open the food bank on Mondays and Fridays.\r\n\r\nCan you offer a few hours each week to help this service continue to improve the lives of members of the community? If yes, We would love to hear from you.  \r\n This is a varied and interesting role that includes:\r\n-Dealing with the public\r\n-Understanding and updating relevant Food Bank documentation\r\n-Stocking shelves\r\n-Confidentiality to respect the identity and dignity of Food Bank users.\r\n\r\nInduction and training will be provided.  You will always be facilitating the Food Bank with another volunteer.\r\n\r\nInterested? You could make a real difference by volunteering! Please contact us on ayr@salvationarmy.org.uk or 01292 269286  to find out more\n\n## Experience required\n\nDesirable:\r\nGood people skills\r\nCustomer Service\r\nUnderstanding of impact of poverty\r\nLiteracy (to complete Food Bank records)\r\nUnderstanding of need for confidentiality to respect the identity and dignity of Food Bank users.",
