            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000007nTEYYA2",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000007nTEYYA2/aberdeen-ethnic-minority-womens-group-volunteers",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Aberdeen Ethnic Minority Women’s Group Volunteers",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nAberdeen Ethnic Minority Women’s Group CIC, a community interest company dedicated to supporting and empowering ethnic minority women in the Aberdeen area are currently seeking passionate volunteers for the following exciting roles:\r\n\r\n      •     Fundraising/Social Impact Volunteers: This role involves developing and implementing strategies to secure funding and enhance our social impact initiatives.\r\nroles:\r\n      •    Legal Support Volunteers: This role involves providing legal advice and support to our organisation, ensuring compliance with nonprofit regulations, and assisting with legal matters related to our programs and operations.\r\n      •     Finance Volunteers: We require skilled individuals to help manage our financial records, ensuring transparency and compliance with nonprofit regulations.\r\n      •     Community Engagement Volunteers: This position focuses on building and maintaining relationships with community members and stakeholders to foster collaboration and support for our programs.\r\n\r\nFantastic opportunities to make a real difference helping us continue our mission to empower and uplift ethnic minority women in our community. All help is greatly appreciated. For more information about any of the roles or ways you can help please contact Elizabeth Spencer, Founder & Managing Director, Aberdeen Ethnic Minority Women’s Group CIC  at email: volunteer@abdn-emwomen.org.uk\n\n## Description\n\nAberdeen Ethnic Minority Women’s Group CIC, a community interest company dedicated to supporting and empowering ethnic minority women in the Aberdeen area are currently seeking passionate volunteers for the following exciting roles:\r\n\r\n      •     Fundraising/Social Impact Volunteers: This role involves developing and implementing strategies to secure funding and enhance our social impact initiatives.\r\nroles:\r\n      •    Legal Support Volunteers: This role involves providing legal advice and support to our organisation, ensuring compliance with nonprofit regulations, and assisting with legal matters related to our programs and operations.\r\n      •     Finance Volunteers: We require skilled individuals to help manage our financial records, ensuring transparency and compliance with nonprofit regulations.\r\n      •     Community Engagement Volunteers: This position focuses on building and maintaining relationships with community members and stakeholders to foster collaboration and support for our programs.\r\n\r\nFantastic opportunities to make a real difference helping us continue our mission to empower and uplift ethnic minority women in our community. All help is greatly appreciated. For more information about any of the roles or ways you can help please contact Elizabeth Spencer, Founder & Managing Director, Aberdeen Ethnic Minority Women’s Group CIC  at email: volunteer@abdn-emwomen.org.uk\n\n## Training details\n\nGuidance and excellent support is provided to all volunteers.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to volunteer. All help makes a real difference and is greatly appreciated.",
