        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000U50W2YAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000U50W2YAJ/action-for-happiness",
            "name": "Action for Happiness",
            "description": "Our vision is a happier world, where everyone can thrive.\r\n\r\nThe mission of Action for Happiness is to help people create a happier world, with a culture that prioritises happiness and kindness.\r\nWe do this by helping people get together regularly (face-to-face where possible) to learn evidence-based skills for happier living, feel a sense of belonging and commit to personal action to create more happiness, both for themselves and others.\r\n\r\nWe have no religious, political or commercial affiliations and welcome people of all faiths (or none) and all parts of society. Members of the movement make a simple pledge: to try to create more happiness in the world.",
            "website": "https://actionforhappiness.org/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityDevelopment",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Development"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SelfHelpSupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Self-Help / Support"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEngagement",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Engagement"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GTdJKYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GTdJKYA1/action-for-happiness-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-04-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-31",
                    "title": "Action for Happiness Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe mission of Action for Happiness is to help people create a happier world, with a culture that prioritises happiness and kindness. We do this by helping people get together regularly to learn evidence-based skills for happier living, feel a sense of belonging and commit to personal action to create more happiness, both for themselves and others.\r\n\r\nOur work is underpinned by Positive Psychology. We provide daily actions people can take through our app and calendar, which has been used by millions of people. Our fantastic volunteers lead our online courses or coordinate our groups where members meet to learn tools to increase wellbeing and commit to action. A peer-reviewed Randomised Control Trial found our course provides significant benefits for happiness and wellbeing. We host regular live webinars with leading thinkers on happiness, wellbeing and mental health, which have had over 250,000 attendees.\r\n\r\nDo you want to see more happiness and kindness in the world? We’re looking for dynamic Volunteers to be part of creating exactly that! Our volunteers bring people together for shared learning experiences, based on positive psychology, that boost the wellbeing of everyone involved.  Our groups and courses can be run online or in-person in your local area.\r\n\r\nThe amazing 6-week Happiness Habits Course is designed to be run by pairs of volunteers. It features expert videos, science-backed exercises and the chance to form meaningful connections. Our course has been specially designed to gather the insights of the world's leading experts on six fundamental aspects of a happy and meaningful life: Gratitude, Self-Care, Relationships, Resilience, Kindness, and Meaning. It is a very impactful (many say life-changing) experience.\r\n\r\nAlternatively, you can get involved by supporting a Monthly Group, bringing like-minded people together to learn evidence-based tools for creating a happier and more meaningful life. Explore the monthly themes and encourage people to set personal actions towards happiness, that support both themselves and others.\r\n\r\nVolunteering with Action for Happiness is a path of action that consistently feels like you are making a difference in the world. You don’t have to be an expert - or be happy all the time. If you are a warm and enthusiastic person that is more than enough to get started.\n\n## Experience required\n\nAction for Happiness welcomes a wide range of applicants through our Volunteer Training.\r\nYou don't need to be a professional coach or trainer, as long as your motivations and character align with our values you have it in you to be an Action for Happiness volunteer.  We embrace diversity of all kinds and encourage a broad spectrum of people to apply.\n\n## Training details\n\nInduction, training and support provided. \r\n\r\nCLICK TO ACCESS OUR VOLUNTEER TRAINING:\r\nhttps://actionforhappiness.org/volunteer-training?utm=AD-FALK\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\n2 hours per week for 6 weeks (course), or 2 hours per month (group).\r\nBecause we invest in our volunteers (our training and support is high quality), we ask that volunteers see this not as a short-term role but something you're likely to do more long-term.\n\n## Travel details\n\nCourses and groups can be run online or in-person at AfH approved local venues volunteers identify.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nIf volunteers run an in-person course in their local community venue expenses will be reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://actionforhappiness.org/themes/custom/afh/logo.svg",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GTdJKYA1#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Action for Happiness Volunteer",
