            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000UoLWNYA3",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000UoLWNYA3/royal-national-institute-of-blind-people-rnib",
            "name": "Royal National Institute of Blind People - RNIB",
            "website": "https://stirlingvolunteering.org/profile/RoyalNationalInstituteofBlindPeople-RNIB",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000084ilqYAA",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000084ilqYAA/sooty-box-collections-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-01-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-13",
                    "title": "Sooty Box Collections Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSooty Box Collections Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\n<p>Sooty, the famous loveable bear and national treasure, has featured on RNIB&rsquo;s collection boxes for more than 50 years. With your support, RNIB has raised more than &pound;13 million in public donations collected in our iconic Sooty boxes.<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nJoin our community of amazing volunteer Sooty box collectors and help us to provide blind and partially sighted people with the support they need. RNIB urgently needs volunteers to collect and bank donations received through our Sooty boxes, which play a vital role in generating income and raising our profile in local communities. This role is completely flexible, can be performed by individuals, pairs or groups and the time you dedicate to it is entirely up to you and your commitments. You can give your time as little or as often as you like!<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nPlease note: Volunteers will be expected to use their own transportation and ideally should have access to a car. Mileage or transport costs will be reimbursed.</p>\n\n## Experience required\n\nGood organisational skills\nTrustworthy, enthusiastic and self-motivated\nAre willing to travel in and around the local area\nComfortable working on your own\nAbility to send and receive emails.",
