        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000UsuYiYAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000UsuYiYAJ/community-carrot-ltd-east-lothian",
            "name": "Community Carrot Ltd (East Lothian)",
            "description": "The Crunchy is a whole foods gem; a community hub; a beacon of sustainability; a social whirl; a refillery; a local employer; a supplier to local businesses; a green campaigner; a local produce purchaser; a cooking tips and recipe exchange; a purveyor of food for tight budgets, seasonal celebrations, exotic recipe demands, luxurious treats and the simple basics of the weekly shop.",
            "website": "https://communitycarrot.scot/",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEngagement",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Engagement"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HFEthYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HFEthYAH/community-connector",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-09",
                    "title": "Community Connector",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThis is a food delivery service and befriending role connecting some of our more vulnerable members of the community to the Crunchy Carrot. Being a volunteer connector (befriender) means making a real difference to someone’s life. You will carry out a purely social role and do not undertake any personal care or domestic duties. Volunteers are matched with a suitable Crunchy Customer. A variety of factors are considered in the matching process, including where both parties live and their interests. Each match will be for 4-12 months, depending on the needs of the person receiving support.\n\n## Experience required\n\nBefriending / Mentoring; Driving; First Aid / Medical / Therapy\n\n## Training details\n\nAn induction to the role and the Community Carrot and additional training might come available to support the role. for example, grief training and first aid.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nCommitment 1 Year 2 Hours, Weekly\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nAll transport costs are covered at 45p per mile\r\nExpenses also paid for electric cars and even riding a bike!",
