        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000VAyNlYAL",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000VAyNlYAL/lets-talk-about-loss",
            "name": "Let’s Talk About Loss",
            "description": "Let’s Talk About Loss is a charity supporting 18-35 year olds who have been bereaved. Our vision is that no young griever grieves alone, and we offer peer-led meet ups, a blog with advice and tips, and events and campaigns to tackle the taboo of grief across the UK.",
            "website": "https://www.letstalkaboutloss.org",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/SelfHelpSupport",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Self-Help / Support"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/YoungPeople",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Young People"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008FewbYAC",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008FewbYAC/grief-meet-up-host",
                    "publishStart": "2025-01-31",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Grief Meet Up Host",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nVolunteer Hosts organise and facilitate monthly peer-led meet up groups to provide safe, welcoming spaces for young grievers aged 18-35 to talk about loss.\n\n## Description\n\nCreate spaces with your Co-Host that are safe, supportive, open and empowering through organising a monthly meet up in a social setting. Some months might be reflective, others activity based. \r\n\r\nEach group has at least 2 Hosts who work together to plan the meet ups, ensuring that all activities are accessible and appropriate, and venues booked in advance if required. Facilitate conversations about grief during the meet up. Be the admin of a Facebook group for your meet up to promote up-coming events. Access an email account for your group where you can reply to any enquiries that come in for your meet up and keep on top of communications. Complete safeguarding training and follow the process if a concern is raised. Update your Host Co-ordinator on how your group is going, and contact them at any point if you need support with running your meet up.\n\n## Experience required\n\n· Aged 18-35\r\n· Personal bereavement experience\r\n· Bereaved for at least 1 year\r\n· Empathetic, organised, reliable\r\n· Minimum commitment to the role of 1 year\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining and induction includes afeguarding, facilitation and specific types of bereavement. Induction is before/during the first 3 months including interactive onboarding journal. Regular support from a Host Coordinator and ongoing training offered to all volunteers.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDundee City Centre\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe don’t cover travel expenses (once a month to city centre) but don’t expect volunteers to be out of pocket by running these groups so we invite Hosts to get in touch to discuss this if required.\n\n## Taster details\n\nWe ask potential volunteer Hosts to attend 3 meet ups to understand how they run and get a feel for if it is the right role at this time.",
