        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000VF6xvYAD",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000VF6xvYAD/prince-princess-of-wales-hospice",
            "name": "Prince & Princess of Wales Hospice",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/PrincePrincessofWalesHospice",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HnlbtYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HnlbtYAB/drive-for-a-cause-volunteer-retail-driver-clutha-house-glasgow",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-22",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-03",
                    "title": "Drive for a Cause – Volunteer Retail Driver (Clutha House, Glasgow)",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDrive for a Cause – Volunteer Retail Driver (Clutha House, Glasgow)\n\n## Description\n\n<p><strong>Drive. Deliver. Make a difference across Glasgow.</strong></p>\n\n<p>A flexible, Glasgow-wide volunteering role that keeps the hospice shops stocked and running, helping raise vital funds for local hospice care through practical driving and stock support.</p>\n\n<h3>Looking for a volunteering role that gets you <strong>out and about across Glasgow</strong>, meets great people, and directly supports a vital local cause?</h3>\n\n<p>The Prince &amp; Princess of Wales Hospice charity shops raise essential funds to support hospice care for patients and families across the city. We&rsquo;re looking for <strong>friendly, reliable Volunteer Retail Drivers &amp; Stock Support Volunteers</strong> to help keep our retail operations running smoothly behind the scenes.</p>\n\n<p>This is a practical, active role where you&rsquo;ll support the movement of donated stock between our <strong>warehouse and hospice shops across the Glasgow area</strong>. You&rsquo;ll work closely with shop managers and the retail team to ensure shops are well stocked and ready for customers.</p>\n\n<p>Some days you&rsquo;ll be working alongside others, and other times you may be working independently &mdash; <strong>no two shifts are the same</strong>.</p>\n\n<p><strong>What you&rsquo;ll be doing</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Driving between our warehouse and hospice shops across Glasgow</li>\n\t<li>Delivering and collecting donated stock between shop locations</li>\n\t<li>Assisting with the movement of donations, including bags and small furniture items</li>\n\t<li>Helping deliver or collect small furniture items to and from customers&rsquo; homes</li>\n\t<li>Supporting shop managers with stock distribution and logistics</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>What we&rsquo;re looking for</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>A full, valid UK driving licence</li>\n\t<li>Confidence driving around Glasgow</li>\n\t<li>Comfortable lifting and carrying donation bags and items</li>\n\t<li>Happy working both independently and as part of a team</li>\n\t<li>Friendly and reliable</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>No previous experience is needed&mdash;just a positive attitude and a willingness to help. You&rsquo;ll be making a real difference, meeting new people, and supporting hospice care in your local community.</p>\n\n<h3><strong>Support You&rsquo;ll Receive</strong></h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>A warm welcome and introduction to the hospice retail operation</li>\n\t<li>Role guidance and ongoing support from shop/retail staff</li>\n\t<li>Training and support around safe working practices (including manual handling where required)</li>\n\t<li>Clear instructions for collections/deliveries and who to contact during shifts</li>\n\t<li>A chance to build confidence and skills in a supportive team environment</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3><strong>Commitment &amp; Timing</strong></h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Volunteering is <strong>flexible</strong> and can be arranged to suit your availability</li>\n\t<li>Shifts are typically agreed in advance with the retail team</li>\n\t<li>Regular weekly or fortnightly support is welcomed, but this can be discussed</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><em>(Exact days/times may vary depending on shop needs, stock movements and planned collections.)</em></p>\n\n<h3><strong>Location: Glasgow Wide Area</strong> &ndash; across the Prince &amp; Princess of Wales Hospice shop network and associated stock/warehouse locations.</h3>\n\n<p><strong>Interested?</strong><br />\nPlease click the &lsquo;apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). A coordinator will be in touch by email or phone. If you haven&rsquo;t heard back within 5 working days, please check your junk/spam folder or contact the organisation using the details provided. You can also contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org or apply online:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.princeandprincessofwaleshospice.org.uk/how-you-can-help/volunteering\">The Prince &amp; Princess of Wales Hospice | Volunteering | The Prince &amp; Princess of Wales Hospice</a></p>\n\n<p>After you click <strong>Apply online</strong>:</p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Your application is sent to the hospice</li>\n\t<li>They review it</li>\n\t<li>They contact you by <strong>email/phone</strong> to discuss next steps (chat/induction/first shift)</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>If you don&rsquo;t hear back in <strong>5 working days</strong>, check junk/spam or follow up.</p>\n\n## Experience required\n\nFull, valid UK driving licence\nConfident driving in and around Glasgow\nFriendly, reliable and punctual\nGood communication and interpersonal skills\nAble to work independently and as part of a team\nComfortable lifting and carrying bags of donations and small furniture items\nOrganised and able to follow instructions\nPositive attitude and willingness to help\n\nNo previous retail or volunteering experience is required – full training and support will be provided.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBy Subway: Approximately a 5-minute walk from Kinning Park Station.\nBy Bus: Several local bus routes stop nearby on Paisley Road West and Scotland Street.\nBy Car: Limited on-street parking is available in the surrounding area.\nBy Bike or Walking: Easily accessible via local walking and cycling routes.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nbus travel to and from shift",
