                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000ILTflYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000ILTflYAH/book-sorting-for-prince-princess-of-wales-hospice",
                    "publishStart": "2026-10-05",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-02",
                    "title": "Book Sorting for Prince & Princess of Wales Hospice",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBook Sorting for Prince & Princess of Wales Hospice\n\n## Description\n\nThe The Prince &amp; Princess of Wales Hospice is expanding its online retail operations and is looking for a dedicated Books Sorting &amp; Curation Volunteer to help increase sales through our online shop. You will play an important part in raising vital funds that enable us to provide specialist palliative care for individuals and families across Glasgow.\n\nThis role focuses on sorting donated books into different categories and identifying rare or collectible items that could be suitable for selling online. Your contribution will help us maximise the value of donated books and support our fundraising efforts.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nAs a Books Sorting &amp; Curation Volunteer, you will:\n\n\n\t\n\tSort donated books by genre, author, and condition\n\t\n\t\n\tOrganise books into clear, logical categories\n\t\n\t\n\tIdentify rare, unusual, or collectible items for sale\n\t\n\t\n\tWork collaboratively with our existing online sales volunteers\n\t\n\t\n\tQuality-check books before they move to the sales team\n\t\n\t\n\tHelp maintain an organised work area and book storage system\n\t\n\n\nThis role is ideal for people who love books, enjoy organising, and want to support hospice care in a practical, flexible way.\n\nWhat We&rsquo;re Looking For\n\n\n\tSomeone who enjoys books and organising\n\tGood attention to detail\n\tAbility to work independently or with a small team\n\n\nCommitment &amp; Timing\n\n\n\tFlexible hours &ndash; typically 3&ndash;4 hour shifts\n\tWeekdays and weekends available\n\tMinimum suggested commitment: 2&ndash;4 hours per week\n\tThe role can accommodate volunteers who need flexible or changing schedules\n\n\nSupport You&rsquo;ll Receive\n\n\n\tA friendly, welcoming volunteer team\n\tClear guidance, checklists, and templates for creating book bundles and listings\n\tStaff available on-site to assist with questions and quality checking\n\n\nIf you are interested please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on info@volunteerglasgow.org.&nbsp;\n\n## Experience required\n\n•\tStrong organisational skills for sorting and categorising books\n•\tGood attention to detail when checking condition and quality\n•\tAbility to identify genres, authors, and popular themes\n•\tAbility to work independently and manage small tasks\n•\tInterest in books, reading, or online selling (helpful but not required)\n\n## Travel details\n\nAddress: 120 Cornwall Street South, Kinning Park, Glasgow, G41 1AF\nBy Subway: Kinning Park Subway Station is approximately a 10-minute walk away. \nBy bus: Several bus services stop in the Kinning Park area, including services along Paisley Road West. Moovit\nBy car: The location is close to the M8, M74 and M77, with easy access from Glasgow city centre. \nOn foot: The building is Clutha House, on the west side of Cornwall Street South, opposite the Claremont Centre.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\ncity bus travel to and from opportunity",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
