                    "title": "The Prince & Princess of Wales Hospice Retail Shop Volunteer - Oswald Street",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThe Prince & Princess of Wales Hospice Retail Shop Volunteer - Oswald Street\n\n## Description\n\nWould you like to make a difference in your community while meeting new people and having fun?\nJoin our welcoming team of volunteers at our Oswald Street shop location. Help keep our Hospice shops running &mdash; raising vital funds to support people and families across Glasgow and East Renfrewshire living with life-limiting conditions.\n\nWhat you&rsquo;ll do:\n\n\n\tGreet and help customers, creating a friendly shopping experience\n\n\n\n\tSort, price, and display donated items\n\n\n\n\tKeep the shop tidy, organised, and inviting\n\n\n\n\tUse the till and card machine (full training provided)\n\n\n\n\tBe part of a supportive, caring team\n\n\nWhat you&rsquo;ll gain:\n\n\n\tA real sense of purpose and community connection\n\n\n\n\tNew friends and valuable retail skills\n\n\n\n\tExperience for your CV or future job applications\n\n\n\n\tThe satisfaction of knowing your time helps others receive free, specialist care\n\n\nWhat we&rsquo;re looking for:\n\n\n\tFriendly, reliable people with a positive attitude\n\n\n\n\tTeam players who enjoy helping others\n\n\n\n\tNo experience needed &mdash; just enthusiasm and kindness!\n\n\nTime commitment:\n\nWe&rsquo;re flexible &mdash; most volunteers give&nbsp;2&ndash;3 hours a week, but any time you can spare makes a difference.\n\nHow to apply:\n\nYou can&nbsp;apply online here:&nbsp;??&nbsp;www.princeandprincessofwaleshospice.org.uk/volunteer\nOr simply pop into one of our&nbsp;City Centre shops&nbsp;&mdash; on&nbsp;Queen Street, Union Street, or Oswald Street&nbsp;&mdash; and speak to the Shop Manager for a friendly chat.\n\nYour time and smile can brighten someone&rsquo;s day &mdash; join us and be part of something special.\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). The coordinator will then contact you by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder for your emails, just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow at&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org\n\n## Experience required\n\nFriendly and approachable with good customer service skills\nGood communication skills and the ability to work as part of a team\nEnthusiastic and willing to get involved\nReliable and punctual\nA positive attitude and willingness to learn\nAn interest in retail is helpful but no previous retail experience is required\n\n## Travel details\n\nBy train: Travel to Glasgow Central Station. Exit the station onto Hope Street, turn left and walk down toward Argyle Street. Turn right onto Argyle Street, then left onto Oswald Street. 5 Oswald Street is a few minutes’ walk from the station.\n\nBy subway: Travel to St Enoch Station. From St Enoch Square, walk west along Argyle Street, then turn left onto Oswald Street. It’s roughly a 5-minute walk.\n\nBy bus: Get off at Oswald Street/Midland Street or Oswald Street/Argyle Street. Both stops ar\n\n## Travel expenses\n\ncity bus travel to and from shop",
