                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Faw3FYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Faw3FYAR/copy-be-part-of-something-new-sauchiehall-street-hospice-shop-volunteers-wanted",
                    "publishStart": "2026-02-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-28",
                    "title": "COPY - Be Part of Something New – Sauchiehall Street Hospice Shop Volunteers Wanted!",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCOPY - Be Part of Something New – Sauchiehall Street Hospice Shop Volunteers Wanted!\n\n## Description\n\n<p>We&rsquo;re opening a brand new hospice retail shop on Sauchiehall Street this June &mdash; and we&rsquo;re looking for enthusiastic volunteers to help us launch it!</p>\n\n<p>This is your chance to be part of something from the very beginning. You&rsquo;ll join our retail team ahead of the opening, train in our busy city centre shops (Union Street and Oswald Street), and then move into our brand new Sauchiehall Street location when the doors open.</p>\n\n<p>If you enjoy meeting people, working as part of a friendly team, and supporting a great local cause, we&rsquo;d love to hear from you.</p>\n\n<p><strong>What you&rsquo;ll be doing:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Welcoming and assisting customers</li>\n\t<li>Sorting, pricing, and displaying donated items</li>\n\t<li>Creating eye-catching shop displays</li>\n\t<li>Operating the till (full training provided)</li>\n\t<li>Helping keep the shop tidy, organised, and inviting</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>What we&rsquo;re looking for:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Friendly and approachable</li>\n\t<li>Reliable and happy to get involved</li>\n\t<li>Comfortable working both independently and as part of a team</li>\n\t<li>Interested in supporting hospice care in your local community</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Training Details:&nbsp;</strong><br />\nVolunteers will begin training in our Union Street and Oswald Street shops before moving to the new Sauchiehall Street location ahead of its estimated June opening.</p>\n\n<p>Whether you can volunteer one shift a week or more, we&rsquo;d love you to join us and help make this exciting new shop a success.</p>\n\n<p>If you are interested,&nbsp;please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when&nbsp;registered and&nbsp;logged in). You&nbsp;will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that&nbsp;doesn&rsquo;t&nbsp;work&nbsp;out,&nbsp;then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:info@volunteerglasgow.org\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">info@volunteerglasgow.org.</a>&nbsp;</p>\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous retail experience needed — we’ll show you everything\n\n## Travel details\n\nYou will start off training at the Union Street and/or Oswald Street shop locations, then move to Sauchiehall Street when the shop opens.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\ntravel",
