                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000G2iN7YAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000G2iN7YAJ/join-our-treasure-hunting-team-hospice-volunteer-donation-sorter-at-clutha-house",
                    "publishStart": "2026-03-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-17",
                    "title": "Join Our Treasure-Hunting Team! – Hospice Volunteer Donation Sorter at Clutha House",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nJoin Our Treasure-Hunting Team! – Hospice Volunteer Donation Sorter at Clutha House\n\n## Description\n\n<p>Volunteering at The Prince &amp; Princess of Wales Hospice offers an incredible opportunity to make a meaningful difference to patients, their families, and the wider community. Whether you&rsquo;re looking to give back, gain new skills, or become part of a community-driven environment, our hospice offers a variety of volunteer roles to suit everyone. By joining our volunteer team, you can help in our hospice, shops, warehouse, or support fundraising efforts.</p>\n\n<p>If you&rsquo;re ready to make a real impact, this could be your chance. Here&#39;s why our volunteers are vital to the success of our hospice and how you can get involved.</p>\n\n<p>The Prince &amp; Princess of Wales retail team is looking for volunteer Donation Sorters.&nbsp;You&#39;ll play an important behind-the-scenes role by identifying and preparing items with online selling potential. Every hidden gem you uncover helps maximise the value of donations and supports specialist hospice care.</p>\n\n<p>Gain practical experience in retail, stock handling, and identifying quality items while developing valuable skills for your CV. Be part of a welcoming team, meet new people, and enjoy flexible volunteering opportunities (around 3 hours per week).</p>\n\n<p>No previous experience is required&mdash;just a good eye for detail, an interest in fashion, collectibles or unique items, and a willingness to learn. Full training will be provided.</p>\n\n<h3><strong>Who Would Suit This Role?</strong></h3>\n\n<p>Someone who:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Enjoys practical, hands-on activities.</li>\n\t<li>Likes discovering hidden gems among donations.</li>\n\t<li>Can work as part of a team.</li>\n\t<li>Wants to support a local charity.</li>\n\t<li>Is reasonably active and happy with light lifting and sorting tasks.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3><strong>What you&#39;ll be doing</strong></h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Sort through donated items to identify those suitable for online sale</li>\n\t<li>Spot unique, collectible or high-value items</li>\n\t<li>Prepare and organise stock for the eBay team</li>\n\t<li>Work with staff and volunteers to maximise the value of donations</li>\n\t<li>Help grow our online sales and boost hospice fundraising</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3><strong>What You&#39;ll Gain</strong></h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Experience in retail and warehouse operations.</li>\n\t<li>Knowledge of stock processing and merchandising.</li>\n\t<li>Teamworking and communication skills.</li>\n\t<li>Flexible volunteering to fit around your schedule.</li>\n\t<li>References and skills certification.</li>\n\t<li>The satisfaction of directly supporting hospice care across Glasgow.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3><strong>Support to Volunteers</strong><br />\nYou&#39;ll receive a warm welcome from our Volunteer Services Team, along with a comprehensive induction and orientation before you begin.&nbsp;</h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>A comprehensive introduction/orientation before starting.</li>\n\t<li>On-the-job training and job shadowing.</li>\n\t<li>A designated point of contact for support.</li>\n\t<li>Recognition and appreciation for their contribution.</li>\n\t<li>Reimbursement of reasonable travel expenses.</li>\n\t<li>Flexible volunteering to fit around personal commitments.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>If you are interested, please click the <strong>&#39;Apply&#39;</strong> button below (available when registered and logged in). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, please check your junk/spam folder before contacting the organisation using the details provided. If you&#39;re still unable to reach us, you can also contact Volunteer Glasgow at <strong>info@volunteerglasgow.org</strong></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n## Experience required\n\nComfortable using a computer (or happy to learn)\nFriendly, reliable, and detail-focused\nAn interest in online selling, fashion, collectibles, or photography\nNo experience needed — full training provided\n\n## Travel details\n\nBy subway (fastest from city centre)\n\nTake the Glasgow Subway to Kinning Park station.\n\nExit the station and turn right onto Scotland Street.\n\nWalk 2–3 minutes.\n\nTurn left onto Cornwall Street South.\n\nClutha House is a short walk along the street.\n\nBy train\n\nGo to Glasgow Central Station.\n\nTake a local train to Exhibition Centre or Pollokshields East.\n\nFrom either station, take a short taxi or local bus to Kinning Park.\n\nAsk for Cornwall Street South — Clutha House is there.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
