                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HiIsHYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HiIsHYAV/join-our-union-street-shop-as-a-retail-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-10",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-06",
                    "title": "Join Our Union Street Shop as a Retail Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nJoin Our Union Street Shop as a Retail Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nYour time in our shop helps people when they need it most.\n\nBe part of a welcoming retail team where every volunteer shift helps transform donated items into vital funding for specialist hospice care across Glasgow. Gain valuable retail experience, develop new skills, meet new people, and make a genuine difference in your local community&mdash;all with flexible volunteering to suit your lifestyle.\n\nLocation\n\nUnion Street Hospice Shop\nGlasgow City Centre\n\nAbout PPWH Shops\n\nThe Prince &amp; Princess of Wales Hospice runs a network of vibrant retail shops across Glasgow, helping to raise vital funds to support people living with life-limiting illnesses and their families. These shops offer high-quality pre-loved clothing, accessories, homeware and unique finds, all while promoting sustainability and community connection. Our shops are friendly, welcoming spaces where volunteers play a key role in delivering great customer experiences and ensuring every donation makes a difference. Our busy Union Street shop is looking for volunteers!\n\nAbout the Role\n\nWe&rsquo;re looking for friendly and reliable Retail Volunteers to help and support our&nbsp; Hospice Shop on Union Street, Glasgow. Our shops play a vital role in funding specialist hospice care across Glasgow, and volunteers are at the heart of everything we do.\n\nAs a Retail Volunteer, you&rsquo;ll help create a warm, welcoming, and organised shop environment for customers, donors, and supporters. Whether you&#39;re on the shop floor greeting customers or helping behind the scenes with donations, your time will directly support the work of the Hospice.\n\nWhat You&rsquo;ll Do\n\nTypical volunteering activities include:\n\n\n\tGiving customers a warm and friendly welcome\n\tAssisting with sales and serving on the till (full training provided)\n\tSorting, organising, and preparing donated items for the shop floor\n\tCreating eye-catching displays and helping merchandise stock\n\tKeeping the shop clean, tidy, and safe for everyone\n\tHelping accept donations and thanking donors\n\tSupporting safe customer flow in a busy city-centre environment\n\tWorking alongside shop staff and other volunteers as part of a supportive team\n\n\nWhen We Need You (Suggested Timings)\n\nWe offer flexible volunteering to suit you.\n\nTypical shifts include:\n\n\n\tMorning: 10:00am &ndash; 1:00pm\n\tAfternoon: 1:00pm &ndash; 4:00pm\n\tFull day (optional): 10:00am &ndash; 4:00pm\n\n\nYou can volunteer:\n\n\n\tOnce a week\n\tOnce a fortnight\n\tOr on a flexible, ad-hoc basis\n\n\nMost volunteers give 2&ndash;3 hours per week, but any time is welcomed.\n\nThe shop will be open Monday&ndash;Sunday.\n\nHow We Will Support You&nbsp;\n\nVolunteers at PPWH are fully supported by our staff and volunteer team. We provide:\n\nComprehensive induction\n\nIncluding:\n\n\n\tWelcome briefing\n\tIntroduction to PPWH and the retail team\n\tShop tour and meet-and-greet\n\tHealth &amp; safety orientation\n\tRole overview tailored to your interests\n\n\nFull training\n\nYou&rsquo;ll receive training in:\n\n\n\tCustomer service\n\tTill and card-machine use\n\tDonation handling\n\tDisplay &amp; merchandising\n\tShop safety procedures\n\tEmergency protocols\n\tManual handling (if needed)\n\n\nOngoing supervision &amp; support\n\n\n\tA named Shop Manager and Assistant Manager will support you each shift\n\tRegular check-ins to see how you&rsquo;re getting on\n\tOpen-door approach &ndash; ask questions anytime\n\tOpportunities to learn new tasks at your pace\n\n\nExpenses &amp; wellbeing\n\n\n\tTravel expenses reimbursed (in line with PPWH volunteer policy)\n\tBreaks provided during longer shifts\n\tA friendly, supportive environment where volunteers are valued\n\n\nDevelopment opportunities\n\n\n\tConfidence building\n\tRetail skills for your CV\n\tChance to take on additional responsibilities if you wish\n\tInvitations to volunteer celebration events\n\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on info@volunteerglasgow.org\n\nFollow this link to apply online:&nbsp;Volunteer Application | The Prince &amp; Princess of Wales Hospice\n\nAfter You Hit &quot;Apply&quot;\n\n\n\tConfirmation email sent.\n\tFollow-up contact (email or call) to arrange a chat.\n\tInduction session at the location\n\tStart volunteering with agreed-upon shift times.\n\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## Experience required\n\nExperience is not required. We can train you!\n\n## Travel details\n\nOur Union Street shop is located in the heart of Glasgow city centre, directly opposite Glasgow Central Station and just a short walk from St Enoch Subway Station.\n\nBy train: Exit Glasgow Central Station via the main entrance. Cross the road onto Union Street – the shop is directly opposite the station.\nBy Subway: From St Enoch Station, it's approximately a 3-minute walk via Argyle Street to Union Street.\nBy bus: Numerous bus services stop near Glasgow Central Station and along Union Street,\n\n## Travel expenses\n\ncity bus travel to and from shifts",
