        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000W4oJzYAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000W4oJzYAJ/hanover-scotland-aberdeen-city",
            "name": "Hanover Scotland (Aberdeen City)",
            "description": "Hanover has been housing and supporting people in Scotland for more than forty years.\r\n\r\nOur core purpose is to help older people feel safe and secure at home and to live fulfilling and independent lives. This sums up our commitment to housing for life.\r\n\r\nWe provide and manage a wide range of housing and services, mainly for older people. We currently manage more than 5,000 homes throughout Scotland.\r\n\r\nWe provide a range of housing and tenure types to meet the different support needs of older people, allowing them to retain their independence within a local community and enjoy as much privacy or company as they wish.",
            "website": "https://www.hanover.scot/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC014738"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/HousingHomelessnessness",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Housing / Homelessnessness"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/HousingAssociation",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Housing Association"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/Volunteering",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Volunteering"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEngagement",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Engagement"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009VsgTYAS",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009VsgTYAS/volunteer-gardeners",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-10",
                    "title": "Volunteer Gardeners",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nHanover has been housing and supporting people in Scotland for more than forty years. Our core purpose is to help older people feel safe and secure at home and to live fulfilling and independent lives. This sums up our commitment to housing for life. We provide and manage a wide range of housing and services, mainly for older people. We currently manage more than 5,000 homes throughout Scotland.  We provide a range of housing and tenure types to meet the different support needs of older people, allowing people to retain their independence within a local community and enjoy as much privacy or company as they wish.\r\n\r\nWe currently have a great opportunity to help with gardening tasks in one of our developments based in Aberdeen City.\r\n\r\nThe role involves assisting with general light gardening activities in our residents’ areas to provide an attractive and enhanced environment. Garden maintenance (light activities) – including weeding, pruning, tidying and path maintenance. Working alongside our residents creating a gardening club. Volunteers will have access to tools required for the role. Relevant guidance, induction and support is provided to all volunteers.\r\n\r\nA great opportunity to help and make a difference for our residents and the local community. If interested in helping/for more information please contact James Brown at email: jbrown@hanover.scot or telephone: 07484532052\n\n## Description\n\nHanover has been housing and supporting people in Scotland for more than forty years. Our core purpose is to help older people feel safe and secure at home and to live fulfilling and independent lives. This sums up our commitment to housing for life. We provide and manage a wide range of housing and services, mainly for older people. We currently manage more than 5,000 homes throughout Scotland.  We provide a range of housing and tenure types to meet the different support needs of older people, allowing people to retain their independence within a local community and enjoy as much privacy or company as they wish.\r\n\r\nWe currently have a great opportunity to help with gardening tasks in one of our developments based in Aberdeen City.\r\n\r\nThe role involves assisting with general light gardening activities in our residents’ areas to provide an attractive and enhanced environment. Garden maintenance (light activities) – including weeding, pruning, tidying and path maintenance. Working alongside our residents creating a gardening club. Volunteers will have access to tools required for the role. Excellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. All volunteers will get an induction, where we will introduce them to our staff, residents and go over safety features within our developments. We look to offer training as appropriate for the role. Our volunteers all get a named member of staff for direct support as well.\r\n\r\nA great opportunity to help and make a difference for our residents and the local community. If interested in helping/for more information please contact James Brown at email: jbrown@hanover.scot or telephone: 07484532052\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Horticultural qualifications are necessary, as long as you have the willingness to help, are patient and have confidence in your own gardening skills, being fond of a chat is helpful too, as this will help you build a rapport with our residents.\n\n## Training details\n\nExcellent support and relevant guidance is provided to all volunteers. All volunteers will get an induction, where we will introduce them to our staff, residents and go over safety features within our developments. We look to offer training as appropriate for the role. Our volunteer will have a named member of staff for direct support.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nFlexible times available to volunteer. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe Volunteer Opportunity is within one of our developments based in Aberdeen City.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPublic transport, expenses are reimbursed monthly.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/scvo-org.appspot.com/o/milo%2FVolunteering_Opportunity__c%2Fcbb47dc3-252e-4191-8646-e2e41bf68b9b%2FzlyK8ILxtla7uggEID8JdqJPokR2%2Flisting.jpg?alt=media&token=7177ba9d-8dc1-42db-8c1a-f9ed051348d7",
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000009VsgTYAS#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Volunteer Gardeners",
                        "description": "No Horticultural qualifications are necessary, as long as you have the willingness to help, are patient and have confidence in your own gardening skills, being fond of a chat is helpful too, as this will help you build a rapport with our residents.",
                        "commitment": "Flexible times available to volunteer. All help makes a difference and is greatly appreciated.",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000009VsgTYAS/volunteer-gardeners?#modal_register_a0gQD000009VsgTYAS",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
