        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000W8TCEYA3",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000W8TCEYA3/cace-cumbernauld-action-for-care-of-the-elderly",
            "name": "CACE - Cumbernauld Action for Care of the Elderly",
            "website": "https://vanl.teamkinetic.co.uk/profile/CACE-CumbernauldActionforCareoftheElderly",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000EzrLwYAJ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000EzrLwYAJ/befriender-in-the-g69-area",
                    "publishStart": "2026-01-26",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-11",
                    "title": "Befriender in the G69 area",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBefriender in the G69 area\n\n## Description\n\n<p><strong>Help Turn Loneliness into Connection - Become a Volunteer Befriender with CACE</strong></p>\n\n<p>Loneliness can affect anyone &mdash; but together, we can change that.</p>\n\n<p>CACE is a vibrant, community-based charity supporting people across Cumbernauld, Kilsyth, Croy, the Northern Corridor and surrounding areas. We&rsquo;re looking for kind, friendly and reliable volunteers to join our Befriending Team and make a genuine difference in someone&rsquo;s life.</p>\n\n<p>As a volunteer befriender, you&rsquo;ll be matched with an older person (65+) and offer something incredibly powerful: your time, your company, and a friendly face. The support you provide could include:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Enjoying relaxed chats over a cup of tea&nbsp;</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Offering a listening ear and meaningful companionship</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Reminiscing together using memory boxes</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Encouraging and supporting attendance at social activities</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Helping someone reconnect with their community and rebuild confidence</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>What&rsquo;s in it for you?</strong><br />\nVolunteering with CACE isn&rsquo;t just rewarding &mdash; it&rsquo;s also a great way to build skills, confidence and experience that really stand out on your CV. You&rsquo;ll develop highly valued soft skills such as compassion, active listening and reflection, all while improving lives and strengthening communities.</p>\n\n<p>We&rsquo;re committed to supporting our volunteers every step of the way. You&rsquo;ll receive:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Comprehensive training and a full induction</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Ongoing support and supervision</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Fun volunteer social events ??</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Opportunities to get involved in other volunteering roles</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Many of our volunteers go on to careers in health and social care, and we&rsquo;re always happy to provide references for successful volunteers.</p>\n\n<p>Befriending can take place <strong>in person</strong> (in the service user&rsquo;s home) or <strong>by telephone</strong>, depending on your availability and preferences.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Ready to make a difference?</strong><br />\nClick the apply button below to get started.<br />\nOr, if you&rsquo;d like to find out more, email us at <strong>info@careatcace.com</strong>.</p>\n\n<p>Your time could mean the world to someone.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><u>Training dates:</u></p>\n\n<p>Wednesday 18th&nbsp;February 5:30pm - 7:30pm</p>\n\n<p>Thursday 12th&nbsp;March 1:30pm - 3:30pm</p>\n\n<p><br />\nIf you&#39;re interested, please click the &lsquo;apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will then be contacted by the Engagement and Development Lead, Stewart by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, please phone Stewart on 01236 451 393 or 07876 771 510 or email stewart@careatcace.com or info@careatcace.com</p>\n\n## Experience required\n\n• Is trustworthy and reliable\n• Is responsible and patient\n• Communicates easily with different people\n• Is resourceful and well organised\n• Truly cares about others",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
