                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JPqq7YAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JPqq7YAD/befriending-in-kilsyth",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-04",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-08",
                    "title": "Befriending in Kilsyth",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nBefriending in Kilsyth\n\n## Description\n\nCould One Hour a Week Change Someone&rsquo;s Life? ??\n\nHelp turn loneliness into friendship. Become a Volunteer Befriender with CACE!\n\nDo you have just one hour a week to spare? Could you make time for a friendly chat, a cup of tea and a little companionship?\n\nFor an older person experiencing loneliness, that one hour could mean the world.\n\nAt CACE, we believe nobody should feel alone. We&rsquo;re a vibrant, community-based charity supporting people across Cumbernauld, Kilsyth, Croy, the Northern Corridor and surrounding areas. We&#39;re looking for kind, friendly and reliable volunteers to join our Befriending Team and help bring connection, confidence and friendship into the lives of older people aged 65+.\n\nWhat does being a Befriender involve?\n\nIt&#39;s simple: sharing your time and being there for someone.\n\nYou&#39;ll be matched with an older person and, together, you&#39;ll build a friendly connection through activities such as:\n\n\n? Enjoying a relaxed chat over a cuppa.\n?? Sharing stories, experiences and a listening ear.\n?? Providing companionship and helping someone feel less alone.\n?? Reminiscing together using memory boxes and treasured memories.\n?? Encouraging participation in social activities and helping someone reconnect with their community.\n?? Bringing a little friendship, laughter and something to look forward to each week.\n\n\nYou don&#39;t need special qualifications or previous experience. What matters most is that you&#39;re approachable, reliable, a good listener and happy to give someone your time.\n\nWhat will you get out of volunteering?\n\nVolunteering isn&#39;t just about what you give &ndash; it&#39;s also about what you gain!\n\nBeing a CACE Befriender is a fantastic opportunity to meet new people, develop valuable skills and make a real difference in your local community.\n\nYou&#39;ll have the opportunity to:\n\n\nDevelop communication, listening and interpersonal skills.\nBuild confidence and gain valuable volunteering experience.\nMake new connections and become part of a friendly team.\nGain experience that could support future opportunities in health, social care and other career paths.\nEnjoy volunteer get-togethers and social events.\nExplore other volunteering opportunities within CACE.\n\n\nAnd we&#39;ll support you every step of the way!\n\nYou&#39;ll receive:\n\n\nFull induction and comprehensive training.\nOngoing guidance, support and supervision.\nOpportunities to meet and socialise with other CACE volunteers.\nA reference for successful volunteers, where appropriate.\n\n\nMany of our volunteers have gone on to rewarding careers in health and social care, and your volunteering experience could be a great first step.\n\nWhere and how can I volunteer?\n\nWe understand that everyone has different commitments, so we aim to make befriending as flexible as possible.\n\nYou can offer support either:\n\n\nFace-to-face: Visiting an older person in their own home.\nBy telephone: Providing regular friendly chats and companionship over the phone.\n\n\nAll we ask is for around one hour a week and a commitment to building a reliable, friendly connection.\n\nCould you be the friendly face someone looks forward to seeing?\n\nYou don&#39;t have to change the world. You could change someone&#39;s week &ndash; simply by being there.\n\nOne hour. One friendship. A world of difference.\n\nIf you have a little time to give and a lot of kindness to share, we&#39;d love to hear from you!\n\nReady to get involved?\n\nClick the &#39;Apply&#39; button below to register your interest and take the first step towards becoming a CACE Volunteer Befriender.\n\nOnce you&#39;ve applied, our Engagement and Development Lead, Stewart, will get in touch by email or telephone to chat with you about the opportunity.\n\nWould you like to find out more before applying? We&#39;d be delighted to hear from you.\n\nContact Stewart:\n\n\nTelephone: 01236 451 393 or 07876 771 510\nEmail: stewart@careatcace.com\n\n\nAlternatively, email: info@careatcace.com\n\nIf you haven&#39;t heard from us within five working days of applying, please get in touch using the contact details above.\n\nGive an hour. Make a connection. Help someone feel less alone.\n\nWe look forward to welcoming you to the CACE Befriending Team!\n\n## Experience required\n\nStrong listening and good communication\nEmpathy\nUnderstanding\nPlanning\nKind\nPatient\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nMilage and token towards lunch and dinner where appropriate",
