        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000WNExbYAH",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000WNExbYAH/loch-lomond-south-community-development-trust",
            "name": "Loch Lomond South Community Development Trust",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC820718"
                }
            ],
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityCouncil",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Council"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GGUx0YAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000GGUx0YAH/chair-of-the-board-of-directors",
                    "publishStart": "2026-04-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-08",
                    "title": "Chair of the Board of Directors",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWe’re delighted to share an exciting opportunity to become Chair of the Board of Directors for Loch Lomond South Community Development Trust.\r\n\r\nWe are seeking an exceptional and passionate individual to help guide and shape the future of one of Scotland’s most iconic locations—the gateway to the Highlands and the southern shores of Loch Lomond.  At the heart of vibrant communities and a world-renowned landscape, the Trust plays a vital role in driving sustainable development, supporting local people, and shaping a shared vision for the area’s future.\r\n\r\nAs Chair, you will provide strategic leadership, support and guide the Board, build and strengthen partnerships, and help unlock opportunities that balance community wellbeing, economic growth, and environmental stewardship.  If you have the leadership experience, vision, and passion to make a lasting impact in a truly special place, we would love to hear from you.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000GGUx0YAH#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Chair of the Board of Directors",
                        "applyLink": "https://lochlomondscdt-chair.lovable.app/",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false,
                        "minimumAge": "21",
                        "theme": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Theme/LocalCommunity",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Local Community"
                            }
                        ],
                        "specialistRole": [
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/SpecialistRole/BoardTrusteeRole",
                                "skos:prefLabel": "Board/trustee role"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    "session": {
                        "type": "Session",
                        "location": [
                            {
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "G83 8QL",
                                "address": "G83 8QL",
                                "latitude": 56.00528078147448,
                                "longitude": -4.591919676250031,
                                "simd": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/SIMD/G838QL"
                            },
                            {
                                "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Geography/LocalAuthority/WestDunbartonshire",
                                "type": "Location",
                                "name": "West Dunbartonshire"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008X9sjYAC",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008X9sjYAC/trust-treasurer-director",
                    "publishStart": "2025-02-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-14",
                    "title": "Trust Treasurer (Director)",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nNo matter how good our services are, we can't properly support our users/community well if we don't have a good Board behind the team. If this sounds like you?... we would love you to consider volunteering with us for a few\r\nhours per month.\r\n\r\nThe role Treasurer, as the financial watchdog, ensuring the protection of the Trust's funds. The Treasurer is also responsible for reconciling bank statements, managing cash flow, and investing funds in accordance with the law.\r\nOur friendly forward thinking Board, is an ideal place for you to put your finance Skills to great use – previous financial practice experience, understanding the role, keeping an overview of the organisations finances, creating and presenting reports to the committee meetings and ensuring that the organisations financial policies and procedures are in place.\r\n\r\nSo, whether you are looking to use your time well, update your skills or have the chance to do something a bit new, we would love to hear from you. In return, we can offer you a warm welcome and all of the support and help you could need.\r\n\r\nWe are seeing a rise in demand for our services, everyday. Having your help will\r\nallow us to be there for the people who need us. Any time you can give will\r\nmake a real difference.\n\n## Experience required\n\nMust have a background in finance\n\n## Travel details\n\nRemote location",
