            "website": "https://ctsi.teamkinetic.co.uk/profile/Home-StartClackmanshire",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hpsm9YAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hpsm9YAB/family-support-hub-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-31",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-27",
                    "title": "Family Support Hub Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFamily Support Hub Volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nThe role of a Family Support Hub volunteer\nVolunteers will be based in public community settings, where local people can approach them for advice and guidance. Enquiries may relate to a wide range of issues, including parenting, financial pressures, or accessing local support. Where appropriate, volunteers will listen to each person&rsquo;s needs and signpost them to services that can help.\n\nKey aspects of the role\nFamily Support Hub volunteers help local people find the support they need by:\n\n\nProviding a listening ear\nUsing knowledge of local services\nCommitting to two hours per week on a scheduled day\nBeing a friendly and approachable presence\nOffering informed support through training and lived or professional experience\n\n## Experience required\n\nKindness and Compassion \nGood listener",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
