        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000Xv1VvYAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000Xv1VvYAJ/common-thread-vision",
            "name": "Common Thread Vision",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/CommonThreadVision",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000CuHldYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000CuHldYAF/fundraising-group-leader",
                    "publishStart": "2025-10-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-31",
                    "title": "Fundraising Group Leader",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nFundraising Group Leader\n\n## Description\n\n<p><strong>Fundraising Leader</strong></p>\n\n<p>Make a difference for women, with women.</p>\n\n<p>Common Thread Vision (CTV) is a small Glasgow charity &ndash; in Pollokshields &ndash; supporting older women to stay connected, independent, and well. Reducing feelings of loneliness, and isolation. We&rsquo;re looking for a&nbsp;<strong>passionate female volunteer</strong>&nbsp;to lead a friendly fundraising group and help raise vital funds for our services.</p>\n\n<p>You&rsquo;ll bring women together, share ideas, and lead enjoyable community fundraising activities like coffee mornings and bake sales &ndash; all with flexible hours and plenty of support.</p>\n\n<p><strong>This role is ideal if you want to:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Support other women in your community</li>\n\t<li>Build confidence, leadership, and teamwork skills</li>\n\t<li>Meet like-minded women and feel part of something meaningful</li>\n\t<li>Volunteer flexibly, around family or other commitments</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>What we offer:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Training, ongoing support, and expenses covered</li>\n\t<li>Flexible, home-based volunteering with local events</li>\n\t<li>Free lunch (Thursdays) and free yoga (Wednesdays)</li>\n\t<li>A welcoming, inclusive women-led environment</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>You&rsquo;ll need to be:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Aged 18+</li>\n\t<li>Friendly, organised, and enthusiastic</li>\n\t<li>Happy working with and supporting other women</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Join us and help women thrive &ndash; together.</strong></p>\n\n<p>To apply, or to find out more or for an informal chat, please contact: Hana.<br />\nEmail: commonthreadvision2024@gmail.com&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>If you&#39;re interested, send in a CV, or please click the &lsquo;apply&rsquo; button below.</p>\n\n## Experience required\n\nRequirements:\n•\tAged 18 or over\n•\tConfident, friendly, and organised\n•\tStrong communication and leadership skills\n•\tAccess to transport and flexibility to attend meetings/events\n•\tComfortable assisting at events (support provided if needed)\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nWe reimburse all pre-agreed costs at public transport rates on production of valid tickets and/or receipts.",
