                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpvSIYAZ",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HpvSIYAZ/respite-fosterer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-31",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-29",
                    "title": "Respite Fosterer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nCould you provide a temporary home for a dog awaiting rehoming? Whether they are a retired working guide dog or a dog withdrawn from training, these dogs need a safe and supportive place to stay while they await their forever home. Some may have additional medical or behavioural needs, and full training and support will be provided. Help make a difference in a dog's journey to a new family.\n\n## Description\n\nWe're looking for compassionate volunteers to provide respite fostering for dogs awaiting their forever homes. These dogs may have been withdrawn from the Guide Dogs training programme or may be retired guide dogs making the transition from working life to life as a much-loved pet. \r\n\r\nDogs leave training or retire from guiding for a variety of reasons. Some may have medical conditions, others may need support with behavioural challenges, and some are simply better suited to a different lifestyle. \r\n\r\nWhile many settle quickly, some may require extra patience, understanding and reassurance as they adjust to a new environment and routine. As a respite fosterer, you'll provide a safe, caring and supportive home during this important transition period. Your role could involve helping a dog build confidence, managing an ongoing medical condition, or simply offering stability and companionship while they await their permanent family.\r\n\r\nFull training and ongoing support are provided by Guide Dogs. By opening your home to a dog in need of temporary care, you'll play a vital role in helping them take the next step towards a happy and successful future.\n\n## Experience required\n\n• Patience and understanding.\r\n• Confidence caring for dogs.\r\n• Ability to provide a safe, stable home.\r\n• Willingness to follow training and guidance.\r\n• Good observation and communication skills.\r\n• Reliability and commitment.\r\n• Flexibility to meet individual dog needs.\r\n• Compassion and a positive attitude.\n\n## Training details\n\nFull training and ongoing support are provided to help you feel confident in your role as a Respite Fosterer. Training covers caring for a dog in your home, understanding their individual needs, and guidance on any specific health or behavioural requirements\n\n## Travel details\n\nHomebased.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note: No expenses are payable for this opportunity.",
