                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IMSGDYA5",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000IMSGDYA5/listening-ear-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-28",
                    "title": "Listening Ear Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur Listening Ear project provides social support to people who are feeling isolated as a result of their involvement with the criminal justice system.  \r\nPeople are often isolated because of the stigma that can be attached to their offence.  People with a conviction for a sexual offence (and their family members) often face the most significant isolation due to societal stigma.\r\nWe are looking for people who would be happy to volunteer one hour a week to provide social contact to someone who is feeling isolated.  \r\nNo specialist knowledge is required, simply an open, non-judgemental attitude and a friendly, listening ear. \r\nAccess to a phone is required to enable you to stay in touch with the person you have been matched with.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nOne initial, online training session. \r\nOne hour per week once matched with a supported person.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000IMSGDYA5#role",
