                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD0000095dMvYAI",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD0000095dMvYAI/ad-hoc-delivery-driver",
                    "publishStart": "2025-03-25",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-05",
                    "title": "Ad hoc delivery driver",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nRecycle Ayr is a volunteer led group that started over 2 years ago and we meet on the  first Saturday of every month at Newton Primary School with our main objective of reducing landfill waste by recycling, up cycling or reusing donations to benefit the people of Ayrshire and beyond. This is achieved by people in the community bringing unwanted items that will benefit others.\r\nThe group also support the local community of Wallacetown in the provision of furniture, clothing  and household items. \r\nThe collections are also used to support charity fundraising by collecting items that can be converted for cash. \r\n\r\nThe list of items accepted is considerable and is constantly evolving. Donated items are then used in a variety of ways in order to benefit a number of causes and persons. For example, donated milk bottle tops are passed to Pathfinder Dogs, a charity which helps visually impaired people; stationery is passed to local schools; jewellery and watches go to Kidney Research UK; used stamps are passed on to Bone Cancer Research Trust UK; used fabrics go to sewing groups for upcycling; and blankets etc. are passed on by Newton Primary School to refugees and other needy families in the area\r\nWe are currently looking to fill the following volunteer role.\r\n\r\nRole Title   Ad hoc Delivery Driver\r\nOutline of role :-\r\n\r\n-\tto drive a van on an ad hoc basis taking donated household goods and clothes to and  from Newton Primary, Ayr to a storage unit.\r\n-\tdelivering household items to homes within Wallacetown area.\r\n-\tto uplift household items from various places within Ayr area. \r\n-       the group fund the costs of hiring vehicles as required\n\n## Experience required\n\nSkills and experience required\r\nA clean driving license is required and the ability to communicate with a variety of people.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
