                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-27",
                    "title": "Volunteer Director/Board Member",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nWillow Tree Performing Arts is a Falkirk-based not-for-profit organisation providing inclusive music, drama and creative experiences for children and adults with disabilities and additional support needs, alongside opportunities for the wider community. Their structured, person-centred approach helps people feel safe enough to participate, express themselves, connect and belong. Willow Tree Performing Arts work with individuals, families, schools, care providers and community partners.\r\n\r\nWillow Tree Performing Arts are seeking 2–3 additional volunteer directors to strengthen their board and help shape the next stage of Willow Tree’s development. This is a governance and strategic leadership role rather than a session assistant role.\r\n\r\nDirectors will contribute to board discussions and decisions; help set priorities and review progress; oversee finances, sustainability and organisational risk; support good governance and inclusive practice; and bring constructive challenge and encouragement to the Founder and fellow directors. Depending on interests and experience, directors may also help develop funding opportunities, partnerships, marketing and community connections.\r\n\r\nWillow Tree particularly welcome skills in finance and governance; strategic marketing, communications or audience development; third-sector funding, commissioning or organisational development; ASN, social care or community services; and relevant lived or family experience. Applicants do not need expertise in every area or a performing arts background. A commitment to inclusion, sound judgement, reliability and the ability to work collaboratively are important.\r\n\r\nProspective volunteer directors can request a board recruitment pack and an informal conversation with the founder before applying.\n\n## Experience required\n\nCommitment to inclusion and to opportunities for people with disabilities and additional support needs; sound judgement, integrity, reliability and collaborative working.\r\nWillingness to read papers, contribute to decisions and constructively support and challenge the organisation. \r\nWelcomed experience in one or more of; finance, governance, marketing, communications, funding, organisational development, ASN, social care or community services. \r\nRelevant lived or family experience is valued. \r\nA performing arts background is not essential.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers will have a named contact and be provided with an induction and ongoing support. \r\nA Board Recruitment Pack and an informal introductory discussion or visit are available. Induction will introduce Willow Tree’s aims, activities and the director role. \r\nFurther training and development needs will be discussed and appropriate opportunities identified.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nAs a newly establishing board, Willow Tree anticipate meeting approximately every two months, with the day, time and venue to be agreed with all volunteer directors so that meetings are as accessible as possible.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe organisation is based in the Falkirk area. \r\nBoard meeting venue, online participation and any travel requirements can be discussed. Meetings can be arranged at a mutually agreed venue, with wheelchair access and accessible toilets as needed.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses for agreed Board activities will be reimbursed monthly against receipts or an agreed mileage claim.  Travel arrangements and mileage rate will be agreed in advance.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "image": "https://shorturl.at/qfKzj",
