        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000czv21YAA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000czv21YAA/penumbra-self-harm-recovery-network-scotland",
            "name": "Penumbra Self-Harm Recovery Network Scotland",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/PenumbraSelf-HarmRecoveryNetworkScotland",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000JItb2YAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000JItb2YAD/self-harm-network-scotland-live-chat-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-30",
                    "title": "Self-Harm Network Scotland - Live Chat volunteer",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nSelf-Harm Network Scotland - Live Chat volunteer\n\n## Description\n\nOur volunteers will utilise their unique understanding gained from managing their own mental health to assist staff in the smooth delivery of our Self-Harm support web chat.&nbsp;\n\nThe chat operates between 6pm-10pm, 7 days a week. We are looking for a commitment of one 4-hour shift a week, including 1 Friday or Saturday a moth. One year commitment.\n\nApplication Process \n\nApply here:&nbsp;Self-Harm Volunteer - National Self-Harm Job at Penumbra\n\nShortlisted candidates will be invited to the interview on Monday 14th Dec, and Wednesday 16th Dec 2026 interviews\n\nShortlisted candidates will need to attend Training:\n\n\n\to Self-Harm Awareness Training: Wednesday 13th January 2027 6.00 pm &ndash; 9.00 pm\n\to Text base support training: Saturday 23rd January 2027 9.00 am &ndash; 5.00 pm\n\to Escalation and Safeguarding training: Wednesday 27th January 2027 6.00 pm &ndash; 9.00 pm\n\n\nSuccessful candidates will be offered a place as a volunteer and will start their onboarding process, which includes an hour online induction and shadowing. All volunteers will need to provide 2 references and complete PVG check\n\nAll stages of the application process are online, including training and induction.\n\nClosing day to apply: Sunday 23rd Nov 2026 7pm\n\nApplication pack&nbsp;Self-Harm Volunteer Recruitment Pack.pdf\n\nGet in touch\n\nIf you have any questions please do get in touch! &nbsp;SHNSVolunteer1@penumbra.org.uk&nbsp;\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when registered and logged in). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\nPerson specification  \nAged 18 or over \nGood communication and excellent listening skills \nOpen to supporting a diverse range of people with a non-judgemental \napproach \nA kind, caring and empathetic person with a positive and hopeful attitude \nReliable and respectful \nAbility to reflect and build on experience and ask for additional support if \nrequired \nConfidence in volunteering as part of a team",
