            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000AGVoUYAX",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000AGVoUYAX/biodiversity-action-team-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2025-06-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-05-03",
                    "title": "Biodiversity Action Team Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nIn Partnership with West Dunbartonshire Council\r\nAre you passionate about nature and the great outdoors? Want to spend time making a real impact on your local environment, meet new people, and learn new skills? Then we want YOU to join our friendly conservation team!\r\n\r\nThe Conservation Volunteers, working in partnership with West Dunbartonshire Council, are on the lookout for enthusiastic volunteers to help us protect and enhance the beautiful green spaces across West Dunbartonshire. \r\n\r\nWhat You'll Be Doing: Our hands-on conservation days offer a variety of important tasks designed to improve local habitats and learn about biodiversity in your local area. Activities vary with the seasons and may include:\r\n\r\n- Removing invasive species like bracken to make way for native wildflowers\r\n- Carrying out citizen-science wildlife surveys\r\n- Repairing boardwalks to help people safely access natural areas\r\n- Tree planting to boost biodiversity and fight climate change\r\n- Building paths to improve accessibility for everyone\r\n- Clearing overgrown scrub to maintain healthy habitats\r\n\r\nNo previous experience is needed—just a willingness to get stuck in and enjoy the outdoors! \r\n\r\nWhat You'll Need: Volunteers must be 18 years or older\r\nDress for the outdoors: wear sturdy footwear and weather-appropriate clothing\r\nBring your lunch. We'll keep the kettle on with tea, coffee, and biscuits provided! Travel expenses of up to £6 are available (with a valid transport ticket) \r\n\r\nWhy Volunteer? \r\nConnect with like-minded people in your community\r\nBoost your physical and mental wellbeing\r\nLearn practical conservation skills\r\nMake a real difference to your local environment\r\nEnjoy the satisfaction of seeing the direct results of your work\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo previous experience is needed—just a willingness to get stuck in and enjoy the outdoors!\n\n## Travel details\n\nWhen and Where: Volunteering sessions run regularly every Tuesday and Friday, 10:30am – 14:30pm and will take place in The Salting Local Nature Reserve, Auchnacraig Woodland, and Faifley Knowes. \r\nThere will also be weekend sessions happening once a month, which will be advertised on the TCV Scotland Eventbrite.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses of up to £5 are available (with a valid transport ticket)",
