            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000e2Yt7YAE/biggar-museum-trust",
            "name": "Biggar Museum Trust",
            "description": "The Biggar and Upper Clydesdale Museum explores 14,000 years of rural and small town life in Upper Clydesdale. It is an independent museum managed by Biggar Museum Trust, and is heavily dependent on the work of its volunteers. \nBiggar & Upper Clydesdale Museums mission is to preserve and interpret the historic heritage of Biggar and the Upper Ward of Clydesdale. The vision of Biggar Museum Trust is upheld by the following aims, to provide an educational and enjoyable experience for all ages, to make the collection and archive as accessible to as many people as possible and to act as one of the focal points for local community endeavour. Volunteering Opportunities include Till Operators, Cataloguers, Archivist, Maintenance, Operational volunteers",
            "website": "https://www.biggarmuseumtrust.co.uk/",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC003695"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000AOnOPYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000AOnOPYA1/front-of-house-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-11-09",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-04-05",
                    "title": "Front of House Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nAs part of the ongoing customer service provided at Biggar and Upper Clydesdale Museum we are seeking to recruit Front of House Service Volunteers. This involves meeting and greeting visitors, providing information about the museum and services, assisting customers purchasing in our shop and supporting display and merchandising within the retail area. Maintaining a high standard of housekeeping and customer guidance. Opportunities to support events, school and nursery visits, some archival and collection support.\n\n## Experience required\n\nEvent Management / Organising,No Expertise,Retail / Customer Service, Creative,Good Communicator,Good Listener,Organised,Reliable / Dependable,Trustworthy,Happy yet professional disposition.\n\n## Training details\n\nStructured induction with continuous progression development.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nAcross South Lanarkshire,Biggar",
