                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000B7qtBYAR",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000B7qtBYAR/sports-coach",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-17",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-01",
                    "title": "Sports Coach",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nGet involved, grow your skills, and be part of a great team!\n\n📩 Contact us today: sldisabilitysport@outlook.com\n\n🏅 Join Our Coaching Team at South Lanarkshire Disability Sport!\n\nAre you a qualified coach with a passion for inclusion and sport?\n\nSouth Lanarkshire Disability Sport is looking for Level 1 (or above) coaches to support a variety of fun, active sessions for children and adults with disabilities across the area.\n\nYou’ll play a key role in delivering safe, engaging sessions in sports like football, athletics, swimming, boccia and more.\nIt’s a brilliant opportunity to develop your coaching experience, make connections, and most importantly — make a difference.\n\nWe’re looking for:\n✔ A Level 1 coaching qualification (or higher)\n✔ Great communication skills\n✔ A positive, supportive attitude\n\nOur weekly sessions take place on Friday evenings, 5-7pm, at Alistair McCoist Sport Centre, East Kilbride!\n\nIf you're up for a rewarding challenge and want to be part of a fantastic team, we’d love to hear from you!\n\nGet in touch on South Lanarkshire Disability Sport Social Media platforms, or email the team at SLDisabilitysport@outlook.com to find out more or apply.\n\n## Experience required\n\nSports Coaching, Good Communicator,Open minded,Team Player,\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire Yes\nAcross South Lanarkshire,East Kilbride\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nTravel expenses paid.",
