        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000eVbabYAC",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000eVbabYAC/barnardos",
            "name": "Barnardos",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/Barnardos",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000AXCnpYAH",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000AXCnpYAH/retail-volunteer-various-glasgow-stores",
                    "publishStart": "2025-06-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-24",
                    "title": "Retail Volunteer – Various Glasgow Stores",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nRetail Volunteer – Various Glasgow Stores\n\n## Description\n\n<p><strong>Join Our Vibrant Volunteer Team</strong></p>\n\n<p>Our amazing team of vibrant and diverse volunteers helps us run over 600 shops across the UK. These shops sell a fantastic range of donated and new goods, raising vital funds to support disadvantaged children, young people and families.</p>\n\n<p>Our retail stores are the face of our charity on the high street and in local communities. Volunteering with us means being part of something meaningful while making a real difference.</p>\n\n<p><strong>What You&#39;ll Be Doing</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Sorting and preparing donated items for sale</li>\n\t<li>Steaming, pricing, tagging, and displaying stock</li>\n\t<li>Creating eye-catching displays to attract customers</li>\n\t<li>Assisting on the till (full training provided)</li>\n\t<li>Keeping the shop clean, organised, and welcoming</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>We receive loads of amazing stock every week, and your help ensures it&rsquo;s ready for sale. Making sure the shop looks fantastic is a big part of what we do. You&rsquo;ll also be a friendly face for our customers, helping create a warm and inclusive shopping experience.</p>\n\n<p><strong>How We Support You</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>A full <strong>induction and training package</strong> to help you feel confident in your role</li>\n\t<li>Ongoing support and supervision from your <strong>dedicated shop manager or volunteer coordinator</strong></li>\n\t<li>A friendly team environment where questions are always welcome</li>\n\t<li>Access to our <strong>Volunteer Handbook</strong>, policies, and online learning portal</li>\n\t<li>Regular check-ins to make sure you&#39;re getting the most from your experience</li>\n\t<li>Opportunities to explore other volunteering roles or additional responsibilities if you wish</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>What We Offer You</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><strong>20% volunteer discount</strong> across all Barnardo&rsquo;s shops</li>\n\t<li><strong>Flexible shifts</strong> that work around your availability</li>\n\t<li><strong>Certificated online training</strong> in areas such as Health &amp; Safety and Data Protection</li>\n\t<li><strong>Access to our Wellbeing Hub</strong> for mental health and personal support</li>\n\t<li>A supportive, inclusive environment where everyone is valued</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Skills You&rsquo;ll Gain</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Customer service and retail experience</li>\n\t<li>Communication and teamwork skills</li>\n\t<li>Time management and problem-solving</li>\n\t<li>Experience with handling stock and operating tills</li>\n\t<li>Confidence and social interaction in a community setting</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>How to Apply:</strong><br />\nIf you&#39;re interested, please click the &lsquo;apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will then be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone call. If you have not heard back after 5 working days, the first step is to contact the organisation with the contact details provided. You could also check your junk/spam folder on your emails, just in case the response is there. If that doesn&rsquo;t work out, then please feel free to contact Volunteer Glasgow on info@volunteerglasgow.org.</p>\n\n<div style=\"margin-bottom:11px; text-align:center\">\n<hr /></div>\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Experience? No Problem!\nThere are no set skills required to volunteer with us. All we ask is that you’re friendly, willing to learn, and passionate about the work Barnardo’s does. We’ll provide all the training and support you need.\n\n## Travel details\n\nBy Subway\nGlasgow Subway (Inner/Outer Circle): Catch the subway from Buchanan Street or St Enoch toward Govan. Get off at Govan station, which is right next to the shopping centre—just a 2-minute walk\n\nMultiple First Glasgow and Stagecoach routes operate frequent services:\nBus numbers 3, 23, 26, 34, 49, 90, 121, 189, X19:\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses to and from the shop can be reimbursed, with prior agreement from the shop manager, to ensure volunteers are not out of pocket.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000AXCnpYAH#role",
