        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000eZtRMYA0",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000eZtRMYA0/marie-curie",
            "name": "Marie Curie",
            "website": "https://opportunities.volunteerglasgow.org/profile/httpswwwmariecurieorgukget-involved",
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HpDcXYAV",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HpDcXYAV/retail-assistant-shawlands-store",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-28",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-24",
                    "title": "Retail Assistant - Shawlands Store",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nRetail Assistant - Shawlands Store\n\n## Description\n\nJoin Our Team at the Marie Curie Store in Shawlands Glasgow!&nbsp;\n\nAre you passionate about making a difference in your community? Our Marie Curie charity shop in Shawlands&nbsp;is looking for enthusiastic volunteers aged 14 and over to join our vibrant team. By donating your time, you&#39;ll help us raise crucial funds that support our nurses in providing care to terminally ill people and their families.&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\nWhy Volunteer with Us?&nbsp;\n\nOur charity shops thrive on the generosity of the public, who donate a wide variety of items, from clothes and homeware to books, CDs, and DVDs. As a volunteer, you&#39;ll play a vital role in ensuring we offer high-quality items at affordable prices, making a real difference in the lives of those we support.&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\nWhat You&#39;ll Do:&nbsp;\n\nTreasure Hunting:?Dive into donations to uncover hidden gems and high-quality brands.&nbsp;\n\nPreparation:?Check, hang, steam, size, and price items to get them ready for sale.&nbsp;\n\nCustomer Service:?Engage with shoppers on the shop floor, providing excellent service and creating a welcoming atmosphere.&nbsp;\n\nTill Operation:?Handle transactions and assist customers with their purchases.&nbsp;\n\nHousekeeping:?Help maintain a clean and tidy shop, ensuring a pleasant shopping experience for everyone.&nbsp;\n\nWhat We Offer:&nbsp;\n\nA Friendly Team:?Join a supportive and passionate group of volunteers who share your commitment to making a difference.&nbsp;\n\nSkill Development:?Gain valuable retail and customer service experience that can enhance your CV.&nbsp;\n\nFlexible Hours:?Volunteer at times that suit your schedule, whether you can give a few hours a week or more.&nbsp;\n\nMake a Difference:?Know that your efforts are directly helping to provide essential care and support to those in need.&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\nHow to Get Involved:&nbsp;\n\nYoung Volunteers\n\nPlease note: A signed&nbsp;Parent/Guardian Consent Form&nbsp;is required as part of the application process for all volunteers aged 14-17 years&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\nFor more information or if you have any questions about this volunteer role, please contact us at?recruitment@mariecurie.org.uk. We can&#39;t wait to welcome you to our team and work together to support a cause that truly matter.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\nIf you haven&#39;t heard from us within five working days, please contact the organisation using the details provided on this page. It&#39;s also worth checking your junk or spam folder in case our response has been filtered. If you still haven&#39;t received a reply, you can contact Volunteer Glasgow at&nbsp;info@volunteerglasgow.org&nbsp;for further assistance.\n\n## Experience required\n\nApproachable and patient attitude\nPunctual and professional\n\n## Travel details\n\nregular train and bus links to Shawlands from city centre and surrounding areas",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
