                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HX4r3YAD",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HX4r3YAD/marie-curie-volunteer-hairdresserbarber-glasgow-hospice",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-30",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-27",
                    "title": "Marie Curie - Volunteer - Hairdresser/Barber - Glasgow Hospice",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nMarie Curie - Volunteer - Hairdresser/Barber - Glasgow Hospice\n\n## Description\n\nAt our hospices, we aim to provide the best possible service to those requiring end of life care.&nbsp; We are looking for a qualified hairdresser or barber to pamper our patients, giving them time and attention and making a difference to their lives.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\nYour role will include some of, but is not restricted to, the following tasks:\n\n\n\tProvide a hairdressing service to patients at the hospice&nbsp;\n\tConsult staff about which patients would like to use the service&nbsp;\n\tChat to patients&nbsp;\n\tKeep the hairdressing room clean and tidy&nbsp;\n\tLet staff know about any issues concerning patients&rsquo; well-being&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\tHelp with other related tasks when necessary&nbsp;\n\n\nFor more information or if you have any questions regarding this volunteer role, please contact the Volunteering Operations Centre at recruitment@mariecurie.org.uk or Sheila Morrison Morrison Wellbeing Therapy Lead at sheila.morrison@mariecurie.org.uk&nbsp;\n\nIf you are interested, please click the &lsquo;Apply&rsquo; button below (available when logged in and registered). You will be contacted by the coordinator by email or phone. If you don&rsquo;t hear back within 5 working days, please contact the organisation using the provided details. Check your junk/spam folder for responses. If there&rsquo;s still no response, contact Volunteer Glasgow at info@volunteerglasgow.org.\n\n## Experience required\n\n-Qualified hairdresser or barber with relevant experience.\n-Friendly, compassionate and empathetic approach to working with patients.\n-Ability to maintain a clean, safe and organised working environment.\n-Reliable, professional and able to work respectfully with hospice staff.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe hospice is easily accessible by public transport and car.\n\nBy bus: Services 29, 31, 45, 45A, 88 and 371 stop close to the hospice. Route 29 stops at the main entrance to Stobhill Hospital (approximately a 5-minute walk), while routes 31, 45, 45A, 88 and 371 stop on Balgrayhill Road (around a 10-minute walk).\nBy train: The nearest station is Springburn, approximately a 30-minute walk or a short taxi journey from the hospice.\nBy car: Limited on-site parking is available, including accessible parking spaces.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReimbursement for travel and reasonable out-of-pocket expenses.",
