                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HqqdRYAR/tidy-up-squad-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-06",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-02",
                    "title": "Tidy Up Squad Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nOur project is to create one of Scotland’s largest murals through the Alloway Railway Tunnel. \r\nWe want to transform an old, dilapidated tunnel that has been defaced with graffiti into a safe, inspiring place, with a beautiful hand painted mural by one of the UK’s top muralists and visionaries. Chris Rutterford. \r\n\r\nhttps://www.allowaytunnel.org.uk/\r\n\r\n\r\nMain duties:\r\nWe are currently establishing a Tidy up Squad who will predominantly work in the garden at the entrance to the tunnel, and looking to recruit volunteers who can help us to plant and maintain this area.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe volunteer would be given initial training to enable them to feel comfortable in the role.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nBus or train to Ayr then bus from Ayr to Alloway – expenses paid",
