        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000HkeS6YAJ",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000HkeS6YAJ/newfield-community-group-scio",
            "name": "Newfield Community Group SCIO",
            "description": "We are a community charity that provides a base and hosts the coming together of other 3rd sector organisations to work within the East of Dundee supported by a community kitchen/hub run by the volunteers. The charity benefits from a full-time community coordinator who is employed by the local GP practice to serve the charity. We support various activities and workshops to run from the base in Whitfield.",
            "charityRegistration": [
                {
                    "registrar": "https://www.oscr.org.uk",
                    "registrationNumber": "SC052862"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FR3pBYAT",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FR3pBYAT/trustee",
                    "publishStart": "2026-02-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Trustee",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nThinking about become a trustee? Can you help to make a difference in your local community?\n\n## Description\n\nWe are recruiting trustees for Newfield Community Group. Are you passionate about making a difference in your local community? Newfield Community Group is seeking dedicated and skilled individuals to join our Board of Trustees. This is a unique opportunity to contribute your expertise, shape our strategic direction, and help us achieve our mission.\r\n\r\nAbout the Role\r\nAs a Trustee, you will play a crucial role in ensuring strong governance, financial sustainability and impactful delivery of our charitable objectives. Our mission is to improve the mental health and wellbeing of those living in the community by working with Third Sector organisations from our base in Whitfield.\r\n\r\nWho We’re Looking For\r\nWe welcome applicants with experience in governance, finance, fundraising, legal compliance,community engagement or organisational development. Above all, a commitment to our vision and values is essential. We welcome those who may have lived experience.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities\r\nProvide strategic leadership and oversight\r\nEnsure compliance with legal and financial obligations\r\nSupport fundraising and income generation efforts\r\nAct as an ambassador for the charity\r\nAttend quarterly Board meetings and relevant committees.\r\n\r\nPlease send a CV and a brief statement outlining your interest and relevant experience to Rebecca.Forrester@nhs.scot.\n\n## Experience required\n\nStrong communication and decision-making skills\r\nIntegrity, independence and sound judgement\r\nCollaborative and inclusive approach\r\nWillingness to dedicate time and effort to the role.\n\n## Training details\n\nWe are signed up to ‘ trustee-connect’ which offers regular training.\n\n## Travel details\n\nDundee east end . Whitfield .\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nPlease note - No expenses are payable with this opportunity.",
