        {
            "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Organisation/001QD00000Hnu4AYAR",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/organisations/001QD00000Hnu4AYAR/the-glebe-community-garden",
            "name": "The Glebe Community Garden",
            "description": "The Glebe is a Community Garden run by a small committee and volunteers to improve the health and well-being of individuals coping with Mental Health issues and to support people to regain their confidence with a health diagnosis.",
            "cause": [
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/MentalHealth",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Mental Health"
                },
                {
                    "@id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Taxonomy/Cause/CommunityEngagement",
                    "skos:prefLabel": "Community Engagement"
                }
            ],
            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HvqhdYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000HvqhdYAB/volunteer-community-gardener-helper",
                    "publishStart": "2026-08-24",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-22",
                    "title": "Volunteer Community Gardener Helper",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe role involves helping to maintain our Community Garden and working with individuals/volunteers to show them how to plant/grow/harvest fruit & vegetables to maintain a healthier lifestyle.\r\n\r\nCommunity Garden Role is:\r\n\r\n•\tWeeding & watering the garden and polytunnels.\r\n•\tPlanting seeds/seedlings to grow in the garden beds/polytunnels.\r\n•\tErecting supports/trellising for the plants.\r\n•\tHarvesting the fruit/vegetables for people who attend the garden plus the volunteers and the Foodbank.\r\n•\tTaking care of the composting areas and rotating compost.\r\n•\tCleaning the shed area and making sure all the tools/equipment are cleaned put away safely.\r\n•\tTo help maintain the fruit bed area.\r\n•\tTo help maintain the pond area.\r\n•\tBeing part of the team and participating in the running of the garden and contributing your knowledge and skills to benefit the garden.\r\n•\tHelp the team find sources of fundraising to improve and continue the community garden.\r\n\r\nThe volunteer role does not have to involve all of these jobs, it is whatever you are capable of doing.\r\n\r\nThe main aspect is to come and enjoy the community garden, socialise with other volunteers and the team and you get to take home freshly picked produce to maintain a healthy lifestyle.\n\n## Experience required\n\nRole is open to beginners, no experience is required.\n\n## Training details\n\nTraining provided:\r\n\r\n•\tHow to grow/plant/harvest fruit & vegetables.\r\n•\tHow to fertilise the produce grown and soil maintenance\r\n•\tHow to collect seeds to reuse.\r\n•\tHow to build frames/structures for the plants.\r\n•\tHow to maintain the compost beds and rotate the compost.\r\n•\tHow to use the produce harvested to make jams/chutney.\r\n•\tHow to dehydrate the harvested produce.\r\n•\tMeal ideas/recipes from the produce harvested.\r\n•\tHow to reduce your carbon footprint and how to recycle/reuse items.\r\n\r\nVolunteer will be supported whilst attending the garden by members of the team/committee if any issues occur.\n\n## Frequency commitment details\n\nVolunteers can access the named contact if they cannot attend the garden or if they have concerns whilst at the garden.\r\nContact can be made in person or via phone.\r\nVolunteers are supported every time they attend the community garden by all of the team members.\n\n## Travel details\n\nVolunteers travel to the community garden individually by their own transport or public transport/or on foot.\r\nSome volunteers share transport with other volunteers to attend the garden.\r\nParking is available at the front of the house, before you walk to the community garden behind the house or you can park further down the road or in Peebles High Street and walk to the Community Garden from there.\r\n\r\nVolunteering hours 10.00am - 2.00pm\n\n## Taster details\n\nVolunteers can attend and see what is involved in the everyday running of the Community Garden and what type of role they would like to do if they decide to come back and get involved at our Community Garden.\r\n\r\nThe volunteer will be given time to decide whether they would like to come and work in the Community Garden after they visit or can let us know on the day if they wish to come back and volunteer.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000HvqhdYAB#role",
                        "type": "Role",
