                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000Hm5hxYAB",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000Hm5hxYAB/catering-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-07-16",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-01-14",
                    "title": "Catering Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe advancement of public participation in sport and in citizenship or community development.\r\nThe advancement of education and improving the lives of people for whom the facility and activities are\r\nintended.\r\nDescribe the volunteering Opportunity\r\nThe complex has a kitchen facility to provide hot and cold food and drinks when football matches are\r\nplayed at the stadium and when other lets of the pitch are taken.\r\nMatches are played mainly on Saturdays and Sundays when there is both men's and women's games.\r\nWe are looking for people who are willing to help out and provide refreshments for all the visitors to the\r\nfacility, who are friendly and customer focussed so that service is excellent and enjoyable.\r\nThis is an opportunity to become part of the match day team and experience working in a modern facility.\n\n## Experience required\n\nWe are looking for enthusiastic people who enjoy the retail environment and dealing with customers.\r\nThis may appeal to students who plan to have a career in hospitality and need some hands on experience\r\nto complement their studies. The opportunity allows input of ideas so that we listen to customers and\r\nprovide what they need as well as being able to test out new products.\r\nAnyone with relevant experience will be welcome.\n\n## Training details\n\nThe Faculty Manager will explain the layout, risk assessments and how we operate. There will be debrief\r\nsessions so that we keep improving.\n\n## Travel details\n\nkirkintilloch",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
