            "activity": [
                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000FfP6fYAF",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000FfP6fYAF/unit-helper",
                    "publishStart": "2026-03-02",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-02-01",
                    "title": "Unit Helper",
                    "description": "## Summary\n\nDiscover the joy of being a Brownies unit helper at 20th B Brownies in Broughty Ferry. Unit helpers help girls with arts, crafts, and games, building their confidence along the way.\n\n## Description\n\nBrownies is aimed at girls aged 7-10 for nonstop fun, learning and adventure.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for a person/people to come and help with the 20th B Brownies Unit in Broughty Ferry. As a Unit Helper, you will be hands on with the running of a unit meeting such as setting up activities,supervising girls when undertaking activities, and helping them when they have questions or need assistance completing an activity. In this school year alone, we’ve had a visit from Guide Dogs, had a Halloween party, visited the cinema,completed many crafts, and played countless games.\r\n\r\nYou’ll discover the joy of being a unit helper – helping girls do things for the first time, encouraging teamwork, and building their confidence and self-esteem.The unit is very friendly and full of enthusiasm. You’re guaranteed to leave every unit meeting with a smile on your face!\n\n## Experience required\n\ninterest in some of the following would be beneficial:\r\n\r\n• Arts and crafts\r\n• Activities such as games, quizzes\r\n• Camping/walking/the outdoors\r\n• Mental wellbeing\r\n• Physical wellbeing\r\n• Music/drama\r\n• Children’s education and literacy\r\n• Learning new skills e.g. building, baking\r\n\r\nHaving an interest in working with young people and guiding them to do their best is essential.\n\n## Training details\n\nVolunteers must complete child safeguarding training within 40 days of starting in the role. First Aid training is also available.\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nReasonable travel expenses and expenses incurred for unit activities (e.g. purchasing craft items as agreed with Unit Leader) is reimbursed.",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
