                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BVxQTYA1",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BVxQTYA1/advice-line-know-your-rights-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-09-07",
                    "publishEnd": "2027-03-01",
                    "title": "Advice Line Know Your Rights Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nThe Chest Heart & Stroke Scotland (CHSS) refreshed No Life Half Lived strategy is to ensure that we can be there for anyone who needs us. Our vision is to help shape a Scotland where people with our conditions can live their lives well. Full Lives, with the right support, at the right time, and in the right place.\r\n\r\nThe Advice Line team offer a single point of access to our services and offer support to people to manage their condition and live life to the full.\r\n\r\nJoin our Advice Line team providing telephone and/or video call support to people affected by chest or heart conditions, stroke or Long Covid, to gain information about their rights living with a long-term condition to feel better prepared to make choices about their health care.\r\n\r\nYou will have the opportunity to meet new people and make a real difference to those impacted by one or more of our conditions.\n\n## Experience required\n\nReliable and committed\r\nExcellent listening and communication skills\r\nPatient & empathic qualities\r\nEncouraging & Supportive\r\nAbility to work independently with guidance and support\r\nRespectful of the opinions of others\r\nUnderstand the need for confidentiality\r\nAbility to maintain boundaries\r\nComfortable to use IT equipment and databases for the purpose of the role (training and support will be provided)\r\nAbility to commit to initial and ongoing training and development\r\nAmbassador for Chest, Heart & Stroke Scotland",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
                    "role": {
                        "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD00000BVxQTYA1#role",
                        "type": "Role",
                        "title": "Advice Line Know Your Rights Volunteer",
                        "description": "Reliable and committed\r\nExcellent listening and communication skills\r\nPatient & empathic qualities\r\nEncouraging & Supportive\r\nAbility to work independently with guidance and support\r\nRespectful of the opinions of others\r\nUnderstand the need for confidentiality\r\nAbility to maintain boundaries\r\nComfortable to use IT equipment and databases for the purpose of the role (training and support will be provided)\r\nAbility to commit to initial and ongoing training and development\r\nAmbassador for Chest, Heart & Stroke Scotland",
                        "applyLink": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD00000BVxQTYA1/advice-line-know-your-rights-volunteer?#modal_register_a0gQD00000BVxQTYA1",
                        "allowsRemoteParticipation": false
