                {
                    "id": "https://data.volunteer.scot/Activity/a0gQD000008AOFnYAO",
                    "type": "Activity",
                    "dc:source": "https://volunteer.scot/search/a0gQD000008AOFnYAO/mum-volunteer",
                    "publishStart": "2026-06-11",
                    "publishEnd": "2026-12-04",
                    "title": "Mum Volunteer",
                    "description": "## Description\n\nIf you are expecting a baby or have a little one under 5, and are living in Lanarkshire, join the Volunteer and Wellbeing Programme for Mums at Swaddle. Volunteer and meet other mums in a fun and supportive space. Swaddle offers weekly volunteering sessions in the Hamilton shop where you can connect with other mums at a similar stage to you, with the space you need to take a pause from motherhood and support your mental health. Swaddle offers free social and wellbeing activities, a store discount, travel expenses and 1:1 support from a project leader. You will be helping with ironing, bundling, serving customers, tidying and sorting donations.\n\n## Experience required\n\nNo Expertise, Caring,\n\n## Training details\n\nA tailored and flexible induction and training.\n\n## Travel details\n\nThe opportunity takes place at multiple location across South Lanarkshire \nHamilton\n\n## Travel expenses\n\nLocal Bus or Train Expenses to attend Volunteering",
                    "requiresEmergencyParticipation": false,
